    56: "אָבַל (ʼâbal | aw-bal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to bewail\nKJV: lament, mourn.\n\nCognate Group: H57 (mourn), H60 (mourning), H56 (lament)\nGreek Equivalents: G2354 θρηνέω, G2400 ἰδού, G3996 πενθέω, G4133 πλήν, G4727 στενάζω",
    57: "אָבֵל (ʼâbêl | aw-bale')\n\nDerivation: from H56 אָבַל\nStrong's: lamenting\nKJV: mourn(-er, -ing).\n\nCognate Group: H57 (mourn), H60 (mourning), H56 (lament)\nGreek Equivalents: G93 ἀδικία, G93 ἀδικία, G94 ἄδικος, G458 ἀνομία, G1342 δίκαιος, G3076 λυπέω, G3900 παράπτωμα, G4835 συμπαθής",
    58: "אָבֵל (ʼâbêl | aw-bale')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (meaning to be grassy)\nStrong's: a meadow\nKJV: plain. Compare also the proper names beginning with Abel-.\n\nCognate Group: H59 (Abel), H65 (Abel-meholah), H62 (Abel-beth-maachah), H67 (Abel-mizraim), H64 (plain of the vineyards), H58 (plain), H66 (Abel-maim), H63 (Abelshittim)\nGreek Equivalents: G9 Ἀβιληνή",
