    68: "אֶבֶן (ʼeben | eh'-ben)\n\nDerivation: from the root of H1129 בָּנָה through the meaning to build\nStrong's: a stone\nKJV: [phrase] carbuncle, [phrase] mason, [phrase] plummet, (chalk-, hail-, head-, sling-) stone(-ny), (divers) weight(-s).\n\nCognate Group: H72 (Ebenezer), H70 (wheel), H68 (carbuncle)\nGreek Equivalents: G2729 κατισχύω, G3035 λίθινος, G3037 λίθος, G3398 μικρός, G5464 χάλαζα",
    69: "אֶבֶן (ʼeben | eh'-ben)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H68 אֶבֶן \nStrong's: a stone\nKJV: stone.\n\nCognate Group: H104 (letter), H116 (now), H149 (diligently), H69 (stone), H147 (threshingfloor), H2 (father), H148 (judge), H144 (Adar)",
