    72: "אֶבֶן הָעֵזֶר (ʼEben hâ-ʻÊzer | eh'-ben haw-e'-zer)\n\nDerivation: from H68 אֶבֶן and H5828 עֵזֶר with the article inserted; stone of the help\nStrong's: Eben-ha-Ezer, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Ebenezer.\n\nCognate Group: H72 (Ebenezer), H70 (wheel), H68 (carbuncle)",
