    81: "אֲבָקָה (ʼăbâqâh | ab-aw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H80 אָבָק \nStrong's: light particles (as volatile)\nKJV: powder.\n\nCognate Group: H79 (wrestle), H81 (powder), H80 (dust)",
    82: "אָבַר (ʼâbar | aw-bar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to soar\nKJV: fly.\n\nCognate Group: H82 (fly), H84 (feather), H46 (mighty), H47 (angel), H83 (wing)",
    83: "אֵבֶר (ʼêber | ay-ber')\n\nDerivation: from H82 אָבַר\nStrong's: a pinion\nKJV: (long-) wing(-ed).\n\nCognate Group: H82 (fly), H84 (feather), H46 (mighty), H47 (angel), H83 (wing)",
    84: "אֶבְרָה (ʼebrâh | eb-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H83 אֵבֶר \nStrong's: a pinion\nKJV: feather, wing.\n\nCognate Group: H82 (fly), H84 (feather), H46 (mighty), H47 (angel), H83 (wing)",
    85: "אַבְרָהָם (ʼAbrâhâm | ab-raw-hawm')\n\nDerivation: contracted from H1 אָב and an unused root (probably meaning to be populous); father of a multitude\nStrong's: Abraham, the later name of Abram\nKJV: Abraham.\n\nCognate Group: H44 (Abiezer), H21 (Abi), H43 (Ebiasaph), H23 (Abiasaph), H372 (Jeezer), H42 (Abinoam), H36 (Abitub), H51 (Abishur), H32 (Abihail), H49 (Abishag), H31 (Abihud), H53 (Abishalom), H27 (Abidan), H45 (Abialbon), H40 (Abimelech), H38 (Abijam), H30 (Abihu), H28 (Abida), H26 (Abigal), H54 (Abiathar), H85 (Abraham), H1 (chief), H33 (Abiezrite), H52 (Abishai), H373 (Jezerite), H39 (Abimael), H22 (Abiel), H37 (Abital), H48 (Abiram), H87 (Abram), H41 (Abinadab), H29 (Abiah), H74 (Abner), H50 (Abishua)\nGreek Equivalents: G11 Ἀβραάμ",
