    87: "אַבְרָם (ʼAbrâm | ab-rawm')\n\nDerivation: contracted from H48 אֲבִירָם ; high father\nStrong's: Abram, the original name of Abraham\nKJV: Abram.\n\nCognate Group: H44 (Abiezer), H21 (Abi), H43 (Ebiasaph), H23 (Abiasaph), H372 (Jeezer), H42 (Abinoam), H36 (Abitub), H51 (Abishur), H32 (Abihail), H49 (Abishag), H31 (Abihud), H53 (Abishalom), H27 (Abidan), H45 (Abialbon), H40 (Abimelech), H38 (Abijam), H30 (Abihu), H28 (Abida), H26 (Abigal), H54 (Abiathar), H85 (Abraham), H1 (chief), H33 (Abiezrite), H52 (Abishai), H373 (Jezerite), H39 (Abimael), H22 (Abiel), H37 (Abital), H48 (Abiram), H87 (Abram), H41 (Abinadab), H29 (Abiah), H74 (Abner), H50 (Abishua)",
    88: "אֹבֹת (ʼôbôth | o-both')\n\nDerivation: plural of H178 אֹוב ; water-skins\nStrong's: Oboth, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Oboth.\n\nCognate Group: H178 (bottle), H88 (Oboth)",
    89: "אָגֵא (ʼÂgêʼ | aw-gay')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation (compare H90 אֲגַג)\nStrong's: Age, an Israelite\nKJV: Agee.\n\nCognate Group: H91 (Agagite), H90 (Agag), H89 (Agee)",
