    92: "אֲגֻדָּה (ʼăguddâh | ag-ood-daw')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of an unused root (meaning to bind)\nStrong's: a band, bundle, knot, or arch\nKJV: bunch, burden, troop.\n\nCognate Group: H92 (bunch), H93 (nut)\nGreek Equivalents: G1197 δέσμη, G1860 ἐπαγγελία",
    93: "אֱגֹוז (ʼĕgôwz | eg-oze')\n\nDerivation: prob of Persian origin\nStrong's: a nut\nKJV: nut.\n\nCognate Group: H92 (bunch), H93 (nut)",
    94: "אָגוּר (ʼÂgûwr | aw-goor')\n\nDerivation: passive participle of H103 אָגַר ; gathered (i.e. received among the sages)\nStrong's: Agur, a fanciful name for Solomon\nKJV: Agur.\n\nCognate Group: H107 (letter), H95 (piece silver), H94 (Agur)",
    95: "אֲגֹורָה (ʼăgôwrâh | ag-o-raw')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H94 אָגוּר\nStrong's: properly, something gathered, i.e. perhaps a grain or berry; used only of a small (silver) coin\nKJV: piece (of) silver.\n\nCognate Group: H107 (letter), H95 (piece silver), H94 (Agur)",
    96: "אֶגֶל (ʼegel | eh'-ghel)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (meaning to flow down or together as drops)\nStrong's: a reservoir\nKJV: drop.\n\nCognate Group: H97 (Eglaim), H96 (drop)",
    97: "אֶגְלַיִם (ʼEglayim | eg-lah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: dual of H96 אֶגֶל .; a double pond\nStrong's: Eglajim, a place in Moab\nKJV: Eglaim.\n\nCognate Group: H97 (Eglaim), H96 (drop)",
    98: "אֲגַם (ʼăgam | ag-am')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (meaning to collect as water)\nStrong's: a marsh; hence a rush (as growing in swamps); hence a stockade of reeds\nKJV: pond, pool, standing (water).\n\nCognate Group: H100 (bulrush), H98 (pond), H99 (pond)\nGreek Equivalents: G3041 λίμνη",
