    114: "אַדֹּון (ʼAddôwn | ad-done')\n\nDerivation: probably intensive for H113 אָדֹון ; powerful\nStrong's: Addon, apparently an Israelite\nKJV: Addon.\n\nCognate Group: H141 (Adoniram), H139 (Adonizedec), H135 (Addan), H138 (Adonijah), H113 (lord), H151 (Adoram), H114 (Addon), H140 (Adonikam), H137 (Adonibezek), H136 (Lord), H134 (foundation)",
    115: "אֲדֹורַיִם (ʼĂdôwrayim | ad-o-rah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: dual from H142 אָדַר (in the sense of eminence); double mound\nStrong's: Adorajim, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Adoraim.\n\nCognate Group: H155 (garment), H152 (Adrammelech), H143 (Adar), H146 (Addar), H145 (goodly), H117 (excellent), H142 (glorious), H115 (Adoraim)",
    116: "אֱדַיִן (ʼĕdayin | ed-ah'-yin)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: then (of time)\nKJV: now, that time, then.\n\nCognate Group: H104 (letter), H116 (now), H149 (diligently), H69 (stone), H147 (threshingfloor), H2 (father), H148 (judge), H144 (Adar)",
    117: "אַדִּיר (ʼaddîyr | ad-deer')\n\nDerivation: from H142 אָדַר\nStrong's: wide or (generally) large; figuratively, powerful\nKJV: excellent, famous, gallant, glorious, goodly, lordly, mighty(-ier one), noble, principal, worthy.\n\nCognate Group: H155 (garment), H152 (Adrammelech), H143 (Adar), H146 (Addar), H145 (goodly), H117 (excellent), H142 (glorious), H115 (Adoraim)\nGreek Equivalents: G1413 δυνάστης, G1415 δυνατός, G2298 θαυμαστός, G2478 ἰσχυρός, G2479 ἰσχύς, G2900 κραταιός, G3173 μέγας, G3175 μεγιστᾶνες, G4731 στερεός, G5242 ὑπερέχω",
    118: "אֲדַלְיָא (ʼĂdalyâʼ | ad-al-yaw')\n\nDerivation: of Persian derivation\nStrong's: Adalja, a son of Haman\nKJV: Adalia.\n\nCognate Group: H118 (Adalia), H112 (Iddo)",
    119: "אָדַם (ʼâdam | aw-dam')\n\nDerivation: to show blood (in the face), i.e.\nStrong's: flush or turn rosy\nKJV: be (dyed, made) red (ruddy).\n\nCognate Group: H132 (red), H130 (Edomite), H133 (Admatha), H122 (red), H123 (Edom), H124 (sardius), H726 (Syrian), H119 (be made red), H125 (reddish)\nGreek Equivalents: G4448 πυρόω",
    120: "אָדָם (ʼâdâm | aw-dawm')\n\nDerivation: from H119 אָדַם\nStrong's: ruddy i.e. a human being (an individual or the species, mankind, etc.)\nKJV: [idiom] another, [phrase] hypocrite, [phrase] common sort, [idiom] low, man (mean, of low degree), person.\n\nCognate Group: H126 (Admah), H121 (Adam), H128 (Adamah), H127 (country), H129 (Adami), H120 ([idiom] another)\nGreek Equivalents: G435 ἀνήρ, G444 ἄνθρωπος, G1538 ἕκαστος, G2349 θνητός, G2992 λαός",
    121: "אָדָם (ʼÂdâm | aw-dawm')\n\nDerivation: the same as H120 אָדָם\nStrong's: Adam the name of the first man, also of a place in Palestine\nKJV: Adam.\n\nCognate Group: H126 (Admah), H121 (Adam), H128 (Adamah), H127 (country), H129 (Adami), H120 ([idiom] another)\nGreek Equivalents: G76 Ἀδάμ",
    122: "אָדֹם (ʼâdôm | aw-dome')\n\nDerivation: from H119 אָדַם\nStrong's: rosy\nKJV: red, ruddy.\n\nCognate Group: H132 (red), H130 (Edomite), H133 (Admatha), H122 (red), H123 (Edom), H124 (sardius), H726 (Syrian), H119 (be made red), H125 (reddish)",
    123: "אֱדֹם (ʼĔdôm | ed-ome')\n\nDerivation: or (fully) אֱדֹום ; from H122 אָדֹם ; red (see Genesis 25:25)\nStrong's: Edom, the elder twin-brother of Jacob; hence the region (Idumaea) occupied by him\nKJV: Edom, Edomites, Idumea.\n\nCognate Group: H132 (red), H130 (Edomite), H133 (Admatha), H122 (red), H123 (Edom), H124 (sardius), H726 (Syrian), H119 (be made red), H125 (reddish)\nGreek Equivalents: G2063 ἐρυθρός, G4450 πυῤῥός, G2401 Ἰδουμαία",
    124: "אֹדֶם (ʼôdem | o'-dem)\n\nDerivation: from H119 אָדַם\nStrong's: redness, i.e. the ruby, garnet, or some other red gem\nKJV: sardius.\n\nCognate Group: H132 (red), H130 (Edomite), H133 (Admatha), H122 (red), H123 (Edom), H124 (sardius), H726 (Syrian), H119 (be made red), H125 (reddish)\nGreek Equivalents: G4556 σάρδιος",
