    168: "אֹהֶל (ʼôhel | o'-hel)\n\nDerivation: from H166 אָהַל\nStrong's: a tent (as clearly conspicuous from a distance)\nKJV: covering, (dwelling) (place), home, tabernacle, tent.\n\nCognate Group: H171 (Aholiab), H167 (pitch a tent), H173 (Aholibamah), H169 (Ohel), H168 (covering), H172 (Aholibah), H170 (Aholah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2646 κατάλυμα, G3624 οἶκος, G4633 σκηνή, G4638 σκήνωμα",
