    170: "אׇהֳלָה (ʼOhŏlâh | o-hol-aw')\n\nDerivation: in form a feminine of H168 אֹהֶל, but in fact for אׇהֳלָהּ; from H168 אֹהֶל ; her tent (i.e. idolatrous sanctuary)\nStrong's: Oholah, a symbolic name for Samaria\nKJV: Aholah.\n\nCognate Group: H171 (Aholiab), H167 (pitch a tent), H173 (Aholibamah), H169 (Ohel), H168 (covering), H172 (Aholibah), H170 (Aholah)",
