    172: "אׇהֳלִיבָה (ʼOhŏlîybâh | o''-hol-ee-baw')\n\nDerivation: (similarly with H170 אׇהֳלָה) for אׇהֳלִיבָהּ ; from H168 אֹהֶל ; my tent (is) in her\nStrong's: Oholibah, a symbolic name for Judah\nKJV: Aholibah.\n\nCognate Group: H171 (Aholiab), H167 (pitch a tent), H173 (Aholibamah), H169 (Ohel), H168 (covering), H172 (Aholibah), H170 (Aholah)",
