    174: "אֲהָלִים (ʼăhâlîym | a-haw-leem')\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) אֲהָלֹות (only used thus in the plural); of foreign origin\nStrong's: aloe wood (i.e. sticks)\nKJV: (tree of lign-) aloes.\n\nCognate Group: H175 (Aaron), H174 (aloes)\nGreek Equivalents: G250 ἀλόη",
    175: "אַהֲרֹון (ʼAhărôwn | a-har-one')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Aharon, the brother of Moses\nKJV: Aaron.\n\nCognate Group: H175 (Aaron), H174 (aloes)\nGreek Equivalents: G2 Ἀαρών",
    176: "אֹו (ʼôw | o)\n\nDerivation: presumed to be the 'constructive' or genitival form of אַו ; short for H185 אַוָּה\nStrong's: desire (and so probably in Proverbs 31:4); hence (by way of alternative) or, also if\nKJV: also, and, either, if, at the least, [idiom] nor, or, otherwise, then, whether.\n\nCognate Group: H177 (Uel), H176 (also)",
    177: "אוּאֵל (ʼÛwʼêl | oo-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H176 אֹו and H410 אֵל ; wish of God\nStrong's: Uel, and Israelite\nKJV: Uel.\n\nCognate Group: H177 (Uel), H176 (also)",
    178: "אֹוב (ʼôwb | obe)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H1 אָב (apparently through the idea of prattling a father's name)\nStrong's: properly, a mumble, i.e. a water skin (from its hollow sound); hence a necromancer (ventriloquist, as from a jar)\nKJV: bottle, familiar spirit.\n\nCognate Group: H178 (bottle), H88 (Oboth)\nGreek Equivalents: G1093 γῆ",
    179: "אֹובִיל (ʼôwbîyl | o-beel')\n\nDerivation: probably from H56 אָבַל ; mournful\nStrong's: Obil, an Ishmaelite\nKJV: Obil.\n\nCognate Group: H179 (Obil)",
    180: "אוּבָל (ʼûwbâl | oo-bawl')\n\nDerivation: or (shortened) אֻבָל ; from H2986 יָבַל (in the sense of H2988 יָבָל)\nStrong's: a stream\nKJV: river.\n\nCognate Group: H2986 (bring), H2991 (Ibleam), H3106 (Jubal), H3105 (river), H2989 (Jabal), H944 (food), H2988 (course), H180 (river), H2990 (wen), H8398 (habitable part), H3104 (jubile), H2981 (fruit)",
    181: "אוּד (ʼûwd | ood)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to rake together\nStrong's: a poker (for turning or gathering embers)\nKJV: (fire-) brand.\n\nCognate Group: H182 (cause), H343 (calamity), H181 (brand), H108 (mist)",
    182: "אֹודֹות (ʼôwdôwth | o-doth')\n\nDerivation: or (shortened) אֹדֹות (only thus in the plural); from the same as H181 אוּד\nStrong's: turnings (i.e. occasions); (adverb) on account of\nKJV: (be-) cause, concerning, sake.\n\nCognate Group: H182 (cause), H343 (calamity), H181 (brand), H108 (mist)",
    183: "אָוָה (ʼâvâh | aw-vaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to wish for\nKJV: covet, (greatly) desire, be desirous, long, lust (after).\n\nCognate Group: H189 (Evi), H3970 (desire), H185 (desire), H176 (also), H8378 (dainty), H183 (covet)\nGreek Equivalents: G1937 ἐπιθυμέω, G1938 ἐπιθυμητής, G1939 ἐπιθυμία",
    184: "אָוָה (ʼâvâh | aw-vaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to extend or mark out\nKJV: point out.\n\nCognate Group: H184 (point out), H186 (Uzai), H226 (mark)",
    185: "אַוָּה (ʼavvâh | av-vaw')\n\nDerivation: from H183 אָוָה\nStrong's: longing\nKJV: desire, lust after, pleasure.\n\nCognate Group: H189 (Evi), H3970 (desire), H185 (desire), H176 (also), H8378 (dainty), H183 (covet)\nGreek Equivalents: G93 ἀδικία, G1939 ἐπιθυμία",
    186: "אוּזַי (ʼÛwzay | oo-zah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: perhaps by permutation for H5813 עֻזִּי, strong\nStrong's: Uzai, an Israelite\nKJV: Uzai.\n\nCognate Group: H184 (point out), H186 (Uzai), H226 (mark)",
    187: "אוּזָל (ʼÛwzâl | oo-zawl')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Uzal, a son of Joktan\nKJV: Uzal.\n\nCognate Group: H235 (fail), H187 (Uzal), H237 (Ezel)",
    188: "אֹוי (ʼôwy | o'-ee)\n\nDerivation: probably from H183 אָוָה (in the sense of crying out after)\nStrong's: lamentation; also interjectionally Oh!\nKJV: alas, woe.\n\nCognate Group: H188 (alas), H190 (woe)",
    189: "אֱוִי (ʼĔvîy | ev-ee')\n\nDerivation: probably from H183 אָוָה ; desirous\nStrong's: Evi, a Midianitish chief\nKJV: Evi.\n\nCognate Group: H189 (Evi), H3970 (desire), H185 (desire), H176 (also), H8378 (dainty), H183 (covet)",
    190: "אֹויָה (ʼôwyâh | o-yaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H188 אֹוי \nStrong's: lamentation; also interjectionally Oh!\nKJV: woe.\n\nCognate Group: H188 (alas), H190 (woe)",
    191: "אֱוִיל (ʼĕvîyl | ev-eel')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (meaning to be perverse)\nStrong's: (figuratively) silly\nKJV: fool(-ish) (man).\n\nCognate Group: H200 (folly), H196 (foolish), H191 (fool)\nGreek Equivalents: G453 ἀνόητος, G521 ἀπαίδευτος, G765 ἀσεβής, G878 ἄφρων, G2233 ἡγέομαι, G3474 μωρός, G4312 προπετής, G5337 φαῦλος",
    192: "אֱוִיל מְרֹדַךְ (ʼĔvîyl Mᵉrôdak | ev-eel' mer-o-dak')\n\nDerivation: of Aramaic derivation and probably meaning soldier of Merodak\nStrong's: Evil-Merodak, a Babylonian king\nKJV: Evil-merodach.\n\nCognate Group: H344 (kite), H338 (wild beast of the islands), H345 (Aiah), H192 (Evil-merodach)",
    193: "אוּל (ʼûwl | ool)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to twist, i.e. (by implication) be strong\nStrong's: the body (as being rolled together); also powerful\nKJV: mighty, strength.\n\nCognate Group: H365 (hind), H355 (hind), H425 (Elah), H198 (Ulam), H440 (Elonites), H354 (hart), H357 (Aijalon), H362 (Elim), H197 (porch), H195 (Ulai), H356 (Elon), H193 (mighty), H361 (arch), H424 (elm), H364 (El-paran), H352 (mighty), H359 (Elath), H436 (plain)",
    194: "אוּלַי (ʼûwlay | oo-lah'ee)\n\nDerivation: or (shortened) אֻלַי; from H176 אֹו\nStrong's: if not; hence perhaps\nKJV: if so be, may be, peradventure, unless.\n\nCognate Group: H194 (if so be)\nGreek Equivalents: G2481 ἴσως",
    195: "אוּלַי (ʼÛwlay | oo-lah'ee)\n\nDerivation: of Persian derivation\nStrong's: the Ulai (or Eulaeus), a river of Persia\nKJV: Ulai.\n\nCognate Group: H365 (hind), H355 (hind), H425 (Elah), H198 (Ulam), H440 (Elonites), H354 (hart), H357 (Aijalon), H362 (Elim), H197 (porch), H195 (Ulai), H356 (Elon), H193 (mighty), H361 (arch), H424 (elm), H364 (El-paran), H352 (mighty), H359 (Elath), H436 (plain)",
    196: "אֱוִלִי (ʼĕvilîy | ev-ee-lee')\n\nDerivation: from H191 אֱוִיל\nStrong's: silly, foolish; hence (morally) impious\nKJV: foolish.\n\nCognate Group: H200 (folly), H196 (foolish), H191 (fool)\nGreek Equivalents: G552 ἄπειρος",
    197: "אוּלָם (ʼûwlâm | oo-lawm')\n\nDerivation: or (shortened), אֻלָם ; from H481 אָלַם (in the sense of tying)\nStrong's: a vestibule (as bound to the building)\nKJV: porch.\n\nCognate Group: H365 (hind), H355 (hind), H425 (Elah), H198 (Ulam), H440 (Elonites), H354 (hart), H357 (Aijalon), H362 (Elim), H197 (porch), H195 (Ulai), H356 (Elon), H193 (mighty), H361 (arch), H424 (elm), H364 (El-paran), H352 (mighty), H359 (Elath), H436 (plain)\nGreek Equivalents: G3485 ναός, G4133 πλήν",
    198: "אוּלָם (ʼÛwlâm | oo-lawm')\n\nDerivation: appar, from H481 אָלַם (in the sense of dumbness); solitary\nStrong's: Ulam, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Ulam.\n\nCognate Group: H365 (hind), H355 (hind), H425 (Elah), H198 (Ulam), H440 (Elonites), H354 (hart), H357 (Aijalon), H362 (Elim), H197 (porch), H195 (Ulai), H356 (Elon), H193 (mighty), H361 (arch), H424 (elm), H364 (El-paran), H352 (mighty), H359 (Elath), H436 (plain)",
    199: "אוּלָם (ʼûwlâm | oo-lawm')\n\nDerivation: apparently a variation of H194 אוּלַי\nStrong's: however or on the contrary\nKJV: as for, but, howbeit, in very deed, surely, truly, wherefore.\n\nCognate Group: H199 (as for)",
    200: "אִוֶּלֶת (ʼivveleth | iv-veh'-leth)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H191 אֱוִיל\nStrong's: silliness\nKJV: folly, foolishly(-ness).\n\nCognate Group: H200 (folly), H196 (foolish), H191 (fool)\nGreek Equivalents: G454 ἄνοια, G685 ἀρά, G877 ἀφροσύνη, G2556 κακός",
    201: "אֹומָר (ʼÔwmâr | o-mawr')\n\nDerivation: from H559 אָמַר ; talkative\nStrong's: Omar, a grandson of Esau\nKJV: Omar.\n\nCognate Group: H568 (Amariah), H559 (answer), H567 (Amorite), H569 (Amraphel), H3982 (commandment), H566 (Imri), H534 (bough), H561 (answer), H570 (former time), H562 (promise), H564 (Immer), H201 (Omar), H565 (commandment), H204 (On), H577 (I beseech thee)",
    202: "אֹון (ʼôwn | one)\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as H205 אָוֶן (in the sense of effort, but successful)\nStrong's: ability, power, (figuratively) wealth\nKJV: force, goods, might, strength, substance.\n\nCognate Group: H211 (Ophir), H210 (Uphaz), H208 (Onam), H207 (Ono), H202 (force), H203 (On), H209 (Onan)\nGreek Equivalents: G1391 δόξα, G1411 δύναμις, G2246 ἥλιος, G2873 κόπος, G4172 πόλις, G5225 ὑπάρχω",
    203: "אֹון (ʼÔwn | one)\n\nDerivation: the same as H202 אֹון\nStrong's: On, an Israelite\nKJV: On.\n\nCognate Group: H211 (Ophir), H210 (Uphaz), H208 (Onam), H207 (Ono), H202 (force), H203 (On), H209 (Onan)",
    204: "אֹון (ʼÔwn | one)\n\nDerivation: or (shortened); אֹן; of Egyptian derivation\nStrong's: On, a city of Egypt\nKJV: On.\n\nCognate Group: H568 (Amariah), H559 (answer), H567 (Amorite), H569 (Amraphel), H3982 (commandment), H566 (Imri), H534 (bough), H561 (answer), H570 (former time), H562 (promise), H564 (Immer), H201 (Omar), H565 (commandment), H204 (On), H577 (I beseech thee)",
    205: "אָוֶן (ʼâven | aw-ven')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root perhaps meaning properly, to pant (hence, to exert oneself, usually in vain; to come to naught)\nStrong's: strictly nothingness; also trouble. vanity, wickedness; specifically an idol\nKJV: affliction, evil, false, idol, iniquity, mischief, mourners(-ing), naught, sorrow, unjust, unrighteous, vain, vanity, wicked(-ness). Compare H369 אַיִן .\n\nCognate Group: H8383 (lie), H205 (affliction), H206 (Aven)\nGreek Equivalents: G94 ἄδικος, G458 ἀνομία, G459 ἄνομος, G765 ἀσεβής, G824 ἄτοπος, G878 ἄφρων, G1112 γογγυσμός, G2556 κακός, G2756 κενός, G2873 κόπος, G3152 μάταιος, G3154 ματαιόω, G3449 μόχθος, G3601 ὀδύνη, G3997 πένθος, G4189 πονηρία, G4192 πόνος, G5225 ὑπάρχω",
    206: "אָוֶן (ʼÂven | aw'-ven)\n\nDerivation: the same as H205 אָוֶן ; idolatry\nStrong's: Aven, the contemptuous synonym of three places, one in Coele-Syria, one in Egypt (On), and one in Palestine (Bethel)\nKJV: Aven. See also H204 אֹון, H1007 בֵּית אָוֶן .\n\nCognate Group: H8383 (lie), H205 (affliction), H206 (Aven)",
    207: "אֹונֹו (ʼÔwnôw | o-no')\n\nDerivation: or (shortened) אֹנֹו; prolonged from H202 אֹון ; strong\nStrong's: Ono, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Ono.\n\nCognate Group: H211 (Ophir), H210 (Uphaz), H208 (Onam), H207 (Ono), H202 (force), H203 (On), H209 (Onan)",
    208: "אֹונָם (ʼÔwnâm | o-nawm')\n\nDerivation: a variation of H209 אֹונָן ; strong\nStrong's: Onam, the name of an Edomite and of an Israelite\nKJV: Onam.\n\nCognate Group: H211 (Ophir), H210 (Uphaz), H208 (Onam), H207 (Ono), H202 (force), H203 (On), H209 (Onan)",
    209: "אֹונָן (ʼÔwnân | o-nawn')\n\nDerivation: a variation of H207 אֹונֹו ; strong\nStrong's: Onan, a son of Judah\nKJV: Onan.\n\nCognate Group: H211 (Ophir), H210 (Uphaz), H208 (Onam), H207 (Ono), H202 (force), H203 (On), H209 (Onan)",
    210: "אוּפָז (ʼÛwphâz | oo-fawz')\n\nDerivation: perhaps a corruption of H211 אֹופִיר\nStrong's: Uphaz, a famous gold region\nKJV: Uphaz.\n\nCognate Group: H211 (Ophir), H210 (Uphaz), H208 (Onam), H207 (Ono), H202 (force), H203 (On), H209 (Onan)",
    211: "אֹופִיר (ʼÔwphîyr | o-feer')\n\nDerivation: or (shortened) אֹפִיר; and אֹופִר; of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Ophir, the name of a son of Joktan, and of a gold region in the East\nKJV: Ophir.\n\nCognate Group: H211 (Ophir), H210 (Uphaz), H208 (Onam), H207 (Ono), H202 (force), H203 (On), H209 (Onan)",
    212: "אֹופָן (ʼôwphân | o-fawn')\n\nDerivation: or (shortened) אֹפָן; from an unused root meaning to revolve\nStrong's: a wheel\nKJV: wheel.\n\nCognate Group: H655 (fitly), H212 (wheel)\nGreek Equivalents: G5164 τροχός",
    213: "אוּץ (ʼûwts | oots)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to press; (by implication) to be close, hurry, withdraw\nKJV: (make) haste(-n, -y), labor, be narrow.\n\nCognate Group: H213 (haste)\nGreek Equivalents: G1011 βουλεύω, G2729 κατισχύω, G2872 κοπιάω, G4313 προπορεύομαι, G4704 σπουδάζω, G4729 στενοχωρέω, G5035 ταχύ, G5036 ταχύς",
    214: "אֹוצָר (ʼôwtsâr | o-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: from H686 אָצַר\nStrong's: a depository\nKJV: armory, cellar, garner, store(-house), treasure(-house) (-y).\n\nCognate Group: H687 (Ezer), H214 (armory), H689 (wild goat), H686 (store), H690 (Ara)\nGreek Equivalents: G596 ἀποθήκη, G2344 θησαυρός, G4149 πλοῦτος",
