    216: "אֹור (ʼôwr | ore)\n\nDerivation: from H215 אֹור\nStrong's: illumination or (concrete) luminary (in every sense, including lightning, happiness, etc.)\nKJV: bright, clear, [phrase] day, light (-ning), morning, sun.\n\nCognate Group: H2971 (Jair), H222 (Uriel), H3975 (den), H221 (Uri), H218 (Ur), H216 (bright), H224 (Urim), H223 (Uriah), H2972 (Jairite), H215 ([idiom] break of day), H3974 (bright), H217 (fire), H219 (herb)\nGreek Equivalents: G808 ἀσχημοσύνη, G1192 δέρμα, G1193 δερμάτινος, G2246 ἥλιος, G2250 ἡμέρα, G3314 μεσημβρία, G4983 σῶμα, G5338 φέγγος, G5457 φῶς, G5462 φωτισμός, G5559 χρώς",
    217: "אוּר (ʼûwr | ore)\n\nDerivation: from H215 אֹור\nStrong's: flame; hence (in the plural) the East (as being the region of light)\nKJV: fire, light. See also H224 אוּרִים .\n\nCognate Group: H2971 (Jair), H222 (Uriel), H3975 (den), H221 (Uri), H218 (Ur), H216 (bright), H224 (Urim), H223 (Uriah), H2972 (Jairite), H215 ([idiom] break of day), H3974 (bright), H217 (fire), H219 (herb)\nGreek Equivalents: G225 ἀλήθεια, G892 ἄχυρον, G1212 δῆλος, G2868 κονιορτός, G4442 πῦρ, G5561 χώρα",
    218: "אוּר (ʼÛwr | oor)\n\nDerivation: the same as H217 אוּר\nStrong's: Ur, a place in Chaldaea; also an Israelite\nKJV: Ur.\n\nCognate Group: H2971 (Jair), H222 (Uriel), H3975 (den), H221 (Uri), H218 (Ur), H216 (bright), H224 (Urim), H223 (Uriah), H2972 (Jairite), H215 ([idiom] break of day), H3974 (bright), H217 (fire), H219 (herb)",
    219: "אֹורָה (ʼôwrâh | o-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H216 אֹור\nStrong's: luminousness, i.e. (figuratively) prosperity; also a plant (as being bright)\nKJV: herb, light.\n\nCognate Group: H2971 (Jair), H222 (Uriel), H3975 (den), H221 (Uri), H218 (Ur), H216 (bright), H224 (Urim), H223 (Uriah), H2972 (Jairite), H215 ([idiom] break of day), H3974 (bright), H217 (fire), H219 (herb)",
    220: "אֲוֵרָה (ʼăvêrâh | av-ay-raw')\n\nDerivation: by transposition for H723 אֻרְוָה\nStrong's: a stall\nKJV: cote.\n\nCognate Group: H691 (valiant one), H220 (cote), H717 (gather), H740 (Ariel), H692 (Areli), H723 (stall), H745 (Arieh), H739 (lionlike men), H738 (lion)",
    221: "אוּרִי (ʼÛwrîy | oo-ree')\n\nDerivation: from H217 אוּר ; fiery\nStrong's: Uri, the name of three Israelites\nKJV: Uri.\n\nCognate Group: H2971 (Jair), H222 (Uriel), H3975 (den), H221 (Uri), H218 (Ur), H216 (bright), H224 (Urim), H223 (Uriah), H2972 (Jairite), H215 ([idiom] break of day), H3974 (bright), H217 (fire), H219 (herb)",
    222: "אוּרִיאֵל (ʼÛwrîyʼêl | oo-ree-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H217 אוּר and H410 אֵל ; flame of God\nStrong's: Uriel, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Uriel.\n\nCognate Group: H2971 (Jair), H222 (Uriel), H3975 (den), H221 (Uri), H218 (Ur), H216 (bright), H224 (Urim), H223 (Uriah), H2972 (Jairite), H215 ([idiom] break of day), H3974 (bright), H217 (fire), H219 (herb)",
    223: "אוּרִיָּה (ʼÛwrîyâh | oo-ree-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or (prolonged) אוּרִיָּהוּ ; from H217 אוּר and H3050 יָהּ ; flame of Jah\nStrong's: Urijah, the name of one Hittite and five Israelites\nKJV: Uriah, Urijah.\n\nCognate Group: H2971 (Jair), H222 (Uriel), H3975 (den), H221 (Uri), H218 (Ur), H216 (bright), H224 (Urim), H223 (Uriah), H2972 (Jairite), H215 ([idiom] break of day), H3974 (bright), H217 (fire), H219 (herb)\nGreek Equivalents: G3774 Οὐρίας",
    224: "אוּרִים (ʼÛwrîym | oo-reem')\n\nDerivation: plural of H217 אוּר ; lights\nStrong's: Urim, the oracular brilliancy of the figures in the high-priest's breastplate\nKJV: Urim.\n\nCognate Group: H2971 (Jair), H222 (Uriel), H3975 (den), H221 (Uri), H218 (Ur), H216 (bright), H224 (Urim), H223 (Uriah), H2972 (Jairite), H215 ([idiom] break of day), H3974 (bright), H217 (fire), H219 (herb)\nGreek Equivalents: G5321 φανέρωσις, G5461 φωτίζω",
    225: "אוּת (ʼûwth | ooth)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to come, i.e. (implied) to assent\nKJV: consent.\n\nCognate Group: H231 (hyssop), H229 (Ezbai), H227 (beginning), H225 (consent), H233 (then)\nGreek Equivalents: G3666 ὁμοιόω, G4855 συμφύω",
    226: "אֹות (ʼôwth | oth)\n\nDerivation: probably from H225 אוּת (in the sense of appearing)\nStrong's: a signal (literally or figuratively), as aflag, beacon, monument, omen, prodigy, evidence, etc.\nKJV: mark, miracle, (en-) sign, token.\n\nCognate Group: H184 (point out), H186 (Uzai), H226 (mark)\nGreek Equivalents: G2297 θαυμάσιος, G4592 σημεῖον",
    227: "אָז (ʼâz | awz)\n\nDerivation: a demonstrative adverb\nStrong's: at that time or place; also as a conjunction, therefore\nKJV: beginning, for, from, hitherto, now, of old, once, since, then, at which time, yet.\n\nCognate Group: H231 (hyssop), H229 (Ezbai), H227 (beginning), H225 (consent), H233 (then)\nGreek Equivalents: G3819 πάλαι, G3820 παλαιός",
    228: "אֲזָא (ʼăzâʼ | az-zaw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or אֲזָה (Aramaic)\nStrong's: to kindle; (by implication) to heat\nKJV: heat, hot.\n\nCognate Group: H230 (be gone), H228 (heat)\nGreek Equivalents: G1572 ἐκκαίω, G2545 καίω",
    229: "אֶזְבַּי (ʼEzbay | ez-bah'ee)\n\nDerivation: probably from H231 אֵזֹוב ; hyssop-like\nStrong's: Ezbai, an Israelite\nKJV: Ezbai.\n\nCognate Group: H231 (hyssop), H229 (Ezbai), H227 (beginning), H225 (consent), H233 (then)",
    230: "אֲזָד (ʼăzâd | az-zawd')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: firm\nKJV: be gone.\n\nCognate Group: H230 (be gone), H228 (heat)\nGreek Equivalents: G868 ἀφίστημι",
    231: "אֵזֹוב (ʼêzôwb | ay-zobe')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign derivation\nStrong's: hyssop\nKJV: hyssop.\n\nCognate Group: H231 (hyssop), H229 (Ezbai), H227 (beginning), H225 (consent), H233 (then)\nGreek Equivalents: G5301 ὕσσωπος",
    232: "אֵזֹור (ʼêzôwr | ay-zore')\n\nDerivation: from H246 אֲזִקִּים\nStrong's: something girt; a belt, also a band\nKJV: girdle.\n\nCognate Group: H305 (O that), H253 (ah), H247 (bind about), H232 (girdle)\nGreek Equivalents: G2223 ζώνη",
    233: "אֲזַי (ʼăzay | az-ah'ee)\n\nDerivation: probably from H227 אָז\nStrong's: at that time\nKJV: then.\n\nCognate Group: H231 (hyssop), H229 (Ezbai), H227 (beginning), H225 (consent), H233 (then)",
    234: "אַזְכָּרָה (ʼazkârâh | az-kaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H2142 זָכַר\nStrong's: a reminder; specifically remembrance-offering\nKJV: memorial.\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2144 (Zeker), H2138 (males), H2147 (Zichri), H2139 (Zaccur), H2145 ([idiom] him), H234 (memorial), H2146 (memorial), H2142 ([idiom] burn), H2143 (memorial)\nGreek Equivalents: G364 ἀνάμνησις",
    235: "אָזַל (ʼâzal | aw-zal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to go away, hence, to disappear\nKJV: fail, gad about, go to and fro (but in Ezekiel 27:19 the word is rendered by many 'from Uzal,' by others 'yarn'), be gone (spent).\n\nCognate Group: H235 (fail), H187 (Uzal), H237 (Ezel)\nGreek Equivalents: G565 ἀπέρχομαι, G1525 εἰσέρχομαι, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G4198 πορεύομαι, G5290 ὑποστρέφω",
    236: "אֲזַל (ʼăzal | az-al')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) the same as H235 אָזַל\nStrong's: to depart\nKJV: go (up).\n\nCognate Group: H236 (go)",
    237: "אֶזֶל (ʼezel | eh'-zel)\n\nDerivation: from H235 אָזַל ; departure\nStrong's: Ezel, a memorial stone in Palestine\nKJV: Ezel.\n\nCognate Group: H235 (fail), H187 (Uzal), H237 (Ezel)",
    238: "אָזַן (ʼâzan | aw-zan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; probably to expand; but used only as a denominative from H241 אֹזֶן\nStrong's: to broaden out the ear (with the hand), i.e. (by implication) to listen\nKJV: give (perceive by the) ear, hear(-ken). See H239 אָזַן .\n\nCognate Group: H238 (give ear), H240 (weapon), H243 (Aznoth-tabor), H2970 (Jaazaniah), H244 (Ozni), H241 (advertise), H245 (Azaniah), H3153 (Jezaniah)\nGreek Equivalents: G191 ἀκούω, G1522 εἰσακούω, G1801 ἐνωτίζομαι, G1873 ἐπακούω, G4337 προσέχω, G5219 ὑπακούω",
    239: "אָזַן (ʼâzan | aw-zan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (rather identical with H238 אָזַן through the idea of scales as if two ears)\nStrong's: to weigh, i.e. (figuratively) ponder\nKJV: give good heed.\n\nCognate Group: H3976 (balances), H242 (Uzzen-sherah), H239 (give good heed)",
