    241: "אֹזֶן (ʼôzen | o'-zen)\n\nDerivation: from H238 אָזַן\nStrong's: broadness. i.e. (concrete) the ear (from its form in man)\nKJV: [phrase] advertise, audience, [phrase] displease, ear, hearing, [phrase] show.\n\nCognate Group: H238 (give ear), H240 (weapon), H243 (Aznoth-tabor), H2970 (Jaazaniah), H244 (Ozni), H241 (advertise), H245 (Azaniah), H3153 (Jezaniah)\nGreek Equivalents: G3563 νοῦς, G3775 οὖς, G5621 ὠτίον",
    242: "אֻזֵּן שֶׁאֱרָה (ʼUzzên Sheʼĕrâh | ooz-zane' sheh-er-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H238 אָזַן and H7609 שֶׁאֱרָה ; plot of Sheerah (i.e. settled by him)\nStrong's: Uzzen-Sheerah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Uzzen-sherah.\n\nCognate Group: H3976 (balances), H242 (Uzzen-sherah), H239 (give good heed)",
    243: "אַזְנֹות תָּבֹור (ʼAznôwth Tâbôwr | az-noth' taw-bore')\n\nDerivation: from H238 אָזַן and H8396 תָּבֹור ; flats (i.e. tops) of Tabor (i.e. situated on it)\nStrong's: Aznoth-Tabor, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Aznoth-tabor.\n\nCognate Group: H238 (give ear), H240 (weapon), H243 (Aznoth-tabor), H2970 (Jaazaniah), H244 (Ozni), H241 (advertise), H245 (Azaniah), H3153 (Jezaniah)",
    244: "אׇזְנִי (ʼOznîy | oz-nee')\n\nDerivation: from H241 אֹזֶן ; having (quick) ears\nStrong's: Ozni, an Israelite; also an Oznite (collectively), his descendant\nKJV: Ozni, Oznites.\n\nCognate Group: H238 (give ear), H240 (weapon), H243 (Aznoth-tabor), H2970 (Jaazaniah), H244 (Ozni), H241 (advertise), H245 (Azaniah), H3153 (Jezaniah)",
    245: "אֲזַנְיָה (ʼĂzanyâh | az-an-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H238 אָזַן and H3050 יָהּ ; heard by Jah\nStrong's: Azanjah, an Israelite\nKJV: Azaniah.\n\nCognate Group: H238 (give ear), H240 (weapon), H243 (Aznoth-tabor), H2970 (Jaazaniah), H244 (Ozni), H241 (advertise), H245 (Azaniah), H3153 (Jezaniah)",
