    247: "אָזַר (ʼâzar | aw-zar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to belt\nKJV: bind (compass) about, gird (up, with).\n\nCognate Group: H305 (O that), H253 (ah), H247 (bind about), H232 (girdle)\nGreek Equivalents: G450 ἀνίστημι, G482 ἀντιλαμβάνομαι, G996 βοήθεια, G998 βοηθός, G1765 ἐνισχύω, G1807 ἐξαιρέω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2224 ζώννυμι, G2480 ἰσχύω, G2729 κατισχύω, G2729 κατισχύω, G4023 περιέχω, G4024 περιζώννυμι, G4982 σώζω, G5623 ὠφελέω",
    248: "אֶזְרֹועַ (ʼezrôwaʻ | ez-ro'-a)\n\nDerivation: a variation for H2220 זְרֹועַ\nStrong's: the arm\nKJV: arm.\n\nCognate Group: H2220 (arm), H248 (arm)\nGreek Equivalents: G1023 βραχίων",
    249: "אֶזְרָח (ʼezrâch | ez-rawkh')\n\nDerivation: from H2224 זָרַח (in the sense of springing up)\nStrong's: a spontaneous growth, i.e. native (tree or persons)\nKJV: bay tree, (home-) born (in the land), of the (one's own) country (nation).\n\nCognate Group: H2224 (arise), H2227 (Zarchite), H2225 (rising), H3156 (Izrahiah), H249 (bay tree), H4217 (east), H3155 (Izrahite), H250 (Ezrahite), H2228 (Zerahiah), H2226 (Zarah)",
