    251: "אָח (ʼâch | awkh)\n\nDerivation: a primitive word\nStrong's: a brother (used in the widest sense of literal relationship and metaphorical affinity or resemblance (like father))\nKJV: another, brother(-ly); kindred, like, other. Compare also the proper names beginning with 'Ah-' or 'Ahi-'.\n\nCognate Group: H289 (Ahiman), H298 (Ahiramites), H302 (Ahithophel), H286 (Ahilud), H279 (Ahiam), H300 (Ahishar), H293 (Ahinoam), H257 (Ahban), H287 (Ahimoth), H264 (brotherhood), H295 (Ahiezer), H294 (Ahisamach), H281 (Ahiah), H2361 (Huram), H260 (flag), H2438 (Hiram), H292 (Ahinadab), H277 (Ahi), H288 (Ahimelech), H296 (Ahikam), H282 (Ahihud), H299 (Ahira), H285 (Ahitub), H251 (another), H284 (Ahihud), H269 (other), H283 (Ahio), H301 (Ahishar), H256 (Ahab), H290 (Ahimaaz), H267 (Ahumai), H297 (Ahiram), H291 (Ahian)\nGreek Equivalents: G80 ἀδελφός, G1451 ἐγγύς, G2087 ἕτερος",
    252: "אַח (ʼach | akh)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H251 אָח \nStrong's: a brother (used in the widest sense of literal relationship and metaphorical affinity or resemblance)\nKJV: brother.\n\nCognate Group: H252 (brother), H307 (Achmetha)",
