    258: "אָחַד (ʼâchad | aw-khad')\n\nDerivation: perhaps a primitive root\nStrong's: to unify, i.e. (figuratively) collect (one's thoughts)\nKJV: go one way or other.\n\nCognate Group: H2299 (sharp), H2316 (Hadar), H258 (go one way or other), H2307 (Hadid), H2301 (Hadad), H2303 (sharp), H2300 (be fierce)\nGreek Equivalents: G1279 διαπορεύομαι",
