    267: "אֲחוּמַי (ʼĂchûwmay | akh-oo-mah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: perhaps from H251 אָח and H4325 מַיִם ; brother (i.e. neighbour) of water\nStrong's: Achumai, an Israelite\nKJV: Ahumai.\n\nCognate Group: H289 (Ahiman), H298 (Ahiramites), H302 (Ahithophel), H286 (Ahilud), H279 (Ahiam), H300 (Ahishar), H293 (Ahinoam), H257 (Ahban), H287 (Ahimoth), H264 (brotherhood), H295 (Ahiezer), H294 (Ahisamach), H281 (Ahiah), H2361 (Huram), H260 (flag), H2438 (Hiram), H292 (Ahinadab), H277 (Ahi), H288 (Ahimelech), H296 (Ahikam), H282 (Ahihud), H299 (Ahira), H285 (Ahitub), H251 (another), H284 (Ahihud), H269 (other), H283 (Ahio), H301 (Ahishar), H256 (Ahab), H290 (Ahimaaz), H267 (Ahumai), H297 (Ahiram), H291 (Ahian)",
    268: "אָחֹור (ʼâchôwr | aw-khore')\n\nDerivation: or (shortened) אָחֹר ; from H299 אֲחִירַע\nStrong's: the hinder part; hence (adverb) behind, backward; also (as facing north) the West\nKJV: after(-ward), back (part, -side, -ward), hereafter, (be-) hind(-er part), time to come, without.\n\nCognate Group: H323 (lieutenant), H327 (camel), H322 (back), H310 (after), H325 (Ahasuerus), H316 (Aharhel), H313 (Aher), H315 (Aharah), H326 (Haakashtari), H268 (after), H309 (continue), H3186 (tarry longer), H314 (after), H312 (other man), H319 (end)\nGreek Equivalents: G1424 δυσμή, G1715 ἔμπροσθεν, G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G2087 ἕτερος, G2246 ἥλιος, G2756 κενός, G3693 ὄπισθεν, G3694 ὀπίσω",
    269: "אָחֹות (ʼâchôwth | aw-khoth')\n\nDerivation: irregular feminine of H251 אָח\nStrong's: a sister (used very widely (like brother), literally and figuratively)\nKJV: (an-) other, sister, together.\n\nCognate Group: H289 (Ahiman), H298 (Ahiramites), H302 (Ahithophel), H286 (Ahilud), H279 (Ahiam), H300 (Ahishar), H293 (Ahinoam), H257 (Ahban), H287 (Ahimoth), H264 (brotherhood), H295 (Ahiezer), H294 (Ahisamach), H281 (Ahiah), H2361 (Huram), H260 (flag), H2438 (Hiram), H292 (Ahinadab), H277 (Ahi), H288 (Ahimelech), H296 (Ahikam), H282 (Ahihud), H299 (Ahira), H285 (Ahitub), H251 (another), H284 (Ahihud), H269 (other), H283 (Ahio), H301 (Ahishar), H256 (Ahab), H290 (Ahimaaz), H267 (Ahumai), H297 (Ahiram), H291 (Ahian)\nGreek Equivalents: G79 ἀδελφή, G2087 ἕτερος",
    270: "אָחַז (ʼâchaz | aw-khaz')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to seize (often with the accessory idea of holding in possession)\nKJV: [phrase] be affrighted, bar, (catch, lay, take) hold (back), come upon, fasten, handle, portion, (get, have or take) possess(-ion).\n\nCognate Group: H276 (Ahuzzath), H273 (Ahasai), H270 (be affrighted), H271 (Ahaz), H275 (Ahuzam), H274 (Ahaziah), H272 (possession)\nGreek Equivalents: G472 ἀντέχομαι, G680 ἅπτομαι, G681 ἅπτω, G881 Ἀχάζ, G1949 ἐπιλαμβάνομαι, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G2192 ἔχω, G2340 θηρεύω, G2624 κατακληροδοτέω, G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G2722 κατέχω, G2816 κληρονομέω, G2902 κρατέω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G4084 πιάζω, G4912 συνέχω, G5021 τάσσω, G5274 ὑπολαμβάνω",
    271: "אָחָז (ʼÂchâz | aw-khawz')\n\nDerivation: from H270 אָחַז ; possessor\nStrong's: Achaz, the name of a Jewish king and of an Israelite\nKJV: Ahaz.\n\nCognate Group: H276 (Ahuzzath), H273 (Ahasai), H270 (be affrighted), H271 (Ahaz), H275 (Ahuzam), H274 (Ahaziah), H272 (possession)\nGreek Equivalents: G881 Ἀχάζ",
