    274: "אֲחַזְיָה (ʼĂchazyâh | akh-az-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or (prolonged) אֲחַזְיָהוּ ; from H270 אָחַז and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has seized\nStrong's: Achazjah, the name of a Jewish and an Israelite king\nKJV: Ahaziah.\n\nCognate Group: H276 (Ahuzzath), H273 (Ahasai), H270 (be affrighted), H271 (Ahaz), H275 (Ahuzam), H274 (Ahaziah), H272 (possession)",
