    369: "אַיִן (ʼayin | ah'-yin)\n\nDerivation: as if from a primitive root meaning to be nothing or not exist\nStrong's: a non-entity; generally used as a negative particle\nKJV: else, except, fail, (father-) less, be gone, in(-curable), neither, never, no (where), none, nor, (any, thing), not, nothing, to nought, past, un(-searchable), well-nigh, without. Compare H370 אַיִן .\n\nCognate Group: H371 (not), H369 (else), H374 (ephah)\nGreek Equivalents: G134 αἰνέω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G853 ἀφανίζω, G3641 ὀλίγος",
