    481: "אָלַם (ʼâlam | aw-lam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tie fast; hence (of the mouth) to be tongue-tied\nKJV: bind, be dumb, put to silence.\n\nCognate Group: H495 (Ellasar), H482 (congregation), H491 (widow), H492 (one), H490 (desolate house), H485 (sheaf), H483 (dumb), H489 (widowhood), H481 (bind), H488 (forsaken), H480 (woe)\nGreek Equivalents: G1195 δεσμεύω",
