    502: "אָלַף (ʼâlaph | aw-lof')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root, to associate with\nStrong's: hence, to learn (and causatively to teach)\nKJV: learn, teach, utter.\n\nCognate Group: H441 (captain), H502 (learn), H504 (family)\nGreek Equivalents: G1321 διδάσκω, G1777 ἔνοχος, G3129 μανθάνω",
    503: "אָלַף (ʼâlaph | aw-laf')\n\nDerivation: denominative from H505 אֶלֶף\nStrong's: causative, to make athousandfold\nKJV: bring forth thousands.\n\nCognate Group: H441 (captain), H503 (bring forth thousands), H507 (Eleph), H505 (thousand)",
    504: "אֶלֶף (ʼeleph | eh'-lef)\n\nDerivation: from H502 אָלַף\nStrong's: a family; also (from the sense of yoking or taming) an ox or cow\nKJV: family, kine, oxen.\n\nCognate Group: H441 (captain), H502 (learn), H504 (family)\nGreek Equivalents: G5022 ταῦρος",
    505: "אֶלֶף (ʼeleph | eh'-lef)\n\nDerivation: prop, the same as H504 אֶלֶף\nStrong's: hence (the ox's head being the first letter of the alphabet, and this eventually used as a numeral) a thousand\nKJV: thousand.\n\nCognate Group: H441 (captain), H503 (bring forth thousands), H507 (Eleph), H505 (thousand)\nGreek Equivalents: G5505 χιλιάς",
