    680: "אָצַל (ʼâtsal | aw-tsal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; properly, to join; used only as a denominative from H681 אֵצֶל\nStrong's: to separate; hence, to select, refuse, contract\nKJV: keep, reserve, straiten, take.\n\nCognate Group: H681 (at), H679 (hole), H680 (keep), H683 (Azaliah), H682 (Azal), H678 (chief man), H1018 (Beth-ezel)\nGreek Equivalents: G851 ἀφαιρέω, G3635 ὀκνέω, G5275 ὑπολείπω",
    681: "אֵצֶל (ʼêtsel | ay'-tsel)\n\nDerivation: from H680 אָצַל (in the sense of joining)\nStrong's: a side; (as a preposition) near\nKJV: at, (hard) by, (from) (beside), near (unto), toward, with. See also H1018 בֵּית הָאֵצֶל .\n\nCognate Group: H681 (at), H679 (hole), H680 (keep), H683 (Azaliah), H682 (Azal), H678 (chief man), H1018 (Beth-ezel)",
    682: "אָצֵל (ʼÂtsêl | aw-tsale')\n\nDerivation: from H680 אָצַל ; noble\nStrong's: Atsel, the name of an Israelite, and of a place in Palestine\nKJV: Azal, Azel.\n\nCognate Group: H681 (at), H679 (hole), H680 (keep), H683 (Azaliah), H682 (Azal), H678 (chief man), H1018 (Beth-ezel)",
    683: "אֲצַלְיָהוּ (ʼĂtsalyâhûw | ats-al-yaw'-hoo)\n\nDerivation: from H680 אָצַל and H3050 יָהּ prolonged; Jah has reserved\nStrong's: Atsaljah, an Israelite\nKJV: Azaliah.\n\nCognate Group: H681 (at), H679 (hole), H680 (keep), H683 (Azaliah), H682 (Azal), H678 (chief man), H1018 (Beth-ezel)",
    684: "אֹצֶם (ʼÔtsem | o'-tsem)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to be strong; strength (i.e. strong)\nStrong's: Otsem, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Ozem.\n\nCognate Group: H684 (Ozem)",
    685: "אֶצְעָדָה (ʼetsʻâdâh | ets-aw-daw')\n\nDerivation: a variation from H6807 צְעָדָה\nStrong's: properly, a step-chain; by analogy, a bracelet\nKJV: bracelet, chain.\n\nCognate Group: H685 (bracelet), H6807 (going)",
    686: "אָצַר (ʼâtsar | aw-tsar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to store up\nKJV: (lay up in) store, [phrase] (make) treasure(-r).\n\nCognate Group: H687 (Ezer), H214 (armory), H689 (wild goat), H686 (store), H690 (Ara)",
