    688: "אֶקְדָּח (ʼeqdâch | ek-dawkh')\n\nDerivation: from H6916 קִדָּה\nStrong's: burning, i.e. a carbuncle or other fiery gem\nKJV: carbuncle.\n\nCognate Group: H6919 (burn), H688 (carbuncle), H6920 (burning ague)",
    689: "אַקֹּו (ʼaqqôw | ak-ko')\n\nDerivation: probably from H602 אָנַק\nStrong's: slender, i.e. the ibex\nKJV: wild goat.\n\nCognate Group: H687 (Ezer), H214 (armory), H689 (wild goat), H686 (store), H690 (Ara)",
    690: "אֲרָא (ʼărâʼ | ar-aw')\n\nDerivation: probably for H738 אֲרִי ; lion\nStrong's: Ara, an Israelite\nKJV: Ara.\n\nCognate Group: H687 (Ezer), H214 (armory), H689 (wild goat), H686 (store), H690 (Ara)",
    691: "אֶרְאֵל (ʼerʼêl | er-ale')\n\nDerivation: probably for H739 אֲרִיאֵל\nStrong's: a hero (collectively)\nKJV: valiant one.\n\nCognate Group: H691 (valiant one), H220 (cote), H717 (gather), H740 (Ariel), H692 (Areli), H723 (stall), H745 (Arieh), H739 (lionlike men), H738 (lion)",
    692: "אַרְאֵלִי (ʼArʼêlîy | ar-ay-lee')\n\nDerivation: from H691 אֶרְאֵל ; heroic\nStrong's: Areli (or an Arelite, collectively), an Israelite and his descendants\nKJV: Areli, Arelites.\n\nCognate Group: H691 (valiant one), H220 (cote), H717 (gather), H740 (Ariel), H692 (Areli), H723 (stall), H745 (Arieh), H739 (lionlike men), H738 (lion)",
    693: "אָרַב (ʼârab | aw-rab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to lurk\nKJV: (lie in) ambush(-ment), lay (lie in) wait.\n\nCognate Group: H701 (Arbite), H696 (wait), H693 (ambush), H698 (spoils), H695 (den), H700 (Aruboth), H3993 (lie in ambush), H699 (chimney), H694 (Arab)\nGreek Equivalents: G1748 ἐνεδρεύω",
