    696: "אֹרֶב (ʼôreb | o'-reb)\n\nDerivation: the same as H695 אֶרֶב \nStrong's: ambuscade\nKJV: wait.\n\nCognate Group: H701 (Arbite), H696 (wait), H693 (ambush), H698 (spoils), H695 (den), H700 (Aruboth), H3993 (lie in ambush), H699 (chimney), H694 (Arab)",
    697: "אַרְבֶּה (ʼarbeh | ar-beh')\n\nDerivation: from H7235 רָבָה\nStrong's: a locust (from its rapid increase)\nKJV: grasshopper, locust.\n\nCognate Group: H4768 (greatest part), H4766 (great), H4767 (much), H8635 (increase), H697 (grasshopper), H7235 (abundance), H8636 (increase)\nGreek Equivalents: G200 ἀκρίς",
    698: "אׇרֳבָה (ʼorŏbâh | or-ob-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H696 אֹרֶב (only in the plural)\nStrong's: ambuscades\nKJV: spoils.\n\nCognate Group: H701 (Arbite), H696 (wait), H693 (ambush), H698 (spoils), H695 (den), H700 (Aruboth), H3993 (lie in ambush), H699 (chimney), H694 (Arab)\nGreek Equivalents: G1911 ἐπιβάλλω",
    699: "אֲרֻבָּה (ʼărubbâh | ar-oob-baw')\n\nDerivation: feminine participle passive of H693 אָרַב (as if for lurking)\nStrong's: a lattice; (by implication) a window, dovecot (because of the pigeon-holes), chimney (with its apertures for smoke), sluice (with openings for water)\nKJV: chimney, window.\n\nCognate Group: H701 (Arbite), H696 (wait), H693 (ambush), H698 (spoils), H695 (den), H700 (Aruboth), H3993 (lie in ambush), H699 (chimney), H694 (Arab)\nGreek Equivalents: G2376 θυρίς, G3692 ὀπή",
    700: "אֲרֻבֹּות (ʼĂrubbôwth | ar-oob-both)\n\nDerivation: plural of H699 אֲרֻבָּה\nStrong's: Arubboth, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Aruboth.\n\nCognate Group: H701 (Arbite), H696 (wait), H693 (ambush), H698 (spoils), H695 (den), H700 (Aruboth), H3993 (lie in ambush), H699 (chimney), H694 (Arab)",
    701: "אַרְבִּי (ʼArbîy | ar-bee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H694 אֲרָב\nStrong's: an Arbite or native of Arab\nKJV: Arbite.\n\nCognate Group: H701 (Arbite), H696 (wait), H693 (ambush), H698 (spoils), H695 (den), H700 (Aruboth), H3993 (lie in ambush), H699 (chimney), H694 (Arab)",
    702: "אַרְבַּע (ʼarbaʻ | ar-bah')\n\nDerivation: masculine אַרְבָּעָה; from H7251 רָבַע\nStrong's: four\nKJV: four.\n\nCognate Group: H7255 (fourth participle), H7256 (fourth), H7251 (square), H705 (-forty), H702 (four), H7253 (fourth part), H7243 (foursquare), H706 (fourfold)\nGreek Equivalents: G5067 τέταρτος",
    703: "אַרְבַּע (ʼarbaʻ | ar-bah')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H702 אַרְבַּע \nStrong's: four\nKJV: four.\n\nCognate Group: H7244 (fourth), H703 (four)",
    704: "אַרְבַּע (ʼArbaʻ | ar-bah')\n\nDerivation: the same as H702 אַרְבַּע\nStrong's: Arba, one of the Anakim\nKJV: Arba.\n\nCognate Group: H7153 (Kirjath-arba), H7177 (Kartah), H7136 (appoint), H7178 (Kartan), H7158 (Kirjath-sannah), H7155 (Kirjath-huzoth), H4746 (building), H7157 (Kirjath), H7151 (city), H7176 (city), H6982 (beam), H7147 (contrary), H704 (Arba), H7156 (Kiriathaim), H7154 (Kirjathbaal), H7137 (uncleanness that chanceth), H4745 (something befallen), H7152 (Kerioth)",
