    809: "אֲשִׁישָׁה (ʼăshîyshâh | ash-ee-shaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H808 אָשִׁישׁ\nStrong's: something closely pressed together, i.e. a cake of raisins or other comfits\nKJV: flagon.\n\nCognate Group: H850 (Eshton), H808 (foundation), H848 (Eshtaulites), H851 (Eshtemoa), H809 (flagon), H847 (Eshtaol), H377 (show self a man)",
    810: "אֶשֶׁךְ (ʼeshek | eh'-shek)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (probably meaning to bunch together)\nStrong's: a testicle (as a lump)\nKJV: stone.\n\nCognate Group: H2977 (Josiah), H810 (stone), H805 (Asshurim), H807 (Ashima), H804 (Asshur), H803 (foundation), H812 (Eshcol), H811 (cluster), H813 (Ashkenaz)\nGreek Equivalents: G3693 ὄπισθεν",
    811: "אֶשְׁכֹּול (ʼeshkôwl | esh-kole')\n\nDerivation: or אֶשְׁכֹּל; probably prolonged from H810 אֶשֶׁךְ\nStrong's: a bunch of grapes or other fruit\nKJV: cluster (of grapes).\n\nCognate Group: H2977 (Josiah), H810 (stone), H805 (Asshurim), H807 (Ashima), H804 (Asshur), H803 (foundation), H812 (Eshcol), H811 (cluster), H813 (Ashkenaz)\nGreek Equivalents: G1009 βότρυς",
    812: "אֶשְׁכֹּל (ʼEshkôl | esh-kole')\n\nDerivation: the same as H811 אֶשְׁכֹּול\nStrong's: Eshcol, the name of an Amorite, also of a valley in Palestine\nKJV: Eshcol.\n\nCognate Group: H2977 (Josiah), H810 (stone), H805 (Asshurim), H807 (Ashima), H804 (Asshur), H803 (foundation), H812 (Eshcol), H811 (cluster), H813 (Ashkenaz)",
    813: "אַשְׁכְּנַז (ʼAshkᵉnaz | ash-ken-az')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Ashkenaz, a Japhethite, also his descendants\nKJV: Ashkenaz.\n\nCognate Group: H2977 (Josiah), H810 (stone), H805 (Asshurim), H807 (Ashima), H804 (Asshur), H803 (foundation), H812 (Eshcol), H811 (cluster), H813 (Ashkenaz)",
    814: "אֶשְׁכָּר (ʼeshkâr | esh-cawr')\n\nDerivation: for H7939 שָׂכָר\nStrong's: a gratuity\nKJV: gift, present.\n\nCognate Group: H814 (gift), H7946 (being at ease), H7944 (error)\nGreek Equivalents: G1435 δῶρον, G3408 μισθός",
    815: "אֵשֶׁל (ʼêshel | ay'-shel)\n\nDerivation: from a root of uncertain signification\nStrong's: a tamarisk tree; by extension, a grove of any kind\nKJV: grove, tree.\n\nCognate Group: H815 (grove)",
    816: "אָשַׁם (ʼâsham | aw-sham')\n\nDerivation: or אָשֵׁם; a primitive root\nStrong's: to be guilty; by implication to be punished or perish\nKJV: [idiom] certainly, be(-come, made) desolate, destroy, [idiom] greatly, be(-come, found, hold) guilty, offend (acknowledge offence), trespass.\n\nCognate Group: H819 (offend), H816 ([idiom] certainly), H818 (one which is faulty), H817 (guiltiness)\nGreek Equivalents: G50 ἀγνοέω, G264 ἁμαρτάνω, G447 ἀνίημι, G853 ἀφανίζω, G1842 ἐξολοθρεύω, G3338 μεταμέλλομαι, G3895 παραπίπτω",
    817: "אָשָׁם (ʼâshâm | aw-shawm')\n\nDerivation: from H816 אָשַׁם\nStrong's: guilt; by implication, a fault; also a sin-offering\nKJV: guiltiness, (offering for) sin, trespass (offering).\n\nCognate Group: H819 (offend), H816 ([idiom] certainly), H818 (one which is faulty), H817 (guiltiness)\nGreek Equivalents: G52 ἄγνοια, G93 ἀδικία, G266 ἁμαρτία, G931 βάσανος, G2512 καθαρισμός",
    818: "אָשֵׁם (ʼâshêm | aw-shame')\n\nDerivation: from H816 אָשַׁם\nStrong's: guilty; hence, presenting asin-offering\nKJV: one which is faulty, guilty.\n\nCognate Group: H819 (offend), H816 ([idiom] certainly), H818 (one which is faulty), H817 (guiltiness)",
    819: "אַשְׁמָה (ʼashmâh | ash-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H817 אָשָׁם\nStrong's: guiltiness, a fault, the presentation of asin-offering\nKJV: offend, sin, (cause of) trespass(-ing, offering).\n\nCognate Group: H819 (offend), H816 ([idiom] certainly), H818 (one which is faulty), H817 (guiltiness)\nGreek Equivalents: G52 ἄγνοια, G1651 ἐλέγχω, G2250 ἡμέρα, G2434 ἱλασμός",
    820: "אַשְׁמָן (ʼashmân | ash-mawn')\n\nDerivation: probably from H8081 שֶׁמֶן\nStrong's: a fat-field\nKJV: desolate place.\n\nCognate Group: H8082 (fat), H4925 (Mishmannah), H4924 (fat), H8081 (anointing), H8080 (become fat), H820 (desolate place)",
    821: "אַשְׁמֻרָה (ʼashmurâh | ash-moo-raw')\n\nDerivation: or אַשׁמוּרָה; or אַשׁמֹרֶת; (feminine) from H8104 שָׁמַר\nStrong's: a night watch\nKJV: watch.\n\nCognate Group: H4931 (charge), H8109 (waking), H8119 (Shimrath), H3461 (Ishmerai), H8111 (Samaria), H8114 (Shamariah), H821 (watch), H8113 (Shimri), H8108 (watch), H8107 ([idiom] be observed), H8116 (Shimrith), H7763 (Shomer), H8112 (Shimon-meron), H8106 (Shamer), H8110 (Shimron), H8118 (Samaritans), H8104 (beward), H4929 (diligence), H8117 (Shimronites)\nGreek Equivalents: G3722 ὄρθρος, G5438 φυλακή",
    822: "אֶשְׁנָב (ʼeshnâb | esh-nawb')\n\nDerivation: apparently from an unused root (probably meaning to leave interstices)\nStrong's: a latticed window\nKJV: casement, lattice.\n\nCognate Group: H822 (casement)",
    823: "אַשְׁנָה (ʼAshnâh | ash-naw')\n\nDerivation: probably a variation for H3466 יְשָׁנָה\nStrong's: Ashnah, the name of two places in Palestine\nKJV: Ashnah.\n\nCognate Group: H823 (Ashnah)",
    824: "אֶשְׁעָן (ʼEshʻân | esh-awn')\n\nDerivation: from H8172 שָׁעַן ; support\nStrong's: Eshan, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Eshean.\n\nCognate Group: H8172 (lean), H824 (Eshean), H4938 (staff), H4937 (stay)",
    825: "אַשָּׁף (ʼashshâph | ash-shawf')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (probably meaning to lisp, i.e. practice enchantment)\nStrong's: a conjurer\nKJV: astrologer.\n\nCognate Group: H825 (astrologer)\nGreek Equivalents: G3097 μάγος, G5386 φιλόσοφος",
    826: "אַשָּׁף (ʼashshâph | ash-shawf')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H825 אַשָּׁף \nStrong's: a conjurer\nKJV: astrologer.\n\nCognate Group: H783 (Artaxerxes), H773 (bottom), H846 (wall), H778 (earth), H772 (earth), H749 (be meet), H826 (astrologer), H756 (Archevite), H785 (flame), H787 (foundation)",
    827: "אַשְׁפָּה (ʼashpâh | ash-paw')\n\nDerivation: perhaps (feminine) from the same as H825 אַשָּׁף (in the sense of covering)\nStrong's: a quiver or arrow-case\nKJV: quiver.\n\nCognate Group: H827 (quiver), H832 (Eshkalonites), H828 (Ashpenaz), H831 (Ashkelon), H829 (good piece)\nGreek Equivalents: G1939 ἐπιθυμία, G5115 τόξον",
    828: "אַשְׁפְּנַז (ʼAshpᵉnaz | ash-pen-az')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Ashpenaz, a Babylonian eunuch\nKJV: Ashpenaz.\n\nCognate Group: H827 (quiver), H832 (Eshkalonites), H828 (Ashpenaz), H831 (Ashkelon), H829 (good piece)",
    829: "אֶשְׁפָּר (ʼeshpâr | esh-pawr')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a measured portion\nKJV: good piece (of flesh).\n\nCognate Group: H827 (quiver), H832 (Eshkalonites), H828 (Ashpenaz), H831 (Ashkelon), H829 (good piece)",
    830: "אַשְׁפֹּת (ʼashpôth | ash-pohth')\n\nDerivation: or אַשְׁפֹּות; or שְׁפֹת; (contraction) plural of a noun of the same form as H827 אַשְׁפָּה, from H8192 שָׁפָה (in the sense of scraping)\nStrong's: a heap of rubbish or filth\nKJV: dung (hill).\n\nCognate Group: H8239 (bring), H4942 (burden), H8240 (hook), H830 (dung)\nGreek Equivalents: G2874 κοπρία",
    831: "אַשְׁקְלֹון (ʼAshqᵉlôwn | ash-kel-one')\n\nDerivation: probably from H8254 שָׁקַל in the sense of weighing-place (i.e. mart)\nStrong's: Ashkelon, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Ashkelon, Askalon.\n\nCognate Group: H827 (quiver), H832 (Eshkalonites), H828 (Ashpenaz), H831 (Ashkelon), H829 (good piece)",
    832: "אֶשְׁקְלֹונִי (ʼEshqᵉlôwnîy | esh-kel-o-nee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H831 אַשְׁקְלֹון\nStrong's: Ashkelonite (collectively) or inhabitant of Ashkelon\nKJV: Eshkalonites.\n\nCognate Group: H827 (quiver), H832 (Eshkalonites), H828 (Ashpenaz), H831 (Ashkelon), H829 (good piece)",
    833: "אָשַׁר (ʼâshar | aw-shar')\n\nDerivation: or אָשֵׁר; a primitive root\nStrong's: to be straight (used in the widest sense, especially to be level, right, happy); figuratively, to go forward, be honest, proper\nKJV: (call, be) bless(-ed, happy), go, guide, lead, relieve.\n\nCognate Group: H843 (Asherites), H835 (blessed), H838 (going), H842 (grove), H837 (happy), H836 (Asher), H833 (bless), H839 (Ashurite), H8391 (box)\nGreek Equivalents: G804 ἀσφαλής, G2206 ζηλόω, G2720 κατευθύνω, G3106 μακαρίζω, G4105 πλανάω",
    834: "אֲשֶׁר (ʼăsher | ash-er')\n\nDerivation: a primitive relative pronoun (of every gender and number)\nStrong's: who, which, what, that; also (as an adverb and a conjunction) when, where, how, because, in order that, etc.\nKJV: [idiom] after, [idiom] alike, as (soon as), because, [idiom] every, for, [phrase] forasmuch, [phrase] from whence, [phrase] how(-soever), [idiom] if, (so) that ((thing) which, wherein), [idiom] though, [phrase] until, [phrase] whatsoever, when, where ([phrase] -as, -in, -of, -on, -soever, -with), which, whilst, [phrase] whither(-soever), who(-m, -soever, -se). As it is indeclinable, it is often accompanied by the personal pronoun expletively, used to show the connection.\n\nCognate Group: H834 ([idiom] after)\nGreek Equivalents: G2509 καθάπερ, G2526 καθό, G2530 καθότι, G3778 οὗτος, G5101 τίς, G5101 τίς, G5158 τρόπος, G5158 τρόπος",
    835: "אֶשֶׁר (ʼesher | eh'-sher)\n\nDerivation: from H833 אָשַׁר\nStrong's: happiness; only in masculine plural construction as interjection, how happy!\nKJV: blessed, happy.\n\nCognate Group: H843 (Asherites), H835 (blessed), H838 (going), H842 (grove), H837 (happy), H836 (Asher), H833 (bless), H839 (Ashurite), H8391 (box)",
    836: "אָשֵׁר (ʼÂshêr | aw-share')\n\nDerivation: from H833 אָשַׁר,\nStrong's: happy; Asher, a son of Jacob, and the tribe descended from him, with its territory; also a place in Palestine\nKJV: Asher\n\nCognate Group: H843 (Asherites), H835 (blessed), H838 (going), H842 (grove), H837 (happy), H836 (Asher), H833 (bless), H839 (Ashurite), H8391 (box)\nGreek Equivalents: G768 Ἀσήρ",
    837: "אֹשֶׁר (ʼôsher | o'-sher)\n\nDerivation: from H833 אָשַׁר\nStrong's: happiness\nKJV: happy.\n\nCognate Group: H843 (Asherites), H835 (blessed), H838 (going), H842 (grove), H837 (happy), H836 (Asher), H833 (bless), H839 (Ashurite), H8391 (box)\nGreek Equivalents: G3107 μακάριος",
    838: "אָשֻׁר (ʼâshur | aw-shoor')\n\nDerivation: or אַשֻּׁר; from H833 אָשַׁר in the sense of going\nStrong's: a step\nKJV: going, step.\n\nCognate Group: H843 (Asherites), H835 (blessed), H838 (going), H842 (grove), H837 (happy), H836 (Asher), H833 (bless), H839 (Ashurite), H8391 (box)\nGreek Equivalents: G1778 ἔνταλμα, G4228 πούς",
    839: "אֲשֻׁר (ʼăshur | ash-oor')\n\nDerivation: contracted for H8391 תְּאַשּׁוּר\nStrong's: the cedar tree or some other light elastic wood\nKJV: Ashurite.\n\nCognate Group: H843 (Asherites), H835 (blessed), H838 (going), H842 (grove), H837 (happy), H836 (Asher), H833 (bless), H839 (Ashurite), H8391 (box)",
    840: "אֲשַׂרְאֵל (ʼĂsarʼêl | as-ar-ale')\n\nDerivation: by orthographical variation from H833 אָשַׁר and H410 אֵל ; right of God\nStrong's: Asarel, an Israelite\nKJV: Asareel.\n\nCognate Group: H844 (Ashriel), H783 (Artaxerxes), H840 (Asareel), H845 (Asrielites), H841 (Asarelah), H782 (request)",
    841: "אֲשַׂרְאֵלָה (ʼĂsarʼêlâh | as-ar-ale'-aw)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H840 אֲשַׂרְאֵל ; right toward God\nStrong's: Asarelah, an Israelite\nKJV: Asarelah. Compare H3480 יְשַׂרְאֵלָה .\n\nCognate Group: H844 (Ashriel), H783 (Artaxerxes), H840 (Asareel), H845 (Asrielites), H841 (Asarelah), H782 (request)\nGreek Equivalents: G1093 γῆ, G2949 κῦμα",
    842: "אֲשֵׁרָה (ʼăshêrâh | ash-ay-raw')\n\nDerivation: or אֲשֵׁירָה; from H833 אָשַׁר ; happy\nStrong's: Asherah (or Astarte) a Phoenician goddess; also an image of the same\nKJV: grove. Compare H6253 עַשְׁתֹּרֶת .\n\nCognate Group: H843 (Asherites), H835 (blessed), H838 (going), H842 (grove), H837 (happy), H836 (Asher), H833 (bless), H839 (Ashurite), H8391 (box)\nGreek Equivalents: G1186 δένδρον",
    843: "אָשֵׁרִי (ʼÂshêrîy | aw-shay-ree')\n\nDerivation: patronymic from H836 אָשֵׁר\nStrong's: an Asherite (collectively) or descendant of Asher\nKJV: Asherites.\n\nCognate Group: H843 (Asherites), H835 (blessed), H838 (going), H842 (grove), H837 (happy), H836 (Asher), H833 (bless), H839 (Ashurite), H8391 (box)",
    844: "אַשְׂרִיאֵל (ʼAsrîyʼêl | as-ree-ale')\n\nDerivation: an orthographical variation for H840 אֲשַׂרְאֵל\nStrong's: Asriel, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Ashriel, Asriel.\n\nCognate Group: H844 (Ashriel), H783 (Artaxerxes), H840 (Asareel), H845 (Asrielites), H841 (Asarelah), H782 (request)",
    845: "אַשְׂרִאֵלִי (ʼAsriʼêlîy | as-ree-ale-ee')\n\nDerivation: patronymic from H844 אַשְׂרִיאֵל\nStrong's: an Asrielite (collectively) or descendant of Asriel\nKJV: Asrielites.\n\nCognate Group: H844 (Ashriel), H783 (Artaxerxes), H840 (Asareel), H845 (Asrielites), H841 (Asarelah), H782 (request)",
    846: "אֻשַּׁרְנָא (ʼushsharnâʼ | oosh-ar-naw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H833 אָשַׁר\nStrong's: a wall (from its uprightness)\nKJV: wall.\n\nCognate Group: H783 (Artaxerxes), H773 (bottom), H846 (wall), H778 (earth), H772 (earth), H749 (be meet), H826 (astrologer), H756 (Archevite), H785 (flame), H787 (foundation)",
    847: "אֶשְׁתָּאֹל (ʼEshtâʼôl | esh-taw-ole')\n\nDerivation: or אֶשְׁתָּאֹול; probably from H7592 שָׁאַל ; intreaty\nStrong's: Eshtaol, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Eshtaol.\n\nCognate Group: H850 (Eshton), H808 (foundation), H848 (Eshtaulites), H851 (Eshtemoa), H809 (flagon), H847 (Eshtaol), H377 (show self a man)",
    848: "אֶשְׁתָּאֻלִי (ʼEshtâʼulîy | esh-taw-oo-lee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H847 אֶשְׁתָּאֹל\nStrong's: an Eshtaolite (collectively) or inhabitant of Eshtaol\nKJV: Eshtaulites.\n\nCognate Group: H850 (Eshton), H808 (foundation), H848 (Eshtaulites), H851 (Eshtemoa), H809 (flagon), H847 (Eshtaol), H377 (show self a man)",
    849: "אֶשְׁתַּדּוּר (ʼeshtaddûwr | esh-tad-dure')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H7712 שְׁדַר (in a bad sense)\nStrong's: rebellion\nKJV: sedition.\n\nCognate Group: H7712 (labour), H849 (sedition), H7715 (Shadrach)",
    850: "אֶשְׁתֹּון (ʼEshtôwn | esh-tone')\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as H7764 שׁוּנִי ; restful\nStrong's: Eshton, an Israelite\nKJV: Eshton.\n\nCognate Group: H850 (Eshton), H808 (foundation), H848 (Eshtaulites), H851 (Eshtemoa), H809 (flagon), H847 (Eshtaol), H377 (show self a man)",
    851: "אֶשְׁתְּמֹעַ (ʼEshtᵉmôaʻ | esh-tem-o'-ah)\n\nDerivation: or אֶשְׁתְּמֹועַ; or אֶשְׁתְּמֹה; from H8085 שָׁמַע (in the sense of obedience)\nStrong's: Eshtemoa or Eshtemoh, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Eshtemoa, Eshtemoh.\n\nCognate Group: H850 (Eshton), H808 (foundation), H848 (Eshtaulites), H851 (Eshtemoa), H809 (flagon), H847 (Eshtaol), H377 (show self a man)",
    852: "אָת (ʼâth | awth)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H226 אֹות\nStrong's: a portent\nKJV: sign.\n\nCognate Group: H852 (sign)",
    853: "אֵת (ʼêth | ayth)\n\nDerivation: apparent contracted from H226 אֹות in the demonstrative sense of entity\nStrong's: properly, self (but generally used to point out more definitely the object of a verb or preposition, even or namely)\nKJV: (as such unrepresented in English).\n\nCognate Group: H853 (self)",
    854: "אֵת (ʼêth | ayth)\n\nDerivation: probably from H579 אָנָה\nStrong's: properly, nearness (used only as a preposition or an adverb), near; hence, generally, with, by, at, among, etc.\nKJV: against, among, before, by, for, from, in(-to), (out) of, with. Often with another prepositional prefix.\n\nCognate Group: H863 (Ithai), H384 (Ithiel), H854 (against), H856 (Ethbaal)\nGreek Equivalents: G3694 ὀπίσω",
    855: "אֵת (ʼêth | ayth)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a hoe or other digging implement\nKJV: coulter, plowshare.\n\nCognate Group: H855 (coulter)",
    856: "אֶתְבַּעַל (ʼEthbaʻal | eth-bah'-al)\n\nDerivation: from H854 אֵת and H1168 בַּעַל ; with Baal\nStrong's: Ethbaal, a Phoenician king\nKJV: Ethbaal.\n\nCognate Group: H863 (Ithai), H384 (Ithiel), H854 (against), H856 (Ethbaal)",
    857: "אָתָה (ʼâthâh | aw-thaw')\n\nDerivation: or אָתָא; a primitive root (collateral to H225 אוּת contraction)\nStrong's: to arrive\nKJV: (be-, things to) come (upon), bring.\n\nCognate Group: H857 (come), H2978 (entrance), H864 (Etham)\nGreek Equivalents: G4863 συνάγω",
    858: "אָתָה (ʼâthâh | aw-thaw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or אָתָא; (Aramaic), corresponding to H857 אָתָה \nStrong's: to arrive\nKJV: (be-) come, bring.\n\nCognate Group: H858 (come), H861 (furnace)",
    859: "אַתָּה (ʼattâh | at-taw')\n\nDerivation: or (shortened); אַתָּ; or אַת; feminine (irregular) sometimes אַתִּי; plural masculine אַתֶּם; feminine אַתֶּן; or אַתֵּנָה\n\nTypo: lemma אתֵּנָה missing vowel, corrected to אַתֵּנָה\n\n; or אַתֵּנָּה; a primitive pronoun of the second person\nStrong's: thou and thee, or (plural) ye and you\nKJV: thee, thou, ye, you.\n\nCognate Group: H859 (thee)",
    860: "אָתֹון (ʼâthôwn | aw-thone')\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as H386 אֵיתָן (in the sense of patience)\nStrong's: a female donkey (from its docility)\nKJV: (she) ass.\n\nCognate Group: H867 (Ethni), H871 (spies), H862 (gallery), H860 (ass)\nGreek Equivalents: G2338 θῆλυς, G3688 ὄνος, G5268 ὑποζύγιον",
    861: "אַתּוּן (ʼattûwn | at-toon')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) probably from the corresponding to H784 אֵשׁ\nStrong's: probably a fire-place, i.e. furnace\nKJV: furnace.\n\nCognate Group: H858 (come), H861 (furnace)\nGreek Equivalents: G2575 κάμινος",
    862: "אַתּוּק (ʼattûwq | at-tooke')\n\nDerivation: or אַתִּיק; from H5423 נָתַק in the sense of decreasing\nStrong's: a ledge or offset in abuilding\nKJV: gallery.\n\nCognate Group: H867 (Ethni), H871 (spies), H862 (gallery), H860 (ass)",
