    909: "בָּדַד (bâdad | baw-dad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to divide, i.e. (reflex.) be solitary\nKJV: alone.\n\nCognate Group: H910 (alone), H909 (alone), H905 (alone)",
    910: "בָּדָד (bâdâd | baw-dawd')\n\nDerivation: from H909 בָּדַד\nStrong's: separate; adverb, separately\nKJV: alone, desolate, only, solitary.\n\nCognate Group: H910 (alone), H909 (alone), H905 (alone)\nGreek Equivalents: G5563 χωρίζω",
    911: "בְּדַד (Bᵉdad | bed-ad')\n\nDerivation: from H909 בָּדַד ; separation\nStrong's: Bedad, an Edomite\nKJV: Bedad.\n\nCognate Group: H912 (Bedeiah), H911 (Bedad), H907 (liar)\nGreek Equivalents: G229 ἀλήθω, G2617 καταισχύνω",
    912: "בֵּדְיָה (Bêdᵉyâh | bay-de-yaw')\n\nDerivation: probably a shortened form H5662 עֹבַדְיָה ; servant of Jehovah\nStrong's: Bedejah, an Israelite\nKJV: Bedeiah.\n\nCognate Group: H912 (Bedeiah), H911 (Bedad), H907 (liar)",
    913: "בְּדִיל (bᵉdîyl | bed-eel')\n\nDerivation: from H914 בָּדַל\nStrong's: alloy (because removed by smelting); by analogy, tin\nKJV: [phrase] plummet, tin.\n\nCognate Group: H917 (Bedan), H913 (plummet), H914 (difference), H915 (piece), H3995 (separate), H916 (bdellium)\nGreek Equivalents: G459 ἄνομος",
    914: "בָּדַל (bâdal | baw-dal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to divide (in variation senses literally or figuratively, separate, distinguish, differ, select, etc.)\nKJV: (make, put) difference, divide (asunder), (make) separate (self, -ation), sever (out), [idiom] utterly.\n\nCognate Group: H917 (Bedan), H913 (plummet), H914 (difference), H915 (piece), H3995 (separate), H916 (bdellium)\nGreek Equivalents: G873 ἀφορίζω, G1244 διαιρέω, G1291 διαστέλλομαι, G1316 διαχωρίζομαι, G2476 ἵστημι, G5563 χωρίζω",
    915: "בָּדָל (bâdâl | baw-dawl')\n\nDerivation: from H914 בָּדַל\nStrong's: a part\nKJV: piece.\n\nCognate Group: H917 (Bedan), H913 (plummet), H914 (difference), H915 (piece), H3995 (separate), H916 (bdellium)",
    916: "בְּדֹלַח (bᵉdôlach | bed-o'-lakh)\n\nDerivation: probably from H914 בָּדַל\nStrong's: something in pieces, i.e. bdellium, a (fragrant) gum (perhaps amber); others a pearl\nKJV: bdellium.\n\nCognate Group: H917 (Bedan), H913 (plummet), H914 (difference), H915 (piece), H3995 (separate), H916 (bdellium)\nGreek Equivalents: G440 ἄνθραξ, G2930 κρύσταλλος",
    917: "בְּדָן (Bᵉdân | bed-awn')\n\nDerivation: probably shortened for H5658 עַבְדֹון ; servile\nStrong's: Bedan, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Bedan.\n\nCognate Group: H917 (Bedan), H913 (plummet), H914 (difference), H915 (piece), H3995 (separate), H916 (bdellium)",
    918: "בָּדַק (bâdaq | baw-dak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; to gap open; used only as a denominative from H919 בֶּדֶק\nStrong's: to mend a breach\nKJV: repair.\n\nCognate Group: H918 (repair), H919 (breach), H920 (Bidkar)\nGreek Equivalents: G643 ἀποσκευάζω",
    919: "בֶּדֶק (bedeq | beh'-dek)\n\nDerivation: from H918 בָּדַק\nStrong's: a gap or leak (in a building or a ship)\nKJV: breach, [phrase] calker.\n\nCognate Group: H918 (repair), H919 (breach), H920 (Bidkar)",
    920: "בִּדְקַר (Bidqar | bid-car')\n\nDerivation: probably from H1856 דָּקַר with a prepositional prefix; by stabbing, i.e. assassin\nStrong's: Bidkar, an Israelite\nKJV: Bidkar.\n\nCognate Group: H918 (repair), H919 (breach), H920 (Bidkar)",
    921: "בְּדַר (bᵉdar | bed-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding (by transposition) to H6504 פָּרַד\nStrong's: to scatter\nKJV: scatter.\n\nCognate Group: H921 (scatter)\nGreek Equivalents: G1287 διασκορπίζω",
    922: "בֹּהוּ (bôhûw | bo'-hoo)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (meaning to be empty)\nStrong's: a vacuity, i.e. (superficially) an undistinguishable ruin\nKJV: emptiness, void.\n\nCognate Group: H922 (emptiness), H923 (red)",
    923: "בַּהַט (bahaṭ | bah'-hat)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (probably meaning to glisten)\nStrong's: white marble or perhaps alabaster\nKJV: red (marble).\n\nCognate Group: H922 (emptiness), H923 (red)\nGreek Equivalents: G4665 σμάραγδος",
    924: "בְּהִילוּ (bᵉhîylûw | be-hee-loo')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H927 בְּהַל\nStrong's: a hurry; only adverb, hastily\nKJV: in haste.\n\nCognate Group: H927 (in haste), H924 (in haste)\nGreek Equivalents: G4710 σπουδή",
    925: "בָּהִיר (bâhîyr | baw-here')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (meaning to be bright)\nStrong's: shining\nKJV: bright.\n\nCognate Group: H934 (bright spot), H925 (bright)",
    926: "בָּהַל (bâhal | baw-hal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tremble inwardly (or palpitate), i.e. (figuratively) be (causative, make) (suddenly) alarmed or agitated; by implication to hasten anxiously\nKJV: be (make) affrighted (afraid, amazed, dismayed, rash), (be, get, make) haste(-n, -y, -ily), (give) speedy(-ily), thrust out, trouble, vex.\n\nCognate Group: H926 (be affrighted), H928 (terror)\nGreek Equivalents: G1831 ἐξέρχομαι, G3886 παραλύω, G3935 παρίημι, G4692 σπεύδω, G4704 σπουδάζω, G4710 σπουδή, G5015 ταράσσω",
    927: "בְּהַל (bᵉhal | be-hal')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H926 בָּהַל\nStrong's: to terrify, hasten\nKJV: in haste, trouble.\n\nCognate Group: H927 (in haste), H924 (in haste)\nGreek Equivalents: G1611 ἔκστασις",
    928: "בֶּהָלָה (behâlâh | beh-haw-law')\n\nDerivation: from H926 בָּהַל\nStrong's: panic, destruction\nKJV: terror, trouble.\n\nCognate Group: H926 (be affrighted), H928 (terror)\nGreek Equivalents: G640 ἀπορία, G2671 κατάρα",
    929: "בְּהֵמָה (bᵉhêmâh | be-hay-maw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (probably meaning to be mute)\nStrong's: properly, a dumb beast; especially any large quadruped or animal (often collective)\nKJV: beast, cattle.\n\nCognate Group: H930 (Behemoth), H929 (beast)\nGreek Equivalents: G2342 θηρίον, G2934 κτῆνος, G5074 τετράπους",
    930: "בְּהֵמֹות (bᵉhêmôwth | be-hay-mohth')\n\nDerivation: in form a plural or H929 בְּהֵמָה, but really a singular of Egyptian derivation\nStrong's: a water-ox, i.e. the hippopotamus or Nile-horse\nKJV: Behemoth.\n\nCognate Group: H930 (Behemoth), H929 (beast)",
    931: "בֹּהֶן (bôhen | bo'-hen)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root apparently meaning to be thick\nStrong's: the thumb of the hand or great toe of the foot\nKJV: thumb, great toe.\n\nCognate Group: H932 (Bohan), H931 (thumb)\nGreek Equivalents: G206 ἄκρον, G1291 διαστέλλομαι",
    932: "בֹּהַן (Bôhan | bo'han)\n\nDerivation: an orthographical variation of H931 בֹּהֶן\nStrong's: thumb, Bohan, an Israelite\nKJV: Bohan.\n\nCognate Group: H932 (Bohan), H931 (thumb)\nGreek Equivalents: G1680 ἐλπίς",
    933: "בֹּהַק (bôhaq | bo'-hak)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be pale\nStrong's: white scurf\nKJV: freckled spot.\n\nCognate Group: H933 (freckled spot)",
    934: "בֹּהֶרֶת (bôhereth | bo-heh'-reth)\n\nDerivation: feminine active participle of the same as H925 בָּהִיר\nStrong's: a whitish spot on the skin\nKJV: bright spot.\n\nCognate Group: H934 (bright spot), H925 (bright)\nGreek Equivalents: G826 αὐγάζω",
    935: "בֹּוא (bôwʼ | bo)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to go or come (in a wide variety of applications)\nKJV: abide, apply, attain, [idiom] be, befall, [phrase] besiege, bring (forth, in, into, to pass), call, carry, [idiom] certainly, (cause, let, thing for) to come (against, in, out, upon, to pass), depart, [idiom] doubtless again, [phrase] eat, [phrase] employ, (cause to) enter (in, into, -tering, -trance, -try), be fallen, fetch, [phrase] follow, get, give, go (down, in, to war), grant, [phrase] have, [idiom] indeed, (in-) vade, lead, lift (up), mention, pull in, put, resort, run (down), send, set, [idiom] (well) stricken (in age), [idiom] surely, take (in), way.\n\nCognate Group: H872 (entry), H935 (abide), H3996 (by which came), H4126 (coming), H3997 (entry), H8393 (fruit)\nGreek Equivalents: G25 ἀγαπάω, G71 ἄγω, G142 αἴρω, G305 ἀναβαίνω, G321 ἀνάγω, G390 ἀναστρέφω, G393 ἀνατέλλω, G399 ἀναφέρω, G433 ἀνήκω, G450 ἀνίστημι, G455 ἀνοίγω, G467 ἀνταποδίδωμι, G520 ἀπάγω, G565 ἀπέρχομαι, G566 ἀπέχει, G567 ἀπέχομαι, G649 ἀποστέλλω, G667 ἀποφέρω, G705 ἀριθμέω, G864 ἀφικνέομαι, G911 βάπτω, G1096 γίνομαι, G1224 διαβαίνω, G1236 διάγω, G1279 διαπορεύομαι, G1292 διάστημα, G1325 δίδωμι, G1330 διέρχομαι, G1416 δύνω, G1424 δυσμή, G1521 εἰσάγω, G1524 εἴσειμι, G1525 εἰσέρχομαι, G1529 εἴσοδος, G1530 εἰσπηδάω, G1531 εἰσπορεύομαι, G1533 εἰσφέρω, G1563 ἐκεῖ, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1607 ἐκπορεύομαι, G1684 ἐμβαίνω, G1685 ἐμβάλλω, G1806 ἐξάγω, G1831 ἐξέρχομαι, G1841 ἔξοδος, G1863 ἐπάγω, G1880 ἐπανέρχομαι, G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G1925 ἐπιδείκνυμι, G1929 ἐπιδίδωμι, G1931 ἐπιδύω, G1994 ἐπιστρέφω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G2147 εὑρίσκω, G2240 ἥκω, G2309 θέλω, G2523 καθίζω, G2525 καθίστημι, G2564 καλέω, G2597 καταβαίνω, G2609 κατάγω, G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G2702 καταφέρω, G2902 κρατέω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3708 ὁράω, G3854 παραγίνομαι, G3860 παραδίδωμι, G3918 πάρειμι, G3928 παρέρχομαι, G4126 πλέω, G4198 πορεύομαι, G4260 προβαίνω, G4317 προσάγω, G4327 προσδέ