    936: "בּוּז (bûwz | booz)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to disrespect\nKJV: contemn, despise, [idiom] utterly.\n\nCognate Group: H941 (Buzi), H942 (Bavai), H936 (contemn), H938 (Buz), H937 (contempt), H940 (Buzite), H939 (despised)\nGreek Equivalents: G818 ἀτιμάζω, G1847 ἐξουδενόω, G2706 καταφρονέω, G3456 μυκτηρίζω",
    937: "בּוּז (bûwz | booz)\n\nDerivation: from H936 בּוּז\nStrong's: disrespect\nKJV: contempt(-uously), despised, shamed.\n\nCognate Group: H941 (Buzi), H942 (Bavai), H936 (contemn), H938 (Buz), H937 (contempt), H940 (Buzite), H939 (despised)\nGreek Equivalents: G819 ἀτιμία",
    938: "בּוּז (Bûwz | booz)\n\nDerivation: the same as H937 בּוּז\nStrong's: Buz, the name of a son of Nahor, and of an Israelite\nKJV: Buz.\n\nCognate Group: H941 (Buzi), H942 (Bavai), H936 (contemn), H938 (Buz), H937 (contempt), H940 (Buzite), H939 (despised)",
    939: "בּוּזָה (bûwzâh | boo-zaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of H936 בּוּז\nStrong's: something scorned; an object of contempt\nKJV: despised.\n\nCognate Group: H941 (Buzi), H942 (Bavai), H936 (contemn), H938 (Buz), H937 (contempt), H940 (Buzite), H939 (despised)\nGreek Equivalents: G5595 ψωμίζω",
    940: "בּוּזִי (Bûwzîy | boo-zee')\n\nDerivation: patronymic from H938 בּוּז\nStrong's: a Buzite or descendant of Buz\nKJV: Buzite.\n\nCognate Group: H941 (Buzi), H942 (Bavai), H936 (contemn), H938 (Buz), H937 (contempt), H940 (Buzite), H939 (despised)",
    941: "בּוּזִי (Bûwzîy | boo-zee')\n\nDerivation: the same as H940 בּוּזִי\nStrong's: Buzi, an Israelite\nKJV: Buzi.\n\nCognate Group: H941 (Buzi), H942 (Bavai), H936 (contemn), H938 (Buz), H937 (contempt), H940 (Buzite), H939 (despised)",
    942: "בַּוַּי (Bavvay | bav-vah'ee)\n\nDerivation: probably of Persian origin\nStrong's: Bavvai, an Israelite\nKJV: Bavai.\n\nCognate Group: H941 (Buzi), H942 (Bavai), H936 (contemn), H938 (Buz), H937 (contempt), H940 (Buzite), H939 (despised)",
    943: "בּוּךְ (bûwk | book)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to involve (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: be entangled, (perplexed).\n\nCognate Group: H943 (be entangled), H3998 (perplexity), H945 (Bul)\nGreek Equivalents: G4105 πλανάω, G5015 ταράσσω",
    944: "בּוּל (bûwl | bool)\n\nDerivation: for H2981 יְבוּל\nStrong's: produce (of the earth, etc.)\nKJV: food, stock.\n\nCognate Group: H2986 (bring), H2991 (Ibleam), H3106 (Jubal), H3105 (river), H2989 (Jabal), H944 (food), H2988 (course), H180 (river), H2990 (wen), H8398 (habitable part), H3104 (jubile), H2981 (fruit)",
    945: "בּוּל (Bûwl | bool)\n\nDerivation: the same as H944 בּוּל (in the sense of rain)\nStrong's: Bul, the eighth Hebrew month\nKJV: Bul.\n\nCognate Group: H943 (be entangled), H3998 (perplexity), H945 (Bul)",
    946: "בּוּנָה (Bûwnâh | boo-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H995 בִּין ; discretion\nStrong's: Bunah, an Israelite\nKJV: Bunah.\n\nCognate Group: H8394 (discretion), H2985 (Jabin), H1004 (court), H1003 (castle), H1002 (palace), H998 (knowledge), H4000 (taught), H995 (attend), H946 (Bunah), H996 (among), H1143 (champion)",
    947: "בּוּס (bûwç | boos)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to trample (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: loath, tread (down, under (foot)), be polluted.\n\nCognate Group: H8395 (destruction), H947 (loath), H4001 (treading down), H2983 (Jebusite), H2982 (Jebus)\nGreek Equivalents: G1702 ἐμπαίζω, G1847 ἐξουδενόω, G2662 καταπατέω, G3435 μολύνω, G3961 πατέω",
    948: "בּוּץ (bûwts | boots)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (of the same form) meaning to bleach, i.e. (intransitive) be white\nStrong's: probably cotton (of some sort)\nKJV: fine (white) linen.\n\nCognate Group: H948 (fine linen), H1000 (egg)\nGreek Equivalents: G1039 βύσσινος, G1040 βύσσος",
    949: "בֹּוצֵץ (Bôwtsêts | bo-tsates')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H948 בּוּץ ; shining\nStrong's: Botsets, a rock near Michmash\nKJV: Bozez.\n\nCognate Group: H1207 (fen), H1206 (mire), H949 (Bozez)",
    950: "בּוּקָה (bûwqâh | boo-kaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of an unused root (meaning to be hollow)\nStrong's: emptiness (as adjective)\nKJV: empty.\n\nCognate Group: H950 (empty), H4003 (void)",
    951: "בֹּוקֵר (bôwqêr | bo-kare')Typo: lemma בֹּוקִר second vowel, corrected to בֹּוקֵר\n\nTypo: xlit bôwkêr corrected to bôwqêr\n\nDerivation: properly, active participle from H1239 בָּקַר as denominative from H1241 בָּקָר\nStrong's: a cattle-tender\nKJV: herdman.\n\nCognate Group: H1243 (seek out), H1241 (beeve), H1244 (scourged), H1239 (inquire), H1242 (day), H951 (herdman)",
    952: "בּוּר (bûwr | boor)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to bore, i.e. (figuratively) examine\nKJV: declare.\n\nCognate Group: H952 (declare)",
    953: "בֹּור (bôwr | bore)\n\nDerivation: from H952 בּוּר (in the sense of H877 בֹּאר)\nStrong's: a pit hole (especially one used as a cistern or a prison)\nKJV: cistern, dungeon, fountain, pit, well.\n\nCognate Group: H884 (Beer-shebah), H1275 (Beri), H882 (Beeri), H883 (Beer-lahai-roi), H879 (Beer-elim), H3565 (Chorashan), H1268 (Berothah), H880 (Beerah), H875 (pit), H876 (Beer), H1307 (Berothite), H874 (declare), H878 (Beera), H886 (Beerothite), H877 (cistern), H885 (Beeroth of the children of Jaakan), H881 (Beeroth), H953 (cistern), H5626 (Sirah)\nGreek Equivalents: G30 ἀγγεῖον, G1093 γῆ, G3794 ὀχύρωμα, G5421 φρέαρ",
    954: "בּוּשׁ (bûwsh | boosh)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to pale, i.e. by implication to be ashamed; also (by implication) to be disappointed or delayed\nKJV: (be, make, bring to, cause, put to, with, a-) shamed(-d), be (put to) confounded(-fusion), become dry, delay, be long.\n\nCognate Group: H4016 (secrets), H954 (shamed), H1317 (shame), H1322 (ashamed), H955 (shame)\nGreek Equivalents: G152 αἰσχύνη, G153 αἰσχύνομαι, G819 ἀτιμία, G878 ἄφρων, G1135 γυνή, G1870 ἐπαισχύνομαι, G2555 κακοποιός, G2617 καταισχύνω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3784 ὀφείλω, G5549 χρονίζω",
    955: "בּוּשָׁה (bûwshâh | boo-shaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine participle passive of H954 בּוּשׁ\nStrong's: shame\nKJV: shame.\n\nCognate Group: H4016 (secrets), H954 (shamed), H1317 (shame), H1322 (ashamed), H955 (shame)",
    956: "בּוּת (bûwth | booth)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) apparent denominative from H1005 בַּיִת\nStrong's: to lodge over night\nKJV: pass the night.\n\nCognate Group: H1005 (house), H956 (pass the night)\nGreek Equivalents: G835 αὐλίζομαι, G2837 κοιμάω",
    957: "בַּז (baz | baz)\n\nDerivation: from H962 בָּזַז\nStrong's: plunder\nKJV: booty, prey, spoil(-ed).\n\nCognate Group: H962 (catch), H961 (prey), H957 (booty), H897 (spoil), H964 (Bizjothjah)\nGreek Equivalents: G1283 διαρπάζω, G4661 σκῦλον",
    958: "בָּזָא (bâzâʼ | baw-zaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: probably to cleave\nKJV: spoil.\n\nCognate Group: H958 (spoil)\nGreek Equivalents: G3313 μέρος",
    959: "בָּזָה (bâzâh | baw-zaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to disesteem\nKJV: despise, disdain, contemn(-ptible), [phrase] think to scorn, vile person.\n\nCognate Group: H960 (despise), H959 (despise), H963 (contempt), H5240 (vile)\nGreek Equivalents: G820 ἄτιμος, G821 ἀτιμόω, G1847 ἐξουδενόω, G2706 καταφρονέω, G3456 μυκτηρίζω",
    960: "בָּזֹה (bâzôh | baw-zo')\n\nDerivation: from H959 בָּזָה\nStrong's: scorned\nKJV: despise.\n\nCognate Group: H960 (despise), H959 (despise), H963 (contempt), H5240 (vile)",
