    990: "בֶּטֶן (beṭen | beh'-ten)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to be hollow\nStrong's: the belly, especially the womb; also the bosom or body of anything\nKJV: belly, body, [phrase] as they be born, [phrase] within, womb.\n\nCognate Group: H990 (belly), H991 (Beten)\nGreek Equivalents: G1064 γαστήρ, G2588 καρδία, G2836 κοιλία, G4698 σπλάγχνον",
