    1057: "בָּכָא (bâkâʼ | baw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H1056 בָּכָא\nStrong's: the weeping tree (some gum-distilling tree, perhaps the balsam)\nKJV: mulberry tree.\n\nCognate Group: H1039 (Beth-Nimrah), H1055 (palace), H1004 (court), H1041 (Bethaz-maveth), H1054 (Beth-tappuah), H1053 (Beth-shemesh), H1052 (Beth-shean), H1048 (Beth-pazzez), H1024 (Bethmarcaboth), H1051 (Beth-rapha), H1012 (Beth-barah), H1194 (Beon), H1044 (shearing house), H1038 (Beth-maachah), H1040 (Beth-eden), H1050 (Beth-rehob), H358 (Elon-bethhanan), H1010 (Beth-baal-meon), H1046 (Beth-palet), H6407 (Paltite), H1033 (Beth-car), H1056 (Baca), H1016 (Beth-dagon), H1027 (Beth-aram), H1022 (Bethlehemite), H7462 ([idiom] break), H1008 (Beth-el), H1025 (Beth-emek), H1006 (Bajith), H1035 (Bethlehem), H2772 (Horonite), H1017 (Bethelite), H1031 (Beth-hoglah), H1013 (Beth-gader), H1023 (place that was far off), H1014 (Beth-gamul), H1032 (Beth-horon), H1057 (mulberry tree), H1028 (Beth-haran), H1049 (Beth-zur), H1026 (Beth-arabah), H1015 (Beth-diblathaim), H1034 (Beth-lebaoth), H1029 (Beth-shittah), H1030 (Bethshemite), H1011 (Bethbirei), H1043 (Beth-anath), H1042 (Beth-anoth), H6164 (Arbahite), H1047 (Bethpeor), H1020 (Beth-jeshimoth), H1036 (house of Aphrah), H1021 (Beth-haccerem), H1009 (Beth-Arbel), H1007 (Beth-aven)",
    1058: "בָּכָה (bâkâh | baw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to weep; generally to bemoan\nKJV: [idiom] at all, bewail, complain, make lamentation, [idiom] more, mourn, [idiom] sore, [idiom] with tears, weep.\n\nCognate Group: H1068 (mourning), H1066 (Bochim), H1065 (overflowing), H1058 ([idiom] at all), H1059 ([idiom] sore), H439 (Allon-bachuth)\nGreek Equivalents: G1145 δακρύω, G1653 ἐλεέω, G1968 ἐπιπίπτω, G2354 θρηνέω, G2799 κλαίω, G2805 κλαυθμός, G3996 πενθέω",
    1059: "בֶּכֶה (bekeh | beh'-keh)\n\nDerivation: from H1058 בָּכָה\nStrong's: a weeping\nKJV: [idiom] sore.\n\nCognate Group: H1068 (mourning), H1066 (Bochim), H1065 (overflowing), H1058 ([idiom] at all), H1059 ([idiom] sore), H439 (Allon-bachuth)",
    1060: "בְּכֹור (bᵉkôwr | bek-ore')\n\nDerivation: from H1069 בָּכַר\nStrong's: firstborn; hence, chief\nKJV: eldest (son), firstborn(-ling).\n\nCognate Group: H1060 (eldest), H1076 (Bachrites), H1073 (firstripe), H1081 (Baladan), H1069 (make firstborn), H1061 (first fruit), H1067 (firstborn), H1064 (Bechorath), H1074 (Bocheru), H1063 (firstripe), H1072 (dromedary), H1062 (birthright), H1070 (dromedary), H1075 (Bichri), H1071 (Becher)\nGreek Equivalents: G3813 παιδίον, G4416 πρωτότοκος",
    1061: "בִּכּוּר (bikkûwr | bik-koor')\n\nDerivation: from H1069 בָּכַר\nStrong's: the first-fruits of the crop\nKJV: first fruit (-ripe (figuratively)), hasty fruit.\n\nCognate Group: H1060 (eldest), H1076 (Bachrites), H1073 (firstripe), H1081 (Baladan), H1069 (make firstborn), H1061 (first fruit), H1067 (firstborn), H1064 (Bechorath), H1074 (Bocheru), H1063 (firstripe), H1072 (dromedary), H1062 (birthright), H1070 (dromedary), H1075 (Bichri), H1071 (Becher)\nGreek Equivalents: G746 ἀρχή, G2590 καρπός, G3501 νέος, G4274 πρόδρομος",
    1062: "בְּכֹורָה (bᵉkôwrâh | bek-o-raw')\n\nDerivation: or (short) בְּכֹרָה; feminine of H1060 בְּכֹור\nStrong's: the firstling of man or beast; abstractly primogeniture\nKJV: birthright, firstborn(-ling).\n\nCognate Group: H1060 (eldest), H1076 (Bachrites), H1073 (firstripe), H1081 (Baladan), H1069 (make firstborn), H1061 (first fruit), H1067 (firstborn), H1064 (Bechorath), H1074 (Bocheru), H1063 (firstripe), H1072 (dromedary), H1062 (birthright), H1070 (dromedary), H1075 (Bichri), H1071 (Becher)\nGreek Equivalents: G2129 εὐλογία, G4415 πρωτοτόκια",
    1063: "בִּכּוּרָה (bikkûwrâh | bik-koo-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H1061 בִּכּוּר\nStrong's: the early fig\nKJV: firstripe (fruit).\n\nCognate Group: H1060 (eldest), H1076 (Bachrites), H1073 (firstripe), H1081 (Baladan), H1069 (make firstborn), H1061 (first fruit), H1067 (firstborn), H1064 (Bechorath), H1074 (Bocheru), H1063 (firstripe), H1072 (dromedary), H1062 (birthright), H1070 (dromedary), H1075 (Bichri), H1071 (Becher)\nGreek Equivalents: G4274 πρόδρομος, G4406 πρώϊμος, G4810 σῦκον",
    1064: "בְּכֹורַת (Bᵉkôwrath | bek-o-rath')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H1062 בְּכֹורָה ; primogeniture\nStrong's: Bekorath, an Israelite\nKJV: Bechorath.\n\nCognate Group: H1060 (eldest), H1076 (Bachrites), H1073 (firstripe), H1081 (Baladan), H1069 (make firstborn), H1061 (first fruit), H1067 (firstborn), H1064 (Bechorath), H1074 (Bocheru), H1063 (firstripe), H1072 (dromedary), H1062 (birthright), H1070 (dromedary), H1075 (Bichri), H1071 (Becher)",
    1065: "בְּכִי (Bᵉkîy | bek-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H1058 בָּכָה\nStrong's: a weeping; by analogy, a dripping\nKJV: overflowing, [idiom] sore, (continual) weeping, wept.\n\nCognate Group: H1068 (mourning), H1066 (Bochim), H1065 (overflowing), H1058 ([idiom] at all), H1059 ([idiom] sore), H439 (Allon-bachuth)\nGreek Equivalents: G2805 κλαυθμός, G2870 κοπετός, G2906 κραυγή",
    1066: "בֹּכִים (Bôkîym | bo-keem')\n\nDerivation: plural active participle of H1058 בָּכָה ; (with the article) the weepers\nStrong's: Bo-kim, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Bochim.\n\nCognate Group: H1068 (mourning), H1066 (Bochim), H1065 (overflowing), H1058 ([idiom] at all), H1059 ([idiom] sore), H439 (Allon-bachuth)",
