    1145: "בֶּן־יְמִינִי (Ben-yᵉmîynîy | ben-yem-ee-nee')\n\nDerivation: sometimes (with the article inserted) בֵּן־הַיּמִינִי; with H376 אִישׁ inserted (1 Samuel 9:1) בֶּן־אִישׁ ימִינִי; son of a man of Jemini; or shortened אִישׁ יְמִינִי; (1 Samuel 9:4; Esther 2:5) a man of Jemini, or (1 Samuel 20:1) simply יְמִינִי\n\nTypo: xlit Yᵉmînîy corrected to Yᵉmîynîy\n\n; a Jeminite; (plural) בְּנֵי יְמִינִי\n\nTypo: xlit Bᵉnîy corrected to Bᵉnêy\n\n; patron from H1144 בִּנְיָמִין\nStrong's: a Benjaminite, or descendent of Benjamin\nKJV: Benjamite, of Benjamin.\n\nCognate Group: H1135 (Ben-hanan), H1134 (Ben-hail), H1133 (the son of Hur), H1337 (Bath-rabbim), H1125 (the son of Abinadab), H1323 (apple), H1148 (Beninu), H1121 (afflicted), H1142 (Bene-jaakan), H1132 (Ben-zoketh), H1144 (Benjamin), H1128 (the son of Dekar), H1127 (the son of Geber), H1332 (Bithiah), H1126 (Ben-oni), H2618 (Hesed), H1340 (Bath-shua), H1122 (Ben), H1139 (Bene-barak), H1145 (Benjamite), H1136 (the son of Hesed), H1339 (Bath-sheba), H1151 (Ben-ammi), H1130 (Benhadad)",
    1146: "בִּנְיָן (binyân | bin-yawn')\n\nDerivation: from H1129 בָּנָה\nStrong's: an edifice\nKJV: building.\n\nCognate Group: H1131 (Binnui), H1137 (Bani), H1138 (Bunni), H4012 (Mebunnai), H8403 (figure), H1129 (build), H1146 (building), H2998 (Ibnijah), H2996 (Jabneh), H1141 (Benaiah), H1140 (building), H4011 (frame), H2997 (Ibneiah), H2995 (Jabneel)\nGreek Equivalents: G1292 διάστημα",
    1147: "בִּנְיָן (binyân | bin-yawn')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H1146 בִּנְיָן \nStrong's: an edifice\nKJV: building.\n\nCognate Group: H1147 (building), H1124 (build)",
    1148: "בְּנִינוּ (Bᵉnîynûw | ben-ee-noo')\n\nDerivation: probably from H1121 בֵּן with pron. suff.; our son\nStrong's: Beninu, an Israelite\nKJV: Beninu.\n\nCognate Group: H1135 (Ben-hanan), H1134 (Ben-hail), H1133 (the son of Hur), H1337 (Bath-rabbim), H1125 (the son of Abinadab), H1323 (apple), H1148 (Beninu), H1121 (afflicted), H1142 (Bene-jaakan), H1132 (Ben-zoketh), H1144 (Benjamin), H1128 (the son of Dekar), H1127 (the son of Geber), H1332 (Bithiah), H1126 (Ben-oni), H2618 (Hesed), H1340 (Bath-shua), H1122 (Ben), H1139 (Bene-barak), H1145 (Benjamite), H1136 (the son of Hesed), H1339 (Bath-sheba), H1151 (Ben-ammi), H1130 (Benhadad)",
    1149: "בְּנַס (bᵉnaç | ben-as')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: to be enraged\nKJV: be angry.\n\nCognate Group: H1149 (be angry)\nGreek Equivalents: G2372 θυμός",
    1150: "בִּנְעָא (Binʻâʼ | bin-aw')\n\nDerivation: or בִּנְעָה; of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Bina or Binah, an Israelite\nKJV: Binea, Bineah.\n\nCognate Group: H1152 (Besodeiah), H1150 (Binea), H73 (girdle), H1153 (Besai)",
    1151: "בֶּן־עַמִּי (Ben-ʻAmmîy | ben-am-mee')\n\nDerivation: from H1121 בֵּן and H5971 עַם with pronomial suffix; son of my people\nStrong's: Ben-Ammi, a son of Lot\nKJV: Ben-ammi.\n\nCognate Group: H1135 (Ben-hanan), H1134 (Ben-hail), H1133 (the son of Hur), H1337 (Bath-rabbim), H1125 (the son of Abinadab), H1323 (apple), H1148 (Beninu), H1121 (afflicted), H1142 (Bene-jaakan), H1132 (Ben-zoketh), H1144 (Benjamin), H1128 (the son of Dekar), H1127 (the son of Geber), H1332 (Bithiah), H1126 (Ben-oni), H2618 (Hesed), H1340 (Bath-shua), H1122 (Ben), H1139 (Bene-barak), H1145 (Benjamite), H1136 (the son of Hesed), H1339 (Bath-sheba), H1151 (Ben-ammi), H1130 (Benhadad)",
    1152: "בְּסֹודְיָה (Bᵉçôwdᵉyâh | bes-o-deh-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5475 סֹוד and H3050 יָהּ with prepositional prefix; in (the) counsel of Jehovah\nStrong's: Besodejah, an Israelite\nKJV: Besodeiah.\n\nCognate Group: H1152 (Besodeiah), H1150 (Binea), H73 (girdle), H1153 (Besai)",
