    1154: "בֶּסֶר (beçer | beh'-ser)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be sour\nStrong's: an immature grape\nKJV: unripe grape.\n\nCognate Group: H1155 (sour grape), H1154 (unripe grape)",
    1155: "בֹּסֶר (bôçer | bo'ser)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H1154 בֶּסֶר \nStrong's: an immature grape\nKJV: sour grape.\n\nCognate Group: H1155 (sour grape), H1154 (unripe grape)",
    1156: "בְּעָא (bᵉʻâʼ | beh-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or בְּעָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to H1158 בָּעָה\nStrong's: to seek or ask\nKJV: ask, desire, make (petition), pray, request, seek.\n\nCognate Group: H1156 (ask), H1236 (plain), H1169 (chancellor), H1159 (petition)\nGreek Equivalents: G154 αἰτέω, G515 ἀξιόω, G2172 εὔχομαι, G2212 ζητέω",
    1157: "בְּעַד (bᵉʻad | beh-ad')\n\nDerivation: from H5704 עַד with prepositional prefix\nStrong's: in up to or over against; generally at, beside, among, behind, for, etc.\nKJV: about, at by (means of), for, over, through, up (-on), within.\n\nCognate Group: H1157 (about)\nGreek Equivalents: G1622 ἐκτός, G1855 ἔξωθεν",
    1158: "בָּעָה (bâʻâh | baw-aw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to gush over, i.e. to swell; (figuratively) to desire earnestly; by implication to ask\nKJV: cause, inquire, seek up, swell out.\n\nCognate Group: H1158 (cause)\nGreek Equivalents: G2212 ζητέω, G2618 κατακαίω, G2638 καταλαμβάνω",
