    1160: "בְּעֹור (Bᵉʻôwr | beh-ore')\n\nDerivation: from H1197 בָּעַר (in the sense of burning); a lamp\nStrong's: Beor, the name of the father of an Edomitish king; also of that of Balaam\nKJV: Beor.\n\nCognate Group: H1198 (brutish), H1160 (Beor), H8404 (Taberah), H1202 (Baaseiah), H1203 (Beeshterah), H1199 (Baara), H1200 (fire), H1165 (beast), H1201 (Baasha), H1197 (be brutish)\nGreek Equivalents: G1007 Βοσόρ",
    1161: "בִּעוּתִים (biʻûwthîym | be-oo-theme')\n\nDerivation: masculine plural from H1204 בָּעַת\nStrong's: alarms\nKJV: terrors.\n\nCognate Group: H1205 (trouble), H1209 (Bezai), H1161 (terrors), H1204 (affright)",
    1162: "בֹּעַז (Bôʻaz | bo'-az)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root of uncertain meaning\nStrong's: Boaz, the ancestor of David; also the name of a pillar in front of the temple\nKJV: Boaz.\n\nCognate Group: H1162 (Boaz)\nGreek Equivalents: G1003 Βοόζ",
    1163: "בָּעַט (bâʻaṭ | baw-at')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to trample down, i.e. (figuratively) despise\nKJV: kick.\n\nCognate Group: H1163 (kick)",
