    1197: "בָּעַר (bâʻar | baw-ar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; also as denominative from H1198 בַּעַר \nStrong's: to kindle, i.e. consume (by fire or by eating); to be(-come) brutish\nKJV: be brutish, bring (put, take) away, burn, (cause to) eat (up), feed, heat, kindle, set (on fire), waste.\n\nCognate Group: H1198 (brutish), H1160 (Beor), H8404 (Taberah), H1202 (Baaseiah), H1203 (Beeshterah), H1199 (Baara), H1200 (fire), H1165 (beast), H1201 (Baasha), H1197 (be brutish)\nGreek Equivalents: G381 ἀνάπτω, G853 ἀφανίζω, G1285 διασαφέω, G1571 ἐκκαθαίρω, G1572 ἐκκαίω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1825 ἐξεγείρω, G1842 ἐξολοθρεύω, G1951 ἐπιλέγομαι, G2511 καθαρίζω, G2545 καίω, G2618 κατακαίω, G2719 κατεσθίω, G2740 καῦσις, G3154 ματαιόω, G3471 μωραίνω",
