    1214: "בָּצַע (bâtsaʻ | baw-tsah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root to break off, i.e. (usually) plunder\nStrong's: figuratively, to finish, or (intransitively) stop\nKJV: (be) covet(-ous), cut (off), finish, fulfill, gain (greedily), get, be given to (covetousness), greedy, perform, be wounded.\n\nCognate Group: H1215 (covetousness), H1214 (covet)\nGreek Equivalents: G91 ἀδικέω, G337 ἀναιρέω, G1907 ἐπέχω, G2005 ἐπιτελέω, G4122 πλεονεκτέω, G4931 συντελέω, G4931 συντελέω",
