    1227: "בַּקְבּוּק (Baqbûwq | bak-book')\n\nDerivation: the same as H1228 בַּקְבֻּק \n\nTypo: xlit baqbûk corrected to baqbuq\n\nStrong's: Bakbuk, one of the Nethinim\nKJV: Bakbuk.\n\nCognate Group: H1238 (empty), H1229 (Bakbukiah), H1228 (bottle), H1227 (Bakbuk), H2999 (Jabbok)",
    1228: "בַּקְבֻּק (baqbuq | bak-book')Typo: xlit baqbûk corrected to baqbuq\n\nGreek Equivalents: G4713 στάμνος \n\nDerivation: from H1238 בָּקַק\nStrong's: a bottle (from the gurgling in emptying)\n\nKJV: bottle, cruse.\n\nCognate Group: H1238 (empty), H1229 (Bakbukiah), H1228 (bottle), H1227 (Bakbuk), H2999 (Jabbok)",
    1229: "בַּקְבֻּקְיָה (Baqbuqyâh | bak-book-yaw')\n\nTypo: xlit Baqbukyâh corrected to Baqbuqyâh\n\nDerivation: from H1228 בַּקְבֻּק \n\nTypo: xlit baqbûk corrected to baqbuq\n\n and H3050 יָהּ ; emptying (i.e. wasting) of Jah\nStrong's: Bakbukjah, an Israelite\nKJV: Bakbukiah.\n\nCognate Group: H1238 (empty), H1229 (Bakbukiah), H1228 (bottle), H1227 (Bakbuk), H2999 (Jabbok)",
    1230: "בַּקְבַּקַּר (Baqbaqqar | bak-bak-kar')\n\nDerivation: reduplicated from H1239 בָּקַר ; searcher\nStrong's: Bakbakkar, an Israelite\nKJV: Bakbakkar.\n\nCognate Group: H1226 (dearth), H1223 (Bozrah), H1208 (vintage), H1221 (Bezer), H1220 (gold defence), H1224 (Bozrah), H4013 (fenced), H1230 (Bakbakkar), H6869 (adversary), H1219 (cut off), H1225 (stronghold), H1210 (vintage)",
    1231: "בֻּקִּי (Buqqîy | book-kee')\n\nDerivation: from H1238 בָּקַק ; wasteful\nStrong's: Bukki, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Bukki.\n\nCognate Group: H1232 (Bukkiah), H1231 (Bukki)",
    1232: "בֻּקִּיָּה (Buqqîyâh | book-kee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H1238 בָּקַק and H3050 יָהּ ; wasting of Jah\nStrong's: Bukkijah, an Israelite\nKJV: Bukkiah.\n\nCognate Group: H1232 (Bukkiah), H1231 (Bukki)",
    1233: "בְּקִיעַ (bᵉqîyaʻ | bek-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from H1234 בָּקַע\nStrong's: a fissure\nKJV: breach, cleft.\n\nCognate Group: H1234 (make a breach), H1235 (bekah), H1237 (plain), H1233 (breach)\nGreek Equivalents: G2927 κρυπτός, G4485 ῥῆγμα",
    1234: "בָּקַע (bâqaʻ | baw-kah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to cleave; generally, to rend, break, rip or open\nKJV: make a breach, break forth (into, out, in pieces, through, up), be ready to burst, cleave (asunder), cut out, divide, hatch, rend (asunder), rip up, tear, win.\n\nCognate Group: H1234 (make a breach), H1235 (bekah), H1237 (plain), H1233 (breach)\nGreek Equivalents: G455 ἀνοίγω, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G1288 διασπάω, G2147 εὑρίσκω, G2616 καταδυναστεύω, G4486 ῥήγνυμι, G4977 σχίζω, G5080 τήκω",
    1235: "בֶּקַע (beqaʻ | beh'-kah)\n\nDerivation: from H1234 בָּקַע\nStrong's: a section (half) of ashekel, i.e. a beka (a weight and a coin)\nKJV: bekah, half a shekel.\n\nCognate Group: H1234 (make a breach), H1235 (bekah), H1237 (plain), H1233 (breach)\nGreek Equivalents: G1406 δραχμή",
    1236: "בִּקְעָא (biqʻâʼ | bik-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H1237 בִּקְעָה \nStrong's: properly, a split, i.e. a wide level valley between mountains\nKJV: plain.\n\nCognate Group: H1156 (ask), H1236 (plain), H1169 (chancellor), H1159 (petition)",
    1237: "בִּקְעָה (biqʻâh | bik-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H1234 בָּקַע\nStrong's: properly, a split, i.e. a wide level valley between mountains\nKJV: plain, valley.\n\nCognate Group: H1234 (make a breach), H1235 (bekah), H1237 (plain), H1233 (breach)\nGreek Equivalents: G3006 λεῖος, G3977 πεδινός",
    1238: "בָּקַק (bâqaq | baw-kah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to pour out, i.e. to empty, figuratively, to depopulate; by analogy, to spread out (as a fruitful vine)\nKJV: (make) empty (out), fail, [idiom] utterly, make void.\n\nCognate Group: H1238 (empty)\nGreek Equivalents: G1621 ἐκτινάσσω, G2704 καταφθείρω, G3075 λυμαίνομαι, G5015 ταράσσω, G5351 φθείρω, G5356 φθορά",
    1239: "בָּקַר (bâqar | baw-kar)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to plough, or (generally) break forth, i.e. (figuratively) to inspect, admire, care for, consider\nKJV: (make) inquire (-ry), (make) search, seek out.\n\nCognate Group: H1243 (seek out), H1241 (beeve), H1244 (scourged), H1239 (inquire), H1242 (day), H951 (herdman)\nGreek Equivalents: G1567 ἐκζητέω, G1980 ἐπισκέπτομαι",
    1240: "בְּקַר (bᵉqar | bek-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H1239 בָּקַר \nStrong's: properly, to plough, or (generally) break forth, i.e. (figuratively) to inspect, admire, care for, consider\nKJV: inquire, make search.\n\nCognate Group: H1247 ([idiom] old), H1123 (child), H1240 (inquire)",
    1241: "בָּקָר (bâqâr | baw-kawr')\n\nDerivation: from H1239 בָּקַר\nStrong's: beef cattle or an animal of the ox family of either gender (as used for plowing); collectively, a herd\nKJV: beeve, bull ([phrase] -ock), [phrase] calf, [phrase] cow, great (cattle), [phrase] heifer, herd, kine, ox.\n\nCognate Group: H1243 (seek out), H1241 (beeve), H1244 (scourged), H1239 (inquire), H1242 (day), H951 (herdman)\nGreek Equivalents: G1016 βοῦς, G1151 δάμαλις, G2934 κτῆνος, G3448 μόσχος",
    1242: "בֹּקֶר (bôqer | bo'-ker)\n\nDerivation: from H1239 בָּקַר\nStrong's: properly, dawn (as the break of day); generally, morning\nKJV: ([phrase]) day, early, morning, morrow.\n\nCognate Group: H1243 (seek out), H1241 (beeve), H1244 (scourged), H1239 (inquire), H1242 (day), H951 (herdman)\nGreek Equivalents: G2250 ἡμέρα, G3722 ὄρθρος, G4404 πρωΐ, G4407 πρωϊνός, G5338 φέγγος",
    1243: "בַּקָּרָה (baqqârâh | bak-kaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: intensive from H1239 בָּקַר\nStrong's: a looking after\nKJV: seek out.\n\nCognate Group: H1243 (seek out), H1241 (beeve), H1244 (scourged), H1239 (inquire), H1242 (day), H951 (herdman)\nGreek Equivalents: G2212 ζητέω",
    1244: "בִּקֹּרֶת (biqqôreth | bik-ko-reth)\n\nDerivation: from H1239 בָּקַר\nStrong's: properly, examination, i.e. (by implication) punishment\nKJV: scourged.\n\nCognate Group: H1243 (seek out), H1241 (beeve), H1244 (scourged), H1239 (inquire), H1242 (day), H951 (herdman)\nGreek Equivalents: G1984 ἐπισκοπή",
    1245: "בָּקַשׁ (bâqash | baw-kash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to search out (by any method, specifically in worship or prayer); by implication, to strive after\nKJV: ask, beg, beseech, desire, enquire, get, make inquisition, procure, (make) request, require, seek (for).\n\nCognate Group: H1248 (son), H1246 (request), H1245 (ask)\nGreek Equivalents: G114 ἀθετέω, G327 ἀναζητέω, G426 ἀνετάζω, G515 ἀξιόω, G1011 βουλεύω, G1567 ἐκζητέω, G1905 ἐπερωτάω, G1914 ἐπιβλέπω, G1934 ἐπιζητέω, G1980 ἐπισκέπτομαι, G2045 ἐρευνάω, G2147 εὑρίσκω, G2212 ζητέω, G2323 θεραπεύω, G3868 παραιτέομαι, G4347 προσκολλάω",
    1246: "בַּקָּשָׁה (baqqâshâh | bak-kaw-shaw')\n\nDerivation: from H1245 בָּקַשׁ\nStrong's: a petition\nKJV: request.\n\nCognate Group: H1248 (son), H1246 (request), H1245 (ask)\nGreek Equivalents: G2212 ζητέω",
    1247: "בַּר (bar | bar)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H1121 בֵּן\nStrong's: a son, grandson, etc.\nKJV: [idiom] old, son.\n\nCognate Group: H1247 ([idiom] old), H1123 (child), H1240 (inquire)\nGreek Equivalents: G5207 υἱός",
    1248: "בַּר (bar | bar)\n\nDerivation: borrowed (as a title) from H1247 בַּר\nStrong's: the heir (apparent to the throne)\nKJV: son.\n\nCognate Group: H1248 (son), H1246 (request), H1245 (ask)\nGreek Equivalents: G3809 παιδεία, G5043 τέκνον",
    1249: "בַּר (bar | bar)\n\nDerivation: from H1305 בָּרַר (in its various senses)\nStrong's: beloved; also pure, empty\nKJV: choice, clean, clear, pure.\n\nCognate Group: H1287 (sope), H1249 (choice), H1257 (fowl), H1252 (cleanness), H1305 (make bright), H1250 (corn), H1253 ([idiom] never so)\nGreek Equivalents: G273 ἄμεμπτος, G1080 γεννάω, G1588 ἐκλεκτός, G1729 ἐνδεής, G1854 ἔξω, G2112 εὐθέως, G2117 εὐθύς, G2344 θησαυρός, G2513 καθαρός, G4621 σῖτος",
    1250: "בָּר (bâr | bawr)\n\nDerivation: or בַּר; from H1305 בָּרַר (in the sense of winnowing)\nStrong's: grain of any kind (even while standing in the field); by extension the open country\nKJV: corn, wheat.\n\nCognate Group: H1287 (sope), H1249 (choice), H1257 (fowl), H1252 (cleanness), H1305 (make bright), H1250 (corn), H1253 ([idiom] never so)\nGreek Equivalents: G66 ἄγριος, G68 ἀγρός, G1093 γῆ",
    1251: "בַּר (bar | bar)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H1250 בָּר\nStrong's: a field\nKJV: field.\n\nCognate Group: H1321 (flesh), H1251 (field), H1325 (bath)",
    1252: "בֹּר (bôr | bore)\n\nDerivation: from H1305 בָּרַר\nStrong's: purify\nKJV: cleanness, pureness.\n\nCognate Group: H1287 (sope), H1249 (choice), H1257 (fowl), H1252 (cleanness), H1305 (make bright), H1250 (corn), H1253 ([idiom] never so)",
    1253: "בֹּר (bôr | bore)\n\nDerivation: the same as H1252 בֹּר\nStrong's: vegetable lye (from its cleansing); used as a soap forwashing, or a flux formetals\nKJV: [idiom] never so, purely.\n\nCognate Group: H1287 (sope), H1249 (choice), H1257 (fowl), H1252 (cleanness), H1305 (make bright), H1250 (corn), H1253 ([idiom] never so)",
    1254: "בָּרָא (bârâʼ | baw-raw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: (absolutely) to create; (qualified) to cut down (a wood), select, feed (as formative processes)\nKJV: choose, create (creator), cut down, dispatch, do, make (fat).\n\nCognate Group: H1254 (choose), H1278 (new thing), H1256 (Beraiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G757 ἄρχω, G1081 γέννημα, G1096 γίνομαι, G1166 δεικνύω, G1299 διατάσσω, G1571 ἐκκαθαίρω, G1757 ἐνευλογέω, G2090 ἑτοιμάζω, G2680 κατασκευάζω, G2936 κτίζω, G4160 ποιέω",
    1255: "בְּרֹאדַךְ בַּלְאֲדָן (Bᵉrôʼdak Balʼădân | ber-o-dak' bal-ad-awn')\n\nDerivation: a variation of H4757 מְרֹאדַךְ בַּלְאָדָן\nStrong's: Berodak-Baladan, a Babylonian king\nKJV: Berodach-baladan.Birliy.\n\nCognate Group: H4777 (rebellion), H4775 (rebel), H4782 (Mordecai), H4757 (Merodach-baladan), H4778 (Mered), H4780 ([idiom] rebellious), H1255 (Berodach-baladan), H4781 (Merodach)",
    1256: "בְּרָאיָה (Bᵉrâʼyâh | ber-aw-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H1254 בָּרָא and H8050 שְׁמוּאֵל ; Jah has created\nStrong's: Berajah, an Israelite\nKJV: Beraiah.\n\nCognate Group: H1254 (choose), H1278 (new thing), H1256 (Beraiah)",
    1257: "בַּרְבֻּר (barbur | bar-boor')\n\nDerivation: by reduplication from H1250 בָּר\nStrong's: a fowl (as fattened on grain)\nKJV: fowl.\n\nCognate Group: H1287 (sope), H1249 (choice), H1257 (fowl), H1252 (cleanness), H1305 (make bright), H1250 (corn), H1253 ([idiom] never so)\nGreek Equivalents: G3733 ὄρνις",
    1258: "בָּרַד (bârad | baw-rad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root,\nStrong's: to hail\nKJV: hail.\n\nCognate Group: H1259 (hail), H1260 (Bered), H1258 (hail), H1261 (grisled)",
    1259: "בָּרָד (bârâd | baw-rawd')\n\nDerivation: from H1258 בָּרַד\nStrong's: hail\nKJV: hail(stones).\n\nCognate Group: H1259 (hail), H1260 (Bered), H1258 (hail), H1261 (grisled)\nGreek Equivalents: G2171 εὐχή, G5464 χάλαζα",
    1260: "בֶּרֶד (Bered | beh'red)\n\nDerivation: from H1258 בָּרַד ; hail\nStrong's: Bered, the name of a place south of Palestine, also of an Israelite\nKJV: Bered.\n\nCognate Group: H1259 (hail), H1260 (Bered), H1258 (hail), H1261 (grisled)",
    1261: "בָּרֹד (bârôd | baw-rode')\n\nDerivation: from H1258 בָּרַד\nStrong's: spotted (as if with hail)\nKJV: grisled.\n\nCognate Group: H1259 (hail), H1260 (Bered), H1258 (hail), H1261 (grisled)\nGreek Equivalents: G4164 ποικίλος",
    1262: "בָּרָה (bârâh | baw-raw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; to select; also (as denominative from H1250 בָּר) to feed; also (as equivalent to H1305 בָּרַר) to render clear (Ecclesiastes 3:18)\n\nStrong's: to select; to feed; to render clear\nKJV: choose, (cause to) eat, manifest, (give) meat.\n\nCognate Group: H1267 (meat), H1262 (choose), H1279 (meat)\nGreek Equivalents: G1035 βρῶσις, G1586 ἐκλέγομαι, G2068 ἐσθίω, G4906 συνεσθίω, G5595 ψωμίζω",
    1263: "בָּרוּךְ (Bârûwk | baw-rook')\n\nDerivation: passive participle from H1288 בָרַךְ ; blessed\nStrong's: Baruk, the name of three Israelites\nKJV: Baruch.\n\nCognate Group: H1294 (Berachah), H1292 (Barachel), H1263 (Baruch), H3000 (Jeberechiah), H1293 (blessing), H1296 (Berachiah), H1295 (pool), H1288 ([idiom] abundantly), H1290 (knee)",
    1264: "בְּרֹום (bᵉrôwm | ber-ome')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: damask (stuff of variegated thread)\nKJV: rich apparel.\n\nCognate Group: H1298 (Bera), H1284 (Beerites), H1283 (Beriah), H1264 (rich apparel)\nGreek Equivalents: G1588 ἐκλεκτός",
    1265: "בְּרֹושׁ (bᵉrôwsh | ber-osh')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a cypress (?) tree; hence, a lance or a musical instrument (as made of that wood)\nKJV: fir (tree).\n\nCognate Group: H1266 (fir), H1306 (Birsha), H1265 (fir)\nGreek Equivalents: G2748 Κεδρών, G4285 προηγέομαι",
    1266: "בְּרֹות (bᵉrôwth | ber-oth')Typo: lemma בֻּרֹות first vowel, corrected to בְּרֹות\n\nDerivation: a variation of H1265 בְּרֹושׁ\nStrong's: the cypress (or some elastic tree)\n\nKJV: fir.\n\nCognate Group: H1266 (fir), H1306 (Birsha), H1265 (fir)",
    1267: "בָּרוּת (bârûwth | baw-rooth)\n\nDerivation: from H1262 בָּרָה\nStrong's: food\nKJV: meat.\n\nCognate Group: H1267 (meat), H1262 (choose), H1279 (meat)\nGreek Equivalents: G1033 βρῶμα",
    1268: "בֵּרֹותָה (Bêrôwthâh | bay-ro-thaw')\n\nDerivation: or בֵּרֹתַי; probably from H1266 בְּרֹות \n\nTypo: lemma בֻּרֹות first vowel, corrected to בְּרֹות\n\n; cypress or cypresslike\nStrong's: Berothah or Berothai, a place north of Palestine\nKJV: Berothah, Berothai.\n\nCognate Group: H884 (Beer-shebah), H1275 (Beri), H882 (Beeri), H883 (Beer-lahai-roi), H879 (Beer-elim), H3565 (Chorashan), H1268 (Berothah), H880 (Beerah), H875 (pit), H876 (Beer), H1307 (Berothite), H874 (declare), H878 (Beera), H886 (Beerothite), H877 (cistern), H885 (Beeroth of the children of Jaakan), H881 (Beeroth), H953 (cistern), H5626 (Sirah)",
    1269: "בִּרְזֹות (Birzôwth | beer-zoth')\n\nDerivation: probably feminine plural from an unused root (apparently mean to pierce); holes\nStrong's: Birzoth, an Israelite\nKJV: Birzavith (from the marg.).\n\nCognate Group: H1270 (head), H1271 (Barzillai), H1269 (Birzavith)",
    1270: "בַּרְזֶל (barzel | bar-zel')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from the root of H1269 בִּרְזֹות\nStrong's: iron (as cutting); by extension, an iron implement\nKJV: (ax) head, iron.\n\nCognate Group: H1270 (head), H1271 (Barzillai), H1269 (Birzavith)\nGreek Equivalents: G3162 μάχαιρα, G4603 σιδήρεος, G4604 σίδηρος",
    1271: "בַּרְזִלַּי (Barzillay | bar-zil-lah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H1270 בַּרְזֶל ; iron-hearted\nStrong's: Barzillai, the name of three Israelites\nKJV: Barzillai.\n\nCognate Group: H1270 (head), H1271 (Barzillai), H1269 (Birzavith)",
    1272: "בָּרַח (bârach | baw-rakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to bolt, i.e. figuratively, to flee suddenly\nKJV: chase (away); drive away, fain, flee (away), put to flight, make haste, reach, run away, shoot.\n\nCognate Group: H1273 (Barhumite), H1282 (Bariah), H1272 (chase ; drive away), H1281 (crooked), H1280 (bar), H4015 (fugitive), H1276 (Berites)\nGreek Equivalents: G402 ἀναχωρέω, G683 ἀπωθέομαι, G1338 διϊκνέομαι, G1377 διώκω, G1559 ἐκδιώκω, G1633 ἐκχωρέω, G4982 σώζω, G5343 φεύγω, G5437 φυγή",
    1273: "בַּרְחֻמִי (Barchumîy | bar-khoo-mee')\n\nDerivation: by transposition for H978 בַּחֲרוּמִי\nStrong's: a Barchumite, or native of Bachurim\nKJV: Barhumite.\n\nCognate Group: H1273 (Barhumite), H1282 (Bariah), H1272 (chase ; drive away), H1281 (crooked), H1280 (bar), H4015 (fugitive), H1276 (Berites)",
