    1322: "בֹּשֶׁת (bôsheth | bo'-sheth)\n\nDerivation: from H954 בּוּשׁ\nStrong's: shame (the feeling and the condition, as well as its cause); by implication (specifically) an idol\nKJV: ashamed, confusion, [phrase] greatly, (put to) shame(-ful thing).\n\nCognate Group: H4016 (secrets), H954 (shamed), H1317 (shame), H1322 (ashamed), H955 (shame)\nGreek Equivalents: G152 αἰσχύνη",
