    1325: "בַּת (bath | bath)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H1324 בַּת \nStrong's: a bath or Hebrew measure (as a means of division) of liquids\nKJV: bath.\n\nCognate Group: H1321 (flesh), H1251 (field), H1325 (bath)\nGreek Equivalents: G5547 Χριστός",
    1326: "בָּתָה (bâthâh | baw-thaw')\n\nDerivation: probably an orthographical variation for H1327 בַּתָּה\nStrong's: desolation\nKJV: waste.\n\nCognate Group: H1324 (bath), H1326 (waste), H1327 (desolate)\nGreek Equivalents: G3004 λέγω",
