    1328: "בְּתוּאֵל (Bᵉthûwʼêl | beth-oo-ale')\n\nDerivation: apparently from the same as H1326 בָּתָה and H410 אֵל ; destroyed of God\nStrong's: Bethuel, the name of a nephew of Abraham, and of a place in Palestine\nKJV: Bethuel. Compare H1329 בְּתוּל .\n\nCognate Group: H1328 (Bethuel), H1329 (Bethuel), H1318 (tread)",
    1329: "בְּתוּל (Bᵉthûwl | beth-ool')\n\nDerivation: for H1328 בְּתוּאֵל\nStrong's: Bethul (i.e. Bethuel), a place in Palestine\nKJV: Bethuel.\n\nCognate Group: H1328 (Bethuel), H1329 (Bethuel), H1318 (tread)",
