    1336: "בֶּתֶר (Bether | beh'-ther)\n\nDerivation: the same as H1335 בֶּתֶר\nStrong's: Bether, a (craggy) place in Palestine\nKJV: Bether.\n\nCognate Group: H1334 (divide), H1335 (part), H1338 (Bithron), H1336 (Bether)",
    1337: "בַּת רַבִּים (Bath Rabbîym | bath rab-beem')\n\nDerivation: from H1323 בַּת and a masculine plural from H7227 רַב\nStrong's: the daughter (i.e. city) of Rabbah\nKJV: Bath-rabbim.\n\nCognate Group: H1135 (Ben-hanan), H1134 (Ben-hail), H1133 (the son of Hur), H1337 (Bath-rabbim), H1125 (the son of Abinadab), H1323 (apple), H1148 (Beninu), H1121 (afflicted), H1142 (Bene-jaakan), H1132 (Ben-zoketh), H1144 (Benjamin), H1128 (the son of Dekar), H1127 (the son of Geber), H1332 (Bithiah), H1126 (Ben-oni), H2618 (Hesed), H1340 (Bath-shua), H1122 (Ben), H1139 (Bene-barak), H1145 (Benjamite), H1136 (the son of Hesed), H1339 (Bath-sheba), H1151 (Ben-ammi), H1130 (Benhadad)",
    1338: "בִּתְרֹון (Bithrôwn | bith-rone')\n\nDerivation: from H1334 בָּתַר ; (with the article) the craggy spot\nStrong's: Bithron, a place East of the Jordan\nKJV: Bithron.\n\nCognate Group: H1334 (divide), H1335 (part), H1338 (Bithron), H1336 (Bether)",
    1339: "בַּת־שֶׁבַע (Bath-Shebaʻ | bath-sheh'-bah)\n\nDerivation: from H1323 בַּת and H7651 שֶׁבַע (in the sense of H7650 שָׁבַע); daughter of an oath\nStrong's: Bath-Sheba, the mother of Solomon\nKJV: Bath-sheba.\n\nCognate Group: H1135 (Ben-hanan), H1134 (Ben-hail), H1133 (the son of Hur), H1337 (Bath-rabbim), H1125 (the son of Abinadab), H1323 (apple), H1148 (Beninu), H1121 (afflicted), H1142 (Bene-jaakan), H1132 (Ben-zoketh), H1144 (Benjamin), H1128 (the son of Dekar), H1127 (the son of Geber), H1332 (Bithiah), H1126 (Ben-oni), H2618 (Hesed), H1340 (Bath-shua), H1122 (Ben), H1139 (Bene-barak), H1145 (Benjamite), H1136 (the son of Hesed), H1339 (Bath-sheba), H1151 (Ben-ammi), H1130 (Benhadad)",
    1340: "בַּת־שׁוּעַ (Bath-Shûwaʻ | bath-shoo'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from H1323 בַּת and H7771 שֹׁועַ ; daughter of wealth; the same as H1339 בַּת־שֶׁבַע \nStrong's: Bath-shua,\nKJV: Bath-shua.\n\nCognate Group: H1135 (Ben-hanan), H1134 (Ben-hail), H1133 (the son of Hur), H1337 (Bath-rabbim), H1125 (the son of Abinadab), H1323 (apple), H1148 (Beninu), H1121 (afflicted), H1142 (Bene-jaakan), H1132 (Ben-zoketh), H1144 (Benjamin), H1128 (the son of Dekar), H1127 (the son of Geber), H1332 (Bithiah), H1126 (Ben-oni), H2618 (Hesed), H1340 (Bath-shua), H1122 (Ben), H1139 (Bene-barak), H1145 (Benjamite), H1136 (the son of Hesed), H1339 (Bath-sheba), H1151 (Ben-ammi), H1130 (Benhadad)",
    1341: "גֵּא (gêʼ | gay')\n\nDerivation: for H1343 גֵּאֶה\nStrong's: haughty\nKJV: proud.\n\nCognate Group: H1346 (excellency), H1341 (proud), H1348 (excellent things), H1344 (pride), H1466 (lifting up), H1345 (Geuel), H1342 (gloriously), H1349 (proud), H1343 (proud), H1347 (arrogancy)\nGreek Equivalents: G1067 γέεννα, G1067 γέεννα, G1067 γέεννα, G5197 ὑβριστής, G5493 χείμαῤῥος",
    1342: "גָּאָה (gâʼâh | gaw-aw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to mount up; hence, in general, to rise, (figuratively) be majestic\nKJV: gloriously, grow up, increase, be risen, triumph.\n\nCognate Group: H1346 (excellency), H1341 (proud), H1348 (excellent things), H1344 (pride), H1466 (lifting up), H1345 (Geuel), H1342 (gloriously), H1349 (proud), H1343 (proud), H1347 (arrogancy)\nGreek Equivalents: G64 ἀγρεύω, G1392 δοξάζω",
    1343: "גֵּאֶה (gêʼeh | gay-eh')\n\nDerivation: from H1342 גָּאָה\nStrong's: lofty; figuratively, arrogant\nKJV: proud.\n\nCognate Group: H1346 (excellency), H1341 (proud), H1348 (excellent things), H1344 (pride), H1466 (lifting up), H1345 (Geuel), H1342 (gloriously), H1349 (proud), H1343 (proud), H1347 (arrogancy)\nGreek Equivalents: G5195 ὑβρίζω, G5195 ὑβρίζω, G5197 ὑβριστής, G5244 ὑπερήφανος, G5308 ὑψηλός",
    1344: "גֵּאָה (gêʼâh | gay-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine from H1342 גָּאָה\nStrong's: arrogance\nKJV: pride.\n\nCognate Group: H1346 (excellency), H1341 (proud), H1348 (excellent things), H1344 (pride), H1466 (lifting up), H1345 (Geuel), H1342 (gloriously), H1349 (proud), H1343 (proud), H1347 (arrogancy)\nGreek Equivalents: G5196 ὕβρις",
    1345: "גְּאוּאֵל (Gᵉʼûwʼêl | gheh-oo-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H1342 גָּאָה and H410 אֵל ; majesty of God\nStrong's: Geuel, an Israelite\nKJV: Geuel.\n\nCognate Group: H1346 (excellency), H1341 (proud), H1348 (excellent things), H1344 (pride), H1466 (lifting up), H1345 (Geuel), H1342 (gloriously), H1349 (proud), H1343 (proud), H1347 (arrogancy)",
    1346: "גַּאֲוָה (gaʼăvâh | gah-av-aw')Typo: xlit gaʻăvâh corrected to gaʼăvâh\n\nGreek Equivalents: G2745 καύχημα, G3169 μεγαλοπρεπής \n\nDerivation: from H1342 גָּאָה\nStrong's: arrogance or majesty; by implication, (concretely) ornament\nKJV: excellency, haughtiness, highness, pride, proudly, swelling.\n\nCognate Group: H1346 (excellency), H1341 (proud), H1348 (excellent things), H1344 (pride), H1466 (lifting up), H1345 (Geuel), H1342 (gloriously), H1349 (proud), H1343 (proud), H1347 (arrogancy)",
    1347: "גָּאֹון (gâʼôwn | gaw-ohn')\n\nDerivation: from H1342 גָּאָה ; the same as H1346 גַּאֲוָה \n\nTypo: xlit gaʻăvâh corrected to gaʼăvâh\n\nStrong's: arrogance or majesty; by implication, (concretely) ornament\nKJV: arrogancy, excellency(-lent), majesty, pomp, pride, proud, swelling.\n\nCognate Group: H1346 (excellency), H1341 (proud), H1348 (excellent things), H1344 (pride), H1466 (lifting up), H1345 (Geuel), H1342 (gloriously), H1349 (proud), H1343 (proud), H1347 (arrogancy)\nGreek Equivalents: G93 ἀδικία, G1391 δόξα, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G2479 ἰσχύς, G5196 ὕβρις, G5243 ὑπερηφανία, G5311 ὕψος, G5312 ὑψόω",
    1348: "גֵּאוּת (gêʼûwth | gay-ooth')\n\nDerivation: from H1342 גָּאָה ; the same as H1346 גַּאֲוָה \n\nTypo: xlit gaʻăvâh corrected to gaʼăvâh\n\nStrong's: arrogance or majesty; by implication, (concretely) ornament\nKJV: excellent things, lifting up, majesty, pride, proudly, raging.\n\nCognate Group: H1346 (excellency), H1341 (proud), H1348 (excellent things), H1344 (pride), H1466 (lifting up), H1345 (Geuel), H1342 (gloriously), H1349 (proud), H1343 (proud), H1347 (arrogancy)\nGreek Equivalents: G2143 εὐπρέπεια, G2904 κράτος",
    1349: "גַּאֲיֹון (gaʼăyôwn | gah-ah-yone')\n\nDerivation: from H1342 גָּאָה\nStrong's: haughty\nKJV: proud.\n\nCognate Group: H1346 (excellency), H1341 (proud), H1348 (excellent things), H1344 (pride), H1466 (lifting up), H1345 (Geuel), H1342 (gloriously), H1349 (proud), H1343 (proud), H1347 (arrogancy)",
    1350: "גָּאַל (gâʼal | gaw-al')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root, to redeem (according to the Oriental law of kinship), i.e.\nStrong's: to be the next of kin (and as such to buy back a relative's property, marry his widow, etc.)\nKJV: [idiom] in any wise, [idiom] at all, avenger, deliver, (do, perform the part of near, next) kinsfolk(-man), purchase, ransom, redeem(-er), revenger.\n\nCognate Group: H3008 (Igal), H1350 ([idiom] in any wise), H1353 (kindred)\nGreek Equivalents: G683 ἀπωθέομαι, G868 ἀφίστημι, G948 βδελύσσω, G1590 ἐκλύω, G1653 ἐλεέω, G1807 ἐξαιρέω, G3084 λυτρόω, G3086 λυτρωτής, G4360 προσοχθίζω, G4506 ῥύομαι",
    1351: "גָּאַל (gâʼal | gaw-al')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root, (rather identified with H1350 גָּאַל, through the idea of freeing, i.e. repudiating)\nStrong's: to soil or (figuratively) desecrate\nKJV: defile, pollute, stain.\n\nCognate Group: H1352 (defile), H1351 (defile)\nGreek Equivalents: G3435 μολύνω",
    1352: "גֹּאֶל (gôʼel | go'-el)\n\nDerivation: from H1351 גָּאַל\nStrong's: profanation\nKJV: defile.\n\nCognate Group: H1352 (defile), H1351 (defile)",
    1353: "גְּאֻלָּה (gᵉʼullâh | gheh-ool-law')Typo: xlit gᵉullâh corrected to gᵉʼullâh\n\nGreek Equivalents: G3083 λύτρον, G3085 λύτρωσις, G3085 λύτρωσις \n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of H1350 גָּאַל\nStrong's: redemption (including the right and the object); by implication, relationship\nKJV: kindred, redeem, redemption, right.\n\nCognate Group: H3008 (Igal), H1350 ([idiom] in any wise), H1353 (kindred)",
    1354: "גַב (gab | gab)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to hollow or curve; (compare H1460 גֵּו and H1479 גּוּף)\n\nStrong's: the back (as rounded); by analogy, the top or rim, a boss, a vault, arch of eye, bulwarks, etc.\nKJV: back, body, boss, eminent (higher) place, (eye) brows, nave, ring.\n\nCognate Group: H1354 (back), H1373 (Gabbai), H1359 (Gob), H5543 (Sallai), H1405 (Gibbethon)\nGreek Equivalents: G3577 νῶτος, G3612 οἴκημα, G3790 ὀφρῦς",
    1355: "גַּב (gab | gab)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H1354 גַב \nStrong's: the back (as rounded); by analogy, the top or rim, a boss, a vault, arch of eye, bulwarks, etc.\nKJV: back.\n\nCognate Group: H1358 (den), H1467 (pride), H1355 (back)\nGreek Equivalents: G1042 γαββαθά",
    1356: "גֵּב (gêb | gabe)\n\nDerivation: from H1461 גּוּב\nStrong's: a log (as cut out); also well or cistern (as dug)\nKJV: beam, ditch, pit.\n\nCognate Group: H1463 (Gog), H1374 (Gebim), H1461 (husbandman), H1356 (beam), H4031 (Magog)",
    1357: "גֵּב (gêb | gabe)\n\nDerivation: probably from H1461 גּוּב (compare H1462 גֹּוב)\nStrong's: a locust (from its cutting)\nKJV: locust.\n\nCognate Group: H1462 (grasshopper), H1357 (locust)",
    1358: "גֹּב (gôb | gobe)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H1461 גּוּב\nStrong's: a pit (for wild animals) (as cut out)\nKJV: den.\n\nCognate Group: H1358 (den), H1467 (pride), H1355 (back)",
    1359: "גֹּב (Gôb | gobe)\n\nDerivation: or (fully) גֹּוב; from H1461 גּוּב ; pit\nStrong's: Gob, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Gob.\n\nCognate Group: H1354 (back), H1373 (Gabbai), H1359 (Gob), H5543 (Sallai), H1405 (Gibbethon)",
    1360: "גֶּבֶא (gebeʼ | geh'-beh)Typo: xlit gebe corrected to gebeʼ\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning probably to collect\nStrong's: a reservoir; by analogy, a marsh\nKJV: marish, pit.\n\nCognate Group: H1360 (marish)",
    1361: "גָּבַהּ (gâbahh | gaw-bah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to soar, i.e. be lofty; figuratively, to be haughty\nKJV: exalt, be haughty, be (make) high(-er), lift up, mount up, be proud, raise up great height, upward.\n\nCognate Group: H1364 (haughty), H3011 (Jogbehah), H1363 (excellency), H1365 (loftiness), H1362 (high), H1361 (exalt)\nGreek Equivalents: G566 ἀπέχει, G567 ἀπέχομαι, G568 ἀπέχω, G1392 δοξάζω, G1869 ἐπαίρω, G3166 μεγαλαυχέω, G3173 μέγας, G3349 μετεωρίζω, G5308 ὑψηλός, G5312 ὑψόω",
    1362: "גָּבָהּ (gâbâhh | gaw-bawh')\n\nDerivation: from H1361 גָּבַהּ\nStrong's: lofty (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: high, proud.\n\nCognate Group: H1364 (haughty), H3011 (Jogbehah), H1363 (excellency), H1365 (loftiness), H1362 (high), H1361 (exalt)\nGreek Equivalents: G873 ἀφορίζω, G2476 ἵστημι, G3724 ὁρίζω",
    1363: "גֹּבַהּ (gôbahh | go'-bah)\n\nDerivation: from H1361 גָּבַהּ\nStrong's: elation, grandeur, arrogance\nKJV: excellency, haughty, height, high, loftiness, pride.\n\nCognate Group: H1364 (haughty), H3011 (Jogbehah), H1363 (excellency), H1365 (loftiness), H1362 (high), H1361 (exalt)\nGreek Equivalents: G1411 δύναμις, G3174 μέγεθος, G4128 πλῆθος, G5311 ὕψος",
    1364: "גָּבֹהַּ (gâbôahh | gaw-bo'-ah)\n\nDerivation: or גָּבֹוהַּ; (fully) from H1361 גָּבַהּ\nStrong's: elevated (or elated), powerful, arrogant\nKJV: haughty, height, high(-er), lofty, proud, [idiom] exceeding proudly.\n\nCognate Group: H1364 (haughty), H3011 (Jogbehah), H1363 (excellency), H1365 (loftiness), H1362 (high), H1361 (exalt)\nGreek Equivalents: G5244 ὑπερήφανος, G5247 ὑπεροχή, G5308 ὑψηλός",
