    1471: "גֹּוי (gôwy | go'-ee)\n\nDerivation: rarely (shortened) גֹּי; apparently from the same root as H1465 גֵּוָה (in the sense of massing)\nStrong's: a foreign nation; hence, a Gentile; also (figuratively) a troop of animals, or a flight of locusts\nKJV: Gentile, heathen, nation, people.\n\nCognate Group: H1458 (back), H1472 (body), H1465 (body), H1471 (Gentile), H1460 (among)\nGreek Equivalents: G444 ἄνθρωπος, G1093 γῆ, G1484 ἔθνος, G2190 ἐχθρός, G2992 λαός, G3941 πάροικος, G5443 φυλή",
