    1510: "גְּזֵרָה (gᵉzêrâh | ghez-ay-raw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H1505 גְּזַר (as H1504 גָּזַר)\nStrong's: a decree\nKJV: decree.\n\nCognate Group: H1505 (cut out), H1510 (decree), H1519 (strive)",
    1511: "גִּזְרִי (Gizrîy | ghiz-ree')\n\nDerivation: (in the m patrial from H1507 גֶּזֶר ; a Gezerite (collectively) or inhabitants of Gezer; but better (as in the text) bytransposition גִּזְרִי\n\nTypo: xlit Girzîy corrected to Gizrîy\n\n; patrial of H1630 גְּרִזִים\nStrong's: a Grizite (collectively) or member of a native tribe in Palestine\nKJV: Gezrites.\n\nCognate Group: H1507 (Gazer), H1504 (cut down), H1511 (Gezrites), H1506 (part), H1509 (not inhabited), H1508 (polishing), H4037 (axe)",
    1512: "גָּחֹון (gâchôwn | gaw-khone')\n\nDerivation: probably from H1518 גִּיחַ \n\nTypo: lemma גּיחַ missing vowel, corrected to גִּיחַ\n\n; (compare H1521 גִּיחֹון)\n\nStrong's: the external abdomen, belly (as the source of the faetus)\nKJV: belly.\n\nCognate Group: H1512 (belly)\nGreek Equivalents: G2836 κοιλία, G4738 στῆθος",
    1513: "גֶּחֶל (gechel | geh'-khel)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) גַּחֶלֶת; from an unused root meaning to glow or kindle\nStrong's: an ember\nKJV: (burning) coal.\n\nCognate Group: H1513 (coal)\nGreek Equivalents: G440 ἄνθραξ",
    1514: "גַּחַם (Gacham | gah'-kham)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to burn; flame\nStrong's: Gacham, a son of Nahor\nKJV: Gaham.\n\nCognate Group: H1514 (Gaham)",
    1515: "גַּחַר (Gachar | gah'-khar)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to hide; lurker\nStrong's: Gachar, one of the Nethinim\nKJV: Gahar.\n\nCognate Group: H1515 (Gahar), H1522 (Gehazi), H1516 (valley)",
    1516: "גַּיְא (gayʼ | gah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: or (shortened) גַּי; probably (by transmutation) from the same root as H1466 גֵּוָה (abbreviated)\nStrong's: a gorge (from its lofty sides; hence, narrow, but not a gully or winter-torrent)\nKJV: valley.\n\nCognate Group: H1515 (Gahar), H1522 (Gehazi), H1516 (valley)\nGreek Equivalents: G1093 γῆ, G5327 φάραγξ, G1067 γέεννα",
    1517: "גִּיד (gîyd | gheed)\n\nDerivation: probably from H1464 גּוּד\nStrong's: a thong (as compressing); by analogy, a tendon\nKJV: sinew.\n\nCognate Group: H1517 (sinew)",
    1518: "גִּיחַ (gîyach | ghee'-akh)Typo: lemma גּיחַ missing vowel, corrected to גִּיחַ\n\nGreek Equivalents: G1904 ἐπέρχομαι \n\nDerivation: or (shortened) גֹּחַ; a primitive root\nStrong's: to gush forth (as water), generally to issue\nKJV: break forth, labor to bring forth, come forth, draw up, take out.\n\nCognate Group: H1521 (Gihon), H1520 (Giah), H1518 (break forth)",
    1519: "גִּיחַ (gîyach | ghee'-akh)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or (shortened) גּוּחַ; (Aramaic), corresponding to H1518 גִּיחַ \n\nTypo: lemma גּיחַ missing vowel, corrected to גִּיחַ\n\nStrong's: to rush forth\nKJV: strive.\n\nCognate Group: H1505 (cut out), H1510 (decree), H1519 (strive)\nGreek Equivalents: G1706 ἐμπίπτω",
    1520: "גִּיחַ (Gîyach | ghee'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H1518 גִּיחַ \n\nTypo: lemma גּיחַ missing vowel, corrected to גִּיחַ\n\n; a fountain\nStrong's: Giach, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Giah.\n\nCognate Group: H1521 (Gihon), H1520 (Giah), H1518 (break forth)",
    1521: "גִּיחֹון (Gîychôwn | ghee-khone')\n\nDerivation: or (shortened) גִּחֹון; from H1518 גִּיחַ \n\nTypo: lemma גּיחַ missing vowel, corrected to גִּיחַ\n\n; stream\nStrong's: Gichon, a river of Paradise; also a valley (or pool) near Jerusalem\nKJV: Gihon.\n\nCognate Group: H1521 (Gihon), H1520 (Giah), H1518 (break forth)",
    1522: "גֵּיחֲזִי (Gêychăzîy | gay-khah-zee')\n\nDerivation: or גֵּחֲזִי; apparently from H1516 גַּיְא and H2372 חָזָה ; valley of a visionary\nStrong's: Gechazi, the servant of Elisha\nKJV: Gehazi.\n\nCognate Group: H1515 (Gahar), H1522 (Gehazi), H1516 (valley)",
    1523: "גִּיל (gîyl | gheel)\n\nDerivation: or (by permutation) גּוּל; a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to spin round (under the influence of any violent emotion), i.e. usually rejoice, or (as cringing) fear\nKJV: be glad, joy, be joyful, rejoice.\n\nCognate Group: H1525 (joy), H1524 ([idiom] exceedingly), H1526 (Gilonite), H1542 (Giloh), H1523 (be glad)\nGreek Equivalents: G21 ἀγαλλιάω, G1705 ἐμπίπλημι, G1869 ἐπαίρω, G5463 χαίρω",
    1524: "גִּיל (gîyl | gheel)\n\nDerivation: from H1523 גִּיל\nStrong's: a revolution (of time, i.e. an age); also joy\nKJV: [idiom] exceedingly, gladness, [idiom] greatly, joy, rejoice(-ing), sort.\n\nCognate Group: H1525 (joy), H1524 ([idiom] exceedingly), H1526 (Gilonite), H1542 (Giloh), H1523 (be glad)\nGreek Equivalents: G20 ἀγαλλίασις, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G2244 ἡλικία, G5479 χαρά",
    1525: "גִּילָה (gîylâh | ghee-law')\n\nDerivation: or גִּילַת; feminine of H1524 גִּיל\nStrong's: joy\nKJV: joy, rejoicing.\n\nCognate Group: H1525 (joy), H1524 ([idiom] exceedingly), H1526 (Gilonite), H1542 (Giloh), H1523 (be glad)",
