    1542: "גִּלֹה (Gilôh | ghee-lo')\n\nDerivation: or (fully) גִּילֹה; from H1540 גָּלָה ; open\nStrong's: Giloh, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Giloh.\n\nCognate Group: H1525 (joy), H1524 ([idiom] exceedingly), H1526 (Gilonite), H1542 (Giloh), H1523 (be glad)",
    1543: "גֻּלָּה (gullâh | gool-law')\n\nDerivation: feminine from H1556 גָּלַל\nStrong's: a fountain, bowl or globe (all as round)\nKJV: bowl, pommel, spring.\n\nCognate Group: H1019 (Beth-gilgal), H1551 (Galilee), H1557 (dung), H1550 (folding), H1543 (bowl), H1559 (Galal), H4039 (roll), H1530 (billow), H1567 (Galeed), H1537 (Gilgal), H1553 (Geliloth), H1538 (head), H1561 (dung), H1562 (Gilalai), H1552 (border), H1554 (Gallim), H1556 (commit), H1544 (idol), H1536 (wheel), H1534 (heaven), H1531 (bowl)",
