    1981: "הֲלַךְ (hălak | hal-ak')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H1980 הָלַךְ (compare H1946 הוּךְ)\nStrong's: to walk\nKJV: walk.\n\nCognate Group: H1946 (bring again), H1981 (walk), H1983 (custom)",
    1982: "הֵלֶךְ (hêlek | hay'-lek)\n\nDerivation: from H1980 הָלַךְ\nStrong's: properly, a journey, i.e. (by implication) a wayfarer; also a flowing\nKJV: [idiom] dropped, traveller.\n\nCognate Group: H1982 ([idiom] dropped), H4109 (journey), H3212 ([idiom] again), H1980 (along), H8418 ([idiom] went), H1978 (step), H4108 (place to walk), H1979 (company)\nGreek Equivalents: G3938 πάροδος",
    1983: "הֲלָךְ (hălâk | hal-awk')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H1981 הֲלַךְ\nStrong's: properly, a journey, i.e. (by implication) toll on goods at aroad\nKJV: custom.\n\nCognate Group: H1946 (bring again), H1981 (walk), H1983 (custom)",
    1984: "הָלַל (hâlal | haw-lal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be clear (orig. of sound, but usually of color); to shine; hence, to make ashow, to boast; and thus to be (clamorously) foolish; to rave; causatively, to celebrate; also to stultify\nKJV: (make) boast (self), celebrate, commend, (deal, make), fool(-ish, -ly), glory, give (light), be (make, feign self) mad (against), give in marriage, (sing, be worthy of) praise, rage, renowned, shine.\n\nCognate Group: H1966 (lucifer), H1984 (boast)\nGreek Equivalents: G21 ἀγαλλιάω, G133 αἴνεσις, G134 αἰνέω, G136 αἶνος, G459 ἄνομος, G1325 δίδωμι, G1740 ἐνδοξάζω, G1839 ἐξίστημι, G1843 ἐξομολογέω, G1867 ἐπαινέω, G2017 ἐπιφαύω, G2020 ἐπιφώσκω, G2127 εὐλογέω, G2620 κατακαυχάομαι, G2744 καυχάομαι, G3105 μαίνομαι, G3891 παρανομέω, G3911 παραφέρω, G3996 πενθέω, G4064 περιφέρω, G4364 προσποιέομαι, G5214 ὑμνέω, G5215 ὕμνος, G239 ἀλληλουϊα",
    1985: "הִלֵּל (Hillêl | hil-layl')\n\nDerivation: from H1984 הָלַל ; praising (namely God)\nStrong's: Hillel, an Israelite\nKJV: Hillel.\n\nCognate Group: H1947 (madness), H4111 (Mahalaleel), H1984 (boast), H1974 (merry), H8416 (praise), H3094 (Jehalellel), H1948 (madness), H4110 (praise), H1985 (Hillel)",
    1986: "הָלַם (hâlam | haw-lam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to strike down; by implication, to hammer, stamp, conquer, disband\nKJV: beat (down), break (down), overcome, smite (with the hammer).\n\nCognate Group: H3095 (diamond), H1987 (Helem), H4112 (stripe), H1986 (beat), H1989 (hammer)\nGreek Equivalents: G609 ἀποκόπτω, G1643 ἐλαύνω, G1702 ἐμπαίζω, G2662 καταπατέω, G3182 μεθύσκω, G3811 παιδεύω",
    1987: "הֶלֶם (Helem | hay'-lem)\n\nDerivation: from H1986 הָלַם ; smiter\nStrong's: Helem, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Helem.\n\nCognate Group: H3095 (diamond), H1987 (Helem), H4112 (stripe), H1986 (beat), H1989 (hammer)",
