    1992: "הֵם (hêm | haym)\n\nDerivation: or (prolonged) הֵמָּה; masculine plural from H1981 הֲלַךְ\nStrong's: they (only used when emphatic)\nKJV: it, like, [idiom] (how, so) many (soever, more as) they (be), (the) same, [idiom] so, [idiom] such, their, them, these, they, those, which, who, whom, withal, ye.\n\nCognate Group: H1992 (it)\nGreek Equivalents: G1563 ἐκεῖ, G1565 ἐκεῖνος, G1565 ἐκεῖνος, G2398 ἴδιος",
