    1996: "הֲמֹון גֹּוג (Hămôwn Gôwg | ham-one' gohg)\n\nDerivation: from H1995 הָמֹון and H1463 גֹּוג\nStrong's: the multitude of Gog; the fanciful name of an emblematic place in Palestine\nKJV: Hamogog.\n\nCognate Group: H1996 (Hamogog), H1993 (clamorous), H1995 (abundance), H1997 (Hamonah), H1998 (noise)",
