    1998: "הֶמְיָה (hemyâh | hem-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H1993 הָמָה\nStrong's: sound\nKJV: noise.\n\nCognate Group: H1996 (Hamogog), H1993 (clamorous), H1995 (abundance), H1997 (Hamonah), H1998 (noise)",
    1999: "הֲמֻלָּה (hămullâh | ham-ool-law')\n\nDerivation: or (too fully) הֲמוּלָּה; (Jeremiah 11:16), feminine passive participle of an unused root meaning to rush (as rain with a windy roar)\nStrong's: a sound\nKJV: speech, tumult.\n\nCognate Group: H1999 (speech)",
