    2001: "הָמָן (Hâmân | haw-mawn')\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Haman, a Persian vizier\nKJV: Haman.\n\nCognate Group: H2000 (break), H1995 (abundance), H1967 (Hemam), H2001 (Haman), H1950 (Homam)",
    2002: "הַמְנִיךְ (hamnîyk | ham-neek')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) but the text is הֲמוּנֵךְ; of foreign origin\nStrong's: a necklace\nKJV: chain.\n\nCognate Group: H1994 ([idiom] are), H2002 (chain)",
