    2004: "הֵן (hên | hane)\n\nDerivation: feminine plural from H1931 הוּא\nStrong's: they (only used when emphatic)\nKJV: [idiom] in, such like, (with) them, thereby, therein, (more than) they, wherein, in which, whom, withal.\n\nCognate Group: H2004 ([idiom] in)",
