    2011: "הִנֹּם (Hinnôm | hin-nome')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: Hinnom, apparently a Jebusite\nKJV: Hinnom.\n\nCognate Group: H2005 (behold), H2008 (here), H2012 (Hena), H2011 (Hinnom), H2009 (behold)\nGreek Equivalents: G1067 γέεννα",
    2012: "הֵנַע (Hênaʻ | hay-nah')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Hena, a place apparently in Mesopotamia\nKJV: Hena.\n\nCognate Group: H2005 (behold), H2008 (here), H2012 (Hena), H2011 (Hinnom), H2009 (behold)",
    2013: "הָסָה (hâçâh | haw-saw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to hush\nKJV: hold peace (tongue), (keep) silence, be silent, still.\n\nCognate Group: H2013 (hold peace)\nGreek Equivalents: G2125 εὐλαβέομαι, G4601 σιγάω, G4623 σιωπάω",
