    2015: "הָפַךְ (hâphak | haw-fak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to turn about or over; by implication, to change, overturn, return, pervert\nKJV: [idiom] become, change, come, be converted, give, make (a bed), overthrow (-turn), perverse, retire, tumble, turn (again, aside, back, to the contrary, every way).\n\nCognate Group: H2021 (chariot), H2018 (overthrow), H2015 ([idiom] become), H2017 (turning of things upside down), H4115 (prison), H2019 (froward), H8419 (froward), H2023 (Hor), H2024 (Hara), H2016 (contrary), H4114 (when)\nGreek Equivalents: G236 ἀλλάσσω, G390 ἀναστρέφω, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G1294 διαστρέφω, G1612 ἐκστρέφω, G1624 ἐκτρέπω, G1881 ἐπανίσταμαι, G1910 ἐπιβαίνω, G1994 ἐπιστρέφω, G2233 ἡγέομαι, G2690 καταστρέφω, G2947 κυλιόω, G3328 μεταβάλλω, G3344 μεταστρέφω, G4762 στρέφω",
    2016: "הֶפֶךְ (hephek | heh'-fek)\n\nDerivation: ; or הֵפֶךְ; from H2015 הָפַךְ\nStrong's: a turn, i.e. the reverse\nKJV: contrary.\n\nCognate Group: H2021 (chariot), H2018 (overthrow), H2015 ([idiom] become), H2017 (turning of things upside down), H4115 (prison), H2019 (froward), H8419 (froward), H2023 (Hor), H2024 (Hara), H2016 (contrary), H4114 (when)",
    2017: "הֹפֶךְ (hôphek | ho'-fek)\n\nDerivation: from H2015 הָפַךְ\nStrong's: an upset, i.e. (abstract) perversity\nKJV: turning of things upside down.\n\nCognate Group: H2021 (chariot), H2018 (overthrow), H2015 ([idiom] become), H2017 (turning of things upside down), H4115 (prison), H2019 (froward), H8419 (froward), H2023 (Hor), H2024 (Hara), H2016 (contrary), H4114 (when)",
    2018: "הֲפֵכָה (hăphêkâh | haf-ay-kaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H2016 הֶפֶךְ\nStrong's: destruction\nKJV: overthrow.\n\nCognate Group: H2021 (chariot), H2018 (overthrow), H2015 ([idiom] become), H2017 (turning of things upside down), H4115 (prison), H2019 (froward), H8419 (froward), H2023 (Hor), H2024 (Hara), H2016 (contrary), H4114 (when)\nGreek Equivalents: G2692 καταστροφή",
    2019: "הֲפַכְפַּךְ (hăphakpak | haf-ak-pak')\n\nDerivation: by reduplication from H2015 הָפַךְ\nStrong's: very perverse\nKJV: froward.\n\nCognate Group: H2021 (chariot), H2018 (overthrow), H2015 ([idiom] become), H2017 (turning of things upside down), H4115 (prison), H2019 (froward), H8419 (froward), H2023 (Hor), H2024 (Hara), H2016 (contrary), H4114 (when)\nGreek Equivalents: G4646 σκολιός",
    2020: "הַצָּלָה (hatstsâlâh | hats-tsaw-law')\n\nDerivation: from H5337 נָצַל\nStrong's: rescue\nKJV: deliverance.\n\nCognate Group: H2020 (deliverance), H5337 ([idiom] at all)",
    2021: "הֹצֶן (hôtsen | ho'-tsen)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning apparently to be sharp or strong\nStrong's: a weapon of war\nKJV: chariot.\n\nCognate Group: H2021 (chariot), H2018 (overthrow), H2015 ([idiom] become), H2017 (turning of things upside down), H4115 (prison), H2019 (froward), H8419 (froward), H2023 (Hor), H2024 (Hara), H2016 (contrary), H4114 (when)",
    2022: "הַר (har | har)\n\nDerivation: a shortened form of H2042 הָרָר\nStrong's: a mountain or range of hills (sometimes used figuratively)\nKJV: hill (country), mount(-ain), [idiom] promotion.\n\nCognate Group: H2047 (Hatach), H2022 (hill), H2042 (hill), H2044 (Hashem), H2043 (Hararite)\nGreek Equivalents: G717 Ἀρμαγεδδών, G1015 βουνός, G1093 γῆ, G3714 ὀρεινός, G3714 ὀρεινός, G3735 ὄρος, G3735 ὄρος",
    2023: "הֹר (Hôr | hore)\n\nDerivation: another form of H2022 הַר ; mountain\nStrong's: Hor, the name of a peak in Idumaea and of one in Syria\nKJV: Hor.\n\nCognate Group: H2021 (chariot), H2018 (overthrow), H2015 ([idiom] become), H2017 (turning of things upside down), H4115 (prison), H2019 (froward), H8419 (froward), H2023 (Hor), H2024 (Hara), H2016 (contrary), H4114 (when)",
