    2083: "זְבֻל (Zᵉbul | zeb-ool')\n\nDerivation: the same as H2073 זְבוּל ; dwelling\nStrong's: Zebul, an Israelite\nKJV: Zebul. Compare H2073 זְבוּל .\n\nCognate Group: H2082 (dwell with), H2073 (dwell in), H2083 (Zebul), H2074 (Zebulun), H2075 (Zebulonite)",
    2084: "זְבַן (zᵉban | zeb-an')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to the root of H2081 זְבִינָא\nStrong's: to acquire by purchase\nKJV: gain.\n\nCognate Group: H2084 (gain)\nGreek Equivalents: G1805 ἐξαγοράζω",
    2085: "זָג (zâg | zawg)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to inclose\nStrong's: the skin of a grape\nKJV: husk.\n\nCognate Group: H2085 (husk)",
    2086: "זֵד (zêd | zade')\n\nDerivation: from H2102 זוּד\nStrong's: arrogant\nKJV: presumptuous, proud.\n\nCognate Group: H2121 (proud), H2132 (olive), H5138 (pottage), H2133 (Zethan), H2087 (presumptuously), H2102 (be proud), H2128 (Ziph), H2086 (presumptuous), H2129 (Ziphah), H2130 (Ziphim)\nGreek Equivalents: G459 ἄνομος, G5244 ὑπερήφανος",
    2087: "זָדֹון (zâdôwn | zaw-done')\n\nDerivation: from H2102 זוּד\nStrong's: arrogance\nKJV: presumptuously, pride, proud (man).\n\nCognate Group: H2121 (proud), H2132 (olive), H5138 (pottage), H2133 (Zethan), H2087 (presumptuously), H2102 (be proud), H2128 (Ziph), H2086 (presumptuous), H2129 (Ziphah), H2130 (Ziphim)\nGreek Equivalents: G763 ἀσέβεια, G5196 ὕβρις, G5243 ὑπερηφανία",
    2088: "זֶה (zeh | zeh)\n\nDerivation: a primitive word\nStrong's: the masculine demonstrative pronoun, this or that\nKJV: he, [idiom] hence, [idiom] here, it(-self), [idiom] now, [idiom] of him, the one...the other, [idiom] than the other, ([idiom] out of) the (self) same, such (a one) that, these, this (hath, man), on this side...on that side, [idiom] thus, very, which. Compare H2063 זֹאת, H2090 זֹה, H2097 זֹו, H2098 זוּ .\n\nCognate Group: H2088 (he), H2063 (hereby)\nGreek Equivalents: G243 ἄλλος, G1565 ἐκεῖνος, G1782 ἐντεῦθεν, G1782 ἐντεῦθεν, G2087 ἕτερος, G2400 ἰδού, G3778 οὗτος, G4169 ποῖος, G5101 τίς, G5602 ὧδε",
    2089: "זֶה (zeh | zeh)\n\nDerivation: (1 Samuel by permutation for H7716 שֶׂה\nStrong's: a sheep\nKJV: lamb.\n\nCognate Group: H7716 (cattle), H2089 (lamb), H7704 (country), H7717 (record)",
    2090: "זֹה (zôh | zo)\n\nDerivation: for H2088 זֶה\nStrong's: this or that\nKJV: as well as another, it, this, that, thus and thus.\n\nCognate Group: H2090 (as well as another)",
    2091: "זָהָב (zâhâb | zaw-hawb')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to shimmer\nStrong's: gold, figuratively, something gold-colored (i.e. yellow), as oil, a clear sky\nKJV: gold(-en), fair weather.\n\nCognate Group: H2091 (gold)\nGreek Equivalents: G3509 νέφος, G5552 χρύσεος, G5553 χρυσίον, G5557 χρυσός",
    2092: "זָהַם (zâham | zaw-ham')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be rancid, i.e. (transitively) to loathe\nKJV: abhor.\n\nCognate Group: H2093 (Zaham), H2092 (abhor)",
    2093: "זַהַם (Zaham | zah'-ham)\n\nDerivation: from H2092 זָהַם ; loathing\nStrong's: Zaham, an Israelite\nKJV: Zaham.\n\nCognate Group: H2093 (Zaham), H2092 (abhor)",
    2094: "זָהַר (zâhar | zaw-har')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to gleam; figuratively, to enlighten (by caution)\nKJV: admonish, shine, teach, (give) warn(-ing).\n\nCognate Group: H2094 (admonish), H2096 (brightness)",
    2095: "זְהַר (zᵉhar | zeh-har')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H2094 זָהַר\nStrong's: (passively) be admonished\nKJV: take heed.\n\nCognate Group: H2095 (take heed)\nGreek Equivalents: G868 ἀφίστημι, G1263 διαμαρτύρομαι, G1291 διαστέλλομαι, G1584 ἐκλάμπω, G2989 λάμπω, G4337 προσέχω, G4591 σημαίνω, G5316 φαίνω, G5442 φυλάσσω",
    2096: "זֹהַר (zôhar | zo'-har)\n\nDerivation: from H2094 זָהַר\nStrong's: brilliancy\nKJV: brightness.\n\nCognate Group: H2094 (admonish), H2096 (brightness)\nGreek Equivalents: G2987 λαμπρότης, G5458 φωστήρ",
    2097: "זֹו (zôw | zo)\n\nDerivation: for H2088 זֶה\nStrong's: this or that\nKJV: that, this.\n\nCognate Group: H2097 (that)",
    2098: "זוּ (zûw | zoo)\n\nDerivation: for H2088 זֶה\nStrong's: this or that\nKJV: that, this, [idiom] wherein, which, whom.\n\nCognate Group: H2098 (that)",
    2099: "זִו (Ziv | zeev')\n\nDerivation: probably from an unused root meaning to be prominent; properly, brightness (compare H2122 זִיו), i.e. (figuratively) the month of flowers\nStrong's: Ziv (corresponding to Ijar or May)\nKJV: Zif.\n\nCognate Group: H2099 (Zif), H2094 (admonish)",
    2100: "זוּב (zûwb | zoob)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to flow freely (as water), i.e. (specifically) to have a (sexual) flux; figuratively, to waste away; also to overflow\nKJV: flow, gush out, have a (running) issue, pine away, run.\n\nCognate Group: H2100 (flow), H2101 (issue)\nGreek Equivalents: G4482 ῥέω, G4511 ῥύσις",
    2101: "זֹוב (zôwb | zobe)\n\nDerivation: from H2100 זוּב\nStrong's: a seminal or menstrual flux\nKJV: issue.\n\nCognate Group: H2100 (flow), H2101 (issue)\nGreek Equivalents: G4511 ῥύσις",
    2102: "זוּד (zûwd | zood)\n\nDerivation: or (by permutation) זִיד; a primitive root\nStrong's: to seethe; figuratively, to be insolent\nKJV: be proud, deal proudly, presume, (come) presumptuously, sod.\n\nCognate Group: H2121 (proud), H2132 (olive), H5138 (pottage), H2133 (Zethan), H2087 (presumptuously), H2102 (be proud), H2128 (Ziph), H2086 (presumptuous), H2129 (Ziphah), H2130 (Ziphim)\nGreek Equivalents: G436 ἀνθίστημι, G764 ἀσεβέω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G3849 παραβιάζομαι",
    2103: "זוּד (zûwd | zood)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H2102 זוּד\nStrong's: to be proud\nKJV: in pride.\n\nCognate Group: H2103 (in pride)",
    2104: "זוּזִים (Zûwzîym | zoo-zeem')\n\nDerivation: plural probably from the same as H2123 זִיז ; prominent\nStrong's: Zuzites, an aboriginal tribe of Palestine\nKJV: Zuzims.\n\nCognate Group: H2105 (Zoheth), H2123 (abundance), H2104 (Zuzims)\nGreek Equivalents: G1484 ἔθνος",
    2105: "זֹוחֵת (Zôwchêth | zo-khayth')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain origin\nStrong's: Zocheth, an Israelite\nKJV: Zoheth.\n\nCognate Group: H2105 (Zoheth), H2123 (abundance), H2104 (Zuzims)",
    2106: "זָוִית (zâvîyth | zaw-veeth')\n\nDerivation: apparently from the same root as H2099 זִו (in the sense of prominence)\nStrong's: an angle (as projecting), i.e. (by implication) a corner-column (or anta)\nKJV: corner(stone).\n\nCognate Group: H2106 (corner), H4200 (garner)",
    2107: "זוּל (zûwl | zool)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2151 זָלַל)\nStrong's: probably to shake out, i.e. (by implication) to scatter profusely; figuratively, to treat lightly\nKJV: lavish, despise.\n\nCognate Group: H2107 (lavish)",
    2108: "זוּלָה (zûwlâh | zoo-law')\n\nDerivation: from H2107 זוּל\nStrong's: probably scattering, i.e. removal; used adverbially, except\nKJV: beside, but, only, save.\n\nCognate Group: H2108 (beside)\nGreek Equivalents: G1622 ἐκτός, G4133 πλήν",
    2109: "זוּן (zûwn | zoon)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: perhaps properly, to be plump, i.e. (transitively) to nourish\nKJV: feed.\n\nCognate Group: H2109 (feed), H4202 (meat)",
    2110: "זוּן (zûwn | zoon)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H2109 זוּן \nStrong's: perhaps properly, to be plump, i.e. (transitively) to nourish\nKJV: feed.\n\nCognate Group: H4203 (meat), H2110 (feed)\nGreek Equivalents: G5142 τρέφω, G5524 χορηγέω",
    2111: "זוּעַ (zûwaʻ | zoo'-ah)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to shake off, i.e. (figuratively) to agitate (as with fear)\nKJV: move, tremble, vex.\n\nCognate Group: H2127 (Zia), H2189 ([idiom] removed), H2111 (move), H2113 (be removed)\nGreek Equivalents: G4352 προσκυνέω, G4531 σαλεύω",
    2112: "זוּעַ (zûwaʻ | zoo'-ah)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H2111 זוּעַ\nStrong's: to shake (with fear)\nKJV: tremble.\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2122 (brightness), H2112 (tremble), H2136 (innocency)",
    2113: "זְוָעָה (zᵉvâʻâh | zev-aw-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H2111 זוּעַ\nStrong's: agitation, fear\nKJV: be removed, trouble, vexation. Compare H2189 זַעֲוָה .\n\nCognate Group: H2127 (Zia), H2189 ([idiom] removed), H2111 (move), H2113 (be removed)\nGreek Equivalents: G318 ἀνάγκη, G1290 διασπορά, G1611 ἔκστασις, G1680 ἐλπίς, G2368 θυμίαμα, G2378 θυσία, G3646 ὁλοκαύτωμα, G4968 σφάγιον",
    2114: "זוּר (zûwr | zoor)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to turn aside (especially for lodging); hence to be aforeigner, strange, profane; specifically (active participle) to commit adultery\nKJV: (come from) another (man, place), fanner, go away, (e-) strange(-r, thing, woman).\n\nCognate Group: H2114 (another)\nGreek Equivalents: G241 ἀλλογενής, G243 ἄλλος, G245 ἀλλότριος, G526 ἀπαλλοτριόω, G765 ἀσεβής, G1135 γυνή, G1448 ἐγγίζω, G4372 πρόσφατος, G4650 σκορπίζω",
    2115: "זוּר (zûwr | zoor)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H6695 צֹוק)\nStrong's: to press together, tighten\nKJV: close, rush, thrust together.\n\nCognate Group: H2115 (close), H2116 (that which is crushed), H4205 (bound up), H2213 (crown), H2223 (greyhound)",
    2116: "זוּרֶה (zûwreh | zoo-reh')\n\nDerivation: from H2115 זוּר\nStrong's: trodden on\nKJV: that which is crushed.\n\nCognate Group: H2115 (close), H2116 (that which is crushed), H4205 (bound up), H2213 (crown), H2223 (greyhound)\nGreek Equivalents: G4937 συντρίβω",
    2117: "זָזָא (zâzâʼ | zaw-zaw')\n\nDerivation: probably from the root of H2123 זִיז ; prominent\nStrong's: Zaza, an Israelite\nKJV: Zaza.\n\nCognate Group: H4201 (post), H2124 (Ziza), H2123 (abundance), H2117 (Zaza), H3151 (Jaziz), H2125 (Zizah), H2126 (Zina)",
    2118: "זָחַח (zâchach | zaw-khakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to shove or displace\nKJV: loose.\n\nCognate Group: H2118 (loose)\nGreek Equivalents: G5465 χαλάω",
    2119: "זָחַל (zâchal | zaw-khal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to crawl; by implication, to fear\nKJV: be afraid, serpent, worm.\n\nCognate Group: H2119 (be afraid), H2120 (Zoheleth)\nGreek Equivalents: G2270 ἡσυχάζω, G4951 σύρω",
    2120: "זֹחֶלֶת (Zôcheleth | zo-kheh'-leth)\n\nDerivation: feminine active participle of H2119 זָחַל ; crawling (i.e. serpent)\nStrong's: Zocheleth, a boundary stone in. Palestine\nKJV: Zoheleth.\n\nCognate Group: H2119 (be afraid), H2120 (Zoheleth)",
    2121: "זֵידֹון (zêydôwn | zay-dohn')\n\nDerivation: from H2102 זוּד\nStrong's: boiling of water, i.e. wave\nKJV: proud.\n\nCognate Group: H2121 (proud), H2132 (olive), H5138 (pottage), H2133 (Zethan), H2087 (presumptuously), H2102 (be proud), H2128 (Ziph), H2086 (presumptuous), H2129 (Ziphah), H2130 (Ziphim)",
    2122: "זִיו (zîyv | zeev)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H2099 זִו\nStrong's: (figuratively) cheerfulness\nKJV: brightness, countenance.\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2122 (brightness), H2112 (tremble), H2136 (innocency)\nGreek Equivalents: G1529 εἴσοδος, G3444 μορφή, G3706 ὅρασις, G3799 ὄψις",
    2123: "זִיז (zîyz | zeez)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root apparently meaning to be conspicuous\nStrong's: fulness of the breast; also a moving creature\nKJV: abundance, wild beast.\n\nCognate Group: H4201 (post), H2124 (Ziza), H2123 (abundance), H2117 (Zaza), H3151 (Jaziz), H2125 (Zizah), H2126 (Zina)",
    2124: "זִיזָא (Zîyzâʼ | zee-zaw')\n\nDerivation: apparently from the same as H2123 זִיז ; prominence\nStrong's: Ziza, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Ziza.\n\nCognate Group: H4201 (post), H2124 (Ziza), H2123 (abundance), H2117 (Zaza), H3151 (Jaziz), H2125 (Zizah), H2126 (Zina)",
    2125: "זִיזָה (Zîyzâh | zee-zaw')\n\nDerivation: another form for H2124 זִיזָא\nStrong's: Zizah, an Israelite\nKJV: Zizah.\n\nCognate Group: H4201 (post), H2124 (Ziza), H2123 (abundance), H2117 (Zaza), H3151 (Jaziz), H2125 (Zizah), H2126 (Zina)",
    2126: "זִינָא (Zîynâʼ | zee-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H2109 זוּן ; well-fed; or perhaps an orthographical error for H2124 זִיזָא\nStrong's: Zina, an Israelite\nKJV: Zina.\n\nCognate Group: H4201 (post), H2124 (Ziza), H2123 (abundance), H2117 (Zaza), H3151 (Jaziz), H2125 (Zizah), H2126 (Zina)",
    2127: "זִיעַ (Zîyaʻ | zee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from H2111 זוּעַ ; agitation\nStrong's: Zia, an Israelite\nKJV: Zia.\n\nCognate Group: H2127 (Zia), H2189 ([idiom] removed), H2111 (move), H2113 (be removed)",
    2128: "זִיף (Zîyph | zeef)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H2203 זֶפֶת ; flowing\nStrong's: Ziph, the name of a place in Palestine; also of an Israelite\nKJV: Ziph.\n\nCognate Group: H2121 (proud), H2132 (olive), H5138 (pottage), H2133 (Zethan), H2087 (presumptuously), H2102 (be proud), H2128 (Ziph), H2086 (presumptuous), H2129 (Ziphah), H2130 (Ziphim)",
    2129: "זִיפָה (Zîyphâh | zee-faw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H2128 זִיף ; a flowing\nStrong's: Ziphah, an Israelite\nKJV: Ziphah.\n\nCognate Group: H2121 (proud), H2132 (olive), H5138 (pottage), H2133 (Zethan), H2087 (presumptuously), H2102 (be proud), H2128 (Ziph), H2086 (presumptuous), H2129 (Ziphah), H2130 (Ziphim)",
    2130: "זִיפִי (Zîyphîy | zee-fee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H2128 זִיף\nStrong's: a Ziphite or inhabitant of Ziph\nKJV: Ziphim, Ziphite.\n\nCognate Group: H2121 (proud), H2132 (olive), H5138 (pottage), H2133 (Zethan), H2087 (presumptuously), H2102 (be proud), H2128 (Ziph), H2086 (presumptuous), H2129 (Ziphah), H2130 (Ziphim)",
    2131: "זִיקָה (zîyqâh | zee-kaw')\n\nDerivation: (Isaiah 50: (feminine); and זִק; or זֵק; from H2187 זָנַק\nStrong's: properly, what leaps forth, i.e. flash of fire, or a burning arrow; also (from the original sense of the root) a bond\nKJV: chain, fetter, firebrand, spark.\n\nCognate Group: H4213 (few), H2203 (pitch), H2131 (chain), H2202 (Ziphron), H2191 (little)\nGreek Equivalents: G3976 πέδη, G5395 φλόξ",
    2132: "זַיִת (zayith | zay'-yith)\n\nDerivation: probably from an unused root (akin to H2099 זִו)\nStrong's: an olive (as yielding illuminating oil), the tree, the branch or the berry\nKJV: olive (tree, -yard), Olivet.\n\nCognate Group: H2121 (proud), H2132 (olive), H5138 (pottage), H2133 (Zethan), H2087 (presumptuously), H2102 (be proud), H2128 (Ziph), H2086 (presumptuous), H2129 (Ziphah), H2130 (Ziphim)\nGreek Equivalents: G1636 ἐλαία, G1638 ἐλαιών",
    2133: "זֵיתָן (Zêythân | zay-thawn')\n\nDerivation: from H2132 זַיִת ; olive grove\nStrong's: Zethan, an Israelite\nKJV: Zethan.\n\nCognate Group: H2121 (proud), H2132 (olive), H5138 (pottage), H2133 (Zethan), H2087 (presumptuously), H2102 (be proud), H2128 (Ziph), H2086 (presumptuous), H2129 (Ziphah), H2130 (Ziphim)",
    2134: "זַךְ (zak | zak)\n\nDerivation: from H2141 זָכַךְ\nStrong's: clear\nKJV: clean, pure.\n\nCognate Group: H2137 (crystal), H2141 (be clean), H2140 (Zaccai), H2134 (clean)\nGreek Equivalents: G53 ἁγνός, G1307 διαφανής, G2513 καθαρός, G3741 ὅσιος",
    2135: "זָכָה (zâkâh | zaw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2141 זָכַךְ)\nStrong's: to be translucent; figuratively, to be innocent\nKJV: be (make) clean, cleanse, be clear, count pure.\n\nCognate Group: H2135 (be clean)\nGreek Equivalents: G53 ἁγνός, G273 ἄμεμπτος, G1344 δικαιόω, G2513 καθαρός, G3528 νικάω",
    2136: "זָכוּ (zâkûw | zaw-koo')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2135 זָכָה\nStrong's: purity\nKJV: innocency.\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2122 (brightness), H2112 (tremble), H2136 (innocency)\nGreek Equivalents: G1343 δικαιοσύνη, G2118 εὐθύτης",
    2137: "זְכוּכִית (zᵉkûwkîyth | zek-oo-keeth)\n\nDerivation: from H2135 זָכָה\nStrong's: properly, transparency, i.e. glass\nKJV: crystal.\n\nCognate Group: H2137 (crystal), H2141 (be clean), H2140 (Zaccai), H2134 (clean)\nGreek Equivalents: G5194 ὕαλος",
    2138: "זָכוּר (zâkûwr | zaw-koor')\n\nDerivation: properly, passive participle of H2142 זָכַר, but used for H2145 זָכָר\nStrong's: a male (of man or animals)\nKJV: males, men-children.\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2144 (Zeker), H2138 (males), H2147 (Zichri), H2139 (Zaccur), H2145 ([idiom] him), H234 (memorial), H2146 (memorial), H2142 ([idiom] burn), H2143 (memorial)",
    2139: "זַכּוּר (Zakkûwr | zaw-koor')\n\nDerivation: from H2142 זָכַר ; mindful\nStrong's: Zakkur, the name of seven Israelites\nKJV: Zaccur, Zacchur.\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2144 (Zeker), H2138 (males), H2147 (Zichri), H2139 (Zaccur), H2145 ([idiom] him), H234 (memorial), H2146 (memorial), H2142 ([idiom] burn), H2143 (memorial)",
    2140: "זַכַּי (Zakkay | zak-kah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H2141 זָכַךְ ; pure\nStrong's: Zakkai, an Israelite\nKJV: Zaccai.\n\nCognate Group: H2137 (crystal), H2141 (be clean), H2140 (Zaccai), H2134 (clean)\nGreek Equivalents: G2195 Ζακχαῖος",
    2141: "זָכַךְ (zâkak | zaw-kak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2135 זָכָה)\nStrong's: to be transparent or clean (phys. or morally)\nKJV: be (make) clean, be pure(-r).\n\nCognate Group: H2137 (crystal), H2141 (be clean), H2140 (Zaccai), H2134 (clean)",
    2142: "זָכַר (zâkar | zaw-kar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; also as denominative from H2145 זָכָר \nStrong's: properly, to mark (so as to be recognized), i.e. to remember; by implication, to mention; to be male\nKJV: [idiom] burn (incense), [idiom] earnestly, be male, (make) mention (of), be mindful, recount, record(-er), remember, make to be remembered, bring (call, come, keep, put) to (in) remembrance, [idiom] still, think on, [idiom] well.\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2144 (Zeker), H2138 (males), H2147 (Zichri), H2139 (Zaccur), H2145 ([idiom] him), H234 (memorial), H2146 (memorial), H2142 ([idiom] burn), H2143 (memorial)\nGreek Equivalents: G21 ἀγαλλιάω, G25 ἀγαπάω, G363 ἀναμιμνήσκω, G364 ἀνάμνησις, G400 ἀναφωνέω, G1941 ἐπικαλέομαι, G2028 ἐπονομάζω, G2564 καλέω, G3403 μιμνήσκω, G3417 μνεία, G3421 μνημονεύω, G3422 μνημόσυνον, G3687 ὀνομάζω, G5279 ὑπομιμνήσκω",
    2143: "זֵכֶר (zêker | zay'-ker)\n\nDerivation: or זֶכֶר; from H2142 זָכַר\nStrong's: a memento, abstractly recollection (rarely if ever); by implication, commemoration\nKJV: memorial, memory, remembrance, scent.\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2144 (Zeker), H2138 (males), H2147 (Zichri), H2139 (Zaccur), H2145 ([idiom] him), H234 (memorial), H2146 (memorial), H2142 ([idiom] burn), H2143 (memorial)\nGreek Equivalents: G3420 μνήμη, G3422 μνημόσυνον, G3686 ὄνομα",
    2144: "זֶכֶר (Zeker | zeh'-ker)\n\nDerivation: the same as H2143 זֵכֶר\nStrong's: Zeker, an Israelite\nKJV: Zeker.\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2144 (Zeker), H2138 (males), H2147 (Zichri), H2139 (Zaccur), H2145 ([idiom] him), H234 (memorial), H2146 (memorial), H2142 ([idiom] burn), H2143 (memorial)",
    2145: "זָכָר (zâkâr | zaw-kawr')\n\nDerivation: from H2142 זָכַר\nStrong's: properly, remembered, i.e. a male (of man or animals, as being the most noteworthy sex)\nKJV: [idiom] him, male, man(child, -kind).\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2144 (Zeker), H2138 (males), H2147 (Zichri), H2139 (Zaccur), H2145 ([idiom] him), H234 (memorial), H2146 (memorial), H2142 ([idiom] burn), H2143 (memorial)\nGreek Equivalents: G435 ἀνήρ, G730 ἄῤῥην, G3417 μνεία",
    2146: "זִכְרֹון (zikrôwn | zik-rone')\n\nDerivation: from H2142 זָכַר\nStrong's: a memento (or memorable thing, day or writing)\nKJV: memorial, record.\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2144 (Zeker), H2138 (males), H2147 (Zichri), H2139 (Zaccur), H2145 ([idiom] him), H234 (memorial), H2146 (memorial), H2142 ([idiom] burn), H2143 (memorial)\nGreek Equivalents: G364 ἀνάμνησις, G3420 μνήμη, G3422 μνημόσυνον",
    2147: "זִכְרִי (Zikrîy | zik-ree')\n\nDerivation: from H2142 זָכַר ; memorable\nStrong's: Zicri, the name of twelve Israelites\nKJV: Zichri.\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2144 (Zeker), H2138 (males), H2147 (Zichri), H2139 (Zaccur), H2145 ([idiom] him), H234 (memorial), H2146 (memorial), H2142 ([idiom] burn), H2143 (memorial)",
    2148: "זְכַרְיָה (Zᵉkaryâh | zek-ar-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or זְכַרְיָהוּ; from H2142 זָכַר and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has remembered\nStrong's: Zecarjah, the name of twenty-nine Israelites\nKJV: Zachariah, Zechariah.\n\nCognate Group: H2148 (Zachariah), H2144 (Zeker), H2138 (males), H2147 (Zichri), H2139 (Zaccur), H2145 ([idiom] him), H234 (memorial), H2146 (memorial), H2142 ([idiom] burn), H2143 (memorial)\nGreek Equivalents: G2197 Ζαχαρίας",
    2149: "זֻלּוּת (zullûwth | zool-looth')\n\nDerivation: from H2151 זָלַל\nStrong's: properly, a shaking, i.e. perhaps a tempest\nKJV: vilest.\n\nCognate Group: H2151 (blow down), H2149 (vilest)",
    2150: "זַלְזַל (zalzal | zal-zal')\n\nDerivation: by reduplication from H2151 זָלַל\nStrong's: tremulous, i.e. a twig\nKJV: sprig.\n\nCognate Group: H2151 (blow down), H2150 (sprig)",
    2151: "זָלַל (zâlal | zaw-lal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2107 זוּל)\nStrong's: to shake (as in the wind), i.e. to quake; figuratively, to be loose morally, worthless or prodigal\nKJV: blow down, glutton, riotous (eater), vile.\n\nCognate Group: H2151 (blow down), H2150 (sprig)\nGreek Equivalents: G370 ἀνάξιος, G810 ἀσωτία, G821 ἀτιμόω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G4531 σαλεύω, G5013 ταπεινόω",
    2152: "זַלְעָפָה (zalʻâphâh | zal-aw-faw')\n\nDerivation: or זִלְעָפָה\n\nTypo: xlit zilʻâphâph corrected to zilʻâphâh\n\n; from H2196 זָעַף\nStrong's: a glow (of wind or anger); also a famine (as consuming)\nKJV: horrible, horror, terrible.\n\nCognate Group: H2152 (horrible)",
    2153: "זִלְפָּה (Zilpâh | zil-paw)\n\nDerivation: ; from an unused root apparently meaning to trickle, as myrrh; fragrant dropping\nStrong's: Zilpah, Leah's maid\nKJV: Zilpah.\n\nCognate Group: H2153 (Zilpah)",
    2154: "זִמָּה (zimmâh | zim-maw')\n\nDerivation: or זַמָּה; from H2161 זָמַם\nStrong's: a plan, especially a bad one\nKJV: heinous crime, lewd(-ly, -ness), mischief, purpose, thought, wicked (device, mind, -ness).\n\nCognate Group: H4209 (device), H2155 (Zimmah), H2157 (Zamzummim), H2162 (wicked device), H2161 (consider), H2154 (heinous crime)\nGreek Equivalents: G458 ἀνομία, G459 ἄνομος, G462 ἀνόσιος, G763 ἀσέβεια, G764 ἀσεβέω, G877 ἀφροσύνη, G2556 κακός",
    2155: "זִמָּה (Zimmâh | zim-maw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H2154 זִמָּה\nStrong's: Zimmah, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Zimmah.\n\nCognate Group: H4209 (device), H2155 (Zimmah), H2157 (Zamzummim), H2162 (wicked device), H2161 (consider), H2154 (heinous crime)",
    2156: "זְמֹורָה (zᵉmôwrâh | zem-o-raw')\n\nDerivation: or זְמֹרָה (feminine); and זְמֹר (masculine); from H2168 זָמַר\nStrong's: a twig (as pruned)\nKJV: vine, branch, slip.\n\nCognate Group: H2156 (vine), H4212 (snuffers), H2168 (prune), H2159 (branch), H4211 (pruning-hook)\nGreek Equivalents: G2814 κλῆμα, G5568 ψαλμός",
    2157: "זַמְזֹם (Zamzôm | zam-zome')\n\nDerivation: from H2161 זָמַם ; intriguing\nStrong's: a Zamzumite, or native tribe of Palestine\nKJV: Zamzummim.\n\nCognate Group: H4209 (device), H2155 (Zimmah), H2157 (Zamzummim), H2162 (wicked device), H2161 (consider), H2154 (heinous crime)",
    2158: "זָמִיר (zâmîyr | zaw-meer')\n\nDerivation: or זָמִר; and (feminine) זְמִרָה; from H2167 זָמַר\nStrong's: a song to be accompanied with instrumental music\nKJV: psalm(-ist), singing, song.\n\nCognate Group: H2172 (melody), H4210 (psalm), H2158 (psalm), H2176 (song), H2167 (give praise)",
    2159: "זָמִיר (zâmîyr | zaw-meer')\n\nDerivation: from H2168 זָמַר\nStrong's: a twig (as pruned)\nKJV: branch.\n\nCognate Group: H2156 (vine), H4212 (snuffers), H2168 (prune), H2159 (branch), H4211 (pruning-hook)",
    2160: "זְמִירָה (Zᵉmîyrâh | zem-ee-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H2158 זָמִיר ; song\nStrong's: Zemirah, an Israelite\nKJV: Zemira.\n\nCognate Group: H2173 (best fruit), H2175 (Zimran), H2174 (Zimri), H2160 (Zemira), H2169 (chamois), H2177 (divers kinds)",
    2161: "זָמַם (zâmam | zaw-mam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to plan, usually in a bad sense\nKJV: consider, devise, imagine, plot, purpose, think (evil).\n\nCognate Group: H4209 (device), H2155 (Zimmah), H2157 (Zamzummim), H2162 (wicked device), H2161 (consider), H2154 (heinous crime)\nGreek Equivalents: G1011 βουλεύω, G1260 διαλογίζομαι, G1614 ἐκτείνω, G1760 ἐνθυμέομαι, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2334 θεωρέω, G3906 παρατηρέω, G5550 χρόνος",
    2162: "זָמָם (zâmâm | zaw-mawm')\n\nDerivation: from H2161 זָמַם\nStrong's: a plot\nKJV: wicked device.\n\nCognate Group: H4209 (device), H2155 (Zimmah), H2157 (Zamzummim), H2162 (wicked device), H2161 (consider), H2154 (heinous crime)\nGreek Equivalents: G93 ἀδικία",
    2163: "זָמַן (zâman | zaw-man')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to fix (a time)\nKJV: appoint.\n\nCognate Group: H2165 (season), H2163 (appoint)",
    2164: "זְמַן (zᵉman | zem-an')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H2163 זָמַן\nStrong's: to agree (on a time and place)\nKJV: prepare.\n\nCognate Group: H2166 (season), H2164 (prepare)\nGreek Equivalents: G2005 ἐπιτελέω, G4160 ποιέω, G4934 συντίθεμαι",
    2165: "זְמָן (zᵉmân | zem-awn')\n\nDerivation: from H2163 זָמַן\nStrong's: an appointed occasion\nKJV: season, time.\n\nCognate Group: H2165 (season), H2163 (appoint)\nGreek Equivalents: G2540 καιρός",
    2166: "זְמָן (zᵉmân | zem-awn')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H2165 זְמָן ; the same as H2165 זְמָן \nStrong's: an appointed occasion\nKJV: season, time.\n\nCognate Group: H2166 (season), H2164 (prepare)",
    2167: "זָמַר (zâmar | zaw-mar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (perhaps identical with H2168 זָמַר through the idea of striking with the fingers); properly, to touch the strings or parts of a musical instrument, i.e.\nStrong's: play upon it; to make music, accompanied by the voice; hence to celebrate in song and music\nKJV: give praise, sing forth praises, psalms.\n\nCognate Group: H2172 (melody), H4210 (psalm), H2158 (psalm), H2176 (song), H2167 (give praise)\nGreek Equivalents: G5214 ὑμνέω, G5567 ψάλλω",
    2168: "זָמַר (zâmar | zaw-mar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2167 זָמַר, H5568 סָמַר, H6785 צֶמֶר)\nStrong's: to trim (a vine)\nKJV: prune.\n\nCognate Group: H2156 (vine), H4212 (snuffers), H2168 (prune), H2159 (branch), H4211 (pruning-hook)",
    2169: "זֶמֶר (zemer | zeh'-mer)\n\nDerivation: apparently from H2167 זָמַר or H2168 זָמַר\nStrong's: a gazelle (from its lightly touching the ground)\nKJV: chamois.\n\nCognate Group: H2173 (best fruit), H2175 (Zimran), H2174 (Zimri), H2160 (Zemira), H2169 (chamois), H2177 (divers kinds)",
    2170: "זְמָר (zᵉmâr | zem-awr')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2167 זָמַר\nStrong's: instrumental music\nKJV: musick.\n\nCognate Group: H2200 (cry), H2170 (musick), H2171 (singer), H2178 (kind)\nGreek Equivalents: G3451 μουσικός",
    2171: "זַמָּר (zammâr | zam-mawr')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from the same as H2170 זְמָר\nStrong's: an instrumental musician\nKJV: singer.\n\nCognate Group: H2200 (cry), H2170 (musick), H2171 (singer), H2178 (kind)\nGreek Equivalents: G103 ᾄδω",
    2172: "זִמְרָה (zimrâh | zim-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H2167 זָמַר\nStrong's: a musical piece or song to be accompanied by an instrument\nKJV: melody, psalm.\n\nCognate Group: H2172 (melody), H4210 (psalm), H2158 (psalm), H2176 (song), H2167 (give praise)\nGreek Equivalents: G133 αἴνεσις, G2590 καρπός",
    2173: "זִמְרָה (zimrâh | zim-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H2168 זָמַר\nStrong's: pruned (i.e. choice) fruit\nKJV: best fruit.\n\nCognate Group: H2173 (best fruit), H2175 (Zimran), H2174 (Zimri), H2160 (Zemira), H2169 (chamois), H2177 (divers kinds)",
    2174: "זִמְרִי (Zimrîy | zim-ree')\n\nDerivation: from H2167 זָמַר ; musical\nStrong's: Zimri, the name of five Israelites, and of an Arabian tribe\nKJV: Zimri.\n\nCognate Group: H2173 (best fruit), H2175 (Zimran), H2174 (Zimri), H2160 (Zemira), H2169 (chamois), H2177 (divers kinds)",
    2175: "זִמְרָן (Zimrân | zim-rawn')\n\nDerivation: from H2167 זָמַר ; musical\nStrong's: Zimran, a son of Abraham by Keturah\nKJV: Zimran.\n\nCognate Group: H2173 (best fruit), H2175 (Zimran), H2174 (Zimri), H2160 (Zemira), H2169 (chamois), H2177 (divers kinds)",
    2176: "זִמְרָת (zimrâth | zim-rawth')\n\nDerivation: from H2167 זָמַר\nStrong's: instrumental music; by implication, praise\nKJV: song.\n\nCognate Group: H2172 (melody), H4210 (psalm), H2158 (psalm), H2176 (song), H2167 (give praise)",
    2177: "זַן (zan | zan)\n\nDerivation: from H2109 זוּן\nStrong's: properly, nourished (or fully developed), i.e. a form or sort\nKJV: divers kinds, [idiom] all manner of store.\n\nCognate Group: H2173 (best fruit), H2175 (Zimran), H2174 (Zimri), H2160 (Zemira), H2169 (chamois), H2177 (divers kinds)\nGreek Equivalents: G1085 γένος",
    2178: "זַן (zan | zan)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H2177 זַן\nStrong's: sort\nKJV: kind.\n\nCognate Group: H2200 (cry), H2170 (musick), H2171 (singer), H2178 (kind)",
    2179: "זָנַב (zânab | zaw-nab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root meaning to wag; used only as a denominative from H2180 זָנָב\nStrong's: to curtail, i.e. cut off the rear\nKJV: smite the hindmost.\n\nCognate Group: H2179 (smite the hindmost), H2180 (tail)\nGreek Equivalents: G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G2875 κόπτω",
    2180: "זָנָב (zânâb | zaw-nawb')\n\nDerivation: from H2179 זָנַב (in the original sense of flapping)\nStrong's: the tail (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: tail.\n\nCognate Group: H2179 (smite the hindmost), H2180 (tail)\nGreek Equivalents: G3769 οὐρά",
    2181: "זָנָה (zânâh | zaw-naw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (highly-fed and therefore wanton)\nStrong's: to commit adultery (usually of the female, and less often of simple fornication, rarely of involuntary ravishment); figuratively, to commit idolatry (the Jewish people being regarded as the spouse of Jehovah)\nKJV: (cause to) commit fornication, [idiom] continually, [idiom] great, (be an, play the) harlot, (cause to be, play the) whore, (commit, fall to) whoredom, (cause to) go a-whoring, whorish.\n\nCognate Group: H2183 (whoredom), H2181 (commit fornication), H8457 (fornication), H2185 (armour), H2184 (whoredom)\nGreek Equivalents: G1608 ἐκπορνεύω, G1712 ἐμπόριον, G4203 πορνεύω, G4204 πόρνη",
    2182: "זָנֹוחַ (Zânôwach | zaw-no'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H2186 זָנַח ; rejected\nStrong's: Zanoach, the name of two places in Palestine\nKJV: Zanoah.\n\nCognate Group: H2186 (cast away), H2182 (Zanoah)",
    2183: "זָנוּן (zânûwn | zaw-noon')\n\nDerivation: from H2181 זָנָה\nStrong's: adultery; figuratively, idolatry\nKJV: whoredom.\n\nCognate Group: H2183 (whoredom), H2181 (commit fornication), H8457 (fornication), H2185 (armour), H2184 (whoredom)\nGreek Equivalents: G4202 πορνεία",
    2184: "זְנוּת (zᵉnûwth | zen-ooth')\n\nDerivation: from H2181 זָנָה\nStrong's: adultery, i.e. (figuratively) infidelity, idolatry\nKJV: whoredom.\n\nCognate Group: H2183 (whoredom), H2181 (commit fornication), H8457 (fornication), H2185 (armour), H2184 (whoredom)",
    2185: "זֹנֹות (zônôwth | zo-noth')\n\nDerivation: regarded by some as if from H2109 זוּן or an unused root, and applied to military equipments; but evidently the feminine plural active participle of H2181 זָנָה\nStrong's: harlots\nKJV: armour.\n\nCognate Group: H2183 (whoredom), H2181 (commit fornication), H8457 (fornication), H2185 (armour), H2184 (whoredom)",
    2186: "זָנַח (zânach | zaw-nakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root meaning to push aside, i.e.\nStrong's: reject, forsake, fail\nKJV: cast away (off), remove far away (off).\n\nCognate Group: H2186 (cast away)\nGreek Equivalents: G654 ἀποστρέφω, G683 ἀπωθέομαι, G1544 ἐκβάλλω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G2641 καταλείπω, G3392 μιαίνω",
    2187: "זָנַק (zânaq | zaw-nak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to draw together the feet (as an animal about to dart upon its prey), i.e. to spring forward\nKJV: leap.\n\nCognate Group: H2190 (Zaavan), H2187 (leap)\nGreek Equivalents: G1530 εἰσπηδάω",
    2188: "זֵעָה (zêʻâh | zay-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H2111 זוּעַ (in the sense of H3154 יֶזַע)\nStrong's: perspiration\nKJV: sweat.\n\nCognate Group: H3154 (any thing that causeth sweat), H2188 (sweat)\nGreek Equivalents: G2402 ἱδρώς",
    2189: "זַעֲוָה (zaʻăvâh | zah-av-aw')\n\nDerivation: by transposition for H2113 זְוָעָה\nStrong's: agitation, maltreatment\nKJV: [idiom] removed, trouble.\n\nCognate Group: H2127 (Zia), H2189 ([idiom] removed), H2111 (move), H2113 (be removed)\nGreek Equivalents: G1290 διασπορά, G5016 ταραχή",
    2190: "זַעֲוָן (Zaʻăvân | zah-av-awn')\n\nDerivation: from H2111 זוּעַ ; disquiet\nStrong's: Zaavan, an Idumaean\nKJV: Zaavan.\n\nCognate Group: H2190 (Zaavan), H2187 (leap)",
    2191: "זְעֵיר (zᵉʻêyr | zeh-ayr')Typo: xlit zeʻêyr corrected to zᵉʻêyr\n\nGreek Equivalents: G3398 μικρός \n\nDerivation: from an unused root (akin (by permutation) to H6819 צָעַר), meaning to dwindle\nStrong's: small\nKJV: little.\n\nCognate Group: H4213 (few), H2203 (pitch), H2131 (chain), H2202 (Ziphron), H2191 (little)",
    2192: "זְעֵיר (zᵉʻêyr | zeh-ayr')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H2191 זְעֵיר \n\nTypo: xlit zeʻêyr corrected to zᵉʻêyr\n\nStrong's: small\nKJV: little.\n\nCognate Group: H2192 (little)",
    2193: "זָעַךְ (zâʻak | zaw-ak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to extinguish\nKJV: be extinct.\n\nCognate Group: H2193 (be extinct)",
    2194: "זָעַם (zâʻam | zaw-am')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to foam at the mouth, i.e. to be enraged\nKJV: abhor, abominable, (be) angry, defy, (have) indignation.\n\nCognate Group: H2195 (angry), H2194 (abhor)\nGreek Equivalents: G546 ἀπειλέω, G1863 ἐπάγω, G2373 θυμόω, G2672 καταράομαι, G3404 μισέω, G3710 ὀργίζω",
    2195: "זַעַם (zaʻam | zah'-am)\n\nDerivation: from H2194 זָעַם\nStrong's: strictly froth at the mouth, i.e. (figuratively) fury (especially of God's displeasure with sin)\nKJV: angry, indignation, rage.\n\nCognate Group: H2195 (angry), H2194 (abhor)\nGreek Equivalents: G93 ἀδικία, G547 ἀπειλή, G2372 θυμός, G3709 ὀργή, G4088 πικρία",
    2196: "זָעַף (zâʻaph | zaw-af')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to boil up, i.e. (figuratively) to be peevish or angry\nKJV: fret, sad, worse liking, be wroth.\n\nCognate Group: H2197 (indignation), H2198 (displeased), H2196 (fret)\nGreek Equivalents: G2373 θυμόω, G3710 ὀργίζω, G5015 ταράσσω",
    2197: "זַעַף (zaʻaph | zah'-af)\n\nDerivation: from H2196 זָעַף\nStrong's: anger\nKJV: indignation, rage(-ing), wrath.\n\nCognate Group: H2197 (indignation), H2198 (displeased), H2196 (fret)\nGreek Equivalents: G547 ἀπειλή, G772 ἀσθενής, G2372 θυμός, G3709 ὀργή, G4535 σάλος, G4659 σκυθρωπός",
    2198: "זָעֵף (zâʻêph | zaw-afe')\n\nDerivation: from H2196 זָעַף\nStrong's: angry\nKJV: displeased.\n\nCognate Group: H2197 (indignation), H2198 (displeased), H2196 (fret)\nGreek Equivalents: G1590 ἐκλύω",
    2199: "זָעַק (zâʻaq | zaw-ak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to shriek (from anguish or danger); by analogy, (as a herald) to announce or convene publicly\nKJV: assemble, call (together), (make a) cry (out), come with such a company, gather (together), cause to be proclaimed.\n\nCognate Group: H2201 (cry), H2199 (assemble)\nGreek Equivalents: G305 ἀναβαίνω, G310 ἀναβοάω, G349 ἀνακράζω, G994 βοάω, G2564 καλέω, G2784 κηρύσσω, G2896 κράζω, G2906 κραυγή, G3853 παραγγέλλω, G4727 στενάζω",
    2200: "זְעִק (zᵉʻiq | zek'-eek)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H2199 זָעַק\nStrong's: to make an outcry\nKJV: cry.\n\nCognate Group: H2200 (cry), H2170 (musick), H2171 (singer), H2178 (kind)",
    2201: "זַעַק (zaʻaq | zah'-ak)\n\nDerivation: and (feminine) זְעָקָה\n\nTypo: xlit zᵉâqâh corrected to zᵉʻâqâh\n\n; from H2199 זָעַק\nStrong's: a shriek or outcry\nKJV: cry(-ing).\n\nCognate Group: H2201 (cry), H2199 (assemble)\nGreek Equivalents: G994 βοάω, G995 βοή, G5456 φωνή",
    2202: "זִפְרֹן (Ziphrôn | zi-frone')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (meaning to be fragrant)\nStrong's: Ziphron, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Ziphron.\n\nCognate Group: H4213 (few), H2203 (pitch), H2131 (chain), H2202 (Ziphron), H2191 (little)",
    2203: "זֶפֶת (zepheth | zeh'-feth)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (meaning to liquify)\nStrong's: asphalt (from its tendency to soften in the sun)\nKJV: pitch.\n\nCognate Group: H4213 (few), H2203 (pitch), H2131 (chain), H2202 (Ziphron), H2191 (little)",
    2204: "זָקֵן (zâqên | zaw-kane')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be old\nKJV: aged man, be (wax) old (man).\n\nCognate Group: H2205 (aged), H2209 (old), H2206 (beard), H2204 (aged man), H2208 (old age), H2207 (age)\nGreek Equivalents: G1095 γηράσκω",
    2205: "זָקֵן (zâqên | zaw-kane')\n\nDerivation: from H2204 זָקֵן\nStrong's: old\nKJV: aged, ancient (man), elder(-est), old (man, men and...women), senator.\n\nCognate Group: H2205 (aged), H2209 (old), H2206 (beard), H2204 (aged man), H2208 (old age), H2207 (age)\nGreek Equivalents: G435 ἀνήρ, G1087 γερουσία, G1088 γέρων, G4246 πρεσβύτης",
    2206: "זָקָן (zâqân | zaw-kawn')\n\nDerivation: from H2204 זָקֵן\nStrong's: the beard (as indicating age)\nKJV: beard.\n\nCognate Group: H2205 (aged), H2209 (old), H2206 (beard), H2204 (aged man), H2208 (old age), H2207 (age)",
    2207: "זֹקֶן (zôqen | zo'-ken)\n\nDerivation: from H2204 זָקֵן\nStrong's: old age\nKJV: age.\n\nCognate Group: H2205 (aged), H2209 (old), H2206 (beard), H2204 (aged man), H2208 (old age), H2207 (age)\nGreek Equivalents: G1094 γῆρας",
    2208: "זָקֻן (zâqun | zaw-koon')Typo: lemma זָקֻ missing final nun, corrected to זָקֻן\n\nDerivation: properly, passive participle of H2204 זָקֵן (used only in the plural as a noun)\n\nStrong's: old age\nKJV: old age.\n\nCognate Group: H2205 (aged), H2209 (old), H2206 (beard), H2204 (aged man), H2208 (old age), H2207 (age)",
    2209: "זִקְנָה (ziqnâh | zik-naw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H2205 זָקֵן\nStrong's: old age\nKJV: old (age).\n\nCognate Group: H2205 (aged), H2209 (old), H2206 (beard), H2204 (aged man), H2208 (old age), H2207 (age)",
    2210: "זָקַף (zâqaph | zaw-kaf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to life, i.e. (figuratively) comfort\nKJV: raise (up).\n\nCognate Group: H2210 (raise)\nGreek Equivalents: G461 ἀνορθόω",
    2211: "זְקַף (zᵉqaph | zek-af')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H2210 זָקַף\nStrong's: to hang, i.e. impale\nKJV: set up.\n\nCognate Group: H2234 (seed), H2217 (Zerubbabel), H2211 (set up)",
    2212: "זָקַק (zâqaq | zaw-kak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to strain, (figuratively) extract, clarify\nKJV: fine, pour down, purge, purify, refine.\n\nCognate Group: H2212 (fine)\nGreek Equivalents: G1383 δοκίμιον, G1384 δόκιμος, G1632 ἐκχέω, G2022 ἐπιχέω, G2511 καθαρίζω",
    2213: "זֵר (zêr | zare)\n\nDerivation: from H2237 זָרַר (in the sense of scattering)\nStrong's: a chaplet (as spread around the top), i.e. (specifically) a border moulding\nKJV: crown.\n\nCognate Group: H2115 (close), H2116 (that which is crushed), H4205 (bound up), H2213 (crown), H2223 (greyhound)\nGreek Equivalents: G2087 ἕτερος, G2190 ἐχθρός, G2992 λαός",
    2214: "זָרָא (zârâʼ | zaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H2114 זוּר (in the sense of estrangement) (compare H2219 זָרָה)\nStrong's: disgust\nKJV: loathsome.\n\nCognate Group: H2214 (loathsome), H2114 (another)",
    2215: "זָרַב (zârab | zaw-rab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to flow away\nKJV: wax warm.\n\nCognate Group: H2218 (Zared), H2216 (Zerubbabel), H2215 (wax warm)\nGreek Equivalents: G5080 τήκω",
    2216: "זְרֻבָּבֶל (Zᵉrubbâbel | zer-oob-baw-bel')\n\nDerivation: from H2215 זָרַב and H894 בָּבֶל ; descended of (i.e. from) Babylon, i.e. born there\nStrong's: Zerubbabel, an Israelite\nKJV: Zerubbabel.\n\nCognate Group: H2218 (Zared), H2216 (Zerubbabel), H2215 (wax warm)\nGreek Equivalents: G2216 Ζοροβάβελ",
    2217: "זְרֻבָּבֶל (Zᵉrubbâbel | zer-oob-baw-bel')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H2216 זְרֻבָּבֶל \nStrong's: Zerubbabel, an Israelite\nKJV: Zerubbabel.\n\nCognate Group: H2234 (seed), H2217 (Zerubbabel), H2211 (set up)",
    2218: "זֶרֶד (Zered | zeh'-red)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be exuberant in growth; lined with shrubbery\nStrong's: Zered, a brook East of the Dead Sea\nKJV: Zared, Zered.\n\nCognate Group: H2218 (Zared), H2216 (Zerubbabel), H2215 (wax warm)",
    2219: "זָרָה (zârâh | zaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2114 זוּר)\nStrong's: to toss about; by implication, to diffuse, winnow\nKJV: cast away, compass, disperse, fan, scatter (away), spread, strew, winnow.\n\nCognate Group: H4215 (north), H2219 (cast away), H4214 (fan)\nGreek Equivalents: G1287 διασκορπίζω, G1289 διασπείρω, G1614 ἐκτείνω, G2513 καθαρός, G3039 λικμάω, G4204 πόρνη, G4650 σκορπίζω, G4687 σπείρω",
    2220: "זְרֹועַ (zᵉrôwaʻ | zer-o'-ah)\n\nDerivation: or (shortened) זְרֹעַ; and (feminine) זְרֹועָה; or זְרֹעָה; from H2232 זָרַע\nStrong's: the arm (as stretched out), or (of animals) the foreleg; figuratively, force\nKJV: arm, [phrase] help, mighty, power, shoulder, strength.\n\nCognate Group: H2220 (arm), H248 (arm)\nGreek Equivalents: G484 ἀντίληψις, G1023 βραχίων",
    2221: "זֵרוּעַ (zêrûwaʻ | zay-roo'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from H2232 זָרַע\nStrong's: something sown, i.e. a plant\nKJV: sowing, thing that is sown.\n\nCognate Group: H2221 (sowing), H2233 ([idiom] carnally), H2235 (pulse), H4218 (thing sown), H3159 (Jezreelitess), H3157 (Jezreel), H3158 (Jezreelite), H2232 (bear)",
    2222: "זַרְזִיף (zarzîyph | zar-zeef')\n\nDerivation: by reduplication from an unused root meaning to flow\nStrong's: a pouring rain\nKJV: water.\n\nCognate Group: H2222 (water)",
    2223: "זַרְזִיר (zarzîyr | zar-zeer')\n\nDerivation: by reduplication from H2115 זוּר\nStrong's: properly, tightly girt, i.e. probably a racer, or some fleet animal (as being slender in the waist)\nKJV: [phrase] greyhound.\n\nCognate Group: H2115 (close), H2116 (that which is crushed), H4205 (bound up), H2213 (crown), H2223 (greyhound)\nGreek Equivalents: G220 ἀλέκτωρ",
    2224: "זָרַח (zârach | zaw-rakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to irradiate (or shoot forth beams), i.e. to rise (as the sun); specifically, to appear (as a symptom of leprosy)\nKJV: arise, rise (up), as soon as it is up.\n\nCognate Group: H2224 (arise), H2227 (Zarchite), H2225 (rising), H3156 (Izrahiah), H249 (bay tree), H4217 (east), H3155 (Izrahite), H250 (Ezrahite), H2228 (Zerahiah), H2226 (Zarah)\nGreek Equivalents: G393 ἀνατέλλω, G1816 ἐξανατέλλω, G2014 ἐπιφαίνω, G5316 φαίνω",
    2225: "זֶרַח (zerach | zeh'-rakh)\n\nDerivation: from H2224 זָרַח\nStrong's: a rising of light\nKJV: rising.\n\nCognate Group: H2224 (arise), H2227 (Zarchite), H2225 (rising), H3156 (Izrahiah), H249 (bay tree), H4217 (east), H3155 (Izrahite), H250 (Ezrahite), H2228 (Zerahiah), H2226 (Zarah)",
    2226: "זֶרַח (Zerach | zeh'-rakh)\n\nDerivation: the same as H2225 זֶרַח\nStrong's: Zerach, the name of three Israelites, also of an Idumaean and an Ethiopian prince\nKJV: Zarah, Zerah.\n\nCognate Group: H2224 (arise), H2227 (Zarchite), H2225 (rising), H3156 (Izrahiah), H249 (bay tree), H4217 (east), H3155 (Izrahite), H250 (Ezrahite), H2228 (Zerahiah), H2226 (Zarah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2196 Ζαρά",
    2227: "זַרְחִי (Zarchîy | zar-khee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H2226 זֶרַח\nStrong's: a Zarchite or descendant of Zerach\nKJV: Zarchite.\n\nCognate Group: H2224 (arise), H2227 (Zarchite), H2225 (rising), H3156 (Izrahiah), H249 (bay tree), H4217 (east), H3155 (Izrahite), H250 (Ezrahite), H2228 (Zerahiah), H2226 (Zarah)",
    2228: "זְרַחְיָה (Zᵉrachyâh | zer-akh-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H2225 זֶרַח and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has risen\nStrong's: Zerachjah, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Zerahiah.\n\nCognate Group: H2224 (arise), H2227 (Zarchite), H2225 (rising), H3156 (Izrahiah), H249 (bay tree), H4217 (east), H3155 (Izrahite), H250 (Ezrahite), H2228 (Zerahiah), H2226 (Zarah)",
    2229: "זָרַם (zâram | zaw-ram')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to gush (as water)\nKJV: carry away as with a flood, pour out.\n\nCognate Group: H2229 (carry away as with a flood), H2230 (flood), H2231 (issue)",
    2230: "זֶרֶם (zerem | zeh'-rem)\n\nDerivation: from H2229 זָרַם\nStrong's: a gush of water\nKJV: flood, overflowing, shower, storm, tempest.\n\nCognate Group: H2229 (carry away as with a flood), H2230 (flood), H2231 (issue)",
    2231: "זִרְמָה (zirmâh | zir-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H2230 זֶרֶם\nStrong's: a gushing of fluid (semen)\nKJV: issue.\n\nCognate Group: H2229 (carry away as with a flood), H2230 (flood), H2231 (issue)",
    2232: "זָרַע (zâraʻ | zaw-rah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to sow; figuratively, to disseminate, plant, fructify\nKJV: bear, conceive seed, set with sow(-er), yield.\n\nCognate Group: H2221 (sowing), H2233 ([idiom] carnally), H2235 (pulse), H4218 (thing sown), H3159 (Jezreelitess), H3157 (Jezreel), H3158 (Jezreelite), H2232 (bear)\nGreek Equivalents: G393 ἀνατέλλω, G4687 σπείρω, G4701 σπορά, G4702 σπόριμος",
    2233: "זֶרַע (zeraʻ | zeh'-rah)\n\nDerivation: from H2232 זָרַע\nStrong's: seed; figuratively, fruit, plant, sowing-time, posterity\nKJV: [idiom] carnally, child, fruitful, seed(-time), sowing-time.\n\nCognate Group: H2221 (sowing), H2233 ([idiom] carnally), H2235 (pulse), H4218 (thing sown), H3159 (Jezreelitess), H3157 (Jezreel), H3158 (Jezreelite), H2232 (bear)\nGreek Equivalents: G1074 γενεά, G1078 γένεσις, G1085 γένος, G1484 ἔθνος, G2593 καρποφόρος, G2961 κυριεύω, G4690 σπέρμα, G4703 σπόρος, G5207 υἱός",
    2234: "זְרַע (zᵉraʻ | zer-ah')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H2233 זֶרַע\nStrong's: posterity\nKJV: seed.\n\nCognate Group: H2234 (seed), H2217 (Zerubbabel), H2211 (set up)",
    2235: "זֵרֹעַ (zêrôaʻ | zay-ro'-ah)\n\nDerivation: or זֵרָעֹן; from H2232 זָרַע\nStrong's: something sown (only in the plural), i.e. a vegetable (as food)\nKJV: pulse.\n\nCognate Group: H2221 (sowing), H2233 ([idiom] carnally), H2235 (pulse), H4218 (thing sown), H3159 (Jezreelitess), H3157 (Jezreel), H3158 (Jezreelite), H2232 (bear)",
    2236: "זָרַק (zâraq | zaw-rak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to sprinkle (fluid or solid particles)\nKJV: be here and there, scatter, sprinkle, strew.\n\nCognate Group: H4219 (bason), H2236 (be here and there)\nGreek Equivalents: G1209 δέχομαι, G1287 διασκορπίζω, G1632 ἐκχέω, G4687 σπείρω",
    2237: "זָרַר (zârar | zaw-rar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2114 זוּר)\nStrong's: perhaps to diffuse, i.e. (specifically) to sneeze\nKJV: sneeze.\n\nCognate Group: H2240 (Zattu), H2238 (Zeresh), H2242 (Zethar), H2237 (sneeze), H2239 (span), H2241 (Zetham)",
    2238: "זֶרֶשׁ (Zeresh | zeh'-resh)\n\nDerivation: of Persian origin\nStrong's: Zeresh, Haman's wife\nKJV: Zeresh.\n\nCognate Group: H2240 (Zattu), H2238 (Zeresh), H2242 (Zethar), H2237 (sneeze), H2239 (span), H2241 (Zetham)",
    2239: "זֶרֶת (zereth | zeh'-reth)\n\nDerivation: from H2219 זָרָה\nStrong's: the spread of the fingers, i.e. a span\nKJV: span.\n\nCognate Group: H2240 (Zattu), H2238 (Zeresh), H2242 (Zethar), H2237 (sneeze), H2239 (span), H2241 (Zetham)",
    2240: "זַתּוּא (Zattûwʼ | zat-too')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Zattu, an Israelite\nKJV: Zattu.\n\nCognate Group: H2240 (Zattu), H2238 (Zeresh), H2242 (Zethar), H2237 (sneeze), H2239 (span), H2241 (Zetham)",
    2241: "זֵתָם (Zêthâm | zay-thawm')\n\nDerivation: apparently a variation for H2133 זֵיתָן\nStrong's: Zetham, an Israelite\nKJV: Zetham.\n\nCognate Group: H2240 (Zattu), H2238 (Zeresh), H2242 (Zethar), H2237 (sneeze), H2239 (span), H2241 (Zetham)",
    2242: "זֵתַר (Zêthar | zay-thar')\n\nDerivation: of Persian origin\nStrong's: Zethar, a eunuch of Xerxes\nKJV: Zethar. j\n\nCognate Group: H2240 (Zattu), H2238 (Zeresh), H2242 (Zethar), H2237 (sneeze), H2239 (span), H2241 (Zetham)",
    2243: "חֹב (chôb | khobe)\n\nDerivation: by contraction from H2245 חָבַב\nStrong's: properly, a cherisher, i.e. the bosom\nKJV: bosom.\n\nCognate Group: H3160 (Jehubbah), H2243 (bosom), H2245 (love), H2246 (Hobab)\nGreek Equivalents: G3784 ὀφείλω",
    2244: "חָבָא (châbâʼ | khaw-baw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2245 חָבַב)\nStrong's: to secrete\nKJV: [idiom] held, hide (self), do secretly.\n\nCognate Group: H2244 ([idiom] held), H4224 (hiding place)\nGreek Equivalents: G1470 ἐγκρύπτω, G2597 καταβαίνω, G2703 καταφεύγω, G2928 κρύπτω, G2931 κρυφῆ, G5419 φράζω",
    2245: "חָבַב (châbab | khaw-bab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2244 חָבָא, H2247 חָבָה)\nStrong's: properly, to hide (as in the bosom), i.e. to cherish (with affection)\nKJV: love.\n\nCognate Group: H3160 (Jehubbah), H2243 (bosom), H2245 (love), H2246 (Hobab)",
    2246: "חֹבָב (Chôbâb | kho-bawb')\n\nDerivation: from H2245 חָבַב ; cherished\nStrong's: Chobab, father-in-law of Moses\nKJV: Hobab.\n\nCognate Group: H3160 (Jehubbah), H2243 (bosom), H2245 (love), H2246 (Hobab)",
    2247: "חָבָה (châbâh | khaw-bah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2245 חָבַב)\nStrong's: to secrete\nKJV: hide (self).\n\nCognate Group: H2252 (Habaiah), H2247 (hide), H2253 (hiding), H5147 (Nakbi)\nGreek Equivalents: G613 ἀποκρύπτω, G1886 ἔπαυλις, G2096 Εὖα, G2222 ζωή, G2968 κώμη",
    2248: "חֲבוּלָה (chăbûwlâh | khab-oo-law')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H2255 חֲבַל\nStrong's: properly, overthrown, i.e. (morally) crime\nKJV: hurt.\n\nCognate Group: H2255 (destroy), H2248 (hurt), H2257 (damage)\nGreek Equivalents: G266 ἁμαρτία, G3900 παράπτωμα",
    2249: "חָבֹור (Châbôwr | khaw-bore')\n\nDerivation: from H2266 חָבַר ; united\nStrong's: Chabor, a river of Assyria\nKJV: Habor.\n\nCognate Group: H2250 (blueness), H4226 (coupling), H4225 (coupling), H2268 (Heber), H2279 (which coupleth), H2266 (charm), H2276 (Hebronites), H2274 (company), H2267 (charmer), H2272 (spot), H2249 (Habor), H2270 (companion), H2271 (companion), H2275 (Hebron), H2277 (Heberites), H2278 (companion)",
