    2552: "חָמַם (châmam | khaw-mam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be hot (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: enflame self, get (have) heat, be (wax) hot, (be, wax) warm (self, at).\n\nCognate Group: H2535 (heat), H2540 (Hammon), H2527 (heat), H2525 (hot), H2552 (enflame self), H2575 (Hammath), H2553 (idol), H2536 (Hamuel), H2576 (Hamath-Dor)\nGreek Equivalents: G92 ἀδίκημα, G2282 θάλπω, G2328 θερμαίνω, G2329 θέρμη",
