    2556: "חָמֵץ (châmêts | khaw-mates')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be pungent; i.e. in taste (sour, i.e. literally fermented, or figuratively, harsh), in color (dazzling)\nKJV: cruel (man), dyed, be grieved, leavened.\n\nCognate Group: H2556 (cruel), H2558 (vinegar), H2548 (clean), H2557 (leaven)\nGreek Equivalents: G91 ἀδικέω, G1572 ἐκκαίω, G2220 ζυμόω",
