    2648: "חָפַז (châphaz | khaw-faz')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to start up suddenly, i.e. (by implication) to hasten away, to fear\nKJV: (make) haste (away), tremble.\n\nCognate Group: H2649 (haste), H2648 (haste)\nGreek Equivalents: G143 αἰσθάνομαι, G1168 δειλιάω, G1611 ἔκστασις, G2284 θαμβέω, G2352 θραύω, G4531 σαλεύω, G4692 σπεύδω",
    2649: "חִפָּזֹון (chippâzôwn | khip-paw-zone')\n\nDerivation: from H2468 חֻלְדָּה\nStrong's: hasty flight\nKJV: haste.\n\nCognate Group: H2649 (haste), H2648 (haste)\nGreek Equivalents: G4710 σπουδή, G5016 ταραχή",
    2650: "חֻפִּים (Chuppîym | khoop-peem')\n\nDerivation: plural of H2646 חֻפָּה (compare H2349 חוּפָם)\nStrong's: Chuppim, an Israelite\nKJV: Huppim.\n\nCognate Group: H2650 (Huppim), H2348 (coast), H2647 (Huppah), H2646 (chamber), H2653 (cover)",
    2651: "חֹפֶן (chôphen | kho'-fen)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root of uncertain signification\nStrong's: a fist (only in the dual)\nKJV: fists, (both) hands, hand(-ful).\n\nCognate Group: H2652 (Hophni), H2651 (fists)\nGreek Equivalents: G2859 κόλπος, G5495 χείρ",
    2652: "חׇפְנִי (Chophnîy | khof-nee')\n\nDerivation: from H2651 חֹפֶן ; perhaps pugilist\nStrong's: Chophni, an Israelite\nKJV: Hophni.\n\nCognate Group: H2652 (Hophni), H2651 (fists)",
    2653: "חׇפַף (chophaph | khaw-faf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2645 חָפָה, H3182 יָחֵף)\nStrong's: to cover (in protection)\nKJV: cover.\n\nCognate Group: H2650 (Huppim), H2348 (coast), H2647 (Huppah), H2646 (chamber), H2653 (cover)",
    2654: "חָפֵץ (châphêts | khaw-fates')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to incline to; by implication (literally but rarely) to bend; figuratively, to be pleased with, desire\nKJV: [idiom] any at all, (have, take) delight, desire, favour, like, move, be (well) pleased, have pleasure, will, would.\n\nCognate Group: H2654 ([idiom] any at all), H2657 (Hephzi-bah), H2655 (delight in), H2656 (acceptable)\nGreek Equivalents: G25 ἀγαπάω, G138 αἱρέομαι, G140 αἱρετίζω, G1013 βούλημα, G1937 ἐπιθυμέω, G2106 εὐδοκέω, G2309 θέλω, G2476 ἵστημι",
    2655: "חָפֵץ (châphêts | khaw-fates')\n\nDerivation: from H2654 חָפֵץ\nStrong's: pleased with\nKJV: delight in, desire, favour, please, have pleasure, whosoever would, willing, wish.\n\nCognate Group: H2654 ([idiom] any at all), H2657 (Hephzi-bah), H2655 (delight in), H2656 (acceptable)\nGreek Equivalents: G2307 θέλημα",
    2656: "חֵפֶץ (chêphets | khay'-fets)\n\nDerivation: from H2654 חָפֵץ\nStrong's: pleasure; hence (abstractly) desire; concretely, a valuable thing; hence (by extension) a matter (as something in mind)\nKJV: acceptable, delight(-some), desire, things desired, matter, pleasant(-ure), purpose, willingly.\n\nCognate Group: H2654 ([idiom] any at all), H2657 (Hephzi-bah), H2655 (delight in), H2656 (acceptable)\nGreek Equivalents: G1011 βουλεύω, G1588 ἐκλεκτός, G2173 εὔχρηστος, G2308 θέλησις, G3195 μέλλω, G3199 μέλω, G4229 πρᾶγμα, G5093 τίμιος",
    2657: "חֶפְצִי בָּהּ (Chephtsîy bâhh | khef-tsee'baw)\n\nDerivation: from H2656 חֵפֶץ with suffixes; my delight (is) in her\nStrong's: Cheptsi-bah, a fanciful name for Palestine\nKJV: Hephzi-bah.\n\nCognate Group: H2654 ([idiom] any at all), H2657 (Hephzi-bah), H2655 (delight in), H2656 (acceptable)",
    2658: "חָפַר (châphar | khaw-far')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to pry into; by implication, to delve, to explore\nKJV: dig, paw, search out, seek.\n\nCognate Group: H2663 (Haphraim), H6512 (mole), H2658 (dig), H2660 (Hepher), H2661 (mole), H2662 (Hepherites)\nGreek Equivalents: G2212 ζητέω, G3736 ὀρύσσω",
    2659: "חָפֵר (châphêr | khaw-fare')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (perhaps rather the same as H2658 חָפַר through the idea of detection)\nStrong's: to blush; figuratively, to be ashamed, disappointed; causatively, to shame, reproach\nKJV: be ashamed, be confounded, be brought to confusion (unto shame), come (be put to) shame, bring reproach.\n\nCognate Group: H6548 (Pharaoh-hophra), H2659 (be ashamed)\nGreek Equivalents: G153 αἰσχύνομαι, G1788 ἐντρέπω, G1870 ἐπαισχύνομαι, G2606 καταγελάω, G2617 καταισχύνω, G3679 ὀνειδίζω",
    2660: "חֵפֶר (Chêpher | khay'-fer)\n\nDerivation: from H2658 חָפַר or H2659 חָפֵר ; a pit of shame\nStrong's: Chepher, a place in Palestine; also the name of three Israelites\nKJV: Hepher.\n\nCognate Group: H2663 (Haphraim), H6512 (mole), H2658 (dig), H2660 (Hepher), H2661 (mole), H2662 (Hepherites)",
    2661: "חֲפֹר (chăphôr | khaf-ore')\n\nDerivation: from H2658 חָפַר ; a hole; only in connection with H6512 פֵּרָה, which ought rather to be joined as one word, thus חַפַרְפֵּרָה; by reduplication from H2658 חָפַר\nStrong's: a burrower, i.e. probably a rat\nKJV: [phrase] mole.\n\nCognate Group: H2663 (Haphraim), H6512 (mole), H2658 (dig), H2660 (Hepher), H2661 (mole), H2662 (Hepherites)",
    2662: "חֶפְרִי (Chephrîy | khef-ree')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H2660 חֵפֶר\nStrong's: a Chephrite (collectively) or descendants of Chepher\nKJV: Hepherites.\n\nCognate Group: H2663 (Haphraim), H6512 (mole), H2658 (dig), H2660 (Hepher), H2661 (mole), H2662 (Hepherites)",
    2663: "חֲפָרַיִם (Chăphârayim | khaf-aw-rah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: dual of H2660 חֵפֶר ; double pit\nStrong's: Chapharajim, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Haphraim.\n\nCognate Group: H2663 (Haphraim), H6512 (mole), H2658 (dig), H2660 (Hepher), H2661 (mole), H2662 (Hepherites)",
    2664: "חָפַשׂ (châphas | khaw-fas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to seek; causatively, to conceal oneself (i.e. let be sought), or mask\nKJV: change, (make) diligent (search), disquise self, hide, search (for, out).\n\nCognate Group: H2665 (search), H2664 (change)\nGreek Equivalents: G2045 ἐρευνάω, G2045 ἐρευνάω, G2611 καταδέω, G2619 κατακαλύπτω, G2901 κραταιόω, G4028 περικαλύπτω",
    2665: "חֵפֶשׂ (chêphes | khay'-fes)\n\nDerivation: from H2664 חָפַשׂ\nStrong's: something covert, i.e. a trick\nKJV: search.\n\nCognate Group: H2665 (search), H2664 (change)",
    2666: "חָפַשׁ (châphash | khaw-fash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to spread loose; figuratively, to manumit\nKJV: be free.\n\nCognate Group: H2670 (free), H2667 (precious), H2666 (be free), H2669 (several), H2668 (freedom)",
    2667: "חֹפֶשׁ (Chôphesh | kho'-fesh)\n\nDerivation: from H2666 חָפַשׁ\nStrong's: something spread loosely, i.e. a carpet\nKJV: precious.\n\nCognate Group: H2670 (free), H2667 (precious), H2666 (be free), H2669 (several), H2668 (freedom)\nGreek Equivalents: G1588 ἐκλεκτός",
    2668: "חֻפְשָׁה (chuphshâh | khoof-shaw')\n\nDerivation: from H2666 חָפַשׁ\nStrong's: liberty (from slavery)\nKJV: freedom.\n\nCognate Group: H2670 (free), H2667 (precious), H2666 (be free), H2669 (several), H2668 (freedom)\nGreek Equivalents: G1657 ἐλευθερία",
    2669: "חׇפְשׁוּת (chophshûwth | khof-shooth')\n\nDerivation: and חׇפְשִׁית; from H2666 חָפַשׁ ; (with H1004 בַּיִת, a hospital)\n\nStrong's: prostration by sickness\nKJV: several.\n\nCognate Group: H2670 (free), H2667 (precious), H2666 (be free), H2669 (several), H2668 (freedom)",
    2670: "חׇפְשִׁי (chophshîy | khof-shee')\n\nDerivation: from H2666 חָפַשׁ\nStrong's: exempt (from bondage, tax or care)\nKJV: free, liberty.\n\nCognate Group: H2670 (free), H2667 (precious), H2666 (be free), H2669 (several), H2668 (freedom)\nGreek Equivalents: G859 ἄφεσις, G1658 ἐλεύθερος",
    2671: "חֵץ (chêts | khayts)\n\nDerivation: from H2686 חָצַץ ; also by interchange for H6086 עֵץ \nStrong's: properly, a piercer, i.e. an arrow; by implication, a wound; figuratively, (of God) thunderbolt; the shaft of aspear\nKJV: [phrase] archer, arrow, dart, shaft, staff, wound.\n\nCognate Group: H2688 (Hazezon-tamar), H2686 (archer), H2687 (arrow), H2671 (archer)\nGreek Equivalents: G956 βέλος, G1002 βολίς, G5115 τόξον",
    2672: "חָצַב (châtsab | khaw-tsab')\n\nDerivation: or חָצֵב; a primitive root\nStrong's: to cut or carve (wood, stone or other material); by implication, to hew, split, square, quarry, engrave\nKJV: cut, dig, divide, grave, hew (out, -er), made, mason.\n\nCognate Group: H4274 (hewed), H2672 (cut)\nGreek Equivalents: G2875 κόπτω, G2998 λατομέω, G3736 ὀρύσσω, G4160 ποιέω, G5079 τεχνίτης",
    2673: "חָצָה (châtsâh | khaw-tsaw')Typo: lemma חָעָה ayin, corrected to חָצָה\n\nGreek Equivalents: G1244 διαιρέω, G3307 μερίζω \n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2086 זֵד))\n\nStrong's: to cut or split in two; to halve\nKJV: divide, [idiom] live out half, reach to the midst, participle\n\nCognate Group: H3185 (Jahziel), H2676 (mid), H4276 (half), H2677 (half), H4275 (half), H2678 (arrow), H3184 (Jahzeelites), H2673 (divide), H3183 (Jahzeel)",
    2674: "חָצֹור (Châtsôwr | khaw-tsore')\n\nDerivation: a collective form of H2691 חָצֵר ; village\nStrong's: Chatsor, the name (thus simply) of two places in Palestine and of one in Arabia\nKJV: Hazor.\n\nCognate Group: H2697 (Hezronites), H2702 (Hazar-susim), H2694 (Hazar-hatticon), H2696 (Hezron), H2695 (Hezro), H2691 (court), H2681 (court), H2698 (Hazeroth), H2693 (Hazar-gaddah), H2701 (Hazar-susah), H2674 (Hazor), H2699 (Hazerim), H2705 (Hazar-shual), H2703 (Hazar-enon), H2675 (Hazor), H2692 (Hazar-addar), H2704 (Hazar-enan), H2700 (Hazarmaveth)",
    2675: "חָצֹור חֲדַתָּה (Châtsôwr Chădattâh | khaw-tsore' khad-attaw')\n\nDerivation: from H2674 חָצֹור and a Aramaizing form of the feminine of H2319 חָדָשׁ (compare H2323 חֲדָת)\nStrong's: new Chatsor, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Hazor, Hadattah (as if two places).\n\nCognate Group: H2697 (Hezronites), H2702 (Hazar-susim), H2694 (Hazar-hatticon), H2696 (Hezron), H2695 (Hezro), H2691 (court), H2681 (court), H2698 (Hazeroth), H2693 (Hazar-gaddah), H2701 (Hazar-susah), H2674 (Hazor), H2699 (Hazerim), H2705 (Hazar-shual), H2703 (Hazar-enon), H2675 (Hazor), H2692 (Hazar-addar), H2704 (Hazar-enan), H2700 (Hazarmaveth)",
    2676: "חָצֹות (châtsôwth | khaw-tsoth')Typo: lemma חָעֹות ayin, corrected to חָצֹות\n\nGreek Equivalents: G3317 μεσονύκτιον \n\nDerivation: from H2673 חָצָה \n\nTypo: lemma חָעָה ayin, corrected to חָצָה\n\nStrong's: the middle (of the night)\n\nKJV: mid(-night).\n\nCognate Group: H3185 (Jahziel), H2676 (mid), H4276 (half), H2677 (half), H4275 (half), H2678 (arrow), H3184 (Jahzeelites), H2673 (divide), H3183 (Jahzeel)",
    2677: "חֵצִי (chêtsîy | khay-tsee')\n\nDerivation: from H2673 חָצָה \n\nTypo: lemma חָעָה ayin, corrected to חָצָה\n\nStrong's: the half or middle\nKJV: half, middle, mid(-night), midst, part, two parts.\n\nCognate Group: H3185 (Jahziel), H2676 (mid), H4276 (half), H2677 (half), H4275 (half), H2678 (arrow), H3184 (Jahzeelites), H2673 (divide), H3183 (Jahzeel)\nGreek Equivalents: G2255 ἥμισυ, G3317 μεσονύκτιον, G3319 μέσος, G3322 μεσόω",
    2678: "חִצִּי (chitstsîy | khits-tsee')\n\nDerivation: or חֵצִי; prolongation from H2671 חֵץ\nStrong's: an arrow\nKJV: arrow.\n\nCognate Group: H3185 (Jahziel), H2676 (mid), H4276 (half), H2677 (half), H4275 (half), H2678 (arrow), H3184 (Jahzeelites), H2673 (divide), H3183 (Jahzeel)",
    2679: "חֲצִי הַמְּנֻחֹות (Chătsîy ham-Mᵉnuchôwth | chat-tsee' hammen-oo-khoth')\n\nDerivation: from H2677 חֵצִי and the plural of H4496 מְנוּחָה, with the article interposed; midst of the resting-places\nStrong's: Chatsi-ham-Menuchoth, an Israelite\nKJV: half of the Manahethites.\n\nCognate Group: H2680 (half of the Manahethites), H5183 (lighting down), H5118 (rest), H4494 (rest), H5119 (Nohah), H5146 (Noah), H5207 (sweet), H4495 (Manoah), H3240 (bestow), H5117 (cease), H4496 (comfortable), H2010 (release), H4506 (Manahath), H2679 (half of the Manahethites), H3239 (Janoah)",
    2680: "חֲצִי הַמְּנַחְתִּי (Chătsîy ham-Mᵉnachtîy | khat-see' ham-menakh-tee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H2679 חֲצִי הַמְּנֻחֹות\nStrong's: a Chatsi-ham-Menachtite or descendant of Chatsi-ham-Menuchoth\nKJV: half of the Manahethites.\n\nCognate Group: H2680 (half of the Manahethites), H5183 (lighting down), H5118 (rest), H4494 (rest), H5119 (Nohah), H5146 (Noah), H5207 (sweet), H4495 (Manoah), H3240 (bestow), H5117 (cease), H4496 (comfortable), H2010 (release), H4506 (Manahath), H2679 (half of the Manahethites), H3239 (Janoah)",
    2681: "חָצִיר (châtsîyr | khaw-tseer')\n\nDerivation: a collateral form of H2691 חָצֵר\nStrong's: a court or abode\nKJV: court.\n\nCognate Group: H2697 (Hezronites), H2702 (Hazar-susim), H2694 (Hazar-hatticon), H2696 (Hezron), H2695 (Hezro), H2691 (court), H2681 (court), H2698 (Hazeroth), H2693 (Hazar-gaddah), H2701 (Hazar-susah), H2674 (Hazor), H2699 (Hazerim), H2705 (Hazar-shual), H2703 (Hazar-enon), H2675 (Hazor), H2692 (Hazar-addar), H2704 (Hazar-enan), H2700 (Hazarmaveth)",
    2682: "חָצִיר (châtsîyr | khaw-tseer')\n\nDerivation: perhaps originally the same as H2681 חָצִיר, from the greenness of a courtyard\nStrong's: grass; also a leek (collectively)\nKJV: grass, hay, herb, leek.\n\nCognate Group: H2682 (grass)\nGreek Equivalents: G833 αὐλή, G1008 βοτάνη, G5515 χλωρός, G5528 χόρτος",
    2683: "חֵצֶן (chêtsen | khay'-tsen)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to hold firmly\nStrong's: the bosom (as comprised between the arms)\nKJV: bosom.\n\nCognate Group: H2683 (bosom), H2684 (arm)",
    2684: "חֹצֶן (chôtsen | kho'tsen)\n\nDerivation: a collateral form of H2683 חֵצֶן, and meaning the same\nStrong's: the bosom (as comprised between the arms)\nKJV: arm, lap.\n\nCognate Group: H2683 (bosom), H2684 (arm)\nGreek Equivalents: G2859 κόλπος",
    2685: "חֲצַף (chătsaph | khats-af')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to shear or cut close; figuratively, to be severe\nKJV: hasty, be urgent.\n\nCognate Group: H2685 (hasty)",
    2686: "חָצַץ (châtsats | khaw-tsats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2673 חָצָה \n\nTypo: lemma חָעָה ayin, corrected to חָצָה\n\n); also as denominative from H2671 חֵץ \nStrong's: properly, to chop into, pierce or sever; hence, to curtail, to distribute (into ranks); to shoot an arrow\nKJV: archer, [idiom] bands, cut off in the midst.\n\nCognate Group: H2688 (Hazezon-tamar), H2686 (archer), H2687 (arrow), H2671 (archer)\nGreek Equivalents: G1244 διαιρέω",
    2687: "חָצָץ (châtsâts | khaw-tsawts')\n\nDerivation: from H2687 חָצָץ ; also like H2671 חֵץ \nStrong's: properly, something cutting; hence, gravel (as grit); an arrow\nKJV: arrow, gravel (stone).\n\nCognate Group: H2688 (Hazezon-tamar), H2686 (archer), H2687 (arrow), H2671 (archer)\nGreek Equivalents: G5586 ψῆφος",
    2688: "חַצְצֹון תָּמָר (Chatsᵉtsôwn Tâmâr | khats-ets-one' taw-mawr')\n\nDerivation: or חַצֲצֹן תָּמָר; from H2686 חָצַץ and H8558 תָּמָר ; division (i.e. perhaps row) of (the) palm-tree\nStrong's: Chatsetson-tamar, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Hazezon-tamar.\n\nCognate Group: H2688 (Hazezon-tamar), H2686 (archer), H2687 (arrow), H2671 (archer)",
    2689: "חֲצֹצְרָה (chătsôtsᵉrâh | khats-o-tser-aw')\n\nDerivation: by reduplication from H2690 חָצַר\nStrong's: a trumpet (from its sundered or quavering note)\nKJV: trumpet(-er).\n\nCognate Group: H2689 (trumpet), H2690 (blow)\nGreek Equivalents: G2278 ἠχέω, G4536 σάλπιγξ",
    2690: "חָצַר (châtsar | khaw-tsar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; properly, to surround with a stockade, and thus separate from the open country; but used only in the reduplicated form חֲצֹצֵר; or (2 Chronicles 5:12) חֲצֹרֵר; as dem. from H2689 חֲצֹצְרָה\nStrong's: to trumpet, i.e. blow on that instrument\nKJV: blow, sound, trumpeter.\n\nCognate Group: H2689 (trumpet), H2690 (blow)\nGreek Equivalents: G4537 σαλπίζω",
    2691: "חָצֵר (châtsêr | khaw-tsare')\n\nDerivation: (masculine and feminine); from H2690 חָצַר in its original sense\nStrong's: a yard (as inclosed by a fence); also a hamlet (as similarly surrounded with walls)\nKJV: court, tower, village.\n\nCognate Group: H2691 (court)\nGreek Equivalents: G833 αὐλή, G1857 ἐξώτερος, G1886 ἔπαυλις, G2968 κώμη, G4633 σκηνή",
    2692: "חֲצַר אַדָּר (Chătsar ʼAddâr | khats-ar' addawr')\n\nTypo: xlit Addâr corrected to ʼAddâr\n\nDerivation: from H2691 חָצֵר and H146 אַדָּר ; (the) village of Addar\nStrong's: Chatsar-Addar, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Hazar-addar.\n\nCognate Group: H2697 (Hezronites), H2702 (Hazar-susim), H2694 (Hazar-hatticon), H2696 (Hezron), H2695 (Hezro), H2691 (court), H2681 (court), H2698 (Hazeroth), H2693 (Hazar-gaddah), H2701 (Hazar-susah), H2674 (Hazor), H2699 (Hazerim), H2705 (Hazar-shual), H2703 (Hazar-enon), H2675 (Hazor), H2692 (Hazar-addar), H2704 (Hazar-enan), H2700 (Hazarmaveth)",
    2693: "חֲצַר גַּדָּה (Chătsar Gaddâh | khats-ar' gad-daw')\n\nDerivation: from H2691 חָצֵר and a feminine of H1408 גַּד ; (the) village of (female) Fortune\nStrong's: Chatsar-Gaddah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Hazar-gaddah.\n\nCognate Group: H2697 (Hezronites), H2702 (Hazar-susim), H2694 (Hazar-hatticon), H2696 (Hezron), H2695 (Hezro), H2691 (court), H2681 (court), H2698 (Hazeroth), H2693 (Hazar-gaddah), H2701 (Hazar-susah), H2674 (Hazor), H2699 (Hazerim), H2705 (Hazar-shual), H2703 (Hazar-enon), H2675 (Hazor), H2692 (Hazar-addar), H2704 (Hazar-enan), H2700 (Hazarmaveth)",
