    2712: "חֻקֹּק (Chuqqôq | Khook-koke')\n\nDerivation: or (fully) חוּקֹק; from H2710 חָקַק ; appointed\nStrong's: Chukkok or Chukok, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Hukkok, Hukok.\n\nCognate Group: H2708 (appointed), H2711 (decree), H2710 (appoint), H2712 (Hukkok), H2706 (appointed)",
    2713: "חָקַר (châqar | khaw-kar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to penetrate; hence, to examine intimately\nKJV: find out, (make) search (out), seek (out), sound, try.\n\nCognate Group: H2713 (find out), H4278 (deep place), H2714 (finding out)\nGreek Equivalents: G350 ἀνακρίνω, G1381 δοκιμάζω, G1567 ἐκζητέω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1651 ἐλέγχω, G2045 ἐρευνάω, G2045 ἐρευνάω, G2065 ἐρωτάω, G2607 καταγινώσκω",
    2714: "חֵקֶר (chêqer | khay'-ker)\n\nDerivation: from H2713 חָקַר\nStrong's: examination, enumeration, deliberation\nKJV: finding out, number, (un-) search(-able, -ed, out, -ing).\n\nCognate Group: H2713 (find out), H4278 (deep place), H2714 (finding out)\nGreek Equivalents: G2487 ἴχνος, G4009 πέρας",
    2715: "חֹר (chôr | khore)\n\nDerivation: or (fully) חֹור; from H2787 חָרַר ; (compare H2751 חֹרִי)\n\nStrong's: properly, white or pure (from the cleansing or shining power of fire; hence (figuratively) noble (in rank)\nKJV: noble.\n\nCognate Group: H2715 (noble)",
