    2732: "חֲרָדָה (Chărâdâh | khar-aw-daw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H2731 חֲרָדָה\nStrong's: Charadah, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Haradah.\n\nCognate Group: H2733 (Harodite), H5878 (well of Harod), H2731 (care), H2730 (afraid), H2729 (be afraid), H2732 (Haradah)",
    2733: "חֲרֹדִי (Chărôdîy | khar-o-dee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from a derivative of H2729 חָרַד (compare H5878 עֵין חֲרֹד)\nStrong's: a Charodite, or inhabitant of Charod\nKJV: Harodite.\n\nCognate Group: H2733 (Harodite), H5878 (well of Harod), H2731 (care), H2730 (afraid), H2729 (be afraid), H2732 (Haradah)",
    2734: "חָרָה (chârâh | khaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H2787 חָרַר)\nStrong's: to glow or grow warm; figuratively (usually) to blaze up, of anger, zeal, jealousy\nKJV: be angry, burn, be displeased, [idiom] earnestly, fret self, grieve, be (wax) hot, be incensed, kindle, [idiom] very, be wroth. See H8474 תַּחָרָה .\n\nCognate Group: H2739 (Harumaph), H2734 (be angry), H8474 (close), H2750 (fierce), H2740 (sore displeasure)\nGreek Equivalents: G120 ἀθυμέω, G480 ἀντίκειμαι, G611 ἀποκρίνομαι, G917 βαρέως, G1096 γίνομαι, G1572 ἐκκαίω, G2373 θυμόω, G2373 θυμόω, G3076 λυπέω, G3164 μάχομαι, G3710 ὀργίζω, G3863 παραζηλόω, G3947 παροξύνω, G4642 σκληρός, G5316 φαίνω, G5316 φαίνω, G5316 φαίνω, G5342 φέρω",
    2735: "חֹר הַגִּדְגָּד (Chôr hag-Gidgâd | khore hag-ghid-gawd')\n\nDerivation: from H2356 חֹור and a collateral (masculine) form of H1412 גֻּדְגֹּדָה, with the article interposed; hole of the cleft\nStrong's: Chor-hag-Gidgad, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Hor-hagidgad.\n\nCognate Group: H2735 (Hor-hagidgad), H2362 (Hauran)",
    2736: "חַרְהֲיָה (Charhăyâh | khar-hah-yaw')\n\nDerivation: ; from H2734 חָרָה and H3050 יָהּ ; fearing Jah\nStrong's: Charhajah, an Israelite\nKJV: Harhaiah.\n\nCognate Group: H2737 (chain), H2745 (Harhas), H2736 (Harhaiah)",
    2737: "חָרוּז (chârûwz | khaw-rooz')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to perforate\nStrong's: properly, pierced, i.e. a bead of pearl, gems or jewels (as strung)\nKJV: chain.\n\nCognate Group: H2737 (chain), H2745 (Harhas), H2736 (Harhaiah)",
    2738: "חָרוּל (chârûwl | khaw-rool')\n\nDerivation: or (shortened) חָרֻל; apparently, a passive participle of an unused root probably meaning to be prickly\nStrong's: properly, pointed, i.e. a bramble or other thorny weed\nKJV: nettle.\n\nCognate Group: H2738 (nettle)\nGreek Equivalents: G66 ἄγριος, G5434 φρύγανον",
    2739: "חֲרוּמַף (chărûwmaph | khar-oo-maf')\n\nDerivation: from passive participle of H2763 חָרַם and H639 אַף ; snub-nosed\nStrong's: Charumaph, an Israelite\nKJV: Harumaph.\n\nCognate Group: H2739 (Harumaph), H2734 (be angry), H8474 (close), H2750 (fierce), H2740 (sore displeasure)",
    2740: "חָרֹון (chârôwn | khaw-rone')\n\nDerivation: or (shortened) חָרֹן; from H2734 חָרָה\nStrong's: a burning of anger\nKJV: sore displeasure, fierce(-ness), fury, (fierce) wrath(-ful).\n\nCognate Group: H2739 (Harumaph), H2734 (be angry), H8474 (close), H2750 (fierce), H2740 (sore displeasure)\nGreek Equivalents: G2372 θυμός, G2372 θυμός, G3709 ὀργή",
    2741: "חֲרוּפִי (Chărûwphîy | khar-oo-fee')\n\nDerivation: a patrial from (probably) a collateral form of H2756 חָרִיף\nStrong's: a Charuphite or inhabitant of Charuph (or Chariph)\nKJV: Haruphite.\n\nCognate Group: H2778 (betroth), H2780 (Hareph), H2741 (Haruphite), H2779 (cold), H2756 (Hariph)",
    2742: "חֲרוּץ (chărûwts | khaw-roots')\n\nDerivation: or חָרֻץ; passive participle of H2782 חָרַץ\nStrong's: properly, incised or (active) incisive; hence (as noun masculine or feminine) a trench (as dug), gold (as mined), a threshing-sledge (having sharp teeth); (figuratively) determination; also eager\nKJV: decision, diligent, (fine) gold, pointed things, sharp, threshing instrument, wall.\n\nCognate Group: H2782 (bestir self), H2757 (cheese), H2742 (decision), H2785 (kernel), H2743 (Haruz)\nGreek Equivalents: G248 ἀλοάω, G1349 δίκη, G1588 ἐκλεκτός, G4643 σκληρότης, G5038 τεῖχος, G5553 χρυσίον, G5557 χρυσός",
    2743: "חָרוּץ (Chârûwts | khaw-roots')\n\nDerivation: the same as H2742 חֲרוּץ ; earnest\nStrong's: Charuts, an Israelite\nKJV: Haruz.\n\nCognate Group: H2782 (bestir self), H2757 (cheese), H2742 (decision), H2785 (kernel), H2743 (Haruz)",
    2744: "חַרְחוּר (Charchûwr | khar-khoor')\n\nDerivation: a fuller form of H2746 חַרְחֻר ; inflammation\nStrong's: Charchur, one of the Nethinim\nKJV: Harhur.\n\nCognate Group: H2744 (Harhur), H2787 (be angry), H2788 (parched place), H2746 (extreme burning)",
    2745: "חַרְחַס (Charchaç | khar-khas')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H2775 חֶרֶס ; perhaps shining\nStrong's: Charchas, an Israelite\nKJV: Harhas.\n\nCognate Group: H2737 (chain), H2745 (Harhas), H2736 (Harhaiah)",
    2746: "חַרְחֻר (charchur | khar-khoor')\n\nDerivation: from H2787 חָרַר\nStrong's: fever (as hot)\nKJV: extreme burning.\n\nCognate Group: H2744 (Harhur), H2787 (be angry), H2788 (parched place), H2746 (extreme burning)",
    2747: "חֶרֶט (chereṭ | kheh'-ret)\n\nDerivation: from a primitive root meaning to engrave\nStrong's: a chisel or graver; also a style forwriting\nKJV: graving tool, pen.\n\nCognate Group: H2747 (graving tool), H2748 (magician)",
    2748: "חַרְטֹם (charṭôm | khar-tome')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H2747 חֶרֶט\nStrong's: a horoscopist (as drawing magical lines or circles)\nKJV: magician.\n\nCognate Group: H2747 (graving tool), H2748 (magician)\nGreek Equivalents: G4680 σοφός, G5333 φάρμακος",
    2749: "חַרְטֹם (charṭôm | khar-tome')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) the same as H2748 חַרְטֹם \nStrong's: a horoscopist (as drawing magical lines or circles)\nKJV: magician.\n\nCognate Group: H2749 (magician), H2718 (destroy)",
    2750: "חֳרִי (chŏrîy | khor-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H2734 חָרָה\nStrong's: a burning (i.e. intense) anger\nKJV: fierce, [idiom] great, heat.\n\nCognate Group: H2739 (Harumaph), H2734 (be angry), H8474 (close), H2750 (fierce), H2740 (sore displeasure)\nGreek Equivalents: G2372 θυμός, G2372 θυμός",
    2751: "חֹרִי (chôrîy | kho-ree')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H2353 חוּר\nStrong's: white bread\nKJV: white.\n\nCognate Group: H2751 (white), H2355 (network), H2353 (white), H2354 (Hur), H2357 (wax pale), H2360 (Hurai), H2437 (Hirah), H2359 (Huri)",
    2752: "חֹרִי (Chôrîy | kho-ree')\n\nDerivation: from H2356 חֹור ; cave-dweller or troglodyte\nStrong's: a Chorite or aboriginal Idumaean\nKJV: Horims, Horites.\n\nCognate Group: H2356 (cave), H2352 (hole), H2752 (Horims), H2753 (Hori)",
    2753: "חֹרִי (Chôrîy | kho-ree')\n\nDerivation: or חֹורִי; the same as H2752 חֹרִי\nStrong's: Chori, the name of two men\nKJV: Hori.\n\nCognate Group: H2356 (cave), H2352 (hole), H2752 (Horims), H2753 (Hori)",
    2754: "חָרִיט (chârîyṭ | khaw-reet')\n\nDerivation: or חָרִט; from the same as H2747 חֶרֶט\nStrong's: properly, cut out (or hollow), i.e. (by implication) a pocket\nKJV: bag, crisping pin.\n\nCognate Group: H2754 (bag)",
    2755: "חֲרֵי־יֹונִים (chărêy-yôwnîym | khar-ay'-yo-neem')\n\nDerivation: from the plural of H2716 חֶרֶא and the plural of H3123 יֹונָה ; or perhaps rather the plural of a single word חֲרָאיֹון, probably a kind of vegetable\nStrong's: excrements of doves or a vegetable\nKJV: doves' dung.\n\nCognate Group: H1681 (defaming), H1677 (bear), H1680 (cause to speak), H2755 (doves' dung), H1686 (dove's dung)",
    2756: "חָרִיף (Chârîyph | khaw-reef')\n\nDerivation: from H2778 חָרַף ; autumnal\nStrong's: Chariph, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Hariph.\n\nCognate Group: H2778 (betroth), H2780 (Hareph), H2741 (Haruphite), H2779 (cold), H2756 (Hariph)",
    2757: "חָרִיץ (chârîyts | khaw-reets')\n\nDerivation: or חֲרִץ; from H2782 חָרַץ ; (compare H2742 חֲרוּץ)\n\nStrong's: properly, incisure or (passively) incised; hence, a threshing-sledge (with sharp teeth); also a slice (as cut)\nKJV: [phrase] cheese, harrow.\n\nCognate Group: H2782 (bestir self), H2757 (cheese), H2742 (decision), H2785 (kernel), H2743 (Haruz)\nGreek Equivalents: G5146 τρίβολος",
    2758: "חָרִישׁ (chârîysh | khaw-reesh')\n\nDerivation: from H2790 חָרַשׁ\nStrong's: ploughing or its season\nKJV: earing (time), ground.\n\nCognate Group: H2794 (artificer), H4282 (share), H2798 (Charashim), H2799 (carving), H4281 (mattock), H2758 (earing), H2796 (artificer), H2790 ([idiom] altogether)\nGreek Equivalents: G2326 θερισμός, G4703 σπόρος",
    2759: "חֲרִישִׁי (chărîyshîy | khar-ee-shee')\n\nDerivation: from H2790 חָרַשׁ in the sense of silence\nStrong's: quiet, i.e. sultry (as feminine noun, the sirocco or hot east wind)\nKJV: vehement.\n\nCognate Group: H2792 (Heresh), H2759 (vehement), H2791 (cunning), H2797 (Harsha), H2800 (Harosheth)",
    2760: "חָרַךְ (chârak | khaw-rak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to braid (i.e. to entangle or snare) or catch (game) in anet\nKJV: roast.\n\nCognate Group: H2760 (roast)\nGreek Equivalents: G2013 ἐπιτυγχάνω, G2618 κατακαίω, G5394 φλογίζω",
    2761: "חֲרַךְ (chărak | khar-ak')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) a root probably allied to the equivalent of H2787 חָרַר\nStrong's: to scorch\nKJV: singe.\n\nCognate Group: H2783 (loin), H2761 (singe)",
    2762: "חֶרֶךְ (cherek | kheh'-rek)\n\nDerivation: from H2760 חָרַךְ\nStrong's: properly, a net, i.e. (by analogy) lattice\nKJV: lattice.\n\nCognate Group: H2762 (lattice)\nGreek Equivalents: G1350 δίκτυον",
    2763: "חָרַם (châram | khaw-ram')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to seclude; specifically (by a ban) to devote to religious uses (especially destruction); physical and reflexive, to be blunt as to the nose\nKJV: make accursed, consecrate, (utterly) destroy, devote, forfeit, have a flat nose, utterly (slay, make away).\n\nCognate Group: H2765 (Horem), H2768 (Hermon), H2769 (the Hermonites), H2766 (Harim), H2763 (make accursed), H2764 (curse), H2767 (Hormah)\nGreek Equivalents: G332 ἀναθεματίζω, G337 ἀναιρέω, G394 ἀνατίθεμαι, G615 ἀποκτείνω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G853 ἀφανίζω, G854 ἀφανισμός, G1760 ἐνθυμέομαι, G1842 ἐξολοθρεύω, G2049 ἐρημόω, G3645 ὀλοθρεύω, G5407 φονεύω",
    2764: "חֵרֶם (chêrem | khay'-rem)\n\nDerivation: or (Zechariah 14:11) חֶרֶם; from H2763 חָרַם\nStrong's: physical (as shutting in) a net (either literally or figuratively); usually a doomed object; abstractly extermination\nKJV: (ac-) curse(-d, -d thing), dedicated thing, things which should have been utterly destroyed, (appointed to) utter destruction, devoted (thing), net.\n\nCognate Group: H2765 (Horem), H2768 (Hermon), H2769 (the Hermonites), H2766 (Harim), H2763 (make accursed), H2764 (curse), H2767 (Hormah)\nGreek Equivalents: G44 ἄγκιστρον, G293 ἀμφίβληστρον, G331 ἀνάθεμα, G684 ἀπώλεια, G873 ἀφορίζω, G3639 ὄλεθρος, G4522 σαγήνη",
    2765: "חֳרֵם (Chŏrêm | khor-ame')\n\nDerivation: from H2763 חָרַם ; devoted\nStrong's: Chorem, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Horem.\n\nCognate Group: H2765 (Horem), H2768 (Hermon), H2769 (the Hermonites), H2766 (Harim), H2763 (make accursed), H2764 (curse), H2767 (Hormah)",
    2766: "חָרִם (Chârim | khaw-reem')\n\nDerivation: from H2763 חָרַם ; snub-nosed\nStrong's: Charim, an Israelite\nKJV: Harim.\n\nCognate Group: H2765 (Horem), H2768 (Hermon), H2769 (the Hermonites), H2766 (Harim), H2763 (make accursed), H2764 (curse), H2767 (Hormah)",
    2767: "חׇרְמָה (Chormâh | khor-maw')\n\nDerivation: from H2763 חָרַם ; devoted\nStrong's: Chormah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Hormah.\n\nCognate Group: H2765 (Horem), H2768 (Hermon), H2769 (the Hermonites), H2766 (Harim), H2763 (make accursed), H2764 (curse), H2767 (Hormah)",
    2768: "חֶרְמֹון (Chermôwn | kher-mone')\n\nDerivation: from H2763 חָרַם ; abrupt\nStrong's: Chermon, a mount of Palestine\nKJV: Hermon.\n\nCognate Group: H2765 (Horem), H2768 (Hermon), H2769 (the Hermonites), H2766 (Harim), H2763 (make accursed), H2764 (curse), H2767 (Hormah)",
    2769: "חֶרְמֹונִים (Chermôwnîym | kher-mo-neem')\n\nDerivation: plural of H2768 חֶרְמֹון\nStrong's: Hermons, i.e. its peaks\nKJV: the Hermonites.\n\nCognate Group: H2765 (Horem), H2768 (Hermon), H2769 (the Hermonites), H2766 (Harim), H2763 (make accursed), H2764 (curse), H2767 (Hormah)",
    2770: "חֶרְמֵשׁ (chermêsh | kher-mashe')\n\nDerivation: from H2763 חָרַם\nStrong's: a sickle (as cutting)\nKJV: sickle.\n\nCognate Group: H2773 (Horonaim), H2771 (Haran), H2763 (make accursed), H2770 (sickle), H2764 (curse), H2774 (Harnepher)\nGreek Equivalents: G1407 δρέπανον",
    2771: "חָרָן (Chârân | kaw-rawn')\n\nDerivation: from H2787 חָרַר ; parched\nStrong's: Charan, the name of a man and also of a place\nKJV: Haran.\n\nCognate Group: H2773 (Horonaim), H2771 (Haran), H2763 (make accursed), H2770 (sickle), H2764 (curse), H2774 (Harnepher)\nGreek Equivalents: G5488 Χαῤῥάν",
    2772: "חֹרֹנִי (Chôrônîy | kho-ro-nee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H2773 חֹרֹנַיִם\nStrong's: a Choronite or inhabitant of Choronaim\nKJV: Horonite.\n\nCognate Group: H1039 (Beth-Nimrah), H1055 (palace), H1004 (court), H1041 (Bethaz-maveth), H1054 (Beth-tappuah), H1053 (Beth-shemesh), H1052 (Beth-shean), H1048 (Beth-pazzez), H1024 (Bethmarcaboth), H1051 (Beth-rapha), H1012 (Beth-barah), H1194 (Beon), H1044 (shearing house), H1038 (Beth-maachah), H1040 (Beth-eden), H1050 (Beth-rehob), H358 (Elon-bethhanan), H1010 (Beth-baal-meon), H1046 (Beth-palet), H6407 (Paltite), H1033 (Beth-car), H1056 (Baca), H1016 (Beth-dagon), H1027 (Beth-aram), H1022 (Bethlehemite), H7462 ([idiom] break), H1008 (Beth-el), H1025 (Beth-emek), H1006 (Bajith), H1035 (Bethlehem), H2772 (Horonite), H1017 (Bethelite), H1031 (Beth-hoglah), H1013 (Beth-gader), H1023 (place that was far off), H1014 (Beth-gamul), H1032 (Beth-horon), H1057 (mulberry tree), H1028 (Beth-haran), H1049 (Beth-zur), H1026 (Beth-arabah), H1015 (Beth-diblathaim), H1034 (Beth-lebaoth), H1029 (Beth-shittah), H1030 (Bethshemite), H1011 (Bethbirei), H1043 (Beth-anath), H1042 (Beth-anoth), H6164 (Arbahite), H1047 (Bethpeor), H1020 (Beth-jeshimoth), H1036 (house of Aphrah), H1021 (Beth-haccerem), H1009 (Beth-Arbel), H1007 (Beth-aven)",
    2773: "חֹרֹנַיִם (Chôrônayim | kho-ro-nah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: dual of a derivative from H2356 חֹור ; double cave-town\nStrong's: Choronajim, a place in Moab\nKJV: Horonaim.\n\nCognate Group: H2773 (Horonaim), H2771 (Haran), H2763 (make accursed), H2770 (sickle), H2764 (curse), H2774 (Harnepher)",
    2774: "חַרְנֶפֶר (Charnepher | khar-neh'fer)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Charnepher, an Israelite\nKJV: Harnepher.\n\nCognate Group: H2773 (Horonaim), H2771 (Haran), H2763 (make accursed), H2770 (sickle), H2764 (curse), H2774 (Harnepher)",
    2775: "חֶרֶס (chereç | kheh'-res)\n\nDerivation: or (with a directive enclitic) חַרְסָה; from an unused root meaning to scrape; also perhaps from the mediating idea of H2777 חַרְסוּת \nStrong's: the itch; the sun\nKJV: itch, sun.\n\nCognate Group: H2776 (Heres), H2775 (itch)",
    2776: "חֶרֶס (Chereç | kheh'-res)\n\nDerivation: the same as H2775 חֶרֶס ; shining\nStrong's: Cheres, a mountain in Palestine\nKJV: Heres.\n\nCognate Group: H2776 (Heres), H2775 (itch)",
    2777: "חַרְסוּת (charçûwth | khar-sooth')\n\nDerivation: from H2775 חֶרֶס (apparently in the sense of a red tile used for scraping)\nStrong's: a potsherd, i.e. (by implication) a pottery; the name of a gate at Jerusalem\nKJV: east.\n\nCognate Group: H2789 (earth), H2775 (itch), H2777 (east)",
    2778: "חָרַף (châraph | khaw-raf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; also denominative (from H2779 חֹרֶף)\n\nStrong's: to pull off, i.e. (by implication) to expose (as by stripping); specifically, to betroth (as if a surrender); figuratively, to carp at, i.e. defame; to spend the winter\nKJV: betroth, blaspheme, defy, jeopard, rail, reproach, upbraid.\n\nCognate Group: H2778 (betroth), H2781 (rebuke)\nGreek Equivalents: G824 ἄτοπος, G1314 διαφυλάσσω, G2240 ἥκω, G3679 ὀνειδίζω, G3681 ὄνειδος, G3947 παροξύνω",
    2779: "חֹרֶף (chôreph | kho'-ref)\n\nDerivation: from H2778 חָרַף\nStrong's: properly, the crop gathered, i.e. (by implication) the autumn (and winter) season; figuratively, ripeness of age\nKJV: cold, winter (-house), youth.\n\nCognate Group: H2778 (betroth), H2780 (Hareph), H2741 (Haruphite), H2779 (cold), H2756 (Hariph)",
    2780: "חָרֵף (Chârêph | khaw-rafe')\n\nDerivation: from H2778 חָרַף ; reproachful\nStrong's: Chareph, an Israelite\nKJV: Hareph.\n\nCognate Group: H2778 (betroth), H2780 (Hareph), H2741 (Haruphite), H2779 (cold), H2756 (Hariph)",
    2781: "חֶרְפָּה (cherpâh | kher-paw')\n\nDerivation: from H2778 חָרַף\nStrong's: contumely, disgrace, the pudenda\nKJV: rebuke, reproach(-fully), shame.\n\nCognate Group: H2778 (betroth), H2781 (rebuke)\nGreek Equivalents: G152 αἰσχύνη, G1290 διασπορά, G3680 ὀνειδισμός, G3681 ὄνειδος",
    2782: "חָרַץ (chârats | khaw-rats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to point sharply, i.e. (literally) to wound; figuratively, to be alert, to decide\nKJV: bestir self, decide, decree, determine, maim, move.\n\nCognate Group: H2782 (bestir self), H2757 (cheese), H2742 (decision), H2785 (kernel), H2743 (Haruz)\nGreek Equivalents: G2597 καταβαίνω, G4932 συντέμνω",
    2783: "חֲרַץ (chărats | khar-ats')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2782 חָרַץ in the sense of vigor\nStrong's: the loin (as the seat of strength)\nKJV: loin.\n\nCognate Group: H2783 (loin), H2761 (singe)\nGreek Equivalents: G3751 ὀσφῦς",
