    2977: "יֹאשִׁיָּה (Yôʼshîyâh | yo-shee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or יֹאשִׁיָּהוּ; from the same root as H803 אֲשׁוּיָה and H3050 יָהּ ; founded of Jah\nStrong's: Joshijah, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Josiah.\n\nCognate Group: H2977 (Josiah), H810 (stone), H805 (Asshurim), H807 (Ashima), H804 (Asshur), H803 (foundation), H812 (Eshcol), H811 (cluster), H813 (Ashkenaz)\nGreek Equivalents: G2502 Ἰωσίας",
    2978: "יְאִתֹון (yᵉʼithôwn | yeh-ee-thone')\n\nDerivation: from H857 אָתָה\nStrong's: an entry\nKJV: entrance.\n\nCognate Group: H857 (come), H2978 (entrance), H864 (Etham)",
    2979: "יְאָתְרַי (yᵉʼâthᵉray | yeh-aw-ther-ah'ee)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H871 אֲתָרִים ; stepping\nStrong's: Jeatherai, an Israelite\nKJV: Jeaterai.\n\nCognate Group: H2979 (Jeaterai), H2976 (despair)",
    2980: "יָבַב (yâbab | yaw-bab)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to bawl\nKJV: cry out.\n\nCognate Group: H3103 (Jobab), H2980 (cry out)\nGreek Equivalents: G2648 καταμανθάνω",
    2981: "יְבוּל (yᵉbûwl | yeb-ool')\n\nDerivation: from H2986 יָבַל\nStrong's: produce, i.e. a crop or (figuratively) wealth\nKJV: fruit, increase.\n\nCognate Group: H2986 (bring), H2991 (Ibleam), H3106 (Jubal), H3105 (river), H2989 (Jabal), H944 (food), H2988 (course), H180 (river), H2990 (wen), H8398 (habitable part), H3104 (jubile), H2981 (fruit)\nGreek Equivalents: G1080 γεννάω, G2479 ἰσχύς, G2590 καρπός, G4703 σπόρος",
    2982: "יְבוּס (Yᵉbûwç | yeb-oos')\n\nDerivation: from H947 בּוּס ; trodden, i.e. threshing-place\nStrong's: Jebus, the original name of Jerusalem\nKJV: Jebus.\n\nCognate Group: H8395 (destruction), H947 (loath), H4001 (treading down), H2983 (Jebusite), H2982 (Jebus)",
