    2995: "יַבְנְאֵל (Yabnᵉʼêl | yab-neh-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H1129 בָּנָה and H410 אֵל ; built of God\nStrong's: Jabneel, the name of two places in Palestine\nKJV: Jabneel.\n\nCognate Group: H1131 (Binnui), H1137 (Bani), H1138 (Bunni), H4012 (Mebunnai), H8403 (figure), H1129 (build), H1146 (building), H2998 (Ibnijah), H2996 (Jabneh), H1141 (Benaiah), H1140 (building), H4011 (frame), H2997 (Ibneiah), H2995 (Jabneel)",
    2996: "יַבְנֶה (Yabneh | yab-neh')\n\nDerivation: from H1129 בָּנָה ; a building\nStrong's: Jabneh, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Jabneh.\n\nCognate Group: H1131 (Binnui), H1137 (Bani), H1138 (Bunni), H4012 (Mebunnai), H8403 (figure), H1129 (build), H1146 (building), H2998 (Ibnijah), H2996 (Jabneh), H1141 (Benaiah), H1140 (building), H4011 (frame), H2997 (Ibneiah), H2995 (Jabneel)",
    2997: "יִבְנְיָה (Yibnᵉyâh | yib-neh-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H1129 בָּנָה and H3050 יָהּ ; built of Jah\nStrong's: Jibnejah, an Israelite\nKJV: Ibneiah.\n\nCognate Group: H1131 (Binnui), H1137 (Bani), H1138 (Bunni), H4012 (Mebunnai), H8403 (figure), H1129 (build), H1146 (building), H2998 (Ibnijah), H2996 (Jabneh), H1141 (Benaiah), H1140 (building), H4011 (frame), H2997 (Ibneiah), H2995 (Jabneel)",
    2998: "יִבְנִיָּה (Yibnîyâh | yib-nee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H1129 בָּנָה and H3050 יָהּ ; building of Jah\nStrong's: Jibnijah, an Israelite\nKJV: Ibnijah.\n\nCognate Group: H1131 (Binnui), H1137 (Bani), H1138 (Bunni), H4012 (Mebunnai), H8403 (figure), H1129 (build), H1146 (building), H2998 (Ibnijah), H2996 (Jabneh), H1141 (Benaiah), H1140 (building), H4011 (frame), H2997 (Ibneiah), H2995 (Jabneel)",
    2999: "יַבֹּק (Yabbôq | yab-boke')\n\nDerivation: probably from H1238 בָּקַק ; pouring forth\nStrong's: Jabbok, a river east of the Jordan\nKJV: Jabbok.\n\nCognate Group: H1238 (empty), H1229 (Bakbukiah), H1228 (bottle), H1227 (Bakbuk), H2999 (Jabbok)",
    3000: "יְבֶרֶכְיָהוּ (Yᵉberekyâhûw | yeb-eh-rek-yaw'-hoo)\n\nDerivation: from H1288 בָרַךְ and H3050 יָהּ ; blessed of Jah\nStrong's: Jeberekjah, an Israelite\nKJV: Jeberechiah.\n\nCognate Group: H1294 (Berachah), H1292 (Barachel), H1263 (Baruch), H3000 (Jeberechiah), H1293 (blessing), H1296 (Berachiah), H1295 (pool), H1288 ([idiom] abundantly), H1290 (knee)",
    3001: "יָבֵשׁ (yâbêsh | yaw-bashe')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be ashamed, confused or disappointed; also (as failing) to dry up (as water) or wither (as herbage)\nKJV: be ashamed, clean, be confounded, (make) dry (up), (do) shame(-fully), [idiom] utterly, wither (away).\n\nCognate Group: H3006 (dry land), H3001 (be ashamed), H3002 (dried), H3004 (dry), H3003 (Jobesh)\nGreek Equivalents: G1808 ἐξαίρω, G3133 μαραίνω, G3583 ξηραίνω",
