    3102: "יֹוב (Yôwb | yobe)\n\nDerivation: perhaps a form of H3103 יֹובָב, but more probably by erroneous transcription for H3437 יָשׁוּב\nStrong's: Job, an Israelite\nKJV: Job.\n\nCognate Group: H3093 (haughty), H3102 (Job), H3109 (Joha)",
    3103: "יֹובָב (Yôwbâb | yo-bawb')\n\nDerivation: from H2980 יָבַב ; howler\nStrong's: Jobab, the name of two Israelites and of three foreigners\nKJV: Jobab.\n\nCognate Group: H3103 (Jobab), H2980 (cry out)",
    3104: "יֹובֵל (yôwbêl | yo-bale')\n\nDerivation: or יֹבֵל; apparently from H2986 יָבַל\nStrong's: the blast of a horn (from its continuous sound); specifically, the signal of the silver trumpets; hence, the instrument itself and the festival thus introduced\nKJV: jubile, ram's horn, trumpet.\n\nCognate Group: H2986 (bring), H2991 (Ibleam), H3106 (Jubal), H3105 (river), H2989 (Jabal), H944 (food), H2988 (course), H180 (river), H2990 (wen), H8398 (habitable part), H3104 (jubile), H2981 (fruit)\nGreek Equivalents: G859 ἄφεσις, G2413 ἱερός, G4536 σάλπιγξ",
