    3116: "יוּכַל (Yûwkal | yoo-kal')\n\nDerivation: a form of H3081 יְהוּכַל\nStrong's: Jukal, an Israelite\nKJV: Jucal.\n\nCognate Group: H3059 (Jehoahaz), H3050 (Jah), H3060 (Jehoash), H3100 (Joel), H3098 (Joah), H1942 (calamity), H3141 (Joram), H3135 (Joash), H3086 (Jehoaddan), H3089 (Jehosheba), H3078 (Jehoiachin), H3133 (Joed), H3122 (Jonadab), H3107 (Josabad), H3099 (Jehoahaz), H3110 (Johanan), H3113 (Joiakim), H3077 (Jehoiada), H3091 (Jehoshua), H3115 (Jochebed), H3097 (Joab), H1953 (Hoshama), H3068 (Jehovah), H3090 (Jehoshabeath), H3058 (Jehu), H3088 (Jehoram), H3108 (Jozachar), H1933 (be), H3087 (Jehozadek), H3129 (Jonathan), H3080 (Jehoiarib), H3079 (Jehoiakim), H3114 (Joiarib), H3134 (Joezer), H3085 (Jehoada), H1944 (Hoham), H3101 (Joash), H3083 (Jonathan), H3111 (Jehoiada), H3076 (Jehohanan), H3137 (Jokim), H3116 (Jucal), H1943 (mischief), H3082 (Jehonadab), H1962 (calamity), H3146 (Joshaphat), H3092 (Jehoshaphat), H3112 (Jehoiachin), H3136 (Jozadak), H3147 (Jotham), H3069 (God), H3075 (Jehozabad), H3081 (Jehucal), H3442 (Jeshua), H3659 (Coniah)",
    3117: "יֹום (yôwm | yome)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be hot\nStrong's: a day (as the warm hours), whether literal (from sunrise to sunset, or from one sunset to the next), or figurative (a space of time defined by an associated term), (often used adverb)\nKJV: age, [phrase] always, [phrase] chronicals, continually(-ance), daily, ((birth-), each, to) day, (now a, two) days (agone), [phrase] elder, [idiom] end, [phrase] evening, [phrase] (for) ever(-lasting, -more), [idiom] full, life, as (so) long as (... live), (even) now, [phrase] old, [phrase] outlived, [phrase] perpetually, presently, [phrase] remaineth, [idiom] required, season, [idiom] since, space, then, (process of) time, [phrase] as at other times, [phrase] in trouble, weather, (as) when, (a, the, within a) while (that), [idiom] whole ([phrase] age), (full) year(-ly), [phrase] younger.\n\nCognate Group: H3117 (age), H3119 (daily)\nGreek Equivalents: G746 ἀρχή, G979 βίος, G1074 γενεά, G1538 ἕκαστος, G2094 ἔτος, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G2222 ζωή, G2250 ἡμέρα, G2250 ἡμέρα, G2250 ἡμέρα, G2250 ἡμέρα, G2520 καθήκω, G2540 καιρός, G3568 νῦν, G3598 ὁδός, G4594 σήμερον, G5550 χρόνος",
    3118: "יֹום (yôwm | yome)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3117 יֹום\nStrong's: a day\nKJV: day (by day), time.\n\nCognate Group: H3062 (Jew), H3118 (day), H3061 (Jewry), H3052 (deliver), H3136 (Jozadak)",
    3119: "יֹומָם (yôwmâm | yo-mawm')\n\nDerivation: from H3117 יֹום\nStrong's: daily\nKJV: daily, (by, in the) day(-time).\n\nCognate Group: H3117 (age), H3119 (daily)\nGreek Equivalents: G2250 ἡμέρα",
    3120: "יָוָן (Yâvân | yaw-vawn')\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as H3196 יַיִן ; effervescing (i.e. hot and active)\nStrong's: Javan, the name of a son of Joktan, and of the race (Ionians, i.e. Greeks) descended from him, with their territory; also of a place in Arabia\nKJV: Javan.\n\nCognate Group: H3123 (dove), H3128 (Jonath-elem-rechokim), H3124 (Jonah), H3120 (Javan), H3125 (Grecian)",
    3121: "יָוֵן (yâvên | yaw-ven')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3196 יַיִן\nStrong's: properly, dregs (as effervescing); hence, mud\nKJV: mire, miry.\n\nCognate Group: H3121 (mire)\nGreek Equivalents: G5208 ὕλη",
    3122: "יֹונָדָב (Yôwnâdâb | yo-naw-dawb')\n\nDerivation: a form of H3082 יְהֹונָדָב\nStrong's: Jonadab, the name of an Israelite and of a Rechabite\nKJV: Jonadab.\n\nCognate Group: H3059 (Jehoahaz), H3050 (Jah), H3060 (Jehoash), H3100 (Joel), H3098 (Joah), H1942 (calamity), H3141 (Joram), H3135 (Joash), H3086 (Jehoaddan), H3089 (Jehosheba), H3078 (Jehoiachin), H3133 (Joed), H3122 (Jonadab), H3107 (Josabad), H3099 (Jehoahaz), H3110 (Johanan), H3113 (Joiakim), H3077 (Jehoiada), H3091 (Jehoshua), H3115 (Jochebed), H3097 (Joab), H1953 (Hoshama), H3068 (Jehovah), H3090 (Jehoshabeath), H3058 (Jehu), H3088 (Jehoram), H3108 (Jozachar), H1933 (be), H3087 (Jehozadek), H3129 (Jonathan), H3080 (Jehoiarib), H3079 (Jehoiakim), H3114 (Joiarib), H3134 (Joezer), H3085 (Jehoada), H1944 (Hoham), H3101 (Joash), H3083 (Jonathan), H3111 (Jehoiada), H3076 (Jehohanan), H3137 (Jokim), H3116 (Jucal), H1943 (mischief), H3082 (Jehonadab), H1962 (calamity), H3146 (Joshaphat), H3092 (Jehoshaphat), H3112 (Jehoiachin), H3136 (Jozadak), H3147 (Jotham), H3069 (God), H3075 (Jehozabad), H3081 (Jehucal), H3442 (Jeshua), H3659 (Coniah)",
    3123: "יֹונָה (yôwnâh | yo-naw')\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as H3196 יַיִן\nStrong's: a dove (apparently from the warmth of their mating)\nKJV: dove, pigeon.\n\nCognate Group: H3123 (dove), H3128 (Jonath-elem-rechokim), H3124 (Jonah), H3120 (Javan), H3125 (Grecian)\nGreek Equivalents: G4058 περιστερά",
    3124: "יֹונָה (Yôwnâh | yo-naw')\n\nTypo: xlit Yônâh corrected to Yôwnâh\n\nGreek Equivalents: G2495 Ἰωνᾶς, G920 Βαριωνᾶς \n\nDerivation: the same as H3123 יֹונָה\nStrong's: Jonah, an Israelite\nKJV: Jonah.\n\nCognate Group: H3123 (dove), H3128 (Jonath-elem-rechokim), H3124 (Jonah), H3120 (Javan), H3125 (Grecian)",
    3125: "יְוָנִי (Yᵉvânîy | yev-aw-nee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H3121 יָוֵן\nStrong's: a Jevanite, or descendant of Javan\nKJV: Grecian.\n\nCognate Group: H3123 (dove), H3128 (Jonath-elem-rechokim), H3124 (Jonah), H3120 (Javan), H3125 (Grecian)",
    3126: "יֹונֵק (yôwnêq | yo-nake')\n\nDerivation: active participle of H3243 יָנַק\nStrong's: a sucker; hence, a twig (of a tree felled and sprouting)\nKJV: tender plant.\n\nCognate Group: H3126 (tender plant), H3243 (milch), H3127 (branch), H3242 (young twig)\nGreek Equivalents: G3813 παιδίον, G3813 παιδίον",
    3127: "יֹונֶקֶת (yôwneqeth | yo-neh'-keth)\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3126 יֹונֵק\nStrong's: a sprout\nKJV: (tender) branch, young twig.\n\nCognate Group: H3126 (tender plant), H3243 (milch), H3127 (branch), H3242 (young twig)\nGreek Equivalents: G2798 κλάδος",
