    3209: "יִלֹּוד (yillôwd | yil-lode')\n\nDerivation: passive from H3205 יָלַד\nStrong's: born\nKJV: born.\n\nCognate Group: H3206 (boy), H3205 (bear), H2056 (child), H8434 (Tolad), H4138 (begotten), H4137 (Moladah), H3209 (born), H3208 (childhood), H3207 (damsel), H4140 (Molid), H3211 (born), H8435 (birth), H3210 (Jalon)",
    3210: "יָלֹון (Yâlôwn | yaw-lone')\n\nDerivation: from H3885 לוּן ; lodging\nStrong's: Jalon, an Israelite\nKJV: Jalon.\n\nCognate Group: H3206 (boy), H3205 (bear), H2056 (child), H8434 (Tolad), H4138 (begotten), H4137 (Moladah), H3209 (born), H3208 (childhood), H3207 (damsel), H4140 (Molid), H3211 (born), H8435 (birth), H3210 (Jalon)",
    3211: "יָלִיד (yâlîyd | yaw-leed')\n\nDerivation: from H3205 יָלַד\nStrong's: born\nKJV: (home-) born, child, son.\n\nCognate Group: H3206 (boy), H3205 (bear), H2056 (child), H8434 (Tolad), H4138 (begotten), H4137 (Moladah), H3209 (born), H3208 (childhood), H3207 (damsel), H4140 (Molid), H3211 (born), H8435 (birth), H3210 (Jalon)\nGreek Equivalents: G1074 γενεά, G1549 ἔκγονον",
    3212: "יָלַךְ (yâlak | yaw-lak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H1980 הָלַךְ)\nStrong's: to walk (literally or figuratively); causatively, to carry (in various senses)\nKJV: [idiom] again, away, bear, bring, carry (away), come (away), depart, flow, [phrase] follow(-ing), get (away, hence, him), (cause to, made) go (away, -ing, -ne, one's way, out), grow, lead (forth), let down, march, prosper, [phrase] pursue, cause to run, spread, take away (-journey), vanish, (cause to) walk(-ing), wax, [idiom] be weak.\n\nCognate Group: H1982 ([idiom] dropped), H4109 (journey), H3212 ([idiom] again), H1980 (along), H8418 ([idiom] went), H1978 (step), H4108 (place to walk), H1979 (company)\nGreek Equivalents: G1096 γίνομαι, G1204 δεῦρο, G1204 δεῦρο, G1205 δεῦτε",
    3213: "יָלַל (yâlal | yaw-lal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to howl (with a wailing tone) or yell (with a boisterous one)\nKJV: (make to) howl, be howling.\n\nCognate Group: H3213 (howl), H3215 (a howling), H3214 (howling)\nGreek Equivalents: G214 ἀλαλάζω, G2354 θρηνέω, G3649 ὀλολύζω",
    3214: "יְלֵל (yᵉlêl | yel-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H3213 יָלַל\nStrong's: a howl\nKJV: howling.\n\nCognate Group: H3213 (howl), H3215 (a howling), H3214 (howling)\nGreek Equivalents: G2738 καῦμα",
    3215: "יְלָלָה (yᵉlâlâh | yel-aw-law')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3214 יְלֵל \nStrong's: a howl\nKJV: a howling.\n\nCognate Group: H3213 (howl), H3215 (a howling), H3214 (howling)",
    3216: "יָלַע (yâlaʻ | yaw-lah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to blurt or utter inconsiderately\nKJV: devour.\n\nCognate Group: H3216 (devour), H3886 (swallow down)",
    3217: "יַלֶּפֶת (yallepheth | yal-leh'-feth)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root apparently meaning to stick or scrape\nStrong's: scurf or tetter\nKJV: scabbed.\n\nCognate Group: H3217 (scabbed)",
    3218: "יֶלֶק (yeleq | yeh'-lek)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to lick up\nStrong's: a devourer; specifically, the young locust\nKJV: cankerworm, caterpillar.\n\nCognate Group: H3224 (Jemimah), H3218 (cankerworm), H3223 (Jemuel)\nGreek Equivalents: G200 ἀκρίς",
    3219: "יַלְקוּט (yalqûwṭ | yal-koot')\n\nDerivation: from H3950 לָקַט\nStrong's: a travelling pouch (as if for gleanings)\nKJV: scrip.\n\nCognate Group: H3219 (scrip), H3950 (gather), H3951 (gleaning)",
    3220: "יָם (yâm | yawm)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to roar\nStrong's: a sea (as breaking in noisy surf) or large body of water; specifically (with the article), the Mediterranean Sea; sometimes a large river, or an artifical basin; locally, the west, or (rarely) the south\nKJV: sea ([idiom] -faring man, (-shore)), south, west (-ern, side, -ward).\n\nCognate Group: H3222 (mule), H3220 (sea)\nGreek Equivalents: G1424 δυσμή, G2281 θάλασσα, G3882 παράλιος",
    3221: "יָם (yâm | yawm)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3220 יָם \nStrong's: a sea (as breaking in noisy surf) or large body of water; specifically (with the article), the Mediterranean Sea; sometimes a large river, or an artifical basin; locally, the west, or (rarely) the south\nKJV: sea.\n\nCognate Group: H3202 (be able), H3221 (sea)",
    3222: "יֵם (yêm | yame)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3117 יֹום\nStrong's: a warm spring\nKJV: mule.\n\nCognate Group: H3222 (mule), H3220 (sea)\nGreek Equivalents: G1695 Ἐμμαούς",
    3223: "יְמוּאֵל (Yᵉmûwʼêl | yem-oo-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H3117 יֹום and H410 אֵל ; day of God\nStrong's: Jemuel, an Israelite\nKJV: Jemuel.\n\nCognate Group: H3224 (Jemimah), H3218 (cankerworm), H3223 (Jemuel)",
    3224: "יְמִימָה (Yᵉmîymâh | yem-ee-maw')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from the same as H3117 יֹום ; properly, warm, i.e. affectionate; hence, dove (compare H3123 יֹונָה)\nStrong's: Jemimah, one of Job's daughters\nKJV: Jemimah.\n\nCognate Group: H3224 (Jemimah), H3218 (cankerworm), H3223 (Jemuel)\nGreek Equivalents: G2250 ἡμέρα",
    3225: "יָמִין (yâmîyn | yaw-meen')\n\nDerivation: from H3231 יָמַן\nStrong's: the right hand or side (leg, eye) of a person or other object (as the stronger and more dexterous); locally, the south\nKJV: [phrase] left-handed, right (hand, side), south.\n\nCognate Group: H8486 (south), H3231 (go to the right hand), H3227 (right), H8488 (Temeni), H3226 (Jamin), H3232 (Imna), H8487 (south), H3228 (Jaminites), H3225 (left-handed), H541 (turn to the right), H3233 (right), H8489 (Temani)\nGreek Equivalents: G1188 δεξιός, G2281 θάλασσα, G5495 χείρ",
    3226: "יָמִין (Yâmîyn | yaw-meen')\n\nDerivation: the same as H3225 יָמִין\nStrong's: Jamin, the name of three Israelites\nKJV: Jamin. See also H1144 בִּנְיָמִין .\n\nCognate Group: H8486 (south), H3231 (go to the right hand), H3227 (right), H8488 (Temeni), H3226 (Jamin), H3232 (Imna), H8487 (south), H3228 (Jaminites), H3225 (left-handed), H541 (turn to the right), H3233 (right), H8489 (Temani)",
    3227: "יְמִינִי (yᵉmîynîy | yem-ee-nee')\n\nDerivation: for H3225 יָמִין\nStrong's: right\nKJV: (on the) right (hand).\n\nCognate Group: H8486 (south), H3231 (go to the right hand), H3227 (right), H8488 (Temeni), H3226 (Jamin), H3232 (Imna), H8487 (south), H3228 (Jaminites), H3225 (left-handed), H541 (turn to the right), H3233 (right), H8489 (Temani)",
