    3231: "יָמַן (yâman | yaw-man')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; to be (physically) right (i.e. firm); but used only as denominative from H3225 יָמִין and transitive,\nStrong's: to be right-handed or take the right-hand side\nKJV: go (turn) to (on, use) the right hand.\n\nCognate Group: H8486 (south), H3231 (go to the right hand), H3227 (right), H8488 (Temeni), H3226 (Jamin), H3232 (Imna), H8487 (south), H3228 (Jaminites), H3225 (left-handed), H541 (turn to the right), H3233 (right), H8489 (Temani)",
    3232: "יִמְנָה (Yimnâh | yim-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H3231 יָמַן ; prosperity (as betokened by the right hand)\nStrong's: Jimnah, the name of two Israelites; also (with the article) of the posterity of one of them\nKJV: Imna, Imnah, Jimnah, Jimnites.\n\nCognate Group: H8486 (south), H3231 (go to the right hand), H3227 (right), H8488 (Temeni), H3226 (Jamin), H3232 (Imna), H8487 (south), H3228 (Jaminites), H3225 (left-handed), H541 (turn to the right), H3233 (right), H8489 (Temani)",
