    3238: "יָנָה (yânâh | yaw-naw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to rage or be violent; by implication, to suppress, to maltreat\nKJV: destroy, (thrust out by) oppress(-ing, -ion, -or), proud, vex, do violence.\n\nCognate Group: H3238 (destroy)\nGreek Equivalents: G3664 ὅμοιος, G3664 ὅμοιος, G2388 Ἰαννά",
    3239: "יָנֹוחַ (Yânôwach | yaw-no'-akh or (with enclitic) Yanowchah yaw-no'-khaw)\n\nDerivation: from H3240 יָנַח ; quiet\nStrong's: Janoach or Janochah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Janoah, Janohah.\n\nCognate Group: H2680 (half of the Manahethites), H5183 (lighting down), H5118 (rest), H4494 (rest), H5119 (Nohah), H5146 (Noah), H5207 (sweet), H4495 (Manoah), H3240 (bestow), H5117 (cease), H4496 (comfortable), H2010 (release), H4506 (Manahath), H2679 (half of the Manahethites), H3239 (Janoah)",
    3240: "יָנַח (yânach | yaw-nakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to deposit; by implication, to allow to stay\nKJV: bestow, cast down, lay (down, up), leave (off), let alone (remain), pacify, place, put, set (down), suffer, withdraw, withhold. (The Hiphil forms with the dagesh are here referred to, in accordance with the older grammarians; but if any distinction of the kind is to be made, these should rather be referred to H5117 נוּחַ, and the others here.)\n\nCognate Group: H2680 (half of the Manahethites), H5183 (lighting down), H5118 (rest), H4494 (rest), H5119 (Nohah), H5146 (Noah), H5207 (sweet), H4495 (Manoah), H3240 (bestow), H5117 (cease), H4496 (comfortable), H2010 (release), H4506 (Manahath), H2679 (half of the Manahethites), H3239 (Janoah)",
