    3244: "יַנְשׁוּף (yanshûwph | yan-shoof')\n\nDerivation: or יַנְשֹׁוף; apparently from H5398 נָשַׁף ; (compare H5399 נֶשֶׁף)\n\nStrong's: an unclean (acquatic) bird; probably the heron (perhaps from its blowing cry, or because the nightheron is meant))\nKJV: (great) owl.s\n\nCognate Group: H5398 (blow), H3244 (owl), H5399 (dark)",
    3245: "יָסַד (yâçad | yaw-sad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to set (literally or figuratively); intensively, to found; reflexively, to sit down together, i.e. settle, consult\nKJV: appoint, take counsel, establish, (lay the, lay for a) found(-ation), instruct, lay, ordain, set, [idiom] sure.\n\nCognate Group: H4144 (foundation), H4146 (foundation), H4328 (foundation), H3248 (foundation), H4527 (foundation), H4143 (foundation), H3245 (appoint), H3246 ([idiom] began), H4145 (foundation), H3247 (bottom)\nGreek Equivalents: G757 ἄρχω, G1685 ἐμβάλλω, G2004 ἐπιτάσσω, G2309 θέλω, G2310 θεμέλιος, G2310 θεμέλιος, G2311 θεμελιόω, G2476 ἵστημι, G2675 καταρτίζω, G2936 κτίζω, G4863 συνάγω",
