    3510: "כָּאַב (kâʼab | kaw-ab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to feel pain; by implication, to grieve; figuratively, to spoil\nKJV: grieving, mar, have pain, make sad (sore), (be) sorrowful.\n\nCognate Group: H3510 (grieving), H3511 (grief), H4341 (grief)\nGreek Equivalents: G889 ἀχρειόω, G1294 διαστρέφω, G4192 πόνος",
    3511: "כְּאֵב (kᵉʼêb | keh-abe')\n\nDerivation: from H3510 כָּאַב\nStrong's: suffering (physical or mental), adversity\nKJV: grief, pain, sorrow.\n\nCognate Group: H3510 (grieving), H3511 (grief), H4341 (grief)\nGreek Equivalents: G3076 λυπέω, G3077 λύπη, G4127 πληγή, G4192 πόνος",
    3512: "כָּאָה (kâʼâh | kaw-aw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to despond; causatively, to deject\nKJV: broken, be grieved, make sad.\n\nCognate Group: H3512 (broken)\nGreek Equivalents: G1294 διαστρέφω, G1856 ἐξωθέω, G2660 κατανύσσω, G5013 ταπεινόω",
    3513: "כָּבַד (kâbad | kaw-bad')\n\nDerivation: or כָּבֵד; a primitive root\nStrong's: to be heavy, i.e. in a bad sense (burdensome, severe, dull) or in a good sense (numerous, rich, honorable; causatively, to make weighty (in the same two senses)\nKJV: abounding with, more grievously afflict, boast, be chargeable, [idiom] be dim, glorify, be (make) glorious (things), glory, (very) great, be grievous, harden, be (make) heavy, be heavier, lay heavily, (bring to, come to, do, get, be had in) honour (self), (be) honourable (man), lade, [idiom] more be laid, make self many, nobles, prevail, promote (to honour), be rich, be (go) sore, stop.\n\nCognate Group: H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)\nGreek Equivalents: G191 ἀκούω, G916 βαρέω, G916 βαρέω, G917 βαρέως, G926 βαρύς, G1391 δόξα, G1392 δοξάζω, G1740 ἐνδοξάζω, G1741 ἔνδοξος, G1765 ἐνισχύω, G1784 ἔντιμος, G2127 εὐλογέω, G2729 κατισχύω, G3173 μέγας, G4060 περιτίθημι, G4121 πλεονάζω, G4645 σκληρύνω, G5091 τιμάω, G5092 τιμή",
    3514: "כֹּבֶד (kôbed | ko'-bed)\n\nDerivation: from H3513 כָּבַד\nStrong's: weight, multitude, vehemence\nKJV: grievousness, heavy, great number.\n\nCognate Group: H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)",
    3515: "כָּבֵד (kâbêd | kaw-bade')\n\nDerivation: from H3513 כָּבַד\nStrong's: heavy; figuratively in a good sense (numerous) or in a bad sense (severe, difficult, stupid)\nKJV: (so) great, grievous, hard(-ened), (too) heavy(-ier), laden, much, slow, sore, thick.\n\nCognate Group: H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)\nGreek Equivalents: G926 βαρύς, G2478 ἰσχυρός, G4128 πλῆθος, G4134 πλήρης, G4145 πλούσιος",
    3516: "כָּבֵד (kâbêd | kaw-bade')\n\nDerivation: the same as H3515 כָּבֵד\nStrong's: the liver (as the heaviest of the viscera)\nKJV: liver.\n\nCognate Group: H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)",
    3517: "כְּבֵדֻת (kᵉbêduth | keb-ay-dooth')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3515 כָּבֵד\nStrong's: difficulty\nKJV: [idiom] heavily.\n\nCognate Group: H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)\nGreek Equivalents: G970 βία",
    3518: "כָּבָה (kâbâh | kaw-baw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to expire or (causatively) to extinguish (fire, light, anger)\nKJV: go (put) out, quench.\n\nCognate Group: H3518 (go out), H3521 (Cabul)",
    3519: "כָּבֹוד (kâbôwd | kaw-bode')\n\nDerivation: rarely כָּבֹד; from H3513 כָּבַד\nStrong's: properly, weight, but only figuratively in a good sense, splendor or copiousness\nKJV: glorious(-ly), glory, honour(-able).\n\nCognate Group: H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)\nGreek Equivalents: G922 βάρος, G1100 γλῶσσα, G1391 δόξα, G1411 δύναμις, G2570 καλός, G4149 πλοῦτος, G4766 στρώννυμι, G5092 τιμή",
    3520: "כְּבוּדָּה (kᵉbûwddâh | keb-ood-daw')\n\nDerivation: irregular feminine passive participle of H3513 כָּבַד\nStrong's: weightiness, i.e. magnificence, wealth\nKJV: carriage, all glorious, stately.\n\nCognate Group: H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)",
    3521: "כָּבוּל (Kâbûwl | kaw-bool')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3525 כֶּבֶל in the sense of limitation; sterile\nStrong's: Cabul, the name of two places in Palestine\nKJV: Cabul.\n\nCognate Group: H3518 (go out), H3521 (Cabul)",
    3522: "כַּבֹּון (Kabbôwn | kab-bone')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to heap up; hilly\nStrong's: Cabon, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Cabbon.\n\nCognate Group: H4344 (Machbanai), H3522 (Cabbon), H4343 (Machbenah)",
    3523: "כְּבִיר (kᵉbîyr | keb-eer)\n\nDerivation: from H3527 כָּבַר in the original sense of plaiting\nStrong's: a matrass (of intertwined materials)\nKJV: pillow.\n\nCognate Group: H4346 (thick cloth), H3535 (lamb), H4345 (grate), H3523 (pillow), H3776 (lamb), H3775 (lamb), H3531 (sieve), H3532 (lamb)",
    3524: "כַּבִּיר (kabbîyr | kab-beer')\n\nDerivation: from H3527 כָּבַר\nStrong's: vast, whether in extent (figuratively, of power, mighty; of time, aged), or in number, many\nKJV: [phrase] feeble, mighty, most, much, strong, valiant.\n\nCognate Group: H3528 (already), H3527 (in abundance), H4342 (abundance), H3529 (Chebar), H3530 ([idiom] little), H3524 (feeble)\nGreek Equivalents: G926 βαρύς, G1415 δυνατός, G1741 ἔνδοξος, G1784 ἔντιμος, G4128 πλῆθος",
    3525: "כֶּבֶל (kebel | keh'-bel)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to twine or braid together\nStrong's: a fetter\nKJV: fetter.\n\nCognate Group: H3525 (fetter)\nGreek Equivalents: G3976 πέδη",
    3526: "כָּבַס (kâbaç | kaw-bas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to trample; hence, to wash (properly, by stamping with the feet), whether literal (including the fulling process) or figurative\nKJV: fuller, wash(-ing).\n\nCognate Group: H3526 (fuller)\nGreek Equivalents: G637 ἀποπλύνω, G1102 γναφεύς, G4150 πλύνω",
    3527: "כָּבַר (kâbar | kaw-bar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to plait together, i.e. (figuratively) to augment (especially in number or quantity, to accumulate)\nKJV: in abundance, multiply.\n\nCognate Group: H3528 (already), H3527 (in abundance), H4342 (abundance), H3529 (Chebar), H3530 ([idiom] little), H3524 (feeble)\nGreek Equivalents: G2480 ἰσχύω",
    3528: "כְּבָר (kᵉbâr | keb-awr')\n\nDerivation: from H3527 כָּבַר\nStrong's: properly, extent of time, i.e. a great while; hence, long ago, formerly, hitherto\nKJV: already, (seeing that which), now.\n\nCognate Group: H3528 (already), H3527 (in abundance), H4342 (abundance), H3529 (Chebar), H3530 ([idiom] little), H3524 (feeble)",
    3529: "כְּבָר (Kᵉbâr | keb-awr')\n\nDerivation: the same as H3528 כְּבָר ; length\nStrong's: Kebar, a river of Mesopotamia\nKJV: Chebar. Compare H2249 חָבֹור .\n\nCognate Group: H3528 (already), H3527 (in abundance), H4342 (abundance), H3529 (Chebar), H3530 ([idiom] little), H3524 (feeble)",
    3530: "כִּבְרָה (kibrâh | kib-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3528 כְּבָר\nStrong's: properly, length, i.e. a measure (of uncertain dimension)\nKJV: [idiom] little.\n\nCognate Group: H3528 (already), H3527 (in abundance), H4342 (abundance), H3529 (Chebar), H3530 ([idiom] little), H3524 (feeble)",
    3531: "כְּבָרָה (kᵉbârâh | keb-aw-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H3527 כָּבַר in its original sense\nStrong's: a sieve (as netted)\nKJV: sieve.\n\nCognate Group: H4346 (thick cloth), H3535 (lamb), H4345 (grate), H3523 (pillow), H3776 (lamb), H3775 (lamb), H3531 (sieve), H3532 (lamb)",
    3532: "כֶּבֶשׂ (kebes | keh-bes')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to dominate\nStrong's: a ram (just old enough to butt)\nKJV: lamb, sheep.\n\nCognate Group: H4346 (thick cloth), H3535 (lamb), H4345 (grate), H3523 (pillow), H3776 (lamb), H3775 (lamb), H3531 (sieve), H3532 (lamb)\nGreek Equivalents: G286 ἀμνός, G704 ἀρήν, G721 ἀρνίον, G4263 πρόβατον",
    3533: "כָּבַשׁ (kâbash | kaw-bash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tread down; hence, negatively, to disregard; positively, to conquer, subjugate, violate\nKJV: bring into bondage, force, keep under, subdue, bring into subjection.\n\nCognate Group: H3533 (bring into bondage), H3534 (footstool), H3536 (furnace)\nGreek Equivalents: G971 βιάζω, G2616 καταδυναστεύω, G2634 κατακυριεύω, G2901 κραταιόω, G2902 κρατέω, G5293 ὑποτάσσω",
    3534: "כֶּבֶשׁ (kebesh | keh'-besh)\n\nDerivation: from H3533 כָּבַשׁ\nStrong's: a footstool (as trodden upon)\nKJV: footstool.\n\nCognate Group: H3533 (bring into bondage), H3534 (footstool), H3536 (furnace)",
    3535: "כִּבְשָׂה (kibsâh | kib-saw')\n\nDerivation: or כַּבְשָׂה; feminine of H3532 כֶּבֶשׂ\nStrong's: a ewe\nKJV: (ewe) lamb.\n\nCognate Group: H4346 (thick cloth), H3535 (lamb), H4345 (grate), H3523 (pillow), H3776 (lamb), H3775 (lamb), H3531 (sieve), H3532 (lamb)",
    3536: "כִּבְשָׁן (kibshân | kib-shawn')\n\nDerivation: from H3533 כָּבַשׁ\nStrong's: a smelting furnace (as reducing metals)\nKJV: furnace.\n\nCognate Group: H3533 (bring into bondage), H3534 (footstool), H3536 (furnace)\nGreek Equivalents: G2575 κάμινος",
    3537: "כַּד (kad | kad)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to deepen\nStrong's: properly, a pail; but generally of earthenware; a jar for domestic purposes\nKJV: barrel, pitcher.\n\nCognate Group: H3539 (agate), H3537 (barrel), H3590 (spark)\nGreek Equivalents: G5201 ὑδρία",
    3538: "כְּדַב (kᵉdab | ked-ab')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H3576 כָּזַב\nStrong's: false\nKJV: lying.\n\nCognate Group: H3538 (lying)",
    3539: "כַּדְכֹּד (kadkôd | kad-kode')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3537 כַּד in the sense of striking fire from a metal forged\nStrong's: a sparkling gem, probably the ruby\nKJV: agate.\n\nCognate Group: H3539 (agate), H3537 (barrel), H3590 (spark)\nGreek Equivalents: G2393 ἴασπις",
    3540: "כְּדׇרְלָעֹמֶר (Kᵉdorlâʻômer | ked-or-law-o'-mer)\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Kedorlaomer, an early Persian king\nKJV: Chedorlaomer.\n\nCognate Group: H3540 (Chedorlaomer), H1754 (ball), H3593 (battle)",
    3541: "כֹּה (kôh | ko)\n\nDerivation: from the prefix k and H1931 הוּא\nStrong's: properly, like this, i.e. by implication, (of manner) thus (or so); also (of place) here (or hither); or (of time) now\nKJV: also, here, + hitherto, like, on the other side, so (and much), such, on that manner, (on) this (manner, side, way, way and that way), + mean while, yonder.\n\nCognate Group: H3541 (also), H3602 (after that manner)\nGreek Equivalents: G1782 ἐντεῦθεν, G2400 ἰδού, G3778 οὗτος, G5602 ὧδε",
    3542: "כָּה (kâh | kaw)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3541 כֹּה \nStrong's: properly, like this, i.e. by implication, (of manner) thus (or so); also (of place) here (or hither); or (of time) now\nKJV: hitherto.\n\nCognate Group: H3542 (hitherto)",
    3543: "כָּהָה (kâhâh | kaw-haw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be weak, i.e. (figuratively) to despond (causatively, rebuke), or (of light, the eye) to grow dull\nKJV: darken, be dim, fail, faint, restrain, [idiom] utterly.\n\nCognate Group: H3545 (healing), H3543 (darken), H3544 (somewhat dark)\nGreek Equivalents: G1634 ἐκψύχω, G3560 νουθετέω, G4456 πωρόω",
    3544: "כֵּהֶה (kêheh | kay-heh')\n\nDerivation: from H3543 כָּהָה\nStrong's: feeble, obscure\nKJV: somewhat dark, darkish, wax dim, heaviness, smoking.\n\nCognate Group: H3545 (healing), H3543 (darken), H3544 (somewhat dark)\nGreek Equivalents: G826 αὐγάζω",
    3545: "כֵּהָה (kêhâh | kay-haw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3544 כֵּהֶה\nStrong's: properly, a weakening; figuratively, alleviation, i.e. cure\nKJV: healing.\n\nCognate Group: H3545 (healing), H3543 (darken), H3544 (somewhat dark)\nGreek Equivalents: G2392 ἴασις",
    3546: "כְּהַל (kᵉhal | keh-hal')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) a root corresponding to and H3557 כּוּל\nStrong's: to be able\nKJV: be able, could.\n\nCognate Group: H3567 (Cyrus), H3549 (priest), H3546 (be able), H3734 (cor), H3551 (window)\nGreek Equivalents: G1410 δύναμαι",
    3547: "כָּהַן (kâhan | kaw-han')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root, apparently meaning to mediate in religious services; but used only as denominative from H3548 כֹּהֵן\nStrong's: to officiate as a priest; figuratively, to put on regalia\nKJV: deck, be (do the office of a, execute the, minister in the) priest('s office).\n\nCognate Group: H3547 (deck), H3553 (helmet), H3552 (Chub), H3548 (chief ruler), H3550 (priesthood)\nGreek Equivalents: G80 ἀδελφός, G749 ἀρχιερεύς, G2405 ἱερατεία, G2406 ἱεράτευμα, G2407 ἱερατεύω, G2409 ἱερεύς, G2420 ἱερωσύνη, G3008 λειτουργέω, G4060 περιτίθημι",
    3548: "כֹּהֵן (kôhên | ko-hane')\n\nDerivation: active participle of H3547 כָּהַן\nStrong's: literally one officiating, a priest; also (by courtesy) an acting priest (although a layman)\nKJV: chief ruler, [idiom] own, priest, prince, principal officer.\n\nCognate Group: H3547 (deck), H3553 (helmet), H3552 (Chub), H3548 (chief ruler), H3550 (priesthood)",
    3549: "כָּהֵן (kâhên | kaw-hane')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3548 כֹּהֵן \nStrong's: one officiating, a priest; also (by courtesy) an acting priest (although a layman)\nKJV: priest.\n\nCognate Group: H3567 (Cyrus), H3549 (priest), H3546 (be able), H3734 (cor), H3551 (window)\nGreek Equivalents: G2409 ἱερεύς",
    3550: "כְּהֻנָּה (kᵉhunnâh | keh-hoon-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H3547 כָּהַן\nStrong's: priesthood\nKJV: priesthood, priest's office.\n\nCognate Group: H3547 (deck), H3553 (helmet), H3552 (Chub), H3548 (chief ruler), H3550 (priesthood)\nGreek Equivalents: G2405 ἱερατεία",
    3551: "כַּו (kav | kav)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H3854 לַהַג in the sense of piercing\nStrong's: a window (as a perforation)\nKJV: window.\n\nCognate Group: H3567 (Cyrus), H3549 (priest), H3546 (be able), H3734 (cor), H3551 (window)\nGreek Equivalents: G2376 θυρίς",
    3552: "כּוּב (Kûwb | koob)\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Kub, a country near Egypt\nKJV: Chub.\n\nCognate Group: H3547 (deck), H3553 (helmet), H3552 (Chub), H3548 (chief ruler), H3550 (priesthood)",
    3553: "כֹּובַע (kôwbaʻ | ko'-bah)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be high or rounded\nStrong's: a helmet (as arched)\nKJV: helmet. Compare H6959 קֹובַע .\n\nCognate Group: H3547 (deck), H3553 (helmet), H3552 (Chub), H3548 (chief ruler), H3550 (priesthood)\nGreek Equivalents: G4030 περικεφαλαία",
    3554: "כָּוָה (kâvâh | kaw-vaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to prick or penetrate; hence, to blister (as smarting or eating into)\nKJV: burn.\n\nCognate Group: H3554 (burn), H4348 (that burneth), H3587 (burning), H3555 (burning)\nGreek Equivalents: G643 ἀποσκευάζω, G2618 κατακαίω, G4570 σβέννυμι",
    3555: "כְּוִיָּה (kᵉvîyâh | kev-ee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H3554 כָּוָה\nStrong's: a branding\nKJV: burning.\n\nCognate Group: H3554 (burn), H4348 (that burneth), H3587 (burning), H3555 (burning)",
    3556: "כֹּוכָב (kôwkâb | ko-kawb')\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as H3522 כַּבֹּון (in the sense of rolling) or H3554 כָּוָה (in the sense of blazing)\nStrong's: a star (as round or as shining); figuratively, a prince\nKJV: star(-gazer).\n\nCognate Group: H3556 (star)\nGreek Equivalents: G792 ἀστήρ, G798 ἄστρον",
    3557: "כּוּל (kûwl | kool)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to keep in; hence, to measure; figuratively, to maintain (in various senses)\nKJV: (be able to, can) abide, bear, comprehend, contain, feed, forbearing, guide, hold(-ing in), nourish(-er), be present, make provision, receive, sustain, provide sustenance (victuals).\n\nCognate Group: H3557 (abide), H3633 (Calcol)\nGreek Equivalents: G714 ἀρκέω, G1209 δέχομαι, G1410 δύναμαι, G1625 ἐκτρέφω, G2425 ἱκανός, G2720 κατευθύνω, G3621 οἰκονομέω, G4912 συνέχω, G5142 τρέφω, G5278 ὑπομένω, G5297 ὑποφέρω, G5342 φέρω, G5524 χορηγέω, G5562 χωρέω",
    3558: "כּוּמָז (kûwmâz | koo-mawz')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to store away\nStrong's: a jewel (probably gold beads)\nKJV: tablet.\n\nCognate Group: H3558 (tablet)",
    3559: "כּוּן (kûwn | koon)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to be erect (i.e. stand perpendicular); hence (causatively) to set up, in a great variety of applications, whether literal (establish, fix, prepare, apply), or figurative (appoint, render sure, proper or prosperous)\nKJV: certain(-ty), confirm, direct, faithfulness, fashion, fasten, firm, be fitted, be fixed, frame, be meet, ordain, order, perfect, (make) preparation, prepare (self), provide, make provision, (be, make) ready, right, set (aright, fast, forth), be stable, (e-) stablish, stand, tarry, [idiom] very deed.\n\nCognate Group: H3561 (cake), H8499 (seat), H3200 (Jachinites), H3559 (certain), H3651 (after that), H3560 (Chun), H8498 (fashion), H3562 (Conaniah), H4369 (base), H4349 (foundation), H4350 (base), H3199 (Jachin), H3204 (Jeconiah), H5225 (Nachon), H3563 (cup)\nGreek Equivalents: G18 ἀγαθός, G225 ἀλήθεια, G227 ἀληθής, G461 ἀνορθόω, G1011 βουλεύω, G1096 γίνομαι, G1325 δίδωμι, G1415 δυνατός, G1717 ἐμφανής, G1741 ἔνδοξος, G1991 ἐπιστηρίζω, G2090 ἑτοιμάζω, G2091 ἑτοιμασία, G2092 ἕτοιμος, G2112 εὐθέως, G2117 εὐθύς, G2192 ἔχω, G2311 θεμελιόω, G2476 ἵστημι, G2513 καθαρός, G2525 καθίστημι, G2675 καταρτίζω, G2680 κατασκευάζω, G2720 κατευθύνω, G2936 κτίζω, G3306 μένω, G3618 οἰκοδομέω, G4111 πλάσσω, G4732 στερεόω, G4878 συναντιλαμβάνομαι, G4920 συνίημι, G4921 συνιστάω, G5087 τίθημι, G5297 ὑποφέρω, G5342 φέρω",
    3560: "כּוּן (Kûwn | koon)\n\nDerivation: probably from H3559 כּוּן ; established\nStrong's: Kun, a place in Syria\nKJV: Chun.\n\nCognate Group: H3561 (cake), H8499 (seat), H3200 (Jachinites), H3559 (certain), H3651 (after that), H3560 (Chun), H8498 (fashion), H3562 (Conaniah), H4369 (base), H4349 (foundation), H4350 (base), H3199 (Jachin), H3204 (Jeconiah), H5225 (Nachon), H3563 (cup)",
    3561: "כַּוָּן (kavvân | kav-vawn')\n\nDerivation: from H3559 כּוּן\nStrong's: something prepared, i.e. a sacrificial wafer\nKJV: cake.\n\nCognate Group: H3561 (cake), H8499 (seat), H3200 (Jachinites), H3559 (certain), H3651 (after that), H3560 (Chun), H8498 (fashion), H3562 (Conaniah), H4369 (base), H4349 (foundation), H4350 (base), H3199 (Jachin), H3204 (Jeconiah), H5225 (Nachon), H3563 (cup)",
    3562: "כֹּונַנְיָהוּ (Kôwnanyâhûw | ko-nan-yaw'-hoo)\n\nDerivation: from H3559 כּוּן and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has sustained\nStrong's: Conanjah, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Conaniah, Cononiah. Compare H3663 כְּנַנְיָה .\n\nCognate Group: H3561 (cake), H8499 (seat), H3200 (Jachinites), H3559 (certain), H3651 (after that), H3560 (Chun), H8498 (fashion), H3562 (Conaniah), H4369 (base), H4349 (foundation), H4350 (base), H3199 (Jachin), H3204 (Jeconiah), H5225 (Nachon), H3563 (cup)",
    3563: "כֹּוס (kôwç | koce)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to hold together\nStrong's: a cup (as a container), often figuratively, a lot (as if a potion); also some unclean bird, probably an owl (perhaps from the cup-like cavity of its eye)\nKJV: cup, (small) owl. Compare H3599 כִּיס .\n\nCognate Group: H3561 (cake), H8499 (seat), H3200 (Jachinites), H3559 (certain), H3651 (after that), H3560 (Chun), H8498 (fashion), H3562 (Conaniah), H4369 (base), H4349 (foundation), H4350 (base), H3199 (Jachin), H3204 (Jeconiah), H5225 (Nachon), H3563 (cup)\nGreek Equivalents: G4221 ποτήριον, G5357 φιάλη",
    3564: "כּוּר (kûwr | koor)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning properly, to dig through\nStrong's: a pot or furnace (as if excavated)\nKJV: furnace. Compare H3600 כִּיר .\n\nCognate Group: H3564 (furnace), H3600 (ranges for pots), H3595 (hearth), H3733 (captain)\nGreek Equivalents: G2575 κάμινος, G4451 πύρωσις",
    3565: "כֹּור עָשָׁן (Kôwr ʻÂshân | kore aw-shawn')\n\nDerivation: from H3564 כּוּר and H6227 עָשָׁן ; furnace of smoke\nStrong's: Cor-Ashan, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Chorashan.\n\nCognate Group: H884 (Beer-shebah), H1275 (Beri), H882 (Beeri), H883 (Beer-lahai-roi), H879 (Beer-elim), H3565 (Chorashan), H1268 (Berothah), H880 (Beerah), H875 (pit), H876 (Beer), H1307 (Berothite), H874 (declare), H878 (Beera), H886 (Beerothite), H877 (cistern), H885 (Beeroth of the children of Jaakan), H881 (Beeroth), H953 (cistern), H5626 (Sirah)",
    3566: "כֹּורֶשׁ (Kôwresh | ko'-resh)\n\nDerivation: or (Ezra 1:1 (last time),2) כֹּרֶשׁ; from the Persians\nStrong's: Koresh (or Cyrus), the Persian king\nKJV: Cyrus.\n\nCognate Group: H3566 (Cyrus), H3738 (dig), H4380 (habitation), H4351 (birth)",
    3567: "כֹּורֶשׁ (Kôwresh | ko'-resh)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3566 כֹּורֶשׁ \nStrong's: Koresh (or Cyrus), the Persian king\nKJV: Cyrus.\n\nCognate Group: H3567 (Cyrus), H3549 (priest), H3546 (be able), H3734 (cor), H3551 (window)",
    3568: "כּוּשׁ (Kûwsh | koosh)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: Cush (or Ethiopia), the name of a son of Ham, and of his territory; also of an Israelite\nKJV: Chush, Cush, Ethiopia.\n\nCognate Group: H3573 (Chushan-rishathayim), H3569 (Cushi), H3570 (Cushi), H3575 (Cuth), H3568 (Chush), H3571 (Ethiopian), H3572 (Cushan)",
    3569: "כּוּשִׁי (Kûwshîy | koo-shee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H3568 כּוּשׁ\nStrong's: a Cushite, or descendant of Cush\nKJV: Cushi, Cushite, Ethiopian(-s).\n\nCognate Group: H3573 (Chushan-rishathayim), H3569 (Cushi), H3570 (Cushi), H3575 (Cuth), H3568 (Chush), H3571 (Ethiopian), H3572 (Cushan)",
    3570: "כּוּשִׁי (Kûwshîy | koo-shee')\n\nDerivation: the same as H3569 כּוּשִׁי\nStrong's: Cushi, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Cushi.\n\nCognate Group: H3573 (Chushan-rishathayim), H3569 (Cushi), H3570 (Cushi), H3575 (Cuth), H3568 (Chush), H3571 (Ethiopian), H3572 (Cushan)",
    3571: "כּוּשִׁית (Kûwshîyth | koo-sheeth')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3569 כּוּשִׁי\nStrong's: a Cushite woman\nKJV: Ethiopian.\n\nCognate Group: H3573 (Chushan-rishathayim), H3569 (Cushi), H3570 (Cushi), H3575 (Cuth), H3568 (Chush), H3571 (Ethiopian), H3572 (Cushan)",
    3572: "כּוּשָׁן (Kûwshân | koo-shawn')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from H3568 כּוּשׁ\nStrong's: Cushan, a region of Arabia\nKJV: Cushan.\n\nCognate Group: H3573 (Chushan-rishathayim), H3569 (Cushi), H3570 (Cushi), H3575 (Cuth), H3568 (Chush), H3571 (Ethiopian), H3572 (Cushan)",
    3573: "כּוּשַׁן רִשְׁעָתַיִם (Kûwshan Rishʻâthayim | koo-shan' rish-awthah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: apparently from H3572 כּוּשָׁן and the dual of H7564 רִשְׁעָה ; Cushan of double wickedness\nStrong's: Cushan-Rishathajim, a Mesopotamian king\nKJV: Chushan-rishathayim.\n\nCognate Group: H3573 (Chushan-rishathayim), H3569 (Cushi), H3570 (Cushi), H3575 (Cuth), H3568 (Chush), H3571 (Ethiopian), H3572 (Cushan)",
    3574: "כֹּושָׁרָה (kôwshârâh | ko-shaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H3787 כָּשֵׁר\nStrong's: prosperity; in plural freedom\nKJV: [idiom] chain.\n\nCognate Group: H3788 (equity), H3601 (spindle), H3574 ([idiom] chain), H3787 (direct)",
    3575: "כּוּת (Kûwth | kooth)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) כּוּתָה; of foreign origin\nStrong's: Cuth or Cuthah, a province of Assyria\nKJV: Cuth.\n\nCognate Group: H3573 (Chushan-rishathayim), H3569 (Cushi), H3570 (Cushi), H3575 (Cuth), H3568 (Chush), H3571 (Ethiopian), H3572 (Cushan)",
    3576: "כָּזַב (kâzab | kaw-zab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to lie (i.e. deceive), literally or figuratively\nKJV: fail, (be found a, make a) liar, lie, lying, be in vain.\n\nCognate Group: H391 (liar), H3576 (fail), H3577 (deceitful), H3580 (Chezib), H3579 (Cozbi), H3578 (Choseba), H392 (Achzib)\nGreek Equivalents: G669 ἀποφθέγγομαι, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G2756 κενός, G3004 λέγω, G5571 ψευδής, G5571 ψευδής",
    3577: "כָּזָב (kâzâb | kaw-zawb')\n\nDerivation: from H3576 כָּזַב\nStrong's: falsehood; literally (untruth) or figuratively (idol)\nKJV: deceitful, false, leasing, + liar, lie, lying.\n\nCognate Group: H391 (liar), H3576 (fail), H3577 (deceitful), H3580 (Chezib), H3579 (Cozbi), H3578 (Choseba), H392 (Achzib)\nGreek Equivalents: G95 ἀδίκως, G3152 μάταιος, G5571 ψευδής, G5579 ψεῦδος, G5583 ψεύστης",
    3578: "כֹּזְבָא (Kôzᵉbâʼ | ko-zeb-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H3576 כָּזַב ; fallacious\nStrong's: Cozeba, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Choseba.\n\nCognate Group: H391 (liar), H3576 (fail), H3577 (deceitful), H3580 (Chezib), H3579 (Cozbi), H3578 (Choseba), H392 (Achzib)",
    3579: "כֹּזְבִי (Kôzᵉbîy | koz-bee')\n\nDerivation: from H3576 כָּזַב ; false\nStrong's: Cozbi, a Midianitess\nKJV: Cozbi.\n\nCognate Group: H391 (liar), H3576 (fail), H3577 (deceitful), H3580 (Chezib), H3579 (Cozbi), H3578 (Choseba), H392 (Achzib)",
    3580: "כְּזִיב (Kᵉzîyb | kez-eeb')\n\nDerivation: from H3576 כָּזַב ; falsified\nStrong's: Kezib, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Chezib.\n\nCognate Group: H391 (liar), H3576 (fail), H3577 (deceitful), H3580 (Chezib), H3579 (Cozbi), H3578 (Choseba), H392 (Achzib)",
    3581: "כֹּחַ (kôach | ko'-akh)\n\nDerivation: or (Daniel 11:6) כֹּוחַ; from an unused root meaning to be firm\nStrong's: vigor, literally (force, in a good or a bad sense) or figuratively (capacity, means, produce); also (from its hardiness) a large lizard\nKJV: ability, able, chameleon, force, fruits, might, power(-ful), strength, substance, wealth.\n\nCognate Group: H3581 (ability), H394 (cruel), H395 (cruel), H393 (cruel)\nGreek Equivalents: G1411 δύναμις, G2372 θυμός, G2479 ἰσχύς, G2480 ἰσχύω, G5495 χείρ",
    3582: "כָּחַד (kâchad | kaw-khad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to secrete, by act or word; hence (intensively) to destroy\nKJV: conceal, cut down (off), desolate, hide.\n\nCognate Group: H3582 (conceal)\nGreek Equivalents: G548 ἄπειμι, G613 ἀποκρύπτω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G853 ἀφανίζω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1842 ἐξολοθρεύω, G2048 ἔρημος, G2928 κρύπτω, G2990 λανθάνω, G3639 ὄλεθρος",
    3583: "כָּחַל (kâchal | kaw-khal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to paint (with stibium)\nKJV: paint.\n\nCognate Group: H3583 (paint)",
    3584: "כָּחַשׁ (kâchash | kaw-khash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be untrue, in word (to lie, feign, disown) or deed (to disappoint, fail, cringe)\nKJV: deceive, deny, dissemble, fail, deal falsely, be found liars, (be-) lie, lying, submit selves.\n\nCognate Group: H3584 (deceive), H3585 (leanness), H3586 (lying)\nGreek Equivalents: G720 ἀρνέομαι",
    3585: "כַּחַשׁ (kachash | kakh'-ash)\n\nDerivation: from H3584 כָּחַשׁ\nStrong's: literally a failure of flesh, i.e. emaciation; figuratively, hypocrisy\nKJV: leanness, lies, lying.\n\nCognate Group: H3584 (deceive), H3585 (leanness), H3586 (lying)\nGreek Equivalents: G5571 ψευδής, G5579 ψεῦδος",
    3586: "כֶּחָשׁ (kechâsh | kekh-awsh')\n\nDerivation: from H3584 כָּחַשׁ\nStrong's: faithless\nKJV: lying.\n\nCognate Group: H3584 (deceive), H3585 (leanness), H3586 (lying)",
    3587: "כִּי (kîy | kee)\n\nDerivation: from H3554 כָּוָה\nStrong's: a brand or scar\nKJV: burning.\n\nCognate Group: H3554 (burn), H4348 (that burneth), H3587 (burning), H3555 (burning)",
    3588: "כִּי (kîy | kee)\n\nDerivation: a primitive particle (the full form of the prepositional prefix) indicating causal relations of all kinds, antecedent or consequent\nStrong's: (by implication) very widely used as a relative conjunction or adverb (as below); often largely modified by other particles annexed\nKJV: and, + (forasmuch, inasmuch, where-) as, assured(-ly), + but, certainly, doubtless, + else, even, + except, for, how, (because, in, so, than) that, + nevertheless, now, rightly, seeing, since, surely, then, therefore, + (al-) though, + till, truly, + until, when, whether, while, whom, yea, yet.\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H518 (but), H3589 (destruction), H3651 (after that), H3588 (and)\nGreek Equivalents: G1346 δικαίως, G3778 οὗτος, G4133 πλήν",
    3589: "כִּיד (kîyd | keed)\n\nDerivation: from a primitive root meaning to strike\nStrong's: a crushing; figuratively, calamity\nKJV: destruction.\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H518 (but), H3589 (destruction), H3651 (after that), H3588 (and)\nGreek Equivalents: G4967 σφαγή",
    3590: "כִידֹוד (kîydôwd | kee-dode')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3589 כִּיד (compare H3539 כַּדְכֹּד)\nStrong's: properly, something struck off, i.e. a spark (as struck)\nKJV: spark.\n\nCognate Group: H3539 (agate), H3537 (barrel), H3590 (spark)",
    3591: "כִּידֹון (kîydôwn | kee-dohn')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3589 כִּיד ; (perhaps smaller than H2595 חֲנִית \n\nTypo: lemma חֲניִת second vowel, corrected to חֲנִית\n\n)\n\nStrong's: properly, something to strike with, i.e. a dart\nKJV: lance, shield, spear, target.\n\nCognate Group: H3597 (hammer), H3591 (lance), H3599 (bag), H3594 (Chiun), H3592 (Chidon)",
    3592: "כִּידֹון (Kîydôwn | kee-dohn')\n\nDerivation: the same as H3591 כִּידֹון\nStrong's: Kidon, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Chidon.\n\nCognate Group: H3597 (hammer), H3591 (lance), H3599 (bag), H3594 (Chiun), H3592 (Chidon)",
    3593: "כִּידֹור (kîydôwr | kee-dore')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: perhaps tumult\nKJV: battle.\n\nCognate Group: H3540 (Chedorlaomer), H1754 (ball), H3593 (battle)",
    3594: "כִּיּוּן (Kîyûwn | kee-yoon')\n\nDerivation: from H3559 כּוּן\nStrong's: properly, a statue, i.e. idol; but used (by euphemism) forsome heathen deity (perhaps corresponding to Priapus or Baal-peor)\nKJV: Chiun.\n\nCognate Group: H3597 (hammer), H3591 (lance), H3599 (bag), H3594 (Chiun), H3592 (Chidon)\nGreek Equivalents: G4481 Ῥεμφάν",
    3595: "כִּיֹּור (kîyôwr | kee-yore')\n\nDerivation: or כִּיֹּר; from the same as H3564 כּוּר\nStrong's: properly, something round (as excavated or bored), i.e. a chafing-dish forcoals or a caldron forcooking; hence (from similarity of form) a washbowl; also (for the same reason) a pulpit or platform\nKJV: hearth, laver, pan, scaffold.\n\nCognate Group: H3564 (furnace), H3600 (ranges for pots), H3595 (hearth), H3733 (captain)\nGreek Equivalents: G939 βάσις",
    3596: "כִּילַי (kîylay | kee-lah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: or כֵּלַי; from H3557 כּוּל in the sense of withholding\nStrong's: niggardly\nKJV: churl.\n\nCognate Group: H5231 (wile), H5230 (beguile), H3596 (churl), H5233 (riches)\nGreek Equivalents: G5257 ὑπηρέτης",
    3597: "כֵּילַף (kêylaph | kay-laf')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to clap or strike with noise\nStrong's: a club or sledge-hammer\nKJV: hammer.\n\nCognate Group: H3597 (hammer), H3591 (lance), H3599 (bag), H3594 (Chiun), H3592 (Chidon)",
    3598: "כִּימָה (Kîymâh | kee-maw')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3558 כּוּמָז\nStrong's: a cluster of stars, i.e. the Pleiades\nKJV: Pleiades, seven stars.\n\nCognate Group: H3598 (Pleiades)",
    3599: "כִּיס (kîyç | keece)\n\nDerivation: a form for H3563 כֹּוס\nStrong's: a cup; also a bag formoney or weights\nKJV: bag, cup, purse.\n\nCognate Group: H3597 (hammer), H3591 (lance), H3599 (bag), H3594 (Chiun), H3592 (Chidon)\nGreek Equivalents: G905 βαλάντιον",
    3600: "כִּיר (kîyr | keer)\n\nDerivation: a form for H3564 כּוּר (only in the dual)\nStrong's: a cooking range (consisting of two parallel stones, across which the boiler is set)\nKJV: ranges for pots.\n\nCognate Group: H3564 (furnace), H3600 (ranges for pots), H3595 (hearth), H3733 (captain)",
    3601: "כִּישֹׁור (kîyshôwr | kee-shore')\n\nDerivation: from H3787 כָּשֵׁר ; compare H6418 פֶּלֶךְ \nStrong's: literally a director, i.e. the spindle or shank of adistaff, by which it is twirled\nKJV: spindle.\n\nCognate Group: H3788 (equity), H3601 (spindle), H3574 ([idiom] chain), H3787 (direct)",
    3602: "כָּכָה (kâkâh | kaw'-kaw)\n\nDerivation: from H3541 כֹּה\nStrong's: just so, referring to the previous or following context\nKJV: after that (this) manner, this matter, (even) so, in such a case, thus.\n\nCognate Group: H3541 (also), H3602 (after that manner)\nGreek Equivalents: G3778 οὗτος",
    3603: "כִּכָּר (kikkâr | kik-kawr')\n\nDerivation: from H3769 כָּרַר\nStrong's: a circle, i.e. (by implication) a circumjacent tract or region, especially the Ghor or valley of the Jordan; also a (round) loaf; also a talent (or large [round] coin)\nKJV: loaf, morsel, piece, plain, talent.\n\nCognate Group: H3603 (loaf), H3753 (swift beast), H3769 (dance), H3733 (captain)\nGreek Equivalents: G30 ἀγγεῖον, G4040 περίοικος, G4066 περίχωρος, G5007 τάλαντον",
    3604: "כִּכֵּר (kikkêr | kik-kare')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3603 כִּכָּר\nStrong's: a talent\nKJV: talent.\n\nCognate Group: H3679 (Chaldean), H3604 (talent), H3779 (Chaldean)",
    3605: "כֹּל (kôl | kole)\n\nDerivation: or (Jeremiah 33:8) כֹּול; from H3634 כָּלַל\nStrong's: properly, the whole; hence, all, any or every (in the singular only, but often in a plural sense)\nKJV: (in) all (manner, (ye)), altogether, any (manner), enough, every (one, place, thing), howsoever, as many as, (no-) thing, ought, whatsoever, (the) whole, whoso(-ever).\n\nCognate Group: H4359 (perfection), H4358 (most gorgeously), H3605 (all), H3634 (perfect), H4360 (all sorts), H3632 (all)\nGreek Equivalents: G243 ἄλλος, G1538 ἕκαστος, G2087 ἕτερος, G2943 κυκλόθεν, G3062 λοιποί, G3063 λοιπόν, G3064 λοιποῦ, G3650 ὅλος, G3956 πᾶς, G4931 συντελέω",
    3606: "כֹּל (kôl | kole)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3605 כֹּל \nStrong's: properly, the whole; hence, all, any or every (in the singular only, but often in a plural sense)\nKJV: all, any, + (forasmuch) as, + be-(for this) cause, every, + no (manner, -ne), + there (where) -fore, + though, what (where, who) -soever, (the) whole.\n\nCognate Group: H3660 (so), H3635 (finish), H3652 (thus), H3606 (all)",
    3607: "כָּלָא (kâlâʼ | kaw-law')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to restrict, by act (hold back or in) or word (prohibit)\nKJV: finish, forbid, keep (back), refrain, restrain, retain, shut up, be stayed, withhold.\n\nCognate Group: H4356 (fold), H3608 (prison), H3609 (Chileab), H3610 (divers seeds), H3607 (finish), H3628 (prison)\nGreek Equivalents: G430 ἀνέχομαι, G2623 κατακλείω, G2967 κωλύω, G3860 παραδίδωμι, G4912 συνέχω, G5288 ὑποστέλλω",
    3608: "כֶּלֶא (keleʼ | keh'-leh)\n\nDerivation: from H3607 כָּלָא\nStrong's: a prison\nKJV: prison. Compare H3610 כִּלְאַיִם, H3628 כְּלִיא .\n\nCognate Group: H4356 (fold), H3608 (prison), H3609 (Chileab), H3610 (divers seeds), H3607 (finish), H3628 (prison)\nGreek Equivalents: G5438 φυλακή",
    3609: "כִּלְאָב (Kilʼâb | kil-awb')\n\nDerivation: apparently from H3607 כָּלָא and H1 אָב ; restraint of (his) father\nStrong's: Kilab, an Israelite\nKJV: Chileab.\n\nCognate Group: H4356 (fold), H3608 (prison), H3609 (Chileab), H3610 (divers seeds), H3607 (finish), H3628 (prison)",
    3610: "כִּלְאַיִם (kilʼayim | kil-ah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: dual of H3608 כֶּלֶא in the original sense of separation\nStrong's: two heterogeneities\nKJV: divers seeds (-e kinds), mingled (seed).\n\nCognate Group: H4356 (fold), H3608 (prison), H3609 (Chileab), H3610 (divers seeds), H3607 (finish), H3628 (prison)\nGreek Equivalents: G1313 διάφορος, G5306 ὕστερος, G5307 ὑφαντός",
    3611: "כֶּלֶב (keleb | keh'-leb)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root means. to yelp, or else to attack\nStrong's: a dog; hence (by euphemism) a male prostitute\nKJV: dog.\n\nCognate Group: H3619 (basket), H3614 (of the house of Caleb), H3621 (Chelubai), H3620 (Chelub), H3612 (Caleb), H3611 (dog)\nGreek Equivalents: G2965 κύων",
    3612: "כָּלֵב (Kâlêb | kaw-labe')\n\nDerivation: perhaps a form of H3611 כֶּלֶב, or else from the same root in the sense of forcible\nStrong's: Caleb, the name of three Israelites\nKJV: Caleb.\n\nCognate Group: H3619 (basket), H3614 (of the house of Caleb), H3621 (Chelubai), H3620 (Chelub), H3612 (Caleb), H3611 (dog)",
    3613: "כָּלֵב אֶפְרָתָה (Kâlêb ʼEphrâthâh | kaw-labe' ef-raw'-thaw)\n\nDerivation: from H3612 כָּלֵב and H672 אֶפְרָת\nStrong's: Caleb-Ephrathah, a place in Egypt (if the text is correct)\nKJV: Caleb-ephrathah.\n\nCognate Group: H668 (chariot), H3613 (Caleb-ephrathah), H672 (once perhaps for Ephraim; also of an Israelitish woman; Ephrath), H673 (Ephraimite), H669 (Ephraim), H666 (ashes)",
    3614: "כָּלִבֹּו (Kâlibbôw | kaw-lib-bo')\n\nDerivation: probably by erroneous transcription for כָּלֵבִי; patronymically from H3612 כָּלֵב\nStrong's: a Calebite or descendant of Caleb\nKJV: of the house of Caleb.\n\nCognate Group: H3619 (basket), H3614 (of the house of Caleb), H3621 (Chelubai), H3620 (Chelub), H3612 (Caleb), H3611 (dog)",
    3615: "כָּלָה (kâlâh | kaw-law')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to end, whether intransitive (to cease, be finished, perish) or transitived (to complete, prepare, consume)\nKJV: accomplish, cease, consume (away), determine, destroy (utterly), be (when... were) done, (be an) end (of), expire, (cause to) fail, faint, finish, fulfil, [idiom] fully, [idiom] have, leave (off), long, bring to pass, wholly reap, make clean riddance, spend, quite take away, waste.\n\nCognate Group: H3617 (altogether), H3630 (Chilion), H3627 (armour), H3615 (accomplish), H8503 (end), H8502 (perfection), H4357 (perfect), H3622 (Chelluh), H3631 (consumption), H3616 (fail)\nGreek Equivalents: G355 ἀναλίσκω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G853 ἀφανίζω, G1097 γινώσκω, G1300 διατελέω, G1325 δίδωμι, G1410 δύναμαι, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1615 ἐκτελέω, G1842 ἐξολοθρεύω, G2005 ἐπιτελέω, G2719 κατεσθίω, G2869 κοπάζω, G3840 πάντοθεν, G3928 παρέρχομαι, G3973 παύω, G4137 πληρόω, G4595 σήπω, G4931 συντελέω, G4932 συντέμνω, G5048 τελειόω, G5055 τελέω, G5056 τέλος, G5080 τήκω",
    3616: "כָּלֶה (kâleh | kaw-leh')\n\nDerivation: from H3615 כָּלָה\nStrong's: pining\nKJV: fail.\n\nCognate Group: H3617 (altogether), H3630 (Chilion), H3627 (armour), H3615 (accomplish), H8503 (end), H8502 (perfection), H4357 (perfect), H3622 (Chelluh), H3631 (consumption), H3616 (fail)",
    3617: "כָּלָה (kâlâh | kaw-law')\n\nDerivation: from H3615 כָּלָה\nStrong's: a completion; adverb, completely; also destruction\nKJV: altogether, (be, utterly) consume(-d), consummation(-ption), was determined, (full, utter) end, riddance.\n\nCognate Group: H3617 (altogether), H3630 (Chilion), H3627 (armour), H3615 (accomplish), H8503 (end), H8502 (perfection), H4357 (perfect), H3622 (Chelluh), H3631 (consumption), H3616 (fail)\nGreek Equivalents: G3956 πᾶς",
    3618: "כַּלָּה (kallâh | kal-law')Typo: lemma כַּלָה missing dagesh, corrected to כַּלָּה\n\nGreek Equivalents: G3565 νύμφη \n\nDerivation: from H3634 כָּלַל\nStrong's: a bride (as if perfect); hence, a son's wife\nKJV: bride, daughter-in-law, spouse.\n\nCognate Group: H3623 (espousal), H3618 (bride), H3636 (Chelal)",
    3619: "כְּלוּב (kᵉlûwb | kel-oob')Typo: xlit kᵉlûb corrected to kᵉlûwb\n\nGreek Equivalents: G30 ἀγγεῖον, G32 ἄγγελος, G3803 παγίς \n\nDerivation: from the same as H3611 כֶּלֶב\nStrong's: a bird-trap (as furnished with a clap-stick or treadle to spring it); hence, a basket (as resembling a wicker cage)\n\nKJV: basket, cage.\n\nCognate Group: H3619 (basket), H3614 (of the house of Caleb), H3621 (Chelubai), H3620 (Chelub), H3612 (Caleb), H3611 (dog)",
    3620: "כְּלוּב (Kᵉlûwb | kel-oob')\n\nDerivation: the same as H3619 כְּלוּב \n\nTypo: xlit kᵉlûb corrected to kᵉlûwb\n\nStrong's: Kelub, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Chelub.\n\nCognate Group: H3619 (basket), H3614 (of the house of Caleb), H3621 (Chelubai), H3620 (Chelub), H3612 (Caleb), H3611 (dog)",
    3621: "כְּלוּבַי (Kᵉlûwbay | kel-oo-bay'-ee)\n\nDerivation: a form of H3612 כָּלֵב\nStrong's: Kelubai, an Israelite\nKJV: Chelubai.\n\nCognate Group: H3619 (basket), H3614 (of the house of Caleb), H3621 (Chelubai), H3620 (Chelub), H3612 (Caleb), H3611 (dog)",
    3622: "כְּלוּהַי (Kᵉlûwhay | kel-oo-hah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H3615 כָּלָה ; completed\nStrong's: Keluhai, an Israelite\nKJV: Chelluh.\n\nCognate Group: H3617 (altogether), H3630 (Chilion), H3627 (armour), H3615 (accomplish), H8503 (end), H8502 (perfection), H4357 (perfect), H3622 (Chelluh), H3631 (consumption), H3616 (fail)",
    3623: "כְּלוּלָה (kᵉlûwlâh | kel-oo-law')\n\nDerivation: denominative passive participle from H3618 כַּלָּה \n\nTypo: lemma כַּלָה missing dagesh, corrected to כַּלָּה\n\nStrong's: bridehood (only in the plural)\nKJV: espousal.\n\nCognate Group: H3623 (espousal), H3618 (bride), H3636 (Chelal)",
    3624: "כֶּלַח (kelach | keh'-lakh)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be complete\nStrong's: maturity\nKJV: full (old) age.\n\nCognate Group: H3624 (full age), H3626 (Col-hozeh), H3625 (Calah)",
    3625: "כֶּלַח (Kelach | keh'-lakh)\n\nDerivation: the same as H3624 כֶּלַח\nStrong's: Kelach, a place in Assyria\nKJV: Calah.\n\nCognate Group: H3624 (full age), H3626 (Col-hozeh), H3625 (Calah)",
