    3630: "כִּלְיֹון (Kilyôwn | kil-yone')\n\nDerivation: a form of H3631 כִּלָּיֹון\nStrong's: Kiljon, an Israelite\nKJV: Chilion.\n\nCognate Group: H3617 (altogether), H3630 (Chilion), H3627 (armour), H3615 (accomplish), H8503 (end), H8502 (perfection), H4357 (perfect), H3622 (Chelluh), H3631 (consumption), H3616 (fail)",
    3631: "כִּלָּיֹון (killâyôwn | kil-law-yone')\n\nDerivation: from H3615 כָּלָה\nStrong's: pining, destruction\nKJV: consumption, failing.\n\nCognate Group: H3617 (altogether), H3630 (Chilion), H3627 (armour), H3615 (accomplish), H8503 (end), H8502 (perfection), H4357 (perfect), H3622 (Chelluh), H3631 (consumption), H3616 (fail)",
    3632: "כָּלִיל (kâlîyl | kaw-leel')\n\nDerivation: from H3634 כָּלַל\nStrong's: complete; as noun, the whole (specifically, a sacrifice entirely consumed); as adverb, fully\nKJV: all, every whit, flame, perfect(-ion), utterly, whole burnt offering (sacrifice), wholly.\n\nCognate Group: H4359 (perfection), H4358 (most gorgeously), H3605 (all), H3634 (perfect), H4360 (all sorts), H3632 (all)\nGreek Equivalents: G3646 ὁλοκαύτωμα, G3956 πᾶς, G3956 πᾶς, G4060 περιτίθημι, G4735 στέφανος",
    3633: "כַּלְכֹּל (Kalkôl | kal-kole')\n\nDerivation: from H3557 כּוּל ; sustenance\nStrong's: Calcol, an Israelite\nKJV: Calcol, Chalcol.\n\nCognate Group: H3557 (abide), H3633 (Calcol)",
