    3635: "כְּלַל (kᵉlal | kel-al')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3634 כָּלַל\nStrong's: to complete\nKJV: finish, make (set) up.\n\nCognate Group: H3660 (so), H3635 (finish), H3652 (thus), H3606 (all)\nGreek Equivalents: G2675 καταρτίζω",
    3636: "כְּלָל (Kᵉlâl | kel-awl')\n\nDerivation: from H3634 כָּלַל ; complete\nStrong's: Kelal, an Israelite\nKJV: Chelal.\n\nCognate Group: H3623 (espousal), H3618 (bride), H3636 (Chelal)",
    3637: "כָּלַם (kâlam | kaw-lawm')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to wound; but only figuratively, to taunt or insult\nKJV: be (make) ashamed, blush, be confounded, be put to confusion, hurt, reproach, (do, put to) shame.\n\nCognate Group: H3639 (confusion), H3640 (shame), H3637 (be ashamed), H3641 (Calneh), H3638 (Chilmad)\nGreek Equivalents: G153 αἰσχύνομαι, G818 ἀτιμάζω, G819 ἀτιμία, G821 ἀτιμόω, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1788 ἐντρέπω, G2617 καταισχύνω, G2635 καταλαλέω, G2851 κόλασις, G2869 κοπάζω, G3679 ὀνειδίζω, G3837 πανταχοῦ",
    3638: "כִּלְמָד (Kilmâd | kil-mawd')\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Kilmad, a place apparently in the Assyrian empire\nKJV: Chilmad.\n\nCognate Group: H3639 (confusion), H3640 (shame), H3637 (be ashamed), H3641 (Calneh), H3638 (Chilmad)",
