    3640: "כְּלִמּוּת (kᵉlimmûwth | kel-im-mooth')\n\nDerivation: from H3639 כְּלִמָּה\nStrong's: disgrace\nKJV: shame.\n\nCognate Group: H3639 (confusion), H3640 (shame), H3637 (be ashamed), H3641 (Calneh), H3638 (Chilmad)",
    3641: "כַּלְנֶה (Kalneh | kal-neh')\n\nDerivation: or כַּלְנֵה; also כַּלְנֹו; of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Calneh or Calno, a place in the Assyrian empire\nKJV: Calneh, Calno. Compare H3656 כַּנֶּה .\n\nCognate Group: H3639 (confusion), H3640 (shame), H3637 (be ashamed), H3641 (Calneh), H3638 (Chilmad)",
    3642: "כָּמַהּ (kâmahh | kaw-mah)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to pine after\nKJV: long.\n\nCognate Group: H3642 (long), H3643 (Chimham), H3645 (Chemosh)\nGreek Equivalents: G4080 πηλίκος, G5101 τίς",
    3643: "כִּמְהָם (Kimhâm | kim-hawm')\n\nDerivation: from H3642 כָּמַהּ ; pining\nStrong's: Kimham, an Israelite\nKJV: Chimham.\n\nCognate Group: H3642 (long), H3643 (Chimham), H3645 (Chemosh)",
