    3651: "כֵּן (kên | kane)\n\nDerivation: from H3559 כּוּן\nStrong's: properly, set upright; hence (figuratively as adjective) just; but usually (as adverb or conjunction) rightly or so (in various applications to manner, time and relation; often with other particles)\nKJV: [phrase] after that (this, -ward, -wards), as... as, [phrase] (for-) asmuch as yet, [phrase] be (for which) cause, [phrase] following, howbeit, in (the) like (manner, -wise), [idiom] the more, right, (even) so, state, straightway, such (thing), surely, [phrase] there (where) -fore, this, thus, true, well, [idiom] you.\n\nCognate Group: H3561 (cake), H8499 (seat), H3200 (Jachinites), H3559 (certain), H3651 (after that), H3560 (Chun), H8498 (fashion), H3562 (Conaniah), H4369 (base), H4349 (foundation), H4350 (base), H3199 (Jachin), H3204 (Jeconiah), H5225 (Nachon), H3563 (cup)",
    3652: "כֵּן (kên | kane)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3651 כֵּן\nStrong's: so\nKJV: thus.\n\nCognate Group: H3660 (so), H3635 (finish), H3652 (thus), H3606 (all)",
    3653: "כֵּן (kên | kane)\n\nDerivation: the same as H3651 כֵּן, used as a noun\nStrong's: a stand, i.e. pedestal or station\nKJV: base, estate, foot, office, place, well.\n\nCognate Group: H3663 (Chenaniah), H3662 (Chenani), H3653 (base)\nGreek Equivalents: G746 ἀρχή, G804 ἀσφαλής, G939 βάσις, G1516 εἰρηνικός, G1565 ἐκεῖνος, G2091 ἑτοιμασία, G3664 ὅμοιος, G3778 οὗτος, G3779 οὕτω, G4491 ῥίζα, G5117 τόπος",
    3654: "כֵּן (kên | kane)\n\nDerivation: from H3661 כָּנַן in the sense of fastening; (from infixing its sting; used only in plural (and irregular in Exodus 8:17,18; Hebrews 13:14))\n\nStrong's: a gnat\nKJV: lice, [idiom] manner.\n\nCognate Group: H3657 ([idiom] vineyard), H3661 ([idiom] vineyard), H3654 (lice)",
    3655: "כָּנָה (kânâh | kaw-naw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to address by an additional name; hence, to eulogize\nKJV: give flattering titles, surname (himself).\n\nCognate Group: H3655 (give flattering titles), H3656 (Canneh)\nGreek Equivalents: G994 βοάω, G1788 ἐντρέπω, G2296 θαυμάζω",
    3656: "כַּנֶּה (Kanneh | kan-neh')\n\nDerivation: for H3641 כַּלְנֶה\nStrong's: Canneh, a place in Assyria\nKJV: Canneh.\n\nCognate Group: H3655 (give flattering titles), H3656 (Canneh)",
    3657: "כַּנָּה (kannâh | kaw-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H3661 כָּנַן\nStrong's: a plant (as set)\nKJV: [idiom] vineyard.\n\nCognate Group: H3657 ([idiom] vineyard), H3661 ([idiom] vineyard), H3654 (lice)",
    3658: "כִּנֹּור (kinnôwr | kin-nore')\n\nDerivation: from a unused root meaning to twang\nStrong's: a harp\nKJV: harp.\n\nCognate Group: H3677 (appointed), H3678 (seat), H3658 (harp), H3672 (Chinnereth), H3676 (sworn), H3674 (companion)\nGreek Equivalents: G2788 κιθάρα",
    3659: "כׇּנְיָהוּ (Konyâhûw | kon-yaw'-hoo)\n\nDerivation: for H3204 יְכׇנְיָה\nStrong's: Conjah, an Israelite king\nKJV: Coniah.\n\nCognate Group: H3059 (Jehoahaz), H3050 (Jah), H3060 (Jehoash), H3100 (Joel), H3098 (Joah), H1942 (calamity), H3141 (Joram), H3135 (Joash), H3086 (Jehoaddan), H3089 (Jehosheba), H3078 (Jehoiachin), H3133 (Joed), H3122 (Jonadab), H3107 (Josabad), H3099 (Jehoahaz), H3110 (Johanan), H3113 (Joiakim), H3077 (Jehoiada), H3091 (Jehoshua), H3115 (Jochebed), H3097 (Joab), H1953 (Hoshama), H3068 (Jehovah), H3090 (Jehoshabeath), H3058 (Jehu), H3088 (Jehoram), H3108 (Jozachar), H1933 (be), H3087 (Jehozadek), H3129 (Jonathan), H3080 (Jehoiarib), H3079 (Jehoiakim), H3114 (Joiarib), H3134 (Joezer), H3085 (Jehoada), H1944 (Hoham), H3101 (Joash), H3083 (Jonathan), H3111 (Jehoiada), H3076 (Jehohanan), H3137 (Jokim), H3116 (Jucal), H1943 (mischief), H3082 (Jehonadab), H1962 (calamity), H3146 (Joshaphat), H3092 (Jehoshaphat), H3112 (Jehoiachin), H3136 (Jozadak), H3147 (Jotham), H3069 (God), H3075 (Jehozabad), H3081 (Jehucal), H3442 (Jeshua), H3659 (Coniah)",
    3660: "כְּנֵמָא (kᵉnêmâʼ | ken-ay-maw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3644 כְּמֹו\nStrong's: so or thus\nKJV: so, (in) this manner (sort), thus.\n\nCognate Group: H3660 (so), H3635 (finish), H3652 (thus), H3606 (all)\nGreek Equivalents: G3778 οὗτος",
    3661: "כָּנַן (kânan | kaw-nan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to set out, i.e. plant\nKJV: [idiom] vineyard.\n\nCognate Group: H3657 ([idiom] vineyard), H3661 ([idiom] vineyard), H3654 (lice)\nGreek Equivalents: G2675 καταρτίζω",
    3662: "כְּנָנִי (Kᵉnânîy | ken-aw-nee')\n\nDerivation: from H3661 כָּנַן ; planted\nStrong's: Kenani, an Israelite\nKJV: Chenani.\n\nCognate Group: H3663 (Chenaniah), H3662 (Chenani), H3653 (base)",
    3663: "כְּנַנְיָה (Kᵉnanyâh | ken-an-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or כְּנַנְיָהוּ; from H3661 כָּנַן and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has planted\nStrong's: Kenanjah, an Israelite\nKJV: Chenaniah.\n\nCognate Group: H3663 (Chenaniah), H3662 (Chenani), H3653 (base)",
    3664: "כָּנַס (kânaç | kaw-nas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to collect; hence, to enfold\nKJV: gather (together), heap up, wrap self.\n\nCognate Group: H3664 (gather), H4370 (breeches)\nGreek Equivalents: G4863 συνάγω",
    3665: "כָּנַע (kânaʻ | kaw-nah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to bend the knee; hence, to humiliate, vanquish\nKJV: bring down (low), into subjection, under, humble (self), subdue.\n\nCognate Group: H3665 (bring down), H3666 (wares), H3669 (Canaanite), H3667 (Canaan), H3668 (Chenaanah)\nGreek Equivalents: G153 αἰσχύνομαι, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G1788 ἐντρέπω, G1994 ἐπιστρέφω, G2660 κατανύσσω, G5013 ταπεινόω",
    3666: "כִּנְעָה (kinʻâh | kin-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H3665 כָּנַע in the sense of folding (compare H3664 כָּנַס)\nStrong's: a package\nKJV: wares.\n\nCognate Group: H3665 (bring down), H3666 (wares), H3669 (Canaanite), H3667 (Canaan), H3668 (Chenaanah)\nGreek Equivalents: G5287 ὑπόστασις",
    3667: "כְּנַעַן (Kᵉnaʻan | ken-ah'-an)\n\nDerivation: from H3665 כָּנַע ; humiliated\nStrong's: Kenaan, a son a Ham; also the country inhabited by him\nKJV: Canaan, merchant, traffick.\n\nCognate Group: H3665 (bring down), H3666 (wares), H3669 (Canaanite), H3667 (Canaan), H3668 (Chenaanah)\nGreek Equivalents: G5477 Χαναάν",
    3668: "כְּנַעֲנָה (Kᵉnaʻănâh | ken-ah-an-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3667 כְּנַעַן\nStrong's: Kenaanah, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Chenaanah.\n\nCognate Group: H3665 (bring down), H3666 (wares), H3669 (Canaanite), H3667 (Canaan), H3668 (Chenaanah)",
    3669: "כְּנַעַנִי (Kᵉnaʻanîy | ken-ah-an-ee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H3667 כְּנַעַן\nStrong's: a Kenaanite or inhabitant of Kenaan; by implication, a pedlar (the Canaanites standing for their neighbors the Ishmaelites, who conducted mercantile caravans)\nKJV: Canaanite, merchant, trafficker.\n\nCognate Group: H3665 (bring down), H3666 (wares), H3669 (Canaanite), H3667 (Canaan), H3668 (Chenaanah)",
    3670: "כָּנַף (kânaph | kaw-naf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to project laterally, i.e. probably (reflexive) to withdraw\nKJV: be removed.\n\nCognate Group: H3671 (bird), H3670 (be removed)",
    3671: "כָּנָף (kânâph | kaw-nawf')\n\nDerivation: from H3670 כָּנַף\nStrong's: an edge or extremity; specifically (of a bird or army) a wing, (of a garment or bedclothing) a flap, (of the earth) a quarter, (of a building) a pinnacle\nKJV: [phrase] bird, border, corner, end, feather(-ed), [idiom] flying, [phrase] (one an-) other, overspreading, [idiom] quarters, skirt, [idiom] sort, uttermost part, wing(-ed).\n\nCognate Group: H3671 (bird), H3670 (be removed)\nGreek Equivalents: G206 ἄκρον, G1448 ἐγγίζω, G2413 ἱερός, G2899 κράσπεδον, G4071 πετεινόν, G4419 πτερύγιον, G4420 πτέρυξ",
    3672: "כִּנְּרֹות (Kinnᵉrôwth | kin-ner-oth')\n\nDerivation: or כִּנֶּרֶת\n\nTypo: lemma כִּנֶרֶת missing dagesh, corrected to כִּנֶּרֶת\n\n; respectively plural and singular feminine from the same as H3658 כִּנֹּור ; perhaps harp-shaped\nStrong's: Kinneroth or Kinnereth, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Chinnereth, Chinneroth, Cinneroth.\n\nCognate Group: H3677 (appointed), H3678 (seat), H3658 (harp), H3672 (Chinnereth), H3676 (sworn), H3674 (companion)\nGreek Equivalents: G1082 Γεννησαρέτ",
    3673: "כָּנַשׁ (kânash | kaw-nash')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3664 כָּנַס\nStrong's: to assemble\nKJV: gather together.\n\nCognate Group: H3673 (gather together), H3675 (companion)",
    3674: "כְּנָת (kᵉnâth | ken-awth')\n\nDerivation: from H3655 כָּנָה\nStrong's: a colleague (as having the same title)\nKJV: companion.\n\nCognate Group: H3677 (appointed), H3678 (seat), H3658 (harp), H3672 (Chinnereth), H3676 (sworn), H3674 (companion)\nGreek Equivalents: G4889 σύνδουλος",
    3675: "כְּנָת (kᵉnâth | ken-awth')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3674 כְּנָת \nStrong's: a colleague (as having the same title)\nKJV: companion.\n\nCognate Group: H3673 (gather together), H3675 (companion)",
    3676: "כֵּס (kêç | kace)\n\nDerivation: apparently a contraction for H3678 כִּסֵּא, but probably by erroneous transcription for H5251 נֵס \nStrong's: a flag; also a sail; by implication, a flagstaff; generally a signal; figuratively, a token\nKJV: sworn.\n\nCognate Group: H3677 (appointed), H3678 (seat), H3658 (harp), H3672 (Chinnereth), H3676 (sworn), H3674 (companion)",
    3677: "כֶּסֶא (keçeʼ | keh'-seh)\n\nDerivation: or כֶּסֶה; apparently from H3680 כָּסָה\nStrong's: properly, fulness or the full moon, i.e. its festival\nKJV: (time) appointed.\n\nCognate Group: H3677 (appointed), H3678 (seat), H3658 (harp), H3672 (Chinnereth), H3676 (sworn), H3674 (companion)\nGreek Equivalents: G2154 εὔσημος",
    3678: "כִּסֵּא (kiççêʼ | kis-say')\n\nDerivation: or כִּסֵּה; from H3680 כָּסָה\nStrong's: properly, covered, i.e. a throne (as canopied)\nKJV: seat, stool, throne.\n\nCognate Group: H3677 (appointed), H3678 (seat), H3658 (harp), H3672 (Chinnereth), H3676 (sworn), H3674 (companion)\nGreek Equivalents: G2362 θρόνος",
    3679: "כַּסְדַּי (Kaçday | kas-dah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: for H3778 כַּשְׂדִּי \nStrong's: a Kasdite, or descendant of Kesed; by implication, a Chaldaean (as if so descended); also an astrologer (as if proverbial of that people\nKJV: Chaldean.\n\nCognate Group: H3679 (Chaldean), H3604 (talent), H3779 (Chaldean)",
    3680: "כָּסָה (kâçâh | kaw-saw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to plump, i.e. fill up hollows; by implication, to cover (for clothing or secrecy)\nKJV: clad self, close, clothe, conceal, cover (self), (flee to) hide, overwhelm. Compare H3780 כָּשָׂה .\n\nCognate Group: H4374 (clothing), H3680 (clad self), H3681 (covering), H3682 (covering), H4372 (covering)\nGreek Equivalents: G380 ἀναπτύσσω, G1943 ἐπικαλύπτω, G2186 ἐφίστημι, G2572 καλύπτω, G2619 κατακαλύπτω, G2703 καταφεύγω, G2927 κρυπτός, G2928 κρύπτω, G4016 περιβάλλω, G4028 περικαλύπτω, G4115 πλατύνω",
    3681: "כָּסוּי (kâçûwy | kaw-soo'-ee)\n\nDerivation: passive participle of H3680 כָּסָה\nStrong's: properly, covered, i.e. (as noun) a covering\nKJV: covering.\n\nCognate Group: H4374 (clothing), H3680 (clad self), H3681 (covering), H3682 (covering), H4372 (covering)\nGreek Equivalents: G2571 κάλυμα",
    3682: "כְּסוּת (kᵉçûwth | kes-ooth')\n\nDerivation: from H3680 כָּסָה\nStrong's: a cover (garment); figuratively, a veiling\nKJV: covering, raiment, vesture.\n\nCognate Group: H4374 (clothing), H3680 (clad self), H3681 (covering), H3682 (covering), H4372 (covering)\nGreek Equivalents: G294 ἀμφιέννυμι, G2441 ἱματισμός, G4018 περιβόλαιον",
    3683: "כָּסַח (kâçach | kaw-sakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to cut off\nKJV: cut down (up).\n\nCognate Group: H3683 (cut down)",
    3684: "כְּסִיל (kᵉçîyl | kes-eel')\n\nDerivation: from H3688 כָּסַל\nStrong's: properly, fat, i.e. (figuratively) stupid or silly\nKJV: fool(-ish).\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)",
    3685: "כְּסִיל (Kᵉçîyl | kes-eel')\n\nDerivation: the same as H3684 כְּסִיל\nStrong's: any notable constellation; specifically Orion (as if a burly one)\nKJV: constellation, Orion.\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)\nGreek Equivalents: G521 ἀπαίδευτος, G765 ἀσεβής, G801 ἀσύνετος, G877 ἀφροσύνη, G878 ἄφρων, G1729 ἐνδεής, G5424 φρήν",
    3686: "כְּסִיל (Kᵉçîyl | kes-eel')\n\nDerivation: the same as H3684 כְּסִיל\nStrong's: Kesil, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Chesil.\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)",
    3687: "כְּסִילוּת (kᵉçîylûwth | kes-eel-ooth')\n\nDerivation: from H3684 כְּסִיל\nStrong's: silliness\nKJV: foolish.\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)",
    3688: "כָּסַל (kâçal | kaw-sal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to be fat, i.e. (figuratively) silly\nKJV: be foolish.\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)",
    3689: "כֶּסֶל (keçel | keh'-sel)\n\nDerivation: from H3688 כָּסַל\nStrong's: properly, fatness, i.e. by implication (literally) the loin (as the seat of the leaf fat) or (generally) the viscera; also (figuratively) silliness or (in a good sense) trust\nKJV: confidence, flank, folly, hope, loin.\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)\nGreek Equivalents: G1680 ἐλπίς, G3382 μηρός, G4625 σκάνδαλον",
    3690: "כִּסְלָה (kiçlâh | kis-law')Typo: lemma כְּסִלָה first two vowels, corrected to כִּסְלָה\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3689 כֶּסֶל\nStrong's: in a good sense, trust; in a bad one, silliness\nKJV: confidence, folly.\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)",
    3691: "כִּסְלֵו (Kiçlêv | kis-lave')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: Kisleu, the 9th Hebrew month\nKJV: Chisleu.\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)",
    3692: "כִּסְלֹון (Kiçlôwn | kis-lone')\n\nDerivation: from H3688 כָּסַל ; hopeful\nStrong's: Kislon, an Israelite\nKJV: Chislon.\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)",
    3693: "כְּסָלֹון (Kᵉçâlôwn | kes-aw-lone')\n\nDerivation: from H3688 כָּסַל ; fertile\nStrong's: Kesalon, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Chesalon.\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)",
    3694: "כְּסֻלֹּות (Kᵉçullôwth | kes-ool-loth')\n\nDerivation: feminine plural of passive participle of H3688 כָּסַל ; fattened\nStrong's: Kesulloth, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Chesulloth.\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)",
    3695: "כַּסְלֻחִים (Kaçluchîym | kas-loo'-kheem)\n\nDerivation: a plural probably of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Casluchim, a people cognate to the Egyptians\nKJV: Casluhim.\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)",
    3696: "כִּסְלֹת תָּבֹר (Kiçlôth Tâbôr | kis-loth' taw-bore')\n\nDerivation: from the feminine plural of H3689 כֶּסֶל and H8396 תָּבֹור ; flanks of Tabor\nStrong's: Kisloth-Tabor, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Chisloth-tabor.\n\nCognate Group: H3685 (constellation), H3690 (confidence), H3688 (be foolish), H3692 (Chislon), H3696 (Chisloth-tabor), H3693 (Chesalon), H3684 (fool), H3695 (Casluhim), H3687 (foolish), H3686 (Chesil), H3694 (Chesulloth), H3689 (confidence), H3691 (Chisleu)",
    3697: "כָּסַם (kâçam | kaw-sam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to shear\nKJV: [idiom] only, poll. Compare H3765 כִּרְסֵם .\n\nCognate Group: H3697 ([idiom] only), H3698 (fitches), H3765 (waste)",
    3698: "כֻּסֶּמֶת (kuççemeth | koos-seh'-meth)\n\nDerivation: from H3697 כָּסַם\nStrong's: spelt (from its bristliness as if just shorn)\nKJV: fitches, rie.\n\nCognate Group: H3697 ([idiom] only), H3698 (fitches), H3765 (waste)",
    3699: "כָּסַס (kâçaç | kaw-sas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to estimate\nKJV: make count.\n\nCognate Group: H4373 (number), H3699 (make count), H4371 (tribute)",
    3700: "כָּסַף (kâçaph | kaw-saf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to become pale, i.e. (by implication) to pine after; also to fear\nKJV: (have) desire, be greedy, long, sore.\n\nCognate Group: H3703 (Casiphia), H3700 (desire), H3701 (money)\nGreek Equivalents: G1937 ἐπιθυμέω, G1939 ἐπιθυμία, G1971 ἐπιποθέω, G2092 ἕτοιμος, G3700 ὀπτάνομαι",
    3701: "כֶּסֶף (keçeph | keh'-sef)\n\nDerivation: from H3700 כָּסַף\nStrong's: silver (from its pale color); by implication, money\nKJV: money, price, silver(-ling).\n\nCognate Group: H3703 (Casiphia), H3700 (desire), H3701 (money)\nGreek Equivalents: G693 ἀργύρεος, G694 ἀργύριον, G696 ἄργυρος, G1323 δίδραχμον, G5092 τιμή, G5536 χρῆμα",
    3702: "כְּסַף (kᵉçaph | kes-af')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3701 כֶּסֶף \nStrong's: silver (from its pale color); by implication, money\nKJV: money, silver.\n\nCognate Group: H3702 (money), H3764 (throne)",
    3703: "כָּסִפְיָא (Kâçiphyâʼ | kaw-sif-yaw')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from H3701 כֶּסֶף ; silvery\nStrong's: Casiphja, a place in Babylon\nKJV: Casiphia.\n\nCognate Group: H3703 (Casiphia), H3700 (desire), H3701 (money)",
    3704: "כֶּסֶת (keçeth | keh'-seth)\n\nDerivation: from H3680 כָּסָה\nStrong's: a cushion or pillow (as covering a seat or bed)\nKJV: pillow.\n\nCognate Group: H3704 (pillow)\nGreek Equivalents: G4344 προσκεφάλαιον",
    3705: "כְּעַן (kᵉʻan | keh-an')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) probably from H3652 כֵּן\nStrong's: now\nKJV: now.\n\nCognate Group: H3705 (now), H6032 (answer), H3706 (at such a time)",
    3706: "כְּעֶנֶת (kᵉʻeneth | keh-eh'-neth)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or כְּעֶת; (Aramaic), feminine of H3705 כְּעַן\nStrong's: thus (only in the formula 'and so forth')\nKJV: at such a time.\n\nCognate Group: H3705 (now), H6032 (answer), H3706 (at such a time)",
    3707: "כַּעַס (kaʻaç | kaw-as')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to trouble; by implication, to grieve, rage, be indignant\nKJV: be angry, be grieved, take indignation, provoke (to anger, unto wrath), have sorrow, vex, be wroth.\n\nCognate Group: H3707 (be angry), H3710 (rock), H3708 (anger)\nGreek Equivalents: G120 ἀθυμέω, G2373 θυμόω, G3309 μεριμνάω, G3893 παραπικραίνω, G3947 παροξύνω, G3949 παροργίζω, G4087 πικραίνω",
    3708: "כַּעַס (kaʻaç | kah'-as)\n\nDerivation: or (in Job) כַּעַשׂ; from H3707 כַּעַס\nStrong's: vexation\nKJV: anger, angry, grief, indignation, provocation, provoking, [idiom] sore, sorrow, spite, wrath.\n\nCognate Group: H3707 (be angry), H3710 (rock), H3708 (anger)\nGreek Equivalents: G1108 γνῶσις, G2372 θυμός, G3709 ὀργή, G3709 ὀργή, G3711 ὀργίλος, G3950 παροργισμός",
    3709: "כַּף (kaph | kaf)\n\nDerivation: from H3721 כָּפַף\nStrong's: the hollow hand or palm (so of the paw of an animal, of the sole, and even of the bowl of a dish or sling, the handle of a bolt, the leaves of a palm-tree); figuratively, power\nKJV: branch, [phrase] foot, hand((-ful), -dle, (-led)), hollow, middle, palm, paw, power, sole, spoon.\n\nCognate Group: H3712 (branch), H3721 (bow down), H3709 (branch)\nGreek Equivalents: G1147 δάκτυλος, G2487 ἴχνος, G2798 κλάδος, G4083 πῆχυς, G4114 πλάτος, G5165 τρύβλιον, G5495 χείρ",
    3710: "כֵּף (kêph | kafe)\n\nDerivation: from H3721 כָּפַף\nStrong's: a hollow rock\nKJV: rock.\n\nCognate Group: H3707 (be angry), H3710 (rock), H3708 (anger)\nGreek Equivalents: G4073 πέτρα, G2786 Κηφᾶς",
    3711: "כָּפָה (kâphâh | kaw-faw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to bend, i.e. (figuratively) to tame or subdue\nKJV: pacify.\n\nCognate Group: H3711 (pacify)",
    3712: "כִּפָּה (kippâh | kip-paw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3709 כַּף\nStrong's: a leaf of a palmtree\nKJV: branch.\n\nCognate Group: H3712 (branch), H3721 (bow down), H3709 (branch)\nGreek Equivalents: G746 ἀρχή",
    3713: "כְּפֹור (kᵉphôwr | kef-ore')\n\nDerivation: from H3722 כָּפַר\nStrong's: properly, a cover, i.e. (by implication) a tankard (or covered goblet); also white frost (as covering the ground)\nKJV: bason, hoar(-y) frost.\n\nCognate Group: H3713 (bason)\nGreek Equivalents: G3509 νέφος",
    3714: "כָּפִיס (kâphîyç | kaw-fece')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to connect\nStrong's: a girder\nKJV: beam.\n\nCognate Group: H3714 (beam)",
    3715: "כְּפִיר (kᵉphîyr | kef-eer')\n\nDerivation: from H3722 כָּפַר\nStrong's: a village (as covered in by walls); also a young lion (perhaps as covered with a mane)\nKJV: (young) lion, village. Compare H3723 כָּפָר .\n\nCognate Group: H3724 (bribe), H3715 (lion), H3726 (Chefarhaamonai), H3716 (Chephirah), H3723 (village)\nGreek Equivalents: G1404 δράκων, G3023 λέων, G4145 πλούσιος",
    3716: "כְּפִירָה (Kᵉphîyrâh | kef-ee-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3715 כְּפִיר ; the village (always with the art.)\nStrong's: Kephirah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Chephirah.\n\nCognate Group: H3724 (bribe), H3715 (lion), H3726 (Chefarhaamonai), H3716 (Chephirah), H3723 (village)",
    3717: "כָּפַל (kâphal | kaw-fal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to fold together; figuratively, to repeat\nKJV: double.\n\nCognate Group: H3717 (double), H4375 (Machpelah), H3718 (double)\nGreek Equivalents: G1362 διπλοῦς",
    3718: "כֶּפֶל (kephel | keh'-fel)\n\nDerivation: from H3717 כָּפַל\nStrong's: a duplicate\nKJV: double.\n\nCognate Group: H3717 (double), H4375 (Machpelah), H3718 (double)",
    3719: "כָּפַן (kâphan | kaw-fan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to bend\nKJV: bend.\n\nCognate Group: H3720 (famine), H3719 (bend)",
    3720: "כָּפָן (kâphân | kaw-fawn')\n\nDerivation: from H3719 כָּפַן\nStrong's: hunger (as making to stoop with emptiness and pain)\nKJV: famine.\n\nCognate Group: H3720 (famine), H3719 (bend)\nGreek Equivalents: G3042 λιμός",
    3721: "כָּפַף (kâphaph | kaw-faf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to curve\nKJV: bow down (self).\n\nCognate Group: H3712 (branch), H3721 (bow down), H3709 (branch)\nGreek Equivalents: G482 ἀντιλαμβάνομαι",
    3722: "כָּפַר (kâphar | kaw-far')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to cover (specifically with bitumen); figuratively, to expiate or condone, to placate or cancel\nKJV: appease, make (an atonement, cleanse, disannul, forgive, be merciful, pacify, pardon, purge (away), put off, (make) reconcile(-liation).\n\nCognate Group: H3724 (bribe), H3725 (atonement), H3727 (mercy seat), H3722 (appease)\nGreek Equivalents: G37 ἁγιάζω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G863 ἀφίημι, G2433 ἱλάσκομαι, G2511 καθαρίζω",
    3723: "כָּפָר (kâphâr | kaw-fawr')\n\nDerivation: from H3722 כָּפַר\nStrong's: a village (as protected by walls)\nKJV: village. Compare H3715 כְּפִיר .\n\nCognate Group: H3724 (bribe), H3715 (lion), H3726 (Chefarhaamonai), H3716 (Chephirah), H3723 (village)\nGreek Equivalents: G2436 ἵλεως, G2968 κώμη, G2584 Καπερναούμ",
    3724: "כֹּפֶר (kôpher | ko'-fer)\n\nDerivation: from H3722 כָּפַר\nStrong's: properly, a cover, i.e. (literally) a village (as covered in); (specifically) bitumen (as used for coating), and the henna plant (as used for dyeing); figuratively, a redemption-price\nKJV: bribe, camphire, pitch, ransom, satisfaction, sum of money, village.\n\nCognate Group: H3724 (bribe), H3725 (atonement), H3727 (mercy seat), H3722 (appease)\nGreek Equivalents: G465 ἀντάλλαγμα, G3083 λύτρον, G4027 περικάθαρμα",
    3725: "כִּפֻּר (kippur | kip-poor')\n\nDerivation: from H3722 כָּפַר\nStrong's: expiation (only in plural)\nKJV: atonement.\n\nCognate Group: H3724 (bribe), H3725 (atonement), H3727 (mercy seat), H3722 (appease)\nGreek Equivalents: G2434 ἱλασμός, G2512 καθαρισμός",
    3726: "כְּפַר הָעַמֹּונִי (Kᵉphar hâ-ʻAmmôwnîy | kef-ar' haw-am-monee')\n\nDerivation: from H3723 כָּפָר and H5984 עַמֹּונִי, with the article interposed; village of the Ammonite\nStrong's: Kefar-ha-Ammoni, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Chefarhaamonai.\n\nCognate Group: H3724 (bribe), H3715 (lion), H3726 (Chefarhaamonai), H3716 (Chephirah), H3723 (village)",
    3727: "כַּפֹּרֶת (kappôreth | kap-po'-reth)\n\nDerivation: from H3722 כָּפַר\nStrong's: a lid (used only of the cover of the sacred Ark)\nKJV: mercy seat.\n\nCognate Group: H3724 (bribe), H3725 (atonement), H3727 (mercy seat), H3722 (appease)\nGreek Equivalents: G2435 ἱλαστήριον",
    3728: "כָּפַשׁ (kâphash | kaw-fash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tread down; figuratively, to humiliate\nKJV: cover.\n\nCognate Group: H3736 (clothed), H3728 (cover), H3732 (Caphthorim), H3730 (knop), H3734 (cor), H3733 (captain), H3731 (Caphtor)",
    3729: "כְּפַת (kᵉphath | kef-ath')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) a root of uncertain correspondence\nStrong's: to fetter\nKJV: bind.\n\nCognate Group: H3729 (bind)",
    3730: "כַּפְתֹּר (kaphtôr | kaf-tore')\n\nDerivation: or (Amos 9:1) כַּפְתֹּור; probably from an unused root meaning to encircle\nStrong's: a chaplet; but used only in an architectonic sense, i.e. the capital of acolumn, or a wreath-like button or disk on the candelabrum\nKJV: knop, (upper) lintel.\n\nCognate Group: H3736 (clothed), H3728 (cover), H3732 (Caphthorim), H3730 (knop), H3734 (cor), H3733 (captain), H3731 (Caphtor)",
    3731: "כַּפְתֹּר (Kaphtôr | kaf-tore')\n\nDerivation: or (Amos 9:7) כַּפְתֹּור; apparently the same as H3730 כַּפְתֹּר\nStrong's: Caphtor (i.e. a wreath-shaped island), the original seat of the Philistines\nKJV: Caphtor.\n\nCognate Group: H3736 (clothed), H3728 (cover), H3732 (Caphthorim), H3730 (knop), H3734 (cor), H3733 (captain), H3731 (Caphtor)",
    3732: "כַּפְתֹּרִי (Kaphtôrîy | kaf-to-ree')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H3731 כַּפְתֹּר\nStrong's: a Caphtorite (collectively) or native of Caphtor\nKJV: Caphthorim, Caphtorim(-s).\n\nCognate Group: H3736 (clothed), H3728 (cover), H3732 (Caphthorim), H3730 (knop), H3734 (cor), H3733 (captain), H3731 (Caphtor)",
    3733: "כַּר (kar | kar)\n\nDerivation: from H3769 כָּרַר in the sense of plumpness\nStrong's: a ram (as full-grown and fat), including a battering-ram (as butting); hence, a meadow (as for sheep); also a pad or camel's saddle (as puffed out)\nKJV: captain, furniture, lamb, (large) pasture, ram. See also H1033 בֵּית כַּר, H3746 כָּרִי .\n\nCognate Group: H3564 (furnace), H3600 (ranges for pots), H3595 (hearth), H3733 (captain)\nGreek Equivalents: G2055 ἐρίφιον, G2056 ἔριφος, G2062 ἑρπετόν, G5117 τόπος, G5482 χάραξ",
    3734: "כֹּר (kôr | kore)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3564 כּוּר\nStrong's: properly, a deep round vessel, i.e. (specifically) a cor or measure for things dry\nKJV: cor, measure. Aramaic the same.\n\nCognate Group: H3736 (clothed), H3728 (cover), H3732 (Caphthorim), H3730 (knop), H3734 (cor), H3733 (captain), H3731 (Caphtor)\nGreek Equivalents: G2884 κόρος",
    3735: "כָּרָא (Kârâʼ | kaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) probably corresponding to H3738 כָּרָה in the sense of piercing(figuratively)\nStrong's: to grieve\nKJV: be grieved.\n\nCognate Group: H3735 (be grieved), H3744 (herald), H3737 (hat), H3745 (make a proclamation)\nGreek Equivalents: G5425 φρίσσω",
    3736: "כַּרְבֵּל (karbêl | kar-bale')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3525 כֶּבֶל\nStrong's: to gird or clothe\nKJV: clothed.\n\nCognate Group: H3736 (clothed), H3728 (cover), H3732 (Caphthorim), H3730 (knop), H3734 (cor), H3733 (captain), H3731 (Caphtor)\nGreek Equivalents: G4024 περιζώννυμι",
    3737: "כַּרְבְּלָא (karbᵉlâʼ | kar-bel-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a verb corresponding to that of H3736 כַּרְבֵּל\nStrong's: a mantle\nKJV: hat.\n\nCognate Group: H3735 (be grieved), H3744 (herald), H3737 (hat), H3745 (make a proclamation)",
    3738: "כָּרָה (kârâh | kaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to dig; figuratively, to plot; generally, to bore or open\nKJV: dig, [idiom] make (a banquet), open.\n\nCognate Group: H3566 (Cyrus), H3738 (dig), H4380 (habitation), H4351 (birth)\nGreek Equivalents: G1334 διηγέομαι, G2998 λατομέω, G3409 μισθόω, G3736 ὀρύσσω, G3908 παρατίθημι",
    3739: "כָּרָה (kârâh | kaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: usually assigned as a primitive root, but probably only a special application of H3738 כָּרָה (through the common idea of planning implied in a bargain)\nStrong's: to purchase\nKJV: buy, prepare.\n\nCognate Group: H3739 (buy)",
    3740: "כֵּרָה (kêrâh | kay-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H3739 כָּרָה\nStrong's: a purchase\nKJV: provision.\n\nCognate Group: H3742 (cherub), H3746 (captains), H3740 (provision), H3743 (Cherub), H3739 (buy)",
    3741: "כָּרָה (kârâh | kaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3733 כַּר\nStrong's: a meadow\nKJV: cottage.\n\nCognate Group: H4379 (pit), H3738 (dig), H3741 (cottage)",
    3742: "כְּרוּב (kᵉrûwb | ker-oob')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a cherub or imaginary figure\nKJV: cherub, (plural) cherubims.\n\nCognate Group: H3742 (cherub), H3746 (captains), H3740 (provision), H3743 (Cherub), H3739 (buy)\nGreek Equivalents: G5502 χερουβίμ",
    3743: "כְּרוּב (Kᵉrûwb | ker-oob')\n\nDerivation: the same as H3742 כְּרוּב\nStrong's: Kerub, a place in Babylon\nKJV: Cherub.\n\nCognate Group: H3742 (cherub), H3746 (captains), H3740 (provision), H3743 (Cherub), H3739 (buy)",
    3744: "כָּרֹוז (kârôwz | kaw-roze')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H3745 כְּרַז\nStrong's: a herald\nKJV: herald.\n\nCognate Group: H3735 (be grieved), H3744 (herald), H3737 (hat), H3745 (make a proclamation)\nGreek Equivalents: G2783 κῆρυξ",
    3745: "כְּרַז (kᵉraz | ker-az')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) probably of Greek origin\nStrong's: to proclaim\nKJV: make a proclamation.\n\nCognate Group: H3735 (be grieved), H3744 (herald), H3737 (hat), H3745 (make a proclamation)\nGreek Equivalents: G2784 κηρύσσω",
    3746: "כָּרִי (kârîy | kaw-ree')\n\nDerivation: perhaps an abridged plural of H3733 כַּר in the sense of leader (of the flock)\nStrong's: a life-guardsman\nKJV: captains, Cherethites (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H3742 (cherub), H3746 (captains), H3740 (provision), H3743 (Cherub), H3739 (buy)",
    3747: "כְּרִית (Kᵉrîyth | ker-eeth')\n\nDerivation: from H3772 כָּרַת ; a cut\nStrong's: Kerith, a brook of Palestine\nKJV: Cherith.\n\nCognate Group: H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)",
    3748: "כְּרִיתוּת (kᵉrîythûwth | ker-ee-thooth')\n\nDerivation: from H3772 כָּרַת\nStrong's: a cutting (of the matrimonial bond), i.e. divorce\nKJV: divorce(-ment).\n\nCognate Group: H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)\nGreek Equivalents: G647 ἀποστάσιον",
    3749: "כַּרְכֹּב (karkôb | kar-kobe')\n\nDerivation: expanded from the same as H3522 כַּבֹּון\nStrong's: a rim or top margin\nKJV: compass.\n\nCognate Group: H3750 (saffron), H3751 (Carchemish), H3752 (Carcas), H3749 (compass)",
    3750: "כַּרְכֹּם (karkôm | kar-kome')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: the crocus\nKJV: saffron.\n\nCognate Group: H3750 (saffron), H3751 (Carchemish), H3752 (Carcas), H3749 (compass)",
    3751: "כַּרְכְּמִישׁ (Karkᵉmîysh | kar-kem-eesh')\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Karkemish, a place in Syria\nKJV: Carchemish.\n\nCognate Group: H3750 (saffron), H3751 (Carchemish), H3752 (Carcas), H3749 (compass)",
    3752: "כַּרְכַּס (Karkaç | kar-kas')\n\nDerivation: of Persian origin\nStrong's: Karkas, a eunuch of Xerxes\nKJV: Carcas.\n\nCognate Group: H3750 (saffron), H3751 (Carchemish), H3752 (Carcas), H3749 (compass)",
    3753: "כַּרְכָּרָה (karkârâh | kar-kaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H3769 כָּרַר\nStrong's: a dromedary (from its rapid motion as if dancing)\nKJV: swift beast.\n\nCognate Group: H3603 (loaf), H3753 (swift beast), H3769 (dance), H3733 (captain)",
    3754: "כֶּרֶם (kerem | keh'-rem)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root of uncertain meaning\nStrong's: a garden or vineyard\nKJV: vines, (increase of the) vineyard(-s), vintage. See also H1021 בֵּית הַכֶּרֶם .\n\nCognate Group: H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)\nGreek Equivalents: G288 ἄμπελος, G290 ἀμπελών, G2933 κτῆμα, G5564 χωρίον",
    3755: "כֹּרֵם (kôrêm | ko-rame')\n\nDerivation: active participle of an imaginary denominative from H3754 כֶּרֶם\nStrong's: a vinedresser\nKJV: vine dresser (as one or two words).\n\nCognate Group: H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)\nGreek Equivalents: G289 ἀμπελουργός",
    3756: "כַּרְמִי (Karmîy | kar-mee')\n\nDerivation: from H3754 כֶּרֶם ; gardener\nStrong's: Karmi, the name of three Israelites\nKJV: Carmi.\n\nCognate Group: H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)",
    3757: "כַּרְמִי (Karmîy | kar-mee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H3756 כַּרְמִי\nStrong's: a Karmite or descendant of Karmi\nKJV: Carmites.\n\nCognate Group: H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)",
    3758: "כַּרְמִיל (karmîyl | kar-mele')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: carmine, a deep red\nKJV: crimson.\n\nCognate Group: H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)\nGreek Equivalents: G2847 κόκκινος",
    3759: "כַּרְמֶל (karmel | kar-mel')\n\nDerivation: from H3754 כֶּרֶם\nStrong's: a planted field (garden, orchard, vineyard or park); by implication, garden produce\nKJV: full (green) ears (of corn), fruitful field (place), plentiful (field).\n\nCognate Group: H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)\nGreek Equivalents: G290 ἀμπελών",
    3760: "כַּרְמֶל (Karmel | kar-mel')\n\nDerivation: the same as H3759 כַּרְמֶל\nStrong's: Karmel, the name of a hill and of a town in Palestine\nKJV: Carmel, fruitful (plentiful) field, (place).\n\nCognate Group: H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)",
    3761: "כַּרְמְלִי (Karmᵉlîy | kar-mel-ee')\n\nDerivation: patron from H3760 כַּרְמֶל\nStrong's: a Karmelite or inhabitant of Karmel (the town)\nKJV: Carmelite.\n\nCognate Group: H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)",
    3762: "כַּרְמְלִית (Karmᵉlîyth | kar-mel-eeth')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3761 כַּרְמְלִי\nStrong's: a Karmelitess or female inhabitant of Karmel\nKJV: Carmelitess.\n\nCognate Group: H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)",
    3763: "כְּרָן (Kᵉrân | ker-awn')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Keran, an aboriginal Idumaean\nKJV: Cheran.\n\nCognate Group: H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)",
    3764: "כׇּרְסֵא (korçêʼ | kor-say')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3678 כִּסֵּא\nStrong's: a throne\nKJV: throne.\n\nCognate Group: H3702 (money), H3764 (throne)\nGreek Equivalents: G2362 θρόνος",
    3765: "כִּרְסֵם (kirçêm | kir-same')\n\nDerivation: from H3697 כָּסַם\nStrong's: to lay waste\nKJV: waste.\n\nCognate Group: H3697 ([idiom] only), H3698 (fitches), H3765 (waste)\nGreek Equivalents: G3075 λυμαίνομαι",
    3766: "כָּרַע (kâraʻ | kaw-rah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to bend the knee; by implication, to sink, to prostrate\nKJV: bow (down, self), bring down (low), cast down, couch, fall, feeble, kneeling, sink, smite (stoop) down, subdue, [idiom] very.\n\nCognate Group: H3766 (bow), H3768 (green), H3767 (leg)\nGreek Equivalents: G101 ἀδυνατέω, G377 ἀναπίπτω, G1625 ἐκτρέφω, G1706 ἐμπίπτω, G2480 ἰσχύω, G2578 κάμπτω, G2625 κατακλίνω, G2799 κλαίω, G2827 κλίνω, G4098 πίπτω, G4352 προσκυνέω, G4363 προσπίπτω, G5013 ταπεινόω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5016 ταραχή",
    3767: "כָּרָע (kârâʻ | kaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H3766 כָּרַע\nStrong's: the leg (from the knee to the ankle) of men or locusts (only in the dual)\nKJV: leg.\n\nCognate Group: H3766 (bow), H3768 (green), H3767 (leg)\nGreek Equivalents: G4228 πούς, G4628 σκέλος",
    3768: "כַּרְפַּס (karpaç | kar-pas')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: byssus or fine vegetable wool\nKJV: green.\n\nCognate Group: H3766 (bow), H3768 (green), H3767 (leg)\nGreek Equivalents: G1039 βύσσινος",
    3769: "כָּרַר (kârar | kaw-rar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to dance (i.e. whirl)\nKJV: dance(-ing).\n\nCognate Group: H3603 (loaf), H3753 (swift beast), H3769 (dance), H3733 (captain)\nGreek Equivalents: G3738 ὀρχέομαι",
    3770: "כְּרֵשׂ (kᵉrês | ker-ace')\n\nDerivation: by variation from H7164 קָרַס\nStrong's: the paunch or belly (as swelling out)\nKJV: belly.\n\nCognate Group: H3771 (Carshena), H3770 (belly)\nGreek Equivalents: G2836 κοιλία",
    3771: "כַּרְשְׁנָא (Karshᵉnâʼ | kar-shen-aw')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Karshena, a courtier of Xerxes\nKJV: Carshena.\n\nCognate Group: H3771 (Carshena), H3770 (belly)",
    3772: "כָּרַת (kârath | kaw-rath')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to cut (off, down or asunder); by implication, to destroy or consume; specifically, to covenant (i.e. make an alliance or bargain, originally by cutting flesh and passing between the pieces)\nKJV: be chewed, be con-(feder-) ate, covenant, cut (down, off), destroy, fail, feller, be freed, hew (down), make a league (covenant), [idiom] lose, perish, [idiom] utterly, [idiom] want.\n\nCognate Group: H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)\nGreek Equivalents: G355 ἀναλίσκω, G599 ἀποθνήσκω, G609 ἀποκόπτω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G645 ἀποσπάω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G853 ἀφανίζω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G1303 διατίθεμαι, G1459 ἐγκαταλείπω, G1581 ἐκκόπτω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1806 ἐξάγω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1831 ἐξέρχομαι, G1842 ἐξολοθρεύω, G2476 ἵστημι, G2507 καθαιρέω, G2629 κατακόπτω, G2875 κόπτω, G3645 ὀλοθρεύω, G4059 περιτέμνω, G4141 πλήσσω, G4160 ποιέω, G4931 συντελέω, G5087 τίθημι",
    3773: "כָּרֻתָה (kâruthâh | kaw-rooth-aw')\n\nDerivation: passive participle feminine of H3772 כָּרַת\nStrong's: something cut, i.e. a hewn timber\nKJV: beam.\n\nCognate Group: H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)\nGreek Equivalents: G2716 κατεργάζομαι",
    3774: "כְּרֵתִי (Kᵉrêthîy | ker-ay-thee')\n\nDerivation: probably from H3772 כָּרַת in the sense of executioner; (compare H2876 טַבָּח) (only collectively in the singular as plural)\n\nStrong's: a Kerethite or life-guardsman\nKJV: Cherethims, Cherethites.\n\nCognate Group: H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)",
    3775: "כֶּשֶׂב (keseb | keh'-seb)\n\nDerivation: apparently by transposition for H3532 כֶּבֶשׂ\nStrong's: a young sheep\nKJV: lamb.\n\nCognate Group: H4346 (thick cloth), H3535 (lamb), H4345 (grate), H3523 (pillow), H3776 (lamb), H3775 (lamb), H3531 (sieve), H3532 (lamb)\nGreek Equivalents: G4263 πρόβατον",
    3776: "כִּשְׂבָּה (kisbâh | kis-baw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H3775 כֶּשֶׂב\nStrong's: a young ewe\nKJV: lamb.\n\nCognate Group: H4346 (thick cloth), H3535 (lamb), H4345 (grate), H3523 (pillow), H3776 (lamb), H3775 (lamb), H3531 (sieve), H3532 (lamb)",
    3777: "כֶּשֶׂד (Kesed | keh'-sed)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root of uncertain meaning\nStrong's: Kesed, a relative of Abraham\nKJV: Chesed.\n\nCognate Group: H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)",
    3778: "כַּשְׂדִּי (Kasdîy | kas-dee')\n\nDerivation: (occasionally with enclitic) כַּשְׂדִּימָה; towards the Kasdites into Chaldea), patronymically from H3777 כֶּשֶׂד (only in the plural)\nStrong's: a Kasdite, or descendant of Kesed; by implication, a Chaldaean (as if so descended); also an astrologer (as if proverbial of that people\nKJV: Chaldeans, Chaldees, inhabitants of Chaldea.\n\nCognate Group: H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)\nGreek Equivalents: G5466 Χαλδαῖος",
    3779: "כַּשְׂדַּי (Kasday | kas-dah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3778 כַּשְׂדִּי\nStrong's: a Chaldaean or inhabitant of Chaldaea; by implication, a Magian or professional astrologer\nKJV: Chaldean.\n\nCognate Group: H3679 (Chaldean), H3604 (talent), H3779 (Chaldean)",
    3780: "כָּשָׂה (kâsâh | kaw-saw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to grow fat (i.e. be covered with flesh)\nKJV: be covered. Compare H3680 כָּסָה .\n\nCognate Group: H3780 (be covered)",
    3781: "כַּשִּׁיל (kashshîyl | kash-sheel')\n\nDerivation: from H3782 כָּשַׁל\nStrong's: properly, a feller, i.e. an axe\nKJV: ax.\n\nCognate Group: H4383 (caused to fall), H4384 (ruin), H3783 (fall), H3782 (bereave), H3781 (ax)",
    3782: "כָּשַׁל (kâshal | kaw-shal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to totter or waver (through weakness of the legs, especially the ankle); by implication, to falter, stumble, faint or fall\nKJV: bereave (from the margin), cast down, be decayed, (cause to) fail, (cause, make to) fall (down, -ing), feeble, be (the) ruin(-ed, of), (be) overthrown, (cause to) stumble, [idiom] utterly, be weak.\n\nCognate Group: H4383 (caused to fall), H4384 (ruin), H3783 (fall), H3782 (bereave), H3781 (ax)\nGreek Equivalents: G101 ἀδυνατέω, G447 ἀνίημι, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G769 ἀσθένεια, G770 ἀσθενέω, G1847 ἐξουδενόω, G2559 κακόω, G2654 καταναλίσκω, G2872 κοπιάω, G3886 παραλύω, G4098 πίπτω, G4105 πλανάω, G4350 προσκόπτω, G4624 σκανδαλίζω, G4937 συντρίβω",
    3783: "כִּשָּׁלֹון (kishshâlôwn | kish-shaw-lone')\n\nDerivation: from H3782 כָּשַׁל\nStrong's: properly, a tottering, i.e. ruin\nKJV: fall.\n\nCognate Group: H4383 (caused to fall), H4384 (ruin), H3783 (fall), H3782 (bereave), H3781 (ax)\nGreek Equivalents: G4430 πτῶμα",
    3784: "כָּשַׁף (kâshaph | kaw-shaf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to whisper aspell, i.e. to inchant or practise magic\nKJV: sorcerer, (use) witch(-craft).\n\nCognate Group: H3784 (sorcerer), H3786 (sorcerer), H3785 (sorcery)\nGreek Equivalents: G5333 φάρμακος",
    3785: "כֶּשֶׁף (kesheph | keh'-shef)\n\nDerivation: from H3784 כָּשַׁף\nStrong's: magic\nKJV: sorcery, witchcraft.\n\nCognate Group: H3784 (sorcerer), H3786 (sorcerer), H3785 (sorcery)\nGreek Equivalents: G5331 φαρμακεία, G5332 φαρμακεύς",
    3786: "כַּשָּׁף (kashshâph | kash-shawf')\n\nDerivation: from H3784 כָּשַׁף\nStrong's: a magician\nKJV: sorcerer.\n\nCognate Group: H3784 (sorcerer), H3786 (sorcerer), H3785 (sorcery)",
    3787: "כָּשֵׁר (kâshêr | kaw-share')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root properly, to be straight or right\nStrong's: by implication, to be acceptable; also to succeed or prosper\nKJV: direct, be right, prosper.\n\nCognate Group: H3788 (equity), H3601 (spindle), H3574 ([idiom] chain), H3787 (direct)\nGreek Equivalents: G4748 στοιχέω",
    3788: "כִּשְׁרֹון (kishrôwn | kish-rone')\n\nDerivation: from H3787 כָּשֵׁר\nStrong's: success, advantage\nKJV: equity, good, right.\n\nCognate Group: H3788 (equity), H3601 (spindle), H3574 ([idiom] chain), H3787 (direct)",
    3789: "כָּתַב (kâthab | kaw-thab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to grave, by implication, to write (describe, inscribe, prescribe, subscribe)\nKJV: describe, record, prescribe, subscribe, write(-ing, -ten).\n\nCognate Group: H3789 (describe), H3794 (Chittim), H4385 (writing), H3791 (register), H3793 ([idiom] any)\nGreek Equivalents: G583 ἀπογράφω, G1121 γράμμα, G1124 γραφή, G1125 γράφω, G1125 γράφω, G1242 διαθήκη, G1379 δογματίζω, G1722 ἐν, G1924 ἐπιγράφω, G2192 ἔχω, G3307 μερίζω",
    3790: "כְּתַב (kᵉthab | keth-ab')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3789 כָּתַב \nStrong's: to grave, by implication, to write (describe, inscribe, prescribe, subscribe)\nKJV: write(-ten).\n\nCognate Group: H3790 (write), H3797 (wall), H3792 (prescribing)",
    3791: "כָּתָב (kâthâb | kaw-thawb')\n\nDerivation: from H3789 כָּתַב\nStrong's: something written, i.e. a writing, record or book\nKJV: register, scripture, writing.\n\nCognate Group: H3789 (describe), H3794 (Chittim), H4385 (writing), H3791 (register), H3793 ([idiom] any)\nGreek Equivalents: G582 ἀπογραφή, G1124 γραφή, G1378 δόγμα, G1992 ἐπιστολή",
    3792: "כְּתָב (kᵉthâb | keth-awb')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3791 כָּתָב \nStrong's: something written, i.e. a writing, record or book\nKJV: prescribing, writing(-ten).\n\nCognate Group: H3790 (write), H3797 (wall), H3792 (prescribing)",
    3793: "כְּתֹבֶת (kᵉthôbeth | keth-o'-beth)\n\nDerivation: from H3789 כָּתַב\nStrong's: a letter or other mark branded on the skin\nKJV: [idiom] any (mark).\n\nCognate Group: H3789 (describe), H3794 (Chittim), H4385 (writing), H3791 (register), H3793 ([idiom] any)",
    3794: "כִּתִּי (Kittîy | kit-tee')\n\nDerivation: or כִּתִּיִּי; patrial from an unused name denoting Cyprus (only in the plural)\nStrong's: a Kittite or Cypriote; hence, an islander in general, i.e. the Greeks or Romans on the shores opposite Palestine\nKJV: Chittim, Kittim.\n\nCognate Group: H3789 (describe), H3794 (Chittim), H4385 (writing), H3791 (register), H3793 ([idiom] any)",
    3795: "כָּתִית (kâthîyth | kaw-theeth')\n\nDerivation: from H3807 כָּתַת\nStrong's: beaten, i.e. pure (oil)\nKJV: beaten.\n\nCognate Group: H3795 (beaten), H4386 (bursting), H3807 (beat)",
    3796: "כֹּתֶל (kôthel | ko'-thel)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to compact\nStrong's: a wall (as gathering inmates)\nKJV: wall.\n\nCognate Group: H3796 (wall), H3798 (Kithlish)\nGreek Equivalents: G5109 τοῖχος",
    3797: "כְּתַל (kᵉthal | keth-al')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3796 כֹּתֶל \nStrong's: a wall (as gathering inmates)\nKJV: wall.\n\nCognate Group: H3790 (write), H3797 (wall), H3792 (prescribing)",
    3798: "כִּתְלִישׁ (Kithlîysh | kith-leesh')\n\nTypo: lemma כְּתִלִישׁ first two vowels, corrected to כִּתְלִישׁ\n\nDerivation: from H3796 כֹּתֶל and H376 אִישׁ ; wall of a man\nStrong's: Kithlish, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Kithlish.\n\nCognate Group: H3796 (wall), H3798 (Kithlish)",
    3799: "כָּתַם (kâtham | kaw-tham')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to carve or engrave, i.e. (by implication) to inscribe indelibly\nKJV: mark.\n\nCognate Group: H3799 (mark)",
    3800: "כֶּתֶם (kethem | keh'-them)\n\nDerivation: from H3799 כָּתַם\nStrong's: properly, something carved out, i.e. ore; hence, gold (pure as originally mined)\nKJV: ((most) fine, pure) gold(-en wedge).\n\nCognate Group: H4387 (Michtam), H3800 (gold)\nGreek Equivalents: G694 ἀργύριον, G2441 ἱματισμός, G3037 λίθος, G4185 πολυτελής, G5553 χρυσίον",
    3801: "כְּתֹנֶת (kᵉthôneth | keth-o'-neth)\n\nDerivation: or כֻּתֹּנֶת; from an unused root meaning to cover (compare H3802 כָּתֵף)\nStrong's: a shirt\nKJV: coat, garment, robe.\n\nCognate Group: H3801 (coat)\nGreek Equivalents: G2440 ἱμάτιον, G4749 στολή, G5509 χιτών, G5509 χιτών",
    3802: "כָּתֵף (kâthêph | kaw-thafe')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to clothe\nStrong's: the shoulder (proper, i.e. upper end of the arm; as being the spot where the garments hang); figuratively, side-piece or lateral projection of anything\nKJV: arm, corner, shoulder(-piece), side, undersetter.\n\nCognate Group: H3802 (arm)\nGreek Equivalents: G1137 γωνία, G3558 νότος, G3577 νῶτος, G5606 ὦμος",
    3803: "כָּתַר (kâthar | kaw-thar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to enclose; hence (in a friendly sense) to crown, (in a hostile one) to besiege; also to wait (as restraining oneself)\nKJV: beset round, compass about, be crowned inclose round, suffer.\n\nCognate Group: H3803 (beset round), H3805 (chapiter), H3804 (crown)\nGreek Equivalents: G2616 καταδυναστεύω, G2902 κρατέω, G3306 μένω, G4023 περιέχω",
    3804: "כֶּתֶר (kether | keh'-ther)\n\nDerivation: from H3803 כָּתַר\nStrong's: properly, a circlet, i.e. a diadem\nKJV: crown.\n\nCognate Group: H3803 (beset round), H3805 (chapiter), H3804 (crown)\nGreek Equivalents: G1238 διάδημα",
    3805: "כֹתֶרֶת (kôthereth | ko-theh'-reth)\n\nDerivation: feminine active participle of H3803 כָּתַר\nStrong's: the capital of a column\nKJV: chapiter.\n\nCognate Group: H3803 (beset round), H3805 (chapiter), H3804 (crown)\nGreek Equivalents: G2346 θλίβω, G2777 κεφαλίς, G4768 στυγνάζω",
    3806: "כָּתַשׁ (kâthash | kaw-thash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to butt or pound\nKJV: bray.\n\nCognate Group: H4388 (hollow place), H4389 (Maktesh), H3806 (bray)\nGreek Equivalents: G3146 μαστιγόω",
    3807: "כָּתַת (kâthath | kaw-thath')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to bruise or violently strike\nKJV: beat (down, to pieces), break in pieces, crushed, destroy, discomfit, smite, stamp. l\n\nCognate Group: H3795 (beaten), H4386 (bursting), H3807 (beat)\nGreek Equivalents: G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G2629 κατακόπτω, G2875 κόπτω, G3765 οὐκέτι, G4937 συντρίβω",
    3808: "לֹא (lôʼ | lo)\n\nDerivation: or לֹוא; or לֹה; (Deuteronomy 3:11), a primitive particle\nStrong's: not (the simple or abs. negation); by implication, no; often used with other particles\nKJV: [idiom] before, [phrase] or else, ere, [phrase] except, ig(-norant), much, less, nay, neither, never, no((-ne), -r, (-thing)), ([idiom] as though...,(can-), for) not (out of), of nought, otherwise, out of, [phrase] surely, [phrase] as truly as, [phrase] of a truth, [phrase] verily, for want, [phrase] whether, without.\n\nCognate Group: H3810 (Debir), H3808 ([idiom] before), H3819 (Lo-ruhamah), H3818 (Lo-ammi)\nGreek Equivalents: G512 ἀνωφελής, G544 ἀπειθέω, G544 ἀπειθέω, G564 ἀπερίτμητος, G762 ἄσβεστος, G878 ἄφρων, G1210 δέω, G1262 διαλύω, G1538 ἕκαστος, G1718 ἐμφανίζω, G1726 ἐναντίον, G1727 ἐναντίος, G2125 εὐλαβέομαι, G2756 κενός, G2756 κενός, G3763 οὐδέποτε, G3765 οὐκέτι",
    3809: "לָא (lâʼ | law)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or לָה; (Aramaic) (Daniel 4:32), corresponding to H3808 לֹא \nStrong's: not (the simple or abs. negation); by implication, no;\nKJV: or even, neither, no(-ne, -r), (can-) not, as nothing, without.\n\nCognate Group: H3809 (or even)",
    3810: "לֹא דְבַר (Lôʼ Dᵉbar | lo deb-ar')\n\nDerivation: or לֹו דבַר; (Samuel 9:4,5), or לִדְבִר; (Joshua 13:26), (probably rather לֹדְבַר); from H3808 לֹא and H1699 דֹּבֶר ; pastureless\nStrong's: Lo-Debar, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Debir, Lodebar.\n\nCognate Group: H3810 (Debir), H3808 ([idiom] before), H3819 (Lo-ruhamah), H3818 (Lo-ammi)",
    3811: "לָאָה (lâʼâh | law-aw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tire; (figuratively) to be (or make) disgusted\nKJV: faint, grieve, lothe, (be, make) weary (selves).\n\nCognate Group: H4972 (what a weariness), H8513 (travail), H3811 (faint), H3812 (Leah)\nGreek Equivalents: G73 ἀγών, G770 ἀσθενέω, G1410 δύναμαι, G1590 ἐκλύω, G1907 ἐπέχω, G2872 κοπιάω, G3076 λυπέω, G3886 παραλύω, G3926 παρενοχλέω, G3930 παρέχω, G3935 παρίημι",
    3812: "לֵאָה (Lêʼâh | lay-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H3811 לָאָה ; weary\nStrong's: Leah, a wife of Jacob\nKJV: Leah.\n\nCognate Group: H4972 (what a weariness), H8513 (travail), H3811 (faint), H3812 (Leah)",
    3813: "לָאַט (lâʼaṭ | law-at')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to muffle\nKJV: cover.\n\nCognate Group: H3813 (cover)",
    3814: "לָאט (lâʼṭ | lawt)\n\nDerivation: from H3813 לָאַט (or perhaps for active participle of H3874 לוּט)\nStrong's: properly, muffled, i.e. silently\nKJV: softly.\n\nCognate Group: H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)",
    3815: "לָאֵל (Lâʼêl | law-ale')\n\nDerivation: from the prepositional prefix and H410 אֵל ; (belonging) to God\nStrong's: Lael an Israelite\nKJV: Lael.\n\nCognate Group: H4399 (business), H4401 (Malachi), H3815 (Lael), H4397 (ambassador), H4400 (message)",
    3816: "לְאֹם (lᵉʼôm | leh-ome')Typo: xlit lᵉôm corrected to lᵉʼôm\n\nGreek Equivalents: G758 ἄρχων, G2992 λαός, G5443 φυλή \n\nDerivation: or לְאֹום; from an unused root meaning to gather\nStrong's: a community\nKJV: nation, people.\n\nCognate Group: H3817 (Leummim), H3816 (nation)",
    3817: "לְאֻמִּים (Lᵉʼummîym | leh-oom-meem')\n\nDerivation: plural of H3816 לְאֹם ; communities\nStrong's: Leum mim, an Arabian\nKJV: Leummim.\n\nCognate Group: H3817 (Leummim), H3816 (nation)",
    3818: "לֹא עַמִּי (Lôʼ ʻAmmîy | lo am-mee')\n\nDerivation: from H3808 לֹא and H5971 עַם with pronominal suffix; not my people\nStrong's: Lo-Ammi, the symbolic name of a son of Hosea\nKJV: Lo-ammi.\n\nCognate Group: H3810 (Debir), H3808 ([idiom] before), H3819 (Lo-ruhamah), H3818 (Lo-ammi)",
    3819: "לֹא רֻחָמָה (Lôʼ Ruchâmâh | lo roo-khaw-maw')\n\nDerivation: from H3808 לֹא and H7355 רָחַם ; not pitied\nStrong's: Lo-Ruchamah, the symbolic name of a son of Hosea\nKJV: Lo-ruhamah.\n\nCognate Group: H3810 (Debir), H3808 ([idiom] before), H3819 (Lo-ruhamah), H3818 (Lo-ammi)",
    3820: "לֵב (lêb | labe)\n\nDerivation: a form of H3824 לֵבָב\nStrong's: the heart; also used (figuratively) very widely for the feelings, the will and even the intellect; likewise for the centre of anything\nKJV: [phrase] care for, comfortably, consent, [idiom] considered, courag(-eous), friend(-ly), ((broken-), (hard-), (merry-), (stiff-), (stout-), double) heart(-ed), [idiom] heed, [idiom] I, kindly, midst, mind(-ed), [idiom] regard(-ed), [idiom] themselves, [idiom] unawares, understanding, [idiom] well, willingly, wisdom.\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H3820 (care for), H3824 (bethink themselves), H3834 (cake), H3826 (heart), H3823 (make cakes)\nGreek Equivalents: G1271 διάνοια, G2588 καρδία, G3563 νοῦς, G4738 στῆθος, G5424 φρήν, G5428 φρόνησις, G5590 ψυχή",
    3821: "לֵב (lêb | labe)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3820 לֵב \nStrong's: the heart; also used (figuratively) very widely for the feelings, the will and even the intellect; likewise for the centre of anything\nKJV: heart.\n\nCognate Group: H3821 (heart), H3825 (heart)",
    3822: "לְבָאֹות (Lᵉbâʼôwth | leb-aw-oth')\n\nDerivation: plural of H3833 לָבִיא ; lionesses\nStrong's: Lebaoth, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Lebaoth. See also H1034 בֵּית לְבָאֹות .\n\nCognate Group: H3822 (Lebaoth), H3833 (lion)",
    3823: "לָבַב (lâbab | law-bab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; properly, to be enclosed (as if with fat); by implication (as denominative from H3824 לֵבָב); to unheart; also as denominative from H3834 לָבִיבָה i.e.\nStrong's: (in a good sense) transport (with love), or (in a bad sense) stultify; to make cakes\nKJV: make cakes, ravish, be wise.\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H3820 (care for), H3824 (bethink themselves), H3834 (cake), H3826 (heart), H3823 (make cakes)",
    3824: "לֵבָב (lêbâb | lay-bawb')\n\nDerivation: from H3823 לָבַב ; used also like H3820 לֵב \nStrong's: the heart (as the most interior organ)\nKJV: [phrase] bethink themselves, breast, comfortably, courage, ((faint), (tender-) heart(-ed), midst, mind, [idiom] unawares, understanding.\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H3820 (care for), H3824 (bethink themselves), H3834 (cake), H3826 (heart), H3823 (make cakes)\nGreek Equivalents: G1271 διάνοια, G1939 ἐπιθυμία, G2588 καρδία, G3563 νοῦς, G5590 ψυχή",
