    3828: "לְבֹונָה (lᵉbôwnâh | leb-o-naw')\n\nDerivation: or לְבֹנָה; from H3836 לָבָן\nStrong's: frankincense (from its whiteness or perhaps that of its smoke)\nKJV: (frank-) incense.\n\nCognate Group: H3844 (Lebanon), H3843 (brick), H3838 (Lebana), H4192 (death), H3839 (poplar), H3846 (Libnites), H3840 (paved), H4404 (brickkiln), H3845 (Libni), H3835 (make brick), H3828 (incense), H3837 (Laban), H3836 (white), H3841 (Libnah), H3842 (moon), H3829 (Lebonah)\nGreek Equivalents: G3030 λίβανος, G3031 λιβανωτός",
