    3849: "לֹג (lôg | lohg)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root apparently meaning to deepen or hollow (like H3537 כַּד)\nStrong's: a log or measure forliquids\nKJV: log (of oil).\n\nCognate Group: H3850 (Lod), H8516 (clothing), H3847 (apparel), H3849 (log), H3830 (apparel), H4403 (apparel), H1688 (Debir)",
    3850: "לֹד (Lôd | lode)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root of uncertain signification\nStrong's: Lod, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Lod.\n\nCognate Group: H3850 (Lod), H8516 (clothing), H3847 (apparel), H3849 (log), H3830 (apparel), H4403 (apparel), H1688 (Debir)\nGreek Equivalents: G3069 Λύδδα",
    3851: "לַהַב (lahab | lah'-hab)\n\nDerivation: from an usused root meaning to gleam\nStrong's: a flash; figuratively, a sharply polished blade or point of aweapon\nKJV: blade, bright, flame, glittering.\n\nCognate Group: H3852 (flame), H3851 (blade), H7957 (flame), H3827 (flame), H3853 (Lehabim)\nGreek Equivalents: G4744 στίλβω, G5395 φλόξ",
    3852: "לֶהָבָה (lehâbâh | leh-aw-baw')\n\nDerivation: or לַהֶבֶת; feminine of H3851 לַהַב, and meaning the same\nStrong's: a flash; figuratively, a sharply polished blade or point of aweapon\nKJV: flame(-ming), head (of a spear).\n\nCognate Group: H3852 (flame), H3851 (blade), H7957 (flame), H3827 (flame), H3853 (Lehabim)\nGreek Equivalents: G2545 καίω, G3057 λόγχη, G4442 πῦρ, G5338 φέγγος, G5395 φλόξ",
    3853: "לְהָבִים (Lᵉhâbîym | leh-haw-beem')\n\nDerivation: plural of H3851 לַהַב ; flames\nStrong's: Lehabim, a son of Mizraim, and his descendants\nKJV: Lehabim.\n\nCognate Group: H3852 (flame), H3851 (blade), H7957 (flame), H3827 (flame), H3853 (Lehabim)",
    3854: "לַהַג (lahag | lah'-hag)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be eager\nStrong's: intense mental application\nKJV: study.\n\nCognate Group: H3855 (Lahad), H3854 (study)",
    3855: "לַהַד (Lahad | lah'-had)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to glow (compare H3851 לַהַב) or else to be earnest (compare H3854 לַהַג)\nStrong's: Lahad, an Israelite\nKJV: Lahad.\n\nCognate Group: H3855 (Lahad), H3854 (study)",
    3856: "לָהַהּ (lâhahh | law-hah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root meaning properly, to burn, i.e. (by implication)\n\nStrong's: to be rabid (figuratively, insane); also (from the exhaustion of frenzy) to languish\nKJV: faint, mad.\n\nCognate Group: H3856 (faint)\nGreek Equivalents: G1587 ἐκλείπω",
    3857: "לָהַט (lâhaṭ | law-hat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to lick, i.e. (by implication) to blaze\nKJV: burn (up), set on fire, flaming, kindle.\n\nCognate Group: H3858 (flaming), H3857 (burn)\nGreek Equivalents: G381 ἀνάπτω, G2618 κατακαίω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5394 φλογίζω",
    3858: "לַהַט (lahaṭ | lah'-hat)\n\nDerivation: from H3857 לָהַט\nStrong's: a blaze; also (from the idea of enwrapping) magic (as covert)\nKJV: flaming, enchantment.\n\nCognate Group: H3858 (flaming), H3857 (burn)",
    3859: "לָהַם (lâham | law-ham')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to burn in, i.e. (figuratively) to rankle\nKJV: wound.\n\nCognate Group: H3862 (company), H3859 (wound), H3860 (for them)",
    3860: "לָהֵן (lâhên | law-hane')\n\nDerivation: from the prepositional prefix meaning to or for and H2005 הֵן\nStrong's: popularly for if; hence, therefore\nKJV: for them (by mistake for prepositional suffix).\n\nCognate Group: H3862 (company), H3859 (wound), H3860 (for them)",
    3861: "לָהֵן (lâhên | law-hane')\n\nTypo: xlit lâwhên corrected to lâhên\n\nGreek Equivalents: G3568 νῦν, G4133 πλήν \n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3860 לָהֵן\nStrong's: therefore; also except\nKJV: but, except, save, therefore, wherefore.\n\nCognate Group: H3904 (concubine), H3861 (but), H3916 (night), H3900 (feast), H3879 (Levite), H3961 (language), H3890 ([idiom] thee)",
    3862: "לַהֲקָה (lahăqâh | lah-hak-aw')\n\nDerivation: probably from an unused root meaning to gather\nStrong's: an assembly\nKJV: company.\n\nCognate Group: H3862 (company), H3859 (wound), H3860 (for them)\nGreek Equivalents: G1577 ἐκκλησία",
    3863: "לוּא (lûwʼ | loo)\n\nDerivation: or לֻא; or לוּ\nStrong's: a conditional particle; if; by implication (interj. as a wish) would that!\nKJV: if (haply), peradventure, I pray thee, though, I would, would God (that).\n\nCognate Group: H3884 (except), H3863 (if), H3864 (Lubim), H3866 (Ludim), H3865 (Lud)\nGreek Equivalents: G3784 ὀφείλω",
    3864: "לוּבִי (Lûwbîy | loo-bee')\n\nDerivation: or לֻבִּי; (Daniel 11:43), partrial from a name probably derived from an unused root meaning to thirst, i.e. a dry region; apparently\nStrong's: a Libyan or inhabitant of interior Africa (only in plural)\nKJV: Lubim(-s), Libyans.\n\nCognate Group: H3884 (except), H3863 (if), H3864 (Lubim), H3866 (Ludim), H3865 (Lud)",
    3865: "לוּד (Lûwd | lood)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Lud, the name of two nations\nKJV: Lud, Lydia.\n\nCognate Group: H3884 (except), H3863 (if), H3864 (Lubim), H3866 (Ludim), H3865 (Lud)",
    3866: "לוּדִי (Lûwdîy | loo-dee')\n\nDerivation: or לוּדִיִּי; patrial from H3865 לוּד\nStrong's: a Ludite or inhabitants of Lud (only in plural)\nKJV: Ludim. Lydians.\n\nCognate Group: H3884 (except), H3863 (if), H3864 (Lubim), H3866 (Ludim), H3865 (Lud)",
    3867: "לָוָה (lâvâh | law-vaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to twine, i.e. (by implication) to unite, to remain; also to borrow (as a form of obligation) or (caus.) to lend\nKJV: abide with, borrow(-er), cleave, join (self), lend(-er).\n\nCognate Group: H3867 (abide with)\nGreek Equivalents: G1155 δανείζω, G2703 καταφεύγω, G4369 προστίθημι, G4388 προτίθεμαι, G5531 χράω",
    3868: "לוּז (lûwz | looz)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; (compare H3867 לָוָה, H3874 לוּט and H3885 לוּן)\n\nStrong's: to turn aside, i.e. (literally) to depart, (figuratively) be perverse\nKJV: depart, froward, perverse(-ness).\n\nCognate Group: H3869 (hazel), H3891 (perverse), H3870 (Luz), H3868 (depart)",
    3869: "לוּז (lûwz | looz)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: some kind of nuttree, perhaps the almond\nKJV: hazel.\n\nCognate Group: H3869 (hazel), H3891 (perverse), H3870 (Luz), H3868 (depart)\nGreek Equivalents: G1111 γογγύζω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G3007 λείπω, G3901 παραῤῥυέω",
    3870: "לוּז (Lûwz | looz)\n\nDerivation: probably from H3869 לוּז (as growing there)\nStrong's: Luz, the name of two places in Palestine\nKJV: Luz.\n\nCognate Group: H3869 (hazel), H3891 (perverse), H3870 (Luz), H3868 (depart)",
    3871: "לוּחַ (lûwach | loo'-akh)\n\nDerivation: or לֻחַ; from a primitive root\nStrong's: probably meaning to glisten; a tablet (as polished), of stone, wood or metal\nKJV: board, plate, table.\n\nCognate Group: H3872 (Luhith), H3871 (board)\nGreek Equivalents: G746 ἀρχή, G4109 πλάξ, G4114 πλάτος, G4548 σανίς",
    3872: "לוּחִית (Lûwchîyth | loo-kheeth')\n\nDerivation: or לֻחֹות; (Jeremiah 48:5), from the same as H3871 לוּחַ ; floored\nStrong's: Luchith, a place East of the Jordan\nKJV: Luhith.\n\nCognate Group: H3872 (Luhith), H3871 (board)",
    3873: "לֹוחֵשׁ (Lôwchêsh | lo-khashe')\n\nDerivation: active participle of H3907 לָחַשׁ ; (the) enchanter\nStrong's: Lochesh, an Israelite\nKJV: Hallohesh, Haloshesh (includ. the article).\n\nCognate Group: H3910 (myrrh), H3908 (charmed), H3907 (charmer), H3873 (Hallohesh)",
    3874: "לוּט (lûwṭ | loot)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to wrap up\nKJV: cast, wrap.\n\nCognate Group: H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)\nGreek Equivalents: G1750 ἐνειλέω, G1943 ἐπικαλύπτω",
    3875: "לֹוט (lôwṭ | lote)\n\nDerivation: from H3874 לוּט\nStrong's: a veil\nKJV: covering.\n\nCognate Group: H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)",
    3876: "לֹוט (Lôwṭ | lote)\n\nDerivation: the same as H3875 לֹוט\nStrong's: Lot, Abraham's nephew\nKJV: Lot.\n\nCognate Group: H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)\nGreek Equivalents: G3091 Λώτ",
    3877: "לֹוטָן (Lôwṭân | lo-tawn')\n\nDerivation: from H3875 לֹוט ; covering\nStrong's: Lotan, an Idumaean\nKJV: Lotan.\n\nCognate Group: H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)",
    3878: "לֵוִי (Lêvîy | lay-vee')\n\nDerivation: from H3867 לָוָה ; attached\nStrong's: Levi, a son of Jacob\nKJV: Levi. See also H3879 לֵוִי, H3881 לֵוִיִּי .\n\nCognate Group: H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)\nGreek Equivalents: G3017 Λευΐ, G3018 Λευΐς",
    3879: "לֵוִי (Lêvîy | lay-vee')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3880 לִוְיָה \nStrong's: something attached, i.e. a wreath\nKJV: Levite.\n\nCognate Group: H3904 (concubine), H3861 (but), H3916 (night), H3900 (feast), H3879 (Levite), H3961 (language), H3890 ([idiom] thee)",
    3880: "לִוְיָה (livyâh | liv-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H3867 לָוָה\nStrong's: something attached, i.e. a wreath\nKJV: ornament.\n\nCognate Group: H3882 (leviathan), H3914 (addition), H3880 (ornament)\nGreek Equivalents: G4735 στέφανος",
    3881: "לֵוִיִּי (Lêvîyîy | lay-vee-ee')\n\nDerivation: or לֵוִי; patronymically from H3878 לֵוִי\nStrong's: a Levite or descendant of Levi\nKJV: Leviite.\n\nCognate Group: H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)",
    3882: "לִוְיָתָן (livyâthân | liv-yaw-thawn')\n\nDerivation: from H3867 לָוָה\nStrong's: a wreathed animal, i.e. a serpent (especially the crocodile or some other large sea-monster); figuratively, the constellation of the dragon; also as a symbol of Babylon\nKJV: leviathan, mourning.\n\nCognate Group: H3882 (leviathan), H3914 (addition), H3880 (ornament)\nGreek Equivalents: G1404 δράκων, G2785 κῆτος, G3173 μέγας",
    3883: "לוּל (lûwl | lool)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to fold back\nStrong's: a spiral step\nKJV: winding stair. Compare H3924 לֻלָאָה .\n\nCognate Group: H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)",
    3884: "לוּלֵא (lûwlêʼ | loo-lay')\n\nDerivation: or לוּלֵי; from H3863 לוּא and H3808 לֹא\nStrong's: if not\nKJV: except, had not, if (...not), unless, were it not that.\n\nCognate Group: H3884 (except), H3863 (if), H3864 (Lubim), H3866 (Ludim), H3865 (Lud)",
    3885: "לוּן (lûwn | loon)\n\nDerivation: or לִין; a primitive root\nStrong's: to stop (usually over night); by implication, to stay permanently; hence (in a bad sense) to be obstinate (especially in words, to complain)\nKJV: abide (all night), continue, dwell, endure, grudge, be left, lie all night, (cause to) lodge (all night, in, -ing, this night), (make to) murmur, remain, tarry (all night, that night).\n\nCognate Group: H3885 (abide), H4411 (inn), H4412 (cottage)\nGreek Equivalents: G835 αὐλίζομαι, G1111 γογγύζω, G1234 διαγογγύζω, G2646 κατάλυμα, G2647 καταλύω, G2664 καταπαύω, G2837 κοιμάω, G3306 μένω, G4016 περιβάλλω, G5225 ὑπάρχω",
    3886: "לוּעַ (lûwaʻ | loo'-ah)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to gulp; figuratively, to be rash\nKJV: swallow down (up).\n\nCognate Group: H3886 (swallow down), H3930 (throat)\nGreek Equivalents: G2597 καταβαίνω, G5337 φαῦλος",
    3887: "לוּץ (lûwts | loots)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to make mouths at, i.e. to scoff; hence (from the effort to pronounce a foreign language) to interpret, or (generally) intercede\nKJV: ambassador, have in derision, interpreter, make a mock, mocker, scorn(-er, -ful), teacher.\n\nCognate Group: H3945 (scorn), H3944 (scornful), H3887 (ambassador), H4426 (interpretation)\nGreek Equivalents: G213 ἀλαζών, G498 ἀντιτάσσομαι, G521 ἀπαίδευτος, G758 ἄρχων, G878 ἄφρων, G2059 ἑρμηνεύω, G2556 κακός, G3061 λοιμός, G3891 παρανομέω, G4246 πρεσβύτης, G5244 ὑπερήφανος",
    3888: "לוּשׁ (lûwsh | loosh)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to knead\nKJV: knead.\n\nCognate Group: H3888 (knead)",
    3889: "לוּשׁ (Lûwsh | loosh)\n\nDerivation: from H3888 לוּשׁ ; kneading\nStrong's: Lush, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Laish (from the margin). Compare H3919 לַיִשׁ .\n\nCognate Group: H3919 (Laish), H3889 (Laish), H3918 (lion)",
    3890: "לְוָת (lᵉvâth | lev-awth')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H3867 לָוָה\nStrong's: properly, adhesion, i.e. (as preposition) with\nKJV: [idiom] thee.\n\nCognate Group: H3904 (concubine), H3861 (but), H3916 (night), H3900 (feast), H3879 (Levite), H3961 (language), H3890 ([idiom] thee)",
    3891: "לְזוּת (lᵉzûwth | lez-ooth')\n\nDerivation: from H3868 לוּז\nStrong's: perverseness\nKJV: perverse.\n\nCognate Group: H3869 (hazel), H3891 (perverse), H3870 (Luz), H3868 (depart)\nGreek Equivalents: G94 ἄδικος",
    3892: "לַח (lach | lakh)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be new\nStrong's: fresh, i.e. unused or undried\nKJV: green, moist.\n\nCognate Group: H3892 (green), H3893 (natural force)\nGreek Equivalents: G4372 πρόσφατος, G5200 ὑγρός, G5515 χλωρός",
    3893: "לֵחַ (lêach | lay'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3892 לַח\nStrong's: freshness, i.e. vigor\nKJV: natural force.\n\nCognate Group: H3892 (green), H3893 (natural force)",
    3894: "לָחוּם (lâchûwm | law-khoom')\n\nDerivation: or לָחֻם; passive participle of H3898 לָחַם\nStrong's: properly, eaten, i.e. food; also flesh, i.e. body\nKJV: while...is eating, flesh.\n\nCognate Group: H3901 (war), H3898 (devour), H4421 (battle), H3894 (while)\nGreek Equivalents: G4561 σάρξ",
    3895: "לְחִי (lᵉchîy | lekh-ee')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be soft\nStrong's: the cheek (from its fleshiness); hence, the jaw-bone\nKJV: cheek (bone), jaw (bone).\n\nCognate Group: H3895 (cheek), H3896 (Lehi)\nGreek Equivalents: G4600 σιαγών, G5491 χεῖλος",
    3896: "לֶחִי (Lechîy | lekh'-ee)\n\nDerivation: a form of H3895 לְחִי\nStrong's: Lechi, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Lehi. Compare also H7437 רָמַת לֶחִי .\n\nCognate Group: H3895 (cheek), H3896 (Lehi)",
    3897: "לָחַךְ (lâchak | law-khak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to lick\nKJV: lick (up).\n\nCognate Group: H3897 (lick)",
    3898: "לָחַם (lâcham | law-kham')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to feed on; figuratively, to consume; by implication, to battle (as destruction)\nKJV: devour, eat, [idiom] ever, fight(-ing), overcome, prevail, (make) war(-ring).\n\nCognate Group: H3901 (war), H3898 (devour), H4421 (battle), H3894 (while)\nGreek Equivalents: G1035 βρῶσις, G1172 δειπνέω, G1264 διαμάχομαι, G2186 ἐφίστημι, G3164 μάχομαι, G3960 πατάσσω, G4160 ποιέω, G4170 πολεμέω, G4776 συγκαθίζω",
    3899: "לֶחֶם (lechem | lekh'-em)\n\nDerivation: from H3898 לָחַם ; See also H1036 בֵּית לְעַפְרָה \nStrong's: food (for man or beast), especially bread, or grain (for making it)\nKJV: (shew-) bread, [idiom] eat, food, fruit, loaf, meat, victuals.\n\nCognate Group: H3902 (Lahmi), H3898 (devour), H3903 (Lahmam), H3899 (bread)\nGreek Equivalents: G712 ἄριστον, G740 ἄρτος, G979 βίος, G1163 δεῖ, G1173 δεῖπνον, G1403 δοχή, G1435 δῶρον, G2222 ζωή, G3145 μασσάομαι, G4621 σῖτος, G4621 σῖτος, G5132 τράπεζα, G5160 τροφή",
    3900: "לְחֶם (lᵉchem | lekh-em')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3899 לֶחֶם \nStrong's: (for man or beast), especially bread, or grain (for making it)\nKJV: feast.\n\nCognate Group: H3904 (concubine), H3861 (but), H3916 (night), H3900 (feast), H3879 (Levite), H3961 (language), H3890 ([idiom] thee)",
    3901: "לָחֶם (lâchem | law-khem')\n\nDerivation: from H3898 לָחַם,\nStrong's: battle\nKJV: war.\n\nCognate Group: H3901 (war), H3898 (devour), H4421 (battle), H3894 (while)",
    3902: "לַחְמִי (Lachmîy | lakh-mee')\n\nDerivation: from H3899 לֶחֶם ; foodful; (or perhaps erroneous transcription) for H1022 בֵּית הַלַּחְמִי \nStrong's: Lachmi, an Israelite; or rather probably a brief form\nKJV: Lahmi. See also H3433 יָשֻׁבִי לֶחֶם .\n\nCognate Group: H3902 (Lahmi), H3898 (devour), H3903 (Lahmam), H3899 (bread)",
    3903: "לַחְמָס (Lachmâç | lakh-maws')\n\nDerivation: probably by erroneous transcription for לַחְמָם; from H3899 לֶחֶם ; food-like\nStrong's: Lachmam or Lachmas, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Lahmam.\n\nCognate Group: H3902 (Lahmi), H3898 (devour), H3903 (Lahmam), H3899 (bread)",
    3904: "לְחֵנָה (lᵉchênâh | lekh-ay-naw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from an unused root of uncertain meaning\nStrong's: a concubine\nKJV: concubine.\n\nCognate Group: H3904 (concubine), H3861 (but), H3916 (night), H3900 (feast), H3879 (Levite), H3961 (language), H3890 ([idiom] thee)",
    3905: "לָחַץ (lâchats | law-khats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to press, i.e. (figuratively) to distress\nKJV: afflict, crush, force, hold fast, oppress(-or), thrust self.\n\nCognate Group: H3905 (afflict), H3906 (affliction)\nGreek Equivalents: G598 ἀποθλίβω, G2559 κακόω",
    3906: "לַחַץ (lachats | lakh'-ats)\n\nDerivation: from H3905 לָחַץ\nStrong's: distress\nKJV: affliction, oppression.\n\nCognate Group: H3905 (afflict), H3906 (affliction)\nGreek Equivalents: G2347 θλῖψις, G4728 στενός",
    3907: "לָחַשׁ (lâchash | law-khash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to whisper; by implication, to mumble aspell (as a magician)\nKJV: charmer, whisper (together).\n\nCognate Group: H3910 (myrrh), H3908 (charmed), H3907 (charmer), H3873 (Hallohesh)",
    3908: "לַחַשׁ (lachash | lakh'-ash)\n\nDerivation: from H3907 לָחַשׁ\nStrong's: properly, a whisper, i.e. by implication, (in a good sense) a private prayer, (in a bad one) an incantation; concretely, an amulet\nKJV: charmed, earring, enchantment, orator, prayer.\n\nCognate Group: H3910 (myrrh), H3908 (charmed), H3907 (charmer), H3873 (Hallohesh)\nGreek Equivalents: G202 ἀκροατής, G5587 ψιθυρισμός",
    3909: "לָט (lâṭ | lawt)\n\nDerivation: a form of H3814 לָאט or else participle from H3874 לוּט\nStrong's: properly, covered, i.e. secret; by implication, incantation; also secrecy or (adverb) covertly\nKJV: enchantment, privily, secretly, softly.\n\nCognate Group: H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)",
    3910: "לֹט (lôṭ | lote)\n\nDerivation: probably from H3874 לוּט\nStrong's: a gum (from its sticky nature), probably ladanum\nKJV: myrrh.\n\nCognate Group: H3910 (myrrh), H3908 (charmed), H3907 (charmer), H3873 (Hallohesh)",
    3911: "לְטָאָה (lᵉṭâʼâh | let-aw-aw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to hide\nStrong's: a kind of lizard (from its covert habits)\nKJV: lizard.\n\nCognate Group: H3911 (lizard)",
    3912: "לְטוּשִׁם (Lᵉṭûwshim | let-oo-sheem')\n\nDerivation: masculine plural of passive participle of H3913 לָטַשׁ ; hammered (i.e. oppressed) ones\nStrong's: Letushim, an Arabian tribe\nKJV: Letushim.\n\nCognate Group: H3912 (Letushim), H3913 (instructer), H3915 (night), H3917 (screech owl)",
    3913: "לָטַשׁ (lâṭash | law-tash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to hammer out (an edge), i.e. to sharpen\nKJV: instructer, sharp(-en), whet.\n\nCognate Group: H3912 (Letushim), H3913 (instructer), H3915 (night), H3917 (screech owl)",
    3914: "לֹיָה (lôyâh | lo-yaw')\n\nDerivation: a form of H3880 לִוְיָה\nStrong's: a wreath\nKJV: addition.\n\nCognate Group: H3882 (leviathan), H3914 (addition), H3880 (ornament)",
    3915: "לַיִל (layil | lah'-yil)\n\nDerivation: or (Isaiah 21:11) לֵיל; also לַיְלָה; from the same as H3883 לוּל\nStrong's: properly, a twist (away of the light), i.e. night; figuratively, adversity\nKJV: (mid-)night (season).\n\nCognate Group: H3912 (Letushim), H3913 (instructer), H3915 (night), H3917 (screech owl)\nGreek Equivalents: G3571 νύξ",
    3916: "לֵילְיָא (lêylᵉyâʼ | lay-leh-yaw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3815 לָאֵל \nStrong's: Lael an Israelite\nKJV: night.\n\nCognate Group: H3904 (concubine), H3861 (but), H3916 (night), H3900 (feast), H3879 (Levite), H3961 (language), H3890 ([idiom] thee)\nGreek Equivalents: G3571 νύξ",
    3917: "לִילִית (lîylîyth | lee-leeth')\n\nDerivation: from H3915 לַיִל\nStrong's: a night spectre\nKJV: screech owl.\n\nCognate Group: H3912 (Letushim), H3913 (instructer), H3915 (night), H3917 (screech owl)",
    3918: "לַיִשׁ (layish | lah'-yish)\n\nDerivation: from H3888 לוּשׁ in the sense of crushing\nStrong's: a lion (from his destructive blows)\nKJV: (old) lion.\n\nCognate Group: H3919 (Laish), H3889 (Laish), H3918 (lion)",
    3919: "לַיִשׁ (Layish | lah'-yish)\n\nDerivation: the same as H3918 לַיִשׁ\nStrong's: Laish, the name of two places in Palestine\nKJV: Laish. Compare H3889 לוּשׁ .\n\nCognate Group: H3919 (Laish), H3889 (Laish), H3918 (lion)",
    3920: "לָכַד (lâkad | law-kad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to catch (in a net, trap or pit); generally, to capture or occupy; also to choose (by lot); figuratively, to cohere\nKJV: [idiom] at all, catch (self), be frozen, be holden, stick together, take.\n\nCognate Group: H3920 ([idiom] at all), H3922 (Lecah), H4434 (trap), H3921 (being taken), H3923 (Lachish)\nGreek Equivalents: G64 ἀγρεύω, G726 ἁρπάζω, G1166 δεικνύω, G1731 ἐνδείκνυμι, G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G2722 κατέχω, G2816 κληρονομέω, G2820 κληρόω, G2902 κρατέω, G2961 κυριεύω, G2975 λαγχάνω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3960 πατάσσω, G4815 συλλαμβάνω, G4912 συνέχω",
    3921: "לֶכֶד (leked | leh'ked)\n\nDerivation: from H3920 לָכַד\nStrong's: something to capture with, i.e. a noose\nKJV: being taken.\n\nCognate Group: H3920 ([idiom] at all), H3922 (Lecah), H4434 (trap), H3921 (being taken), H3923 (Lachish)\nGreek Equivalents: G4531 σαλεύω",
    3922: "לֵכָה (lêkâh | lay-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from H3212 יָלַךְ ; a journey\nStrong's: Lekah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Lecah.\n\nCognate Group: H3920 ([idiom] at all), H3922 (Lecah), H4434 (trap), H3921 (being taken), H3923 (Lachish)",
    3923: "לָכִישׁ (Lâkîysh | law-keesh')\n\nTypo: xlit Lâchîysh corrected to Lâkîysh\n\nDerivation: from an unused root of uncertain meaning\nStrong's: Lakish, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Lachish.\n\nCognate Group: H3920 ([idiom] at all), H3922 (Lecah), H4434 (trap), H3921 (being taken), H3923 (Lachish)",
    3924: "לֻלָאָה (lulâʼâh | loo-law-aw')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3883 לוּל\nStrong's: a loop\nKJV: loop.\n\nCognate Group: H3924 (loop)",
    3925: "לָמַד (lâmad | law-mad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to goad, i.e. (by implication) to teach (the rod being an Oriental incentive)\nKJV: (un-) accustomed, [idiom] diligently, expert, instruct, learn, skilful, teach(-er, -ing).\n\nCognate Group: H3927 (Lemuel), H3928 (accustomed), H3929 (Lamech), H3925 (accustomed), H4451 (goad), H8527 (scholar)\nGreek Equivalents: G1166 δεικνύω, G1319 διδασκαλία, G1321 διδάσκω, G1322 διδαχή, G3129 μανθάνω",
    3926: "לְמֹו (lᵉmôw | lem-o')\n\nDerivation: a prolonged and separable form of the prepositional prefix\nStrong's: to or for\nKJV: at, for, to, upon.\n\nCognate Group: H3926 (at)",
    3927: "לְמוּאֵל (Lᵉmûwʼêl | lem-oo-ale')\n\nDerivation: or לְמֹואֵל; from H3926 לְמֹו and H410 אֵל ; (belonging) to God\nStrong's: Lemuel or Lemoel, a symbolic name of Solomon\nKJV: Lemuel.\n\nCognate Group: H3927 (Lemuel), H3928 (accustomed), H3929 (Lamech), H3925 (accustomed), H4451 (goad), H8527 (scholar)",
    3928: "לִמּוּד (limmûwd | lim-mood')\n\nDerivation: or לִמֻּד; from H3925 לָמַד\nStrong's: instructed\nKJV: accustomed, disciple, learned, taught, used.\n\nCognate Group: H3927 (Lemuel), H3928 (accustomed), H3929 (Lamech), H3925 (accustomed), H4451 (goad), H8527 (scholar)\nGreek Equivalents: G1318 διδακτός, G3809 παιδεία",
    3929: "לֶמֶךְ (Lemek | leh'-mek)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root of uncertain meaning\nStrong's: Lemek, the name of two antediluvian patriarchs\nKJV: Lamech.\n\nCognate Group: H3927 (Lemuel), H3928 (accustomed), H3929 (Lamech), H3925 (accustomed), H4451 (goad), H8527 (scholar)\nGreek Equivalents: G2984 Λάμεχ",
    3930: "לֹעַ (lôaʻ | lo'ah)\n\nDerivation: from H3886 לוּעַ\nStrong's: the gullet\nKJV: throat.\n\nCognate Group: H3886 (swallow down), H3930 (throat)",
    3931: "לָעַב (lâʻab | law-ab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to deride\nKJV: mock.\n\nCognate Group: H3931 (mock)\nGreek Equivalents: G3456 μυκτηρίζω",
    3932: "לָעַג (lâʻag | law-ag')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to deride; by implication (as if imitating a foreigner) to speak unintelligibly\nKJV: have in derision, laugh (to scorn), mock (on), stammering.\n\nCognate Group: H3934 (mocker), H3933 (derision), H3936 (Laadan), H3935 (Laadah), H3932 (have in derision)\nGreek Equivalents: G1592 ἐκμυκτηρίζω, G2606 καταγελάω, G3456 μυκτηρίζω",
    3933: "לַעַג (laʻag | lah'-ag)\n\nDerivation: from H3932 לָעַג\nStrong's: derision, scoffing\nKJV: derision, scorn (-ing).\n\nCognate Group: H3934 (mocker), H3933 (derision), H3936 (Laadan), H3935 (Laadah), H3932 (have in derision)\nGreek Equivalents: G3681 ὄνειδος",
    3934: "לָעֵג (lâʻêg | law-ayg')\n\nDerivation: from H3932 לָעַג\nStrong's: a buffoon; also a foreigner\nKJV: mocker, stammering.\n\nCognate Group: H3934 (mocker), H3933 (derision), H3936 (Laadan), H3935 (Laadah), H3932 (have in derision)",
    3935: "לַעְדָּה (Laʻdâh | lah-daw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root of uncertain meaning\nStrong's: Ladah, an Israelite\nKJV: Laadah.\n\nCognate Group: H3934 (mocker), H3933 (derision), H3936 (Laadan), H3935 (Laadah), H3932 (have in derision)",
    3936: "לַעְדָּן (Laʻdân | lah-dawn')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3935 לַעְדָּה\nStrong's: Ladan, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Laadan.\n\nCognate Group: H3934 (mocker), H3933 (derision), H3936 (Laadan), H3935 (Laadah), H3932 (have in derision)",
    3937: "לָעַז (lâʻaz | law-az')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to speak in a foreign tongue\nKJV: strange language.\n\nCognate Group: H3937 (strange language)\nGreek Equivalents: G915 βάρβαρος",
    3938: "לָעַט (lâʻaṭ | law-at')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to swallow greedily; causatively, to feed\nKJV: feed.\n\nCognate Group: H3938 (feed), H3939 (hemlock)\nGreek Equivalents: G1089 γεύομαι, G2928 κρύπτω, G5339 φείδομαι",
    3939: "לַעֲנָה (laʻănâh | lah-an-aw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root supposed to mean to curse\nStrong's: wormwood (regarded as poisonous, and therefore accursed)\nKJV: hemlock, wormwood.\n\nCognate Group: H3938 (feed), H3939 (hemlock)\nGreek Equivalents: G318 ἀνάγκη, G3601 ὀδύνη, G4088 πικρία, G5521 χολή",
    3940: "לַפִּיד (lappîyd | lap-peed')\n\nDerivation: or לַפִּד; from an unused root probably meaning to shine\nStrong's: a flambeau, lamp or flame\nKJV: (fire-) brand, (burning) lamp, lightning, torch.\n\nCognate Group: H3940 (brand), H3941 (Lappidoth)\nGreek Equivalents: G2985 λαμπάς",
    3941: "לַפִּידֹות (Lappîydôwth | lap-pee-doth')\n\nDerivation: feminine plural of H3940 לַפִּיד\nStrong's: Lappidoth, the husband of Deborah\nKJV: Lappidoth.\n\nCognate Group: H3940 (brand), H3941 (Lappidoth)",
    3942: "לִפְנַי (liphnay | lif-nah'ee)\n\nDerivation: from the prepositional prefix (to or for) and H6440 פָּנִים\nStrong's: anterior\nKJV: before.\n\nCognate Group: H3312 (Jephunneh), H6437 (appear), H6441 (inner), H3942 (before), H6442 (inner), H6440 (accept), H6439 (Peniel)",
    3943: "לָפַת (lâphath | law-fath')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to bend, i.e. (by implication) to clasp; also (reflexively) to turn around or aside\nKJV: take hold, turn aside (self).\n\nCognate Group: H3943 (take hold), H3946 (Lakum)\nGreek Equivalents: G2641 καταλείπω, G5015 ταράσσω",
    3944: "לָצֹון (lâtsôwn | law-tsone')\n\nDerivation: from H3887 לוּץ\nStrong's: derision\nKJV: scornful(-ning).\n\nCognate Group: H3945 (scorn), H3944 (scornful), H3887 (ambassador), H4426 (interpretation)\nGreek Equivalents: G459 ἄνομος, G2346 θλίβω, G5196 ὕβρις",
    3945: "לָצַץ (lâtsats | law-tsats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to deride\nKJV: scorn.\n\nCognate Group: H3945 (scorn), H3944 (scornful), H3887 (ambassador), H4426 (interpretation)",
    3946: "לַקּוּם (Laqqûwm | lak-koom')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root thought to mean to stop up by a barricade; perhaps fortification\nStrong's: Lakkum, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Lakum.\n\nCognate Group: H3943 (take hold), H3946 (Lakum)",
    3947: "לָקַח (lâqach | law-kakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to take (in the widest variety of applications)\nKJV: accept, bring, buy, carry away, drawn, fetch, get, infold, [idiom] many, mingle, place, receive(-ing), reserve, seize, send for, take (away, -ing, up), use, win.\n\nCognate Group: H3949 (Likhi), H3947 (accept), H4728 (ware), H4727 (taking), H4455 (booty), H3948 (doctrine), H4457 (snuffers)\nGreek Equivalents: G59 ἀγοράζω, G59 ἀγοράζω, G64 ἀγρεύω, G71 ἄγω, G142 αἴρω, G162 αἰχμαλωτεύω, G337 ἀναιρέω, G353 ἀναλαμβάνω, G385 ἀνασπάω, G618 ἀπολαμβάνω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G667 ἀποφέρω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G1096 γίνομαι, G1097 γινώσκω, G1209 δέχομαι, G1521 εἰσάγω, G1525 εἰσέρχομαι, G1544 ἐκβάλλω, G1586 ἐκλέγομαι, G1627 ἐκφέρω, G1806 ἐξάγω, G1807 ἐξαιρέω, G1823 ἐξαστράπτω, G1831 ἐξέρχομαι, G1856 ἐξωθέω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G2192 ἔχω, G2564 καλέω, G2598 καταβάλλω, G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G2865 κομίζω, G2932 κτάομαι, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3343 μεταπέμπω, G3346 μετατίθημι, G3557 νοσφίζομαι, G3811 παιδεύω, G3880 παραλαμβάνω, G4317 προσάγω, G4327 προσδέχομαι, G4355 προσλαμβάνω, G4400 προχειρίζομαι, G4815 συλλαμβάνω, G4816 συλλέγω, G4879 συναπάγω, G4884 συναρπάζω, G5111 τολμάω, G5342 φέρω, G5394 φλογίζω",
    3948: "לֶקַח (leqach | leh'-kakh)\n\nDerivation: from H3947 לָקַח\nStrong's: properly, something received, i.e. (mentally) instruction (whether on the part of the teacher or hearer); also (in an active and sinister sense) inveiglement\nKJV: doctrine, learning, fair speech.\n\nCognate Group: H3949 (Likhi), H3947 (accept), H4728 (ware), H4727 (taking), H4455 (booty), H3948 (doctrine), H4457 (snuffers)\nGreek Equivalents: G191 ἀκούω, G1435 δῶρον, G1515 εἰρήνη, G2041 ἔργον, G3657 ὁμιλία",
    3949: "לִקְחִי (Liqchîy | lik-khee')\n\nDerivation: from H3947 לָקַח ; learned\nStrong's: Likchi, an Israelite\nKJV: Likhi.\n\nCognate Group: H3949 (Likhi), H3947 (accept), H4728 (ware), H4727 (taking), H4455 (booty), H3948 (doctrine), H4457 (snuffers)",
    3950: "לָקַט (lâqaṭ | law-kat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to pick up, i.e. (generally) to gather; specifically, to glean\nKJV: gather (up), glean.\n\nCognate Group: H3219 (scrip), H3950 (gather), H3951 (gleaning)\nGreek Equivalents: G1533 εἰσφέρω, G4816 συλλέγω, G4863 συνάγω, G4962 συστρέφω",
    3951: "לֶקֶט (leqeṭ | leh'-ket)\n\nDerivation: from H3950 לָקַט\nStrong's: the gleaning\nKJV: gleaning.\n\nCognate Group: H3219 (scrip), H3950 (gather), H3951 (gleaning)\nGreek Equivalents: G634 ἀποπίπτω",
    3952: "לָקַק (lâqaq | law-kak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to lick or lap\nKJV: lap, lick.\n\nCognate Group: H3952 (lap)",
    3953: "לָקַשׁ (lâqash | law-kash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to gather the after crop\nKJV: gather.\n\nCognate Group: H3954 (latter growth), H4456 (latter rain), H3953 (gather)\nGreek Equivalents: G2038 ἐργάζομαι",
    3954: "לֶקֶשׁ (leqesh | leh'-kesh)\n\nDerivation: from H3953 לָקַשׁ\nStrong's: the after crop\nKJV: latter growth.\n\nCognate Group: H3954 (latter growth), H4456 (latter rain), H3953 (gather)",
    3955: "לְשַׁד (lᵉshad | lesh-ad')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root of uncertain meaning; apparently juice, i.e.\nStrong's: (figuratively) vigor; also a sweet or fat cake\nKJV: fresh, moisture.\n\nCognate Group: H3955 (fresh)",
    3956: "לָשֹׁון (lâshôwn | law-shone')\n\nDerivation: or לָשֹׁן; also (in plural) feminine לְשֹׁנָה; from H3960 לָשַׁן\nStrong's: the tongue (of man or animals), used literally (as the instrument of licking, eating, or speech), and figuratively (speech, an ingot, a fork of flame, a cove of water)\nKJV: [phrase] babbler, bay, [phrase] evil speaker, language, talker, tongue, wedge.\n\nCognate Group: H3956 (babbler), H3962 (Lasha), H3960 (accuse)\nGreek Equivalents: G440 ἄνθραξ, G1100 γλῶσσα, G1258 διάλεκτος, G5456 φωνή",
    3957: "לִשְׁכָּה (lishkâh | lish-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root of uncertain meaning\nStrong's: a room in a building (whether for storage, eating, or lodging)\nKJV: chamber, parlour. Compare H5393 נִשְׁכָּה .\n\nCognate Group: H3957 (chamber), H3958 (ligure), H3959 (Leshem)\nGreek Equivalents: G833 αὐλή, G1049 γαζοφυλάκιον, G2344 θησαυρός, G2646 κατάλυμα, G3624 οἶκος",
    3958: "לֶשֶׁם (leshem | leh'-shem)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root of uncertain meaning\nStrong's: a gem, perhaps the jacinth\nKJV: ligure.\n\nCognate Group: H3957 (chamber), H3958 (ligure), H3959 (Leshem)",
    3959: "לֶשֶׁם (Leshem | leh'-shem)\n\nDerivation: the same as H3958 לֶשֶׁם\nStrong's: Leshem, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Leshem.\n\nCognate Group: H3957 (chamber), H3958 (ligure), H3959 (Leshem)",
    3960: "לָשַׁן (lâshan | law-shan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; properly, to lick; but used only as a denominative from H3956 לָשֹׁון\nStrong's: to wag the tongue, i.e. to calumniate\nKJV: accuse, slander.\n\nCognate Group: H3956 (babbler), H3962 (Lasha), H3960 (accuse)\nGreek Equivalents: G2635 καταλαλέω, G3860 παραδίδωμι",
    3961: "לִשָּׁן (lishshân | lish-shawn')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H3956 לָשֹׁון\nStrong's: speech, i.e. a nation\nKJV: language.\n\nCognate Group: H3904 (concubine), H3861 (but), H3916 (night), H3900 (feast), H3879 (Levite), H3961 (language), H3890 ([idiom] thee)",
    3962: "לֶשַׁע (Leshaʻ | leh'-shah)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root thought to mean to break through; a boiling spring\nStrong's: Lesha, a place probably East of the Jordan\nKJV: Lasha.\n\nCognate Group: H3956 (babbler), H3962 (Lasha), H3960 (accuse)",
    3963: "לֶתֶךְ (lethek | leh'-thek)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root of uncertain meaning\nStrong's: a measure for things dry\nKJV: half homer. m\n\nCognate Group: H3963 (half homer)",
    3964: "מָא (mâʼ | maw)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H4100 מָה\nStrong's: (as indefinitely) that\nKJV: [phrase] what.\n\nCognate Group: H4101 (how great), H4193 (death), H3964 (what)",
