    4022: "מֶגֶד (meged | meh'-ghed)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to be eminent\nStrong's: properly, a distinguished thing; hence something valuable, as aproduct or fruit\nKJV: pleasant, precious fruit (thing).\n\nCognate Group: H4022 (pleasant), H4025 (Magdiel), H4030 (precious thing), H4047 (Magpiash)\nGreek Equivalents: G5610 ὥρα",
    4023: "מְגִדֹּון (Mᵉgiddôwn | meg-id-done')\n\nDerivation: (Zechariah H12 אַבְדָן) or מְגִדֹּו; from H1413 גָּדַד ; rendezvous\nStrong's: Megiddon or Megiddo, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Megiddo, Megiddon.\n\nCognate Group: H1410 (Gad), H4023 (Megiddo), H1409 (troop), H1418 (cutting), H1426 (Gaddi), H1417 (furrow), H1427 (Gaddiel), H1413 (assemble), H1407 (coriander), H1424 (Gadi), H1425 (Gadites), H1408 (that troop), H1416 (army), H1412 (Gudgodah)\nGreek Equivalents: G717 Ἀρμαγεδδών",
    4024: "מִגְדֹּול (Migdôwl | mig-dole')\n\nDerivation: or מִגְדֹּל; probably of Egyptian origin\nStrong's: Migdol, a place in Egypt\nKJV: Migdol, tower.\n\nCognate Group: H4029 (Migdal-eder), H4024 (Migdol), H1419 (aloud), H1432 (great), H1433 (greatness), H4026 (castle), H1434 (fringe), H1420 (dignity), H4028 (Migdal-gad), H1431 (advance), H4027 (Migdal-el), H1435 (Giddel), H3012 (Igdaliah), H1436 (Gedaliah), H1437 (Giddalti)\nGreek Equivalents: G3093 Μαγδαλά",
    4025: "מַגְדִּיאֵל (Magdîyʼêl | mag-dee-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H4022 מֶגֶד and H410 אֵל ; preciousness of God\nStrong's: Magdiel, an Idumaean\nKJV: Magdiel.\n\nCognate Group: H4022 (pleasant), H4025 (Magdiel), H4030 (precious thing), H4047 (Magpiash)",
    4026: "מִגְדָּל (migdâl | mig-dawl')\n\nDerivation: also (in plural) feminine מִגְדָּלָה; from H1431 גָּדַל\nStrong's: a tower (from its size or height); by analogy, a rostrum; figuratively, a (pyramidal) bed of flowers\nKJV: castle, flower, tower. Compare the names following.\n\nCognate Group: H4029 (Migdal-eder), H4024 (Migdol), H1419 (aloud), H1432 (great), H1433 (greatness), H4026 (castle), H1434 (fringe), H1420 (dignity), H4028 (Migdal-gad), H1431 (advance), H4027 (Migdal-el), H1435 (Giddel), H3012 (Igdaliah), H1436 (Gedaliah), H1437 (Giddalti)\nGreek Equivalents: G968 βῆμα, G4444 πύργος, G3093 Μαγδαλά",
    4027: "מִגְדַּל־אֵל (Migdal-ʼÊl | mig-dal-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H4026 מִגְדָּל and H410 אֵל ; tower of God\nStrong's: Migdal-El, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Migdal-el.\n\nCognate Group: H4029 (Migdal-eder), H4024 (Migdol), H1419 (aloud), H1432 (great), H1433 (greatness), H4026 (castle), H1434 (fringe), H1420 (dignity), H4028 (Migdal-gad), H1431 (advance), H4027 (Migdal-el), H1435 (Giddel), H3012 (Igdaliah), H1436 (Gedaliah), H1437 (Giddalti)",
    4028: "מִגְדַּל־גָּד (Migdal-Gâd | migdal-gawd')\n\nDerivation: from H4026 מִגְדָּל and H1408 גַּד ; tower of Fortune\nStrong's: Migdal-Gad, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Migdal-gad.\n\nCognate Group: H4029 (Migdal-eder), H4024 (Migdol), H1419 (aloud), H1432 (great), H1433 (greatness), H4026 (castle), H1434 (fringe), H1420 (dignity), H4028 (Migdal-gad), H1431 (advance), H4027 (Migdal-el), H1435 (Giddel), H3012 (Igdaliah), H1436 (Gedaliah), H1437 (Giddalti)",
    4029: "מִגְדַּל־עֵדֶר (Migdal-ʻÊder | mig-dal'-ay'-der)\n\nDerivation: from H4026 מִגְדָּל and H5739 עֵדֶר ; tower of a flock\nStrong's: Migdal-Eder, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Migdal-eder, tower of the flock.\n\nCognate Group: H4029 (Migdal-eder), H4024 (Migdol), H1419 (aloud), H1432 (great), H1433 (greatness), H4026 (castle), H1434 (fringe), H1420 (dignity), H4028 (Migdal-gad), H1431 (advance), H4027 (Migdal-el), H1435 (Giddel), H3012 (Igdaliah), H1436 (Gedaliah), H1437 (Giddalti)",
    4030: "מִגְדָּנָה (migdânâh | mig-daw-naw')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H4022 מֶגֶד\nStrong's: preciousness, i.e. a gem\nKJV: precious thing, present.\n\nCognate Group: H4022 (pleasant), H4025 (Magdiel), H4030 (precious thing), H4047 (Magpiash)\nGreek Equivalents: G1390 δόμα, G1435 δῶρον",
    4031: "מָגֹוג (Mâgôwg | maw-gogue')\n\nDerivation: from H1463 גֹּוג\nStrong's: Magog, a son of Japheth; also a barbarous northern region\nKJV: Magog.\n\nCognate Group: H1463 (Gog), H1374 (Gebim), H1461 (husbandman), H1356 (beam), H4031 (Magog)\nGreek Equivalents: G1136 Γώγ, G3098 Μαγώγ",
    4032: "מָגֹור (mâgôwr | maw-gore')\n\nDerivation: or (Lamentations 2:22) מָגוּר; from H1481 גּוּר in the sense of fearing\nStrong's: a fright (objective or subjective)\nKJV: fear, terror. Compare H4036 מָגֹור מִסָּבִיב .\n\nCognate Group: H4032 (fear), H4034 (fear), H1481 (abide)\nGreek Equivalents: G684 ἀπώλεια, G3940 παροικία, G4867 συναθροίζω",
    4033: "מָגוּר (mâgûwr | maw-goor')\n\nDerivation: or מָגֻר; from H1481 גּוּר in the sense of lodging\nStrong's: a temporary abode; by extension, a permanent residence\nKJV: dwelling, pilgrimage, where sojourn, be a stranger. Compare H4032 מָגֹור .\n\nCognate Group: H1485 (Gur-baal), H3017 (Jagur), H1616 (alien), H1628 (habitation), H4460 (barn), H1483 (Gur), H4035 (barn), H4033 (dwelling), H1481 (abide)",
    4034: "מְגֹורַה (mᵉgôwrah | meg-o-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4032 מָגֹור\nStrong's: affright\nKJV: fear.\n\nCognate Group: H4032 (fear), H4034 (fear), H1481 (abide)",
    4035: "מְגוּרָה (mᵉgûwrâh | meg-oo-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4032 מָגֹור or of H4033 מָגוּר\nStrong's: a fright; also a granary\nKJV: barn, fear.\n\nCognate Group: H1485 (Gur-baal), H3017 (Jagur), H1616 (alien), H1628 (habitation), H4460 (barn), H1483 (Gur), H4035 (barn), H4033 (dwelling), H1481 (abide)\nGreek Equivalents: G2347 θλῖψις",
    4036: "מָגֹור מִסָּבִיב (Mâgôwr miç-Çâbîyb | maw-gore' mis-saw-beeb')\n\nDerivation: from H4032 מָגֹור and H5439 סָבִיב with the preposition inserted; affright from around\nStrong's: Magor-mis-Sabib, a symbolic name of Pashur\nKJV: Magormissabib.\n\nCognate Group: H5439 (about), H5437 (bring), H4142 (being changed), H5252 (cause), H4524 (that compass about), H4036 (Magormissabib), H5438 (cause), H4141 (winding about)",
    4037: "מַגְזֵרָה (magzêrâh | mag-zay-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H1504 גָּזַר\nStrong's: a cutting implement, i.e. a blade\nKJV: axe.\n\nCognate Group: H1507 (Gazer), H1504 (cut down), H1511 (Gezrites), H1506 (part), H1509 (not inhabited), H1508 (polishing), H4037 (axe)",
    4038: "מַגָּל (maggâl | mag-gawl')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to reap\nStrong's: a sickle\nKJV: sickle.\n\nCognate Group: H4038 (sickle)\nGreek Equivalents: G1407 δρέπανον",
    4039: "מְגִלָּה (mᵉgillâh | meg-il-law')\n\nDerivation: from H1556 גָּלַל\nStrong's: a roll\nKJV: roll, volume.\n\nCognate Group: H1019 (Beth-gilgal), H1551 (Galilee), H1557 (dung), H1550 (folding), H1543 (bowl), H1559 (Galal), H4039 (roll), H1530 (billow), H1567 (Galeed), H1537 (Gilgal), H1553 (Geliloth), H1538 (head), H1561 (dung), H1562 (Gilalai), H1552 (border), H1554 (Gallim), H1556 (commit), H1544 (idol), H1536 (wheel), H1534 (heaven), H1531 (bowl)\nGreek Equivalents: G975 βιβλίον, G2777 κεφαλίς, G5489 χάρτης",
    4040: "מְגִלָּה (mᵉgillâh | meg-il-law')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H4039 מְגִלָּה \nStrong's: a roll\nKJV: roll.\n\nCognate Group: H1560 (great), H4040 (roll), H1535 (wheel)",
    4041: "מְגַמָּה (mᵉgammâh | meg-am-maw')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H1571 גַּם\nStrong's: properly, accumulation, i.e. impulse or direction\nKJV: sup up.\n\nCognate Group: H1571 (again), H4041 (sup up)",
    4042: "מָגַן (mâgan | maw-gan')\n\nDerivation: a denominative from H4043 מָגֵן\nStrong's: properly, to shield; encompass with; figuratively, to rescue, to hand safely over (i.e. surrender)\nKJV: deliver.\n\nCognate Group: H1599 (Ginnetho), H1598 (defend), H1594 (garden), H4042 (deliver), H4043 ([idiom] armed), H1588 (garden), H1527 (Ginath), H1593 (garden), H4044 (sorrow)\nGreek Equivalents: G3860 παραδίδωμι",
    4043: "מָגֵן (mâgên | maw-gane')\n\nDerivation: also (in plural) feminine מְגִנָּה; from H1598 גָּנַן\nStrong's: a shield (i.e. the small one or buckler); figuratively, a protector; also the scaly hide of the crocodile\nKJV: [idiom] armed, buckler, defence, ruler, [phrase] scale, shield.\n\nCognate Group: H1599 (Ginnetho), H1598 (defend), H1594 (garden), H4042 (deliver), H4043 ([idiom] armed), H1588 (garden), H1527 (Ginath), H1593 (garden), H4044 (sorrow)\nGreek Equivalents: G484 ἀντίληψις, G996 βοήθεια, G2375 θυρεός, G2900 κραταιός, G3696 ὅπλον",
    4044: "מְגִנָּה (mᵉginnâh | meg-in-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H4042 מָגַן\nStrong's: a covering (in a bad sense), i.e. blindness or obduracy\nKJV: sorrow. See also H4043 מָגֵן .\n\nCognate Group: H1599 (Ginnetho), H1598 (defend), H1594 (garden), H4042 (deliver), H4043 ([idiom] armed), H1588 (garden), H1527 (Ginath), H1593 (garden), H4044 (sorrow)",
    4045: "מִגְעֶרֶת (migʻereth | mig-eh'-reth)\n\nDerivation: from H1605 גָּעַר\nStrong's: reproof (i.e. curse)\nKJV: rebuke.\n\nCognate Group: H1606 (rebuke), H1605 (corrupt), H4045 (rebuke)",
    4046: "מַגֵּפָה (maggêphâh | mag-gay-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H5062 נָגַף\nStrong's: a pestilence; by analogy, defeat\nKJV: ([idiom] be) plague(-d), slaughter, stroke.\n\nCognate Group: H4046 (plague), H5063 (plague), H5062 (beat)\nGreek Equivalents: G684 ἀπώλεια, G4127 πληγή",
    4047: "מַגְפִּיעָשׁ (Magpîyʻâsh | mag-pee-awsh')\n\nDerivation: apparently from H1479 גּוּף or H5062 נָגַף and H6211 עָשׁ ; exterminator of (the) moth\nStrong's: Magpiash, an Israelite\nKJV: Magpiash.\n\nCognate Group: H4022 (pleasant), H4025 (Magdiel), H4030 (precious thing), H4047 (Magpiash)",
    4048: "מָגַר (mâgar | maw-gar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to yield up; intensively, to precipitate\nKJV: cast down, terror.\n\nCognate Group: H4051 (Migron), H4048 (cast down)",
    4049: "מְגַר (mᵉgar | meg-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H4048 מָגַר\nStrong's: to overthrow\nKJV: destroy.\n\nCognate Group: H4076 (Mede), H4049 (destroy), H3969 (hundred), H4077 (Median), H3984 (vessel)\nGreek Equivalents: G2690 καταστρέφω",
    4050: "מְגֵרָה (mᵉgêrâh | meg-ay-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H1641 גָּרַר\nStrong's: a saw\nKJV: axe, saw.\n\nCognate Group: H1641 (catch), H1625 (cud), H4050 (axe), H1642 (Gerar), H1626 (gerah), H1621 (neck), H1620 (berry)",
    4051: "מִגְרֹון (Migrôwn | mig-rone')\n\nDerivation: from H4048 מָגַר ; precipice\nStrong's: Migron, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Migron.\n\nCognate Group: H4051 (Migron), H4048 (cast down)",
    4052: "מִגְרָעָה (migrâʻâh | mig-raw-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H1639 גָּרַע\nStrong's: a ledge or offset\nKJV: narrowed rest.\n\nCognate Group: H4052 (narrowed rest), H1639 (abate)\nGreek Equivalents: G1292 διάστημα",
    4053: "מִגְרָפָה (migrâphâh | mig-raw-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H1640 גָּרַף\nStrong's: something thrown off (by the spade), i.e. a clod\nKJV: clod.\n\nCognate Group: H4053 (clod), H1640 (sweep away), H106 (fist)",
    4054: "מִגְרָשׁ (migrâsh | mig-rawsh')\n\nDerivation: also (in plural) feminine (Ezekiel 27:28) מִגְרָשָׁה; from H1644 גָּרַשׁ\nStrong's: a suburb (i.e. open country whither flocks are driven from pasture); hence, the area around abuilding, or the margin of the sea\nKJV: cast out, suburb.\n\nCognate Group: H1647 (Gershom), H4054 (cast out), H1645 (put forth), H1646 (exaction), H1648 (Gershon), H1644 (cast up), H1649 (Gershonite)\nGreek Equivalents: G873 ἀφορίζω, G1292 διάστημα, G2697 κατάσχεσις, G4066 περίχωρος",
    4055: "מַד (mad | mad)\n\nDerivation: or מֵד; from H4058 מָדַד\nStrong's: properly, extent, i.e. height; also a measure; by implication, a vesture (as measured); also a carpet\nKJV: armour, clothes, garment, judgment, measure, raiment, stature.\n\nCognate Group: H4461 (measure), H4055 (armour), H4081 (Middin), H4058 (measure), H4067 (stature), H4060 (garment), H4059 (be gone)\nGreek Equivalents: G2440 ἱμάτιον, G5509 χιτών",
    4056: "מַדְבַּח (madbach | mad-bakh')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H1684 דְּבַח\nStrong's: a sacrificial altar\nKJV: altar.\n\nCognate Group: H4056 (altar), H1685 (sacrifice), H1684 (offer)\nGreek Equivalents: G2379 θυσιαστήριον",
    4057: "מִדְבָּר (midbâr | mid-bawr')\n\nDerivation: from H1696 דָבַר in the sense of driving\nStrong's: a pasture (i.e. open field, whither cattle are driven); by implication, a desert; also speech (including its organs)\nKJV: desert, south, speech, wilderness.\n\nCognate Group: H1697 (act), H1702 (float), H1698 (murrain), H1696 (answer), H1703 (word), H1700 (cause), H1688 (Debir), H1683 (Deborah), H1704 (Dibri), H4057 (desert), H1682 (bee), H1687 (oracle), H1699 (fold), H1705 (Dabareh)\nGreek Equivalents: G68 ἀγρός, G504 ἄνυδρος, G2048 ἔρημος, G2048 ἔρημος, G2049 ἐρημόω, G5117 τόπος",
    4058: "מָדַד (mâdad | maw-dad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to stretch; by implication, to measure (as if by stretching a line); figuratively, to be extended\nKJV: measure, mete, stretch self.\n\nCognate Group: H4461 (measure), H4055 (armour), H4081 (Middin), H4058 (measure), H4067 (stature), H4060 (garment), H4059 (be gone)\nGreek Equivalents: G591 ἀποδίδωμι, G1096 γίνομαι, G1299 διατάσσω, G1720 ἐμφυσάω, G3354 μετρέω",
    4059: "מִדַּד (middad | mid-dad')\n\nDerivation: from H5074 נָדַד\nStrong's: flight\nKJV: be gone.\n\nCognate Group: H4461 (measure), H4055 (armour), H4081 (Middin), H4058 (measure), H4067 (stature), H4060 (garment), H4059 (be gone)",
    4060: "מִדָּה (middâh | mid-daw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4055 מַד\nStrong's: properly, extension, i.e. height or breadth; also a measure (including its standard); hence a portion (as measured) or a vestment; specifically, tribute (as measured)\nKJV: garment, measure(-ing, meteyard, piece, size, (great) stature, tribute, wide.\n\nCognate Group: H4461 (measure), H4055 (armour), H4081 (Middin), H4058 (measure), H4067 (stature), H4060 (garment), H4059 (be gone)\nGreek Equivalents: G706 ἀριθμός, G1292 διάστημα, G1742 ἔνδυμα, G2476 ἵστημι, G3358 μέτρον, G5308 ὑψηλός, G5411 φόρος",
    4061: "מִדָּה (middâh | mid-daw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or מִנְדָּה; (Aramaic), corresponding to H4060 מִדָּה\nStrong's: tribute in money\nKJV: toll, tribute.\n\nCognate Group: H4061 (toll), H4481 (according)",
    4062: "מַדְהֵבָה (madhêbâh | mad-hay-baw')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from the equivalent of H1722 דְּהַב\nStrong's: goldmaking, i.e. exactness\nKJV: golden city.\n\nCognate Group: H7293 (proud), H7294 (Rahab), H4062 (golden city), H7296 (strength), H7295 (proud), H7292 (overcome)",
    4063: "מֶדֶו (medev | meh'-dev)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to stretch\nStrong's: properly, extent, i.e. measure; by implication, a dress (as measured)\nKJV: garment.\n\nCognate Group: H4074 (Madai), H4063 (garment), H4075 (Mede)",
    4064: "מַדְוֶה (madveh | mad-veh')\n\nDerivation: from H1738 דָּוָה\nStrong's: sickness\nKJV: disease.\n\nCognate Group: H1739 (faint), H4064 (disease), H1738 (infirmity), H1773 (ink), H1742 (faint), H1741 (languishing)\nGreek Equivalents: G3554 νόσος, G3601 ὀδύνη",
    4065: "מַדּוּחַ (maddûwach | mad-doo'akh)\n\nDerivation: from H5080 נָדַח\nStrong's: seduction\nKJV: cause of banishment.\n\nCognate Group: H5083 (gift), H4065 (cause of banishment), H5084 (sheath), H5080 (banish)",
    4066: "מָדֹון (mâdôwn | maw-dohn')\n\nDerivation: from H1777 דִּין\nStrong's: a contest or quarrel\nKJV: brawling, contention(-ous), discord, strife. Compare H4079 מִדְיָן, H4090 מְדָן .\n\nCognate Group: H1839 (Danites), H1835 (Daniel), H4082 (province), H4079 (brawling), H3036 (Jadon), H1781 (judge), H4090 (discord), H1840 (Daniel), H4068 (Madon), H1783 (Dinah), H1777 (with a straight course), H4084 (Midianite), H4080 (Midian), H7384 (Riphath), H4091 (Medan), H4092 (Midianite), H1779 (cause), H1842 (Dan-jaan), H4066 (brawling)\nGreek Equivalents: G485 ἀντιλογία, G1343 δικαιοσύνη, G2556 κακός, G3060 λοίδορος, G3163 μάχη",
    4067: "מָדֹון (mâdôwn | maw-dohn')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H4063 מֶדֶו\nStrong's: extensiveness, i.e. height\nKJV: stature.\n\nCognate Group: H4461 (measure), H4055 (armour), H4081 (Middin), H4058 (measure), H4067 (stature), H4060 (garment), H4059 (be gone)",
