    4100: "מָה (mâh | maw)\n\nDerivation: or מַה; or מָ; or מַ; also מֶה; a primitive particle\nStrong's: properly, interrogative what? (including how? why? when?); but also exclamation, what! (including how!), or indefinitely what (including whatever, and even relatively, that which); often used with prefixes in various adverbial or conjunctive senses\nKJV: how (long, oft, (-soever)), (no-) thing, what (end, good, purpose, thing), whereby(-fore, -in, -to, -with), (for) why.\n\nCognate Group: H4100 (how)\nGreek Equivalents: G155 αἴτημα, G2425 ἱκανός, G2425 ἱκανός, G3029 λίαν, G4169 ποῖος, G5101 τίς, G5101 τίς, G5101 τίς, G5101 τίς, G2982 λαμά",
