    4117: "מָהַר (mâhar | maw-har')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (perhaps rather the same as H4116 מָהַר through the idea of readiness in assent)\nStrong's: to bargain (for a wife), i.e. to wed\nKJV: endow, [idiom] surely.\n\nCognate Group: H4116 (be carried headlong), H4117 (endow), H4119 (dowry)",
    4118: "מַהֵר (mahêr | mah-hare')\n\nDerivation: from H4116 מָהַר\nStrong's: properly, hurrying; hence (adverbially) in ahurry\nKJV: hasteth, hastily, at once, quickly, soon, speedily, suddenly.\n\nCognate Group: H4116 (be carried headlong), H4121 (Maharai), H4106 (diligent), H4120 (hastily), H4118 (hasteth), H4122 (Maher-sha-lal-bash-baz)",
    4119: "מֹהַר (môhar | mo'-har)\n\nDerivation: from H4117 מָהַר\nStrong's: a price (for a wife)\nKJV: dowry.\n\nCognate Group: H4116 (be carried headlong), H4117 (endow), H4119 (dowry)\nGreek Equivalents: G1390 δόμα",
    4120: "מְהֵרָה (mᵉhêrâh | meh-hay-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4118 מַהֵר\nStrong's: properly, a hurry; hence (adverbially) promptly\nKJV: hastily, quickly, shortly, soon, make (with) speed(-ily), swiftly.\n\nCognate Group: H4116 (be carried headlong), H4121 (Maharai), H4106 (diligent), H4120 (hastily), H4118 (hasteth), H4122 (Maher-sha-lal-bash-baz)\nGreek Equivalents: G5030 ταχέως, G5032 τάχιον, G5034 τάχος",
    4121: "מַהֲרַי (Mahăray | mah-har-ah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H4116 מָהַר ; hasty\nStrong's: Maharai, an Israelite\nKJV: Maharai.\n\nCognate Group: H4116 (be carried headlong), H4121 (Maharai), H4106 (diligent), H4120 (hastily), H4118 (hasteth), H4122 (Maher-sha-lal-bash-baz)",
    4122: "מַהֵר שָׁלָל חָשׁ בַּז (Mahêr Shâlâl Châsh Baz | mah-hare' shaw-lawl' khawsh baz)\n\nDerivation: from H4118 מַהֵר and H7998 שָׁלָל and H2363 חוּשׁ and H957 בַּז ; hasting (is he (the enemy) to the) booty, swift (to the) prey\nStrong's: Maher-Shalal-Chash-Baz; the symbolical name of the son of Isaiah\nKJV: Maher-sha-lal-bash-baz.\n\nCognate Group: H4116 (be carried headlong), H4121 (Maharai), H4106 (diligent), H4120 (hastily), H4118 (hasteth), H4122 (Maher-sha-lal-bash-baz)",
    4123: "מַהֲתַלָּה (mahăthallâh | mah-hath-al-law')\n\nDerivation: from H2048 הָתַל\nStrong's: a delusion\nKJV: deceit.\n\nCognate Group: H2048 (deal deceitfully), H4123 (deceit)",
    4124: "מֹואָב (Môwʼâb | mo-awb)\n\nDerivation: from a prolonged form of the prepositional prefix m-and H1 אָב ; from (her (the mother's)) father\nStrong's: Moab, an incestuous son of Lot; also his territory and descendants\nKJV: Moab.\n\nCognate Group: H4124 (Moab), H4125 (of Moab)",
    4125: "מֹואָבִי (Môwʼâbîy | mo-aw-bee')\n\nDerivation: feminine מֹואָבִיָּה; or מֹואָבִית\n\nTypo: xlit Môwâbîyth corrected to Môwʼâbîyth\n\n; patronymical from H4124 מֹואָב\nStrong's: a Moabite or Moabitess, i.e. a descendant from Moab\nKJV: (woman) of Moab, Moabite(-ish, -ss).\n\nCognate Group: H4124 (Moab), H4125 (of Moab)",
    4126: "מֹובָא (môwbâʼ | mo-baw')\n\nDerivation: by transp. for H3996 מָבֹוא\nStrong's: an entrance\nKJV: coming.\n\nCognate Group: H872 (entry), H935 (abide), H3996 (by which came), H4126 (coming), H3997 (entry), H8393 (fruit)",
    4127: "מוּג (mûwg | moog)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to melt, i.e. literally (to soften, flow down, disappear), or figuratively (to fear, faint)\nKJV: consume, dissolve, (be) faint(-hearted), melt (away), make soft.\n\nCognate Group: H4127 (consume)\nGreek Equivalents: G641 ἀποῤῥίπτω, G1839 ἐξίστημι, G2352 θραύω, G4531 σαλεύω, G4854 σύμφυτος, G5015 ταράσσω, G5080 τήκω",
    4128: "מוּד (mûwd | mood)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to shake\nKJV: measure.\n\nCognate Group: H4128 (measure)\nGreek Equivalents: G4531 σαλεύω",
    4129: "מֹודַע (môwdaʻ | mo-dah')\n\nDerivation: or rather מֹדָע; from H3045 יָדַע\nStrong's: an acquaintance\nKJV: kinswoman.\n\nCognate Group: H1847 (cunning), H4129 (kinswoman), H3045 (acknowledge), H3047 (Jada), H4093 (knowledge), H1845 (Deuel), H3043 (Jediael), H3048 (Jedaiah), H3037 (Jaddua), H1844 (knowledge), H1843 (knowledge), H3049 (wizard), H4130 (kindred), H4069 (how)",
