    4133: "מֹוטָה (môwṭâh | mo-taw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4132 מֹוט\nStrong's: a pole; by implication, an ox-bow; hence, a yoke (either literal or figurative)\nKJV: bands, heavy, staves, yoke.\n\nCognate Group: H4131 (be carried), H4133 (bands), H4132 (bar)\nGreek Equivalents: G1199 δεσμόν, G4886 σύνδεσμος",
    4134: "מוּךְ (mûwk | mook)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to become thin, i.e. (figuratively) be impoverished\nKJV: be (waxen) poor(-er).\n\nCognate Group: H4134 (be poor)\nGreek Equivalents: G639 ἀπορέω, G5011 ταπεινός, G5013 ταπεινόω",
    4135: "מוּל (mûwl | mool)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to cut short, i.e. curtail (specifically the prepuce, i.e. to circumcise); by implication, to blunt; figuratively, to destroy\nKJV: circumcise(-ing), selves), cut down (in pieces), destroy, [idiom] must needs.\n\nCognate Group: H4135 (circumcise), H4139 (circumcision)\nGreek Equivalents: G292 ἀμύνομαι, G770 ἀσθενέω, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G2192 ἔχω, G3725 ὅριον, G4059 περιτέμνω, G4061 περιτομή",
    4136: "מוּל (mûwl | mool)\n\nDerivation: or מֹול; (Deuteronomy 1:1), or מֹואל; (Nehemiah 12:38), or מֻל; (Numbers 22:5), from H4135 מוּל\nStrong's: properly, abrupt, i.e. a precipice; by implication, the front; used only adverbially (with prepositional prefix) opposite\nKJV: (over) against, before, (fore-) front, from, (God-) ward, toward, with.\n\nCognate Group: H4136 (against)\nGreek Equivalents: G1451 ἐγγύς, G3313 μέρος, G4876 συναντάω",
    4137: "מֹולָדָה (Môwlâdâh | mo-law-daw')\n\nDerivation: from H3205 יָלַד ; birth\nStrong's: Moladah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Moladah.\n\nCognate Group: H3206 (boy), H3205 (bear), H2056 (child), H8434 (Tolad), H4138 (begotten), H4137 (Moladah), H3209 (born), H3208 (childhood), H3207 (damsel), H4140 (Molid), H3211 (born), H8435 (birth), H3210 (Jalon)",
    4138: "מֹולֶדֶת (môwledeth | mo-leh'-deth)\n\nDerivation: from H3205 יָלַד\nStrong's: nativity (plural birth-place); by implication, lineage, native country; also offspring, family\nKJV: begotten, born, issue, kindred, native(-ity).\n\nCognate Group: H3206 (boy), H3205 (bear), H2056 (child), H8434 (Tolad), H4138 (begotten), H4137 (Moladah), H3209 (born), H3208 (childhood), H3207 (damsel), H4140 (Molid), H3211 (born), H8435 (birth), H3210 (Jalon)\nGreek Equivalents: G3968 πατρίς, G4772 συγγένεια, G5443 φυλή",
