    4144: "מֹוסָד (môwçâd | mo-sawd')\n\nDerivation: from H3245 יָסַד\nStrong's: a foundation\nKJV: foundation.\n\nCognate Group: H4144 (foundation), H4146 (foundation), H4328 (foundation), H3248 (foundation), H4527 (foundation), H4143 (foundation), H3245 (appoint), H3246 ([idiom] began), H4145 (foundation), H3247 (bottom)\nGreek Equivalents: G1475 ἔδαφος, G2310 θεμέλιος",
    4145: "מוּסָדָה (mûwçâdâh | moo-saw-daw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4143 מוּסָד\nStrong's: a foundation; figuratively, an appointment\nKJV: foundation, grounded. Compare H4328 מְיֻסָּדָה .\n\nCognate Group: H4144 (foundation), H4146 (foundation), H4328 (foundation), H3248 (foundation), H4527 (foundation), H4143 (foundation), H3245 (appoint), H3246 ([idiom] began), H4145 (foundation), H3247 (bottom)",
    4146: "מֹוסָדָה (môwçâdâh | mo-saw-daw')\n\nDerivation: or מֹסָדָה; feminine of H4144 מֹוסָד\nStrong's: a foundation\nKJV: foundation.\n\nCognate Group: H4144 (foundation), H4146 (foundation), H4328 (foundation), H3248 (foundation), H4527 (foundation), H4143 (foundation), H3245 (appoint), H3246 ([idiom] began), H4145 (foundation), H3247 (bottom)",
    4147: "מֹוסֵר (môwçêr | mo-sare')\n\nDerivation: also (in plural) feminine מֹוסֵרָה; or מֹסְרָה; from H3256 יָסַר\nStrong's: properly, chastisement, i.e. (by implication) a halter; figuratively, restraint\nKJV: band, bond.\n\nCognate Group: H615 (bound), H4147 (band), H635 (Esther), H4149 (Mosera), H634 (Esar-haddon), H4562 (bond), H631 (bind), H632 (binding), H612 (band), H616 (prisoner), H617 (Assir)",
    4148: "מוּסָר (mûwçâr | moo-sawr')\n\nDerivation: from H3256 יָסַר\nStrong's: properly, chastisement; figuratively, reproof, warning or instruction; also restraint\nKJV: bond, chastening(-eth), chastisement, check, correction, discipline, doctrine, instruction, rebuke.\n\nCognate Group: H4148 (bond), H3256 (bind), H4561 (instruction), H3250 (instruct)\nGreek Equivalents: G3809 παιδεία, G3810 παιδευτής, G4678 σοφία",
    4149: "מֹוסֵרָה (Môwçêrâh | mo-say-raw')\n\nDerivation: or (plural) מֹסְרֹות feminine of H4147 מֹוסֵר ; correction or corrections\nStrong's: Moserah or Moseroth, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Mosera, Moseroth.\n\nCognate Group: H615 (bound), H4147 (band), H635 (Esther), H4149 (Mosera), H634 (Esar-haddon), H4562 (bond), H631 (bind), H632 (binding), H612 (band), H616 (prisoner), H617 (Assir)",
