    4151: "מֹועָד (môwʻâd | mo-awd')\n\nDerivation: from H3259 יָעַד ; (as in H4150 מֹועֵד)\nStrong's: properly, an assembly figuratively, a troop\nKJV: appointed time.\n\nCognate Group: H5129 (Noadiah), H4151 (appointed time), H4150 (appointed), H3259 (agree), H4152 (appointed), H5712 (assembly), H3260 (Iddo See H3035)",
    4152: "מוּעָדָה (mûwʻâdâh | moo-aw-daw')\n\nDerivation: from H3259 יָעַד\nStrong's: an appointed place, i.e. asylum\nKJV: appointed.\n\nCognate Group: H5129 (Noadiah), H4151 (appointed time), H4150 (appointed), H3259 (agree), H4152 (appointed), H5712 (assembly), H3260 (Iddo See H3035)",
    4153: "מֹועַדְיָה (Môwʻadyâh | mo-ad-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H4151 מֹועָד and H3050 יָהּ ; assembly of Jah\nStrong's: Moadjah, an Israelite\nKJV: Moadiah. Compare H4573 מַעֲדְיָה .\n\nCognate Group: H5976 (be at a stand), H4153 (Moadiah), H4571 (make to shake), H4572 (Maadai), H4154 (out of joint), H4573 (Maadiah)",
    4154: "מוּעֶדֶת (mûwʻedeth | moo-ay'-deth)\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of H4571 מָעַד\nStrong's: properly, made to slip, i.e. dislocated\nKJV: out of joint.\n\nCognate Group: H5976 (be at a stand), H4153 (Moadiah), H4571 (make to shake), H4572 (Maadai), H4154 (out of joint), H4573 (Maadiah)",
    4155: "מוּעָף (mûwʻâph | moo-awf')\n\nDerivation: from H5774 עוּף\nStrong's: properly, covered, i.e. dark; abstractly, obscurity, i.e. distress\nKJV: dimness.\n\nCognate Group: H5778 (Ephai), H5774 (brandish), H4588 (dimness), H5890 (darkness), H5891 (Ephah), H4155 (dimness)",
    4156: "מֹועֵצָה (môwʻêtsâh | mo-ay-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: from H3289 יָעַץ\nStrong's: a purpose\nKJV: counsel, device.\n\nCognate Group: H4156 (counsel), H3289 (advertise), H6098 (advice)\nGreek Equivalents: G763 ἀσέβεια, G3598 ὁδός",
    4157: "מוּעָקָה (mûwʻâqâh | moo-aw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5781 עוּק\nStrong's: pressure, i.e. (figuratively) distress\nKJV: affliction.\n\nCognate Group: H4157 (affliction), H5781 (be pressed), H6125 (oppression)\nGreek Equivalents: G2347 θλῖψις",
    4158: "מֹופַעַת (Môwphaʻath | mo-fah'-ath)\n\nDerivation: (Jeremiah 48:21) or מֵיפַעַת; or מֵפַעַת; from H3313 יָפַע ; illuminative\nStrong's: Mophaath or Mephaath, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Mephaath.\n\nCognate Group: H4158 (Mephaath), H3309 (Japhia), H3313 (be light), H3314 (brightness)",
    4159: "מֹופֵת (môwphêth | mo-faith')\n\nDerivation: or מֹפֵת; from H3302 יָפָה in the sense of conspicuousness\nStrong's: a miracle; by implication, a token or omen\nKJV: miracle, sign, wonder(-ed at).\n\nCognate Group: H4159 (miracle), H675 (Ezbon)\nGreek Equivalents: G4592 σημεῖον, G5059 τέρας",
    4160: "מוּץ (mûwts | moots)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to press, i.e. (figuratively) to oppress\nKJV: extortioner.\n\nCognate Group: H4160 (extortioner), H4352 (Machi), H4335 (Meshak), H4330 (churning), H4331 (Mesha)",
    4161: "מֹוצָא (môwtsâʼ | mo-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: or מֹצָא\n\nTypo: xlit môtsâ corrected to môtsâʼ\n\n; from H3318 יָצָא\nStrong's: a going forth, i.e. (the act) an egress, or (the place) an exit; hence, a source or product; specifically, dawn, the rising of the sun (the East), exportation, utterance, a gate, a fountain, a mine, a meadow (as producing grass)\nKJV: brought out, bud, that which came out, east, going forth, goings out, that which (thing that) is gone out, outgoing, proceeded out, spring, vein, (water-) course (springs).\n\nCognate Group: H4161 (brought out), H6631 (that which cometh forth), H8444 (border), H4163 (draught house; going forth), H3329 (those that came forth), H3318 ([idiom] after), H4162 (Moza)\nGreek Equivalents: G1841 ἔξοδος, G4077 πηγή, G4197 πορεία, G5117 τόπος",
    4162: "מֹוצָא (môwtsâʼ | mo-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H4161 מֹוצָא\nStrong's: Motsa, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Moza.\n\nCognate Group: H4161 (brought out), H6631 (that which cometh forth), H8444 (border), H4163 (draught house; going forth), H3329 (those that came forth), H3318 ([idiom] after), H4162 (Moza)",
    4163: "מֹוצָאָה (môwtsâʼâh | mo-tsaw-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4161 מֹוצָא ; (marg.; compare H6675 צֹואָה)\n\nStrong's: a family descent; also a sewer\nKJV: draught house; going forth.\n\nCognate Group: H4161 (brought out), H6631 (that which cometh forth), H8444 (border), H4163 (draught house; going forth), H3329 (those that came forth), H3318 ([idiom] after), H4162 (Moza)",
    4164: "מוּצַק (mûwtsaq | moo-tsak')\n\nDerivation: or מוּצָק; from H3332 יָצַק\nStrong's: narrowness; figuratively, distress\nKJV: anguish, is straitened, straitness.\n\nCognate Group: H4164 (anguish), H6695 (anguish), H6693 (constrain), H4691 (anguish), H4689 (anguish)\nGreek Equivalents: G5010 τάξις",
    4165: "מוּצָק (mûwtsâq | moo-tsawk')\n\nDerivation: from H5694 עָגִיל\nStrong's: properly, fusion, i.e. literally, a casting (of metal); figuratively, a mass (of clay)\nKJV: casting, hardness.\n\nCognate Group: H3333 (when it was cast), H3332 (cast), H4166 (when it was cast), H4165 (casting)",
    4166: "מוּצָקָה (mûwtsâqâh | moo-tsaw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: or מֻצָקָה; from H3332 יָצַק\nStrong's: properly, something poured out, i.e. a casting (of metal); by implication, a tube (as cast)\nKJV: when it was cast, pipe.\n\nCognate Group: H3333 (when it was cast), H3332 (cast), H4166 (when it was cast), H4165 (casting)",
    4167: "מוּק (mûwq | mook)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to jeer, i.e. (intens.) blaspheme\nKJV: be corrupt.\n\nCognate Group: H4167 (be corrupt)",
    4168: "מֹוקֵד (môwqêd | mo-kade')\n\nDerivation: from H3344 יָקַד\nStrong's: a fire or fuel; abstractly, a conflagration\nKJV: burning, hearth.\n\nCognate Group: H3347 (Jokdeam), H4168 (burning), H3344 (burn), H4169 (burning), H3350 (burning)",
    4169: "מֹוקְדָה (môwqᵉdâh | mo-ked-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4168 מֹוקֵד\nStrong's: fuel\nKJV: burning.\n\nCognate Group: H3347 (Jokdeam), H4168 (burning), H3344 (burn), H4169 (burning), H3350 (burning)",
    4170: "מֹוקֵשׁ (môwqêsh | mo-kashe')\n\nDerivation: or מֹקֵשׁ; from H3369 יָקֹשׁ\nStrong's: a noose (for catching animals) (literally or figuratively); by implication, a hook (for the nose)\nKJV: be ensnared, gin, (is) snare(-d), trap.\n\nCognate Group: H3371 (Joktheel), H3353 (fowler), H3370 (Jokshan), H3369 (fowler snare), H4170 (be ensnared), H3352 (fowler)\nGreek Equivalents: G1029 βρόχος, G3803 παγίς, G3803 παγίς, G4348 πρόσκομμα, G4625 σκάνδαλον, G4643 σκληρότης",
    4171: "מוּר (mûwr | moor)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to alter; by implication, to barter, to dispose of\nKJV: [idiom] at all, (ex-) change, remove.\n\nCognate Group: H4171 ([idiom] at all), H4185 (cease), H8545 (change), H4177 (razor), H4173 (threshing instrument)\nGreek Equivalents: G114 ἀθετέω, G236 ἀλλάσσω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5087 τίθημι",
    4172: "מֹורָא (môwrâʼ | mo-raw')\n\nDerivation: or מֹרָא; or מֹורָה\n\nTypo: xlit môrâh corrected to môwrâh\n\n; (Psalm 9:20), from H3372 יָרֵא\nStrong's: fear; by implication, a fearful thing or deed\nKJV: dread, (that ought to be) fear(-ed), terribleness, terror.\n\nCognate Group: H3373 (afraid), H3375 (Iron), H3374 ([idiom] dreadful), H3372 (affright), H8493 (Tiria), H4172 (dread)\nGreek Equivalents: G2297 θαυμάσιος, G3705 ὅραμα, G5156 τρόμος, G5398 φοβερός",
    4173: "מֹורַג (môwrag | mo-rag')\n\nDerivation: or מֹרַג; from an unused root meaning to triturate\nStrong's: a threshing sledge\nKJV: threshing instrument.\n\nCognate Group: H4171 ([idiom] at all), H4185 (cease), H8545 (change), H4177 (razor), H4173 (threshing instrument)\nGreek Equivalents: G723 ἄροτρον, G5164 τροχός",
    4174: "מֹורָד (môwrâd | mo-rawd')\n\nDerivation: from H3381 יָרַד\nStrong's: a descent; as architecture, an ornamental appendage, perhaps a festoon\nKJV: going down, steep place, thin work.\n\nCognate Group: H3382 (Jared), H3381 ([idiom] abundantly), H3383 (Jordan), H4174 (going down)\nGreek Equivalents: G3598 ὁδός",
    4175: "מֹורֶה (môwreh | mo-reh')\n\nDerivation: from H3384 יָרָה ; (see H3138 יֹורֶה)\n\nStrong's: an archer; also teacher or teaching; also the early rain\nKJV: (early) rain.\n\nCognate Group: H4175 (rain), H3140 (Jorai), H8451 (law), H3138 (first rain), H4176 (Moreh), H3404 (Jeriah), H8452 (manner), H3385 (Jeruel), H3139 (Jorah), H3384 (archer), H3400 (Jeriel)\nGreek Equivalents: G5308 ὑψηλός",
    4176: "מֹורֶה (Môwreh | mo-reh')\n\nDerivation: or מֹרֶה; the same as H4175 מֹורֶה\nStrong's: Moreh, a Canaanite; also a hill (perhaps named from him)\nKJV: Moreh.\n\nCognate Group: H4175 (rain), H3140 (Jorai), H8451 (law), H3138 (first rain), H4176 (Moreh), H3404 (Jeriah), H8452 (manner), H3385 (Jeruel), H3139 (Jorah), H3384 (archer), H3400 (Jeriel)",
    4177: "מֹורָה (môwrâh | mo-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H4171 מוּר in the sense of shearing\nStrong's: a razor\nKJV: razor.\n\nCognate Group: H4171 ([idiom] at all), H4185 (cease), H8545 (change), H4177 (razor), H4173 (threshing instrument)\nGreek Equivalents: G4604 σίδηρος",
    4178: "מֹורָט (môwrâṭ | mo-rawt')\n\nDerivation: from H3399 יָרַט\nStrong's: obstinate, i.e. independent\nKJV: peeled.\n\nCognate Group: H4825 (Meres), H4813 (Miriam), H4179 (Moriah), H4803 (bright), H4178 (peeled), H4821 (Mirma), H4826 (Marsena), H4812 (Meraioth), H4824 (Meronothite), H4811 (Meraiah), H4593 (wrapped up), H4831 (Maralah), H4822 (Meremoth)",
    4179: "מֹורִיָּה (Môwrîyâh | mo-ree-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or מֹרִיָּה; from H7200 רָאָה and H3050 יָהּ ; seen of Jah\nStrong's: Morijah, a hill in Palestine\nKJV: Moriah.\n\nCognate Group: H4825 (Meres), H4813 (Miriam), H4179 (Moriah), H4803 (bright), H4178 (peeled), H4821 (Mirma), H4826 (Marsena), H4812 (Meraioth), H4824 (Meronothite), H4811 (Meraiah), H4593 (wrapped up), H4831 (Maralah), H4822 (Meremoth)",
    4180: "מֹורָשׁ (môwrâsh | mo-rawsh')\n\nDerivation: from H3423 יָרַשׁ\nStrong's: a possession; figuratively, delight\nKJV: possession, thought.\n\nCognate Group: H3424 (possession), H3425 (heritage), H8492 (wine), H4181 (heritage), H3423 (cast out), H7568 (net), H4180 (possession), H4182 (Moresheth-gath), H3388 (Jerusha), H4183 (Morashthite)\nGreek Equivalents: G2048 ἔρημος",
