    4182: "מֹורֶשֶׁת גַּת (Môwresheth Gath | mo-reh'-sheth gath)\n\nDerivation: from H3423 יָרַשׁ and H1661 גַּת ; possession of Gath\nStrong's: Moresheth-Gath, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Moresheth-gath.\n\nCognate Group: H3424 (possession), H3425 (heritage), H8492 (wine), H4181 (heritage), H3423 (cast out), H7568 (net), H4180 (possession), H4182 (Moresheth-gath), H3388 (Jerusha), H4183 (Morashthite)",
    4183: "מֹורַשְׁתִּי (Môwrashtîy | mo-rash-tee')\n\nTypo: xlit Morashtîy corrected to Môwrashtîy\n\nDerivation: patrial from H4182 מֹורֶשֶׁת גַּת\nStrong's: a Morashtite or inhabitant of Moresheth-Gath\nKJV: Morashthite.\n\nCognate Group: H3424 (possession), H3425 (heritage), H8492 (wine), H4181 (heritage), H3423 (cast out), H7568 (net), H4180 (possession), H4182 (Moresheth-gath), H3388 (Jerusha), H4183 (Morashthite)",
    4184: "מוּשׁ (mûwsh | moosh)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to touch\nKJV: feel, handle.\n\nCognate Group: H4187 (Mushi), H4184 (feel), H4188 (Mushites)",
    4185: "מוּשׁ (mûwsh | moosh)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (perhaps rather the same as H4184 מוּשׁ through the idea of receding by contact)\nStrong's: to withdraw (both literally and figuratively, whether intransitive or transitive)\nKJV: cease, depart, go back, remove, take away.\n\nCognate Group: H4171 ([idiom] at all), H4185 (cease), H8545 (change), H4177 (razor), H4173 (threshing instrument)\nGreek Equivalents: G868 ἀφίστημι, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G2795 κινέω, G2827 κλίνω, G2967 κωλύω, G3179 μεθίστημι, G3973 παύω, G5563 χωρίζω, G5584 ψηλαφάω",
    4186: "מֹושָׁב (môwshâb | mo-shawb')\n\nDerivation: or מֹשָׁב; from H3427 יָשַׁב\nStrong's: a seat; figuratively, a site; abstractly, a session; by extension an abode (the place or the time); by implication, population\nKJV: assembly, dwell in, dwelling(-place), wherein (that) dwelt (in), inhabited place, seat, sitting, situation, sojourning.\n\nCognate Group: H3430 (Ishbi-benob), H3428 (Jeshebeab), H3436 (Joshbekashah), H3429 (that sat in the seat), H3427 (abide), H7871 (while), H4186 (assembly), H8453 (foreigner), H7675 (place), H3143 (Josibiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2515 καθέδρα, G2697 κατάσχεσις, G2731 κατοίκησις, G2732 κατοικητήριον, G2733 κατοικία",
    4187: "מוּשִׁי (Mûwshîy | moo-shee')\n\nDerivation: or מֻשִּׁי; from H4184 מוּשׁ ; sensitive\nStrong's: Mushi, a Levite\nKJV: Mushi.\n\nCognate Group: H4187 (Mushi), H4184 (feel), H4188 (Mushites)",
    4188: "מוּשִׁי (Mûwshîy | moo-shee')\n\nDerivation: patronymical from H4187 מוּשִׁי\nStrong's: a Mushite (collectively) or descendants of Mushi\nKJV: Mushites.\n\nCognate Group: H4187 (Mushi), H4184 (feel), H4188 (Mushites)",
    4189: "מֹושְׁכָה (môwshᵉkâh | mo-shek-aw')\n\nDerivation: act participle feminine of H4900 מָשַׁךְ\nStrong's: something drawing, i.e. (figuratively) a cord\nKJV: band.\n\nCognate Group: H4189 (band), H4900 (draw), H4902 (Mesech), H4901 (precious)\nGreek Equivalents: G5418 φραγμός",
    4190: "מֹושָׁעָה (môwshâʻâh | mo-shaw-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H3467 יָשַׁע\nStrong's: deliverance\nKJV: salvation.\n\nCognate Group: H8668 (deliverance), H3471 (jasper), H3470 (Isaiah), H1954 (Hosea), H7774 (Shua), H3444 (deliverance), H7769 (cry), H7770 (Shua), H4190 (salvation), H3469 (Ishi), H7771 (bountiful), H4338 (Mesha), H3468 (safety), H4337 (Mesha), H3467 ([idiom] at all), H1955 (Hoshaiah)",
    4191: "מוּת (mûwth | mooth)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to die (literally or figuratively); causatively, to kill\nKJV: [idiom] at all, [idiom] crying, (be) dead (body, man, one), (put to, worthy of) death, destroy(-er), (cause to, be like to, must) die, kill, necro(-mancer), [idiom] must needs, slay, [idiom] surely, [idiom] very suddenly, [idiom] in (no) wise.\n\nCognate Group: H4463 (death), H4191 ([idiom] at all), H4194 (dead), H8546 (death)\nGreek Equivalents: G25 ἀγαπάω, G86 ᾅδης, G101 ἀδυνατέω, G337 ἀναιρέω, G355 ἀναλίσκω, G599 ἀποθνήσκω, G615 ἀποκτείνω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1626 ἔκτρωμα, G1777 ἔνοχος, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1929 ἐπιδίδωμι, G2287 θανατήφορος, G2288 θάνατος, G2288 θάνατος, G2289 θανατόω, G2289 θανατόω, G2348 θνήσκω, G2349 θνητός, G2795 κινέω, G2827 κλίνω, G3179 μεθίστημι, G3334 μετακινέω, G3337 μεταλλάσσω, G3346 μετατίθημι, G3498 νεκρός, G3960 πατάσσω, G4098 πίπτω, G4098 πίπτω, G4531 σαλεύω, G4931 συντελέω, G5053 τελευτάω, G5054 τελευτή",
    4192: "מוּת (Mûwth | mooth)\n\nDerivation: (Psalm H48 אֲבִירָם or מוּת לַבֵּן; from H4191 מוּת and H1121 בֵּן with the preposition and article interposed\nStrong's: 'To die for the son', probably the title of a popular song\nKJV: death, Muthlabben.\n\nCognate Group: H3844 (Lebanon), H3843 (brick), H3838 (Lebana), H4192 (death), H3839 (poplar), H3846 (Libnites), H3840 (paved), H4404 (brickkiln), H3845 (Libni), H3835 (make brick), H3828 (incense), H3837 (Laban), H3836 (white), H3841 (Libnah), H3842 (moon), H3829 (Lebonah)",
    4193: "מֹות (môwth | mohth)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H4194 מָוֶת\nStrong's: death\nKJV: death.\n\nCognate Group: H4101 (how great), H4193 (death), H3964 (what)\nGreek Equivalents: G435 ἀνήρ, G706 ἀριθμός, G1024 βραχύς, G2041 ἔργον, G2190 ἐχθρός, G3641 ὀλίγος, G4892 συνέδριον",
    4194: "מָוֶת (mâveth | maw'-veth)\n\nDerivation: from H4191 מוּת\nStrong's: death (natural or violent); concretely, the dead, their place or state (hades); figuratively, pestilence, ruin\nKJV: (be) dead(-ly), death, die(-d).\n\nCognate Group: H4463 (death), H4191 ([idiom] at all), H4194 (dead), H8546 (death)\nGreek Equivalents: G86 ᾅδης, G5054 τελευτή",
    4195: "מֹותָר (môwthâr | mo-thar')\n\nDerivation: from H3498 יָתַר\nStrong's: literally gain; figuratively, superiority\nKJV: plenteousness, preeminence, profit.\n\nCognate Group: H1956 (Hothir), H4340 (cord), H3502 (abundance), H3503 (Jethro), H3504 (better), H3508 (caul), H4195 (plenteousness), H3505 (Ithrite), H3492 (Jattir), H3148 (better), H3506 (Ithran), H3500 (Jether), H3498 (excel), H3501 (Ithra), H3499 (abundant), H3509 (Jetheth), H3507 (Ithream)",
    4196: "מִזְבֵּחַ (mizbêach | miz-bay'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H2076 זָבַח\nStrong's: an altar\nKJV: altar.\n\nCognate Group: H2081 (Zebina), H2078 (Zebah), H4196 (altar), H2077 (offer), H2076 (kill)\nGreek Equivalents: G1041 βωμός, G2379 θυσιαστήριον",
    4197: "מֶזֶג (mezeg | meh'-zeg)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to mingle (water with wine)\nStrong's: tempered wine\nKJV: liquor.\n\nCognate Group: H4197 (liquor)",
    4198: "מָזֶה (mâzeh | maw-zeh')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to suck out\nStrong's: exhausted\nKJV: burnt.\n\nCognate Group: H4198 (burnt), H4199 (Mizzah)\nGreek Equivalents: G5080 τήκω",
    4199: "מִזָּה (Mizzâh | miz-zaw')\n\nDerivation: probably from an unused root meaning to faint with fear; terror\nStrong's: Mizzah, an Edomite\nKJV: Mizzah.\n\nCognate Group: H4198 (burnt), H4199 (Mizzah)",
    4200: "מֶזֶו (mezev | meh'-zev)\n\nDerivation: probably from an unused root meaning to gather in\nStrong's: a granary\nKJV: garner.\n\nCognate Group: H2106 (corner), H4200 (garner)\nGreek Equivalents: G5009 ταμεῖον",
    4201: "מְזוּזָה (mᵉzûwzâh | mez-oo-zaw')\n\nDerivation: or מְזֻזָה; from the same as H2123 זִיז\nStrong's: a door-post (as prominent)\nKJV: (door, side) post.\n\nCognate Group: H4201 (post), H2124 (Ziza), H2123 (abundance), H2117 (Zaza), H3151 (Jaziz), H2125 (Zizah), H2126 (Zina)\nGreek Equivalents: G380 ἀναπτύσσω, G4745 στοά",
    4202: "מָזֹון (mâzôwn | maw-zone')\n\nDerivation: from H2109 זוּן\nStrong's: food\nKJV: meat, victual.\n\nCognate Group: H2109 (feed), H4202 (meat)\nGreek Equivalents: G5160 τροφή",
    4203: "מָזֹון (mâzôwn | maw-zone')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H4202 מָזֹון \nStrong's: food\nKJV: meat.\n\nCognate Group: H4203 (meat), H2110 (feed)",
    4204: "מָזֹור (mâzôwr | maw-zore')\n\nDerivation: from H2114 זוּר in the sense of turning aside from truth\nStrong's: treachery, i.e. a plot\nKJV: wound.\n\nCognate Group: H4204 (wound), H4216 (Mazzoroth)",
    4205: "מָזֹור (mâzôwr | maw-zore')\n\nDerivation: or מָזֹר; from H2115 זוּר in the sense of binding up\nStrong's: a bandage, i.e. remedy; hence, a sore (as needing a compress)\nKJV: bound up, wound.\n\nCognate Group: H2115 (close), H2116 (that which is crushed), H4205 (bound up), H2213 (crown), H2223 (greyhound)\nGreek Equivalents: G3601 ὀδύνη",
    4206: "מָזִיחַ (mâzîyach | maw-zee'-akh)\n\nDerivation: or מֵזַח; from H2118 זָחַח\nStrong's: a belt (as movable)\nKJV: girdle, strength.\n\nCognate Group: H4208 (planet), H4206 (girdle)\nGreek Equivalents: G2223 ζώνη",
    4207: "מַזְלֵג (mazlêg | maz-layg')\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) מִזְלָגָה; from an unused root meaning to draw up\nStrong's: a fork\nKJV: fleshhook.\n\nCognate Group: H4207 (fleshhook)",
    4208: "מַזָּלָה (mazzâlâh | maz-zaw-law')\n\nDerivation: apparently from H5140 נָזַל in the sense of raining\nStrong's: a constellation, i.e. Zodiacal sign (perhaps as affecting the weather)\nKJV: planet. Compare H4216 מַזָּרָה .\n\nCognate Group: H4208 (planet), H4206 (girdle)",
    4209: "מְזִמָּה (mᵉzimmâh | mez-im-maw')\n\nDerivation: from H2161 זָמַם\nStrong's: a plan, usually evil (machination), sometimes good (sagacity)\nKJV: (wicked) device, discretion, intent, witty invention, lewdness, mischievous (device), thought, wickedly.\n\nCognate Group: H4209 (device), H2155 (Zimmah), H2157 (Zamzummim), H2162 (wicked device), H2161 (consider), H2154 (heinous crime)\nGreek Equivalents: G946 βδέλυγμα, G1012 βουλή, G1771 ἔννοια, G2570 καλός, G3892 παρανομία, G5429 φρόνιμος",
    4210: "מִזְמֹור (mizmôwr | miz-more')\n\nDerivation: from H2167 זָמַר\nStrong's: properly, instrumental music; by implication, a poem set to notes\nKJV: psalm.\n\nCognate Group: H2172 (melody), H4210 (psalm), H2158 (psalm), H2176 (song), H2167 (give praise)\nGreek Equivalents: G5568 ψαλμός, G5603 ᾠδή",
