    4412: "מְלוּנָה (mᵉlûwnâh | mel-oo-naw')\n\nDerivation: feminine from H3885 לוּן\nStrong's: a hut, a hammock\nKJV: cottage, lodge.\n\nCognate Group: H3885 (abide), H4411 (inn), H4412 (cottage)",
    4413: "מַלֹּותִי (Mallôwthîy | mal-lo'-thee)\n\nDerivation: apparently from H4448 מָלַל ; I have talked (i.e. loquacious)\n\nStrong's: Mallothi, an Israelite\nKJV: Mallothi.\n\nCognate Group: H4413 (Mallothi), H4405 (answer), H4450 (Milalai), H4448 (say)",
    4414: "מָלַח (mâlach | maw-lakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; also as denominative from H4417 מֶלַח \nStrong's: properly, to rub to pieces or pulverize; intransitively, to disappear as dust; to salt whether internally (to season with salt) or externally (to rub with salt)\nKJV: [idiom] at all, salt, season, temper together, vanish away.\n\nCognate Group: H4414 ([idiom] at all), H4418 (rotten rag)\nGreek Equivalents: G217 ἅλας, G233 ἁλίζω, G3396 μίγνυμι",
    4415: "מְלַח (mᵉlach | mel-akh')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H4414 מָלַח\nStrong's: to eat salt, i.e. (generally) subsist\nKJV: [phrase] have maintenance.\n\nCognate Group: H4416 (maintenance), H4415 (have maintenance)",
    4416: "מְלַח (mᵉlach | mel-akh')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H4415 מְלַח\nStrong's: salt\nKJV: [phrase] maintenance, salt.\n\nCognate Group: H4416 (maintenance), H4415 (have maintenance)\nGreek Equivalents: G217 ἅλας, G252 ἁλυκός",
    4417: "מֶלַח (melach | meh'-lakh)\n\nDerivation: from H4414 מָלַח\nStrong's: properly, powder, i.e. (specifically) salt (as easily pulverized and dissolved)\nKJV: salt(-pit).\n\nCognate Group: H4419 (mariner), H4420 (barren land), H4408 (mallows), H4414 ([idiom] at all), H4417 (salt)",
    4418: "מָלָח (mâlâch | maw-lawkh')\n\nDerivation: from H4414 מָלַח in its original sense\nStrong's: a rag or old garment\nKJV: rotten rag.\n\nCognate Group: H4414 ([idiom] at all), H4418 (rotten rag)",
    4419: "מַלָּח (mallâch | mal-lawkh')\n\nDerivation: from H4414 מָלַח in its second. sense\nStrong's: a sailor (as following 'the salt')\nKJV: mariner.\n\nCognate Group: H4419 (mariner), H4420 (barren land), H4408 (mallows), H4414 ([idiom] at all), H4417 (salt)",
    4420: "מְלֵחָה (mᵉlêchâh | mel-ay-khaw')\n\nDerivation: from H4414 מָלַח (in its denominative sense); understood as land (H776 אֶרֶץ)\n\nStrong's: properly, salted (i.e. land), i.e. a desert\nKJV: barren land(-ness), salt (land).\n\nCognate Group: H4419 (mariner), H4420 (barren land), H4408 (mallows), H4414 ([idiom] at all), H4417 (salt)",
