    4502: "מִנְּזָר (minnᵉzâr | min-ez-awr')\n\nDerivation: from H5144 נָזַר\nStrong's: a prince\nKJV: crowned.\n\nCognate Group: H5139 (Nazarite), H5145 (consecration), H4502 (crowned), H5144 (consecrate)",
    4503: "מִנְחָה (minchâh | min-khaw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to apportion, i.e. bestow\nStrong's: a donation; euphemistically, tribute; specifically a sacrificial offering (usually bloodless and voluntary)\nKJV: gift, oblation, (meat) offering, present, sacrifice.\n\nCognate Group: H4503 (gift), H4508 (Minni)\nGreek Equivalents: G1435 δῶρον, G2378 θυσία, G3131 μάννα, G3646 ὁλοκαύτωμα, G4376 προσφορά",
    4504: "מִנְחָה (minchâh | min-khaw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H4503 מִנְחָה\nStrong's: a sacrificial offering\nKJV: oblation, meat offering.\n\nCognate Group: H4483 (number), H4577 (belly), H4484 (Mene), H4756 (lord), H4779 (rebellious), H4776 (rebellion), H4510 (number), H4504 (oblation)",
