    4509: "מִנְיָמִין (Minyâmîyn | min-yaw-meen')\n\nDerivation: from H4480 מִן and H3225 יָמִין ; from (the) right hand\nStrong's: Minjamin, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Miniamin. Compare H4326 מִיָּמִן .\n\nCognate Group: H4326 (Miamin), H4316 (Micha), H4318 (Micah), H4323 (brook), H4319 (Micaiah), H4509 (Miniamin), H4321 (Micah), H4332 (Mishael), H4322 (Michaiah), H4311 (Medeba), H4310 (any), H4320 (Micah), H4317 (Michael), H4324 (Michal)",
    4510: "מִנְיָן (minyân | min-yawn')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H4483 מְנָא\nStrong's: enumeration\nKJV: number.\n\nCognate Group: H4483 (number), H4577 (belly), H4484 (Mene), H4756 (lord), H4779 (rebellious), H4776 (rebellion), H4510 (number), H4504 (oblation)\nGreek Equivalents: G706 ἀριθμός",
