    4512: "מִנְלֶה (minleh | min-leh')\n\nDerivation: from H5239 נָלָה\nStrong's: completion, i.e. (in produce) wealth\nKJV: perfection.\n\nCognate Group: H5239 (make an end), H5241 (Nemuel), H5242 (Nemuelite), H4512 (perfection)",
    4513: "מָנַע (mânaʻ | maw-nah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to debar (negatively or positively) from benefit or injury\nKJV: deny, keep (back), refrain, restrain, withhold.\n\nCognate Group: H8555 (Timna), H4522 (discomfited), H4520 (of Manasseh), H4519 (Manasseh), H4513 (deny), H3234 (Imna)\nGreek Equivalents: G430 ἀνέχομαι, G566 ἀπέχει, G567 ἀπέχομαι, G568 ἀπέχω, G650 ἀποστερέω, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G1257 διαλείπω, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1907 ἐπέχω, G2186 ἐφίστημι, G2928 κρύπτω, G2967 κωλύω, G3635 ὀκνέω, G4863 συνάγω, G4912 συνέχω, G5302 ὑστερέω",
    4514: "מַנְעוּל (manʻûwl | man-ool')\n\nDerivation: or מַנְעֻל; from H5274 נָעַל\nStrong's: a bolt\nKJV: lock.\n\nCognate Group: H4514 (lock), H5274 (bolt), H5275 (dryshod), H4515 (shoe)",
    4515: "מִנְעָל (minʻâl | man-awl')Typo: xlit manʻâl corrected to minʻâl\n\nDerivation: from H5274 נָעַל\nStrong's: a bolt\nKJV: shoe.\n\nCognate Group: H4514 (lock), H5274 (bolt), H5275 (dryshod), H4515 (shoe)",
    4516: "מַנְעַם (manʻam | man-am')\n\nDerivation: from H5276 נָעֵם\nStrong's: a delicacy\nKJV: dainty.\n\nCognate Group: H5282 (pleasant), H5280 (Naamites), H5273 (pleasant), H5278 (beauty), H5276 (pass in beauty), H5283 (Naaman), H5284 (Naamathite), H4516 (dainty), H5281 (Naomi), H5277 (Naam), H5279 (Naamah)\nGreek Equivalents: G1588 ἐκλεκτός",
    4517: "מְנַעְנַע (mᵉnaʻnaʻ | men-ah-ah')\n\nDerivation: from H5128 נוּעַ\nStrong's: a sistrum (so called from its rattling sound)\nKJV: cornet.\n\nCognate Group: H5128 (continually), H5269 (Neah), H4517 (cornet), H5270 (Noah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2950 κύμβαλον",
    4518: "מְנַקִּית (mᵉnaqqîyth | men-ak-keeth')\n\nDerivation: from H5352 נָקָה\nStrong's: a sacrificial basin (for holding blood)\nKJV: bowl.\n\nCognate Group: H5352 (acquit [idiom] at all), H4518 (bowl), H5356 (cleanness), H5355 (blameless)",
    4519: "מְנַשֶּׁה (Mᵉnashsheh | men-ash-sheh')\n\nDerivation: from H5382 נָשָׁה ; causing to forget\nStrong's: Menashsheh, a grandson of Jacob, also the tribe descended from him, and its territory\nKJV: Manasseh.\n\nCognate Group: H8555 (Timna), H4522 (discomfited), H4520 (of Manasseh), H4519 (Manasseh), H4513 (deny), H3234 (Imna)\nGreek Equivalents: G3128 Μανασσῆς",
    4520: "מְנַשִּׁי (Mᵉnashshîy | men-ash-shee')\n\nDerivation: from H4519 מְנַשֶּׁה\nStrong's: a Menashshite or descendant of Menashsheh\nKJV: of Manasseh, Manassites.\n\nCognate Group: H8555 (Timna), H4522 (discomfited), H4520 (of Manasseh), H4519 (Manasseh), H4513 (deny), H3234 (Imna)",
    4521: "מְנָת (mᵉnâth | men-awth')\n\nDerivation: from H4487 מָנָה\nStrong's: an allotment (by courtesy, law or providence)\nKJV: portion.\n\nCognate Group: H8553 (Timnah), H4487 (appoint), H4521 (portion), H4507 (number), H8556 (Timnath-heres), H4490 (such things as belonged), H4489 (time), H4497 (son), H8554 (Timnite), H4488 (maneh)",
    4522: "מַס (maç | mas)\n\nDerivation: or מִס; from H4549 מָסַס\nStrong's: properly, a burden (as causing to faint), i.e. a tax in the form of forced labor\nKJV: discomfited, levy, task(-master), tribute(-tary).\n\nCognate Group: H8555 (Timna), H4522 (discomfited), H4520 (of Manasseh), H4519 (Manasseh), H4513 (deny), H3234 (Imna)\nGreek Equivalents: G2041 ἔργον, G2275 ἥττημα, G5056 τέλος, G5255 ὑπήκοος, G5411 φόρος",
    4523: "מָס (mâç | mawce)\n\nDerivation: from H4549 מָסַס\nStrong's: fainting, i.e. (figuratively) disconsolate\nKJV: is afflicted.\n\nCognate Group: H4531 (temptation), H8557 (melt), H4523 (is afflicted), H4549 (discourage)",
    4524: "מֵסַב (mêçab | may-sab')\n\nDerivation: plural masculine מְסִבִּים; or feminine מְסִבֹּות; from H5437 סָבַב\nStrong's: a divan (as enclosing the room); abstractly (adverbial) around\nKJV: that compass about, (place) round about, at table.\n\nCognate Group: H5439 (about), H5437 (bring), H4142 (being changed), H5252 (cause), H4524 (that compass about), H4036 (Magormissabib), H5438 (cause), H4141 (winding about)",
    4525: "מַסְגֵּר (maçgêr | mas-gare')\n\nDerivation: from H5462 סָגַר\nStrong's: a fastener, i.e. (of a person) a smith, (of a thing) a prison\nKJV: prison, smith.\n\nCognate Group: H5458 (caul), H4525 (prison), H5462 (close up), H5474 (ward), H4526 (border)\nGreek Equivalents: G1199 δεσμόν, G1202 δεσμώτης, G3794 ὀχύρωμα, G5438 φυλακή",
    4526: "מִסְגֶּרֶת (miçgereth | mis-gheh'-reth)\n\nDerivation: from H5462 סָגַר\nStrong's: something enclosing, i.e. a margin (of a region, of a panel); concretely, a stronghold\nKJV: border, close place, hole.\n\nCognate Group: H5458 (caul), H4525 (prison), H5462 (close up), H5474 (ward), H4526 (border)",
