    4545: "מַסֶּכֶת (maççeketh | mas-seh'-keth)\n\nDerivation: from H5259 נָסַךְ in the sense of spreading out\nStrong's: something expanded, i.e. the warp in aloom (as stretched out to receive the woof)\nKJV: web.\n\nCognate Group: H4545 (web), H5259 (that is spread), H4541 (covering)",
    4546: "מְסִלָּה (mᵉçillâh | mes-il-law')\n\nDerivation: from H5549 סָלַל\nStrong's: a thoroughfare (as turnpiked), literally or figuratively; specifically a viaduct, a staircase\nKJV: causeway, course, highway, path, terrace.\n\nCognate Group: H4547 (highway), H5542 (Selah), H4546 (causeway), H5550 (bank), H5549 (cast up), H5551 (ladder)\nGreek Equivalents: G3598 ὁδός, G5010 τάξις, G5147 τρίβος",
    4547: "מַסְלוּל (maçlûwl | mas-lool')\n\nDerivation: from H5549 סָלַל\nStrong's: a thoroughfare (as turnpiked)\nKJV: highway.\n\nCognate Group: H4547 (highway), H5542 (Selah), H4546 (causeway), H5550 (bank), H5549 (cast up), H5551 (ladder)\nGreek Equivalents: G3598 ὁδός",
    4548: "מַסְמֵר (maçmêr | mas-mare')\n\nDerivation: or מִסְמֵר; also (feminine) מַסְמְרָה; or מִסְמְרָה; or even מַשְׂמְרָה; (Ecclesiastes 12:11), from H5568 סָמַר\nStrong's: a peg (as bristling from the surface)\nKJV: nail.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)\nGreek Equivalents: G2247 ἧλος, G2247 ἧλος",
    4549: "מָסַס (mâçaç | maw-sas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to liquefy; figuratively, to waste (with disease), to faint (with fatigue, fear or grief)\nKJV: discourage, faint, be loosed, melt (away), refuse, [idiom] utterly.\n\nCognate Group: H4531 (temptation), H8557 (melt), H4523 (is afflicted), H4549 (discourage)\nGreek Equivalents: G868 ἀφίστημι, G1026 βρέχω, G1168 δειλιάω, G1262 διαλύω, G1839 ἐξίστημι, G2274 ἡττάω, G2352 θραύω, G4422 πτοέω, G4531 σαλεύω, G5080 τήκω",
    4550: "מַסַּע (maççaʻ | mas-sah')\n\nDerivation: from H5265 נָסַע\nStrong's: a departure (from striking the tents), i.e. march (not necessarily a single day's travel); by implication, a station (or point of departure)\nKJV: journey(-ing).\n\nCognate Group: H4551 (before it was brought), H5265 (cause to blow), H4550 (journey)",
    4551: "מַסָּע (maççâʻ | mas-saw')\n\nDerivation: from H5265 נָסַע in the sense of projecting\nStrong's: a missile (spear or arrow); also a quarry (whence stones are, as it were, ejected)\nKJV: before it was brought, dart.\n\nCognate Group: H4551 (before it was brought), H5265 (cause to blow), H4550 (journey)",
    4552: "מִסְעָד (miçʻâd | mis-awd')\n\nDerivation: ' from H5582 סָעַד\nStrong's: a balustrade (for stairs)\nKJV: pillar.\n\nCognate Group: H4552 (pillar), H5582 (comfort)",
    4553: "מִסְפֵּד (miçpêd | mis-pade')\n\nDerivation: from H5594 סָפַד\nStrong's: a lamentation\nKJV: lamentation, one mourneth, mourning, wailing.\n\nCognate Group: H5594 (lament), H4553 (lamentation)\nGreek Equivalents: G2870 κοπετός, G3997 πένθος",
    4554: "מִסְפֹּוא (miçpôwʼ | mis-po')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to collect\nStrong's: fodder\nKJV: provender.\n\nCognate Group: H4554 (provender)\nGreek Equivalents: G5527 χόρτασμα",
    4555: "מִסְפָּחָה (miçpâchâh | mis-paw-khaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5596 סָפַח\nStrong's: a veil (as spread out)\nKJV: kerchief.\n\nCognate Group: H5596 (abiding), H4555 (kerchief), H4556 (scab), H5602 (bowl), H5601 (sapphire), H5597 (scab)\nGreek Equivalents: G4018 περιβόλαιον",
    4556: "מִסְפַּחַת (miçpachath | mis-pakh'-ath)\n\nDerivation: from H5596 סָפַח\nStrong's: scruf (as spreading over the surface)\nKJV: scab.\n\nCognate Group: H5596 (abiding), H4555 (kerchief), H4556 (scab), H5602 (bowl), H5601 (sapphire), H5597 (scab)",
