    4565: "מִסְתָּר (miçtâr | mis-tawr')\n\nDerivation: from H5641 סָתַר\nStrong's: properly, a concealer, i.e. a covert\nKJV: secret(-ly, place).\n\nCognate Group: H5644 (Zithri), H4563 (covert), H5641 (be absent), H4565 (secret), H5639 (Sethur), H4564 (hid), H5643 (backbiting)\nGreek Equivalents: G517 ἀόρατος, G2927 κρυπτός, G2927 κρυπτός, G2977 λάθρα",
