    4569: "מַעֲבָר (maʻăbâr | mah-ab-awr')\n\nDerivation: or feminine מַעֲבָרָה; from H5674 עָבַר\nStrong's: a crossing-place (of a river, a ford; of a mountain, a pass); abstractly, a transit, i.e. (figuratively) overwhelming\nKJV: ford, place where...pass, passage.\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)\nGreek Equivalents: G5327 φάραγξ",
    4570: "מַעְגָּל (maʻgâl | mah-gawl')\n\nDerivation: or feminine מַעְגָּלָה; from the same as H5696 עָגֹל\nStrong's: a track (literally or figuratively); also a rampart (as circular)\nKJV: going, path, trench, way(-side).\n\nCognate Group: H4570 (going), H5696 (round), H5700 (Eglon), H5699 (cart), H5697 (calf), H5695 (bullock), H5698 (Eglah), H5694 (earring)\nGreek Equivalents: G3598 ὁδός, G5147 τρίβος, G5163 τροχιά",
