    4577: "מְעָה (mᵉʻâh | meh-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or מְעָא; (Aramaic), corresponding to H4578 מֵעֶה \n\nTypo: xlit mêʻâh corrected to mêʻeh\n\nStrong's: only in plural the bowels\nKJV: belly.\n\nCognate Group: H4483 (number), H4577 (belly), H4484 (Mene), H4756 (lord), H4779 (rebellious), H4776 (rebellion), H4510 (number), H4504 (oblation)",
    4578: "מֵעֶה (mêʻeh | may-aw')Typo: xlit mêʻâh corrected to mêʻeh\n\nGreek Equivalents: G2836 κοιλία \n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to be soft\nStrong's: used only in plural the intestines, or (collectively) the abdomen, figuratively, sympathy; by implication, a vest; by extension the stomach, the uterus (or of men, the seat of generation), the heart (figuratively)\n\nKJV: belly, bowels, [idiom] heart, womb.\n\nCognate Group: H4586 (Mehunim), H4579 (gravel), H4578 (belly)",
    4579: "מֵעָה (mêʻâh | may-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4578 מֵעֶה \n\nTypo: xlit mêʻâh corrected to mêʻeh\n\nStrong's: the belly, i.e. (figuratively) interior\nKJV: gravel.\n\nCognate Group: H4586 (Mehunim), H4579 (gravel), H4578 (belly)",
