    4581: "מָעֹוז (mâʻôwz | maw-oze')\n\nDerivation: (also מָעוּז); or מָעֹז (also מָעֻז; from H5810 עָזַז\nStrong's: a fortified place; figuratively, a defence\nKJV: force, fort(-ress), rock, strength(-en), ([idiom] most) strong (hold).\n\nCognate Group: H5761 (Avim), H5762 (Avith), H5756 (gather), H4581 (force)\nGreek Equivalents: G407 ἀνδρίζομαι, G2478 ἰσχυρός, G4714 στάσις",
    4582: "מָעֹוךְ (Mâʻôwk | maw-oke')\n\nDerivation: from H4600 מָעַךְ ; oppressed\nStrong's: Maok, a Philistine\nKJV: Maoch.\n\nCognate Group: H4600 (bruised), H4602 (Maachathite), H4601 (Maachah), H4582 (Maoch)",
    4583: "מָעֹון (mâʻôwn | maw-ohn')\n\nDerivation: or מָעִין; (1 Chronicles 4:41), from the same as H5772 עֹונָה\nStrong's: an abode, of God (the Tabernacle or the Temple), men (their home) or animals (their lair); hence, a retreat (asylum)\nKJV: den, dwelling((-) place), habitation.\n\nCognate Group: H4587 (Meonothai), H4584 (Maon), H4585 (den), H6030 (give account), H4583 (den), H5868 (mighty)\nGreek Equivalents: G2143 εὐπρέπεια, G2732 κατοικητήριον, G3624 οἶκος, G5117 τόπος",
    4584: "מָעֹון (Mâʻôwn | maw-ohn')\n\nDerivation: the same as H4583 מָעֹון ; a residence\nStrong's: Maon, the name of an Israelite and of a place in Palestine\nKJV: Maon, Maonites. Compare H1010 בֵּית בַּעַל מְעֹון, H4586 מְעוּנִי \n\nTypo: lemma מְעוּנָי third vowel, corrected to מְעוּנִי\n\n.\n\nCognate Group: H4587 (Meonothai), H4584 (Maon), H4585 (den), H6030 (give account), H4583 (den), H5868 (mighty)",
