    4589: "מָעֹור (mâʻôwr | maw-ore')\n\nDerivation: from H5783 עוּר\nStrong's: nakedness, i.e. (in plural) the pudenda\nKJV: nakedness.\n\nCognate Group: H6174 (naked), H5783 (be made naked), H4589 (nakedness), H4636 (naked), H5903 (naked)",
    4590: "מַעַזְיָה (Maʻazyâh | mah-az-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or מַעַזְיָהוּ; probably from H5756 עוּז (in the sense of protection) and H3050 יָהּ ; rescue of Jah\nStrong's: Maazjah, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Maaziah.\n\nCognate Group: H4590 (Maaziah)",
    4591: "מָעַט (mâʻaṭ | maw-at')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to pare off, i.e. lessen; intransitively, to be (or causatively, to make) small or few (or figuratively, ineffective)\nKJV: suffer to decrease, diminish, (be, [idiom] borrow a, give, make) few (in number, -ness), gather least (little), be (seem) little, ([idiom] give the) less, be minished, bring to nothing.\n\nCognate Group: H4592 (almost few), H4591 (suffer to decrease), H4597 (Maai)\nGreek Equivalents: G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1640 ἐλάσσων, G1641 ἐλαττονέω, G1642 ἐλαττόω, G3398 μικρός, G3641 ὀλίγος, G3641 ὀλίγος",
