    4594: "מַעֲטֶה (maʻăṭeh | mah-at-eh')\n\nDerivation: from H5844 עָטָה\nStrong's: a vestment\nKJV: garment.\n\nCognate Group: H5844 (array self), H4594 (garment)\nGreek Equivalents: G2689 καταστολή",
    4595: "מַעֲטָפָה (maʻăṭâphâh | mah-at-aw-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H5848 עָטַף\nStrong's: a cloak\nKJV: mantle.\n\nCognate Group: H5848 (cover), H4595 (mantle)",
    4596: "מְעִי (mᵉʻîy | meh-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H5753 עָוָה ; (compare H5856 עִי)\n\nStrong's: a pile of rubbish (as contorted), i.e. a ruin\nKJV: heap.\n\nCognate Group: H4596 (heap), H5754 ([idiom] overturn), H1164 (grave), H5856 (heap), H5753 (do amiss), H5773 ([idiom] perverse)\nGreek Equivalents: G1656 ἔλεος, G2588 καρδία, G5529 Χουζᾶς",
    4597: "מָעַי (Mâʻay | maw-ah'-ee)\n\nTypo: xlit Mâʻai corrected to Mâʻay\n\nDerivation: probably from H4578 מֵעֶה \n\nTypo: xlit mêʻâh corrected to mêʻeh\n\n; sympathetic\nStrong's: Maai, an Israelite\nKJV: Maai.\n\nCognate Group: H4592 (almost few), H4591 (suffer to decrease), H4597 (Maai)",
