    4600: "מָעַךְ (mâʻak | maw-ak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to press, i.e. to pierce, emasculate, handle\nKJV: bruised, stuck, be pressed.\n\nCognate Group: H4600 (bruised), H4602 (Maachathite), H4601 (Maachah), H4582 (Maoch)\nGreek Equivalents: G4098 πίπτω",
    4601: "מַעֲכָה (Maʻăkâh | mah-ak-aw')\n\nDerivation: or מַעֲכָת; (Joshua 13:13), from H4600 מָעַךְ ; depression\nStrong's: Maakah (or Maakath), the name of a place in Syria, also of a Mesopotamian, of three Israelites, and of four Israelitesses and one Syrian woman\nKJV: Maachah, Maachathites. See also H1038 בֵּית מַעֲכָה .\n\nCognate Group: H4600 (bruised), H4602 (Maachathite), H4601 (Maachah), H4582 (Maoch)",
    4602: "מַעֲכָתִי (Maʻăkâthîy | mah-ak-aw-thee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H4601 מַעֲכָה\nStrong's: a Maakathite, or inhabitant of Maakah\nKJV: Maachathite.\n\nCognate Group: H4600 (bruised), H4602 (Maachathite), H4601 (Maachah), H4582 (Maoch)",
    4603: "מָעַל (mâʻal | maw-al')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to cover up; used only figuratively, to act covertly, i.e. treacherously\nKJV: transgress, (commit, do a) trespass(-ing).\n\nCognate Group: H4598 (cloke), H4603 (transgress), H4604 (falsehood)\nGreek Equivalents: G91 ἀδικέω, G114 ἀθετέω, G264 ἁμαρτάνω, G544 ἀπειθέω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G2990 λανθάνω, G3845 παραβαίνω, G3895 παραπίπτω, G4105 πλανάω",
