    4653: "מִפְלַגָּה (miphlaggâh | mif-lag-gaw')\n\nDerivation: from H6385 פָּלַג\nStrong's: a classification\nKJV: division.\n\nCognate Group: H6391 (division), H6385 (divide), H6388 (river), H4653 (division), H6394 (Pildash), H6393 (torch), H6370 (concubine), H6390 (division), H6389 (Peleg)",
    4654: "מַפָּלָה (mappâlâh | map-paw-law')\n\nDerivation: or מַפֵּלָה; from H5307 נָפַל\nStrong's: something fallen, i.e. a ruin\nKJV: ruin(-ous).\n\nCognate Group: H4651 (flake), H5307 (be accepted), H5303 (giant), H4658 (carcase), H5309 (untimely birth), H4654 (ruin)\nGreek Equivalents: G4431 πτῶσις",
    4655: "מִפְלָט (miphlâṭ | mif-lawt')\n\nDerivation: from H6403 פָּלַט\nStrong's: an escape\nKJV: escape.\n\nCognate Group: H6403 (calve), H6410 (Pelatiah), H4655 (escape), H6412 (escape), H3311 (Japhleti), H6405 (deliverance), H6406 (Palti), H6408 (Piltai), H6409 (Paltiel), H6413 (deliverance), H6404 (Pelet), H3310 (Japhlet)",
    4656: "מִפְלֶצֶת (miphletseth | mif-leh'-tseth)\n\nDerivation: from H6426 פָּלַץ\nStrong's: a terror, i.e. an idol\nKJV: idol.\n\nCognate Group: H4656 (idol), H6427 (fearfulness), H8606 (terrible), H6426 (tremble)\nGreek Equivalents: G1497 εἴδωλον",
    4657: "מִפְלָשׂ (miphlâs | mif-lawce')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to balance\nStrong's: a poising\nKJV: balancing.\n\nCognate Group: H6424 (make), H6425 (scales), H4657 (balancing)\nGreek Equivalents: G1253 διάκρισις",
    4658: "מַפֶּלֶת (mappeleth | map-peh'-leth)\n\nDerivation: from H5307 נָפַל\nStrong's: fall, i.e. decadence; concretely, a ruin; specifically a carcase\nKJV: carcase, fall, ruin.\n\nCognate Group: H4651 (flake), H5307 (be accepted), H5303 (giant), H4658 (carcase), H5309 (untimely birth), H4654 (ruin)\nGreek Equivalents: G4430 πτῶμα, G4431 πτῶσις",
    4659: "מִפְעָל (miphʻâl | mif-awl')\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) מִפְעָלָה; from H6466 פָּעַל\nStrong's: a performance\nKJV: work.\n\nCognate Group: H6467 (act), H6466 (commit), H4659 (work), H6469 (Peulthai), H6468 (labour)",
    4660: "מַפָּץ (mappâts | map-pawts')\n\nDerivation: from H5310 נָפַץ\nStrong's: a smiting to pieces\nKJV: slaughter.\n\nCognate Group: H4661 (battle ax), H5310 (be beaten in sunder), H5311 (scattering), H4660 (slaughter)",
    4661: "מַפֵּץ (mappêts | map-pates')\n\nDerivation: from H5310 נָפַץ\nStrong's: a smiter, i.e. a war club\nKJV: battle ax.\n\nCognate Group: H4661 (battle ax), H5310 (be beaten in sunder), H5311 (scattering), H4660 (slaughter)",
    4662: "מִפְקָד (miphqâd | mif-kawd')\n\nDerivation: from H6485 פָּקַד\nStrong's: an appointment, i.e. mandate; concretely, a designated spot; specifically, a census\nKJV: appointed place, commandment, number.\n\nCognate Group: H4663 (Miphkad), H4662 (appointed place), H6487 (that which was delivered), H6490 (commandment), H6485 (appoint), H6496 (which had the charge), H6488 (ward), H6489 (Pekod), H6486 (account)\nGreek Equivalents: G673 ἀποχωρίζω, G4367 προστάσσω",
    4663: "מִפְקָד (Miphqâd | mif-kawd')\n\nDerivation: the same as H4662 מִפְקָד ; assignment\nStrong's: Miphkad, the name of a gate in Jerusalem\nKJV: Miphkad.\n\nCognate Group: H4663 (Miphkad), H4662 (appointed place), H6487 (that which was delivered), H6490 (commandment), H6485 (appoint), H6496 (which had the charge), H6488 (ward), H6489 (Pekod), H6486 (account)",
    4664: "מִפְרָץ (miphrâts | mif-rawts')\n\nDerivation: from H6555 פָּרַץ \n\nTypo: lemma פּרַץ missing vowel, corrected to פָּרַץ\n\nStrong's: a break (in the shore), i.e. a haven\nKJV: breach.\n\nCognate Group: H4664 (breach)\nGreek Equivalents: G1327 διέξοδος",
    4665: "מִפְרֶקֶת (miphreqeth | mif-reh'-keth)Typo: xlit miphreketh corrected to miphreqeth\n\nGreek Equivalents: G3577 νῶτος \n\nDerivation: from H6561 פָּרַק\nStrong's: properly, a fracture, i.e. joint (vertebrae) of the neck\nKJV: neck.\n\nCognate Group: H6561 (break), H6563 (crossway), H4665 (neck), H6564 (broth)",
    4666: "מִפְרָשׂ (miphrâs | mif-rawce')\n\nDerivation: from H6566 פָּרַשׂ\nStrong's: an expansion\nKJV: that which...spreadest forth, spreading.\n\nCognate Group: H6566 (break), H6576 (spread), H4666 (that which)",
    4667: "מִפְשָׂעָה (miphsâʻâh | mif-saw-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H6585 פָּשַׂע\nStrong's: a stride, i.e. (by euphemism) the crotch\nKJV: buttocks.\n\nCognate Group: H6585 (go), H4667 (buttocks), H6587 (step)",
    4668: "מַפְתֵּחַ (maphtêach | maf-tay'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H6605 פָּתַח\nStrong's: an opener, i.e. a key\nKJV: key.\n\nCognate Group: H6608 (entrance), H5318 (Neptoah), H4668 (key), H6605 (appear), H6607 (door), H4669 (opening), H6611 (Pethakiah), H3317 (Jiphthah-el), H6609 (drawn sword), H6610 (open), H3316 (Jephthah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2807 κλείς",
    4669: "מִפְתָּח (miphtâch | mif-tawkh')\n\nDerivation: from H6605 פָּתַח\nStrong's: an aperture, i.e. (figuratively) utterance\nKJV: opening.\n\nCognate Group: H6608 (entrance), H5318 (Neptoah), H4668 (key), H6605 (appear), H6607 (door), H4669 (opening), H6611 (Pethakiah), H3317 (Jiphthah-el), H6609 (drawn sword), H6610 (open), H3316 (Jephthah)\nGreek Equivalents: G399 ἀναφέρω",
    4670: "מִפְתָּן (miphtân | mif-tawn')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H6620 פֶּתֶן\nStrong's: a stretcher, i.e. a sill\nKJV: threshold.\n\nCognate Group: H4670 (threshold), H6620 (adder)\nGreek Equivalents: G898 βαθμός",
    4671: "מֹץ (môts | motes)\n\nDerivation: or מֹוץ; (Zephaniah 2:2), from H4160 מוּץ\nStrong's: chaff (as pressed out, i.e. winnowed or (rather) threshed loose)\nKJV: chaff.\n\nCognate Group: H4671 (chaff)\nGreek Equivalents: G892 ἄχυρον, G2868 κονιορτός, G5529 Χουζᾶς",
    4672: "מָצָא (mâtsâʼ | maw-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to come forth to, i.e. appear or exist; transitively, to attain, i.e. find or acquire; figuratively, to occur, meet or be present\nKJV: [phrase] be able, befall, being, catch, [idiom] certainly, (cause to) come (on, to, to hand), deliver, be enough (cause to) find(-ing, occasion, out), get (hold upon), [idiom] have (here), be here, hit, be left, light (up-) on, meet (with), [idiom] occasion serve, (be) present, ready, speed, suffice, take hold on.\n\nCognate Group: H4672 (be able), H4677 (Mesobaite)\nGreek Equivalents: G114 ἀθετέω, G322 ἀναδείκνυμι, G700 ἀρέσκω, G714 ἀρκέω, G864 ἀφικνέομαι, G1096 γίνομαι, G1097 γινώσκω, G1410 δύναμαι, G1941 ἐπικαλέομαι, G2014 ἐπιφαίνω, G2111 εὔθετος, G2141 εὐπορέω, G2147 εὑρίσκω, G2192 ἔχω, G2212 ζητέω, G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G2641 καταλείπω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3860 παραδίδωμι, G4374 προσφέρω, G4393 προφέρω, G4819 συμβαίνω, G4876 συναντάω, G5177 τυγχάνω, G5297 ὑποφέρω",
    4673: "מַצָּב (matstsâb | mats-tsawb')\n\nDerivation: from H5324 נָצַב\nStrong's: a fixed spot; figuratively, an office, a military post\nKJV: garrison, station, place where...stood.\n\nCognate Group: H5324 (appointed), H5325 (haft), H5334 (Nezib), H5333 (garrison), H4674 (mount), H4673 (garrison), H4678 (pillar), H4676 (garrison), H4675 (army)\nGreek Equivalents: G3622 οἰκονομία, G5287 ὑπόστασις",
    4674: "מֻצָּב (mutstsâb | moots-tsawb')\n\nDerivation: from H5324 נָצַב\nStrong's: a station, i.e. military post\nKJV: mount.\n\nCognate Group: H5324 (appointed), H5325 (haft), H5334 (Nezib), H5333 (garrison), H4674 (mount), H4673 (garrison), H4678 (pillar), H4676 (garrison), H4675 (army)\nGreek Equivalents: G4714 στάσις, G5482 χάραξ",
    4675: "מַצָּבָה (matstsâbâh | mats-tsaw-baw')\n\nDerivation: or מִצָּבָה; feminine of H4673 מַצָּב\nStrong's: a military guard\nKJV: army, garrison.\n\nCognate Group: H5324 (appointed), H5325 (haft), H5334 (Nezib), H5333 (garrison), H4674 (mount), H4673 (garrison), H4678 (pillar), H4676 (garrison), H4675 (army)",
    4676: "מַצֵּבָה (matstsêbâh | mats-tsay-baw')\n\nDerivation: feminine (causatively) participle of H5324 נָצַב\nStrong's: something stationed, i.e. a column or (memorial stone); by analogy, an idol\nKJV: garrison, (standing) image, pillar.\n\nCognate Group: H5324 (appointed), H5325 (haft), H5334 (Nezib), H5333 (garrison), H4674 (mount), H4673 (garrison), H4678 (pillar), H4676 (garrison), H4675 (army)\nGreek Equivalents: G2379 θυσιαστήριον, G3037 λίθος, G4768 στυγνάζω",
    4677: "מְצֹבָיָה (Mᵉtsôbâyâh | mets-o-baw-yaw')\n\nDerivation: apparently from H4672 מָצָא and H3050 יָהּ ; found of Jah\nStrong's: Metsobajah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Mesobaite.\n\nCognate Group: H4672 (be able), H4677 (Mesobaite)",
    4678: "מַצֶּבֶת (matstsebeth | mats-tseh'-beth)\n\nDerivation: from H5324 נָצַב\nStrong's: something stationary, i.e. a monumental stone; also the stock of atree\nKJV: pillar, substance.\n\nCognate Group: H5324 (appointed), H5325 (haft), H5334 (Nezib), H5333 (garrison), H4674 (mount), H4673 (garrison), H4678 (pillar), H4676 (garrison), H4675 (army)\nGreek Equivalents: G2336 θήκη",
    4679: "מְצַד (mᵉtsad | mets-ad')\n\nDerivation: or מְצָד; or (feminine) מְצָדָה; from H6679 צוּד\nStrong's: a fastness (as a covert of ambush)\nKJV: castle, fort, (strong) hold, munition.\n\nCognate Group: H6719 (hunter), H4685 (bulwark), H6679 (chase), H4686 (castle), H6718 ([idiom] catcheth), H4679 (castle)\nGreek Equivalents: G996 βοήθεια, G3794 ὀχύρωμα, G4042 περιοχή, G4728 στενός",
    4680: "מָצָה (mâtsâh | maw-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to suck out; by implication, to drain, to squeeze out\nKJV: suck, wring (out).\n\nCognate Group: H4680 (suck), H4681 (Mozah)\nGreek Equivalents: G106 ἄζυμος",
    4681: "מֹצָה (Môtsâh | mo-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: active participle feminine of H4680 מָצָה ; drained\nStrong's: Motsah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Mozah.\n\nCognate Group: H4680 (suck), H4681 (Mozah)",
    4682: "מַצָּה (matstsâh | mats-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: from H4711 מָצַץ in the sense of greedily devouring for sweetness\nStrong's: properly, sweetness; concretely, sweet (i.e. not soured or bittered with yeast); specifically, an unfermented cake or loaf, or (elliptically) the festival of Passover (because no leaven was then used)\nKJV: unleaved (bread, cake), without leaven.\n\nCognate Group: H4682 (unleaved), H4711 (milk)\nGreek Equivalents: G740 ἄρτος, G2556 κακός, G3163 μάχη",
    4683: "מַצָּה (matstsâh | mats-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5327 נָצָה\nStrong's: a quarrel\nKJV: contention, debate, strife.\n\nCognate Group: H5327 (be laid waste), H4695 (that contended), H4683 (contention)",
    4684: "מַצְהָלָה (matshâlâh | mats-haw-law')\n\nDerivation: from H6670 צָהַל\nStrong's: a whinnying (through impatience for battle or lust)\nKJV: neighing.\n\nCognate Group: H4684 (neighing), H6670 (bellow)",
    4685: "מָצֹוד (mâtsôwd | maw-tsode')\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) מְצֹודָה; or מצֹדָה; from H6679 צוּד ; also (by interchange for H4679 מְצַד)\n\nStrong's: a net (for capturing animals or fishes); afastness or (beseiging) tower\nKJV: bulwark, hold, munition, net, snare.\n\nCognate Group: H6719 (hunter), H4685 (bulwark), H6679 (chase), H4686 (castle), H6718 ([idiom] catcheth), H4679 (castle)\nGreek Equivalents: G293 ἀμφίβληστρον, G5438 φυλακή, G5482 χάραξ",
    4686: "מָצוּד (mâtsûwd | maw-tsood')\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) מְצוּדָה; or מְצֻדָה; for H4685 מָצֹוד\nStrong's: a net, or (abstractly) capture; also a fastness\nKJV: castle, defense, fort(-ress), (strong) hold, be hunted, net, snare, strong place.\n\nCognate Group: H6719 (hunter), H4685 (bulwark), H6679 (chase), H4686 (castle), H6718 ([idiom] catcheth), H4679 (castle)\nGreek Equivalents: G3803 παγίς, G4042 περιοχή",
    4687: "מִצְוָה (mitsvâh | mits-vaw')\n\nDerivation: from H6680 צָוָה\nStrong's: a command, whether human or divine (collectively, the Law)\nKJV: (which was) commanded(-ment), law, ordinance, precept.\n\nCognate Group: H6673 (commandment), H4687 (commanded), H6725 (sign), H6680 (appoint)\nGreek Equivalents: G1345 δικαίωμα, G1778 ἔνταλμα, G1785 ἐντολή, G2920 κρίσις, G3004 λέγω, G3056 λόγος, G3551 νόμος, G3598 ὁδός, G4487 ῥῆμα, G5456 φωνή",
    4688: "מְצֹולָה (mᵉtsôwlâh | mets-o-law')\n\nDerivation: or מְצֹלָה; also מְצוּלָה; or מְצֻלָה; from the same as H6683 צוּלָה\nStrong's: a deep place (of water or mud)\nKJV: bottom, deep, depth.\n\nCognate Group: H6683 (deep), H4699 (bottom), H4688 (bottom)\nGreek Equivalents: G12 ἄβυσσος, G899 βάθος, G1037 βυθός, G1037 βυθός, G2288 θάνατος",
    4689: "מָצֹוק (mâtsôwq | maw-tsoke')\n\nDerivation: from H6693 צוּק\nStrong's: a narrow place, i.e. (abstractly and figuratively) confinement or disability\nKJV: anguish, distress, straitness.\n\nCognate Group: H4164 (anguish), H6695 (anguish), H6693 (constrain), H4691 (anguish), H4689 (anguish)\nGreek Equivalents: G318 ἀνάγκη, G2347 θλῖψις",
    4690: "מָצוּק (mâtsûwq | maw-tsook')\n\nDerivation: or מָצֻק; from H6693 צוּק\nStrong's: something narrow, i.e. a column or hilltop\nKJV: pillar, situate.\n\nCognate Group: H6694 (be molten), H4690 (pillar)",
    4691: "מְצוּקָה (mᵉtsûwqâh | mets-oo-kaw')\n\nDerivation: or מְצֻקָה; feminine of H4690 מָצוּק\nStrong's: narrowness, i.e. (figuratively) trouble\nKJV: anguish, distress.\n\nCognate Group: H4164 (anguish), H6695 (anguish), H6693 (constrain), H4691 (anguish), H4689 (anguish)",
    4692: "מָצֹור (mâtsôwr | maw-tsore')\n\nDerivation: or מָצוּר; from H6696 צוּר\nStrong's: something hemming in, i.e. (objectively) a mound (of besiegers), (abstractly) a siege, (figuratively) distress; or (subjectively) a fastness\nKJV: besieged, bulwark, defence, fenced, fortress, siege, strong (hold), tower.\n\nCognate Group: H6696 (adversary), H6887 (adversary), H4694 (fenced), H4692 (besieged)\nGreek Equivalents: G3794 ὀχύρωμα, G4042 περιοχή, G4730 στενοχωρία, G4928 συνοχή, G5482 χάραξ",
    4693: "מָצֹור (mâtsôwr | maw-tsore')\n\nDerivation: the same as H4692 מָצֹור in the sense of a limit\nStrong's: Egypt (as the border of Palestine)\nKJV: besieged places, defense, fortified.\n\nCognate Group: H4714 (Egypt), H4739 (Makaz), H4693 (besieged places), H4719 (Makkedah), H4713 (Egyptian), H4731 (rod), H4732 (Mikloth)",
    4694: "מְצוּרָה (mᵉtsûwrâh | mets-oo-raw')\n\nDerivation: or מְצֻרָה; feminine of H4692 מָצֹור\nStrong's: a hemming in, i.e. (objectively) a mound (of siege), or (subjectively) a rampart (of protection), (abstractly) fortification\nKJV: fenced (city, fort, munition, strong hold.\n\nCognate Group: H6696 (adversary), H6887 (adversary), H4694 (fenced), H4692 (besieged)\nGreek Equivalents: G4444 πύργος, G5038 τεῖχος",
    4695: "מַצּוּת (matstsûwth | mats-tsooth')\n\nDerivation: from H5327 נָצָה\nStrong's: a quarrel\nKJV: that contended.\n\nCognate Group: H5327 (be laid waste), H4695 (that contended), H4683 (contention)",
    4696: "מֵצַח (mêtsach | may'-tsakh)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be clear, i.e. conspicuous\nStrong's: the forehead (as open and prominent)\nKJV: brow, forehead, [phrase] impudent.\n\nCognate Group: H4696 (brow), H4697 (greaves)\nGreek Equivalents: G3359 μέτωπον, G3799 ὄψις",
    4697: "מִצְחָה (mitschâh | mits-khaw')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H4696 מֵצַח\nStrong's: a shinpiece of armor (as prominent), only plural\nKJV: greaves.\n\nCognate Group: H4696 (brow), H4697 (greaves)",
    4698: "מְצִלָּה (mᵉtsillâh | mets-il-law')\n\nDerivation: from H6750 צָלַל\nStrong's: a tinkler, i.e. a bell\nKJV: bell.\n\nCognate Group: H6767 (cymbal), H4698 (bell), H4700 (cymbals), H6750 (quiver)\nGreek Equivalents: G2950 κύμβαλον",
    4699: "מְצֻלָּה (mᵉtsullâh | mets-ool-law')\n\nDerivation: from H6751 צָלַל\nStrong's: shade\nKJV: bottom.\n\nCognate Group: H6683 (deep), H4699 (bottom), H4688 (bottom)",
    4700: "מְצֵלֶת (mᵉtsêleth | mets-ay'-leth)\n\nDerivation: from H6750 צָלַל\nStrong's: (only dual) double tinklers, i.e. cymbals\nKJV: cymbals.\n\nCognate Group: H6767 (cymbal), H4698 (bell), H4700 (cymbals), H6750 (quiver)",
    4701: "מִצְנֶפֶת (mitsnepheth | mits-neh'-feth)\n\nDerivation: from H6801 צָנַף\nStrong's: a tiara, i.e. official turban (of a king or high priest)\nKJV: diadem, mitre.\n\nCognate Group: H6797 (diadem), H6801 (be attired), H6802 ([idiom] toss), H4701 (diadem)",
    4702: "מַצָּע (matstsâʻ | mats-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: from H3331 יַצַע\nStrong's: a couch\nKJV: bed.\n\nCognate Group: H3326 (bed), H4702 (bed), H3331 (make bed)",
    4703: "מִצְעָד (mitsʻâd | mits-awd')\n\nDerivation: from H6805 צָעַד\nStrong's: a step; figuratively, companionship\nKJV: going, step.\n\nCognate Group: H4703 (going), H6807 (going), H6805 (bring), H6806 (pace)",
    4704: "מִצְּעִירָה (mitstsᵉʻîyrâh | mits-tseh-ee-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4705 מִצְעָר\nStrong's: properly, littleness; concretely, diminutive\nKJV: little.\n\nCognate Group: H4706 (Mizar), H4705 (little one), H6730 (Zior), H6811 (Zair), H4704 (little), H6686 (Zuar), H6810 (least), H6819 (be brought low), H6820 (Zoar), H6812 (youth)",
    4705: "מִצְעָר (mitsʻâr | mits-awr')\n\nDerivation: from H6819 צָעַר\nStrong's: petty (in size or number); adverbially, a short (time)\nKJV: little one (while), small.\n\nCognate Group: H4706 (Mizar), H4705 (little one), H6730 (Zior), H6811 (Zair), H4704 (little), H6686 (Zuar), H6810 (least), H6819 (be brought low), H6820 (Zoar), H6812 (youth)\nGreek Equivalents: G3398 μικρός, G3641 ὀλίγος",
    4706: "מִצְעָר (Mitsʻâr | mits-awr')\n\nDerivation: the same as H4705 מִצְעָר\nStrong's: Mitsar, a peak of Lebanon\nKJV: Mizar.\n\nCognate Group: H4706 (Mizar), H4705 (little one), H6730 (Zior), H6811 (Zair), H4704 (little), H6686 (Zuar), H6810 (least), H6819 (be brought low), H6820 (Zoar), H6812 (youth)",
    4707: "מִצְפֶּה (mitspeh | mits-peh')\n\nDerivation: from H6822 צָפָה\nStrong's: an observatory, especially formilitary purposes\nKJV: watch tower.\n\nCognate Group: H6837 (Ziphion), H6836 (watching), H4709 (Mitspah), H6827 (Zephon), H6831 (Zephonites), H4707 (watch tower), H6822 (behold), H6825 (Zephi), H4708 (Mizpeh), H6839 (Zophim)\nGreek Equivalents: G3706 ὅρασις",
    4708: "מִצְפֶּה (Mitspeh | mits-peh')\n\nDerivation: the same as H4707 מִצְפֶּה\nStrong's: Mitspeh, the name of five places in Palestine\nKJV: Mizpeh, watch tower. Compare H4709 מִצְפָּה .\n\nCognate Group: H6837 (Ziphion), H6836 (watching), H4709 (Mitspah), H6827 (Zephon), H6831 (Zephonites), H4707 (watch tower), H6822 (behold), H6825 (Zephi), H4708 (Mizpeh), H6839 (Zophim)",
    4709: "מִצְפָּה (Mitspâh | mits-paw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4708 מִצְפֶּה\nStrong's: Mitspah, the name of two places in Palestine\nKJV: Mitspah. (This seems rather to be only an orthographic variation of H4708 מִצְפֶּה when 'in pause'.)\n\nCognate Group: H6837 (Ziphion), H6836 (watching), H4709 (Mitspah), H6827 (Zephon), H6831 (Zephonites), H4707 (watch tower), H6822 (behold), H6825 (Zephi), H4708 (Mizpeh), H6839 (Zophim)",
    4710: "מִצְפֻּן (mitspun | mits-poon')\n\nDerivation: from H6845 צָפַן\nStrong's: a secret (place or thing, perhaps, treasure)\nKJV: hidden thing.\n\nCognate Group: H6830 (northern), H6846 (Zephaniah), H4710 (hidden thing), H6829 (Zaphon), H6828 (north), H6845 (esteem), H6840 (hid), H6847 (Zaphnath-paaneah)",
    4711: "מָצַץ (mâtsats | maw-tsats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to suck\nKJV: milk.\n\nCognate Group: H4682 (unleaved), H4711 (milk)",
    4712: "מֵצַר (mêtsar | may-tsar')\n\nDerivation: from H6896 קֵבָה\nStrong's: something tight, i.e. (figuratively) trouble\nKJV: distress, pain, strait.\n\nCognate Group: H6862 (adversary), H3334 (be distressed), H6872 (bag), H4712 (distress), H6887 (adversary), H6869 (adversary), H1222 (gold)\nGreek Equivalents: G2794 κίνδυνος",
    4713: "מִצְרִי (Mitsrîy | mits-ree')\n\nDerivation: from H4714 מִצְרַיִם\nStrong's: a Mitsrite, or inhabitant of Mitsrajim\nKJV: Egyptian, of Egypt.\n\nCognate Group: H4714 (Egypt), H4739 (Makaz), H4693 (besieged places), H4719 (Makkedah), H4713 (Egyptian), H4731 (rod), H4732 (Mikloth)",
    4714: "מִצְרַיִם (Mitsrayim | mits-rah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: dual of H4693 מָצֹור\nStrong's: Mitsrajim, i.e. Upper and Lower Egypt\nKJV: Egypt, Egyptians, Mizraim.\n\nCognate Group: H4714 (Egypt), H4739 (Makaz), H4693 (besieged places), H4719 (Makkedah), H4713 (Egyptian), H4731 (rod), H4732 (Mikloth)",
    4715: "מִצְרֵף (mitsrêph | mits-rafe')\n\nDerivation: from H6884 צָרַף\nStrong's: a crucible\nKJV: fining pot.\n\nCognate Group: H6886 (Zarephath), H4715 (fining pot), H6885 (goldsmith's), H6884 (cast)\nGreek Equivalents: G1383 δοκίμιον",
    4716: "מַק (maq | mak)\n\nDerivation: from H4743 מָקַק\nStrong's: properly, a melting, i.e. putridity\nKJV: rottenness, stink.\n\nCognate Group: H4743 (consume away), H4716 (rottenness)\nGreek Equivalents: G2868 κονιορτός",
    4717: "מַקָּבָה (maqqâbâh | mak-kaw-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H5344 נָקַב\nStrong's: properly, a perforatrix, i.e. a hammer (as piercing)\nKJV: hammer.\n\nCognate Group: H5344 (appoint), H4718 (hammer), H5346 (Nekeb), H4717 (hammer), H5347 (female), H5345 (pipe)",
    4718: "מַקֶּבֶת (maqqebeth | mak-keh'-beth)\n\nDerivation: from H5344 נָקַב\nStrong's: properly, a perforator, i.e. a hammer (as piercing); also (intransitively) a perforation, i.e. a quarry\nKJV: hammer, hole.\n\nCognate Group: H5344 (appoint), H4718 (hammer), H5346 (Nekeb), H4717 (hammer), H5347 (female), H5345 (pipe)\nGreek Equivalents: G999 βόθυνος",
    4719: "מַקֵּדָה (Maqqêdâh | mak-kay-daw')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5348 נָקֹד in the denominative sense of herding (compare H5349 נֹקֵד); fold\nStrong's: Makkedah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Makkedah.\n\nCognate Group: H4714 (Egypt), H4739 (Makaz), H4693 (besieged places), H4719 (Makkedah), H4713 (Egyptian), H4731 (rod), H4732 (Mikloth)",
    4720: "מִקְדָּשׁ (miqdâsh | mik-dawsh')\n\nDerivation: or מִקְּדָשׁ; (Exodus 15:17), from H6942 קָדַשׁ\nStrong's: a consecrated thing or place, especially, a palace, sanctuary (whether of Jehovah or of idols) or asylum\nKJV: chapel, hallowed part, holy place, sanctuary.\n\nCognate Group: H6947 (Kadeshbarnea), H4720 (chapel), H6945 (sodomite), H6918 (holy), H6944 (consecrated), H6946 (Kadesh), H6948 (harlot), H6942 (appoint), H6943 (Kedesh)\nGreek Equivalents: G37 ἁγιάζω, G38 ἁγιασμός, G39 ἅγιον, G873 ἀφορίζω, G2413 ἱερός, G3741 ὅσιος",
    4721: "מַקְהֵל (maqhêl | mak-hale')\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) מַקְהֵלָה; from H6950 קָהַל\nStrong's: an assembly\nKJV: congregation.\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)",
    4722: "מַקְהֵלֹת (Maqhêlôth | mak-hay-loth')\n\nDerivation: plural of H4721 מַקְהֵל (feminine); assemblies\nStrong's: Makheloth, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Makheloth.\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)",
    4723: "מִקְוֶה (miqveh | mik-veh')\n\nDerivation: or מִקְוֵה; (1 Kings 10:28), or מִקְוֵא\n\nTypo: lemma מִּקְוֵא extra dagesh, corrected to מִקְוֵא\n\n; (2 Chronicles 1:16), from H6960 קָוָה\nStrong's: something waited for, i.e. confidence (objective or subjective); also a collection, i.e. (of water) a pond, or (of men and horses) a caravan or drove\nKJV: abiding, gathering together, hope, linen yarn, plenty (of water), pool.\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)\nGreek Equivalents: G4864 συναγωγή, G4921 συνιστάω, G5281 ὑπομονή",
    4724: "מִקְוָה (miqvâh | mik-vaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4723 מִקְוֶה\nStrong's: a collection, i.e. (of water) a reservoir\nKJV: ditch.\n\nCognate Group: H6960 (gather), H4724 (ditch), H4723 (abiding)",
    4725: "מָקֹום (mâqôwm | maw-kome')\n\nDerivation: or מָקֹם; also (feminine) מְקֹומָה; or מְקֹמָה; from H6965 קוּם\nStrong's: properly, a standing, i.e. a spot; but used widely of a locality (general or specific); also (figuratively) of a condition (of body or mind)\nKJV: country, [idiom] home, [idiom] open, place, room, space, [idiom] whither(-soever).\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H6970 (Koa), H3351 (substance), H4725 (country), H3360 (Jekameam), H6968 (upright), H8617 (power to stand), H3359 (Jekamiah), H8618 (rise up against), H3356 (Jakim), H7054 (corn), H3361 (Jokmeam), H7056 (Camon), H7009 (substance), H6971 (ape), H7012 (rising up), H6967 ([idiom] along)\nGreek Equivalents: G39 ἅγιον, G1093 γῆ, G2310 θεμέλιος, G2362 θρόνος, G2992 λαός, G3598 ὁδός, G3624 οἶκος, G4172 πόλις, G4864 συναγωγή, G5010 τάξις, G5117 τόπος, G5561 χώρα",
    4726: "מָקֹור (mâqôwr | maw-kore')\n\nDerivation: or מָקֹר; from H6979 קוּר\nStrong's: properly, something dug, i.e. a (general) source (of water, even when naturally flowing; also of tears, blood (by euphemism, of the female pudenda); figuratively, of happiness, wisdom, progeny)\nKJV: fountain, issue, spring, well(-spring).\n\nCognate Group: H6979 (break down), H4726 (fountain)\nGreek Equivalents: G1841 ἔξοδος, G4077 πηγή, G4511 ῥύσις, G5204 ὕδωρ",
    4727: "מִקָּח (miqqâch | mik-kawkh')\n\nDerivation: from H3947 לָקַח\nStrong's: reception\nKJV: taking.\n\nCognate Group: H3949 (Likhi), H3947 (accept), H4728 (ware), H4727 (taking), H4455 (booty), H3948 (doctrine), H4457 (snuffers)",
    4728: "מַקָּחָה (maqqâchâh | mak-kaw-khaw')\n\nDerivation: from H3947 לָקַח\nStrong's: something received, i.e. merchandise (purchased)\nKJV: ware.\n\nCognate Group: H3949 (Likhi), H3947 (accept), H4728 (ware), H4727 (taking), H4455 (booty), H3948 (doctrine), H4457 (snuffers)",
    4729: "מִקְטָר (miqṭâr | mik-tawr')\n\nDerivation: from H6999 קָטַר\nStrong's: something to fume (incense) on i.e. a hearth place\nKJV: to burn...upon.\n\nCognate Group: H7008 (smoke), H7004 (incense), H4730 (censer), H4729 (to burn), H7002 (incense), H6989 (Keturah), H6999 (burn), H6988 (incense)\nGreek Equivalents: G2368 θυμίαμα",
    4730: "מִקְטֶרֶת (miqṭereth | mik-teh'-reth)\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4729 מִקְטָר\nStrong's: something to fume (incense) in, i.e. a coal-pan\nKJV: censer.\n\nCognate Group: H7008 (smoke), H7004 (incense), H4730 (censer), H4729 (to burn), H7002 (incense), H6989 (Keturah), H6999 (burn), H6988 (incense)",
    4731: "מַקֵּל (maqqêl | mak-kale)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) מַקְּלָה; from an unused root meaning apparently to germinate\nStrong's: a shoot, i.e. stick (with leaves on, or for walking, striking, guiding, divining)\nKJV: rod, (hand-)staff.\n\nCognate Group: H4714 (Egypt), H4739 (Makaz), H4693 (besieged places), H4719 (Makkedah), H4713 (Egyptian), H4731 (rod), H4732 (Mikloth)\nGreek Equivalents: G4464 ῥάβδος",
    4732: "מִקְלֹות (Miqlôwth | mik-lohth')\n\nDerivation: (or perhaps mik-kel-ohth') plural of (feminine) H4731 מַקֵּל ; rods\nStrong's: Mikloth, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Mikloth.\n\nCognate Group: H4714 (Egypt), H4739 (Makaz), H4693 (besieged places), H4719 (Makkedah), H4713 (Egyptian), H4731 (rod), H4732 (Mikloth)",
    4733: "מִקְלָט (miqlâṭ | mik-lawt')\n\nDerivation: from H7038 קָלַט in the sense of taking in\nStrong's: an asylum (as a receptacle)\nKJV: refuge.\n\nCognate Group: H4733 (refuge)\nGreek Equivalents: G873 ἀφορίζω",
    4734: "מִקְלַעַת (miqlaʻath | mik-lah'-ath)\n\nDerivation: from H7049 קָלַע\nStrong's: a sculpture (probably in bas-relief)\nKJV: carved (figure), carving, graving.\n\nCognate Group: H7053 (fork), H7049 (carve), H4734 (carved), H7055 (Kemuel)",
    4735: "מִקְנֶה (miqneh | mik-neh')\n\nDerivation: from H7069 קָנָה\nStrong's: something bought, i.e. property, but only livestock; abstractly, acquisition\nKJV: cattle, flock, herd, possession, purchase, substance.\n\nCognate Group: H7075 (getting), H4736 (bought), H4737 (Mikneiah), H4735 (cattle), H7069 (attain)\nGreek Equivalents: G2934 κτῆνος, G5223 ὕπαρξις, G5225 ὑπάρχω",
    4736: "מִקְנָה (miqnâh | mik-naw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4735 מִקְנֶה\nStrong's: properly, a buying, i.e. acquisition; concretely, a piece of property (land or living); also the sum paid\nKJV: (he that is) bought, possession, piece, purchase.\n\nCognate Group: H7075 (getting), H4736 (bought), H4737 (Mikneiah), H4735 (cattle), H7069 (attain)",
    4737: "מִקְנֵיָהוּ (Miqnêyâhûw | mik-nay-yaw'-hoo)\n\nDerivation: from H4735 מִקְנֶה and H3050 יָהּ ; possession of Jah\nStrong's: Miknejah, an Israelite\nKJV: Mikneiah.\n\nCognate Group: H7075 (getting), H4736 (bought), H4737 (Mikneiah), H4735 (cattle), H7069 (attain)",
    4738: "מִקְסָם (miqçâm | mik-sawn')\n\nDerivation: from H7080 קָסַם\nStrong's: an augury\nKJV: divination.\n\nCognate Group: H7081 (divination), H4738 (divination), H7080 (divine)",
    4739: "מָקַץ (Mâqats | maw-kats')\n\nDerivation: from H7112 קָצַץ ; end\nStrong's: Makats, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Makaz.\n\nCognate Group: H4714 (Egypt), H4739 (Makaz), H4693 (besieged places), H4719 (Makkedah), H4713 (Egyptian), H4731 (rod), H4732 (Mikloth)",
    4740: "מַקְצֹועַ (maqtsôwaʻ | mak-tso'-ah)\n\nDerivation: or מַקְצֹעַ; or (feminine) מַקְצֹעָה; from H7106 קָצַע in the denominative sense of bending\nStrong's: an angle or recess\nKJV: corner, turning.\n\nCognate Group: H4742 (corner), H7106 (cause to scrape), H4740 (corner)\nGreek Equivalents: G1137 γωνία, G2768 κέρας, G3313 μέρος",
    4741: "מַקְצֻעָה (maqtsuʻâh | mak-tsoo-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H7106 קָצַע\nStrong's: a scraper, i.e. a carving chisel\nKJV: plane.\n\nCognate Group: H7102 (cassia), H7103 (Kezia), H4741 (plane), H7106 (cause to scrape)",
    4742: "מְקֻצְעָה (mᵉqutsʻâh | mek-oots-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H7106 קָצַע in the denominative sense of bending\nStrong's: an angle\nKJV: corner.\n\nCognate Group: H4742 (corner), H7106 (cause to scrape), H4740 (corner)",
    4743: "מָקַק (mâqaq | maw-kak')\n\nDerivation: ' a primitive root\nStrong's: to melt; figuratively, to flow, dwindle, vanish\nKJV: consume away, be corrupt, dissolve, pine away.\n\nCognate Group: H4743 (consume away), H4716 (rottenness)\nGreek Equivalents: G2704 καταφθείρω, G4482 ῥέω, G4595 σήπω, G5080 τήκω",
    4744: "מִקְרָא (miqrâʼ | mik-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H7121 קָרָא\nStrong's: something called out, i.e. a public meeting (the act, the persons, or the place); also a rehearsal\nKJV: assembly, calling, convocation, reading.\n\nCognate Group: H7150 (preaching), H6981 (Kore), H7121 (bewray), H7148 (famous), H4744 (assembly), H7124 (partridge)\nGreek Equivalents: G320 ἀνάγνωσις, G2822 κλητός",
    4745: "מִקְרֶה (miqreh | mik-reh')\n\nDerivation: from H7136 קָרָה\nStrong's: something met with, i.e. an accident or fortune\nKJV: something befallen, befalleth, chance, event, hap(-peneth).\n\nCognate Group: H7153 (Kirjath-arba), H7177 (Kartah), H7136 (appoint), H7178 (Kartan), H7158 (Kirjath-sannah), H7155 (Kirjath-huzoth), H4746 (building), H7157 (Kirjath), H7151 (city), H7176 (city), H6982 (beam), H7147 (contrary), H704 (Arba), H7156 (Kiriathaim), H7154 (Kirjathbaal), H7137 (uncleanness that chanceth), H4745 (something befallen), H7152 (Kerioth)",
    4746: "מְקָרֶה (mᵉqâreh | mek-aw-reh')\n\nDerivation: from H7136 קָרָה\nStrong's: properly, something meeting, i.e. a frame (of timbers)\nKJV: building.\n\nCognate Group: H7153 (Kirjath-arba), H7177 (Kartah), H7136 (appoint), H7178 (Kartan), H7158 (Kirjath-sannah), H7155 (Kirjath-huzoth), H4746 (building), H7157 (Kirjath), H7151 (city), H7176 (city), H6982 (beam), H7147 (contrary), H704 (Arba), H7156 (Kiriathaim), H7154 (Kirjathbaal), H7137 (uncleanness that chanceth), H4745 (something befallen), H7152 (Kerioth)",
    4747: "מְקֵרָה (mᵉqêrâh | mek-ay-raw')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7119 קַר\nStrong's: a cooling off\nKJV: [idiom] summer.\n\nCognate Group: H7120 (cold), H4747 ([idiom] summer), H6979 (break down), H7119 (cold), H7135 (cold)\nGreek Equivalents: G2846 κοιτών",
    4748: "מִקְשֶׁה (miqsheh | mik-sheh')\n\nDerivation: from H7185 קָשָׁה in the sense of knotting up round and hard\nStrong's: something turned (rounded), i.e. a curl (of tresses)\nKJV: [idiom] well (set) hair.\n\nCognate Group: H4749 (beaten), H4748 ([idiom] well hair)",
    4749: "מִקְשָׁה (miqshâh | mik-shaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4748 מִקְשֶׁה\nStrong's: rounded work, i.e. moulded by hammering (repousse)\nKJV: beaten (out of one piece, work), upright, whole piece.\n\nCognate Group: H4749 (beaten), H4748 ([idiom] well hair)\nGreek Equivalents: G4731 στερεός",
    4750: "מִקְשָׁה (miqshâh | mik-shaw')\n\nDerivation: denominative from H7180 קִשֻּׁא\nStrong's: literally a cucumbered field, i.e. a cucumber patch\nKJV: garden of cucumbers.\n\nCognate Group: H7180 (cucumber), H4750 (garden of cucumbers)",
    4751: "מַר (mar | mar)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) מָרָה; from H4843 מָרַר\nStrong's: bitter (literally or figuratively); also (as noun) bitterness, or (adverbially) bitterly\nKJV: [phrase] angry, bitter(-ly, -ness), chafed, discontented, [idiom] great, heavy.\n\nCognate Group: H4753 (myrrh), H4844 (bitter), H4785 (Marah), H4787 (bitterness), H4843 (bitter), H4786 (grief), H4848 (Merarites), H4755 (Mara), H4815 (bitter), H4845 (gall), H8563 ([idiom] most bitter), H4847 (Merari), H4814 (bitterness), H4472 (bitterness), H4846 (bitter), H4751 (angry), H4470 (bitterness)\nGreek Equivalents: G1650 ἔλεγχος, G3601 ὀδύνη, G3601 ὀδύνη, G4088 πικρία, G4089 πικρός, G4090 πικρῶς",
