    4758: "מַרְאֶה (marʼeh | mar-eh')\n\nDerivation: from H7200 רָאָה\nStrong's: a view (the act of seeing); also an appearance (the thing seen), whether (real) a shape (especially if handsome, comeliness; often plural the looks), or (mental) a vision\nKJV: [idiom] apparently, appearance(-reth), [idiom] as soon as beautiful(-ly), countenance, fair, favoured, form, goodly, to look (up) on (to), look(-eth), pattern, to see, seem, sight, visage, vision.\n\nCognate Group: H3070 (Jehovah-jireh), H7207 (behold), H7209 (looking glass), H7204 (Haroeh), H7200 (advise self), H4758 ([idiom] apparently), H7206 (children of Reuben), H7205 (Reuben), H7211 (Reaia), H4759 (looking glass), H7210 (gazingstock), H7203 (vision), H7202 (see), H7212 (beholding), H3376 (Irijah)\nGreek Equivalents: G1391 δόξα, G1491 εἶδος, G2397 ἰδέα, G3667 ὁμοίωμα, G3701 ὀπτασία, G3705 ὅραμα, G3706 ὅρασις, G3788 ὀφθαλμός, G3799 ὄψις, G4383 πρόσωπον",
    4759: "מַרְאָה (marʼâh | mar-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4758 מַרְאֶה\nStrong's: a vision; also (causatively) a mirror\nKJV: looking glass, vision.\n\nCognate Group: H3070 (Jehovah-jireh), H7207 (behold), H7209 (looking glass), H7204 (Haroeh), H7200 (advise self), H4758 ([idiom] apparently), H7206 (children of Reuben), H7205 (Reuben), H7211 (Reaia), H4759 (looking glass), H7210 (gazingstock), H7203 (vision), H7202 (see), H7212 (beholding), H3376 (Irijah)\nGreek Equivalents: G545 ἀπειθής, G3701 ὀπτασία, G4088 πικρία",
    4760: "מֻרְאָה (murʼâh | moor-aw')\n\nDerivation: apparently feminine passive causative participle of H7200 רָאָה\nStrong's: something conspicuous, i.e. the craw of abird (from its prominence)\nKJV: crop.\n\nCognate Group: H4806 (fat beast), H4760 (crop), H4764 (Merab)",
    4761: "מַרְאָשָׁה (marʼâshâh | mar-aw-shaw')\n\nDerivation: denominative from H7218 רֹאשׁ\nStrong's: properly, headship, i.e. (plural for collective) dominion\nKJV: principality.\n\nCognate Group: H7226 (bolster), H7219 (gall), H7220 (Rosh), H7224 (first), H7221 (beginning), H7218 (band), H7225 (beginning), H7222 (head), H4763 (bolster), H4761 (principality), H7223 (ancestor)",
    4762: "מַרְאֵשָׁה (Marʼêshâh | mar-ay-shaw')\n\nDerivation: or מַרֵשָׁה; formed like H4761 מַרְאָשָׁה ; summit\nStrong's: Mareshah, the name of two Israelites and of a place in Palestine\nKJV: Mareshah.\n\nCognate Group: H4884 (measure), H4854 (Massa), H4861 (Mishal), H4852 (Mesha), H4863 (kneading trough), H4850 (Merathaim), H4958 (pan), H4913 (Mashal), H4752 (drop), H4851 (Mash), H4762 (Mareshah)",
