    4770: "מַרְבֵּק (marbêq | mar-bake')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to tie up\nStrong's: a stall (for cattle)\nKJV: [idiom] fat(-ted), stall.\n\nCognate Group: H4770 ([idiom] fat), H7259 (Rebekah)\nGreek Equivalents: G447 ἀνίημι, G1199 δεσμόν, G4618 σιτευτός, G5142 τρέφω",
