    4785: "מָרָה (Mârâh | maw-raw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H4751 מַר feminine; bitter\nStrong's: Marah, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Marah.\n\nCognate Group: H4753 (myrrh), H4844 (bitter), H4785 (Marah), H4787 (bitterness), H4843 (bitter), H4786 (grief), H4848 (Merarites), H4755 (Mara), H4815 (bitter), H4845 (gall), H8563 ([idiom] most bitter), H4847 (Merari), H4814 (bitterness), H4472 (bitterness), H4846 (bitter), H4751 (angry), H4470 (bitterness)",
