    4787: "מׇרָּה (morrâh | mor-raw')Typo: lemma מָרָה missing dagesh, corrected to מׇרָּה\n\nDerivation: a form of H4786 מֹרָה\nStrong's: trouble\nKJV: bitterness.\n\nCognate Group: H4753 (myrrh), H4844 (bitter), H4785 (Marah), H4787 (bitterness), H4843 (bitter), H4786 (grief), H4848 (Merarites), H4755 (Mara), H4815 (bitter), H4845 (gall), H8563 ([idiom] most bitter), H4847 (Merari), H4814 (bitterness), H4472 (bitterness), H4846 (bitter), H4751 (angry), H4470 (bitterness)",
    4788: "מָרוּד (mârûwd | maw-rood')\n\nDerivation: from H7300 רוּד in the sense of maltreatment\nStrong's: an outcast; (abstractly) destitution\nKJV: cast out, misery.\n\nCognate Group: H7300 (have the dominion), H4788 (cast out)\nGreek Equivalents: G1375 διωγμός",
