    4793: "מֵרֹוץ (mêrôwts | may-rotes')\n\nDerivation: from H7323 רוּץ\nStrong's: a run (the trial of speed)\nKJV: race.\n\nCognate Group: H4793 (race), H4794 (course), H7323 (break down)\nGreek Equivalents: G1408 δρόμος",
    4794: "מְרוּצָה (mᵉrûwtsâh | mer-oo-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: or מְרֻצָה; feminine of H4793 מֵרֹוץ\nStrong's: a race (the act), whether the manner or the progress\nKJV: course, running. Compare H4835 מְרֻצָה .\n\nCognate Group: H4793 (race), H4794 (course), H7323 (break down)\nGreek Equivalents: G1408 δρόμος",
    4795: "מָרוּק (mârûwq | maw-rook')\n\nDerivation: from H4838 מָרַק\nStrong's: properly, rubbed; but used abstractly, a rubbing (with perfumery)\nKJV: purification.\n\nCognate Group: H4838 (bright), H4795 (purification), H8562 ([idiom] cleanse)\nGreek Equivalents: G2322 θεραπεία",
    4796: "מָרֹות (Mârôwth | maw-rohth')\n\nDerivation: plural of H4751 מַר feminine; bitter springs\nStrong's: Maroth, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Maroth.\n\nCognate Group: H4796 (Maroth), H4805 (bitter), H4792 (Merom), H4784 (bitter), H4790 (broken), H3236 (Imrah)",
    4797: "מִרְזַח (mirzach | meer-zakh')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to scream\nStrong's: a cry, i.e. (of job), a revel\nKJV: banquet.\n\nCognate Group: H4798 (mourning), H4797 (banquet)",
    4798: "מַרְזֵחַ (marzêach | mar-zay'-akh)\n\nDerivation: formed like H4797 מִרְזַח\nStrong's: a cry, i.e. (of grief) a lamentation\nKJV: mourning.\n\nCognate Group: H4798 (mourning), H4797 (banquet)",
