    4904: "מִשְׁכָּב (mishkâb | mish-kawb')\n\nDerivation: from H7901 שָׁכַב\nStrong's: a bed (figuratively, a bier); abstractly, sleep; by euphemism, carnal intercourse\nKJV: bed(-chamber), couch, lieth (lying) with.\n\nCognate Group: H7902 ([idiom] carnally), H7901 ([idiom] at all), H7903 ([idiom] lie), H4904 (bed)\nGreek Equivalents: G2825 κλίνη, G2845 κοίτη, G2846 κοιτών",
    4905: "מַשְׂכִּיל (maskîyl | mas-keel')\n\nDerivation: from H7919 שָׂכַל\nStrong's: instructive, i.e. a didactic poem\nKJV: Maschil.\n\nCognate Group: H4905 (Maschil), H7922 (discretion), H7919 (consider)",
    4906: "מַשְׂכִּית (maskîyth | mas-keeth')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7906 שֵׂכוּ\nStrong's: a figure (carved on stone, the wall, or any object); figuratively, imagination\nKJV: conceit, image(-ry), picture, [idiom] wish.\n\nCognate Group: H7914 (picture), H7907 (heart), H4906 (conceit), H7906 (Sechu), H7634 (Shachia), H7915 (knife)\nGreek Equivalents: G2927 κρυπτός, G4649 σκοπός, G4907 σύνεσις",
