    4932: "מִשְׁנֶה (mishneh | mish-neh')\n\nDerivation: from H8138 שָׁנָה\nStrong's: properly, a repetition, i.e. a duplicate (copy of a document), or a double (in amount); by implication, a second (in order, rank, age, quality or location)\nKJV: college, copy, double, fatlings, next, second (order), twice as much.\n\nCognate Group: H8145 (again), H4932 (college), H8136 ([idiom] angels), H8147 (both), H8138 (do again)\nGreek Equivalents: G1237 διαδέχομαι, G1240 διάδοχος, G1362 διπλοῦς",
    4933: "מְשִׁסָּה (mᵉshiççâh | mesh-is-saw')\n\nDerivation: from H8155 שָׁסַס\nStrong's: plunder\nKJV: booty, spoil.\n\nCognate Group: H7601 (spoil), H4882 (spoil), H8155 (rifle), H4933 (booty)",
    4934: "מִשְׁעֹול (mishʻôwl | mish-ole')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H8168 שֹׁעַל\nStrong's: a hollow, i.e. a narrow passage\nKJV: path.\n\nCognate Group: H8168 (handful), H4934 (path)",
    4935: "מִשְׁעִי (mishʻîy | mish-ee')\n\nDerivation: probably from H8159 שָׁעָה\nStrong's: inspection\nKJV: to supple.\n\nCognate Group: H4936 (Misham), H4935 (to supple)",
    4936: "מִשְׁעָם (Mishʻâm | mish-awm')\n\nDerivation: apparently from H8159 שָׁעָה ; inspection\nStrong's: Misham, an Israelite\nKJV: Misham.\n\nCognate Group: H4936 (Misham), H4935 (to supple)",
    4937: "מִשְׁעֵן (mishʻên | mish-ane')\n\nDerivation: or מִשְׁעָן; from H8172 שָׁעַן\nStrong's: a support (concretely), i.e. (figuratively) a protector or sustenance\nKJV: stay.\n\nCognate Group: H8172 (lean), H824 (Eshean), H4938 (staff), H4937 (stay)\nGreek Equivalents: G2479 ἰσχύς, G2480 ἰσχύω, G5349 φθαρτός",
    4938: "מִשְׁעֵנָה (mishʻênâh | mish-ay-naw')\n\nDerivation: or מִשְׁעֶנֶת; feminine of H4937 מִשְׁעֵן\nStrong's: support (abstractly), i.e. (figuratively) sustenance or (concretely) a walking-stick\nKJV: staff.\n\nCognate Group: H8172 (lean), H824 (Eshean), H4938 (staff), H4937 (stay)\nGreek Equivalents: G2961 κυριεύω, G4464 ῥάβδος",
    4939: "מִשְׂפָּח (mispâch | mis-pawkh')\n\nDerivation: from H5596 סָפַח\nStrong's: slaughter\nKJV: oppression.\n\nCognate Group: H4939 (oppression), H5599 (things as grow)\nGreek Equivalents: G458 ἀνομία",
    4940: "מִשְׁפָּחָה (mishpâchâh | mish-paw-khaw')\n\nDerivation: from H8192 שָׁפָה (compare H8198 שִׁפְחָה)\nStrong's: a family, i.e. circle of relatives; figuratively, a class (of persons), a species (of animals) or sort (of things); by extension a tribe or people\nKJV: family, kind(-red).\n\nCognate Group: H4940 (family), H8198 (maid)\nGreek Equivalents: G1074 γενεά, G1078 γένεσις, G1083 γέννησις, G1085 γένος, G1218 δῆμος, G1491 εἶδος, G2819 κλῆρος, G2992 λαός, G3624 οἶκος, G3965 πατριά, G3968 πατρίς, G4772 συγγένεια, G4773 συγγενής, G5207 υἱός, G5443 φυλή",
    4941: "מִשְׁפָּט (mishpâṭ | mish-pawt')\n\nDerivation: from H8199 שָׁפַט\nStrong's: properly, a verdict (favorable or unfavorable) pronounced judicially, especially a sentence or formal decree (human or (participant's) divine law, individual or collective), including the act, the place, the suit, the crime, and the penalty; abstractly, justice, including a participant's right or privilege (statutory or customary), or even a style\nKJV: [phrase] adversary, ceremony, charge, [idiom] crime, custom, desert, determination, discretion, disposing, due, fashion, form, to be judged, judgment, just(-ice, -ly), (manner of) law(-ful), manner, measure, (due) order, ordinance, right, sentence, usest, [idiom] worthy, [phrase] wrong.\n\nCognate Group: H4941 (adversary), H8196 (judgment), H8204 (Shiphtan), H8199 (avenge), H8202 (Shaphat), H8203 (Shephatiah), H8201 (judgment)\nGreek Equivalents: G92 ἀδίκημα, G226 ἀληθεύω, G746 ἀρχή, G1342 δίκαιος, G1343 δικαιοσύνη, G1345 δικαίωμα, G1347 δικαίωσις, G1349 δίκη, G1491 εἶδος, G1785 ἐντολή, G1995 ἐπιστροφή, G2520 καθήκω, G2917 κρίμα, G2920 κρίσις, G2922 κριτήριον, G3551 νόμος",
    4942: "מִשְׁפָּת (mishpâth | mish-pawth')\n\nDerivation: from H8192 שָׁפָה\nStrong's: a stall for cattle (only dual)\nKJV: burden, sheepfold.\n\nCognate Group: H8239 (bring), H4942 (burden), H8240 (hook), H830 (dung)",
    4943: "מֶשֶׁק (mesheq | meh'-shek)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to hold\nStrong's: possession\nKJV: [phrase] steward.\n\nCognate Group: H4943 (steward), H4954 (Mishraites), H4476 (breeding)",
    4944: "מַשָּׁק (mashshâq | mash-shawk')\n\nDerivation: from H8264 שָׁקַק\nStrong's: a traversing, i.e. rapid motion\nKJV: running to and fro.\n\nCognate Group: H8264 (have appetite), H4944 (running to and fro)",
    4945: "מַשְׁקֶה (mashqeh | mash-keh')\n\nDerivation: from H8248 שָׁקָה\nStrong's: properly, causing to drink, i.e. a butler; by implication (intransitively), drink (itself); figuratively, a well-watered region\nKJV: butler(-ship), cupbearer, drink(-ing), fat pasture, watered.\n\nCognate Group: H8250 (drink), H4945 (butler), H8249 (drink), H8248 (cause to drink), H8268 (trough)\nGreek Equivalents: G746 ἀρχή",
    4946: "מִשְׁקֹול (mishqôwl | mish-kole')\n\nDerivation: from H8254 שָׁקַל\nStrong's: weight\nKJV: weight.\n\nCognate Group: H4949 (plummet), H4948 (weight), H8254 (pay), H4946 (weight), H8255 (shekel), H8256 (sycamore)",
    4947: "מַשְׁקֹוף (mashqôwph | mash-kofe')\n\nDerivation: from H8259 שָׁקַף in its original sense of overhanging\nStrong's: a lintel\nKJV: lintel.\n\nCognate Group: H8261 (light), H4947 (lintel), H8260 (window)",
    4948: "מִשְׁקָל (mishqâl | mish-kawl')\n\nDerivation: from H8254 שָׁקַל\nStrong's: weight (numerically estimated); hence, weighing (the act)\nKJV: (full) weight.\n\nCognate Group: H4949 (plummet), H4948 (weight), H8254 (pay), H4946 (weight), H8255 (shekel), H8256 (sycamore)",
    4949: "מִשְׁקֶלֶת (mishqeleth | mish-keh'-leth)\n\nDerivation: or מִשְׁקֹלֶת; feminine of H4948 מִשְׁקָל or H4947 מַשְׁקֹוף\nStrong's: a weight, i.e. a plummet (with line attached)\nKJV: plummet.\n\nCognate Group: H4949 (plummet), H4948 (weight), H8254 (pay), H4946 (weight), H8255 (shekel), H8256 (sycamore)",
    4950: "מִשְׁקָע (mishqâʻ | mish-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from H8257 שָׁקַע\nStrong's: a settling place (of water), i.e. a pond\nKJV: deep.\n\nCognate Group: H8257 (make deep), H4950 (deep)\nGreek Equivalents: G2525 καθίστημι",
    4951: "מִשְׂרָה (misrâh | mis-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H8280 שָׂרָה\nStrong's: empire\nKJV: government.\n\nCognate Group: H8294 (Sarah), H4951 (government)\nGreek Equivalents: G746 ἀρχή",
    4952: "מִשְׁרָה (mishrâh | mish-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H8281 שָׁרָה in the sense of loosening\nStrong's: maceration, i.e. steeped juice\nKJV: liquor.\n\nCognate Group: H4952 (liquor)\nGreek Equivalents: G2716 κατεργάζομαι",
    4953: "מַשְׁרֹוקִי (mashrôwqîy | mash-ro-kee')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H8319 שָׁרַק\nStrong's: a (musical) pipe (from its whistling sound)\nKJV: flute.\n\nCognate Group: H4953 (flute)",
    4954: "מִשְׁרָעִי (Mishrâʻîy | mish-raw-ee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from an unused noun from an unused root; probably meaning to stretch out; extension\nStrong's: a Mishraite, or inhabitant (collectively) of Mishra\nKJV: Mishraites.\n\nCognate Group: H4943 (steward), H4954 (Mishraites), H4476 (breeding)",
