    4956: "מִשְׂרְפֹות מַיִם (Misrᵉphôwth mayim | mis-ref-ohth' mah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: from the plural of H4955 מִשְׂרָפָה and H4325 מַיִם ; burnings of water\nStrong's: Misrephoth-Majim, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Misrephoth-mayim.\n\nCognate Group: H4956 (Misrephoth-mayim), H8314 (fiery), H8315 (Saraph), H5635 (burn), H8316 (burning), H8313 (burn), H4955 (burning)",
    4957: "מַשְׂרֵקָה (Masrêqâh | mas-ray-kaw')\n\nDerivation: a form for H7796 שֹׂורֵק used denominatively; vineyard\nStrong's: Masrekah, a place in Idumaea\nKJV: Masrekah.\n\nCognate Group: H7796 (Sorek), H8291 (principal plant), H8321 (choice wine), H4957 (Masrekah), H8320 (speckled)",
    4958: "מַשְׂרֵת (masrêth | mas-rayth')\n\nDerivation: apparently from an unused root meaning to perforate, i.e. hollow out\nStrong's: a pan\nKJV: pan.\n\nCognate Group: H4884 (measure), H4854 (Massa), H4861 (Mishal), H4852 (Mesha), H4863 (kneading trough), H4850 (Merathaim), H4958 (pan), H4913 (Mashal), H4752 (drop), H4851 (Mash), H4762 (Mareshah)",
    4959: "מָשַׁשׁ (mâshash | maw-shash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to feel of; by implication, to grope\nKJV: feel, grope, search.\n\nCognate Group: H4959 (feel)\nGreek Equivalents: G2045 ἐρευνάω, G5584 ψηλαφάω",
    4960: "מִשְׁתֶּה (mishteh | mish-teh')\n\nDerivation: from H8354 שָׁתָה\nStrong's: drink, by implication, drinking (the act); also (by implication) a banquet or (generally) feast\nKJV: banquet, drank, drink, feast((-ed), -ing).\n\nCognate Group: H4960 (banquet), H8354 ([idiom] assuredly), H8360 (drinking), H8358 (drunkenness)\nGreek Equivalents: G1062 γάμος, G1403 δοχή, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G4188 πόμα, G4213 πόσις, G4224 πότος, G4849 συμπόσιον",
    4961: "מִשְׁתֶּה (mishteh | mish-teh')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H4960 מִשְׁתֶּה\nStrong's: a banquet\nKJV: banquet.\n\nCognate Group: H4961 (banquet), H8370 (Shetharboznai), H8355 (drink)",
    4962: "מַת (math | math)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H4970 מָתַי\nStrong's: properly, an adult (as of full length); by implication, a man (only in the plural)\nKJV: [phrase] few, [idiom] friends, men, persons, [idiom] small.\n\nCognate Group: H4967 (Methusael), H4962 (few), H4968 (Methuselah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2192 ἔχω, G4859 σύμφωνος",
