    4967: "מְתוּשָׁאֵל (Mᵉthûwshâʼêl | meth-oo-shaw-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H4962 מַת and H410 אֵל, with the relative interposed; man who (is) of God\nStrong's: Methusael, an antediluvian patriarch\nKJV: Methusael.\n\nCognate Group: H4967 (Methusael), H4962 (few), H4968 (Methuselah)\nGreek Equivalents: G1542 ἑκατονταπλασίων",
    4968: "מְתוּשֶׁלַח (Mᵉthûwshelach | meth-oo-sheh'-lakh)\n\nDerivation: from H4962 מַת and H7973 שֶׁלַח ; man of a dart\nStrong's: Methushelach, an antediluvian patriarch\nKJV: Methuselah.\n\nCognate Group: H4967 (Methusael), H4962 (few), H4968 (Methuselah)\nGreek Equivalents: G3103 Μαθουσάλα",
    4969: "מָתַח (mâthach | maw-thakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to stretch out\nKJV: spread out.\n\nCognate Group: H572 (sack), H4969 (spread out)",
    4970: "מָתַי (mâthay | maw-thah'ee)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to extend\nStrong's: properly, extent (of time); but used only adverbially (especially with other particle prefixes), when (either relative or interrogative)\nKJV: long, when.\n\nCognate Group: H4970 (long)",
