    4977: "מַתָּן (Mattân | mat-tawn')\n\nDerivation: the same as H4976 מַתָּן\nStrong's: Mattan, the name of a priest of Baal, and of an Israelite\nKJV: Mattan.\n\nCognate Group: H4982 (Mattenai), H5417 (Nethaneel), H5416 (Nathan), H4977 (Mattan), H4979 (gift), H5418 (Nethaniah), H4991 (gift), H4976 (gift), H4983 (Mattaniah), H5414 (add), H5419 (Nathanmelech), H4992 (Mattathah), H4980 (Mattanah), H4993 (Mattithiah), H5411 (Nethinims)\nGreek Equivalents: G3157 Ματθάν",
    4978: "מַתְּנָא (mattᵉnâʼ | mat-ten-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H4979 מַתָּנָה \nStrong's: a present; specifically (in a good sense), a sacrificial offering, (in a bad sense) a bribe\nKJV: gift.\n\nCognate Group: H4978 (gift), H5426 (shake off), H5415 (bestow)\nGreek Equivalents: G1431 δωρεά",
    4979: "מַתָּנָה (mattânâh | mat-taw-naw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H4976 מַתָּן\nStrong's: a present; specifically (in a good sense), a sacrificial offering, (in a bad sense) a bribe\nKJV: gift.\n\nCognate Group: H4982 (Mattenai), H5417 (Nethaneel), H5416 (Nathan), H4977 (Mattan), H4979 (gift), H5418 (Nethaniah), H4991 (gift), H4976 (gift), H4983 (Mattaniah), H5414 (add), H5419 (Nathanmelech), H4992 (Mattathah), H4980 (Mattanah), H4993 (Mattithiah), H5411 (Nethinims)\nGreek Equivalents: G1390 δόμα, G1411 δύναμις, G1435 δῶρον",
    4980: "מַתָּנָה (Mattânâh | mat-taw-naw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H4979 מַתָּנָה\nStrong's: Mattanah, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Mattanah.\n\nCognate Group: H4982 (Mattenai), H5417 (Nethaneel), H5416 (Nathan), H4977 (Mattan), H4979 (gift), H5418 (Nethaniah), H4991 (gift), H4976 (gift), H4983 (Mattaniah), H5414 (add), H5419 (Nathanmelech), H4992 (Mattathah), H4980 (Mattanah), H4993 (Mattithiah), H5411 (Nethinims)",
    4981: "מִתְנִי (Mithnîy | mith-nee')\n\nDerivation: probably patrial from an unused noun meaning slenderness\nStrong's: a Mithnite, or inhabitant of Methen\nKJV: Mithnite.\n\nCognate Group: H4975 (greyhound), H4981 (Mithnite)",
