    5167: "נַחֲמָנִי (Nachămânîy | nakh-am-aw-nee')\n\nDerivation: from H5162 נָחַם ; consolatory\nStrong's: Nachamani, an Israelite\nKJV: Nahamani.\n\nCognate Group: H5164 (repentance), H5165 (comfort), H4505 (Menahem), H8575 (comfort), H5163 (Naham), H5151 (Nahum), H5149 (Nehum), H5150 (comfort), H5162 (comfort), H5167 (Nahamani), H5166 (Nehemiah), H8576 (Tanhumeth)",
    5168: "נַחְנוּ (nachnûw | nakh-noo')\n\nDerivation: for H587 אֲנַחְנוּ\nStrong's: we\nKJV: we.\n\nCognate Group: H594 (plumb-line), H5168 (we), H587 (ourselves)",
    5169: "נָחַץ (nâchats | naw-khats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be urgent\nKJV: require haste.\n\nCognate Group: H5169 (require haste)\nGreek Equivalents: G4710 σπουδή",
    5170: "נַחַר (nachar | nakh'-ar)\n\nDerivation: and (feminine) נַחֲרָה; from an unused root meaning to snort or snore\nStrong's: a snorting\nKJV: nostrils, snorting.\n\nCognate Group: H5156 (nostrils), H5170 (nostrils), H5152 (Nahor), H5171 (Naharai)",
    5171: "נַחֲרַי (Nachăray | nakh-ar-ah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: or נַחְרַי; from the same as H5170 נַחַר ; snorer\nStrong's: Nacharai or Nachrai, an Israelite\nKJV: Naharai, Nahari.\n\nCognate Group: H5156 (nostrils), H5170 (nostrils), H5152 (Nahor), H5171 (Naharai)",
    5172: "נָחַשׁ (nâchash | naw-khash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to hiss, i.e. whisper a (magic) spell; generally, to prognosticate\nKJV: [idiom] certainly, divine, enchanter, (use) [idiom] enchantment, learn by experience, [idiom] indeed, diligently observe.\n\nCognate Group: H5172 ([idiom] certainly), H5173 (enchantment)",
    5173: "נַחַשׁ (nachash | nakh'-ash)\n\nDerivation: from H5172 נָחַשׁ\nStrong's: an incantation or augury\nKJV: enchantment.\n\nCognate Group: H5172 ([idiom] certainly), H5173 (enchantment)",
    5174: "נְחָשׁ (nᵉchâsh | nekh-awsh')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5154 נְחוּשָׁה\nStrong's: copper\nKJV: brass.\n\nCognate Group: H5142 (have damage), H5174 (brass)",
