    5178: "נְחֹשֶׁת (nᵉchôsheth | nekh-o'-sheth)\n\nDerivation: for H5154 נְחוּשָׁה\nStrong's: copper, hence, something made of that metal, i.e. coin, a fetter; figuratively, base (as compared with gold or silver)\nKJV: brasen, brass, chain, copper, fetter (of brass), filthiness, steel.\n\nCognate Group: H5178 (brasen), H5153 (of brass), H5180 (Nehushtan), H5154 (brass), H5179 (Nehushta)\nGreek Equivalents: G3976 πέδη, G5470 χάλκεος, G5475 χαλκός",
    5179: "נְחֻשְׁתָּא (Nᵉchushtâʼ | nekh-oosh-taw')\n\nDerivation: from H5178 נְחֹשֶׁת ; copper\nStrong's: Nechushta, an Israelitess\nKJV: Nehushta.\n\nCognate Group: H5178 (brasen), H5153 (of brass), H5180 (Nehushtan), H5154 (brass), H5179 (Nehushta)",
    5180: "נְחֻשְׁתָּן (Nᵉchushtân | nekh-oosh-tawn')\n\nDerivation: from H5178 נְחֹשֶׁת\nStrong's: something made of copper, i.e. the copper serpent of the Desert\nKJV: Nehushtan.\n\nCognate Group: H5178 (brasen), H5153 (of brass), H5180 (Nehushtan), H5154 (brass), H5179 (Nehushta)",
    5181: "נָחַת (nâchath | naw-khath')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to sink, i.e. descend; causatively, to press or lead down\nKJV: be broken, (cause to) come down, enter, go down, press sore, settle, stick fast.\n\nCognate Group: H5184 (Nahath), H5181 (be broken), H5185 (come down), H5183 (lighting down)\nGreek Equivalents: G1991 ἐπιστηρίζω, G2597 καταβαίνω, G2608 κατάγνυμι, G2837 κοιμάω, G5087 τίθημι",
    5182: "נְחַת (nᵉchath | nekh-ath')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5181 נָחַת\nStrong's: to descend; causatively, to bring away, deposit, depose\nKJV: carry, come down, depose, lay up, place.\n\nCognate Group: H5182 (carry)\nGreek Equivalents: G649 ἀποστέλλω, G2702 καταφέρω, G2749 κεῖμαι",
    5183: "נַחַת (Nachath | nakh'-ath)\n\nDerivation: from H5182 נְחַת ; also (intransitively; perhaps from H5117 נוּחַ)\n\nStrong's: a descent, i.e. imposition, unfavorable (punishment) or favorable (food); restfulness\nKJV: lighting down, quiet(-ness), to rest, be set on.\n\nCognate Group: H2680 (half of the Manahethites), H5183 (lighting down), H5118 (rest), H4494 (rest), H5119 (Nohah), H5146 (Noah), H5207 (sweet), H4495 (Manoah), H3240 (bestow), H5117 (cease), H4496 (comfortable), H2010 (release), H4506 (Manahath), H2679 (half of the Manahethites), H3239 (Janoah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2372 θυμός",
    5184: "נַחַת (Nachath | nakh'-ath)\n\nDerivation: the same as H5183 נַחַת ; quiet\nStrong's: Nachath, the name of an Edomite and of two Israelites\nKJV: Nahath.\n\nCognate Group: H5184 (Nahath), H5181 (be broken), H5185 (come down), H5183 (lighting down)",
    5185: "נָחֵת (nâchêth | naw-khayth')\n\nDerivation: from H5181 נָחַת\nStrong's: descending\nKJV: come down.\n\nCognate Group: H5184 (Nahath), H5181 (be broken), H5185 (come down), H5183 (lighting down)\nGreek Equivalents: G2928 κρύπτω",
    5186: "נָטָה (nâṭâh | naw-taw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to stretch or spread out; by implication, to bend away (including moral deflection); used in a great variety of application\nKJV: [phrase] afternoon, apply, bow (down, -ing), carry aside, decline, deliver, extend, go down, be gone, incline, intend, lay, let down, offer, outstretched, overthrown, pervert, pitch, prolong, put away, shew, spread (out), stretch (forth, out), take (aside), turn (aside, away), wrest, cause to yield.\n\nCognate Group: H4296 (bed), H5186 (afternoon), H4294 (rod), H4298 (stretching out), H3194 (Juttah), H4297 (perverseness), H4295 (beneath)\nGreek Equivalents: G138 αἱρέομαι, G142 αἴρω, G635 ἀποπλανάω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G864 ἀφικνέομαι, G906 βάλλω, G941 βαστάζω, G1294 διαστρέφω, G1576 ἐκκλείω, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1614 ἐκτείνω, G1620 ἐκτίθημι, G1863 ἐπάγω, G1869 ἐπαίρω, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G1914 ἐπιβλέπω, G2116 εὐθύνω, G2476 ἵστημι, G2708 καταχέω, G2827 κλίνω, G3846 παραβάλλω, G4078 πήγνυμι, G4105 πλανάω, G4160 ποιέω, G4337 προσέχω, G4531 σαλεύω, G4732 στερεόω, G5294 ὑποτίθημι, G5308 ὑψηλός, G5312 ὑψόω",
    5187: "נְטִיל (nᵉṭîyl | net-eel')\n\nDerivation: from H5190 נָטַל\nStrong's: laden\nKJV: that bear.\n\nCognate Group: H5190 (bear), H5187 (that bear), H5192 (weighty)\nGreek Equivalents: G1869 ἐπαίρω",
    5188: "נְטִיפָה (nᵉṭîyphâh | net-ee-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H5197 נָטַף\nStrong's: a pendant for the ears (especially of pearls)\nKJV: chain, collar.\n\nCognate Group: H5198 (drop), H5188 (chain), H5199 (Netophah), H5200 (Netophathite), H5197 (drop)",
    5189: "נְטִישָׁה (nᵉṭîyshâh | net-ee-shaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5203 נָטַשׁ\nStrong's: a tendril (as an offshoot)\nKJV: battlement, branch, plant.\n\nCognate Group: H5203 (cast off), H5189 (battlement)\nGreek Equivalents: G2814 κλῆμα",
    5190: "נָטַל (nâṭal | naw-tal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to lift; by implication, to impose\nKJV: bear, offer, take up.\n\nCognate Group: H5190 (bear), H5187 (that bear), H5192 (weighty)\nGreek Equivalents: G142 αἴρω, G353 ἀναλαμβάνω",
    5191: "נְטַל (nᵉṭal | net-al')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5190 נָטַל\nStrong's: to raise\nKJV: take up.\n\nCognate Group: H5191 (take up)\nGreek Equivalents: G182 ἀκατάστατος, G1611 ἔκστασις, G2830 κλύδων, G2978 λαῖλαψ, G3709 ὀργή",
    5192: "נֵטֶל (nêṭel | nay'-tel)\n\nDerivation: ; from H5190 נָטַל\nStrong's: a burden\nKJV: weighty.\n\nCognate Group: H5190 (bear), H5187 (that bear), H5192 (weighty)\nGreek Equivalents: G1419 δυσβάστακτος",
    5193: "נָטַע (nâṭaʻ | naw-tah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to strike in, i.e. fix; specifically, to plant (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: fastened, plant(-er).\n\nCognate Group: H5195 (plant), H5193 (fastened), H5196 (plants), H4302 (plant), H5194 (plant)\nGreek Equivalents: G2476 ἵστημι, G4078 πήγνυμι, G5451 φυτεία, G5452 φυτεύω, G5453 φύω",
    5194: "נֶטַע (neṭaʻ | neh'-tah)\n\nDerivation: from H5193 נָטַע\nStrong's: a plant; collectively, a plantation; abstractly, a planting\nKJV: plant.\n\nCognate Group: H5195 (plant), H5193 (fastened), H5196 (plants), H4302 (plant), H5194 (plant)\nGreek Equivalents: G3504 νεόφυτος",
    5195: "נָטִיעַ (nâṭîyaʻ | naw-tee'-ah)Typo: xlit nâṭîaʻ corrected to nâṭîyaʻ\n\nDerivation: from H5193 נָטַע\nStrong's: a plant\nKJV: plant.\n\nCognate Group: H5195 (plant), H5193 (fastened), H5196 (plants), H4302 (plant), H5194 (plant)",
    5196: "נְטָעִים (Nᵉṭâʻîym | net-aw-eem')\n\nDerivation: plural of H5194 נֶטַע\nStrong's: Netaim, a place in Palestine\nKJV: plants.\n\nCognate Group: H5195 (plant), H5193 (fastened), H5196 (plants), H4302 (plant), H5194 (plant)",
    5197: "נָטַף (nâṭaph | naw-taf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to ooze, i.e. distil gradually; by implication, to fall in drops; figuratively, to speak by inspiration\nKJV: drop(-ping), prophesy(-et).\n\nCognate Group: H5198 (drop), H5188 (chain), H5199 (Netophah), H5200 (Netophathite), H5197 (drop)",
    5198: "נָטָף (nâṭâph | naw-tawf')\n\nDerivation: from H5197 נָטַף\nStrong's: a drop; specifically, an aromatic gum (probably stacte)\nKJV: drop, stacte.\n\nCognate Group: H5198 (drop), H5188 (chain), H5199 (Netophah), H5200 (Netophathite), H5197 (drop)\nGreek Equivalents: G1144 δάκρυ, G1145 δακρύω, G1839 ἐξίστημι, G1914 ἐπιβλέπω, G2799 κλαίω",
    5199: "נְטֹפָה (Nᵉṭôphâh | net-o-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H5197 נָטַף ; distillation\nStrong's: Netophah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Netophah.\n\nCognate Group: H5198 (drop), H5188 (chain), H5199 (Netophah), H5200 (Netophathite), H5197 (drop)",
    5200: "נְטֹפָתִי (Nᵉṭôphâthîy | net-o-faw-thee')\n\nDerivation: patronymic from H5199 נְטֹפָה\nStrong's: a Netophathite, or inhabitant of Netophah\nKJV: Netophathite.\n\nCognate Group: H5198 (drop), H5188 (chain), H5199 (Netophah), H5200 (Netophathite), H5197 (drop)",
    5201: "נָטַר (nâṭar | naw-tar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to guard; figuratively, to cherish (anger)\nKJV: bear grudge, keep(-er), reserve.\n\nCognate Group: H4307 (mark), H5201 (bear grudge)",
    5202: "נְטַר (nᵉṭar | net-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5201 נָטַר\nStrong's: to retain\nKJV: keep.\n\nCognate Group: H5208 (sweet odour), H5202 (keep), H5232 (goods), H5245 (leopard)",
    5203: "נָטַשׁ (nâṭash | naw-tash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to pound, i.e. smite; by implication (as if beating out, and thus expanding) to disperse; also, to thrust off, down, out or upon (inclusively, reject, let alone, permit, remit, etc.)\nKJV: cast off, drawn, let fall, forsake, join (battle), leave (off), lie still, loose, spread (self) abroad, stretch out, suffer.\n\nCognate Group: H5203 (cast off), H5189 (battlement)",
    5204: "נִי (nîy | nee)\n\nDerivation: a doubtful word; apparently from H5091 נָהָה\nStrong's: lamentation\nKJV: wailing.\n\nCognate Group: H5204 (wailing), H5091 (lament), H5093 (doleful), H5092 (lamentation)",
    5205: "נִיד (nîyd | need)\n\nDerivation: from H5110 נוּד\nStrong's: motion (of the lips in speech)\nKJV: moving.\n\nCognate Group: H4493 (shaking), H5205 (moving), H5112 (wandering), H5113 (Nod), H5110 (bemoan)\nGreek Equivalents: G2796 κίνησις",
    5206: "נִידָה (nîydâh | nee-daw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5205 נִיד\nStrong's: removal, i.e. exile\nKJV: removed.\n\nCognate Group: H5076 (tossing to and fro), H5074 (chase), H5206 (removed), H5079 ([idiom] far)\nGreek Equivalents: G4535 σάλος",
    5207: "נִיחֹוחַ (nîychôwach | nee-kho'-akh)\n\nDerivation: or נִיחֹחַ; from H5117 נוּחַ\nStrong's: properly, restful, i.e. pleasant; abstractly, delight\nKJV: sweet (odour).\n\nCognate Group: H2680 (half of the Manahethites), H5183 (lighting down), H5118 (rest), H4494 (rest), H5119 (Nohah), H5146 (Noah), H5207 (sweet), H4495 (Manoah), H3240 (bestow), H5117 (cease), H4496 (comfortable), H2010 (release), H4506 (Manahath), H2679 (half of the Manahethites), H3239 (Janoah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2175 εὐωδία, G2378 θυσία",
    5208: "נִיחֹוחַ (nîychôwach | nee-kho'-akh)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or נִיחֹחַ; (shorter) (Aramaic), corresponding to H5207 נִיחֹוחַ\nStrong's: pleasure\nKJV: sweet odour (savour).\n\nCognate Group: H5208 (sweet odour), H5202 (keep), H5232 (goods), H5245 (leopard)",
    5209: "נִין (nîyn | neen)\n\nDerivation: from H5125 נוּן\nStrong's: progeny\nKJV: son.\n\nCognate Group: H5125 (be continued), H5126 (Non), H5209 (son)\nGreek Equivalents: G4690 σπέρμα, G4772 συγγένεια",
    5210: "נִינְוֵה (Nîynᵉvêh | nee-nev-ay')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Nineveh, the capital of Assyria\nKJV: Nineveh.\n\nCognate Group: H4995 (raw), H5212 (Nisan), H5210 (Nineveh)\nGreek Equivalents: G3535 Νινευΐ",
    5211: "נִיס (nîyç | neece)\n\nDerivation: from H5127 נוּס\nStrong's: fugitive\nKJV: that fleeth.\n\nCognate Group: H5127 ([idiom] abate), H4498 ([idiom] apace), H5211 (that fleeth), H4499 (fleeing)",
    5212: "נִיסָן (Nîyçân | nee-sawn')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: Nisan, the first month of the Jewish sacred year\nKJV: Nisan.\n\nCognate Group: H4995 (raw), H5212 (Nisan), H5210 (Nineveh)",
    5213: "נִיצֹוץ (nîytsôwts | nee-tsotes')\n\nDerivation: from H5340 נָצַץ\nStrong's: a spark\nKJV: spark.\n\nCognate Group: H5328 (flower), H5339 (flower), H5322 (blossom), H5340 (sparkle), H5213 (spark), H5132 (flee away)",
    5214: "נִיר (nîyr | neer)\n\nDerivation: a root probably identical with that of H5216 נִיר, through the idea of the gleam of a fresh furrow\nStrong's: to till the soil\nKJV: break up.\n\nCognate Group: H5214 (break up), H5215 (fallow ground)\nGreek Equivalents: G5461 φωτίζω",
    5215: "נִיר (nîyr | neer)\n\nDerivation: or נִר; from H5214 נִיר\nStrong's: properly, plowing, i.e. (concretely) freshly plowed land\nKJV: fallow ground, plowing, tillage.\n\nCognate Group: H5214 (break up), H5215 (fallow ground)",
    5216: "נִיר (nîyr | neer)\n\nDerivation: or נִר; also נֵיר; or נֵר; or (feminine) נֵרָה; from a primitive root (see H5214 נִיר ; H5135 נוּר) properly, meaning to glisten\nStrong's: a lamp (i.e. the burner) or light (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: candle, lamp, light.\n\nCognate Group: H5369 (Ner), H5374 (Neriah), H4501 (candlestick), H5216 (candle)\nGreek Equivalents: G2640 κατάλειμμα, G3088 λύχνος, G3088 λύχνος, G5457 φῶς",
    5217: "נָכָא (nâkâʼ | naw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to smite, i.e. drive away\nKJV: be viler.\n\nCognate Group: H5217 (be viler), H5218 (broken), H5219 (spicery)",
    5218: "נָכֵא (nâkêʼ | naw-kay')\n\nDerivation: or נָכָא; from H5217 נָכָא\nStrong's: smitten, i.e. (figuratively) afflicted\nKJV: broken, stricken, wounded.\n\nCognate Group: H5217 (be viler), H5218 (broken), H5219 (spicery)\nGreek Equivalents: G4570 σβέννυμι",
    5219: "נְכֹאת (nᵉkôʼth | nek-ohth')\n\nDerivation: from H5218 נָכֵא\nStrong's: properly, a smiting, i.e. (concretely) an aromatic gum (perhaps styrax) (as powdered)\nKJV: spicery(-ces).\n\nCognate Group: H5217 (be viler), H5218 (broken), H5219 (spicery)",
    5220: "נֶכֶד (neked | neh'-ked)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to propagate\nStrong's: offspring\nKJV: nephew, son's son.\n\nCognate Group: H5220 (nephew)\nGreek Equivalents: G3686 ὄνομα, G4690 σπέρμα",
    5221: "נָכָה (nâkâh | naw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to strike (lightly or severely, literally or figuratively)\nKJV: beat, cast forth, clap, give (wounds), [idiom] go forward, [idiom] indeed, kill, make (slaughter), murderer, punish, slaughter, slay(-er, -ing), smite(-r, -ing), strike, be stricken, (give) stripes, [idiom] surely, wound.\n\nCognate Group: H5223 (contrite), H5222 (abject), H6549 (Pharaoh-necho), H5221 (beat), H3559 (certain), H5224 (Necho), H4347 (beaten)\nGreek Equivalents: G91 ἀδικέω, G337 ἀναιρέω, G615 ἀποκτείνω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G906 βάλλω, G1289 διασπείρω, G1572 ἐκκαίω, G1581 ἐκκόπτω, G1842 ἐξολοθρεύω, G1863 ἐπάγω, G2289 θανατόω, G2608 κατάγνυμι, G2609 κατάγω, G2629 κατακόπτω, G2871 κοπή, G2875 κόπτω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3146 μαστιγόω, G3147 μαστίζω, G3164 μάχομαι, G3817 παίω, G3860 παραδίδωμι, G3960 πατάσσω, G4098 πίπτω, G4141 πλήσσω, G4937 συντρίβω, G5180 τύπτω, G5407 φονεύω",
    5222: "נֵכֶה (nêkeh | nay-keh')\n\nDerivation: from H5221 נָכָה\nStrong's: a smiter, i.e. (figuratively) traducer\nKJV: abject.\n\nCognate Group: H5223 (contrite), H5222 (abject), H6549 (Pharaoh-necho), H5221 (beat), H3559 (certain), H5224 (Necho), H4347 (beaten)\nGreek Equivalents: G2272 ἡσύχιος, G3148 μάστιξ",
    5223: "נָכֶה (nâkeh | naw-keh')Cognate Group: H5223 (contrite), H5222 (abject), H6549 (Pharaoh-necho), H5221 (beat), H3559 (certain), H5224 (Necho), H4347 (beaten)\n\nGreek Equivalents: G5536 χρῆμα \nStrong's: smitten, i.e. (literally) maimed, or (figuratively) dejected\nKJV: contrite, lame.",
    5224: "נְכֹו (Nᵉkôw | nek-o')\n\nDerivation: probably of Egyptian origin\nStrong's: Neko, an Egyptian king\nKJV: Necho. Compare H6549 פַּרְעֹה נְכֹה .\n\nCognate Group: H5223 (contrite), H5222 (abject), H6549 (Pharaoh-necho), H5221 (beat), H3559 (certain), H5224 (Necho), H4347 (beaten)",
    5225: "נָכֹון (Nâkôwn | naw-kone')\n\nDerivation: from H3559 כּוּן ; prepared\nStrong's: Nakon, probably an Israelite\nKJV: Nachon.\n\nCognate Group: H3561 (cake), H8499 (seat), H3200 (Jachinites), H3559 (certain), H3651 (after that), H3560 (Chun), H8498 (fashion), H3562 (Conaniah), H4369 (base), H4349 (foundation), H4350 (base), H3199 (Jachin), H3204 (Jeconiah), H5225 (Nachon), H3563 (cup)",
    5226: "נֵכַח (nêkach | nay'-kakh)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be straightforward\nStrong's: properly, the fore part; used adverbially, opposite\nKJV: before, over against.\n\nCognate Group: H5226 (before), H5229 (equity), H5227 (against), H5228 (plain)",
    5227: "נֹכַח (nôkach | no'-kakh)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5226 נֵכַח\nStrong's: properly, the front part; used adverbially (especially with preposition), opposite, in front of, forward, in behalf of\nKJV: (over) against, before, direct(-ly), for, right (on).\n\nCognate Group: H5226 (before), H5229 (equity), H5227 (against), H5228 (plain)\nGreek Equivalents: G1726 ἐναντίον, G1727 ἐναντίος, G3717 ὀρθός",
    5228: "נָכֹחַ (nâkôach | naw-ko'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5226 נֵכַח\nStrong's: straightforward, i.e. (figuratively), equitable, correct, or (abstractly), integrity\nKJV: plain, right, uprightness.\n\nCognate Group: H5226 (before), H5229 (equity), H5227 (against), H5228 (plain)\nGreek Equivalents: G18 ἀγαθός, G225 ἀλήθεια, G1799 ἐνώπιον, G2112 εὐθέως, G2117 εὐθύς, G4680 σοφός",
    5229: "נְכֹחָה (nᵉkôchâh | nek-o-khaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5228 נָכֹחַ\nStrong's: properly, straightforwardness, i.e. (figuratively) integrity, or (concretely) a truth\nKJV: equity, right (thing), uprightness.\n\nCognate Group: H5226 (before), H5229 (equity), H5227 (against), H5228 (plain)",
    5230: "נָכַל (nâkal | naw-kal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to defraud, i.e. act treacherously\nKJV: beguile, conspire, deceiver, deal subtilly.\n\nCognate Group: H5231 (wile), H5230 (beguile), H3596 (churl), H5233 (riches)\nGreek Equivalents: G1387 δολιόω",
    5231: "נֵכֶל (nêkel | nay'-kel)\n\nDerivation: from H5230 נָכַל\nStrong's: deceit\nKJV: wile.\n\nCognate Group: H5231 (wile), H5230 (beguile), H3596 (churl), H5233 (riches)",
    5232: "נְכַס (nᵉkaç | nek-as')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5233 נֶכֶס \nStrong's: treasure\nKJV: goods.\n\nCognate Group: H5208 (sweet odour), H5202 (keep), H5232 (goods), H5245 (leopard)\nGreek Equivalents: G979 βίος",
    5233: "נֶכֶס (nekeç | neh'-kes)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to accumulate\nStrong's: treasure\nKJV: riches, wealth.\n\nCognate Group: H5231 (wile), H5230 (beguile), H3596 (churl), H5233 (riches)",
    5234: "נָכַר (nâkar | naw-kar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to scrutinize, i.e. look intently at; hence (with recognition implied), to acknowledge, be acquainted with, care for, respect, revere, or (with suspicion implied), to disregard, ignore, be strange toward, reject, resign, dissimulate (as if ignorant or disowning)\nKJV: acknowledge, [idiom] could, deliver, discern, dissemble, estrange, feign self to be another, know, take knowledge (notice), perceive, regard, (have) respect, behave (make) self strange(-ly).\n\nCognate Group: H5234 (acknowledge), H4378 (acquaintance), H1971 (shew)\nGreek Equivalents: G153 αἰσχύνομαι, G526 ἀπαλλοτριόω, G1097 γινώσκω, G1107 γνωρίζω, G1921 ἐπιγινώσκω, G1962 ἐπινεύω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G4097 πιπράσκω",
    5235: "נֶכֶר (neker | neh'-ker)\n\nDerivation: or נֹכֶר; from H5234 נָכַר\nStrong's: something strange, i.e. unexpected calamity\nKJV: strange.\n\nCognate Group: H5235 (strange), H5234 (acknowledge), H5237 (alien), H5238 (precious things), H5236 (alien)",
    5236: "נֵכָר (nêkâr | nay-kawr')\n\nDerivation: ' from H5234 נָכַר\nStrong's: foreign, or (concretely) a foreigner, or (abstractly) heathendom\nKJV: alien, strange ([phrase] -er).\n\nCognate Group: H5235 (strange), H5234 (acknowledge), H5237 (alien), H5238 (precious things), H5236 (alien)\nGreek Equivalents: G241 ἀλλογενής, G245 ἀλλότριος, G2087 ἕτερος",
    5237: "נׇכְרִי (nokrîy | nok-ree')\n\nDerivation: from H5235 נֶכֶר (second form)\nStrong's: strange, in a variety of degrees and applications (foreign, non-relative, adulterous, different, wonderful)\nKJV: alien, foreigner, outlandish, strange(-r, woman).\n\nCognate Group: H5235 (strange), H5234 (acknowledge), H5237 (alien), H5238 (precious things), H5236 (alien)\nGreek Equivalents: G2398 ἴδιος, G3581 ξένος",
    5238: "נְכֹת (nᵉkôth | nek-oth')\n\nDerivation: probably for H5219 נְכֹאת\nStrong's: spicery, i.e. (generally) valuables\nKJV: precious things.\n\nCognate Group: H5235 (strange), H5234 (acknowledge), H5237 (alien), H5238 (precious things), H5236 (alien)\nGreek Equivalents: G2368 θυμίαμα",
    5239: "נָלָה (nâlâh | naw-law')\n\nDerivation: apparently a primitive root\nStrong's: to complete\nKJV: make an end.\n\nCognate Group: H5239 (make an end), H5241 (Nemuel), H5242 (Nemuelite), H4512 (perfection)\nGreek Equivalents: G3708 ὁράω",
    5240: "נְמִבְזֶה (nᵉmibzeh | nem-ib-zeh')\n\nDerivation: from H959 בָּזָה,\nStrong's: despised\nKJV: vile.\n\nCognate Group: H960 (despise), H959 (despise), H963 (contempt), H5240 (vile)",
    5241: "נְמוּאֵל (Nᵉmûwʼêl | nem-oo-ale')\n\nDerivation: apparently for H3223 יְמוּאֵל\nStrong's: Nemuel, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Nemuel.\n\nCognate Group: H5239 (make an end), H5241 (Nemuel), H5242 (Nemuelite), H4512 (perfection)",
    5242: "נְמוּאֵלִי (Nᵉmûwʼêlîy | nem-oo-ay-lee')\n\nDerivation: from H5241 נְמוּאֵל\nStrong's: a Nemuelite, or descendant of Nemuel\nKJV: Nemuelite.\n\nCognate Group: H5239 (make an end), H5241 (Nemuel), H5242 (Nemuelite), H4512 (perfection)",
    5243: "נָמַל (nâmal | naw-mal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to become clipped or (specifically) circumcised\nKJV: (branch to) be cut down (off), circumcise.\n\nCognate Group: H5243 (be cut down)",
    5244: "נְמָלָה (nᵉmâlâh | nem-aw-law')\n\nDerivation: feminine from H5243 נָמַל\nStrong's: an ant (probably from its almost bisected form)\nKJV: ant.\n\nCognate Group: H5244 (ant)",
    5245: "נְמַר (nᵉmar | nem-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5246 נָמֵר \nStrong's: a leopard (from its stripes)\nKJV: leopard.\n\nCognate Group: H5208 (sweet odour), H5202 (keep), H5232 (goods), H5245 (leopard)",
    5246: "נָמֵר (nâmêr | naw-mare')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning properly, to filtrate, i.e. be limpid (comp H5247 נִמְרָה and H5249 נִמְרִים); and thus to spot or stain as if by dripping\nStrong's: a leopard (from its stripes)\nKJV: leopard.\n\nCognate Group: H5246 (leopard), H5250 (Nimshi), H5248 (Nimrod), H5247 (Nimrah), H5249 (Nimrim)\nGreek Equivalents: G3917 πάρδαλις",
    5247: "נִמְרָה (Nimrâh | nim-raw')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5246 נָמֵר ; clear water\nStrong's: Nimrah, a place East of the Jordan\nKJV: Nimrah. See also H1039 בֵּית נִמְרָה, H5249 נִמְרִים .\n\nCognate Group: H5246 (leopard), H5250 (Nimshi), H5248 (Nimrod), H5247 (Nimrah), H5249 (Nimrim)",
    5248: "נִמְרֹוד (Nimrôwd | nim-rode')\n\nDerivation: or נִמְרֹד; probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: Nimrod, a son of Cush\nKJV: Nimrod.\n\nCognate Group: H5246 (leopard), H5250 (Nimshi), H5248 (Nimrod), H5247 (Nimrah), H5249 (Nimrim)",
    5249: "נִמְרִים (Nimrîym | nim-reem')\n\nDerivation: plural of a masculine corresponding to H5247 נִמְרָה ; clear waters\nStrong's: Nimrim, a place East of the Jordan\nKJV: Nimrim. Compare H1039 בֵּית נִמְרָה .\n\nCognate Group: H5246 (leopard), H5250 (Nimshi), H5248 (Nimrod), H5247 (Nimrah), H5249 (Nimrim)",
    5250: "נִמְשִׁי (Nimshîy | nim-shee')\n\nDerivation: probably from H4871 מָשָׁה ; extricated\nStrong's: Nimshi, the (grand-) father of Jehu\nKJV: Nimshi.\n\nCognate Group: H5246 (leopard), H5250 (Nimshi), H5248 (Nimrod), H5247 (Nimrah), H5249 (Nimrim)",
    5251: "נֵס (nêç | nace)\n\nDerivation: from H5264 נָסַס\nStrong's: a flag; also a sail; by implication, a flagstaff; generally a signal; figuratively, a token\nKJV: banner, pole, sail, (en-) sign, standard.\n\nCognate Group: H5251 (banner), H3071 (Jehovah-nissi), H5264 (lift up as an ensign)\nGreek Equivalents: G757 ἄρχω, G1391 δόξα, G4592 σημεῖον, G4953 σύσσημον",
    5252: "נְסִבָּה (nᵉçibbâh | nes-ib-baw')\n\nDerivation: feminine participle passive of H5437 סָבַב\nStrong's: properly, an environment, i.e. circumstance or turn of affairs\nKJV: cause.\n\nCognate Group: H5439 (about), H5437 (bring), H4142 (being changed), H5252 (cause), H4524 (that compass about), H4036 (Magormissabib), H5438 (cause), H4141 (winding about)",
    5253: "נָסַג (nâçag | naw-sag')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to retreat\nKJV: departing away, remove, take (hold), turn away.\n\nCognate Group: H7873 (pursuing), H5472 (backslider), H5253 (departing away), H7734 (turn back), H5509 (dross)",
    5254: "נָסָה (nâçâh | naw-saw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to test; by implication, to attempt\nKJV: adventure, assay, prove, tempt, try.\n\nCognate Group: H4531 (temptation), H5254 (adventure), H4532 (Massah)\nGreek Equivalents: G1598 ἐκπειράζω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3984 πεῖρα, G3985 πειράζω, G3987 πειράω",
    5255: "נָסַח (nâçach | naw-sakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tear away\nKJV: destroy, pluck, root.\n\nCognate Group: H5255 (destroy)\nGreek Equivalents: G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1856 ἐξωθέω",
    5256: "נְסַח (nᵉçach | nes-akh')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5255 נָסַח \nStrong's: to tear away\nKJV: pull down.\n\nCognate Group: H5256 (pull down)\nGreek Equivalents: G2507 καθαιρέω",
    5257: "נְסִיךְ (nᵉçîyk | nes-eek')\n\nDerivation: from H5258 נָסַךְ\nStrong's: properly, something poured out, i.e. a libation; also a molten image; by implication, a prince (as anointed)\nKJV: drink offering, duke, prince(-ipal).\n\nCognate Group: H5257 (drink offering), H5258 (cover), H4541 (covering), H5262 (cover)\nGreek Equivalents: G757 ἄρχω, G758 ἄρχων",
    5258: "נָסַךְ (nâçak | naw-sak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to pour out, especially a libation, or to cast (metal); by analogy, to anoint aking\nKJV: cover, melt, offer, (cause to) pour (out), set (up).\n\nCognate Group: H5257 (drink offering), H5258 (cover), H4541 (covering), H5262 (cover)\nGreek Equivalents: G2311 θεμελιόω, G2525 καθίστημι, G4160 ποιέω, G4222 ποτίζω, G4689 σπένδω",
    5259: "נָסַךְ (nâçak | naw-sak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (probably identical with H5258 נָסַךְ through the idea of fusion)\nStrong's: to interweave, i.e. (figuratively) to overspread\nKJV: that is spread.\n\nCognate Group: H4545 (web), H5259 (that is spread), H4541 (covering)",
    5260: "נְסַךְ (nᵉçak | nes-ak')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5258 נָסַךְ\nStrong's: to pour out a libation\nKJV: offer.\n\nCognate Group: H5261 (drink offering), H5260 (offer)",
    5261: "נְסַךְ (nᵉçak | nes-ak')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5262 נֶסֶךְ\nStrong's: a libation\nKJV: drink offering.\n\nCognate Group: H5261 (drink offering), H5260 (offer)",
    5262: "נֶסֶךְ (neçek | neh'-sek)\n\nDerivation: or נֵסֶךְ; from H5258 נָסַךְ\nStrong's: a libation; also a cast idol\nKJV: cover, drink offering, molten image.\n\nCognate Group: H5257 (drink offering), H5258 (cover), H4541 (covering), H5262 (cover)",
    5263: "נָסַס (nâçaç | naw-sas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to wane, i.e. be sick\nKJV: faint.\n\nCognate Group: H5263 (faint)",
    5264: "נָסַס (nâçaç | naw-sas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; to gleam from afar, i.e. to be conspicuous as a signal; or rather perhaps a denominative from H5251 נֵס (and identical with H5263 נָסַס, through the idea of a flag as fluttering in the wind)\nStrong's: to raise a beacon\nKJV: lift up as an ensign.\n\nCognate Group: H5251 (banner), H3071 (Jehovah-nissi), H5264 (lift up as an ensign)\nGreek Equivalents: G2947 κυλιόω, G5343 φεύγω",
    5265: "נָסַע (nâçaʻ | naw-sah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to pull up, especially the tent-pins, i.e. start on ajourney\nKJV: cause to blow, bring, get, (make to) go (away, forth, forward, onward, out), (take) journey, march, remove, set aside (forward), [idiom] still, be on his (go their) way.\n\nCognate Group: H4551 (before it was brought), H5265 (cause to blow), H4550 (journey)",
    5266: "נָסַק (nâçaq | naw-sak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to go up\nKJV: ascend.\n\nCognate Group: H5562 (Samgar-nebo), H5266 (ascend), H5563 (tender grape), H5560 (flour)",
    5267: "נְסַק (nᵉçaq | nes-ak')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5266 נָסַק \nStrong's: to go up\nKJV: take up.\n\nCognate Group: H5267 (take up), H5559 (come)",
    5268: "נִסְרֹךְ (Niçrôk | nis-roke')\n\nTypo: lemma נְסִרֹךְ first vowel, corrected to נִסְרֹךְ\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Nisrok, a Babylonian idol\nKJV: Nisroch.\n\nCognate Group: H5272 (Neiel), H5268 (Nisroch)",
    5269: "נֵעָה (Nêʻâh | nay-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H5128 נוּעַ ; motion\nStrong's: Neah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Neah.\n\nCognate Group: H5128 (continually), H5269 (Neah), H4517 (cornet), H5270 (Noah)",
    5270: "נֹעָה (Nôʻâh | no-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H5128 נוּעַ ; movement\nStrong's: Noah, an Israelitess\nKJV: Noah.\n\nCognate Group: H5128 (continually), H5269 (Neah), H4517 (cornet), H5270 (Noah)",
    5271: "נָעוּר (nâʻûwr | naw-oor')\n\nDerivation: or נָעֻר; and (feminine) נְעֻרָה; properly, passive participle from H5288 נַעַר as denominative\nStrong's: (only in plural collectively or emphatic form) youth, the state (juvenility) or the persons (young people)\nKJV: childhood, youth.\n\nCognate Group: H5294 (Neariah), H5298 (Nepheg), H5271 (childhood), H5292 (Naarah), H5290 (child), H5291 (damsel), H5288 (babe), H5295 (Naaran), H5293 (Naarai)\nGreek Equivalents: G1078 γένεσις, G3503 νεότης, G3932 παρθενία",
    5272: "נְעִיאֵל (Nᵉʻîyʼêl | neh-ee-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H5128 נוּעַ and H410 אֵל ; moved of God\nStrong's: Neiel, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Neiel.\n\nCognate Group: H5272 (Neiel), H5268 (Nisroch)",
    5273: "נָעִים (nâʻîym | naw-eem')\n\nDerivation: from H5276 נָעֵם\nStrong's: delightful (objective or subjective, literal or figurative)\nKJV: pleasant(-ure), sweet.\n\nCognate Group: H5282 (pleasant), H5280 (Naamites), H5273 (pleasant), H5278 (beauty), H5276 (pass in beauty), H5283 (Naaman), H5284 (Naamathite), H4516 (dainty), H5281 (Naomi), H5277 (Naam), H5279 (Naamah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2143 εὐπρέπεια, G2570 καλός, G2908 κρεῖσσον, G2909 κρείττων, G5611 ὡραῖος",
    5274: "נָעַל (nâʻal | naw-al')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; also denominative from H5275 נַעַל \nStrong's: properly, to fasten up, i.e. with abar or cord; hence, to sandal, i.e. furnish with slippers\nKJV: bolt, inclose, lock, shoe, shut up.\n\nCognate Group: H4514 (lock), H5274 (bolt), H5275 (dryshod), H4515 (shoe)\nGreek Equivalents: G608 ἀποκλείω, G2808 κλείω, G3112 μακράν, G4547 σανδάλιον, G5265 ὑποδέω, G5266 ὑπόδημα",
    5275: "נַעַל (naʻal | nah'-al)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) נַעֲלָה; from H5274 נָעַל\nStrong's: properly, a sandal tongue; by extension a sandal or slipper (sometimes as a symbol of occupancy, a refusal to marry, or of something valueless)\nKJV: dryshod, (pair of) shoe((-latchet), -s).\n\nCognate Group: H4514 (lock), H5274 (bolt), H5275 (dryshod), H4515 (shoe)",
    5276: "נָעֵם (nâʻêm | naw-ame')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be agreeable (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: pass in beauty, be delight, be pleasant, be sweet.\n\nCognate Group: H5282 (pleasant), H5280 (Naamites), H5273 (pleasant), H5278 (beauty), H5276 (pass in beauty), H5283 (Naaman), H5284 (Naamathite), H4516 (dainty), H5281 (Naomi), H5277 (Naam), H5279 (Naamah)\nGreek Equivalents: G957 βελτίον, G2234 ἡδέως, G2570 καλός, G2908 κρεῖσσον, G2909 κρείττων",
    5277: "נַעַם (Naʻam | nah'-am)\n\nDerivation: from H5276 נָעֵם ; pleasure\nStrong's: Naam, an Israelite\nKJV: Naam.\n\nCognate Group: H5282 (pleasant), H5280 (Naamites), H5273 (pleasant), H5278 (beauty), H5276 (pass in beauty), H5283 (Naaman), H5284 (Naamathite), H4516 (dainty), H5281 (Naomi), H5277 (Naam), H5279 (Naamah)",
    5278: "נֹעַם (nôʻam | no'-am)\n\nDerivation: from H5276 נָעֵם\nStrong's: agreeableness, i.e. delight, suitableness, splendor or grace\nKJV: beauty, pleasant(-ness).\n\nCognate Group: H5282 (pleasant), H5280 (Naamites), H5273 (pleasant), H5278 (beauty), H5276 (pass in beauty), H5283 (Naaman), H5284 (Naamathite), H4516 (dainty), H5281 (Naomi), H5277 (Naam), H5279 (Naamah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2987 λαμπρότης, G4586 σεμνός",
    5279: "נַעֲמָה (Naʻămâh | nah-am-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5277 נַעַם ; pleasantness\nStrong's: Naamah, the name of an antediluvian woman, of an Ammonitess, and of a place in Palestine\nKJV: Naamah.\n\nCognate Group: H5282 (pleasant), H5280 (Naamites), H5273 (pleasant), H5278 (beauty), H5276 (pass in beauty), H5283 (Naaman), H5284 (Naamathite), H4516 (dainty), H5281 (Naomi), H5277 (Naam), H5279 (Naamah)",
    5280: "נַעֲמִי (Naʻămîy | nah-am-ee')\n\nDerivation: patronymic from H5283 נַעֲמָן\nStrong's: a Naamanite, or descendant of Naaman (collectively)\nKJV: Naamites.\n\nCognate Group: H5282 (pleasant), H5280 (Naamites), H5273 (pleasant), H5278 (beauty), H5276 (pass in beauty), H5283 (Naaman), H5284 (Naamathite), H4516 (dainty), H5281 (Naomi), H5277 (Naam), H5279 (Naamah)",
    5281: "נׇעֳמִי (Noʻŏmîy | no-om-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H5278 נֹעַם ; pleasant\nStrong's: Noomi, an Israelitess\nKJV: Naomi.\n\nCognate Group: H5282 (pleasant), H5280 (Naamites), H5273 (pleasant), H5278 (beauty), H5276 (pass in beauty), H5283 (Naaman), H5284 (Naamathite), H4516 (dainty), H5281 (Naomi), H5277 (Naam), H5279 (Naamah)",
    5282: "נַעֲמָן (naʻămân | nah-am-awn')\n\nDerivation: from H5276 נָעֵם\nStrong's: pleasantness (plural as concrete)\nKJV: pleasant.\n\nCognate Group: H5282 (pleasant), H5280 (Naamites), H5273 (pleasant), H5278 (beauty), H5276 (pass in beauty), H5283 (Naaman), H5284 (Naamathite), H4516 (dainty), H5281 (Naomi), H5277 (Naam), H5279 (Naamah)",
    5283: "נַעֲמָן (Naʻămân | nah-am-awn')\n\nDerivation: the same as H5282 נַעֲמָן\nStrong's: Naaman, the name of an Israelite and of a Damascene\nKJV: Naaman.\n\nCognate Group: H5282 (pleasant), H5280 (Naamites), H5273 (pleasant), H5278 (beauty), H5276 (pass in beauty), H5283 (Naaman), H5284 (Naamathite), H4516 (dainty), H5281 (Naomi), H5277 (Naam), H5279 (Naamah)\nGreek Equivalents: G3497 Νεεμάν",
    5284: "נַעֲמָתִי (Naʻămâthîy | nah-am-aw-thee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from a place corresponding in name (but not identical) with H5279 נַעֲמָה\nStrong's: a Naamathite, or inhabitant of Naamah\nKJV: Naamathite.\n\nCognate Group: H5282 (pleasant), H5280 (Naamites), H5273 (pleasant), H5278 (beauty), H5276 (pass in beauty), H5283 (Naaman), H5284 (Naamathite), H4516 (dainty), H5281 (Naomi), H5277 (Naam), H5279 (Naamah)",
    5285: "נַעֲצוּץ (naʻătsûwts | nah-ats-oots')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to prick\nStrong's: probably a brier; by implication, a thicket of thorny bushes\nKJV: thorn.\n\nCognate Group: H5285 (thorn)",
    5286: "נָעַר (nâʻar | naw-ar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to growl\nKJV: yell.\n\nCognate Group: H5286 (yell)",
    5287: "נָעַר (nâʻar | naw-ar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (probably identical with H5286 נָעַר, through the idea of the rustling of mane, which usually accompanies the lion's roar)\nStrong's: to tumble about\nKJV: shake (off, out, self), overthrow, toss up and down.\n\nCognate Group: H5287 (shake), H5296 (tow), H5289 (young one)\nGreek Equivalents: G660 ἀποτινάσσω, G660 ἀποτινάσσω, G1287 διασκορπίζω, G1614 ἐκτείνω, G1621 ἐκτινάσσω, G1825 ἐξεγείρω, G2690 καταστρέφω, G4650 σκορπίζω",
    5288: "נַעַר (naʻar | nah'-ar)\n\nDerivation: from H5287 נָעַר\nStrong's: (concretely) a boy (as active), from the age of infancy to adolescence; by implication, a servant; also (by interch. of sex), a girl (of similar latitude in age)\nKJV: babe, boy, child, damsel (from the margin), lad, servant, young (man).\n\nCognate Group: H5294 (Neariah), H5298 (Nepheg), H5271 (childhood), H5292 (Naarah), H5290 (child), H5291 (damsel), H5288 (babe), H5295 (Naaran), H5293 (Naarai)\nGreek Equivalents: G1248 διακονία, G1249 διάκονος, G2877 κοράσιον, G3494 νεανίας, G3495 νεανίσκος, G3501 νέος, G3501 νέος, G3808 παιδάριον, G3813 παιδίον, G3816 παῖς, G3933 παρθένος",
    5289: "נַעַר (naʻar | nah'-ar)\n\nDerivation: from H5287 נָעַר in its derivative sense of tossing about\nStrong's: a wanderer\nKJV: young one.\n\nCognate Group: H5287 (shake), H5296 (tow), H5289 (young one)",
    5290: "נֹעַר (nôʻar | no'-ar)\n\nDerivation: from H5287 נָעַר ; (compare H5288 נַעַר)\n\nStrong's: (abstractly) boyhood\nKJV: child, youth.\n\nCognate Group: H5294 (Neariah), H5298 (Nepheg), H5271 (childhood), H5292 (Naarah), H5290 (child), H5291 (damsel), H5288 (babe), H5295 (Naaran), H5293 (Naarai)\nGreek Equivalents: G3503 νεότης, G3516 νήπιος",
    5291: "נַעֲרָה (naʻărâh | nah-ar-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5288 נַעַר\nStrong's: a girl (from infancy to adolescence)\nKJV: damsel, maid(-en), young (woman).\n\nCognate Group: H5294 (Neariah), H5298 (Nepheg), H5271 (childhood), H5292 (Naarah), H5290 (child), H5291 (damsel), H5288 (babe), H5295 (Naaran), H5293 (Naarai)\nGreek Equivalents: G1135 γυνή, G1399 δούλη, G1400 δοῦλον, G1401 δοῦλος, G2324 θεράπων, G2877 κοράσιον, G3814 παιδίσκη, G3816 παῖς, G3933 παρθένος",
    5292: "נַעֲרָה (Naʻărâh | nah-ar-aw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H5291 נַעֲרָה\nStrong's: Naarah, the name of an Israelitess, and of a place in Palestine\nKJV: Naarah, Naarath.\n\nCognate Group: H5294 (Neariah), H5298 (Nepheg), H5271 (childhood), H5292 (Naarah), H5290 (child), H5291 (damsel), H5288 (babe), H5295 (Naaran), H5293 (Naarai)",
    5293: "נַעֲרַי (Naʻăray | nah-ar-ah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H5288 נַעַר ; youthful\nStrong's: Naarai, an Israelite\nKJV: Naarai.\n\nCognate Group: H5294 (Neariah), H5298 (Nepheg), H5271 (childhood), H5292 (Naarah), H5290 (child), H5291 (damsel), H5288 (babe), H5295 (Naaran), H5293 (Naarai)",
    5294: "נְעַרְיָה (Nᵉʻaryâh | neh-ar-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5288 נַעַר and H3050 יָהּ ; servant of Jah\nStrong's: Nearjah, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Neariah.\n\nCognate Group: H5294 (Neariah), H5298 (Nepheg), H5271 (childhood), H5292 (Naarah), H5290 (child), H5291 (damsel), H5288 (babe), H5295 (Naaran), H5293 (Naarai)",
    5295: "נַעֲרָן (Naʻărân | nah-ar-awn')\n\nDerivation: from H5288 נַעַר ; juvenile\nStrong's: Naaran, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Naaran.\n\nCognate Group: H5294 (Neariah), H5298 (Nepheg), H5271 (childhood), H5292 (Naarah), H5290 (child), H5291 (damsel), H5288 (babe), H5295 (Naaran), H5293 (Naarai)",
