    5298: "נֶפֶג (Nepheg | neh'-feg)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to spring forth; a sprout\nStrong's: Nepheg, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Nepheg.\n\nCognate Group: H5294 (Neariah), H5298 (Nepheg), H5271 (childhood), H5292 (Naarah), H5290 (child), H5291 (damsel), H5288 (babe), H5295 (Naaran), H5293 (Naarai)",
    5299: "נָפָה (nâphâh | naw-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H5130 נוּף in the sense of lifting\nStrong's: a height; also a sieve\nKJV: border, coast, region, sieve.\n\nCognate Group: H5130 (lift up), H8573 (offering), H5299 (border)",
    5300: "נְפוּשְׁסִים (Nᵉphûwshᵉçîym | nef-oo-shes-eem')\n\nDerivation: for H5304 נְפִיסִים\nStrong's: Nephushesim, a Temple-servant\nKJV: Nephisesim (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H5887 (En-tappuah), H5300 (Nephisesim), H4646 (giving up), H8598 (apple), H5304 (Nephusim), H5301 (blow), H4647 (bellows), H8599 (Tappuah), H5306 (emerald), H5302 (Nophah)",
    5301: "נָפַח (nâphach | naw-fakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to puff, in various applications (literally, to inflate, blow hard, scatter, kindle, expire; figuratively, to disesteem)\nKJV: blow, breath, give up, cause to lose (life), seething, snuff.\n\nCognate Group: H5887 (En-tappuah), H5300 (Nephisesim), H4646 (giving up), H8598 (apple), H5304 (Nephusim), H5301 (blow), H4647 (bellows), H8599 (Tappuah), H5306 (emerald), H5302 (Nophah)\nGreek Equivalents: G1720 ἐμφυσάω, G2545 καίω",
    5302: "נֹפַח (Nôphach | no'-fakh)\n\nDerivation: from H5301 נָפַח ; a gust\nStrong's: Nophach, a place in Moab\nKJV: Nophah.\n\nCognate Group: H5887 (En-tappuah), H5300 (Nephisesim), H4646 (giving up), H8598 (apple), H5304 (Nephusim), H5301 (blow), H4647 (bellows), H8599 (Tappuah), H5306 (emerald), H5302 (Nophah)",
    5303: "נְפִיל (nᵉphîyl | nef-eel')\n\nDerivation: or נְפִל; from H5307 נָפַל\nStrong's: properly, a feller, i.e. a bully or tyrant\nKJV: giant.\n\nCognate Group: H4651 (flake), H5307 (be accepted), H5303 (giant), H4658 (carcase), H5309 (untimely birth), H4654 (ruin)",
    5304: "נְפִיסִים (Nᵉphîyçîym | nef-ee-seem')\n\nDerivation: plural from an unused root meaning to scatter; expansions\nStrong's: Nephisim, a Temple-servant\nKJV: Nephusim (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H5887 (En-tappuah), H5300 (Nephisesim), H4646 (giving up), H8598 (apple), H5304 (Nephusim), H5301 (blow), H4647 (bellows), H8599 (Tappuah), H5306 (emerald), H5302 (Nophah)",
    5305: "נָפִישׁ (Nâphîysh | naw-feesh')\n\nDerivation: from H5314 נָפַשׁ ; refreshed\nStrong's: Naphish, a son of Ishmael, and his posterity\nKJV: Naphish.\n\nCognate Group: H5305 (Naphish), H5314 (refresh selves), H5317 (honeycomb), H5315 (any), H5320 (Naptuhim)",
    5306: "נֹפֶךְ (nôphek | no'-fek)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to glisten\nStrong's: shining; a gem, probably the garnet\nKJV: emerald.\n\nCognate Group: H5887 (En-tappuah), H5300 (Nephisesim), H4646 (giving up), H8598 (apple), H5304 (Nephusim), H5301 (blow), H4647 (bellows), H8599 (Tappuah), H5306 (emerald), H5302 (Nophah)\nGreek Equivalents: G440 ἄνθραξ",
    5307: "נָפַל (nâphal | naw-fal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to fall, in a great variety of applications (intransitive or causative, literal or figurative)\nKJV: be accepted, cast (down, self, (lots), out), cease, die, divide (by lot), (let) fail, (cause to, let, make, ready to) fall (away, down, -en, -ing), fell(-ing), fugitive, have (inheritance), inferior, be judged (by mistake for H6419 פָּלַל), lay (along), (cause to) lie down, light (down), be ([idiom] hast) lost, lying, overthrow, overwhelm, perish, present(-ed, -ing), (make to) rot, slay, smite out, [idiom] surely, throw down.\n\nCognate Group: H4651 (flake), H5307 (be accepted), H5303 (giant), H4658 (carcase), H5309 (untimely birth), H4654 (ruin)\nGreek Equivalents: G249 ἄλογος, G634 ἀποπίπτω, G641 ἀποῤῥίπτω, G801 ἀσύνετος, G868 ἀφίστημι, G906 βάλλω, G1096 γίνομαι, G1239 διαδίδωμι, G1581 ἐκκόπτω, G1601 ἐκπίπτω, G1685 ἐμβάλλω, G1706 ἐμπίπτω, G1707 ἐμπλέκω, G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G1968 ἐπιπίπτω, G1977 ἐπιῤῥίπτω, G1994 ἐπιστρέφω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G2068 ἐσθίω, G2523 καθίζω, G2598 καταβάλλω, G2625 κατακλίνω, G2667 καταπίπτω, G2703 καταφεύγω, G2722 κατέχω, G2730 κατοικέω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3895 παραπίπτω, G4016 περιβάλλω, G4045 περιπίπτω, G4098 πίπτω, G4141 πλήσσω, G4336 προσεύχομαι, G4363 προσπίπτω, G4369 προστίθημι, G4741 στηρίζω, G5013 ταπεινόω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5053 τελευτάω, G5087 τίθημι, G5343 φεύγω",
    5308: "נְפַל (nᵉphal | nef-al')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5307 נָפַל \nStrong's: to fall, in a great variety of applications (intransitive or causative, literal or figurative)\nKJV: fall (down), have occasion.\n\nCognate Group: H5308 (fall)\nGreek Equivalents: G1621 ἐκτινάσσω, G5316 φαίνω",
    5309: "נֶפֶל (nephel | neh'-fel)\n\nDerivation: or נֵפֶל; from H5307 נָפַל\nStrong's: something fallen, i.e. an abortion\nKJV: untimely birth.\n\nCognate Group: H4651 (flake), H5307 (be accepted), H5303 (giant), H4658 (carcase), H5309 (untimely birth), H4654 (ruin)\nGreek Equivalents: G1626 ἔκτρωμα",
    5310: "נָפַץ (nâphats | naw-fats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to dash to pieces, or scatter\nKJV: be beaten in sunder, break (in pieces), broken, dash (in pieces), cause to be discharged, dispersed, be overspread, scatter.\n\nCognate Group: H4661 (battle ax), H5310 (be beaten in sunder), H5311 (scattering), H4660 (slaughter)\nGreek Equivalents: G859 ἄφεσις, G1287 διασκορπίζω, G1289 διασπείρω, G1474 ἐδαφίζω, G1621 ἐκτινάσσω, G2629 κατακόπτω, G4937 συντρίβω",
    5311: "נֶפֶץ (nephets | neh'-fets)\n\nDerivation: from H5310 נָפַץ\nStrong's: a storm (as dispersing)\nKJV: scattering.\n\nCognate Group: H4661 (battle ax), H5310 (be beaten in sunder), H5311 (scattering), H4660 (slaughter)",
    5312: "נְפַק (nᵉphaq | nef-ak')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) a primitive root\nStrong's: to issue; causatively, to bring out\nKJV: come (go, take) forth (out).\n\nCognate Group: H5313 (expense), H5312 (come forth), H5326 (strength)\nGreek Equivalents: G1607 ἐκπορεύομαι, G1627 ἐκφέρω, G1831 ἐξέρχομαι, G5342 φέρω",
