    5314: "נָפַשׁ (nâphash | naw-fash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to breathe; passively, to be breathed upon, i.e. (figuratively) refreshed (as if by a current of air)\nKJV: (be) refresh selves (-ed).\n\nCognate Group: H5305 (Naphish), H5314 (refresh selves), H5317 (honeycomb), H5315 (any), H5320 (Naptuhim)\nGreek Equivalents: G373 ἀναπαύω, G373 ἀναπαύω, G404 ἀναψύχω, G404 ἀναψύχω, G2664 καταπαύω, G3973 παύω",
    5315: "נֶפֶשׁ (nephesh | neh'-fesh)\n\nDerivation: from H5314 נָפַשׁ\nStrong's: properly, a breathing creature, i.e. animal of (abstractly) vitality; used very widely in a literal, accommodated or figurative sense (bodily or mental)\nKJV: any, appetite, beast, body, breath, creature, [idiom] dead(-ly), desire, [idiom] (dis-) contented, [idiom] fish, ghost, [phrase] greedy, he, heart(-y), (hath, [idiom] jeopardy of) life ([idiom] in jeopardy), lust, man, me, mind, mortally, one, own, person, pleasure, (her-, him-, my-, thy-) self, them (your) -selves, [phrase] slay, soul, [phrase] tablet, they, thing, ([idiom] she) will, [idiom] would have it.\n\nCognate Group: H5305 (Naphish), H5314 (refresh selves), H5317 (honeycomb), H5315 (any), H5320 (Naptuhim)\nGreek Equivalents: G435 ἀνήρ, G1658 ἐλεύθερος, G1680 ἐλπίς, G1798 ἐνύπνιον, G2588 καρδία, G2776 κεφαλή, G4157 πνοή, G4983 σῶμα, G5590 ψυχή",
    5316: "נֶפֶת (nepheth | neh'-feth)\n\nDerivation: for H5299 נָפָה\nStrong's: a height\nKJV: country.\n\nCognate Group: H5316 (country), H5299 (border), H5131 (situation)",
    5317: "נֹפֶת (nôpheth | no'-feth)\n\nDerivation: from H5130 נוּף in the sense of shaking to pieces\nStrong's: a dripping i.e. of honey (from the comb)\nKJV: honeycomb.\n\nCognate Group: H5305 (Naphish), H5314 (refresh selves), H5317 (honeycomb), H5315 (any), H5320 (Naptuhim)\nGreek Equivalents: G2781 κηρίον, G3192 μέλι",
    5318: "נֶפְתֹּוחַ (Nephtôwach | nef-to'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H6605 פָּתַח ; opened, i.e. a spring\nStrong's: Nephtoach, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Neptoah.\n\nCognate Group: H6608 (entrance), H5318 (Neptoah), H4668 (key), H6605 (appear), H6607 (door), H4669 (opening), H6611 (Pethakiah), H3317 (Jiphthah-el), H6609 (drawn sword), H6610 (open), H3316 (Jephthah)",
    5319: "נַפְתּוּל (naphtûwl | naf-tool')\n\nDerivation: from H6617 פָּתַל\nStrong's: properly, wrestled; but used (in the plural) transitively, a struggle\nKJV: wrestling.\n\nCognate Group: H5319 (wrestling), H6617 (froward), H5321 (Naphtali), H6619 (Pithom), H6618 (crooked), H6616 (bound)",
    5320: "נַפְתֻּחִים (Naphtuchîym | naf-too-kheem)\n\nDerivation: plural of foreign origin,\nStrong's: Naphtuchim, an Egyptian tribe\nKJV: Naptuhim.\n\nCognate Group: H5305 (Naphish), H5314 (refresh selves), H5317 (honeycomb), H5315 (any), H5320 (Naptuhim)",
    5321: "נַפְתָּלִי (Naphtâlîy | naf-taw-lee')\n\nDerivation: from H6617 פָּתַל ; my wrestling\nStrong's: Naphtali, a son of Jacob, with the tribe descended from him, and its territory\nKJV: Naphtali.\n\nCognate Group: H5319 (wrestling), H6617 (froward), H5321 (Naphtali), H6619 (Pithom), H6618 (crooked), H6616 (bound)\nGreek Equivalents: G3508 Νεφθαλείμ",
    5322: "נֵץ (nêts | nayts)\n\nDerivation: from H5340 נָצַץ\nStrong's: a flower (from its brilliancy); also a hawk (from it flashing speed)\nKJV: blossom, hawk.\n\nCognate Group: H5328 (flower), H5339 (flower), H5322 (blossom), H5340 (sparkle), H5213 (spark), H5132 (flee away)",
    5323: "נָצָא (nâtsâʼ | naw-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to go away\nKJV: flee.\n\nCognate Group: H5323 (flee)",
    5324: "נָצַב (nâtsab | naw-tsab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to station, in various applications (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: appointed, deputy, erect, establish, [idiom] Huzzah (by mistake for a proper name), lay, officer, pillar, present, rear up, set (over, up), settle, sharpen, establish, (make to) stand(-ing, still, up, upright), best state.\n\nCognate Group: H5324 (appointed), H5325 (haft), H5334 (Nezib), H5333 (garrison), H4674 (mount), H4673 (garrison), H4678 (pillar), H4676 (garrison), H4675 (army)\nGreek Equivalents: G950 βεβαιόω, G1265 διαμένω, G1991 ἐπιστηρίζω, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G2186 ἐφίστημι, G2476 ἵστημι, G2525 καθίστημι, G3648 ὁλόκληρος, G3936 παρίστημι, G4026 περιΐστημι, G4078 πήγνυμι, G4160 ποιέω, G4732 στερεόω, G4741 στηρίζω, G5287 ὑπόστασις",
    5325: "נִצָּב (nitstsâb | nits-twawb')\n\nDerivation: passive participle of H5324 נָצַב\nStrong's: fixed, i.e. a handle\nKJV: haft.\n\nCognate Group: H5324 (appointed), H5325 (haft), H5334 (Nezib), H5333 (garrison), H4674 (mount), H4673 (garrison), H4678 (pillar), H4676 (garrison), H4675 (army)",
    5326: "נִצְבָּה (nitsbâh | nits-baw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H5324 נָצַב\nStrong's: fixedness, i.e. firmness\nKJV: strength.\n\nCognate Group: H5313 (expense), H5312 (come forth), H5326 (strength)",
    5327: "נָצָה (nâtsâh | naw-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to go forth, i.e. (by implication) to be expelled, and (consequently) desolate; causatively, to lay waste; also (specifically), to quarrel\nKJV: be laid waste, runinous, strive (together).\n\nCognate Group: H5327 (be laid waste), H4695 (that contended), H4683 (contention)\nGreek Equivalents: G381 ἀνάπτω, G1999 ἐπισύστασις, G2186 ἐφίστημι, G2507 καθαιρέω, G3164 μάχομαι",
    5328: "נִצָּה (nitstsâh | nits-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5322 נֵץ\nStrong's: a blossom\nKJV: flower.\n\nCognate Group: H5328 (flower), H5339 (flower), H5322 (blossom), H5340 (sparkle), H5213 (spark), H5132 (flee away)\nGreek Equivalents: G438 ἄνθος",
    5329: "נָצַח (nâtsach | naw-tsakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; also as denominative from H5331 נֶצַח \nStrong's: properly, to glitter from afar, i.e. to be eminent (as a superintendent, especially of the Temple services and its music); to be permanent\nKJV: excel, chief musician (singer), oversee(-r), set forward.\n\nCognate Group: H5331 (alway), H5329 (excel)\nGreek Equivalents: G1765 ἐνισχύω, G1983 ἐπισκοπέω, G1988 ἐπιστάτης, G2480 ἰσχύω, G3528 νικάω",
    5330: "נְצַח (nᵉtsach | nets-akh')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5329 נָצַח\nStrong's: to become chief\nKJV: be preferred.\n\nCognate Group: H5330 (be preferred)",
    5331: "נֶצַח (netsach | neh'-tsakh)\n\nDerivation: or נֵצַח; from H5329 נָצַח\nStrong's: properly, a goal, i.e. the bright object at adistance travelled towards; hence (figuratively), splendor, or (subjectively) truthfulness, or (objectively) confidence; but usually (adverbially), continually (i.e. to the most distant point of view)\nKJV: alway(-s), constantly, end, ([phrase] n-) ever(more), perpetual, strength, victory.\n\nCognate Group: H5331 (alway), H5329 (excel)\nGreek Equivalents: G129 αἷμα, G165 αἰών, G3529 νίκη, G3534 νῖκος, G5056 τέλος",
    5332: "נֵצַח (Nêtsach | nay'-tsakh)\n\nDerivation: probably identical with H5331 נֶצַח, through the idea of brilliancy of color\nStrong's: juice of the grape (as blood red)\nKJV: blood, strength.\n\nCognate Group: H5335 (Neziah), H5332 (blood)",
    5333: "נְצִיב (nᵉtsîyb | nets-eeb')\n\nDerivation: or נְצִב; from H5324 נָצַב\nStrong's: something stationary, i.e. a prefect, a military post, a statue\nKJV: garrison, officer, pillar.\n\nCognate Group: H5324 (appointed), H5325 (haft), H5334 (Nezib), H5333 (garrison), H4674 (mount), H4673 (garrison), H4678 (pillar), H4676 (garrison), H4675 (army)\nGreek Equivalents: G2233 ἡγέομαι",
    5334: "נְצִיב (Nᵉtsîyb | nets-eeb')\n\nDerivation: the same as H5333 נְצִיב ; station\nStrong's: Netsib, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Nezib.\n\nCognate Group: H5324 (appointed), H5325 (haft), H5334 (Nezib), H5333 (garrison), H4674 (mount), H4673 (garrison), H4678 (pillar), H4676 (garrison), H4675 (army)",
    5335: "נְצִיחַ (nᵉtsîyach | nets-ee'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H5329 נָצַח ; conspicuous\nStrong's: Netsiach, a Temple-servant\nKJV: Neziah.\n\nCognate Group: H5335 (Neziah), H5332 (blood)",
    5336: "נָצִיר (nâtsîyr | naw-tsere')\n\nDerivation: from H5341 נָצַר\nStrong's: properly, conservative; but used passively, delivered\nKJV: preserved.\n\nCognate Group: H5336 (preserved), H5341 (besieged)",
    5337: "נָצַל (nâtsal | naw-tsal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to snatch away, whether in a good or a bad sense\nKJV: [idiom] at all, defend, deliver (self), escape, [idiom] without fail, part, pluck, preserve, recover, rescue, rid, save, spoil, strip, [idiom] surely, take (out).\n\nCognate Group: H2020 (deliverance), H5337 ([idiom] at all)\nGreek Equivalents: G556 ἀπελαύνω, G566 ἀπέχει, G567 ἀπέχομαι, G568 ἀπέχω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G996 βοήθεια, G1807 ἐξαιρέω, G2511 καθαρίζω, G2720 κατευθύνω, G4014 περιαιρέω, G4506 ῥύομαι, G4863 συνάγω, G4982 σώζω",
    5338: "נְצַל (nᵉtsal | nets-al')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5337 נָצַל\nStrong's: to extricate\nKJV: deliver, rescue.\n\nCognate Group: H5338 (deliver), H5343 (pure)",
    5339: "נִצָּן (nitstsân | nits-tsawn')\n\nDerivation: from H5322 נֵץ\nStrong's: a blossom\nKJV: flower.\n\nCognate Group: H5328 (flower), H5339 (flower), H5322 (blossom), H5340 (sparkle), H5213 (spark), H5132 (flee away)",
    5340: "נָצַץ (nâtsats | naw-tsats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to glare, i.e. be bright-colored\nKJV: sparkle.\n\nCognate Group: H5328 (flower), H5339 (flower), H5322 (blossom), H5340 (sparkle), H5213 (spark), H5132 (flee away)",
    5341: "נָצַר (nâtsar | naw-tsar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to guard, in a good sense (to protect, maintain, obey, etc.) or a bad one (to conceal, etc.)\nKJV: besieged, hidden thing, keep(-er, -ing), monument, observe, preserve(-r), subtil, watcher(-man).\n\nCognate Group: H5336 (preserved), H5341 (besieged)\nGreek Equivalents: G482 ἀντιλαμβάνομαι, G1290 διασπορά, G1301 διατηρέω, G1314 διαφυλάσσω, G1567 ἐκζητέω, G1765 ἐνισχύω, G1781 ἐντέλλομαι, G1807 ἐξαιρέω, G1987 ἐπίσταμαι, G2045 ἐρευνάω, G2212 ζητέω, G2853 κολλάω, G3973 παύω, G4023 περιέχω, G4111 πλάσσω, G4160 ποιέω, G4506 ῥύομαι, G4693 σπήλαιον, G5083 τηρέω, G5438 φυλακή, G5442 φυλάσσω, G5452 φυτεύω",
    5342: "נֵצֶר (nêtser | nay'-tser)\n\nDerivation: from H5341 נָצַר in the sense of greenness as a striking color\nStrong's: a shoot; figuratively, a descendant\nKJV: branch.\n\nCognate Group: H5342 (branch)\nGreek Equivalents: G438 ἄνθος",
    5343: "נְקֵא (nᵉqêʼ | nek-ay')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H5352 נָקָה\nStrong's: clean\nKJV: pure.\n\nCognate Group: H5338 (deliver), H5343 (pure)\nGreek Equivalents: G2513 καθαρός, G3022 λευκός",
    5344: "נָקַב (nâqab | naw-kab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to puncture, literally (to perforate, with more or less violence) or figuratively (to specify, designate, libel)\nKJV: appoint, blaspheme, bore, curse, express, with holes, name, pierce, strike through.\n\nCognate Group: H5344 (appoint), H4718 (hammer), H5346 (Nekeb), H4717 (hammer), H5347 (female), H5345 (pipe)\nGreek Equivalents: G1291 διαστέλλομαι, G1941 ἐπικαλέομαι, G2028 ἐπονομάζω, G2672 καταράομαι, G3687 ὀνομάζω, G4863 συνάγω",
    5345: "נֶקֶב (neqeb | neh'keb)KJV: pipe.\n\nCognate Group: H5344 (appoint), H4718 (hammer), H5346 (Nekeb), H4717 (hammer), H5347 (female), H5345 (pipe)Strong's: a bezel (for a gem)",
    5346: "נֶקֶב (Neqeb | neh'-keb)\n\nDerivation: the same as H5345 נֶקֶב ; dell\nStrong's: Nekeb, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Nekeb.\n\nCognate Group: H5344 (appoint), H4718 (hammer), H5346 (Nekeb), H4717 (hammer), H5347 (female), H5345 (pipe)",
    5347: "נְקֵבָה (nᵉqêbâh | nek-ay-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H5344 נָקַב\nStrong's: female (from the sexual form)\nKJV: female.\n\nCognate Group: H5344 (appoint), H4718 (hammer), H5346 (Nekeb), H4717 (hammer), H5347 (female), H5345 (pipe)\nGreek Equivalents: G2338 θῆλυς",
    5348: "נָקֹד (nâqôd | naw-kode')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to mark (by puncturing or branding)\nStrong's: spotted\nKJV: speckled.\n\nCognate Group: H5348 (speckled), H5350 (cracknel), H5351 (stud)\nGreek Equivalents: G3022 λευκός, G4164 ποικίλος",
    5349: "נֹקֵד (nôqêd | no-kade')\n\nDerivation: active participle from the same as H5348 נָקֹד\nStrong's: a spotter (of sheep or cattle), i.e. the owner or tender (who thus marks them)\nKJV: herdman, sheepmaster.\n\nCognate Group: H5353 (Nekoda), H5349 (herdman)",
    5350: "נִקֻּד (niqqud | nik-kood')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5348 נָקֹד\nStrong's: a crumb (as broken to spots); also a biscuit (as pricked)\nKJV: cracknel, mouldy.\n\nCognate Group: H5348 (speckled), H5350 (cracknel), H5351 (stud)\nGreek Equivalents: G977 βιβρώσκω",
    5351: "נְקֻדָּה (nᵉquddâh | ned-ood-daw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5348 נָקֹד\nStrong's: a boss\nKJV: stud.\n\nCognate Group: H5348 (speckled), H5350 (cracknel), H5351 (stud)\nGreek Equivalents: G4742 στίγμα",
    5352: "נָקָה (nâqâh | naw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be (or make) clean (literally or figuratively); by implication (in an adverse sense) to be bare, i.e. extirpated\nKJV: acquit [idiom] at all, [idiom] altogether, be blameless, cleanse, (be) clear(-ing), cut off, be desolate, be free, be (hold) guiltless, be (hold) innocent, [idiom] by no means, be quit, be (leave) unpunished, [idiom] utterly, [idiom] wholly.\n\nCognate Group: H5352 (acquit [idiom] at all), H4518 (bowl), H5356 (cleanness), H5355 (blameless)\nGreek Equivalents: G121 ἄθωος, G121 ἄθωος, G1439 ἐάω, G1567 ἐκζητέω, G2511 καθαρίζω, G2512 καθαρισμός, G2513 καθαρός, G2641 καταλείπω",
    5353: "נְקֹודָא (Nᵉqôwdâʼ | nek-o-daw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5348 נָקֹד (in the figurative sense of marked); distinction\nStrong's: Nekoda, a Temple-servant\nKJV: Nekoda.\n\nCognate Group: H5353 (Nekoda), H5349 (herdman)",
    5354: "נָקַט (nâqaṭ | naw-kat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to loathe\nKJV: weary.\n\nCognate Group: H6962 (begrieved), H5354 (weary)",
    5355: "נָקִי (nâqîy | naw-kee')\n\nDerivation: or נָקִיא; (Joel 4:19; Jonah [1:14), from H5352 נָקָה\nStrong's: innocent\nKJV: blameless, clean, clear, exempted, free, guiltless, innocent, quit.\n\nCognate Group: H5352 (acquit [idiom] at all), H4518 (bowl), H5356 (cleanness), H5355 (blameless)\nGreek Equivalents: G121 ἄθωος, G228 ἀληθινός, G273 ἄμεμπτος, G338 ἀναίτιος, G1342 δίκαιος, G2513 καθαρός",
    5356: "נִקָּיֹון (niqqâyôwn | nik-kaw-yone')\n\nDerivation: or נִקָּיֹן; from H5352 נָקָה\nStrong's: clearness (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: cleanness, innocency.\n\nCognate Group: H5352 (acquit [idiom] at all), H4518 (bowl), H5356 (cleanness), H5355 (blameless)\nGreek Equivalents: G121 ἄθωος, G1343 δικαιοσύνη",
    5357: "נָקִיק (nâqîyq | naw-keek')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to bore\nStrong's: a cleft\nKJV: hole.\n\nCognate Group: H5357 (hole)\nGreek Equivalents: G5168 τρυμαλιά",
    5358: "נָקַם (nâqam | naw-kam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to grudge, i.e. avenge or punish\nKJV: avenge(-r, self), punish, revenge (self), [idiom] surely, take vengeance.\n\nCognate Group: H5358 (avenge), H5360 (avenge), H5359 (avenged)\nGreek Equivalents: G292 ἀμύνομαι, G467 ἀνταποδίδωμι, G469 ἀνταπόδοσις, G1556 ἐκδικέω, G1559 ἐκδιώκω, G1817 ἐξανίστημι, G2920 κρίσις, G3886 παραλύω",
    5359: "נָקָם (nâqâm | naw-kawm')\n\nDerivation: from H5358 נָקַם\nStrong's: revenge\nKJV: [phrase] avenged, quarrel, vengeance.\n\nCognate Group: H5358 (avenge), H5360 (avenge), H5359 (avenged)\nGreek Equivalents: G1342 δίκαιος, G1349 δίκη, G1557 ἐκδίκησις, G2920 κρίσις",
    5360: "נְקָמָה (nᵉqâmâh | nek-aw-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5359 נָקָם\nStrong's: avengement, whether the act of the passion\nKJV: [phrase] avenge, revenge(-ing), vengeance.\n\nCognate Group: H5358 (avenge), H5360 (avenge), H5359 (avenged)",
    5361: "נָקַע (nâqaʻ | naw-kah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to feel aversion\nKJV: be alienated.\n\nCognate Group: H5361 (be alienated)",
