    5364: "נִקְפָּה (niqpâh | nik-paw')\n\nDerivation: from H5362 נָקַף\nStrong's: probably a rope (as encircling)\nKJV: rent.\n\nCognate Group: H5364 (rent), H5362 (compass)\nGreek Equivalents: G4979 σχοινίον",
    5365: "נָקַר (nâqar | naw-kar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to bore (penetrate, quarry)\nKJV: dig, pick out, pierce, put (thrust) out.\n\nCognate Group: H5366 (cleft), H5365 (dig)\nGreek Equivalents: G1581 ἐκκόπτω, G1846 ἐξορύσσω, G3736 ὀρύσσω, G4917 συνθλάω",
    5366: "נְקָרָה (nᵉqârâh | nek-aw-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H5365 נָקַר, a fissure\nStrong's: to bore (penetrate, quarry)\nKJV: cleft, clift.\n\nCognate Group: H5366 (cleft), H5365 (dig)\nGreek Equivalents: G3692 ὀπή",
    5367: "נָקַשׁ (nâqash | naw-kash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to entrap (with a noose), literally or figuratively\nKJV: catch (lay a) snare.\n\nCognate Group: H5371 (Nergal-sharezer), H5367 (catch snare), H5373 (spikenard), H5370 (Nergal)\nGreek Equivalents: G1567 ἐκζητέω, G2045 ἐρευνάω, G3802 παγιδεύω, G4815 συλλαμβάνω",
    5368: "נְקַשׁ (nᵉqash | nek-ash')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5367 נָקַשׁ ; used in the sense of H5362 נָקַף\nStrong's: to knock\nKJV: smote.\n\nCognate Group: H5368 (smote)",
    5369: "נֵר (Nêr | nare)\n\nDerivation: the same as H5216 נִיר ; lamp\nStrong's: Ner, an Israelite\nKJV: Ner.\n\nCognate Group: H5369 (Ner), H5374 (Neriah), H4501 (candlestick), H5216 (candle)",
    5370: "נֵרְגַּל (Nêrᵉgal | nare-gal')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Nergal, a Cuthite deity\nKJV: Nergal.\n\nCognate Group: H5371 (Nergal-sharezer), H5367 (catch snare), H5373 (spikenard), H5370 (Nergal)",
    5371: "נֵרְגַּל שַׁרְאֶצֶר (Nêrᵉgal Sharʼetser | nare-gal' shar-eh'-tser)\n\nDerivation: from H5370 נֵרְגַּל and H8272 שַׁרְאֶצֶר\nStrong's: Nergal-Sharetser, the name of two Babylonians\nKJV: Nergal-sharezer.\n\nCognate Group: H5371 (Nergal-sharezer), H5367 (catch snare), H5373 (spikenard), H5370 (Nergal)",
    5372: "נִרְגָּן (nirgân | neer-gawn')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to roll to pieces\nStrong's: a slanderer\nKJV: talebearer, whisperer.\n\nCognate Group: H7279 (murmur), H5372 (talebearer)",
    5373: "נֵרְדְּ (nêrd | nayrd)\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: nard, an aromatic\nKJV: spikenard.\n\nCognate Group: H5371 (Nergal-sharezer), H5367 (catch snare), H5373 (spikenard), H5370 (Nergal)\nGreek Equivalents: G3487 νάρδος",
    5374: "נֵרִיָּה (Nêrîyâh | nay-ree-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or נֵרִיָּהוּ; from H5216 נִיר and H3050 יָהּ ; light of Jah\nStrong's: Nerijah, an Israelite\nKJV: Neriah.\n\nCognate Group: H5369 (Ner), H5374 (Neriah), H4501 (candlestick), H5216 (candle)\nGreek Equivalents: G3518 Νηρί",
    5375: "נָשָׂא (nâsâʼ | naw-saw')\n\nDerivation: or נָסָה; (Psalm 4:6 (H7 אֲבַד)), a primitive root\nStrong's: to lift, in a great variety of applications, literal and figurative, absolute and relative\nKJV: accept, advance, arise, (able to, (armor), suffer to) bear(-er, up), bring (forth), burn, carry (away), cast, contain, desire, ease, exact, exalt (self), extol, fetch, forgive, furnish, further, give, go on, help, high, hold up, honorable ([phrase] man), lade, lay, lift (self) up, lofty, marry, magnify, [idiom] needs, obtain, pardon, raise (up), receive, regard, respect, set (up), spare, stir up, [phrase] swear, take (away, up), [idiom] utterly, wear, yield.\n\nCognate Group: H5375 (accept), H5387 (captain), H4858 (burden), H4864 (burden), H7863 (excellency), H4853 (burden), H7613 (be accepted), H5379 (gift), H7865 (Sion), H4856 (respect), H5385 (carriage), H4984 (exalted), H7721 (arise)\nGreek Equivalents: G140 αἱρετίζω, G142 αἴρω, G142 αἴρω, G142 αἴρω, G153 αἰσχύνομαι, G308 ἀναβλέπω, G310 ἀναβοάω, G337 ἀναιρέω, G352 ἀνακύπτω, G353 ἀναλαμβάνω, G399 ἀναφέρω, G447 ἀνίημι, G450 ἀνίστημι, G482 ἀντιλαμβάνομαι, G498 ἀντιτάσσομαι, G501 ἀντλέω, G515 ἀξιόω, G522 ἀπαίρω, G565 ἀπέρχομαι, G667 ἀποφέρω, G837 αὐξάνω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G863 ἀφίημι, G906 βάλλω, G941 βαστάζω, G994 βοάω, G1013 βούλημα, G1073 γέμω, G1107 γνωρίζω, G1135 γυνή, G1209 δέχομαι, G1325 δίδωμι, G1380 δοκέω, G1390 δόμα, G1392 δοξάζω, G1581 ἐκκόπτω, G1596 ἑκουσίως, G1614 ἐκτείνω, G1627 ἐκφέρω, G1679 ἐλπίζω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1831 ἐξέρχομαι, G1863 ἐπάγω, G1869 ἐπαίρω, G1869 ἐπαίρω, G1870 ἐπαισχύνομαι, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2068 ἐσθίω, G2147 εὑρίσκω, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G2172 εὔχομαι, G2192 ἔχω, G2210 ζημιόω, G2296 θαυμάζω, G2436 ἵλεως, G2616 καταδυναστεύω, G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G2719 κατεσθίω, G2795 κινέω, G2865 κομίζω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3024 λήθη, G3089 λύω, G3332 μεταίρω, G3349 μετεωρίζω, G3403 μιμνήσκω, G3811 παιδεύω, G3858 παραδέχομαι, G4060 περιτίθημι, G4137 πληρόω, G4313 προπορεύομαι, G43