    5376: "נְשָׂא (nᵉsâʼ | nes-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5375 נָשָׂא \nStrong's: to lift\nKJV: carry away, make insurrection, take.\n\nCognate Group: H5403 (eagle), H5376 (carry away), H5396 (breath), H5407 (letter), H5412 (Nethinims)\nGreek Equivalents: G4494 ῥιπίζω",
    5377: "נָשָׁא (nâshâʼ | naw-shaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to lead astray, i.e. (mentally) to delude, or (morally) to seduce\nKJV: beguile, deceive, [idiom] greatly, [idiom] utterly.\n\nCognate Group: H5377 (beguile), H4860 (deceit), H4876 (desolation)\nGreek Equivalents: G374 ἀναπείθω, G436 ἀνθίστημι, G523 ἀπαιτέω, G538 ἀπατάω, G1869 ἐπαίρω, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G3784 ὀφείλω, G3982 πείθω",
    5378: "נָשָׁא (nâshâʼ | naw-shaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (perhaps identical with H5377 נָשָׁא, through the idea of imposition)\nStrong's: to lend on interest; by implication, to dun fordebt\nKJV: [idiom] debt, exact, giver of usury.\n\nCognate Group: H5378 ([idiom] debt), H4855 (exaction), H4859 ([idiom] any)",
    5379: "נִשֵּׂאת (nissêʼth | nis-sayth')\n\nDerivation: passive participle feminine of H5375 נָשָׂא\nStrong's: something taken, i.e. a present\nKJV: gift.\n\nCognate Group: H5375 (accept), H5387 (captain), H4858 (burden), H4864 (burden), H7863 (excellency), H4853 (burden), H7613 (be accepted), H5379 (gift), H7865 (Sion), H4856 (respect), H5385 (carriage), H4984 (exalted), H7721 (arise)",
    5380: "נָשַׁב (nâshab | naw-shab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to blow; by implication, to disperse\nKJV: (cause to) blow, drive away.\n\nCognate Group: H5380 (blow)\nGreek Equivalents: G4154 πνέω",
    5381: "נָשַׂג (nâsag | naw-sag')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to reach (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: ability, be able, attain (unto), (be able to, can) get, lay at, put, reach, remove, wax rich, [idiom] surely, (over-) take (hold of, on, upon).\n\nCognate Group: H5381 (ability)\nGreek Equivalents: G864 ἀφικνέομαι, G1842 ἐξολοθρεύω, G1994 ἐπιστρέφω, G2141 εὐπορέω, G2147 εὑρίσκω, G2480 ἰσχύω, G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G4876 συναντάω",
    5382: "נָשָׁה (nâshâh | naw-shaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to forget; figuratively, to neglect; causatively, to remit, remove\nKJV: forget, deprive, exact.\n\nCognate Group: H5384 (which shrank), H3449 (Ishiah), H5388 (forgetfulness), H5382 (forget)\nGreek Equivalents: G1156 δάνειον, G1157 δανειστής, G1627 ἐκφέρω, G1950 ἐπιλανθάνομαι, G3783 ὀφείλημα, G3784 ὀφείλω, G5623 ὠφελέω",
    5383: "נָשָׁה (nâshâh | naw-shaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (rather identical with H5382 נָשָׁה, in the sense of H5378 נָשָׁא)\nStrong's: to lend or (by reciprocity) borrow on security or interest\nKJV: creditor, exact, extortioner, lend, usurer, lend on (taker on) usury.\n\nCognate Group: H5383 (creditor), H5386 (debt), H4874 (creditor)",
    5384: "נָשֶׁה (nâsheh | naw-sheh')\n\nDerivation: from H5382 נָשָׁה, in the sense of failure\nStrong's: rheumatic or crippled (from the incident to Jacob)\nKJV: which shrank.\n\nCognate Group: H5384 (which shrank), H3449 (Ishiah), H5388 (forgetfulness), H5382 (forget)",
    5385: "נְשׂוּאָה (nᵉsûwʼâh | nes-oo-aw')\n\nDerivation: or rather, נְשֻׂאָה; feminine. passive participle of H5375 נָשָׂא\nStrong's: something borne, i.e. a load\nKJV: carriage.\n\nCognate Group: H5375 (accept), H5387 (captain), H4858 (burden), H4864 (burden), H7863 (excellency), H4853 (burden), H7613 (be accepted), H5379 (gift), H7865 (Sion), H4856 (respect), H5385 (carriage), H4984 (exalted), H7721 (arise)",
    5386: "נְשִׁי (nᵉshîy | nesh-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H5383 נָשָׁה\nStrong's: a debt\nKJV: debt.\n\nCognate Group: H5383 (creditor), H5386 (debt), H4874 (creditor)\nGreek Equivalents: G5110 τόκος",
    5387: "נָשִׂיא (nâsîyʼ | naw-see')\n\nDerivation: or נָשִׂא; from H5375 נָשָׂא\nStrong's: properly, an exalted one, i.e. a king or sheik; also a rising mist\nKJV: captain, chief, cloud, governor, prince, ruler, vapour.\n\nCognate Group: H5375 (accept), H5387 (captain), H4858 (burden), H4864 (burden), H7863 (excellency), H4853 (burden), H7613 (be accepted), H5379 (gift), H7865 (Sion), H4856 (respect), H5385 (carriage), H4984 (exalted), H7721 (arise)\nGreek Equivalents: G435 ἀνήρ, G747 ἀρχηγός, G758 ἄρχων, G935 βασιλεύς, G1484 ἔθνος, G2233 ἡγέομαι, G3507 νεφέλη, G3509 νέφος",
    5388: "נְשִׁיָּה (nᵉshîyâh | nesh-ee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5382 נָשָׁה\nStrong's: oblivion\nKJV: forgetfulness.\n\nCognate Group: H5384 (which shrank), H3449 (Ishiah), H5388 (forgetfulness), H5382 (forget)",
    5389: "נָשִׁין (nâshîyn | naw-sheen')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) irregular plural feminine of H606 אֱנָשׁ \nStrong's: a man\nKJV: women.\n\nCognate Group: H5389 (women)",
    5390: "נְשִׁיקָה (nᵉshîyqâh | nesh-ee-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5401 נָשַׁק\nStrong's: a kiss\nKJV: kiss.\n\nCognate Group: H5401 (armed), H5390 (kiss)\nGreek Equivalents: G5370 φίλημα",
    5391: "נָשַׁךְ (nâshak | naw-shak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to strike with a sting (as a serpent); figuratively, to oppress with interest on a loan\nKJV: bite, lend upon usury.\n\nCognate Group: H5391 (bite), H5392 (usury), H5393 (chamber)\nGreek Equivalents: G1143 δάκνω, G4141 πλήσσω",
    5392: "נֶשֶׁךְ (neshek | neh'-shek)\n\nDerivation: from H5391 נָשַׁךְ\nStrong's: interest on a debt\nKJV: usury.\n\nCognate Group: H5391 (bite), H5392 (usury), H5393 (chamber)\nGreek Equivalents: G5110 τόκος",
    5393: "נִשְׁכָּה (nishkâh | nish-kaw')\n\nDerivation: for H3957 לִשְׁכָּה\nStrong's: a cell\nKJV: chamber.\n\nCognate Group: H5391 (bite), H5392 (usury), H5393 (chamber)",
    5394: "נָשַׁל (nâshal | naw-shal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to pluck off, i.e. divest, eject or drop\nKJV: cast (out), drive, loose, put off (out), slip.\n\nCognate Group: H5394 (cast)\nGreek Equivalents: G1544 ἐκβάλλω, G1601 ἐκπίπτω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G2654 καταναλίσκω, G3089 λύω",
    5395: "נָשַׁם (nâsham | naw-sham')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to blow away, i.e. destroy\nKJV: destroy.\n\nCognate Group: H8580 (mole), H5395 (destroy), H5397 (blast)",
    5396: "נִשְׁמָא (nishmâʼ | nish-maw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5397 נְשָׁמָה\nStrong's: vital breath\nKJV: breath.\n\nCognate Group: H5403 (eagle), H5376 (carry away), H5396 (breath), H5407 (letter), H5412 (Nethinims)",
    5397: "נְשָׁמָה (nᵉshâmâh | nesh-aw-maw')\n\nDerivation: from H5395 נָשַׁם\nStrong's: a puff, i.e. wind, angry or vital breath, divine inspiration, intellect. or (concretely) an animal\nKJV: blast, (that) breath(-eth), inspiration, soul, spirit.\n\nCognate Group: H8580 (mole), H5395 (destroy), H5397 (blast)\nGreek Equivalents: G2372 θυμός, G4151 πνεῦμα, G4157 πνοή",
    5398: "נָשַׁף (nâshaph | naw-shaf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to breeze, i.e. blow up fresh (as the wind)\nKJV: blow.\n\nCognate Group: H5398 (blow), H3244 (owl), H5399 (dark)\nGreek Equivalents: G649 ἀποστέλλω, G4154 πνέω",
    5399: "נֶשֶׁף (nesheph | neh'-shef)\n\nDerivation: from H5398 נָשַׁף\nStrong's: properly, a breeze, i.e. (by implication) dusk (when the evening breeze prevails)\nKJV: dark, dawning of the day (morning), night, twilight.\n\nCognate Group: H5398 (blow), H3244 (owl), H5399 (dark)\nGreek Equivalents: G3317 μεσονύκτιον, G3571 νύξ, G3796 ὀψέ, G4404 πρωΐ, G4652 σκοτεινός, G4655 σκότος",
    5400: "נָשַׂק (nâsaq | naw-sak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to catch fire\nKJV: burn, kindle.\n\nCognate Group: H5400 (burn)\nGreek Equivalents: G381 ἀνάπτω, G2545 καίω",
    5401: "נָשַׁק (nâshaq | naw-shak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (identical with H5400 נָשַׂק, through the idea of fastening up; compare H2388 חָזַק, H2836 חָשַׁק)\nStrong's: to kiss, literally or figuratively (touch); also (as a mode of attachment), to equip with weapons\nKJV: armed (men), rule, kiss, that touched.\n\nCognate Group: H5401 (armed), H5390 (kiss)\nGreek Equivalents: G1405 δράσσομαι, G2705 καταφιλέω, G4352 προσκυνέω, G5219 ὑπακούω, G5368 φιλέω",
    5402: "נֶשֶׁק (nesheq | neh'-shek)\n\nDerivation: or נֵשֶׁק; from H5401 נָשַׁק\nStrong's: military equipment, i.e. (collectively) arms (offensive or defensive), or (concretely) an arsenal\nKJV: armed men, armour(-y), battle, harness, weapon.\n\nCognate Group: H5401 (armed), H5402 (armed men)\nGreek Equivalents: G956 βέλος, G3696 ὅπλον, G4171 πόλεμος",
    5403: "נְשַׁר (nᵉshar | nesh-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5404 נֶשֶׁר\nStrong's: an eagle\nKJV: eagle.\n\nCognate Group: H5403 (eagle), H5376 (carry away), H5396 (breath), H5407 (letter), H5412 (Nethinims)\nGreek Equivalents: G105 ἀετός",
    5404: "נֶשֶׁר (nesher | neh'-sher)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to lacerate\nStrong's: the eagle (or other large bird of prey)\nKJV: eagle.\n\nCognate Group: H5404 (eagle)\nGreek Equivalents: G105 ἀετός",
    5405: "נָשַׁת (nâshath | naw-shath')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to eliminate, i.e. (intransitively) to dry up\nKJV: fail.\n\nCognate Group: H5406 (letter), H5405 (fail)\nGreek Equivalents: G2352 θραύω, G3583 ξηραίνω, G4095 πίνω",
    5406: "נִשְׁתְּוָן (nishtᵉvân | nish-tev-awn')\n\nDerivation: probably of Persian origin\nStrong's: an epistle\nKJV: letter.\n\nCognate Group: H5406 (letter), H5405 (fail)\nGreek Equivalents: G1297 διάταγμα",
    5407: "נִשְׁתְּוָן (nishtᵉvân | nish-tev-awn')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5406 נִשְׁתְּוָן \nStrong's: an epistle\nKJV: letter.\n\nCognate Group: H5403 (eagle), H5376 (carry away), H5396 (breath), H5407 (letter), H5412 (Nethinims)",
    5408: "נָתַח (nâthach | naw-thakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to dismember\nKJV: cut (in pieces), divide, hew in pieces.\n\nCognate Group: H5409 (part), H5408 (cut)\nGreek Equivalents: G1244 διαιρέω, G1371 διχοτομέω",
    5409: "נֵתַח (nêthach | nay'-thakh)\n\nDerivation: from H5408 נָתַח\nStrong's: a fragment\nKJV: part, piece.\n\nCognate Group: H5409 (part), H5408 (cut)\nGreek Equivalents: G3196 μέλος, G3310 μερίς",
    5410: "נָתִיב (nâthîyb | naw-theeb')\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) נְתִיבָה; or נְתִבָה; (Jeremiah 6:16), from an unused root meaning to tramp\nStrong's: a (beaten) track\nKJV: path(-way), [idiom] travel(-ler), way.\n\nCognate Group: H5410 (path)\nGreek Equivalents: G3598 ὁδός, G5147 τρίβος",
    5411: "נָתִין (Nâthîyn | naw-theen')\n\nDerivation: or נָתוּן (Ezra 8:17), (the proper form as passive participle), from H5414 נָתַן ; one given, i.e. (in the plural only)\n\nStrong's: the Nethinim, or Temple-servants (as given to that duty)\nKJV: Nethinims.\n\nCognate Group: H4982 (Mattenai), H5417 (Nethaneel), H5416 (Nathan), H4977 (Mattan), H4979 (gift), H5418 (Nethaniah), H4991 (gift), H4976 (gift), H4983 (Mattaniah), H5414 (add), H5419 (Nathanmelech), H4992 (Mattathah), H4980 (Mattanah), H4993 (Mattithiah), H5411 (Nethinims)\nGreek Equivalents: G1325 δίδωμι",
    5412: "נְתִין (Nᵉthîyn | netheen')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5411 נָתִין \nStrong's: the Nethinim, or Temple-servants (as given to that duty)\nKJV: Nethinims.\n\nCognate Group: H5403 (eagle), H5376 (carry away), H5396 (breath), H5407 (letter), H5412 (Nethinims)",
    5413: "נָתַךְ (nâthak | naw-thak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to flow forth (literally or figuratively); by implication, to liquify\nKJV: drop, gather (together), melt, pour (forth, out).\n\nCognate Group: H5413 (drop), H2046 (is melted)\nGreek Equivalents: G1145 δακρύω, G1572 ἐκκαίω, G1632 ἐκχέω, G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G5080 τήκω",
    5414: "נָתַן (nâthan | naw-than')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to give, used with greatest latitude of application (put, make, etc.)\nKJV: add, apply, appoint, ascribe, assign, [idiom] avenge, [idiom] be (healed), bestow, bring (forth, hither), cast, cause, charge, come, commit, consider, count, [phrase] cry, deliver (up), direct, distribute, do, [idiom] doubtless, [idiom] without fail, fasten, frame, [idiom] get, give (forth, over, up), grant, hang (up), [idiom] have, [idiom] indeed, lay (unto charge, up), (give) leave, lend, let (out), [phrase] lie, lift up, make, [phrase] O that, occupy, offer, ordain, pay, perform, place, pour, print, [idiom] pull, put (forth), recompense, render, requite, restore, send (out), set (forth), shew, shoot forth (up), [phrase] sing, [phrase] slander, strike, (sub-) mit, suffer, [idiom] surely, [idiom] take, thrust, trade, turn, utter, [phrase] weep, [phrase] willingly, [phrase] withdraw, [phrase] would (to) God, yield.\n\nCognate Group: H4982 (Mattenai), H5417 (Nethaneel), H5416 (Nathan), H4977 (Mattan), H4979 (gift), H5418 (Nethaniah), H4991 (gift), H4976 (gift), H4983 (Mattaniah), H5414 (add), H5419 (Nathanmelech), H4992 (Mattathah), H4980 (Mattanah), H4993 (Mattithiah), H5411 (Nethinims)\nGreek Equivalents: G71 ἄγω, G154 αἰτέω, G306 ἀναβάλλομαι, G450 ἀνίστημι, G591 ἀποδίδωμι, G649 ἀποστέλλω, G661 ἀποτίνω, G863 ἀφίημι, G1096 γίνομαι, G1166 δεικνύω, G1184 δεκτός, G1239 διαδίδωμι, G1303 διατίθεμαι, G1325 δίδωμι, G1390 δόμα, G1433 δωρέομαι, G1439 ἐάω, G1544 ἐκβάλλω, G1554 ἐκδίδωμι, G1620 ἐκτίθημι, G1632 ἐκχέω, G1653 ἐλεέω, G1685 ἐμβάλλω, G1744 ἐνδύνω, G1746 ἐνδύω, G1869 ἐπαίρω, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G1929 ἐπιδίδωμι, G1945 ἐπίκειμαι, G2004 ἐπιτάσσω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2022 ἐπιχέω, G2106 εὐδοκέω, G2186 ἐφίστημι, G2192 ἔχω, G2476 ἵστημι, G2524 καθίημι, G2525 καθίστημι, G2619 κατακαλύπτω, G2624 κατακληροδοτέω, G2698 κατατίθημι, G2784 κηρύσσω, G2910 κρεμάννυμι, G3481 Ναθάν, G3611 οἰκέω, G3627 οἰκτείρω, G3860 παραδίδωμι, G3862 πα