    5415: "נְתַן (nᵉthan | neth-an')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5414 נָתַן\nStrong's: give\nKJV: bestow, give pay.\n\nCognate Group: H4978 (gift), H5426 (shake off), H5415 (bestow)",
    5416: "נָתָן (Nâthân | naw-thawn')\n\nDerivation: from H5414 נָתַן ; given\nStrong's: Nathan, the name of five Israelites\nKJV: Nathan.\n\nCognate Group: H4982 (Mattenai), H5417 (Nethaneel), H5416 (Nathan), H4977 (Mattan), H4979 (gift), H5418 (Nethaniah), H4991 (gift), H4976 (gift), H4983 (Mattaniah), H5414 (add), H5419 (Nathanmelech), H4992 (Mattathah), H4980 (Mattanah), H4993 (Mattithiah), H5411 (Nethinims)\nGreek Equivalents: G3481 Ναθάν",
    5417: "נְתַנְאֵל (Nᵉthanʼêl | neth-an-ale')\n\nTypo: xlit Nᵉthanêʼl corrected to Nᵉthanʼêl\n\nGreek Equivalents: G3482 Ναθαναήλ \n\nDerivation: from H5414 נָתַן and H410 אֵל ; given of God\nStrong's: Nethanel, the name of ten Israelites\nKJV: Nethaneel.\n\nCognate Group: H4982 (Mattenai), H5417 (Nethaneel), H5416 (Nathan), H4977 (Mattan), H4979 (gift), H5418 (Nethaniah), H4991 (gift), H4976 (gift), H4983 (Mattaniah), H5414 (add), H5419 (Nathanmelech), H4992 (Mattathah), H4980 (Mattanah), H4993 (Mattithiah), H5411 (Nethinims)",
    5418: "נְתַנְיָה (Nᵉthanyâh | neth-an-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or נְתַנְיָהוּ; from H5414 נָתַן and H3050 יָהּ ; given of Jah\nStrong's: Nethanjah, the name of four Israelites\nKJV: Nethaniah.\n\nCognate Group: H4982 (Mattenai), H5417 (Nethaneel), H5416 (Nathan), H4977 (Mattan), H4979 (gift), H5418 (Nethaniah), H4991 (gift), H4976 (gift), H4983 (Mattaniah), H5414 (add), H5419 (Nathanmelech), H4992 (Mattathah), H4980 (Mattanah), H4993 (Mattithiah), H5411 (Nethinims)",
    5419: "נְתַן־מֶלֶךְ (Nᵉthan-Melek | neth-an' meh'-lek)\n\nDerivation: from H5414 נָתַן and H4428 מֶלֶךְ ; given of (the) king\nStrong's: Nethan-Melek, an Israelite\nKJV: Nathanmelech.\n\nCognate Group: H4982 (Mattenai), H5417 (Nethaneel), H5416 (Nathan), H4977 (Mattan), H4979 (gift), H5418 (Nethaniah), H4991 (gift), H4976 (gift), H4983 (Mattaniah), H5414 (add), H5419 (Nathanmelech), H4992 (Mattathah), H4980 (Mattanah), H4993 (Mattithiah), H5411 (Nethinims)",
    5420: "נָתָס (nâthâç | naw-thas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tear up\nKJV: mar.\n\nCognate Group: H5420 (mar)",
    5421: "נָתַע (nâthaʻ | naw-thah')\n\nDerivation: for H5422 נָתַץ\nStrong's: to tear out\nKJV: break.\n\nCognate Group: H5421 (break)",
    5422: "נָתַץ (nâthats | naw-thats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tear down\nKJV: beat down, break down (out), cast down, destroy, overthrow, pull down, throw down.\n\nCognate Group: H5422 (beat down)\nGreek Equivalents: G853 ἀφανίζω, G1288 διασπάω, G2507 καθαιρέω, G2598 καταβάλλω, G2647 καταλύω, G2679 κατασκάπτω, G2690 καταστρέφω, G4917 συνθλάω",
    5423: "נָתַק (nâthaq | naw-thak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tear off\nKJV: break (off), burst, draw (away), lift up, pluck (away, off), pull (out), root out.\n\nCognate Group: H5423 (break), H5424 (scall)\nGreek Equivalents: G645 ἀποσπάω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G1288 διασπάω, G1828 ἐξέλκω, G3855 παράγω, G4486 ῥήγνυμι, G4685 σπάω",
    5424: "נֶתֶק (netheq | neh'-thek)\n\nDerivation: from H5423 נָתַק\nStrong's: scurf\nKJV: (dry) scall.\n\nCognate Group: H5423 (break), H5424 (scall)\nGreek Equivalents: G5134 τραῦμα",
    5425: "נָתַר (nâthar | naw-thar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to jump, i.e. be violently agitated; causatively, to terrify, shake off, untie\nKJV: drive asunder, leap, (let) loose, [idiom] make, move, undo.\n\nCognate Group: H5425 (drive asunder)\nGreek Equivalents: G1262 διαλύω, G1265 διαμένω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G3089 λύω, G5442 φυλάσσω",
    5426: "נְתַר (nᵉthar | neth-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5425 נָתַר \nStrong's: to jump, i.e. be violently agitated; causatively, to terrify, shake off, untie\nKJV: shake off.\n\nCognate Group: H4978 (gift), H5426 (shake off), H5415 (bestow)\nGreek Equivalents: G1301 διατηρέω, G1621 ἐκτινάσσω, G4741 στηρίζω, G4933 συντηρέω",
    5427: "נֶתֶר (nether | neh'-ther)\n\nDerivation: from H5425 נָתַר\nStrong's: mineral potash (so called from effervescing with acid)\nKJV: nitre.\n\nCognate Group: H5427 (nitre), H5425 (drive asunder)",
    5428: "נָתַשׁ (nâthash | naw-thash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tear away\nKJV: destroy, forsake, pluck (out, up, by the roots), pull up, root out (up), [idiom] utterly. s\n\nCognate Group: H5428 (destroy)\nGreek Equivalents: G447 ἀνίημι, G515 ἀξιόω, G645 ἀποσπάω, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G660 ἀποτινάσσω, G683 ἀπωθέομαι, G863 ἀφίημι, G1459 ἐγκαταλείπω, G1474 ἐδαφίζω, G1544 ἐκβάλλω, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1581 ἐκκόπτω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1610 ἐκριζόω, G1614 ἐκτείνω, G1615 ἐκτελέω, G1632 ἐκχέω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G2507 καθαιρέω, G2598 καταβάλλω, G2622 κατακλάω, G2827 κλίνω",
    5429: "סְאָה (çᵉʼâh | seh-aw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to define\nStrong's: a seah, or certain measure (as determinative) forgrain\nKJV: measure.\n\nCognate Group: H5431 (warrior), H5429 (measure), H5430 (battle)\nGreek Equivalents: G3355 μετρητής, G3358 μέτρον, G4568 σάτον",
    5430: "סְאֹון (çᵉʼôwn | seh-own')\n\nDerivation: from H5431 סָאַן\nStrong's: perhaps a military boot (as aprotection from mud\nKJV: battle.\n\nCognate Group: H5431 (warrior), H5429 (measure), H5430 (battle)",
    5431: "סָאַן (çâʼan | saw-an')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; to be miry; used only as denominative from H5430 סְאֹון\nStrong's: to shoe, i.e. (active participle) a soldier shod\nKJV: warrior.\n\nCognate Group: H5431 (warrior), H5429 (measure), H5430 (battle)",
    5432: "סַאסְּאָה (çaʼçᵉʼâh | sah-seh-aw')Typo: lemma סַאסְאָה missing dagesh, corrected to סַאסְּאָה\n\nDerivation: for H5429 סְאָה\nStrong's: measurement, i.e. moderation\nKJV: measure.\n\nCognate Group: H5432 (measure)",
    5433: "סָבָא (çâbâʼ | saw-baw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to quaff to satiety, i.e. become tipsy\nKJV: drunkard, fill self, Sabean, (wine-) bibber.\n\nCognate Group: H5436 (Sabean), H5435 (drink), H5433 (drunkard), H5434 (Seba)",
