    5437: "סָבַב (çâbab | saw-bab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to revolve, surround, or border; used in various applications, literally and figuratively\nKJV: bring, cast, fetch, lead, make, walk, [idiom] whirl, [idiom] round about, be about on every side, apply, avoid, beset (about), besiege, bring again, carry (about), change, cause to come about, [idiom] circuit, (fetch a) compass (about, round), drive, environ, [idiom] on every side, beset (close, come, compass, go, stand) round about, inclose, remove, return, set, sit down, turn (self) (about, aside, away, back).\n\nCognate Group: H5439 (about), H5437 (bring), H4142 (being changed), H5252 (cause), H4524 (that compass about), H4036 (Magormissabib), H5438 (cause), H4141 (winding about)\nGreek Equivalents: G158 αἴτιον, G159 αἴτιος, G402 ἀναχωρέω, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G1330 διέρχομαι, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1607 ἐκπορεύομαι, G1994 ἐπιστρέφω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2625 κατακλίνω, G2944 κυκλόω, G2944 κυκλόω, G3344 μεταστρέφω, G3928 παρέρχομαι, G4013 περιάγω, G4014 περιαιρέω, G4022 περιέρχομαι, G4026 περιΐστημι, G4033 περικυκλόω, G4160 ποιέω, G4317 προσάγω, G4762 στρέφω, G5087 τίθημι",
    5438: "סִבָּה (çibbâh | sib-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H5437 סָבַב\nStrong's: a (providential) turn (of affairs)\nKJV: cause.\n\nCognate Group: H5439 (about), H5437 (bring), H4142 (being changed), H5252 (cause), H4524 (that compass about), H4036 (Magormissabib), H5438 (cause), H4141 (winding about)",
    5439: "סָבִיב (çâbîyb | saw-beeb')\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) סְבִיבָה; from H5437 סָבַב\nStrong's: (as noun) a circle, neighbour, or environs; but chiefly (as adverb, with or without preposition) around\nKJV: (place, round) about, circuit, compass, on every side.\n\nCognate Group: H5439 (about), H5437 (bring), H4142 (being changed), H5252 (cause), H4524 (that compass about), H4036 (Magormissabib), H5438 (cause), H4141 (winding about)\nGreek Equivalents: G2943 κυκλόθεν, G2943 κυκλόθεν, G2945 κύκλῳ, G4040 περίοικος",
    5440: "סָבַךְ (çâbak | saw-bak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to entwine\nKJV: fold together, wrap.\n\nCognate Group: H5440 (fold together), H5442 (thick), H5444 (Sibbecai), H5441 (thicket)\nGreek Equivalents: G2837 κοιμάω",
