    5442: "סְבָךְ (çᵉbâk | seb-awk')\n\nDerivation: from H5440 סָבַךְ,\nStrong's: a copse\nKJV: thick(-et).\n\nCognate Group: H5440 (fold together), H5442 (thick), H5444 (Sibbecai), H5441 (thicket)\nGreek Equivalents: G1350 δίκτυον",
    5443: "סַבְּכָא (çabbᵉkâʼ | sab-bek-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or שַׂבְּכָא; (Aramaic), from a root corresponding to H5440 סָבַךְ\nStrong's: a lyre\nKJV: sackbut.\n\nCognate Group: H5443 (sackbut)",
    5444: "סִבְּכַי (Çibbᵉkay | sib-bek-ah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H5440 סָבַךְ ; copse-like\nStrong's: Sibbecai, an Israelite\nKJV: Sibbecai, Sibbechai.\n\nCognate Group: H5440 (fold together), H5442 (thick), H5444 (Sibbecai), H5441 (thicket)",
    5445: "סָבַל (çâbal | saw-bal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to carry (literally or figuratively), or (reflexively) be burdensome; specifically, to be gravid\nKJV: bear, be a burden, carry, strong to labour.\n\nCognate Group: H5451 (Sibboleth), H5445 (bear), H5454 (Sabta), H5448 (burden), H5453 (Sibraim), H5447 (burden), H5455 (Sabtecha), H5449 (burden), H5450 (burden)\nGreek Equivalents: G353 ἀναλαμβάνω, G399 ἀναφέρω, G430 ἀνέχομαι, G1679 ἐλπίζω, G3975 παχύνω, G4327 προσδέχομαι, G4328 προσδοκάω, G5254 ὑπέχω",
