    5463: "סְגַר (çᵉgar | seg-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5462 סָגַר \nStrong's: to shut up; figuratively, to surrender\nKJV: shut up.\n\nCognate Group: H5452 (think), H5481 (dulcimer), H5457 (worship), H5463 (shut up), H5460 (governor)",
    5464: "סַגְרִיד (çagrîyd | sag-reed')\n\nDerivation: probably from H5462 סָגַר in the sense of sweeping away\nStrong's: a pouring rain\nKJV: very rainy.\n\nCognate Group: H5467 (Sodom), H5464 (very rainy), H5465 (stocks), H5466 (fine linen)",
