    5481: "סוּמְפֹּונְיָה (çûwmᵉpôwnᵉyâh | soom-po-neh-yaw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or סוּמְפֹּנְיָה; (Aramaic), or סִיפֹנְיָא; (Daniel 3:10) (Aramaic), of Greek origin\nStrong's: a bagpipe (with a double pipe)\nKJV: dulcimer.\n\nCognate Group: H5452 (think), H5481 (dulcimer), H5457 (worship), H5463 (shut up), H5460 (governor)",
    5482: "סְוֵנֵה (Çᵉvênêh | sev-ay-nay')\n\nDerivation: (rather to be written סְוֵנָה; for סְוֵן; i.e to Seven); of Egyptian derivation\nStrong's: Seven, a place in Upper Egypt\nKJV: Syene.\n\nCognate Group: H5526 (cover), H5485 (Susi), H4534 (thorn hedge), H5483 (crane), H5484 (company of horses), H5482 (Syene)",
    5483: "סוּס (çûwç | soos)\n\nDerivation: or סֻס; from an unused root meaning to skip (properly, for joy)\nStrong's: a horse (as leaping); also a swallow (from its rapid flight)\nKJV: crane, horse (-back, -hoof). Compare H6571 פָּרָשׁ .\n\nCognate Group: H5526 (cover), H5485 (Susi), H4534 (thorn hedge), H5483 (crane), H5484 (company of horses), H5482 (Syene)\nGreek Equivalents: G1980 ἐπισκέπτομαι, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G2460 ἱππεύς, G2462 ἵππος",
    5484: "סוּסָה (çûwçâh | soo-saw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5483 סוּס\nStrong's: a mare\nKJV: company of horses.\n\nCognate Group: H5526 (cover), H5485 (Susi), H4534 (thorn hedge), H5483 (crane), H5484 (company of horses), H5482 (Syene)",
    5485: "סוּסִי (Çûwçîy | soo-see')\n\nDerivation: from H5483 סוּס ; horse-like\nStrong's: Susi, an Israelite\nKJV: Susi.\n\nCognate Group: H5526 (cover), H5485 (Susi), H4534 (thorn hedge), H5483 (crane), H5484 (company of horses), H5482 (Syene)",
    5486: "סוּף (çûwph | soof)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to snatch away, i.e. terminate\nKJV: consume, have an end, perish, [idiom] be utterly.\n\nCognate Group: H5489 (Red Sea), H5486 (consume), H5492 (Red Sea), H5488 (flag), H5490 (conclusion)\nGreek Equivalents: G355 ἀναλίσκω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G2063 ἐρυθρός, G2078 ἔσχατος, G2654 καταναλίσκω, G4931 συντελέω, G5055 τελέω",
    5487: "סוּף (çûwph | soof)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5486 סוּף\nStrong's: to come to an end\nKJV: consume, fulfill.\n\nCognate Group: H5487 (consume), H5491 (end)\nGreek Equivalents: G853 ἀφανίζω, G3039 λικμάω",
    5488: "סוּף (çûwph | soof)\n\nDerivation: probably of Egyptian origin\nStrong's: a reed, especially the papyrus\nKJV: flag, Red (sea), weed. Compare H5489 סוּף .\n\nCognate Group: H5489 (Red Sea), H5486 (consume), H5492 (Red Sea), H5488 (flag), H5490 (conclusion)",
    5489: "סוּף (Çûwph | soof)\n\nDerivation: for H5488 סוּף (by ellipsis of H3220 יָם)\nStrong's: the Reed (Sea)\nKJV: Red Sea.\n\nCognate Group: H5489 (Red Sea), H5486 (consume), H5492 (Red Sea), H5488 (flag), H5490 (conclusion)",
    5490: "סֹוף (çôwph | sofe)\n\nDerivation: from H5486 סוּף\nStrong's: a termination\nKJV: conclusion, end, hinder participle\n\nCognate Group: H5489 (Red Sea), H5486 (consume), H5492 (Red Sea), H5488 (flag), H5490 (conclusion)\nGreek Equivalents: G206 ἄκρον, G2692 καταστροφή, G4009 πέρας, G5056 τέλος",
    5491: "סֹוף (çôwph | sofe)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5490 סֹוף \nStrong's: a termination\nKJV: end.\n\nCognate Group: H5487 (consume), H5491 (end)",
    5492: "סוּפָה (çûwphâh | soo-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H5486 סוּף\nStrong's: a hurricane\nKJV: Red Sea, storm, tempest, whirlwind, Red sea.\n\nCognate Group: H5489 (Red Sea), H5486 (consume), H5492 (Red Sea), H5488 (flag), H5490 (conclusion)\nGreek Equivalents: G1105 γνόφος, G2692 καταστροφή, G2978 λαῖλαψ, G3601 ὀδύνη, G3709 ὀργή",
    5493: "סוּר (çûwr | soor)\n\nDerivation: or שׂוּר; (Hosea 9:12), a primitive root\nStrong's: to turn off (literal or figurative)\nKJV: be(-head), bring, call back, decline, depart, eschew, get (you), go (aside), [idiom] grievous, lay away (by), leave undone, be past, pluck away, put (away, down), rebel, remove (to and fro), revolt, [idiom] be sour, take (away, off), turn (aside, away, in), withdraw, be without.\n\nCognate Group: H3249 (they that depart), H5495 (Sur), H5493 (be), H5494 (degenerate), H5627 ([idiom] continual)\nGreek Equivalents: G114 ἀθετέω, G138 αἱρέομαι, G140 αἱρετίζω, G142 αἴρω, G344 ἀνακάμπτω, G525 ἀπαλλάσσω, G565 ἀπέρχομαι, G566 ἀπέχει, G567 ἀπέχομαι, G568 ἀπέχω, G601 ἀποκαλύπτω, G649 ἀποστέλλω, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G757 ἄρχω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G1259 διαλλάσσω, G1282 διαπρίω, G1291 διαστέλλομαι, G1316 διαχωρίζομαι, G1576 ἐκκλείω, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1593 ἐκνεύω, G1601 ἐκπίπτω, G1628 ἐκφεύγω, G1765 ἐνισχύω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1821 ἐξαποστέλλω, G1994 ἐπιστρέφω, G2090 ἑτοιμάζω, G2507 καθαιρέω, G2795 κινέω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3112 μακράν, G3179 μεθίστημι, G3329 μετάγω, G3332 μεταίρω, G3845 παραβαίνω, G3928 παρέρχομαι, G4014 περιαιρέω, G4059 περιτέμνω, G4105 πλανάω, G4317 προσάγω, G4531 σαλεύω",
    5494: "סוּר (çûwr | soor)\n\nDerivation: probably passive participle of H5493 סוּר\nStrong's: turned off, i.e. deteriorated\nKJV: degenerate.\n\nCognate Group: H3249 (they that depart), H5495 (Sur), H5493 (be), H5494 (degenerate), H5627 ([idiom] continual)",
    5495: "סוּר (Çûwr | soor)\n\nDerivation: the same as H5494 סוּר\nStrong's: Sur, a gate of the temple\nKJV: Sur.\n\nCognate Group: H3249 (they that depart), H5495 (Sur), H5493 (be), H5494 (degenerate), H5627 ([idiom] continual)",
    5496: "סוּת (çûwth | sooth)\n\nDerivation: perhaps denominative from H7898 שַׁיִת\nStrong's: properly, to prick, i.e. (figuratively) stimulate; by implication, to seduce\nKJV: entice, move, persuade, provoke, remove, set on, stir up, take away.\n\nCognate Group: H5496 (entice)\nGreek Equivalents: G538 ἀπατάω, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G1311 διαφθείρω, G3346 μετατίθημι, G3870 παρακαλέω, G4820 συμβάλλω",
    5497: "סוּת (çûwth | sooth)\n\nDerivation: probably from the same root as H4533 מַסְוֶה\nStrong's: covering, i.e. clothing\nKJV: clothes.\n\nCognate Group: H5497 (clothes), H4533 (vail)",
    5498: "סָחַב (çâchab | saw-khab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to trail along\nKJV: draw (out), tear.\n\nCognate Group: H5499 (cast clout), H5498 (draw)\nGreek Equivalents: G4951 σύρω",
    5499: "סְחָבָה (çᵉchâbâh | seh-khaw-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H5498 סָחַב\nStrong's: a rag\nKJV: cast clout.\n\nCognate Group: H5499 (cast clout), H5498 (draw)\nGreek Equivalents: G4470 ῥάκος",
    5500: "סָחָה (çâchâh | saw-khaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to sweep away\nKJV: scrape.\n\nCognate Group: H7823 (which springeth of the same), H5501 (offscouring), H5500 (scrape)\nGreek Equivalents: G3039 λικμάω",
    5501: "סְחִי (çᵉchîy | seh-khee')\n\nDerivation: from H5500 סָחָה\nStrong's: refuse (as swept off)\nKJV: offscouring.\n\nCognate Group: H7823 (which springeth of the same), H5501 (offscouring), H5500 (scrape)",
    5502: "סָחַף (çâchaph | saw-khaf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to scrape off\nKJV: sweep (away).\n\nCognate Group: H5502 (sweep)",
    5503: "סָחַר (çâchar | saw-khar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to travel round (specifically as a pedlar); intensively, to palpitate\nKJV: go about, merchant(-man), occupy with, pant, trade, traffick.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)\nGreek Equivalents: G1710 ἐμπορεύομαι, G1711 ἐμπορία, G1713 ἔμπορος, G2038 ἐργάζομαι, G4198 πορεύομαι, G5015 ταράσσω",
    5504: "סַחַר (çachar | sakh'-ar)\n\nDerivation: from H5503 סָחַר\nStrong's: profit (from trade)\nKJV: merchandise.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5505: "סָחַר (çâchar | saw-khar')\n\nDerivation: from H5503 סָחַר\nStrong's: an emporium; abstractly, profit (from trade)\nKJV: mart, merchandise.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5506: "סְחֹרָה (çᵉchôrâh | sekh-o-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H5503 סָחַר\nStrong's: traffic\nKJV: merchandise.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5507: "סֹחֵרָה (çôchêrâh | so-khay-raw')\n\nDerivation: properly, active participle feminine of H5503 סָחַר\nStrong's: something surrounding the person, i.e. a shield\nKJV: buckler.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)\nGreek Equivalents: G2944 κυκλόω",
    5508: "סֹחֵרֶת (çôchêreth | so-kheh'-reth)\n\nDerivation: similar to H5507 סֹחֵרָה\nStrong's: probably a (black) tile (or tessara) forlaying borders with\nKJV: black marble.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5509: "סִיג (çîyg | seeg)\n\nDerivation: or סוּג; (Ezekiel 22:18), from H5472 סוּג in the sense of refuse\nStrong's: scoria\nKJV: dross.\n\nCognate Group: H7873 (pursuing), H5472 (backslider), H5253 (departing away), H7734 (turn back), H5509 (dross)\nGreek Equivalents: G96 ἀδόκιμος",
    5510: "סִיוָן (Çîyvân | see-vawn')\n\nDerivation: probably of Persian origin\nStrong's: Sivan, the third Hebrew month\nKJV: Sivan.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5511: "סִיחֹון (Çîychôwn | see-khone')\n\nDerivation: or סִיחֹן; from the same as H5477 סוּחַ ; tempestuous\nStrong's: Sichon, an Amoritish king\nKJV: Sihon.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5512: "סִין (Çîyn | seen)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Sin the name of an Egyptian town and (probably) desert adjoining\nKJV: Sin.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5513: "סִינִי (Çîynîy | see-nee')\n\nDerivation: from an otherwise unknown name of a man\nStrong's: a Sinite, or descendant of one of the sons of Canaan\nKJV: Sinite.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5514: "סִינַי (Çîynay | see-nah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Sinai, mountain of Arabia\nKJV: Sinai.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)\nGreek Equivalents: G4614 Σινᾶ",
    5515: "סִינִים (Çîynîym | see-neem')\n\nDerivation: plural of an otherwise unknown name\nStrong's: Sinim, a distant Oriental region\nKJV: Sinim.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5516: "סִיסְרָא (Çîyçᵉrâʼ | see-ser-aw')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Sisera, the name of a Canaanitish king and of one of the Nethinim\nKJV: Sisera.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5517: "סִיעָא (Çîyʻâʼ | see-ah')\n\nDerivation: or סִיעֲהָא; from an unused root meaning to converse; congregation\nStrong's: Sia or Siaha, one of the Nethinim\nKJV: Sia, Siaha.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5518: "סִיר (çîyr | seer)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) סִירָה; or סִרָה; (Jeremiah 52:18), from a primitive root meaning to boil up\nStrong's: a pot; also a thorn (as springing up rapidly); by implication, a hook\nKJV: caldron, fishhook, pan, (wash-)pot, thorn.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)\nGreek Equivalents: G173 ἄκανθα, G174 ἀκάνθινος, G4647 σκόλοψ, G5473 χαλκίον",
    5519: "סָךְ (çâk | sawk)\n\nDerivation: from H5526 סָכַךְ\nStrong's: properly, a thicket of men, i.e. a crowd\nKJV: multitude.\n\nCognate Group: H5519 (multitude), H5521 (booth), H5526 (cover), H5523 (Succoth), H5520 (covert), H5527 (Secacah)\nGreek Equivalents: G5117 τόπος",
    5520: "סֹךְ (çôk | soke)\n\nDerivation: from H5526 סָכַךְ\nStrong's: a hut (as of entwined boughs); also a lair\nKJV: covert, den, pavilion, tabernacle.\n\nCognate Group: H5519 (multitude), H5521 (booth), H5526 (cover), H5523 (Succoth), H5520 (covert), H5527 (Secacah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2646 κατάλυμα, G2798 κλάδος, G4633 σκηνή, G4638 σκήνωμα, G5413 φορτίον",
    5521: "סֻכָּה (çukkâh | sook-kaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5520 סֹךְ\nStrong's: a hut or lair\nKJV: booth, cottage, covert, pavilion, tabernacle, tent.\n\nCognate Group: H5519 (multitude), H5521 (booth), H5526 (cover), H5523 (Succoth), H5520 (covert), H5527 (Secacah)\nGreek Equivalents: G4633 σκηνή, G4634 σκηνοπηγία, G4638 σκήνωμα, G5208 ὕλη",
    5522: "סִכּוּת (çikkûwth | sik-kooth')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5519 סָךְ\nStrong's: an (idolatrous) booth\nKJV: tabernacle.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5523: "סֻכֹּות (Çukkôwth | sook-kohth')\n\nDerivation: or סֻכֹּת; plural of H5521 סֻכָּה ; booths\nStrong's: Succoth, the name of a place in Egypt and of three in Palestine\nKJV: Succoth.\n\nCognate Group: H5519 (multitude), H5521 (booth), H5526 (cover), H5523 (Succoth), H5520 (covert), H5527 (Secacah)",
    5524: "סֻכֹּות בְּנֹות (Çukkôwth bᵉnôwth | sook-kohth' ben-ohth')\n\nDerivation: from H5523 סֻכֹּות and the (irregular) plural of H1323 בַּת\nStrong's: booths of (the) daughters; brothels, i.e. idoalatrous tents forimpure purpose\nKJV: Succothbenoth.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5525: "סֻכִּי (Çukkîy | sook-kee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from an unknown name (perhaps H5520 סֹךְ)\nStrong's: a Sukkite, or inhabitant of some place near Egypt (i.e. hut-dwellers)\nKJV: Sukkiims.\n\nCognate Group: H5513 (Sinite), H5506 (merchandise), H5511 (Sihon), H5515 (Sinim), H5510 (Sivan), H5514 (Sinai), H5525 (Sukkiims), H5518 (caldron), H5504 (merchandise), H5522 (tabernacle), H5516 (Sisera), H5524 (Succothbenoth), H5512 (Sin), H5507 (buckler), H5503 (go about), H4536 (traffic), H5508 (black marble), H5505 (mart), H5517 (Sia)",
    5526: "סָכַךְ (çâkak | saw-kak')\n\nDerivation: or שָׂכַךְ; (Exodus 33:22), a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to entwine as ascreen; by implication, to fence in, cover over, (figuratively) protect\nKJV: cover, defence, defend, hedge in, join together, set, shut up.\n\nCognate Group: H5526 (cover), H5485 (Susi), H4534 (thorn hedge), H5483 (crane), H5484 (company of horses), H5482 (Syene)\nGreek Equivalents: G1892 ἐπεγείρω, G1982 ἐπισκιάζω, G2521 κάθημαι, G2681 κατασκηνόω, G4028 περικαλύπτω, G5420 φράσσω",
    5527: "סְכָכָה (Çᵉkâkâh | sek-aw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5526 סָכַךְ ; inclosure\nStrong's: Secacah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Secacah.\n\nCognate Group: H5519 (multitude), H5521 (booth), H5526 (cover), H5523 (Succoth), H5520 (covert), H5527 (Secacah)",
    5528: "סָכַל (çâkal | saw-kal')\n\nDerivation: for H3688 כָּסַל\nStrong's: to be silly\nKJV: do (make, play the, turn into) fool(-ish, -ishly, -ishness).\n\nCognate Group: H5531 (folly), H5528 (do fool), H5529 (folly), H5530 (fool)",
    5529: "סֶכֶל (çekel | seh'-kal)\n\nDerivation: from H5528 סָכַל\nStrong's: silliness; concretely and collectively, dolts\nKJV: folly.\n\nCognate Group: H5531 (folly), H5528 (do fool), H5529 (folly), H5530 (fool)",
    5530: "סָכָל (çâkâl | saw-kawl')\n\nDerivation: from H5528 סָכַל\nStrong's: silly\nKJV: fool(-ish), sottish.\n\nCognate Group: H5531 (folly), H5528 (do fool), H5529 (folly), H5530 (fool)",
    5531: "סִכְלוּת (çiklûwth | sik-looth')\n\nDerivation: or שִׂכְלוּת; (Ecclesiastes 1:17), from H5528 סָכַל\nStrong's: silliness\nKJV: folly, foolishness.\n\nCognate Group: H5531 (folly), H5528 (do fool), H5529 (folly), H5530 (fool)\nGreek Equivalents: G2167 εὐφροσύνη",
    5532: "סָכַן (çâkan | saw-kan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be familiar with; by implication, to minister to, be serviceable to, be customary\nKJV: acquaint (self), be advantage, [idiom] ever, (be, (un-)) profit(-able), treasurer, be wont.\n\nCognate Group: H5532 (acquaint), H4543 (store)\nGreek Equivalents: G1321 διδάσκω, G1984 ἐπισκοπή, G2282 θάλπω, G4276 προελπίζω",
    5533: "סָכַן (çâkan | saw-kan')\n\nDerivation: probably a denominative from H7915 שַׂכִּין\nStrong's: properly, to cut, i.e. damage; also to grow (causatively, make) poor\nKJV: endanger, impoverish.\n\nCognate Group: H5533 (endanger)\nGreek Equivalents: G2793 κινδυνεύω",
    5534: "סָכַר (çâkar | saw-kar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to shut up; by implication, to surrender\nKJV: stop, give over. See also H5462 סָגַר, H7936 שָׂכַר .\n\nCognate Group: H5534 (stop)\nGreek Equivalents: G3860 παραδίδωμι",
    5535: "סָכַת (çâkath | saw-kath')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root to be silent\nStrong's: by implication, to observe quietly\nKJV: take heed.\n\nCognate Group: H5538 (Silla), H5535 (take heed)\nGreek Equivalents: G4623 σιωπάω",
    5536: "סַל (çal | sal)\n\nDerivation: from H5549 סָלַל\nStrong's: properly, a willow twig (as pendulous), i.e. an osier; but only as woven into abasket\nKJV: basket.\n\nCognate Group: H5536 (basket), H5552 (basket)\nGreek Equivalents: G2894 κόφινος",
    5537: "סָלָא (çâlâʼ | saw-law')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to suspend in a balance, i.e. weigh\nKJV: compare.\n\nCognate Group: H5537 (compare)\nGreek Equivalents: G1869 ἐπαίρω",
    5538: "סִלָּא (Çillâʼ | sil-law')\n\nDerivation: from H5549 סָלַל ; an embankment\nStrong's: Silla, a place in Jerusalem\nKJV: Silla.\n\nCognate Group: H5538 (Silla), H5535 (take heed)",
    5539: "סָלַד (çâlad | saw-lad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: probably to leap (with joy), i.e. exult\nKJV: harden self.\n\nCognate Group: H5539 (harden self), H5540 (Seled)",
    5540: "סֶלֶד (Çeled | seh'-led)\n\nDerivation: from H5539 סָלַד ; exultation\nStrong's: Seled, an Israelite\nKJV: Seled.\n\nCognate Group: H5539 (harden self), H5540 (Seled)",
    5541: "סָלָה (çâlâh | saw-law')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to hang up, i.e. weigh, or (figuratively) contemn\nKJV: tread down (under foot), value.\n\nCognate Group: H5541 (tread down)\nGreek Equivalents: G1808 ἐξαίρω",
    5542: "סֶלָה (çelâh | seh'-law)\n\nDerivation: from H5541 סָלָה\nStrong's: suspension (of music), i.e. pause\nKJV: Selah.\n\nCognate Group: H4547 (highway), H5542 (Selah), H4546 (causeway), H5550 (bank), H5549 (cast up), H5551 (ladder)",
    5543: "סַלּוּ (Çallûw | sal-loo')\n\nDerivation: or סַלּוּא; or סָלוּא; or סַלַּי; from H5541 סָלָה ; weighed\nStrong's: Sallu or Sallai, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Sallai, Sallu, Salu.\n\nCognate Group: H1354 (back), H1373 (Gabbai), H1359 (Gob), H5543 (Sallai), H1405 (Gibbethon)",
    5544: "סִלֹּון (çillôwn | sil-lone')\n\nDerivation: or סַלֹּון; from H5541 סָלָה\nStrong's: a prickle (as if pendulous)\nKJV: brier, thorn.\n\nCognate Group: H5543 (Sallai), H5541 (tread down), H5544 (brier)\nGreek Equivalents: G4647 σκόλοψ",
    5545: "סָלַח (çâlach | saw-lakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to forgive\nKJV: forgive, pardon, spare.\n\nCognate Group: H5546 (ready to forgive), H5547 (forgiveness), H5545 (forgive), H5548 (Salcah)\nGreek Equivalents: G851 ἀφαιρέω, G863 ἀφίημι, G2433 ἱλάσκομαι, G2436 ἵλεως, G2511 καθαρίζω, G3403 μιμνήσκω",
    5546: "סַלָּח (çallâch | saw-lawkh')\n\nDerivation: from H5545 סָלַח\nStrong's: placable\nKJV: ready to forgive.\n\nCognate Group: H5546 (ready to forgive), H5547 (forgiveness), H5545 (forgive), H5548 (Salcah)\nGreek Equivalents: G1933 ἐπιεικής",
    5547: "סְלִיחָה (çᵉlîychâh | sel-ee-khaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5545 סָלַח\nStrong's: pardon\nKJV: forgiveness, pardon.\n\nCognate Group: H5546 (ready to forgive), H5547 (forgiveness), H5545 (forgive), H5548 (Salcah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2434 ἱλασμός",
    5548: "סַלְכָה (Çalkâh | sal-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root. meaning to walk; walking\nStrong's: Salcah, a place East of the Jordan\nKJV: Salcah, Salchah.\n\nCognate Group: H5546 (ready to forgive), H5547 (forgiveness), H5545 (forgive), H5548 (Salcah)",
    5549: "סָלַל (çâlal | saw-lal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to mound up (especially a turnpike); figurative, to exalt; reflexively, to oppose (as by a dam)\nKJV: cast up, exalt (self), extol, make plain, raise up.\n\nCognate Group: H4547 (highway), H5542 (Selah), H4546 (causeway), H5550 (bank), H5549 (cast up), H5551 (ladder)\nGreek Equivalents: G2045 ἐρευνάω, G3596 ὁδοιπορέω",
    5550: "סֹלְלָה (çôlᵉlâh | so-lel-aw')\n\nDerivation: or סֹולְלָה; active participle feminine of H5549 סָלַל, but used passively\nStrong's: a military mound, i.e. rampart of besiegers\nKJV: bank, mount.\n\nCognate Group: H4547 (highway), H5542 (Selah), H4546 (causeway), H5550 (bank), H5549 (cast up), H5551 (ladder)\nGreek Equivalents: G5482 χάραξ",
    5551: "סֻלָּם (çullâm | sool-lawm')\n\nDerivation: from H5549 סָלַל\nStrong's: a stair-case\nKJV: ladder.\n\nCognate Group: H4547 (highway), H5542 (Selah), H4546 (causeway), H5550 (bank), H5549 (cast up), H5551 (ladder)",
    5552: "סַלְסִלָּה (çalçillâh | sal-sil-law')\n\nDerivation: from H5541 סָלָה\nStrong's: a twig (as pendulous)\nKJV: basket.\n\nCognate Group: H5536 (basket), H5552 (basket)",
    5553: "סֶלַע (çelaʻ | seh'-lah)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be lofty\nStrong's: a craggy rock, literally or figuratively (a fortress)\nKJV: (ragged) rock, stone(-ny), strong hold.\n\nCognate Group: H5553 (rock), H5554 (rock), H5556 (bald locust)\nGreek Equivalents: G2911 κρημνός, G4073 πέτρα, G4733 στερέωμα",
    5554: "סֶלַע (Çelaʻ | seh'-lah)\n\nDerivation: the same as H5553 סֶלַע\nStrong's: Sela, the rock-city of Idumaea\nKJV: rock, Sela(-h).\n\nCognate Group: H5553 (rock), H5554 (rock), H5556 (bald locust)",
    5555: "סֶלַע הַמַּחְלְקֹות (Çelaʻ ham-machlᵉqôwth | seh'-lah hammakh-lek-oth')\n\nDerivation: from H5553 סֶלַע and the plural of H4256 מַחֲלֹקֶת with the article interposed; rock of the divisions\nStrong's: Sela-ham-Machlekoth, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Sela-hammalekoth.\n\nCognate Group: H2511 (smooth), H2519 (flattery), H5555 (Sela-hammalekoth), H2513 (field), H2505 (deal), H2506 (flattery), H2509 (flattering), H2514 (flattery), H2512 (smooth), H2510 (Halak)",
    5556: "סׇלְעָם (çolʻâm | sol-awm')\n\nDerivation: apparently from the same as H5553 סֶלַע in the sense of crushing as with a rock, i.e. consuming\nStrong's: a kind of locust (from its destructiveness)\nKJV: bald locust.\n\nCognate Group: H5553 (rock), H5554 (rock), H5556 (bald locust)",
    5557: "סָלַף (çâlaph | saw-laf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to wrench, i.e. (figuratively) to subvert\nKJV: overthrow, pervert.\n\nCognate Group: H5557 (overthrow), H5558 (perverseness)\nGreek Equivalents: G1808 ἐξαίρω, G2690 καταστρέφω, G3075 λυμαίνομαι, G5337 φαῦλος",
    5558: "סֶלֶף (çeleph | seh'-lef)\n\nDerivation: from H5557 סָלַף\nStrong's: distortion, i.e. (figuratively) viciousness\nKJV: perverseness.\n\nCognate Group: H5557 (overthrow), H5558 (perverseness)",
    5559: "סְלִק (çᵉliq | sel-eek')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) a primitive root\nStrong's: to ascend\nKJV: come (up).\n\nCognate Group: H5267 (take up), H5559 (come)\nGreek Equivalents: G305 ἀναβαίνω, G305 ἀναβαίνω, G399 ἀναφέρω",
    5560: "סֹלֶת (çôleth | so'-leth)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to strip\nStrong's: flour (as chipped off)\nKJV: (fine) flour, meal.\n\nCognate Group: H5562 (Samgar-nebo), H5266 (ascend), H5563 (tender grape), H5560 (flour)\nGreek Equivalents: G4585 σεμίδαλις",
    5561: "סַם (çam | sam)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to smell sweet\nStrong's: an aroma\nKJV: sweet (spice).\n\nCognate Group: H5561 (sweet)\nGreek Equivalents: G2368 θυμίαμα",
    5562: "סַמְגַּר נְבֹו (Çamgar Nᵉbôw | sam-gar' neb-o')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Samgar-Nebo, a Babylonian general\nKJV: Samgar-nebo.\n\nCognate Group: H5562 (Samgar-nebo), H5266 (ascend), H5563 (tender grape), H5560 (flour)",
    5563: "סְמָדַר (çᵉmâdar | sem-aw-dar')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a vine blossom; used also adverbially, abloom\nKJV: tender grape.\n\nCognate Group: H5562 (Samgar-nebo), H5266 (ascend), H5563 (tender grape), H5560 (flour)",
    5564: "סָמַךְ (çâmak | saw-mak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to prop (literally or figuratively); reflexively, to lean upon or take hold of (in a favorable or unfavorable sense)\nKJV: bear up, establish, (up-) hold, lay, lean, lie hard, put, rest self, set self, stand fast, stay (self), sustain.\n\nCognate Group: H5566 (figure), H5564 (bear up), H5565 (Semachiah), H3253 (Ismachiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G482 ἀντιλαμβάνομαι, G1991 ἐπιστηρίζω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2186 ἐφίστημι, G2476 ἵστημι, G4317 προσάγω, G4741 στηρίζω",
    5565: "סְמַכְיָהוּ (Çᵉmakyâhûw | sem-ak-yaw'-hoo)\n\nDerivation: from H5564 סָמַךְ and H3050 יָהּ ; supported of Jah\nStrong's: Semakjah, an Israelite\nKJV: Semachiah.\n\nCognate Group: H5566 (figure), H5564 (bear up), H5565 (Semachiah), H3253 (Ismachiah)",
    5566: "סֶמֶל (çemel | seh'-mel)\n\nDerivation: or סֵמֶל; from an unused root meaning to resemble\nStrong's: a likeness\nKJV: figure, idol, image.\n\nCognate Group: H5566 (figure), H5564 (bear up), H5565 (Semachiah), H3253 (Ismachiah)",
    5567: "סָמַן (çâman | saw-man')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to designate\nKJV: appointed.\n\nCognate Group: H5567 (appointed)",
    5568: "סָמַר (çâmar | saw-mar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be erect, i.e. bristle as hair\nKJV: stand up, tremble.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)\nGreek Equivalents: G5425 φρίσσω",
    5569: "סָמָר (çâmâr | saw-mar')\n\nDerivation: from H5568 סָמַר\nStrong's: bristling, i.e. shaggy\nKJV: rough.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)",
    5570: "סְנָאָה (Çᵉnâʼâh | sen-aw-aw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to prick; thorny\nStrong's: Senaah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Senaah, Hassenaah (with the article).\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)",
    5571: "סַנְבַלַּט (Çanballaṭ | san-bal-lat')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Sanballat, a Persian satrap of Samaria\nKJV: Sanballat.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)",
    5572: "סְנֶה (çᵉneh | sen-eh')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to prick\nStrong's: a bramble\nKJV: bush.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)\nGreek Equivalents: G942 βάτος",
    5573: "סֶנֶה (Çeneh | seh-neh')\n\nDerivation: the same as H5572 סְנֶה ; thorn\nStrong's: Seneh, a crag in Palestine\nKJV: Seneh.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)",
    5574: "סְנוּאָה (Çᵉnûwʼâh | sen-oo-aw')\n\nDerivation: or סְנֻאָה from the same as H5570 סְנָאָה\nStrong's: pointed; (used with the article as a proper name) Senuah, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Hasenuah (including the art), Senuah.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)",
    5575: "סַנְוֵר (çanvêr | san-vare')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: (in plural) blindness\nKJV: blindness.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)",
    5576: "סַנְחֵרִיב (Çanchêrîyb | san-khay-reeb')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Sancherib, an Assyrian king\nKJV: Sennacherib.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)",
    5577: "סַנְסִן (çançin | san-seen')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be pointed\nStrong's: a twig (as tapering)\nKJV: bough.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)",
    5578: "סַנְסַנָּה (Çançannâh | san-san-naw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of a form of H5577 סַנְסִן ; a bough\nStrong's: Sansannah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Sansannah.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)",
    5579: "סְנַפִּיר (çᵉnappîyr | sen-ap-peer')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a fin (collectively)\nKJV: fins.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)\nGreek Equivalents: G4419 πτερύγιον",
    5580: "סָס (çâç | sawce)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5483 סוּס\nStrong's: a moth (from the agility of the fly)\nKJV: moth.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)\nGreek Equivalents: G4597 σής",
    5581: "סִסְמַי (Çiçmay | sis-mah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Sismai, an Israelite\nKJV: Sisamai.\n\nCognate Group: H5575 (blindness), H5581 (Sisamai), H5572 (bush), H5576 (Sennacherib), H5568 (stand up), H5569 (rough), H5573 (Seneh), H4548 (nail), H5580 (moth), H5570 (Senaah), H5579 (fins), H5577 (bough), H5571 (Sanballat), H5574 (Hasenuah), H5578 (Sansannah), H4930 (nail)",
    5582: "סָעַד (çâʻad | saw-ad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to suport (mostly figurative)\nKJV: comfort, establish, hold up, refresh self, strengthen, be upholden.\n\nCognate Group: H4552 (pillar), H5582 (comfort)\nGreek Equivalents: G482 ἀντιλαμβάνομαι, G709 ἀριστάω, G2068 ἐσθίω, G4033 περικυκλόω, G4741 στηρίζω",
    5583: "סְעַד (çᵉʻad | seh-ad')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5582 סָעַד\nStrong's: to aid\nKJV: helping.\n\nCognate Group: H5583 (helping)\nGreek Equivalents: G997 βοηθέω",
    5584: "סָעָה (çâʻâh | saw-aw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to rush\nKJV: storm.\n\nCognate Group: H5584 (storm)",
    5585: "סָעִיף (çâʻîyph | saw-eef')\n\nDerivation: from H5586 סָעַף\nStrong's: a fissure (of rocks); also a bough (as subdivided)\nKJV: (outmost) branch, clift, top.\n\nCognate Group: H5587 (opinion), H5586 (top), H5588 (thought), H5589 (bough), H5634 (bough), H5585 (branch)",
    5586: "סָעַף (çâʻaph | saw-af')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; properly, to divide up; but used only as denominative from H5585 סָעִיף,\nStrong's: to disbranch (a tree)\nKJV: top.\n\nCognate Group: H5587 (opinion), H5586 (top), H5588 (thought), H5589 (bough), H5634 (bough), H5585 (branch)",
    5587: "סָעִף (çâʻiph | saw-eef')\n\nDerivation: or שָׂעִף; from H5586 סָעַף\nStrong's: divided (in mind), i.e. (abstractly) a sentiment\nKJV: opinion.\n\nCognate Group: H5587 (opinion), H5586 (top), H5588 (thought), H5589 (bough), H5634 (bough), H5585 (branch)",
    5588: "סֵעֵף (çêʻêph | say-afe')\n\nDerivation: from H5586 סָעַף\nStrong's: divided (in mind), i.e. (concretely) a skeptic\nKJV: thought.\n\nCognate Group: H5587 (opinion), H5586 (top), H5588 (thought), H5589 (bough), H5634 (bough), H5585 (branch)\nGreek Equivalents: G3601 ὀδύνη",
    5589: "סְעַפָּה (çᵉʻappâh | seh-ap-paw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5585 סָעִיף\nStrong's: a twig\nKJV: bough, branch. Compare H5634 סַרְעַפָּה .\n\nCognate Group: H5587 (opinion), H5586 (top), H5588 (thought), H5589 (bough), H5634 (bough), H5585 (branch)",
    5590: "סָעַר (çâʻar | saw-ar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to rush upon; by implication, to toss (transitive or intransitive, literal or figurative)\nKJV: be (toss with) tempest(-uous), be sore, troubled, come out as a (drive with the, scatter with a) whirlwind.\n\nCognate Group: H5591 (storm), H5590 (be tempest)\nGreek Equivalents: G1544 ἐκβάλλω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1825 ἐξεγείρω, G1839 ἐξίστημι, G2666 καταπίνω, G2702 καταφέρω, G3039 λικμάω, G4579 σείω, G4863 συνάγω, G5425 φρίσσω",
    5591: "סַעַר (çaʻar | sah'-ar)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) סְעָרָה; from H5590 סָעַר\nStrong's: a hurricane\nKJV: storm(-y), tempest, whirlwind.\n\nCognate Group: H5591 (storm), H5590 (be tempest)\nGreek Equivalents: G1105 γνόφος, G2978 λαῖλαψ, G3709 ὀργή, G4535 σάλος, G4578 σεισμός, G5342 φέρω",
    5592: "סַף (çaph | saf)\n\nDerivation: from H5605 סָפַף, in its original sense of containing\nStrong's: a vestibule (as a limit); also a dish (for holding blood or wine)\nKJV: bason, bowl, cup, door (post), gate, post, threshold.\n\nCognate Group: H5598 (Sippai), H5593 (Saph), H5605 (be a doorkeeper), H5592 (bason)\nGreek Equivalents: G833 αὐλή, G1529 εἴσοδος, G2374 θύρα, G4439 πύλη, G4440 πυλών",
    5593: "סַף (Çaph | saf)\n\nDerivation: the same as H5592 סַף\nStrong's: Saph, a Philistine\nKJV: Saph. Compare H5598 סִפַּי .\n\nCognate Group: H5598 (Sippai), H5593 (Saph), H5605 (be a doorkeeper), H5592 (bason)",
    5594: "סָפַד (çâphad | saw-fad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to tear the hair and beat the breasts (as Orientals do in grief); generally to lament; by implication, to wail\nKJV: lament, mourn(-er), wail.\n\nCognate Group: H5594 (lament), H4553 (lamentation)\nGreek Equivalents: G2799 κλαίω, G2875 κόπτω",
    5595: "סָפָה (çâphâh | saw-faw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to scrape (literally, to shave; but usually figuratively) together (i.e. to accumulate or increase) or away (i.e. to scatter, remove, or ruin; intransitively, to perish)\nKJV: add, augment, consume, destroy, heap, join, perish, put.\n\nCognate Group: H5595 (add)\nGreek Equivalents: G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G853 ἀφανίζω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G2798 κλάδος, G3692 ὀπή, G4369 προστίθημι, G4693 σπήλαιον, G4863 συνάγω, G4881 συναπόλλυμι, G5168 τρυμαλιά",
    5596: "סָפַח (çâphach | saw-fakh')\n\nDerivation: or שָׂפַח; (Isaiah 3:17), a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to scrape out, but in certain peculiar senses (of removal or association)\nKJV: abiding, gather together, cleave, smite with the scab.\n\nCognate Group: H5596 (abiding)\nGreek Equivalents: G4369 προστίθημι, G4741 στηρίζω",
    5597: "סַפַּחַת (çappachath | sap-pakh'-ath)\n\nDerivation: from H5596 סָפַח\nStrong's: the mange (as making the hair fall off)\nKJV: scab.\n\nCognate Group: H5596 (abiding), H4555 (kerchief), H4556 (scab), H5602 (bowl), H5601 (sapphire), H5597 (scab)",
    5598: "סִפַּי (Çippay | sip-pah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H5592 סַף ; bason-like\nStrong's: Sippai, a Philistine\nKJV: Sippai. Compare H5593 סַף .\n\nCognate Group: H5598 (Sippai), H5593 (Saph), H5605 (be a doorkeeper), H5592 (bason)",
    5599: "סָפִיחַ (çâphîyach | saw-fee'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H5596 סָפַח\nStrong's: something (spontaneously) falling off, i.e. a self-sown crop; figuratively, a freshet\nKJV: (such) things as (which) grow (of themselves), which groweth of its own accord (itself).\n\nCognate Group: H4939 (oppression), H5599 (things as grow)\nGreek Equivalents: G305 ἀναβαίνω, G844 αὐτόματος",
    5600: "סְפִינָה (çᵉphîynâh | sef-ee-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H5603 סָפַן\nStrong's: a (sea-going) vessel (as ceiled with a deck)\nKJV: ship.\n\nCognate Group: H5603 (cieled), H8226 (treasure), H5600 (ship), H5604 (cieling)\nGreek Equivalents: G4143 πλοῖον",
    5601: "סַפִּיר (çappîyr | sap-peer')\n\nDerivation: from H5608 סָפַר\nStrong's: a gem (perhaps used for scratching other substances), probably the sapphire\nKJV: sapphire.\n\nCognate Group: H5596 (abiding), H4555 (kerchief), H4556 (scab), H5602 (bowl), H5601 (sapphire), H5597 (scab)\nGreek Equivalents: G4552 σάπφειρος",
    5602: "סֵפֶל (çêphel | say'-fel)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to depress\nStrong's: a basin (as deepened out)\nKJV: bowl, dish.\n\nCognate Group: H5596 (abiding), H4555 (kerchief), H4556 (scab), H5602 (bowl), H5601 (sapphire), H5597 (scab)",
    5603: "סָפַן (çâphan | saw-fan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to hide by covering; specifically, to roof (passive participle as noun, a roof) or wainscot; figuratively, to reserve\nKJV: cieled, cover, seated.\n\nCognate Group: H5603 (cieled), H8226 (treasure), H5600 (ship), H5604 (cieling)\nGreek Equivalents: G1712 ἐμπόριον",
    5604: "סִפֻּן (çippun | sip-poon')\n\nDerivation: from H5603 סָפַן\nStrong's: a wainscot\nKJV: cieling.\n\nCognate Group: H5603 (cieled), H8226 (treasure), H5600 (ship), H5604 (cieling)\nGreek Equivalents: G1385 δοκός",
    5605: "סָפַף (çâphaph | saw-faf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; properly, to snatch away, i.e. terminate; but used only as denominative from H5592 סַף (in the sense of a vestibule),\nStrong's: to wait at the threshold\nKJV: be a doorkeeper.\n\nCognate Group: H5598 (Sippai), H5593 (Saph), H5605 (be a doorkeeper), H5592 (bason)",
    5606: "סָפַק (çâphaq | saw-fak')\n\nDerivation: or שָׂפַק; (1 Kings 20:10; Job 27:23; Isaiah 2:6), a primitive root\nStrong's: to clap the hands (in token of compact, derision, grief, indignation, or punishment); by implication of satisfaction, to be enough; by implication of excess, to vomit\nKJV: clap, smite, strike, suffice, wallow.\n\nCognate Group: H5607 (stroke), H5606 (clap)",
    5607: "סֵפֶק (çêpheq | say'-fek)\n\nDerivation: or שֶׂפֶק; (Job 20:22; Job 36:18), from H5606 סָפַק\nStrong's: chastisement; also satiety\nKJV: stroke, sufficiency.\n\nCognate Group: H5607 (stroke), H5606 (clap)",
    5608: "סָפַר (çâphar | saw-far')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to score with a mark as a tally or record, i.e. (by implication) to inscribe, and also to enumerate; intensively, to recount, i.e. celebrate\nKJV: commune, (ac-) count; declare, number, [phrase] penknife, reckon, scribe, shew forth, speak, talk, tell (out), writer.\n\nCognate Group: H5618 (Sophereth), H5617 (Sepharvites), H5616 (Sepharvite), H5615 (number), H4558 (Mizpar), H5611 (Sephar), H5608 (commune), H4557 (abundance), H5614 (Sepharad), H4559 (Mispereth), H5610 (numbering), H5612 (bill)\nGreek Equivalents: G312 ἀναγγέλλω, G518 ἀπαγγέλλω, G705 ἀριθμέω, G1122 γραμματεύς, G1229 διαγγέλλω, G1334 διηγέομαι, G1555 ἐκδιηγέομαι, G1804 ἐξαγγέλλω, G1834 ἐξηγέομαι, G2980 λαλέω, G3004 λέγω, G4863 συνάγω, G5263 ὑποδείκνυμι, G5585 ψηφίζω",
    5609: "סְפַר (çᵉphar | sef-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H5608 סָפַר\nStrong's: a book\nKJV: book, roll.\n\nCognate Group: H5622 (coat), H5609 (book), H5613 (scribe), H5632 (president)",
    5610: "סְפָר (çᵉphâr | sef-awr')\n\nDerivation: from H5608 סָפַר\nStrong's: a census\nKJV: numbering.\n\nCognate Group: H5618 (Sophereth), H5617 (Sepharvites), H5616 (Sepharvite), H5615 (number), H4558 (Mizpar), H5611 (Sephar), H5608 (commune), H4557 (abundance), H5614 (Sepharad), H4559 (Mispereth), H5610 (numbering), H5612 (bill)\nGreek Equivalents: G706 ἀριθμός",
    5611: "סְפָר (Çᵉphâr | sef-awr')\n\nDerivation: the same as H5610 סְפָר\nStrong's: Sephar, a place in Arabia\nKJV: Sephar.\n\nCognate Group: H5618 (Sophereth), H5617 (Sepharvites), H5616 (Sepharvite), H5615 (number), H4558 (Mizpar), H5611 (Sephar), H5608 (commune), H4557 (abundance), H5614 (Sepharad), H4559 (Mispereth), H5610 (numbering), H5612 (bill)",
    5612: "סֵפֶר (çêpher | say'-fer)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) סִפְרָה; (Psalm 56:8 (H9 אֲבֵדָה)), from H5608 סָפַר\nStrong's: properly, writing (the art or a document); by implication, a book\nKJV: bill, book, evidence, [idiom] learn(-ed) (-ing), letter, register, scroll.\n\nCognate Group: H5618 (Sophereth), H5617 (Sepharvites), H5616 (Sepharvite), H5615 (number), H4558 (Mizpar), H5611 (Sephar), H5608 (commune), H4557 (abundance), H5614 (Sepharad), H4559 (Mispereth), H5610 (numbering), H5612 (bill)\nGreek Equivalents: G975 βιβλίον, G976 βίβλος, G1121 γράμμα, G1860 ἐπαγγελία, G1992 ἐπιστολή, G3056 λόγος",
    5613: "סָפֵר (çâphêr | saw-fare')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from the same as H5609 סְפַר\nStrong's: a scribe (secular or sacred)\nKJV: scribe.\n\nCognate Group: H5622 (coat), H5609 (book), H5613 (scribe), H5632 (president)",
    5614: "סְפָרָד (Çᵉphârâd | sef-aw-rawd')\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Sepharad, a region of Assyria\nKJV: Sepharad.\n\nCognate Group: H5618 (Sophereth), H5617 (Sepharvites), H5616 (Sepharvite), H5615 (number), H4558 (Mizpar), H5611 (Sephar), H5608 (commune), H4557 (abundance), H5614 (Sepharad), H4559 (Mispereth), H5610 (numbering), H5612 (bill)",
    5615: "סְפֹרָה (çᵉphôrâh | sef-o-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H5608 סָפַר\nStrong's: a numeration\nKJV: number.\n\nCognate Group: H5618 (Sophereth), H5617 (Sepharvites), H5616 (Sepharvite), H5615 (number), H4558 (Mizpar), H5611 (Sephar), H5608 (commune), H4557 (abundance), H5614 (Sepharad), H4559 (Mispereth), H5610 (numbering), H5612 (bill)",
    5616: "סְפַרְוִי (Çᵉpharvîy | sef-ar-vee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H5617 סְפַרְוַיִם\nStrong's: a Sepharvite or inhabitant of Sepharvain\nKJV: Sepharvite.\n\nCognate Group: H5618 (Sophereth), H5617 (Sepharvites), H5616 (Sepharvite), H5615 (number), H4558 (Mizpar), H5611 (Sephar), H5608 (commune), H4557 (abundance), H5614 (Sepharad), H4559 (Mispereth), H5610 (numbering), H5612 (bill)",
    5617: "סְפַרְוַיִם (Çᵉpharvayim | sef-ar-vah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: (dual)\n\nStrong's: Sepharvites\n\nCognate Group: H5618 (Sophereth), H5617 (Sepharvites), H5616 (Sepharvite), H5615 (number), H4558 (Mizpar), H5611 (Sephar), H5608 (commune), H4557 (abundance), H5614 (Sepharad), H4559 (Mispereth), H5610 (numbering), H5612 (bill)",
    5618: "סֹפֶרֶת (Çôphereth | so-feh'-reth)\n\nDerivation: feminine active participle of H5608 סָפַר ; a scribe (properly, female)\nStrong's: Sophereth, a temple servant\nKJV: Sophereth.\n\nCognate Group: H5618 (Sophereth), H5617 (Sepharvites), H5616 (Sepharvite), H5615 (number), H4558 (Mizpar), H5611 (Sephar), H5608 (commune), H4557 (abundance), H5614 (Sepharad), H4559 (Mispereth), H5610 (numbering), H5612 (bill)",
    5619: "סָקַל (çâqal | saw-kal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to be weighty; but used only in the sense of lapidation or its contrary (as if a delapidation)\nKJV: (cast, gather out, throw) stone(-s), [idiom] surely.\n\nCognate Group: H5623 (Sargon), H5621 (brier), H5619 (stone)\nGreek Equivalents: G3034 λιθάζω, G3036 λιθοβολέω, G3037 λίθος",
    5620: "סַר (çar | sar)\n\nDerivation: contracted from H5637 סָרַר\nStrong's: peevish\nKJV: heavy, sad.\n\nCognate Group: H5638 (winter), H5620 (heavy), H5637 ([idiom] away)",
    5621: "סָרָב (çârâb | saw-rawb')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to sting\nStrong's: a thistle\nKJV: brier.\n\nCognate Group: H5623 (Sargon), H5621 (brier), H5619 (stone)",
    5622: "סַרְבַּל (çarbal | sar-bal')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a cloak\nKJV: coat.\n\nCognate Group: H5622 (coat), H5609 (book), H5613 (scribe), H5632 (president)",
    5623: "סַרְגֹּון (Çargôwn | sar-gone')\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Sargon, an Assyrian king\nKJV: Sargon.\n\nCognate Group: H5623 (Sargon), H5621 (brier), H5619 (stone)",
    5624: "סֶרֶד (Çered | seh'-red)\n\nDerivation: from a primitive root meaning to tremble; trembling\nStrong's: Sered, an Israelite\nKJV: Sered.\n\nCognate Group: H5624 (Sered), H5625 (Sardites)",
    5625: "סַרְדִּי (Çardîy | sar-dee')\n\nDerivation: patron from H5624 סֶרֶד\nStrong's: a Seredite (collectively) or descendants of Sered\nKJV: Sardites.\n\nCognate Group: H5624 (Sered), H5625 (Sardites)",
    5626: "סִרָה (Çirâh | see-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H5493 סוּר ; departure\nStrong's: Sirah, a cistern so-called\nKJV: Sirah. See also H5518 סִיר .\n\nCognate Group: H884 (Beer-shebah), H1275 (Beri), H882 (Beeri), H883 (Beer-lahai-roi), H879 (Beer-elim), H3565 (Chorashan), H1268 (Berothah), H880 (Beerah), H875 (pit), H876 (Beer), H1307 (Berothite), H874 (declare), H878 (Beera), H886 (Beerothite), H877 (cistern), H885 (Beeroth of the children of Jaakan), H881 (Beeroth), H953 (cistern), H5626 (Sirah)",
    5627: "סָרָה (çârâh | saw-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H5493 סוּר\nStrong's: apostasy, crime; figuratively, remission\nKJV: [idiom] continual, rebellion, revolt(-ed), turn away, wrong.\n\nCognate Group: H3249 (they that depart), H5495 (Sur), H5493 (be), H5494 (degenerate), H5627 ([idiom] continual)\nGreek Equivalents: G458 ἀνομία, G459 ἄνομος, G763 ἀσέβεια",
    5628: "סָרַח (çârach | saw-rakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to extend (even to excess)\nKJV: exceeding, hand, spread, stretch self, banish.\n\nCognate Group: H5628 (exceeding), H5631 (chamberlain), H5633 (lord), H5636 (brier), H5630 (brigandine), H5629 (remnant)\nGreek Equivalents: G1943 ἐπικαλύπτω",
    5629: "סֶרַח (çerach | seh'-rakh)\n\nDerivation: from H5628 סָרַח\nStrong's: a redundancy\nKJV: remnant.\n\nCognate Group: H5628 (exceeding), H5631 (chamberlain), H5633 (lord), H5636 (brier), H5630 (brigandine), H5629 (remnant)",
