    5667: "עֲבֹוט (ʻăbôwṭ | ab-ote')\n\nDerivation: or עֲבֹט; from H5670 עָבַט\nStrong's: a pawn\nKJV: pledge.\n\nCognate Group: H5667 (pledge), H5671 (thick clay), H5670 (borrow)",
    5668: "עָבוּר (ʻâbûwr | aw-boor')\n\nDerivation: or עָבֻר; passive participle of H5674 עָבַר\nStrong's: properly, crossed, i.e. (abstractly) transit; used only adverbially, on account of, in order that\nKJV: because of, for (...'s sake), (intent) that, to.\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)",
    5669: "עָבוּר (ʻâbûwr | aw-boor')\n\nDerivation: the same as H5668 עָבוּר\nStrong's: passed, i.e. kept over; used only of stored grain\nKJV: old corn.\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)\nGreek Equivalents: G4621 σῖτος",
    5670: "עָבַט (ʻâbaṭ | aw-bat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to pawn; causatively, to lend (on security); figuratively, to entangle\nKJV: borrow, break (ranks), fetch (a pledge), lend, [idiom] surely.\n\nCognate Group: H5667 (pledge), H5671 (thick clay), H5670 (borrow)",
    5671: "עַבְטִיט (ʻabṭîyṭ | ab-teet')\n\nDerivation: from H5670 עָבַט\nStrong's: something pledged, i.e. (collectively) pawned goods\nKJV: thick clay (by a false etym.).\n\nCognate Group: H5667 (pledge), H5671 (thick clay), H5670 (borrow)",
    5672: "עֲבִי (ʻăbîy | ab-ee')\n\nDerivation: or עֳבִי]; from H5666 עָבָה\nStrong's: density, i.e. depth or width\nKJV: thick(-ness). Compare H5645 עָב .\n\nCognate Group: H4568 (clay), H5672 (thick), H5666 (be thick)\nGreek Equivalents: G4114 πλάτος",
    5673: "עֲבִידָה (ʻăbîydâh | ab-ee-daw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H5648 עֲבַד\nStrong's: labor or business\nKJV: affairs, service, work.\n\nCognate Group: H5648 ([idiom] cut), H5649 (servant), H5675 (beyond), H5673 (affairs), H4567 (work), H5665 (Abed-nego)\nGreek Equivalents: G4229 πρᾶγμα",
    5674: "עָבַר (ʻâbar | aw-bar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to cross over; used very widely of any transition (literal or figurative; transitive, intransitive, intensive, causative); specifically, to cover (in copulation)\nKJV: alienate, alter, [idiom] at all, beyond, bring (over, through), carry over, (over-) come (on, over), conduct (over), convey over, current, deliver, do away, enter, escape, fail, gender, get over, (make) go (away, beyond, by, forth, his way, in, on, over, through), have away (more), lay, meddle, overrun, make partition, (cause to, give, make to, over) pass(-age, along, away, beyond, by, -enger, on, out, over, through), (cause to, make) [phrase] proclaim(-amation), perish, provoke to anger, put away, rage, [phrase] raiser of taxes, remove, send over, set apart, [phrase] shave, cause to (make) sound, [idiom] speedily, [idiom] sweet smelling, take (away), (make to) transgress(-or), translate, turn away, (way-) faring man, be wrath.\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)\nGreek Equivalents: G305 ἀναβαίνω, G306 ἀναβάλλομαι, G307 ἀναβιβάζω, G373 ἀναπαύω, G399 ἀναφέρω, G520 ἀπάγω, G565 ἀπέρχομαι, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G873 ἀφορίζω, G1096 γίνομαι, G1224 διαβαίνω, G1229 διαγγέλλω, G1236 διάγω, G1276 διαπεράω, G1279 διαπορεύομαι, G1330 διέρχομαι, G1353 διοδεύω, G1384 δόκιμος, G1525 εἰσέρχομαι, G1531 εἰσπορεύομαι, G1544 ἐκβάλλω, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1607 ἐκπορεύομαι, G1806 ἐξάγω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1825 ἐξεγείρω, G1831 ἐξέρχομαι, G1863 ἐπάγω, G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G1975 ἐπιπορεύομαι, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G2240 ἥκω, G2476 ἵστημι, G2476 ἵστημι, G2512 καθαρισμός, G2647 καταλύω, G3845 παραβαίνω, G3853 παραγγέλλω, G3855 παράγω, G3878 παρακούω, G3899 παραπορεύομαι, G3911 παραφέρω, G3928 παρέρχομαι, G3930 παρέχω, G3938 πάροδος, G3947 παροξύνω, G4013 περιάγω, G4014 περιαιρέω, G4022 περιέρχομαι, G4134 πλήρης, G4198 πορεύομαι, G4281 προέρχομαι, G4313 προπορεύομαι, G4317 προσάγω, G4334 προσέρχομαι, G4912 συνέχω, G5229 ὑπεραίρομαι, G5233 ὑπερβαίνω, G5342 φέρω",
    5675: "עֲבַר (ʻăbar | ab-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5676 עֵבֶר \nStrong's: properly, a region across; but used only adverbially (with or without a preposition) on the opposite side (especially of the Jordan; ususally meaning the east)\nKJV: beyond, this side.\n\nCognate Group: H5648 ([idiom] cut), H5649 (servant), H5675 (beyond), H5673 (affairs), H4567 (work), H5665 (Abed-nego)",
    5676: "עֵבֶר (ʻêber | ay'-ber)\n\nDerivation: from H5674 עָבַר\nStrong's: properly, a region across; but used only adverbially (with or without a preposition) on the opposite side (especially of the Jordan; ususally meaning the east)\nKJV: [idiom] against, beyond, by, [idiom] from, over, passage, quarter, (other, this) side, straight.\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)\nGreek Equivalents: G1445 Ἑβραῖος, G3313 μέρος, G4008 πέραν, G4420 πτέρυξ",
    5677: "עֵבֵר (ʻÊbêr | ay'-ber)\n\nDerivation: the same as H5676 עֵבֶר\nStrong's: Eber, the name of two patriarchs and four Israelites\nKJV: Eber, Heber.\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)\nGreek Equivalents: G1443 Ἐβέρ",
    5678: "עֶבְרָה (ʻebrâh | eb-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5676 עֵבֶר\nStrong's: an outburst of passion\nKJV: anger, rage, wrath.\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)\nGreek Equivalents: G32 ἄγγελος, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G2372 θυμός, G3709 ὀργή, G3731 ὅρμημα",
    5679: "עֲבָרָה (ʻăbârâh | ab-aw-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H5674 עָבַר\nStrong's: a crossing-place\nKJV: ferry, plain (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)\nGreek Equivalents: G3688 ὄνος, G962 Βηθαβαρά",
    5680: "עִבְרִי (ʻIbrîy | ib-ree')\n\nDerivation: patronymic from H5677 עֵבֵר\nStrong's: an Eberite (i.e. Hebrew) or descendant of Eber\nKJV: Hebrew(-ess, woman).\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)",
    5681: "עִבְרִי (ʻIbrîy | ib-ree')\n\nDerivation: the same as H5680 עִבְרִי\nStrong's: Ibri, an Israelite\nKJV: Ibri.\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)",
    5682: "עֲבָרִים (ʻĂbârîym | ab-aw-reem')\n\nTypo: xlit ʻĂbârîm corrected to ʻĂbârîym\n\nDerivation: plural of H5676 עֵבֶר ; regions beyond\nStrong's: Abarim, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Abarim, passages.\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)",
    5683: "עֶבְרֹן (ʻEbrôn | eb-rone')\n\nDerivation: from H5676 עֵבֶר ; transitional\nStrong's: Ebron, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Hebron. Perhaps a clerical error for H5658 עַבְדֹון .\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)",
    5684: "עֶבְרֹנָה (ʻEbrônâh | eb-raw-naw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5683 עֶבְרֹן\nStrong's: Ebronah, place in the Desert\nKJV: Ebronah.\n\nCognate Group: H5676 ([idiom] against), H5681 (Ibri), H5683 (Hebron), H5669 (old corn), H5677 (Eber), H4569 (ford), H5679 (ferry), H5674 (alienate), H5678 (anger), H5684 (Ebronah), H5680 (Hebrew), H5682 (Abarim), H5668 (because of)",
    5685: "עָבַשׁ (ʻâbash | aw-bash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to dry up\nKJV: be rotten.\n\nCognate Group: H5685 (be rotten)",
    5686: "עָבַת (ʻâbath | aw-bath')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to interlace, i.e. (figuratively) to pervert\nKJV: wrap up.\n\nCognate Group: H5686 (wrap up), H5688 (band), H5687 (thick)",
    5687: "עָבֹת (ʻâbôth | aw-both')\n\nDerivation: or עָבֹות; from H5686 עָבַת\nStrong's: intwined, i.e. dense\nKJV: thick.\n\nCognate Group: H5686 (wrap up), H5688 (band), H5687 (thick)",
    5688: "עֲבֹת (ʻăbôth | ab-oth')\n\nDerivation: or עֲבֹות; or (feminine) עֲבֹתָה; the same as H5687 עָבֹת\nStrong's: something intwined, i.e. a string, wreath or foliage\nKJV: band, cord, rope, thick bough (branch), wreathen (chain).\n\nCognate Group: H5686 (wrap up), H5688 (band), H5687 (thick)\nGreek Equivalents: G1199 δεσμόν, G2218 ζυγός, G2438 ἱμάς, G2440 ἱμάτιον, G3507 νεφέλη, G4120 πλέκω",
    5689: "עֲגַב (ʻăgab | aw-gab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to breathe after, i.e. to love (sensually)\nKJV: dote, lover.\n\nCognate Group: H5690 (much love), H5691 (inordinate love), H5689 (dote), H5748 (organ)\nGreek Equivalents: G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G25 ἀγαπάω",
    5690: "עֶגֶב (ʻegeb | eh'-gheb)\n\nDerivation: from H5689 עֲגַב\nStrong's: love (concretely), i.e. amative words\nKJV: much love, very lovely.\n\nCognate Group: H5690 (much love), H5691 (inordinate love), H5689 (dote), H5748 (organ)",
    5691: "עֲגָבָה (ʻăgâbâh | ag-aw-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H5689 עֲגַב\nStrong's: love (abstractly), i.e. amorousness\nKJV: inordinate love.\n\nCognate Group: H5690 (much love), H5691 (inordinate love), H5689 (dote), H5748 (organ)\nGreek Equivalents: G1936 ἐπίθεσις",
    5692: "עֻגָּה (ʻuggâh | oog-gaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5746 עוּג\nStrong's: an ash-cake (as round)\nKJV: cake (upon the hearth).\n\nCognate Group: H5746 (bake), H5747 (Og), H5692 (cake), H4580 (cake)",
    5693: "עָגוּר (ʻâgûwr | aw-goor')\n\nDerivation: passive part (but with active sense) of an unused root meaning to twitter\nStrong's: probably the swallow\nKJV: swallow.\n\nCognate Group: H5693 (swallow)",
    5694: "עָגִיל (ʻâgîyl | aw-gheel')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5696 עָגֹל\nStrong's: something round, i.e. a ring (for the ears)\nKJV: earring.\n\nCognate Group: H4570 (going), H5696 (round), H5700 (Eglon), H5699 (cart), H5697 (calf), H5695 (bullock), H5698 (Eglah), H5694 (earring)",
    5695: "עֵגֶל (ʻêgel | ay-ghel)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5696 עָגֹל\nStrong's: a (male) calf (as frisking round), especially one nearly grown (i.e. a steer)\nKJV: bullock, calf.\n\nCognate Group: H4570 (going), H5696 (round), H5700 (Eglon), H5699 (cart), H5697 (calf), H5695 (bullock), H5698 (Eglah), H5694 (earring)\nGreek Equivalents: G1151 δάμαλις, G3448 μόσχος",
    5696: "עָגֹל (ʻâgôl | aw-gole')\n\nDerivation: or עָגֹול; from an unused root meaning to revolve,\nStrong's: circular\nKJV: round.\n\nCognate Group: H4570 (going), H5696 (round), H5700 (Eglon), H5699 (cart), H5697 (calf), H5695 (bullock), H5698 (Eglah), H5694 (earring)",
    5697: "עֶגְלָה (ʻeglâh | eg-law')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5695 עֵגֶל\nStrong's: a (female) calf, especially one nearly grown (i.e. a heifer)\nKJV: calf, cow, heifer.\n\nCognate Group: H4570 (going), H5696 (round), H5700 (Eglon), H5699 (cart), H5697 (calf), H5695 (bullock), H5698 (Eglah), H5694 (earring)\nGreek Equivalents: G1151 δάμαλις",
    5698: "עֶגְלָה (ʻEglâh | eg-law')\n\nDerivation: the same as H5697 עֶגְלָה\nStrong's: Eglah, a wife of David\nKJV: Eglah.\n\nCognate Group: H4570 (going), H5696 (round), H5700 (Eglon), H5699 (cart), H5697 (calf), H5695 (bullock), H5698 (Eglah), H5694 (earring)\nGreek Equivalents: G4765 στρουθίον",
    5699: "עֲגָלָה (ʻăgâlâh | ag-aw-law')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5696 עָגֹל\nStrong's: something revolving, i.e. a wheeled vehicle\nKJV: cart, chariot, wagon\n\nCognate Group: H4570 (going), H5696 (round), H5700 (Eglon), H5699 (cart), H5697 (calf), H5695 (bullock), H5698 (Eglah), H5694 (earring)\nGreek Equivalents: G2375 θυρεός",
    5700: "עֶגְלֹון (ʻEglôwn | eg-lawn')\n\nDerivation: from H5695 עֵגֶל ; vituline\nStrong's: Eglon, the name of a place in Palestine and of a Moabitish king\nKJV: Eglon.\n\nCognate Group: H4570 (going), H5696 (round), H5700 (Eglon), H5699 (cart), H5697 (calf), H5695 (bullock), H5698 (Eglah), H5694 (earring)",
    5701: "עָגַם (ʻâgam | aw-gam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be sad\nKJV: grieve.\n\nCognate Group: H5701 (grieve)\nGreek Equivalents: G3076 λυπέω, G4727 στενάζω",
    5702: "עָגַן (ʻâgan | aw-gan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to debar, i.e. from marriage\nKJV: stay.\n\nCognate Group: H5702 (stay)\nGreek Equivalents: G2722 κατέχω",
    5703: "עַד (ʻad | ad)\n\nDerivation: from H5710 עָדָה\nStrong's: properly, a (peremptory) terminus, i.e. (by implication) duration, in the sense of advance or perpetuity (substantially as a noun, either with or without a preposition)\nKJV: eternity, ever(-lasting, -more), old, perpetually, [phrase] world without end.\n\nCognate Group: H5728 (yet), H5710 (adorn), H5704 (against), H5703 (eternity), H5706 (prey)\nGreek Equivalents: G165 αἰών",
    5704: "עַד (ʻad | ad)\n\nDerivation: properly, the same as H5703 עַד (used as a preposition, adverb or conjunction; especially with a preposition)\nStrong's: as far (or long, or much) as, whether of space (even unto) or time (during, while, until) or degree (equally with)\nKJV: against, and, as, at, before, by (that), even (to), for(-asmuch as), (hither-) to, [phrase] how long, into, as long (much) as, (so) that, till, toward, until, when, while, ([phrase] as) yet.\n\nCognate Group: H5728 (yet), H5710 (adorn), H5704 (against), H5703 (eternity), H5706 (prey)\nGreek Equivalents: G1900 ἐπέκεινα, G2094 ἔτος, G2540 καιρός, G3029 λίαν, G4206 πόῤῥω, G4208 ποῤῥωτέρω, G4404 πρωΐ, G4970 σφόδρα, G4970 σφόδρα, G5056 τέλος, G5101 τίς, G5550 χρόνος, G5550 χρόνος",
    5705: "עַד (ʻad | ad)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5704 עַד \nStrong's: as far (or long, or much) as, whether of space (even unto) or time (during, while, until) or degree (equally with)\nKJV: [idiom] and, at, for, (hither-) to, on till, (un-) to, until, within.\n\nCognate Group: H5705 ([idiom] and), H5732 (time)",
    5706: "עַד (ʻad | ad)\n\nDerivation: the same as H5703 עַד in the sense of the aim of an attack\nStrong's: booty\nKJV: prey.\n\nCognate Group: H5728 (yet), H5710 (adorn), H5704 (against), H5703 (eternity), H5706 (prey)",
    5707: "עֵד (ʻêd | ayd)\n\nDerivation: contracted from H5749 עוּד\nStrong's: concretely, a witness; abstractly, testimony; specifically, a recorder, i.e. prince\nKJV: witness.\n\nCognate Group: H5713 (testimony), H5707 (witness), H8584 (testimony), H5749 (admonish), H5715 (testimony), H5750 (again), H5752 (Oded)\nGreek Equivalents: G3140 μαρτυρέω, G3141 μαρτυρία, G3142 μαρτύριον, G3144 μάρτυς",
    5708: "עֵד (ʻêd | ayd)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to set a period (compare H5710 עָדָה, H5749 עוּד)\nStrong's: the menstrual flux (as periodical); by implication (in plural) soiling\nKJV: filthy.\n\nCognate Group: H5708 (filthy), H5714 (Iddo)",
    5709: "עֲדָא (ʻădâʼ | ad-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or עֲדָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to H5710 עָדָה \nStrong's: to advance, i.e. pass on or continue; causatively, to remove; specifically, to bedeck (i.e. bring an ornament upon)\nKJV: alter, depart, pass (away), remove, take (away).\n\nCognate Group: H5709 (alter)",
    5710: "עָדָה (ʻâdâh | aw-daw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to advance, i.e. pass on or continue; causatively, to remove; specifically, to bedeck (i.e. bring an ornament upon)\nKJV: adorn, deck (self), pass by, take away.\n\nCognate Group: H5728 (yet), H5710 (adorn), H5704 (against), H5703 (eternity), H5706 (prey)\nGreek Equivalents: G142 αἴρω, G353 ἀναλαμβάνω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G1949 ἐπιλαμβάνομαι, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G2885 κοσμέω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3179 μεθίστημι, G3306 μένω, G3928 παρέρχομαι, G4060 περιτίθημι",
    5711: "עָדָה (ʻÂdâh | aw-daw')\n\nDerivation: from H5710 עָדָה ; ornament\nStrong's: Adah, the name of two women\nKJV: Adah.\n\nCognate Group: H5710 (adorn), H5711 (Adah), H5717 (Adiel), H5716 ([idiom] excellent), H5723 (Adithaim), H5718 (Adaiah)",
    5712: "עֵדָה (ʻêdâh | ay-daw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5707 עֵד in the original sense of fixture\nStrong's: a stated assemblage (specifically, a concourse, or generally, a family or crowd)\nKJV: assembly, company, congregation, multitude, people, swarm. Compare H5713 עֵדָה .\n\nCognate Group: H5129 (Noadiah), H4151 (appointed time), H4150 (appointed), H3259 (agree), H4152 (appointed), H5712 (assembly), H3260 (Iddo See H3035)\nGreek Equivalents: G1999 ἐπισύστασις, G3925 παρεμβολή, G4864 συναγωγή, G4963 συστροφή",
