    5716: "עֲדִי (ʻădîy | ad-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H5710 עָדָה in the sense of trappings\nStrong's: finery; generally an outfit; specifically, a headstall\nKJV: [idiom] excellent, mouth, ornament.\n\nCognate Group: H5710 (adorn), H5711 (Adah), H5717 (Adiel), H5716 ([idiom] excellent), H5723 (Adithaim), H5718 (Adaiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G1939 ἐπιθυμία, G2889 κόσμος, G2889 κόσμος, G4749 στολή, G78 Ἀδδί",
