    5768: "עֹולֵל (ʻôwlêl | o-lale')\n\nDerivation: or עֹלָל; from H5763 עוּל\nStrong's: a suckling\nKJV: babe, (young) child, infant, little one.\n\nCognate Group: H5768 (babe), H5953 (abuse)\nGreek Equivalents: G3516 νήπιος, G5043 τέκνον",
    5769: "עֹולָם (ʻôwlâm | o-lawm')\n\nDerivation: or עֹלָם; from H5956 עָלַם\nStrong's: properly, concealed, i.e. the vanishing point; generally, time out of mind (past or future), i.e. (practically) eternity; frequentatively, adverbial (especially with prepositional prefix) always\nKJV: alway(-s), ancient (time), any more, continuance, eternal, (for, (n-)) ever(-lasting, -more, of old), lasting, long (time), (of) old (time), perpetual, at any time, (beginning of the) world ([phrase] without end). Compare H5331 נֶצַח, H5703 עַד .\n\nCognate Group: H5865 (ever), H5769 (alway)\nGreek Equivalents: G104 ἀεί, G165 αἰών, G166 αἰώνιος, G746 ἀρχή",
