    5771: "עָוֺן (ʻâvôn | aw-vone')\n\nDerivation: or עָוֹון; (2 Kings 7:9; Psalm 51:5 (H7 אֲבַד)), from H5753 עָוָה\nStrong's: perversity, i.e. (moral) evil\nKJV: fault, iniquity, mischeif, punishment (of iniquity), sin.\n\nCognate Group: H5755 (Ava), H5757 (Avims), H5753 (do amiss), H5771 (fault)\nGreek Equivalents: G52 ἄγνοια, G92 ἀδίκημα, G93 ἀδικία, G156 αἰτία, G264 ἁμαρτάνω, G265 ἁμάρτημα, G266 ἁμαρτία, G458 ἀνομία, G459 ἄνομος, G763 ἀσέβεια, G819 ἀτιμία, G3892 παρανομία",
    5772: "עֹונָה (ʻôwnâh | o-naw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root apparently meaning to dwell together\nStrong's: sexual (cohabitation)\nKJV: duty of marriage.\n\nCognate Group: H3282 (because), H6261 (fit), H6256 (after), H5772 (duty of marriage), H4616 (because of), H6258 (henceforth), H6278 (Ittahkazin), H4617 (answer), H6030 (give account), H6262 (Attai)\nGreek Equivalents: G3657 ὁμιλία",
