    5849: "עָטַר (ʻâṭar | aw-tar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to encircle (for attack or protection); especially to crown (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: compass, crown.\n\nCognate Group: H5855 (Atroth), H5852 (Ataroth), H5854 (Ataroth the house of Joab), H5850 (crown), H5853 (Ataroth-adar), H5851 (Atarah), H5849 (compass)",
    5850: "עֲטָרָה (ʻăṭârâh | at-aw-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H5849 עָטַר\nStrong's: a crown\nKJV: crown.\n\nCognate Group: H5855 (Atroth), H5852 (Ataroth), H5854 (Ataroth the house of Joab), H5850 (crown), H5853 (Ataroth-adar), H5851 (Atarah), H5849 (compass)\nGreek Equivalents: G4735 στέφανος",
    5851: "עֲטָרָה (ʻĂṭârâh | at-aw-raw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H5850 עֲטָרָה\nStrong's: Atarah, an Israelitess\nKJV: Atarah.\n\nCognate Group: H5855 (Atroth), H5852 (Ataroth), H5854 (Ataroth the house of Joab), H5850 (crown), H5853 (Ataroth-adar), H5851 (Atarah), H5849 (compass)",
    5852: "עֲטָרֹות (ʻĂṭârôwth | at-aw-roth')\n\nDerivation: or עֲטָרֹת; plural of H5850 עֲטָרָה\nStrong's: Ataroth, the name (thus simply) of two places in Palestine\nKJV: Ataroth.\n\nCognate Group: H5855 (Atroth), H5852 (Ataroth), H5854 (Ataroth the house of Joab), H5850 (crown), H5853 (Ataroth-adar), H5851 (Atarah), H5849 (compass)",
