    5854: "עַטְרֹות בֵּית יֹואָב (ʻAṭrôwth bêyth Yôwʼâb | at-roth' bayth yoawb')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5852 עֲטָרֹות and H1004 בַּיִת and H3097 יֹואָב ; crowns of the house of Joab\nStrong's: Atroth-beth-Joab, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Ataroth the house of Joab.\n\nCognate Group: H5855 (Atroth), H5852 (Ataroth), H5854 (Ataroth the house of Joab), H5850 (crown), H5853 (Ataroth-adar), H5851 (Atarah), H5849 (compass)",
    5855: "עַטְרֹות שֹׁופָן (ʻAṭrôwth Shôwphân | at-roth' sho-fawn')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5852 עֲטָרֹות and a name otherwise unused (being from the same as H8226 שָׂפַן) meaning hidden; crowns of Shophan\nStrong's: Atroth-Shophan, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Atroth, Shophan (as if two places).\n\nCognate Group: H5855 (Atroth), H5852 (Ataroth), H5854 (Ataroth the house of Joab), H5850 (crown), H5853 (Ataroth-adar), H5851 (Atarah), H5849 (compass)",
    5856: "עִי (ʻîy | ee)\n\nDerivation: from H5753 עָוָה\nStrong's: a ruin (as if overturned)\nKJV: heap.\n\nCognate Group: H4596 (heap), H5754 ([idiom] overturn), H1164 (grave), H5856 (heap), H5753 (do amiss), H5773 ([idiom] perverse)",
    5857: "עַי (ʻAy | ah'ee)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) עַיָּא; (Nehemiah 11:31), or עַיָּת; (Isaiah 10:28), for H5856 עִי\nStrong's: Ai, Aja or Ajath, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Ai, Aija, Aijath, Hai.\n\nCognate Group: H5859 (Ijon), H5857 (Ai), H5846 (sneezing)",
    5858: "עֵיבָל (ʻÊybâl | ay-bawl')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from an unused root probably meaning to be bald; bare\nStrong's: Ebal, a mountain of Palestine\nKJV: Ebal.\n\nCognate Group: H5858 (Ebal), H5745 (Obal)",
    5859: "עִיֹּון (ʻÎyôwn | ee-yone')\n\nDerivation: from H5856 עִי ; ruin\nStrong's: Ijon, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Ijon.\n\nCognate Group: H5859 (Ijon), H5857 (Ai), H5846 (sneezing)",
    5860: "עִיט (ʻîyṭ | eet)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to swoop down upon (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: fly, rail.\n\nCognate Group: H5863 (Ije-abarim), H5860 (fly), H5867 (Elam), H5861 (bird), H5866 (Ilai), H5862 (Etam), H5864 (Iim), H5868 (mighty)\nGreek Equivalents: G2827 κλίνω, G3729 ὁρμάω",
