    5927: "עָלָה (ʻâlâh | aw-law')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to ascend, intransitively (be high) or actively (mount); used in a great variety of senses, primary and secondary, literal and figurative\nKJV: arise (up), (cause to) ascend up, at once, break (the day) (up), bring (up), (cause to) burn, carry up, cast up, [phrase] shew, climb (up), (cause to, make to) come (up), cut off, dawn, depart, exalt, excel, fall, fetch up, get up, (make to) go (away, up); grow (over) increase, lay, leap, levy, lift (self) up, light, (make) up, [idiom] mention, mount up, offer, make to pay, [phrase] perfect, prefer, put (on), raise, recover, restore, (make to) rise (up), scale, set (up), shoot forth (up), (begin to) spring (up), stir up, take away (up), work.\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H5941 (Eli), H5942 (upper), H131 (Adummim), H5930 (ascent), H5940 (pestle), H4610 (Maaleh-accrabim), H4607 (lifting up), H5935 (Alian), H5927 (arise), H8585 (conduit), H4605 (above), H4609 (things that come up), H5920 (above), H4608 (ascent), H5944 (ascent), H5929 (branch), H5945 (high), H5933 (Aliah)\nGreek Equivalents: G71 ἄγω, G91 ἀδικέω, G305 ἀναβαίνω, G307 ἀναβιβάζω, G321 ἀνάγω, G353 ἀναλαμβάνω, G381 ἀνάπτω, G385 ἀνασπάω, G399 ἀναφέρω, G450 ἀνίστημι, G565 ἀπέρχομαι, G643 ἀποσκευάζω, G685 ἀρά, G868 ἀφίστημι, G1096 γίνομαι, G1125 γράφω, G1224 διαβαίνω, G1525 εἰσέρχομαι, G1531 εἰσπορεύομαι, G1544 ἐκβάλλω, G1684 ἐμβαίνω, G1744 ἐνδύνω, G1746 ἐνδύω, G1806 ἐξάγω, G1831 ἐξέρχομαι, G1831 ἐξέρχομαι, G1844 ἐξορκίζω, G1863 ἐπάγω, G1869 ἐπαίρω, G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G1910 ἐπιβαίνω, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G2240 ἥκω, G2325 θερίζω, G2354 θρηνέω, G2476 ἵστημι, G2545 καίω, G2671 κατάρα, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3727 ὅρκος, G3728 ὁρκωμοσία, G3928 παρέρχομαι, G4160 ποιέω, G4198 πορεύομαι, G4319 προσαιτέω, G4374 προσφέρω, G4863 συνάγω, G4872 συναναβαίνω, G5087 τίθημι, G5229 ὑπεραίρομαι, G5251 ὑπερυψόω, G5306 ὕστερος, G5307 ὑφαντός, G5342 φέρω, G5453 φύω",
    5928: "עֲלָה (ʻălâh | al-law')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5930 עֹלָה\nStrong's: a holocaust\nKJV: burnt offering.\n\nCognate Group: H5952 (chamber), H5946 (Most high), H5943 (high), H5928 (burnt offering)",
    5929: "עָלֶה (ʻâleh | aw-leh')\n\nDerivation: from H5927 עָלָה\nStrong's: a leaf (as coming up on a tree); collectively, foliage\nKJV: branch, leaf.\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H5941 (Eli), H5942 (upper), H131 (Adummim), H5930 (ascent), H5940 (pestle), H4610 (Maaleh-accrabim), H4607 (lifting up), H5935 (Alian), H5927 (arise), H8585 (conduit), H4605 (above), H4609 (things that come up), H5920 (above), H4608 (ascent), H5944 (ascent), H5929 (branch), H5945 (high), H5933 (Aliah)\nGreek Equivalents: G5444 φύλλον",
    5930: "עֹלָה (ʻôlâh | o-law')\n\nDerivation: or עֹולָה; feminine active participle of H5927 עָלָה\nStrong's: a step or (collectively, stairs, as ascending); usually a holocaust (as going up in smoke)\nKJV: ascent, burnt offering (sacrifice), go up to. See also H5766 עֶוֶל .\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H5941 (Eli), H5942 (upper), H131 (Adummim), H5930 (ascent), H5940 (pestle), H4610 (Maaleh-accrabim), H4607 (lifting up), H5935 (Alian), H5927 (arise), H8585 (conduit), H4605 (above), H4609 (things that come up), H5920 (above), H4608 (ascent), H5944 (ascent), H5929 (branch), H5945 (high), H5933 (Aliah)\nGreek Equivalents: G93 ἀδικία, G2378 θυσία, G3646 ὁλοκαύτωμα",
    5931: "עִלָּה (ʻillâh | il-law')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) feminine from a root corresponding to H5927 עָלָה\nStrong's: a pretext (as arising artificially)\nKJV: occasion.\n\nCognate Group: H5931 (occasion), H5924 (over), H5922 (about)\nGreek Equivalents: G266 ἁμαρτία, G4392 πρόφασις",
    5932: "עַלְוָה (ʻalvâh | al-vaw')\n\nDerivation: for H5766 עֶוֶל\nStrong's: moral perverseness\nKJV: iniquity.\n\nCognate Group: H5766 (iniquity), H5765 (deal unjustly), H5767 (unjust), H5760 (ungodly), H5932 (iniquity)",
    5933: "עַלְוָה (ʻAlvâh | al-vaw')\n\nDerivation: or עַליָה; the same as H5932 עַלְוָה\nStrong's: Alvah or Aljah, an Idumaean\nKJV: Aliah, Alvah.\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H5941 (Eli), H5942 (upper), H131 (Adummim), H5930 (ascent), H5940 (pestle), H4610 (Maaleh-accrabim), H4607 (lifting up), H5935 (Alian), H5927 (arise), H8585 (conduit), H4605 (above), H4609 (things that come up), H5920 (above), H4608 (ascent), H5944 (ascent), H5929 (branch), H5945 (high), H5933 (Aliah)",
    5934: "עָלוּם (ʻâlûwm | aw-loom')\n\nDerivation: passive participle of H5956 עָלַם in the denominative sense of H5958 עֶלֶם\nStrong's: (only in plural as abstract) adolescence; figuratively, vigor\nKJV: youth.\n\nCognate Group: H5959 (damsel), H5934 (youth), H5961 (Alamoth), H5958 (young man)\nGreek Equivalents: G3503 νεότης",
    5935: "עַלְוָן (ʻAlvân | al-vawn')\n\nDerivation: or עַלְיָן; from H5927 עָלָה ; lofty\nStrong's: Alvan or Aljan, an Idumaean\nKJV: Alian, Alvan.\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H5941 (Eli), H5942 (upper), H131 (Adummim), H5930 (ascent), H5940 (pestle), H4610 (Maaleh-accrabim), H4607 (lifting up), H5935 (Alian), H5927 (arise), H8585 (conduit), H4605 (above), H4609 (things that come up), H5920 (above), H4608 (ascent), H5944 (ascent), H5929 (branch), H5945 (high), H5933 (Aliah)\nGreek Equivalents: G1563 ἐκεῖ",
    5936: "עֲלוּקָה (ʻălûwqâh | al-oo-kaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of an unused root meaning to suck\nStrong's: the leech\nKJV: horse-leech.\n\nCognate Group: H5936 (horse-leech)",
    5937: "עָלַז (ʻâlaz | aw-laz')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to jump for joy, i.e. exult\nKJV: be joyful, rejoice, triumph.\n\nCognate Group: H5947 (joyous), H5938 (that rejoiceth), H5939 (dark), H5937 (be joyful)\nGreek Equivalents: G21 ἀγαλλιάω, G330 ἀναθάλλω, G1309 διαφεύγω, G2125 εὐλαβέομαι, G2620 κατακαυχάομαι, G2744 καυχάομαι, G5195 ὑβρίζω, G5312 ὑψόω, G5463 χαίρω",
    5938: "עָלֵז (ʻâlêz | aw-laze')\n\nDerivation: from H5937 עָלַז\nStrong's: exultant\nKJV: that rejoiceth.\n\nCognate Group: H5947 (joyous), H5938 (that rejoiceth), H5939 (dark), H5937 (be joyful)\nGreek Equivalents: G3061 λοιμός",
    5939: "עֲלָטָה (ʻălâṭâh | al-aw-taw')\n\nDerivation: feminine from an unused root meaning to cover\nStrong's: dusk\nKJV: dark, twilight.\n\nCognate Group: H5947 (joyous), H5938 (that rejoiceth), H5939 (dark), H5937 (be joyful)",
    5940: "עֱלִי (ʻĕlîy | el-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H5927 עָלָה\nStrong's: a pestle (as lifted)\nKJV: pestle.\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H5941 (Eli), H5942 (upper), H131 (Adummim), H5930 (ascent), H5940 (pestle), H4610 (Maaleh-accrabim), H4607 (lifting up), H5935 (Alian), H5927 (arise), H8585 (conduit), H4605 (above), H4609 (things that come up), H5920 (above), H4608 (ascent), H5944 (ascent), H5929 (branch), H5945 (high), H5933 (Aliah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2241 ἠλί",
    5941: "עֵלִי (ʻÊlîy | ay-lee')\n\nDerivation: from H5927 עָלָה ; lofty\nStrong's: Eli, an Israelite highpriest\nKJV: Eli.\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H5941 (Eli), H5942 (upper), H131 (Adummim), H5930 (ascent), H5940 (pestle), H4610 (Maaleh-accrabim), H4607 (lifting up), H5935 (Alian), H5927 (arise), H8585 (conduit), H4605 (above), H4609 (things that come up), H5920 (above), H4608 (ascent), H5944 (ascent), H5929 (branch), H5945 (high), H5933 (Aliah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2242 Ἡλί",
    5942: "עִלִּי (ʻillîy | il-lee')\n\nDerivation: from H5927 עָלָה\nStrong's: high; i.e. comparative\nKJV: upper.\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H5941 (Eli), H5942 (upper), H131 (Adummim), H5930 (ascent), H5940 (pestle), H4610 (Maaleh-accrabim), H4607 (lifting up), H5935 (Alian), H5927 (arise), H8585 (conduit), H4605 (above), H4609 (things that come up), H5920 (above), H4608 (ascent), H5944 (ascent), H5929 (branch), H5945 (high), H5933 (Aliah)",
    5943: "עִלַּי (ʻillay | il-lah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5942 עִלִּי\nStrong's: supreme (i.e. God)\nKJV: (most) high.\n\nCognate Group: H5952 (chamber), H5946 (Most high), H5943 (high), H5928 (burnt offering)\nGreek Equivalents: G2316 θεός",
    5944: "עֲלִיָּה (ʻălîyâh | al-ee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine from H5927 עָלָה\nStrong's: something lofty, i.e. a stair-way; also a second-story room (or even one on the roof); figuratively, the sky\nKJV: ascent, (upper) chamber, going up, loft, parlour.\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H5941 (Eli), H5942 (upper), H131 (Adummim), H5930 (ascent), H5940 (pestle), H4610 (Maaleh-accrabim), H4607 (lifting up), H5935 (Alian), H5927 (arise), H8585 (conduit), H4605 (above), H4609 (things that come up), H5920 (above), H4608 (ascent), H5944 (ascent), H5929 (branch), H5945 (high), H5933 (Aliah)\nGreek Equivalents: G1574 ἐκκεντέω",
    5945: "עֶלְיֹון (ʻelyôwn | el-yone')\n\nDerivation: from H5927 עָלָה\nStrong's: an elevation, i.e. (adj.) lofty (compar.); as title, the Supreme\nKJV: (Most, on) high(-er, -est), upper(-most).\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H5941 (Eli), H5942 (upper), H131 (Adummim), H5930 (ascent), H5940 (pestle), H4610 (Maaleh-accrabim), H4607 (lifting up), H5935 (Alian), H5927 (arise), H8585 (conduit), H4605 (above), H4609 (things that come up), H5920 (above), H4608 (ascent), H5944 (ascent), H5929 (branch), H5945 (high), H5933 (Aliah)\nGreek Equivalents: G511 ἀνώτερος, G1883 ἐπάνω, G2082 ἐσώτερος, G5231 ὑπεράνω, G5308 ὑψηλός, G5310 ὕψιστος",
    5946: "עֶלְיֹון (ʻelyôwn | el-yone')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5945 עֶלְיֹון\nStrong's: the Supreme\nKJV: Most high.\n\nCognate Group: H5952 (chamber), H5946 (Most high), H5943 (high), H5928 (burnt offering)",
    5947: "עַלִּיז (ʻallîyz | al-leez')\n\nDerivation: from H5937 עָלַז\nStrong's: exultant\nKJV: joyous, (that) rejoice(-ing)\n\nCognate Group: H5947 (joyous), H5938 (that rejoiceth), H5939 (dark), H5937 (be joyful)\nGreek Equivalents: G765 ἀσεβής, G4145 πλούσιος, G5196 ὕβρις",
    5948: "עֲלִיל (ʻălîyl | al-eel')\n\nDerivation: from H5953 עָלַל in the sense of completing\nStrong's: probably a crucible (as working over the metal)\nKJV: furnace.\n\nCognate Group: H5923 (yoke), H5948 (furnace), H5953 (abuse)\nGreek Equivalents: G1383 δοκίμιον",
    5949: "עֲלִילָה (ʻălîylâh | al-ee-law')\n\nDerivation: or עֲלִלָה; from H5953 עָלַל in the sense of effecting\nStrong's: an exploit (of God), or a performance (of man, often in a bad sense); by implication, an opportunity\nKJV: act(-ion), deed, doing, invention, occasion, work.\n\nCognate Group: H5955 (grapes), H5949 (act), H4611 (doing), H5950 (work), H8586 (babe), H5953 (abuse)\nGreek Equivalents: G266 ἁμαρτία, G458 ἀνομία, G763 ἀσέβεια, G1741 ἔνδοξος, G2041 ἔργον, G2108 εὐεργεσία, G2307 θέλημα, G3167 μεγαλεῖος, G4392 πρόφασις",
    5950: "עֲלִילִיָּה (ʻălîylîyâh | al-ee-lee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: for H5949 עֲלִילָה\nStrong's: (miraculous) execution\nKJV: work.\n\nCognate Group: H5955 (grapes), H5949 (act), H4611 (doing), H5950 (work), H8586 (babe), H5953 (abuse)\nGreek Equivalents: G5253 ὑπερῷον",
    5951: "עֲלִיצוּת (ʻălîytsûwth | al-ee-tsooth')\n\nDerivation: from H5970 עָלַץ\nStrong's: exultation\nKJV: rejoicing.\n\nCognate Group: H5970 (be joyful), H5951 (rejoicing)",
    5952: "עַלִּית (ʻallîyth | al-leeth')\n\nDerivation: from H5927 עָלָה\nStrong's: a second-story room\nKJV: chamber. Compare H5944 עֲלִיָּה .\n\nCognate Group: H5952 (chamber), H5946 (Most high), H5943 (high), H5928 (burnt offering)",
    5953: "עָלַל (ʻâlal | aw-lal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to effect thoroughly; specifically, to glean (also figuratively); by implication (in a bad sense) to overdo, i.e. maltreat, be saucy to, pain, impose (also literal)\nKJV: abuse, affect, [idiom] child, defile, do, glean, mock, practise, thoroughly, work (wonderfully).\n\nCognate Group: H5955 (grapes), H5949 (act), H4611 (doing), H5950 (work), H8586 (babe), H5953 (abuse)\nGreek Equivalents: G1096 γίνομαι, G1531 εἰσπορεύομαι, G1702 ἐμπαίζω, G2064 ἔρχομαι",
    5954: "עֲלַל (ʻălal | al-al')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5953 עָלַל (in the sense of thrusting oneself in),\nStrong's: to enter; causatively, to introduce\nKJV: bring in, come in, go in.\n\nCognate Group: H5957 (for ever), H5954 (bring in), H4606 (going down), H5972 (people), H5962 (Elamite), H5967 (rib)\nGreek Equivalents: G1521 εἰσάγω, G1525 εἰσέρχομαι, G1533 εἰσφέρω, G2564 καλέω",
    5955: "עֹלֵלָה (ʻôlêlâh | o-lay-law')\n\nDerivation: feminine active participle of H5953 עָלַל\nStrong's: only in plural gleanings; by extension gleaning-time\nKJV: (gleaning) (of the) grapes, grapegleanings.\n\nCognate Group: H5955 (grapes), H5949 (act), H4611 (doing), H5950 (work), H8586 (babe), H5953 (abuse)\nGreek Equivalents: G2562 καλάμη, G2640 κατάλειμμα",
    5956: "עָלַם (ʻâlam | aw-lam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to veil from sight, i.e. conceal (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: [idiom] any ways, blind, dissembler, hide (self), secret (thing).\n\nCognate Group: H8587 (thing that is hid), H5963 (Almondilathaim), H5956 ([idiom] any ways), H5960 (Almon), H3281 (Jalam), H5964 (Alameth)\nGreek Equivalents: G216 ἄλαλος, G613 ἀποκρύπτω, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G880 ἄφωνος, G1968 ἐπιπίπτω, G2660 κατανύσσω, G2928 κρύπτω, G2990 λανθάνω, G3871 παρακαλύπτω, G3891 παρανομέω, G3928 παρέρχομαι, G4623 σιωπάω, G4912 συνέχω, G5237 ὑπερείδω",
    5957: "עָלַם (ʻâlam | aw-lam')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5769 עֹולָם\nStrong's: remote time, i.e. the future or past indefinitely; often adverb, forever\nKJV: for (n-)ever (lasting), old.\n\nCognate Group: H5957 (for ever), H5954 (bring in), H4606 (going down), H5972 (people), H5962 (Elamite), H5967 (rib)",
    5958: "עֶלֶם (ʻelem | eh'-lem)\n\nDerivation: from H5956 עָלַם ; (compare H5959 עַלְמָה)\n\nStrong's: properly, something kept out of sight, i.e. a lad\nKJV: young man, stripling.\n\nCognate Group: H5959 (damsel), H5934 (youth), H5961 (Alamoth), H5958 (young man)\nGreek Equivalents: G3495 νεανίσκος",
    5959: "עַלְמָה (ʻalmâh | al-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H5958 עֶלֶם\nStrong's: a lass (as veiled or private)\nKJV: damsel, maid, virgin.\n\nCognate Group: H5959 (damsel), H5934 (youth), H5961 (Alamoth), H5958 (young man)\nGreek Equivalents: G3933 παρθένος",
    5960: "עַלְמֹון (ʻAlmôwn | al-mone')\n\nDerivation: from H5956 עָלַם ; hidden; See also H5963 עַלְמֹן דִּבְלָתָיְמָה .\nStrong's: Almon, a place in Palestine\n\nCognate Group: H8587 (thing that is hid), H5963 (Almondilathaim), H5956 ([idiom] any ways), H5960 (Almon), H3281 (Jalam), H5964 (Alameth)",
    5961: "עֲלָמֹות (ʻĂlâmôwth | al-aw-moth')\n\nDerivation: plural of H5959 עַלְמָה\nStrong's: properly, girls, i.e. the soprano or female voice, perhaps falsetto\nKJV: Alamoth.\n\nCognate Group: H5959 (damsel), H5934 (youth), H5961 (Alamoth), H5958 (young man)",
    5962: "עַלְמִי (ʻAlmîy | al-mee')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) patrial from a name corresponding to H5867 עֵילָם contracted\nStrong's: an Elamite or inhabitant of Elam\nKJV: Elamite.\n\nCognate Group: H5957 (for ever), H5954 (bring in), H4606 (going down), H5972 (people), H5962 (Elamite), H5967 (rib)",
    5963: "עַלְמֹן דִּבְלָתָיְמָה (ʻAlmôn Diblâthâyᵉmâh | al-mone' dib-lawthaw'-yem-aw)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5960 עַלְמֹון and the dual of H1960 הֻיְּדָה (compare H1015 בֵּית דִּבְלָתַיִם) with enclitic of direction; Almon towards Diblathajim\nStrong's: Almon-Diblathajemah, a place in Moab\nKJV: Almondilathaim.\n\nCognate Group: H8587 (thing that is hid), H5963 (Almondilathaim), H5956 ([idiom] any ways), H5960 (Almon), H3281 (Jalam), H5964 (Alameth)",
    5964: "עָלֶמֶת (ʻÂlemeth | aw-leh'-meth)\n\nDerivation: from H5956 עָלַם ; a covering\nStrong's: Alemeth, the name of a place in Palestine and of two Israelites\nKJV: Alameth, Alemeth.\n\nCognate Group: H8587 (thing that is hid), H5963 (Almondilathaim), H5956 ([idiom] any ways), H5960 (Almon), H3281 (Jalam), H5964 (Alameth)",
    5965: "עָלַס (ʻâlaç | aw-las')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to leap for joy, i.e. exult, wave joyously\nKJV: [idiom] peacock, rejoice, solace self.\n\nCognate Group: H5965 ([idiom] peacock)",
    5966: "עָלַע (ʻâlaʻ | aw-lah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to sip up\nKJV: suck up.\n\nCognate Group: H5966 (suck up)\nGreek Equivalents: G402 ἀναχωρέω, G2928 κρύπτω, G4125 πλευρά",
    5967: "עֲלַע (ʻălaʻ | al-ah')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H6763 צֵלָע\nStrong's: a rib\nKJV: rib.\n\nCognate Group: H5957 (for ever), H5954 (bring in), H4606 (going down), H5972 (people), H5962 (Elamite), H5967 (rib)",
    5968: "עָלַף (ʻâlaph | aw-laf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to veil or cover; figuratively, to be languid\nKJV: faint, overlaid, wrap self.\n\nCognate Group: H5968 (faint), H5969 (fainted)\nGreek Equivalents: G639 ἀπορέω, G1587 ἐκλείπω",
    5969: "עֻלְפֶּה (ʻulpeh | ool-peh')\n\nDerivation: from H5968 עָלַף\nStrong's: an envelope, i.e. (figuratively) mourning\nKJV: fainted.\n\nCognate Group: H5968 (faint), H5969 (fainted)\nGreek Equivalents: G1590 ἐκλύω, G1839 ἐξίστημι",
