    6064: "עָנַשׁ (ʻânash | aw-nash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to urge; by implication, to inflict apenalty, specifically, to fine\nKJV: amerce, condemn, punish, [idiom] surely.\n\nCognate Group: H6070 (Antothijah), H6067 (Anath), H6064 (amerce), H6069 (of Anathoth), H6068 (Anathoth), H6066 (punishment)\nGreek Equivalents: G972 βίαιος, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G2209 ζημία, G2210 ζημιόω, G4731 στερεός, G5099 τίνω, G5411 φόρος",
    6065: "עֲנַשׁ (ʻănash | an-ash')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H6066 עֹנֶשׁ\nStrong's: a mulct\nKJV: confiscation.\n\nCognate Group: H6065 (confiscation), H6050 (cloud), H6056 (bough), H5796 (goat)",
    6066: "עֹנֶשׁ (ʻônesh | o'-nesh)\n\nDerivation: from H6064 עָנַשׁ\nStrong's: a fine\nKJV: punishment, tribute.\n\nCognate Group: H6070 (Antothijah), H6067 (Anath), H6064 (amerce), H6069 (of Anathoth), H6068 (Anathoth), H6066 (punishment)\nGreek Equivalents: G2209 ζημία",
    6067: "עֲנָת (ʻĂnâth | an-awth')\n\nDerivation: from H6030 עָנָה ; answer\nStrong's: Anath, an Israelite\nKJV: Anath.\n\nCognate Group: H6070 (Antothijah), H6067 (Anath), H6064 (amerce), H6069 (of Anathoth), H6068 (Anathoth), H6066 (punishment)",
    6068: "עֲנָתֹות (ʻĂnâthôwth | an-aw-thoth')\n\nDerivation: plural of H6067 עֲנָת\nStrong's: Anathoth, the name of two Israelites, also of a place in Pal\nKJV: Anathoth.\n\nCognate Group: H6070 (Antothijah), H6067 (Anath), H6064 (amerce), H6069 (of Anathoth), H6068 (Anathoth), H6066 (punishment)",
    6069: "עַנְתֹתִי (ʻAnthôthîy | an-tho-thee')\n\nDerivation: or עַנְּתֹותִי; patrial from H6068 עֲנָתֹות\nStrong's: a Antothite or inhabitant of Anathoth\nKJV: of Anathoth, Anethothite, Anetothite, Antothite.\n\nCognate Group: H6070 (Antothijah), H6067 (Anath), H6064 (amerce), H6069 (of Anathoth), H6068 (Anathoth), H6066 (punishment)",
    6070: "עַנְתֹתִיָּה (ʻAnthôthîyâh | an-tho-thee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H6068 עֲנָתֹות and H3050 יָהּ ; answers of Jah\nStrong's: Anthothijah, an Israelite\nKJV: Antothijah.\n\nCognate Group: H6070 (Antothijah), H6067 (Anath), H6064 (amerce), H6069 (of Anathoth), H6068 (Anathoth), H6066 (punishment)",
    6071: "עָסִיס (ʻâçîyç | aw-sees')\n\nDerivation: from H6072 עָסַס\nStrong's: must or fresh grape-juice (as just trodden out)\nKJV: juice, new (sweet) wine.\n\nCognate Group: H6071 (juice), H6072 (tread down), H6073 (branch)\nGreek Equivalents: G3178 μέθη, G3501 νέος, G3631 οἶνος",
    6072: "עָסַס (ʻâçaç | aw-sas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to squeeze out juice; figuratively, to trample\nKJV: tread down.\n\nCognate Group: H6071 (juice), H6072 (tread down), H6073 (branch)\nGreek Equivalents: G2662 καταπατέω",
    6073: "עֳפֶא (ʻŏpheʼ | of-eh')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to cover\nStrong's: a bough (as covering the tree)\nKJV: branch.\n\nCognate Group: H6071 (juice), H6072 (tread down), H6073 (branch)",
    6074: "עֳפִי (ʻŏphîy | of-ee')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H6073 עֳפֶא\nStrong's: a twig; bough, i.e. (collectively) foliage\nKJV: leaves.\n\nCognate Group: H6074 (leaves)\nGreek Equivalents: G5444 φύλλον",
    6075: "עָפַל (ʻâphal | aw-fal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to swell; figuratively, be elated\nKJV: be lifted up, presume.\n\nCognate Group: H6077 (Ophel), H6075 (be lifted up), H6076 (emerod)\nGreek Equivalents: G5288 ὑποστέλλω",
    6076: "עֹפֶל (ʻôphel | o'-fel)\n\nDerivation: from H6075 עָפַל\nStrong's: a tumor; also a mound, i.e. fortress\nKJV: emerod, fort, strong hold, tower.\n\nCognate Group: H6077 (Ophel), H6075 (be lifted up), H6076 (emerod)",
