    6078: "עׇפְנִי (ʻOphnîy | of-nee')\n\nDerivation: from an unused noun (denoting a place in Palestine; from an unused root of uncertain meaning)\nStrong's: an Ophnite (collectively) or inhabitants of Ophen\nKJV: Ophni.\n\nCognate Group: H6075 (be lifted up), H6078 (Ophni)",
    6079: "עַפְעַף (ʻaphʻaph | af-af')\n\nDerivation: from H5774 עוּף\nStrong's: an eyelash (as fluttering); figuratively, morning ray\nKJV: dawning, eye-lid.\n\nCognate Group: H6079 (dawning), H5774 (brandish), H5775 (bird)\nGreek Equivalents: G393 ἀνατέλλω, G1491 εἶδος, G3788 ὀφθαλμός",
    6080: "עָפַר (ʻâphar | aw-far')\n\nDerivation: ; a primitive root; meaning either to be gray or perhaps rather to pulverize; used only as denominative from H6083 עָפָר,\nStrong's: to be dust\nKJV: cast (dust).\n\nCognate Group: H6080 (cast), H6083 (ashes)",
    6081: "עֵפֶר (ʻÊpher | ay'-fer)\n\nDerivation: probably a variation of H6082 עֹפֶר ; gazelle\nStrong's: Epher, the name of an Arabian and of two Israelites\nKJV: Epher.\n\nCognate Group: H6085 (Ephron), H6082 (young roe), H6081 (Epher), H6084 (Ophrah), H5777 (lead)",
    6082: "עֹפֶר (ʻôpher | o'-fer)\n\nDerivation: from H6080 עָפַר\nStrong's: a fawn (from the dusty color)\nKJV: young roe (hart).\n\nCognate Group: H6085 (Ephron), H6082 (young roe), H6081 (Epher), H6084 (Ophrah), H5777 (lead)",
    6083: "עָפָר (ʻâphâr | aw-fawr')\n\nDerivation: from H6080 עָפַר\nStrong's: dust (as powdered or gray); hence, clay, earth, mud\nKJV: ashes, dust, earth, ground, morter, powder, rubbish.\n\nCognate Group: H6080 (cast), H6083 (ashes)\nGreek Equivalents: G285 ἄμμος, G1093 γῆ, G1475 ἔδαφος, G2868 κονιορτός, G4081 πηλός, G5529 Χουζᾶς",
    6084: "עׇפְרָה (ʻOphrâh | of-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H6082 עֹפֶר ; female fawn\nStrong's: Ophrah, the name of an Israelite and of two places in Palestine\nKJV: Ophrah.\n\nCognate Group: H6085 (Ephron), H6082 (young roe), H6081 (Epher), H6084 (Ophrah), H5777 (lead)",
    6085: "עֶפְרֹון (ʻEphrôwn | ef-rone')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H6081 עֵפֶר ; fawn-like\nStrong's: Ephron, the name of a Canaanite and of two places in Palestine\nKJV: Ephron, Ephrain (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H6085 (Ephron), H6082 (young roe), H6081 (Epher), H6084 (Ophrah), H5777 (lead)\nGreek Equivalents: G2187 Ἐφραίμ",
    6086: "עֵץ (ʻêts | ates)\n\nDerivation: from H6095 עָצָה\nStrong's: a tree (from its firmness); hence, wood (plural sticks)\nKJV: [phrase] carpenter, gallows, helve, [phrase] pine, plank, staff, stalk, stick, stock, timber, tree, wood.\n\nCognate Group: H6097 (trees), H6086 (carpenter)\nGreek Equivalents: G1186 δένδρον, G2748 Κεδρών, G3585 ξύλινος, G3586 ξύλον, G4464 ῥάβδος",
    6087: "עָצַב (ʻâtsab | aw-tsab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to carve, i.e. fabricate or fashion; hence (in a bad sense) to worry, pain or anger\nKJV: displease, grieve, hurt, make, be sorry, vex, worship, wrest.\n\nCognate Group: H6094 (sorrow), H6089 (grievous), H6090 (idol), H6093 (sorrow), H4620 (sorrow), H6092 (labour), H6087 (displease)\nGreek Equivalents: G948 βδελύσσω, G1278 διαπονέω, G2352 θραύω, G2660 κατανύσσω, G2667 καταπίπτω, G3076 λυπέω, G3947 παροξύνω, G3949 παροργίζω, G4111 πλάσσω, G4160 ποιέω, G5013 ταπεινόω",
