    6090: "עֹצֶב (ʻôtseb | o'-tseb)\n\nDerivation: a variation of H6089 עֶצֶב\nStrong's: an idol (as fashioned); also pain (bodily or mental)\nKJV: idol, sorrow, [idiom] wicked.\n\nCognate Group: H6094 (sorrow), H6089 (grievous), H6090 (idol), H6093 (sorrow), H4620 (sorrow), H6092 (labour), H6087 (displease)\nGreek Equivalents: G458 ἀνομία, G1497 εἴδωλον",
    6091: "עָצָב (ʻâtsâb | aw-tsawb')\n\nDerivation: from H6087 עָצַב\nStrong's: an (idolatrous) image\nKJV: idol, image.\n\nCognate Group: H6089 (grievous), H6090 (idol), H6087 (displease), H6091 (idol)\nGreek Equivalents: G2316 θεός, G2478 ἰσχυρός, G2805 κλαυθμός, G3173 μέγας",
    6092: "עָצֵב (ʻâtsêb | aw-tsabe')\n\nDerivation: from H6087 עָצַב\nStrong's: a (hired) workman\nKJV: labour.\n\nCognate Group: H6094 (sorrow), H6089 (grievous), H6090 (idol), H6093 (sorrow), H4620 (sorrow), H6092 (labour), H6087 (displease)",
    6093: "עִצָּבֹון (ʻitstsâbôwn | its-tsaw-bone')\n\nDerivation: from H6087 עָצַב\nStrong's: worrisomeness, i.e. labor or pain\nKJV: sorrow, toil.\n\nCognate Group: H6094 (sorrow), H6089 (grievous), H6090 (idol), H6093 (sorrow), H4620 (sorrow), H6092 (labour), H6087 (displease)",
    6094: "עַצֶּבֶת (ʻatstsebeth | ats-tseh'-beth)\n\nDerivation: from H6087 עָצַב\nStrong's: a idol; also, a pain or wound\nKJV: sorrow, wound.\n\nCognate Group: H6094 (sorrow), H6089 (grievous), H6090 (idol), H6093 (sorrow), H4620 (sorrow), H6092 (labour), H6087 (displease)\nGreek Equivalents: G769 ἀσθένεια, G4938 σύντριμμα",
    6095: "עָצָה (ʻâtsâh | aw-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to fasten (or make firm), i.e. to close (the eyes)\nKJV: shut.\n\nCognate Group: H6095 (shut)",
    6096: "עָצֶה (ʻâtseh | aw-tseh')\n\nDerivation: from H6095 עָצָה\nStrong's: the spine (as giving firmness to the body)\nKJV: backbone.\n\nCognate Group: H6096 (backbone)",
    6097: "עֵצָה (ʻêtsâh | ay-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H6086 עֵץ\nStrong's: timber\nKJV: trees.\n\nCognate Group: H6097 (trees), H6086 (carpenter)",
