    6100: "עֶצְיֹון גֶּבֶר (ʻEtsyôwn Geber | ets-yone' gheh'ber)\n\nDerivation: from H6096 עָצֶה and H1397 גֶּבֶר ; backbone-like of a man\nStrong's: Etsjon-Geber, a place on the Red Sea\nKJV: Ezion-geber.\n\nCognate Group: H6100 (Ezion-geber)\nGreek Equivalents: G2039 ἐργασία",
    6101: "עָצַל (ʻâtsal | aw-tsal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to lean idly, i.e. to be indolent or slack\nKJV: be slothful.\n\nCognate Group: H6101 (be slothful), H6103 (slothfulness), H6102 (slothful), H6104 (idleness)",
