    6105: "עָצַם (ʻâtsam | aw-tsam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; also denominatively (from H6106 עֶצֶם)\n\nStrong's: to bind fast, i.e. close (the eyes); intransitively, to be (causatively, make) powerful or numerous; to crunch the bones\nKJV: break the bones, close, be great, be increased, be (wax) mighty(-ier), be more, shut, be(-come, make) strong(-er).\n\nCognate Group: H6099 (feeble), H8592 (power), H6106 (body), H6111 (Azmon), H6107 (Azem), H6105 (break the bones), H6108 (might), H6109 (abundance)\nGreek Equivalents: G1415 δυνατός, G2480 ἰσχύω, G2576 καμμύω, G2729 κατισχύω, G2900 κραταιός, G2901 κραταιόω, G4129 πληθύνω, G4732 στερεόω",
    6106: "עֶצֶם (ʻetsem | eh'tsem)\n\nDerivation: from H6105 עָצַם\nStrong's: a bone (as strong); by extension, the body; figuratively, the substance, i.e. (as pron.) selfsame\nKJV: body, bone, [idiom] life, (self-) same, strength, [idiom] very.\n\nCognate Group: H6099 (feeble), H8592 (power), H6106 (body), H6111 (Azmon), H6107 (Azem), H6105 (break the bones), H6108 (might), H6109 (abundance)\nGreek Equivalents: G1491 εἶδος, G2540 καιρός, G2904 κράτος, G3747 ὀστέον, G4125 πλευρά",
    6107: "עֶצֶם (ʻEtsem | eh'-tsem)\n\nDerivation: the same as H6106 עֶצֶם ; bone\nStrong's: Etsem, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Azem, Ezem.\n\nCognate Group: H6099 (feeble), H8592 (power), H6106 (body), H6111 (Azmon), H6107 (Azem), H6105 (break the bones), H6108 (might), H6109 (abundance)",
    6108: "עֹצֶם (ʻôtsem | o'-tsem)\n\nDerivation: from H6105 עָצַם\nStrong's: power; hence, body\nKJV: might, strong, substance.\n\nCognate Group: H6099 (feeble), H8592 (power), H6106 (body), H6111 (Azmon), H6107 (Azem), H6105 (break the bones), H6108 (might), H6109 (abundance)",
    6109: "עׇצְמָה (ʻotsmâh | ots-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H6108 עֹצֶם\nStrong's: powerfulness; by extension, numerousness\nKJV: abundance, strength.\n\nCognate Group: H6099 (feeble), H8592 (power), H6106 (body), H6111 (Azmon), H6107 (Azem), H6105 (break the bones), H6108 (might), H6109 (abundance)\nGreek Equivalents: G2479 ἰσχύς",
    6110: "עַצֻּמָה (ʻatstsumâh | ats-tsoo-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H6099 עָצוּם\nStrong's: a bulwark, i.e. (figuratively) argument\nKJV: strong.\n\nCognate Group: H6110 (strong)\nGreek Equivalents: G1012 βουλή",
    6111: "עַצְמֹון (ʻAtsmôwn | ats-mone')\n\nDerivation: or עַצְמֹן; from H6107 עֶצֶם ; bone-like\nStrong's: Atsmon, a place near Palestine\nKJV: Azmon.\n\nCognate Group: H6099 (feeble), H8592 (power), H6106 (body), H6111 (Azmon), H6107 (Azem), H6105 (break the bones), H6108 (might), H6109 (abundance)",
    6112: "עֵצֶן (ʻêtsen | ay'-tsen)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be sharp or strong\nStrong's: a spear\nKJV: Eznite (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H5731 (Eden), H5734 (Adnah), H5730 (delicate), H4574 (dainty), H5722 (Adino), H5721 (Adina), H5733 (Adna), H5719 (given to pleasures), H6112 (Eznite), H5727 (delight self), H5720 (Adin)",
    6113: "עָצָר (ʻâtsâr | aw-tsar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to inclose; by analogy, to hold back; also to maintain, rule, assemble\nKJV: [idiom] be able, close up, detain, fast, keep (self close, still), prevail, recover, refrain, [idiom] reign, restrain, retain, shut (up), slack, stay, stop, withhold (self).\n\nCognate Group: H4622 (restraint), H6116 (assembly), H6113 ([idiom] be able), H4623 (rule), H6114 (magistrate), H6115 ([idiom] barren)\nGreek Equivalents: G566 ἀπέχει, G567 ἀπέχομαι, G568 ἀπέχω, G757 ἄρχω, G971 βιάζω, G1210 δέω, G1410 δύναμαι, G1781 ἐντέλλομαι, G1907 ἐπέχω, G2192 ἔχω, G2343 θησαυρίζω, G2480 ἰσχύω, G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G2722 κατέχω, G2729 κατισχύω, G2869 κοπάζω, G2902 κρατέω, G2967 κωλύω, G3973 παύω, G4723 στείρος, G4863 συνάγω, G4912 συνέχω, G5442 φυλάσσω",
    6114: "עֶצֶר (ʻetser | eh'-tser)\n\nDerivation: from H6113 עָצָר\nStrong's: restraint\nKJV: [phrase] magistrate.\n\nCognate Group: H4622 (restraint), H6116 (assembly), H6113 ([idiom] be able), H4623 (rule), H6114 (magistrate), H6115 ([idiom] barren)",
    6115: "עֹצֶר (ʻôtser | o'-tser)\n\nDerivation: from H6113 עָצָר\nStrong's: closure; also constraint\nKJV: [idiom] barren, oppression, [idiom] prison.\n\nCognate Group: H4622 (restraint), H6116 (assembly), H6113 ([idiom] be able), H4623 (rule), H6114 (magistrate), H6115 ([idiom] barren)\nGreek Equivalents: G2347 θλῖψις, G5014 ταπείνωσις",
    6116: "עֲצָרָה (ʻătsârâh | ats-aw-raw')\n\nDerivation: or עֲצֶרֶת; from H6113 עָצָר\nStrong's: an assembly, especially on afestival or holiday\nKJV: (solemn) assembly (meeting).\n\nCognate Group: H4622 (restraint), H6116 (assembly), H6113 ([idiom] be able), H4623 (rule), H6114 (magistrate), H6115 ([idiom] barren)\nGreek Equivalents: G2322 θεραπεία, G3831 πανήγυρις",
    6117: "עָקַב (ʻâqab | aw-kab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; properly, to swell out or up; used only as denominative from H6119 עָקֵב,\nStrong's: to seize by the heel; figuratively, to circumvent (as if tripping up the heels); also to restrain (as if holding by the heel)\nKJV: take by the heel, stay, supplant, [idiom] utterly.\n\nCognate Group: H6121 (crooked), H6126 (Akkub), H3290 (Jacob), H6117 (take by the heel), H3291 (Jaakobah), H6120 (heel), H6119 (heel), H6118 ([idiom] because), H6122 (subtilty)",
    6118: "עֵקֶב (ʻêqeb | ay'-keb)\n\nDerivation: from H6117 עָקַב in the sense of H6119 עָקֵב\nStrong's: a heel, i.e. (figuratively) the last of anything (used adverbially, for ever); also result, i.e. compensation; and so (adverb with preposition or relatively) on account of\nKJV: [idiom] because, by, end, for, if, reward.\n\nCognate Group: H6121 (crooked), H6126 (Akkub), H3290 (Jacob), H6117 (take by the heel), H3291 (Jaakobah), H6120 (heel), H6119 (heel), H6118 ([idiom] because), H6122 (subtilty)\nGreek Equivalents: G469 ἀνταπόδοσις, G4133 πλήν",
    6119: "עָקֵב (ʻâqêb | aw-kabe')\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) עִקְּבָה; from H6117 עָקַב\nStrong's: a heel (as protuberant); hence, a track; figuratively, the rear (of an army)\nKJV: heel, (horse-) hoof, last, lier in wait (by mistake for H6120 עָקֵב), (foot-) step.\n\nCognate Group: H6121 (crooked), H6126 (Akkub), H3290 (Jacob), H6117 (take by the heel), H3291 (Jaakobah), H6120 (heel), H6119 (heel), H6118 ([idiom] because), H6122 (subtilty)\nGreek Equivalents: G2487 ἴχνος, G4228 πούς, G4418 πτέρνα",
    6120: "עָקֵב (ʻâqêb | aw-kabe')\n\nDerivation: from H6117 עָקַב in its denominative sense\nStrong's: a lier in wait\nKJV: heel (by mistake for H6119 עָקֵב).\n\nCognate Group: H6121 (crooked), H6126 (Akkub), H3290 (Jacob), H6117 (take by the heel), H3291 (Jaakobah), H6120 (heel), H6119 (heel), H6118 ([idiom] because), H6122 (subtilty)",
    6121: "עָקֹב (ʻâqôb | aw-kobe')\n\nDerivation: from H6117 עָקַב ; in the original sense, a knoll (as swelling up); in the denominative sense\nStrong's: (transitive) fraudulent or (intransitive) tracked\nKJV: crooked, deceitful, polluted.\n\nCognate Group: H6121 (crooked), H6126 (Akkub), H3290 (Jacob), H6117 (take by the heel), H3291 (Jaakobah), H6120 (heel), H6119 (heel), H6118 ([idiom] because), H6122 (subtilty)\nGreek Equivalents: G901 βαθύς, G3022 λευκός, G4646 σκολιός",
    6122: "עׇקְבָה (ʻoqbâh | ok-baw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of an unused form from H6117 עָקַב meaning a trick\nStrong's: trickery\nKJV: subtilty.\n\nCognate Group: H6121 (crooked), H6126 (Akkub), H3290 (Jacob), H6117 (take by the heel), H3291 (Jaakobah), H6120 (heel), H6119 (heel), H6118 ([idiom] because), H6122 (subtilty)",
    6123: "עָקַד (ʻâqad | aw-kad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tie with thongs\nKJV: bind.\n\nCognate Group: H6123 (bind)",
    6124: "עָקֹד (ʻâqôd | aw-kode')\n\nDerivation: from H6123 עָקַד\nStrong's: striped (with bands)\nKJV: ring straked.\n\nCognate Group: H6124 (ring straked)",
    6125: "עָקָה (ʻâqâh | aw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5781 עוּק\nStrong's: constraint\nKJV: oppression.\n\nCognate Group: H4157 (affliction), H5781 (be pressed), H6125 (oppression)\nGreek Equivalents: G2347 θλῖψις",
    6126: "עַקּוּב (ʻAqqûwb | ak-koob')\n\nDerivation: from H6117 עָקַב ; insidious\nStrong's: Akkub, the name of five Israelites\nKJV: Akkub.\n\nCognate Group: H6121 (crooked), H6126 (Akkub), H3290 (Jacob), H6117 (take by the heel), H3291 (Jaakobah), H6120 (heel), H6119 (heel), H6118 ([idiom] because), H6122 (subtilty)",
    6127: "עָקַל (ʻâqal | aw-kal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to wrest\nKJV: wrong.\n\nCognate Group: H6130 (Akan), H6127 (wrong), H6129 (crooked), H6128 (by), H3292 (Jaakan)\nGreek Equivalents: G1294 διαστρέφω",
    6128: "עֲקַלְקַל (ʻăqalqal | ak-al-kal')\n\nDerivation: from H6127 עָקַל\nStrong's: winding\nKJV: by(-way), crooked way.\n\nCognate Group: H6130 (Akan), H6127 (wrong), H6129 (crooked), H6128 (by), H3292 (Jaakan)",
    6129: "עֲקַלָּתֹון (ʻăqallâthôwn | ak-al-law-thone')\n\nDerivation: from H6127 עָקַל\nStrong's: tortuous\nKJV: crooked.\n\nCognate Group: H6130 (Akan), H6127 (wrong), H6129 (crooked), H6128 (by), H3292 (Jaakan)\nGreek Equivalents: G4646 σκολιός",
    6130: "עָקָן (ʻÂqân | aw-kawn')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to twist; tortuous\nStrong's: Akan, an Idummaean\nKJV: Akan. Compare H3292 יַעֲקָן .\n\nCognate Group: H6130 (Akan), H6127 (wrong), H6129 (crooked), H6128 (by), H3292 (Jaakan)",
    6131: "עָקַר (ʻâqar | aw-kar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to pluck up (especially by the roots); specifically, to hamstring; figuratively, to exterminate\nKJV: dig down, hough, pluck up, root up.\n\nCognate Group: H6133 (stock), H6139 (Ekronite), H6135 (barren), H6131 (dig down), H6137 (scorpion), H6134 (Eker), H6138 (Ekron)\nGreek Equivalents: G1610 ἐκριζόω, G3886 παραλύω",
    6132: "עֲקַר (ʻăqar | ak-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H6131 עָקַר \nStrong's: to pluck up (especially by the roots); specifically, to hamstring; figuratively, to exterminate\nKJV: pluck up by the roots.\n\nCognate Group: H6132 (pluck up by the roots), H6136 (stump)\nGreek Equivalents: G576 ἀποβαίνω",
    6133: "עֵקֶר (ʻêqer | ay'-ker)\n\nDerivation: from H6131 עָקַר\nStrong's: figuratively, a transplanted person, i.e. naturalized citizen\nKJV: stock.\n\nCognate Group: H6133 (stock), H6139 (Ekronite), H6135 (barren), H6131 (dig down), H6137 (scorpion), H6134 (Eker), H6138 (Ekron)\nGreek Equivalents: G1079 γενετή",
    6134: "עֵקֶר (ʻÊqer | ay'-ker)\n\nDerivation: the same as H6133 עֵקֶר\nStrong's: Eker, an Israelite\nKJV: Eker.\n\nCognate Group: H6133 (stock), H6139 (Ekronite), H6135 (barren), H6131 (dig down), H6137 (scorpion), H6134 (Eker), H6138 (Ekron)",
    6135: "עָקָר (ʻâqâr | aw-kawr')\n\nDerivation: from H6131 עָקַר\nStrong's: sterile (as if extirpated in the generative organs)\nKJV: ([idiom] male or female) barren (woman).\n\nCognate Group: H6133 (stock), H6139 (Ekronite), H6135 (barren), H6131 (dig down), H6137 (scorpion), H6134 (Eker), H6138 (Ekron)\nGreek Equivalents: G4723 στείρος",
    6136: "עִקַּר (ʻiqqar | ik-kar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H6132 עֲקַר\nStrong's: a stock\nKJV: stump.\n\nCognate Group: H6132 (pluck up by the roots), H6136 (stump)",
    6137: "עַקְרָב (ʻaqrâb | ak-rawb')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a scorpion; figuratively, a scourge or knotted whip\nKJV: scorpion.\n\nCognate Group: H6133 (stock), H6139 (Ekronite), H6135 (barren), H6131 (dig down), H6137 (scorpion), H6134 (Eker), H6138 (Ekron)\nGreek Equivalents: G4651 σκορπίος",
    6138: "עֶקְרֹון (ʻEqrôwn | ek-rone')\n\nDerivation: from H6131 עָקַר ; eradication\nStrong's: Ekron, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Ekron.\n\nCognate Group: H6133 (stock), H6139 (Ekronite), H6135 (barren), H6131 (dig down), H6137 (scorpion), H6134 (Eker), H6138 (Ekron)",
    6139: "עֶקְרֹונִי (ʻEqrôwnîy | ek-ro-nee')\n\nDerivation: or עֶקְרֹנִי; patrial from H6138 עֶקְרֹון\nStrong's: an Ekronite or inhabitant of Ekron\nKJV: Ekronite.\n\nCognate Group: H6133 (stock), H6139 (Ekronite), H6135 (barren), H6131 (dig down), H6137 (scorpion), H6134 (Eker), H6138 (Ekron)",
    6140: "עָקַשׁ (ʻâqash | aw-kash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to knot or distort; figuratively, to pervert (act or declare perverse)\nKJV: make crooked, (prove, that is) perverse(-rt).\n\nCognate Group: H6140 (make crooked), H6142 (Ikkesh), H6141 (crooked), H6144 (Ar), H6143 ([idiom] froward), H6145 (enemy), H4625 (crooked thing)\nGreek Equivalents: G1294 διαστρέφω, G4646 σκολιός",
    6141: "עִקֵּשׁ (ʻiqqêsh | ik-kashe')\n\nDerivation: from H6140 עָקַשׁ\nStrong's: distorted; hence, false\nKJV: crooked, froward, perverse.\n\nCognate Group: H6140 (make crooked), H6142 (Ikkesh), H6141 (crooked), H6144 (Ar), H6143 ([idiom] froward), H6145 (enemy), H4625 (crooked thing)\nGreek Equivalents: G4646 σκολιός, G4646 σκολιός",
    6142: "עִקֵּשׁ (ʻIqqêsh | ik-kashe')\n\nDerivation: the same as H6141 עִקֵּשׁ ; perverse\nStrong's: Ikkesh, an Israelite\nKJV: Ikkesh.\n\nCognate Group: H6140 (make crooked), H6142 (Ikkesh), H6141 (crooked), H6144 (Ar), H6143 ([idiom] froward), H6145 (enemy), H4625 (crooked thing)",
    6143: "עִקְּשׁוּת (ʻiqqᵉshûwth | ik-kesh-ooth')\n\nDerivation: from H6141 עִקֵּשׁ\nStrong's: perversity\nKJV: [idiom] froward.\n\nCognate Group: H6140 (make crooked), H6142 (Ikkesh), H6141 (crooked), H6144 (Ar), H6143 ([idiom] froward), H6145 (enemy), H4625 (crooked thing)\nGreek Equivalents: G18 ἀγαθός",
    6144: "עָר (ʻÂr | awr)\n\nDerivation: the same as H5892 עִיר ; a city\nStrong's: Ar, a place in Moab\nKJV: Ar.\n\nCognate Group: H6140 (make crooked), H6142 (Ikkesh), H6141 (crooked), H6144 (Ar), H6143 ([idiom] froward), H6145 (enemy), H4625 (crooked thing)",
    6145: "עָר (ʻâr | awr)\n\nDerivation: from H5782 עוּר\nStrong's: a foe (as watchful for mischief)\nKJV: enemy.\n\nCognate Group: H6140 (make crooked), H6142 (Ikkesh), H6141 (crooked), H6144 (Ar), H6143 ([idiom] froward), H6145 (enemy), H4625 (crooked thing)",
    6146: "עָר (ʻâr | awr)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H6145 עָר \nStrong's: a foe (as watchful for mischief)\nKJV: enemy.\n\nCognate Group: H6211 (moth), H6146 (enemy)\nGreek Equivalents: G2190 ἐχθρός",
    6147: "עֵר (ʻÊr | ayr)\n\nDerivation: from H5782 עוּר ; watchful\nStrong's: Er, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Er.\n\nCognate Group: H5782 (wake), H6197 (Eran), H6180 (Erites), H6179 (Eri), H6198 (Eranites), H6147 (Er), H3265 (Jair), H5892 (Ai)\nGreek Equivalents: G2262 Ἤρ",
    6148: "עָרַב (ʻârab | aw-rab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to braid, i.e. intermix; technically, to traffic (as if by barter); also or give to be security (as a kind of exchange)\nKJV: engage, (inter-) meddle (with), mingle (self), mortgage, occupy, give pledges, be(-come, put in) surety, undertake.\n\nCognate Group: H6162 (pledge), H6148 (engage), H8594 (hostage), H6161 (pledge), H4627 (market)\nGreek Equivalents: G700 ἀρέσκω, G1325 δίδωμι, G1551 ἐκδέχομαι, G1735 ἐνδέχεται, G1747 ἐνέδρα, G2073 ἑσπέρα, G2190 ἐχθρός, G2234 ἡδέως, G2340 θηρεύω, G2841 κοινωνέω, G3396 μίγνυμι, G3855 παράγω, G3973 παύω",
    6149: "עָרֵב (ʻârêb | aw-rabe')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (rather identical with H6148 עָרַב through the idea of close association)\nStrong's: to be agreeable\nKJV: be pleasant(-ing), take pleasure in, be sweet.\n\nCognate Group: H6156 (sweet), H6149 (be pleasant)",
    6150: "עָרַב (ʻârab | aw-rab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (rather identical with H6148 עָרַב through the idea of covering with a texture)\nStrong's: to grow dusky at sundown\nKJV: be darkened, (toward) evening.\n\nCognate Group: H6150 (be darkened), H6153 (day), H4628 (west)",
    6151: "עֲרַב (ʻărab | ar-ab')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H6148 עָרַב\nStrong's: to commingle\nKJV: mingle (self), mix.\n\nCognate Group: H6151 (mingle), H6167 (wild ass), H6173 (dishonor)",
    6152: "עֲרָב (ʻĂrâb | ar-awb')\n\nDerivation: or עֲרַב; from H6150 עָרַב in the figurative sense of sterility\nStrong's: Arab (i.e. Arabia), a country East of Palestine\nKJV: Arabia.\n\nCognate Group: H6160 (Arabah), H6152 (Arabia), H6163 (Arabian)\nGreek Equivalents: G688 Ἀραβία",
    6153: "עֶרֶב (ʻereb | eh'-reb)\n\nDerivation: from H6150 עָרַב\nStrong's: dusk\nKJV: [phrase] day, even(-ing, tide), night.\n\nCognate Group: H6150 (be darkened), H6153 (day), H4628 (west)\nGreek Equivalents: G2073 ἑσπέρα, G2073 ἑσπέρα, G2250 ἡμέρα, G3796 ὀψέ",
    6154: "עֵרֶב (ʻêreb | ay'-reb)\n\nDerivation: or עֶרֶב; (1 Kings 10:15), (with the article [prefix), from H6148 עָרַב\nStrong's: the web (or transverse threads of cloth); also a mixture, (or mongrel race)\nKJV: Arabia, mingled people, mixed (multitude), woof.\n\nCognate Group: H6157 (divers sorts of flies), H6154 (Arabia)",
    6155: "עָרָב (ʻârâb | aw-rawb')\n\nDerivation: from H6148 עָרַב\nStrong's: a willow (from the use of osiers as wattles)\nKJV: willow.\n\nCognate Group: H6159 (Oreb), H6158 (raven), H6155 (willow)",
    6156: "עָרֵב (ʻârêb | aw-rabe')\n\nDerivation: from H6149 עָרֵב\nStrong's: pleasant\nKJV: sweet.\n\nCognate Group: H6156 (sweet), H6149 (be pleasant)",
    6157: "עָרֹב (ʻârôb | aw-robe')\n\nDerivation: from H6148 עָרַב\nStrong's: a mosquito (from its swarming)\nKJV: divers sorts of flies, swarm.\n\nCognate Group: H6157 (divers sorts of flies), H6154 (Arabia)",
    6158: "עֹרֵב (ʻôrêb | o-rabe')\n\nDerivation: or עֹורֵב; from H6150 עָרַב\nStrong's: a raven (from its dusky hue)\nKJV: raven.\n\nCognate Group: H6159 (Oreb), H6158 (raven), H6155 (willow)\nGreek Equivalents: G2189 ἔχθρα, G2876 κόραξ",
    6159: "עֹרֵב (ʻÔrêb | o-rabe')\n\nDerivation: or עֹורֵב; the same as H6158 עֹרֵב\nStrong's: Oreb, the name of a Midianite and of the cliff near the Jordan\nKJV: Oreb.\n\nCognate Group: H6159 (Oreb), H6158 (raven), H6155 (willow)",
    6160: "עֲרָבָה (ʻărâbâh | ar-aw-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H6150 עָרַב (in the sense of sterility)\nStrong's: a desert; especially (with the article prefix) the (generally) sterile valley of the Jordan and its continuation to the Red Sea\nKJV: Arabah, champaign, desert, evening, heaven, plain, wilderness. See also H1026 בֵּית הָעֲרָבָה .\n\nCognate Group: H6160 (Arabah), H6152 (Arabia), H6163 (Arabian)\nGreek Equivalents: G552 ἄπειρος, G1093 γῆ, G1372 διψάω, G1424 δυσμή, G2048 ἔρημος",
    6161: "עֲרֻבָּה (ʻărubbâh | ar-oob-baw')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of H6048 עֲנַמֶּלֶךְ in the sense of a bargain or exchange\nStrong's: something given as security, i.e. (literally) a token (of safety) or (metaphorically) a bondsman\nKJV: pledge, surety.\n\nCognate Group: H6162 (pledge), H6148 (engage), H8594 (hostage), H6161 (pledge), H4627 (market)",
    6162: "עֲרָבֹון (ʻărâbôwn | ar-aw-bone')\n\nDerivation: from H6148 עָרַב (in the sense of exchange)\nStrong's: a pawn (given as security)\nKJV: pledge.\n\nCognate Group: H6162 (pledge), H6148 (engage), H8594 (hostage), H6161 (pledge), H4627 (market)\nGreek Equivalents: G728 ἀῤῥαβών",
    6163: "עֲרָבִי (ʻĂrâbîy | ar-aw-bee')\n\nDerivation: or עַרְבִי; patrial from H6152 עֲרָב\nStrong's: an Arabian or inhabitant of Arab (i.e. Arabia)\nKJV: Arabian.\n\nCognate Group: H6160 (Arabah), H6152 (Arabia), H6163 (Arabian)",
    6164: "עַרְבָתִי (ʻArbâthîy | ar-baw-thee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H1026 בֵּית הָעֲרָבָה\nStrong's: an Arbathite or inhabitant of (Beth-) Arabah\nKJV: Arbahite.\n\nCognate Group: H1039 (Beth-Nimrah), H1055 (palace), H1004 (court), H1041 (Bethaz-maveth), H1054 (Beth-tappuah), H1053 (Beth-shemesh), H1052 (Beth-shean), H1048 (Beth-pazzez), H1024 (Bethmarcaboth), H1051 (Beth-rapha), H1012 (Beth-barah), H1194 (Beon), H1044 (shearing house), H1038 (Beth-maachah), H1040 (Beth-eden), H1050 (Beth-rehob), H358 (Elon-bethhanan), H1010 (Beth-baal-meon), H1046 (Beth-palet), H6407 (Paltite), H1033 (Beth-car), H1056 (Baca), H1016 (Beth-dagon), H1027 (Beth-aram), H1022 (Bethlehemite), H7462 ([idiom] break), H1008 (Beth-el), H1025 (Beth-emek), H1006 (Bajith), H1035 (Bethlehem), H2772 (Horonite), H1017 (Bethelite), H1031 (Beth-hoglah), H1013 (Beth-gader), H1023 (place that was far off), H1014 (Beth-gamul), H1032 (Beth-horon), H1057 (mulberry tree), H1028 (Beth-haran), H1049 (Beth-zur), H1026 (Beth-arabah), H1015 (Beth-diblathaim), H1034 (Beth-lebaoth), H1029 (Beth-shittah), H1030 (Bethshemite), H1011 (Bethbirei), H1043 (Beth-anath), H1042 (Beth-anoth), H6164 (Arbahite), H1047 (Bethpeor), H1020 (Beth-jeshimoth), H1036 (house of Aphrah), H1021 (Beth-haccerem), H1009 (Beth-Arbel), H1007 (Beth-aven)",
    6165: "עָרַג (ʻârag | aw-rag')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to long for\nKJV: cry, pant.\n\nCognate Group: H6170 (bed), H6166 (Arad), H6165 (cry)",
    6166: "עֲרָד (ʻĂrâd | ar-awd')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to sequester itself; fugitive\nStrong's: Arad, the name of a place near Palestine, also of a Canaanite and an Israelite\nKJV: Arad.\n\nCognate Group: H6170 (bed), H6166 (Arad), H6165 (cry)",
    6167: "עֲרָד (ʻărâd | ar-awd')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H6171 עָרֹוד\nStrong's: an onager\nKJV: wild ass.\n\nCognate Group: H6151 (mingle), H6167 (wild ass), H6173 (dishonor)",
    6168: "עָרָה (ʻârâh | aw-raw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be (causatively, make) bare; hence, to empty, pour out, demolish\nKJV: leave destitute, discover, empty, make naked, pour (out), rase, spread self, uncover.\n\nCognate Group: H4638 (Maarath), H6168 (leave destitute), H6181 (bare), H8593 (knife), H6172 (nakedness), H4629 (meadows), H4626 (nakedness), H6171 (wild ass), H6169 (paper reed)\nGreek Equivalents: G343 ἀνακαλύπτω, G601 ἀποκαλύπτω, G1869 ἐπαίρω, G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G3860 παραδίδωμι, G5166 τρυγάω, G5515 χλωρός",
    6169: "עָרָה (ʻârâh | aw-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine from H6168 עָרָה\nStrong's: a naked (i.e. level) plot\nKJV: paper reed.\n\nCognate Group: H4638 (Maarath), H6168 (leave destitute), H6181 (bare), H8593 (knife), H6172 (nakedness), H4629 (meadows), H4626 (nakedness), H6171 (wild ass), H6169 (paper reed)",
    6170: "עֲרוּגָה (ʻărûwgâh | ar-oo-gaw')\n\nDerivation: or עֲרֻגָה; feminine passive participle of H6165 עָרַג\nStrong's: something piled up (as if (figuratively) raised by mental aspiration), i.e. a paterre\nKJV: bed, furrow.\n\nCognate Group: H6170 (bed), H6166 (Arad), H6165 (cry)\nGreek Equivalents: G5357 φιάλη",
    6171: "עָרֹוד (ʻârôwd | aw-rode')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H6166 עֲרָד\nStrong's: an onager (from his lonesome habits)\nKJV: wild ass.\n\nCognate Group: H4638 (Maarath), H6168 (leave destitute), H6181 (bare), H8593 (knife), H6172 (nakedness), H4629 (meadows), H4626 (nakedness), H6171 (wild ass), H6169 (paper reed)",
    6172: "עֶרְוָה (ʻervâh | er-vaw')\n\nDerivation: from H6168 עָרָה\nStrong's: nudity, literally (especially the pudenda) or figuratively (disgrace, blemish)\nKJV: nakedness, shame, unclean(-ness).\n\nCognate Group: H4638 (Maarath), H6168 (leave destitute), H6181 (bare), H8593 (knife), H6172 (nakedness), H4629 (meadows), H4626 (nakedness), H6171 (wild ass), H6169 (paper reed)\nGreek Equivalents: G152 αἰσχύνη, G602 ἀποκάλυψις, G808 ἀσχημοσύνη, G809 ἀσχήμων, G2487 ἴχνος",
    6173: "עַרְוָה (ʻarvâh | ar-vaw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H6172 עֶרְוָה\nStrong's: nakedness, i.e. (figuratively) impoverishment\nKJV: dishonor.\n\nCognate Group: H6151 (mingle), H6167 (wild ass), H6173 (dishonor)",
    6174: "עָרֹום (ʻârôwm | aw-rome')\n\nDerivation: or עָרֹם; from H6191 עָרַם (in its original sense)\nStrong's: nude, either partially or totally\nKJV: naked.\n\nCognate Group: H6174 (naked), H5783 (be made naked), H4589 (nakedness), H4636 (naked), H5903 (naked)\nGreek Equivalents: G1131 γυμνός",
    6175: "עָרוּם (ʻârûwm | aw-room')\n\nDerivation: passive participle of H6191 עָרַם\nStrong's: cunning (usually in a bad sense)\nKJV: crafty, prudent, subtil.\n\nCognate Group: H6175 (crafty), H6193 (craftiness), H6195 (guile), H6191 ([idiom] very)\nGreek Equivalents: G3835 πανοῦργος, G4908 συνετός, G5429 φρόνιμος",
    6176: "עֲרֹועֵר (ʻărôwʻêr | ar-o-ayr')\n\nDerivation: or עַרְעָר; from H6209 עָרַר reduplicated\nStrong's: a juniper (from its nudity of situation)\nKJV: health.\n\nCognate Group: H6177 (Aroer), H6209 (make bare), H6199 (destitute), H5735 (Adadah), H6200 (Aroerite), H6185 (childless), H6176 (health)",
    6177: "עֲרֹועֵר (ʻĂrôwʻêr | ar-o-ayr')\n\nDerivation: or עֲרֹעֵר; or עַרְעֹור; the same as H6176 עֲרֹועֵר ; nudity of situation\nStrong's: Aroer, the name of three places in or near Palestine\nKJV: Aroer.\n\nCognate Group: H6177 (Aroer), H6209 (make bare), H6199 (destitute), H5735 (Adadah), H6200 (Aroerite), H6185 (childless), H6176 (health)",
    6178: "עָרוּץ (ʻârûwts | aw-roots')\n\nDerivation: passive participle of H6206 עָרַץ\nStrong's: feared, i.e. (concretely) a horrible place or chasm\nKJV: cliffs.\n\nCognate Group: H6206 (be affrighted), H6178 (cliffs), H4637 (terror), H6184 (mighty)",
    6179: "עֵרִי (ʻÊrîy | ay-ree')\n\nDerivation: from H5782 עוּר ; watchful\nStrong's: Eri, an Israelite\nKJV: Eri.\n\nCognate Group: H5782 (wake), H6197 (Eran), H6180 (Erites), H6179 (Eri), H6198 (Eranites), H6147 (Er), H3265 (Jair), H5892 (Ai)",
    6180: "עֵרִי (ʻÊrîy | ay-ree')\n\nDerivation: patronymically of H6179 עֵרִי\nStrong's: a Erite (collectively) or descendants of Eri\nKJV: Erites.\n\nCognate Group: H5782 (wake), H6197 (Eran), H6180 (Erites), H6179 (Eri), H6198 (Eranites), H6147 (Er), H3265 (Jair), H5892 (Ai)",
    6181: "עֶרְיָה (ʻeryâh | er-yaw')\n\nDerivation: for H6172 עֶרְוָה\nStrong's: nudity\nKJV: bare, naked, [idiom] quite.\n\nCognate Group: H4638 (Maarath), H6168 (leave destitute), H6181 (bare), H8593 (knife), H6172 (nakedness), H4629 (meadows), H4626 (nakedness), H6171 (wild ass), H6169 (paper reed)\nGreek Equivalents: G153 αἰσχύνομαι, G807 ἀσχημονέω",
    6182: "עֲרִיסָה (ʻărîyçâh | ar-ee-saw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to comminute\nStrong's: meal\nKJV: dough.\n\nCognate Group: H6182 (dough)\nGreek Equivalents: G4621 σῖτος, G5445 φύραμα",
    6183: "עָרִיף (ʻârîyph | aw-reef')\n\nDerivation: from H6201 עָרַף\nStrong's: the sky (as dropping at the horizon)\nKJV: heaven.\n\nCognate Group: H6183 (heaven), H6201 (drop), H6205 (dark)\nGreek Equivalents: G640 ἀπορία",
    6184: "עָרִיץ (ʻârîyts | aw-reets')\n\nDerivation: from H6206 עָרַץ\nStrong's: fearful, i.e. powerful or tyrannical\nKJV: mighty, oppressor, in great power, strong, terrible, violent.\n\nCognate Group: H6206 (be affrighted), H6178 (cliffs), H4637 (terror), H6184 (mighty)\nGreek Equivalents: G91 ἀδικέω, G459 ἄνομος, G1413 δυνάστης, G2478 ἰσχυρός, G2480 ἰσχύω, G2616 καταδυναστεύω, G2900 κραταιός, G3061 λοιμός, G5244 ὑπερήφανος, G5251 ὑπερυψόω, G5401 φόβος",
    6185: "עֲרִירִי (ʻărîyrîy | ar-e-ree')\n\nDerivation: from H6209 עָרַר\nStrong's: bare, i.e. destitute (of children)\nKJV: childless.\n\nCognate Group: H6177 (Aroer), H6209 (make bare), H6199 (destitute), H5735 (Adadah), H6200 (Aroerite), H6185 (childless), H6176 (health)\nGreek Equivalents: G815 ἄτεκνος",
    6186: "עָרַךְ (ʻârak | aw-rak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to set in a row, i.e. arrange, put in order (in a very wide variety of applications)\nKJV: put (set) (the battle, self) in array, compare, direct, equal, esteem, estimate, expert (in war), furnish, handle, join (battle), ordain, (lay, put, reckon up, set) (in) order, prepare, tax, value.\n\nCognate Group: H4633 (preparation), H4630 (army), H4634 (army), H6187 (equal), H6186 (put in array), H4635 (row)\nGreek Equivalents: G142 αἴρω, G353 ἀναλαμβάνω, G430 ἀνέχομαι, G997 βοηθέω, G1166 δεικνύω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2010 ἐπιτρέπω, G2090 ἑτοιμάζω, G2092 ἕτοιμος, G2545 καίω, G2885 κοσμέω, G3112 μακράν, G3114 μακροθυμέω, G3306 μένω, G3666 ὁμοιόω, G3903 παρασκευάζω, G3936 παρίστημι, G4023 περιέχω, G4115 πλατύνω, G4121 πλεονάζω, G4129 πληθύνω, G4369 προστίθημι, G4388 προτίθεμαι, G5091 τιμάω, G5242 ὑπερέχω, G5312 ὑψόω, G5465 χαλάω",
    6187: "עֵרֶךְ (ʻêrek | eh'rek)\n\nDerivation: from H6186 עָרַךְ\nStrong's: a pile, equipment, estimate\nKJV: equal, estimation, (things that are set in) order, price, proportion, [idiom] set at, suit, taxation, [idiom] valuest.\n\nCognate Group: H4633 (preparation), H4630 (army), H4634 (army), H6187 (equal), H6186 (put in array), H4635 (row)\nGreek Equivalents: G2201 ζεῦγος, G2473 ἰσόψυχος, G3115 μακροθυμία, G4286 πρόθεσις, G4749 στολή, G5092 τιμή",
    6188: "עָרֵל (ʻârêl | aw-rale')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; properly, to strip; but used as denominative from H6189 עָרֵל\nStrong's: to expose or remove the prepuce, whether literal (to go naked) or figurative (to refrain from using)\nKJV: count uncircumcised, foreskin to be uncovered.\n\nCognate Group: H6188 (count uncircumcised), H6189 (uncircumcised), H6190 (foreskin)",
    6189: "עָרֵל (ʻârêl | aw-rale')\n\nDerivation: from H6188 עָרֵל ; properly, exposed, i.e. projecting loose (as to the prepuce); used only technically,\nStrong's: uncircumcised (i.e. still having the prepuce uncurtailed)\nKJV: uncircumcised (person).\n\nCognate Group: H6188 (count uncircumcised), H6189 (uncircumcised), H6190 (foreskin)\nGreek Equivalents: G564 ἀπερίτμητος",
    6190: "עׇרְלָה (ʻorlâh | or-law')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H6189 עָרֵל\nStrong's: the prepuce\nKJV: foreskin, [phrase] uncircumcised.\n\nCognate Group: H6188 (count uncircumcised), H6189 (uncircumcised), H6190 (foreskin)\nGreek Equivalents: G167 ἀκαθαρσία, G203 ἀκροβυστία",
    6191: "עָרַם (ʻâram | aw-ram')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to be (or make) bare; but used only in the derivative sense (through the idea perhaps of smoothness) to be cunning (usually in a bad sense)\nKJV: [idiom] very, beware, take crafty (counsel), be prudent, deal subtilly.\n\nCognate Group: H6175 (crafty), H6193 (craftiness), H6195 (guile), H6191 ([idiom] very)\nGreek Equivalents: G246 ἀλλόφυλος, G1339 διΐστημι, G3835 πανοῦργος",
    6192: "עָרַם (ʻâram | aw-ram')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to pile up\nKJV: gather together.\n\nCognate Group: H6194 (heap), H6192 (gather together)",
    6193: "עֹרֶם (ʻôrem | o'-rem)\n\nDerivation: from H6191 עָרַם\nStrong's: a stratagem\nKJV: craftiness.\n\nCognate Group: H6175 (crafty), H6193 (craftiness), H6195 (guile), H6191 ([idiom] very)",
    6194: "עָרֵם (ʻârêm | aw-rame')\n\nDerivation: (Jeremiah 50:26) or (feminine) עֲרֵמָה; from H6192 עָרַם\nStrong's: a heap; specifically, a sheaf\nKJV: heap (of corn), sheaf.\n\nCognate Group: H6194 (heap), H6192 (gather together)\nGreek Equivalents: G2310 θεμέλιος",
    6195: "עׇרְמָה (ʻormâh | or-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H6193 עֹרֶם\nStrong's: trickery; or (in a good sense) discretion\nKJV: guile, prudence, subtilty, wilily, wisdom.\n\nCognate Group: H6175 (crafty), H6193 (craftiness), H6195 (guile), H6191 ([idiom] very)\nGreek Equivalents: G1012 βουλή, G1388 δόλος, G3834 πανουργία, G5428 φρόνησις",
    6196: "עַרְמֹון (ʻarmôwn | ar-mone')\n\nDerivation: probably from H6191 עָרַם\nStrong's: the plane tree (from its smooth and shed bark)\nKJV: chestnut tree.\n\nCognate Group: H6196 (chestnut tree)",
    6197: "עֵרָן (ʻÊrân | ay-rawn')\n\nDerivation: probably from H5782 עוּר ; watchful\nStrong's: Eran, an Israelite\nKJV: Eran.\n\nCognate Group: H5782 (wake), H6197 (Eran), H6180 (Erites), H6179 (Eri), H6198 (Eranites), H6147 (Er), H3265 (Jair), H5892 (Ai)",
    6198: "עֵרָנִי (ʻÊrânîy | ay-raw-nee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H6197 עֵרָן\nStrong's: an Eranite or descendant (collectively) of Eran\nKJV: Eranites.\n\nCognate Group: H5782 (wake), H6197 (Eran), H6180 (Erites), H6179 (Eri), H6198 (Eranites), H6147 (Er), H3265 (Jair), H5892 (Ai)",
    6199: "עַרעָר (ʻarʻâr | ar-awr')\n\nDerivation: from H6209 עָרַר\nStrong's: naked, i.e. (figuratively) poor\nKJV: destitute. See also H6176 עֲרֹועֵר .\n\nCognate Group: H6177 (Aroer), H6209 (make bare), H6199 (destitute), H5735 (Adadah), H6200 (Aroerite), H6185 (childless), H6176 (health)",
    6200: "עֲרֹעֵרִי (ʻĂrôʻêrîy | ar-o-ay-ree')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H6177 עֲרֹועֵר\nStrong's: an Aroerite or inhabitant of Aroer\nKJV: Aroerite.\n\nCognate Group: H6177 (Aroer), H6209 (make bare), H6199 (destitute), H5735 (Adadah), H6200 (Aroerite), H6185 (childless), H6176 (health)",
    6201: "עָרַף (ʻâraph | aw-raf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to droop; hence, to drip\nKJV: drop (down).\n\nCognate Group: H6183 (heaven), H6201 (drop), H6205 (dark)",
    6202: "עָרַף (ʻâraph | aw-raf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (identical with through the idea of sloping); properly, to bend downward; but used only as a denominative from H6203 עֹרֶף,\nStrong's: to break the neck; hence (figuratively) to destroy\nKJV: that is beheaded, break down, break (cut off, strike off) neck.\n\nCognate Group: H6202 (that is beheaded), H6204 (Orpah), H6203 (back neck)\nGreek Equivalents: G615 ἀποκτείνω, G2679 κατασκάπτω, G3084 λυτρόω",
    6203: "עֹרֶף (ʻôreph | o-ref')\n\nDerivation: from H6202 עָרַף\nStrong's: the nape or back of the neck (as declining); hence, the back generally (whether literal or figurative)\nKJV: back ((stiff-) neck((-ed).\n\nCognate Group: H6202 (that is beheaded), H6204 (Orpah), H6203 (back neck)\nGreek Equivalents: G2588 καρδία, G2864 κόμη, G3577 νῶτος, G5137 τράχηλος",
    6204: "עׇרְפָּה (ʻOrpâh | or-paw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H6203 עֹרֶף ; mane\nStrong's: Orpah, a Moabites\nKJV: Orpah.\n\nCognate Group: H6202 (that is beheaded), H6204 (Orpah), H6203 (back neck)",
    6205: "עֲרָפֶל (ʻărâphel | ar-aw-fel')\n\nDerivation: probably from H6201 עָרַף\nStrong's: gloom (as of a lowering sky)\nKJV: (gross, thick) dark (cloud, -ness).\n\nCognate Group: H6183 (heaven), H6201 (drop), H6205 (dark)\nGreek Equivalents: G1105 γνόφος, G2366 θύελλα, G3509 νέφος, G4655 σκότος",
    6206: "עָרַץ (ʻârats | aw-rats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to awe or (intransitive) to dread; hence, to harass\nKJV: be affrighted (afraid, dread, feared, terrified), break, dread, fear, oppress, prevail, shake terribly.\n\nCognate Group: H6206 (be affrighted), H6178 (cliffs), H4637 (terror), H6184 (mighty)\nGreek Equivalents: G1168 δειλιάω, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1740 ἐνδοξάζω, G2125 εὐλαβέομαι, G2352 θραύω, G3166 μεγαλαυχέω, G4422 πτοέω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5399 φοβέω",
    6207: "עָרַק (ʻâraq | aw-rak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to gnaw, i.e. (figuratively) eat (by hyberbole); also (participle) a pain\nKJV: fleeing, sinew.\n\nCognate Group: H6207 (fleeing), H6208 (Arkite)\nGreek Equivalents: G5343 φεύγω",
    6208: "עַרְקִי (ʻArqîy | ar-kee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from an unused name meaning a tush\nStrong's: an Arkite or inhabitant of Erek\nKJV: Arkite.\n\nCognate Group: H6207 (fleeing), H6208 (Arkite)",
    6209: "עָרַר (ʻârar | aw-rar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to bare; figuratively, to demolish\nKJV: make bare, break, raise up (perhaps by clerical error for raze), [idiom] utterly.\n\nCognate Group: H6177 (Aroer), H6209 (make bare), H6199 (destitute), H5735 (Adadah), H6200 (Aroerite), H6185 (childless), H6176 (health)\nGreek Equivalents: G2679 κατασκάπτω",
    6210: "עֶרֶשׂ (ʻeres | eh'res)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning perhaps to arch\nStrong's: a couch (properly, with a canopy)\nKJV: bed(-stead), couch.\n\nCognate Group: H6210 (bed)\nGreek Equivalents: G2825 κλίνη",
    6211: "עָשׁ (ʻâsh | awsh)\n\nDerivation: from H6244 עָשֵׁשׁ\nStrong's: a moth\nKJV: moth. See also H5906 עַיִשׁ .\n\nCognate Group: H6211 (moth), H6244 (be consumed)\nGreek Equivalents: G4597 σής",
    6212: "עֶשֶׂב (ʻeseb | eh'seb)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to glisten (or be green)\nStrong's: grass (or any tender shoot)\nKJV: grass, herb.\n\nCognate Group: H6212 (grass)\nGreek Equivalents: G1008 βοτάνη, G5515 χλωρός, G5527 χόρτασμα, G5528 χόρτος",
    6213: "עָשָׂה (ʻâsâh | aw-saw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to do or make, in the broadest sense and widest application\nKJV: accomplish, advance, appoint, apt, be at, become, bear, bestow, bring forth, bruise, be busy, [idiom] certainly, have the charge of, commit, deal (with), deck, [phrase] displease, do, (ready) dress(-ed), (put in) execute(-ion), exercise, fashion, [phrase] feast, (fight-) ing man, [phrase] finish, fit, fly, follow, fulfill, furnish, gather, get, go about, govern, grant, great, [phrase] hinder, hold (a feast), [idiom] indeed, [phrase] be industrious, [phrase] journey, keep, labour, maintain, make, be meet, observe, be occupied, offer, [phrase] officer, pare, bring (come) to pass, perform, pracise, prepare, procure, provide, put, requite, [idiom] sacrifice, serve, set, shew, [idiom] sin, spend, [idiom] surely, take, [idiom] thoroughly, trim, [idiom] very, [phrase] vex, be (warr-) ior, work(-man), yield, use.\n\nCognate Group: H6222 (Asaiah), H3299 (Jaasau), H4640 (Maasiai), H4639 (act), H3300 (Jaasiel), H6214 (Asahel), H6221 (Asiel), H6213 (accomplish), H4641 (Maaseiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G25 ἀγαπάω, G71 ἄγω, G264 ἁμαρτάνω, G390 ἀναστρέφω, G399 ἀναφέρω, G435 ἀνήρ, G576 ἀποβαίνω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G997 βοηθέω, G1090 γεωργέω, G1096 γίνομαι, G1122 γραμματεύς, G1325 δίδωμι, G1653 ἐλεέω, G1873 ἐπακούω, G1941 ἐπικαλέομαι, G2005 ἐπιτελέω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2038 ἐργάζομαι, G2041 ἔργον, G2090 ἑτοιμάζω, G2323 θεραπεύω, G2680 κατασκευάζω, G2716 κατεργάζομαι, G2827 κλίνω, G2875 κόπτω, G2932 κτάομαι, G3309 μεριμνάω, G3539 νοιέω, G3618 οἰκοδομέω, G3878 παρακούω, G4017 περιβλέπω, G4111 πλάσσω, G4160 ποιέω, G4231 πραγματεύομαι, G4238 πράσσω, G4355 προσλαμβάνω, G4374 προσφέρω, G4732 στερεόω, G4819 συμβαίνω, G4931 συντελέω, G5048 τελειόω, G5055 τελέω, G5087 τίθημι, G5342 φέρω, G5442 φυλάσσω, G5452 φυτεύω, G5530 χράομαι",
    6214: "עֲשָׂהאֵל (ʻĂsâhʼêl | as-aw-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H6213 עָשָׂה and H410 אֵל ; God has made\nStrong's: Asahel, the name of four Israelites\nKJV: Asahel.\n\nCognate Group: H6222 (Asaiah), H3299 (Jaasau), H4640 (Maasiai), H4639 (act), H3300 (Jaasiel), H6214 (Asahel), H6221 (Asiel), H6213 (accomplish), H4641 (Maaseiah)",
    6215: "עֵשָׂו (ʻÊsâv | ay-sawv')\n\nDerivation: apparently a form of the passive participle of H6213 עָשָׂה in the original sense of handling; rough (i.e. sensibly felt)\nStrong's: Esav, a son of Isaac, including his posterity\nKJV: Esau.\n\nCognate Group: H6215 (Esau), H6213 (accomplish)\nGreek Equivalents: G2269 Ἠσαῦ",
