    6231: "עָשַׁק (ʻâshaq | aw-shak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H6229 עָשַׂק)\nStrong's: to press upon, i.e. oppress, defraud, violate, overflow\nKJV: get deceitfully, deceive, defraud, drink up, (use) oppress(-ion), -or), do violence (wrong).\n\nCognate Group: H6217 (oppressed), H6216 (oppressor), H6231 (get deceitfully), H6233 (cruelly), H6234 (oppressed), H6232 (Eshek), H4642 (oppression)\nGreek Equivalents: G71 ἄγω, G91 ἀδικέω, G156 αἰτία, G650 ἀποστερέω, G764 ἀσεβέω, G1283 διαρπάζω, G2346 θλίβω, G2616 καταδυναστεύω, G4132 πλήμμυρα, G4811 συκοφαντέω",
