    6235: "עֶשֶׂר (ʻeser | eh'ser)\n\nDerivation: masculine of term עֲשָׂרָה; from H6237 עָשַׂר\nStrong's: ten (as an accumulation to the extent of the digits)\nKJV: ten, (fif-, seven-) teen.\n\nCognate Group: H6235 (ten), H6241 (tenth deal), H6237 ([idiom] surely), H4643 (tenth), H6218 (ten), H6240 (teen[-th]), H6220 (Ashvath), H6224 (tenth), H6242 (score)",
    6236: "עֲשַׂר (ʻăsar | as-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) masculine עֲשְׂרָה (Aramaic); corresponding to H6235 עֶשֶׂר\nStrong's: ten\nKJV: ten, [phrase] twelve.\n\nCognate Group: H6236 (ten), H6263 (ready), H6268 (ancient), H6243 (twenty), H6246 (think)",
