    6238: "עָשַׁר (ʻâshar | aw-shar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to accumulate; chiefly (specifically) to grow (causatively, make) rich\nKJV: be(-come, en-, make, make self, wax) rich, make (1 Kings 22:48 marg). See H6240 עָשָׂר .\n\nCognate Group: H6223 (rich), H6239 ([idiom] far), H6238 (be rich)\nGreek Equivalents: G4147 πλουτέω, G4148 πλουτίζω",
