    6256: "עֵת (ʻêth | ayth)\n\nDerivation: from H5703 עַד\nStrong's: time, especially (adverb with preposition) now, when, etc.\nKJV: [phrase] after, (al-) ways, [idiom] certain, [phrase] continually, [phrase] evening, long, (due) season, so (long) as, (even-, evening-, noon-) tide, (meal-), what) time, when.\n\nCognate Group: H3282 (because), H6261 (fit), H6256 (after), H5772 (duty of marriage), H4616 (because of), H6258 (henceforth), H6278 (Ittahkazin), H4617 (answer), H6030 (give account), H6262 (Attai)\nGreek Equivalents: G723 ἄροτρον, G1565 ἐκεῖνος, G1622 ἐκτός, G1883 ἐπάνω, G2120 εὐκαιρία, G2121 εὔκαιρος, G2192 ἔχω, G2250 ἡμέρα, G2540 καιρός, G2563 κάλαμος, G3314 μεσημβρία, G3326 μετά, G3348 μετέχω, G4009 πέρας, G5550 χρόνος, G5610 ὥρα",
