    6268: "עַתִּיק (ʻattîyq | at-teek')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H6267 עַתִּיק\nStrong's: venerable\nKJV: ancient.\n\nCognate Group: H6236 (ten), H6263 (ready), H6268 (ancient), H6243 (twenty), H6246 (think)\nGreek Equivalents: G645 ἀποσπάω, G3820 παλαιός, G4745 στοά",
    6269: "עֲתָךְ (ʻĂthâk | ath-awk')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to sojourn; lodging\nStrong's: Athak, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Athach.\n\nCognate Group: H6259 (ready), H6257 (make fit), H6269 (Athach), H6260 (chief one), H6264 (things that shall come), H6265 (Athaiah)",
