    6271: "עֲתַלְיָה (ʻĂthalyâh | ath-al-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or עֲתַלְיָהוּ; from the same as H6270 עַתְלַי and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has constrained\nStrong's: Athaljah, the name of an Israelitess and two Israelites\nKJV: Athaliah.\n\nCognate Group: H6270 (Athlai), H6271 (Athaliah)",
    6272: "עָתַם (ʻâtham | aw-tham)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: probably to glow, i.e. (figuratively) be desolated\nKJV: be darkened.\n\nCognate Group: H6273 (Othni), H6274 (Othniel), H6272 (be darkened)",
