    6275: "עָתַק (ʻâthaq | aw-thak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to remove (intransitive or transitive) figuratively, to grow old; specifically, to transcribe\nKJV: copy out, leave off, become (wax) old, remove.\n\nCognate Group: H6277 (arrogancy), H6266 (durable), H6267 (ancient), H6275 (copy out), H6276 (durable)\nGreek Equivalents: G93 ἀδικία, G458 ἀνομία, G522 ἀπαίρω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G2690 καταστρέφω, G3822 παλαιόω",
