    6278: "עֵת קָצִין (ʻÊth Qâtsîyn | ayth kaw-tseen')\n\nDerivation: from H6256 עֵת and H7011 קַיָּם ; time of a judge\nStrong's: Eth-Katsin, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Ittahkazin (by including directive enclitic).\n\nCognate Group: H3282 (because), H6261 (fit), H6256 (after), H5772 (duty of marriage), H4616 (because of), H6258 (henceforth), H6278 (Ittahkazin), H4617 (answer), H6030 (give account), H6262 (Attai)",
    6279: "עָתַר (ʻâthar | aw-thar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (rather denominative from H6281 עֶתֶר)\nStrong's: to burn incense in worship, i.e. intercede (reciprocally, listen to prayer)\nKJV: intreat, (make) pray(-er).\n\nCognate Group: H6282 (suppliant), H6279 (intreat)\nGreek Equivalents: G1522 εἰσακούω, G1595 ἑκούσιον, G1873 ἐπακούω, G2172 εὔχομαι, G4016 περιβάλλω, G4336 προσεύχομαι, G4737 στεφανόω, G4912 συνέχω, G5117 τόπος",
