    6285: "פֵּאָה (pêʼâh | pay-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H6311 פֹּה\nStrong's: properly, mouth in a figurative sense, i.e. direction, region, extremity\nKJV: corner, end, quarter, side.\n\nCognate Group: H6284 (scatter into corners), H6285 (corner)\nGreek Equivalents: G747 ἀρχηγός, G2326 θερισμός, G2864 κόμη, G3062 λοιποί, G3063 λοιπόν, G3064 λοιποῦ, G3313 μέρος, G3568 νῦν, G3725 ὅριον, G3799 ὄψις, G4383 πρόσωπον",
    6286: "פָּאַר (pâʼar | paw-ar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; also denominative from H6288 פְּאֹרָה,\nStrong's: to gleam, i.e. (causatively) embellish; figuratively, to boast; also to explain (i.e. make clear) oneself; to shake a tree\nKJV: beautify, boast self, go over the boughs, glorify (self), glory, vaunt self.\n\nCognate Group: H6286 (beautify), H8597 (beauty), H6287 (beauty)\nGreek Equivalents: G455 ἀνοίγω, G1272 διανοίγω, G1391 δόξα, G1392 δοξάζω, G1740 ἐνδοξάζω, G1741 ἔνδοξος, G2744 καυχάομαι, G5021 τάσσω, G5312 ὑψόω",
    6287: "פְּאֵר (pᵉʼêr | peh-ayr')\n\nDerivation: from H6286 פָּאַר\nStrong's: an embellishment, i.e. fancy head-dress\nKJV: beauty, bonnet, goodly, ornament, tire.\n\nCognate Group: H6286 (beautify), H8597 (beauty), H6287 (beauty)\nGreek Equivalents: G2864 κόμη",
