    6292: "פִּגּוּל (piggûwl | pig-gool')\n\nDerivation: or פִּגֻּל; from an unused root meaning to stink\nStrong's: properly, fetid, i.e. (figuratively) unclean (ceremonially)\nKJV: abominable(-tion, thing).\n\nCognate Group: H6292 (abominable)\nGreek Equivalents: G952 βέβηλος, G3393 μίασμα, G3435 μολύνω",
    6293: "פָּגַע (pâgaʻ | paw-gah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to impinge, by accident or violence, or (figuratively) by importunity\nKJV: come (betwixt), cause to entreat, fall (upon), make intercession, intercessor, intreat, lay, light (upon), meet (together), pray, reach, run.\n\nCognate Group: H6295 (Pagiel), H6293 (come), H6294 (chance), H4645 (mark)\nGreek Equivalents: G337 ἀναιρέω, G482 ἀντιλαμβάνομαι, G528 ἀπαντάω, G615 ἀποκτείνω, G1330 διέρχομαι, G1706 ἐμπίπτω, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G2289 θανατόω, G2980 λαλέω, G3860 παραδίδωμι, G4334 προσέρχομαι, G4876 συναντάω, G5294 ὑποτίθημι",
    6294: "פֶּגַע (pegaʻ | peh'-gah)\n\nDerivation: from H6293 פָּגַע\nStrong's: impact (casual)\nKJV: chance, occurent.\n\nCognate Group: H6295 (Pagiel), H6293 (come), H6294 (chance), H4645 (mark)",
    6295: "פַּגְעִיאֵל (Pagʻîyʼêl | pag-ee-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H6294 פֶּגַע and H410 אֵל ; accident of God\nStrong's: Pagiel, an Israelite\nKJV: Pagiel.\n\nCognate Group: H6295 (Pagiel), H6293 (come), H6294 (chance), H4645 (mark)",
    6296: "פָּגַר (pâgar | paw-gar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to relax, i.e. become exhausted\nKJV: be faint.\n\nCognate Group: H6297 (carcase), H6296 (be faint)\nGreek Equivalents: G1590 ἐκλύω, G2523 καθίζω",
    6297: "פֶּגֶר (peger | peh'gher)\n\nDerivation: from H6296 פָּגַר\nStrong's: a carcase (as limp), whether of man or beast; figuratively, an idolatrous image\nKJV: carcase, corpse, dead body.\n\nCognate Group: H6297 (carcase), H6296 (be faint)\nGreek Equivalents: G2966 κῶλον, G3498 νεκρός, G4098 πίπτω, G4430 πτῶμα, G4431 πτῶσις, G4983 σῶμα, G5408 φόνος",
    6298: "פָּגַשׁ (pâgash | paw-gash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to come in contact with, whether by accident or violence; figuratively, to concur\nKJV: meet (with, together).\n\nCognate Group: H6298 (meet)\nGreek Equivalents: G528 ἀπαντάω, G1706 ἐμπίπτω, G4876 συναντάω, G4905 συνέρχομαι",
    6299: "פָּדָה (pâdâh | paw-daw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to sever, i.e. ransom; gener. to release, preserve\nKJV: [idiom] at all, deliver, [idiom] by any means, ransom, (that are to be, let be) redeem(-ed), rescue, [idiom] surely.\n\nCognate Group: H6305 (Pedaiah), H6307 (Padan), H6306 (ransom), H6303 (Padon), H6299 ([idiom] at all), H6304 (division), H6301 (Pedahzur), H6302 (to be redeemed), H6300 (Pedahel)\nGreek Equivalents: G236 ἀλλάσσω, G873 ἀφορίζω, G3084 λυτρόω, G3085 λύτρωσις, G4506 ῥύομαι, G4863 συνάγω, G4982 σώζω",
