    6419: "פָּלַל (pâlal | paw-lal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to judge (officially or mentally); by extension, to intercede, pray\nKJV: intreat, judge(-ment), (make) pray(-er, -ing), make supplication.\n\nCognate Group: H6415 (judgment), H6397 (Pelonite), H6414 (judge), H654 (Ephlal), H8605 (prayer), H6421 (Pelaliah), H6419 (intreat), H6417 (judgment), H6420 (Palal), H6416 (judge)\nGreek Equivalents: G1311 διαφθείρω, G2172 εὔχομαι, G4336 προσεύχομαι",
    6420: "פָּלָל (Pâlâl | paw-lawl')\n\nDerivation: from H6419 פָּלַל ; judge\nStrong's: Palal, an Israelite\nKJV: Palal.\n\nCognate Group: H6415 (judgment), H6397 (Pelonite), H6414 (judge), H654 (Ephlal), H8605 (prayer), H6421 (Pelaliah), H6419 (intreat), H6417 (judgment), H6420 (Palal), H6416 (judge)",
    6421: "פְּלַלְיָה (Pᵉlalyâh | pel-al-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H6419 פָּלַל and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has judged\nStrong's: Pelaljah, an Israelite\nKJV: Pelaliah.\n\nCognate Group: H6415 (judgment), H6397 (Pelonite), H6414 (judge), H654 (Ephlal), H8605 (prayer), H6421 (Pelaliah), H6419 (intreat), H6417 (judgment), H6420 (Palal), H6416 (judge)",
    6422: "פַּלְמֹונִי (palmôwnîy | pal-mo-nee')\n\nDerivation: probably for H6423 פְּלֹנִי\nStrong's: a certain one, i.e. so-and-so\nKJV: certain.\n\nCognate Group: H6395 (put a difference), H6422 (certain), H6423 (such)",
    6423: "פְּלֹנִי (pᵉlônîy | pel-o-nee')\n\nDerivation: from H6395 פָּלָה\nStrong's: such a one, i.e. a specified person\nKJV: such.\n\nCognate Group: H6395 (put a difference), H6422 (certain), H6423 (such)",
    6424: "פָּלַס (pâlaç | paw-las')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to roll flat, i.e. prepare (a road); also to revolve, i.e. weigh (mentally)\nKJV: make, ponder, weigh.\n\nCognate Group: H6424 (make), H6425 (scales), H4657 (balancing)\nGreek Equivalents: G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G3596 ὁδοιπορέω, G3717 ὀρθός, G3903 παρασκευάζω",
    6425: "פֶּלֶס (peleç | peh'-les)\n\nDerivation: from H6424 פָּלַס\nStrong's: a balance\nKJV: scales, weight.\n\nCognate Group: H6424 (make), H6425 (scales), H4657 (balancing)\nGreek Equivalents: G4493 ῥιπή",
    6426: "פָּלַץ (pâlats | paw-lats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, perhaps to rend, i.e. (by implication) to quiver\nKJV: tremble.\n\nCognate Group: H4656 (idol), H6427 (fearfulness), H8606 (terrible), H6426 (tremble)\nGreek Equivalents: G4531 σαλεύω",
    6427: "פַּלָּצוּת (pallâtsûwth | pal-law-tsooth')\n\nDerivation: from H6426 פָּלַץ\nStrong's: affright\nKJV: fearfulness, horror, trembling.\n\nCognate Group: H4656 (idol), H6427 (fearfulness), H8606 (terrible), H6426 (tremble)\nGreek Equivalents: G2285 θάμβος, G3601 ὀδύνη",
    6428: "פָּלַשׁ (pâlash | paw-lash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to roll (in dust)\nKJV: roll (wallow) self.\n\nCognate Group: H6432 (Pelethites), H6436 (Pannag), H6435 (), H6431 (Peleth), H6429 (Palestina), H6430 (Philistine), H6428 (roll self)\nGreek Equivalents: G2875 κόπτω, G4766 στρώννυμι, G5291 ὑποστρώννυμι",
    6429: "פְּלֶשֶׁת (Pᵉlesheth | pel-eh'-sheth)\n\nDerivation: from H6428 פָּלַשׁ ; rolling, i.e. migratory\nStrong's: Pelesheth, a region of Syria\nKJV: Palestina, Palestine, Philistia, Philistines.\n\nCognate Group: H6432 (Pelethites), H6436 (Pannag), H6435 (), H6431 (Peleth), H6429 (Palestina), H6430 (Philistine), H6428 (roll self)\nGreek Equivalents: G246 ἀλλόφυλος",
    6430: "פְּלִשְׁתִּי (Pᵉlishtîy | pel-ish-tee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H6429 פְּלֶשֶׁת\nStrong's: a Pelishtite or inhabitant of Pelesheth\nKJV: Philistine.\n\nCognate Group: H6432 (Pelethites), H6436 (Pannag), H6435 (), H6431 (Peleth), H6429 (Palestina), H6430 (Philistine), H6428 (roll self)",
    6431: "פֶּלֶת (Peleth | peh'-leth)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to flee; swiftness\nStrong's: Peleth, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Peleth.\n\nCognate Group: H6432 (Pelethites), H6436 (Pannag), H6435 (), H6431 (Peleth), H6429 (Palestina), H6430 (Philistine), H6428 (roll self)",
    6432: "פְּלֵתִי (Pᵉlêthîy | pel-ay-thee')\n\nDerivation: from the same form as H6431 פֶּלֶת\nStrong's: a courier (collectively) or official messenger\nKJV: Pelethites.\n\nCognate Group: H6432 (Pelethites), H6436 (Pannag), H6435 (), H6431 (Peleth), H6429 (Palestina), H6430 (Philistine), H6428 (roll self)",
    6433: "פֻּם (pum | poom)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) probably for H6310 פֶּה\nStrong's: the mouth (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: mouth.\n\nCognate Group: H6460 (psaltery), H6433 (mouth), H6402 (service), H6399 (minister)\nGreek Equivalents: G4750 στόμα",
    6434: "פֵּן (pên | pane)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to turn\nStrong's: an angle (of a street or wall)\nKJV: corner.\n\nCognate Group: H6434 (corner), H6443 (ruby), H6444 (Peninnah), H6438 (bulwark)",
    6435: "פֵּן (pên | pane)\n\nDerivation: from H6437 פָּנָה\nStrong's: properly, removal; used only (in the construction) adverb as conjunction, lest\nKJV: (lest) (peradventure), that...not.\n\nCognate Group: H6432 (Pelethites), H6436 (Pannag), H6435 (), H6431 (Peleth), H6429 (Palestina), H6430 (Philistine), H6428 (roll self)",
    6436: "פַּנַּג (pannag | pan-nag')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: probably pastry\nKJV: Pannag.\n\nCognate Group: H6432 (Pelethites), H6436 (Pannag), H6435 (), H6431 (Peleth), H6429 (Palestina), H6430 (Philistine), H6428 (roll self)",
    6437: "פָּנָה (pânâh | paw-naw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to turn; by implication, to face, i.e. appear, look, etc.\nKJV: appear, at (even-) tide, behold, cast out, come on, [idiom] corner, dawning, empty, go away, lie, look, mark, pass away, prepare, regard, (have) respect (to), (re-) turn (aside, away, back, face, self), [idiom] right (early).\n\nCognate Group: H3312 (Jephunneh), H6437 (appear), H6441 (inner), H3942 (before), H6442 (inner), H6440 (accept), H6439 (Peniel)\nGreek Equivalents: G190 ἀκολουθέω, G308 ἀναβλέπω, G390 ἀναστρέφω, G578 ἀποβλέπω, G643 ἀποσκευάζω, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G991 βλέπω, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1593 ἐκνεύω, G1689 ἐμβλέπω, G1781 ἐντέλλομαι, G1811 ἐξακολουθέω, G1872 ἐπακολουθέω, G1914 ἐπιβλέπω, G1994 ἐπιστρέφω, G2014 ἐπιφαίνω, G2090 ἑτοιμάζω, G2597 καταβαίνω, G2827 κλίνω, G3179 μεθίστημι, G3596 ὁδοιπορέω, G3708 ὁράω, G3729 ὁρμάω, G4017 περιβλέπω, G4105 πλανάω, G4337 προσέχω, G4762 στρέφω, G4887 συνδέω, G5290 ὑποστρέφω, G5342 φέρω",
    6438: "פִּנָּה (pinnâh | pin-naw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H6434 פֵּן\nStrong's: an angle; by implication, a pinnacle; figuratively, a chieftain\nKJV: bulwark, chief, corner, stay, tower.\n\nCognate Group: H6434 (corner), H6443 (ruby), H6444 (Peninnah), H6438 (bulwark)\nGreek Equivalents: G204 ἀκρογωνιαῖος, G1137 γωνία, G2824 κλίμα",
    6439: "פְּנוּאֵל (Pᵉnûwʼêl | pen-oo-ale')\n\nDerivation: or (more properly,) פְּנִיאֵל; from H6437 פָּנָה and H410 אֵל ; face of God\nStrong's: Penuel or Peniel, a place East of Jordan; also (as Penuel) the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Peniel, Penuel.\n\nCognate Group: H3312 (Jephunneh), H6437 (appear), H6441 (inner), H3942 (before), H6442 (inner), H6440 (accept), H6439 (Peniel)\nGreek Equivalents: G5323 Φανουήλ",
    6440: "פָּנִים (pânîym | paw-neem')\n\nDerivation: plural (but always as singular) of an unused noun פָּנֶה; from H6437 פָּנָה)\nStrong's: the face (as the part that turns); used in a great variety of applications (literally and figuratively); also (with prepositional prefix) as a preposition (before, etc.)\nKJV: [phrase] accept, a-(be-) fore(-time), against, anger, [idiom] as (long as), at, [phrase] battle, [phrase] because (of), [phrase] beseech, countenance, edge, [phrase] employ, endure, [phrase] enquire, face, favour, fear of, for, forefront(-part), form(-er time, -ward), from, front, heaviness, [idiom] him(-self), [phrase] honourable, [phrase] impudent, [phrase] in, it, look(-eth) (-s), [idiom] me, [phrase] meet, [idiom] more than, mouth, of, off, (of) old (time), [idiom] on, open, [phrase] out of, over against, the partial, person, [phrase] please, presence, propect, was purposed, by reason of, [phrase] regard, right forth, [phrase] serve, [idiom] shewbread, sight, state, straight, [phrase] street, [idiom] thee, [idiom] them(-selves), through ([phrase] -out), till, time(-s) past, (un-) to(-ward), [phrase] upon, upside ([phrase] down), with(-in, [phrase] -stand), [idiom] ye, [idiom] you.\n\nCognate Group: H3312 (Jephunneh), H6437 (appear), H6441 (inner), H3942 (before), H6442 (inner), H6440 (accept), H6439 (Peniel)\nGreek Equivalents: G746 ἀρχή, G991 βλέπω, G1715 ἔμπροσθεν, G1799 ἐνώπιον, G2082 ἐσώτερος, G3788 ὀφθαλμός, G4286 πρόθεσις, G4295 πρόκειμαι, G4376 προσφορά, G4383 πρόσωπον, G4383 πρόσωπον, G4383 πρόσωπον, G4383 πρόσωπον, G4383 πρόσωπον, G4386 πρότερον, G5222 ὑπάντησις, G5288 ὑποστέλλω",
    6441: "פְּנִימָה (pᵉnîymâh | pen-ee'-maw)\n\nDerivation: from H6440 פָּנִים with directive enclitic\nStrong's: faceward, i.e. indoors\nKJV: (with-) in(-ner part, -ward).\n\nCognate Group: H3312 (Jephunneh), H6437 (appear), H6441 (inner), H3942 (before), H6442 (inner), H6440 (accept), H6439 (Peniel)\nGreek Equivalents: G2080 ἔσω, G4383 πρόσωπον",
    6442: "פְּנִימִי (pᵉnîymîy | pen-ee-mee')\n\nDerivation: from H6440 פָּנִים\nStrong's: interior\nKJV: (with-) in(-ner, -ward).\n\nCognate Group: H3312 (Jephunneh), H6437 (appear), H6441 (inner), H3942 (before), H6442 (inner), H6440 (accept), H6439 (Peniel)\nGreek Equivalents: G2082 ἐσώτερος",
    6443: "פָּנִין (pânîyn | paw-neen')\n\nDerivation: or פָּנִי; from the same as H6434 פֵּן\nStrong's: probably a pearl (as round)\nKJV: ruby.\n\nCognate Group: H6434 (corner), H6443 (ruby), H6444 (Peninnah), H6438 (bulwark)\nGreek Equivalents: G3037 λίθος, G3037 λίθος, G4185 πολυτελής",
    6444: "פְּנִנָּה (Pᵉninnâh | pen-in-naw')\n\nDerivation: probably feminine from H6443 פָּנִין contr.\nStrong's: Peninnah, an Israelitess\nKJV: Peninnah.\n\nCognate Group: H6434 (corner), H6443 (ruby), H6444 (Peninnah), H6438 (bulwark)",
    6445: "פָּנַק (pânaq | paw-nak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to enervate\nKJV: bring up.\n\nCognate Group: H6445 (bring up)",
    6446: "פַּס (paç | pas)\n\nDerivation: from H6461 פָּסַס ; properly, the palm (of the hand) or sole (of the foot) (compare H6447 פַּס); by implication (plural)\n\nStrong's: a long and sleeved tunic (perhaps simply a wide one; from the original sense of the root, i.e. of many breadths)\nKJV: (divers) colours.\n\nCognate Group: H6446 (colours), H6451 (handful)",
    6447: "פַּס (paç | pas)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H6461 פָּסַס\nStrong's: the palm (of the hand, as being spread out)\nKJV: participle\n\nCognate Group: H6447 (participle), H6523 (iron)\nGreek Equivalents: G4164 ποικίλος",
    6448: "פָּסַג (pâçag | paw-sag')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to cut up, i.e. (figuratively) contemplate\nKJV: consider.\n\nCognate Group: H798 (Ashdoth-pisgah), H6448 (consider), H6449 (Pisgah)",
    6449: "פִּסְגָּה (Piçgâh | pis-gaw')\n\nDerivation: from H6448 פָּסַג ; a cleft\nStrong's: Pisgah, a Mountain East of Jordan\nKJV: Pisgah.\n\nCognate Group: H798 (Ashdoth-pisgah), H6448 (consider), H6449 (Pisgah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2991 λαξευτός",
    6450: "פַּס דַּמִּים (Paç Dammîym | pas dam-meem')\n\nDerivation: from H6446 פַּס and the plural of H1818 דָּם ; palm (i.e. dell) of bloodshed\nStrong's: Pas-Dammim, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Pas-dammim. Compare H658 אֶפֶס דַּמִּים .\n\nCognate Group: H656 (be clean gone), H6450 (Pas-dammim), H659 (of nought), H657 (ankle), H658 (Ephes-dammim)",
    6451: "פִּסָּה (piççâh | pis-saw')\n\nDerivation: from H6461 פָּסַס\nStrong's: expansion, i.e. abundance\nKJV: handful.\n\nCognate Group: H6446 (colours), H6451 (handful)",
    6452: "פָּסַח (pâçach | paw-sakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to hop, i.e. (figuratively) skip over (or spare); by implication, to hesitate; also (literally) to limp, to dance\nKJV: halt, become lame, leap, pass over.\n\nCognate Group: H6453 (passover), H8607 (Tipsah), H6452 (halt)\nGreek Equivalents: G3928 παρέρχομαι, G4046 περιποιέομαι",
    6453: "פֶּסַח (peçach | peh'-sakh)\n\nDerivation: from H6452 פָּסַח\nStrong's: a pretermission, i.e. exemption; used only techically of the Jewish Passover (the festival or the victim)\nKJV: passover (offering).\n\nCognate Group: H6453 (passover), H8607 (Tipsah), H6452 (halt)\nGreek Equivalents: G3957 πάσχα",
    6454: "פָּסֵחַ (Pâçêach | paw-say'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H6452 פָּסַח ; limping\nStrong's: Paseach, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Paseah, Phaseah.\n\nCognate Group: H6455 (lame), H6452 (halt), H6457 (Pasach), H6454 (Paseah)",
    6455: "פִּסֵּחַ (piççêach | pis-say'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H6452 פָּסַח\nStrong's: lame\nKJV: lame.\n\nCognate Group: H6455 (lame), H6452 (halt), H6457 (Pasach), H6454 (Paseah)\nGreek Equivalents: G5560 χωλός",
    6456: "פְּסִיל (pᵉçîyl | pes-eel')\n\nDerivation: from H6458 פָּסַל\nStrong's: an idol\nKJV: carved (graven) image, quarry.\n\nCognate Group: H6456 (carved image), H6458 (grave), H6459 (carved image)",
    6457: "פָּסַךְ (Pâçak | paw-sak')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to divide; divider\nStrong's: Pasak, an Israelite\nKJV: Pasach.\n\nCognate Group: H6455 (lame), H6452 (halt), H6457 (Pasach), H6454 (Paseah)",
    6458: "פָּסַל (pâçal | paw-sal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to carve, whether wood or stone\nKJV: grave, hew.\n\nCognate Group: H6456 (carved image), H6458 (grave), H6459 (carved image)",
    6459: "פֶּסֶל (peçel | peh'-sel)Typo: lemma פֶסֶל missing dagesh, corrected to פֶּסֶל\n\nGreek Equivalents: G1497 εἴδωλον \n\nDerivation: from H6458 פָּסַל\nStrong's: an idol\nKJV: carved (graven) image.\n\nCognate Group: H6456 (carved image), H6458 (grave), H6459 (carved image)",
    6460: "פְּסַנְטֵרִין (pᵉçanṭêrîyn | pes-an-tay-reen')\n\nTypo: lemma פִּסַנְטֵרִין first vowel, corrected to פְּסַנְטֵרִין\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or פְּסַנְתֵּרִין; a transliteration of the Greek,\nStrong's: psalterion; a lyre\nKJV: psaltery.\n\nCognate Group: H6460 (psaltery), H6433 (mouth), H6402 (service), H6399 (minister)",
    6461: "פָּסַס (pâçaç | paw-sas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: probably to disperse, i.e. (intransitive) disappear\nKJV: cease.\n\nCognate Group: H6462 (Pispah), H6461 (cease)",
    6462: "פִּסְפָּה (Piçpâh | pis-paw')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from H6461 פָּסַס ; dispersion\nStrong's: Pispah, an Israelite\nKJV: Pispah.\n\nCognate Group: H6462 (Pispah), H6461 (cease)",
    6463: "פָּעָה (pâʻâh | paw-aw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to scream\nKJV: cry.\n\nCognate Group: H6463 (cry), H660 (viper), H6464 (Pai)",
    6464: "פָּעוּ (Pâʻûw | paw-oo')\n\nDerivation: or פָּעִי; from H6463 פָּעָה ; screaming\nStrong's: Pau or Pai, a place in Edom\nKJV: Pai, Pau.\n\nCognate Group: H6463 (cry), H660 (viper), H6464 (Pai)",
    6465: "פְּעֹור (Pᵉʻôwr | peh-ore')\n\nDerivation: from H6473 פָּעַר ; a gap; also H1187 בַּעַל פְּעֹור)\n\nStrong's: Peor, a mountain East of Jordan; Baal Peor, (for a deity worshipped there\nKJV: Peor. See also H1047 בֵּית פְּעֹור .\n\nCognate Group: H6474 (Paarai), H6465 (Peor), H6473 (gape)",
    6466: "פָּעַל (pâʻal | paw-al')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to do or make (systematically and habitually), especially to practise\nKJV: commit, (evil-) do(-er), make(-r), ordain, work(-er).\n\nCognate Group: H6467 (act), H6466 (commit), H4659 (work), H6469 (Peulthai), H6468 (labour)\nGreek Equivalents: G1754 ἐνεργέω, G1863 ἐπάγω, G2005 ἐπιτελέω, G2038 ἐργάζομαι, G2041 ἔργον, G2675 καταρτίζω, G2716 κατεργάζομαι, G4160 ποιέω, G4238 πράσσω",
    6467: "פֹּעַל (pôʻal | po'-al)\n\nDerivation: from H6466 פָּעַל\nStrong's: an act or work (concretely)\nKJV: act, deed, do, getting, maker, work.\n\nCognate Group: H6467 (act), H6466 (commit), H4659 (work), H6469 (Peulthai), H6468 (labour)\nGreek Equivalents: G91 ἀδικέω, G2039 ἐργασία, G2041 ἔργον, G3408 μισθός, G4161 ποίημα, G4234 πρᾶξις, G5010 τάξις",
    6468: "פְּעֻלָּה (pᵉʻullâh | peh-ool-law')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of H6466 פָּעַל\nStrong's: (abstractly) work\nKJV: labour, reward, wages, work.\n\nCognate Group: H6467 (act), H6466 (commit), H4659 (work), H6469 (Peulthai), H6468 (labour)\nGreek Equivalents: G1397 δουλεία, G3009 λειτουργία, G3449 μόχθος, G4192 πόνος",
    6469: "פְּעֻלְּתַי (Pᵉʻullᵉthay | peh-ool-leh-thah'-ee)\n\nTypo: xlit Pᵉullʻthay corrected to Pᵉʻullᵉthay\n\nDerivation: from H6468 פְּעֻלָּה ; laborious\nStrong's: Peullethai, an Israelite\nKJV: Peulthai.\n\nCognate Group: H6467 (act), H6466 (commit), H4659 (work), H6469 (Peulthai), H6468 (labour)",
    6470: "פָּעַם (pâʻam | paw-am')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tap, i.e. beat regularly; hence (generally) to impel or agitate\nKJV: move, trouble.\n\nCognate Group: H6470 (move), H6471 (anvil), H6472 (bell)",
