    6490: "פִּקּוּד (piqqûwd | pik-kood')\n\nDerivation: or פִּקֻּד; from H6485 פָּקַד\nStrong's: properly, appointed, i.e. a mandate (of God; plural only, collectively, for the Law)\nKJV: commandment, precept, statute.\n\nCognate Group: H4663 (Miphkad), H4662 (appointed place), H6487 (that which was delivered), H6490 (commandment), H6485 (appoint), H6496 (which had the charge), H6488 (ward), H6489 (Pekod), H6486 (account)\nGreek Equivalents: G1345 δικαίωμα, G1785 ἐντολή",
