    6934: "קַדְמִיאֵל (Qadmîyʼêl | kad-mee-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H6924 קֶדֶם and H410 אֵל ; presence of God\nStrong's: Kadmiel, the name of three Israelites\nKJV: Kadmiel.\n\nCognate Group: H6924 (aforetime), H6926 (east), H6917 (ancient), H6935 (Kadmonites), H6921 (east), H6923 (come before), H6931 (ancient), H6927 (afore), H6929 (Kedemah), H6934 (Kadmiel), H6932 (Kedemoth), H6930 (east)",
    6935: "קַדְמֹנִי (Qadmônîy | kad-mo-nee')\n\nDerivation: the same as H6931 קַדְמֹונִי ; ancient, i.e. aboriginal\nStrong's: Kadmonite (collectively), the name of a tribe in Palestine\nKJV: Kadmonites.\n\nCognate Group: H6924 (aforetime), H6926 (east), H6917 (ancient), H6935 (Kadmonites), H6921 (east), H6923 (come before), H6931 (ancient), H6927 (afore), H6929 (Kedemah), H6934 (Kadmiel), H6932 (Kedemoth), H6930 (east)",
    6936: "קׇדְקֹד (qodqôd | kod-kode')\n\nDerivation: from H6915 קָדַד\nStrong's: the crown of the head (as the part most bowed)\nKJV: crown (of the head), pate, scalp, top of the head.\n\nCognate Group: H6936 (crown), H6916 (cassia)\nGreek Equivalents: G758 ἄρχων, G2776 κεφαλή",
    6937: "קָדַר (qâdar | kaw-dar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be ashy, i.e. darkcolored; by implication, to mourn (in sackcloth or sordid garments)\nKJV: be black(-ish), be (make) dark(-en), [idiom] heavily, (cause to) mourn.\n\nCognate Group: H6937 (be black), H6939 (Kidron), H6938 (Kedar), H6940 (blackness), H6941 (mournfully)\nGreek Equivalents: G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G640 ἀπορία, G3996 πενθέω, G4656 σκοτόω",
    6938: "קֵדָר (Qêdâr | kay-dawr')\n\nDerivation: from H6937 קָדַר ; dusky (of the skin or the tent)\nStrong's: Kedar, a son of Ishmael; also (collectively) Bedouin (as his descendants or representatives)\nKJV: Kedar.\n\nCognate Group: H6937 (be black), H6939 (Kidron), H6938 (Kedar), H6940 (blackness), H6941 (mournfully)",
    6939: "קִדְרֹון (Qidrôwn | kid-rone')\n\nDerivation: from H6937 קָדַר ; dusky place\nStrong's: Kidron, a brook near Jerusalem\nKJV: Kidron.\n\nCognate Group: H6937 (be black), H6939 (Kidron), H6938 (Kedar), H6940 (blackness), H6941 (mournfully)\nGreek Equivalents: G2748 Κεδρών",
    6940: "קַדְרוּת (qadrûwth | kad-rooth')\n\nDerivation: from H6937 קָדַר\nStrong's: duskiness\nKJV: blackness.\n\nCognate Group: H6937 (be black), H6939 (Kidron), H6938 (Kedar), H6940 (blackness), H6941 (mournfully)\nGreek Equivalents: G4655 σκότος",
    6941: "קְדֹרַנִּית (qᵉdôrannîyth | ked-o-ran-neeth')\n\nDerivation: adverb from H6937 קָדַר\nStrong's: blackish ones (i.e. in sackcloth); used adverbially, in mourning weeds\nKJV: mournfully.\n\nCognate Group: H6937 (be black), H6939 (Kidron), H6938 (Kedar), H6940 (blackness), H6941 (mournfully)",
    6942: "קָדַשׁ (qâdash | kaw-dash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be (causatively, make, pronounce or observe as) clean (ceremonially or morally)\nKJV: appoint, bid, consecrate, dedicate, defile, hallow, (be, keep) holy(-er, place), keep, prepare, proclaim, purify, sanctify(-ied one, self), [idiom] wholly.\n\nCognate Group: H6947 (Kadeshbarnea), H4720 (chapel), H6945 (sodomite), H6918 (holy), H6944 (consecrated), H6946 (Kadesh), H6948 (harlot), H6942 (appoint), H6943 (Kedesh)\nGreek Equivalents: G37 ἁγιάζω, G38 ἁγιασμός, G39 ἅγιον, G48 ἁγνίζω, G307 ἀναβιβάζω, G1291 διαστέλλομαι, G1392 δοξάζω, G1521 εἰσάγω, G2511 καθαρίζω, G3903 παρασκευάζω",
    6943: "קֶדֶשׁ (Qedesh | keh'-desh)\n\nDerivation: from H6942 קָדַשׁ ; a sanctum\nStrong's: Kedesh, the name of four places in Palestine\nKJV: Kedesh.\n\nCognate Group: H6947 (Kadeshbarnea), H4720 (chapel), H6945 (sodomite), H6918 (holy), H6944 (consecrated), H6946 (Kadesh), H6948 (harlot), H6942 (appoint), H6943 (Kedesh)",
