    6945: "קָדֵשׁ (qâdêsh | kaw-dashe')\n\nDerivation: from H6942 קָדַשׁ\nStrong's: a (quasi) sacred person, i.e. (technically) a (male) devotee (by prostitution) to licentious idolatry\nKJV: sodomite, unclean.\n\nCognate Group: H6947 (Kadeshbarnea), H4720 (chapel), H6945 (sodomite), H6918 (holy), H6944 (consecrated), H6946 (Kadesh), H6948 (harlot), H6942 (appoint), H6943 (Kedesh)\nGreek Equivalents: G1863 ἐπάγω, G4203 πορνεύω, G4204 πόρνη, G5055 τελέω",
    6946: "קָדֵשׁ (Qâdêsh | kaw-dashe')\n\nDerivation: the same as H6945 קָדֵשׁ ; sanctuary\nStrong's: Kadesh, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Kadesh. Compare H6947 קָדֵשׁ בַּרְנֵעַ .\n\nCognate Group: H6947 (Kadeshbarnea), H4720 (chapel), H6945 (sodomite), H6918 (holy), H6944 (consecrated), H6946 (Kadesh), H6948 (harlot), H6942 (appoint), H6943 (Kedesh)",
    6947: "קָדֵשׁ בַּרְנֵעַ (Qâdêsh Barnêaʻ | kaw-dashe' bar-nay'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H6946 קָדֵשׁ and an otherwise unused word (apparently compounded of a correspondent to H1251 בַּר and a derivative of H5128 נוּעַ) meaning desert of a fugitive; Kadesh of (the) Wilderness of Wandering\nStrong's: Kadesh-Barnea, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Kadeshbarnea.\n\nCognate Group: H6947 (Kadeshbarnea), H4720 (chapel), H6945 (sodomite), H6918 (holy), H6944 (consecrated), H6946 (Kadesh), H6948 (harlot), H6942 (appoint), H6943 (Kedesh)",
    6948: "קְדֵשָׁה (qᵉdêshâh | ked-ay-shaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H6945 קָדֵשׁ\nStrong's: a female devotee (i.e. prostitute)\nKJV: harlot, whore.\n\nCognate Group: H6947 (Kadeshbarnea), H4720 (chapel), H6945 (sodomite), H6918 (holy), H6944 (consecrated), H6946 (Kadesh), H6948 (harlot), H6942 (appoint), H6943 (Kedesh)",
