    6950: "קָהַל (qâhal | 'kaw-hal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to convoke\nKJV: assemble (selves) (together), gather (selves) (together).\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)\nGreek Equivalents: G4863 συνάγω, G4867 συναθροίζω, G4867 συναθροίζω, G4921 συνιστάω",
    6951: "קָהָל (qâhâl | kaw-hawl')\n\nDerivation: from H6950 קָהַל\nStrong's: assemblage (usually concretely)\nKJV: assembly, company, congregation, multitude.\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)\nGreek Equivalents: G1577 ἐκκλησία, G2992 λαός, G3624 οἶκος, G3793 ὄχλος, G4128 πλῆθος, G4864 συναγωγή, G4892 συνέδριον",
    6952: "קְהִלָּה (qᵉhillâh | keh-hil-law')\n\nDerivation: from H6950 קָהַל\nStrong's: an assemblage\nKJV: assembly, congregation.\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)",
    6953: "קֹהֶלֶת (qôheleth | ko-heh'-leth)\n\nDerivation: feminine of active participle from H6950 קָהַל\nStrong's: a (female) assembler (i.e. lecturer); abstractly, preaching (used as a 'nom de plume', Koheleth)\nKJV: preacher.\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)",
    6954: "קְהֵלָתָה (Qᵉhêlâthâh | keh-hay-law'-thaw)\n\nDerivation: from H6950 קָהַל ; convocation\nStrong's: Kehelathah, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Kehelathah.\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)",
    6955: "קְהָת (Qᵉhâth | keh-hawth')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to ally oneself; allied\nStrong's: Kehath, an Israelite\nKJV: Kohath.\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)",
    6956: "קֳהָתִי (Qŏhâthîy | ko-haw-thee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H6955 קְהָת\nStrong's: a Kohathite (collectively) or descendants of Kehath\nKJV: Kohathites.\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)",
    6957: "קַו (qav | kav)\n\nDerivation: or קָו; from H6960 קָוָה (compare H6961 קָוֶה)\nStrong's: a cord (as connecting), especially formeasuring; figuratively, a rule; also a rim, a musical string or accord\nKJV: line. Compare H6978 קַו־קַו \n\nTypo: lemma קַו־קַי yod, corrected to קַו־קַו\n\n.\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)\nGreek Equivalents: G1680 ἐλπίς, G3358 μέτρον, G5353 φθόγγος",
    6958: "קֹוא (qôwʼ | ko)\n\nDerivation: or קָיָה; (Jeremiah 25:27), a primitive root\nStrong's: to vomit\nKJV: spue (out), vomit (out, up, up again).\n\nCognate Group: H6958 (spue), H6892 (vomit)\nGreek Equivalents: G1544 ἐκβάλλω, G4360 προσοχθίζω",
    6959: "קֹובַע (qôwbaʻ | ko'-bah or ko-bah')\n\nDerivation: a form collateral to H3553 כֹּובַע\nStrong's: a helmet\nKJV: helmet.\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)\nGreek Equivalents: G4030 περικεφαλαία",
    6960: "קָוָה (qâvâh | kaw-vaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to bind together (perhaps by twisting), i.e. collect; (figuratively) to expect\nKJV: gather (together), look, patiently, tarry, wait (for, on, upon).\n\nCognate Group: H6978 ([idiom] meted out), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H8615 (expectation), H6960 (gather), H8616 (Tikvah), H6961 (line), H8445 (Tikvath)\nGreek Equivalents: G362 ἀναμένω, G1448 ἐγγίζω, G1679 ἐλπίζω, G1907 ἐπέχω, G3306 μένω, G3982 πείθω, G4037 περιμένω, G4328 προσδοκάω, G4863 συνάγω, G5278 ὑπομένω",
    6961: "קָוֶה (qâveh | kaw-veh')\n\nDerivation: from H6960 קָוָה\nStrong's: a (measuring) cord (as if for binding)\nKJV: line.\n\nCognate Group: H6978 ([idiom] meted out), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H8615 (expectation), H6960 (gather), H8616 (Tikvah), H6961 (line), H8445 (Tikvath)",
    6962: "קוּט (qûwṭ | koot)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to cut off, i.e. (figuratively) detest\nKJV: begrieved, loathe self.\n\nCognate Group: H6962 (begrieved), H5354 (weary)\nGreek Equivalents: G2577 κάμνω, G2875 κόπτω, G4360 προσοχθίζω",
