    6964: "קֹולָיָה (Qôwlâyâh | ko-law-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H6963 קֹול and H3050 יָהּ ; voice of Jah\nStrong's: Kolajah, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Kolaiah.\n\nCognate Group: H7041 (Kelaiah), H6964 (Kolaiah), H6963 (aloud)",
    6965: "קוּם (qûwm | koom)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to rise (in various applications, literal, figurative, intensive and causative)\nKJV: abide, accomplish, [idiom] be clearer, confirm, continue, decree, [idiom] be dim, endure, [idiom] enemy, enjoin, get up, make good, help, hold, (help to) lift up (again), make, [idiom] but newly, ordain, perform, pitch, raise (up), rear (up), remain, (a-) rise (up) (again, against), rouse up, set (up), (e-) stablish, (make to) stand (up), stir up, strengthen, succeed, (as-, make) sure(-ly), (be) up(-hold, -rising).\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H3820 (care for), H3824 (bethink themselves), H3834 (cake), H3826 (heart), H3823 (make cakes)\nGreek Equivalents: G305 ἀναβαίνω, G386 ἀνάστασις, G393 ἀνατέλλω, G436 ἀνθίστημι, G450 ἀνίστημι, G450 ἀνίστημι, G478 ἀντικαθίστημι, G482 ἀντιλαμβάνομαι, G950 βεβαιόω, G1096 γίνομαι, G1303 διατίθεμαι, G1453 ἐγείρω, G1454 ἔγερσις, G1525 εἰσέρχομαι, G1696 ἐμμένω, G1817 ἐξανίστημι, G1825 ἐξεγείρω, G1881 ἐπανίσταμαι, G1892 ἐπεγείρω, G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G2004 ἐπιτάσσω, G2186 ἐφίστημι, G2190 ἐχθρός, G2240 ἥκω, G2250 ἡμέρα, G2476 ἵστημι, G2525 καθίστημι, G2891 κοῦμι, G2902 κρατέω, G2964 κυρόω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3306 μένω, G3404 μισέω, G4104 πιστόω, G4160 ποιέω, G5083 τηρέω, G5087 τίθημι, G5227 ὑπεναντίος, G5278 ὑπομένω",
    6966: "קוּם (qûwm | koom)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H6965 קוּם \nStrong's: to rise (in various applications, literal, figurative, intensive and causative)\nKJV: appoint, establish, make, raise up self, (a-) rise (up), (make to) stand, set (up).\n\nCognate Group: H7011 (stedfast), H7010 (decree), H6966 (appoint)\nGreek Equivalents: G1325 δίδωμι, G2891 κοῦμι",
    6967: "קֹומָה (qôwmâh | ko-maw')\n\nDerivation: from H6965 קוּם\nStrong's: height\nKJV: [idiom] along, height, high, stature, tall.\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H6970 (Koa), H3351 (substance), H4725 (country), H3360 (Jekameam), H6968 (upright), H8617 (power to stand), H3359 (Jekamiah), H8618 (rise up against), H3356 (Jakim), H7054 (corn), H3361 (Jokmeam), H7056 (Camon), H7009 (substance), H6971 (ape), H7012 (rising up), H6967 ([idiom] along)\nGreek Equivalents: G2244 ἡλικία, G3174 μέγεθος, G5247 ὑπεροχή, G5311 ὕψος",
    6968: "קֹומְמִיּוּת (qôwmᵉmîyûwth | ko-mem-ee-yooth')\n\nDerivation: from H6965 קוּם\nStrong's: elevation, i.e. (adverbially) erectly (figuratively)\nKJV: upright.\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H6970 (Koa), H3351 (substance), H4725 (country), H3360 (Jekameam), H6968 (upright), H8617 (power to stand), H3359 (Jekamiah), H8618 (rise up against), H3356 (Jakim), H7054 (corn), H3361 (Jokmeam), H7056 (Camon), H7009 (substance), H6971 (ape), H7012 (rising up), H6967 ([idiom] along)",
    6969: "קוּן (qûwn | koon)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to strike a musical note, i.e. chant or wail (at a funeral)\nKJV: lament, mourning woman.\n\nCognate Group: H7018 (Cainan), H7013 (spear), H7016 (Kinah), H6969 (lament), H7017 (Kenite), H7015 (lamentation), H7014 (Cain)",
    6970: "קֹועַ (Qôwaʻ | ko'-ah)\n\nDerivation: probably from H6972 קוּץ in the original sense of cutting off; curtailment\nStrong's: Koa, a region of Babylon\nKJV: Koa.\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H6970 (Koa), H3351 (substance), H4725 (country), H3360 (Jekameam), H6968 (upright), H8617 (power to stand), H3359 (Jekamiah), H8618 (rise up against), H3356 (Jakim), H7054 (corn), H3361 (Jokmeam), H7056 (Camon), H7009 (substance), H6971 (ape), H7012 (rising up), H6967 ([idiom] along)",
    6971: "קֹוף (qôwph | kofe)\n\nDerivation: or קֹף; of foreign origin,\nStrong's: a monkey\nKJV: ape.\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H6970 (Koa), H3351 (substance), H4725 (country), H3360 (Jekameam), H6968 (upright), H8617 (power to stand), H3359 (Jekamiah), H8618 (rise up against), H3356 (Jakim), H7054 (corn), H3361 (Jokmeam), H7056 (Camon), H7009 (substance), H6971 (ape), H7012 (rising up), H6967 ([idiom] along)",
    6972: "קוּץ (qûwts | koots)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; to clip off; used only as denominative from H7019 קַיִץ\nStrong's: to spend the harvest season\nKJV: summer.\n\nCognate Group: H7023 (mason), H6972 (summer), H7027 (Kish), H7028 (Kishon), H7025 (Kir-haraseth), H7024 (Kir), H7021 (gourd), H7019 (summer)",
    6973: "קוּץ (qûwts | koots)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (identical with through the idea of severing oneself from (compare H6962 קוּט))\nStrong's: to be (causatively, make) disgusted or anxious\nKJV: abhor, be distressed, be grieved, loathe, vex, be weary.\n\nCognate Group: H6973 (abhor)\nGreek Equivalents: G948 βδελύσσω, G1590 ἐκλύω, G4360 προσοχθίζω, G4863 συνάγω",
    6974: "קוּץ (qûwts | koots)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (identical with through the idea of abruptness in starting up from sleep (compare H3364 יָקַץ))\nStrong's: to awake (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: arise, (be) (a-) wake, watch.\n\nCognate Group: H6974 (arise)\nGreek Equivalents: G450 ἀνίστημι, G1817 ἐξανίστημι",
    6975: "קֹוץ (qôwts | kotse)\n\nDerivation: or קֹץ; from H6972 קוּץ (in the sense of pricking)\nStrong's: a thorn\nKJV: thorn.\n\nCognate Group: H6977 (lock), H6975 (thorn), H6976 (Koz)\nGreek Equivalents: G173 ἄκανθα",
    6976: "קֹוץ (Qôwts | kotse)\n\nDerivation: the same as H6975 קֹוץ\nStrong's: Kots, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Koz, Hakkoz (including the article).\n\nCognate Group: H6977 (lock), H6975 (thorn), H6976 (Koz)",
    6977: "קְוֻצָּה (qᵉvutstsâh | kev-oots-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of H6972 קוּץ in its original sense\nStrong's: a forelock (as shorn)\nKJV: lock.\n\nCognate Group: H6977 (lock), H6975 (thorn), H6976 (Koz)",
    6978: "קַו־קַו (qav-qav | kav-kav')Typo: lemma קַו־קַי yod, corrected to קַו־קַו\n\nDerivation: from H6957 קַו (in the sense of a fastening)\n\nStrong's: stalwart\nKJV: [idiom] meted out.\n\nCognate Group: H6978 ([idiom] meted out), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H8615 (expectation), H6960 (gather), H8616 (Tikvah), H6961 (line), H8445 (Tikvath)",
    6979: "קוּר (qûwr | koor)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; also denominative from H7023 קִיר \nStrong's: to trench; by implication, to throw forth; to wall up, whether literal (to build a wall) or figurative (to estop)\nKJV: break down, cast out, destroy, dig.\n\nCognate Group: H6979 (break down), H4726 (fountain)\nGreek Equivalents: G5087 τίθημι, G5594 ψύχω",
    6980: "קוּר (qûwr | koor)\n\nDerivation: from H6979 קוּר\nStrong's: (only plural) trenches, i.e. a web (as if so formed)\nKJV: web.\n\nCognate Group: H6980 (web)",
    6981: "קֹורֵא (Qôwrêʼ | ko-ray')\n\nDerivation: or קֹרֵא; (1 Chronicles 26:1), active participle of H7121 קָרָא ; crier\nStrong's: Kore, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Kore.\n\nCognate Group: H7150 (preaching), H6981 (Kore), H7121 (bewray), H7148 (famous), H4744 (assembly), H7124 (partridge)",
