    6983: "קֹושׁ (qôwsh | koshe)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; to bend; used only as denominative for H3369 יָקֹשׁ,\nStrong's: to set a trap\nKJV: lay a snare.\n\nCognate Group: H7029 (Kishi), H6985 (very), H6983 (lay a snare), H6984 (Kushaiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G4348 πρόσκομμα, G5087 τίθημι",
    6984: "קוּשָׁיָהוּ (qûwshâyâhûw | koo-shaw-yaw'-hoo)\n\nDerivation: from the passive participle of H6983 קֹושׁ and H3050 יָהּ ; entrapped of Jah\nStrong's: Kushajah, an Israelite\nKJV: Kushaiah.\n\nCognate Group: H7029 (Kishi), H6985 (very), H6983 (lay a snare), H6984 (Kushaiah)",
    6985: "קַט (qaṭ | kat)\n\nDerivation: from H6990 קָטַט in the sense of abbreviation\nStrong's: a little, i.e. (adverbially) merely\nKJV: very.\n\nCognate Group: H7029 (Kishi), H6985 (very), H6983 (lay a snare), H6984 (Kushaiah)",
    6986: "קֶטֶב (qeṭeb | keh'-teb)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to cut off\nStrong's: ruin\nKJV: destroying, destruction.\n\nCognate Group: H6986 (destroying), H6987 (destruction)\nGreek Equivalents: G970 βία, G2702 καταφέρω",
