    6988: "קְטֹורָה (qᵉṭôwrâh | ket-o-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H6999 קָטַר\nStrong's: perfume\nKJV: incense.\n\nCognate Group: H7008 (smoke), H7004 (incense), H4730 (censer), H4729 (to burn), H7002 (incense), H6989 (Keturah), H6999 (burn), H6988 (incense)",
    6989: "קְטוּרָה (Qᵉṭûwrâh | ket-oo-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of H6999 קָטַר ; perfumed\nStrong's: Keturah, a wife of Abraham\nKJV: Keturah.\n\nCognate Group: H7008 (smoke), H7004 (incense), H4730 (censer), H4729 (to burn), H7002 (incense), H6989 (Keturah), H6999 (burn), H6988 (incense)",
    6990: "קָטַט (qâṭaṭ | kaw-tat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to clip off, i.e. (figuratively) destroy\nKJV: be cut off.\n\nCognate Group: H6990 (be cut off)",
