    6994: "קָטֹן (qâṭôn | kaw-tone')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (rather denominative from H6996 קָטָן)\nStrong's: to diminish, i.e. be (causatively, make) diminutive or (figuratively) of no account\nKJV: be a (make) small (thing), be not worthy.\n\nCognate Group: H6995 (little finger), H6997 (Hakkatan), H6994 (be a small), H6996 (least)\nGreek Equivalents: G2427 ἱκανόω",
    6995: "קֹטֶן (qôṭen | ko'-ten)\n\nDerivation: from H6994 קָטֹן\nStrong's: a pettiness, i.e. the little finger\nKJV: little finger.\n\nCognate Group: H6995 (little finger), H6997 (Hakkatan), H6994 (be a small), H6996 (least)\nGreek Equivalents: G1147 δάκτυλος, G3398 μικρός",
    6996: "קָטָן (qâṭân | kaw-tawn')\n\nDerivation: or קָטֹן; from H6962 קוּט\nStrong's: abbreviated, i.e. diminutive, literally (in quantity, size or number) or figuratively (in age or importance)\nKJV: least, less(-er), little (one), small(-est, one, quantity, thing), young(-er, -est).\n\nCognate Group: H6995 (little finger), H6997 (Hakkatan), H6994 (be a small), H6996 (least)\nGreek Equivalents: G1024 βραχύς, G1640 ἐλάσσων, G1645 ἐλαφρός, G3398 μικρός, G3398 μικρός, G3398 μικρός, G3398 μικρός, G3501 νέος, G4434 πτωχός",
