    6998: "קָטַף (qâṭaph | kaw-taf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to strip off\nKJV: crop off, cut down (up), pluck.\n\nCognate Group: H6998 (crop off)\nGreek Equivalents: G2325 θερίζω, G3954 παῤῥησία, G4816 συλλέγω, G4863 συνάγω",
    6999: "קָטַר (qâṭar | kaw-tar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (identical with through the idea of fumigation in a close place and perhaps thus driving out the occupants)\nStrong's: to smoke, i.e. turn into fragrance by fire (especially as an act of worship)\nKJV: burn (incense, sacrifice) (upon), (altar for) incense, kindle, offer (incense, a sacrifice).\n\nCognate Group: H7008 (smoke), H7004 (incense), H4730 (censer), H4729 (to burn), H7002 (incense), H6989 (Keturah), H6999 (burn), H6988 (incense)\nGreek Equivalents: G399 ἀναφέρω, G2005 ἐπιτελέω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2368 θυμίαμα, G2370 θυμιάω, G2380 θύω, G4374 προσφέρω",
    7000: "קָטַר (qâṭar | kaw-tar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to inclose\nKJV: join.\n\nCognate Group: H7003 (Kitron), H7000 (join), H7005 (Kattath)",
    7001: "קְטַר (qᵉṭar | ket-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H7000 קָטַר\nStrong's: a knot (as tied up), i.e. (figuratively) a riddle; also a vertebra (as if a knot)\nKJV: doubt, joint.\n\nCognate Group: H7007 (summer), H7030 (harp), H7001 (doubt)\nGreek Equivalents: G4886 σύνδεσμος",
    7002: "קִטֵּר (qiṭṭêr | kit-tare')\n\nDerivation: from H6999 קָטַר\nStrong's: perfume\nKJV: incense.\n\nCognate Group: H7008 (smoke), H7004 (incense), H4730 (censer), H4729 (to burn), H7002 (incense), H6989 (Keturah), H6999 (burn), H6988 (incense)",
    7003: "קִטְרֹון (Qiṭrôwn | kit-rone')\n\nDerivation: from H6999 קָטַר ; fumigative\nStrong's: Kitron, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Kitron.\n\nCognate Group: H7003 (Kitron), H7000 (join), H7005 (Kattath)",
    7004: "קְטֹרֶת (qᵉṭôreth | ket-o'-reth)\n\nDerivation: from H6999 קָטַר\nStrong's: a fumigation\nKJV: (sweet) incense, perfume.\n\nCognate Group: H7008 (smoke), H7004 (incense), H4730 (censer), H4729 (to burn), H7002 (incense), H6989 (Keturah), H6999 (burn), H6988 (incense)\nGreek Equivalents: G2368 θυμίαμα",
