    7008: "קִיטֹור (qîyṭôwr | kee-tore')\n\nDerivation: or קִיטֹר; from H6999 קָטַר\nStrong's: a fume, i.e. cloud\nKJV: smoke, vapour.\n\nCognate Group: H7008 (smoke), H7004 (incense), H4730 (censer), H4729 (to burn), H7002 (incense), H6989 (Keturah), H6999 (burn), H6988 (incense)\nGreek Equivalents: G822 ἀτμίς, G2930 κρύσταλλος, G5395 φλόξ",
    7009: "קִים (qîym | keem)\n\nDerivation: from H6965 קוּם\nStrong's: an opponent (as rising against one), i.e. (collectively) enemies\nKJV: substance.\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H6970 (Koa), H3351 (substance), H4725 (country), H3360 (Jekameam), H6968 (upright), H8617 (power to stand), H3359 (Jekamiah), H8618 (rise up against), H3356 (Jakim), H7054 (corn), H3361 (Jokmeam), H7056 (Camon), H7009 (substance), H6971 (ape), H7012 (rising up), H6967 ([idiom] along)",
