    7011: "קַיָּם (qayâm | kah-yawm')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H6966 קוּם\nStrong's: permanent (as rising firmly)\nKJV: stedfast, sure.\n\nCognate Group: H7011 (stedfast), H7010 (decree), H6966 (appoint)\nGreek Equivalents: G4933 συντηρέω",
    7012: "קִימָה (qîymâh | kee-maw')\n\nDerivation: from H6965 קוּם\nStrong's: an arising\nKJV: rising up.\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H6970 (Koa), H3351 (substance), H4725 (country), H3360 (Jekameam), H6968 (upright), H8617 (power to stand), H3359 (Jekamiah), H8618 (rise up against), H3356 (Jakim), H7054 (corn), H3361 (Jokmeam), H7056 (Camon), H7009 (substance), H6971 (ape), H7012 (rising up), H6967 ([idiom] along)\nGreek Equivalents: G386 ἀνάστασις",
    7013: "קַיִן (qayin | kah'-yin)\n\nDerivation: from H6969 קוּן in the original sense of fixity\nStrong's: a lance (as striking fast)\nKJV: spear.\n\nCognate Group: H7018 (Cainan), H7013 (spear), H7016 (Kinah), H6969 (lament), H7017 (Kenite), H7015 (lamentation), H7014 (Cain)\nGreek Equivalents: G2535 Κάϊν",
    7014: "קַיִן (Qayin | kah'-yin)\n\nDerivation: the same as H7013 קַיִן (with a play upon the affinity to H7069 קָנָה)\nStrong's: Kajin, the name of the first child, also of a place in Palestine, and of an Oriental tribe\nKJV: Cain, Kenite(-s).\n\nCognate Group: H7018 (Cainan), H7013 (spear), H7016 (Kinah), H6969 (lament), H7017 (Kenite), H7015 (lamentation), H7014 (Cain)\nGreek Equivalents: G2535 Κάϊν",
    7015: "קִינָה (qîynâh | kee-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H6969 קוּן\nStrong's: a dirge (as accompanied by beating the breasts or on instruments)\nKJV: lamentation.\n\nCognate Group: H7018 (Cainan), H7013 (spear), H7016 (Kinah), H6969 (lament), H7017 (Kenite), H7015 (lamentation), H7014 (Cain)\nGreek Equivalents: G2354 θρηνέω",
    7016: "קִינָה (Qîynâh | kee-naw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7015 קִינָה\nStrong's: Kinah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Kinah.\n\nCognate Group: H7018 (Cainan), H7013 (spear), H7016 (Kinah), H6969 (lament), H7017 (Kenite), H7015 (lamentation), H7014 (Cain)",
    7017: "קֵינִי (Qêynîy | kay-nee')\n\nDerivation: or קִינִי; (1 Chronicles 2:55), patronymic from H7014 קַיִן\nStrong's: a Kenite or member of the tribe of Kajin\nKJV: Kenite.\n\nCognate Group: H7018 (Cainan), H7013 (spear), H7016 (Kinah), H6969 (lament), H7017 (Kenite), H7015 (lamentation), H7014 (Cain)",
    7018: "קֵינָן (Qêynân | kay-nawn')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7064 קֵן ; fixed\nStrong's: Kenan, an antediluvian\nKJV: Cainan, Kenan.\n\nCognate Group: H7018 (Cainan), H7013 (spear), H7016 (Kinah), H6969 (lament), H7017 (Kenite), H7015 (lamentation), H7014 (Cain)\nGreek Equivalents: G2536 Καϊνάν",
    7019: "קַיִץ (qayits | kah'-yits)\n\nDerivation: from H6972 קוּץ\nStrong's: harvest (as the crop), whether the product (grain or fruit) or the (dry) season\nKJV: summer (fruit, house).\n\nCognate Group: H7023 (mason), H6972 (summer), H7027 (Kish), H7028 (Kishon), H7025 (Kir-haraseth), H7024 (Kir), H7021 (gourd), H7019 (summer)\nGreek Equivalents: G2326 θερισμός, G2330 θέρος, G2738 καῦμα, G3703 ὀπώρα",
    7020: "קִיצֹון (qîytsôwn | kee-tsone')\n\nDerivation: from H6972 קוּץ\nStrong's: terminal\nKJV: out-(utter-) most.\n\nCognate Group: H7104 (Keziz), H7112 (cut), H7020 (out- most), H7093 (after)\nGreek Equivalents: G1857 ἐξώτερος",
    7021: "קִיקָיֹון (qîyqâyôwn | kee-kaw-yone')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from H7006 קָיָה\nStrong's: the gourd (as nauseous)\nKJV: gourd.\n\nCognate Group: H7023 (mason), H6972 (summer), H7027 (Kish), H7028 (Kishon), H7025 (Kir-haraseth), H7024 (Kir), H7021 (gourd), H7019 (summer)",
    7022: "קִיקָלֹון (qîyqâlôwn | kee-kaw-lone')\n\nDerivation: from H7036 קָלֹון\nStrong's: intense disgrace\nKJV: shameful spewing.\n\nCognate Group: H7031 (light), H7040 (Kallai), H6963 (aloud), H7052 (light), H7044 (burnished), H7045 (curse), H7022 (shameful spewing), H7043 (abate)",
    7023: "קִיר (qîyr | keer)\n\nDerivation: or קִר; (Isaiah 22:5), or (feminine) קִירָה; from H6979 קוּר\nStrong's: a wall (as built in a trench)\nKJV: [phrase] mason, side, town, [idiom] very, wall.\n\nCognate Group: H7023 (mason), H6972 (summer), H7027 (Kish), H7028 (Kishon), H7025 (Kir-haraseth), H7024 (Kir), H7021 (gourd), H7019 (summer)\nGreek Equivalents: G145 αἰσθητήριον, G939 βάσις, G1385 δοκός, G5038 τεῖχος, G5109 τοῖχος",
    7024: "קִיר (Qîyr | keer)\n\nDerivation: the same as H7023 קִיר ; fortress\nStrong's: Kir, a place in Assyrian; also one in Moab\nKJV: Kir. Compare H7025 קִיר חֶרֶשׂ .\n\nCognate Group: H7023 (mason), H6972 (summer), H7027 (Kish), H7028 (Kishon), H7025 (Kir-haraseth), H7024 (Kir), H7021 (gourd), H7019 (summer)",
    7025: "קִיר חֶרֶשׂ (Qîyr Cheres | keer kheh'-res)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine of the latter word) קִיר חֲרֶשֶׂת; from H7023 קִיר and H2789 חֶרֶשׂ ; fortress of earthenware\nStrong's: Kir-Cheres or Kir-Chareseth, a place in Moab\nKJV: Kir-haraseth, Kir-hareseth, Kirharesh, Kir-heres.\n\nCognate Group: H7023 (mason), H6972 (summer), H7027 (Kish), H7028 (Kishon), H7025 (Kir-haraseth), H7024 (Kir), H7021 (gourd), H7019 (summer)",
    7026: "קֵירֹס (Qêyrôç | kay-roce')\n\nDerivation: or קֵרֹס; from the same as H7166 קַרְסֹל ; ankled\nStrong's: Keros, one of the Nethinim\nKJV: Keros.\n\nCognate Group: H7166 (foot), H7165 (tache), H7026 (Keros), H7164 (stoop)",
    7027: "קִישׁ (Qîysh | keesh)\n\nDerivation: from H6983 קֹושׁ ; a bow\nStrong's: Kish, the name of five Israelites\nKJV: Kish.\n\nCognate Group: H7023 (mason), H6972 (summer), H7027 (Kish), H7028 (Kishon), H7025 (Kir-haraseth), H7024 (Kir), H7021 (gourd), H7019 (summer)\nGreek Equivalents: G2797 Κίς",
    7028: "קִישֹׁון (Qîyshôwn | kee-shone')\n\nDerivation: from H6983 קֹושׁ ; winding\nStrong's: Kishon, a river of Palestine\nKJV: Kishon, Kison.\n\nCognate Group: H7023 (mason), H6972 (summer), H7027 (Kish), H7028 (Kishon), H7025 (Kir-haraseth), H7024 (Kir), H7021 (gourd), H7019 (summer)",
    7029: "קִישִׁי (Qîyshîy | kee-shee')\n\nDerivation: from H6983 קֹושׁ ; bowed\nStrong's: Kishi, an Israelite\nKJV: Kishi.\n\nCognate Group: H7029 (Kishi), H6985 (very), H6983 (lay a snare), H6984 (Kushaiah)",
