    7032: "קָל (qâl | kawl)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H6963 קֹול \nStrong's: a voice or sound\nKJV: sound, voice.\n\nCognate Group: H7032 (sound)",
    7033: "קָלָה (qâlâh | kaw-law')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (rather identical with H7034 קָלָה through the idea of shrinkage by heat)\nStrong's: to toast, i.e. scorch partially or slowly\nKJV: dried, loathsome, parch, roast.\n\nCognate Group: H7039 (parched corn), H7033 (dried)",
