    7035: "קָלַהּ (qâlahh | kaw-lah')\n\nDerivation: for H6950 קָהַל\nStrong's: to assemble\nKJV: gather together.\n\nCognate Group: H6959 (helmet), H6955 (Kohath), H4721 (congregation), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H6951 (assembly), H6954 (Kehelathah), H7035 (gather together), H6952 (assembly), H6950 (assemble), H4722 (Makheloth), H6956 (Kohathites), H6953 (preacher)",
    7036: "קָלֹון (qâlôwn | kaw-lone')\n\nDerivation: from H7034 קָלָה\nStrong's: disgrace; (by implication) the pudenda\nKJV: confusion, dishonour, ignominy, reproach, shame.\n\nCognate Group: H7034 (base), H7037 (caldron), H7036 (confusion)\nGreek Equivalents: G458 ἀνομία, G819 ἀτιμία",
