    7038: "קָלַט (qâlaṭ | kaw-lat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to maim\nKJV: lacking in his parts.\n\nCognate Group: H7038 (lacking in his parts), H7042 (Kelita)",
    7039: "קָלִי (qâlîy | kaw-lee')\n\nDerivation: or קָלִיא; from H7033 קָלָה\nStrong's: roasted ears of grain\nKJV: parched corn.\n\nCognate Group: H7039 (parched corn), H7033 (dried)",
    7040: "קַלַּי (Qallay | kal-lah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H7043 קָלַל ; frivolous\nStrong's: Kallai, an Israelite\nKJV: Kallai.\n\nCognate Group: H7031 (light), H7040 (Kallai), H6963 (aloud), H7052 (light), H7044 (burnished), H7045 (curse), H7022 (shameful spewing), H7043 (abate)",
    7041: "קֵלָיָה (Qêlâyâh | kay-law-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H7034 קָלָה ; insignificance\nStrong's: Kelajah, an Israelite\nKJV: Kelaiah.\n\nCognate Group: H7041 (Kelaiah), H6964 (Kolaiah), H6963 (aloud)",
