    7043: "קָלַל (qâlal | kaw-lal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be (causatively, make) light, literally (swift, small, sharp, etc.) or figuratively (easy, trifling, vile, etc.)\nKJV: abate, make bright, bring into contempt, (ac-) curse, despise, (be) ease(-y, -ier), (be a, make, make somewhat, move, seem a, set) light(-en, -er, -ly, -ly afflict, -ly esteem, thing), [idiom] slight(-ly), be swift(-er), (be, be more, make, re-) vile, whet.\n\nCognate Group: H7031 (light), H7040 (Kallai), H6963 (aloud), H7052 (light), H7044 (burnished), H7045 (curse), H7022 (shameful spewing), H7043 (abate)\nGreek Equivalents: G447 ἀνίημι, G601 ἀποκαλύπτω, G821 ἀτιμόω, G863 ἀφίημι, G1814 ἐξάλλομαι, G1823 ἐξαστράπτω, G2425 ἱκανός, G2551 κακολογέω, G2560 κακῶς, G2672 καταράομαι, G2869 κοπάζω, G2893 κουφίζω, G3398 μικρός, G4744 στίλβω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5195 ὑβρίζω",
    7044: "קָלָל (qâlâl | kaw-lawl')\n\nDerivation: from H7043 קָלַל\nStrong's: brightened (as if sharpened)\nKJV: burnished, polished.\n\nCognate Group: H7031 (light), H7040 (Kallai), H6963 (aloud), H7052 (light), H7044 (burnished), H7045 (curse), H7022 (shameful spewing), H7043 (abate)\nGreek Equivalents: G1645 ἐλαφρός",
    7045: "קְלָלָה (qᵉlâlâh | kel-aw-law')\n\nDerivation: from H7043 קָלַל\nStrong's: vilification\nKJV: (ac-) curse(-d, -ing).\n\nCognate Group: H7031 (light), H7040 (Kallai), H6963 (aloud), H7052 (light), H7044 (burnished), H7045 (curse), H7022 (shameful spewing), H7043 (abate)\nGreek Equivalents: G685 ἀρά, G2671 κατάρα",
    7046: "קָלַס (qâlaç | kaw-las')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to disparage, i.e. ridicule\nKJV: mock, scoff, scorn.\n\nCognate Group: H7047 (derision), H7048 (mocking), H7046 (mock)\nGreek Equivalents: G1702 ἐμπαίζω, G1792 ἐντρυφάω",
    7047: "קֶלֶס (qeleç | keh'-les)\n\nDerivation: from H7046 קָלַס\nStrong's: a laughing-stock\nKJV: derision.\n\nCognate Group: H7047 (derision), H7048 (mocking), H7046 (mock)",
    7048: "קַלָּסָה (qallâçâh | kal-law-saw')\n\nDerivation: intensive from H7046 קָלַס\nStrong's: ridicule\nKJV: mocking.\n\nCognate Group: H7047 (derision), H7048 (mocking), H7046 (mock)\nGreek Equivalents: G1701 ἐμπαιγμός",
    7049: "קָלַע (qâlaʻ | kaw-lah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to sling; also to carve (as if a circular motion, or into light forms)\nKJV: carve, sling (out).\n\nCognate Group: H7051 (slinger), H7050 (hanging), H7049 (carve)\nGreek Equivalents: G906 βάλλω, G1125 γράφω",
    7050: "קֶלַע (qelaʻ | keh'-lah)\n\nDerivation: from H7049 קָלַע\nStrong's: a sling; also a (door) screen (as if slung across), or the valve (of the door) itself\nKJV: hanging, leaf, sling.\n\nCognate Group: H7051 (slinger), H7050 (hanging), H7049 (carve)",
    7051: "קַלָּע (qallâʻ | kal-law')\n\nDerivation: intensive from H7049 קָלַע\nStrong's: a slinger\nKJV: slinger.\n\nCognate Group: H7051 (slinger), H7050 (hanging), H7049 (carve)",
    7052: "קְלֹקֵל (qᵉlôqêl | kel-o-kale')\n\nDerivation: from H7043 קָלַל\nStrong's: insubstantial\nKJV: light.\n\nCognate Group: H7031 (light), H7040 (Kallai), H6963 (aloud), H7052 (light), H7044 (burnished), H7045 (curse), H7022 (shameful spewing), H7043 (abate)",
    7053: "קִלְּשֹׁון (qillᵉshôwn | kil-lesh-one')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to prick\nStrong's: a prong, i.e. hay-fork\nKJV: fork.\n\nCognate Group: H7053 (fork), H7049 (carve), H4734 (carved), H7055 (Kemuel)",
    7054: "קָמָה (qâmâh | kuw-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of active participle of H6965 קוּם\nStrong's: something that rises, i.e. a stalk of grain\nKJV: (standing) corn, grown up, stalk.\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H6970 (Koa), H3351 (substance), H4725 (country), H3360 (Jekameam), H6968 (upright), H8617 (power to stand), H3359 (Jekamiah), H8618 (rise up against), H3356 (Jakim), H7054 (corn), H3361 (Jokmeam), H7056 (Camon), H7009 (substance), H6971 (ape), H7012 (rising up), H6967 ([idiom] along)\nGreek Equivalents: G3717 ὀρθός, G4719 στάχυς",
    7055: "קְמוּאֵל (Qᵉmûwʼêl | kem-oo-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H6965 קוּם and H410 אֵל ; raised of God\nStrong's: Kemuel, the name of a relative of Abraham, and of two Israelites\nKJV: Kemuel.\n\nCognate Group: H7053 (fork), H7049 (carve), H4734 (carved), H7055 (Kemuel)",
    7056: "קָמֹון (Qâmôwn | kaw-mone')\n\nDerivation: from H6965 קוּם ; an elevation\nStrong's: Kamon, a place East of the Jordan\nKJV: Camon.\n\nCognate Group: H6965 (abide), H6970 (Koa), H3351 (substance), H4725 (country), H3360 (Jekameam), H6968 (upright), H8617 (power to stand), H3359 (Jekamiah), H8618 (rise up against), H3356 (Jakim), H7054 (corn), H3361 (Jokmeam), H7056 (Camon), H7009 (substance), H6971 (ape), H7012 (rising up), H6967 ([idiom] along)",
    7057: "קִמֹּושׁ (qimmôwsh | kim-moshe')\n\nDerivation: or קִימֹושׁ; from an unused root meaning to sting\nStrong's: a prickly plant\nKJV: nettle. Compare H7063 קִמָּשֹׁון .\n\nCognate Group: H7063 (thorn), H7057 (nettle)\nGreek Equivalents: G3639 ὄλεθρος",
    7058: "קֶמַח (qemach | keh'-makh)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to grind\nStrong's: flour\nKJV: flour, meal.\n\nCognate Group: H7058 (flour)\nGreek Equivalents: G224 ἄλευρον, G4585 σεμίδαλις",
    7059: "קָמַט (qâmaṭ | kaw-mat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to pluck, i.e. destroy\nKJV: cut down, fill with wrinkles.\n\nCognate Group: H7059 (cut down)\nGreek Equivalents: G1949 ἐπιλαμβάνομαι, G4815 συλλαμβάνω",
    7060: "קָמַל (qâmal | kaw-mal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to wither\nKJV: hew down, wither.\n\nCognate Group: H7060 (hew down)\nGreek Equivalents: G18 ἀγαθός",
    7061: "קָמַץ (qâmats | kaw-mats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to grasp with the hand\nKJV: take an handful.\n\nCognate Group: H7061 (take an handful), H7062 (handful)\nGreek Equivalents: G1405 δράσσομαι",
    7062: "קֹמֶץ (qômets | ko'mets)\n\nDerivation: from H7061 קָמַץ\nStrong's: a grasp, i.e. handful\nKJV: handful.\n\nCognate Group: H7061 (take an handful), H7062 (handful)",
    7063: "קִמָּשֹׁון (qimmâshôwn | kim-maw-shone')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7057 קִמֹּושׁ\nStrong's: a prickly plant\nKJV: thorn.\n\nCognate Group: H7063 (thorn), H7057 (nettle)",
    7064: "קֵן (qên | kane)\n\nDerivation: contracted from H7077 קָנַן\nStrong's: a nest (as fixed), sometimes including the nestlings; figuratively, a chamber or dwelling\nKJV: nest, room.\n\nCognate Group: H7077 (make), H7064 (nest)\nGreek Equivalents: G3502 νεοσσός, G3555 νοσσιά",
    7065: "קָנָא (qânâʼ | kaw-naw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be (causatively, make) zealous, i.e. (in a bad sense) jealous or envious\nKJV: (be) envy(-ious), be (move to, provoke to) jealous(-y), [idiom] very, (be) zeal(-ous).\n\nCognate Group: H7067 (jealous), H7072 (jealous), H7068 (envy), H7065 (envy)\nGreek Equivalents: G2206 ζηλόω, G3863 παραζηλόω, G3947 παροξύνω, G3949 παροργίζω",
    7066: "קְנָא (qᵉnâʼ | ken-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7069 קָנָה\nStrong's: to purchase\nKJV: buy.\n\nCognate Group: H7066 (buy)",
    7067: "קַנָּא (qannâʼ | kan-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H7065 קָנָא\nStrong's: jealous\nKJV: jealous. Compare H7072 קַנֹּוא .\n\nCognate Group: H7067 (jealous), H7072 (jealous), H7068 (envy), H7065 (envy)\nGreek Equivalents: G2207 ζηλωτής, G2208 Ζηλωτής, G2581 Κανανίτης",
    7068: "קִנְאָה (qinʼâh | kin-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H7065 קָנָא\nStrong's: jealousy or envy\nKJV: envy(-ied), jealousy, [idiom] sake, zeal.\n\nCognate Group: H7067 (jealous), H7072 (jealous), H7068 (envy), H7065 (envy)\nGreek Equivalents: G2205 ζῆλος, G2355 θρῆνος, G2372 θυμός",
    7069: "קָנָה (qânâh | kaw-naw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to erect, i.e. create; by extension, to procure, especially by purchase (causatively, sell); by implication to own\nKJV: attain, buy(-er), teach to keep cattle, get, provoke to jealousy, possess(-or), purchase, recover, redeem, [idiom] surely, [idiom] verily.\n\nCognate Group: H7075 (getting), H4736 (bought), H4737 (Mikneiah), H4735 (cattle), H7069 (attain)\nGreek Equivalents: G25 ἀγαπάω, G59 ἀγοράζω, G1081 γέννημα, G2932 κτάομαι, G2936 κτίζω, G3084 λυτρόω",
    7070: "קָנֶה (qâneh | kaw-neh')\n\nDerivation: from H7069 קָנָה\nStrong's: a reed (as erect); by resemblance a rod (especially for measuring), shaft, tube, stem, the radius (of the arm), beam (of a steelyard)\nKJV: balance, bone, branch, calamus, cane, reed, [idiom] spearman, stalk.\n\nCognate Group: H7070 (balance), H7074 (Kenezite), H7073 (Kenaz), H7076 (cinnamon), H7071 (Kanah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2218 ζυγός, G2368 θυμίαμα, G2563 κάλαμος, G2583 κανών, G4083 πῆχυς",
    7071: "קָנָה (Qânâh | kaw-naw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7070 קָנֶה ; reediness\nStrong's: Kanah, the name of a stream and of a place in Palestine\nKJV: Kanah.\n\nCognate Group: H7070 (balance), H7074 (Kenezite), H7073 (Kenaz), H7076 (cinnamon), H7071 (Kanah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2580 Κανᾶ",
    7072: "קַנֹּוא (qannôwʼ | kan-no')\n\nDerivation: for H7067 קַנָּא\nStrong's: jealous or angry\nKJV: jealous.\n\nCognate Group: H7067 (jealous), H7072 (jealous), H7068 (envy), H7065 (envy)\nGreek Equivalents: G2207 ζηλωτής, G2208 Ζηλωτής",
    7073: "קְנַז (Qᵉnaz | ken-az')\n\nDerivation: probably from an unused root meaning to hunt; hunter\nStrong's: Kenaz, the name of an Edomite and of two Israelites\nKJV: Kenaz.\n\nCognate Group: H7070 (balance), H7074 (Kenezite), H7073 (Kenaz), H7076 (cinnamon), H7071 (Kanah)",
    7074: "קְנִזִּי (Qᵉnizzîy | ken-iz-zee')\n\nDerivation: patronymic from H7073 קְנַז,\nStrong's: a Kenizzite or descendant of Kenaz\nKJV: Kenezite, Kenizzites.\n\nCognate Group: H7070 (balance), H7074 (Kenezite), H7073 (Kenaz), H7076 (cinnamon), H7071 (Kanah)",
    7075: "קִנְיָן (qinyân | kin-yawn')\n\nDerivation: from H7069 קָנָה\nStrong's: creation, i.e. (concretely) creatures; also acquisition, purchase, wealth\nKJV: getting, goods, [idiom] with money, riches, substance.\n\nCognate Group: H7075 (getting), H4736 (bought), H4737 (Mikneiah), H4735 (cattle), H7069 (attain)\nGreek Equivalents: G2934 κτῆνος, G2937 κτίσις",
    7076: "קִנָּמֹון (qinnâmôwn | kin-naw-mone')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (meaning to erect)\nStrong's: cinnamon bark (as in upright rolls)\nKJV: cinnamon.\n\nCognate Group: H7070 (balance), H7074 (Kenezite), H7073 (Kenaz), H7076 (cinnamon), H7071 (Kanah)",
    7077: "קָנַן (qânan | kaw-nan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; to erect; but used only as denominative from H7064 קֵן\nStrong's: to nestle, i.e. build or occupy as anest\nKJV: make...nest.\n\nCognate Group: H7077 (make), H7064 (nest)",
    7078: "קֶנֶץ (qenets | keh'-nets)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to wrench\nStrong's: perversion\nKJV: end.\n\nCognate Group: H7079 (Kenath), H7078 (end)",
    7079: "קְנָת (Qᵉnâth | ken-awth')\n\nDerivation: from H7069 קָנָה ; possession\nStrong's: Kenath, a place East of the Jordan\nKJV: Kenath.\n\nCognate Group: H7079 (Kenath), H7078 (end)\nGreek Equivalents: G206 ἄκρον, G3310 μερίς, G3313 μέρος, G3319 μέσος, G4009 πέρας",
    7080: "קָסַם (qâçam | kaw-sam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to distribute, i.e. determine by lot or magical scroll; by implication, to divine\nKJV: divine(-r, -ation), prudent, soothsayer, use (divination).\n\nCognate Group: H7081 (divination), H4738 (divination), H7080 (divine)\nGreek Equivalents: G669 ἀποφθέγγομαι, G3132 μαντεύομαι",
    7081: "קֶסֶם (qeçem | keh'-sem)\n\nDerivation: from H7080 קָסַם\nStrong's: a lot; also divination (including its fee), oracle\nKJV: (reward of) divination, divine sentence, witchcraft.\n\nCognate Group: H7081 (divination), H4738 (divination), H7080 (divine)\nGreek Equivalents: G2973 Κωσάμ",
    7082: "קָסַס (qâçaç | kaw-sas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to lop off\nKJV: cut off.\n\nCognate Group: H7084 (Keilah), H7082 (cut off)",
    7083: "קֶסֶת (qeçeth | keh'-seth)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3563 כֹּוס (or as H7185 קָשָׁה)\nStrong's: properly, a cup, i.e. an ink-stand\nKJV: inkhorn.\n\nCognate Group: H7083 (inkhorn), H7184 (cover)\nGreek Equivalents: G2223 ζώνη, G5357 φιάλη",
    7084: "קְעִילָה (Qᵉʻîylâh | keh-ee-law')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from H7049 קָלַע in the sense of enclosing; citadel\nStrong's: Keilah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Keilah.\n\nCognate Group: H7084 (Keilah), H7082 (cut off)",
    7085: "קַעֲקַע (qaʻăqaʻ | kah-ak-ah')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H6970 קֹועַ\nStrong's: an incision or gash\nKJV: [phrase] mark.\n\nCognate Group: H7085 (mark)",
    7086: "קְעָרָה (qᵉʻârâh | keh-aw-raw')\n\nDerivation: probably from H7167 קָרַע\nStrong's: a bowl (as cut out hollow)\nKJV: charger, dish.\n\nCognate Group: H7086 (charger), H8258 (hollow strake)\nGreek Equivalents: G5165 τρύβλιον",
    7087: "קָפָא (qâphâʼ | kaw-faw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to shrink, i.e. thicken (as unracked wine, curdled milk, clouded sky, frozen water)\nKJV: congeal, curdle, dark, settle.\n\nCognate Group: H7087 (congeal)\nGreek Equivalents: G4078 πήγνυμι",
    7088: "קָפַד (qâphad | kaw-fad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to contract, i.e. roll together\nKJV: cut off.\n\nCognate Group: H7088 (cut off), H7089 (destruction), H7090 (bittern)",
    7089: "קְפָדָה (qᵉphâdâh | kef-aw-daw')\n\nDerivation: from H7088 קָפַד\nStrong's: shrinking, i.e., terror\nKJV: destruction.\n\nCognate Group: H7088 (cut off), H7089 (destruction), H7090 (bittern)",
    7090: "קִפֹּוד (qippôwd | kip-pode')\n\nDerivation: or קִפֹּד\n\nTypo: lemma קִכֹּד kaf, corrected to קִפֹּד\n\n; from H7088 קָפַד\nStrong's: a species of bird, perhaps the bittern (from its contracted form)\nKJV: bittern.\n\nCognate Group: H7088 (cut off), H7089 (destruction), H7090 (bittern)",
    7091: "קִפֹּוז (qippôwz | kip-poze')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to contract, i.e.\nStrong's: spring forward; an arrow-snake (as darting on its prey)\nKJV: great owl.\n\nCognate Group: H7091 (great owl)",
    7092: "קָפַץ (qâphats | kaw-fats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to draw together, i.e. close; by implication, to leap (by contracting the limbs); specifically, to die (from gathering up the feet)\nKJV: shut (up), skip, stop, take out of the way.\n\nCognate Group: H7092 (shut)\nGreek Equivalents: G4863 συνάγω, G4912 συνέχω",
    7093: "קֵץ (qêts | kates)\n\nDerivation: contracted from H7112 קָצַץ\nStrong's: an extremity; adverbially (with prepositional prefix) after\nKJV: [phrase] after, (utmost) border, end, (in-) finite, [idiom] process.\n\nCognate Group: H7104 (Keziz), H7112 (cut), H7020 (out- most), H7093 (after)\nGreek Equivalents: G378 ἀναπληρόω, G746 ἀρχή, G1581 ἐκκόπτω, G2078 ἔσχατος, G2540 καιρός, G3725 ὅριον, G4009 πέρας, G4137 πληρόω, G5010 τάξις, G5056 τέλος, G5550 χρόνος",
    7094: "קָצַב (qâtsab | kaw-tsab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to clip, or (generally) chop\nKJV: cut down, shorn.\n\nCognate Group: H7094 (cut down), H7095 (bottom)\nGreek Equivalents: G2751 κείρω",
    7095: "קֶצֶב (qetseb | keh'-tseb)\n\nDerivation: from H7094 קָצַב\nStrong's: shape (as if cut out); base (as if there cut off)\nKJV: bottom, size.\n\nCognate Group: H7094 (cut down), H7095 (bottom)",
    7096: "קָצָה (qâtsâh | kaw-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to cut off; (figuratively) to destroy; (partially) to scrape off\nKJV: cut off, cut short, scrape (off).\n\nCognate Group: H7117 (end), H7098 (coast), H7097 ([idiom] after), H7099 (end), H7096 (cut off)",
    7097: "קָצֶה (qâtseh | kaw-tseh')\n\nDerivation: or (negative only) קֵצֶה; from H7096 קָצָה ; (used in a great variety of applications and idioms; compare H7093 קֵץ)\n\nStrong's: an extremity\nKJV: [idiom] after, border, brim, brink, edge, end, (in-) finite, frontier, outmost coast, quarter, shore, (out-) side, [idiom] some, ut(-ter-) most (part).\n\nCognate Group: H7117 (end), H7098 (coast), H7097 ([idiom] after), H7099 (end), H7096 (cut off)\nGreek Equivalents: G706 ἀριθμός",
    7098: "קָצָה (qâtsâh | kaw-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7097 קָצֶה ; (used like H7097 קָצֶה)\n\nStrong's: a termination\nKJV: coast, corner, (selv-) edge, lowest, (uttermost) participle\n\nCognate Group: H7117 (end), H7098 (coast), H7097 ([idiom] after), H7099 (end), H7096 (cut off)\nGreek Equivalents: G4419 πτερύγιον",
    7099: "קֶצֶו (qetsev | keh'-tsev)\n\nDerivation: and (feminine) קִצְוָה; from H7096 קָצָה ; (used like H7097 קָצֶה, but with less variety)\n\nStrong's: a limit\nKJV: end, edge, uttermost participle\n\nCognate Group: H7117 (end), H7098 (coast), H7097 ([idiom] after), H7099 (end), H7096 (cut off)",
    7100: "קֶצַח (qetsach | keh'-tsakh)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root apparently meaning to incise\nStrong's: fennelflower (from its pungency)\nKJV: fitches.\n\nCognate Group: H7100 (fitches)",
    7101: "קָצִין (qâtsîyn | kaw-tseen')\n\nDerivation: from H7096 קָצָה in the sense of determining\nStrong's: a magistrate (as deciding) or other leader\nKJV: captain, guide, prince, ruler. Compare H6278 עֵת קָצִין .\n\nCognate Group: H7101 (captain)\nGreek Equivalents: G747 ἀρχηγός, G758 ἄρχων, G935 βασιλεύς, G1728 ἐνάρχομαι, G2233 ἡγέομαι",
    7102: "קְצִיעָה (qᵉtsîyʻâh | kets-ee-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H7106 קָצַע\nStrong's: cassia (as peeled; plural the bark)\nKJV: cassia.\n\nCognate Group: H7102 (cassia), H7103 (Kezia), H4741 (plane), H7106 (cause to scrape)",
    7103: "קְצִיעָה (Qᵉtsîyʻâh | kets-ee-aw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7102 קְצִיעָה\nStrong's: Ketsiah, a daughter of Job\nKJV: Kezia.\n\nCognate Group: H7102 (cassia), H7103 (Kezia), H4741 (plane), H7106 (cause to scrape)",
    7104: "קְצִיץ (Qᵉtsîyts | kets-eets')\n\nDerivation: from H7112 קָצַץ ; abrupt\nStrong's: Keziz, a valley in Palestine\nKJV: Keziz.\n\nCognate Group: H7104 (Keziz), H7112 (cut), H7020 (out- most), H7093 (after)",
    7105: "קָצִיר (qâtsîyr | kaw-tseer')\n\nDerivation: from H7114 קָצַר\nStrong's: severed, i.e. harvest (as reaped), the crop, the time, the reaper, or figuratively; also a limb (of a tree, or simply foliage)\nKJV: bough, branch, harvest (man).\n\nCognate Group: H7105 (bough), H7114 ([idiom] at all)\nGreek Equivalents: G68 ἀγρός, G2326 θερισμός, G2330 θέρος, G2814 κλῆμα, G4863 συνάγω",
    7106: "קָצַע (qâtsaʻ | kaw-tsah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to strip off, i.e. (partially) scrape; by implication, to segregate (as an angle)\nKJV: cause to scrape, corner.\n\nCognate Group: H7102 (cassia), H7103 (Kezia), H4741 (plane), H7106 (cause to scrape)",
    7107: "קָצַף (qâtsaph | kaw-tsaf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to crack off, i.e. (figuratively) burst out in rage\nKJV: (be) anger(-ry), displease, fret self, (provoke to) wrath (come), be wroth.\n\nCognate Group: H7110 (foam), H7107 (anger)\nGreek Equivalents: G2372 θυμός, G2373 θυμόω, G3076 λυπέω, G3709 ὀργή, G3709 ὀργή, G3710 ὀργίζω, G3947 παροξύνω, G3949 παροργίζω, G4087 πικραίνω",
    7108: "קְצַף (qᵉtsaph | kets-af')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7107 קָצַף\nStrong's: to become enraged\nKJV: be furious.\n\nCognate Group: H7108 (be furious), H7109 (wrath)",
    7109: "קְצַף (qᵉtsaph | kets-af')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H7108 קְצַף\nStrong's: rage\nKJV: wrath.\n\nCognate Group: H7108 (be furious), H7109 (wrath)",
    7110: "קֶצֶף (qetseph | keh'-tsef)\n\nDerivation: from H7107 קָצַף\nStrong's: a splinter (as chipped off); figuratively, rage or strife\nKJV: foam, indignation, [idiom] sore, wrath.\n\nCognate Group: H7110 (foam), H7107 (anger)\nGreek Equivalents: G265 ἁμάρτημα, G2372 θυμός, G3709 ὀργή, G3730 ὁρμή, G3948 παροξυσμός, G3950 παροργισμός, G5434 φρύγανον",
    7111: "קְצָפָה (qᵉtsâphâh | kets-aw-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H7107 קָצַף\nStrong's: a fragment\nKJV: bark(-ed).\n\nCognate Group: H7110 (foam), H7111 (bark)",
    7112: "קָצַץ (qâtsats | kaw-tsats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to chop off (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: cut (asunder, in pieces, in sunder, off), [idiom] utmost.\n\nCognate Group: H7104 (Keziz), H7112 (cut), H7020 (out- most), H7093 (after)\nGreek Equivalents: G609 ἀποκόπτω, G2629 κατακόπτω, G2751 κείρω, G2856 κολοβόω",
    7113: "קְצַץ (qᵉtsats | kets-ats')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7112 קָצַץ \nStrong's: to chop off (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: cut off.\n\nCognate Group: H7118 (end), H7113 (cut off)",
    7114: "קָצַר (qâtsar | kaw-tsar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to dock off, i.e. curtail (transitive or intransitive, literal or figurative); especially to harvest (grass or grain)\nKJV: [idiom] at all, cut down, much discouraged, grieve, harvestman, lothe, mourn, reap(-er), (be, wax) short(-en, -er), straiten, trouble, vex.\n\nCognate Group: H7116 (few), H7115 (anguish), H7114 ([idiom] at all)\nGreek Equivalents: G1551 ἐκδέχομαι, G2325 θερίζω, G3949 παροργίζω, G4729 στενοχωρέω, G5166 τρυγάω",
    7115: "קֹצֶר (qôtser | ko'-tser)\n\nDerivation: from H7114 קָצַר\nStrong's: shortness (of spirit), i.e. impatience\nKJV: anguish.\n\nCognate Group: H7116 (few), H7115 (anguish), H7114 ([idiom] at all)",
    7116: "קָצֵר (qâtsêr | kaw-tsare')\n\nDerivation: from H7114 קָצַר\nStrong's: short (whether in size, number, life, strength or temper)\nKJV: few, hasty, small, soon.\n\nCognate Group: H7116 (few), H7115 (anguish), H7114 ([idiom] at all)\nGreek Equivalents: G2373 θυμόω, G2480 ἰσχύω, G2480 ἰσχύω",
    7117: "קְצָת (qᵉtsâth | kets-awth')\n\nDerivation: from H7096 קָצָה\nStrong's: a termination (literally or figuratively); also (by implication) a portion; adverbially (with prepositional prefix) after\nKJV: end, part, [idiom] some.\n\nCognate Group: H7117 (end), H7098 (coast), H7097 ([idiom] after), H7099 (end), H7096 (cut off)",
    7118: "קְצָת (qᵉtsâth | kets-awth')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7117 קְצָת \nStrong's: a termination (literally or figuratively); also (by implication) a portion; adverbially (with prepositional prefix) after\nKJV: end, partly.\n\nCognate Group: H7118 (end), H7113 (cut off)",
    7119: "קַר (qar | kar)\n\nDerivation: contracted from an unused root meaning to chill\nStrong's: cool; figuratively, quiet\nKJV: cold, excellent (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H7120 (cold), H4747 ([idiom] summer), H6979 (break down), H7119 (cold), H7135 (cold)\nGreek Equivalents: G5593 ψυχρός",
    7120: "קֹר (qôr | kore)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7119 קַר\nStrong's: cold\nKJV: cold.\n\nCognate Group: H7120 (cold), H4747 ([idiom] summer), H6979 (break down), H7119 (cold), H7135 (cold)\nGreek Equivalents: G5592 ψύχος",
    7121: "קָרָא (qârâʼ | kaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (rather identical with H7122 קָרָא through the idea of accosting a person met)\nStrong's: to call out to (i.e. properly, address by name, but used in a wide variety of applications)\nKJV: bewray (self), that are bidden, call (for, forth, self, upon), cry (unto), (be) famous, guest, invite, mention, (give) name, preach, (make) proclaim(-ation), pronounce, publish, read, renowned, say.\n\nCognate Group: H7150 (preaching), H6981 (Kore), H7121 (bewray), H7148 (famous), H4744 (assembly), H7124 (partridge)\nGreek Equivalents: G71 ἄγω, G310 ἀναβοάω, G312 ἀναγγέλλω, G314 ἀναγινώσκω, G349 ἀνακράζω, G455 ἀνοίγω, G472 ἀντέχομαι, G480 ἀντίκειμαι, G518 ἀπαγγέλλω, G528 ἀπαντάω, G529 ἀπάντησις, G994 βοάω, G1284 διαῤῥήσσω, G1291 διαστέλλομαι, G1458 ἐγκαλέω, G1521 εἰσάγω, G1525 εἰσέρχομαι, G1533 εἰσφέρω, G1715 ἔμπροσθεν, G1726 ἐναντίον, G1727 ἐναντίος, G1863 ἐπάγω, G1941 ἐπικαλέομαι, G1941 ἐπικαλέομαι, G1949 ἐπιλαμβάνομαι, G2028 ἐπονομάζω, G2028 ἐπονομάζω, G2564 καλέω, G2784 κηρύσσω, G2799 κλαίω, G2820 κληρόω, G2821 κλῆσις, G2822 κλητός, G2896 κράζω, G2980 λαλέω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3049 λογίζομαι, G3306 μένω, G3333 μετακαλέω, G3522 νηστεύω, G3581 ξένος, G3687 ὀνομάζω, G3870 παρακαλέω, G4046 περιποιέομαι, G4341 προσκαλέομαι, G4486 ῥήγνυμι, G4819 συμβαίνω, G4876 συναντάω, G4977 σχίζω, G5222 ὑπάντησις, G5455 φωνέω",
    7122: "קָרָא (qârâʼ | kaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to encounter, whether accidentally or in a hostile manner\nKJV: befall, (by) chance, (cause to) come (upon), fall out, happen, meet.\n\nCognate Group: H7125 ([idiom] against), H7122 (befall)",
    7123: "קְרָא (qᵉrâʼ | ker-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7121 קָרָא \nStrong's: to call out to (i.e. properly, address by name, but used in a wide variety of applications)\nKJV: call, cry, read.\n\nCognate Group: H7123 (call)",
    7124: "קֹרֵא (qôrêʼ | ko-ray')\n\nDerivation: properly, active participle of H7121 קָרָא\nStrong's: a caller, i.e. partridge (from its cry)\nKJV: partridge. See also H6981 קֹורֵא .\n\nCognate Group: H7150 (preaching), H6981 (Kore), H7121 (bewray), H7148 (famous), H4744 (assembly), H7124 (partridge)",
