    7127: "קְרֵב (qᵉrêb | ker-abe')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7126 קָרַב \nStrong's: to approach (causatively, bring near) for whatever purpose\nKJV: approach, come (near, nigh), draw near.\n\nCognate Group: H7187 (truth), H7170 (accuse), H7162 (horn), H7127 (approach), H7129 (war), H7149 (city)",
    7128: "קְרָב (qᵉrâb | ker-awb')\n\nDerivation: from H7126 קָרַב\nStrong's: hostile encounter\nKJV: battle, war.\n\nCognate Group: H7126 (approach), H7133 (oblation), H7128 (battle), H7132 (approaching), H7138 (allied), H7131 (approach)\nGreek Equivalents: G4171 πόλεμος",
    7129: "קְרָב (qᵉrâb | ker-awb')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7128 קְרָב \nStrong's: hostile encounter\nKJV: war.\n\nCognate Group: H7187 (truth), H7170 (accuse), H7162 (horn), H7127 (approach), H7129 (war), H7149 (city)",
    7130: "קֶרֶב (qereb | keh'-reb)\n\nDerivation: from H7126 קָרַב\nStrong's: properly, the nearest part, i.e. the center, whether literal, figurative or adverbial (especially with preposition)\nKJV: [idiom] among, [idiom] before, bowels, [idiom] unto charge, [phrase] eat (up), [idiom] heart, [idiom] him, [idiom] in, inward ([idiom] -ly, part, -s, thought), midst, [phrase] out of, purtenance, [idiom] therein, [idiom] through, [idiom] within self.\n\nCognate Group: H7134 (ax), H7130 ([idiom] among)\nGreek Equivalents: G1064 γαστήρ, G1271 διάνοια, G1793 ἐντυγχάνω, G2588 καρδία, G2836 κοιλία, G3319 μέσος, G3918 πάρειμι",
    7131: "קָרֵב (qârêb | kaw-rabe')\n\nDerivation: from H7126 קָרַב\nStrong's: near\nKJV: approach, come (near, nigh), draw near.\n\nCognate Group: H7126 (approach), H7133 (oblation), H7128 (battle), H7132 (approaching), H7138 (allied), H7131 (approach)",
    7132: "קְרָבָה (qᵉrâbâh | ker-aw-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H7126 קָרַב\nStrong's: approach\nKJV: approaching, draw near.\n\nCognate Group: H7126 (approach), H7133 (oblation), H7128 (battle), H7132 (approaching), H7138 (allied), H7131 (approach)\nGreek Equivalents: G4347 προσκολλάω",
    7133: "קׇרְבָּן (qorbân | kor-bawn')\n\nDerivation: or קֻרְבָּן; from H7126 קָרַב\nStrong's: something brought near the altar, i.e. a sacrificial present\nKJV: oblation, that is offered, offering.\n\nCognate Group: H7126 (approach), H7133 (oblation), H7128 (battle), H7132 (approaching), H7138 (allied), H7131 (approach)\nGreek Equivalents: G1433 δωρέομαι, G1435 δῶρον, G2819 κλῆρος, G2878 κορβᾶν",
    7134: "קַרְדֹּם (qardôm | kar-dome')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from H6923 קָדַם in the sense of striking upon\nStrong's: an axe\nKJV: ax.\n\nCognate Group: H7134 (ax), H7130 ([idiom] among)\nGreek Equivalents: G513 ἀξίνη",
    7135: "קָרָה (qârâh | kaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7119 קַר\nStrong's: coolness\nKJV: cold.\n\nCognate Group: H7120 (cold), H4747 ([idiom] summer), H6979 (break down), H7119 (cold), H7135 (cold)",
    7136: "קָרָה (qârâh | kaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to light upon (chiefly by accident); causatively, to bring about; specifically, to impose timbers (for roof or floor)\nKJV: appoint, lay (make) beams, befall, bring, come (to pass unto), floor, (hap) was, happen (unto), meet, send good speed.\n\nCognate Group: H7153 (Kirjath-arba), H7177 (Kartah), H7136 (appoint), H7178 (Kartan), H7158 (Kirjath-sannah), H7155 (Kirjath-huzoth), H4746 (building), H7157 (Kirjath), H7151 (city), H7176 (city), H6982 (beam), H7147 (contrary), H704 (Arba), H7156 (Kiriathaim), H7154 (Kirjathbaal), H7137 (uncleanness that chanceth), H4745 (something befallen), H7152 (Kerioth)\nGreek Equivalents: G436 ἀνθίστημι, G528 ἀπαντάω, G1096 γίνομαι, G1291 διαστέλλομαι, G1905 ἐπερωτάω, G2137 εὐοδόω, G3860 παραδίδωμι, G4045 περιπίπτω, G4341 προσκαλέομαι, G4819 συμβαίνω, G4876 συναντάω, G5221 ὑπαντάω, G5316 φαίνω, G5592 ψύχος",
    7137: "קָרֶה (qâreh | kaw-reh')\n\nDerivation: from H7136 קָרָה\nStrong's: an (unfortunate) occurrence, i.e. some accidental (ceremonial) disqualification\nKJV: uncleanness that chanceth.\n\nCognate Group: H7153 (Kirjath-arba), H7177 (Kartah), H7136 (appoint), H7178 (Kartan), H7158 (Kirjath-sannah), H7155 (Kirjath-huzoth), H4746 (building), H7157 (Kirjath), H7151 (city), H7176 (city), H6982 (beam), H7147 (contrary), H704 (Arba), H7156 (Kiriathaim), H7154 (Kirjathbaal), H7137 (uncleanness that chanceth), H4745 (something befallen), H7152 (Kerioth)\nGreek Equivalents: G4511 ῥύσις",
    7138: "קָרֹוב (qârôwb | kaw-robe')\n\nDerivation: or קָרֹב; from H7126 קָרַב\nStrong's: near (in place, kindred or time)\nKJV: allied, approach, at hand, [phrase] any of kin, kinsfold(-sman), (that is) near (of kin), neighbour, (that is) next, (them that come) nigh (at hand), more ready, short(-ly).\n\nCognate Group: H7126 (approach), H7133 (oblation), H7128 (battle), H7132 (approaching), H7138 (allied), H7131 (approach)\nGreek Equivalents: G1451 ἐγγύς, G5035 ταχύ, G5036 ταχύς",
    7139: "קָרַח (qârach | kaw-rakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to depilate\nKJV: make (self) bald.\n\nCognate Group: H7139 (make bald), H7145 (Korahite), H7142 (bald), H7146 (bald head), H7143 (Careah), H7144 (bald), H7141 (Korah)\nGreek Equivalents: G3587 ξυράω",
    7140: "קֶרַח (qerach | keh'-rakh)\n\nDerivation: or קֹרַח; from H7139 קָרַח\nStrong's: ice (as if bald, i.e. smooth); hence, hail; by resemblance, rock crystal\nKJV: crystal, frost, ice.\n\nCognate Group: H7140 (crystal)\nGreek Equivalents: G2879 Κορέ, G2930 κρύσταλλος",
