    7156: "קִרְיָתַיִם (Qiryâthayim | keer-yaw-thah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: dual of H7151 קִרְיָה ; double city\nStrong's: Kirjathaim, the name of two placed in Palestine\nKJV: Kiriathaim, Kirjathaim.\n\nCognate Group: H7153 (Kirjath-arba), H7177 (Kartah), H7136 (appoint), H7178 (Kartan), H7158 (Kirjath-sannah), H7155 (Kirjath-huzoth), H4746 (building), H7157 (Kirjath), H7151 (city), H7176 (city), H6982 (beam), H7147 (contrary), H704 (Arba), H7156 (Kiriathaim), H7154 (Kirjathbaal), H7137 (uncleanness that chanceth), H4745 (something befallen), H7152 (Kerioth)",
    7157: "קִרְיַת יְעָרִים (Qiryath Yᵉʻârîym | keer-yath' yeh-aw-reem')\n\nDerivation: or (Jeremiah 26:20) with the article interposed; or (Joshua 18:28) simply the former part of the word; or קִרְיַת עָרִים; from H7151 קִרְיָה and the plural of H3293 יַעַר or H5892 עִיר ; city of forests, or city of towns\nStrong's: Kirjath-Jearim or Kirjath-Arim, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Kirjath, Kirjath-jearim, Kirjath-arim.\n\nCognate Group: H7153 (Kirjath-arba), H7177 (Kartah), H7136 (appoint), H7178 (Kartan), H7158 (Kirjath-sannah), H7155 (Kirjath-huzoth), H4746 (building), H7157 (Kirjath), H7151 (city), H7176 (city), H6982 (beam), H7147 (contrary), H704 (Arba), H7156 (Kiriathaim), H7154 (Kirjathbaal), H7137 (uncleanness that chanceth), H4745 (something befallen), H7152 (Kerioth)",
    7158: "קִרְיַת סַנָּה (Qiryath Çannâh | keer-yath' san-naw')\n\nDerivation: or קִרְיַת סֵפֶר; from H7151 קִרְיָה and a simpler feminine from the same as H5577 סַנְסִן, or (for the latter name) H5612 סֵפֶר ; city of branches, or of a book\nStrong's: Kirjath-Sannah or Kirjath-Sepher, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Kirjath-sannah, Kirjath-sepher.\n\nCognate Group: H7153 (Kirjath-arba), H7177 (Kartah), H7136 (appoint), H7178 (Kartan), H7158 (Kirjath-sannah), H7155 (Kirjath-huzoth), H4746 (building), H7157 (Kirjath), H7151 (city), H7176 (city), H6982 (beam), H7147 (contrary), H704 (Arba), H7156 (Kiriathaim), H7154 (Kirjathbaal), H7137 (uncleanness that chanceth), H4745 (something befallen), H7152 (Kerioth)",
    7159: "קָרַם (qâram | kaw-ram')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to cover\nKJV: cover.\n\nCognate Group: H7159 (cover)\nGreek Equivalents: G305 ἀναβαίνω, G1614 ἐκτείνω",
    7160: "קָרַן (qâran | kaw-ran')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; to push or gore; used only as denominative from H7161 קֶרֶן,\nStrong's: to shoot out horns; figuratively, rays\nKJV: have horns, shine.\n\nCognate Group: H7161 ([idiom] hill), H7163 (Keren-happuch), H7160 (have horns)\nGreek Equivalents: G1392 δοξάζω, G1627 ἐκφέρω, G2768 κέρας",
    7161: "קֶרֶן (qeren | keh'-ren)\n\nDerivation: from H7160 קָרַן\nStrong's: a horn (as projecting); by implication, a flask, cornet; by resemblance. an elephant's tooth (i.e. ivory), a corner (of the altar), a peak (of a mountain), a ray (of light); figuratively, power\nKJV: [idiom] hill, horn.\n\nCognate Group: H7161 ([idiom] hill), H7163 (Keren-happuch), H7160 (have horns)\nGreek Equivalents: G2768 κέρας, G2776 κεφαλή, G4536 σάλπιγξ",
    7162: "קֶרֶן (qeren | keh'-ren)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7161 קֶרֶן\nStrong's: a horn (literally or for sound)\nKJV: horn, cornet.\n\nCognate Group: H7187 (truth), H7170 (accuse), H7162 (horn), H7127 (approach), H7129 (war), H7149 (city)",
    7163: "קֶרֶן הַפּוּךְ (qeren hap-pûwk | keh'-ren hap-pook')\n\nDerivation: from H7161 קֶרֶן and H6320 פּוּךְ ; horn of cosmetic\nStrong's: Keren-hap-Puk, one of Job's daughters\nKJV: Keren-happuch.\n\nCognate Group: H7161 ([idiom] hill), H7163 (Keren-happuch), H7160 (have horns)",
    7164: "קָרַס (qâraç | kaw-ras')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; properly, to protrude; used only as denominative from H7165 קֶרֶס (for alliteration with H7167 קָרַע),\nStrong's: to hunch, i.e. be hump-backed\nKJV: stoop.\n\nCognate Group: H7166 (foot), H7165 (tache), H7026 (Keros), H7164 (stoop)\nGreek Equivalents: G4937 συντρίβω",
    7165: "קֶרֶס (qereç | keh'-res)\n\nDerivation: from H7164 קָרַס\nStrong's: a knob or belaying-pin (from its swelling form)\nKJV: tache.\n\nCognate Group: H7166 (foot), H7165 (tache), H7026 (Keros), H7164 (stoop)",
    7166: "קַרְסֹל (qarçôl | kar-sole')\n\nDerivation: from H7164 קָרַס\nStrong's: an ankle (as a protuberance or joint)\nKJV: foot.\n\nCognate Group: H7166 (foot), H7165 (tache), H7026 (Keros), H7164 (stoop)",
    7167: "קָרַע (qâraʻ | kaw-rah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to rend, literally or figuratively (revile, paint the eyes, as if enlarging them)\nKJV: cut out, rend, [idiom] surely, tear.\n\nCognate Group: H7167 (cut out), H7168 (piece)\nGreek Equivalents: G1472 ἐγχρίω",
    7168: "קֶרַע (qeraʻ | keh'-rah)\n\nDerivation: from H7167 קָרַע\nStrong's: a rag\nKJV: piece, rag.\n\nCognate Group: H7167 (cut out), H7168 (piece)\nGreek Equivalents: G4485 ῥῆγμα",
    7169: "קָרַץ (qârats | kaw-rats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to pinch, i.e. (partially) to bite the lips, blink the eyes (as a gesture of malice), or (fully) to squeeze off (a piece of clay in order to mould a vessel from it)\nKJV: form, move, wink.\n\nCognate Group: H7172 (bottom), H7171 (destruction), H7174 (Karkor), H7169 (form), H7173 (Karkaa)\nGreek Equivalents: G1269 διανεύω, G1770 ἐννεύω, G3724 ὁρίζω",
    7170: "קְרַץ (qᵉrats | ker-ats')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7171 קֶרֶץ in the sense of a bit (to 'eat the morsels of' any one, i.e.\nStrong's: chew him up (figuratively) by slander\nKJV: [phrase] accuse.\n\nCognate Group: H7187 (truth), H7170 (accuse), H7162 (horn), H7127 (approach), H7129 (war), H7149 (city)",
    7171: "קֶרֶץ (qerets | keh'-rets)\n\nDerivation: from H7169 קָרַץ\nStrong's: extirpation (as if by constriction)\nKJV: destruction.\n\nCognate Group: H7172 (bottom), H7171 (destruction), H7174 (Karkor), H7169 (form), H7173 (Karkaa)",
    7172: "קַרְקַע (qarqaʻ | kar-kah')\n\nDerivation: from H7167 קָרַע\nStrong's: floor (as if a pavement of pieces or tesseroe), of abuilding or the sea\nKJV: bottom, ([idiom] one side of the) floor.\n\nCognate Group: H7172 (bottom), H7171 (destruction), H7174 (Karkor), H7169 (form), H7173 (Karkaa)\nGreek Equivalents: G899 βάθος, G1475 ἔδαφος, G2080 ἔσω",
    7173: "קַרְקַע (Qarqaʻ | kar-kah')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7172 קַרְקַע ; ground-floor\nStrong's: Karka (with the article prefix), a place in Palestine\nKJV: Karkaa.\n\nCognate Group: H7172 (bottom), H7171 (destruction), H7174 (Karkor), H7169 (form), H7173 (Karkaa)",
    7174: "קַרְקֹר (Qarqôr | kar-kore')\n\nDerivation: from H6979 קוּר ; foundation\nStrong's: Karkor, a place East of the Jordan\nKJV: Karkor.\n\nCognate Group: H7172 (bottom), H7171 (destruction), H7174 (Karkor), H7169 (form), H7173 (Karkaa)",
    7175: "קֶרֶשׁ (qeresh | keh'-resh)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to split off\nStrong's: a slab or plank; by implication, a deck of aship\nKJV: bench, board.\n\nCognate Group: H7175 (bench)\nGreek Equivalents: G2777 κεφαλίς, G4768 στυγνάζω",
    7176: "קֶרֶת (qereth | keh'-reth)\n\nDerivation: from H7136 קָרָה in the sense of building\nStrong's: a city\nKJV: city.\n\nCognate Group: H7153 (Kirjath-arba), H7177 (Kartah), H7136 (appoint), H7178 (Kartan), H7158 (Kirjath-sannah), H7155 (Kirjath-huzoth), H4746 (building), H7157 (Kirjath), H7151 (city), H7176 (city), H6982 (beam), H7147 (contrary), H704 (Arba), H7156 (Kiriathaim), H7154 (Kirjathbaal), H7137 (uncleanness that chanceth), H4745 (something befallen), H7152 (Kerioth)\nGreek Equivalents: G2487 ἴχνος, G4628 σκέλος",
    7177: "קַרְתָּה (Qartâh | kar-taw')\n\nDerivation: from H7176 קֶרֶת ; city\nStrong's: Kartah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Kartah.\n\nCognate Group: H7153 (Kirjath-arba), H7177 (Kartah), H7136 (appoint), H7178 (Kartan), H7158 (Kirjath-sannah), H7155 (Kirjath-huzoth), H4746 (building), H7157 (Kirjath), H7151 (city), H7176 (city), H6982 (beam), H7147 (contrary), H704 (Arba), H7156 (Kiriathaim), H7154 (Kirjathbaal), H7137 (uncleanness that chanceth), H4745 (something befallen), H7152 (Kerioth)",
    7178: "קַרְתָּן (Qartân | kar-tawn')\n\nTypo: lemma קַרְתּן missing vowel, corrected to קַרְתָּן\n\nDerivation: from H7176 קֶרֶת ; city-plot\nStrong's: Kartan, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Kartan.\n\nCognate Group: H7153 (Kirjath-arba), H7177 (Kartah), H7136 (appoint), H7178 (Kartan), H7158 (Kirjath-sannah), H7155 (Kirjath-huzoth), H4746 (building), H7157 (Kirjath), H7151 (city), H7176 (city), H6982 (beam), H7147 (contrary), H704 (Arba), H7156 (Kiriathaim), H7154 (Kirjathbaal), H7137 (uncleanness that chanceth), H4745 (something befallen), H7152 (Kerioth)",
    7179: "קַשׁ (qash | kash)\n\nDerivation: from H7197 קָשַׁשׁ\nStrong's: straw (as dry)\nKJV: stubble.\n\nCognate Group: H7179 (stubble), H7197 (gather)\nGreek Equivalents: G2562 καλάμη, G5434 φρύγανον, G5528 χόρτος",
    7180: "קִשֻּׁא (qishshuʼ | kish-shoo')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (meaning to be hard)\nStrong's: a cucumber (from the difficulty of digestion)\nKJV: cucumber.\n\nCognate Group: H7180 (cucumber), H4750 (garden of cucumbers)",
    7181: "קָשַׁב (qâshab | kaw-shab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to prick up the ears, i.e. hearken\nKJV: attend, (cause to) hear(-ken), give heed, incline, mark (well), regard.\n\nCognate Group: H7182 ([idiom] diligently), H7181 (attend), H7183 (attent)\nGreek Equivalents: G191 ἀκούω, G1325 δίδωμι, G1522 εἰσακούω, G1873 ἐπακούω, G4337 προσέχω, G5219 ὑπακούω",
    7182: "קֶשֶׁב (qesheb | keh'-sheb)\n\nDerivation: from H7181 קָשַׁב\nStrong's: a hearkening\nKJV: [idiom] diligently, hearing, much heed, that regarded.\n\nCognate Group: H7182 ([idiom] diligently), H7181 (attend), H7183 (attent)",
    7183: "קַשָּׁב (qashshâb | kash-shawb')\n\nDerivation: or קַשֻּׁב; from H7181 קָשַׁב\nStrong's: hearkening\nKJV: attent(-ive).\n\nCognate Group: H7182 ([idiom] diligently), H7181 (attend), H7183 (attent)",
    7184: "קָשָׂה (qâsâh | kaw-saw')\n\nDerivation: or קַשְׂוָה; from an unused root meaning to be round\nStrong's: a jug (from its shape)\nKJV: cover, cup.\n\nCognate Group: H7083 (inkhorn), H7184 (cover)",
    7185: "קָשָׁה (qâshâh | kaw-shaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to be dense, i.e. tough or severe (in various applications)\nKJV: be cruel, be fiercer, make grievous, be ((ask a), be in, have, seem, would) hard(-en, (labour), -ly, thing), be sore, (be, make) stiff(-en, (-necked)).\n\nCognate Group: H7185 (be cruel), H7186 (churlish), H7191 (Kishion), H7190 (stubbornness)\nGreek Equivalents: G4642 σκληρός, G4642 σκληρός, G4642 σκληρός, G4645 σκληρύνω, G5246 ὑπέρογκος",
    7186: "קָשֶׁה (qâsheh | kaw-sheh')\n\nDerivation: from H7185 קָשָׁה\nStrong's: severe (in various applications)\nKJV: churlish, cruel, grievous, hard((-hearted), thing), heavy, [phrase] impudent, obstinate, prevailed, rough(-ly), sore, sorrowful, stiff(necked), stubborn, [phrase] in trouble.\n\nCognate Group: H7185 (be cruel), H7186 (churlish), H7191 (Kishion), H7190 (stubbornness)",
    7187: "קְשֹׁוט (qᵉshôwṭ | kesh-ote')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or קשֹׁט; (Aramaic), corresponding to H7189 קֹשֶׁט\nStrong's: fidelity\nKJV: truth.\n\nCognate Group: H7187 (truth), H7170 (accuse), H7162 (horn), H7127 (approach), H7129 (war), H7149 (city)\nGreek Equivalents: G225 ἀλήθεια, G228 ἀληθινός",
    7188: "קָשַׁח (qâshach | kaw-shakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be (causatively, make) unfeeling\nKJV: harden.\n\nCognate Group: H7189 (truth), H7188 (harden)\nGreek Equivalents: G4645 σκληρύνω",
    7189: "קֹשֶׁט (qôsheṭ | ko'-shet)\n\nDerivation: or קֹשְׁטְ; from an unused root meaning to balance\nStrong's: equity (as evenly weighed), i.e. reality\nKJV: truth.\n\nCognate Group: H7189 (truth), H7188 (harden)\nGreek Equivalents: G227 ἀληθής",
    7190: "קְשִׁי (qᵉshîy | kesh-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H7185 קָשָׁה\nStrong's: obstinacy\nKJV: stubbornness.\n\nCognate Group: H7185 (be cruel), H7186 (churlish), H7191 (Kishion), H7190 (stubbornness)\nGreek Equivalents: G4643 σκληρότης",
    7191: "קִשְׁיֹון (Qishyôwn | kish-yone')\n\nDerivation: from H7190 קְשִׁי ; hard ground\nStrong's: Kishjon, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Kishion, Keshon.\n\nCognate Group: H7185 (be cruel), H7186 (churlish), H7191 (Kishion), H7190 (stubbornness)",
    7192: "קְשִׂיטָה (qᵉsîyṭâh | kes-ee-taw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (probably meaning to weigh out)\nStrong's: an ingot (as definitely estimated and stamped for a coin)\nKJV: piece of money (silver).\n\nCognate Group: H7192 (piece of money)\nGreek Equivalents: G286 ἀμνός",
    7193: "קַשְׂקֶשֶׂת (qasqeseth | kas-keh'-seth)\n\nDerivation: by reduplication from an unused root meaning to shale off as bark\nStrong's: a scale (of a fish); hence a coat of mail (as composed of or covered with jointed plates of metal)\nKJV: mail, scale.\n\nCognate Group: H7193 (mail)\nGreek Equivalents: G3013 λεπίς",
    7194: "קָשַׁר (qâshar | kaw-shar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tie, physically (gird, confine, compact) or mentally (in love, league)\nKJV: bind (up), (make a) conspire(-acy, -ator), join together, knit, stronger, work (treason).\n\nCognate Group: H7195 (confederacy), H7196 (attire), H7194 (bind)\nGreek Equivalents: G1210 δέω, G1582 ἐκκρέμαμαι, G1978 ἐπίσημος, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G4060 περιτίθημι, G4776 συγκαθίζω, G4863 συνάγω, G4887 συνδέω, G4934 συντίθεμαι, G4962 συστρέφω, G4963 συστροφή",
    7195: "קֶשֶׁר (qesher | keh'-sher)\n\nDerivation: from H7194 קָשַׁר\nStrong's: an (unlawful) alliance\nKJV: confederacy, conspiracy, treason.\n\nCognate Group: H7195 (confederacy), H7196 (attire), H7194 (bind)\nGreek Equivalents: G93 ἀδικία, G1199 δεσμόν, G1936 ἐπίθεσις, G4886 σύνδεσμος, G4963 συστροφή",
    7196: "קִשֻּׁר (qishshur | kish-shoor')\n\nDerivation: from H7194 קָשַׁר\nStrong's: an (ornamental) girdle (for women)\nKJV: attire, headband.\n\nCognate Group: H7195 (confederacy), H7196 (attire), H7194 (bind)",
    7197: "קָשַׁשׁ (qâshash | kaw-shash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; to become sapless through drought; used only as denominative from H7179 קַשׁ\nStrong's: to forage for straw, stubble or wood; figuratively, to assemble\nKJV: gather (selves) (together).\n\nCognate Group: H7179 (stubble), H7197 (gather)\nGreek Equivalents: G4816 συλλέγω, G4863 συνάγω, G4887 συνδέω",
    7198: "קֶשֶׁת (qesheth | keh'-sheth)\n\nDerivation: from H7185 קָשָׁה in the original sense (of H6983 קֹושׁ) of bending\nStrong's: a bow, forshooting (hence, figuratively, strength) or the iris\nKJV: [idiom] arch(-er), [phrase] arrow, bow(-man, -shot).\n\nCognate Group: H7199 ([idiom] archer), H7198 ([idiom] arch), H7197 (gather)\nGreek Equivalents: G5115 τόξον",
    7199: "קַשָּׁת (qashshâth | kash-shawth')\n\nDerivation: intensive (as denominative) from H7198 קֶשֶׁת\nStrong's: a bowman\nKJV: [idiom] archer. r\n\nCognate Group: H7199 ([idiom] archer), H7198 ([idiom] arch), H7197 (gather)",
    7200: "רָאָה (râʼâh | raw-aw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to see, literally or figuratively (in numerous applications, direct and implied, transitive, intransitive and causative)\nKJV: advise self, appear, approve, behold, [idiom] certainly, consider, discern, (make to) enjoy, have experience, gaze, take heed, [idiom] indeed, [idiom] joyfully, lo, look (on, one another, one on another, one upon another, out, up, upon), mark, meet, [idiom] be near, perceive, present, provide, regard, (have) respect, (fore-, cause to, let) see(-r, -m, one another), shew (self), [idiom] sight of others, (e-) spy, stare, [idiom] surely, [idiom] think, view, visions.\n\nCognate Group: H3070 (Jehovah-jireh), H7207 (behold), H7209 (looking glass), H7204 (Haroeh), H7200 (advise self), H4758 ([idiom] apparently), H7206 (children of Reuben), H7205 (Reuben), H7211 (Reaia), H4759 (looking glass), H7210 (gazingstock), H7203 (vision), H7202 (see), H7212 (beholding), H3376 (Irijah)\nGreek Equivalents: G93 ἀδικία, G115 ἀθέτησις, G191 ἀκούω, G266 ἁμαρτία, G308 ἀναβλέπω, G312 ἀναγγέλλω, G578 ἀποβλέπω, G584 ἀποδείκνυμι, G646 ἀποστασία, G684 ἀπώλεια, G763 ἀσέβεια, G991 βλέπω, G1006 βόσκω, G1096 γίνομαι, G1097 γινώσκω, G1166 δεικνύω, G1213 δηλόω, G1451 ἐγγύς, G1525 εἰσέρχομαι, G1689 ἐμβλέπω, G1718 ἐμφανίζω, G1731 ἐνδείκνυμι, G1788 ἐντρέπω, G1896 ἐπεῖδον, G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G1914 ἐπιβλέπω, G1921 ἐπιγινώσκω, G2016 ἐπιφανής, G2041 ἔργον, G2083 ἑταῖρος, G2147 εὑρίσκω, G2300 θεάομαι, G2309 θέλω, G2334 θεωρέω, G2347 θλῖψις, G2400 ἰδού, G2529 καθοράω, G2549 κακία, G2561 κάκωσις, G2597 καταβαίνω, G2628 κατακολουθέω, G2648 καταμανθάνω, G2657 κατανοέω, G2684 κατασκοπέω, G2751 κείρω, G3077 λύπη, G3598 ὁδός, G3701 ὀπτασία, G3708 ὁράω, G4166 ποιμήν, G4189 πονηρία, G4190 πονηρός, G4191 πονηρότερος, G4265 προβλέπω, G4276 προελπίζω, G4920 συνίημι, G4982 σώζω, G5142 τρέφω, G5263 ὑποδείκνυμι, G5316 φαίνω, G5461 φωτίζω",
