    7245: "רַבִּית (Rabbîyth | rab-beeth')\n\nDerivation: from H7231 רָבַב ; multitude\nStrong's: Rabbith, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Rabbith.\n\nCognate Group: H7237 (Rabbah), H7230 (abundance), H7241 (shower), H7231 (increase), H7233 (many), H3379 (Jeroboam), H7227 (abound), H7262 (Rabshakeh), H7245 (Rabbith), H7249 (Rab-saris), H7239 (great things)",
    7246: "רָבַךְ (râbak | raw-bak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to soak (bread in oil)\nKJV: baken, (that which is) fried.\n\nCognate Group: H7247 (Riblah), H7246 (baken)",
    7247: "רִבְלָה (Riblâh | rib-law')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be fruitful; fertile\nStrong's: Riblah, a place in Syria\nKJV: Riblah.\n\nCognate Group: H7247 (Riblah), H7246 (baken)",
    7248: "רַב־מָג (Rab-Mâg | rab-mawg')\n\nDerivation: from H7227 רַב and a foreign word for a Magian; chief Magian\nStrong's: Rab-Mag, a Babylonian official\nKJV: Rab-mag.\n\nCognate Group: H3992 (fretting), H4014 (Mibzar), H7248 (Rab-mag), H3999 (flood)\nGreek Equivalents: G3097 μάγος",
    7249: "רַב־סָרִיס (Rab-Çârîyç | rab-saw-reece')\n\nDerivation: from H7227 רַב and a foreign word for a eunuch; chief chamberlain\nStrong's: Rab-Saris, a Babylonian official\nKJV: Rab-saris.\n\nCognate Group: H7237 (Rabbah), H7230 (abundance), H7241 (shower), H7231 (increase), H7233 (many), H3379 (Jeroboam), H7227 (abound), H7262 (Rabshakeh), H7245 (Rabbith), H7249 (Rab-saris), H7239 (great things)",
    7250: "רָבַע (râbaʻ | raw-bah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to squat or lie out flat, i.e. (specifically) in copulation\nKJV: let gender, lie down.\n\nCognate Group: H7252 (lying down), H7250 (let gender), H7254 (Reba)\nGreek Equivalents: G5068 τετράγωνος",
    7251: "רָבַע (râbaʻ | raw-bah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (rather identical with H7250 רָבַע through the idea of sprawling 'at all fours' (or possibly the reverse is the order of deriv.); compare H702 אַרְבַּע); properly, to be four (sided); used only as denominative of H7253 רֶבַע\nStrong's: to be quadrate\nKJV: (four-) square(-d).\n\nCognate Group: H7255 (fourth participle), H7256 (fourth), H7251 (square), H705 (-forty), H702 (four), H7253 (fourth part), H7243 (foursquare), H706 (fourfold)",
    7252: "רֶבַע (rebaʻ | reh'-bah)\n\nDerivation: from H7250 רָבַע\nStrong's: prostration (for sleep)\nKJV: lying down.\n\nCognate Group: H7252 (lying down), H7250 (let gender), H7254 (Reba)",
    7253: "רֶבַע (rebaʻ | reh'-bah)\n\nDerivation: from H7251 רָבַע\nStrong's: a fourth (part or side)\nKJV: fourth part, side, square.\n\nCognate Group: H7255 (fourth participle), H7256 (fourth), H7251 (square), H705 (-forty), H702 (four), H7253 (fourth part), H7243 (foursquare), H706 (fourfold)",
    7254: "רֶבַע (Rebaʻ | reh'-bah)\n\nDerivation: the same as H7253 רֶבַע\nStrong's: Reba, a Midianite\nKJV: Reba.\n\nCognate Group: H7252 (lying down), H7250 (let gender), H7254 (Reba)",
    7255: "רֹבַע (rôbaʻ | ro'-bah)\n\nDerivation: from H7251 רָבַע\nStrong's: a quarter\nKJV: fourth participle\n\nCognate Group: H7255 (fourth participle), H7256 (fourth), H7251 (square), H705 (-forty), H702 (four), H7253 (fourth part), H7243 (foursquare), H706 (fourfold)\nGreek Equivalents: G1218 δῆμος, G3313 μέρος",
    7256: "רִבֵּעַ (ribbêaʻ | rib-bay'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from H7251 רָבַע\nStrong's: a descendant of the fourth generation, i.e. great great grandchild\nKJV: fourth.\n\nCognate Group: H7255 (fourth participle), H7256 (fourth), H7251 (square), H705 (-forty), H702 (four), H7253 (fourth part), H7243 (foursquare), H706 (fourfold)\nGreek Equivalents: G1074 γενεά, G5067 τέταρτος",
    7257: "רָבַץ (râbats | raw-bats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to crouch (on all four legs folded, like a recumbent animal); be implication, to recline, repose, brood, lurk, imbed\nKJV: crouch (down), fall down, make a fold, lay, (cause to, make to) lie (down), make to rest, sit.\n\nCognate Group: H4769 (couching place), H7258 (where each lay), H7257 (crouch)\nGreek Equivalents: G372 ἀνάπαυσις, G373 ἀναπαύω, G1006 βόσκω, G1096 γίνομαι, G2090 ἑτοιμάζω, G2192 ἔχω, G2270 ἡσυχάζω, G2282 θάλπω, G2647 καταλύω, G2681 κατασκηνόω, G2837 κοιμάω, G2853 κολλάω, G4098 πίπτω, G4875 συναναπαύομαι",
    7258: "רֵבֶץ (rêbets | reh'-bets)\n\nDerivation: from H7257 רָבַץ\nStrong's: a couch or place of repose\nKJV: where each lay, lie down in, resting place.\n\nCognate Group: H4769 (couching place), H7258 (where each lay), H7257 (crouch)",
    7259: "רִבְקָה (Ribqâh | rib-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to clog by tying up the fetlock; fettering (by beauty)\nStrong's: Ribkah, the wife of Isaac\nKJV: Rebekah.\n\nCognate Group: H4770 ([idiom] fat), H7259 (Rebekah)\nGreek Equivalents: G4479 Ῥεβέκκα",
    7260: "רַבְרַב (rabrab | rab-rab')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H7229 רַב\nStrong's: huge (in size); domineering (in character)\nKJV: (very) great (things).\n\nCognate Group: H7240 ([idiom] ten thousand times ten thousand), H7229 (captain), H7261 (lord), H7260 (great)",
    7261: "רַבְרְבָן (rabrᵉbân | rab-reb-awn')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H7260 רַבְרַב\nStrong's: a magnate\nKJV: lord, prince.\n\nCognate Group: H7240 ([idiom] ten thousand times ten thousand), H7229 (captain), H7261 (lord), H7260 (great)\nGreek Equivalents: G3175 μεγιστᾶνες",
    7262: "רַבְשָׁקֵה (Rabshâqêh | rab-shaw-kay')\n\nDerivation: from H7227 רַב and H8248 שָׁקָה ; chief butler\nStrong's: Rabshakeh, a Babylonian official\nKJV: Rabshakeh.\n\nCognate Group: H7237 (Rabbah), H7230 (abundance), H7241 (shower), H7231 (increase), H7233 (many), H3379 (Jeroboam), H7227 (abound), H7262 (Rabshakeh), H7245 (Rabbith), H7249 (Rab-saris), H7239 (great things)",
    7263: "רֶגֶב (regeb | reh'-gheb)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to pile together\nStrong's: a lump of clay\nKJV: clod.\n\nCognate Group: H7263 (clod), H709 (Argob)",
    7264: "רָגַז (râgaz | raw-gaz')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to quiver (with any violent emotion, especially anger or fear)\nKJV: be afraid, stand in awe, disquiet, fall out, fret, move, provoke, quake, rage, shake, tremble, trouble, be wroth.\n\nCognate Group: H7268 (trembling), H712 (coffer), H7269 (trembling), H7264 (be afraid), H7267 (fear)\nGreek Equivalents: G2284 θαμβέω, G2372 θυμός, G2373 θυμόω, G3076 λυπέω, G3309 μεριμνάω, G3601 ὀδύνη, G3710 ὀργίζω, G3926 παρενοχλέω, G3947 παροξύνω, G3949 παροργίζω, G4087 πικραίνω, G4422 πτοέω, G4531 σαλεύω, G4579 σείω, G4863 συνάγω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5399 φοβέω",
    7265: "רְגַז (rᵉgaz | reg-az')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7264 רָגַז \nStrong's: to quiver (with any violent emotion, especially anger or fear)\nKJV: provoke unto wrath.\n\nCognate Group: H7266 (rage), H7271 (foot), H7265 (provoke unto wrath)",
    7266: "רְגַז (rᵉgaz | reg-az')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H7265 רְגַז\nStrong's: violent anger\nKJV: rage.\n\nCognate Group: H7266 (rage), H7271 (foot), H7265 (provoke unto wrath)\nGreek Equivalents: G993 Βοανεργές",
    7267: "רֹגֶז (rôgez | ro'-ghez)\n\nDerivation: from H7264 רָגַז\nStrong's: commotion, restlessness (of a horse), crash (of thunder), disquiet, anger\nKJV: fear, noise, rage, trouble(-ing), wrath.\n\nCognate Group: H7268 (trembling), H712 (coffer), H7269 (trembling), H7264 (be afraid), H7267 (fear)\nGreek Equivalents: G3709 ὀργή, G3709 ὀργή",
    7268: "רַגָּז (raggâz | rag-gawz')\n\nDerivation: intensive from H7264 רָגַז\nStrong's: timid\nKJV: trembling.\n\nCognate Group: H7268 (trembling), H712 (coffer), H7269 (trembling), H7264 (be afraid), H7267 (fear)\nGreek Equivalents: G120 ἀθυμέω",
    7269: "רׇגְזָה (rogzâh | rog-zaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7267 רֹגֶז\nStrong's: trepidation\nKJV: trembling.\n\nCognate Group: H7268 (trembling), H712 (coffer), H7269 (trembling), H7264 (be afraid), H7267 (fear)\nGreek Equivalents: G931 βάσανος",
    7270: "רָגַל (râgal | raw-gal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; also as denominative from H7272 רֶגֶל \nStrong's: to walk along; but only in specifically, applications, to reconnoiter, to be atale-bearer (i.e. slander); to lead about\nKJV: backbite, search, slander, (e-) spy (out), teach to go, view.\n\nCognate Group: H7272 ([idiom] be able to endure), H4772 (feet), H7274 (Rogelim), H8637 (teach to go), H7273 (foot), H7270 (backbite)\nGreek Equivalents: G1389 δολόω, G2684 κατασκοπέω, G2685 κατάσκοπος",
    7271: "רְגַל (rᵉgal | reg-al')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7272 רֶגֶל \nStrong's: a foot, a step; by euphemistically the pudenda\nKJV: foot.\n\nCognate Group: H7266 (rage), H7271 (foot), H7265 (provoke unto wrath)",
    7272: "רֶגֶל (regel | reh'-gel)\n\nDerivation: from H7270 רָגַל\nStrong's: a foot (as used in walking); by implication, a step; by euphemistically the pudenda\nKJV: [idiom] be able to endure, [idiom] according as, [idiom] after, [idiom] coming, [idiom] follow, (broken-)foot(-ed, -stool), [idiom] great toe, [idiom] haunt, [idiom] journey, leg, [phrase] piss, [phrase] possession, time.\n\nCognate Group: H7272 ([idiom] be able to endure), H4772 (feet), H7274 (Rogelim), H8637 (teach to go), H7273 (foot), H7270 (backbite)\nGreek Equivalents: G2540 καιρός, G4228 πούς, G4628 σκέλος",
    7273: "רַגְלִי (raglîy | rag-lee')\n\nDerivation: from H7272 רֶגֶל\nStrong's: a footman (soldier)\nKJV: (on) foot(-man).\n\nCognate Group: H7272 ([idiom] be able to endure), H4772 (feet), H7274 (Rogelim), H8637 (teach to go), H7273 (foot), H7270 (backbite)\nGreek Equivalents: G3979 πεζῇ, G5001 τάγμα",
    7274: "רֹגְלִים (Rôgᵉlîym | ro-gel-eem')\n\nDerivation: plural of active participle of H7270 רָגַל ; fullers (as tramping the cloth in washing)\nStrong's: Rogelim, a place East of the Jordan\nKJV: Rogelim.\n\nCognate Group: H7272 ([idiom] be able to endure), H4772 (feet), H7274 (Rogelim), H8637 (teach to go), H7273 (foot), H7270 (backbite)",
    7275: "רָגַם (râgam | raw-gam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (compare H7263 רֶגֶב, H7321 רוּעַ, H7551 רָקַם)\nStrong's: to cast together (stones), i.e. to lapidate\nKJV: [idiom] certainly, stone.\n\nCognate Group: H7276 (Regem), H7278 (Regem-melech), H7277 (council), H4773 (sling), H7275 ([idiom] certainly)\nGreek Equivalents: G3036 λιθοβολέω, G3037 λίθος",
    7276: "רֶגֶם (Regem | reh'-gem)\n\nDerivation: from H7275 רָגַם ; stoneheap\nStrong's: Regem, an Israelite\nKJV: Regem.\n\nCognate Group: H7276 (Regem), H7278 (Regem-melech), H7277 (council), H4773 (sling), H7275 ([idiom] certainly)",
    7277: "רִגְמָה (rigmâh | rig-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of the same as H7276 רֶגֶם\nStrong's: a pile (of stones), i.e. (figuratively) a throng\nKJV: council.\n\nCognate Group: H7276 (Regem), H7278 (Regem-melech), H7277 (council), H4773 (sling), H7275 ([idiom] certainly)\nGreek Equivalents: G2232 ἡγεμών",
    7278: "רֶגֶם מֶלֶךְ (Regem Melek | reh'-gem meh'-lek)\n\nDerivation: from H7276 רֶגֶם and H4428 מֶלֶךְ ; king's heap\nStrong's: Regem-Melek, an Israelite\nKJV: Regem-melech.\n\nCognate Group: H7276 (Regem), H7278 (Regem-melech), H7277 (council), H4773 (sling), H7275 ([idiom] certainly)",
    7279: "רָגַן (râgan | raw-gan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to grumble, i.e. rebel\nKJV: murmur.\n\nCognate Group: H7279 (murmur), H5372 (talebearer)\nGreek Equivalents: G1111 γογγύζω, G1234 διαγογγύζω",
    7280: "רָגַע (râgaʻ | raw-gah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to toss violently and suddenly (the sea with waves, the skin with boils); figuratively (in a favorable manner) to settle, i.e. quiet; specifically, to wink (from the motion of the eye-lids)\nKJV: break, divide, find ease, be a moment, (cause, give, make to) rest, make suddenly.\n\nCognate Group: H7281 (instant), H7280 (break)\nGreek Equivalents: G373 ἀναπαύω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G2664 καταπαύω, G2906 κραυγή, G5015 ταράσσω, G5030 ταχέως, G5032 τάχιον, G5035 ταχύ, G5036 ταχύς",
    7281: "רֶגַע (regaʻ | reh'-gah)\n\nDerivation: from H7280 רָגַע .\nStrong's: a wink (of the eyes), i.e. a very short space of time\nKJV: instant, moment, space, suddenly.\n\nCognate Group: H7281 (instant), H7280 (break)\nGreek Equivalents: G372 ἀνάπαυσις, G1810 ἐξαίφνης, G1819 ἐξάπινα, G4710 σπουδή, G5034 τάχος, G5550 χρόνος",
    7282: "רָגֵעַ (râgêaʻ | raw-gay'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from H7280 רָגַע\nStrong's: restful, i.e. peaceable\nKJV: that are quiet.\n\nCognate Group: H4771 (rest), H4774 (refreshing), H7282 (that are quiet), H7280 (break)",
    7283: "רָגַשׁ (râgash | raw-gash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be tumultuous\nKJV: rage.\n\nCognate Group: H7283 (rage), H7285 (company)\nGreek Equivalents: G5433 φρυάσσω",
    7284: "רְגַשׁ (rᵉgash | reg-ash')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7283 רָגַשׁ\nStrong's: to gather tumultuously\nKJV: assemble (together).\n\nCognate Group: H7284 (assemble)\nGreek Equivalents: G3936 παρίστημι, G4334 προσέρχομαι",
    7285: "רֶגֶשׁ (regesh | reh'-ghesh)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) רִגְשָׁה; from H7283 רָגַשׁ\nStrong's: a tumultuous crowd\nKJV: company, insurrection.\n\nCognate Group: H7283 (rage), H7285 (company)\nGreek Equivalents: G4128 πλῆθος",
    7286: "רָדַד (râdad | raw-dad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tread in pieces, i.e. (figuratively) to conquer, or (specifically) to overlay\nKJV: spend, spread, subdue.\n\nCognate Group: H7288 (Raddai), H7286 (spend), H7289 (vail)\nGreek Equivalents: G1873 ἐπακούω, G5293 ὑποτάσσω",
    7287: "רָדָה (râdâh | raw-daw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tread down, i.e. subjugate; specifically, to crumble off\nKJV: (come to, make to) have dominion, prevail against, reign, (bear, make to) rule,(-r, over), take.\n\nCognate Group: H7287 (have dominion)\nGreek Equivalents: G757 ἄρχω, G758 ἄρχων, G1377 διώκω, G1807 ἐξαιρέω, G1825 ἐξεγείρω, G1839 ἐξίστημι, G1988 ἐπιστάτης, G2609 κατάγω, G2634 κατακυριεύω, G2716 κατεργάζομαι, G2961 κυριεύω, G3961 πατέω",
    7288: "רַדַּי (Radday | rad-dah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: intensive from H7287 רָדָה ; domineering\nStrong's: Raddai, an Israelite\nKJV: Raddai.\n\nCognate Group: H7288 (Raddai), H7286 (spend), H7289 (vail)",
    7289: "רָדִיד (râdîyd | raw-deed')\n\nDerivation: from H7286 רָדַד in the sense of spreading\nStrong's: a veil (as expanded)\nKJV: vail, veil.\n\nCognate Group: H7288 (Raddai), H7286 (spend), H7289 (vail)",
    7290: "רָדַם (râdam | raw-dam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to stun, i.e. stupefy (with sleep or death)\nKJV: (be fast a-, be in a deep, cast into a dead, that) sleep(-er, -eth).\n\nCognate Group: H8639 (deep sleep), H1719 (Dedan), H7290 (sleep), H1721 (Dodanim)\nGreek Equivalents: G1611 ἔκστασις, G1839 ἐξίστημι, G2284 θαμβέω, G2660 κατανύσσω, G2837 κοιμάω, G3573 νυστάζω, G4098 πίπτω",
    7291: "רָדַף (râdaph | raw-daf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to run after (usually with hostile intent; figuratively (of time) gone by)\nKJV: chase, put to flight, follow (after, on), hunt, (be under) persecute(-ion, -or), pursue(-r).\n\nCognate Group: H4783 (persecuted), H7291 (chase)\nGreek Equivalents: G480 ἀντίκειμαι, G1375 διωγμός, G1377 διώκω, G1559 ἐκδιώκω, G2042 ἐρεθίζω, G2597 καταβαίνω, G2608 κατάγνυμι, G2614 καταδιώκω, G2701 κατατρέχω",
    7292: "רָהַב (râhab | raw-hab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to urge severely, i.e. (figuratively) importune, embolden, capture, act insolently\nKJV: overcome, behave self proudly, make sure, strengthen.\n\nCognate Group: H7293 (proud), H7294 (Rahab), H4062 (golden city), H7296 (strength), H7295 (proud), H7292 (overcome)",
    7293: "רַהַב (rahab | rah'-hab)\n\nDerivation: from H7292 רָהַב,\nStrong's: bluster(-er)\nKJV: proud, strength.\n\nCognate Group: H7293 (proud), H7294 (Rahab), H4062 (golden city), H7296 (strength), H7295 (proud), H7292 (overcome)\nGreek Equivalents: G2785 κῆτος, G4350 προσκόπτω, G5244 ὑπερήφανος",
    7294: "רַהַב (Rahab | rah'-hab)\n\nDerivation: the same as H7293 רַהַב\nStrong's: Rahab (i.e. boaster), an epithet of Egypt\nKJV: Rahab.\n\nCognate Group: H7293 (proud), H7294 (Rahab), H4062 (golden city), H7296 (strength), H7295 (proud), H7292 (overcome)",
    7295: "רָהָב (râhâb | raw-hawb')\n\nDerivation: from H7292 רָהַב\nStrong's: insolent\nKJV: proud.\n\nCognate Group: H7293 (proud), H7294 (Rahab), H4062 (golden city), H7296 (strength), H7295 (proud), H7292 (overcome)",
    7296: "רֹהָב (rôhâb | ro'-hab)\n\nDerivation: from H7292 רָהַב\nStrong's: pride\nKJV: strength.\n\nCognate Group: H7293 (proud), H7294 (Rahab), H4062 (golden city), H7296 (strength), H7295 (proud), H7292 (overcome)",
    7297: "רָהָה (râhâh | raw-haw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to fear\nKJV: be afraid.\n\nCognate Group: H7297 (be afraid)",
    7298: "רַהַט (rahaṭ | rah'-hat)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root apparently meaning to hollow out\nStrong's: a channel or watering-box; by resemblance a ringlet of hair (as forming parallel lines)\nKJV: gallery, gutter, trough.\n\nCognate Group: H7298 (gallery)\nGreek Equivalents: G3025 ληνός",
    7299: "רֵו (rêv | rave)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H7200 רָאָה\nStrong's: aspect\nKJV: form.\n\nCognate Group: H7217 (chief), H7299 (form)\nGreek Equivalents: G3706 ὅρασις",
    7300: "רוּד (rûwd | rood)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tramp about, i.e. ramble (free or disconsolate)\nKJV: have the dominion, be lord, mourn, rule.\n\nCognate Group: H7300 (have the dominion), H4788 (cast out)\nGreek Equivalents: G2507 καθαιρέω, G2961 κυριεύω, G3076 λυπέω",
    7301: "רָוָה (râvâh | raw-vaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to slake the thirst (occasionally of other appetites)\nKJV: bathe, make drunk, (take the) fill, satiate, (abundantly) satisfy, soak, water (abundantly).\n\nCognate Group: H7301 (bathe), H7302 (drunkenness), H7377 (watering), H7310 (runneth over)\nGreek Equivalents: G3184 μεθύω",
    7302: "רָוֶה (râveh | raw-veh')\n\nDerivation: from H7301 רָוָה\nStrong's: sated (with drink)\nKJV: drunkenness, watered.\n\nCognate Group: H7301 (bathe), H7302 (drunkenness), H7377 (watering), H7310 (runneth over)",
    7303: "רֹוהֲגָה (Rôwhăgâh | ro-hag-aw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to cry out; outcry\nStrong's: Rohagah, an Israelite\nKJV: Rohgah.\n\nCognate Group: H7303 (Rohgah)",
    7304: "רָוַח (râvach | raw-vakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (identical with H7306 רוּחַ)\nStrong's: properly, to breathe freely, i.e. revive; by implication, to have ample room\nKJV: be refreshed, large.\n\nCognate Group: H7304 (be refreshed), H7305 (enlargement), H7309 (breathing)",
    7305: "רֶוַח (revach | reh'-vakh)\n\nDerivation: from H7304 רָוַח\nStrong's: room, literally (an interval) or figuratively (deliverance)\nKJV: enlargement, space.\n\nCognate Group: H7304 (be refreshed), H7305 (enlargement), H7309 (breathing)\nGreek Equivalents: G996 βοήθεια, G1292 διάστημα",
    7306: "רוּחַ (rûwach | roo'-akh)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to blow, i.e. breathe; only (literally) to smell or (by implication, perceive (figuratively, to anticipate, enjoy)\nKJV: accept, smell, [idiom] touch, make of quick understanding.\n\nCognate Group: H7381 (savour), H7306 (accept), H7307 (air)\nGreek Equivalents: G1705 ἐμπίπλημι, G3642 ὀλιγόψυχος",
    7307: "רוּחַ (rûwach | roo'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H7306 רוּחַ\nStrong's: wind; by resemblance breath, i.e. a sensible (or even violent) exhalation; figuratively, life, anger, unsubstantiality; by extension, a region of the sky; by resemblance spirit, but only of a rational being (including its expression and functions)\nKJV: air, anger, blast, breath, [idiom] cool, courage, mind, [idiom] quarter, [idiom] side, spirit(-ual), tempest, [idiom] vain, (whirl-) wind(-y).\n\nCognate Group: H7381 (savour), H7306 (accept), H7307 (air)\nGreek Equivalents: G129 αἷμα, G417 ἄνεμος, G435 ἀνήρ, G2250 ἡμέρα, G2372 θυμός, G3313 μέρος, G3563 νοῦς, G4151 πνεῦμα, G4157 πνοή, G5428 φρόνησις, G5590 ψυχή",
