    7324: "רוּק (rûwq | rook)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to pour out (literally or figuratively), i.e. empty\nKJV: [idiom] arm, cast out, draw (out), (make) empty, pour forth (out).\n\nCognate Group: H7386 (emptied), H7387 (without cause), H7324 ([idiom] arm), H7385 (empty)\nGreek Equivalents: G337 ἀναιρέω, G1289 διασπείρω, G1311 διαφθείρω, G1632 ἐκχέω, G1877 ἐπανάγω, G2022 ἐπιχέω",
    7325: "רוּר (rûwr | roor)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to slaver (with spittle), i.e. (by analogy) to emit afluid (ulcerous or natural)\nKJV: run.\n\nCognate Group: H7325 (run), H7388 (spittle)",
