    7393: "רֶכֶב (rekeb | reh'-keb)\n\nDerivation: from H7392 רָכַב\nStrong's: a vehicle; by implication, a team; by extension, cavalry; by analogy a rider, i.e. the upper millstone\nKJV: chariot, (upper) millstone, multitude (from the margin), wagon.\n\nCognate Group: H4818 (chariot), H7398 (chariot), H7392 (bring), H4817 (chariot), H7395 (chariot man), H7396 (chariots), H7397 (Rechah), H7393 (chariot), H7394 (Rechab)\nGreek Equivalents: G2462 ἵππος",
    7394: "רֵכָב (Rêkâb | ray-kawb')\n\nDerivation: from H7392 רָכַב ; rider\nStrong's: Rekab, the name of two Arabs and of two Israelites\nKJV: Rechab.\n\nCognate Group: H4818 (chariot), H7398 (chariot), H7392 (bring), H4817 (chariot), H7395 (chariot man), H7396 (chariots), H7397 (Rechah), H7393 (chariot), H7394 (Rechab)",
    7395: "רַכָּב (rakkâb | rak-kawb')\n\nDerivation: from H7392 רָכַב\nStrong's: a charioteer\nKJV: chariot man, driver of a chariot, horseman.\n\nCognate Group: H4818 (chariot), H7398 (chariot), H7392 (bring), H4817 (chariot), H7395 (chariot man), H7396 (chariots), H7397 (Rechah), H7393 (chariot), H7394 (Rechab)",
