    7401: "רָכַךְ (râkak | raw-kak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to soften (intransitively or transitively), used figuratively\nKJV: (be) faint(-hearted), mollify, (be, make) soft(-er), be tender.\n\nCognate Group: H7391 (tenderness), H4816 (faintness), H7401 (faint), H7390 (faint)\nGreek Equivalents: G770 ἀσθενέω, G1590 ἐκλύω, G1788 ἐντρέπω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι",
    7402: "רָכַל (râkal | raw-kal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to travel for trading\nKJV: (spice) merchant.\n\nCognate Group: H7404 (merchandise), H7403 (Rachal), H7400 (slander), H4819 (merchandise), H7402 (merchant)\nGreek Equivalents: G1710 ἐμπορεύομαι, G1711 ἐμπορία, G1712 ἐμπόριον, G1713 ἔμπορος",
    7403: "רָכָל (Râkâl | raw-kawl')\n\nDerivation: from H7402 רָכַל ; merchant\nStrong's: Rakal, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Rachal.\n\nCognate Group: H7404 (merchandise), H7403 (Rachal), H7400 (slander), H4819 (merchandise), H7402 (merchant)",
    7404: "רְכֻלָּה (rᵉkullâh | rek-ool-law')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of H7402 רָכַל\nStrong's: trade (as peddled)\nKJV: merchandise, traffic.\n\nCognate Group: H7404 (merchandise), H7403 (Rachal), H7400 (slander), H4819 (merchandise), H7402 (merchant)\nGreek Equivalents: G4149 πλοῦτος",
    7405: "רָכַס (râkaç | raw-kas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tie\nKJV: bind.\n\nCognate Group: H7405 (bind), H7406 (rough place), H7407 (pride)",
    7406: "רֶכֶס (rekeç | reh'-kes)\n\nDerivation: from H7405 רָכַס\nStrong's: a mountain ridge (as of tied summits)\nKJV: rough place.\n\nCognate Group: H7405 (bind), H7406 (rough place), H7407 (pride)\nGreek Equivalents: G5138 τραχύς",
    7407: "רֹכֶס (rôkeç | ro'-kes)\n\nDerivation: from H7405 רָכַס\nStrong's: a snare (as of tied meshes)\nKJV: pride.\n\nCognate Group: H7405 (bind), H7406 (rough place), H7407 (pride)\nGreek Equivalents: G5016 ταραχή",
    7408: "רָכַשׁ (râkash | raw-kash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to lay up, i.e. collect\nKJV: gather, get.\n\nCognate Group: H7408 (gather), H7409 (dromedary), H7399 (good)\nGreek Equivalents: G2932 κτάομαι, G4046 περιποιέομαι",
    7409: "רֶכֶשׁ (rekesh | reh'-kesh)\n\nDerivation: from H7408 רָכַשׁ\nStrong's: a relay of animals on a post-route (as stored up for that purpose); by implication, a courser\nKJV: dromedary, mule, swift beast.\n\nCognate Group: H7408 (gather), H7409 (dromedary), H7399 (good)\nGreek Equivalents: G716 ἅρμα",
    7410: "רָם (Râm | rawm)\n\nDerivation: active participle of H7311 רוּם ; high\nStrong's: Ram, the name of an Arabian and of an Israelite\nKJV: Ram. See also H1027 בֵּית הָרָם .\n\nCognate Group: H7312 (haughtiness), H7315 (on high), H7433 (Ramoth-gilead), H7419 (height), H8641 (gift), H7410 (Ram), H7216 (Ramoth), H7318 (be extolled), H7413 (high place), H7319 (high), H7437 (Ramath-lehi), H7414 (Ramah), H4791 (above), H8642 (oblation), H7418 (south Ramoth), H7432 (Remeth), H7427 (lifting up of self), H7435 (Ramathite), H7320 (Romamti-ezer), H7317 (haughtily), H7434 (Ramath-mizpeh), H7316 (Rumah), H7311 (bring up)\nGreek Equivalents: G689 Ἀράμ",
    7411: "רָמָה (râmâh | raw-maw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to hurl; specifically, to shoot; figuratively, to delude or betray (as if causing to fall)\nKJV: beguile, betray, (bow-) man, carry, deceive, throw.\n\nCognate Group: H7411 (beguile)\nGreek Equivalents: G906 βάλλω, G1748 ἐνεδρεύω, G3860 παραδίδωμι, G3884 παραλογίζομαι",
    7412: "רְמָה (rᵉmâh | rem-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7411 רָמָה\nStrong's: to throw, set, (figuratively) assess\nKJV: cast (down), impose.\n\nCognate Group: H7412 (cast)\nGreek Equivalents: G1685 ἐμβάλλω, G2615 καταδουλόω, G5087 τίθημι",
    7413: "רָמָה (râmâh | raw-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine active participle of H7311 רוּם\nStrong's: a height (as a seat of idolatry)\nKJV: high place.\n\nCognate Group: H7312 (haughtiness), H7315 (on high), H7433 (Ramoth-gilead), H7419 (height), H8641 (gift), H7410 (Ram), H7216 (Ramoth), H7318 (be extolled), H7413 (high place), H7319 (high), H7437 (Ramath-lehi), H7414 (Ramah), H4791 (above), H8642 (oblation), H7418 (south Ramoth), H7432 (Remeth), H7427 (lifting up of self), H7435 (Ramathite), H7320 (Romamti-ezer), H7317 (haughtily), H7434 (Ramath-mizpeh), H7316 (Rumah), H7311 (bring up)\nGreek Equivalents: G336 ἀναίρεσις, G939 βάσις, G4471 Ῥαμᾶ, G5401 φόβος",
    7414: "רָמָה (Râmâh | raw-maw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7413 רָמָה\nStrong's: Ramah, the name of four places in Palestine\nKJV: Ramah.\n\nCognate Group: H7312 (haughtiness), H7315 (on high), H7433 (Ramoth-gilead), H7419 (height), H8641 (gift), H7410 (Ram), H7216 (Ramoth), H7318 (be extolled), H7413 (high place), H7319 (high), H7437 (Ramath-lehi), H7414 (Ramah), H4791 (above), H8642 (oblation), H7418 (south Ramoth), H7432 (Remeth), H7427 (lifting up of self), H7435 (Ramathite), H7320 (Romamti-ezer), H7317 (haughtily), H7434 (Ramath-mizpeh), H7316 (Rumah), H7311 (bring up)\nGreek Equivalents: G4471 Ῥαμᾶ, G707 Ἀριμαθαία",
    7415: "רִמָּה (rimmâh | rim-maw')\n\nDerivation: from H7426 רָמַם in the sense of breading (compare H7311 רוּם)\nStrong's: a maggot (as rapidly bred), literally or figuratively\nKJV: worm.\n\nCognate Group: H7415 (worm), H7311 (bring up)\nGreek Equivalents: G4663 σκώληξ",
    7416: "רִמֹּון (rimmôwn | rim-mone')\n\nDerivation: or רִמֹּן; from H7426 רָמַם\nStrong's: a pomegranate, the tree (from its upright growth) or the fruit (also an artificial ornament)\nKJV: pomegranate.\n\nCognate Group: H7416 (pomegranate), H7424 (dromedary), H7423 (deceit), H7428 (Rimmon-parez), H7417 (Remmon), H3414 (Jeremiah), H7420 (buckler), H7422 (Ramiah)",
    7417: "רִמֹּון (Rimmôwn | rim-mone')\n\nDerivation: or (shorter) (רִמֹּן; or רִמֹּונֹו; (1 Chronicles 6:62 (H77 אֶבֶץ)), the same as H7416 רִמֹּון ; in Joshua 19:13: הַמְּתֹאָר is mistaken for part of a name; article with the passive participle of H8388 תָּאַר ; the (one) marked off, i.e. which pertains).\nStrong's: Rimmon, the name of a Syrian deity, also of five places in Palestine\nKJV: Remmon, Rimmon.\n\nCognate Group: H7416 (pomegranate), H7424 (dromedary), H7423 (deceit), H7428 (Rimmon-parez), H7417 (Remmon), H3414 (Jeremiah), H7420 (buckler), H7422 (Ramiah)",
    7418: "רָמֹות (Râmôwth | raw-moth)\n\nDerivation: or רָמַת נֶגֶב; from the plural or construct form of H7413 רָמָה and H5045 נֶגֶב ; heights (or height) of the South\nStrong's: Ramoth-Negeb or Ramath-Negeb, a place in Palestine\nKJV: south Ramoth, Ramath of the south.\n\nCognate Group: H7312 (haughtiness), H7315 (on high), H7433 (Ramoth-gilead), H7419 (height), H8641 (gift), H7410 (Ram), H7216 (Ramoth), H7318 (be extolled), H7413 (high place), H7319 (high), H7437 (Ramath-lehi), H7414 (Ramah), H4791 (above), H8642 (oblation), H7418 (south Ramoth), H7432 (Remeth), H7427 (lifting up of self), H7435 (Ramathite), H7320 (Romamti-ezer), H7317 (haughtily), H7434 (Ramath-mizpeh), H7316 (Rumah), H7311 (bring up)",
    7419: "רָמוּת (râmûwth | raw-mooth')\n\nDerivation: from H7311 רוּם\nStrong's: a heap (of carcases)\nKJV: height.\n\nCognate Group: H7312 (haughtiness), H7315 (on high), H7433 (Ramoth-gilead), H7419 (height), H8641 (gift), H7410 (Ram), H7216 (Ramoth), H7318 (be extolled), H7413 (high place), H7319 (high), H7437 (Ramath-lehi), H7414 (Ramah), H4791 (above), H8642 (oblation), H7418 (south Ramoth), H7432 (Remeth), H7427 (lifting up of self), H7435 (Ramathite), H7320 (Romamti-ezer), H7317 (haughtily), H7434 (Ramath-mizpeh), H7316 (Rumah), H7311 (bring up)",
    7420: "רֹמַח (rômach | ro'-makh)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to hurl\nStrong's: a lance (as thrown); especially the iron point\nKJV: buckler, javelin, lancet, spear.\n\nCognate Group: H7416 (pomegranate), H7424 (dromedary), H7423 (deceit), H7428 (Rimmon-parez), H7417 (Remmon), H3414 (Jeremiah), H7420 (buckler), H7422 (Ramiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G3057 λόγχη",
    7421: "רַמִּי (rammîy | ram-mee')\n\nDerivation: for H761 אֲרַמִּי\nStrong's: a Ramite, i.e. Aramaean\nKJV: Syrian.\n\nCognate Group: H763 (Aham-naharaim), H762 (in the Syrian language), H760 (Aram-zobah), H758 (Aram), H7421 (Syrian), H761 (Syrian)",
    7422: "רַמְיָה (Ramyâh | ram-yaw')\n\nTypo: lemma רמְיָה missing vowel, corrected to רַמְיָה\n\nDerivation: from H7311 רוּם and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has raised\nStrong's: Ramjah, an Israelite\nKJV: Ramiah.\n\nCognate Group: H7416 (pomegranate), H7424 (dromedary), H7423 (deceit), H7428 (Rimmon-parez), H7417 (Remmon), H3414 (Jeremiah), H7420 (buckler), H7422 (Ramiah)",
    7423: "רְמִיָּה (rᵉmîyâh | rem-ee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H7411 רָמָה\nStrong's: remissness, treachery\nKJV: deceit(-ful, -fully), false, guile, idle, slack, slothful.\n\nCognate Group: H7423 (deceit), H7411 (beguile), H8649 (deceit), H4820 (craft)\nGreek Equivalents: G94 ἄδικος, G459 ἄνομος, G1386 δόλιος, G1388 δόλος",
    7424: "רַמָּךְ (rammâk | ram-mawk')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: a brood mare\nKJV: dromedary.\n\nCognate Group: H7416 (pomegranate), H7424 (dromedary), H7423 (deceit), H7428 (Rimmon-parez), H7417 (Remmon), H3414 (Jeremiah), H7420 (buckler), H7422 (Ramiah)",
    7425: "רְמַלְיָהוּ (Rᵉmalyâhûw | rem-al-yaw'-hoo)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root and H3050 יָהּ (perhaps meaning to deck); Jah has bedecked\nStrong's: Remaljah, an Israelite\nKJV: Remaliah.\n\nCognate Group: H7425 (Remaliah)",
