    7427: "רֹמֵמֻת (rômêmuth | ro-may-mooth')\n\nDerivation: from the active participle of H7426 רָמַם\nStrong's: exaltation\nKJV: lifting up of self.\n\nCognate Group: H7312 (haughtiness), H7315 (on high), H7433 (Ramoth-gilead), H7419 (height), H8641 (gift), H7410 (Ram), H7216 (Ramoth), H7318 (be extolled), H7413 (high place), H7319 (high), H7437 (Ramath-lehi), H7414 (Ramah), H4791 (above), H8642 (oblation), H7418 (south Ramoth), H7432 (Remeth), H7427 (lifting up of self), H7435 (Ramathite), H7320 (Romamti-ezer), H7317 (haughtily), H7434 (Ramath-mizpeh), H7316 (Rumah), H7311 (bring up)",
    7428: "רִמֹּן פֶּרֶץ (Rimmôn Perets | rim-mone' peh'-rets)\n\nDerivation: from H7416 רִמֹּון and H6556 פֶּרֶץ ; pomegranate of the breach\nStrong's: Rimmon-Perets, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Rimmon-parez.\n\nCognate Group: H7416 (pomegranate), H7424 (dromedary), H7423 (deceit), H7428 (Rimmon-parez), H7417 (Remmon), H3414 (Jeremiah), H7420 (buckler), H7422 (Ramiah)",
    7429: "רָמַס (râmaç | raw-mas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tread upon (as a potter, in walking or abusively)\nKJV: oppressor, stamp upon, trample (under feet), tread (down, upon).\n\nCognate Group: H4823 (tread -ing), H7429 (oppressor)\nGreek Equivalents: G1291 διαστέλλομαι, G1330 διέρχομαι, G2062 ἑρπετόν, G2662 καταπατέω, G3961 πατέω, G4937 συντρίβω",
    7430: "רָמַשׂ (râmas | raw-mas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to glide swiftly, i.e. to crawl or move with short steps; by analogy to swarm\nKJV: creep, move.\n\nCognate Group: H7430 (creep), H7431 (that creepeth)\nGreek Equivalents: G2795 κινέω",
    7431: "רֶמֶשׂ (remes | reh'-mes)\n\nDerivation: from H7430 רָמַשׂ\nStrong's: a reptile or any other rapidly moving animal\nKJV: that creepeth, creeping (moving) thing.\n\nCognate Group: H7430 (creep), H7431 (that creepeth)",
