    7481: "רָעַם (râʻam | raw-am')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tumble, i.e. be violently agitated; specifically, to crash (of thunder); figuratively, to irritate (with anger)\nKJV: make to fret, roar, thunder, trouble.\n\nCognate Group: H7481 (make to fret), H7484 (Raamah), H7486 (Raamses), H7482 (thunder), H7483 (thunder)\nGreek Equivalents: G120 ἀθυμέω, G994 βοάω, G1145 δακρύω, G2906 κραυγή, G4531 σαλεύω",
