    7483: "רַעְמָה (raʻmâh | rah-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7482 רַעַם\nStrong's: the mane of a horse (as quivering in the wind)\nKJV: thunder.\n\nCognate Group: H7481 (make to fret), H7484 (Raamah), H7486 (Raamses), H7482 (thunder), H7483 (thunder)",
    7484: "רַעְמָה (Raʻmâh | rah-maw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7483 רַעְמָה\nStrong's: Ramah, the name of a grandson of Ham, and of a place (perhaps founded by him)\nKJV: Raamah.\n\nCognate Group: H7481 (make to fret), H7484 (Raamah), H7486 (Raamses), H7482 (thunder), H7483 (thunder)",
    7485: "רַעַמְיָה (Raʻamyâh | rah-am-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H7481 רָעַם and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has shaken\nStrong's: Raamjah, an Israelite\nKJV: Raamiah.\n\nCognate Group: H7478 (trembling), H7480 (Reeliah), H7479 (muffler), H8653 (astonishment), H7485 (Raamiah), H7477 (terribly shake)",
    7486: "רַעְמְסֵס (Raʻmᵉçêç | rah-mes-ace')\n\nDerivation: or רַעַמְסֵס; of Egyptian origin\nStrong's: Rameses or Raamses, a place in Egypt\nKJV: Raamses, Rameses.\n\nCognate Group: H7481 (make to fret), H7484 (Raamah), H7486 (Raamses), H7482 (thunder), H7483 (thunder)",
    7487: "רַעֲנַן (raʻănan | rah-aw-nan')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7488 רַעֲנָן\nStrong's: green, i.e. (figuratively) prosperous\nKJV: flourishing.\n\nCognate Group: H7487 (flourishing), H7476 (cogitation), H7470 (pleasure)",
    7488: "רַעֲנָן (raʻănân | rah-an-awn')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be green\nStrong's: verdant; by analogy, new; figuratively, prosperous\nKJV: green, flourishing.\n\nCognate Group: H7488 (green)",
    7489: "רָעַע (râʻaʻ | raw-ah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to spoil (literally, by breaking to pieces); figuratively, to make (or be) good for nothing, i.e. bad (physically, socially or morally)\nKJV: afflict, associate, break (down, in pieces), [phrase] displease, (be, bring, do) evil (doer, entreat, man), shew himself friendly, do harm, (do) hurt, (behave self, deal) ill, [idiom] indeed, do mischief, punish, still, vex, (do) wicked (doer, -ly), be (deal, do) worse.\n\nCognate Group: H7451 (adversity), H7455 ([idiom] be so bad), H7489 (afflict), H4827 (do mischief)\nGreek Equivalents: G91 ἀδικέω, G683 ἀπωθέομαι, G765 ἀσεβής, G889 ἀχρειόω, G926 βαρύς, G940 βασκαίνω, G2554 κακοποιέω, G2555 κακοποιός, G2556 κακός, G2559 κακόω, G3076 λυπέω, G4190 πονηρός, G4190 πονηρός, G4191 πονηρότερος, G4191 πονηρότερος, G4931 συντελέω, G5015 ταράσσω",
    7490: "רְעַע (rᵉʻaʻ | reh-ah')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7489 רָעַע \nStrong's: properly, to spoil (literally, by breaking to pieces); figuratively, to make (or be) good fornothing, i.e. bad (physically, socially or morally)\nKJV: break, bruise.\n\nCognate Group: H7490 (break)",
    7491: "רָעַף (râʻaph | raw-af')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to drip\nKJV: distil, drop (down).\n\nCognate Group: H7491 (distil)\nGreek Equivalents: G4130 πλήθω, G4482 ῥέω",
    7492: "רָעַץ (râʻats | raw-ats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to break in pieces; figuratively, harass\nKJV: dash in pieces, vex.\n\nCognate Group: H7492 (dash in pieces)\nGreek Equivalents: G2346 θλίβω, G2352 θραύω",
    7493: "רָעַשׁ (râʻash | raw-ash)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to undulate (as the earth, the sky, etc.; also a field of grain), particularly through fear; specifically, to spring (as a locust)\nKJV: make afraid, (re-) move, quake, (make to) shake, (make to) tremble.\n\nCognate Group: H7493 (make afraid), H7494 (commotion)\nGreek Equivalents: G4579 σείω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5399 φοβέω",
