    7495: "רָפָא (râphâʼ | raw-faw')\n\nDerivation: or רָפָה; a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to mend (by stitching), i.e. (figuratively) to cure\nKJV: cure, (cause to) heal, physician, repair, [idiom] thoroughly, make whole. See H7503 רָפָה .\n\nCognate Group: H7501 (Rephael), H7509 (Rephaiah), H4832 (cure), H7495 (cure), H7505 (Raphu), H7500 (health), H3416 (Irpeel), H7498 (Rapha), H7499 (heal)\nGreek Equivalents: G2390 ἰάομαι",
    7496: "רָפָא (râphâʼ | raw-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H7495 רָפָא in the sense of H7503 רָפָה\nStrong's: properly, lax, i.e. (figuratively) a ghost (as dead; in plural only)\nKJV: dead, deceased.\n\nCognate Group: H7497 (giant), H7506 (Rephah), H7496 (dead), H7503 (abate), H7510 (feebleness), H7504 (weak)",
    7497: "רָפָא (râphâʼ | raw-faw')\n\nDerivation: or רָפָה; from H7495 רָפָא in the sense of invigorating\nStrong's: a giant\nKJV: giant, Rapha, Rephaim(-s). See also H1051 בֵּית רָפָא .\n\nCognate Group: H7497 (giant), H7506 (Rephah), H7496 (dead), H7503 (abate), H7510 (feebleness), H7504 (weak)\nGreek Equivalents: G2395 ἰατρός",
    7498: "רָפָא (Râphâʼ | raw-faw')\n\nDerivation: or רָפָה; probably the same as H7497 רָפָא ; giant\nStrong's: Rapha or Raphah, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Rapha.\n\nCognate Group: H7501 (Rephael), H7509 (Rephaiah), H4832 (cure), H7495 (cure), H7505 (Raphu), H7500 (health), H3416 (Irpeel), H7498 (Rapha), H7499 (heal)",
    7499: "רְפֻאָה (rᵉphuʼâh | ref-oo-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of H7495 רָפָא\nStrong's: a medicament\nKJV: heal(-ed), medicine.\n\nCognate Group: H7501 (Rephael), H7509 (Rephaiah), H4832 (cure), H7495 (cure), H7505 (Raphu), H7500 (health), H3416 (Irpeel), H7498 (Rapha), H7499 (heal)",
    7500: "רִפְאוּת (riphʼûwth | rif-ooth')\n\nDerivation: from H7495 רָפָא\nStrong's: a cure\nKJV: health.\n\nCognate Group: H7501 (Rephael), H7509 (Rephaiah), H4832 (cure), H7495 (cure), H7505 (Raphu), H7500 (health), H3416 (Irpeel), H7498 (Rapha), H7499 (heal)",
    7501: "רְפָאֵל (Rᵉphâʼêl | ref-aw-ale')\n\nDerivation: from H7495 רָפָא and H410 אֵל ; God has cured\nStrong's: Rephael, an Israelite\nKJV: Rephael.\n\nCognate Group: H7501 (Rephael), H7509 (Rephaiah), H4832 (cure), H7495 (cure), H7505 (Raphu), H7500 (health), H3416 (Irpeel), H7498 (Rapha), H7499 (heal)",
