    7503: "רָפָה (râphâh | raw-faw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to slacken (in many applications, literal or figurative)\nKJV: abate, cease, consume, draw (toward evening), fail, (be) faint, be (wax) feeble, forsake, idle, leave, let alone (go, down), (be) slack, stay, be still, be slothful, (be) weak(-en). See H7495 רָפָא .\n\nCognate Group: H7497 (giant), H7506 (Rephah), H7496 (dead), H7503 (abate), H7510 (feebleness), H7504 (weak)\nGreek Equivalents: G447 ἀνίημι, G565 ἀπέρχομαι, G770 ἀσθενέω, G863 ἀφίημι, G1439 ἐάω, G1459 ἐγκαταλείπω, G1590 ἐκλύω, G2664 καταπαύω, G2827 κλίνω, G3886 παραλύω, G3935 παρίημι, G3973 παύω, G4980 σχολάζω",
    7504: "רָפֶה (râpheh | raw-feh')\n\nDerivation: from H7503 רָפָה\nStrong's: slack (in body or mind)\nKJV: weak. raphah, Raphah. See H7497 רָפָא, H7498 רָפָא . riphah. See H7383 רִיפָה .\n\nCognate Group: H7497 (giant), H7506 (Rephah), H7496 (dead), H7503 (abate), H7510 (feebleness), H7504 (weak)\nGreek Equivalents: G772 ἀσθενής",
