    7510: "רִפְיֹון (riphyôwn | rif-yone')\n\nDerivation: from H7503 רָפָה\nStrong's: slackness\nKJV: feebleness.\n\nCognate Group: H7497 (giant), H7506 (Rephah), H7496 (dead), H7503 (abate), H7510 (feebleness), H7504 (weak)",
    7511: "רָפַס (râphaç | raw-fas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to trample, i.e. prostrate\nKJV: humble self, submit self.\n\nCognate Group: H7513 (flote), H4833 (that which), H7515 (foul), H7511 (humble self)\nGreek Equivalents: G1576 ἐκκλείω",
