    7516: "רֶפֶשׁ (rephesh | reh'-fesh)\n\nDerivation: from H7515 רָפַשׂ\nStrong's: mud (as roiled)\nKJV: mire.\n\nCognate Group: H7517 (stall), H7516 (mire)",
    7517: "רֶפֶת (repheth | reh'-feth)\n\nDerivation: probably from H7503 רָפָה\nStrong's: a stall for cattle (from their resting there)\nKJV: stall.\n\nCognate Group: H7517 (stall), H7516 (mire)\nGreek Equivalents: G5336 φάτνη",
    7518: "רַץ (rats | rats)\n\nDerivation: contracted from H7533 רָצַץ\nStrong's: a fragment\nKJV: piece.\n\nCognate Group: H7518 (piece), H7533 (break), H4835 (violence)",
