    7532: "רִצְפָּה (Ritspâh | rits-paw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7531 רִצְפָּה\nStrong's: Ritspah, an Israelitess\nKJV: Rizpah.\n\nCognate Group: H7529 (coal), H7532 (Rizpah), H7530 (Rezeph), H7531 (live coal)",
    7533: "רָצַץ (râtsats | raw-tsats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to crack in pieces, literally or figuratively\nKJV: break, bruise, crush, discourage, oppress, struggle together.\n\nCognate Group: H7518 (piece), H7533 (break), H4835 (violence)\nGreek Equivalents: G2352 θραύω, G2616 καταδυναστεύω, G2662 καταπατέω, G2806 κλάω, G3075 λυμαίνομαι, G4640 σκιρτάω, G4917 συνθλάω, G4918 συνθλίβω, G4937 συντρίβω",
