    7596: "שְׁאֵלָה (shᵉʼêlâh | sheh-ay-law')\n\nDerivation: or שֵׁלָה; (1 Samuel 1:17), from H7592 שָׁאַל\nStrong's: a petition; by implication, a loan\nKJV: loan, petition, request.\n\nCognate Group: H7596 (loan), H7594 (Sheal), H7592 (ask), H7587 (Shaulites), H7585 (grave), H4862 (desire), H7586 (Saul), H7597 (Shalthiel)\nGreek Equivalents: G155 αἴτημα, G515 ἀξιόω",
    7597: "שְׁאַלְתִּיאֵל (Shᵉʼaltîyʼêl | sheh-al-tee-ale')\n\nDerivation: or שַׁלְתִּיאֵל; from H7592 שָׁאַל and H410 אֵל ; I have asked God\nStrong's: Shealtiel, an Israelite\nKJV: Shalthiel, Shealtiel.\n\nCognate Group: H7596 (loan), H7594 (Sheal), H7592 (ask), H7587 (Shaulites), H7585 (grave), H4862 (desire), H7586 (Saul), H7597 (Shalthiel)\nGreek Equivalents: G4528 Σαλαθιήλ",
    7598: "שְׁאַלְתִּיאֵל (Shᵉʼaltîyʼêl | sheh-al-tee-ale')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7597 שְׁאַלְתִּיאֵל \nStrong's: Shealtiel, an Israelite\nKJV: Shealtiel.\n\nCognate Group: H7593 (ask), H7598 (Shealtiel), H7595 (demand), H7606 ([idiom] whatsoever more)",
    7599: "שָׁאַן (shâʼan | shaw-an')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to loll, i.e. be peaceful\nKJV: be at ease, be quiet, rest. See also H1052 בֵּית שְׁאָן .\n\nCognate Group: H7599 (be at ease), H7600 (that is at ease)\nGreek Equivalents: G373 ἀναπαύω, G3973 παύω",
    7600: "שַׁאֲנָן (shaʼănân | shah-an-awn')\n\nDerivation: from H7599 שָׁאַן\nStrong's: secure; in a bad sense, haughty\nKJV: that is at ease, quiet, tumult. Compare H7946 שַׁלְאֲנָן .\n\nCognate Group: H7599 (be at ease), H7600 (that is at ease)\nGreek Equivalents: G1847 ἐξουδενόω, G2270 ἡσυχάζω, G4088 πικρία, G4145 πλούσιος, G4764 στρῆνος, G5002 τακτός",
    7601: "שָׁאַס (shâʼaç | shaw-as')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to plunder\nKJV: spoil.\n\nCognate Group: H7601 (spoil), H4882 (spoil), H8155 (rifle), H4933 (booty)",
    7602: "שָׁאַף (shâʼaph | shaw-af')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to inhale eagerly; figuratively, to cover; by implication, to be angry; also to hasten\nKJV: desire (earnestly), devour, haste, pant, snuff up, swallow up.\n\nCognate Group: H7602 (desire)\nGreek Equivalents: G1670 ἑλκύω, G1828 ἐξέλκω, G2662 καταπατέω, G3404 μισέω, G3583 ξηραίνω, G4151 πνεῦμα",
    7603: "שְׂאֹר (sᵉʼôr | seh-ore')\n\nDerivation: from H7604 שָׁאַר\nStrong's: barm or yeast-cake (as swelling by fermentation)\nKJV: leaven.\n\nCognate Group: H7603 (leaven)\nGreek Equivalents: G2219 ζύμη",
    7604: "שָׁאַר (shâʼar | shaw-ar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to swell up, i.e. be (causatively, make) redundant\nKJV: leave, (be) left, let, remain, remnant, reserve, the rest.\n\nCognate Group: H7605 ([idiom] other), H7604 (leave), H7611 (that had escaped), H7610 (Shear-jashub)\nGreek Equivalents: G620 ἀπολείπω, G1459 ἐγκαταλείπω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1952 ἐπιλείπω, G1954 ἐπίλοιπος, G2640 κατάλειμμα, G2641 καταλείπω, G2645 κατάλοιπος, G4035 περιλείπω, G5275 ὑπολείπω",
    7605: "שְׁאָר (shᵉʼâr | sheh-awr')\n\nDerivation: from H7604 שָׁאַר\nStrong's: a remainder\nKJV: [idiom] other, remnant, residue, rest.\n\nCognate Group: H7605 ([idiom] other), H7604 (leave), H7611 (that had escaped), H7610 (Shear-jashub)\nGreek Equivalents: G2640 κατάλειμμα, G2645 κατάλοιπος, G3062 λοιποί, G3063 λοιπόν, G3064 λοιποῦ",
    7606: "שְׁאָר (shᵉʼâr | sheh-awr')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7605 שְׁאָר \nStrong's: a remainder\nKJV: [idiom] whatsoever more, residue, rest.\n\nCognate Group: H7593 (ask), H7598 (Shealtiel), H7595 (demand), H7606 ([idiom] whatsoever more)",
    7607: "שְׁאֵר (shᵉʼêr | sheh-ayr')\n\nDerivation: from H7604 שָׁאַר\nStrong's: flesh (as swelling out), as living or forfood; generally food of any kind; figuratively, kindred by blood\nKJV: body, flesh, food, (near) kin(-sman, -swoman), near (nigh) (of kin).\n\nCognate Group: H7607 (body), H7614 (Sheba), H7608 (near kinswomen), H7609 (Sherah), H7615 (Sabean)\nGreek Equivalents: G1163 δεῖ, G3609 οἰκεῖος, G4561 σάρξ, G4983 σῶμα, G4983 σῶμα, G5132 τράπεζα",
    7608: "שַׁאֲרָה (shaʼărâh | shah-ar-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7607 שְׁאֵר\nStrong's: female kindred by blood\nKJV: near kinswomen.\n\nCognate Group: H7607 (body), H7614 (Sheba), H7608 (near kinswomen), H7609 (Sherah), H7615 (Sabean)",
    7609: "שֶׁאֱרָה (Sheʼĕrâh | sheh-er-aw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7608 שַׁאֲרָה\nStrong's: Sheerah, an Israelitess\nKJV: Sherah.\n\nCognate Group: H7607 (body), H7614 (Sheba), H7608 (near kinswomen), H7609 (Sherah), H7615 (Sabean)",
    7610: "שְׁאָר יָשׁוּב (Shᵉʼâr Yâshûwb | sheh-awr'yaw-shoob')\n\nDerivation: from H7605 שְׁאָר and H7725 שׁוּב ; a remnant will return\nStrong's: Shear-Jashub, the symbolic name of one of Isaiah's sons\nKJV: Shear-jashub.\n\nCognate Group: H7605 ([idiom] other), H7604 (leave), H7611 (that had escaped), H7610 (Shear-jashub)",
    7611: "שְׁאֵרִית (shᵉʼêrîyth | sheh-ay-reeth')\n\nDerivation: from H7604 שָׁאַר\nStrong's: a remainder or residual (surviving, final) portion\nKJV: that had escaped, be left, posterity, remain(-der), remnant, residue, rest.\n\nCognate Group: H7605 ([idiom] other), H7604 (leave), H7611 (that had escaped), H7610 (Shear-jashub)\nGreek Equivalents: G2640 κατάλειμμα, G2640 κατάλειμμα, G2645 κατάλοιπος, G3005 λεῖμμα",
    7612: "שֵׁאת (shêʼth | shayth)\n\nDerivation: from H7582 שָׁאָה\nStrong's: devastation\nKJV: desolation.\n\nCognate Group: H7588 ([idiom] horrible), H7591 (destruction), H7584 (desolation), H7612 (desolation), H8351 (Sheth), H7582 (be desolate)",
    7613: "שְׂאֵת (sᵉʼêth | seh-ayth')\n\nDerivation: from H5375 נָשָׂא\nStrong's: an elevation or leprous scab; figuratively, elation or cheerfulness; exaltation in rank or character\nKJV: be accepted, dignity, excellency, highness, raise up self, rising.\n\nCognate Group: H5375 (accept), H5387 (captain), H4858 (burden), H4864 (burden), H7863 (excellency), H4853 (burden), H7613 (be accepted), H5379 (gift), H7865 (Sion), H4856 (respect), H5385 (carriage), H4984 (exalted), H7721 (arise)\nGreek Equivalents: G3799 ὄψις, G4762 στρέφω, G5092 τιμή",
    7614: "שְׁבָא (Shᵉbâʼ | sheb-aw')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Sheba, the name of three early progenitors of tribes and of an Ethiopian district\nKJV: Sheba, Sabeans.\n\nCognate Group: H7607 (body), H7614 (Sheba), H7608 (near kinswomen), H7609 (Sherah), H7615 (Sabean)",
    7615: "שְׁבָאִי (Shᵉbâʼîy | sheb-aw-ee')\n\nDerivation: patronymic from H7614 שְׁבָא\nStrong's: a Shebaite or descendant of Sheba\nKJV: Sabean.\n\nCognate Group: H7607 (body), H7614 (Sheba), H7608 (near kinswomen), H7609 (Sherah), H7615 (Sabean)",
    7616: "שָׁבָב (shâbâb | shaw-bawb')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to break up\nStrong's: a fragment, i.e. ruin\nKJV: broken in pieces.\n\nCognate Group: H7616 (broken in pieces)",
    7617: "שָׁבָה (shâbâh | shaw-baw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to transport into captivity\nKJV: (bring away, carry, carry away, lead, lead away, take) captive(-s), drive (take) away.\n\nCognate Group: H7633 (captives), H7628 (captive), H7617 (captive), H7618 (agate), H7622 (captive), H7619 (Shebuel), H8664 (Tishbite), H7629 (Shobi), H7630 (Shobai), H8453 (foreigner)\nGreek Equivalents: G162 αἰχμαλωτεύω, G164 αἰχμάλωτος, G498 ἀντιτάσσομαι, G3329 μετάγω",
    7618: "שְׁבוּ (shᵉbûw | sheb-oo')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (probably identical with that of H7617 שָׁבָה through the idea of subdivision into flashes or streamers (compare H7632 שָׁבִיב) meaning to flame\nStrong's: a gem (from its sparkle), probably the agate\nKJV: agate.\n\nCognate Group: H7633 (captives), H7628 (captive), H7617 (captive), H7618 (agate), H7622 (captive), H7619 (Shebuel), H8664 (Tishbite), H7629 (Shobi), H7630 (Shobai), H8453 (foreigner)",
    7619: "שְׁבוּאֵל (Shᵉbûwʼêl | sheb-oo-ale')\n\nDerivation: or שׁוּבָאֵל; from H7617 שָׁבָה (abbreviated form) or H7725 שׁוּב and H410 אֵל ; captive (or returned) of God\nStrong's: Shebuel or Shubael, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Shebuel, Shubael.\n\nCognate Group: H7633 (captives), H7628 (captive), H7617 (captive), H7618 (agate), H7622 (captive), H7619 (Shebuel), H8664 (Tishbite), H7629 (Shobi), H7630 (Shobai), H8453 (foreigner)",
    7620: "שָׁבוּעַ (shâbûwaʻ | shaw-boo'-ah)\n\nDerivation: or שָׁבֻעַ; also (feminine) שְׁבֻעָה; properly, passive participle of H7650 שָׁבַע as a denominative of H7651 שֶׁבַע\nStrong's: literally, sevened, i.e. a week (specifically, of years)\nKJV: seven, week.\n\nCognate Group: H7637 (seventh), H7651 (seven), H7658 (seven), H7621 (curse), H7650 (adjure), H7656 (Shebah), H7657 (seventy), H7652 (Sheba), H7659 (seven), H7620 (seven)",
    7621: "שְׁבוּעָה (shᵉbûwʻâh | sheb-oo-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of H7650 שָׁבַע\nStrong's: properly, something sworn, i.e. an oath\nKJV: curse, oath, [idiom] sworn.\n\nCognate Group: H7637 (seventh), H7651 (seven), H7658 (seven), H7621 (curse), H7650 (adjure), H7656 (Shebah), H7657 (seventy), H7652 (Sheba), H7659 (seven), H7620 (seven)",
    7622: "שְׁבוּת (shᵉbûwth | sheb-ooth')\n\nDerivation: or שְׁבִית; from H7617 שָׁבָה\nStrong's: exile, concretely, prisoners; figuratively, a former state of prosperity\nKJV: captive(-ity).\n\nCognate Group: H7633 (captives), H7628 (captive), H7617 (captive), H7618 (agate), H7622 (captive), H7619 (Shebuel), H8664 (Tishbite), H7629 (Shobi), H7630 (Shobai), H8453 (foreigner)\nGreek Equivalents: G161 αἰχμαλωσία",
    7623: "שָׁבַח (shâbach | shaw-bakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to address in aloud tone, i.e. (specifically) loud; figuratively, to pacify (as if by words)\nKJV: commend, glory, keep in, praise, still, triumph.\n\nCognate Group: H7623 (commend)\nGreek Equivalents: G134 αἰνέω, G1867 ἐπαινέω, G1950 ἐπιλανθάνομαι, G2744 καυχάομαι",
    7624: "שְׁבַח (shᵉbach | sheb-akh')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7623 שָׁבַח\nStrong's: to adulate, i.e. adore\nKJV: praise.\n\nCognate Group: H7624 (praise), H7625 (tribe)\nGreek Equivalents: G437 ἀνθομολογέομαι, G2127 εὐλογέω",
    7625: "שְׁבַט (shᵉbaṭ | sheb-at')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7626 שֵׁבֶט\nStrong's: a clan\nKJV: tribe.\n\nCognate Group: H7624 (praise), H7625 (tribe)",
    7626: "שֵׁבֶט (shêbeṭ | shay'-bet)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to branch off\nStrong's: a scion, i.e. (literally) a stick (for punishing, writing, fighting, ruling, walking, etc.) or (figuratively) a clan\nKJV: [idiom] correction, dart, rod, sceptre, staff, tribe.\n\nCognate Group: H7627 (Sebat), H8275 (sceptre), H7626 ([idiom] correction)\nGreek Equivalents: G444 ἄνθρωπος, G758 ἄρχων, G956 βέλος, G1218 δῆμος, G2218 ζυγός, G2923 κριτής, G3056 λόγος, G3148 μάστιξ, G3809 παιδεία, G4127 πληγή, G4464 ῥάβδος, G5443 φυλή",
    7627: "שְׁבָט (Shᵉbâṭ | sheb-awt')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Shebat, a Jewish month\nKJV: Sebat.\n\nCognate Group: H7627 (Sebat), H8275 (sceptre), H7626 ([idiom] correction)",
    7628: "שְׁבִי (shᵉbîy | sheb-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H7618 שְׁבוּ\nStrong's: exiled; captured; as noun, exile (abstractly or concretely and collectively); by extension, booty\nKJV: captive(-ity), prisoners, [idiom] take away, that was taken.\n\nCognate Group: H7633 (captives), H7628 (captive), H7617 (captive), H7618 (agate), H7622 (captive), H7619 (Shebuel), H8664 (Tishbite), H7629 (Shobi), H7630 (Shobai), H8453 (foreigner)\nGreek Equivalents: G161 αἰχμαλωσία",
    7629: "שֹׁבִי (Shôbîy | sho-bee')\n\nDerivation: from H7617 שָׁבָה ; captor\nStrong's: Shobi, an Ammonite\nKJV: Shobi.\n\nCognate Group: H7633 (captives), H7628 (captive), H7617 (captive), H7618 (agate), H7622 (captive), H7619 (Shebuel), H8664 (Tishbite), H7629 (Shobi), H7630 (Shobai), H8453 (foreigner)",
    7630: "שֹׁבַי (Shôbay | sho-bah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: for H7629 שֹׁבִי\nStrong's: Shobai, an Israelite\nKJV: Shobai.\n\nCognate Group: H7633 (captives), H7628 (captive), H7617 (captive), H7618 (agate), H7622 (captive), H7619 (Shebuel), H8664 (Tishbite), H7629 (Shobi), H7630 (Shobai), H8453 (foreigner)",
    7631: "שְׂבִיב (sᵉbîyb | seb-eeb')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7632 שָׁבִיב \nStrong's: flame (as split into tongues)\nKJV: flame.\n\nCognate Group: H7631 (flame)",
    7632: "שָׁבִיב (shâbîyb | shaw-beeb')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7616 שָׁבָב\nStrong's: flame (as split into tongues)\nKJV: spark.\n\nCognate Group: H7632 (spark)\nGreek Equivalents: G5395 φλόξ",
    7633: "שִׁבְיָה (shibyâh | shib-yaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7628 שְׁבִי\nStrong's: exile (abstractly or concretely and collectively)\nKJV: captives(-ity).\n\nCognate Group: H7633 (captives), H7628 (captive), H7617 (captive), H7618 (agate), H7622 (captive), H7619 (Shebuel), H8664 (Tishbite), H7629 (Shobi), H7630 (Shobai), H8453 (foreigner)",
    7634: "שׇׁבְיָה (Shobyâh | shob-yaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of the same as H7629 שֹׁבִי ; captivation\nStrong's: Shobjah, an Israelite\nKJV: Shachia (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H7914 (picture), H7907 (heart), H4906 (conceit), H7906 (Sechu), H7634 (Shachia), H7915 (knife)",
    7635: "שָׁבִיל (shâbîyl | shaw-beel')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7640 שֹׁבֶל\nStrong's: a track or passage-way (as if flowing along)\nKJV: path.\n\nCognate Group: H7732 (Shobal), H7641 (branch), H7635 (path), H7640 (leg)\nGreek Equivalents: G5147 τρίβος",
    7636: "שָׁבִיס (shâbîyç | shaw-beece')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to interweave\nStrong's: a netting for the hair\nKJV: caul.\n\nCognate Group: H7636 (caul)",
    7637: "שְׁבִיעִי (shᵉbîyʻîy | sheb-ee-ee')\n\nDerivation: or שְׁבִעִי; ordinal from H7657 שִׁבְעִים\nStrong's: seventh\nKJV: seventh (time).\n\nCognate Group: H7637 (seventh), H7651 (seven), H7658 (seven), H7621 (curse), H7650 (adjure), H7656 (Shebah), H7657 (seventy), H7652 (Sheba), H7659 (seven), H7620 (seven)\nGreek Equivalents: G1442 ἕβδομος, G2078 ἔσχατος",
    7638: "שָׂבָךְ (sâbâk | saw-bawk')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to intwine\nStrong's: a netting (ornament to the capital of a column)\nKJV: net.\n\nCognate Group: H7638 (net), H7639 (checker), H7643 (Shebam), H7730 (thick boughs)",
    7639: "שְׂבָכָה (sᵉbâkâh | seb-aw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7638 שָׂבָךְ\nStrong's: a net-work, i.e. (in hunting) a snare, (in architecture) a ballustrade; also a reticulated ornament to apillar\nKJV: checker, lattice, network, snare, wreath(-enwork).\n\nCognate Group: H7638 (net), H7639 (checker), H7643 (Shebam), H7730 (thick boughs)\nGreek Equivalents: G1350 δίκτυον",
    7640: "שֹׁבֶל (shôbel | show'-bel)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to flow\nStrong's: a lady's train (as trailing after her)\nKJV: leg.\n\nCognate Group: H7732 (Shobal), H7641 (branch), H7635 (path), H7640 (leg)",
    7641: "שִׁבֹּל (shibbôl | shib-bole)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) שִׁבֹּלֶת; from the same as H7640 שֹׁבֶל\nStrong's: a stream (as flowing); also an ear of grain (as growing out); by analogy, a branch\nKJV: branch, channel, ear (of corn), (water-)flood, Shibboleth. Compare H5451 סִבֹּלֶת .\n\nCognate Group: H7732 (Shobal), H7641 (branch), H7635 (path), H7640 (leg)\nGreek Equivalents: G2562 καλάμη, G2798 κλάδος, G4719 στάχυς",
    7642: "שַׁבְלוּל (shablûwl | shab-lool')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7640 שֹׁבֶל\nStrong's: a snail (as if floating in its own slime)\nKJV: snail.\n\nCognate Group: H8400 (blemish), H8397 (confusion), H7642 (snail), H1098 (corn), H1101 (anoint)",
    7643: "שְׂבָם (Sᵉbâm | seb-awm')\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) שִׂבְמָה; probably from H1313 בָּשָׂם ; spice\nStrong's: Sebam or Sibmah, a place in Moab\nKJV: Shebam, Shibmah, Sibmah.\n\nCognate Group: H7638 (net), H7639 (checker), H7643 (Shebam), H7730 (thick boughs)",
    7644: "שֶׁבְנָא (Shebnâʼ | sheb-naw')\n\nDerivation: or שֶׁבְנָה; from an unused root meaning to grow; growth\nStrong's: Shebna or Shebnah, an Israelite\nKJV: Shebna, Shebnah.\n\nCognate Group: H7644 (Shebna), H7645 (Shebaniah)",
    7645: "שְׁבַנְיָה (Shᵉbanyâh | sheb-an-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or שְׁבַנְיָהוּ; from the same as H7644 שֶׁבְנָא and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has grown (i.e. prospered)\nStrong's: Shebanjah, the name of three or four Israelites\nKJV: Shebaniah.\n\nCognate Group: H7644 (Shebna), H7645 (Shebaniah)",
    7646: "שָׂבַע (sâbaʻ | saw-bah')\n\nDerivation: or שָׂבֵעַ; a primitive root\nStrong's: to sate, i.e. fill to satisfaction (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: have enough, fill (full, self, with), be (to the) full (of), have plenty of, be satiate, satisfy (with), suffice, be weary of.\n\nCognate Group: H7654 (enough), H7647 (abundance), H7646 (have enough), H7653 (fulness), H7648 (fill), H7649 (full)\nGreek Equivalents: G1705 ἐμπίπλημι, G4129 πληθύνω, G4130 πλήθω, G4137 πληρόω, G5526 χορτάζω",
    7647: "שָׂבָע (sâbâʻ | saw-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H7646 שָׂבַע\nStrong's: copiousness\nKJV: abundance, plenteous(-ness, -ly).\n\nCognate Group: H7654 (enough), H7647 (abundance), H7646 (have enough), H7653 (fulness), H7648 (fill), H7649 (full)\nGreek Equivalents: G3182 μεθύσκω, G4134 πλήρης, G4140 πλησμονή",
