    7650: "שָׁבַע (shâbaʻ | shaw-bah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; properly to be complete, but used only as a denominative from H7651 שֶׁבַע\nStrong's: to seven oneself, i.e. swear (as if by repeating a declaration seven times)\nKJV: adjure, charge (by an oath, with an oath), feed to the full (by mistake for H7646 שָׂבַע), take an oath, [idiom] straitly, (cause to, make to) swear.\n\nCognate Group: H7637 (seventh), H7651 (seven), H7658 (seven), H7621 (curse), H7650 (adjure), H7656 (Shebah), H7657 (seventy), H7652 (Sheba), H7659 (seven), H7620 (seven)\nGreek Equivalents: G163 αἰχμαλωτίζω, G611 ἀποκρίνομαι, G994 βοάω, G1843 ἐξομολογέω, G1844 ἐξορκίζω, G1965 ἐπίορκος, G2896 κράζω, G3660 ὀμνύω, G3670 ὁμολογέω, G3726 ὁρκίζω, G3726 ὁρκίζω, G4727 στενάζω",
