    7697: "שִׁגָּעֹון (shiggâʻôwn | shig-gaw-yone')\n\nDerivation: from H7696 שָׁגַע\nStrong's: craziness\nKJV: furiously, madness.\n\nCognate Group: H7697 (furiously), H7696 (mad)\nGreek Equivalents: G3883 παραλλαγή",
    7698: "שֶׁגֶר (sheger | sheh'-ger)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to eject\nStrong's: the fetus (as finally expelled)\nKJV: that cometh of, increase.\n\nCognate Group: H7698 (that cometh of), H7700 (devil)\nGreek Equivalents: G3388 μήτρα",
    7699: "שַׁד (shad | shad)\n\nDerivation: or שֹׁד; probably from H7736 שׁוּד (in its original sense) contracted\nStrong's: the breast of a woman or animal (as bulging)\nKJV: breast, pap, teat.\n\nCognate Group: H7706 (Almighty), H7707 (Shedeur), H7705 ([idiom] all sorts), H7699 (breast)\nGreek Equivalents: G3149 μαστός",
    7700: "שֵׁד (shêd | shade)\n\nDerivation: from H7736 שׁוּד\nStrong's: a doemon (as malignant)\nKJV: devil.\n\nCognate Group: H7698 (that cometh of), H7700 (devil)\nGreek Equivalents: G1140 δαιμόνιον",
    7701: "שֹׁד (shôd | shode)\n\nDerivation: or שֹׁוד; (Job 5:21), from H7736 שׁוּד\nStrong's: violence, ravage\nKJV: desolation, destruction, oppression, robbery, spoil(-ed, -er, -ing), wasting.\n\nCognate Group: H7736 (waste), H7701 (desolation), H7703 (dead)\nGreek Equivalents: G94 ἄδικος, G2556 κακός, G3639 ὄλεθρος, G4430 πτῶμα, G4938 σύντριμμα, G5004 ταλαιπωρία",
    7702: "שָׂדַד (sâdad | saw-dad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to abrade, i.e. harrow afield\nKJV: break clods, harrow.\n\nCognate Group: H7708 (Siddim), H7702 (break clods)\nGreek Equivalents: G1670 ἑλκύω, G1765 ἐνισχύω, G2038 ἐργάζομαι",
    7703: "שָׁדַד (shâdad | shaw-dad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to be burly, i.e. (figuratively) powerful (passively, impregnable); by implication, to ravage\nKJV: dead, destroy(-er), oppress, robber, spoil(-er), [idiom] utterly, (lay) waste.\n\nCognate Group: H7736 (waste), H7701 (desolation), H7703 (dead)\nGreek Equivalents: G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G684 ἀπώλεια, G818 ἀτιμάζω, G1377 διώκω, G1842 ἐξολοθρεύω, G2692 καταστροφή, G3027 λῃστής, G3639 ὄλεθρος, G3645 ὀλοθρεύω, G5003 ταλαιπωρέω, G5005 ταλαίπωρος",
    7704: "שָׂדֶה (sâdeh | saw-deh')\n\nDerivation: or שָׂדַי; from an unused root meaning to spread out\nStrong's: a field (as flat)\nKJV: country, field, ground, land, soil, [idiom] wild.\n\nCognate Group: H7716 (cattle), H2089 (lamb), H7704 (country), H7717 (record)\nGreek Equivalents: G66 ἄγριος, G68 ἀγρός, G290 ἀμπελών, G1091 γεώργιον, G1093 γῆ, G2233 ἡγέομαι, G3598 ὁδός, G3725 ὅριον, G5561 χώρα",
    7705: "שִׁדָּה (shiddâh | shid-dah')\n\nDerivation: from H7703 שָׁדַד\nStrong's: a wife (as mistress of the house)\nKJV: [idiom] all sorts, musical instrument.\n\nCognate Group: H7706 (Almighty), H7707 (Shedeur), H7705 ([idiom] all sorts), H7699 (breast)",
    7706: "שַׁדַּי (Shadday | shad-dah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H7703 שָׁדַד\nStrong's: the Almighty\nKJV: Almighty.\n\nCognate Group: H7706 (Almighty), H7707 (Shedeur), H7705 ([idiom] all sorts), H7699 (breast)\nGreek Equivalents: G2032 ἐπουράνιος, G2316 θεός, G2425 ἱκανός, G2962 κύριος, G3841 παντοκράτωρ, G3956 πᾶς",
    7707: "שְׁדֵיאוּר (Shᵉdêyʼûwr | shed-ay-oor')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7704 שָׂדֶה and H217 אוּר ; spreader of light\nStrong's: Shedejur, an Israelite\nKJV: Shedeur.\n\nCognate Group: H7706 (Almighty), H7707 (Shedeur), H7705 ([idiom] all sorts), H7699 (breast)",
    7708: "שִׂדִּים (Siddîym | sid-deem')\n\nDerivation: plural from the same as H7704 שָׂדֶה ; flats\nStrong's: Siddim, a valley in Palestine\nKJV: Siddim.\n\nCognate Group: H7708 (Siddim), H7702 (break clods)\nGreek Equivalents: G252 ἁλυκός",
    7709: "שְׁדֵמָה (shᵉdêmâh | shed-ay-maw')\n\nDerivation: apparently from H7704 שָׂדֶה\nStrong's: a cultivated field\nKJV: blasted, field.\n\nCognate Group: H8309 (field), H7709 (blasted)",
    7710: "שָׁדַף (shâdaph | shaw-daf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to scorch\nKJV: blast.\n\nCognate Group: H7714 (Shadrach), H7711 (blasted), H7710 (blast)",
    7711: "שְׁדֵפָה (shᵉdêphâh | shed-ay-faw')\n\nDerivation: or שִׁדָּפֹון; from H7710 שָׁדַף\nStrong's: blight\nKJV: blasted(-ing).\n\nCognate Group: H7714 (Shadrach), H7711 (blasted), H7710 (blast)\nGreek Equivalents: G90 ἀδιαφθορία, G640 ἀπορία, G4451 πύρωσις",
    7712: "שְׁדַר (shᵉdar | shed-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) a primitive root\nStrong's: to endeavor\nKJV: labour.\n\nCognate Group: H7712 (labour), H849 (sedition), H7715 (Shadrach)\nGreek Equivalents: G75 ἀγωνίζομαι",
    7713: "שְׂדֵרָה (sᵉdêrâh | sed-ay-raw')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to regulate\nStrong's: a row, i.e. rank (of soldiers), story (of rooms)\nKJV: board, range.\n\nCognate Group: H7713 (board), H5468 (order), H4528 (porch)",
    7714: "שַׁדְרַךְ (Shadrak | shad-rak')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: Shadrak, the Babylonian name of one of Daniel's companions\nKJV: Shadrach.\n\nCognate Group: H7714 (Shadrach), H7711 (blasted), H7710 (blast)",
    7715: "שַׁדְרַךְ (Shadrak | shad-rak')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) the same as H7714 שַׁדְרַךְ \nStrong's: Shadrak, the Babylonian name of one of Daniel's companions\nKJV: Shadrach.\n\nCognate Group: H7712 (labour), H849 (sedition), H7715 (Shadrach)",
    7716: "שֶׂה (seh | seh)\n\nDerivation: or שֵׂי; probably from H7582 שָׁאָה through the idea of pushing out to graze\nStrong's: a member of a flock, i.e. a sheep or goat\nKJV: (lesser, small) cattle, ewe, goat, lamb, sheep. Compare H2089 זֶה .\n\nCognate Group: H7716 (cattle), H2089 (lamb), H7704 (country), H7717 (record)\nGreek Equivalents: G286 ἀμνός, G4168 ποίμνιον, G4263 πρόβατον",
    7717: "שָׂהֵד (sâhêd | saw-hade')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to testify\nStrong's: a witness\nKJV: record.\n\nCognate Group: H7716 (cattle), H2089 (lamb), H7704 (country), H7717 (record)\nGreek Equivalents: G3141 μαρτυρία, G3144 μάρτυς",
    7718: "שֹׁהַם (shôham | sho'-ham)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably mean to blanch\nStrong's: a gem, probably the beryl (from its pale green color)\nKJV: onyx.\n\nCognate Group: H8346 (sixty), H8341 (give the sixth participle), H7864 (Sheva), H7724 (Sheva), H7719 (Shoham), H8337 (six), H7718 (onyx), H8345 (sixth)\nGreek Equivalents: G4556 σάρδιος, G4665 σμάραγδος",
    7719: "שֹׁהַם (Shôham | sho'-ham)\n\nDerivation: the same as H7718 שֹׁהַם\nStrong's: Shoham, an Israelite\nKJV: Shoham.\n\nCognate Group: H8346 (sixty), H8341 (give the sixth participle), H7864 (Sheva), H7724 (Sheva), H7719 (Shoham), H8337 (six), H7718 (onyx), H8345 (sixth)",
    7720: "שַׂהֲרֹן (sahărôn | sah-har-one')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H5469 סַהַר\nStrong's: a round pendant for the neck\nKJV: ornament, round tire like the moon.\n\nCognate Group: H7720 (ornament)",
    7721: "שֹׂוא (sôwʼ | so)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root (akin to H5375 נָשָׂא and H7722 שֹׁוא) meaning to rise\nStrong's: a rising\nKJV: arise.\n\nCognate Group: H5375 (accept), H5387 (captain), H4858 (burden), H4864 (burden), H7863 (excellency), H4853 (burden), H7613 (be accepted), H5379 (gift), H7865 (Sion), H4856 (respect), H5385 (carriage), H4984 (exalted), H7721 (arise)",
    7722: "שֹׁוא (shôwʼ | sho)\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) שֹׁואָה; or שֹׁאָה; from an unused root meaning to rush over\nStrong's: a tempest; by implication, devastation\nKJV: desolate(-ion), destroy, destruction, storm, wasteness.\n\nCognate Group: H4875 (desolation), H8663 (crying), H7722 (desolate), H7738 ([idiom] substance)\nGreek Equivalents: G684 ἀπώλεια, G2347 θλῖψις, G3730 ὁρμή, G3803 παγίς, G4928 συνοχή, G5004 ταλαιπωρία, G5205 ὑετός",
    7723: "שָׁוְא (shâvᵉʼ | shawv)\n\nDerivation: or שַׁו; from the same as H7722 שֹׁוא in the sense of desolating\nStrong's: evil (as destructive), literally (ruin) or morally (especially guile); figuratively idolatry (as false, subjective), uselessness (as deceptive, objective; also adverbially, in vain)\nKJV: false(-ly), lie, lying, vain, vanity.\n\nCognate Group: H7723 (false)\nGreek Equivalents: G459 ἄνομος, G824 ἄτοπος, G2756 κενός, G3152 μάταιος, G3153 ματαιότης, G3154 ματαιόω, G3154 ματαιόω, G5571 ψευδής",
