    7736: "שׁוּד (shûwd | shood)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to swell up, i.e. figuratively (by implication of insolence) to devastate\nKJV: waste.\n\nCognate Group: H7736 (waste), H7701 (desolation), H7703 (dead)",
    7737: "שָׁוָה (shâvâh | shaw-vaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to level, i.e. equalize; figuratively, to resemble; by implication, to adjust (i.e. counterbalance, be suitable, compose, place, yield, etc.)\nKJV: avail, behave, bring forth, compare, countervail, (be, make) equal, lay, be (make, a-) like, make plain, profit, reckon.\n\nCognate Group: H7737 (avail), H3438 (Ishvah), H3440 (Ishuai), H7741 (Shaveh Kiriathaim), H3441 (Jesuites), H7740 (Shaveh)\nGreek Equivalents: G514 ἄξιος, G520 ἀπάγω, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G700 ἀρέσκω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2675 καταρτίζω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G4308 προοράω, G4851 συμφέρω, G5087 τίθημι",
    7738: "שָׁוָה (shâvâh | shaw-vaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to destroy\nKJV: [idiom] substance (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H4875 (desolation), H8663 (crying), H7722 (desolate), H7738 ([idiom] substance)",
    7739: "שְׁוָה (shᵉvâh | shev-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic); corresponding to H7737 שָׁוָה\nStrong's: to resemble\nKJV: make like.\n\nCognate Group: H7739 (make like)",
    7740: "שָׁוֵה (Shâvêh | shaw-vay')\n\nDerivation: from H7737 שָׁוָה ; plain\nStrong's: Shaveh, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Shaveh.\n\nCognate Group: H7737 (avail), H3438 (Ishvah), H3440 (Ishuai), H7741 (Shaveh Kiriathaim), H3441 (Jesuites), H7740 (Shaveh)",
    7741: "שָׁוֵה קִרְיָתַיִם (Shâvêh Qiryâthayim | shaw-vay' kir-yawthah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7740 שָׁוֵה and the dual of H7151 קִרְיָה ; plain of a double city\nStrong's: Shaveh-Kirjathajim, a place East of the Jordan\nKJV: Shaveh Kiriathaim.\n\nCognate Group: H7737 (avail), H3438 (Ishvah), H3440 (Ishuai), H7741 (Shaveh Kiriathaim), H3441 (Jesuites), H7740 (Shaveh)",
    7742: "שׂוּחַ (sûwach | soo'-akh)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to muse pensively\nKJV: meditate.\n\nCognate Group: H7751 (go), H7850 (scourge), H7752 (scourge), H7885 (oar), H4880 (oar), H7742 (meditate)",
    7743: "שׁוּחַ (shûwach | shoo'-akh)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to sink, literally or figuratively\nKJV: bow down, incline, humble.\n\nCognate Group: H7744 (Shuah), H7845 (corruption), H7745 (ditch), H7746 (Shuah), H7743 (bow down), H7882 (pit), H7749 (Shuhamites), H7747 (Shuhite), H7748 (Shuham)\nGreek Equivalents: G5013 ταπεινόω",
    7744: "שׁוּחַ (Shûwach | shoo'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H7743 שׁוּחַ ; dell\nStrong's: Shuach, a son of Abraham\nKJV: Shuah.\n\nCognate Group: H7744 (Shuah), H7845 (corruption), H7745 (ditch), H7746 (Shuah), H7743 (bow down), H7882 (pit), H7749 (Shuhamites), H7747 (Shuhite), H7748 (Shuham)",
