    7750: "שׂוּט (sûwṭ | soot)\n\nDerivation: or (by permutation) סוּט; a primitive root\nStrong's: to detrude, i.e. (intransitively and figuratively) become derelict (wrongly practise; namely, idolatry)\nKJV: turn aside to.\n\nCognate Group: H7750 (turn aside to), H7846 (revolter)",
    7751: "שׁוּט (shûwṭ | shoot)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to push forth; (but used only figuratively) to lash, i.e. (the sea with oars) to row; by implication, to travel\nKJV: go (about, through, to and fro), mariner, rower, run to and fro.\n\nCognate Group: H7751 (go), H7850 (scourge), H7752 (scourge), H7885 (oar), H4880 (oar), H7742 (meditate)\nGreek Equivalents: G818 ἀτιμάζω, G1279 διαπορεύομαι, G1321 διδάσκω, G1330 διέρχομαι, G1914 ἐπιβλέπω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G4022 περιέρχομαι, G4023 περιέχω, G4063 περιτρέχω",
    7752: "שֹׁוט (shôwṭ | shote)\n\nDerivation: from H7751 שׁוּט\nStrong's: a lash (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: scourge, whip.\n\nCognate Group: H7751 (go), H7850 (scourge), H7752 (scourge), H7885 (oar), H4880 (oar), H7742 (meditate)\nGreek Equivalents: G3148 μάστιξ",
    7753: "שׂוּךְ (sûwk | sook)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to entwine, i.e. shut in (for formation, protection or restraint)\nKJV: fence, (make an) hedge (up).\n\nCognate Group: H4881 (hedge), H7753 (fence)",
