    7757: "שׁוּל (shûwl | shool)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to hang down\nStrong's: a skirt; by implication, a bottom edge\nKJV: hem, skirt, train.\n\nCognate Group: H7762 (garlic), H7759 (Shulamite), H7767 (Shunamite), H7765 (Shunites), H7764 (Shuni), H7757 (hem), H7766 (Shunem)\nGreek Equivalents: G1391 δόξα",
