    7779: "שׁוּף (shûwph | shoof)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to gape, i.e. snap at; figuratively, to overwhelm\nKJV: break, bruise, cover.\n\nCognate Group: H7779 (break)\nGreek Equivalents: G2662 καταπατέω, G2918 κρίνον",
