    7786: "שׂוּר (sûwr | soor)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to vanquish; by implication, to rule (causatively, crown)\nKJV: make princes, have power, reign. See H5493 סוּר .\n\nCognate Group: H7786 (make princes), H8323 ([idiom] altogether), H8269 (captain), H8283 (Sarah), H8297 (Sarai), H8282 (lady)",
    7787: "שׂוּר (sûwr | soor)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (identical with H7786 שׂוּר through the idea of reducing to pieces; compare H4883 מַשֹּׂור)\nStrong's: to saw\nKJV: cut.\n\nCognate Group: H7787 (cut), H7795 (principal)",
    7788: "שׁוּר (shûwr | shoor)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to turn, i.e. travel about (as a harlot or a merchant)\nKJV: go, singular See also H7891 שִׁיר .\n\nCognate Group: H8670 (present), H7788 (go)",
    7789: "שׁוּר (shûwr | shoor)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (identical with through the idea of going round for inspection)\nStrong's: to spy out, i.e. (generally) survey, (for evil) lurk for, (for good) care for\nKJV: behold, lay wait, look, observe, perceive, regard, see.\n\nCognate Group: H7789 (behold), H8324 (enemy), H7790 (enemy)\nGreek Equivalents: G390 ἀναστρέφω, G1330 διέρχομαι, G2190 ἐχθρός, G2648 καταμανθάνω, G2729 κατισχύω, G3708 ὁράω, G4017 περιβλέπω, G4306 προνοέω",
    7790: "שׁוּר (shûwr | shoor)\n\nDerivation: from H7889 שִׁימֹון\nStrong's: a foe (as lying in wait)\nKJV: enemy.\n\nCognate Group: H7789 (behold), H8324 (enemy), H7790 (enemy)",
    7791: "שׁוּר (shûwr | shoor)\n\nDerivation: from H7788 שׁוּר\nStrong's: a wall (as going about)\nKJV: wall.\n\nCognate Group: H7803 (Shuthelah), H8364 (Shuthalhites), H7793 (Shur), H7802 (Shoshannim-Eduth), H7799 (lily), H7800 (Shushan), H8284 (sing), H7791 (wall), H7794 (bull)\nGreek Equivalents: G5038 τεῖχος",
    7792: "שׁוּר (shûwr | shoor)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7791 שׁוּר \nStrong's: a wall (as going about)\nKJV: wall.\n\nCognate Group: H7792 (wall), H8243 (leg), H7801 (Susanchites)",
    7793: "שׁוּר (Shûwr | shoor)\n\nDerivation: the same as H7791 שׁוּר\nStrong's: Shur, a region of the Desert\nKJV: Shur.\n\nCognate Group: H7803 (Shuthelah), H8364 (Shuthalhites), H7793 (Shur), H7802 (Shoshannim-Eduth), H7799 (lily), H7800 (Shushan), H8284 (sing), H7791 (wall), H7794 (bull)",
    7794: "שֹׁור (shôwr | shore)\n\nDerivation: from H7788 שׁוּר\nStrong's: a bullock (as a traveller)\nKJV: bull(-ock), cow, ox, wall (by mistake for H7791 שׁוּר).\n\nCognate Group: H7803 (Shuthelah), H8364 (Shuthalhites), H7793 (Shur), H7802 (Shoshannim-Eduth), H7799 (lily), H7800 (Shushan), H8284 (sing), H7791 (wall), H7794 (bull)\nGreek Equivalents: G1016 βοῦς, G3448 μόσχος, G4618 σιτευτός, G5022 ταῦρος",
    7795: "שֹׂורָה (sôwrâh | so-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H7786 שׂוּר in the primitive sense of H5493 סוּר\nStrong's: properly, a ring, i.e. (by analogy) a row (adverbially)\nKJV: principal.\n\nCognate Group: H7787 (cut), H7795 (principal)",
    7796: "שֹׂורֵק (Sôwrêq | so-rake')\n\nDerivation: the same as H8321 שֹׂרֵק ; a vine\nStrong's: Sorek, a valley in Palestine\nKJV: Sorek.\n\nCognate Group: H7796 (Sorek), H8291 (principal plant), H8321 (choice wine), H4957 (Masrekah), H8320 (speckled)",
    7797: "שׂוּשׂ (sûws | soos)\n\nDerivation: or שִׂישׂ; a primitive root\nStrong's: to be bright, i.e. cheerful\nKJV: be glad, [idiom] greatly, joy, make mirth, rejoice.\n\nCognate Group: H8342 (gladness), H7797 (be glad), H4885 (joy)\nGreek Equivalents: G21 ἀγαλλιάω, G1863 ἐπάγω, G5463 χαίρω",
    7798: "שַׁוְשָׁא (Shavshâʼ | shav-shaw')\n\nDerivation: from H7797 שׂוּשׂ ; joyful\nStrong's: Shavsha, an Israelite\nKJV: Shavsha.\n\nCognate Group: H7798 (Shavsha), H8304 (Seraiah), H3478 (Israel), H3481 (of Israel), H8280 (have power), H3482 (Israelitish)",
    7799: "שׁוּשַׁן (shûwshan | shoo-shan')\n\nDerivation: or שֹׁושָׁן; or שֹׁשָׁן; and (feminine) שֹׁושַׁנָּה; from H7797 שׂוּשׂ\nStrong's: a lily (from its whiteness), as aflower of architectural ornament; also a (straight) trumpet (from the tubular shape)\nKJV: lily, Shoshannim.\n\nCognate Group: H7803 (Shuthelah), H8364 (Shuthalhites), H7793 (Shur), H7802 (Shoshannim-Eduth), H7799 (lily), H7800 (Shushan), H8284 (sing), H7791 (wall), H7794 (bull)\nGreek Equivalents: G2918 κρίνον, G4677 Σουσάννα",
    7800: "שׁוּשַׁן (Shûwshan | shoo-shan')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7799 שׁוּשַׁן\nStrong's: Shushan, a place in Persia\nKJV: Shushan.\n\nCognate Group: H7803 (Shuthelah), H8364 (Shuthalhites), H7793 (Shur), H7802 (Shoshannim-Eduth), H7799 (lily), H7800 (Shushan), H8284 (sing), H7791 (wall), H7794 (bull)",
    7801: "שׁוּשַׁנְכִי (Shûwshankîy | shoo-shan-kee')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) of foreign origin\nStrong's: a Shushankite (collectively) or inhabitants of some unknown place in Assyrian\nKJV: Susanchites.\n\nCognate Group: H7792 (wall), H8243 (leg), H7801 (Susanchites)",
    7802: "שׁוּשַׁן עֵדוּת (Shûwshan ʻÊdûwth | shoo-shan' ay-dooth')\n\nDerivation: or (plural of former) שֹׁושַׁנִּים עֵדוּת\n\nTypo: lemma שֹׁושַׁנִּיס עֵדוּת samekh, corrected to שֹׁושַׁנִּים עֵדוּת\n\n; from H7799 שׁוּשַׁן and H5715 עֵדוּת ; lily (or trumpet) of assemblage\nStrong's: Shushan-Eduth or Shoshannim-Eduth, the title of a popular song\nKJV: Shoshannim-Eduth, Shushan-eduth.\n\nCognate Group: H7803 (Shuthelah), H8364 (Shuthalhites), H7793 (Shur), H7802 (Shoshannim-Eduth), H7799 (lily), H7800 (Shushan), H8284 (sing), H7791 (wall), H7794 (bull)",
    7803: "שׁוּתֶלַח (Shûwthelach | shoo-theh'-lakh)\n\nDerivation: probably from H7582 שָׁאָה and the same as H8520 תֶּלַח ; crash of breakage\nStrong's: Shuthelach, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Shuthelah.\n\nCognate Group: H7803 (Shuthelah), H8364 (Shuthalhites), H7793 (Shur), H7802 (Shoshannim-Eduth), H7799 (lily), H7800 (Shushan), H8284 (sing), H7791 (wall), H7794 (bull)",
    7804: "שְׁזַב (shᵉzab | shez-ab')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H5800 עָזַב\nStrong's: to leave, i.e. (causatively) free\nKJV: deliver.\n\nCognate Group: H7844 (corrupt), H7804 (deliver)\nGreek Equivalents: G482 ἀντιλαμβάνομαι, G1807 ἐξαιρέω, G3084 λυτρόω, G4506 ῥύομαι, G4982 σώζω",
    7805: "שָׁזַף (shâzaph | shaw-zaf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tan (by sunburning); figuratively (as if by a piercing ray) to scan\nKJV: look up, see.\n\nCognate Group: H7805 (look up)",
    7806: "שָׁזַר (shâzar | shaw-zar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to twist (a thread of straw)\nKJV: twine.\n\nCognate Group: H7806 (twine)\nGreek Equivalents: G3514 νήθω",
    7807: "שַׁח (shach | shakh)\n\nDerivation: from H7817 שָׁחַח\nStrong's: sunk, i.e. downcast\nKJV: [phrase] humble.\n\nCognate Group: H7807 (humble), H7817 (bend), H3439 (Jeshoaiah)",
    7808: "שֵׂחַ (sêach | say'-akh)\n\nDerivation: for H7879 שִׂיחַ\nStrong's: communion, i.e. (reflexively) meditation\nKJV: thought.\n\nCognate Group: H7879 (babbling), H7881 (meditation), H7878 (commune), H7808 (thought)",
    7809: "שָׁחַד (shâchad | shaw-khad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to donate, i.e. bribe\nKJV: hire, give a reward.\n\nCognate Group: H7810 (bribe), H7809 (hire)\nGreek Equivalents: G5412 φορτίζω",
    7810: "שַׁחַד (shachad | shakh'-ad)\n\nDerivation: from H7809 שָׁחַד\nStrong's: a donation (venal or redemptive)\nKJV: bribe(-ry), gift, present, reward.\n\nCognate Group: H7810 (bribe), H7809 (hire)\nGreek Equivalents: G1435 δῶρον",
    7811: "שָׂחָה (sâchâh | saw-khaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to swim; causatively, to inundate\nKJV: (make to) swim.\n\nCognate Group: H7811 (swim), H7813 (to swim in)\nGreek Equivalents: G3068 λούω",
    7812: "שָׁחָה (shâchâh | shaw-khaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to depress, i.e. prostrate (especially reflexive, in homage to royalty or God)\nKJV: bow (self) down, crouch, fall down (flat), humbly beseech, do (make) obeisance, do reverence, make to stoop, worship.\n\nCognate Group: H7812 (bow down), H7825 (destruction), H7816 (pit)\nGreek Equivalents: G2705 καταφιλέω, G2955 κύπτω, G4160 ποιέω, G4352 προσκυνέω, G5015 ταράσσω",
    7813: "שָׂחוּ (sâchûw | saw'-khoo)\n\nDerivation: from H7811 שָׂחָה\nStrong's: a pond (for swimming)\nKJV: to swim in.\n\nCognate Group: H7811 (swim), H7813 (to swim in)",
    7814: "שְׂחֹוק (sᵉchôwq | sekh-oke')\n\nDerivation: or שְׂחֹק; from H7832 שָׂחַק\nStrong's: laughter (in merriment or defiance)\nKJV: derision, laughter(-ed to scorn, -ing), mocked, sport.\n\nCognate Group: H4890 (scorn), H7832 (deride), H7814 (derision)\nGreek Equivalents: G1071 γέλως, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G5479 χαρά",
    7815: "שְׁחֹור (shᵉchôwr | shekh-ore')\n\nDerivation: from H7835 שָׁחַר\nStrong's: dinginess, i.e. perhaps soot\nKJV: coal.\n\nCognate Group: H7815 (coal), H806 (Ashur), H7840 (black), H7835 (be black), H7839 (youth), H7838 (black)",
    7816: "שְׁחוּת (shᵉchûwth | shekh-ooth')\n\nDerivation: from H7812 שָׁחָה\nStrong's: pit\nKJV: pit.\n\nCognate Group: H7812 (bow down), H7825 (destruction), H7816 (pit)",
    7817: "שָׁחַח (shâchach | shaw-khakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to sink or depress (reflexive or causative)\nKJV: bend, bow (down), bring (cast) down, couch, humble self, be (bring) low, stoop.\n\nCognate Group: H7807 (humble), H7817 (bend), H3439 (Jeshoaiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G1416 δύνω, G2559 κακόω, G2578 κάμπτω, G2609 κατάγω, G2955 κύπτω, G5013 ταπεινόω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5080 τήκω",
    7818: "שָׂחַט (sâchaṭ | saw-khat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to tread out, i.e. squeeze (grapes)\nKJV: press.\n\nCognate Group: H7818 (press), H7824 (cieled with)",
    7819: "שָׁחַט (shâchaṭ | shaw-khat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to slaughter (in sacrifice or massacre)\nKJV: kill, offer, shoot out, slay, slaughter.\n\nCognate Group: H7821 (killing), H7820 (beat), H7819 (kill)\nGreek Equivalents: G4969 σφάζω",
    7820: "שָׁחַט (shâchaṭ | shaw-khat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (identical with H7819 שָׁחַט through the idea of striking)\nStrong's: to hammer out\nKJV: beat.\n\nCognate Group: H7821 (killing), H7820 (beat), H7819 (kill)",
    7821: "שְׁחִיטָה (shᵉchîyṭâh | shekh-ee-taw')\n\nDerivation: from H7819 שָׁחַט\nStrong's: slaughter\nKJV: killing.\n\nCognate Group: H7821 (killing), H7820 (beat), H7819 (kill)",
    7822: "שְׁחִין (shᵉchîyn | shekh-een')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to burn\nStrong's: inflammation, i.e. an ulcer\nKJV: boil, botch.\n\nCognate Group: H7822 (boil)\nGreek Equivalents: G1668 ἕλκος",
    7823: "שָׁחִיס (shâchîyç | shaw-khece')\n\nDerivation: or סָחִישׁ; from an unused root apparently meaning to sprout\nStrong's: aftergrowth\nKJV: (that) which springeth of the same.\n\nCognate Group: H7823 (which springeth of the same), H5501 (offscouring), H5500 (scrape)\nGreek Equivalents: G393 ἀνατέλλω, G2640 κατάλειμμα",
    7824: "שָׁחִיף (shâchîyph | shaw-kheef')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7828 שַׁחַף\nStrong's: a board (as chipped thin)\nKJV: cieled with.\n\nCognate Group: H7818 (press), H7824 (cieled with)",
    7825: "שְׁחִית (shᵉchîyth | shekh-eeth')\n\nDerivation: from H7812 שָׁחָה\nStrong's: a pit-fall (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: destruction, pit.\n\nCognate Group: H7812 (bow down), H7825 (destruction), H7816 (pit)",
    7826: "שַׁחַל (shachal | shakh'-al)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to roar\nStrong's: a lion (from his characteristic roar)\nKJV: (fierce) lion.\n\nCognate Group: H7826 (lion), H7827 (onycha)\nGreek Equivalents: G3023 λέων",
    7827: "שְׁחֵלֶת (shᵉchêleth | shekh-ay'-leth)Typo: lemma שְׁחֶלֶת second vowel, corrected to שְׁחֵלֶת\n\nDerivation: apparently from the same as H7826 שַׁחַל through some obscure idea, perhaps that of peeling off by concussion of sound\nStrong's: a scale or shell, i.e. the aromatic mussel.\nKJV: onycha.\n\nCognate Group: H7826 (lion), H7827 (onycha)",
    7828: "שַׁחַף (shachaph | shakh'-af)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to peel, i.e. emaciate\nStrong's: the gull (as thin)\nKJV: cuckoo.\n\nCognate Group: H7828 (cuckoo), H7829 (consumption)",
    7829: "שַׁחֶפֶת (shachepheth | shakh-eh'-feth)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7828 שַׁחַף\nStrong's: emaciation\nKJV: consumption.\n\nCognate Group: H7828 (cuckoo), H7829 (consumption)\nGreek Equivalents: G640 ἀπορία",
    7830: "שַׁחַץ (shachats | shakh'-ats)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root apparently meaning to strut\nStrong's: haughtiness (as evinced by the attitude)\nKJV: [idiom] lion, pride.\n\nCognate Group: H7830 ([idiom] lion), H7831 (Shahazimah)\nGreek Equivalents: G213 ἀλαζών",
    7831: "שַׁחֲצֹום (Shachătsôwm | shakh-ats-ome')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7830 שַׁחַץ ; proudly\nStrong's: Shachatsom, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Shahazimah (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H7830 ([idiom] lion), H7831 (Shahazimah)",
    7832: "שָׂחַק (sâchaq | saw-khak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to laugh (in pleasure or detraction); by implication, to play\nKJV: deride, have in derision, laugh, make merry, mock(-er), play, rejoice, (laugh to) scorn, be in (make) sport.\n\nCognate Group: H4890 (scorn), H7832 (deride), H7814 (derision)\nGreek Equivalents: G1070 γελάω, G1702 ἐμπαίζω, G2606 καταγελάω, G3738 ὀρχέομαι, G3815 παίζω",
    7833: "שָׁחַק (shâchaq | shaw-khak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to comminate (by trituration or attrition)\nKJV: beat, wear.\n\nCognate Group: H7833 (beat), H7834 (cloud)",
    7834: "שַׁחַק (shachaq | shakh'-ak)\n\nDerivation: from H7833 שָׁחַק\nStrong's: a powder (as beaten small); by analogy, a thin vapor; by extension, the firmament\nKJV: cloud, small dust, heaven, sky.\n\nCognate Group: H7833 (beat), H7834 (cloud)\nGreek Equivalents: G109 ἀήρ, G798 ἄστρον, G3507 νεφέλη, G3509 νέφος, G3772 οὐρανός, G4493 ῥιπή, G4733 στερέωμα",
    7835: "שָׁחַר (shâchar | shaw-khar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (identical with H7836 שָׁחַר through the idea of the duskiness of early dawn)\nStrong's: to be dim or dark (in color)\nKJV: be black.\n\nCognate Group: H7815 (coal), H806 (Ashur), H7840 (black), H7835 (be black), H7839 (youth), H7838 (black)\nGreek Equivalents: G4656 σκοτόω",
    7836: "שָׁחַר (shâchar | shaw-khar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to dawn, i.e. (figuratively) be (up) early at any task (with the implication of earnestness); by extension, to search for (with painstaking)\nKJV: (do something) betimes, enquire early, rise (seek) betimes, seek diligently) early, in the morning).\n\nCognate Group: H7842 (Shaharaim), H4891 (morning), H7837 (day), H7841 (Shehariah), H7836 (betimes)\nGreek Equivalents: G1960 ἐπιμελῶς, G2212 ζητέω, G3719 ὀρθρίζω, G4406 πρώϊμος",
    7837: "שַׁחַר (shachar | shakh'-ar)\n\nDerivation: from H7836 שָׁחַר\nStrong's: dawn (literal, figurative or adverbial)\nKJV: day(-spring), early, light, morning, whence riseth.\n\nCognate Group: H7842 (Shaharaim), H4891 (morning), H7837 (day), H7841 (Shehariah), H7836 (betimes)\nGreek Equivalents: G3722 ὄρθρος, G4404 πρωΐ",
    7838: "שָׁחֹר (shâchôr | shaw-khore')\n\nDerivation: or שָׁחֹור; from H7835 שָׁחַר\nStrong's: properly, dusky, but also (absol.) jetty\nKJV: black.\n\nCognate Group: H7815 (coal), H806 (Ashur), H7840 (black), H7835 (be black), H7839 (youth), H7838 (black)\nGreek Equivalents: G3189 μέλας",
    7839: "שַׁחֲרוּת (shachărûwth | shakh-ar-ooth')\n\nDerivation: from H7836 שָׁחַר\nStrong's: a dawning, i.e. (figuratively) juvenescence\nKJV: youth.\n\nCognate Group: H7815 (coal), H806 (Ashur), H7840 (black), H7835 (be black), H7839 (youth), H7838 (black)",
    7840: "שְׁחַרְחֹרֶת (shᵉcharchôreth | shekh-ar-kho'-reth)\n\nDerivation: from H7835 שָׁחַר\nStrong's: swarthy\nKJV: black.\n\nCognate Group: H7815 (coal), H806 (Ashur), H7840 (black), H7835 (be black), H7839 (youth), H7838 (black)",
    7841: "שְׁחַרְיָה (Shᵉcharyâh | shekh-ar-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H7836 שָׁחַר and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has sought\nStrong's: Shecharjah, an Israelite\nKJV: Shehariah.\n\nCognate Group: H7842 (Shaharaim), H4891 (morning), H7837 (day), H7841 (Shehariah), H7836 (betimes)",
    7842: "שַׁחֲרַיִם (Shachărayim | shakh-ar-ah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: dual of H7837 שַׁחַר ; double dawn\nStrong's: Shacharajim, an Israelite\nKJV: Shaharaim.\n\nCognate Group: H7842 (Shaharaim), H4891 (morning), H7837 (day), H7841 (Shehariah), H7836 (betimes)",
    7843: "שָׁחַת (shâchath | shaw-khath')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to decay, i.e. (causatively) ruin (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: batter, cast off, corrupt(-er, thing), destroy(-er, -uction), lose, mar, perish, spill, spoiler, [idiom] utterly, waste(-r).\n\nCognate Group: H7848 (shittah), H7843 (batter), H516 (Al-taschith), H4892 (destroying), H4893 (corruption), H4889 (corruption), H7851 (Shittim)\nGreek Equivalents: G64 ἀγρεύω, G142 αἴρω, G264 ἁμαρτάνω, G458 ἀνομία, G459 ἄνομος, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G684 ἀπώλεια, G765 ἀσεβής, G853 ἀφανίζω, G854 ἀφανισμός, G1290 διασπορά, G1311 διαφθείρω, G1312 διαφθορά, G1632 ἐκχέω, G1685 ἐμβάλλω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1813 ἐξαλείφω, G1842 ἐξολοθρεύω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2380 θύω, G2598 καταβάλλω, G2679 κατασκάπτω, G2693 καταστρώννυμι, G2704 καταφθείρω, G3075 λυμαίνομαι, G3539 νοιέω, G3645 ὀλοθρεύω, G4098 πίπτω, G5013 ταπεινόω, G5351 φθείρω",
    7844: "שְׁחַת (shᵉchath | shekh-ath')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7843 שָׁחַת \nStrong's: to decay, i.e. (causatively) ruin (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: corrupt, fault.\n\nCognate Group: H7844 (corrupt), H7804 (deliver)",
    7845: "שַׁחַת (shachath | shakh'-ath)\n\nDerivation: from H7743 שׁוּחַ\nStrong's: a pit (especially as a trap); figuratively, destruction\nKJV: corruption, destruction, ditch, grave, pit.\n\nCognate Group: H7744 (Shuah), H7845 (corruption), H7745 (ditch), H7746 (Shuah), H7743 (bow down), H7882 (pit), H7749 (Shuhamites), H7747 (Shuhite), H7748 (Shuham)\nGreek Equivalents: G999 βόθυνος, G2288 θάνατος, G2513 καθαρός, G4509 ῥύπος, G5356 φθορά",
    7846: "שֵׂט (sêṭ | sayte)\n\nDerivation: or סֵט; from H7750 שׂוּט\nStrong's: a departure from right, i.e. sin\nKJV: revolter, that turn aside.\n\nCognate Group: H7750 (turn aside to), H7846 (revolter)\nGreek Equivalents: G3847 παράβασις",
    7847: "שָׂטָה (sâṭâh | saw-taw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to deviate from duty\nKJV: decline, go aside, turn.\n\nCognate Group: H7847 (decline)\nGreek Equivalents: G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G3845 παραβαίνω",
    7848: "שִׁטָּה (shiṭṭâh | shit-taw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of a derivative (only in the plural שִׁטִּים; meaning the sticks of wood) from the same as H7850 שֹׁטֵט\nStrong's: the acacia (from its scourging thorns)\nKJV: shittah, shittim. See also H1029 בֵּית הַשִּׁטָּה .\n\nCognate Group: H7848 (shittah), H7843 (batter), H516 (Al-taschith), H4892 (destroying), H4893 (corruption), H4889 (corruption), H7851 (Shittim)",
    7849: "שָׁטַח (shâṭach | shaw-takh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to expand\nKJV: all abroad, enlarge, spread, stretch out.\n\nCognate Group: H7849 (all abroad), H4894 (spread)\nGreek Equivalents: G2693 καταστρώννυμι, G5594 ψύχω",
    7850: "שֹׁטֵט (shôṭêṭ | sho-tate')\n\nDerivation: active participle of an otherwise unused root meaning (properly, to pierce; but only as a denominative from H7752 שֹׁוט)\n\nStrong's: to flog; a goad\nKJV: scourge.\n\nCognate Group: H7751 (go), H7850 (scourge), H7752 (scourge), H7885 (oar), H4880 (oar), H7742 (meditate)\nGreek Equivalents: G2247 ἧλος",
    7851: "שִׁטִּים (Shiṭṭîym | shit-teem')\n\nDerivation: the same as the plural of H7848 שִׁטָּה ; acacia trees\nStrong's: Shittim, a place East of the Jordan\nKJV: Shittim.\n\nCognate Group: H7848 (shittah), H7843 (batter), H516 (Al-taschith), H4892 (destroying), H4893 (corruption), H4889 (corruption), H7851 (Shittim)",
    7852: "שָׂטַם (sâṭam | saw-tam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to lurk for, i.e. persecute\nKJV: hate, oppose self against.\n\nCognate Group: H7852 (hate), H4895 (hatred)",
    7853: "שָׂטַן (sâṭan | saw-tan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to attack, (figuratively) accuse\nKJV: (be an) adversary, resist.\n\nCognate Group: H7855 (accusation), H7853 (adversary), H7856 (Sitnah), H7854 (adversary)\nGreek Equivalents: G480 ἀντίκειμαι, G1225 διαβάλλω",
    7854: "שָׂטָן (sâṭân | saw-tawn')\n\nDerivation: from H7853 שָׂטַן\nStrong's: an opponent; especially (with the article prefixed) Satan, the arch-enemy of good\nKJV: adversary, Satan, withstand.\n\nCognate Group: H7855 (accusation), H7853 (adversary), H7856 (Sitnah), H7854 (adversary)\nGreek Equivalents: G1228 διάβολος, G4566 Σατᾶν, G4567 Σατανᾶς",
    7855: "שִׂטְנָה (siṭnâh | sit-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H7853 שָׂטַן\nStrong's: opposition (by letter)\nKJV: accusation.\n\nCognate Group: H7855 (accusation), H7853 (adversary), H7856 (Sitnah), H7854 (adversary)\nGreek Equivalents: G1992 ἐπιστολή",
    7856: "שִׂטְנָה (Siṭnâh | sit-naw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7855 שִׂטְנָה\nStrong's: Sitnah, the name of a well in Pal\nKJV: Sitnah.\n\nCognate Group: H7855 (accusation), H7853 (adversary), H7856 (Sitnah), H7854 (adversary)",
    7857: "שָׁטַף (shâṭaph | shaw-taf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to gush; by implication, to inundate, cleanse; by analogy, to gallop, conquer\nKJV: drown, (over-) flow(-whelm, rinse, run, rush, (throughly) wash (away).\n\nCognate Group: H8241 (little), H7857 (drown), H7858 (flood)\nGreek Equivalents: G633 ἀπονίπτω, G637 ἀποπλύνω, G2626 κατακλύζω, G2670 καταποντίζω, G2694 κατασύρω, G3538 νίπτω, G4937 συντρίβω, G4951 σύρω, G5342 φέρω",
    7858: "שֶׁטֶף (sheṭeph | sheh'-tef)\n\nDerivation: or שֵׁטֶף; from H7857 שָׁטַף\nStrong's: a deluge (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: flood, outrageous, overflowing.\n\nCognate Group: H8241 (little), H7857 (drown), H7858 (flood)\nGreek Equivalents: G2627 κατακλυσμός, G3691 ὀξύς, G5205 ὑετός",
    7859: "שְׁטַר (shᵉṭar | shet-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a side\nKJV: side.\n\nCognate Group: H7859 (side), H7761 (command)",
    7860: "שֹׁטֵר (shôṭêr | sho-tare')\n\nDerivation: active participle of an otherwise unused root probably meaning to write\nStrong's: properly, a scribe, i.e. (by analogy or implication) an official superintendent or magistrate\nKJV: officer, overseer, ruler.\n\nCognate Group: H7884 (Shihor-libnath), H7862 (present), H7889 (Shimon), H7886 (Shiloh), H7866 (Shihon), H4896 (dominion), H7883 (Shihor), H7861 (Shitrai), H7860 (officer), H7876 (be unmindful), H7877 (Shiza)\nGreek Equivalents: G315 ἀναγκάζω, G1122 γραμματεύς, G2923 κριτής",
    7861: "שִׁטְרַי (Shiṭray | shit-rah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7860 שֹׁטֵר ; magisterial\nStrong's: Shitrai, an Israelite\nKJV: Shitrai.\n\nCognate Group: H7884 (Shihor-libnath), H7862 (present), H7889 (Shimon), H7886 (Shiloh), H7866 (Shihon), H4896 (dominion), H7883 (Shihor), H7861 (Shitrai), H7860 (officer), H7876 (be unmindful), H7877 (Shiza)",
    7862: "שַׁי (shay | shah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: probably from H7737 שָׁוָה\nStrong's: a gift (as available)\nKJV: present.\n\nCognate Group: H7884 (Shihor-libnath), H7862 (present), H7889 (Shimon), H7886 (Shiloh), H7866 (Shihon), H4896 (dominion), H7883 (Shihor), H7861 (Shitrai), H7860 (officer), H7876 (be unmindful), H7877 (Shiza)\nGreek Equivalents: G1435 δῶρον",
    7863: "שִׂיא (sîyʼ | see)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7721 שֹׂוא by permutation\nStrong's: elevation\nKJV: excellency.\n\nCognate Group: H5375 (accept), H5387 (captain), H4858 (burden), H4864 (burden), H7863 (excellency), H4853 (burden), H7613 (be accepted), H5379 (gift), H7865 (Sion), H4856 (respect), H5385 (carriage), H4984 (exalted), H7721 (arise)",
    7864: "שְׁיָא (Shᵉyâʼ | sheh-yaw')\n\nDerivation: for H7724 שְׁוָא\nStrong's: Sheja, an Israelite\nKJV: Sheva (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H8346 (sixty), H8341 (give the sixth participle), H7864 (Sheva), H7724 (Sheva), H7719 (Shoham), H8337 (six), H7718 (onyx), H8345 (sixth)",
    7865: "שִׂיאֹן (Sîyʼôn | see-ohn')\n\nDerivation: from H7863 שִׂיא ; peak\nStrong's: Sion, the summit of Mount Hermon\nKJV: Sion.\n\nCognate Group: H5375 (accept), H5387 (captain), H4858 (burden), H4864 (burden), H7863 (excellency), H4853 (burden), H7613 (be accepted), H5379 (gift), H7865 (Sion), H4856 (respect), H5385 (carriage), H4984 (exalted), H7721 (arise)",
    7866: "שִׁיאֹון (Shîyʼôwn | shee-ohn')\n\nTypo: xlit Shîʼyôwn corrected to Shîyʼôwn\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7722 שֹׁוא ; ruin\nStrong's: Shijon, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Shihon.\n\nCognate Group: H7884 (Shihor-libnath), H7862 (present), H7889 (Shimon), H7886 (Shiloh), H7866 (Shihon), H4896 (dominion), H7883 (Shihor), H7861 (Shitrai), H7860 (officer), H7876 (be unmindful), H7877 (Shiza)",
    7867: "שִׂיב (sîyb | seeb)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to become aged, i.e. (by implication) to grow gray\nKJV: (be) grayheaded.\n\nCognate Group: H7869 (age), H7867 (grayheaded), H7872 (gray hairs)",
    7868: "שִׂיב (sîyb | seeb)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7867 שִׂיב \nStrong's: properly, to become aged, i.e. (by implication) to grow gray\nKJV: elder.\n\nCognate Group: H7868 (elder)\nGreek Equivalents: G4246 πρεσβύτης",
    7869: "שֵׂיב (sêyb | sabe)\n\nDerivation: from H7867 שִׂיב\nStrong's: old age\nKJV: age.\n\nCognate Group: H7869 (age), H7867 (grayheaded), H7872 (gray hairs)\nGreek Equivalents: G1094 γῆρας",
    7870: "שִׁיבָה (shîybâh | shee-baw')\n\nDerivation: by permutation from H7725 שׁוּב\nStrong's: a return (of property)\nKJV: captivity.\n\nCognate Group: H3434 (Jashobeam), H8666 (answer), H7725 (to turn back), H3437 (Jashub), H7727 (Shobab), H3142 (Jushab-hesed), H7780 (Shophach), H7728 (backsliding), H7870 (captivity), H3433 (Jashubi-lehem), H4878 (backsliding), H7729 (returning), H7726 (backsliding), H7731 (Shobach), H4877 (Meshobab), H3432 (Jashubites)",
    7871: "שִׁיבָה (shîybâh | shee-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H3427 יָשַׁב\nStrong's: residence\nKJV: while...lay.\n\nCognate Group: H3430 (Ishbi-benob), H3428 (Jeshebeab), H3436 (Joshbekashah), H3429 (that sat in the seat), H3427 (abide), H7871 (while), H4186 (assembly), H8453 (foreigner), H7675 (place), H3143 (Josibiah)",
    7872: "שֵׂיבָה (sêybâh | say-baw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7869 שֵׂיב\nStrong's: old age\nKJV: (be) gray (grey hoar,-y) hairs (head,-ed), old age.\n\nCognate Group: H7869 (age), H7867 (grayheaded), H7872 (gray hairs)\nGreek Equivalents: G1094 γῆρας",
    7873: "שִׂיג (sîyg | seeg)\n\nDerivation: from H7734 שׂוּג\nStrong's: a withdrawal (into a private place)\nKJV: pursuing.\n\nCognate Group: H7873 (pursuing), H5472 (backslider), H5253 (departing away), H7734 (turn back), H5509 (dross)",
    7874: "שִׂיד (sîyd | seed)Typo: lemma שׂיד missing vowel, corrected to שִׂיד\n\nGreek Equivalents: G2867 κονιάω \n\nDerivation: a primitive root probably meaning to boil up (compare H7736 שׁוּד); used only as denominative from H7875 שִׂיד\nStrong's: to plaster\nKJV: plaister.\n\nCognate Group: H7874 (plaister), H7875 (lime)",
    7875: "שִׂיד (sîyd | seed)\n\nDerivation: from H7874 שִׂיד \n\nTypo: lemma שׂיד missing vowel, corrected to שִׂיד\n\nStrong's: lime (as boiling when slacked)\nKJV: lime, plaister.\n\nCognate Group: H7874 (plaister), H7875 (lime)",
    7876: "שָׁיָה (shâyâh | shaw-yaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to keep in memory\nKJV: be unmindful. (Render Deuteronomy 32:18, 'A Rock bore thee, thou must recollect; and (yet) thou hast forgotten,' etc.)\n\nCognate Group: H7884 (Shihor-libnath), H7862 (present), H7889 (Shimon), H7886 (Shiloh), H7866 (Shihon), H4896 (dominion), H7883 (Shihor), H7861 (Shitrai), H7860 (officer), H7876 (be unmindful), H7877 (Shiza)\nGreek Equivalents: G1459 ἐγκαταλείπω",
    7877: "שִׁיזָא (Shîyzâʼ | shee-zaw')\n\nDerivation: of unknown derivation\nStrong's: Shiza, an Israelite\nKJV: Shiza.\n\nCognate Group: H7884 (Shihor-libnath), H7862 (present), H7889 (Shimon), H7886 (Shiloh), H7866 (Shihon), H4896 (dominion), H7883 (Shihor), H7861 (Shitrai), H7860 (officer), H7876 (be unmindful), H7877 (Shiza)",
    7878: "שִׂיחַ (sîyach | see'-akh)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to ponder, i.e. (by implication) converse (with oneself, and hence, aloud) or (transitively) utter\nKJV: commune, complain, declare, meditate, muse, pray, speak, talk (with).\n\nCognate Group: H7879 (babbling), H7881 (meditation), H7878 (commune), H7808 (thought)\nGreek Equivalents: G1334 διηγέομαι, G1555 ἐκδιηγέομαι, G3191 μελετάω, G5350 φθέγγομαι",
    7879: "שִׂיחַ (sîyach | see'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H7878 שִׂיחַ\nStrong's: a contemplation; by implication, an utterance\nKJV: babbling, communication, complaint, meditation, prayer, talk.\n\nCognate Group: H7879 (babbling), H7881 (meditation), H7878 (commune), H7808 (thought)\nGreek Equivalents: G1162 δέησις, G1649 ἔλεγξις, G2189 ἔχθρα, G2237 ἡδονή, G5515 χλωρός",
    7880: "שִׂיחַ (sîyach | see'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H7878 שִׂיחַ\nStrong's: a shoot (as if uttered or put forth), i.e. (generally) shrubbery\nKJV: bush, plant, shrub.\n\nCognate Group: H7880 (bush)",
    7881: "שִׂיחָה (sîychâh | see-khaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7879 שִׂיחַ\nStrong's: reflection; be extension, devotion\nKJV: meditation, prayer.\n\nCognate Group: H7879 (babbling), H7881 (meditation), H7878 (commune), H7808 (thought)",
    7882: "שִׁיחָה (shîychâh | shee-khaw')\n\nDerivation: for H7745 שׁוּחָה\nStrong's: a pit-fall\nKJV: pit.\n\nCognate Group: H7744 (Shuah), H7845 (corruption), H7745 (ditch), H7746 (Shuah), H7743 (bow down), H7882 (pit), H7749 (Shuhamites), H7747 (Shuhite), H7748 (Shuham)",
    7883: "שִׁיחֹור (Shîychôwr | shee-khore')\n\nDerivation: or שִׁחֹור; or שִׁחֹר; probably from H7835 שָׁחַר ; dark, i.e. turbid\nStrong's: Shichor, a stream of Egypt\nKJV: Shihor, Sihor.\n\nCognate Group: H7884 (Shihor-libnath), H7862 (present), H7889 (Shimon), H7886 (Shiloh), H7866 (Shihon), H4896 (dominion), H7883 (Shihor), H7861 (Shitrai), H7860 (officer), H7876 (be unmindful), H7877 (Shiza)",
    7884: "שִׁיחֹור לִבְנָת (Shîychôwr Libnâth | shee-khore' lib-nawth')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7883 שִׁיחֹור and H3835 לָבַן ; darkish whiteness\nStrong's: Shichor-Libnath, a stream of Palestine\nKJV: Shihor-libnath.\n\nCognate Group: H7884 (Shihor-libnath), H7862 (present), H7889 (Shimon), H7886 (Shiloh), H7866 (Shihon), H4896 (dominion), H7883 (Shihor), H7861 (Shitrai), H7860 (officer), H7876 (be unmindful), H7877 (Shiza)",
    7885: "שַׁיִט (shayiṭ | shay'-yit)\n\nDerivation: from H7751 שׁוּט ; also compare H7752 שֹׁוט \nStrong's: an oar; a scourge (figuratively)\nKJV: oar, scourge.\n\nCognate Group: H7751 (go), H7850 (scourge), H7752 (scourge), H7885 (oar), H4880 (oar), H7742 (meditate)",
    7886: "שִׁילֹה (Shîylôh | shee-lo')\n\nDerivation: from H7951 שָׁלָה ; tranquil\nStrong's: Shiloh, an epithet of the Messiah\nKJV: Shiloh.\n\nCognate Group: H7884 (Shihor-libnath), H7862 (present), H7889 (Shimon), H7886 (Shiloh), H7866 (Shihon), H4896 (dominion), H7883 (Shihor), H7861 (Shitrai), H7860 (officer), H7876 (be unmindful), H7877 (Shiza)\nGreek Equivalents: G606 ἀπόκειμαι",
    7887: "שִׁילֹה (Shîylôh | shee-lo')\n\nDerivation: or שִׁלֹה; or שִׁילֹו; or שִׁלֹו; from the same as H7886 שִׁילֹה\nStrong's: Shiloh, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Shiloh.\n\nCognate Group: H8023 (Shiloni), H7988 (young one), H7887 (Shiloh), H7953 (take away), H7888 (Shilonite)",
    7888: "שִׁילֹונִי (Shîylôwnîy | shee-lo-nee')\n\nDerivation: or שִׁילֹנִי; or שִׁלֹנִי; from H7887 שִׁילֹה\nStrong's: a Shilonite or inhabitant of Shiloh\nKJV: Shilonite.\n\nCognate Group: H8023 (Shiloni), H7988 (young one), H7887 (Shiloh), H7953 (take away), H7888 (Shilonite)",
    7889: "שִׁימֹון (Shîymôwn | shee-mone')\n\nDerivation: apparently for H3452 יְשִׁימֹון ; desert\nStrong's: Shimon, an Israelite\nKJV: Shimon.\n\nCognate Group: H7884 (Shihor-libnath), H7862 (present), H7889 (Shimon), H7886 (Shiloh), H7866 (Shihon), H4896 (dominion), H7883 (Shihor), H7861 (Shitrai), H7860 (officer), H7876 (be unmindful), H7877 (Shiza)",
    7890: "שַׁיִן (shayin | shah'-yin)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to urinate\nStrong's: urine\nKJV: piss.\n\nCognate Group: H7890 (piss), H8366 (piss)",
    7891: "שִׁיר (shîyr | sheer)\n\nDerivation: or (the original form) שׁוּר; (1 Samuel 18:6), a primitive root (rather identical with H7788 שׁוּר through the idea of strolling minstrelsy)\nStrong's: to sing\nKJV: behold (by mistake for H7789 שׁוּר), sing(-er, -ing man, -ing woman).\n\nCognate Group: H7892 (musical), H7891 (behold)\nGreek Equivalents: G103 ᾄδω, G103 ᾄδω, G134 αἰνέω, G757 ἄρχω, G758 ἄρχων, G2307 θέλημα, G5455 φωνέω",
    7892: "שִׁיר (shîyr | sheer)\n\nDerivation: or feminine שִׁירָה; from H7891 שִׁיר\nStrong's: a song; abstractly, singing\nKJV: musical(-ick), [idiom] sing(-er, -ing), song.\n\nCognate Group: H7892 (musical), H7891 (behold)\nGreek Equivalents: G3451 μουσικός, G5214 ὑμνέω, G5215 ὕμνος, G5568 ψαλμός, G5603 ᾠδή",
    7893: "שַׁיִשׁ (shayish | shah'-yish)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to bleach, i.e. whiten; See H8336 שֵׁשׁ .\nStrong's: white, i.e. marble.\n\nCognate Group: H8336 ([idiom] blue), H7893 (white), H7895 (Shishak), H7894 (Shisha)",
    7894: "שִׁישָׁא (Shîyshâʼ | shee-shaw')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7893 שַׁיִשׁ ; whiteness\nStrong's: Shisha, an Israelite\nKJV: Shisha.\n\nCognate Group: H8336 ([idiom] blue), H7893 (white), H7895 (Shishak), H7894 (Shisha)",
    7895: "שִׁישַׁק (Shîyshaq | shee-shak')\n\nDerivation: or שׁוּשַׁק; of Egyptian derivation\nStrong's: Shishak, an Egyptian king\nKJV: Shishak.\n\nCognate Group: H8336 ([idiom] blue), H7893 (white), H7895 (Shishak), H7894 (Shisha)",
    7896: "שִׁית (shîyth | sheeth)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to place (in a very wide application)\nKJV: apply, appoint, array, bring, consider, lay (up), let alone, [idiom] look, make, mark, put (on), [phrase] regard, set, shew, be stayed, [idiom] take.\n\nCognate Group: H8352 (Seth), H8356 (foundation), H7896 (apply), H7898 (thorns), H7897 (attire)\nGreek Equivalents: G447 ἀνίημι, G498 ἀντιτάσσομαι, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G1251 διακούομαι, G1252 διακρίνω, G1316 διαχωρίζομαι, G1325 δίδωμι, G1817 ἐξανίστημι, G1863 ἐπάγω, G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2186 ἐφίστημι, G2525 καθίστημι, G3396 μίγνυμι, G3539 νοιέω, G4337 προσέχω, G4369 προστίθημι, G4388 προτίθεμαι, G5021 τάσσω, G5087 τίθημι, G5293 ὑποτάσσω",
    7897: "שִׁית (shîyth | sheeth)\n\nDerivation: from H7896 שִׁית\nStrong's: a dress (as put on)\nKJV: attire.\n\nCognate Group: H8352 (Seth), H8356 (foundation), H7896 (apply), H7898 (thorns), H7897 (attire)\nGreek Equivalents: G1491 εἶδος",
    7898: "שַׁיִת (shayith | shah'-yith)\n\nDerivation: from H7896 שִׁית\nStrong's: scrub or trash, i.e. wild growth of weeds or briers (as if put on the field)\nKJV: thorns.\n\nCognate Group: H8352 (Seth), H8356 (foundation), H7896 (apply), H7898 (thorns), H7897 (attire)\nGreek Equivalents: G173 ἄκανθα, G1643 ἐλαύνω, G2562 καλάμη",
    7899: "שֵׂךְ (sêk | sake)\n\nDerivation: from H5526 סָכַךְ in the sense of H7753 שׂוּךְ\nStrong's: a brier (as of a hedge)\nKJV: prick.\n\nCognate Group: H7905 (barbed iron), H7899 (prick)\nGreek Equivalents: G4647 σκόλοψ",
    7900: "שֹׂךְ (sôk | soke)\n\nDerivation: from H5526 סָכַךְ in the sense of H7753 שׂוּךְ\nStrong's: a booth (as interlaced)\nKJV: tabernacle.\n\nCognate Group: H5526 (cover), H7900 (tabernacle)",
    7901: "שָׁכַב (shâkab | shaw-kab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to lie down (for rest, sexual connection, decease or any other purpose)\nKJV: [idiom] at all, cast down, (lover-)lay (self) (down), (make to) lie (down, down to sleep, still with), lodge, ravish, take rest, sleep, stay.\n\nCognate Group: H7902 ([idiom] carnally), H7901 ([idiom] at all), H7903 ([idiom] lie), H4904 (bed)\nGreek Equivalents: G373 ἀναπαύω, G599 ἀποθνήσκω, G2518 καθεύδω, G2521 κάθημαι, G2621 κατάκειμαι, G2647 καταλύω, G2730 κατοικέω, G2827 κλίνω, G2837 κοιμάω, G2845 κοίτη, G2942 κυβερνήτης, G3435 μολύνω",
    7902: "שְׁכָבָה (shᵉkâbâh | shek-aw-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H7901 שָׁכַב\nStrong's: a lying down (of dew, or for the sexual act)\nKJV: [idiom] carnally, copulation, [idiom] lay, seed.\n\nCognate Group: H7902 ([idiom] carnally), H7901 ([idiom] at all), H7903 ([idiom] lie), H4904 (bed)\nGreek Equivalents: G2664 καταπαύω, G2845 κοίτη",
    7903: "שְׁכֹבֶת (shᵉkôbeth | shek-o'-beth)Typo: lemma שֶׁכֹבֶת first vowel, corrected to שְׁכֹבֶת\n\nDerivation: from H7901 שָׁכַב\nStrong's: a (sexual) lying with\nKJV: [idiom] lie.\n\nCognate Group: H7902 ([idiom] carnally), H7901 ([idiom] at all), H7903 ([idiom] lie), H4904 (bed)",
    7904: "שָׁכָה (shâkâh | shaw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to roam (through lust)\nKJV: in the morning (by mistake for H7925 שָׁכַם).\n\nCognate Group: H7904 (in the morning)",
    7905: "שֻׂכָּה (sukkâh | sook-kaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7900 שֹׂךְ in the sense of H7899 שֵׂךְ\nStrong's: a dart (as pointed like a thorn)\nKJV: barbed iron.\n\nCognate Group: H7905 (barbed iron), H7899 (prick)",
    7906: "שֵׂכוּ (Sêkûw | say'-koo)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root apparently meaning to surmount; an observatory (with the article)\nStrong's: Seku, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Sechu.\n\nCognate Group: H7914 (picture), H7907 (heart), H4906 (conceit), H7906 (Sechu), H7634 (Shachia), H7915 (knife)",
    7907: "שֶׂכְוִי (sekvîy | sek-vee')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H7906 שֵׂכוּ\nStrong's: observant, i.e. (concretely) the mind\nKJV: heart.\n\nCognate Group: H7914 (picture), H7907 (heart), H4906 (conceit), H7906 (Sechu), H7634 (Shachia), H7915 (knife)",
    7908: "שְׁכֹול (shᵉkôwl | shek-ole')\n\nDerivation: infinitive of H7921 שָׁכֹל\nStrong's: bereavement\nKJV: loss of children, spoiling.\n\nCognate Group: H7909 (barren), H7921 (bereave), H7908 (loss of children), H7923 (to have after loss of others)",
    7909: "שַׁכּוּל (shakkûwl | shak-kool')\n\nDerivation: or שַׁכֻּל; from H7921 שָׁכֹל\nStrong's: bereaved\nKJV: barren, bereaved (robbed) of children (whelps).\n\nCognate Group: H7909 (barren), H7921 (bereave), H7908 (loss of children), H7923 (to have after loss of others)\nGreek Equivalents: G639 ἀπορέω",
    7910: "שִׁכֹּור (shikkôwr | shik-kore')\n\nDerivation: or שִׁכֹּר; from H7937 שָׁכַר\nStrong's: intoxicated, as astate or a habit\nKJV: drunk(-ard, -en, -en man).\n\nCognate Group: H7941 (strong drink), H7910 (drunk), H7943 (drunken), H7942 (Shicron), H7937 (drink)\nGreek Equivalents: G3182 μεθύσκω",
    7911: "שָׁכַח (shâkach | shaw-kakh')\n\nDerivation: or שָׁכֵחַ; a primitive root\nStrong's: to mislay, i.e. to be oblivious of, from want of memory or attention\nKJV: [idiom] at all, (cause to) forget.\n\nCognate Group: H7911 ([idiom] at all), H7913 (forget)\nGreek Equivalents: G415 ἀνελεήμων, G1459 ἐγκαταλείπω, G1950 ἐπιλανθάνομαι, G2641 καταλείπω, G3024 λήθη",
    7912: "שְׁכַח (shᵉkach | shek-akh')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7911 שָׁכַח through the idea of disclosure of a covered or forgotten thing\nStrong's: to discover (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: find.\n\nCognate Group: H7912 (find)\nGreek Equivalents: G2147 εὑρίσκω, G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G5083 τηρέω",
    7913: "שָׁכֵחַ (shâkêach | shaw-kay'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H7911 שָׁכַח\nStrong's: oblivious\nKJV: forget.\n\nCognate Group: H7911 ([idiom] at all), H7913 (forget)",
    7914: "שְׂכִיָּה (sᵉkîyâh | sek-ee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine from the same as H7906 שֵׂכוּ\nStrong's: a conspicuous object\nKJV: picture.\n\nCognate Group: H7914 (picture), H7907 (heart), H4906 (conceit), H7906 (Sechu), H7634 (Shachia), H7915 (knife)",
    7915: "שַׂכִּין (sakkîyn | sak-keen')\n\nDerivation: intensive perhaps from the same as H7906 שֵׂכוּ in the sense of H7753 שׂוּךְ\nStrong's: a knife (as pointed or edged)\nKJV: knife.\n\nCognate Group: H7914 (picture), H7907 (heart), H4906 (conceit), H7906 (Sechu), H7634 (Shachia), H7915 (knife)",
    7916: "שָׂכִיר (sâkîyr | saw-keer')\n\nDerivation: from H7936 שָׂכַר\nStrong's: a man at wages by the day or year\nKJV: hired (man, servant), hireling.\n\nCognate Group: H7958 (quails), H7938 (reward), H8073 (Shalmai), H8009 (Salmon), H7940 (Sacar), H7917 (that is hired), H4909 (reward), H8012 (Salmon), H8007 (Salma), H7939 (hire), H7936 (earn wages), H8014 (Shalmai), H7916 (hired)\nGreek Equivalents: G3407 μίσθιος, G3411 μισθωτός",
    7917: "שְׂכִירָה (sᵉkîyrâh | sek-ee-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7916 שָׂכִיר\nStrong's: a hiring\nKJV: that is hired.\n\nCognate Group: H7958 (quails), H7938 (reward), H8073 (Shalmai), H8009 (Salmon), H7940 (Sacar), H7917 (that is hired), H4909 (reward), H8012 (Salmon), H8007 (Salma), H7939 (hire), H7936 (earn wages), H8014 (Shalmai), H7916 (hired)",
    7918: "שָׁכַךְ (shâkak | shaw-kak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to weave (i.e. lay) a trap; figuratively, (through the idea of secreting) to allay (passions; physically, abate a flood)\nKJV: appease, assuage, make to cease, pacify, set.\n\nCognate Group: H7918 (appease)\nGreek Equivalents: G2869 κοπάζω, G4014 περιαιρέω",
    7919: "שָׂכַל (sâkal | saw-kal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be (causatively, make or act) circumspect and hence, intelligent\nKJV: consider, expert, instruct, prosper, (deal) prudent(-ly), (give) skill(-ful), have good success, teach, (have, make to) understand(-ing), wisdom, (be, behave self, consider, make) wise(-ly), guide wittingly.\n\nCognate Group: H4905 (Maschil), H7922 (discretion), H7919 (consider)\nGreek Equivalents: G50 ἀγνοέω, G718 ἁρμόζω, G877 ἀφροσύνη, G878 ἄφρων, G1343 δικαιοσύνη, G1921 ἐπιγινώσκω, G1987 ἐπίσταμαι, G1990 ἐπιστήμων, G2137 εὐοδόω, G2186 ἐφίστημι, G2657 κατανοέω, G3154 ματαιόω, G3471 μωραίνω, G3474 μωρός, G3474 μωρός, G3539 νοιέω, G4907 σύνεσις, G4908 συνετός, G4920 συνίημι, G5263 ὑποδείκνυμι, G5426 φρονέω",
    7920: "שְׂכַל (sᵉkal | sek-al')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7919 שָׂכַל \nStrong's: to be (causatively, make or act) circumspect and hence, intelligent\nKJV: consider.\n\nCognate Group: H7920 (consider), H7924 (understanding)",
    7921: "שָׁכֹל (shâkôl | shaw-kole')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to miscarry, i.e. suffer abortion; by analogy, to bereave (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: bereave (of children), barren, cast calf (fruit, young), be (make) childless, deprive, destroy, [idiom] expect, lose children, miscarry, rob of children, spoil.\n\nCognate Group: H7909 (barren), H7921 (bereave), H7908 (loss of children), H7923 (to have after loss of others)\nGreek Equivalents: G770 ἀσθενέω, G815 ἄτεκνος, G2719 κατεσθίω, G5097 τιμωρέω",
    7922: "שֶׂכֶל (sekel | seh'-kel)\n\nDerivation: or שֵׂכֶל; from H7919 שָׂכַל\nStrong's: intelligence; by implication, success\nKJV: discretion, knowledge, policy, prudence, sense, understanding, wisdom, wise.\n\nCognate Group: H4905 (Maschil), H7922 (discretion), H7919 (consider)\nGreek Equivalents: G1270 διανόημα, G1655 ἐλεήμων, G1771 ἔννοια, G4678 σοφία, G5428 φρόνησις",
    7923: "שִׁכֻּלִים (shikkulîym | shik-koo-leem')\n\nDerivation: plural from H7921 שָׁכֹל\nStrong's: childlessness (by continued bereavements)\nKJV: to have after loss of others.\n\nCognate Group: H7909 (barren), H7921 (bereave), H7908 (loss of children), H7923 (to have after loss of others)\nGreek Equivalents: G622 ἀπόλλυμι",
    7924: "שׇׂכְלְתָנוּ (soklᵉthânûw | sok-leth-aw-noo')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H7920 שְׂכַל\nStrong's: intelligence\nKJV: understanding.\n\nCognate Group: H7920 (consider), H7924 (understanding)",
    7925: "שָׁכַם (shâkam | shaw-kam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; properly, to incline (the shoulder to a burden); but used only as denominative from H7926 שְׁכֶם\nStrong's: literally, to load up (on the back of man or beast), i.e. to start early in the morning\nKJV: (arise, be up, get (oneself) up, rise up) early (betimes), morning.\n\nCognate Group: H7929 (shoulder blade), H7925 (early), H7927 (Shechem), H7930 (Shichemites), H7926 (back), H7928 (Shechem)\nGreek Equivalents: G450 ἀνίστημι, G1817 ἐξανίστημι, G3719 ὀρθρίζω, G3720 ὀρθρινός",
    7926: "שְׁכֶם (shᵉkem | shek-em')\n\nDerivation: from H7925 שָׁכַם\nStrong's: the neck (between the shoulders) as the place of burdens; figuratively, the spur of ahill\nKJV: back, [idiom] consent, portion, shoulder.\n\nCognate Group: H7929 (shoulder blade), H7925 (early), H7927 (Shechem), H7930 (Shichemites), H7926 (back), H7928 (Shechem)\nGreek Equivalents: G2218 ζυγός, G3577 νῶτος, G4966 Συχέμ, G5606 ὦμος",
    7927: "שְׁכֶם (Shᵉkem | shek-em')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7926 שְׁכֶם ; ridge\nStrong's: Shekem, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Shechem.\n\nCognate Group: H7929 (shoulder blade), H7925 (early), H7927 (Shechem), H7930 (Shichemites), H7926 (back), H7928 (Shechem)\nGreek Equivalents: G4966 Συχέμ",
    7928: "שֶׁכֶם (Shekem | sheh'-kem)\n\nDerivation: for H7926 שְׁכֶם\nStrong's: Shekem, the name of a Hivite and two Israelites\nKJV: Shechem.\n\nCognate Group: H7929 (shoulder blade), H7925 (early), H7927 (Shechem), H7930 (Shichemites), H7926 (back), H7928 (Shechem)",
    7929: "שִׁכְמָה (shikmâh | shik-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7926 שְׁכֶם\nStrong's: the shoulderbone\nKJV: shoulder blade.\n\nCognate Group: H7929 (shoulder blade), H7925 (early), H7927 (Shechem), H7930 (Shichemites), H7926 (back), H7928 (Shechem)\nGreek Equivalents: G2807 κλείς",
    7930: "שִׁכְמִי (Shikmîy | shik-mee')\n\nDerivation: patronymic from H7928 שֶׁכֶם\nStrong's: a Shikmite (collectively), or descendants of Shekem\nKJV: Shichemites.\n\nCognate Group: H7929 (shoulder blade), H7925 (early), H7927 (Shechem), H7930 (Shichemites), H7926 (back), H7928 (Shechem)",
    7931: "שָׁכַן (shâkan | shaw-kan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (apparently akin (by transmission) to H7901 שָׁכַב through the idea of lodging; compare H5531 סִכְלוּת, H7925 שָׁכַם)\nStrong's: to reside or permanently stay (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: abide, continue, (cause to, make to) dwell(-er), have habitation, inhabit, lay, place, (cause to) remain, rest, set (up).\n\nCognate Group: H7931 (abide), H4908 (dwelleth), H7933 (habitation), H7935 (Shecaniah), H7934 (inhabitant)\nGreek Equivalents: G373 ἀναπαύω, G373 ἀναπαύω, G835 αὐλίζομαι, G1525 εἰσέρχομαι, G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G1940 ἐπικαθίζω, G1941 ἐπικαλέομαι, G1982 ἐπισκιάζω, G2240 ἥκω, G2270 ἡσυχάζω, G2476 ἵστημι, G2516 καθέζομαι, G2597 καταβαίνω, G2647 καταλύω, G2664 καταπαύω, G2681 κατασκηνόω, G2730 κατοικέω, G2730 κατοικέω, G2936 κτίζω, G3611 οἰκέω, G3708 ὁράω, G3939 παροικέω, G4078 πήγνυμι, G4637 σκηνόω",
    7932: "שְׁכַן (shᵉkan | shek-an')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7931 שָׁכַן \nStrong's: to reside or permanently stay (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: cause to dwell, have habitation.\n\nCognate Group: H4907 (habitation), H7932 (cause to dwell)",
    7933: "שֶׁכֶן (sheken | sheh'-ken)\n\nDerivation: from H7931 שָׁכַן\nStrong's: a residence\nKJV: habitation.\n\nCognate Group: H7931 (abide), H4908 (dwelleth), H7933 (habitation), H7935 (Shecaniah), H7934 (inhabitant)",
    7934: "שָׁכֵן (shâkên | shaw-kane')\n\nDerivation: from H7931 שָׁכַן\nStrong's: a resident; by extension, a fellow-citizen\nKJV: inhabitant, neighbour, nigh.\n\nCognate Group: H7931 (abide), H4908 (dwelleth), H7933 (habitation), H7935 (Shecaniah), H7934 (inhabitant)\nGreek Equivalents: G1069 γείτων, G1069 γείτων, G3941 πάροικος, G4040 περίοικος",
    7935: "שְׁכַנְיָה (Shᵉkanyâh | shek-an-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or (prolonged) שְׁכַנְיָהוּ; from H7931 שָׁכַן and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has dwelt\nStrong's: Shekanjah, the name of nine Israelites\nKJV: Shecaniah, Shechaniah.\n\nCognate Group: H7931 (abide), H4908 (dwelleth), H7933 (habitation), H7935 (Shecaniah), H7934 (inhabitant)",
    7936: "שָׂכַר (sâkar | saw-kar')\n\nDerivation: or (by permutation) סָכַר; (Ezra 4:5), a primitive root (apparently akin (by prosthesis) to H3739 כָּרָה through the idea of temporary purchase; compare H7937 שָׁכַר)\nStrong's: to hire\nKJV: earn wages, hire (out self), reward, [idiom] surely.\n\nCognate Group: H7936 (earn wages)",
    7937: "שָׁכַר (shâkar | shaw-kar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to become tipsy; in a qualified sense, to satiate with astimulating drink or (figuratively) influence\nKJV: (be filled with) drink (abundantly), (be, make) drunk(-en), be merry. (Superlative of H8248 שָׁקָה .)\n\nCognate Group: H7941 (strong drink), H7910 (drunk), H7943 (drunken), H7942 (Shicron), H7937 (drink)\nGreek Equivalents: G3178 μέθη, G3182 μεθύσκω, G3182 μεθύσκω, G3184 μεθύω",
    7938: "שֶׂכֶר (seker | seh'-ker)\n\nDerivation: from H7936 שָׂכַר\nStrong's: wages\nKJV: reward, sluices.\n\nCognate Group: H7958 (quails), H7938 (reward), H8073 (Shalmai), H8009 (Salmon), H7940 (Sacar), H7917 (that is hired), H4909 (reward), H8012 (Salmon), H8007 (Salma), H7939 (hire), H7936 (earn wages), H8014 (Shalmai), H7916 (hired)",
    7939: "שָׂכָר (sâkâr | saw-kawr')\n\nDerivation: from H7936 שָׂכַר\nStrong's: payment of contract; concretely, salary, fare, maintenance; by implication, compensation, benefit\nKJV: hire, price, reward(-ed), wages, worth.\n\nCognate Group: H7958 (quails), H7938 (reward), H8073 (Shalmai), H8009 (Salmon), H7940 (Sacar), H7917 (that is hired), H4909 (reward), H8012 (Salmon), H8007 (Salma), H7939 (hire), H7936 (earn wages), H8014 (Shalmai), H7916 (hired)\nGreek Equivalents: G1943 ἐπικαλύπτω, G3408 μισθός, G3408 μισθός, G3409 μισθόω, G3409 μισθόω, G4863 συνάγω, G4863 συνάγω",
    7940: "שָׂכָר (Sâkâr | saw-kar')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7939 שָׂכָר ; recompense\nStrong's: Sakar, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Sacar.\n\nCognate Group: H7958 (quails), H7938 (reward), H8073 (Shalmai), H8009 (Salmon), H7940 (Sacar), H7917 (that is hired), H4909 (reward), H8012 (Salmon), H8007 (Salma), H7939 (hire), H7936 (earn wages), H8014 (Shalmai), H7916 (hired)",
    7941: "שֵׁכָר (shêkâr | shay-kawr')\n\nDerivation: from H7937 שָׁכַר\nStrong's: an intoxicant, i.e. intensely alcoholic liquor\nKJV: strong drink, [phrase] drunkard, strong wine.\n\nCognate Group: H7941 (strong drink), H7910 (drunk), H7943 (drunken), H7942 (Shicron), H7937 (drink)\nGreek Equivalents: G3178 μέθη, G3631 οἶνος, G4608 σίκερα, G4965 Συχάρ",
    7942: "שִׁכְּרֹון (Shikkᵉrôwn | shik-ker-one')\n\nDerivation: for H7943 שִׁכָּרֹון\nStrong's: drunkenness, Shikkeron, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Shicron.\n\nCognate Group: H7941 (strong drink), H7910 (drunk), H7943 (drunken), H7942 (Shicron), H7937 (drink)",
    7943: "שִׁכָּרֹון (shikkârôwn | shik-kaw-rone')\n\nDerivation: from H7937 שָׁכַר\nStrong's: intoxication\nKJV: (be) drunken(-ness).\n\nCognate Group: H7941 (strong drink), H7910 (drunk), H7943 (drunken), H7942 (Shicron), H7937 (drink)",
    7944: "שַׁל (shal | shal)\n\nDerivation: from H7952 שָׁלָה abbreviated form\nStrong's: a fault\nKJV: error.\n\nCognate Group: H814 (gift), H7946 (being at ease), H7944 (error)",
    7945: "שֶׁל (shel | shel)\n\nDerivation: for the rel. H834 אֲשֶׁר ; used with prepositional prefix, and often followed by some pronominal affix\nStrong's: on account of, whatsoever, whichsoever\nKJV: cause, sake.\n\nCognate Group: H7945 (cause)",
    7946: "שַׁלְאֲנָן (shalʼănân | shal-an-awn')\n\nDerivation: for H7600 שַׁאֲנָן\nStrong's: tranquil\nKJV: being at ease.\n\nCognate Group: H814 (gift), H7946 (being at ease), H7944 (error)",
    7947: "שָׁלַב (shâlab | shaw-lab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to space off; intensive (evenly) to make equidistant\nKJV: equally distant, set in order.\n\nCognate Group: H7948 (ledge), H7947 (equally distant)\nGreek Equivalents: G496 ἀντιπίπτω",
    7948: "שָׁלָב (shâlâb | shaw-lawb')\n\nDerivation: from H7947 שָׁלַב\nStrong's: a spacer or raised interval, i.e. the stile in aframe or panel\nKJV: ledge.\n\nCognate Group: H7948 (ledge), H7947 (equally distant)",
    7949: "שָׁלַג (shâlag | shaw-lag')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; properly, meaning to be white; used only as denominative from H7950 שֶׁלֶג\nStrong's: to be snow-white (with the linen clothing of the slain)\nKJV: be as snow.\n\nCognate Group: H7950 (snow), H7949 (be as snow)",
    7950: "שֶׁלֶג (sheleg | sheh'-leg)\n\nDerivation: from H7949 שָׁלַג\nStrong's: snow (probably from its whiteness)\nKJV: snow(-y).\n\nCognate Group: H7950 (snow), H7949 (be as snow)\nGreek Equivalents: G5510 χιών",
    7951: "שָׁלָה (shâlâh | shaw-law')\n\nDerivation: or שָׁלַו; (Job 3:26), a primitive root\nStrong's: to be tranquil, i.e. secure or successful\nKJV: be happy, prosper, be in safety.\n\nCognate Group: H7956 (Shelah), H7952 (deceive), H7959 (prosperity), H8024 (Shelanites), H7961 (at ease), H7962 (abundance), H7987 (quietly), H7951 (be happy)",
    7952: "שָׁלָה (shâlâh | shaw-law')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (probably identical with H7953 שָׁלָה through the idea of educing)\nStrong's: to mislead\nKJV: deceive, be negligent.\n\nCognate Group: H7956 (Shelah), H7952 (deceive), H7959 (prosperity), H8024 (Shelanites), H7961 (at ease), H7962 (abundance), H7987 (quietly), H7951 (be happy)",
    7953: "שָׁלָה (shâlâh | shaw-law')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (rather cognate (by contraction) to the base of H5394 נָשַׁל, H7997 שָׁלַל and their congeners through the idea of extracting)\nStrong's: to draw out or off, i.e. remove (the soul by death)\nKJV: take away.\n\nCognate Group: H8023 (Shiloni), H7988 (young one), H7887 (Shiloh), H7953 (take away), H7888 (Shilonite)\nGreek Equivalents: G1257 διαλείπω, G4105 πλανάω",
    7954: "שְׁלָה (shᵉlâh | shel-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7951 שָׁלָה\nStrong's: to be secure\nKJV: at rest.\n\nCognate Group: H7963 (tranquillity), H7960 (error), H7954 (at rest), H7955 (thing amiss)\nGreek Equivalents: G1514 εἰρηνεύω",
    7955: "שָׁלָה (shâlâh | shaw-law')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H7952 שָׁלָה\nStrong's: a wrong\nKJV: thing amiss.\n\nCognate Group: H7963 (tranquillity), H7960 (error), H7954 (at rest), H7955 (thing amiss)\nGreek Equivalents: G988 βλασφημία",
    7956: "שֵׁלָה (Shêlâh | shay-law')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7596 שְׁאֵלָה (shortened); request\nStrong's: Shelah, the name of a postdiluvian patriarch and of an Israelite\nKJV: Shelah.\n\nCognate Group: H7956 (Shelah), H7952 (deceive), H7959 (prosperity), H8024 (Shelanites), H7961 (at ease), H7962 (abundance), H7987 (quietly), H7951 (be happy)",
    7957: "שַׁלְהֶבֶת (shalhebeth | shal-heh'-beth)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3851 לַהַב with sibilant prefix\nStrong's: a flare of fire\nKJV: (flaming) flame.\n\nCognate Group: H3852 (flame), H3851 (blade), H7957 (flame), H3827 (flame), H3853 (Lehabim)\nGreek Equivalents: G5395 φλόξ",
    7958: "שְׂלָו (sᵉlâv | sel-awv')\n\nDerivation: or שְׂלָיו; by orthographical variation from H7951 שָׁלָה through the idea of sluggishness\nStrong's: the quail collectively (as slow in flight from its weight)\nKJV: quails.\n\nCognate Group: H7958 (quails), H7938 (reward), H8073 (Shalmai), H8009 (Salmon), H7940 (Sacar), H7917 (that is hired), H4909 (reward), H8012 (Salmon), H8007 (Salma), H7939 (hire), H7936 (earn wages), H8014 (Shalmai), H7916 (hired)",
    7959: "שֶׁלֶו (shelev | sheh'-lev)\n\nDerivation: from H7951 שָׁלָה\nStrong's: security\nKJV: prosperity.\n\nCognate Group: H7956 (Shelah), H7952 (deceive), H7959 (prosperity), H8024 (Shelanites), H7961 (at ease), H7962 (abundance), H7987 (quietly), H7951 (be happy)",
    7960: "שָׁלוּ (shâlûw | shaw-loo')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or שָׁלוּת; (Aramaic), from the same as H7955 שָׁלָה\nStrong's: a fault\nKJV: error, [idiom] fail, thing amiss.\n\nCognate Group: H7963 (tranquillity), H7960 (error), H7954 (at rest), H7955 (thing amiss)\nGreek Equivalents: G425 ἄνεσις, G3900 παράπτωμα",
    7961: "שָׁלֵו (shâlêv | shaw-lave')\n\nDerivation: or שָׁלֵיו; feminine שְׁלֵוָה; from H7951 שָׁלָה\nStrong's: tranquil; (in a bad sense) careless; abstractly, security\nKJV: (being) at ease, peaceable, (in) prosper(-ity), quiet(-ness), wealthy.\n\nCognate Group: H7956 (Shelah), H7952 (deceive), H7959 (prosperity), H8024 (Shelanites), H7961 (at ease), H7962 (abundance), H7987 (quietly), H7951 (be happy)\nGreek Equivalents: G1514 εἰρηνεύω, G2271 ἡσυχία, G4991 σωτηρία",
    7962: "שַׁלְוָה (shalvâh | shal-vaw')\n\nDerivation: from H7951 שָׁלָה\nStrong's: security (genuine or false)\nKJV: abundance, peace(-ably), prosperity, quietness.\n\nCognate Group: H7956 (Shelah), H7952 (deceive), H7959 (prosperity), H8024 (Shelanites), H7961 (at ease), H7962 (abundance), H7987 (quietly), H7951 (be happy)\nGreek Equivalents: G1515 εἰρήνη, G1819 ἐξάπινα",
    7963: "שְׁלֵוָה (shᵉlêvâh | shel-ay-vaw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7962 שַׁלְוָה\nStrong's: safety\nKJV: tranquillity. See also H7961 שָׁלֵו .\n\nCognate Group: H7963 (tranquillity), H7960 (error), H7954 (at rest), H7955 (thing amiss)",
    7964: "שִׁלּוּחַ (shillûwach | shil-loo'-akh)\n\nDerivation: or שִׁלֻּחַ; from H7971 שָׁלַח\nStrong's: (only in plural) a dismissal, i.e. (of a wife) divorce (especially the document); also (of a daughter) dower\nKJV: presents, have sent back.\n\nCognate Group: H7964 (presents), H7975 (Shiloah), H7976 (branch), H7973 (dart), H7971 ([idiom] any wise), H7977 (Shilhi), H4916 (to lay), H7978 (Shilhim), H7974 (Salah), H4917 (discharge)",
    7965: "שָׁלֹום (shâlôwm | shaw-lome')\n\nDerivation: or שָׁלֹם; from H7999 שָׁלַם\nStrong's: safe, i.e. (figuratively) well, happy, friendly; also (abstractly) welfare, i.e. health, prosperity, peace\nKJV: [idiom] do, familiar, [idiom] fare, favour, [phrase] friend, [idiom] great, (good) health, ([idiom] perfect, such as be at) peace(-able, -ably), prosper(-ity, -ous), rest, safe(-ty), salute, welfare, ([idiom] all is, be) well, [idiom] wholly.\n\nCognate Group: H8013 (Shelomith), H8015 (Shelomi), H8011 (recompense), H8006 (Shillem), H8016 (Shillemites), H7966 (recompense), H4918 (Meshullam), H4920 (Meshelemiah), H8022 (Shalmaneser), H8019 (Shelomith), H8003 (full), H7968 (Shallum), H8004 (Salem), H4919 (Meshillemoth), H7967 (Shallum), H7999 (make amends), H7965 ([idiom] do), H8005 (recompense), H4921 (Meshillemith), H4922 (Meshullemeth), H8010 (Solomon), H8020 (Shalman), H8002 (peace offering), H3073 (Jehovah-shalom), H8021 (reward), H8017 (Shelumiel), H8018 (Shelemiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G1515 εἰρήνη, G1516 εἰρηνικός, G2192 ἔχω, G2436 ἵλεως, G3741 ὅσιος, G4539 Σαλώμη, G4991 σωτηρία, G5198 ὑγιαίνω, G5199 ὑγιής, G5384 φίλος, G5463 χαίρω",
    7966: "שִׁלּוּם (shillûwm | shil-loom')\n\nDerivation: or שִׁלֻּם; from H7999 שָׁלַם\nStrong's: a requital, i.e. (secure) retribution, (venal) a fee\nKJV: recompense, reward.\n\nCognate Group: H8013 (Shelomith), H8015 (Shelomi), H8011 (recompense), H8006 (Shillem), H8016 (Shillemites), H7966 (recompense), H4918 (Meshullam), H4920 (Meshelemiah), H8022 (Shalmaneser), H8019 (Shelomith), H8003 (full), H7968 (Shallum), H8004 (Salem), H4919 (Meshillemoth), H7967 (Shallum), H7999 (make amends), H7965 ([idiom] do), H8005 (recompense), H4921 (Meshillemith), H4922 (Meshullemeth), H8010 (Solomon), H8020 (Shalman), H8002 (peace offering), H3073 (Jehovah-shalom), H8021 (reward), H8017 (Shelumiel), H8018 (Shelemiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G469 ἀνταπόδοσις",
    7967: "שַׁלּוּם (Shallûwm | shal-loom')\n\nDerivation: or (shorter) שַׁלֻּם; the same as H7966 שִׁלּוּם\nStrong's: Shallum, the name of fourteen Israelites\nKJV: Shallum.\n\nCognate Group: H8013 (Shelomith), H8015 (Shelomi), H8011 (recompense), H8006 (Shillem), H8016 (Shillemites), H7966 (recompense), H4918 (Meshullam), H4920 (Meshelemiah), H8022 (Shalmaneser), H8019 (Shelomith), H8003 (full), H7968 (Shallum), H8004 (Salem), H4919 (Meshillemoth), H7967 (Shallum), H7999 (make amends), H7965 ([idiom] do), H8005 (recompense), H4921 (Meshillemith), H4922 (Meshullemeth), H8010 (Solomon), H8020 (Shalman), H8002 (peace offering), H3073 (Jehovah-shalom), H8021 (reward), H8017 (Shelumiel), H8018 (Shelemiah)",
    7968: "שַׁלּוּן (Shallûwn | shal-loon')\n\nDerivation: probably for H7967 שַׁלּוּם\nStrong's: Shallun, an Israelite\nKJV: Shallum.\n\nCognate Group: H8013 (Shelomith), H8015 (Shelomi), H8011 (recompense), H8006 (Shillem), H8016 (Shillemites), H7966 (recompense), H4918 (Meshullam), H4920 (Meshelemiah), H8022 (Shalmaneser), H8019 (Shelomith), H8003 (full), H7968 (Shallum), H8004 (Salem), H4919 (Meshillemoth), H7967 (Shallum), H7999 (make amends), H7965 ([idiom] do), H8005 (recompense), H4921 (Meshillemith), H4922 (Meshullemeth), H8010 (Solomon), H8020 (Shalman), H8002 (peace offering), H3073 (Jehovah-shalom), H8021 (reward), H8017 (Shelumiel), H8018 (Shelemiah)",
    7969: "שָׁלֹושׁ (shâlôwsh | shaw-loshe')\n\nDerivation: or שָׁלֹשׁ; masculine שְׁלֹושָׁה; or שְׁלֹשָׁה; a primitive number\nStrong's: three; occasionally (ordinal) third, or (multiple) thrice\nKJV: [phrase] fork, [phrase] often(-times), third, thir(-teen, -teenth), three, [phrase] thrice. Compare H7991 שָׁלִישׁ .\n\nCognate Group: H8027 (do the third time), H8030 (Shilshah), H8028 (Shelesh), H7969 (fork), H7991 (captain), H8032 (before), H8031 (Shalisha), H7970 (thirty), H8029 (third), H7992 (third), H7597 (Shalthiel)",
    7970: "שְׁלֹושִׁים (shᵉlôwshîym | shel-o-sheem')\n\nDerivation: or שְׁלֹשִׁים; multiple of H7969 שָׁלֹושׁ\nStrong's: thirty; or (ordinal) thirtieth\nKJV: thirty, thirtieth. Compare H7991 שָׁלִישׁ .\n\nCognate Group: H8027 (do the third time), H8030 (Shilshah), H8028 (Shelesh), H7969 (fork), H7991 (captain), H8032 (before), H8031 (Shalisha), H7970 (thirty), H8029 (third), H7992 (third), H7597 (Shalthiel)",
    7971: "שָׁלַח (shâlach | shaw-lakh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to send away, for, or out (in a great variety of applications)\nKJV: [idiom] any wise, appoint, bring (on the way), cast (away, out), conduct, [idiom] earnestly, forsake, give (up), grow long, lay, leave, let depart (down, go, loose), push away, put (away, forth, in, out), reach forth, send (away, forth, out), set, shoot (forth, out), sow, spread, stretch forth (out).\n\nCognate Group: H7964 (presents), H7975 (Shiloah), H7976 (branch), H7973 (dart), H7971 ([idiom] any wise), H7977 (Shilhi), H4916 (to lay), H7978 (Shilhim), H7974 (Salah), H4917 (discharge)\nGreek Equivalents: G447 ἀνίημι, G518 ἀπαγγέλλω, G556 ἀπελαύνω, G615 ἀποκτείνω, G641 ἀποῤῥίπτω, G649 ἀποστέλλω, G651 ἀποστολή, G652 ἀπόστολος, G680 ἅπτομαι, G681 ἅπτω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G863 ἀφίημι, G906 βάλλω, G1283 διαρπάζω, G1544 ἐκβάλλω, G1599 ἐκπέμπω, G1614 ἐκτείνω, G1614 ἐκτείνω, G1627 ἐκφέρω, G1685 ἐμβάλλω, G1806 ἐξάγω, G1821 ἐξαποστέλλω, G1863 ἐπάγω, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G1989 ἐπιστέλλω, G1994 ἐπιστρέφω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2018 ἐπιφέρω, G3992 πέμπω, G4105 πλανάω, G4121 πλεονάζω, G4261 προβάλλω, G4400 προχειρίζομαι, G4527 Σαλά, G4882 συναποστέλλω, G4921 συνιστάω, G5342 φέρω, G5465 χαλάω",
    7972: "שְׁלַח (shᵉlach | shel-akh')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7971 שָׁלַח \nStrong's: to send away, for, or out (in a great variety of applications)\nKJV: put, send.\n\nCognate Group: H7972 (put)",
    7973: "שֶׁלַח (shelach | sheh'-lakh)\n\nDerivation: from H7971 שָׁלַח\nStrong's: a missile of attack, i.e. spear; also (figuratively) a shoot of growth; i.e. branch\nKJV: dart, plant, [idiom] put off, sword, weapon.\n\nCognate Group: H7964 (presents), H7975 (Shiloah), H7976 (branch), H7973 (dart), H7971 ([idiom] any wise), H7977 (Shilhi), H4916 (to lay), H7978 (Shilhim), H7974 (Salah), H4917 (discharge)\nGreek Equivalents: G956 βέλος, G1002 βολίς, G3696 ὅπλον, G4171 πόλεμος",
    7974: "שֶׁלַח (Shelach | sheh'-lakh)\n\nDerivation: the same as H7973 שֶׁלַח\nStrong's: Shelach, a postdiluvian patriarch\nKJV: Salah, Shelah. Compare H7975 שִׁלֹחַ \n\nTypo: lemma שִׁלֹּחַ extra dagesh, corrected to שִׁלֹחַ\n\n.\n\nCognate Group: H7964 (presents), H7975 (Shiloah), H7976 (branch), H7973 (dart), H7971 ([idiom] any wise), H7977 (Shilhi), H4916 (to lay), H7978 (Shilhim), H7974 (Salah), H4917 (discharge)\nGreek Equivalents: G4527 Σαλά",
    7975: "שִׁלֹחַ (Shilôach | shee-lo'-akh)\n\nTypo: lemma שִׁלֹּחַ extra dagesh, corrected to שִׁלֹחַ\n\nGreek Equivalents: G4611 Σιλωάμ \n\nDerivation: or (in imitation of H7974 שֶׁלַח) שֶׁלַח; (Nehemiah 3:15), from H7971 שָׁלַח ; rill\nStrong's: Shiloach, a fountain of Jerusalem\nKJV: Shiloah, Siloah.\n\nCognate Group: H7964 (presents), H7975 (Shiloah), H7976 (branch), H7973 (dart), H7971 ([idiom] any wise), H7977 (Shilhi), H4916 (to lay), H7978 (Shilhim), H7974 (Salah), H4917 (discharge)",
    7976: "שִׁלֻּחָה (shilluchâh | shil-loo-khaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H7964 שִׁלּוּחַ\nStrong's: a shoot\nKJV: branch.\n\nCognate Group: H7964 (presents), H7975 (Shiloah), H7976 (branch), H7973 (dart), H7971 ([idiom] any wise), H7977 (Shilhi), H4916 (to lay), H7978 (Shilhim), H7974 (Salah), H4917 (discharge)",
    7977: "שִׁלְחִי (Shilchîy | shil-khee')\n\nDerivation: from H7973 שֶׁלַח ; missive, i.e. armed\nStrong's: Shilchi, an Israelite\nKJV: Shilhi.\n\nCognate Group: H7964 (presents), H7975 (Shiloah), H7976 (branch), H7973 (dart), H7971 ([idiom] any wise), H7977 (Shilhi), H4916 (to lay), H7978 (Shilhim), H7974 (Salah), H4917 (discharge)",
    7978: "שִׁלְחִים (Shilchîym | shil-kheem')\n\nDerivation: plural of H7973 שֶׁלַח ; javelins or sprouts\nStrong's: Shilchim, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Shilhim.\n\nCognate Group: H7964 (presents), H7975 (Shiloah), H7976 (branch), H7973 (dart), H7971 ([idiom] any wise), H7977 (Shilhi), H4916 (to lay), H7978 (Shilhim), H7974 (Salah), H4917 (discharge)",
    7979: "שֻׁלְחָן (shulchân | shool-khawn')\n\nDerivation: from H7971 שָׁלַח\nStrong's: a table (as spread out); by implication, a meal\nKJV: table.\n\nCognate Group: H7979 (table)\nGreek Equivalents: G5132 τράπεζα",
    7980: "שָׁלַט (shâlaṭ | shaw-lat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to dominate, i.e. govern; by implication, to permit\nKJV: (bear, have) rule, have dominion, give (have) power.\n\nCognate Group: H7989 (governor), H7983 (power), H7980 (rule), H7986 (imperious)\nGreek Equivalents: G1850 ἐξουσιάζω, G2634 κατακυριεύω, G2962 κύριος",
    7981: "שְׁלֵט (shᵉlêṭ | shel-ate')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7980 שָׁלַט \nStrong's: to dominate, i.e. govern; by implication, to permit\nKJV: have the mastery, have power, bear rule, be (make) ruler.\n\nCognate Group: H7984 (ruler), H7981 (have the mastery), H7985 (dominion), H7990 (captain)\nGreek Equivalents: G584 ἀποδείκνυμι, G680 ἅπτομαι, G681 ἅπτω, G757 ἄρχω, G2525 καθίστημι, G2961 κυριεύω",
    7982: "שֶׁלֶט (sheleṭ | sheh'-let)\n\nDerivation: from H7980 שָׁלַט\nStrong's: probably a shield (as controlling, i.e. protecting the person)\nKJV: shield.\n\nCognate Group: H7982 (shield)\nGreek Equivalents: G1002 βολίς, G1849 ἐξουσία, G3696 ὅπλον",
    7983: "שִׁלְטֹון (shilṭôwn | shil-tone')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H7980 שָׁלַט\nStrong's: power.\nKJV: power.\n\nCognate Group: H7989 (governor), H7983 (power), H7980 (rule), H7986 (imperious)",
    7984: "שִׁלְטֹון (shilṭôwn | shil-tone')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or שִׁלְטֹן\n\nTypo: lemma שִׁלְטן missing vowel, corrected to שִׁלְטֹן\n\n; corresponding to H7983 שִׁלְטֹון \nStrong's: a potentate\nKJV: ruler.\n\nCognate Group: H7984 (ruler), H7981 (have the mastery), H7985 (dominion), H7990 (captain)\nGreek Equivalents: G758 ἄρχων",
    7985: "שׇׁלְטָן (sholṭân | shol-tawn')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H7981 שְׁלֵט\nStrong's: empire (abstractly or concretely)\nKJV: dominion.\n\nCognate Group: H7984 (ruler), H7981 (have the mastery), H7985 (dominion), H7990 (captain)\nGreek Equivalents: G746 ἀρχή, G932 βασιλεία, G1849 ἐξουσία",
    7986: "שַׁלֶּטֶת (shalleṭeth | shal-leh'-teth)\n\nDerivation: feminine from H7980 שָׁלַט\nStrong's: a vixen\nKJV: imperious.\n\nCognate Group: H7989 (governor), H7983 (power), H7980 (rule), H7986 (imperious)",
    7987: "שְׁלִי (shᵉlîy | shel-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H7951 שָׁלָה\nStrong's: privacy\nKJV: [phrase] quietly.\n\nCognate Group: H7956 (Shelah), H7952 (deceive), H7959 (prosperity), H8024 (Shelanites), H7961 (at ease), H7962 (abundance), H7987 (quietly), H7951 (be happy)\nGreek Equivalents: G1748 ἐνεδρεύω",
    7988: "שִׁלְיָה (shilyâh | shil-yaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine from H7953 שָׁלָה\nStrong's: a fetus or babe (as extruded in birth)\nKJV: young one.\n\nCognate Group: H8023 (Shiloni), H7988 (young one), H7887 (Shiloh), H7953 (take away), H7888 (Shilonite)",
    7989: "שַׁלִּיט (shallîyṭ | shal-leet')\n\nDerivation: from H7980 שָׁלַט\nStrong's: potent; concretely, a prince or warrior\nKJV: governor, mighty, that hath power, ruler.\n\nCognate Group: H7989 (governor), H7983 (power), H7980 (rule), H7986 (imperious)\nGreek Equivalents: G1413 δυνάστης, G1849 ἐξουσία, G2962 κύριος",
    7990: "שַׁלִּיט (shallîyṭ | shal-leet')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7989 שַׁלִּיט\nStrong's: mighty; abstractly, permission; concretely, a premier\nKJV: captain, be lawful, rule(-r).\n\nCognate Group: H7984 (ruler), H7981 (have the mastery), H7985 (dominion), H7990 (captain)",
    7991: "שָׁלִישׁ (shâlîysh | shaw-leesh')\n\nDerivation: or שָׁלֹושׁ; (1 Chronicles 11:11; 1 Chronicles 12:18), or שָׁלֹשׁ; (2 Samuel 23:13), from H7969 שָׁלֹושׁ\nStrong's: a triple, i.e. (as a musical instrument) a triangle (or perhaps rather threestringed lute); also (as an indefinite, great quantity) a three-fold measure (perhaps a treble ephah); also (as an officer) a general of the third rank (upward, i.e. the highest)\nKJV: captain, instrument of musick, (great) lord, (great) measure, prince, three (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H8027 (do the third time), H8030 (Shilshah), H8028 (Shelesh), H7969 (fork), H7991 (captain), H8032 (before), H8031 (Shalisha), H7970 (thirty), H8029 (third), H7992 (third), H7597 (Shalthiel)\nGreek Equivalents: G1415 δυνατός, G2950 κύμβαλον, G3358 μέτρον",
    7992: "שְׁלִישִׁי (shᵉlîyshîy | shel-ee-shee')\n\nDerivation: ordinal from H7969 שָׁלֹושׁ\nStrong's: third; feminine athird (part); by extension, a third (day, year or time); specifically, a third-story cell)\nKJV: third (part, rank, time), three (years old).\n\nCognate Group: H8027 (do the third time), H8030 (Shilshah), H8028 (Shelesh), H7969 (fork), H7991 (captain), H8032 (before), H8031 (Shalisha), H7970 (thirty), H8029 (third), H7992 (third), H7597 (Shalthiel)",
    7993: "שָׁלַךְ (shâlak | shaw-lak)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to throw out, down or away (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: adventure, cast (away, down, forth, off, out), hurl, pluck, throw.\n\nCognate Group: H7993 (adventure), H7996 (Shalleketh), H7995 (when cast), H7994 (cormorant)\nGreek Equivalents: G641 ἀποῤῥίπτω, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G906 βάλλω, G1544 ἐκβάλλω, G1601 ἐκπίπτω, G1614 ἐκτείνω, G1627 ἐκφέρω, G1685 ἐμβάλλω, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G1977 ἐπιῤῥίπτω, G2049 ἐρημόω, G2524 καθίημι, G2630 κατακρημνίζω, G2698 κατατίθημι, G4496 ῥίπτω, G4682 σπαράσσω",
    7994: "שָׁלָךְ (shâlâk | shaw-lawk')\n\nDerivation: from H7993 שָׁלַךְ\nStrong's: bird of prey, usually thought to be the pelican (from casting itself into the sea)\nKJV: cormorant.\n\nCognate Group: H7993 (adventure), H7996 (Shalleketh), H7995 (when cast), H7994 (cormorant)",
    7995: "שַׁלֶּכֶת (shalleketh | shal-leh'-keth)\n\nDerivation: from H7993 שָׁלַךְ\nStrong's: a felling (of trees)\nKJV: when cast.\n\nCognate Group: H7993 (adventure), H7996 (Shalleketh), H7995 (when cast), H7994 (cormorant)",
    7996: "שַׁלֶּכֶת (Shalleketh | shal-leh'-keth)\n\nDerivation: the same as H7995 שַׁלֶּכֶת\nStrong's: Shalleketh, a gate in Jerusalem\nKJV: Shalleketh.\n\nCognate Group: H7993 (adventure), H7996 (Shalleketh), H7995 (when cast), H7994 (cormorant)",
    7997: "שָׁלַל (shâlal | shaw-lal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to drop or strip; by implication, to plunder\nKJV: let fall, make self a prey, [idiom] of purpose, (make a, (take)) spoil.\n\nCognate Group: H7758 (spoiled), H7997 (let fall)\nGreek Equivalents: G3846 παραβάλλω, G4160 ποιέω, G5015 ταράσσω",
    7998: "שָׁלָל (shâlâl | shaw-lawl')\n\nDerivation: from H7997 שָׁלַל\nStrong's: booty\nKJV: prey, spoil.\n\nCognate Group: H7998 (prey), H7997 (let fall)\nGreek Equivalents: G684 ἀπώλεια, G724 ἁρπαγή, G4661 σκῦλον",
