    8021: "שַׁלְמֹן (shalmôn | shal-mone')\n\nDerivation: from H7999 שָׁלַם\nStrong's: a bribe\nKJV: reward.\n\nCognate Group: H8013 (Shelomith), H8015 (Shelomi), H8011 (recompense), H8006 (Shillem), H8016 (Shillemites), H7966 (recompense), H4918 (Meshullam), H4920 (Meshelemiah), H8022 (Shalmaneser), H8019 (Shelomith), H8003 (full), H7968 (Shallum), H8004 (Salem), H4919 (Meshillemoth), H7967 (Shallum), H7999 (make amends), H7965 ([idiom] do), H8005 (recompense), H4921 (Meshillemith), H4922 (Meshullemeth), H8010 (Solomon), H8020 (Shalman), H8002 (peace offering), H3073 (Jehovah-shalom), H8021 (reward), H8017 (Shelumiel), H8018 (Shelemiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G468 ἀνταπόδομα",
    8022: "שַׁלְמַנְאֶסֶר (Shalmanʼeçer | shal-man-eh'-ser)\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Shalmaneser, an Assyrian king\nKJV: Shalmaneser. Comp H8020 שַׁלְמַן .\n\nCognate Group: H8013 (Shelomith), H8015 (Shelomi), H8011 (recompense), H8006 (Shillem), H8016 (Shillemites), H7966 (recompense), H4918 (Meshullam), H4920 (Meshelemiah), H8022 (Shalmaneser), H8019 (Shelomith), H8003 (full), H7968 (Shallum), H8004 (Salem), H4919 (Meshillemoth), H7967 (Shallum), H7999 (make amends), H7965 ([idiom] do), H8005 (recompense), H4921 (Meshillemith), H4922 (Meshullemeth), H8010 (Solomon), H8020 (Shalman), H8002 (peace offering), H3073 (Jehovah-shalom), H8021 (reward), H8017 (Shelumiel), H8018 (Shelemiah)",
    8023: "שִׁלֹנִי (Shilônîy | shee-lo-nee')\n\nDerivation: the same as H7888 שִׁילֹונִי\nStrong's: Shiloni, an Israelite\nKJV: Shiloni.\n\nCognate Group: H8023 (Shiloni), H7988 (young one), H7887 (Shiloh), H7953 (take away), H7888 (Shilonite)",
    8024: "שֵׁלָנִי (Shêlânîy | shay-law-nee')\n\nDerivation: from H7956 שֵׁלָה\nStrong's: a Shelanite (collectively), or descendants of Shelah\nKJV: Shelanites.\n\nCognate Group: H7956 (Shelah), H7952 (deceive), H7959 (prosperity), H8024 (Shelanites), H7961 (at ease), H7962 (abundance), H7987 (quietly), H7951 (be happy)",
    8025: "שָׁלַף (shâlaph | saw-laf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to pull out, up or off\nKJV: draw (off), grow up, pluck off.\n\nCognate Group: H8025 (draw), H8026 (Sheleph)\nGreek Equivalents: G1670 ἑλκύω, G4685 σπάω",
    8026: "שֶׁלֶף (sheleph | sheh'-lef)\n\nDerivation: from H8025 שָׁלַף ; extract\nStrong's: Sheleph, a son of Jokthan\nKJV: Sheleph.\n\nCognate Group: H8025 (draw), H8026 (Sheleph)",
    8027: "שָׁלַשׁ (shâlash | shaw-lash')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root perhaps originally to intensify, i.e. treble; but apparently used only as denominative from H7969 שָׁלֹושׁ,\nStrong's: to be (causatively, make) triplicate (by restoration, in portions, strands, days or years)\nKJV: do the third time, (divide into, stay) three (days, -fold, parts, years old).\n\nCognate Group: H8027 (do the third time), H8030 (Shilshah), H8028 (Shelesh), H7969 (fork), H7991 (captain), H8032 (before), H8031 (Shalisha), H7970 (thirty), H8029 (third), H7992 (third), H7597 (Shalthiel)",
    8028: "שֶׁלֶשׁ (Shelesh | sheh'-lesh)\n\nDerivation: from H8027 שָׁלַשׁ ; triplet\nStrong's: Shelesh, an Israelite\nKJV: Shelesh.\n\nCognate Group: H8027 (do the third time), H8030 (Shilshah), H8028 (Shelesh), H7969 (fork), H7991 (captain), H8032 (before), H8031 (Shalisha), H7970 (thirty), H8029 (third), H7992 (third), H7597 (Shalthiel)",
    8029: "שִׁלֵּשׁ (shillêsh | shil-laysh')\n\nDerivation: from H8027 שָׁלַשׁ\nStrong's: a descendant of the third degree, i.e. great grandchild\nKJV: third (generation).\n\nCognate Group: H8027 (do the third time), H8030 (Shilshah), H8028 (Shelesh), H7969 (fork), H7991 (captain), H8032 (before), H8031 (Shalisha), H7970 (thirty), H8029 (third), H7992 (third), H7597 (Shalthiel)\nGreek Equivalents: G859 ἄφεσις, G1074 γενεά",
    8030: "שִׁלְשָׁה (Shilshâh | shil-shaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine from the same as H8028 שֶׁלֶשׁ ; triplication\nStrong's: Shilshah, an Israelite\nKJV: Shilshah.\n\nCognate Group: H8027 (do the third time), H8030 (Shilshah), H8028 (Shelesh), H7969 (fork), H7991 (captain), H8032 (before), H8031 (Shalisha), H7970 (thirty), H8029 (third), H7992 (third), H7597 (Shalthiel)",
    8031: "שָׁלִשָׁה (Shâlishâh | shaw-lee-shaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine from H8027 שָׁלַשׁ ; trebled land\nStrong's: Shalishah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Shalisha.\n\nCognate Group: H8027 (do the third time), H8030 (Shilshah), H8028 (Shelesh), H7969 (fork), H7991 (captain), H8032 (before), H8031 (Shalisha), H7970 (thirty), H8029 (third), H7992 (third), H7597 (Shalthiel)",
    8032: "שִׁלְשֹׁום (shilshôwm | shil-shome')\n\nDerivation: or שִׁלְשֹׁם; from the same as H8028 שֶׁלֶשׁ\nStrong's: trebly, i.e. (in time) day before yesterday\nKJV: [phrase] before (that time, -time), excellent things (from the margin), [phrase] heretofore, three days, [phrase] time past.\n\nCognate Group: H8027 (do the third time), H8030 (Shilshah), H8028 (Shelesh), H7969 (fork), H7991 (captain), H8032 (before), H8031 (Shalisha), H7970 (thirty), H8029 (third), H7992 (third), H7597 (Shalthiel)\nGreek Equivalents: G2250 ἡμέρα",
    8033: "שָׁם (shâm | shawm)\n\nDerivation: a primitive particle (rather from the relative pronoun, H834 אֲשֶׁר)\nStrong's: there (transferring to time) then; often thither, or thence\nKJV: in it, [phrase] thence, there (-in, [phrase] of, [phrase] out), [phrase] thither, [phrase] whither.\n\nCognate Group: H8061 (Shemida), H8033 (in it), H8050 (Samuel), H8035 (Sem), H8062 (Shemidaites), H8038 (Shemeber), H8034 (base), H3074 (Jehovahshammah), H8070 (Shemiramoth)\nGreek Equivalents: G1563 ἐκεῖ, G1564 ἐκεῖθεν, G1566 ἐκεῖσε",
    8034: "שֵׁם (shêm | shame)\n\nDerivation: a primitive word (perhaps rather from through the idea of definite and conspicuous position; compare H8064 שָׁמַיִם)\nStrong's: an appellation, as amark or memorial of individuality; by implication honor, authority, character\nKJV: [phrase] base, (in-) fame(-ous), named(-d), renown, report.\n\nCognate Group: H8061 (Shemida), H8033 (in it), H8050 (Samuel), H8035 (Sem), H8062 (Shemidaites), H8038 (Shemeber), H8034 (base), H3074 (Jehovahshammah), H8070 (Shemiramoth)\nGreek Equivalents: G2362 θρόνος, G2564 καλέω, G2570 καλός, G2745 καύχημα, G3686 ὄνομα, G3686 ὄνομα, G4590 Σήμ",
    8035: "שֵׁם (Shêm | shame)\n\nDerivation: the same as H8034 שֵׁם ; name\nStrong's: Shem, a son of Noah (often includ. his posterity)\nKJV: Sem, Shem.\n\nCognate Group: H8061 (Shemida), H8033 (in it), H8050 (Samuel), H8035 (Sem), H8062 (Shemidaites), H8038 (Shemeber), H8034 (base), H3074 (Jehovahshammah), H8070 (Shemiramoth)\nGreek Equivalents: G4590 Σήμ",
    8036: "שֻׁם (shum | shoom)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8034 שֵׁם \nStrong's: an appellation, as amark or memorial of individuality; by implication honor, authority, character\nKJV: name.\n\nCognate Group: H8000 (deliver), H8036 (name), H8001 (peace)\nGreek Equivalents: G1941 ἐπικαλέομαι",
    8037: "שַׁמָּא (Shammâʼ | sham-maw')\n\nDerivation: from H8074 שָׁמֵם ; desolation\nStrong's: Shamma, an Israelite\nKJV: Shamma.\n\nCognate Group: H8037 (Shamma), H8076 (desolate), H8048 (Shammah), H8074 (make amazed), H4923 (astonishment), H8077 (desolate), H8047 (astonishment), H8060 (Shammai), H8054 (Shamoth), H8078 (astonishment)",
    8038: "שֶׁמְאֵבֶר (Shemʼêber | shem-ay'-ber)\n\nDerivation: apparently from H8034 שֵׁם and H83 אֵבֶר ; name of pinion, i.e. illustrious\nStrong's: Shemeber, a king of Zeboim\nKJV: Shemeber.\n\nCognate Group: H8061 (Shemida), H8033 (in it), H8050 (Samuel), H8035 (Sem), H8062 (Shemidaites), H8038 (Shemeber), H8034 (base), H3074 (Jehovahshammah), H8070 (Shemiramoth)",
    8039: "שִׁמְאָה (Shimʼâh | shim-aw')\n\nDerivation: perhaps for H8093 שִׁמְעָה\nStrong's: Shimah, an Israelite\nKJV: Shimah. Compare H8043 שִׁמְאָם .\n\nCognate Group: H8044 (Shamgar), H8039 (Shimah), H8043 (Shimeam)",
    8040: "שְׂמֹאול (sᵉmôʼwl | sem-ole')\n\nDerivation: or שְׂמֹאל; a primitive word (rather perhaps from the same as H8071 שִׂמְלָה (by insertion of the aleph) through the idea of wrapping up)\nStrong's: properly, dark (as enveloped), i.e. the north; hence (by orientation), the left hand\nKJV: left (hand, side).\n\nCognate Group: H8042 (left), H8041 (left), H8040 (left)\nGreek Equivalents: G710 ἀριστερός",
    8041: "שָׂמַאל (sâmaʼl | saw-mal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (denominative from H8040 שְׂמֹאול)\nStrong's: to use the left hand or pass in that direction)\nKJV: (go, turn) (on the, to the) left.\n\nCognate Group: H8042 (left), H8041 (left), H8040 (left)",
    8042: "שְׂמָאלִי (sᵉmâʼlîy | sem-aw-lee')\n\nDerivation: from H8040 שְׂמֹאול\nStrong's: situated on the left side\nKJV: left.\n\nCognate Group: H8042 (left), H8041 (left), H8040 (left)",
    8043: "שִׁמְאָם (Shimʼâm | shim-awm')\n\nDerivation: for H8039 שִׁמְאָה (compare H38 אֲבִיָּם)\nStrong's: Shimam, an Israelite\nKJV: Shimeam.\n\nCognate Group: H8044 (Shamgar), H8039 (Shimah), H8043 (Shimeam)",
    8044: "שַׁמְגַּר (Shamgar | sham-gar')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Shamgar, an Israelite judge\nKJV: Shamgar.\n\nCognate Group: H8044 (Shamgar), H8039 (Shimah), H8043 (Shimeam)",
    8045: "שָׁמַד (shâmad | shaw-mad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to desolate\nKJV: destory(-uction), bring to nought, overthrow, perish, pluck down, [idiom] utterly.\n\nCognate Group: H8045 (destory), H8126 (Shumathites)\nGreek Equivalents: G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G684 ἀπώλεια, G853 ἀφανίζω, G854 ἀφανισμός, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1825 ἐξεγείρω, G1842 ἐξολοθρεύω, G2049 ἐρημόω, G3583 ξηραίνω, G3645 ὀλοθρεύω, G4937 συντρίβω",
    8046: "שְׁמַד (shᵉmad | shem-ad')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8045 שָׁמַד \nStrong's: to desolate\nKJV: consume.\n\nCognate Group: H8065 (heaven), H8046 (consume)",
    8047: "שַׁמָּה (shammâh | sham-maw')\n\nDerivation: from H8074 שָׁמֵם\nStrong's: ruin; by implication, consternation\nKJV: astonishment, desolate(-ion), waste, wonderful thing.\n\nCognate Group: H8037 (Shamma), H8076 (desolate), H8048 (Shammah), H8074 (make amazed), H4923 (astonishment), H8077 (desolate), H8047 (astonishment), H8060 (Shammai), H8054 (Shamoth), H8078 (astonishment)\nGreek Equivalents: G135 αἴνιγμα, G854 ἀφανισμός, G1611 ἔκστασις, G5059 τέρας",
    8048: "שַׁמָּה (Shammâh | sham-maw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H8047 שַׁמָּה\nStrong's: Shammah, the name of an Edomite and four Israelites\nKJV: Shammah.\n\nCognate Group: H8037 (Shamma), H8076 (desolate), H8048 (Shammah), H8074 (make amazed), H4923 (astonishment), H8077 (desolate), H8047 (astonishment), H8060 (Shammai), H8054 (Shamoth), H8078 (astonishment)",
    8049: "שַׁמְהוּת (Shamhûwth | sham-hooth')\n\nDerivation: for H8048 שַׁמָּה ; desolation\nStrong's: Shamhuth, an Israelite\nKJV: Shamhuth.\n\nCognate Group: H8064 (air), H8049 (Shamhuth)",
    8050: "שְׁמוּאֵל (Shᵉmûwʼêl | sehm-oo-ale')\n\nDerivation: from the passive participle of H8085 שָׁמַע and H410 אֵל ; heard of God\nStrong's: Shemuel, the name of three Israelites\nKJV: Samuel, Shemuel.\n\nCognate Group: H8061 (Shemida), H8033 (in it), H8050 (Samuel), H8035 (Sem), H8062 (Shemidaites), H8038 (Shemeber), H8034 (base), H3074 (Jehovahshammah), H8070 (Shemiramoth)\nGreek Equivalents: G4545 Σαμουήλ",
    8051: "שַׁמּוּעַ (Shammûwaʻ | sham-moo'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from H8074 שָׁמֵם ; renowned\nStrong's: Shammua, the name of four Israelites\nKJV: Shammua, Shammuah.\n\nCognate Group: H8091 (Shama), H8087 (Shema), H8093 (Shimeah), H3458 (Ishmael), H2045 (to cause to hear), H3460 (Ishmaiah), H4927 (Mishma), H4928 (bidding), H4926 (hearing), H8090 (Shema), H8085 ([idiom] attentively), H8097 (of Shimi), H8094 (Shemaah), H8092 (Shimea), H8088 (bruit), H8052 (bruit), H3459 (Ishmaelite), H8095 (Simeon), H8099 (tribe of Simeon), H8051 (Shammua), H8089 (fame), H8101 (Shimeathites), H8100 (Shimath), H8098 (Shemaiah), H8096 (Shimeah)",
    8052: "שְׁמוּעָה (shᵉmûwʻâh | sehm-oo-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of H8074 שָׁמֵם\nStrong's: something heard, i.e. an announcement\nKJV: bruit, doctrine, fame, mentioned, news, report, rumor, tidings.\n\nCognate Group: H8091 (Shama), H8087 (Shema), H8093 (Shimeah), H3458 (Ishmael), H2045 (to cause to hear), H3460 (Ishmaiah), H4927 (Mishma), H4928 (bidding), H4926 (hearing), H8090 (Shema), H8085 ([idiom] attentively), H8097 (of Shimi), H8094 (Shemaah), H8092 (Shimea), H8088 (bruit), H8052 (bruit), H3459 (Ishmaelite), H8095 (Simeon), H8099 (tribe of Simeon), H8051 (Shammua), H8089 (fame), H8101 (Shimeathites), H8100 (Shimath), H8098 (Shemaiah), H8096 (Shimeah)\nGreek Equivalents: G5345 φήμη",
    8053: "שָׁמוּר (Shâmûwr | shaw-moor')\n\nDerivation: passive participle of H8103 שִׁמְצָה ; observed\nStrong's: Shamur, an Israelite\nKJV: Shamir (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H8053 (Shamir), H8069 (Shamir), H8068 (adamant)",
    8054: "שַׁמֹּות (Shammôwth | sham-moth')\n\nDerivation: plural of H8047 שַׁמָּה ; ruins\nStrong's: Shammoth, an Israelite\nKJV: Shamoth.\n\nCognate Group: H8037 (Shamma), H8076 (desolate), H8048 (Shammah), H8074 (make amazed), H4923 (astonishment), H8077 (desolate), H8047 (astonishment), H8060 (Shammai), H8054 (Shamoth), H8078 (astonishment)",
    8055: "שָׂמַח (sâmach | saw-makh')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: probably to brighten up, i.e. (figuratively) be (causatively, make) blithe or gleesome\nKJV: cheer up, be (make) glad, (have, make) joy(-ful), be (make) merry, (cause to, make to) rejoice, [idiom] very.\n\nCognate Group: H8055 (cheer up), H8056 (glad), H8057 ([idiom] exceeding), H8063 (mantle)\nGreek Equivalents: G21 ἀγαλλιάω, G1070 γελάω, G2165 εὐφραίνω, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G5463 χαίρω",
    8056: "שָׂמֵחַ (sâmêach | saw-may'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H8055 שָׂמַח\nStrong's: blithe or gleeful\nKJV: (be) glad, joyful, (making) merry((-hearted), -ily), rejoice(-ing).\n\nCognate Group: H8055 (cheer up), H8056 (glad), H8057 ([idiom] exceeding), H8063 (mantle)",
    8057: "שִׂמְחָה (simchâh | sim-khaw')\n\nDerivation: from H8056 שָׂמֵחַ\nStrong's: blithesomeness or glee, (religious or festival)\nKJV: [idiom] exceeding(-ly), gladness, joy(-fulness), mirth, pleasure, rejoice(-ing).\n\nCognate Group: H8055 (cheer up), H8056 (glad), H8057 ([idiom] exceeding), H8063 (mantle)\nGreek Equivalents: G133 αἴνεσις, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G5479 χαρά",
    8058: "שָׁמַט (shâmaṭ | shaw-mat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to fling down; incipiently to jostle; figuratively, to let alone, desist, remit\nKJV: discontinue, overthrow, release, let rest, shake, stumble, throw down.\n\nCognate Group: H8059 (release), H8058 (discontinue)\nGreek Equivalents: G859 ἄφεσις, G863 ἀφίημι, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G2666 καταπίνω, G2947 κυλιόω, G4049 περισπάω",
    8059: "שְׁמִטָּה (shᵉmiṭṭâh | shem-it-taw')\n\nDerivation: from H8058 שָׁמַט\nStrong's: remission (of debt) or suspension of labor)\nKJV: release.\n\nCognate Group: H8059 (release), H8058 (discontinue)",
    8060: "שַׁמַּי (Shammay | sham-mah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H8073 שַׁמְלַי ; destructive\nStrong's: Shammai, the name of three Israelites\nKJV: Shammai.\n\nCognate Group: H8037 (Shamma), H8076 (desolate), H8048 (Shammah), H8074 (make amazed), H4923 (astonishment), H8077 (desolate), H8047 (astonishment), H8060 (Shammai), H8054 (Shamoth), H8078 (astonishment)",
    8061: "שְׁמִידָע (Shᵉmîydâʻ | shem-ee-daw')\n\nDerivation: apparently from H8034 שֵׁם and H3045 יָדַע ; name of knowing\nStrong's: Shemida, an Israelite\nKJV: Shemida, Shemidah.\n\nCognate Group: H8061 (Shemida), H8033 (in it), H8050 (Samuel), H8035 (Sem), H8062 (Shemidaites), H8038 (Shemeber), H8034 (base), H3074 (Jehovahshammah), H8070 (Shemiramoth)",
    8062: "שְׁמִידָעִי (Shᵉmîydâʻîy | shem-ee-daw-ee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H8061 שְׁמִידָע\nStrong's: a Shemidaite (collectively) or descendants of Shemida\nKJV: Shemidaites.\n\nCognate Group: H8061 (Shemida), H8033 (in it), H8050 (Samuel), H8035 (Sem), H8062 (Shemidaites), H8038 (Shemeber), H8034 (base), H3074 (Jehovahshammah), H8070 (Shemiramoth)",
    8063: "שְׂמִיכָה (sᵉmîykâh | sem-ee-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from H5564 סָמַךְ\nStrong's: a run (as sustaining the Oriental sitter)\nKJV: mantle.\n\nCognate Group: H8055 (cheer up), H8056 (glad), H8057 ([idiom] exceeding), H8063 (mantle)",
    8064: "שָׁמַיִם (shâmayim | shaw-mah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: dual of an unused singular שָׁמֶה; from an unused root meaning to be lofty\nStrong's: the sky (as aloft; the dual perhaps alluding to the visible arch in which the clouds move, as well as to the higher ether where the celestial bodies revolve)\nKJV: air, [idiom] astrologer, heaven(-s).\n\nCognate Group: H8064 (air), H8049 (Shamhuth)\nGreek Equivalents: G798 ἄστρον, G2032 ἐπουράνιος, G2246 ἥλιος, G3770 οὐράνιος, G3772 οὐρανός",
    8065: "שָׁמַיִן (shâmayin | shaw-mah'-yin)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8064 שָׁמַיִם \nStrong's: the sky (as aloft; the dual perhaps alluding to the visible arch in which the clouds move, as well as to the higher ether where the celestial bodies revolve)\nKJV: heaven.\n\nCognate Group: H8065 (heaven), H8046 (consume)",
    8066: "שְׁמִינִי (shᵉmîynîy | shem-ee-nee')\n\nDerivation: from H8083 שְׁמֹנֶה\nStrong's: eight\nKJV: eight.\n\nCognate Group: H8067 (Sheminith), H8084 (eighty), H8066 (eight), H8083 (eight)",
    8067: "שְׁמִינִית (shᵉmîynîyth | shem-ee-neeth')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H8066 שְׁמִינִי\nStrong's: probably an eight-stringed lyre\nKJV: Sheminith.\n\nCognate Group: H8067 (Sheminith), H8084 (eighty), H8066 (eight), H8083 (eight)",
    8068: "שָׁמִיר (shâmîyr | shaw-meer')\n\nDerivation: from H8104 שָׁמַר in the original sense of pricking\nStrong's: a thorn; also (from its keenness for scratching) a gem, probably the diamond\nKJV: adamant (stone), brier, diamond.\n\nCognate Group: H8053 (Shamir), H8069 (Shamir), H8068 (adamant)\nGreek Equivalents: G5208 ὕλη",
    8069: "שָׁמִיר (Shâmîyr | shaw-meer')\n\nDerivation: the same as H8068 שָׁמִיר\nStrong's: Shamir, the name of two places in Palestine\nKJV: Shamir. Compare H8053 שָׁמוּר .\n\nCognate Group: H8053 (Shamir), H8069 (Shamir), H8068 (adamant)",
    8070: "שְׁמִירָמֹות (Shᵉmîyrâmôwth | shem-ee-raw-moth')\n\nDerivation: or שְׁמָרִימֹות; probably from H8034 שֵׁם and plural of H7413 רָמָה ; name of heights\nStrong's: Shemiramoth, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Shemiramoth.\n\nCognate Group: H8061 (Shemida), H8033 (in it), H8050 (Samuel), H8035 (Sem), H8062 (Shemidaites), H8038 (Shemeber), H8034 (base), H3074 (Jehovahshammah), H8070 (Shemiramoth)",
    8071: "שִׂמְלָה (simlâh | sim-law')\n\nDerivation: perhaps by permutation for the feminine of H5566 סֶמֶל (through the idea of a cover assuming the shape of the object beneath)\nStrong's: a dress, especially a mantle\nKJV: apparel, cloth(-es, -ing), garment, raiment. Compare H8008 שַׂלְמָה .\n\nCognate Group: H8008 (clothes), H8072 (Samlah), H8071 (apparel), H8079 (spider)\nGreek Equivalents: G2440 ἱμάτιον, G2441 ἱματισμός, G4749 στολή",
    8072: "שַׂמְלָה (Samlâh | sam-law')\n\nDerivation: probably for the same as H8071 שִׂמְלָה\nStrong's: Samlah, an Edomite\nKJV: Samlah.\n\nCognate Group: H8008 (clothes), H8072 (Samlah), H8071 (apparel), H8079 (spider)",
    8073: "שַׁמְלַי (Shamlay | sham-lah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: for H8014 שַׂלְמַי\nStrong's: Shamlai, one of the Nethinim\nKJV: Shalmai (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H7958 (quails), H7938 (reward), H8073 (Shalmai), H8009 (Salmon), H7940 (Sacar), H7917 (that is hired), H4909 (reward), H8012 (Salmon), H8007 (Salma), H7939 (hire), H7936 (earn wages), H8014 (Shalmai), H7916 (hired)",
    8074: "שָׁמֵם (shâmêm | shaw-mame')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to stun (or intransitively, grow numb), i.e. devastate or (figuratively) stupefy (both usually in a passive sense)\nKJV: make amazed, be astonied, (be an) astonish(-ment), (be, bring into, unto, lay, lie, make) desolate(-ion, places), be destitute, destroy (self), (lay, lie, make) waste, wonder.\n\nCognate Group: H8037 (Shamma), H8076 (desolate), H8048 (Shammah), H8074 (make amazed), H4923 (astonishment), H8077 (desolate), H8047 (astonishment), H8060 (Shammai), H8054 (Shamoth), H8078 (astonishment)\nGreek Equivalents: G390 ἀναστρέφω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G818 ἀτιμάζω, G853 ἀφανίζω, G1311 διαφθείρω, G1590 ἐκλύω, G1605 ἐκπλήσσω, G1839 ἐξίστημι, G1863 ἐπάγω, G2048 ἔρημος, G2049 ἐρημόω, G2050 ἐρήμωσις, G2295 θαῦμα, G2296 θαυμάζω, G2657 κατανοέω, G2704 καταφθείρω, G4768 στυγνάζω, G4937 συντρίβω, G5015 ταράσσω",
    8075: "שְׁמַם (shᵉmam | shem-am')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8074 שָׁמֵם \nStrong's: to stun (or intransitively, grow numb), i.e. devastate or (figuratively) stupefy (both usually in a passive sense)\nKJV: be astonied.\n\nCognate Group: H8075 (be astonied)",
    8076: "שָׁמֵם (shâmêm | shaw-mame')\n\nDerivation: from H8074 שָׁמֵם\nStrong's: ruined\nKJV: desolate.\n\nCognate Group: H8037 (Shamma), H8076 (desolate), H8048 (Shammah), H8074 (make amazed), H4923 (astonishment), H8077 (desolate), H8047 (astonishment), H8060 (Shammai), H8054 (Shamoth), H8078 (astonishment)",
    8077: "שְׁמָמָה (shᵉmâmâh | shem-aw-maw')\n\nDerivation: or שִׁמָמָה; feminine of H8076 שָׁמֵם\nStrong's: devastation; figuratively, astonishment\nKJV: (laid, [idiom] most) desolate(-ion), waste.\n\nCognate Group: H8037 (Shamma), H8076 (desolate), H8048 (Shammah), H8074 (make amazed), H4923 (astonishment), H8077 (desolate), H8047 (astonishment), H8060 (Shammai), H8054 (Shamoth), H8078 (astonishment)\nGreek Equivalents: G684 ἀπώλεια, G854 ἀφανισμός, G2047 ἐρημία, G2671 κατάρα",
    8078: "שִׁמָּמֹון (shimmâmôwn | shim-maw-mone')\n\nDerivation: from H8074 שָׁמֵם\nStrong's: stupefaction\nKJV: astonishment.\n\nCognate Group: H8037 (Shamma), H8076 (desolate), H8048 (Shammah), H8074 (make amazed), H4923 (astonishment), H8077 (desolate), H8047 (astonishment), H8060 (Shammai), H8054 (Shamoth), H8078 (astonishment)",
    8079: "שְׂמָמִית (sᵉmâmîyth | sem-aw-meeth')\n\nDerivation: probably from H8074 שָׁמֵם (in the sense of poisoning)\nStrong's: a lizard (from the superstition of its noxiousness)\nKJV: spider.\n\nCognate Group: H8008 (clothes), H8072 (Samlah), H8071 (apparel), H8079 (spider)",
    8080: "שָׁמַן (shâman | shaw-man')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to shine, i.e. (by analogy) be (causatively, make) oily or gross\nKJV: become (make, wax) fat.\n\nCognate Group: H8082 (fat), H4925 (Mishmannah), H4924 (fat), H8081 (anointing), H8080 (become fat), H820 (desolate place)\nGreek Equivalents: G4096 πιότης",
    8081: "שֶׁמֶן (shemen | sheh'-men)\n\nDerivation: from H8080 שָׁמַן\nStrong's: grease, especially liquid (as from the olive, often perfumed); figuratively, richness\nKJV: anointing, [idiom] fat (things), [idiom] fruitful, oil(-ed), ointment, olive, [phrase] pine.\n\nCognate Group: H8082 (fat), H4925 (Mishmannah), H4924 (fat), H8081 (anointing), H8080 (become fat), H820 (desolate place)\nGreek Equivalents: G1637 ἔλαιον, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G3464 μύρον, G1068 Γεθσημανῆ",
    8082: "שָׁמֵן (shâmên | shaw-mane')\n\nDerivation: from H8080 שָׁמַן\nStrong's: greasy, i.e. gross; figuratively, rich\nKJV: fat, lusty, plenteous.\n\nCognate Group: H8082 (fat), H4925 (Mishmannah), H4924 (fat), H8081 (anointing), H8080 (become fat), H820 (desolate place)\nGreek Equivalents: G2068 ἐσθίω, G3975 παχύνω",
    8083: "שְׁמֹנֶה (shᵉmôneh | shem-o-neh')\n\nDerivation: or שְׁמֹונֶה; feminine שְׁמֹנָה; or שְׁמֹונָה; apparently from H8082 שָׁמֵן through the idea of plumpness\nStrong's: a cardinal number, eight (as if a surplus above the 'perfect' seven); also (as ordinal) eighth\nKJV: eight(-een, -eenth), eighth.\n\nCognate Group: H8067 (Sheminith), H8084 (eighty), H8066 (eight), H8083 (eight)",
    8084: "שְׁמֹנִים (shᵉmônîym | shem-o-neem')\n\nDerivation: or שְׁמֹונִים; multiple from H8083 שְׁמֹנֶה\nStrong's: eighty, also eightieth\nKJV: eighty(-ieth), fourscore.\n\nCognate Group: H8067 (Sheminith), H8084 (eighty), H8066 (eight), H8083 (eight)",
    8085: "שָׁמַע (shâmaʻ | shaw-mah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to hear intelligently (often with implication of attention, obedience, etc.; causatively, to tell, etc.)\nKJV: [idiom] attentively, call (gather) together, [idiom] carefully, [idiom] certainly, consent, consider, be content, declare, [idiom] diligently, discern, give ear, (cause to, let, make to) hear(-ken, tell), [idiom] indeed, listen, make (a) noise, (be) obedient, obey, perceive, (make a) proclaim(-ation), publish, regard, report, shew (forth), (make a) sound, [idiom] surely, tell, understand, whosoever (heareth), witness.\n\nCognate Group: H8091 (Shama), H8087 (Shema), H8093 (Shimeah), H3458 (Ishmael), H2045 (to cause to hear), H3460 (Ishmaiah), H4927 (Mishma), H4928 (bidding), H4926 (hearing), H8090 (Shema), H8085 ([idiom] attentively), H8097 (of Shimi), H8094 (Shemaah), H8092 (Shimea), H8088 (bruit), H8052 (bruit), H3459 (Ishmaelite), H8095 (Simeon), H8099 (tribe of Simeon), H8051 (Shammua), H8089 (fame), H8101 (Shimeathites), H8100 (Shimath), H8098 (Shemaiah), H8096 (Shimeah)\nGreek Equivalents: G114 ἀθετέω, G189 ἀκοή, G191 ἀκούω, G214 ἀλαλάζω, G312 ἀναγγέλλω, G400 ἀναφωνέω, G518 ἀπαγγέλλω, G1096 γίνομαι, G1097 γινώσκω, G1213 δηλόω, G1251 διακούομαι, G1522 εἰσακούω, G1653 ἐλεέω, G1801 ἐνωτίζομαι, G1873 ἐπακούω, G1994 ἐπιστρέφω, G3853 παραγγέλλω, G3878 παρακούω, G4100 πιστεύω, G4160 ποιέω, G5083 τηρέω, G5219 ὑπακούω, G5255 ὑπήκοος, G5442 φυλάσσω",
    8086: "שְׁמַע (shᵉmaʻ | shem-ah')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8085 שָׁמַע \nStrong's: to hear intelligently (often with implication of attention, obedience, etc.; causatively, to tell, etc.)\nKJV: hear, obey.\n\nCognate Group: H8086 (hear), H8115 (Samaria)\nGreek Equivalents: G3980 πειθαρχέω",
