    8121: "שֶׁמֶשׁ (shemesh | sheh'-mesh)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be brilliant\nStrong's: the sun; by implication, the east; figuratively, a ray, i.e. (architectural) a notched battlement\nKJV: [phrase] east side(-ward), sun (rising), [phrase] west(-ward), window. See also H1053 בֵּית שֶׁמֶשׁ .\n\nCognate Group: H8134 (Shinab), H8137 (Senazar), H8121 (east side), H8123 (Samson), H8125 (Shamsherai)\nGreek Equivalents: G2246 ἥλιος",
