    8126: "שֻׁמָתִי (Shumâthîy | shoo-maw-thee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from an unused name from H7762 שׁוּם probably meaning garlic-smell\nStrong's: a Shumathite (collectively) or descendants of Shumah\nKJV: Shumathites.\n\nCognate Group: H8045 (destory), H8126 (Shumathites)",
