    8134: "שִׁנְאָב (Shinʼâb | shin-awb')\n\nDerivation: probably from H8132 שָׁנָא and H1 אָב ; a father has turned\nStrong's: Shinab, a Canaanite\nKJV: Shinab.\n\nCognate Group: H8134 (Shinab), H8137 (Senazar), H8121 (east side), H8123 (Samson), H8125 (Shamsherai)",
    8135: "שִׂנְאָה (sinʼâh | sin-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H8130 שָׂנֵא\nStrong's: hate\nKJV: [phrase] exceedingly, hate(-ful, -red).\n\nCognate Group: H8149 (Senir), H8130 (enemy), H8146 (hated), H8135 (exceedingly)\nGreek Equivalents: G2189 ἔχθρα",
    8136: "שִׁנְאָן (shinʼân | shin-awn')\n\nDerivation: from H8132 שָׁנָא\nStrong's: change, i.e. repetition\nKJV: [idiom] angels.\n\nCognate Group: H8145 (again), H4932 (college), H8136 ([idiom] angels), H8147 (both), H8138 (do again)",
    8137: "שֶׁנְאַצַּר (Shenʼatstsar | shen-ats-tsar')\n\nTypo: xlit Shenatstsar corrected to Shenʼatstsar\n\nDerivation: apparently of Babylonian origin\nStrong's: Shenatstsar, an Israelite\nKJV: Senazar.\n\nCognate Group: H8134 (Shinab), H8137 (Senazar), H8121 (east side), H8123 (Samson), H8125 (Shamsherai)",
    8138: "שָׁנָה (shânâh | shaw-naw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to fold, i.e. duplicate (literally or figuratively); by implication, to transmute (transitive or intransitive)\nKJV: do (speak, strike) again, alter, double, (be given to) change, disguise, (be) diverse, pervert, prefer, repeat, return, do the second time.\n\nCognate Group: H8132 (change), H8141 (whole age), H8138 (do again)\nGreek Equivalents: G114 ἀθετέω, G390 ἀναστρέφω, G2186 ἐφίστημι, G4369 προστίθημι",
    8139: "שְׁנָה (shᵉnâh | shen-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8142 שֵׁנָה \nStrong's: sleep\nKJV: sleep.\n\nCognate Group: H8139 (sleep)",
    8140: "שְׁנָה (shᵉnâh | shen-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8141 שָׁנֶה \nStrong's: a year (as a revolution of time)\nKJV: year.\n\nCognate Group: H8140 (year), H8133 (alter)",
    8141: "שָׁנֶה (shâneh | shaw-neh')\n\nDerivation: (in plural or (feminine) שָׁנָה; from H8138 שָׁנָה\nStrong's: a year (as a revolution of time)\nKJV: [phrase] whole age, [idiom] long, [phrase] old, year([idiom] -ly).\n\nCognate Group: H8132 (change), H8141 (whole age), H8138 (do again)\nGreek Equivalents: G979 βίος, G1763 ἐνιαυτός, G2094 ἔτος, G2094 ἔτος, G2540 καιρός",
    8142: "שֵׁנָה (shênâh | shay-naw')\n\nDerivation: or שֵׁנָא; (Psalm 127:2), from H3462 יָשֵׁן\nStrong's: sleep\nKJV: sleep.\n\nCognate Group: H8142 (sleep), H8153 (sleep), H3463 (asleep), H3464 (Jashen), H3465 (old), H3462 (old), H3466 (Jeshanah)\nGreek Equivalents: G3573 νυστάζω, G5258 ὕπνος, G5258 ὕπνος",
    8143: "שֶׁנְהַבִּים (shenhabbîym | shen-hab-beem')\n\nDerivation: from H8127 שֵׁן and the plural apparently of a foreign word\nStrong's: probably, tooth of elephants, i.e. ivory tusk\nKJV: ivory.\n\nCognate Group: H8143 (ivory), H8129 (Shen), H8148 (byword), H8150 (prick), H8127 (crag)\nGreek Equivalents: G1661 ἐλεφάντινος",
    8144: "שָׁנִי (shânîy | shaw-nee')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: crimson, properly, the insect or its color, also stuff dyed with it\nKJV: crimson, scarlet (thread).\n\nCognate Group: H8144 (crimson)\nGreek Equivalents: G2847 κόκκινος",
    8145: "שֵׁנִי (shênîy | shay-nee')\n\nDerivation: from H8138 שָׁנָה\nStrong's: properly, double, i.e. second; also adverbially, again\nKJV: again, either (of them), (an-) other, second (time).\n\nCognate Group: H8145 (again), H4932 (college), H8136 ([idiom] angels), H8147 (both), H8138 (do again)\nGreek Equivalents: G2087 ἕτερος, G4618 σιτευτός",
    8146: "שָׂנִיא (sânîyʼ | saw-nee')\n\nDerivation: from H8130 שָׂנֵא\nStrong's: hated\nKJV: hated.\n\nCognate Group: H8149 (Senir), H8130 (enemy), H8146 (hated), H8135 (exceedingly)",
    8147: "שְׁנַיִם (shᵉnayim | shen-ah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: dual of H8145 שֵׁנִי ; feminine שְׁתַּיִם\nStrong's: two; also (as ordinal) twofold\nKJV: both, couple, double, second, twain, [phrase] twelfth, [phrase] twelve, [phrase] twenty (sixscore) thousand, twice, two.\n\nCognate Group: H8145 (again), H4932 (college), H8136 ([idiom] angels), H8147 (both), H8138 (do again)\nGreek Equivalents: G1313 διάφορος, G1366 δίστομος, G2201 ζεῦγος",
    8148: "שְׁנִינָה (shᵉnîynâh | shen-ee-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H8150 שָׁנַן\nStrong's: something pointed, i.e. a gibe\nKJV: byword, taunt.\n\nCognate Group: H8143 (ivory), H8129 (Shen), H8148 (byword), H8150 (prick), H8127 (crag)",
    8149: "שְׁנִיר (Shᵉnîyr | shen-eer')\n\nDerivation: or שְׂנִיר; from an unused root meaning to be pointed; peak\nStrong's: Shenir or Senir, a summit of Lebanon\nKJV: Senir, Shenir.\n\nCognate Group: H8149 (Senir), H8130 (enemy), H8146 (hated), H8135 (exceedingly)",
    8150: "שָׁנַן (shânan | shaw-nan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to point (transitive or intransitive); intensively, to pierce; figuratively, to inculcate\nKJV: prick, sharp(-en), teach diligently, whet.\n\nCognate Group: H8143 (ivory), H8129 (Shen), H8148 (byword), H8150 (prick), H8127 (crag)\nGreek Equivalents: G3691 ὀξύς, G3947 παροξύνω, G4264 προβιβάζω",
    8151: "שָׁנַס (shânaç | shaw-nas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to compress (with a belt)\nKJV: gird up.\n\nCognate Group: H8151 (gird up), H8152 (Shinar)",
    8152: "שִׁנְעָר (Shinʻâr | shin-awr')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Shinar, a plain in Babylonia\nKJV: Shinar.\n\nCognate Group: H8151 (gird up), H8152 (Shinar)",
    8153: "שְׁנָת (shᵉnâth | shen-awth')\n\nDerivation: from H3462 יָשֵׁן\nStrong's: sleep\nKJV: sleep.\n\nCognate Group: H8142 (sleep), H8153 (sleep), H3463 (asleep), H3464 (Jashen), H3465 (old), H3462 (old), H3466 (Jeshanah)",
    8154: "שָׁסָה (shâçâh | shaw-saw')\n\nDerivation: or שָׁשָׂה; (Isaiah 10:13), a primitive root\nStrong's: to plunder\nKJV: destroyer, rob, spoil(-er).\n\nCognate Group: H8154 (destroyer)\nGreek Equivalents: G1283 διαρπάζω, G2662 καταπατέω",
    8155: "שָׁסַס (shâçaç | shaw-sas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to plunder\nKJV: rifle, spoil.\n\nCognate Group: H7601 (spoil), H4882 (spoil), H8155 (rifle), H4933 (booty)\nGreek Equivalents: G1283 διαρπάζω, G2662 καταπατέω",
    8156: "שָׁסַע (shâçaʻ | shaw-sah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to split or tear; figuratively, to upbraid\nKJV: cleave, (be) cloven (footed), rend, stay.\n\nCognate Group: H8156 (cleave), H8157 (cleft)\nGreek Equivalents: G1288 διασπάω, G1575 ἐκκλάω, G3982 πείθω, G4937 συντρίβω",
    8157: "שֶׁסַע (sheçaʻ | sheh'-sah)\n\nDerivation: from H8156 שָׁסַע\nStrong's: a fissure\nKJV: cleft, clovenfooted.\n\nCognate Group: H8156 (cleave), H8157 (cleft)",
    8158: "שָׁסַף (shâçaph | shaw-saf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to cut in pieces, i.e. slaughter\nKJV: hew in pieces.\n\nCognate Group: H8158 (hew in pieces)\nGreek Equivalents: G4969 σφάζω",
    8159: "שָׁעָה (shâʻâh | shaw-aw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to gaze at or about (properly, for help); by implication, to inspect, consider, compassionate, be nonplussed (as looking around in amazement) or bewildered\nKJV: depart, be dim, be dismayed, look (away), regard, have respect, spare, turn.\n\nCognate Group: H8159 (depart)\nGreek Equivalents: G447 ἀνίημι, G863 ἀφίημι, G868 ἀφίστημι, G994 βοάω, G2049 ἐρημόω, G2296 θαυμάζω, G2648 καταμανθάνω, G3191 μελετάω, G3309 μεριμνάω, G4337 προσέχω",
    8160: "שָׁעָה (shâʻâh | shaw-aw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H8159 שָׁעָה\nStrong's: properly, a look, i.e. a moment\nKJV: hour.\n\nCognate Group: H8160 (hour), H8128 (tooth)\nGreek Equivalents: G5610 ὥρα",
    8161: "שַׁעֲטָה (shaʻăṭâh | shah'-at-aw)\n\nDerivation: feminine from an unused root meaning to stamp\nStrong's: a clatter (of hoofs)\nKJV: stamping.\n\nCognate Group: H8162 (garment of divers sorts), H8161 (stamping)\nGreek Equivalents: G3730 ὁρμή",
    8162: "שַׁעַטְנֵז (shaʻaṭnêz | shah-at-naze')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign derivation\nStrong's: linsey-woolsey, i.e. cloth of linen and wool carded and spun together\nKJV: garment of divers sorts, linen and wollen.\n\nCognate Group: H8162 (garment of divers sorts), H8161 (stamping)",
    8163: "שָׂעִיר (sâʻîyr | saw-eer')\n\nDerivation: or שָׂעִר; from H8175 שָׂעַר\nStrong's: shaggy; as noun, a he-goat; by analogy, a faun\nKJV: devil, goat, hairy, kid, rough, satyr.\n\nCognate Group: H8181 (hair), H8165 (Seir), H8185 (hair), H8188 (Seorim), H8166 (kid), H8184 (barley), H8175 (be afraid), H8163 (devil), H8178 (affrighted), H8167 (Seirath)\nGreek Equivalents: G1140 δαιμόνιον, G1497 εἴδωλον, G2055 ἐρίφιον, G2056 ἔριφος, G3152 μάταιος, G3655 ὄμβρος",
    8164: "שָׂעִיר (sâʻîyr | saw-eer')\n\nDerivation: formed the same as H8163 שָׂעִיר\nStrong's: a shower (as tempestuous)\nKJV: small rain.\n\nCognate Group: H8164 (small rain)",
    8165: "שֵׂעִיר (Sêʻîyr | say-eer')\n\nDerivation: formed like H8163 שָׂעִיר ; rough\nStrong's: Seir, a mountain of Idumaea and its aboriginal occupants, also one in Palestine\nKJV: Seir.\n\nCognate Group: H8181 (hair), H8165 (Seir), H8185 (hair), H8188 (Seorim), H8166 (kid), H8184 (barley), H8175 (be afraid), H8163 (devil), H8178 (affrighted), H8167 (Seirath)",
    8166: "שְׂעִירָה (sᵉʻîyrâh | seh-ee-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H8163 שָׂעִיר\nStrong's: a she-goat\nKJV: kid.\n\nCognate Group: H8181 (hair), H8165 (Seir), H8185 (hair), H8188 (Seorim), H8166 (kid), H8184 (barley), H8175 (be afraid), H8163 (devil), H8178 (affrighted), H8167 (Seirath)",
    8167: "שְׂעִירָה (Sᵉʻîyrâh | seh-ee-raw')\n\nDerivation: formed as H8166 שְׂעִירָה ; roughness\nStrong's: Seirah, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Seirath.\n\nCognate Group: H8181 (hair), H8165 (Seir), H8185 (hair), H8188 (Seorim), H8166 (kid), H8184 (barley), H8175 (be afraid), H8163 (devil), H8178 (affrighted), H8167 (Seirath)",
    8168: "שֹׁעַל (shôʻal | sho'-al)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to hollow out\nStrong's: the palm; by extension, a handful\nKJV: handful, hollow of the hand.\n\nCognate Group: H8168 (handful), H4934 (path)\nGreek Equivalents: G5495 χείρ",
    8169: "שַׁעַלְבִים (Shaʻalbîym | shah-al-beem')\n\nDerivation: or שַׁעֲלַבִּין; plural from H7776 שׁוּעָל ; fox-holes\nStrong's: Shaalbim or Shaalabbin, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Shaalabbin, Shaalbim.\n\nCognate Group: H7776 (fox), H8169 (Shaalabbin), H8170 (Shaalbonite), H7777 (Shual), H8171 (Shalim)",
    8170: "שַׁעַלְבֹנִי (Shaʻalbônîy | shah-al-bo-nee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H8169 שַׁעַלְבִים\nStrong's: a Shaalbonite or inhabitant of Shaalbin\nKJV: Shaalbonite.\n\nCognate Group: H7776 (fox), H8169 (Shaalabbin), H8170 (Shaalbonite), H7777 (Shual), H8171 (Shalim)",
    8171: "שַׁעֲלִים (Shaʻălîym | shah-al-eem')\n\nDerivation: plural of H7776 שׁוּעָל ; foxes\nStrong's: Shaalim, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Shalim.\n\nCognate Group: H7776 (fox), H8169 (Shaalabbin), H8170 (Shaalbonite), H7777 (Shual), H8171 (Shalim)",
    8172: "שָׁעַן (shâʻan | shaw-an')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to support one's self\nKJV: lean, lie, rely, rest (on, self), stay.\n\nCognate Group: H8172 (lean), H824 (Eshean), H4938 (staff), H4937 (stay)\nGreek Equivalents: G1679 ἐλπίζω, G1869 ἐπαίρω, G1879 ἐπαναπαύομαι, G1991 ἐπιστηρίζω, G2711 καταψύχω, G3982 πείθω",
    8173: "שָׁעַע (shâʻaʻ | shaw-ah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: (in a good acceptation) to look upon (with complacency), i.e. fondle, please or amuse (self); (in a bad one) to look about (in dismay), i.e. stare\nKJV: cry (out) (by confusion with H7768 שָׁוַע), dandle, delight (self), play, shut.\n\nCognate Group: H8173 (cry)\nGreek Equivalents: G25 ἀγαπάω, G2576 καμμύω, G3191 μελετάω, G3870 παρακαλέω",
    8174: "שַׁעַף (Shaʻaph | shah'-af)\n\nDerivation: from H5586 סָעַף ; fluctuation\nStrong's: Shaaph, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Shaaph.\n\nCognate Group: H8191 (delight), H8174 (Shaaph), H8173 (cry)",
    8175: "שָׂעַר (sâʻar | saw-ar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to storm; by implication, to shiver, i.e. fear\nKJV: be (horribly) afraid, fear, hurl as a storm, be tempestuous, come like (take away as with) a whirlwind.\n\nCognate Group: H8181 (hair), H8165 (Seir), H8185 (hair), H8188 (Seorim), H8166 (kid), H8184 (barley), H8175 (be afraid), H8163 (devil), H8178 (affrighted), H8167 (Seirath)",
    8176: "שָׁעַר (shâʻar | shaw-ar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; to split or open, i.e. (literally, but only as denominative from H8179 שַׁעַר); compare see H7778 שֹׁועֵר \nStrong's: to act as gatekeeper; (figuratively) to estimate\nKJV: think.\n\nCognate Group: H8176 (think), H8180 (fold)",
    8177: "שְׂעַר (sᵉʻar | seh-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8181 שֵׂעָר\nStrong's: hair\nKJV: hair.\n\nCognate Group: H8177 (hair), H8131 (hate)",
    8178: "שַׂעַר (saʻar | sah'-ar)\n\nDerivation: from H8175 שָׂעַר\nStrong's: a tempest; also a terror\nKJV: affrighted, [idiom] horribly, [idiom] sore, storm. See H8181 שֵׂעָר .\n\nCognate Group: H8181 (hair), H8165 (Seir), H8185 (hair), H8188 (Seorim), H8166 (kid), H8184 (barley), H8175 (be afraid), H8163 (devil), H8178 (affrighted), H8167 (Seirath)\nGreek Equivalents: G2295 θαῦμα",
    8179: "שַׁעַר (shaʻar | shah'-ar)\n\nDerivation: from H8176 שָׁעַר in its original sense\nStrong's: an opening, i.e. door or gate\nKJV: city, door, gate, port ([idiom] -er).\n\nCognate Group: H8187 (Sheariah), H7778 (doorkeeper), H8179 (city), H8189 (Shaaraim)\nGreek Equivalents: G833 αὐλή, G2374 θύρα, G4172 πόλις, G4439 πύλη, G4440 πυλών",
    8180: "שַׁעַר (shaʻar | shah'-ar)\n\nDerivation: from H8176 שָׁעַר\nStrong's: a measure (as a section)\nKJV: (hundred-) fold.\n\nCognate Group: H8176 (think), H8180 (fold)",
    8181: "שֵׂעָר (sêʻâr | say-awr')\n\nDerivation: or שַׂעַר; (Isaiah 7:20), from H8175 שָׂעַר in the sense of dishevelling\nStrong's: hair (as if tossed or bristling)\nKJV: hair(-y), [idiom] rough.\n\nCognate Group: H8181 (hair), H8165 (Seir), H8185 (hair), H8188 (Seorim), H8166 (kid), H8184 (barley), H8175 (be afraid), H8163 (devil), H8178 (affrighted), H8167 (Seirath)\nGreek Equivalents: G2355 θρῆνος, G5155 τρίχινος",
    8182: "שֹׁעָר (shôʻâr | sho-awr')\n\nDerivation: from H8176 שָׁעַר\nStrong's: harsh or horrid, i.e. offensive\nKJV: vile.\n\nCognate Group: H8182 (vile), H8186 (horrible thing), H8190 (Shaashgaz)",
    8183: "שְׂעָרָה (sᵉʻârâh | seh-aw-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H8178 שַׂעַר\nStrong's: a hurricane\nKJV: storm, tempest.\n\nCognate Group: H8175 (be afraid), H8183 (storm), H8178 (affrighted)",
    8184: "שְׂעֹרָה (sᵉʻôrâh | seh-o-raw')\n\nDerivation: or שְׂעֹורָה (feminine meaning the plant); and (masculine meaning the grain); also שְׂעֹר; or שְׂעֹור; from H8175 שָׂעַר in the sense of roughness\nStrong's: barley (as villose)\nKJV: barley.\n\nCognate Group: H8181 (hair), H8165 (Seir), H8185 (hair), H8188 (Seorim), H8166 (kid), H8184 (barley), H8175 (be afraid), H8163 (devil), H8178 (affrighted), H8167 (Seirath)\nGreek Equivalents: G2915 κριθή, G2916 κρίθινος",
    8185: "שַׂעֲרָה (saʻărâh | sah-ar-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H8181 שֵׂעָר\nStrong's: hairiness\nKJV: hair.\n\nCognate Group: H8181 (hair), H8165 (Seir), H8185 (hair), H8188 (Seorim), H8166 (kid), H8184 (barley), H8175 (be afraid), H8163 (devil), H8178 (affrighted), H8167 (Seirath)",
    8186: "שַׁעֲרוּרָה (shaʻărûwrâh | shah-ar-oo-raw')\n\nDerivation: or שַׁעֲרִירִיָּה; or שַׁעֲרֻרִת; feminine from H8176 שָׁעַר in the sense of H8175 שָׂעַר\nStrong's: something fearful\nKJV: horrible thing.\n\nCognate Group: H8182 (vile), H8186 (horrible thing), H8190 (Shaashgaz)",
    8187: "שְׁעַרְיָה (Shᵉʻaryâh | sheh-ar-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H8176 שָׁעַר and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has stormed\nStrong's: Shearjah, an Israelite\nKJV: Sheariah.\n\nCognate Group: H8187 (Sheariah), H7778 (doorkeeper), H8179 (city), H8189 (Shaaraim)",
    8188: "שְׂעֹרִים (Sᵉʻôrîym | seh-o-reem')\n\nDerivation: masculine plural of H8184 שְׂעֹרָה ; barley grains\nStrong's: Seorim, an Israelite\nKJV: Seorim.\n\nCognate Group: H8181 (hair), H8165 (Seir), H8185 (hair), H8188 (Seorim), H8166 (kid), H8184 (barley), H8175 (be afraid), H8163 (devil), H8178 (affrighted), H8167 (Seirath)",
    8189: "שַׁעֲרַיִם (Shaʻărayim | shah-ar-ah'-yim)\n\nDerivation: dual of H8179 שַׁעַר ; double gates\nStrong's: Shaarajim, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Shaaraim.\n\nCognate Group: H8187 (Sheariah), H7778 (doorkeeper), H8179 (city), H8189 (Shaaraim)",
    8190: "שַׁעַשְׁגַּז (Shaʻashgaz | shah-ash-gaz')\n\nDerivation: of Persian derivation\nStrong's: Shaashgaz, a eunuch of Xerxes\nKJV: Shaashgaz.\n\nCognate Group: H8182 (vile), H8186 (horrible thing), H8190 (Shaashgaz)",
    8191: "שַׁעְשֻׁעַ (shaʻshuaʻ | shah-shoo'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from H8173 שָׁעַע\nStrong's: enjoyment\nKJV: delight, pleasure.\n\nCognate Group: H8191 (delight), H8174 (Shaaph), H8173 (cry)\nGreek Equivalents: G25 ἀγαπάω, G1792 ἐντρυφάω",
    8192: "שָׁפָה (shâphâh | shaw-faw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to abrade, i.e. bare\nKJV: high, stick out.\n\nCognate Group: H3472 (Ispah), H8205 (high place), H8194 (cheese), H8192 (high), H8195 (Shephi)\nGreek Equivalents: G3977 πεδινός",
    8193: "שָׂפָה (sâphâh | saw-faw')\n\nDerivation: or (in dual and plural) שֶׂפֶת; probably from H5595 סָפָה or H8192 שָׁפָה through the idea of termination (compare H5490 סֹוף)\nStrong's: the lip (as a natural boundary); by implication, language; by analogy, a margin (of a vessel, water, cloth, etc.)\nKJV: band, bank, binding, border, brim, brink, edge, language, lip, prating, (sea-)shore, side, speech, talk, (vain) words.\n\nCognate Group: H8193 (band), H8222 (beard)\nGreek Equivalents: G1100 γλῶσσα, G3056 λόγος, G3313 μέρος, G4750 στόμα, G5456 φωνή, G5491 χεῖλος",
    8194: "שָׁפָה (shâphâh | shaw-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H8192 שָׁפָה in the sense of clarifying\nStrong's: a cheese (as strained from the whey)\nKJV: cheese.\n\nCognate Group: H3472 (Ispah), H8205 (high place), H8194 (cheese), H8192 (high), H8195 (Shephi)",
    8195: "שְׁפֹו (Shᵉphôw | shef-o')\n\nDerivation: or שְׁפִי; from H8192 שָׁפָה ; baldness (compare H8205 שְׁפִי)\nStrong's: Shepho or Shephi, an Idumaean\nKJV: Shephi, Shepho.\n\nCognate Group: H3472 (Ispah), H8205 (high place), H8194 (cheese), H8192 (high), H8195 (Shephi)",
    8196: "שְׁפֹוט (shᵉphôwṭ | shef-ote')\n\nDerivation: or שְׁפוּט; from H8199 שָׁפַט\nStrong's: a judicial sentence, i.e. punishment\nKJV: judgment.\n\nCognate Group: H4941 (adversary), H8196 (judgment), H8204 (Shiphtan), H8199 (avenge), H8202 (Shaphat), H8203 (Shephatiah), H8201 (judgment)",
    8197: "שְׁפוּפָם (Shᵉphûwphâm | shef-oo-fawm')\n\nDerivation: or שְׁפוּפָן; from the same as H8207 שְׁפִיפֹן ; serpent-like\nStrong's: Shephupham or Shephuphan, an Israelite\nKJV: Shephuphan, Shupham.\n\nCognate Group: H7781 (Shuphamite), H8207 (adder), H8206 (Shuppim), H8197 (Shephuphan)",
    8198: "שִׁפְחָה (shiphchâh | shif-khaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine from an unused root meaning to spread out (as a family; see H4940 מִשְׁפָּחָה)\nStrong's: a female slave (as a member of the household)\nKJV: (bond-, hand-) maid(-en, -servant), wench, bondwoman, womanservant.\n\nCognate Group: H4940 (family), H8198 (maid)\nGreek Equivalents: G1135 γυνή, G3814 παιδίσκη",
    8199: "שָׁפַט (shâphaṭ | shaw-fat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to judge, i.e. pronounce sentence (for or against); by implication, to vindicate or punish; by extenssion, to govern; passively, to litigate (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: [phrase] avenge, [idiom] that condemn, contend, defend, execute (judgment), (be a) judge(-ment), [idiom] needs, plead, reason, rule.\n\nCognate Group: H4941 (adversary), H8196 (judgment), H8204 (Shiphtan), H8199 (avenge), H8202 (Shaphat), H8203 (Shephatiah), H8201 (judgment)\nGreek Equivalents: G518 ἀπαγγέλλω, G757 ἄρχω, G1252 διακρίνω, G1325 δίδωμι, G1344 δικαιόω, G1348 δικαστής, G1377 διώκω, G1556 ἐκδικέω, G1557 ἐκδίκησις, G1679 ἐλπίζω, G2186 ἐφίστημι, G2609 κατάγω, G2614 καταδιώκω, G2902 κρατέω, G2920 κρίσις, G2923 κριτής",
    8200: "שְׁפַט (shᵉphaṭ | shef-at')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8199 שָׁפַט\nStrong's: to judge\nKJV: magistrate.\n\nCognate Group: H8200 (magistrate)\nGreek Equivalents: G1122 γραμματεύς",
    8201: "שֶׁפֶט (shepheṭ | sheh'-fet)\n\nDerivation: from H8199 שָׁפַט\nStrong's: a sentence, i.e. infliction\nKJV: judgment.\n\nCognate Group: H4941 (adversary), H8196 (judgment), H8204 (Shiphtan), H8199 (avenge), H8202 (Shaphat), H8203 (Shephatiah), H8201 (judgment)\nGreek Equivalents: G2917 κρίμα, G3148 μάστιξ",
    8202: "שָׁפָט (Shâphâṭ | shaw-fawt')\n\nDerivation: from H8199 שָׁפַט ; judge\nStrong's: Shaphat, the name of four Israelites\nKJV: Shaphat.\n\nCognate Group: H4941 (adversary), H8196 (judgment), H8204 (Shiphtan), H8199 (avenge), H8202 (Shaphat), H8203 (Shephatiah), H8201 (judgment)",
    8203: "שְׁפַטְיָה (Shᵉphaṭyâh | shef-at-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or שְׁפַטְיָהוּ; from H8199 שָׁפַט and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has judged\nStrong's: Shephatjah, the name of ten Israelites\nKJV: Shephatiah.\n\nCognate Group: H4941 (adversary), H8196 (judgment), H8204 (Shiphtan), H8199 (avenge), H8202 (Shaphat), H8203 (Shephatiah), H8201 (judgment)",
    8204: "שִׁפְטָן (Shiphṭân | shif-tawn')\n\nDerivation: from H8199 שָׁפַט ; judge-like\nStrong's: Shiphtan, an Israelite\nKJV: Shiphtan.\n\nCognate Group: H4941 (adversary), H8196 (judgment), H8204 (Shiphtan), H8199 (avenge), H8202 (Shaphat), H8203 (Shephatiah), H8201 (judgment)",
    8205: "שְׁפִי (shᵉphîy | shef-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H8192 שָׁפָה\nStrong's: bareness; concretely, a bare hill or plain\nKJV: high place, stick out.\n\nCognate Group: H3472 (Ispah), H8205 (high place), H8194 (cheese), H8192 (high), H8195 (Shephi)\nGreek Equivalents: G2112 εὐθέως, G2117 εὐθύς, G3735 ὄρος",
    8206: "שֻׁפִּים (Shuppîym | shoop-peem')\n\nDerivation: plural of an unused noun from the same as H8207 שְׁפִיפֹן and meaning the same; serpents\nStrong's: Shuppim, an Israelite\nKJV: Shuppim.\n\nCognate Group: H7781 (Shuphamite), H8207 (adder), H8206 (Shuppim), H8197 (Shephuphan)",
    8207: "שְׁפִיפֹן (shᵉphîyphôn | shef-ee-fone')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning the same as H7779 שׁוּף\nStrong's: a kind of serpent (as snapping), probably the cerastes or horned adder\nKJV: adder.\n\nCognate Group: H7781 (Shuphamite), H8207 (adder), H8206 (Shuppim), H8197 (Shephuphan)",
    8208: "שָׁפִיר (Shâphîyr | shaf-eer')\n\nDerivation: from H8231 שָׁפַר ; beautiful\nStrong's: Shaphir, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Saphir.\n\nCognate Group: H8237 (royal pavilion), H8233 ([idiom] goodly), H8240 (hook), H8231 ([idiom] goodly), H7782 (cornet), H8208 (Saphir), H8235 (garnish), H8234 (Shapper), H8236 (Shiphrah)",
    8209: "שַׁפִּיר (shappîyr | shap-peer')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) intensive of a form corresponding to H8208 שָׁפִיר\nStrong's: beautiful\nKJV: fair.\n\nCognate Group: H8238 ([idiom] very early in the morning), H8209 (fair), H8232 (be acceptable)\nGreek Equivalents: G5611 ὡραῖος",
    8210: "שָׁפַךְ (shâphak | shaw-fak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to spill forth (blood, a libation, liquid metal; or even a solid, i.e. to mound up); also (figuratively) to expend (life, soul, complaint, money, etc.); intensively, to sprawl out\nKJV: cast (up), gush out, pour (out), shed(-der, out), slip.\n\nCognate Group: H8212 (privy member), H8210 (cast), H8211 (are poured out)\nGreek Equivalents: G906 βάλλω, G1590 ἐκλύω, G1632 ἐκχέω, G1863 ἐπάγω, G1994 ἐπιστρέφω, G2944 κυκλόω, G4016 περιβάλλω, G4046 περιποιέομαι, G4160 ποιέω",
    8211: "שֶׁפֶךְ (shephek | sheh'-fek)\n\nDerivation: from H8210 שָׁפַךְ\nStrong's: an emptying place, e.g. an ash-heap\nKJV: are poured out.\n\nCognate Group: H8212 (privy member), H8210 (cast), H8211 (are poured out)",
    8212: "שׇׁפְכָה (shophkâh | shof-kaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of a derivative from H8210 שָׁפַךְ\nStrong's: a pipe (for pouring forth, e.g. wine), i.e. the penis\nKJV: privy member.\n\nCognate Group: H8212 (privy member), H8210 (cast), H8211 (are poured out)",
    8213: "שָׁפֵל (shâphêl | shaw-fale')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to depress or sink (expectation figuratively, to humiliate, intransitive or transitive)\nKJV: abase, bring (cast, put) down, debase, humble (self), be (bring, lay, make, put) low(-er).\n\nCognate Group: H8223 (Shapham), H8221 (Shepham), H8217 (base), H8216 (low estate), H8213 (abase), H8224 (Siphmoth), H8219 (low country), H8225 (Shiphmite), H8220 (idleness), H8218 (low place)\nGreek Equivalents: G769 ἀσθένεια, G818 ἀτιμάζω, G2598 καταβάλλω, G4098 πίπτω, G5013 ταπεινόω, G5391 φιλόφρων",
    8214: "שְׁפַל (shᵉphal | shef-al')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8213 שָׁפֵל \nStrong's: to depress or sink (expectation figuratively, to humiliate, intransitive or transitive)\nKJV: abase, humble, put down, subdue.\n\nCognate Group: H8214 (abase), H8215 (basest)",
    8215: "שְׁפַל (shᵉphal | shef-al')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H8214 שְׁפַל\nStrong's: low\nKJV: basest.\n\nCognate Group: H8214 (abase), H8215 (basest)",
    8216: "שֶׁפֶל (shephel | shay'-fel)\n\nDerivation: from H8213 שָׁפֵל\nStrong's: an humble rank\nKJV: low estate (place).\n\nCognate Group: H8223 (Shapham), H8221 (Shepham), H8217 (base), H8216 (low estate), H8213 (abase), H8224 (Siphmoth), H8219 (low country), H8225 (Shiphmite), H8220 (idleness), H8218 (low place)\nGreek Equivalents: G5014 ταπείνωσις",
    8217: "שָׁפָל (shâphâl | shaw-fawl')\n\nDerivation: from H8213 שָׁפֵל\nStrong's: depressed, literally or figuratively\nKJV: base(-st), humble, low(-er, -ly).\n\nCognate Group: H8223 (Shapham), H8221 (Shepham), H8217 (base), H8216 (low estate), H8213 (abase), H8224 (Siphmoth), H8219 (low country), H8225 (Shiphmite), H8220 (idleness), H8218 (low place)\nGreek Equivalents: G641 ἀποῤῥίπτω, G772 ἀσθενής, G888 ἀχρεῖος, G5011 ταπεινός",
    8218: "שִׁפְלָה (shiphlâh | shif-law')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H8216 שֶׁפֶל\nStrong's: depression\nKJV: low place.\n\nCognate Group: H8223 (Shapham), H8221 (Shepham), H8217 (base), H8216 (low estate), H8213 (abase), H8224 (Siphmoth), H8219 (low country), H8225 (Shiphmite), H8220 (idleness), H8218 (low place)",
    8219: "שְׁפֵלָה (shᵉphêlâh | shef-ay-law')\n\nDerivation: from H8213 שָׁפֵל\nStrong's: Lowland, i.e. (with the article) the maritime slope of Palestine\nKJV: low country, (low) plain, vale(-ley).\n\nCognate Group: H8223 (Shapham), H8221 (Shepham), H8217 (base), H8216 (low estate), H8213 (abase), H8224 (Siphmoth), H8219 (low country), H8225 (Shiphmite), H8220 (idleness), H8218 (low place)\nGreek Equivalents: G3977 πεδινός, G3977 πεδινός, G3977 πεδινός",
    8220: "שִׁפְלוּת (shiphlûwth | shif-looth')\n\nDerivation: from H8213 שָׁפֵל\nStrong's: remissness\nKJV: idleness.\n\nCognate Group: H8223 (Shapham), H8221 (Shepham), H8217 (base), H8216 (low estate), H8213 (abase), H8224 (Siphmoth), H8219 (low country), H8225 (Shiphmite), H8220 (idleness), H8218 (low place)\nGreek Equivalents: G4164 ποικίλος",
    8221: "שְׁפָם (Shᵉphâm | shef-awm')\n\nDerivation: probably from H8192 שָׁפָה ; bare spot\nStrong's: Shepham, a place in or near Palestine\nKJV: Shepham.\n\nCognate Group: H8223 (Shapham), H8221 (Shepham), H8217 (base), H8216 (low estate), H8213 (abase), H8224 (Siphmoth), H8219 (low country), H8225 (Shiphmite), H8220 (idleness), H8218 (low place)",
    8222: "שָׂפָם (sâphâm | saw-fawm')\n\nDerivation: from H8193 שָׂפָה\nStrong's: the beard (as a lippiece)\nKJV: beard, (upper) lip.\n\nCognate Group: H8193 (band), H8222 (beard)",
    8223: "שָׁפָם (Shâphâm | shaw-fawm')\n\nDerivation: formed like H8221 שְׁפָם ; baldly\nStrong's: Shapham, an Israelite\nKJV: Shapham.\n\nCognate Group: H8223 (Shapham), H8221 (Shepham), H8217 (base), H8216 (low estate), H8213 (abase), H8224 (Siphmoth), H8219 (low country), H8225 (Shiphmite), H8220 (idleness), H8218 (low place)",
    8224: "שִׂפְמֹות (Siphmôwth | sif-moth')\n\nDerivation: feminine plural of H8221 שְׁפָם\nStrong's: Siphmoth, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Siphmoth.\n\nCognate Group: H8223 (Shapham), H8221 (Shepham), H8217 (base), H8216 (low estate), H8213 (abase), H8224 (Siphmoth), H8219 (low country), H8225 (Shiphmite), H8220 (idleness), H8218 (low place)",
    8225: "שִׁפְמִי (Shiphmîy | shif-mee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H8221 שְׁפָם\nStrong's: a Shiphmite or inhabitant of Shepham\nKJV: Shiphmite.\n\nCognate Group: H8223 (Shapham), H8221 (Shepham), H8217 (base), H8216 (low estate), H8213 (abase), H8224 (Siphmoth), H8219 (low country), H8225 (Shiphmite), H8220 (idleness), H8218 (low place)",
    8226: "שָׂפַן (sâphan | saw-fan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to conceal (as a valuable)\nKJV: treasure.\n\nCognate Group: H5603 (cieled), H8226 (treasure), H5600 (ship), H5604 (cieling)",
    8227: "שָׁפָן (shâphân | shaw-fawn')\n\nDerivation: from H8226 שָׂפַן\nStrong's: a species of rockrabbit (from its hiding), i.e. probably the hyrax\nKJV: coney.\n\nCognate Group: H3473 (Ishpan), H8227 (coney)",
