    8230: "שִׁפְעִי (Shiphʻîy | shif-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H8228 שֶׁפַע ; copious\nStrong's: Shiphi, an Israelite\nKJV: Shiphi.\n\nCognate Group: H8229 (abundance), H8228 (abundance), H8230 (Shiphi)",
    8231: "שָׁפַר (shâphar | shaw-far')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to glisten, i.e. (figuratively) be (causatively, make) fair\nKJV: [idiom] goodly.\n\nCognate Group: H8237 (royal pavilion), H8233 ([idiom] goodly), H8240 (hook), H8231 ([idiom] goodly), H7782 (cornet), H8208 (Saphir), H8235 (garnish), H8234 (Shapper), H8236 (Shiphrah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2908 κρεῖσσον, G2909 κρείττων",
    8232: "שְׁפַר (shᵉphar | shef-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8231 שָׁפַר\nStrong's: to be beautiful\nKJV: be acceptable, please, [phrase] think good.\n\nCognate Group: H8238 ([idiom] very early in the morning), H8209 (fair), H8232 (be acceptable)\nGreek Equivalents: G700 ἀρέσκω",
    8233: "שֶׁפֶר (shepher | sheh'-fer)\n\nDerivation: from H8231 שָׁפַר\nStrong's: beauty\nKJV: [idiom] goodly.\n\nCognate Group: H8237 (royal pavilion), H8233 ([idiom] goodly), H8240 (hook), H8231 ([idiom] goodly), H7782 (cornet), H8208 (Saphir), H8235 (garnish), H8234 (Shapper), H8236 (Shiphrah)",
    8234: "שֶׁפֶר (Shepher | sheh'-fer)\n\nDerivation: the same as H8233 שֶׁפֶר\nStrong's: Shepher, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Shapper.\n\nCognate Group: H8237 (royal pavilion), H8233 ([idiom] goodly), H8240 (hook), H8231 ([idiom] goodly), H7782 (cornet), H8208 (Saphir), H8235 (garnish), H8234 (Shapper), H8236 (Shiphrah)",
    8235: "שִׁפְרָה (shiphrâh | shif-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H8231 שָׁפַר\nStrong's: brightness\nKJV: garnish.\n\nCognate Group: H8237 (royal pavilion), H8233 ([idiom] goodly), H8240 (hook), H8231 ([idiom] goodly), H7782 (cornet), H8208 (Saphir), H8235 (garnish), H8234 (Shapper), H8236 (Shiphrah)",
    8236: "שִׁפְרָה (Shiphrâh | shif-raw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H8235 שִׁפְרָה\nStrong's: Shiphrah, an Israelitess\nKJV: Shiphrah.\n\nCognate Group: H8237 (royal pavilion), H8233 ([idiom] goodly), H8240 (hook), H8231 ([idiom] goodly), H7782 (cornet), H8208 (Saphir), H8235 (garnish), H8234 (Shapper), H8236 (Shiphrah)",
    8237: "שַׁפְרוּר (shaphrûwr | shaf-roor')\n\nDerivation: from H8231 שָׁפַר\nStrong's: splendid, i.e. a tapestry or canopy\nKJV: royal pavilion.\n\nCognate Group: H8237 (royal pavilion), H8233 ([idiom] goodly), H8240 (hook), H8231 ([idiom] goodly), H7782 (cornet), H8208 (Saphir), H8235 (garnish), H8234 (Shapper), H8236 (Shiphrah)",
    8238: "שְׁפַרְפַר (shᵉpharphar | shef-ar-far')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H8231 שָׁפַר\nStrong's: the dawn (as brilliant with aurora)\nKJV: [idiom] very early in the morning.\n\nCognate Group: H8238 ([idiom] very early in the morning), H8209 (fair), H8232 (be acceptable)",
    8239: "שָׁפַת (shâphath | shaw-fath')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to locate, i.e. (generally) hang on or (figuratively) establish, reduce\nKJV: bring, ordain, set on.\n\nCognate Group: H8239 (bring), H4942 (burden), H8240 (hook), H830 (dung)",
    8240: "שָׁפָת (shâphâth | shaw-fawth')\n\nDerivation: from H8239 שָׁפַת\nStrong's: a (double) stall (for cattle); also a (two-pronged) hook (for flaying animals on)\nKJV: hook, pot.\n\nCognate Group: H8239 (bring), H4942 (burden), H8240 (hook), H830 (dung)",
    8241: "שֶׁצֶף (shetseph | sheh'-tsef)\n\nDerivation: from H7857 שָׁטַף (for alliteration with H7110 קֶצֶף)\nStrong's: an outburst (of anger)\nKJV: little.\n\nCognate Group: H8241 (little), H7857 (drown), H7858 (flood)\nGreek Equivalents: G3398 μικρός",
    8242: "שַׂק (saq | sak)\n\nDerivation: from H8264 שָׁקַק\nStrong's: properly, a mesh (as allowing a liquid to run through), i.e. coarse loose cloth or sacking (used in mourning and for bagging); hence, a bag (for grain, etc.)\nKJV: sack(-cloth, -clothes).\n\nCognate Group: H8242 (sack)\nGreek Equivalents: G4526 σάκκος",
    8243: "שָׁק (shâq | shawk)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7785 שֹׁוק\nStrong's: the leg\nKJV: leg.\n\nCognate Group: H7792 (wall), H8243 (leg), H7801 (Susanchites)",
    8244: "שָׂקַד (sâqad | saw-kad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to fasten\nKJV: bind.\n\nCognate Group: H8244 (bind)",
    8245: "שָׁקַד (shâqad | shaw-kad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be alert, i.e. sleepless; hence to be on the lookout (whether for good or ill)\nKJV: hasten, remain, wake, watch (for).\n\nCognate Group: H8246 (make like almonds), H8245 (hasten), H8247 (almond)\nGreek Equivalents: G69 ἀγρυπνέω, G1127 γρηγορεύω",
    8246: "שָׁקַד (shâqad | shaw-kad')\n\nDerivation: a denominative from H8247 שָׁקֵד\nStrong's: to be (intensively, make) almond-shaped\nKJV: make like (unto, after the fashion of) almonds.\n\nCognate Group: H8246 (make like almonds), H8245 (hasten), H8247 (almond)",
    8247: "שָׁקֵד (shâqêd | shaw-kade')\n\nDerivation: from H8245 שָׁקַד\nStrong's: the almond (tree or nut; as being the earliest in bloom)\nKJV: almond (tree).\n\nCognate Group: H8246 (make like almonds), H8245 (hasten), H8247 (almond)",
    8248: "שָׁקָה (shâqâh | shaw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to quaff, i.e. (causatively) to irrigate or furnish apotion to\nKJV: cause to (give, give to, let, make to) drink, drown, moisten, water. See H7937 שָׁכַר, H8354 שָׁתָה .\n\nCognate Group: H8250 (drink), H4945 (butler), H8249 (drink), H8248 (cause to drink), H8268 (trough)\nGreek Equivalents: G4095 πίνω, G4222 ποτίζω",
    8249: "שִׁקֻּו (shiqquv | shif-koov')\n\nDerivation: from H8248 שָׁקָה\nStrong's: (plural collective) a draught\nKJV: drink.\n\nCognate Group: H8250 (drink), H4945 (butler), H8249 (drink), H8248 (cause to drink), H8268 (trough)",
    8250: "שִׁקּוּי (shiqqûwy | shik-koo'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H8248 שָׁקָה\nStrong's: a beverage; moisture, i.e. (figuratively) refreshment\nKJV: drink, marrow.\n\nCognate Group: H8250 (drink), H4945 (butler), H8249 (drink), H8248 (cause to drink), H8268 (trough)\nGreek Equivalents: G1958 ἐπιμέλεια, G4188 πόμα",
    8251: "שִׁקּוּץ (shiqqûwts | shik-koots')\n\nDerivation: or שִׁקֻּץ; from H8262 שָׁקַץ\nStrong's: disgusting, i.e. filthy; especially idolatrous or (concretely) an idol\nKJV: abominable filth (idol, -ation), detestable (thing).\n\nCognate Group: H8251 (abominable filth), H8263 (abominable), H8262 (abhor)\nGreek Equivalents: G946 βδέλυγμα, G948 βδελύσσω, G1497 εἴδωλον, G3393 μίασμα",
    8252: "שָׁקַט (shâqaṭ | shaw-kat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to repose (usually figurative)\nKJV: appease, idleness, (at, be at, be in, give) quiet(-ness), (be at, be in, give, have, take) rest, settle, be still.\n\nCognate Group: H8253 (quietness), H8252 (appease)\nGreek Equivalents: G372 ἀνάπαυσις, G373 ἀναπαύω, G447 ἀνίημι, G803 ἀσφάλεια, G1514 εἰρηνεύω, G1515 εἰρήνη, G2270 ἡσυχάζω, G2271 ἡσυχία, G2664 καταπαύω, G2869 κοπάζω, G3930 παρέχω, G3982 πείθω, G4684 σπαταλάω",
    8253: "שֶׁקֶט (sheqeṭ | sheh'-ket)\n\nDerivation: from H8252 שָׁקַט\nStrong's: tranquillity\nKJV: quietness.\n\nCognate Group: H8253 (quietness), H8252 (appease)",
    8254: "שָׁקַל (shâqal | shaw-kal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to suspend or poise (especially in trade)\nKJV: pay, receive(-r), spend, [idiom] throughly, weigh.\n\nCognate Group: H4949 (plummet), H4948 (weight), H8254 (pay), H4946 (weight), H8255 (shekel), H8256 (sycamore)\nGreek Equivalents: G600 ἀποκαθίστημι, G661 ἀποτίνω, G2476 ἵστημι, G3936 παρίστημι, G4820 συμβάλλω, G5091 τιμάω",
    8255: "שֶׁקֶל (sheqel | sheh'-kel)\n\nDerivation: from H8254 שָׁקַל\nStrong's: probably a weight; used as a commercial standard\nKJV: shekel.\n\nCognate Group: H4949 (plummet), H4948 (weight), H8254 (pay), H4946 (weight), H8255 (shekel), H8256 (sycamore)\nGreek Equivalents: G1323 δίδραχμον, G1406 δραχμή",
    8256: "שִׁקְמָה (shiqmâh | shik-maw')\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) שִׁקְמָה; of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a sycamore (usually the tree)\nKJV: sycamore (fruit, tree).\n\nCognate Group: H4949 (plummet), H4948 (weight), H8254 (pay), H4946 (weight), H8255 (shekel), H8256 (sycamore)\nGreek Equivalents: G4807 συκάμινος",
    8257: "שָׁקַע (shâqaʻ | shaw-kah')\n\nDerivation: (abbreviated Amos 8:8); a primitive root\nStrong's: to subside; by implication, to be overflowed, cease; causatively, to abate, subdue\nKJV: make deep, let down, drown, quench, sink.\n\nCognate Group: H8257 (make deep), H4950 (deep)\nGreek Equivalents: G2270 ἡσυχάζω, G2597 καταβαίνω, G2869 κοπάζω",
    8258: "שְׁקַעְרוּרָה (shᵉqaʻrûwrâh | shek-ah-roo-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H8257 שָׁקַע\nStrong's: a depression\nKJV: hollow strake.\n\nCognate Group: H7086 (charger), H8258 (hollow strake)",
    8259: "שָׁקַף (shâqaph | shaw-kaf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to lean out (of a window), i.e. (by implication) peep or gaze (passively, be a spectacle)\nKJV: appear, look (down, forth, out).\n\nCognate Group: H8259 (appear)\nGreek Equivalents: G991 βλέπω, G1914 ἐπιβλέπω, G3879 παρακύπτω, G3905 παρατείνω",
    8260: "שֶׁקֶף (sheqeph | sheh'-kef)\n\nDerivation: from H8259 שָׁקַף\nStrong's: a loophole (for looking out), to admit light and air\nKJV: window.\n\nCognate Group: H8261 (light), H4947 (lintel), H8260 (window)",
    8261: "שָׁקֻף (shâquph | shaw-koof')\n\nDerivation: passive participle of H8259 שָׁקַף ; (compare H8260 שֶׁקֶף)\n\nStrong's: an embrasure or opening with bevelled jam\nKJV: light, window.\n\nCognate Group: H8261 (light), H4947 (lintel), H8260 (window)",
    8262: "שָׁקַץ (shâqats | shaw-kats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be filthy, i.e. (intensively) to loathe, pollute\nKJV: abhor, make abominable, have in abomination, detest, [idiom] utterly.\n\nCognate Group: H8251 (abominable filth), H8263 (abominable), H8262 (abhor)\nGreek Equivalents: G948 βδελύσσω, G4360 προσοχθίζω",
    8263: "שֶׁקֶץ (sheqets | sheh'-kets)\n\nDerivation: from H8262 שָׁקַץ\nStrong's: filth, i.e. (figuratively and specifically) an idolatrous object\nKJV: abominable(-tion).\n\nCognate Group: H8251 (abominable filth), H8263 (abominable), H8262 (abhor)\nGreek Equivalents: G946 βδέλυγμα",
    8264: "שָׁקַק (shâqaq | shaw-kak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to course (like a beast of prey); by implication, to seek greedily\nKJV: have appetite, justle one against another, long, range, run (to and fro).\n\nCognate Group: H8264 (have appetite), H4944 (running to and fro)\nGreek Equivalents: G1372 διψάω, G1679 ἐλπίζω, G1949 ἐπιλαμβάνομαι, G2756 κενός",
    8265: "שָׂקַר (sâqar | saw-kar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to ogle, i.e. blink coquettishly\nKJV: wanton.\n\nCognate Group: H8272 (Sharezer), H8265 (wanton)",
    8266: "שָׁקַר (shâqar | shaw-kar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to cheat, i.e. be untrue (usually in words)\nKJV: fail, deal falsely, lie.\n\nCognate Group: H8266 (fail), H8267 (without a cause)\nGreek Equivalents: G91 ἀδικέω, G114 ἀθετέω, G654 ἀποστρέφω, G4811 συκοφαντέω",
    8267: "שֶׁקֶר (sheqer | sheh'-ker)\n\nDerivation: from H8266 שָׁקַר\nStrong's: an untruth; by implication, a sham (often adverbial)\nKJV: without a cause, deceit(-ful), false(-hood, -ly), feignedly, liar, [phrase] lie, lying, vain (thing), wrongfully.\n\nCognate Group: H8266 (fail), H8267 (without a cause)\nGreek Equivalents: G93 ἀδικία, G94 ἄδικος, G95 ἀδίκως, G458 ἀνομία, G459 ἄνομος, G1386 δόλιος, G2756 κενός, G3154 ματαιόω, G5571 ψευδής, G5579 ψεῦδος",
    8268: "שֹׁקֶת (shôqeth | sho'-keth)\n\nDerivation: from H8248 שָׁקָה\nStrong's: a trough (for watering)\nKJV: trough.\n\nCognate Group: H8250 (drink), H4945 (butler), H8249 (drink), H8248 (cause to drink), H8268 (trough)\nGreek Equivalents: G2270 ἡσυχάζω",
    8269: "שַׂר (sar | sar)\n\nDerivation: from H8323 שָׂרַר\nStrong's: a head person (of any rank or class)\nKJV: captain (that had rule), chief (captain), general, governor, keeper, lord,(-task-)master, prince(-ipal), ruler, steward.\n\nCognate Group: H7786 (make princes), H8323 ([idiom] altogether), H8269 (captain), H8283 (Sarah), H8297 (Sarai), H8282 (lady)\nGreek Equivalents: G32 ἄγγελος, G747 ἀρχηγός, G758 ἄρχων, G935 βασιλεύς, G1240 διάδοχος, G1413 δυνάστης, G1543 ἑκατοντάρχης, G1543 ἑκατοντάρχης, G1658 ἐλεύθερος, G1741 ἔνδοξος, G1784 ἔντιμος, G1988 ἐπιστάτης, G2232 ἡγεμών, G2233 ἡγέομαι, G3175 μεγιστᾶνες, G3966 πατριάρχης, G3966 πατριάρχης, G4755 στρατηγός, G5015 ταράσσω, G5506 χιλίαρχος",
    8270: "שֹׁר (shôr | shore)\n\nDerivation: from H8324 שָׁרַר ; (compare H8306 שָׁרִיר)\n\nStrong's: a string (as twisted), i.e. (specifically) the umbilical cord (also figuratively, as the centre of strength)\nKJV: navel.\n\nCognate Group: H8326 (navel), H8307 (imagination), H8285 (bracelet), H8325 (Sharar), H8270 (navel), H8306 (navel), H8333 (chain)",
    8271: "שְׁרֵא (shᵉrêʼ | sher-ay')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) a root corresponding to that of H8293 שֵׁרוּת\nStrong's: to free, separate; figuratively, to unravel, commence; by implication (of unloading beasts) to reside\nKJV: begin, dissolve, dwell, loose.\n\nCognate Group: H8271 (begin)\nGreek Equivalents: G757 ἄρχω, G1262 διαλύω, G3089 λύω",
    8272: "שַׁרְאֶצֶר (Sharʼetser | shar-eh'-tser)\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Sharetser, the name of an Assyrian and an Israelite\nKJV: Sharezer.\n\nCognate Group: H8272 (Sharezer), H8265 (wanton)",
    8273: "שָׁרָב (shârâb | shaw-rawb')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to glare\nStrong's: quivering glow (of the air), expectation. the mirage\nKJV: heat, parched ground.\n\nCognate Group: H8273 (heat), H8274 (Sherebiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G504 ἄνυδρος, G2742 καύσων",
    8274: "שֵׁרֵבְיָה (Shêrêbᵉyâh | shay-rayb-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H8273 שָׁרָב and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has brought heat\nStrong's: Sherebjah, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Sherebiah.\n\nCognate Group: H8273 (heat), H8274 (Sherebiah)",
    8275: "שַׁרְבִיט (sharbîyṭ | shar-beet')\n\nDerivation: for H7626 שֵׁבֶט\nStrong's: a rod of empire\nKJV: sceptre.\n\nCognate Group: H7627 (Sebat), H8275 (sceptre), H7626 ([idiom] correction)\nGreek Equivalents: G4464 ῥάβδος",
    8276: "שָׂרַג (sârag | saw-rag')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to intwine\nKJV: wrap together, wreath.\n\nCognate Group: H8299 (branch), H8286 (Serug), H8276 (wrap together)\nGreek Equivalents: G4553 σαργάνη",
    8277: "שָׂרַד (sârad | saw-rad')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; (compare H8279 שֶׂרֶד)\n\nStrong's: properly, to puncture, i.e. (figuratively through the idea of slipping out) to escape or survive\nKJV: remain.\n\nCognate Group: H8277 (remain), H8301 (Sarid), H8300 ([idiom] alive)\nGreek Equivalents: G1295 διασώζω",
    8278: "שְׂרָד (sᵉrâd | ser-awd')\n\nDerivation: from H8277 שָׂרַד\nStrong's: stitching (as pierced with a needle)\nKJV: service.\n\nCognate Group: H8279 (line), H8278 (service)",
    8279: "שֶׂרֶד (sered | seh'-red)\n\nDerivation: from H8277 שָׂרַד\nStrong's: a (carpenter's) scribing-awl (for pricking or scratching measurements)\nKJV: line.\n\nCognate Group: H8279 (line), H8278 (service)",
    8280: "שָׂרָה (sârâh | saw-raw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to prevail\nKJV: have power (as a prince).\n\nCognate Group: H7798 (Shavsha), H8304 (Seraiah), H3478 (Israel), H3481 (of Israel), H8280 (have power), H3482 (Israelitish)\nGreek Equivalents: G544 ἀπειθέω, G2933 κτῆμα",
    8281: "שָׁרָה (shârâh | shaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to free\nKJV: direct.\n\nCognate Group: H8293 (remnant), H8281 (direct)",
    8282: "שָׂרָה (sârâh | saw-raw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H8269 שַׂר\nStrong's: a mistress, i.e. female noble\nKJV: lady, princess, queen.\n\nCognate Group: H7786 (make princes), H8323 ([idiom] altogether), H8269 (captain), H8283 (Sarah), H8297 (Sarai), H8282 (lady)",
    8283: "שָׂרָה (Sârâh | saw-raw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H8282 שָׂרָה\nStrong's: Sarah, Abraham's wife\nKJV: Sarah.\n\nCognate Group: H7786 (make princes), H8323 ([idiom] altogether), H8269 (captain), H8283 (Sarah), H8297 (Sarai), H8282 (lady)\nGreek Equivalents: G4564 Σάῤῥα",
    8284: "שָׁרָה (shârâh | shaw-raw')\n\nDerivation: probably feminine of H7791 שׁוּר\nStrong's: a fortification (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: sing (by mistake for H7891 שִׁיר), wall.\n\nCognate Group: H7803 (Shuthelah), H8364 (Shuthalhites), H7793 (Shur), H7802 (Shoshannim-Eduth), H7799 (lily), H7800 (Shushan), H8284 (sing), H7791 (wall), H7794 (bull)",
    8285: "שֵׁרָה (shêrâh | shay-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H8324 שָׁרַר in its original sense of pressing\nStrong's: a wrist-band (as compact or clasping)\nKJV: bracelet.\n\nCognate Group: H8326 (navel), H8307 (imagination), H8285 (bracelet), H8325 (Sharar), H8270 (navel), H8306 (navel), H8333 (chain)",
    8286: "שְׂרוּג (Sᵉrûwg | ser-oog')\n\nDerivation: from H8276 שָׂרַג ; tendril\nStrong's: Serug, a postdiluvian patriarch\nKJV: Serug.\n\nCognate Group: H8299 (branch), H8286 (Serug), H8276 (wrap together)\nGreek Equivalents: G4562 Σαρούχ",
    8287: "שָׁרוּחֶן (Shârûwchen | shaw-roo-khen')\n\nDerivation: probably from H8281 שָׁרָה (in the sense of dwelling (compare H8271 שְׁרֵא) and H2580 חֵן ; abode of pleasure\nStrong's: Sharuchen, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Sharuhen.\n\nCognate Group: H8287 (Sharuhen), H8302 (breastplate), H8298 (Sharai)",
    8288: "שְׂרֹוךְ (sᵉrôwk | ser-oke')\n\nDerivation: from H8308 שָׂרַךְ\nStrong's: a thong (as laced or tied)\nKJV: (shoe-)latchet.\n\nCognate Group: H8288 (latchet), H8308 (traverse), H8310 (Sarsechim)\nGreek Equivalents: G2438 ἱμάς",
    8289: "שָׁרֹון (Shârôwn | shaw-rone')\n\nDerivation: probably abridged from H3474 יָשַׁר\nStrong's: plain, Sharon, the name of a place in Palestine\nKJV: Lasharon, Sharon.\n\nCognate Group: H3483 (uprightness), H3474 (direct), H4339 (agreement), H3477 (convenient), H4334 (equity), H3475 (Jesher), H8289 (Lasharon), H8290 (Sharonite), H3484 (Jeshurun), H3476 (equity)\nGreek Equivalents: G4565 Σάρων",
    8290: "שָׁרֹונִי (Shârôwnîy | shaw-ro-nee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H8289 שָׁרֹון\nStrong's: a Sharonite or inhabitant of Sharon\nKJV: Sharonite.\n\nCognate Group: H3483 (uprightness), H3474 (direct), H4339 (agreement), H3477 (convenient), H4334 (equity), H3475 (Jesher), H8289 (Lasharon), H8290 (Sharonite), H3484 (Jeshurun), H3476 (equity)",
    8291: "שָׂרוּק (sârûwq | sar-ook')\n\nDerivation: passive participle from the same as H8321 שֹׂרֵק\nStrong's: a grapevine\nKJV: principal plant. See H8320 שָׂרֻק, H8321 שֹׂרֵק .\n\nCognate Group: H7796 (Sorek), H8291 (principal plant), H8321 (choice wine), H4957 (Masrekah), H8320 (speckled)",
    8292: "שְׁרוּקָה (shᵉrûwqâh | sher-oo-kaw')\n\nDerivation: or (by permutation) שְׁרִיקָה; feminine passive participle of H8319 שָׁרַק\nStrong's: a whistling (in scorn); by analogy, a piping\nKJV: bleating, hissing.\n\nCognate Group: H8319 (hiss), H8322 (hissing), H8292 (bleating)",
    8293: "שֵׁרוּת (shêrûwth | shay-rooth')\n\nDerivation: from H8281 שָׁרָה abbreviated\nStrong's: freedom\nKJV: remnant.\n\nCognate Group: H8293 (remnant), H8281 (direct)",
    8294: "שֶׂרַח (Serach | seh'-rakh)\n\nDerivation: by permutation for H5629 סֶרַח ; superfluity\nStrong's: Serach, an Israelitess\nKJV: Sarah, Serah.\n\nCognate Group: H8294 (Sarah), H4951 (government)",
    8295: "שָׂרַט (sâraṭ | saw-rat')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to gash\nKJV: cut in pieces, make (cuttings) pieces.\n\nCognate Group: H8303 (Sirion), H8296 (cutting), H8295 (cut in pieces)",
    8296: "שֶׂרֶט (sereṭ | seh'-ret)\n\nDerivation: and שָׂרֶטֶת; from H8295 שָׂרַט\nStrong's: an incision\nKJV: cutting.\n\nCognate Group: H8303 (Sirion), H8296 (cutting), H8295 (cut in pieces)",
    8297: "שָׂרַי (Sâray | saw-rah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H8269 שַׂר ; dominative\nStrong's: Sarai, the wife of Abraham\nKJV: Sarai.\n\nCognate Group: H7786 (make princes), H8323 ([idiom] altogether), H8269 (captain), H8283 (Sarah), H8297 (Sarai), H8282 (lady)",
    8298: "שָׁרַי (Shâray | shaw-rah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: probably from H8324 שָׁרַר ; hostile\nStrong's: Sharay, an Israelite\nKJV: Sharai.\n\nCognate Group: H8287 (Sharuhen), H8302 (breastplate), H8298 (Sharai)",
    8299: "שָׂרִיג (sârîyg | saw-reeg')\n\nDerivation: from H8276 שָׂרַג\nStrong's: a tendril (as entwining)\nKJV: branch.\n\nCognate Group: H8299 (branch), H8286 (Serug), H8276 (wrap together)\nGreek Equivalents: G2814 κλῆμα",
    8300: "שָׂרִיד (sârîyd | saw-reed')\n\nDerivation: from H8277 שָׂרַד\nStrong's: a survivor\nKJV: [idiom] alive, left, remain(-ing), remnant, rest.\n\nCognate Group: H8277 (remain), H8301 (Sarid), H8300 ([idiom] alive)\nGreek Equivalents: G1309 διαφεύγω, G2640 κατάλειμμα, G2640 κατάλειμμα, G2641 καταλείπω, G2645 κατάλοιπος, G4982 σώζω, G5343 φεύγω",
    8301: "שָׂרִיד (Sârîyd | suw-reed')\n\nDerivation: the same as H8300 שָׂרִיד\nStrong's: Sarid, a place in Plestine\nKJV: Sarid.\n\nCognate Group: H8277 (remain), H8301 (Sarid), H8300 ([idiom] alive)",
    8302: "שִׁרְיֹון (shiryôwn | shir-yone')\n\nDerivation: or שִׁרְיֹן; and שִׁרְיָן; also (feminine) שִׁרְיָה; and שִׁרְיֹנָה; from H8281 שָׁרָה in the original sense of turning\nStrong's: a corslet (as if twisted)\nKJV: breastplate, coat of mail, habergeon, harness. See H5630 סִרְיֹן .\n\nCognate Group: H8302 (breastplate)\nGreek Equivalents: G2382 θώραξ, G2382 θώραξ",
    8303: "שִׁרְיֹון (Shiryôwn | shir-yone')\n\nDerivation: and שִׂרְיֹן; the same as H8304 שְׂרָיָה (i.e. sheeted with snow)\nStrong's: Shirjon or Sirjon, a peak of the Lebanon\nKJV: Sirion.\n\nCognate Group: H8303 (Sirion), H8296 (cutting), H8295 (cut in pieces)",
    8304: "שְׂרָיָה (Sᵉrâyâh | ser-aw-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or שְׂרָיָהוּ; from H8280 שָׂרָה and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has prevailed\nStrong's: Serajah, the name of nine Israelites\nKJV: Seraiah.\n\nCognate Group: H7798 (Shavsha), H8304 (Seraiah), H3478 (Israel), H3481 (of Israel), H8280 (have power), H3482 (Israelitish)",
    8305: "שְׂרִיקָה (sᵉrîyqâh | ser-ee-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H8321 שֹׂרֵק in the original sense of piercing\nStrong's: hetchelling (or combing flax), i.e. (concretely) tow (by extension, linen cloth)\nKJV: fine.\n\nCognate Group: H8305 (fine)",
    8306: "שָׁרִיר (shârîyr | shaw-reer')\n\nDerivation: from H8324 שָׁרַר in the original sense as in H8270 שֹׁר (compare H8326 שֹׁרֶר)\nStrong's: a cord, i.e. (by analogy) sinew\nKJV: navel.\n\nCognate Group: H8326 (navel), H8307 (imagination), H8285 (bracelet), H8325 (Sharar), H8270 (navel), H8306 (navel), H8333 (chain)",
    8307: "שְׁרִירוּת (shᵉrîyrûwth | sher-ee-rooth')\n\nDerivation: from H8324 שָׁרַר in the sense of twisted, i.e. firm\nStrong's: obstinacy\nKJV: imagination, lust.\n\nCognate Group: H8326 (navel), H8307 (imagination), H8285 (bracelet), H8325 (Sharar), H8270 (navel), H8306 (navel), H8333 (chain)\nGreek Equivalents: G701 ἀρεστός, G2307 θέλημα, G4106 πλάνη",
    8308: "שָׂרַךְ (sârak | saw-rak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to interlace\nKJV: traverse.\n\nCognate Group: H8288 (latchet), H8308 (traverse), H8310 (Sarsechim)\nGreek Equivalents: G2233 ἡγέομαι",
    8309: "שְׁרֵמָה (shᵉrêmâh | sher-ay-maw')\n\nDerivation: probably by an orthographical error for H7709 שְׁדֵמָה\nStrong's: a common\nKJV: field.\n\nCognate Group: H8309 (field), H7709 (blasted)",
    8310: "שַׂרְסְכִים (Sarçᵉkîym | sar-seh-keem')\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Sarsekim, a Babylonian general\nKJV: Sarsechim.\n\nCognate Group: H8288 (latchet), H8308 (traverse), H8310 (Sarsechim)",
    8311: "שָׂרַע (sâraʻ | saw-rah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to prolong, i.e. (reflex) be deformed by excess of members\nKJV: stretch out self, (have any) superfluous thing.\n\nCognate Group: H8311 (stretch out self)",
    8312: "שַׂרְעַף (sarʻaph | sar-af')\n\nDerivation: for H5587 סָעִף\nStrong's: cogitation\nKJV: thought.\n\nCognate Group: H5587 (opinion), H8312 (thought)",
    8313: "שָׂרַף (sâraph | saw-raf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be (causatively, set) on fire\nKJV: (cause to, make a) burn((-ing), up) kindle, [idiom] utterly.\n\nCognate Group: H4956 (Misrephoth-mayim), H8314 (fiery), H8315 (Saraph), H5635 (burn), H8316 (burning), H8313 (burn), H4955 (burning)\nGreek Equivalents: G1143 δάκνω, G2289 θανατόω, G2545 καίω, G2618 κατακαίω, G2664 καταπαύω",
    8314: "שָׂרָף (sârâph | saw-rawf')\n\nDerivation: from H8313 שָׂרַף\nStrong's: burning, i.e. (figuratively) poisonous (serpent); specifically, a saraph or symbolical creature (from their copper color)\nKJV: fiery (serpent), seraph.\n\nCognate Group: H4956 (Misrephoth-mayim), H8314 (fiery), H8315 (Saraph), H5635 (burn), H8316 (burning), H8313 (burn), H4955 (burning)\nGreek Equivalents: G785 ἀσπίς, G3789 ὄφις",
    8315: "שָׂרָף (Sârâph | saw-raf')\n\nDerivation: the same as H8314 שָׂרָף\nStrong's: Saraph, an Israelite\nKJV: Saraph.\n\nCognate Group: H4956 (Misrephoth-mayim), H8314 (fiery), H8315 (Saraph), H5635 (burn), H8316 (burning), H8313 (burn), H4955 (burning)",
    8316: "שְׂרֵפָה (sᵉrêphâh | ser-ay-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H8313 שָׂרַף\nStrong's: cremation\nKJV: burning.\n\nCognate Group: H4956 (Misrephoth-mayim), H8314 (fiery), H8315 (Saraph), H5635 (burn), H8316 (burning), H8313 (burn), H4955 (burning)\nGreek Equivalents: G4442 πῦρ",
    8317: "שָׁרַץ (shârats | shaw-rats')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to wriggle, i.e. (by implication) swarm or abound\nKJV: breed (bring forth, increase) abundantly (in abundance), creep, move.\n\nCognate Group: H8317 (breed abundantly), H8318 (creep)\nGreek Equivalents: G1806 ἐξάγω, G2795 κινέω, G4129 πληθύνω",
    8318: "שֶׁרֶץ (sherets | sheh'-rets)\n\nDerivation: from H8317 שָׁרַץ\nStrong's: a swarm, i.e. active mass of minute animals\nKJV: creep(-ing thing), move(-ing creature).\n\nCognate Group: H8317 (breed abundantly), H8318 (creep)\nGreek Equivalents: G2044 ἐρεύγομαι, G2062 ἑρπετόν",
    8319: "שָׁרַק (shâraq | shaw-rak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: properly, to be shrill, i.e. to whistle or hiss (as a call or in scorn)\nKJV: hiss.\n\nCognate Group: H8319 (hiss), H8322 (hissing), H8292 (bleating)",
    8320: "שָׂרֻק (sâruq | saw-rook')\n\nDerivation: from H8319 שָׁרַק\nStrong's: bright red (as piercing to the sight), i.e. bay\nKJV: speckled. See H8291 שָׂרוּק .\n\nCognate Group: H7796 (Sorek), H8291 (principal plant), H8321 (choice wine), H4957 (Masrekah), H8320 (speckled)",
