    8322: "שְׁרֵקָה (shᵉrêqâh | sher-ay-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from H8319 שָׁרַק\nStrong's: a derision\nKJV: hissing.\n\nCognate Group: H8319 (hiss), H8322 (hissing), H8292 (bleating)",
    8323: "שָׂרַר (sârar | saw-rar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to have (transitively, exercise; reflexively, get) dominion\nKJV: [idiom] altogether, make self a prince, (bear) rule.\n\nCognate Group: H7786 (make princes), H8323 ([idiom] altogether), H8269 (captain), H8283 (Sarah), H8297 (Sarai), H8282 (lady)",
    8324: "שָׁרַר (shârar | shaw-rar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be hostile (only active participle an opponent)\nKJV: enemy.\n\nCognate Group: H7789 (behold), H8324 (enemy), H7790 (enemy)",
    8325: "שָׁרַר (Shârar | shaw-rawr')\n\nDerivation: from H8324 שָׁרַר ; hostile\nStrong's: Sharar, an Israelite\nKJV: Sharar.\n\nCognate Group: H8326 (navel), H8307 (imagination), H8285 (bracelet), H8325 (Sharar), H8270 (navel), H8306 (navel), H8333 (chain)",
    8326: "שֹׁרֶר (shôrer | sho'-rer)\n\nDerivation: from H8324 שָׁרַר in the sense of twisting (compare H8270 שֹׁר)\nStrong's: the umbilical cord, i.e. (by extension) a bodice\nKJV: navel.\n\nCognate Group: H8326 (navel), H8307 (imagination), H8285 (bracelet), H8325 (Sharar), H8270 (navel), H8306 (navel), H8333 (chain)",
