    8336: "שֵׁשׁ (shêsh | shaysh)\n\nDerivation: or (for alliteration with H4897 מֶשִׁי) שְׁשִׁי; for H7893 שַׁיִשׁ\nStrong's: bleached stuff, i.e. white linen or (by analogy) marble\nKJV: [idiom] blue, fine (twined) linen, marble, silk.\n\nCognate Group: H8336 ([idiom] blue), H7893 (white), H7895 (Shishak), H7894 (Shisha)\nGreek Equivalents: G1039 βύσσινος, G1040 βύσσος, G3035 λίθινος, G3461 μυριάς",
    8337: "שֵׁשׁ (shêsh | shaysh)\n\nDerivation: masculine שִׁשָּׁה; a primitive number; compare H7797 שׂוּשׂ \nStrong's: six (as an overplus beyond five or the fingers of the hand); as ord. sixth\nKJV: six(-teen, -teenth), sixth.\n\nCognate Group: H8346 (sixty), H8341 (give the sixth participle), H7864 (Sheva), H7724 (Sheva), H7719 (Shoham), H8337 (six), H7718 (onyx), H8345 (sixth)",
    8338: "שָׁשָׁא (shâshâʼ | shaw-shaw')Typo: xlit shâwshâw corrected to shâshâʼ\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; apparently,\nStrong's: to annihilate\nKJV: leave by the sixth part (by confusion with H8341 שָׁשָׁה).\n\nCognate Group: H8350 (vermillion), H8348 (Sheshan), H8343 (Shashai), H8339 (Sheshbazzar), H8344 (Sheshai), H8347 (Sheshach), H8349 (Shashak), H8338 (leave by the sixth part)",
