    8340: "שֵׁשְׁבַּצַּר (Shêshᵉbatstsar | shaysh-bats-tsar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8339 שֵׁשְׁבַּצַּר \nStrong's: Sheshbatstsar, Zerubbabel's Persian name\nKJV: Sheshbazzar.\n\nCognate Group: H8332 (banishment), H8330 (root), H8340 (Sheshbazzar)",
    8341: "שָׁשָׁה (shâshâh | shaw-shaw')\n\nDerivation: a denominative from H8337 שֵׁשׁ\nStrong's: to sixth or divide into sixths\nKJV: give the sixth participle\n\nCognate Group: H8346 (sixty), H8341 (give the sixth participle), H7864 (Sheva), H7724 (Sheva), H7719 (Shoham), H8337 (six), H7718 (onyx), H8345 (sixth)",
