    8354: "שָׁתָה (shâthâh | shaw-thaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to imbibe (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: [idiom] assuredly, banquet, [idiom] certainly, drink(-er, -ing), drunk ([idiom] -ard), surely. (Prop. intensive of H8248 שָׁקָה .)\n\nCognate Group: H4960 (banquet), H8354 ([idiom] assuredly), H8360 (drinking), H8358 (drunkenness)\nGreek Equivalents: G3182 μεθύσκω, G4095 πίνω",
