    8356: "שָׁתָה (shâthâh | shaw-thaw')\n\nDerivation: from H7896 שִׁית\nStrong's: a basis, i.e. (figuratively) political or moral support\nKJV: foundation, purpose.\n\nCognate Group: H8352 (Seth), H8356 (foundation), H7896 (apply), H7898 (thorns), H7897 (attire)\nGreek Equivalents: G2038 ἐργάζομαι, G2675 καταρτίζω",
    8357: "שֵׁתָה (shêthâh | shay-thaw')\n\nDerivation: from H7896 שִׁית\nStrong's: the seat (of the person)\nKJV: buttock.\n\nCognate Group: H8357 (buttock)",
    8358: "שְׁתִי (shᵉthîy | sheth-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H8354 שָׁתָה\nStrong's: intoxicaion\nKJV: drunkenness.\n\nCognate Group: H4960 (banquet), H8354 ([idiom] assuredly), H8360 (drinking), H8358 (drunkenness)",
    8359: "שְׁתִי (shᵉthîy | sheth-ee')\n\nDerivation: from H7896 שִׁית\nStrong's: a fixture, i.e. the warp in weaving\nKJV: warp.\n\nCognate Group: H8359 (warp)",
    8360: "שְׁתִיָּה (shᵉthîyâh | sheth-ee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H8358 שְׁתִי\nStrong's: potation\nKJV: drinking.\n\nCognate Group: H4960 (banquet), H8354 ([idiom] assuredly), H8360 (drinking), H8358 (drunkenness)",
    8361: "שִׁתִּין (shittîyn | shit-teen')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8346 שִׁשִּׁים (compare H8353 שֵׁת)\nStrong's: sixty\nKJV: threescore.\n\nCognate Group: H8353 (six), H8361 (threescore)",
    8362: "שָׁתַל (shâthal | shaw-thal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to transplant\nKJV: plant.\n\nCognate Group: H8362 (plant), H8363 (plant)\nGreek Equivalents: G5452 φυτεύω",
    8363: "שְׁתִל (shᵉthil | sheth-eel')Typo: xlit shᵉthiyl corrected to shᵉthil\n\nGreek Equivalents: G3504 νεόφυτος \n\nDerivation: from H8362 שָׁתַל\nStrong's: a sprig (as if transplanted), i.e. sucker\nKJV: plant.\n\nCognate Group: H8362 (plant), H8363 (plant)",
    8364: "שֻׁתַלְחִי (Shuthalchîy | shoo-thal-kee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H7803 שׁוּתֶלַח\nStrong's: a Shuthalchite (collectively) or descendants of Shuthelach\nKJV: Shuthalhites.\n\nCognate Group: H7803 (Shuthelah), H8364 (Shuthalhites), H7793 (Shur), H7802 (Shoshannim-Eduth), H7799 (lily), H7800 (Shushan), H8284 (sing), H7791 (wall), H7794 (bull)",
    8365: "שָׁתַם (shâtham | shaw-tham')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to unveil (figuratively)\nKJV: be open.\n\nCognate Group: H8365 (be open)\nGreek Equivalents: G228 ἀληθινός",
    8366: "שָׁתַן (shâthan | shaw-than')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: (causatively) to make water, i.e. urinate\nKJV: piss.\n\nCognate Group: H7890 (piss), H8366 (piss)",
    8367: "שָׁתַק (shâthaq | shaw-thak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to subside\nKJV: be calm, cease, be quiet.\n\nCognate Group: H8369 (Shethar), H8367 (be calm)\nGreek Equivalents: G2270 ἡσυχάζω, G2869 κοπάζω",
    8368: "שָׂתַר (sâthar | saw-thar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to break out (as an eruption)\nKJV: have in (one's) secret parts.\n\nCognate Group: H8368 (have in secret parts)",
    8369: "שֵׁתָר (Shêthâr | shay-thawr')\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Shethar, a Persian satrap\nKJV: Shethar.\n\nCognate Group: H8369 (Shethar), H8367 (be calm)",
    8370: "שְׁתַר בֹּוזְנַי (Shᵉthar Bôwzᵉnay | sheth-ar' bo-zen-ah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Shethar-Bozenai, a Persian officer\nKJV: Shetharboznai.\n\nCognate Group: H4961 (banquet), H8370 (Shetharboznai), H8355 (drink)",
    8371: "שָׁתַת (shâthath | shaw-thath')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to place, i.e. array; reflex. to lie\nKJV: be laid, set. t\n\nCognate Group: H8371 (be laid)\nGreek Equivalents: G5087 τίθημι",
    8372: "תָּא (tâʼ | taw)\n\nDerivation: and (feminine) תָּאָה; (Ezekiel 40:12), from (the base of) H8376 תָּאָה\nStrong's: a room (as circumscribed)\nKJV: (little) chamber.\n\nCognate Group: H8372 (chamber)",
    8373: "תָּאַב (tâʼab | taw-ab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to desire\nKJV: long.\n\nCognate Group: H8373 (long), H8375 (longing)",
    8374: "תָּאַב (tâʼab | taw-ab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (probably identical with H8373 תָּאַב through the idea of puffing disdainfully at; compare H340 אָיַב)\nStrong's: to loathe (morally)\nKJV: abhor.\n\nCognate Group: H8441 (abominable), H8374 (abhor), H8581 (abhor)",
    8375: "תַּאֲבָה (taʼăbâh | tah-ab-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H8374 תָּאַב (compare H15 אָבֶה)\nStrong's: desire\nKJV: longing.\n\nCognate Group: H8373 (long), H8375 (longing)",
    8376: "תָּאָה (tâʼâh | taw-aw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to mark off, i.e. (intensively) designate\nKJV: point out.\n\nCognate Group: H8377 (wild bull), H8376 (point out)",
    8377: "תְּאֹו (tᵉʼôw | teh-o')\n\nDerivation: and תֹּוא; (the original form), from H8376 תָּאָה\nStrong's: a species of antelope (probably from the white stripe on the cheek)\nKJV: wild bull (ox).\n\nCognate Group: H8377 (wild bull), H8376 (point out)\nGreek Equivalents: G654 ἀποστρέφω, G2398 ἴδιος",
    8378: "תַּאֲוָה (taʼăvâh | tah-av-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H183 אָוָה (abbreviated)\nStrong's: a longing; by implication, a delight (subjectively, satisfaction, objectively, a charm)\nKJV: dainty, desire, [idiom] exceedingly, [idiom] greedily, lust(ing), pleasant. See also H6914 קִבְרֹות הַתַּאֲוָה .\n\nCognate Group: H189 (Evi), H3970 (desire), H185 (desire), H176 (also), H8378 (dainty), H183 (covet)\nGreek Equivalents: G701 ἀρεστός, G1939 ἐπιθυμία, G2129 εὐλογία, G2590 καρπός",
    8379: "תַּאֲוָה (taʼăvâh | tah-av-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H8376 תָּאָה\nStrong's: a limit, i.e. full extent\nKJV: utmost bound.\n\nCognate Group: H8379 (utmost bound), H8427 (scrabble), H8420 (desire)",
    8380: "תָּאֹום (tâʼôwm | taw-ome')\n\nDerivation: or תָּאֹם; from H8382 תָּאַם\nStrong's: a twin (in plural only), literally or figuratively\nKJV: twins.\n\nCognate Group: H8380 (twins), H8387 (Taanath-shiloh), H8382 (coupled), H8384 (fig)\nGreek Equivalents: G2381 Θωμᾶς",
    8381: "תַּאֲלָה (taʼălâh | tah-al-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H422 אָלָה\nStrong's: an imprecation\nKJV: curse.\n\nCognate Group: H422 (adjure), H423 (curse), H8381 (curse)",
    8382: "תָּאַם (tâʼam | taw-am')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root; to be complete; but used only as denominative from H8380 תָּאֹום,\nStrong's: to be (causatively, make) twinned, i.e. (figuratively) duplicate or (architectural) jointed\nKJV: coupled (together), bear twins.\n\nCognate Group: H8380 (twins), H8387 (Taanath-shiloh), H8382 (coupled), H8384 (fig)\nGreek Equivalents: G2470 ἴσος",
    8383: "תְּאֻן (tᵉʼun | teh-oon')\n\nDerivation: from H205 אָוֶן\nStrong's: naughtiness, i.e. toil\nKJV: lie.\n\nCognate Group: H8383 (lie), H205 (affliction), H206 (Aven)",
    8384: "תְּאֵן (tᵉʼên | teh-ane')\n\nDerivation: or (in the singular, feminine) תְּאֵנָה; perhaps of foreign derivation\nStrong's: the fig (tree or fruit)\nKJV: fig (tree).\n\nCognate Group: H8380 (twins), H8387 (Taanath-shiloh), H8382 (coupled), H8384 (fig)\nGreek Equivalents: G4808 συκῆ, G4810 σῦκον",
    8385: "תַּאֲנָה (taʼănâh | tah-an-aw')\n\nDerivation: or תֹּאֲנָה; from H579 אָנָה\nStrong's: an opportunity or (subjectively) purpose\nKJV: occasion.\n\nCognate Group: H8385 (occasion), H579 (befall)\nGreek Equivalents: G468 ἀνταπόδομα, G1557 ἐκδίκησις",
    8386: "תַּאֲנִיָּה (taʼănîyâh | tah-an-ee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: from H578 אָנָה\nStrong's: lamentation\nKJV: heaviness, mourning.\n\nCognate Group: H592 (lamentation), H8386 (heaviness), H593 (Aniam), H578 (lament)",
    8387: "תַּאֲנַת שִׁלֹה (Taʼănath Shilôh | tah-an-ath' shee-lo')\n\nDerivation: from H8385 תַּאֲנָה and H7887 שִׁילֹה ; approach of Shiloh\nStrong's: Taanath-Shiloh, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Taanath-shiloh.\n\nCognate Group: H8380 (twins), H8387 (Taanath-shiloh), H8382 (coupled), H8384 (fig)",
    8388: "תָּאַר (tâʼar | taw-ar')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to delineate; reflex. to extend\nKJV: be drawn, mark out, (Rimmon-) methoar (by union with H7417 רִמֹּון).\n\nCognate Group: H8389 (beautiful), H8392 (ark), H8396 (Tabor), H8388 (be drawn)\nGreek Equivalents: G71 ἄγω, G1330 διέρχομαι, G1806 ἐξάγω",
    8389: "תֹּאַר (tôʼar | to'-ar)\n\nDerivation: from H8388 תָּאַר\nStrong's: outline, i.e. figure or appearance\nKJV: [phrase] beautiful, [idiom] comely, countenance, [phrase] fair, [idiom] favoured, form, [idiom] goodly, [idiom] resemble, visage.\n\nCognate Group: H8389 (beautiful), H8392 (ark), H8396 (Tabor), H8388 (be drawn)\nGreek Equivalents: G18 ἀγαθός, G1391 δόξα, G1491 εἶδος, G1491 εἶδος, G3444 μορφή, G3667 ὁμοίωμα, G3799 ὄψις",
    8390: "תַּאֲרֵעַ (Taʼărêaʻ | tah-ar-ay'-ah)\n\nDerivation: perhaps from H772 אֲרַע\nStrong's: Taarea, an Israelite\nKJV: Tarea. See H8475 תַּחְרֵעַ .\n\nCognate Group: H8475 (Tahrea), H8390 (Tarea)",
    8391: "תְּאַשּׁוּר (tᵉʼashshûwr | teh-ash-shoor')\n\nDerivation: from H833 אָשַׁר\nStrong's: a species of cedar (from its erectness)\nKJV: box (tree).\n\nCognate Group: H843 (Asherites), H835 (blessed), H838 (going), H842 (grove), H837 (happy), H836 (Asher), H833 (bless), H839 (Ashurite), H8391 (box)\nGreek Equivalents: G2748 Κεδρών",
    8392: "תֵּבָה (têbâh | tay-baw')\n\nDerivation: perhaps of foreign derivation\nStrong's: a box\nKJV: ark.\n\nCognate Group: H8389 (beautiful), H8392 (ark), H8396 (Tabor), H8388 (be drawn)\nGreek Equivalents: G2296 θαυμάζω, G2787 κιβωτός",
    8393: "תְּבוּאָה (tᵉbûwʼâh | teb-oo-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H935 בֹּוא\nStrong's: income, i.e. produce (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: fruit, gain, increase, revenue.\n\nCognate Group: H872 (entry), H935 (abide), H3996 (by which came), H4126 (coming), H3997 (entry), H8393 (fruit)\nGreek Equivalents: G1080 γεννάω, G2344 θησαυρός, G2590 καρπός",
    8394: "תָּבוּן (tâbûwn | taw-boon')\n\nDerivation: and (feminine) תְּבוּנָה; or תֹּובֻנָה; from H995 בִּין\nStrong's: intelligence; by implication, an argument; by extension, caprice\nKJV: discretion, reason, skilfulness, understanding, wisdom.\n\nCognate Group: H8394 (discretion), H2985 (Jabin), H1004 (court), H1003 (castle), H1002 (palace), H998 (knowledge), H4000 (taught), H995 (attend), H946 (Bunah), H996 (among), H1143 (champion)\nGreek Equivalents: G3056 λόγος, G5428 φρόνησις, G5429 φρόνιμος",
    8395: "תְּבוּסָה (tᵉbûwçâh | teb-oo-saw')\n\nDerivation: from H947 בּוּס\nStrong's: a treading down, i.e. ruin\nKJV: destruction.\n\nCognate Group: H8395 (destruction), H947 (loath), H4001 (treading down), H2983 (Jebusite), H2982 (Jebus)\nGreek Equivalents: G2692 καταστροφή",
    8396: "תָּבֹור (Tâbôwr | taw-bore')\n\nDerivation: from a root corresponding to H8406 תְּבַר ; broken region\nStrong's: Tabor, a mountain in Palestine, also a city adjacent\nKJV: Tabor.\n\nCognate Group: H8389 (beautiful), H8392 (ark), H8396 (Tabor), H8388 (be drawn)",
    8397: "תֶּבֶל (tebel | teh'-bel)\n\nDerivation: apparently from H1101 בָּלַל\nStrong's: mixture, i.e. unnatural bestiality\nKJV: confusion.\n\nCognate Group: H8400 (blemish), H8397 (confusion), H7642 (snail), H1098 (corn), H1101 (anoint)\nGreek Equivalents: G1093 γῆ",
    8398: "תֵּבֵל (têbêl | tay-bale')\n\nDerivation: from H2986 יָבַל\nStrong's: the earth (as moist and therefore inhabited); by extension, the globe; by implication, its inhabitants; specifically, a particular land, as Babylonia, Palestine\nKJV: habitable part, world.\n\nCognate Group: H2986 (bring), H2991 (Ibleam), H3106 (Jubal), H3105 (river), H2989 (Jabal), H944 (food), H2988 (course), H180 (river), H2990 (wen), H8398 (habitable part), H3104 (jubile), H2981 (fruit)\nGreek Equivalents: G764 ἀσεβέω, G3625 οἰκουμένη",
    8399: "תַּבְלִית (tablîyth | tab-leeth')\n\nDerivation: from H1086 בָּלָה\nStrong's: consumption\nKJV: destruction.\n\nCognate Group: H1115 (because un), H1107 (beside), H1094 (old), H1087 (old), H1097 (corruption), H8399 (destruction), H1100 (Belial), H1077 (lest), H1099 (nothing), H1086 (consume)",
    8400: "תְּבַּלֻּל (tᵉballul | teb-al-lool')\n\nDerivation: from H1101 בָּלַל in the original sense of flowing\nStrong's: a cataract (in the eye)\nKJV: blemish.\n\nCognate Group: H8400 (blemish), H8397 (confusion), H7642 (snail), H1098 (corn), H1101 (anoint)",
    8401: "תֶּבֶן (teben | teh'-ben)\n\nDerivation: probably from H1129 בָּנָה\nStrong's: properly, material, i.e. (specifically) refuse haum or stalks of grain (as chopped in threshing and used for fodder)\nKJV: chaff, straw, stubble.\n\nCognate Group: H8402 (Tibni), H8405 (Thebez), H8413 (Tidal), H8407 (Tiglath-pileser), H8412 (Tadmor), H4963 (straw), H8401 (chaff), H8425 (Togarmah)\nGreek Equivalents: G892 ἄχυρον",
    8402: "תִּבְנִי (Tibnîy | tib-nee')\n\nTypo: xlit Tibni corrected to Tibnîy\n\nDerivation: from H8401 תֶּבֶן ; strawy\nStrong's: Tibni, an Israelite\nKJV: Tibni.\n\nCognate Group: H8402 (Tibni), H8405 (Thebez), H8413 (Tidal), H8407 (Tiglath-pileser), H8412 (Tadmor), H4963 (straw), H8401 (chaff), H8425 (Togarmah)",
    8403: "תַּבְנִית (tabnîyth | tab-neeth')\n\nDerivation: from H1129 בָּנָה\nStrong's: structure; by implication, a model, resemblance\nKJV: figure, form, likeness, pattern, similitude.\n\nCognate Group: H1131 (Binnui), H1137 (Bani), H1138 (Bunni), H4012 (Mebunnai), H8403 (figure), H1129 (build), H1146 (building), H2998 (Ibnijah), H2996 (Jabneh), H1141 (Benaiah), H1140 (building), H4011 (frame), H2997 (Ibneiah), H2995 (Jabneel)\nGreek Equivalents: G3444 μορφή, G3667 ὁμοίωμα, G3669 ὁμοίωσις, G5179 τύπος",
    8404: "תַּבְעֵרָה (Tabʻêrâh | tab-ay-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H1197 בָּעַר ; burning\nStrong's: Taberah, a place in the Desert\nKJV: Taberah.\n\nCognate Group: H1198 (brutish), H1160 (Beor), H8404 (Taberah), H1202 (Baaseiah), H1203 (Beeshterah), H1199 (Baara), H1200 (fire), H1165 (beast), H1201 (Baasha), H1197 (be brutish)",
    8405: "תֵּבֵץ (Têbêts | tay-bates')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H948 בּוּץ ; whiteness\nStrong's: Tebets, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Thebez.\n\nCognate Group: H8402 (Tibni), H8405 (Thebez), H8413 (Tidal), H8407 (Tiglath-pileser), H8412 (Tadmor), H4963 (straw), H8401 (chaff), H8425 (Togarmah)",
    8406: "תְּבַר (tᵉbar | teb-ar')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7665 שָׁבַר\nStrong's: to be fragile (figuratively)\nKJV: broken.\n\nCognate Group: H8406 (broken)\nGreek Equivalents: G4937 συντρίβω",
    8407: "תִּגְלַת פִּלְאֶסֶר (Tiglath Pilʼeçer | tig-lath' pil-eh'-ser)\n\nDerivation: or תִּגְלַת פְּלֶסֶר; or תִּלְגַּת פִּלְנְאֶסֶר or תִּלְגַּת פִּלְנֶסֶר; of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Tiglath-Pileser or Tilgath-pilneser, an Assyryrian king\nKJV: Tiglath-pileser, Tilgath-pilneser.\n\nCognate Group: H8402 (Tibni), H8405 (Thebez), H8413 (Tidal), H8407 (Tiglath-pileser), H8412 (Tadmor), H4963 (straw), H8401 (chaff), H8425 (Togarmah)",
    8408: "תַּגְמוּל (tagmûwl | tag-mool')\n\nDerivation: from H1580 גָּמַל\nStrong's: a bestowment\nKJV: benefit.\n\nCognate Group: H1576 (as hast served), H1582 (Gemalli), H1577 (Gamul), H1578 (deed), H8408 (benefit), H1580 (bestow on), H1583 (Gamaliel), H1581 (camel)",
    8409: "תִּגְרָה (tigrâh | tig-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H1624 גָּרָה\nStrong's: strife, i.e. infliction\nKJV: blow.\n\nCognate Group: H1624 (contend), H8409 (blow), H1627 ([idiom] aloud)\nGreek Equivalents: G2479 ἰσχύς",
    8410: "תִּדְהָר (tidhâr | tid-hawr')\n\nDerivation: apparently from H1725 דָּהַר\nStrong's: enduring; a species of hard-wood or lasting tree (perhaps oak)\nKJV: pine (tree).\n\nCognate Group: H8410 (pine), H1725 (pause), H1726 (pransing)",
    8411: "תְּדִירָא (tᵉdîyrâʼ | ted-ee-raw')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H1753 דּוּר in the original sense of enduring\nStrong's: permanence, i.e. (adverb) constantly\nKJV: continually.\n\nCognate Group: H1753 (dwell), H1859 (generation), H8411 (continually), H4070 (dwelling), H1757 (Dura)",
    8412: "תַּדְמֹר (Tadmôr | tad-more')\n\nDerivation: or תַּמֹּר; (1 Kings 9:18), apparently from H8558 תָּמָר ; palm-city\nStrong's: Tadmor, a place near Palestine\nKJV: Tadmor.\n\nCognate Group: H8402 (Tibni), H8405 (Thebez), H8413 (Tidal), H8407 (Tiglath-pileser), H8412 (Tadmor), H4963 (straw), H8401 (chaff), H8425 (Togarmah)",
    8413: "תִּדְעָל (Tidʻâl | tid-awl')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from H1763 דְּחַל ; fearfulness\nStrong's: Tidal, a Canaanite\nKJV: Tidal.\n\nCognate Group: H8402 (Tibni), H8405 (Thebez), H8413 (Tidal), H8407 (Tiglath-pileser), H8412 (Tadmor), H4963 (straw), H8401 (chaff), H8425 (Togarmah)",
    8414: "תֹּהוּ (tôhûw | to'-hoo)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to lie waste\nStrong's: a desolation (of surface), i.e. desert; figuratively, a worthless thing; adverbially, in vain\nKJV: confusion, empty place, without form, nothing, (thing of) nought, vain, vanity, waste, wilderness.\n\nCognate Group: H8417 (folly), H8414 (confusion)\nGreek Equivalents: G94 ἄδικος, G517 ἀόρατος, G1373 δίψος, G2048 ἔρημος, G2756 κενός, G3152 μάταιος",
    8415: "תְּהֹום (tᵉhôwm | teh-home')\n\nDerivation: or תְּהֹם; (usually feminine) from H1949 הוּם\nStrong's: an abyss (as a surging mass of water), especially the deep (the main sea or the subterranean watersupply)\nKJV: deep (place), depth.\n\nCognate Group: H8415 (deep), H8422 (Tubal), H8423 (Tubal-cain)\nGreek Equivalents: G12 ἄβυσσος",
    8416: "תְּהִלָּה (tᵉhillâh | teh-hil-law')\n\nDerivation: from H1984 הָלַל\nStrong's: laudation; specifically (concretely) a hymn\nKJV: praise.\n\nCognate Group: H1947 (madness), H4111 (Mahalaleel), H1984 (boast), H1974 (merry), H8416 (praise), H3094 (Jehalellel), H1948 (madness), H4110 (praise), H1985 (Hillel)\nGreek Equivalents: G133 αἴνεσις, G703 ἀρέτη, G1391 δόξα, G1741 ἔνδοξος, G1868 ἔπαινος, G2745 καύχημα, G5215 ὕμνος, G5280 ὑπόμνησις, G5568 ψαλμός",
    8417: "תׇּהֳלָה (tohŏlâh | to-hol-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of an unused noun (apparently from H1984 הָלַל) meaning bluster\nStrong's: braggadocio, i.e. (by implication) fatuity\nKJV: folly.\n\nCognate Group: H8417 (folly), H8414 (confusion)\nGreek Equivalents: G4646 σκολιός",
    8418: "תַּהֲלֻכָה (tahălukâh | tah-hal-oo-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from H1980 הָלַךְ\nStrong's: a procession\nKJV: [idiom] went.\n\nCognate Group: H1982 ([idiom] dropped), H4109 (journey), H3212 ([idiom] again), H1980 (along), H8418 ([idiom] went), H1978 (step), H4108 (place to walk), H1979 (company)",
    8419: "תַּהְפֻּכָה (tahpukâh | tah-poo-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from H2015 הָפַךְ\nStrong's: a perversity or fraud\nKJV: (very) froward(-ness, thing), perverse thing.\n\nCognate Group: H2021 (chariot), H2018 (overthrow), H2015 ([idiom] become), H2017 (turning of things upside down), H4115 (prison), H2019 (froward), H8419 (froward), H2023 (Hor), H2024 (Hara), H2016 (contrary), H4114 (when)\nGreek Equivalents: G94 ἄδικος, G4103 πιστός, G4646 σκολιός",
    8420: "תָּו (tâv | tawv)\n\nDerivation: from H8427 תָּוָה\nStrong's: a mark; by implication, a signature\nKJV: desire, mark.\n\nCognate Group: H8379 (utmost bound), H8427 (scrabble), H8420 (desire)\nGreek Equivalents: G2513 καθαρός, G4592 σημεῖον, G5495 χείρ",
    8421: "תּוּב (tûwb | toob)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7725 שׁוּב, to come back\nStrong's: specifically (transitive and ellip.) to reply\nKJV: answer, restore, return (an answer).\n\nCognate Group: H8421 (answer)\nGreek Equivalents: G591 ἀποδίδωμι, G649 ἀποστέλλω",
    8422: "תּוּבַל (Tûwbal | too-bal')\n\nDerivation: or תֻּבַל; probably of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Tubal, a postdiluvian patriarch and his posterity\nKJV: Tubal.\n\nCognate Group: H8415 (deep), H8422 (Tubal), H8423 (Tubal-cain)",
    8423: "תּוּבַל קַיִן (Tûwbal Qayin | too-bal' kah'-yin)\n\nDerivation: apparently from H2986 יָבַל (compare H2981 יְבוּל) and H7014 קַיִן ; offspring of Cain\nStrong's: Tubal-Kajin, an antidiluvian patriarch\nKJV: Tubal-cain.\n\nCognate Group: H8415 (deep), H8422 (Tubal), H8423 (Tubal-cain)",
    8424: "תּוּגָה (tûwgâh | too-gaw')\n\nDerivation: from H3013 יָגָה\nStrong's: depression (of spirits); concretely a grief\nKJV: heaviness, sorrow.\n\nCognate Group: H3013 (afflict), H8424 (heaviness), H3015 (grief)\nGreek Equivalents: G3077 λύπη, G3601 ὀδύνη, G3997 πένθος",
    8425: "תֹּוגַרְמָה (Tôwgarmâh | to-gar-maw')\n\nDerivation: or תֹּגַרְמָה; probably of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Togarmah, a son of Gomer and his posterity\nKJV: Togarmah.\n\nCognate Group: H8402 (Tibni), H8405 (Thebez), H8413 (Tidal), H8407 (Tiglath-pileser), H8412 (Tadmor), H4963 (straw), H8401 (chaff), H8425 (Togarmah)",
    8426: "תֹּודָה (tôwdâh | to-daw')\n\nDerivation: from H3034 יָדָה\nStrong's: properly, an extension of the hand, i.e. (by implication) avowal, or (usually) adoration; specifically, a choir of worshippers\nKJV: confession, (sacrifice of) praise, thanks(-giving, offering).\n\nCognate Group: H1939 (Hodaiah), H8426 (confession), H3044 (Jidlaph), H3034 (cast), H3038 (Jeduthun), H1960 (thanksgiving), H3042 (Jedaiah), H1938 (Hodaviah)\nGreek Equivalents: G103 ᾄδω, G133 αἴνεσις, G1435 δῶρον",
    8427: "תָּוָה (tâvâh | taw-vaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to mark out, i.e. (primitive) scratch or (definite) imprint\nKJV: scrabble, set (a mark).\n\nCognate Group: H8379 (utmost bound), H8427 (scrabble), H8420 (desire)\nGreek Equivalents: G3947 παροξύνω, G5178 τυμπανίζω",
    8428: "תָּוָה (tâvâh | taw-vaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (or perhaps identical with H8427 תָּוָה through a similar idea from scraping to pieces)\nStrong's: to grieve\nKJV: limit (by confusion with H8427 תָּוָה).\n\nCognate Group: H8437 (that wasted), H8428 (limit), H8432 (among), H8459 (Tohu), H8430 (Toah), H8484 (middle)",
    8429: "תְּוַהּ (tᵉvahh | tev-ah')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8539 תָּמַהּ or perhaps to H7582 שָׁאָה through the idea of sweeping to ruin (compare H8428 תָּוָה)\nStrong's: to amaze, i.e. (reflex. by implication) take alarm\nKJV: be astonied.\n\nCognate Group: H8450 (bullock), H8460 (under), H8517 (snow), H8479 (under), H8429 (be astonied)",
    8430: "תֹּוחַ (Tôwach | to'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to depress; humble\nStrong's: Toach, an Israelite\nKJV: Toah.\n\nCognate Group: H8437 (that wasted), H8428 (limit), H8432 (among), H8459 (Tohu), H8430 (Toah), H8484 (middle)",
    8431: "תֹּוחֶלֶת (tôwcheleth | to-kheh'-leth)\n\nDerivation: from H3176 יָחַל\nStrong's: expectation\nKJV: hope.\n\nCognate Group: H3178 (Jahleelites), H3176 (hope), H3177 (Jahleel), H8431 (hope), H3175 (should hope)\nGreek Equivalents: G1680 ἐλπίς, G2745 καύχημα, G5287 ὑπόστασις",
    8432: "תָּוֶךְ (tâvek | taw'-vek)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to sever\nStrong's: a bisection, i.e. (by implication) the centre\nKJV: among(-st), [idiom] between, half, [idiom] (there-, where-), in(-to), middle, mid(-night), midst (among), [idiom] out (of), [idiom] through, [idiom] with(-in).\n\nCognate Group: H8437 (that wasted), H8428 (limit), H8432 (among), H8459 (Tohu), H8430 (Toah), H8484 (middle)\nGreek Equivalents: G1388 δόλος, G2873 κόπος, G3319 μέσος, G5009 ταμεῖον, G5110 τόκος",
    8433: "תֹּוכֵחָה (tôwkêchâh | to-kay-khaw')\n\nDerivation: and תֹּוכַחַת; from H3198 יָכַח\nStrong's: chastisement; figuratively (by words) correction, refutation, proof (even in defence)\nKJV: argument, [idiom] chastened, correction, reasoning, rebuke, reproof, [idiom] be (often) reproved.\n\nCognate Group: H3198 (appoint), H8433 (argument)\nGreek Equivalents: G1557 ἐκδίκησις, G1650 ἔλεγχος, G1650 ἔλεγχος, G1785 ἐντολή, G3680 ὀνειδισμός, G3809 παιδεία",
    8434: "תֹּולָד (Tôwlâd | to-lawd')\n\nDerivation: from H3205 יָלַד ; posterity\nStrong's: Tolad, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Tolad. Compare H513 אֶלְתֹּולַד .\n\nCognate Group: H3206 (boy), H3205 (bear), H2056 (child), H8434 (Tolad), H4138 (begotten), H4137 (Moladah), H3209 (born), H3208 (childhood), H3207 (damsel), H4140 (Molid), H3211 (born), H8435 (birth), H3210 (Jalon)",
    8435: "תֹּולְדָה (tôwlᵉdâh | to-led-aw')\n\nDerivation: or תֹּלְדָה; from H3205 יָלַד\nStrong's: (plural only) descent, i.e. family; (figuratively) history\nKJV: birth, generations.\n\nCognate Group: H3206 (boy), H3205 (bear), H2056 (child), H8434 (Tolad), H4138 (begotten), H4137 (Moladah), H3209 (born), H3208 (childhood), H3207 (damsel), H4140 (Molid), H3211 (born), H8435 (birth), H3210 (Jalon)\nGreek Equivalents: G1078 γένεσις, G4772 συγγένεια",
    8436: "תּוּלֹון (Tûwlôwn | too-lone')\n\nTypo: xlit Tûwlôn corrected to Tûwlôwn\n\nDerivation: from H8524 תָּלַל ; suspension\nStrong's: Tulon, an Israelite\nKJV: Tilon (from the margin).\n\nCognate Group: H8494 (Tiras), H8485 (Tema), H8491 (Tizite), H8436 (Tilon), H8481 (lower), H8478 (as), H8480 (Tahath), H8495 (he goat), H8482 (low)",
    8437: "תֹּולָל (tôwlâl | to-lawl')\n\nDerivation: from H3213 יָלַל\nStrong's: causing to howl, i.e. an oppressor\nKJV: that wasted.\n\nCognate Group: H8437 (that wasted), H8428 (limit), H8432 (among), H8459 (Tohu), H8430 (Toah), H8484 (middle)",
    8438: "תֹּולָע (tôwlâʻ | to-law')\n\nDerivation: and (feminine) תֹּולֵעָה; or תֹּולַעַת; or תֹּלַעַת; from H3216 יָלַע ; a maggot (as voracious); specifically (often with ellipsis of H8144 שָׁנִי)\n\nStrong's: the crimson-grub, but used only (in this connection) of the colorfrom it, and cloths dyed therewith\nKJV: crimson, scarlet, worm.\n\nCognate Group: H8530 (armoury), H8439 (Tola), H4459 (great tooth), H4973 (cheek tooth), H8529 ([idiom] scarlet), H8438 (crimson), H8440 (Tolaites)\nGreek Equivalents: G2847 κόκκινος, G2848 κόκκος, G4663 σκώληξ",
    8439: "תֹּולָע (Tôwlâʻ | to-law')\n\nDerivation: the same as H8438 תֹּולָע ; worm\nStrong's: Tola, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Tola.\n\nCognate Group: H8530 (armoury), H8439 (Tola), H4459 (great tooth), H4973 (cheek tooth), H8529 ([idiom] scarlet), H8438 (crimson), H8440 (Tolaites)\nGreek Equivalents: G2847 κόκκινος",
    8440: "תֹּולָעִי (Tôwlâʻîy | to-law-ee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H8439 תֹּולָע\nStrong's: a Tolaite (collectively) or descendants of Tola\nKJV: Tolaites.\n\nCognate Group: H8530 (armoury), H8439 (Tola), H4459 (great tooth), H4973 (cheek tooth), H8529 ([idiom] scarlet), H8438 (crimson), H8440 (Tolaites)",
    8441: "תֹּועֵבַה (tôwʻêbah | to-ay-baw')\n\nDerivation: or תֹּעֵבַה; feminine active participle of H8581 תַּעָב\nStrong's: properly, something disgusting (morally), i.e. (as noun) an abhorrence; especially idolatry or (concretely) an idol\nKJV: abominable (custom, thing), abomination.\n\nCognate Group: H8441 (abominable), H8374 (abhor), H8581 (abhor)\nGreek Equivalents: G167 ἀκαθαρσία, G169 ἀκάθαρτος, G266 ἁμαρτία, G458 ἀνομία, G459 ἄνομος, G763 ἀσέβεια, G946 βδέλυγμα, G947 βδελυκτός, G2041 ἔργον, G4189 πονηρία, G4190 πονηρός, G4191 πονηρότερος",
    8442: "תֹּועָה (tôwʻâh | to-aw')\n\nDerivation: feminine active participle of H8582 תָּעָה\nStrong's: mistake, i.e. (morally) impiety, or (political) injury\nKJV: error, hinder.\n\nCognate Group: H8583 (Toi), H8442 (error), H8590 (Taanach), H8582 (go astray)\nGreek Equivalents: G4579 σείω",
    8443: "תֹּועָפָה (tôwʻâphâh | to-aw-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H3286 יָעַף\nStrong's: (only in plural collective) weariness, i.e. (by implication) toil (treasure so obtained) or speed\nKJV: plenty, strength.\n\nCognate Group: H8443 (plenty)\nGreek Equivalents: G1391 δόξα, G4448 πυρόω, G5311 ὕψος",
    8444: "תֹּוצָאָה (tôwtsâʼâh | to-tsaw-aw')\n\nDerivation: or תֹּצָאָה; from H3318 יָצָא\nStrong's: (only in plural collective) exit, i.e. (geographical) boundary, or (figuratively) deliverance, (actively) source\nKJV: border(-s), going(-s) forth (out), issues, outgoings.\n\nCognate Group: H4161 (brought out), H6631 (that which cometh forth), H8444 (border), H4163 (draught house; going forth), H3329 (those that came forth), H3318 ([idiom] after), H4162 (Moza)\nGreek Equivalents: G1327 διέξοδος",
    8445: "תֹּוקַהַת (Tôwqahath | to-kah'-ath)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H3349 יִקָּהָה ; obedience\nStrong's: Tokahath, an Israelite\nKJV: Tikvath (by correction for H8616 תִּקְוָה).\n\nCognate Group: H6978 ([idiom] meted out), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H8615 (expectation), H6960 (gather), H8616 (Tikvah), H6961 (line), H8445 (Tikvath)",
    8446: "תּוּר (tûwr | toor)\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to meander (causatively, guide) about, especially fortrade or reconnoitring\nKJV: chap(-man), sent to descry, be excellent, merchant(-man), search (out), seek, (e-) spy (out).\n\nCognate Group: H8446 (chap), H3491 (range), H8447 (border), H8448 (estate)\nGreek Equivalents: G1294 διαστρέφω, G1586 ἐκλέγομαι, G1614 ἐκτείνω, G1621 ἐκτινάσσω, G1980 ἐπισκέπτομαι, G2090 ἑτοιμάζω",
    8447: "תֹּור (tôwr | tore)\n\nDerivation: or תֹּר; from H8446 תּוּר\nStrong's: a succession, i.e. a string or (abstractly) order\nKJV: border, row, turn.\n\nCognate Group: H8446 (chap), H3491 (range), H8447 (border), H8448 (estate)\nGreek Equivalents: G2540 καιρός, G3706 ὅρασις, G5167 τρυγών, G5550 χρόνος",
    8448: "תֹּור (tôwr | tore)\n\nDerivation: probably the same as H8447 תֹּור\nStrong's: a manner (as a sort of turn)\nKJV: estate.\n\nCognate Group: H8446 (chap), H3491 (range), H8447 (border), H8448 (estate)",
    8449: "תֹּור (tôwr | tore)\n\nDerivation: or תֹּר; probably the same as H8447 תֹּור\nStrong's: a ring-dove, often (figuratively) as a term of endearment\nKJV: (turtle) dove.\n\nCognate Group: H8630 (prevail), H8640 (Tirhakah), H8673 (ninety), H8660 (Tirshatha), H8659 (Tarshish), H8650 (beacon), H8658 (beryl), H8638 (interpret), H8634 (Taralah), H8645 (cypress), H8633 (authority), H8623 (mightier), H8657 (Teresh), H8646 (Tarah), H8655 (idols), H8661 (Tartan), H8672 (nine), H8449 (dove), H8662 (Tartak), H8654 (Tirathite), H8671 (ninth)",
    8450: "תֹּור (tôwr | tore)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding (by permutation) to H7794 שֹׁור\nStrong's: a bull\nKJV: bullock, ox.\n\nCognate Group: H8450 (bullock), H8460 (under), H8517 (snow), H8479 (under), H8429 (be astonied)",
    8451: "תֹּורָה (tôwrâh | to-raw')\n\nDerivation: or תֹּרָה; from H3384 יָרָה\nStrong's: a precept or statute, especially the Decalogue or Pentateuch\nKJV: law.\n\nCognate Group: H4175 (rain), H3140 (Jorai), H8451 (law), H3138 (first rain), H4176 (Moreh), H3404 (Jeriah), H8452 (manner), H3385 (Jeruel), H3139 (Jorah), H3384 (archer), H3400 (Jeriel)",
    8452: "תֹּורָה (tôwrâh | to-raw')\n\nDerivation: probably feminine of H8448 תֹּור\nStrong's: a custom\nKJV: manner.\n\nCognate Group: H4175 (rain), H3140 (Jorai), H8451 (law), H3138 (first rain), H4176 (Moreh), H3404 (Jeriah), H8452 (manner), H3385 (Jeruel), H3139 (Jorah), H3384 (archer), H3400 (Jeriel)\nGreek Equivalents: G975 βιβλίον, G1242 διαθήκη, G1785 ἐντολή, G3056 λόγος, G3551 νόμος, G5010 τάξις",
    8453: "תֹּושָׁב (tôwshâb | to-shawb')\n\nDerivation: or תֹּשָׁב; (1 Kings 17:1), from H3427 יָשַׁב ; a dweller (but not outlandish (H5237 נׇכְרִי)); especially (as distinguished from a native citizen (active participle of H3427 יָשַׁב) and a temporary inmate (H1616 גֵּר) or mere lodger (H3885 לוּן))\n\nStrong's: resident alien\nKJV: foreigner, inhabitant, sojourner, stranger.\n\nCognate Group: H3430 (Ishbi-benob), H3428 (Jeshebeab), H3436 (Joshbekashah), H3429 (that sat in the seat), H3427 (abide), H7871 (while), H4186 (assembly), H8453 (foreigner), H7675 (place), H3143 (Josibiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G3927 παρεπίδημος, G3941 πάροικος",
    8454: "תּוּשִׁיָּה (tûwshîyâh | too-shee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: or תֻּשִׁיָּה; from an unused root probably meaning to substantiate\nStrong's: support or (by implication) ability, i.e. (direct) help, (in purpose) an undertaking, (intellectual) understanding\nKJV: enterprise, that which (thing as it) is, substance, (sound) wisdom, working.\n\nCognate Group: H3144 (Joshah), H8454 (enterprise), H3145 (Joshaviah)\nGreek Equivalents: G227 ἀληθής, G803 ἀσφάλεια, G996 βοήθεια, G1012 βουλή, G1872 ἐπακολουθέω, G2479 ἰσχύς, G2540 καιρός, G4991 σωτηρία",
    8455: "תֹּותָח (tôwthâch | to-thawkh')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to smite\nStrong's: a club\nKJV: darts.\n\nCognate Group: H8455 (darts)\nGreek Equivalents: G4974 σφυρόν",
    8456: "תָּזַז (tâzaz | taw-zaz')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to lop off\nKJV: cut down.\n\nCognate Group: H8476 (badger), H8472 (Tahpenes), H8456 (cut down), H8477 (Thahash), H8471 (Tahapanes), H8473 (habergeon)\nGreek Equivalents: G609 ἀποκόπτω, G2629 κατακόπτω",
    8457: "תַּזְנוּת (taznûwth | taz-nooth')\n\nDerivation: or תַּזְנֻת; from H2181 זָנָה\nStrong's: harlotry, i.e. (figuratively) idolatry\nKJV: fornication, whoredom.\n\nCognate Group: H2183 (whoredom), H2181 (commit fornication), H8457 (fornication), H2185 (armour), H2184 (whoredom)\nGreek Equivalents: G2041 ἔργον, G4202 πορνεία",
    8458: "תַּחְבֻּלָה (tachbulâh | takh-boo-law')\n\nDerivation: or תַּחְבּוּלָה; from H2254 חָבַל as denominative from H2256 חֶבֶל\nStrong's: (only in plural) properly, steerage (as a management of ropes), i.e. (figuratively) guidance or (by implication) a plan\nKJV: good advice, (wise) counsels.\n\nCognate Group: H2260 (mast), H8458 (good advice), H2258 (pledge), H2254 ([idiom] at all), H2259 (pilot), H2256 (band)\nGreek Equivalents: G1013 βούλημα, G2941 κυβέρνησις",
    8459: "תֹּחוּ (Tôchûw | to'-khoo)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to depress; abasement\nStrong's: Tochu, an Israelite\nKJV: Tohu.\n\nCognate Group: H8437 (that wasted), H8428 (limit), H8432 (among), H8459 (Tohu), H8430 (Toah), H8484 (middle)",
    8460: "תְּחֹות (tᵉchôwth | tekh-oth')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or תּחֹת; (Aramaic), corresponding to H8478 תַּחַת\nStrong's: beneath\nKJV: under.\n\nCognate Group: H8450 (bullock), H8460 (under), H8517 (snow), H8479 (under), H8429 (be astonied)",
    8461: "תַּחְכְּמֹנִי (Tachkᵉmônîy | takh-kem-o-nee')\n\nDerivation: probably for H2453 חַכְמֹונִי ; sagacious\nStrong's: Tachkemoni, an Israelite\nKJV: Tachmonite.\n\nCognate Group: H8461 (Tachmonite), H2449 ([idiom] exceeding), H2453 (Hachmoni), H2454 (wisdom), H2450 (cunning), H2451 (skilful)",
    8462: "תְּחִלָּה (tᵉchillâh | tekh-il-law')\n\nDerivation: from H2490 חָלַל in the sense of opening\nStrong's: a commencement; rel. original (adverb, -ly)\nKJV: begin(-ning), first (time).\n\nCognate Group: H8462 (begin), H2486 (be far), H2491 (kill), H2490 (begin), H2455 (common)\nGreek Equivalents: G746 ἀρχή",
    8463: "תַּחֲלוּא (tachălûwʼ | takh-al-oo')\n\nDerivation: or תַּחֲלֻא; from H2456 חָלָא\nStrong's: a malady\nKJV: disease, [idiom] grievous, (that are) sick(-ness).\n\nCognate Group: H8463 (disease), H2456 (be diseased)\nGreek Equivalents: G3119 μαλακία, G3554 νόσος, G4192 πόνος",
    8464: "תַּחְמָס (tachmâç | takh-mawce')\n\nDerivation: from H2554 חָמַס\nStrong's: a species of unclean bird (from its violence), perhaps an owl\nKJV: night hawk.\n\nCognate Group: H8464 (night hawk), H2555 (cruel), H2554 (make bare)",
    8465: "תַּחַן (Tachan | takh'-an)\n\nDerivation: probably from H2583 חָנָה ; station\nStrong's: Tachan, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Tahan.\n\nCognate Group: H4266 (Mahanaim), H8465 (Tahan), H2595 (javelin), H4264 (army), H8466 (camp), H8470 (Tahanites), H4265 (Mahaneh-dan), H2588 (cabin), H2583 (abide)",
    8466: "תַּחֲנָה (tachănâh | takh-an-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H2583 חָנָה\nStrong's: (only plural collectively) an encampment\nKJV: camp.\n\nCognate Group: H4266 (Mahanaim), H8465 (Tahan), H2595 (javelin), H4264 (army), H8466 (camp), H8470 (Tahanites), H4265 (Mahaneh-dan), H2588 (cabin), H2583 (abide)",
    8467: "תְּחִנָּה (tᵉchinnâh | tekh-in-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H2603 חָנַן\nStrong's: graciousness; causatively, entreaty\nKJV: favour, grace, supplication.\n\nCognate Group: H2581 (Hen), H2607 (Hanani), H2584 (Hannah), H2582 (Henadad), H2608 (Hananiah), H8467 (favour), H2586 (Hanun), H2605 (Canan), H8469 (intreaty), H2592 (Hanniel), H8468 (Tehinnah), H2606 (Hananeel), H2600 (without a cause), H2580 (favour), H2615 (Hannathon), H2433 (comely), H2589 (be gracious), H2603 (beseech), H2594 (favour), H2587 (gracious)\nGreek Equivalents: G995 βοή, G1162 δέησις, G4335 προσευχή, G5456 φωνή",
    8468: "תְּחִנָּה (Tᵉchinnâh | tekh-in-naw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H8467 תְּחִנָּה\nStrong's: Techinnah, an Israelite\nKJV: Tehinnah.\n\nCognate Group: H2581 (Hen), H2607 (Hanani), H2584 (Hannah), H2582 (Henadad), H2608 (Hananiah), H8467 (favour), H2586 (Hanun), H2605 (Canan), H8469 (intreaty), H2592 (Hanniel), H8468 (Tehinnah), H2606 (Hananeel), H2600 (without a cause), H2580 (favour), H2615 (Hannathon), H2433 (comely), H2589 (be gracious), H2603 (beseech), H2594 (favour), H2587 (gracious)",
    8469: "תַּחֲנוּן (tachănûwn | takh-an-oon')\n\nDerivation: or (feminine) תַּחֲנוּנָה; from H2603 חָנַן\nStrong's: earnest prayer\nKJV: intreaty, supplication.\n\nCognate Group: H2581 (Hen), H2607 (Hanani), H2584 (Hannah), H2582 (Henadad), H2608 (Hananiah), H8467 (favour), H2586 (Hanun), H2605 (Canan), H8469 (intreaty), H2592 (Hanniel), H8468 (Tehinnah), H2606 (Hananeel), H2600 (without a cause), H2580 (favour), H2615 (Hannathon), H2433 (comely), H2589 (be gracious), H2603 (beseech), H2594 (favour), H2587 (gracious)\nGreek Equivalents: G3874 παράκλησις",
    8470: "תַּחֲנִי (Tachănîy | takh-an-ee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H8465 תַּחַן\nStrong's: a Tachanite (collectively) or descendants of Tachan\nKJV: Tahanites.\n\nCognate Group: H4266 (Mahanaim), H8465 (Tahan), H2595 (javelin), H4264 (army), H8466 (camp), H8470 (Tahanites), H4265 (Mahaneh-dan), H2588 (cabin), H2583 (abide)",
    8471: "תַּחְפַּנְחֵס (Tachpanchêç | takh-pan-khace')\n\nDerivation: or תְּחַפְנְחֵס; (Ezekiel 30:18), or תַּחְפְּנֵס; (Jeremiah 2:16), of Egyptian derivation\nStrong's: Tachpanches, Techaphneches or Tachpenes, a place in Egypt\nKJV: Tahapanes, Tahpanhes, Tehaphnehes.\n\nCognate Group: H8476 (badger), H8472 (Tahpenes), H8456 (cut down), H8477 (Thahash), H8471 (Tahapanes), H8473 (habergeon)",
    8472: "תַּחְפְּנֵיס (Tachpᵉnêyç | takh-pen-ace')\n\nDerivation: of Egyptian derivation\nStrong's: Tachpenes, an Egyptian woman\nKJV: Tahpenes.\n\nCognate Group: H8476 (badger), H8472 (Tahpenes), H8456 (cut down), H8477 (Thahash), H8471 (Tahapanes), H8473 (habergeon)",
    8473: "תַּחֲרָא (tachărâʼ | takh-ar-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H2734 חָרָה in the original sense of H2352 חוּר or H2353 חוּר\nStrong's: a linen corslet (as white or hollow)\nKJV: habergeon.\n\nCognate Group: H8476 (badger), H8472 (Tahpenes), H8456 (cut down), H8477 (Thahash), H8471 (Tahapanes), H8473 (habergeon)",
    8474: "תַּחָרָה (tachârâh | takh-aw-raw')\n\nDerivation: a facitious root from H2734 חָרָה through the idea of the heat of jealousy\nStrong's: to vie with a rival\nKJV: close, contend.\n\nCognate Group: H2739 (Harumaph), H2734 (be angry), H8474 (close), H2750 (fierce), H2740 (sore displeasure)",
    8475: "תַּחְרֵעַ (Tachrêaʻ | takh-ray'-ah)\n\nDerivation: for H8390 תַּאֲרֵעַ\nStrong's: Tachrea, an Israelite\nKJV: Tahrea.\n\nCognate Group: H8475 (Tahrea), H8390 (Tarea)",
    8476: "תַּחַשׁ (tachash | takh'-ash)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign derivation\nStrong's: a (clean) animal with fur, probably a species of antelope\nKJV: badger.\n\nCognate Group: H8476 (badger), H8472 (Tahpenes), H8456 (cut down), H8477 (Thahash), H8471 (Tahapanes), H8473 (habergeon)\nGreek Equivalents: G5191 ὑακίνθινος, G5192 ὑάκινθος",
    8477: "תַּחַשׁ (Tachash | takh'-ash)\n\nDerivation: the same as H8476 תַּחַשׁ\nStrong's: Tachash, a relative of Abraham\nKJV: Thahash.\n\nCognate Group: H8476 (badger), H8472 (Tahpenes), H8456 (cut down), H8477 (Thahash), H8471 (Tahapanes), H8473 (habergeon)",
    8478: "תַּחַת (tachath | takh'-ath)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H8430 תֹּוחַ\nStrong's: the bottom (as depressed); only adverbially, below (often with prepositional prefix underneath), in lieu of, etc.\nKJV: as, beneath, [idiom] flat, in(-stead), (same) place (where...is), room, for...sake, stead of, under, [idiom] unto, [idiom] when...was mine, whereas, (where-) fore, with.\n\nCognate Group: H8494 (Tiras), H8485 (Tema), H8491 (Tizite), H8436 (Tilon), H8481 (lower), H8478 (as), H8480 (Tahath), H8495 (he goat), H8482 (low)\nGreek Equivalents: G243 ἄλλος, G2736 κάτω, G2945 κύκλῳ, G3624 οἶκος, G3694 ὀπίσω, G5117 τόπος, G5220 ὕπανδρος, G5270 ὑποκάτω, G5561 χώρα",
    8479: "תַּחַת (tachath | takh'-ath)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8478 תַּחַת \nStrong's: the bottom (as depressed); only adverbially, below (often with prepositional prefix underneath), in lieu of, etc.\nKJV: under.\n\nCognate Group: H8450 (bullock), H8460 (under), H8517 (snow), H8479 (under), H8429 (be astonied)",
    8480: "תַּחַת (Tachath | takh'-ath)\n\nDerivation: the same as H8478 תַּחַת\nStrong's: Tachath, the name of a place in the Desert, also of three Israelites\nKJV: Tahath.\n\nCognate Group: H8494 (Tiras), H8485 (Tema), H8491 (Tizite), H8436 (Tilon), H8481 (lower), H8478 (as), H8480 (Tahath), H8495 (he goat), H8482 (low)",
    8481: "תַּחְתֹּון (tachtôwn | takh-tone')\n\nDerivation: or תַּחְתֹּן; from H8478 תַּחַת\nStrong's: bottommost\nKJV: lower(-est), nether(-most).\n\nCognate Group: H8494 (Tiras), H8485 (Tema), H8491 (Tizite), H8436 (Tilon), H8481 (lower), H8478 (as), H8480 (Tahath), H8495 (he goat), H8482 (low)\nGreek Equivalents: G2737 κατώτερος",
    8482: "תַּחְתִּי (tachtîy | takh-tee')\n\nDerivation: from H8478 תַּחַת\nStrong's: lowermost; as noun (feminine plural) the depths (figuratively, a pit, the womb)\nKJV: low (parts, -er, -er parts, -est), nether (part).\n\nCognate Group: H8494 (Tiras), H8485 (Tema), H8491 (Tizite), H8436 (Tilon), H8481 (lower), H8478 (as), H8480 (Tahath), H8495 (he goat), H8482 (low)\nGreek Equivalents: G899 βάθος, G2310 θεμέλιος, G2737 κατώτερος, G5011 ταπεινός",
    8483: "תַּחְתִּים חׇדְשִׁי (Tachtîym Chodshîy | takh-teem' khod-shee')\n\nDerivation: apparently from the plural masculine of H8482 תַּחְתִּי or H8478 תַּחַת and H2320 חֹדֶשׁ ; lower (ones) monthly\nStrong's: Tachtim-Chodshi, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Tahtim-hodshi.\n\nCognate Group: H2322 (Hadashah), H8483 (Tahtim-hodshi), H2318 (renew), H2321 (Hodesh), H2320 (month), H2319 (fresh)",
    8484: "תִּיכֹון (tîykôwn | tee-kone')\n\nDerivation: or תִּיכֹן; from H8432 תָּוֶךְ\nStrong's: central\nKJV: middle(-most), midst.\n\nCognate Group: H8437 (that wasted), H8428 (limit), H8432 (among), H8459 (Tohu), H8430 (Toah), H8484 (middle)\nGreek Equivalents: G3322 μεσόω",
    8485: "תֵּימָא (Têymâʼ | tay-maw')\n\nDerivation: or תֵּמָא; probably of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Tema, a son of Ishmael, and the region settled by him\nKJV: Tema.\n\nCognate Group: H8494 (Tiras), H8485 (Tema), H8491 (Tizite), H8436 (Tilon), H8481 (lower), H8478 (as), H8480 (Tahath), H8495 (he goat), H8482 (low)",
    8486: "תֵּימָן (têymân | tay-mawn')\n\nDerivation: or תֵּמָן; denominative from H3225 יָמִין\nStrong's: the south (as being on the right hand of a person facing the east)\nKJV: south (side, -ward, wind).\n\nCognate Group: H8486 (south), H3231 (go to the right hand), H3227 (right), H8488 (Temeni), H3226 (Jamin), H3232 (Imna), H8487 (south), H3228 (Jaminites), H3225 (left-handed), H541 (turn to the right), H3233 (right), H8489 (Temani)\nGreek Equivalents: G2281 θάλασσα, G3047 λίψ, G3558 νότος",
    8487: "תֵּימָן (Têymân | tay-mawn')\n\nDerivation: or תֵּמָן; the same as H8486 תֵּימָן\nStrong's: Teman, the name of two Edomites, and of the region and descendant of one of them\nKJV: south, Teman.\n\nCognate Group: H8486 (south), H3231 (go to the right hand), H3227 (right), H8488 (Temeni), H3226 (Jamin), H3232 (Imna), H8487 (south), H3228 (Jaminites), H3225 (left-handed), H541 (turn to the right), H3233 (right), H8489 (Temani)",
    8488: "תֵּימְנִי (Têymᵉnîy | tay-men-ee')\n\nDerivation: probably for H8489 תֵּימָנִי\nStrong's: Temeni, an Israelite\nKJV: Temeni.\n\nCognate Group: H8486 (south), H3231 (go to the right hand), H3227 (right), H8488 (Temeni), H3226 (Jamin), H3232 (Imna), H8487 (south), H3228 (Jaminites), H3225 (left-handed), H541 (turn to the right), H3233 (right), H8489 (Temani)",
    8489: "תֵּימָנִי (Têymânîy | tay-maw-nee')\n\nDerivation: patronymically from H8487 תֵּימָן\nStrong's: a Temanite or descendant of Teman\nKJV: Temani, Temanite.\n\nCognate Group: H8486 (south), H3231 (go to the right hand), H3227 (right), H8488 (Temeni), H3226 (Jamin), H3232 (Imna), H8487 (south), H3228 (Jaminites), H3225 (left-handed), H541 (turn to the right), H3233 (right), H8489 (Temani)",
    8490: "תִּימָרָה (tîymârâh | tee-maw-raw')\n\nDerivation: or תִּמָרָה; from the same as H8558 תָּמָר\nStrong's: a column, i.e. cloud\nKJV: pillar.\n\nCognate Group: H8559 (Tamar), H8564 (high heap), H8560 (palm tree), H8558 (palm), H8490 (pillar), H8561 (palm tree)",
    8491: "תִּיצִי (Tîytsîy | tee-tsee')\n\nDerivation: patrial or patronymically from an unused noun of uncertain meaning\nStrong's: a Titsite or descendant or inhabitant of an unknown Tits\nKJV: Tizite.\n\nCognate Group: H8494 (Tiras), H8485 (Tema), H8491 (Tizite), H8436 (Tilon), H8481 (lower), H8478 (as), H8480 (Tahath), H8495 (he goat), H8482 (low)",
    8492: "תִּירֹושׁ (tîyrôwsh | tee-roshe')\n\nDerivation: or תִּירֹשׁ; from H3423 יָרַשׁ in the sense of expulsion\nStrong's: must or fresh grape-juice (as just squeezed out); by implication (rarely) fermented wine\nKJV: (new, sweet) wine.\n\nCognate Group: H3424 (possession), H3425 (heritage), H8492 (wine), H4181 (heritage), H3423 (cast out), H7568 (net), H4180 (possession), H4182 (Moresheth-gath), H3388 (Jerusha), H4183 (Morashthite)\nGreek Equivalents: G3631 οἶνος",
    8493: "תִּירְיָא (Tîyrᵉyâʼ | tee-reh-yaw')\n\nDerivation: probably from H3372 יָרֵא\nStrong's: fearful, Tirja, an Israelite\nKJV: Tiria.\n\nCognate Group: H3373 (afraid), H3375 (Iron), H3374 ([idiom] dreadful), H3372 (affright), H8493 (Tiria), H4172 (dread)",
    8494: "תִּירָס (Tîyrâç | tee-rawce')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Tiras, a son of Japheth\nKJV: Tiras.\n\nCognate Group: H8494 (Tiras), H8485 (Tema), H8491 (Tizite), H8436 (Tilon), H8481 (lower), H8478 (as), H8480 (Tahath), H8495 (he goat), H8482 (low)",
    8495: "תַּיִשׁ (tayish | tah'-yeesh)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to butt\nStrong's: a buck or he-goat (as given to butting)\nKJV: he goat.\n\nCognate Group: H8494 (Tiras), H8485 (Tema), H8491 (Tizite), H8436 (Tilon), H8481 (lower), H8478 (as), H8480 (Tahath), H8495 (he goat), H8482 (low)\nGreek Equivalents: G5131 τράγος",
    8496: "תֹּךְ (tôk | toke)\n\nDerivation: or תֹּוך; (Psalm 72:14), from the same base as H8432 תָּוֶךְ (in the sense of cutting to pieces)\nStrong's: oppression\nKJV: deceit, fraud.\n\nCognate Group: H8504 (blue), H8496 (deceit), H8501 (deceitful)\nGreek Equivalents: G303 ἀνά",
    8497: "תָּכָה (tâkâh | taw-kaw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to strew, i.e. encamp\nKJV: sit down.\n\nCognate Group: H8500 (peacock), H8497 (sit down)",
    8498: "תְּכוּנָה (tᵉkûwnâh | tek-oo-naw')\n\nDerivation: feminine passive participle of H8505 תָּכַן\nStrong's: adjustment, i.e. structure; by implication, equipage\nKJV: fashion, store.\n\nCognate Group: H3561 (cake), H8499 (seat), H3200 (Jachinites), H3559 (certain), H3651 (after that), H3560 (Chun), H8498 (fashion), H3562 (Conaniah), H4369 (base), H4349 (foundation), H4350 (base), H3199 (Jachin), H3204 (Jeconiah), H5225 (Nachon), H3563 (cup)",
    8499: "תְּכוּנָה (tᵉkûwnâh | tek-oo-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H3559 כּוּן ; or probably identical with H8498 תְּכוּנָה\nStrong's: something arranged or fixed, i.e. a place\nKJV: seat.\n\nCognate Group: H3561 (cake), H8499 (seat), H3200 (Jachinites), H3559 (certain), H3651 (after that), H3560 (Chun), H8498 (fashion), H3562 (Conaniah), H4369 (base), H4349 (foundation), H4350 (base), H3199 (Jachin), H3204 (Jeconiah), H5225 (Nachon), H3563 (cup)\nGreek Equivalents: G2889 κόσμος, G5287 ὑπόστασις",
    8500: "תֻּכִּי (tukkîy | took-kee')\n\nDerivation: or תּוּכִּי\nStrong's: probably of foreign derivation; some imported creature, probably a peacock\nKJV: peacock.\n\nCognate Group: H8500 (peacock), H8497 (sit down)",
    8501: "תָּכָךְ (tâkâk | taw-kawk')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning\nStrong's: to dissever, i.e. crush\nKJV: deceitful.\n\nCognate Group: H8504 (blue), H8496 (deceit), H8501 (deceitful)",
    8502: "תִּכְלָה (tiklâh | tik-law')\n\nDerivation: from H3615 כָּלָה\nStrong's: completeness\nKJV: perfection.\n\nCognate Group: H3617 (altogether), H3630 (Chilion), H3627 (armour), H3615 (accomplish), H8503 (end), H8502 (perfection), H4357 (perfect), H3622 (Chelluh), H3631 (consumption), H3616 (fail)",
    8503: "תַּכְלִית (taklîyth | tak-leeth')\n\nDerivation: from H3615 כָּלָה\nStrong's: completion; by implication, an extremity\nKJV: end, perfect(-ion).\n\nCognate Group: H3617 (altogether), H3630 (Chilion), H3627 (armour), H3615 (accomplish), H8503 (end), H8502 (perfection), H4357 (perfect), H3622 (Chelluh), H3631 (consumption), H3616 (fail)\nGreek Equivalents: G2078 ἔσχατος, G4009 πέρας, G5046 τέλειος",
    8504: "תְּכֵלֶת (tᵉkêleth | tek-ay'-leth)\n\nDerivation: probably for H7827 שְׁחֶלֶת\nStrong's: the cerulean mussel, i.e. the color (violet) obtained therefrom or stuff dyed therewith\nKJV: blue.\n\nCognate Group: H8504 (blue), H8496 (deceit), H8501 (deceitful)\nGreek Equivalents: G5098 τιμωρία, G5191 ὑακίνθινος, G5192 ὑάκινθος",
    8505: "תָּכַן (tâkan | taw-kan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to balance, i.e. measure out (by weight or dimension); figuratively, arrange, equalize, through the idea of levelling (ment. estimate, test)\nKJV: bear up, direct, be (un-)equal, mete, ponder, tell, weigh.\n\nCognate Group: H8506 (measure), H8508 (pattern), H8507 (Tochen), H4971 (composition), H8505 (bear up)\nGreek Equivalents: G1097 γινώσκω, G2090 ἑτοιμάζω, G2112 εὐθέως, G2117 εὐθύς, G2720 κατευθύνω, G4732 στερεόω",
    8506: "תֹּכֶן (tôken | to'-ken)\n\nDerivation: from H8505 תָּכַן\nStrong's: a fixed quantity\nKJV: measure, tale.\n\nCognate Group: H8506 (measure), H8508 (pattern), H8507 (Tochen), H4971 (composition), H8505 (bear up)",
    8507: "תֹּכֶן (Tôken | to'-ken)\n\nDerivation: the same as H8506 תֹּכֶן\nStrong's: Token, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Tochen.\n\nCognate Group: H8506 (measure), H8508 (pattern), H8507 (Tochen), H4971 (composition), H8505 (bear up)",
    8508: "תׇּכְנִית (toknîyth | tok-neeth')\n\nDerivation: from H8506 תֹּכֶן\nStrong's: admeasurement, i.e. consummation\nKJV: pattern, sum.\n\nCognate Group: H8506 (measure), H8508 (pattern), H8507 (Tochen), H4971 (composition), H8505 (bear up)\nGreek Equivalents: G3669 ὁμοίωσις",
    8509: "תַּכְרִיךְ (takrîyk | tak-reek')\n\nDerivation: apparently from an unused root meaning to encompass\nStrong's: a wrapper or robe\nKJV: garment.\n\nCognate Group: H8509 (garment)\nGreek Equivalents: G1238 διάδημα",
    8510: "תֵּל (têl | tale)\n\nDerivation: by contraction from H8524 תָּלַל\nStrong's: a mound\nKJV: heap, [idiom] strength.\n\nCognate Group: H8524 (eminent), H8510 (heap), H8521 (Tel-haresha), H8528 (Tel-melah), H8534 (bushy), H8512 (Tel-abib)\nGreek Equivalents: G5038 τεῖχος",
    8511: "תָּלָא (tâlâʼ | taw-law')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to suspend; figuratively (through hesitation) to be uncertain; by implication (of mental dependence) to habituate\nKJV: be bent, hang (in doubt).\n\nCognate Group: H8515 (Telassar), H8511 (be bent)\nGreek Equivalents: G2476 ἵστημι, G2910 κρεμάννυμι",
    8512: "תֵּל אָבִיב (Têl ʼÂbîyb | tale aw-beeb')\n\nDerivation: from H8510 תֵּל and H24 אָבִיב ; mound of green growth\nStrong's: Tel-Abib, a place in Chaldaea\nKJV: Tel-abib.\n\nCognate Group: H8524 (eminent), H8510 (heap), H8521 (Tel-haresha), H8528 (Tel-melah), H8534 (bushy), H8512 (Tel-abib)",
    8513: "תְּלָאָה (tᵉlâʼâh | tel-aw-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H3811 לָאָה\nStrong's: distress\nKJV: travail, travel, trouble.\n\nCognate Group: H4972 (what a weariness), H8513 (travail), H3811 (faint), H3812 (Leah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2552 κακοπάθεια, G3449 μόχθος",
    8514: "תַּלְאוּבָה (talʼûwbâh | tal-oo-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H3851 לַהַב\nStrong's: desiccation\nKJV: great drought.\n\nCognate Group: H8514 (great drought)",
    8515: "תְּלַאשַּׂר (Tᵉlaʼssar | tel-as-sar')\n\nDerivation: or תְּלַשַּׂר; of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Telassar, a region of Assyria\nKJV: Telassar.\n\nCognate Group: H8515 (Telassar), H8511 (be bent)",
    8516: "תַּלְבֹּשֶׁת (talbôsheth | tal-bo'-sheth)\n\nDerivation: from H3847 לָבַשׁ\nStrong's: a garment\nKJV: clothing.\n\nCognate Group: H3850 (Lod), H8516 (clothing), H3847 (apparel), H3849 (log), H3830 (apparel), H4403 (apparel), H1688 (Debir)",
    8517: "תְּלַג (tᵉlag | tel-ag')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H7950 שֶׁלֶג\nStrong's: snow\nKJV: snow.\n\nCognate Group: H8450 (bullock), H8460 (under), H8517 (snow), H8479 (under), H8429 (be astonied)\nGreek Equivalents: G5510 χιών",
    8518: "תָּלָה (tâlâh | taw-law')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to suspend (especially to gibbet)\nKJV: hang (up).\n\nCognate Group: H8522 (quiver), H8518 (hang), H8520 (Telah), H3494 (Jethlah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2910 κρεμάννυμι, G4717 σταυρόω",
    8519: "תְּלוּנָה (tᵉlûwnâh | tel-oo-naw')\n\nDerivation: or תּלֻנָּה; from H3885 לוּן in the sense of obstinacy\nStrong's: a grumbling\nKJV: murmuring.\n\nCognate Group: H3885 (abide), H8519 (murmuring)\nGreek Equivalents: G1112 γογγυσμός",
    8520: "תֶּלַח (Telach | teh'-lakh)\n\nDerivation: probably from an unused root meaning to dissever; breach\nStrong's: Telach, an Israelite\nKJV: Telah.\n\nCognate Group: H8522 (quiver), H8518 (hang), H8520 (Telah), H3494 (Jethlah)",
    8521: "תֵּל חַרְשָׁא (Têl Charshâʼ | tale khar-shaw')\n\nDerivation: from H8510 תֵּל and the feminine of H2798 חֲרָשִׁים ; mound of workmanship\nStrong's: Tel-Charsha, a place in Babylonia\nKJV: Tel-haresha, Tel-harsa.\n\nCognate Group: H8524 (eminent), H8510 (heap), H8521 (Tel-haresha), H8528 (Tel-melah), H8534 (bushy), H8512 (Tel-abib)",
    8522: "תְּלִי (tᵉlîy | tel-ee')\n\nDerivation: probably from H8518 תָּלָה\nStrong's: a quiver (as slung)\nKJV: quiver.\n\nCognate Group: H8522 (quiver), H8518 (hang), H8520 (Telah), H3494 (Jethlah)",
    8523: "תְּלִיתַי (tᵉlîythay | tel-ee-thah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) or תַּלְתִּי; (Aramaic), ordinal from H8532 תְּלָת\nStrong's: third\nKJV: third.\n\nCognate Group: H8532 (third), H8523 (third), H8533 (thirty), H8540 (wonder), H8536 ([idiom] thence), H8531 (third)",
    8524: "תָּלַל (tâlal | taw-lal')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to pile up, i.e. elevate\nKJV: eminent. Compare H2048 הָתַל .\n\nCognate Group: H8524 (eminent), H8510 (heap), H8521 (Tel-haresha), H8528 (Tel-melah), H8534 (bushy), H8512 (Tel-abib)",
    8525: "תֶּלֶם (telem | teh'-lem)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to accumulate\nStrong's: a bank or terrace\nKJV: furrow, ridge.\n\nCognate Group: H8526 (Talmai), H8525 (furrow)",
    8526: "תַּלְמַי (Talmay | tal-mah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from H8525 תֶּלֶם ; ridged\nStrong's: Talmai, the name of a Canaanite and a Syrian\nKJV: Talmai.\n\nCognate Group: H8526 (Talmai), H8525 (furrow)\nGreek Equivalents: G918 Βαρθολομαῖος",
    8527: "תַּלְמִיד (talmîyd | tal-meed')\n\nDerivation: from H3925 לָמַד\nStrong's: a pupil\nKJV: scholar.\n\nCognate Group: H3927 (Lemuel), H3928 (accustomed), H3929 (Lamech), H3925 (accustomed), H4451 (goad), H8527 (scholar)",
    8528: "תֵּל מֶלַח (Têl Melach | tale meh'-lakh)\n\nDerivation: from H8510 תֵּל and H4417 מֶלַח ; mound of salt\nStrong's: Tel-Melach, a place in Babylonia\nKJV: Tel-melah.\n\nCognate Group: H8524 (eminent), H8510 (heap), H8521 (Tel-haresha), H8528 (Tel-melah), H8534 (bushy), H8512 (Tel-abib)",
    8529: "תָּלַע (tâlaʻ | taw-law')\n\nDerivation: a denominative from H8438 תֹּולָע\nStrong's: to crimson, i.e. dye that color\nKJV: [idiom] scarlet.\n\nCognate Group: H8530 (armoury), H8439 (Tola), H4459 (great tooth), H4973 (cheek tooth), H8529 ([idiom] scarlet), H8438 (crimson), H8440 (Tolaites)",
    8530: "תַּלְפִּיָּה (talpîyâh | tal-pee-yaw')\n\nDerivation: feminine from an unused root meaning to tower\nStrong's: something tall, i.e. (plural collective) slenderness\nKJV: armoury.\n\nCognate Group: H8530 (armoury), H8439 (Tola), H4459 (great tooth), H4973 (cheek tooth), H8529 ([idiom] scarlet), H8438 (crimson), H8440 (Tolaites)",
    8531: "תְּלַת (tᵉlath | tel-ath')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H8532 תְּלָת\nStrong's: a tertiary rank\nKJV: third.\n\nCognate Group: H8532 (third), H8523 (third), H8533 (thirty), H8540 (wonder), H8536 ([idiom] thence), H8531 (third)",
    8532: "תְּלָת (tᵉlâth | tel-awth')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) masculine תְּלָתָה; (Aramaic), or תְּלָתָא; (Aramaic), corresponding to H7969 שָׁלֹושׁ\nStrong's: three or third\nKJV: third, three.\n\nCognate Group: H8532 (third), H8523 (third), H8533 (thirty), H8540 (wonder), H8536 ([idiom] thence), H8531 (third)\nGreek Equivalents: G3313 μέρος",
    8533: "תְּלָתִין (tᵉlâthîyn | tel-aw-theen')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) multiple of H8532 תְּלָת\nStrong's: ten times three\nKJV: thirty.\n\nCognate Group: H8532 (third), H8523 (third), H8533 (thirty), H8540 (wonder), H8536 ([idiom] thence), H8531 (third)",
    8534: "תַּלְתַּל (taltal | tal-tal')\n\nDerivation: by reduplication, from H8524 תָּלַל through the idea of vibration\nStrong's: a trailing bough (as pendulous)\nKJV: bushy.\n\nCognate Group: H8524 (eminent), H8510 (heap), H8521 (Tel-haresha), H8528 (Tel-melah), H8534 (bushy), H8512 (Tel-abib)",
    8535: "תָּם (tâm | tawm)\n\nDerivation: from H8552 תָּמַם\nStrong's: complete; usually (morally) pious; specifically, gentle, dear\nKJV: coupled together, perfect, plain, undefiled, upright.\n\nCognate Group: H8549 (without blemish), H8538 (integrity), H8550 (Thummim), H8537 (full), H8535 (coupled together), H8552 (accomplish), H4974 (men)\nGreek Equivalents: G172 ἄκακος, G228 ἀληθινός, G273 ἄμεμπτος",
    8536: "תָּם (tâm | tawm)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8033 שָׁם\nStrong's: there\nKJV: [idiom] thence, there, [idiom] where.\n\nCognate Group: H8532 (third), H8523 (third), H8533 (thirty), H8540 (wonder), H8536 ([idiom] thence), H8531 (third)",
    8537: "תֹּם (tôm | tome)\n\nDerivation: from H8552 תָּמַם\nStrong's: completeness; figuratively, prosperity; usually (morally) innocence\nKJV: full, integrity, perfect(-ion), simplicity, upright(-ly, -ness), at a venture. See H8550 תֻּמִּים .\n\nCognate Group: H8549 (without blemish), H8538 (integrity), H8550 (Thummim), H8537 (full), H8535 (coupled together), H8552 (accomplish), H4974 (men)\nGreek Equivalents: G225 ἀλήθεια, G299 ἄμωμος, G572 ἁπλότης, G575 ἀπό, G1212 δῆλος, G2513 καθαρός, G3350 μετοικεσία, G3741 ὅσιος, G3742 ὁσιότης",
    8538: "תֻּמָּה (tummâh | toom-maw')\n\nDerivation: feminine of H8537 תֹּם\nStrong's: innocence\nKJV: integrity.\n\nCognate Group: H8549 (without blemish), H8538 (integrity), H8550 (Thummim), H8537 (full), H8535 (coupled together), H8552 (accomplish), H4974 (men)\nGreek Equivalents: G5047 τελειότης",
    8539: "תָּמַהּ (tâmahh | taw-mah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to be in consternation\nKJV: be amazed, be astonished, marvel(-lously), wonder.\n\nCognate Group: H8547 (Tamah), H8542 (Tammuz), H8539 (be amazed), H8541 (astonishment)\nGreek Equivalents: G1839 ἐξίστημι, G2296 θαυμάζω, G2297 θαυμάσιος",
    8540: "תְּמַהּ (tᵉmahh | tem-ah')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H8539 תָּמַהּ\nStrong's: a miracle\nKJV: wonder.\n\nCognate Group: H8532 (third), H8523 (third), H8533 (thirty), H8540 (wonder), H8536 ([idiom] thence), H8531 (third)\nGreek Equivalents: G5059 τέρας",
    8541: "תִּמָּהֹון (timmâhôwn | tim-maw-hone')\n\nDerivation: from H8539 תָּמַהּ\nStrong's: consternation\nKJV: astonishment.\n\nCognate Group: H8547 (Tamah), H8542 (Tammuz), H8539 (be amazed), H8541 (astonishment)\nGreek Equivalents: G1611 ἔκστασις",
    8542: "תַּמּוּז (Tammûwz | tam-mooz')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Tammuz, a Phoenician deity\nKJV: Tammuz.\n\nCognate Group: H8547 (Tamah), H8542 (Tammuz), H8539 (be amazed), H8541 (astonishment)",
    8543: "תְּמֹול (tᵉmôwl | tem-ole')\n\nDerivation: or תְּמֹל; probably for H865 אֶתְמֹול ; sometimes with H8032 שִׁלְשֹׁום \nStrong's: properly, ago, i.e. a (short or long) time since; especially yesterday, or day before yesterday\nKJV: [phrase] before (-time), [phrase] these (three) days, [phrase] heretofore, [phrase] time past, yesterday.\n\nCognate Group: H8551 (hold), H865 (before time), H8543 (before)\nGreek Equivalents: G1538 ἕκαστος, G2250 ἡμέρα, G5504 χθές",
    8544: "תְּמוּנָה (tᵉmûwnâh | tem-oo-naw')\n\nDerivation: or תְּמֻנָה; from H4327 מִין\nStrong's: something portioned (i.e. fashioned) out, as ashape, i.e. (indefinitely) phantom, or (specifically) embodiment, or (figuratively) manifestation (of favor)\nKJV: image, likeness, similitude.\n\nCognate Group: H4327 (kind), H8544 (image)\nGreek Equivalents: G1391 δόξα, G3444 μορφή, G3667 ὁμοίωμα",
    8545: "תְּמוּרָה (tᵉmûwrâh | tem-oo-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H4171 מוּר\nStrong's: barter, compensation\nKJV: (ex-) change(-ing), recompense, restitution.\n\nCognate Group: H4171 ([idiom] at all), H4185 (cease), H8545 (change), H4177 (razor), H4173 (threshing instrument)\nGreek Equivalents: G465 ἀντάλλαγμα",
    8546: "תְּמוּתָה (tᵉmûwthâh | tem-oo-thaw')\n\nDerivation: from H4191 מוּת\nStrong's: execution (as a doom)\nKJV: death, die.\n\nCognate Group: H4463 (death), H4191 ([idiom] at all), H4194 (dead), H8546 (death)",
    8547: "תֶּמַח (Temach | teh'-makh)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Temach, one of the Nethinim\nKJV: Tamah, Thamah.\n\nCognate Group: H8547 (Tamah), H8542 (Tammuz), H8539 (be amazed), H8541 (astonishment)",
    8548: "תָּמִיד (tâmîyd | taw-meed')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to stretch\nStrong's: properly, continuance (as indefinite extension); but used only (attributively as adjective) constant (or adverbially, constantly); ellipt. the regular (daily) sacrifice\nKJV: alway(-s), continual (employment, -ly), daily, (n-)ever(-more), perpetual.\n\nCognate Group: H8548 (alway)\nGreek Equivalents: G104 ἀεί, G165 αἰών, G2378 θυσία, G3650 ὅλος, G3956 πᾶς, G3956 πᾶς, G5056 τέλος",
    8549: "תָּמִים (tâmîym | taw-meem')\n\nDerivation: from H8552 תָּמַם\nStrong's: entire (literally, figuratively or morally); also (as noun) integrity, truth\nKJV: without blemish, complete, full, perfect, sincerely (-ity), sound, without spot, undefiled, upright(-ly), whole.\n\nCognate Group: H8549 (without blemish), H8538 (integrity), H8550 (Thummim), H8537 (full), H8535 (coupled together), H8552 (accomplish), H4974 (men)\nGreek Equivalents: G121 ἄθωος, G273 ἄμεμπτος, G299 ἄμωμος, G1342 δίκαιος, G1346 δικαίως, G2118 εὐθύτης, G3648 ὁλόκληρος, G3650 ὅλος, G3741 ὅσιος, G3742 ὁσιότης, G5046 τέλειος, G5047 τελειότης",
    8550: "תֻּמִּים (Tummîym | toom-meem')\n\nDerivation: plural of H8537 תֹּם\nStrong's: perfections, i.e. (techn.) one of the epithets of the objects in the high-priest's breastplate as an emblem of complete Truth\nKJV: Thummim.\n\nCognate Group: H8549 (without blemish), H8538 (integrity), H8550 (Thummim), H8537 (full), H8535 (coupled together), H8552 (accomplish), H4974 (men)",
    8551: "תָּמַךְ (tâmak | taw-mak')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to sustain; by implication, to obtain, keep fast; figuratively, to help, follow close\nKJV: (take, up-) hold (up), maintain, retain, stay (up).\n\nCognate Group: H8551 (hold), H865 (before time), H8543 (before)\nGreek Equivalents: G482 ἀντιλαμβάνομαι, G600 ἀποκαθίστημι, G803 ἀσφάλεια, G805 ἀσφαλίζω, G2043 ἐρείδω, G2675 καταρτίζω, G4741 στηρίζω",
    8552: "תָּמַם (tâmam | taw-mam')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to complete, in a good or a bad sense, literal, or figurative, transitive or intransitive\nKJV: accomplish, cease, be clean (pass-) ed, consume, have done, (come to an, have an, make an) end, fail, come to the full, be all gone, [idiom] be all here, be (make) perfect, be spent, sum, be (shew self) upright, be wasted, whole.\n\nCognate Group: H8549 (without blemish), H8538 (integrity), H8550 (Thummim), H8537 (full), H8535 (coupled together), H8552 (accomplish), H4974 (men)\nGreek Equivalents: G121 ἄθωος, G355 ἀναλίσκω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1810 ἐξαίφνης, G1831 ἐξέρχομαι, G2271 ἡσυχία, G3973 παύω, G4098 πίπτω, G4137 πληρόω, G4931 συντελέω, G4972 σφραγίζω, G5048 τελειόω, G5080 τήκω",
    8553: "תִּמְנָה (Timnâh | tim-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H4487 מָנָה ; a portion assigned\nStrong's: Timnah, the name of two places in Palestine\nKJV: Timnah, Timnath, Thimnathah.\n\nCognate Group: H8553 (Timnah), H4487 (appoint), H4521 (portion), H4507 (number), H8556 (Timnath-heres), H4490 (such things as belonged), H4489 (time), H4497 (son), H8554 (Timnite), H4488 (maneh)",
    8554: "תִּמְנִי (Timnîy | tim-nee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from H8553 תִּמְנָה\nStrong's: a Timnite or inhabitant of Timnah\nKJV: Timnite.\n\nCognate Group: H8553 (Timnah), H4487 (appoint), H4521 (portion), H4507 (number), H8556 (Timnath-heres), H4490 (such things as belonged), H4489 (time), H4497 (son), H8554 (Timnite), H4488 (maneh)",
    8555: "תִּמְנָע (Timnâʻ | tim-naw')\n\nDerivation: from H4513 מָנַע ; restraint\nStrong's: Timna, the name of two Edomites\nKJV: Timna, Timnah.\n\nCognate Group: H8555 (Timna), H4522 (discomfited), H4520 (of Manasseh), H4519 (Manasseh), H4513 (deny), H3234 (Imna)",
    8556: "תִּמְנַת חֶרֶס (Timnath Chereç | tim-nath kheh'-res)\n\nDerivation: or תִּמְנַת סֶרַח; from H8553 תִּמְנָה and H2775 חֶרֶס ; portion of (the) sun\nStrong's: Timnath-Cheres, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Timnath-heres, Timnath-serah.\n\nCognate Group: H8553 (Timnah), H4487 (appoint), H4521 (portion), H4507 (number), H8556 (Timnath-heres), H4490 (such things as belonged), H4489 (time), H4497 (son), H8554 (Timnite), H4488 (maneh)",
    8557: "תֶּמֶס (temeç | teh'-mes)\n\nDerivation: from H4529 מָסָה\nStrong's: liquefaction, i.e. disappearance\nKJV: melt.\n\nCognate Group: H4531 (temptation), H8557 (melt), H4523 (is afflicted), H4549 (discourage)",
    8558: "תָּמָר (tâmâr | taw-mawr')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to be erect\nStrong's: a palm tree\nKJV: palm (tree).\n\nCognate Group: H8559 (Tamar), H8564 (high heap), H8560 (palm tree), H8558 (palm), H8490 (pillar), H8561 (palm tree)",
    8559: "תָּמָר (Tâmâr | taw-mawr')\n\nDerivation: the same as H8558 תָּמָר\nStrong's: Tamar, the name of three women and a place\nKJV: Tamar.\n\nCognate Group: H8559 (Tamar), H8564 (high heap), H8560 (palm tree), H8558 (palm), H8490 (pillar), H8561 (palm tree)\nGreek Equivalents: G2283 Θάμαρ",
    8560: "תֹּמֶר (tômer | to'-mer)\n\nDerivation: from the same root as H8558 תָּמָר\nStrong's: a palm trunk\nKJV: palm tree.\n\nCognate Group: H8559 (Tamar), H8564 (high heap), H8560 (palm tree), H8558 (palm), H8490 (pillar), H8561 (palm tree)",
    8561: "תִּמֹּר (timmôr | tim-more')\n\nDerivation: (plural or (feminine) תִּמֹּרָה; (singular and plural), from the same root as H8558 תָּמָר\nStrong's: (architectural) a palm-like pilaster (i.e. umbellate)\nKJV: palm tree.\n\nCognate Group: H8559 (Tamar), H8564 (high heap), H8560 (palm tree), H8558 (palm), H8490 (pillar), H8561 (palm tree)\nGreek Equivalents: G822 ἀτμίς",
    8562: "תַּמְרוּק (tamrûwq | tam-rook')\n\nDerivation: or תַּמְרֻק; or תַּמְרִיק; from H4838 מָרַק\nStrong's: properly, a scouring, i.e. soap or perfumery forthe bath; figuratively, a detergent\nKJV: [idiom] cleanse, (thing for) purification(-fying).\n\nCognate Group: H4838 (bright), H4795 (purification), H8562 ([idiom] cleanse)",
    8563: "תַּמְרוּר (tamrûwr | tam-roor')\n\nDerivation: from H4843 מָרַר\nStrong's: bitterness (plural as collective)\nKJV: [idiom] most bitter(-ly).\n\nCognate Group: H4753 (myrrh), H4844 (bitter), H4785 (Marah), H4787 (bitterness), H4843 (bitter), H4786 (grief), H4848 (Merarites), H4755 (Mara), H4815 (bitter), H4845 (gall), H8563 ([idiom] most bitter), H4847 (Merari), H4814 (bitterness), H4472 (bitterness), H4846 (bitter), H4751 (angry), H4470 (bitterness)",
    8564: "תַּמְרוּר (tamrûwr | tam-roor')\n\nDerivation: from the same root as H8558 תָּמָר\nStrong's: an erection, i.e. pillar (probably for a guide-board)\nKJV: high heap.\n\nCognate Group: H8559 (Tamar), H8564 (high heap), H8560 (palm tree), H8558 (palm), H8490 (pillar), H8561 (palm tree)\nGreek Equivalents: G3602 ὀδυρμός, G3949 παροργίζω",
    8565: "תַּן (tan | tan)\n\nDerivation: from an unused root probably meaning to elongate\nStrong's: a monster (as preternaturally formed), i.e. a sea-serpent (or other huge marine animal); also a jackal (or other hideous land animal)\nKJV: dragon, whale. Compare H8577 תַּנִּין .\n\nCognate Group: H8565 (dragon), H8577 (dragon), H8568 (dragon)",
    8566: "תָּנָה (tânâh | taw-naw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to present (a mercenary inducement), i.e. bargain with (a harlot)\nKJV: hire.\n\nCognate Group: H3496 (Jathniel), H8566 (hire), H866 (reward)",
    8567: "תָּנָה (tânâh | taw-naw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root (identical with through the idea of attributing honor)\nStrong's: to ascribe (praise), i.e. celebrate, commemorate\nKJV: lament, rehearse.\n\nCognate Group: H8567 (lament)\nGreek Equivalents: G1325 δίδωμι, G2354 θρηνέω",
    8568: "תַּנָּה (tannâh | tan-naw')\n\nDerivation: probably feminine of H8565 תַּן\nStrong's: a female jackal\nKJV: dragon.\n\nCognate Group: H8565 (dragon), H8577 (dragon), H8568 (dragon)",
    8569: "תְּנוּאָה (tᵉnûwʼâh | ten-oo-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H5106 נוּא\nStrong's: alienation; by implication, enmity\nKJV: breach of promise, occasion.\n\nCognate Group: H5106 (break), H8569 (breach of promise)\nGreek Equivalents: G2372 θυμός",
    8570: "תְּנוּבָה (tᵉnûwbâh | ten-oo-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H5107 נוּב\nStrong's: produce\nKJV: fruit, increase.\n\nCognate Group: H5107 (bring forth), H8570 (fruit), H5109 (Nebai), H5108 (fruit)\nGreek Equivalents: G1080 γεννάω, G2590 καρπός",
    8571: "תְּנוּךְ (tᵉnûwk | ten-ook')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from the same as H594 אֲנָךְ through the idea of protraction\nStrong's: a pinnacle, i.e. extremity\nKJV: tip.\n\nCognate Group: H8574 (furnace), H8571 (tip)",
    8572: "תְּנוּמָה (tᵉnûwmâh | ten-oo-maw')\n\nDerivation: from H5123 נוּם\nStrong's: drowsiness, i.e. sleep\nKJV: slumber(-ing).\n\nCognate Group: H5123 (sleep), H5124 (drowsiness), H8572 (slumber), H3241 (Janum)",
    8573: "תְּנוּפָה (tᵉnûwphâh | ten-oo-faw')\n\nDerivation: from H5130 נוּף\nStrong's: a brandishing (in threat); by implication, tumult; specifically, the official undulation of sacrificial offerings\nKJV: offering, shaking, wave (offering).\n\nCognate Group: H5130 (lift up), H8573 (offering), H5299 (border)\nGreek Equivalents: G536 ἀπαρχή, G1390 δόμα",
    8574: "תַּנּוּר (tannûwr | tan-noor')\n\nDerivation: from H5216 נִיר\nStrong's: a fire-pot\nKJV: furnace, oven.\n\nCognate Group: H8574 (furnace), H8571 (tip)\nGreek Equivalents: G2823 κλίβανος",
    8575: "תַּנְחוּם (tanchûwm | tan-khoom')\n\nDerivation: or תַּנְחֻם; and (feminine) תַּנְחוּמָה; from H5162 נָחַם\nStrong's: compassion, solace\nKJV: comfort, consolation.\n\nCognate Group: H5164 (repentance), H5165 (comfort), H4505 (Menahem), H8575 (comfort), H5163 (Naham), H5151 (Nahum), H5149 (Nehum), H5150 (comfort), H5162 (comfort), H5167 (Nahamani), H5166 (Nehemiah), H8576 (Tanhumeth)",
    8576: "תַּנְחֻמֶת (Tanchumeth | tan-khoo'-meth)\n\nDerivation: for H8575 תַּנְחוּם (feminine)\nStrong's: Tanchumeth, an Israelite\nKJV: Tanhumeth.\n\nCognate Group: H5164 (repentance), H5165 (comfort), H4505 (Menahem), H8575 (comfort), H5163 (Naham), H5151 (Nahum), H5149 (Nehum), H5150 (comfort), H5162 (comfort), H5167 (Nahamani), H5166 (Nehemiah), H8576 (Tanhumeth)",
    8577: "תַּנִּין (tannîyn | tan-neen')\n\nDerivation: or תַּנִּים; (Ezekiel 29:3), intensive from the same as H8565 תַּן\nStrong's: a marine or land monster, i.e. sea-serpent or jackal\nKJV: dragon, sea-monster, serpent, whale.\n\nCognate Group: H8565 (dragon), H8577 (dragon), H8568 (dragon)\nGreek Equivalents: G1404 δράκων, G1404 δράκων, G2561 κάκωσις, G2785 κῆτος",
    8578: "תִּנְיָן (tinyân | tin-yawn')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8147 שְׁנַיִם\nStrong's: second\nKJV: second.\n\nCognate Group: H8614 (sheriff), H8578 (second), H8648 (second), H8579 (again)",
    8579: "תִּנְיָנוּת (tinyânûwth | tin-yaw-nooth')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) from H8578 תִּנְיָן\nStrong's: a second time\nKJV: again.\n\nCognate Group: H8614 (sheriff), H8578 (second), H8648 (second), H8579 (again)",
    8580: "תַּנְשֶׁמֶת (tanshemeth | tan-sheh'-meth)\n\nDerivation: from H5395 נָשַׁם\nStrong's: properly, a hard breather, i.e. the name of two unclean creatures, a lizard and abird (both perhaps from changing color through their irascibility), probably the tree-toad and the water-hen\nKJV: mole, swan.\n\nCognate Group: H8580 (mole), H5395 (destroy), H5397 (blast)",
    8581: "תַּעָב (taʻâb | taw-ab')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to loathe, i.e. (morally) detest\nKJV: (make to be) abhor(-red), (be, commit more, do) abominable(-y), [idiom] utterly.\n\nCognate Group: H8441 (abominable), H8374 (abhor), H8581 (abhor)\nGreek Equivalents: G948 βδελύσσω, G948 βδελύσσω, G1937 ἐπιθυμέω, G1971 ἐπιποθέω, G2729 κατισχύω, G3075 λυμαίνομαι, G4360 προσοχθίζω",
    8582: "תָּעָה (tâʻâh | taw-aw')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to vacillate, i.e. reel or stray (literally or figuratively); also causative of both\nKJV: (cause to) go astray, deceive, dissemble, (cause to, make to) err, pant, seduce, (make to) stagger, (cause to) wander, be out of the way.\n\nCognate Group: H8583 (Toi), H8442 (error), H8590 (Taanach), H8582 (go astray)\nGreek Equivalents: G1806 ἐξάγω, G1856 ἐξωθέω, G4105 πλανάω, G4105 πλανάω",
    8583: "תֹּעוּ (Tôʻûw | to'-oo)\n\nDerivation: or תֹּעִי; from H8582 תָּעָה ; error\nStrong's: Tou or Toi, a Syrian king\nKJV: Toi, Tou.\n\nCognate Group: H8583 (Toi), H8442 (error), H8590 (Taanach), H8582 (go astray)",
    8584: "תְּעוּדָה (tᵉʻûwdâh | teh-oo-daw')\n\nDerivation: from H5749 עוּד\nStrong's: attestation, i.e. a precept, usage\nKJV: testimony.\n\nCognate Group: H5713 (testimony), H5707 (witness), H8584 (testimony), H5749 (admonish), H5715 (testimony), H5750 (again), H5752 (Oded)",
    8585: "תְּעָלָה (tᵉʻâlâh | teh-aw-law')\n\nDerivation: from H5927 עָלָה\nStrong's: a channel (into which water is raised for irrigation); also a bandage or plaster (as placed upon a wound)\nKJV: conduit, cured, healing, little river, trench, watercourse.\n\nCognate Group: H5921 (above), H5941 (Eli), H5942 (upper), H131 (Adummim), H5930 (ascent), H5940 (pestle), H4610 (Maaleh-accrabim), H4607 (lifting up), H5935 (Alian), H5927 (arise), H8585 (conduit), H4605 (above), H4609 (things that come up), H5920 (above), H4608 (ascent), H5944 (ascent), H5929 (branch), H5945 (high), H5933 (Aliah)\nGreek Equivalents: G2281 θάλασσα, G4511 ῥύσις",
    8586: "תַּעֲלוּל (taʻălûwl | tah-al-ool')\n\nDerivation: from H5953 עָלַל\nStrong's: caprice (as a fit coming on), i.e. vexation; concretely a tyrant\nKJV: babe, delusion.\n\nCognate Group: H5955 (grapes), H5949 (act), H4611 (doing), H5950 (work), H8586 (babe), H5953 (abuse)\nGreek Equivalents: G1703 ἐμπαίκτης",
    8587: "תַּעֲלֻמָּה (taʻălummâh | tah-al-oom-maw')\n\nDerivation: from H5956 עָלַם\nStrong's: a secret\nKJV: thing that is hid, secret.\n\nCognate Group: H8587 (thing that is hid), H5963 (Almondilathaim), H5956 ([idiom] any ways), H5960 (Almon), H3281 (Jalam), H5964 (Alameth)",
    8588: "תַּעֲנוּג (taʻănûwg | tah-an-oog')\n\nDerivation: or תַּעֲנֻג; and (feminine) תַּעֲנֻגָה; from H6026 עָנַג\nStrong's: luxury\nKJV: delicate, delight, pleasant.\n\nCognate Group: H8588 (delicate), H6027 (delight), H6028 (delicate), H6026 (delicate)\nGreek Equivalents: G5172 τρυφή",
    8589: "תַּעֲנִית (taʻănîyth | tah-an-eeth')\n\nDerivation: from H6031 עָנָה\nStrong's: affliction (of self), i.e. fasting\nKJV: heaviness.\n\nCognate Group: H6031 (abase self), H6040 (afflicted), H6041 (afflicted), H6038 (gentleness), H6035 (humble), H6039 (affliction), H6037 (gentleness), H8589 (heaviness)",
    8590: "תַּעֲנָךְ (Taʻănâk | tah-an-awk')\n\nDerivation: or תַּעְנָךְ; of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Taanak or Tanak, a place in Palestine\nKJV: Taanach, Tanach.\n\nCognate Group: H8583 (Toi), H8442 (error), H8590 (Taanach), H8582 (go astray)",
    8591: "תָּעַע (tâʻaʻ | taw-ah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to cheat; by analogy, to maltreat\nKJV: deceive, misuse.\n\nCognate Group: H8601 (baked piece), H8591 (deceive), H8595 (error)\nGreek Equivalents: G1702 ἐμπαίζω, G2706 καταφρονέω",
    8592: "תַּעֲצֻמָה (taʻătsumâh | tah-ats-oo-maw')\n\nDerivation: from H6105 עָצַם\nStrong's: might (plural collective)\nKJV: power.\n\nCognate Group: H6099 (feeble), H8592 (power), H6106 (body), H6111 (Azmon), H6107 (Azem), H6105 (break the bones), H6108 (might), H6109 (abundance)",
    8593: "תַּעַר (taʻar | tah'-ar)\n\nDerivation: from H6168 עָרָה\nStrong's: a knife or razor (as making bare); also a scabbard (as being bare, i.e. empty)\nKJV: (pen-) knife, razor, scabbard, shave, sheath.\n\nCognate Group: H4638 (Maarath), H6168 (leave destitute), H6181 (bare), H8593 (knife), H6172 (nakedness), H4629 (meadows), H4626 (nakedness), H6171 (wild ass), H6169 (paper reed)",
    8594: "תַּעֲרֻבָה (taʻărubâh | tah-ar-oo-baw')\n\nDerivation: from H6148 עָרַב\nStrong's: suretyship, i.e. (concretely) a pledge\nKJV: [phrase] hostage.\n\nCognate Group: H6162 (pledge), H6148 (engage), H8594 (hostage), H6161 (pledge), H4627 (market)",
    8595: "תַּעְתֻּעַ (taʻtuaʻ | tah-too'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from H8591 תָּעַע\nStrong's: a fraud\nKJV: error.\n\nCognate Group: H8601 (baked piece), H8591 (deceive), H8595 (error)",
    8596: "תֹּף (tôph | tofe)\n\nDerivation: from H8608 תָּפַף contracted\nStrong's: a tambourine\nKJV: tabret, timbrel.\n\nCognate Group: H8596 (tabret), H8608 (taber)\nGreek Equivalents: G836 αὐλός",
    8597: "תִּפְאָרָה (tiphʼârâh | tif-aw-raw')\n\nDerivation: or תִּפְאֶרֶת; from H6286 פָּאַר\nStrong's: ornament (abstractly or concretely, literally or figuratively)\nKJV: beauty(-iful), bravery, comely, fair, glory(-ious), honour, majesty.\n\nCognate Group: H6286 (beautify), H8597 (beauty), H6287 (beauty)\nGreek Equivalents: G1391 δόξα, G2745 καύχημα, G2746 καύχησις, G2889 κόσμος, G3168 μεγαλειότης, G3172 μεγαλωσύνη, G5172 τρυφή",
    8598: "תַּפּוּחַ (tappûwach | tap-poo'-akh)\n\nDerivation: from H5301 נָפַח\nStrong's: an apple (from its fragrance), i.e. the fruit or the tree (probably includ. others of the pome order, as the quince, the orange, etc.)\nKJV: apple (tree). See also H1054 בֵּית תַּפּוּחַ .\n\nCognate Group: H5887 (En-tappuah), H5300 (Nephisesim), H4646 (giving up), H8598 (apple), H5304 (Nephusim), H5301 (blow), H4647 (bellows), H8599 (Tappuah), H5306 (emerald), H5302 (Nophah)",
    8599: "תַּפּוּחַ (Tappûwach | tap-poo'-akh)\n\nDerivation: the same as H8598 תַּפּוּחַ\nStrong's: Tappuach, the name of two places in Palestine, also of an Israelite\nKJV: Tappuah.\n\nCognate Group: H5887 (En-tappuah), H5300 (Nephisesim), H4646 (giving up), H8598 (apple), H5304 (Nephusim), H5301 (blow), H4647 (bellows), H8599 (Tappuah), H5306 (emerald), H5302 (Nophah)",
    8600: "תְּפֹוצָה (tᵉphôwtsâh | tef-o-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: from H6327 פּוּץ\nStrong's: a dispersal\nKJV: dispersion.\n\nCognate Group: H8600 (dispersion), H6327 (break in pieces), H4650 (maul)",
    8601: "תֻּפִין (tuphîyn | too-feen')\n\nDerivation: from H644 אָפָה\nStrong's: cookery, i.e. (concretely) a cake\nKJV: baked piece.\n\nCognate Group: H8601 (baked piece), H8591 (deceive), H8595 (error)",
    8602: "תָּפֵל (tâphêl | taw-fale')\n\nDerivation: from an unused root meaning to smear\nStrong's: plaster (as gummy) or slime; (figuratively) frivolity\nKJV: foolish things, unsavoury, untempered.\n\nCognate Group: H8602 (foolish things), H8604 (folly)\nGreek Equivalents: G877 ἀφροσύνη",
    8603: "תֹּפֶל (Tôphel | to'-fel)\n\nDerivation: from the same as H8602 תָּפֵל ; quagmire\nStrong's: Tophel, a place near the Desert\nKJV: Tophel.\n\nCognate Group: H8602 (foolish things), H8603 (Tophel)",
    8604: "תִּפְלָה (tiphlâh | tif-law')\n\nDerivation: from the same as H8602 תָּפֵל\nStrong's: frivolity\nKJV: folly, foolishly.\n\nCognate Group: H8602 (foolish things), H8604 (folly)",
    8605: "תְּפִלָּה (tᵉphillâh | tef-il-law')\n\nDerivation: from H6419 פָּלַל\nStrong's: intercession, supplication; by implication, a hymn\nKJV: prayer.\n\nCognate Group: H6415 (judgment), H6397 (Pelonite), H6414 (judge), H654 (Ephlal), H8605 (prayer), H6421 (Pelaliah), H6419 (intreat), H6417 (judgment), H6420 (Palal), H6416 (judge)\nGreek Equivalents: G1162 δέησις, G2171 εὐχή, G2172 εὔχομαι, G4335 προσευχή, G5215 ὕμνος",
    8606: "תִּפְלֶצֶת (tiphletseth | tif-leh'-tseth)\n\nDerivation: from H6426 פָּלַץ\nStrong's: fearfulness\nKJV: terrible.\n\nCognate Group: H4656 (idol), H6427 (fearfulness), H8606 (terrible), H6426 (tremble)",
    8607: "תִּפְסַח (Tiphçach | tif-sakh')\n\nDerivation: from H6452 פָּסַח ; ford\nStrong's: Tiphsach, a place in Mesopotamia\nKJV: Tipsah.\n\nCognate Group: H6453 (passover), H8607 (Tipsah), H6452 (halt)",
    8608: "תָּפַף (tâphaph | taw-faf')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to drum, i.e. play (as) on the tambourine\nKJV: taber, play with timbrels.\n\nCognate Group: H8596 (tabret), H8608 (taber)\nGreek Equivalents: G5350 φθέγγομαι",
    8609: "תָּפַר (tâphar | taw-far')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to sew\nKJV: (women that) sew (together).\n\nCognate Group: H8609 (sew)",
    8610: "תָּפַשׂ (tâphas | taw-fas')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to manipulate, i.e. seize; chiefly to capture, wield, specifically, to overlay; figuratively, to use unwarrantably\nKJV: catch, handle, (lay, take) hold (on, over), stop, [idiom] surely, surprise, take.\n\nCognate Group: H8612 (Tophet), H8610 (catch), H8613 (Tophet)\nGreek Equivalents: G259 ἅλωσις, G305 ἀναβαίνω, G472 ἀντέχομαι, G971 βιάζω, G1294 διαστρέφω, G1949 ἐπιλαμβάνομαι, G1986 ἐπισπάομαι, G2043 ἐρείδω, G2340 θηρεύω, G2528 καθοπλίζω, G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G2722 κατέχω, G2902 κρατέω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3660 ὀμνύω, G3860 παραδίδωμι, G4815 συλλαμβάνω",
    8611: "תֹּפֶת (tôpheth | to'-feth)\n\nDerivation: from the base of H8608 תָּפַף\nStrong's: a smiting, i.e. (figuratively) contempt\nKJV: tabret.\n\nCognate Group: H8611 (tabret)",
    8612: "תֹּפֶת (Tôpheth | to'-feth)\n\nDerivation: the same as H8611 תֹּפֶת\nStrong's: Topheth, a place near Jerusalem\nKJV: Tophet, Topheth.\n\nCognate Group: H8612 (Tophet), H8610 (catch), H8613 (Tophet)",
    8613: "תׇּפְתֶּה (Tophteh | tof-teh')\n\nDerivation: probably a form of H8612 תֹּפֶת\nStrong's: Tophteh, a place of cremation\nKJV: Tophet.\n\nCognate Group: H8612 (Tophet), H8610 (catch), H8613 (Tophet)",
    8614: "תִּפְתַּי (tiphtay | tif-tah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) perhaps from H8199 שָׁפַט\nStrong's: judicial, i.e. a lawyer\nKJV: sheriff.\n\nCognate Group: H8614 (sheriff), H8578 (second), H8648 (second), H8579 (again)\nGreek Equivalents: G1849 ἐξουσία",
    8615: "תִּקְוָה (tiqvâh | tik-vaw')\n\nDerivation: from H6960 קָוָה ; (compare H6961 קָוֶה)\n\nStrong's: literally a cord (as an attachment); figuratively, expectancy\nKJV: expectation(-ted), hope, live, thing that I long for.\n\nCognate Group: H6978 ([idiom] meted out), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H8615 (expectation), H6960 (gather), H8616 (Tikvah), H6961 (line), H8445 (Tikvath)\nGreek Equivalents: G18 ἀγαθός, G1680 ἐλπίς, G4592 σημεῖον, G4864 συναγωγή, G5287 ὑπόστασις",
    8616: "תִּקְוָה (Tiqvâh | tik-vaw')\n\nDerivation: the same as H8615 תִּקְוָה\nStrong's: Tikvah, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: Tikvah.\n\nCognate Group: H6978 ([idiom] meted out), H6957 (line), H4723 (abiding), H8615 (expectation), H6960 (gather), H8616 (Tikvah), H6961 (line), H8445 (Tikvath)",
