    8624: "תַּקִּיף (taqqîyph | tak-keef')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8623 תַּקִּיף \nStrong's: powerful\nKJV: mighty, strong.\n\nCognate Group: H8631 (make firm), H8624 (mighty), H8632 (might)",
    8625: "תְּקַל (tᵉqal | tek-al')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8254 שָׁקַל\nStrong's: to balance\nKJV: Tekel, be weighed.\n\nCognate Group: H8625 (Tekel)\nGreek Equivalents: G2476 ἵστημι",
    8626: "תָּקַן (tâqan | taw-kan')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to equalize, i.e. straighten (intransitive or transitive); figuratively, to compose\nKJV: set in order, make straight.\n\nCognate Group: H8626 (set in order)\nGreek Equivalents: G2885 κοσμέω, G2887 κόσμιος",
    8627: "תְּקַן (tᵉqan | tek-an')\n\nDerivation: (Aramaic) corresponding to H8626 תָּקַן\nStrong's: to straighten up, i.e. confirm\nKJV: establish.\n\nCognate Group: H8652 (porter), H8674 (Tatnai), H8651 (gate mouth), H8627 (establish)\nGreek Equivalents: G2901 κραταιόω, G2902 κρατέω",
    8628: "תָּקַע (tâqaʻ | taw-kah')\n\nDerivation: a primitive root\nStrong's: to clatter, i.e. slap (the hands together), clang (an instrument); by analogy, to drive (a nail or tent-pin, a dart, etc.); by implication, to become bondsman by handclasping)\nKJV: blow (a trumpet), cast, clap, fasten, pitch (tent), smite, sound, strike, [idiom] suretiship, thrust.\n\nCognate Group: H8628 (blow), H8621 (Tekoite), H8619 (trumpet), H8620 (Tekoa), H8629 (sound)\nGreek Equivalents: G906 βάλλω, G1685 ἐμβάλλω, G2279 ἦχος, G2476 ἵστημι, G3860 παραδίδωμι, G4078 πήγνυμι, G4537 σαλπίζω, G4591 σημαίνω, G4741 στηρίζω, G4887 συνδέω, G5087 τίθημι, G5455 φωνέω",
