    8649: "תׇּרְמָה (tormâh | tor-maw')\n\nDerivation: and תַּרְמוּת; or תַּרְמִית; from H7411 רָמָה\nStrong's: fraud\nKJV: deceit(-ful), privily.\n\nCognate Group: H7423 (deceit), H7411 (beguile), H8649 (deceit), H4820 (craft)\nGreek Equivalents: G1386 δόλιος, G2307 θέλημα, G2931 κρυφῆ",
    8650: "תֹּרֶן (tôren | to'-ren)\n\nDerivation: probably for H766 אֹרֶן\nStrong's: a pole (as a mast or flagstaff)\nKJV: beacon, mast.\n\nCognate Group: H8630 (prevail), H8640 (Tirhakah), H8673 (ninety), H8660 (Tirshatha), H8659 (Tarshish), H8650 (beacon), H8658 (beryl), H8638 (interpret), H8634 (Taralah), H8645 (cypress), H8633 (authority), H8623 (mightier), H8657 (Teresh), H8646 (Tarah), H8655 (idols), H8661 (Tartan), H8672 (nine), H8449 (dove), H8662 (Tartak), H8654 (Tirathite), H8671 (ninth)",
