    8656: "תִּרְצָה (Tirtsâh | teer-tsaw')\n\nDerivation: from H7521 רָצָה ; delightsomeness\nStrong's: Tirtsah, a place in Palestine; also an Israelitess\nKJV: Tirzah.\n\nCognate Group: H8656 (Tirzah), H7522 (acceptable), H7521 (accept)",
    8657: "תֶּרֶשׁ (Teresh | teh'-resh)\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Teresh, a eunuch of Xerxes\nKJV: Teresh.\n\nCognate Group: H8630 (prevail), H8640 (Tirhakah), H8673 (ninety), H8660 (Tirshatha), H8659 (Tarshish), H8650 (beacon), H8658 (beryl), H8638 (interpret), H8634 (Taralah), H8645 (cypress), H8633 (authority), H8623 (mightier), H8657 (Teresh), H8646 (Tarah), H8655 (idols), H8661 (Tartan), H8672 (nine), H8449 (dove), H8662 (Tartak), H8654 (Tirathite), H8671 (ninth)",
    8658: "תַּרְשִׁישׁ (tarshîysh | tar-sheesh')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign derivation (compare H8659 תַּרְשִׁישׁ)\nStrong's: a gem, perhaps the topaz\nKJV: beryl.\n\nCognate Group: H8630 (prevail), H8640 (Tirhakah), H8673 (ninety), H8660 (Tirshatha), H8659 (Tarshish), H8650 (beacon), H8658 (beryl), H8638 (interpret), H8634 (Taralah), H8645 (cypress), H8633 (authority), H8623 (mightier), H8657 (Teresh), H8646 (Tarah), H8655 (idols), H8661 (Tartan), H8672 (nine), H8449 (dove), H8662 (Tartak), H8654 (Tirathite), H8671 (ninth)\nGreek Equivalents: G440 ἄνθραξ, G2281 θάλασσα, G5555 χρυσόλιθος",
    8659: "תַּרְשִׁישׁ (Tarshîysh | tar-sheesh')\n\nDerivation: probably the same as H8658 תַּרְשִׁישׁ (as the region of the stone, or the reverse)\nStrong's: Tarshish, a place on the Mediterranean, hence, the ephithet of a merchant vessel (as if for or from that port); also the name of a Persian and of an Israelite\nKJV: Tarshish, Tharshish.\n\nCognate Group: H8630 (prevail), H8640 (Tirhakah), H8673 (ninety), H8660 (Tirshatha), H8659 (Tarshish), H8650 (beacon), H8658 (beryl), H8638 (interpret), H8634 (Taralah), H8645 (cypress), H8633 (authority), H8623 (mightier), H8657 (Teresh), H8646 (Tarah), H8655 (idols), H8661 (Tartan), H8672 (nine), H8449 (dove), H8662 (Tartak), H8654 (Tirathite), H8671 (ninth)",
    8660: "תִּרְשָׁתָא (Tirshâthâʼ | teer-shaw-thaw')\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Tirshatha, the title of a Persian deputy or governor\nKJV: Tirshatha.\n\nCognate Group: H8630 (prevail), H8640 (Tirhakah), H8673 (ninety), H8660 (Tirshatha), H8659 (Tarshish), H8650 (beacon), H8658 (beryl), H8638 (interpret), H8634 (Taralah), H8645 (cypress), H8633 (authority), H8623 (mightier), H8657 (Teresh), H8646 (Tarah), H8655 (idols), H8661 (Tartan), H8672 (nine), H8449 (dove), H8662 (Tartak), H8654 (Tirathite), H8671 (ninth)",
    8661: "תַּרְתָּן (Tartân | tar-tawn')\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Tartan, an Assyrian\nKJV: Tartan.\n\nCognate Group: H8630 (prevail), H8640 (Tirhakah), H8673 (ninety), H8660 (Tirshatha), H8659 (Tarshish), H8650 (beacon), H8658 (beryl), H8638 (interpret), H8634 (Taralah), H8645 (cypress), H8633 (authority), H8623 (mightier), H8657 (Teresh), H8646 (Tarah), H8655 (idols), H8661 (Tartan), H8672 (nine), H8449 (dove), H8662 (Tartak), H8654 (Tirathite), H8671 (ninth)",
    8662: "תַּרְתָּק (Tartâq | tar-tawk')\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Tartak, a deity of the Avvites\nKJV: Tartak.\n\nCognate Group: H8630 (prevail), H8640 (Tirhakah), H8673 (ninety), H8660 (Tirshatha), H8659 (Tarshish), H8650 (beacon), H8658 (beryl), H8638 (interpret), H8634 (Taralah), H8645 (cypress), H8633 (authority), H8623 (mightier), H8657 (Teresh), H8646 (Tarah), H8655 (idols), H8661 (Tartan), H8672 (nine), H8449 (dove), H8662 (Tartak), H8654 (Tirathite), H8671 (ninth)",
    8663: "תְּשֻׁאָה (tᵉshuʼâh | tesh-oo-aw')\n\nDerivation: from H7722 שֹׁוא\nStrong's: a crashing or loud clamor\nKJV: crying, noise, shouting, stir.\n\nCognate Group: H4875 (desolation), H8663 (crying), H7722 (desolate), H7738 ([idiom] substance)",
    8664: "תִּשְׁבִּי (Tishbîy | tish-bee')\n\nDerivation: patrial from an unused name meaning recourse\nStrong's: a Tishbite or inhabitant of Tishbeh (in Gilead)\nKJV: Tishbite.\n\nCognate Group: H7633 (captives), H7628 (captive), H7617 (captive), H7618 (agate), H7622 (captive), H7619 (Shebuel), H8664 (Tishbite), H7629 (Shobi), H7630 (Shobai), H8453 (foreigner)",
    8665: "תַּשְׁבֵּץ (tashbêts | tash-bates')\n\nDerivation: from H7660 שָׁבַץ\nStrong's: checkered stuff (as reticulated)\nKJV: broidered.\n\nCognate Group: H7660 (embroider), H8665 (broidered), H7661 (anguish), H4865 (ouch)",
    8666: "תְּשׁוּבָה (tᵉshûwbâh | tesh-oo-baw')\n\nDerivation: or תְּשֻׁבָה; from H7725 שׁוּב\nStrong's: a recurrence (of time or place); a reply (as returned)\nKJV: answer, be expired, return.\n\nCognate Group: H3434 (Jashobeam), H8666 (answer), H7725 (to turn back), H3437 (Jashub), H7727 (Shobab), H3142 (Jushab-hesed), H7780 (Shophach), H7728 (backsliding), H7870 (captivity), H3433 (Jashubi-lehem), H4878 (backsliding), H7729 (returning), H7726 (backsliding), H7731 (Shobach), H4877 (Meshobab), H3432 (Jashubites)",
    8667: "תְּשׂוּמֶת (tᵉsûwmeth | tes-oo-meth')\n\nDerivation: from H7760 שׂוּם\nStrong's: a deposit, i.e. pledging\nKJV: [phrase] fellowship.\n\nCognate Group: H7760 ([idiom] any wise), H8667 (fellowship), H3450 (Jesimael)\nGreek Equivalents: G2842 κοινωνία",
    8668: "תְּשׁוּעָה (tᵉshûwʻâh | tesh-oo-aw')\n\nDerivation: or תְּשֻׁעָה; from H7768 שָׁוַע in the sense of H3467 יָשַׁע\nStrong's: rescue (literal or figurative, persons, national or spiritual)\nKJV: deliverance, help, safety, salvation, victory.\n\nCognate Group: H8668 (deliverance), H3471 (jasper), H3470 (Isaiah), H1954 (Hosea), H7774 (Shua), H3444 (deliverance), H7769 (cry), H7770 (Shua), H4190 (salvation), H3469 (Ishi), H7771 (bountiful), H4338 (Mesha), H3468 (safety), H4337 (Mesha), H3467 ([idiom] at all), H1955 (Hoshaiah)\nGreek Equivalents: G996 βοήθεια, G4991 σωτηρία",
    8669: "תְּשׁוּקָה (tᵉshûwqâh | tesh-oo-kaw')\n\nDerivation: from H7783 שׁוּק in the original sense of stretching out after\nStrong's: a longing\nKJV: desire.\n\nCognate Group: H8669 (desire)\nGreek Equivalents: G1995 ἐπιστροφή",
    8670: "תְּשׁוּרָה (tᵉshûwrâh | tesh-oo-raw')\n\nDerivation: from H7788 שׁוּר in the sense of arrival\nStrong's: a gift\nKJV: present.\n\nCognate Group: H8670 (present), H7788 (go)",
    8671: "תְּשִׁיעִי (tᵉshîyʻîy | tesh-ee-ee')\n\nDerivation: ordinal from H8672 תֵּשַׁע\nStrong's: ninth\nKJV: ninth.\n\nCognate Group: H8630 (prevail), H8640 (Tirhakah), H8673 (ninety), H8660 (Tirshatha), H8659 (Tarshish), H8650 (beacon), H8658 (beryl), H8638 (interpret), H8634 (Taralah), H8645 (cypress), H8633 (authority), H8623 (mightier), H8657 (Teresh), H8646 (Tarah), H8655 (idols), H8661 (Tartan), H8672 (nine), H8449 (dove), H8662 (Tartak), H8654 (Tirathite), H8671 (ninth)",
    8672: "תֵּשַׁע (têshaʻ | tay'-shah)\n\nDerivation: or (masculine) תִּשְׁעָה; perhaps from H8159 שָׁעָה through the idea of a turn to the next or full number ten\nStrong's: nine or (ordinal) ninth\nKJV: nine ([phrase] -teen, [phrase] -teenth, -th).\n\nCognate Group: H8630 (prevail), H8640 (Tirhakah), H8673 (ninety), H8660 (Tirshatha), H8659 (Tarshish), H8650 (beacon), H8658 (beryl), H8638 (interpret), H8634 (Taralah), H8645 (cypress), H8633 (authority), H8623 (mightier), H8657 (Teresh), H8646 (Tarah), H8655 (idols), H8661 (Tartan), H8672 (nine), H8449 (dove), H8662 (Tartak), H8654 (Tirathite), H8671 (ninth)",
    8673: "תִּשְׁעִים (tishʻîym | tish-eem')\n\nDerivation: multiple from H8672 תֵּשַׁע\nStrong's: ninety\nKJV: ninety.\n\nCognate Group: H8630 (prevail), H8640 (Tirhakah), H8673 (ninety), H8660 (Tirshatha), H8659 (Tarshish), H8650 (beacon), H8658 (beryl), H8638 (interpret), H8634 (Taralah), H8645 (cypress), H8633 (authority), H8623 (mightier), H8657 (Teresh), H8646 (Tarah), H8655 (idols), H8661 (Tartan), H8672 (nine), H8449 (dove), H8662 (Tartak), H8654 (Tirathite), H8671 (ninth)",
    8674: "תַּתְּנַי (Tattᵉnay | tat-ten-ah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Tattenai, a Persian\nKJV: Tatnai.\n\nCognate Group: H8652 (porter), H8674 (Tatnai), H8651 (gate mouth), H8627 (establish)",
    8675: "Kethiv Readings\nIn the Hebrew Bible, the scribes did not alter any text they felt had been copied incorrectly. Rather they noted in the margin what they thought the written text should be. The written variation is called a kethiv and the marginal note is called the qere. Where the translators of the Authorised Version followed the qere reading rather than the kethiv, we indicate the kethiv reading by the number 08675. For example, in Ge 24:33 \"was set\" is coded as H7760 08675 H3455. The translators used the qere reading that has Strong's number H7760 but the kethiv reading is Strong's number H3455. Both words have the same meaning, \"was set\".",
    8676: "Qere Readings\nIn the Hebrew Bible, the scribes did not alter any text they felt had been copied incorrectly. Rather they noted in the margin what they thought the written text should be. The written variation is called a kethiv and the marginal note is called the qere. Where the translators of the Authorised Version followed the kethiv reading rather than the qere, we indicate the qere reading by the number 08676. For example, in De 19:6 \"blood\" is coded as H1818 08676 H5315. The translators followed the kethiv reading that has Strong's number H1818, which means \"blood\", but the qere reading is Strong's number H5315, which means \"life\".",
    8677: "Synonym Strong's Numbers\nSometimes, a word or phrase has individual Strong's numbers assigned to it and it has an additional Strong's number for the entire phrase. In Jud 20:18 the phrase \"house of God\" is coded as \"house H1004 H1004 of God H430 H430 H1008 H1008\" In this case the phrase could also mean place Bethel which has the Strong's number H1008. Only by context can you distinguish proper names in Hebrew from individual words. Hence translators do arrive at different renderings for the same Hebrew.",
    8678: "Multiple Qere Readings for a Kethiv\nThere are several marginal or qere readings for a kethiv reading. In Neh 5:7 the word \"exact\" is coded as \"exact H5378 H5378 H8778 H8778 H5383 H5383 H8675 H8675 H5375 H5375\". The two marginal readings, Strong's numbers H5378 and H5383 exist for the one kethiv reading H5375.",
    8679: "(OMITTED TEXT)",
