    379: "ἀναπολόγητος (anapológētos | an-ap-ol-og'-ay-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G626\nStrong's: indefensible\nKJV: —without an excuse, inexcusable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G626 \n\nCognate Group: G4137 (accomplish), G4136 (assurance), G1604 (accomplishment), G4845 (come), G466 (fill up), G378 (fill up), G4134 (full), G4135 (most surely believe), G1603 (fulfill), G4138 (which is put in to fill up)\nVariants: ἀναπολόγητος",
    380: "ἀναπτύσσω (anaptýssō | an-ap-toos'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G303 (in the sense of reversal) and G4428\nStrong's: to unroll (a scroll or volume)\nKJV: —open.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G4428 \n\nCognate Group: G4137 (accomplish), G4136 (assurance), G1604 (accomplishment), G4845 (come), G466 (fill up), G378 (fill up), G4134 (full), G4135 (most surely believe), G1603 (fulfill), G4138 (which is put in to fill up)\nVariants: ἀναπτύσσω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3680 כָּסָה, H4201 מְזוּזָה, H6566 פָּרַשׂ",
    381: "ἀνάπτω (anáptō | an-ap'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G681\nStrong's: to enkindle\nKJV: —kindle, light.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G681 \n\nCognate Group: G4137 (accomplish), G4136 (assurance), G1604 (accomplishment), G4845 (come), G466 (fill up), G378 (fill up), G4134 (full), G4135 (most surely believe), G1603 (fulfill), G4138 (which is put in to fill up)\nVariants: ἀνάπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H215 אֹור, H1197 בָּעַר, H3318 יָצָא, H3341 יָצַת, H3857 לָהַט, H5327 נָצָה, H5400 נָשַׂק, H5927 עָלָה",
    382: "ἀναρίθμητος (anaríthmētos | an-ar-ith'-may-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G705\nStrong's: unnumbered, i.e. without number\nKJV: —innumerable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G705 \n\nCognate Group: G4137 (accomplish), G4136 (assurance), G1604 (accomplishment), G4845 (come), G466 (fill up), G378 (fill up), G4134 (full), G4135 (most surely believe), G1603 (fulfill), G4138 (which is put in to fill up)\nVariants: ἀναρίθμητος",
    383: "ἀνασείω (anaseíō | an-as-i'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G4579\nStrong's: figuratively, to excite\nKJV: —move, stir up.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G4579 \n\nCognate Group: G4137 (accomplish), G4136 (assurance), G1604 (accomplishment), G4845 (come), G466 (fill up), G378 (fill up), G4134 (full), G4135 (most surely believe), G1603 (fulfill), G4138 (which is put in to fill up)\nVariants: ἀνασείω",
    384: "ἀνασκευάζω (anaskeuázō | an-ask-yoo-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G303 (in the sense of reversal) and a derivative of G4632\nStrong's: properly, to pack up (baggage), i.e. (by implication, and figuratively) to upset\nKJV: —subvert.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G4632 \n\nCognate Group: G4137 (accomplish), G4136 (assurance), G1604 (accomplishment), G4845 (come), G466 (fill up), G378 (fill up), G4134 (full), G4135 (most surely believe), G1603 (fulfill), G4138 (which is put in to fill up)\nVariants: ἀνασκευάζω",
    385: "ἀνασπάω (anaspáō | an-as-pah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G4685\nStrong's: to take up or extricate\nKJV: —draw up, pull out.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G4685 \n\nCognate Group: G4137 (accomplish), G4136 (assurance), G1604 (accomplishment), G4845 (come), G466 (fill up), G378 (fill up), G4134 (full), G4135 (most surely believe), G1603 (fulfill), G4138 (which is put in to fill up)\nVariants: ἀνασπάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3947 לָקַח, H5927 עָלָה",
    386: "ἀνάστασις (anástasis | an-as'-tas-is)\n\nDerivation: from G450\nStrong's: a standing up again, i.e. (literally) a resurrection from death (individual, genitive case or by implication, (its author)), or (figuratively) a (moral) recovery (of spiritual truth)\nKJV: —raised to life again, resurrection, rise from the dead, that should rise, rising again.\n\nSee: G450 \n\nCognate Group: G1815 (resurrection), G450 (arise), G386 (raised to life again), G1817 (raise up)\nVariants: ἀνάστασις \nHebrew Equivalents: H6965 קוּם, H7012 קִימָה",
    387: "ἀναστατόω (anastatóō | an-as-tat-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G450 (in the sense of removal)\nStrong's: properly, to drive out of home, i.e. (by implication) to disturb (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —trouble, turn upside down, make an uproar.\n\nSee: G450 \n\nCognate Group: G1815 (resurrection), G450 (arise), G386 (raised to life again), G1817 (raise up)\nVariants: ἀναστατόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1758 דּוּשׁ",
    388: "ἀνασταυρόω (anastauróō | an-as-tow-ro'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G4717\nStrong's: to recrucify (figuratively)\nKJV: —crucify afresh.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G4717 \n\nCognate Group: G4617 (sift), G388 (crucify afresh), G4716 (cross)\nVariants: ἀνασταυρόω",
    389: "ἀναστενάζω (anastenázō | an-as-ten-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G4727\nStrong's: to sigh deeply\nKJV: —sigh deeply.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G4727 \n\nCognate Group: G4617 (sift), G388 (crucify afresh), G4716 (cross)\nVariants: ἀναστενάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H584 אָנַח",
    390: "ἀναστρέφω (anastréphō | an-as-tref'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G4762\nStrong's: to overturn; also to return; by implication, to busy oneself, i.e. remain, live\nKJV: —abide, behave self, have conversation, live, overthrow, pass, return, be used.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G4762 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἀναστρέφω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1443 גָּדַר, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2015 הָפַךְ, H3318 יָצָא, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6437 פָּנָה, H7725 שׁוּב, H7789 שׁוּר, H8074 שָׁמֵם, H8138 שָׁנָה",
    391: "ἀναστροφή (anastrophḗ | an-as-trof-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G390\nStrong's: behavior\nKJV: —conversation.\n\nSee: G390 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἀναστροφή",
    392: "ἀνατάσσομαι (anatássomai | an-at-as'-som-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and the middle voice of G5021\nStrong's: to arrange\nKJV: —set in order.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G5021 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀνατάσσομαι, ἀνατάσσω",
    393: "ἀνατέλλω (anatéllō | an-at-el'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and the base of G5056\nStrong's: to (cause to) arise\nKJV: —(a-, make to) rise, at the rising of, spring (up), be up.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G5056 \n\nCognate Group: G393 (rise), G395 (dayspring)\nVariants: ἀνατέλλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1121 בֵּן, H1869 דָּרַךְ, H2224 זָרַח, H2232 זָרַע, H3318 יָצָא, H6079 עַפְעַף, H6315 פּוּחַ, H6524 פָּרַח, H6605 פָּתַח, H6779 צָמַח, H6965 קוּם, H7823 שָׁחִיס",
    394: "ἀνατίθεμαι (anatíthemai | an-at-ith'-em-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and the middle voice of G5087\nStrong's: to set forth (for oneself), i.e propound\nKJV: —communicate, declare.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G5087 \n\nCognate Group: G334 (gift), G2652 (curse), G4323 (in conference add), G2653 (curse), G332 (curse), G394 (communicate), G331 (accused)\nVariants: ἀνατίθεμαι, ἀνατίθημι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2763 חָרַם, H3322 יָצַג, H7760 שׂוּם",
    395: "ἀνατολή (anatolḗ | an-at-ol-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G393\nStrong's: a rising of light, i.e. dawn (figuratively); by implication, the east (also in plural)\nKJV: —dayspring, east, rising.\n\nSee: G393 \n\nCognate Group: G393 (rise), G395 (dayspring)\nVariants: ἀνατολή \nHebrew Equivalents: H3318 יָצָא, H4217 מִזְרָח, H5051 נֹגַהּ, H6780 צֶמַח, H6921 קָדִים, H6924 קֶדֶם",
    396: "ἀνατρέπω (anatrépō | an-at-rep'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and the base of G5157\nStrong's: to overturn (figuratively)\nKJV: —overthrow, subvert.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G5157 \n\nCognate Group: G393 (rise), G395 (dayspring)\nVariants: ἀνατρέπω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1711 דָּגָה, H1760 דָּחָה, H1920 הָדַף, H7368 רָחַק, H7576 רָתַק",
    397: "ἀνατρέφω (anatréphō | an-at-ref'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G5142\nStrong's: to rear (physically or mentally)\nKJV: —bring up, nourish (up).\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G5142 \n\nCognate Group: G393 (rise), G395 (dayspring)\nVariants: ἀνατρέφω",
    398: "ἀναφαίνω (anaphaínō | an-af-ah'-ee-no)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G5316\nStrong's: to show, i.e. (reflexively) appear, or (passively) to have pointed out\nKJV: —(should) appear, discover.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G5316 \n\nCognate Group: G393 (rise), G395 (dayspring)\nVariants: ἀναφαίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1570 גָּלַשׁ, H6663 צָדַק",
    399: "ἀναφέρω (anaphérō | an-af-er'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G5342\nStrong's: to take up (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —bear, bring (carry, lead) up, offer (up).\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G5342 \n\nCognate Group: G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)\nVariants: ἀναφέρω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H2398 חָטָא, H2986 יָבַל, H3381 יָרַד, H4669 מִפְתָּח, H5130 נוּף, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5445 סָבַל, H5559 סְלִק, H5674 עָבַר, H5927 עָלָה, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6999 קָטַר, H7126 קָרַב, H7725 שׁוּב",
    400: "ἀναφωνέω (anaphōnéō | an-af-o-neh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G5455\nStrong's: to exclaim\nKJV: —speak out.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G5455 \n\nCognate Group: G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)\nVariants: ἀναφωνέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2142 זָכַר, H8085 שָׁמַע",
    401: "ἀνάχυσις (anáchysis | an-akh'-oo-sis)\n\nDerivation: from a comparative of G303 and χέω (to pour)\nStrong's: properly, effusion, i.e. (figuratively) license\nKJV: —excess.\n\nSee: G303 \n\nCognate Group: G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)\nVariants: ἀνάχυσις",
    402: "ἀναχωρέω (anachōréō | an-akh-o-reh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G5562\nStrong's: to retire\nKJV: —depart, give place, go (turn) aside, withdraw self.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G5562 \n\nCognate Group: G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)\nVariants: ἀναχωρέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1272 בָּרַח, H5060 נָגַע, H5123 נוּם, H5437 סָבַב, H5966 עָלַע, H6555 פָּרַץ",
    403: "ἀνάψυξις (anápsyxis | an-aps'-ook-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G404\nStrong's: properly, a recovery of breath, i.e. (figuratively) revival\nKJV: —revival.\n\nSee: G404 \n\nCognate Group: G1374 (double minded), G5591 (natural), G5590 (heart), G3642 (feebleminded), G404 (refresh), G403 (revival)\nVariants: ἀνάψυξις \nHebrew Equivalents: H7309 רְוָחָה",
    404: "ἀναψύχω (anapsýchō | an-aps-oo'-kho)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G5594\nStrong's: properly, to cool off, i.e. (figuratively) relieve\nKJV: —refresh.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G5594 \n\nCognate Group: G1374 (double minded), G5591 (natural), G5590 (heart), G3642 (feebleminded), G404 (refresh), G403 (revival)\nVariants: ἀναψύχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1082 בָּלַג, H2421 חָיָה, H5314 נָפַשׁ, H5314 נָפַשׁ",
    405: "ἀνδραποδιστής (andrapodistḗs | an-drap-od-is-tace')\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of a compound of G435 and G4228\nStrong's: an enslaver (as bringing men to his feet)\nKJV: —menstealer.\n\nSee: G435 \nSee: G4228 \n\nCognate Group: G1374 (double minded), G5591 (natural), G5590 (heart), G3642 (feebleminded), G404 (refresh), G403 (revival)\nVariants: ἀνδραποδιστής",
    406: "Ἀνδρέας (Andréas | an-dreh'-as)\n\nDerivation: from G435\nStrong's: manly; Andreas, an Israelite\nKJV: —Andrew.\n\nSee: G435 \n\nCognate Group: G1374 (double minded), G5591 (natural), G5590 (heart), G3642 (feebleminded), G404 (refresh), G403 (revival)\nVariants: Ἀνδρέας",
    407: "ἀνδρίζομαι (andrízomai | an-drid'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G435\nStrong's: to act manly\nKJV: —quit like men.\n\nSee: G435 \n\nCognate Group: G435 (fellow), G407 (quit like men)\nVariants: ἀνδρίζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H553 אָמַץ, H2388 חָזַק, H4581 מָעֹוז",
    408: "Ἀνδρόνικος (Andrónikos | an-dron'-ee-kos)\n\nDerivation: from G435 and G3534\nStrong's: man of victory; Andronicos, an Israelite\nKJV: —Adronicus.\n\nSee: G435 \nSee: G3534 \n\nCognate Group: G435 (fellow), G407 (quit like men)\nVariants: Ἀνδρόνικος",
    409: "ἀνδροφόνος (androphónos | an-drof-on'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G435 and G5408\nStrong's: a murderer\nKJV: —manslayer.\n\nSee: G435 \nSee: G5408 \n\nCognate Group: G435 (fellow), G407 (quit like men)\nVariants: ἀνδροφόνος",
    410: "ἀνέγκλητος (anénklētos | an-eng'-klay-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G1458\nStrong's: unaccused, i.e. (by implication) irreproachable\nKJV: —blameless.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G1458 \n\nCognate Group: G410 (blameless)\nVariants: ἀνέγκλητος",
    411: "ἀνεκδιήγητος (anekdiḗgētos | an-ek-dee-ay'-gay-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G1555\nStrong's: not expounded in full, i.e. indescribable\nKJV: —unspeakable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G1555 \n\nCognate Group: G410 (blameless)\nVariants: ἀνεκδιήγητος",
    412: "ἀνεκλάλητος (aneklálētos | an-ek-lal'-ay-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G1583\nStrong's: not spoken out, i.e. (by implication) unutterable\nKJV: —unspeakable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G1583 \n\nCognate Group: G410 (blameless)\nVariants: ἀνεκλάλητος",
    413: "ἀνέκλειπτος (anékleiptos | an-ek'-lipe-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G1587\nStrong's: not left out, i.e. (by implication) inexhaustible\nKJV: —that faileth not.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G1587 \n\nCognate Group: G410 (blameless)\nVariants: ἀνέκλειπτος",
    414: "ἀνεκτότερος (anektóteros | an-ek-tot'-er-os)\n\nDerivation: comparative of a derivative of G430\nStrong's: more endurable\nKJV: —more tolerable.\n\nSee: G430 \n\nCognate Group: G463 (forbearance), G414 (more tolerable), G430 (bear with)\nVariants: ἀνεκτότερος, ἀνεκτός",
    415: "ἀνελεήμων (aneleḗmōn | an-eleh-ay'-mone)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G1655\nStrong's: merciless\nKJV: —unmerciful.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G1655 \n\nCognate Group: G448 (without mercy), G1656 (mercy), G415 (unmerciful), G1655 (merciful), G1653 (have compassion), G1654 (alms)\nVariants: ἀνελεήμων \nHebrew Equivalents: H393 אַכְזָר, H7911 שָׁכַח",
    416: "ἀνεμίζω (anemízō | an-em-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G417\nStrong's: to toss with the wind\nKJV: —drive with the wind.\n\nSee: G417 \n\nCognate Group: G448 (without mercy), G1656 (mercy), G415 (unmerciful), G1655 (merciful), G1653 (have compassion), G1654 (alms)\nVariants: ἀνεμίζω, ἀνεμίζομαι",
    417: "ἄνεμος (ánemos | an'-em-os)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G109\nStrong's: wind; (plural) by implication, (the four) quarters (of the earth)\nKJV: —wind.\n\nSee: G109 \n\nCognate Group: G448 (without mercy), G1656 (mercy), G415 (unmerciful), G1655 (merciful), G1653 (have compassion), G1654 (alms)\nVariants: ἄνεμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H7307 רוּחַ",
    418: "ἀνένδεκτος (anéndektos | an-en'-dek-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of the same as G1735\nStrong's: unadmitted, i.e. (by implication) not supposable\nKJV: —impossible.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G1735 \n\nCognate Group: G448 (without mercy), G1656 (mercy), G415 (unmerciful), G1655 (merciful), G1653 (have compassion), G1654 (alms)\nVariants: ἀνένδεκτος",
    419: "ἀνεξερεύνητος (anexereúnētos | an-ex-er-yoo'-nay-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G1830\nStrong's: not searched out, i.e. (by implication) inscrutable\nKJV: —unsearchable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G1830 \n\nCognate Group: G419 (unsearchable)\nVariants: ἀνεξερεύνητος, ἀνεξεραύνητος",
    420: "ἀνεξίκακος (anexíkakos | an-ex-ik'-ak-os)\n\nDerivation: from G430 and G2556\nStrong's: enduring of ill, i.e. forbearing\nKJV: —patient.\n\nSee: G430 \nSee: G2556 \n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: ἀνεξίκακος",
    421: "ἀνεξιχνίαστος (anexichníastos | an-ex-ikh-nee'-as-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of a compound of G1537 and a derivative of G2487\nStrong's: not tracked out, i.e. (by implication) untraceable\nKJV: —past finding out; unsearchable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G1537 \nSee: G2487 \n\nCognate Group: G421 (past finding out; unsearchable)\nVariants: ἀνεξιχνίαστος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5869 עַיִן",
    422: "ἀνεπαίσχυντος (anepaíschyntos | an-ep-ah'-ee-skhoon-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of a compound of G1909 and G153\nStrong's: not ashamed, i.e. irreprehensible: \nKJV: —that needeth not to be ashamed.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G1909 \nSee: G153 \n\nCognate Group: G421 (past finding out; unsearchable)\nVariants: ἀνεπαίσχυντος",
    423: "ἀνεπίληπτος (anepílēptos | an-ep-eel'-ape-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G1949\nStrong's: not arrested, i.e. (by implication) inculpable\nKJV: —blameless, unrebukeable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G1949 \n\nCognate Group: G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)\nVariants: ἀνεπίληπτος, ἀνεπίλημπτος",
    424: "ἀνέρχομαι (anérchomai | an-erkh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G2064\nStrong's: to ascend\nKJV: —go up.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G2064 \n\nCognate Group: G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)\nVariants: ἀνέρχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1980 הָלַךְ",
    425: "ἄνεσις (ánesis | an'-es-is)\n\nDerivation: from G447\nStrong's: relaxation or (figuratively) relief\nKJV: —eased, liberty, rest.\n\nSee: G447 \n\nCognate Group: G447 (forbear), G425 (eased)\nVariants: ἄνεσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H7960 שָׁלוּ",
    426: "ἀνετάζω (anetázō | an-et-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and ἐτάζω (to test)\nStrong's: to investigate (judicially)\nKJV: —(should have) examined(-d).\n\nSee: G303 \n\nCognate Group: G447 (forbear), G425 (eased)\nVariants: ἀνετάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H1875 דָּרַשׁ",
    427: "ἄνευ (áneu | an'-yoo)\n\nDerivation: a primary particle\nStrong's: without\nKJV: —without. Compare G1 .\n\nSee: G1 \n\nCognate Group: G447 (forbear), G425 (eased)\nVariants: ἄνευ",
    428: "ἀνεύθετος (aneúthetos | an-yoo'-the-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G2111\nStrong's: not well set, i.e. inconvenient\nKJV: —not commodious.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G2111 \n\nCognate Group: G447 (forbear), G425 (eased)\nVariants: ἀνεύθετος",
    429: "ἀνευρίσκω (aneurískō | an-yoo-ris'-ko)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G2147\nStrong's: to find out\nKJV: —find.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G2147 \n\nCognate Group: G447 (forbear), G425 (eased)\nVariants: ἀνευρίσκω",
    430: "ἀνέχομαι (anéchomai | an-ekh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G303 and G2192\nStrong's: to hold oneself up against, i.e. (figuratively) put up with\nKJV: —bear with, endure, forbear, suffer.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G2192 \n\nCognate Group: G463 (forbearance), G414 (more tolerable), G430 (bear with)\nVariants: ἀνέχομαι, ἀνέχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H662 אָפַק, H2976 יָאַשׁ, H3201 יָכֹל, H3607 כָּלָא, H4513 מָנַע, H5445 סָבַל, H6186 עָרַךְ, H7725 שׁוּב",
    431: "ἀνεψιός (anepsiós | an-eps'-ee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a particle of union) and an obsolete νέπος (a brood)\nStrong's: properly, akin, i.e. (specially) a cousin\nKJV: —sister's son.\n\nSee: G1 \n\nCognate Group: G463 (forbearance), G414 (more tolerable), G430 (bear with)\nVariants: ἀνεψιός \nHebrew Equivalents: H1121 בֵּן",
    432: "ἄνηθον (ánēthon | an'-ay-thon)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: dill\nKJV: —anise.\n\nCognate Group: G463 (forbearance), G414 (more tolerable), G430 (bear with)\nVariants: ἄνηθον",
    433: "ἀνήκω (anḗkō | an-ay'-ko)\n\nDerivation: from G303 and G2240\nStrong's: to attain to, i.e. (figuratively) be proper\nKJV: —convenient, be fit.\n\nSee: G303 \nSee: G2240 \n\nCognate Group: G433 (convenient)\nVariants: ἀνήκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא",
    434: "ἀνήμερος (anḗmeros | an-ay'-mer-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and ἥμερος (lame)\nStrong's: savage\nKJV: —fierce.\n\nSee: G1 \n\nCognate Group: G433 (convenient)\nVariants: ἀνήμερος",
