    437: "ἀνθομολογέομαι (anthomologéomai | anth-om-ol-og-eh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G473 and the middle voice of G3670\nStrong's: to confess in turn, i.e. respond in praise\nKJV: —give thanks.\n\nSee: G473 \nSee: G3670 \n\nCognate Group: G437 (give thanks), G1843 (confess), G3672 (without controversy), G3671 (con- fession), G3670 (con- fess)\nVariants: ἀνθομολογέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H3034 יָדָה, H7624 שְׁבַח",
    438: "ἄνθος (ánthos | anth'-os)\n\nDerivation: a primary word\nStrong's: a blossom\nKJV: —flower.\n\nCognate Group: G437 (give thanks), G1843 (confess), G3672 (without controversy), G3671 (con- fession), G3670 (con- fess)\nVariants: ἄνθος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2261 חֲבַצֶּלֶת, H4020 מִגְבָּלָה, H5328 נִצָּה, H5342 נֵצֶר, H6525 פֶּרַח, H6731 צִיץ, H6780 צֶמַח, H7218 רֹאשׁ",
