    453: "ἀνόητος (anóētos | an-o'-ay-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G3539\nStrong's: unintelligent; by implication, sensual\nKJV: —fool(-ish), unwise.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G3539 \n\nCognate Group: G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)\nVariants: ἀνόητος, ἀνόνητος \nHebrew Equivalents: H191 אֱוִיל",
    454: "ἄνοια (ánoia | an'-oy-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1 (as a negative particle) and G3563\nStrong's: stupidity; by implication, rage\nKJV: —folly, madness.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G3563 \n\nCognate Group: G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)\nVariants: ἄνοια \nHebrew Equivalents: H200 אִוֶּלֶת",
