    457: "ἄνοιξις (ánoixis | an'-oix-is)\n\nDerivation: from G455\nStrong's: opening (throat)\nKJV: —X open.\n\nSee: G455 \n\nCognate Group: G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)\nVariants: ἄνοιξις",
