    459: "ἄνομος (ánomos | an'-om-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G3551\nStrong's: lawless, i.e. (negatively) not subject to (the Jewish) law; (by implication, a Gentile), or (positively) wicked\nKJV: —without law, lawless, transgressor, unlawful, wicked.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G3551 \n\nCognate Group: G459 (without law), G3892 (iniquity), G3891 (contrary to law), G3545 (lawfully), G460 (without law), G3551 (law), G3547 (doctor of the law), G3550 (lawgiver), G458 (iniquity), G1772 (lawful), G3549 (establish), G3548 (giving of the law), G3544 (about the law)\nVariants: ἄνομος \nHebrew Equivalents: H205 אָוֶן, H913 בְּדִיל, H1215 בֶּצַע, H1984 הָלַל, H2086 זֵד, H2154 זִמָּה, H2400 חַטָּא, H2611 חָנֵף, H3944 לָצֹון, H5627 סָרָה, H5766 עֶוֶל, H5771 עָוֺן, H6049 עָנַן, H6184 עָרִיץ, H6586 פָּשַׁע, H7423 רְמִיָּה, H7562 רֶשַׁע, H7563 רָשָׁע, H7723 שָׁוְא, H7843 שָׁחַת, H8267 שֶׁקֶר, H8441 תֹּועֵבַה",
    460: "ἀνόμως (anómōs | an-om'-oce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G459\nStrong's: lawlessly, i.e. (specially) not amenable to (the Jewish) law\nKJV: —without law.\n\nSee: G459 \n\nCognate Group: G459 (without law), G3892 (iniquity), G3891 (contrary to law), G3545 (lawfully), G460 (without law), G3551 (law), G3547 (doctor of the law), G3550 (lawgiver), G458 (iniquity), G1772 (lawful), G3549 (establish), G3548 (giving of the law), G3544 (about the law)\nVariants: ἀνόμως",
