    464: "ἀνταγωνίζομαι (antagōnízomai | an-tag-o-nid'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G473 and G75\nStrong's: to struggle against (figuratively) (\"antagonize\")\nKJV: —strive against.\n\nSee: G473 \nSee: G75 \n\nCognate Group: G73 (conflict), G464 (strive against), G74 (agony), G1864 (earnestly contend for), G75 (fight), G2610 (subdue)\nVariants: ἀνταγωνίζομαι",
