    473: "ἀντί (antí | an-tee')\n\nDerivation: a primary particle\nStrong's: opposite, i.e. instead or because of (rarely in addition to)\nKJV: —for, in the room of. Often used in composition to denote contrast, requital, substitution, correspondence, etc.\n\nCognate Group: G473 (for)\nVariants: ἀντί",
    474: "ἀντιβάλλω (antibállō | an-tee-bal'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G473 and G906\nStrong's: to bandy\nKJV: —have.\n\nSee: G473 \nSee: G906 \n\nCognate Group: G473 (for)\nVariants: ἀντιβάλλω",
