    476: "ἀντίδικος (antídikos | an-tid'-ee-kos)\n\nDerivation: from G473 and G1349\nStrong's: an opponent (in a lawsuit); specially, Satan (as the arch-enemy)\nKJV: —adversary.\n\nSee: G473 \nSee: G1349 \n\nCognate Group: G476 (adversary)\nVariants: ἀντίδικος \nHebrew Equivalents: H7378 רִיב",
