    494: "Ἀντιπατρίς (Antipatrís | an-tip-at-rece')\n\nDerivation: from the same as G493\nStrong's: Antipatris, a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Antipatris.\n\nSee: G493 \n\nCognate Group: G3408 (hire), G3410 (hired house), G3411 (hired servant), G3405 (recompence of reward), G3407 (hired servant), G489 (recompense), G3406 (rewarder), G3409 (hire)\nVariants: Ἀντιπατρίς",
    495: "ἀντιπέραν (antipéran | an-tee-per'-an)\n\nDerivation: from G473 and G4008\nStrong's: on the opposite side\nKJV: —over against.\n\nSee: G473 \nSee: G4008 \n\nCognate Group: G3408 (hire), G3410 (hired house), G3411 (hired servant), G3405 (recompence of reward), G3407 (hired servant), G489 (recompense), G3406 (rewarder), G3409 (hire)\nVariants: ἀντιπέραν, ἀντιπέρα",
    496: "ἀντιπίπτω (antipíptō | an-tee-pip'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G473 and G4098 (including its alternate)\nStrong's: to oppose\nKJV: —resist.\n\nSee: G473 \nSee: G4098 \n\nCognate Group: G3408 (hire), G3410 (hired house), G3411 (hired servant), G3405 (recompence of reward), G3407 (hired servant), G489 (recompense), G3406 (rewarder), G3409 (hire)\nVariants: ἀντιπίπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H4808 מְרִיבָה, H6901 קָבַל, H7725 שׁוּב, H7947 שָׁלַב",
    497: "ἀντιστρατεύομαι (antistrateúomai | an-tee-strat-yoo'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G473 and G4754\nStrong's: (figuratively) to attack, i.e. (by implication) destroy\nKJV: —war against.\n\nSee: G473 \nSee: G4754 \n\nCognate Group: G3408 (hire), G3410 (hired house), G3411 (hired servant), G3405 (recompence of reward), G3407 (hired servant), G489 (recompense), G3406 (rewarder), G3409 (hire)\nVariants: ἀντιστρατεύομαι",
    498: "ἀντιτάσσομαι (antitássomai | an-tee-tas'-som-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G473 and the middle voice of G5021\nStrong's: to range oneself against, i.e. oppose\nKJV: —oppose themselves, resist.\n\nSee: G473 \nSee: G5021 \n\nCognate Group: G3408 (hire), G3410 (hired house), G3411 (hired servant), G3405 (recompence of reward), G3407 (hired servant), G489 (recompense), G3406 (rewarder), G3409 (hire)\nVariants: ἀντιτάσσομαι, ἀντιτάσσω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3887 לוּץ, H5375 נָשָׂא, H7617 שָׁבָה, H7896 שִׁית",
    499: "ἀντίτυπον (antítypon | an-teet'-oo-pon)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a compound of G473 and G5179\nStrong's: corresponding (\"antitype\"), i.e. a representative, counterpart\nKJV: —(like) figure (whereunto).\n\nSee: G473 \nSee: G5179 \n\nCognate Group: G499 (figure), G5296 (form), G5179 (en-ample)\nVariants: ἀντίτυπον, ἀντίτυπος",
    500: "ἀντίχριστος (antíchristos | an-tee'-khris-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G473 and G5547\nStrong's: an opponent of the Messiah\nKJV: —antichrist.\n\nSee: G473 \nSee: G5547 \n\nCognate Group: G5545 (anointing), G5580 (false Christ), G5546 (Christian), G500 (antichrist), G5547 (Christ), G5548 (anoint)\nVariants: ἀντίχριστος",
    501: "ἀντλέω (antléō | ant-leh-o)\n\nDerivation: from ἄντλος (the hold of a ship)\nStrong's: to bale up (properly, bilge water), i.e. dip water (with a bucket, pitcher, etc.)\nKJV: —draw (out).\n\nCognate Group: G5545 (anointing), G5580 (false Christ), G5546 (Christian), G500 (antichrist), G5547 (Christ), G5548 (anoint)\nVariants: ἀντλέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1802 דָּלָה, H5375 נָשָׂא, H7579 שָׁאַב",
    502: "ἄντλημα (ántlēma | ant'-lay-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G501\nStrong's: a baling-vessel\nKJV: —thing to draw with.\n\nSee: G501 \n\nCognate Group: G5545 (anointing), G5580 (false Christ), G5546 (Christian), G500 (antichrist), G5547 (Christ), G5548 (anoint)\nVariants: ἄντλημα",
    503: "ἀντοφθαλμέω (antophthalméō | ant-of-thal-meh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G473 and G3788\nStrong's: to face\nKJV: —bear up into.\n\nSee: G473 \nSee: G3788 \n\nCognate Group: G5545 (anointing), G5580 (false Christ), G5546 (Christian), G500 (antichrist), G5547 (Christ), G5548 (anoint)\nVariants: ἀντοφθαλμέω",
    504: "ἄνυδρος (ánydros | an'-oo-dros)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5204\nStrong's: waterless, i.e. dry\nKJV: —dry, without water.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5204 \n\nCognate Group: G5545 (anointing), G5580 (false Christ), G5546 (Christian), G500 (antichrist), G5547 (Christ), G5548 (anoint)\nVariants: ἄνυδρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1097 בְּלִי, H3004 יַבָּשָׁה, H3452 יְשִׁימֹון, H4057 מִדְבָּר, H5889 עָיֵף, H6723 צִיָּה, H8273 שָׁרָב",
    505: "ἀνυπόκριτος (anypókritos | an-oo-pok'-ree-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G5271\nStrong's: undissembled, i.e. sincere\nKJV: —without dissimulation (hypocrisy), unfeigned.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5271 \n\nCognate Group: G5273 (hypocrite), G505 (without dissimulation), G5272 (condemnation), G4942 (dissemble with), G5271 (feign)\nVariants: ἀνυπόκριτος",
    506: "ἀνυπότακτος (anypótaktos | an-oo-pot'-ak-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G5293\nStrong's: unsubdued, i.e. insubordinate (in fact or temper)\nKJV: —disobedient, that is not put under, unruly.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5293 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀνυπότακτος",
    507: "ἄνω (ánō | an'-o)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G473\nStrong's: upward or on the top\nKJV: —above, brim, high, up.\n\nSee: G473 \n\nCognate Group: G507 (above), G511 (above), G509 (from above)\nVariants: ἄνω, ἀνεγκλησία",
    508: "ἀνώγεον (anṓgeon | an-ogue'-eh-on)\n\nDerivation: from G507 and G1093\nStrong's: above the ground, i.e. (properly) the second floor of a building; used for a dome or a balcony on the upper story\nKJV: —upper room.\n\nSee: G507 \nSee: G1093 \n\nCognate Group: G507 (above), G511 (above), G509 (from above)\nVariants: ἀνώγεον, ἀνάγαιον",
    509: "ἄνωθεν (ánōthen | an'-o-then)\n\nDerivation: from G507\nStrong's: from above; by analogy, from the first; by implication, anew\nKJV: —from above, again, from the beginning (very first), the top.\n\nSee: G507 \n\nCognate Group: G507 (above), G511 (above), G509 (from above)\nVariants: ἄνωθεν",
    510: "ἀνωτερικός (anōterikós | an-o-ter-ee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G511\nStrong's: superior, i.e. (locally) more remote\nKJV: —upper.\n\nSee: G511 \n\nCognate Group: G507 (above), G511 (above), G509 (from above)\nVariants: ἀνωτερικός, ἀνατολικός",
    511: "ἀνώτερος (anṓteros | an-o'-ter-os)\n\nDerivation: comparative degree of G507\nStrong's: upper, i.e. (neuter as adverb) to a more conspicuous place, in a former part of the book\nKJV: —above, higher.\n\nSee: G507 \n\nCognate Group: G507 (above), G511 (above), G509 (from above)\nVariants: ἀνώτερος, ἀνώτερον \nHebrew Equivalents: H4604 מַעַל, H5945 עֶלְיֹון",
    512: "ἀνωφελής (anōphelḗs | an-o-fel'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and the base of G5624\nStrong's: useless or (neuter) inutility\nKJV: —unprofitable(-ness).\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5624 \n\nCognate Group: G507 (above), G511 (above), G509 (from above)\nVariants: ἀνωφελής \nHebrew Equivalents: H1115 בִּלְתִּי, H3808 לֹא",
    513: "ἀξίνη (axínē | ax-ee'-nay)\n\nDerivation: probably from ἄγνυμι (to break\nStrong's: compare G4486); an axe\nKJV: —axe.\n\nSee: G4486 \n\nCognate Group: G507 (above), G511 (above), G509 (from above)\nVariants: ἀξίνη \nHebrew Equivalents: H1631 גַּרְזֶן, H7134 קַרְדֹּם",
    514: "ἄξιος (áxios | ax'-ee-os)\n\nDerivation: probably from G71\nStrong's: deserving, comparable or suitable (as if drawing praise)\nKJV: —due reward, meet, (un-)worthy.\n\nSee: G71 \n\nCognate Group: G514 (due reward), G2661 (count worthy), G370 (unworthy), G515 (desire)\nVariants: ἄξιος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1121 בֵּן, H4392 מָלֵא, H7737 שָׁוָה",
    515: "ἀξιόω (axióō | ax-ee-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G514\nStrong's: to deem entitled or fit\nKJV: —desire, think good, count (think) worthy.\n\nSee: G514 \n\nCognate Group: G514 (due reward), G2661 (count worthy), G370 (unworthy), G515 (desire)\nVariants: ἀξιόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1156 בְּעָא, H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H2603 חָנַן, H4994 נָא, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5428 נָתַשׁ, H7596 שְׁאֵלָה",
    516: "ἀξίως (axíōs | ax-ee'-oce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G514\nStrong's: appropriately\nKJV: —as becometh, after a godly sort, worthily(-thy).\n\nSee: G514 \n\nCognate Group: G514 (due reward), G2661 (count worthy), G370 (unworthy), G515 (desire)\nVariants: ἀξίως",
    517: "ἀόρατος (aóratos | ah-or'-at-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G3707\nStrong's: invisible\nKJV: —invisible (thing).\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G3707 \n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: ἀόρατος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4565 מִסְתָּר, H8414 תֹּהוּ",
    518: "ἀπαγγέλλω (apangéllō | ap-ang-el'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and the base of G32\nStrong's: to announce\nKJV: —bring word (again), declare, report, shew (again), tell.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G32 \n\nCognate Group: G1229 (declare), G31 (message), G1804 (shew forth), G518 (bring word), G2604 (setter forth), G4293 (foretell), G312 (declare), G2605 (declare)\nVariants: ἀπαγγέλλω, ἀγγέλλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H2324 חֲוָא, H3045 יָדַע, H3289 יָעַץ, H5046 נָגַד, H5608 סָפַר, H6622 פָּתַר, H7121 קָרָא, H7725 שׁוּב, H7971 שָׁלַח, H8085 שָׁמַע, H8199 שָׁפַט",
    519: "ἀπάγχομαι (apánchomai | ap-ang'-khom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and ἄγχω (to choke\nStrong's: akin to the base of G43); to strangle oneself off (i.e. to death)\nKJV: —hang himself.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G43 \n\nCognate Group: G1229 (declare), G31 (message), G1804 (shew forth), G518 (bring word), G2604 (setter forth), G4293 (foretell), G312 (declare), G2605 (declare)\nVariants: ἀπάγχομαι, ἀπάγχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2614 חָנַק",
    520: "ἀπάγω (apágō | ap-ag'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G71\nStrong's: to take off (in various senses)\nKJV: —bring, carry away, lead (away), put to death, take away.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G71 \n\nCognate Group: G1229 (declare), G31 (message), G1804 (shew forth), G518 (bring word), G2604 (setter forth), G4293 (foretell), G312 (declare), G2605 (declare)\nVariants: ἀπάγω \nHebrew Equivalents: H631 אָסַר, H935 בֹּוא, H1540 גָּלָה, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2957 טְרַד, H2986 יָבַל, H4900 מָשַׁךְ, H5090 נָהַג, H5674 עָבַר, H7725 שׁוּב, H7737 שָׁוָה",
    521: "ἀπαίδευτος (apaídeutos | ap-ah'-ee-dyoo-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G3811\nStrong's: uninstructed, i.e. (figuratively) stupid\nKJV: —unlearned.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G3811 \n\nCognate Group: G3811 (chasten), G3809 (chastening), G521 (unlearned), G3807 (instructor), G3810 (which corrected)\nVariants: ἀπαίδευτος \nHebrew Equivalents: H191 אֱוִיל, H3685 כְּסִיל, H3887 לוּץ, H5036 נָבָל, H5869 עַיִן",
    522: "ἀπαίρω (apaírō | ap-ah'-ee-ro)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G142\nStrong's: to lift off, i.e. remove\nKJV: —take (away).\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G142 \n\nCognate Group: G3811 (chasten), G3809 (chastening), G521 (unlearned), G3807 (instructor), G3810 (which corrected)\nVariants: ἀπαίρω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1980 הָלַךְ, H4853 מַשָּׂא, H5375 נָשָׂא, H6275 עָתַק, H6335 פּוּשׁ, H6805 צָעַד, H7311 רוּם",
    523: "ἀπαιτέω (apaitéō | ap-ah'-ee-teh-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G154\nStrong's: to demand back\nKJV: —ask again, require.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G154 \n\nCognate Group: G3868 (avoid), G155 (petition), G523 (ask again), G1809 (desire), G154 (ask)\nVariants: ἀπαιτέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5065 נָגַשׂ, H5377 נָשָׁא",
    524: "ἀπαλγέω (apalgéō | ap-alg-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and ἀλγέω (to smart)\nStrong's: to grieve out, i.e. become apathetic\nKJV: —be past feeling.\n\nSee: G575 \n\nCognate Group: G3868 (avoid), G155 (petition), G523 (ask again), G1809 (desire), G154 (ask)\nVariants: ἀπαλγέω",
    525: "ἀπαλλάσσω (apallássō | ap-al-las'-so)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G236\nStrong's: to change away, i.e. release, (reflexively) remove\nKJV: —deliver, depart.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G236 \n\nCognate Group: G604 (reconcile), G1259 (reconcile), G2644 (reconcile), G3337 (change), G2643 (atonement), G525 (deliver), G465 (in exchange), G236 (change)\nVariants: ἀπαλλάσσω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1980 הָלַךְ, H2986 יָבַל, H5493 סוּר, H5641 סָתַר, H5916 עָכַר",
    526: "ἀπαλλοτριόω (apallotrióō | ap-al-lot-ree-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and a derivative of G245\nStrong's: to estrange away, i.e. (passively and figuratively) to be non-participant\nKJV: — alienate, be alien.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G245 \n\nCognate Group: G245 (alien), G246 (one of another nation), G526 (alienate), G243 (more), G241 (stranger)\nVariants: ἀπαλλοτριόω, ἀπαλλοτριόομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2114 זוּר, H5110 נוּד, H5144 נָזַר, H5234 נָכַר, H7673 שָׁבַת",
    527: "ἀπαλός (apalós | ap-al-os')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: soft\nKJV: —tender.\n\nCognate Group: G245 (alien), G246 (one of another nation), G526 (alienate), G243 (more), G241 (stranger)\nVariants: ἀπαλός, ἁπαλός \nHebrew Equivalents: H7390 רַךְ",
    528: "ἀπαντάω (apantáō | ap-an-tah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and a derivative of G473\nStrong's: to meet away, i.e. encounter\nKJV: —meet.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G473 \n\nCognate Group: G245 (alien), G246 (one of another nation), G526 (alienate), G243 (more), G241 (stranger)\nVariants: ἀπαντάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6293 פָּגַע, H6298 פָּגַשׁ, H7121 קָרָא, H7136 קָרָה, H7760 שׂוּם",
    529: "ἀπάντησις (apántēsis | ap-an'-tay-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G528\nStrong's: a (friendly) encounter\nKJV: —meet.\n\nSee: G528 \n\nCognate Group: G529 (meet)\nVariants: ἀπάντησις \nHebrew Equivalents: H410 אֵל, H6040 עֳנִי, H7121 קָרָא",
    530: "ἅπαξ (hápax | hap'-ax)\n\nDerivation: probably from G537\nStrong's: one (or a single) time (numerically or conclusively)\nKJV: —once.\n\nSee: G537 \n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: ἅπαξ \nHebrew Equivalents: H259 אֶחָד, H6471 פַּעַם",
    531: "ἀπαράβατος (aparábatos | ap-ar-ab'-at-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G3845\nStrong's: not passing away, i.e. untransferable (perpetual)\nKJV: — unchangeable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G3845 \n\nCognate Group: G3845 (transgress), G5233 (go beyond), G531 (unchangeable), G3847 (breaking), G3848 (breaker)\nVariants: ἀπαράβατος",
    532: "ἀπαρασκεύαστος (aparaskeúastos | ap-ar-ask-yoo'-as-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G3903\nStrong's: unready\nKJV: —unprepared.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G3903 \n\nCognate Group: G3845 (transgress), G5233 (go beyond), G531 (unchangeable), G3847 (breaking), G3848 (breaker)\nVariants: ἀπαρασκεύαστος",
    533: "ἀπαρνέομαι (aparnéomai | ap-ar-neh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G720\nStrong's: to deny utterly, i.e. disown, abstain\nKJV: —deny.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G720 \n\nCognate Group: G3845 (transgress), G5233 (go beyond), G531 (unchangeable), G3847 (breaking), G3848 (breaker)\nVariants: ἀπαρνέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H3988 מָאַס",
    534: "ἀπάρτι (apárti | ap-ar'-tee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G737\nStrong's: from now, i.e. henceforth (already)\nKJV: —from henceforth.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G737 \n\nCognate Group: G3845 (transgress), G5233 (go beyond), G531 (unchangeable), G3847 (breaking), G3848 (breaker)\nVariants: ἀπάρτι G567",
    535: "ἀπαρτισμός (apartismós | ap-ar-tis-mos')\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G534\nStrong's: completion\nKJV: —finishing.\n\nSee: G534 \n\nCognate Group: G3845 (transgress), G5233 (go beyond), G531 (unchangeable), G3847 (breaking), G3848 (breaker)\nVariants: ἀπαρτισμός",
    536: "ἀπαρχή (aparchḗ | ap-ar-khay')\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G575 and G756\nStrong's: a beginning of sacrifice, i.e. the (Jewish) first-fruit (figuratively)\nKJV: —first-fruits.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G756 \n\nCognate Group: G758 (chief), G747 (author), G744 (old), G757 (reign over), G536 (first-fruits), G746 (beginning)\nVariants: ἀπαρχή \nHebrew Equivalents: H2459 חֶלֶב, H4643 מַעֲשֵׂר, H7225 רֵאשִׁית, H8573 תְּנוּפָה, H8641 תְּרוּמָה",
    537: "ἅπας (hápas | hap'-as)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a particle of union) and G3956\nStrong's: absolutely all or (singular) every one\nKJV: —all (things), every (one), whole.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G3956 \n\nCognate Group: G537 (all), G3056 (account)\nVariants: ἅπας",
    538: "ἀπατάω (apatáō | ap-at-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: to cheat, i.e. delude\nKJV: —deceive.\n\nCognate Group: G539 (deceit), G1818 (beguile), G538 (deceive)\nVariants: ἀπατάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2926 טָלַל, H5377 נָשָׁא, H5496 סוּת, H6601 פָּתָה",
    539: "ἀπάτη (apátē | ap-at'-ay)\n\nDerivation: from G538\nStrong's: delusion\nKJV: —deceit(-ful, -fulness), deceivableness(-ving).\n\nSee: G538 \n\nCognate Group: G539 (deceit), G1818 (beguile), G538 (deceive)\nVariants: ἀπάτη",
    540: "ἀπάτωρ (apátōr | ap-at'-ore)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G3962\nStrong's: fatherless, i.e. of unrecorded paternity\nKJV: —without father.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G3962 \n\nCognate Group: G3968 (country), G3965 (family), G540 (without father), G3971 (of fathers), G3966 (patriarch), G3967 (of fathers), G3962 (father)\nVariants: ἀπάτωρ",
    541: "ἀπαύγασμα (apaúgasma | ap-ow'-gas-mah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G575 and G826\nStrong's: an off-flash, i.e. effulgence\nKJV: —brightness.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G826 \n\nCognate Group: G541 (brightness), G826 (shine)\nVariants: ἀπαύγασμα",
    542: "ἀπείδω (apeídō | ap-i'-do)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and the same as G1492\nStrong's: to see fully\nKJV: —see.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1492 \n\nCognate Group: G541 (brightness), G826 (shine)\nVariants: ἀπείδω, ἀφοράω G927",
    543: "ἀπείθεια (apeítheia | ap-i'-thi-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G545\nStrong's: disbelief (obstinate and rebellious)\nKJV: —disobedience, unbelief.\n\nSee: G545 \n\nCognate Group: G545 (disobedient), G3981 (enticing), G4006 (confidence), G3980 (hearken), G544 (not believe), G543 (disobedience), G3982 (agree), G3988 (persuasion)\nVariants: ἀπείθεια",
    544: "ἀπειθέω (apeithéō | ap-i-theh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G545\nStrong's: to disbelieve (wilfully and perversely)\nKJV: —not believe, disobedient, obey not, unbelieving.\n\nSee: G545 \n\nCognate Group: G545 (disobedient), G3981 (enticing), G4006 (confidence), G3980 (hearken), G544 (not believe), G543 (disobedience), G3982 (agree), G3988 (persuasion)\nVariants: ἀπειθέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2308 חָדַל, H3808 לֹא, H3808 לֹא, H3985 מָאֵן, H3988 מָאַס, H4603 מָעַל, H4775 מָרַד, H4784 מָרָה, H4843 מָרַר, H5637 סָרַר, H8280 שָׂרָה",
    545: "ἀπειθής (apeithḗs | ap-i-thace')\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G3982\nStrong's: unpersuadable, i.e. contumacious\nKJV: —disobedient.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G3982 \n\nCognate Group: G545 (disobedient), G3981 (enticing), G4006 (confidence), G3980 (hearken), G544 (not believe), G543 (disobedience), G3982 (agree), G3988 (persuasion)\nVariants: ἀπειθής \nHebrew Equivalents: H4759 מַרְאָה, H4806 מְרִיא, H5637 סָרַר",
    546: "ἀπειλέω (apeiléō | ap-i-leh'-o)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: to menace; by implication, to forbid\nKJV: —threaten.\n\nCognate Group: G4445 (be sick of a fever), G546 (threaten), G4446 (fever)\nVariants: ἀπειλέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1605 גָּעַר, H2194 זָעַם",
    547: "ἀπειλή (apeilḗ | ap-i-lay')\n\nDerivation: from G546\nStrong's: a menace\nKJV: —X straitly, threatening.\n\nSee: G546 \n\nCognate Group: G547 (X straitly), G4291 (maintain)\nVariants: ἀπειλή \nHebrew Equivalents: H367 אֵימָה, H1605 גָּעַר, H1606 גְּעָרָה, H2195 זַעַם, H2197 זַעַף",
    548: "ἄπειμι (ápeimi | ap'-i-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G1510\nStrong's: to be away\nKJV: —be absent. Compare G549 .\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1510 \nSee: G549 \n\nCognate Group: G547 (X straitly), G4291 (maintain)\nVariants: ἄπειμι, ἄπειμι1 \nHebrew Equivalents: H3582 כָּחַד, H5080 נָדַח",
    549: "ἄπειμι (ápeimi | ap'-i-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and εἶμι (to go)\nStrong's: to go away\nKJV: —go. Compare G548 .\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G548 \n\nCognate Group: G547 (X straitly), G4291 (maintain)\nVariants: ἄπειμι, ἄπειμι2",
    550: "ἀπειπόμην (apeipómēn | ap-i-pom'-ane)\n\nDerivation: reflexive past of a compound of G575 and G2036\nStrong's: to say off for oneself, i.e. disown\nKJV: —renounce.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G2036 \n\nCognate Group: G547 (X straitly), G4291 (maintain)\nVariants: ἀπειπόμην, ἀπεῖπον \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H2308 חָדַל, H3988 מָאַס",
    551: "ἀπείραστος (apeírastos | ap-i'-ras-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G3987\nStrong's: untried, i.e. not temptable\nKJV: —not to be tempted.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G3987 \n\nCognate Group: G3985 (assay), G3986 (temptation), G551 (not to be tempted), G1598 (tempt), G3984 (assaying), G3987 (assay)\nVariants: ἀπείραστος",
    552: "ἄπειρος (ápeiros | ap'-i-ros)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G3984\nStrong's: inexperienced, i.e. ignorant\nKJV: —unskilful.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G3984 \n\nCognate Group: G3985 (assay), G3986 (temptation), G551 (not to be tempted), G1598 (tempt), G3984 (assaying), G3987 (assay)\nVariants: ἄπειρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H196 אֱוִלִי, H6160 עֲרָבָה",
    553: "ἀπεκδέχομαι (apekdéchomai | ap-ek-dekh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G1551\nStrong's: to expect fully\nKJV: —look (wait) for.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1551 \n\nCognate Group: G1403 (feast), G1209 (accept), G1184 (accepted), G553 (look for), G1523 (receive), G587 (acceptable), G588 (accept), G2144 (acceptable), G4327 (accept), G594 (acceptation), G1561 (looking for)\nVariants: ἀπεκδέχομαι",
    554: "ἀπεκδύομαι (apekdýomai | ap-ek-doo'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G575 and G1562\nStrong's: to divest wholly oneself, or (for oneself) despoil\nKJV: —put off, spoil.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1562 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: ἀπεκδύομαι",
    555: "ἀπέκδυσις (apékdysis | ap-ek'-doo-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G554\nStrong's: divestment\nKJV: —putting off.\n\nSee: G554 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: ἀπέκδυσις",
    556: "ἀπελαύνω (apelaúnō | ap-el-ow'-no)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G1643\nStrong's: to dismiss\nKJV: —drive.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1643 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: ἀπελαύνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5337 נָצַל, H7971 שָׁלַח",
    557: "ἀπελεγμός (apelegmós | ap-el-eg-mos')\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G575 and G1651\nStrong's: refutation, i.e. (by implication) contempt\nKJV: —nought.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1651 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: ἀπελεγμός",
    558: "ἀπελεύθερος (apeleútheros | ap-el-yoo'-ther-os)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G1658\nStrong's: one freed away, i.e. a freedman\nKJV: —freeman.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1658 \n\nCognate Group: G1659 (deliver), G558 (freeman), G1657 (liberty), G1658 (free)\nVariants: ἀπελεύθερος",
    559: "Ἀπελλῆς (Apellēs | ap-el-lace')\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: Apelles, a Christian\nKJV: —Apelles.\n\nCognate Group: G1659 (deliver), G558 (freeman), G1657 (liberty), G1658 (free)\nVariants: Ἀπελλῆς",
    560: "ἀπελπίζω (apelpízō | ap-el-pid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G1679\nStrong's: to hope out, i.e. fully expect\nKJV: —hope for again.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1679 \n\nCognate Group: G1680 (faith), G1679 (hope), G4276 (first trust), G560 (hope for again)\nVariants: ἀπελπίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H34 אֶבְיֹון",
    561: "ἀπέναντι (apénanti | ap-en'-an-tee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G1725\nStrong's: from in front, i.e. opposite, before or against\nKJV: —before, contrary, over against, in the presence of.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1725 \n\nCognate Group: G1680 (faith), G1679 (hope), G4276 (first trust), G560 (hope for again)\nVariants: ἀπέναντι, ἀπεῖπον",
    562: "ἀπέραντος (apérantos | ap-er'-an-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a secondary derivative of G4008\nStrong's: unfinished, i.e. (by implication) interminable\nKJV: —endless.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4008 \n\nCognate Group: G1680 (faith), G1679 (hope), G4276 (first trust), G560 (hope for again)\nVariants: ἀπέραντος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5869 עַיִן",
    563: "ἀπερισπάστως (aperispástōs | ap-er-is-pas-toce')\n\nDerivation: adverb from a compound of G1 (as a negative participle) and a presumed derivative of G4049\nStrong's: undistractedly, i.e. free from (domestic) solicitude\nKJV: —without distraction.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4049 \n\nCognate Group: G1680 (faith), G1679 (hope), G4276 (first trust), G560 (hope for again)\nVariants: ἀπερισπάστως",
    564: "ἀπερίτμητος (aperítmētos | ap-er-eet'-may-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G4059\nStrong's: uncircumcised (figuratively)\nKJV: —uncircumcised.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4059 \n\nCognate Group: G4059 (circumcise), G4061 (X circumcised), G564 (uncircumcised)\nVariants: ἀπερίτμητος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3808 לֹא, H6189 עָרֵל",
    565: "ἀπέρχομαι (apérchomai | ap-erkh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G2064\nStrong's: to go off (i.e. depart), aside (i.e. apart) or behind (i.e. follow), literally or figuratively\nKJV: —come, depart, go (aside, away, back, out, … ways), pass away, be past.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G2064 \n\nCognate Group: G1330 (come), G565 (come), G1525 (X arise), G4905 (accompany), G4281 (go before), G4022 (fetch a compass), G2064 (accompany), G1904 (come), G4334 (come), G1831 (come), G3928 (come), G3922 (come in privily)\nVariants: ἀπέρχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H235 אָזַל, H622 אָסַף, H935 בֹּוא, H1540 גָּלָה, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2498 חָלַף, H3318 יָצָא, H4900 מָשַׁךְ, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5493 סוּר, H5674 עָבַר, H5927 עָלָה, H7503 רָפָה, H7725 שׁוּב",
    566: "ἀπέχει (apéchei | ap-ekh'-i)\n\nDerivation: third person singular present indicative active of G568 used impersonally\nStrong's: it is sufficient\nKJV: —it is enough.\n\nSee: G568 \n\nCognate Group: G1330 (come), G565 (come), G1525 (X arise), G4905 (accompany), G4281 (go before), G4022 (fetch a compass), G2064 (accompany), G1904 (come), G4334 (come), G1831 (come), G3928 (come), G3922 (come in privily)\nVariants: ἀπέχει, ἀπέχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1361 גָּבַהּ, H1481 גּוּר, H2308 חָדַל, H4513 מָנַע, H5337 נָצַל, H5493 סוּר, H6113 עָצָר, H7350 רָחֹוק, H7368 רָחַק, H7368 רָחַק",
    567: "ἀπέχομαι (apéchomai | ap-ekh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice (reflexively) of G568\nStrong's: to hold oneself off, i.e. refrain\nKJV: —abstain.\n\nSee: G568 \n\nCognate Group: G1330 (come), G565 (come), G1525 (X arise), G4905 (accompany), G4281 (go before), G4022 (fetch a compass), G2064 (accompany), G1904 (come), G4334 (come), G1831 (come), G3928 (come), G3922 (come in privily)\nVariants: ἀπέχομαι, ἀπέχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1361 גָּבַהּ, H1481 גּוּר, H2308 חָדַל, H4513 מָנַע, H5337 נָצַל, H5493 סוּר, H6113 עָצָר, H7350 רָחֹוק, H7368 רָחַק, H7368 רָחַק",
    568: "ἀπέχω (apéchō | ap-ekh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G2192\nStrong's: (actively) to have out, i.e. receive in full; (intransitively) to keep (oneself) away, i.e. be distant (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —be, have, receive.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G2192 \n\nCognate Group: G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)\nVariants: ἀπέχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1361 גָּבַהּ, H1481 גּוּר, H2308 חָדַל, H4513 מָנַע, H5337 נָצַל, H5493 סוּר, H6113 עָצָר, H7350 רָחֹוק, H7368 רָחַק, H7368 רָחַק",
    569: "ἀπιστέω (apistéō | ap-is-teh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G571\nStrong's: to be unbelieving, i.e. (transitively) disbelieve, or (by implication) disobey\nKJV: —believe not.\n\nSee: G571 \n\nCognate Group: G570 (unbelief), G571 (that believeth not), G4104 (assure of), G4103 (believe), G4100 (believe), G569 (believe not), G4102 (assurance), G3640 (of little faith)\nVariants: ἀπιστέω",
    570: "ἀπιστία (apistía | ap-is-tee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G571\nStrong's: faithlessness, i.e. (negatively) disbelief (lack of Christian faith), or (positively) unfaithfulness (disobedience)\nKJV: —unbelief.\n\nSee: G571 \n\nCognate Group: G570 (unbelief), G571 (that believeth not), G4104 (assure of), G4103 (believe), G4100 (believe), G569 (believe not), G4102 (assurance), G3640 (of little faith)\nVariants: ἀπιστία, ὀλιγοπιστία",
    571: "ἄπιστος (ápistos | ap'-is-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G4103\nStrong's: (actively) disbelieving, i.e. without Christian faith (specially, a heathen); (passively) untrustworthy (person), or incredible (thing)\nKJV: —that believeth not, faithless, incredible thing, infidel, unbeliever(-ing).\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4103 \n\nCognate Group: G570 (unbelief), G571 (that believeth not), G4104 (assure of), G4103 (believe), G4100 (believe), G569 (believe not), G4102 (assurance), G3640 (of little faith)\nVariants: ἄπιστος",
    572: "ἁπλότης (haplótēs | hap-lot'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G573\nStrong's: singleness, i.e. (subjectively) sincerity (without dissimulation or self-seeking), or (objectively) generosity (copious bestowal)\nKJV: —bountifulness, liberal(-ity), simplicity, singleness.\n\nSee: G573 \n\nCognate Group: G573 (single), G572 (bountifulness)\nVariants: ἁπλότης \nHebrew Equivalents: H3476 יֹשֶׁר, H8537 תֹּם",
    573: "ἁπλοῦς (haploûs | hap-looce')\n\nDerivation: probably from G1 (as a particle of union) and the base of G4120\nStrong's: properly, folded together, i.e. single (figuratively, clear)\nKJV: —single.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4120 \n\nCognate Group: G573 (single), G572 (bountifulness)\nVariants: ἁπλοῦς, ἁπλόος",
    574: "ἁπλῶς (haplōs | hap-loce')\n\nDerivation: adverb from G573 (in the objective sense of G572)\nStrong's: bountifully; \nKJV: —liberally.\n\nSee: G573 \nSee: G572 \n\nCognate Group: G573 (single), G572 (bountifulness)\nVariants: ἁπλῶς",
    575: "ἀπό (apó | apo')\n\nDerivation: a primary particle\nStrong's: \"off,\" i.e. away (from something near), in various senses (of place, time, or relation; literal or figurative)\nKJV: —(X here-)after, ago, at, because of, before, by (the space of), for(-th), from, in, (out) of, off, (up-)on(-ce), since, with. In composition (as a prefix) it usually denotes separation, departure, cessation, completion, reversal, etc.\n\nCognate Group: G573 (single), G572 (bountifulness)\nVariants: ἀπό, ἀπαρτί, ἀποπέμπω \nHebrew Equivalents: H8537 תֹּם",
    576: "ἀποβαίνω (apobaínō | ap-ob-ah'-ee-no)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and the base of G939\nStrong's: literally, to disembark; figuratively, to eventuate\nKJV: —become, go out, turn.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G573 (single), G572 (bountifulness)\nVariants: ἀποβαίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1961 הָיָה, H3318 יָצָא, H6132 עֲקַר, H6213 עָשָׂה",
    577: "ἀποβάλλω (apobállō | ap-ob-al'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G906\nStrong's: to throw off; figuratively, to lose\nKJV: —cast away.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G906 \n\nCognate Group: G573 (single), G572 (bountifulness)\nVariants: ἀποβάλλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5034 נָבֵל",
    578: "ἀποβλέπω (apoblépō | ap-ob-lep'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G991\nStrong's: to look away from everything else, i.e. (figuratively) intently regard\nKJV: —have respect.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G991 \n\nCognate Group: G573 (single), G572 (bountifulness)\nVariants: ἀποβλέπω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6049 עָנַן, H6437 פָּנָה, H6845 צָפַן, H7200 רָאָה",
    579: "ἀπόβλητος (apóblētos | ap-ob'-lay-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G577\nStrong's: cast off, i.e. (figuratively) such as to be rejected\nKJV: —be refused.\n\nSee: G577 \n\nCognate Group: G573 (single), G572 (bountifulness)\nVariants: ἀπόβλητος",
    580: "ἀποβολή (apobolḗ | ap-ob-ol-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G577\nStrong's: rejection; figuratively, loss\nKJV: —casting away, loss.\n\nSee: G577 \n\nCognate Group: G573 (single), G572 (bountifulness)\nVariants: ἀποβολή",
    581: "ἀπογενόμενος (apogenómenos | ap-og-en-om'-en-os)\n\nDerivation: past participle of a compound of G575 and G1096\nStrong's: absent, i.e. deceased (figuratively, renounced)\nKJV: —being dead.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1096 \n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: ἀπογενόμενος, ἀπογίνομαι",
    582: "ἀπογραφή (apographḗ | ap-og-raf-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G583\nStrong's: an enrollment; by implication, an assessment\nKJV: —taxing.\n\nSee: G583 \n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: ἀπογραφή \nHebrew Equivalents: H3791 כָּתָב",
    583: "ἀπογράφω (apográphō | ap-og-raf'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G1125\nStrong's: to write off (a copy or list), i.e. enrol\nKJV: —tax, write.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1125 \n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: ἀπογράφω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3789 כָּתַב",
    584: "ἀποδείκνυμι (apodeíknymi | ap-od-ike'-noo-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G1166\nStrong's: to show off, i.e. exhibit; figuratively, to demonstrate, i.e. accredit\nKJV: —(ap-)prove, set forth, shew.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1166 \n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: ἀποδείκνυμι \nHebrew Equivalents: H7200 רָאָה, H7981 שְׁלֵט",
    585: "ἀπόδειξις (apódeixis | ap-od'-ike-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G584\nStrong's: manifestation\nKJV: —demonstration.\n\nSee: G584 \n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: ἀπόδειξις",
    586: "ἀποδεκατόω (apodekatóō | ap-od-ek-at-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G1183\nStrong's: to tithe (as debtor or creditor)\nKJV: —(give, pay, take) tithe.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1183 \n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: ἀποδεκατόω, ἀποδεκατεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H631 אָסַר",
