    623: "Ἀπολλύων (Apollýōn | ap-ol-loo'-ohn)\n\nDerivation: active participle of G622\nStrong's: a destroyer (i.e. Satan)\nKJV: —Apollyon.\n\nSee: G622 \n\nCognate Group: G622 (destroy), G623 (Apollyon), G684 (damnable)\nVariants: Ἀπολλύων",
    624: "Ἀπολλωνία (Apollōnía | ap-ol-lo-nee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the pagan deity Ἀπόλλων (i.e. the sun\nStrong's: from G622); Apollonia, a place in Macedonia\nKJV: —Apollonia.\n\nSee: G622 \n\nCognate Group: G622 (destroy), G623 (Apollyon), G684 (damnable)\nVariants: Ἀπολλωνία",
    625: "Ἀπολλῶς (Apollōs | ap-ol-loce')\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as G624\nStrong's: Apollos, an Israelite\nKJV: —Apollos.\n\nSee: G624 \n\nCognate Group: G622 (destroy), G623 (Apollyon), G684 (damnable)\nVariants: Ἀπολλῶς, Ἀπολλώς",
    626: "ἀπολογέομαι (apologéomai | ap-ol-og-eh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from a compound of G575 and G3056\nStrong's: to give an account (legal plea) of oneself, i.e. exculpate (self)\nKJV: —answer (for self), make defence, excuse (self), speak for self.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G3056 \n\nCognate Group: G622 (destroy), G623 (Apollyon), G684 (damnable)\nVariants: ἀπολογέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H7379 רִיב",
    627: "ἀπολογία (apología | ap-ol-og-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G626\nStrong's: a plea (\"apology\")\nKJV: —answer (for self), clearing of self, defence.\n\nSee: G626 \n\nCognate Group: G622 (destroy), G623 (Apollyon), G684 (damnable)\nVariants: ἀπολογία",
    628: "ἀπολούω (apoloúō | ap-ol-oo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G3068\nStrong's: to wash fully, i.e. (figuratively) have remitted (reflexively)\nKJV: —wash (away).\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G3068 \n\nCognate Group: G628 (wash), G3067 (washing), G3068 (wash)\nVariants: ἀπολούω, ἀπολούομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H7364 רָחַץ",
    629: "ἀπολύτρωσις (apolýtrōsis | ap-ol-oo'-tro-sis)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G575 and G3083\nStrong's: (the act) ransom in full, i.e. (figuratively) riddance, or (specially) Christian salvation\nKJV: —deliverance, redemption.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G3083 \n\nCognate Group: G2647 (destroy), G3089 (break), G3083 (ransom), G179 (endless), G630 (depart), G1956 (determine), G360 (depart), G3085 (+ redeemed), G2646 (guestchamber), G359 (departure), G3086 (deliverer), G1955 (interpretation), G3084 (redeem), G629 (deliverance), G487 (ransom)\nVariants: ἀπολύτρωσις",
    630: "ἀπολύω (apolýō | ap-ol-oo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G3089\nStrong's: to free fully, i.e. (literally) relieve, release, dismiss (reflexively, depart), or (figuratively) let die, pardon or (specially) divorce\nKJV: —(let) depart, dismiss, divorce, forgive, let go, loose, put (send) away, release, set at liberty.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G3089 \n\nCognate Group: G2647 (destroy), G3089 (break), G3083 (ransom), G179 (endless), G630 (depart), G1956 (determine), G360 (depart), G3085 (+ redeemed), G2646 (guestchamber), G359 (departure), G3086 (deliverer), G1955 (interpretation), G3084 (redeem), G629 (deliverance), G487 (ransom)\nVariants: ἀπολύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1478 גָּוַע, H1644 גָּרַשׁ, H1980 הָלַךְ, H7725 שׁוּב",
    631: "ἀπομάσσομαι (apomássomai | ap-om-as'-som-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G575 and μάσσω (to squeeze, knead, smear)\nStrong's: to scrape away\nKJV: —wipe off.\n\nSee: G575 \n\nCognate Group: G2647 (destroy), G3089 (break), G3083 (ransom), G179 (endless), G630 (depart), G1956 (determine), G360 (depart), G3085 (+ redeemed), G2646 (guestchamber), G359 (departure), G3086 (deliverer), G1955 (interpretation), G3084 (redeem), G629 (deliverance), G487 (ransom)\nVariants: ἀπομάσσομαι, ἀπομάσσω",
    632: "ἀπονέμω (aponémō | ap-on-em'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and the base of G3551\nStrong's: to apportion, i.e. bestow\nKJV: —give.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G3551 \n\nCognate Group: G2647 (destroy), G3089 (break), G3083 (ransom), G179 (endless), G630 (depart), G1956 (determine), G360 (depart), G3085 (+ redeemed), G2646 (guestchamber), G359 (departure), G3086 (deliverer), G1955 (interpretation), G3084 (redeem), G629 (deliverance), G487 (ransom)\nVariants: ἀπονέμω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2505 חָלַק",
    633: "ἀπονίπτω (aponíptō | ap-on-ip'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G3538\nStrong's: to wash off (reflexively, one's own hands symbolically)\nKJV: —wash.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G3538 \n\nCognate Group: G2647 (destroy), G3089 (break), G3083 (ransom), G179 (endless), G630 (depart), G1956 (determine), G360 (depart), G3085 (+ redeemed), G2646 (guestchamber), G359 (departure), G3086 (deliverer), G1955 (interpretation), G3084 (redeem), G629 (deliverance), G487 (ransom)\nVariants: ἀπονίπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H4229 מָחָה, H7364 רָחַץ, H7857 שָׁטַף",
    634: "ἀποπίπτω (apopíptō | ap-op-ip'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G4098\nStrong's: to fall off\nKJV: —fall.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4098 \n\nCognate Group: G2647 (destroy), G3089 (break), G3083 (ransom), G179 (endless), G630 (depart), G1956 (determine), G360 (depart), G3085 (+ redeemed), G2646 (guestchamber), G359 (departure), G3086 (deliverer), G1955 (interpretation), G3084 (redeem), G629 (deliverance), G487 (ransom)\nVariants: ἀποπίπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2502 חָלַץ, H3951 לֶקֶט, H4448 מָלַל, H5034 נָבֵל, H5307 נָפַל",
    635: "ἀποπλανάω (apoplanáō | ap-op-lan-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G4105\nStrong's: to lead astray (figuratively); passively, to stray (from truth)\nKJV: —err, seduce.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4105 \n\nCognate Group: G4105 (go astray), G4107 (wandering), G4108 (deceiver), G4106 (deceit), G635 (err)\nVariants: ἀποπλανάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5080 נָדַח, H5186 נָטָה, H7725 שׁוּב",
    636: "ἀποπλέω (apopléō | ap-op-leh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G4126\nStrong's: to set sail\nKJV: —sail away.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4126 \n\nCognate Group: G4105 (go astray), G4107 (wandering), G4108 (deceiver), G4106 (deceit), G635 (err)\nVariants: ἀποπλέω",
    637: "ἀποπλύνω (apoplýnō | ap-op-loo'-no)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G4150\nStrong's: to rinse off\nKJV: —wash.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4150 \n\nCognate Group: G4105 (go astray), G4107 (wandering), G4108 (deceiver), G4106 (deceit), G635 (err)\nVariants: ἀποπλύνω G677 \nHebrew Equivalents: H3526 כָּבַס, H7857 שָׁטַף",
    638: "ἀποπνίγω (apopnígō | ap-op-nee'-go)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G4155\nStrong's: to stifle (by drowning or overgrowth)\nKJV: —choke.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4155 \n\nCognate Group: G4156 (strangled), G4846 (choke), G638 (choke), G4155 (choke)\nVariants: ἀποπνίγω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2614 חָנַק",
    639: "ἀπορέω (aporéō | ap-or-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1 (as a negative particle) and the base of G4198\nStrong's: to have no way out, i.e. be at a loss (mentally)\nKJV: — (stand in) doubt, be perplexed.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4198 \n\nCognate Group: G4156 (strangled), G4846 (choke), G638 (choke), G4155 (choke)\nVariants: ἀπορέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1742 דַּוָּי, H2637 חָסֵר, H4134 מוּךְ, H5968 עָלַף, H6565 פָּרַר, H6887 צָרַר, H7909 שַׁכּוּל",
    640: "ἀπορία (aporía | ap-or-ee'-a)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G639\nStrong's: a (state of) quandary\nKJV: —perplexity.\n\nSee: G639 \n\nCognate Group: G4156 (strangled), G4846 (choke), G638 (choke), G4155 (choke)\nVariants: ἀπορία \nHebrew Equivalents: H928 בֶּהָלָה, H3994 מְאֵרָה, H6183 עָרִיף, H6565 פָּרַר, H6869 צָרָה, H6937 קָדַר, H7711 שְׁדֵפָה, H7829 שַׁחֶפֶת",
    641: "ἀποῤῥίπτω (aporrhíptō | ap-or-hrip'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G4496\nStrong's: to hurl off, i.e. precipitate (oneself)\nKJV: —cast.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4496 \n\nCognate Group: G4495 (cast off), G641 (cast), G1977 (cast upon), G4496 (cast)\nVariants: ἀποῤῥίπτω, ἀπορίπτω, ἀπο(ρ)ρίπτω, ἀπορρίπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1438 גָּדַע, H1629 גָּרַז, H1644 גָּרַשׁ, H1819 דָּמָה, H1826 דָּמַם, H2904 טוּל, H3988 מָאַס, H4127 מוּג, H5034 נָבֵל, H5307 נָפַל, H7971 שָׁלַח, H7993 שָׁלַךְ, H8217 שָׁפָל",
    642: "ἀπορφανίζω (aporphanízō | ap-or-fan-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and a derivative of G3737\nStrong's: to bereave wholly, i.e. (figuratively) separate (from intercourse)\nKJV: —take.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G3737 \n\nCognate Group: G4495 (cast off), G641 (cast), G1977 (cast upon), G4496 (cast)\nVariants: ἀπορφανίζω",
    643: "ἀποσκευάζω (aposkeuázō | ap-osk-yoo-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and a derivative of G4632\nStrong's: to pack up (one's) baggage\nKJV: —take up… carriages.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4632 \n\nCognate Group: G4495 (cast off), G641 (cast), G1977 (cast upon), G4496 (cast)\nVariants: ἀποσκευάζω, ἐπισκευάζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H918 בָּדַק, H2318 חָדַשׁ, H2388 חָזַק, H3554 כָּוָה, H5927 עָלָה, H6437 פָּנָה",
    644: "ἀποσκίασμα (aposkíasma | ap-os-kee'-as-mah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G575 and a derivative of G4639\nStrong's: a shading off, i.e. obscuration\nKJV: —shadow.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4639 \n\nCognate Group: G644 (shadow), G4639 (shadow), G1982 (overshadow)\nVariants: ἀποσκίασμα",
    645: "ἀποσπάω (apospáō | ap-os-pah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G4685\nStrong's: to drag forth, i.e. (literally) unsheathe (a sword), or relatively (with a degree of force implied) retire (personally or factiously)\nKJV: —(with-)draw (away), after we were gotten from.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4685 \n\nCognate Group: G644 (shadow), G4639 (shadow), G1982 (overshadow)\nVariants: ἀποσπάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3772 כָּרַת, H5423 נָתַק, H5428 נָתַשׁ, H6268 עַתִּיק, H6504 פָּרַד",
    646: "ἀποστασία (apostasía | ap-os-tas-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: feminine of the same as G647\nStrong's: defection from truth (properly, the state) (\"apostasy\")\nKJV: —falling away, forsake.\n\nSee: G647 \n\nCognate Group: G646 (falling away), G1370 (division), G868 (depart)\nVariants: ἀποστασία \nHebrew Equivalents: H1100 בְּלִיַּעַל, H4604 מַעַל, H4777 מֶרֶד, H7200 רָאָה",
    647: "ἀποστάσιον (apostásion | ap-os-tas'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a (presumed) adjective from a derivative of G868\nStrong's: properly, something separative, i.e. (specially) divorce\nKJV: —(writing of) divorcement.\n\nSee: G868 \n\nCognate Group: G646 (falling away), G1370 (division), G868 (depart)\nVariants: ἀποστάσιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H3748 כְּרִיתוּת",
    648: "ἀποστεγάζω (apostegázō | ap-os-teg-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and a derivative of G4721\nStrong's: to unroof\nKJV: —uncover.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4721 \n\nCognate Group: G646 (falling away), G1370 (division), G868 (depart)\nVariants: ἀποστεγάζω",
    649: "ἀποστέλλω (apostéllō | ap-os-tel'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G4724\nStrong's: set apart, i.e. (by implication) to send out (properly, on a mission) literally or figuratively\nKJV: —put in, send (away, forth, out), set (at liberty).\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4724 \n\nCognate Group: G651 (apostleship), G649 (put in), G5570 (false teacher), G1821 (send), G652 (apostle), G3992 (send)\nVariants: ἀποστέλλω, ἐμπέμπω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H2470 חָלָה, H3381 יָרַד, H4284 מַחֲשָׁבָה, H5182 נְחַת, H5398 נָשַׁף, H5414 נָתַן, H5493 סוּר, H5774 עוּף, H6327 פּוּץ, H6680 צָוָה, H7725 שׁוּב, H7971 שָׁלַח, H8421 תּוּב",
    650: "ἀποστερέω (aposteréō | ap-os-ter-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and στερέω (to deprive)\nStrong's: to despoil\nKJV: —defraud, destitute, kept back by fraud.\n\nSee: G575 \n\nCognate Group: G5304 (want), G5305 (afterward), G5303 (that which is behind), G5306 (latter), G650 (defraud), G5302 (come behind)\nVariants: ἀποστερέω, ἀφυστερέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1639 גָּרַע, H4513 מָנַע, H6231 עָשַׁק",
    651: "ἀποστολή (apostolḗ | ap-os-tol-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G649\nStrong's: commission, i.e. (specially) apostolate\nKJV: —apostleship.\n\nSee: G649 \n\nCognate Group: G651 (apostleship), G649 (put in), G5570 (false teacher), G1821 (send), G652 (apostle), G3992 (send)\nVariants: ἀποστολή \nHebrew Equivalents: H4917 מִשְׁלַחַת, H7971 שָׁלַח",
    652: "ἀπόστολος (apóstolos | ap-os'-tol-os)\n\nDerivation: from G649\nStrong's: a delegate; specially, an ambassador of the Gospel; officially a commissioner of Christ (\"apostle\") (with miraculous powers)\nKJV: —apostle, messenger, he that is sent.\n\nSee: G649 \n\nCognate Group: G651 (apostleship), G649 (put in), G5570 (false teacher), G1821 (send), G652 (apostle), G3992 (send)\nVariants: ἀπόστολος \nHebrew Equivalents: H7971 שָׁלַח",
    653: "ἀποστοματίζω (apostomatízō | ap-os-tom-at-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and a (presumed) derivative of G4750\nStrong's: to speak off-hand (properly, dictate), i.e. to catechize (in an invidious manner)\nKJV: —provoke to speak.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4750 \n\nCognate Group: G651 (apostleship), G649 (put in), G5570 (false teacher), G1821 (send), G652 (apostle), G3992 (send)\nVariants: ἀποστοματίζω",
    654: "ἀποστρέφω (apostréphō | ap-os-tref'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G4762\nStrong's: to turn away or back (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —bring again, pervert, turn away (from).\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4762 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἀποστρέφω \nHebrew Equivalents: H553 אָמַץ, H1234 בָּקַע, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2015 הָפַךְ, H2186 זָנַח, H2559 חָמַק, H3427 יָשַׁב, H3665 כָּנַע, H4513 מָנַע, H5066 נָגַשׁ, H5428 נָתַשׁ, H5437 סָבַב, H5472 סוּג, H5493 סוּר, H5496 סוּת, H5641 סָתַר, H5674 עָבַר, H5956 עָלַם, H6437 פָּנָה, H6565 פָּרַר, H6908 קָבַץ, H7673 שָׁבַת, H7725 שׁוּב, H7728 שֹׁובֵב, H7737 שָׁוָה, H7896 שִׁית, H7993 שָׁלַךְ, H8266 שָׁקַר, H8377 תְּאֹו",
    655: "ἀποστυγέω (apostygéō | ap-os-toog-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and the base of G4767\nStrong's: to detest utterly\nKJV: —abhor.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4767 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἀποστυγέω",
    656: "ἀποσυνάγωγος (aposynágōgos | ap-os-oon-ag'-o-gos)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G4864\nStrong's: excommunicated\nKJV: —(put) out of the synagogue(-s).\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G4864 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἀποσυνάγωγος",
    657: "ἀποτάσσομαι (apotássomai | ap-ot-as'-som-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G575 and G5021\nStrong's: literally, to say adieu (by departing or dismissing); figuratively, to renounce\nKJV: —bid farewell, forsake, take leave, send away.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5021 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀποτάσσομαι, ἀποτάσσω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2976 יָאַשׁ",
    658: "ἀποτελέω (apoteléō | ap-ot-el-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G5055\nStrong's: to complete entirely, i.e. consummate\nKJV: —finish.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5055 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀποτελέω",
    659: "ἀποτίθημι (apotíthēmi | ap-ot-eeth'-ay-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G5087\nStrong's: to put away (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —cast off, lay apart (aside, down), put away (off).\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5087 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀποτίθημι \nHebrew Equivalents: H5117 נוּחַ, H7725 שׁוּב, H7760 שׂוּם",
    660: "ἀποτινάσσω (apotinássō | ap-ot-in-as'-so)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and τινάσσω (to jostle)\nStrong's: to brush off\nKJV: —shake off.\n\nSee: G575 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀποτινάσσω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5287 נָעַר, H5287 נָעַר, H5428 נָתַשׁ",
    661: "ἀποτίνω (apotínō | ap-ot-ee'-no)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G5099\nStrong's: to pay in full\nKJV: —repay.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5099 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀποτίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5414 נָתַן, H7760 שׂוּם, H8003 שָׁלֵם, H8254 שָׁקַל",
    662: "ἀποτολμάω (apotolmáō | ap-ot-ol-mah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G5111\nStrong's: to venture plainly\nKJV: —be very bold.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5111 \n\nCognate Group: G662 (be very bold), G5112 (the more boldly), G5113 (presumptuous), G5111 (be bold)\nVariants: ἀποτολμάω",
    663: "ἀποτομία (apotomía | ap-ot-om-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G664\nStrong's: (figuratively) decisiveness, i.e. rigor\nKJV: —severity.\n\nSee: G664 \n\nCognate Group: G2699 (concision), G663 (severity), G3718 (rightly divide), G664 (sharply)\nVariants: ἀποτομία",
    664: "ἀποτόμως (apotómōs | ap-ot-om'-oce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from a derivative of a comparative of G575 and τέμνω (to cut)\nStrong's: abruptly, i.e. peremptorily\nKJV: —sharply(-ness).\n\nSee: G575 \n\nCognate Group: G2699 (concision), G663 (severity), G3718 (rightly divide), G664 (sharply)\nVariants: ἀποτόμως",
    665: "ἀποτρέπω (apotrépō | ap-ot-rep'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and the base of G5157\nStrong's: to deflect, i.e. (reflexively) avoid\nKJV: —turn away.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5157 \n\nCognate Group: G2699 (concision), G663 (severity), G3718 (rightly divide), G664 (sharply)\nVariants: ἀποτρέπω, ἀποτρέπομαι",
    666: "ἀπουσία (apousía | ap-oo-see'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the participle of G548\nStrong's: a being away\nKJV: —absence.\n\nSee: G548 \n\nCognate Group: G2699 (concision), G663 (severity), G3718 (rightly divide), G664 (sharply)\nVariants: ἀπουσία",
    667: "ἀποφέρω (apophérō | ap-of-er'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G5342\nStrong's: to bear off (literally or relatively)\nKJV: —bring, carry (away).\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5342 \n\nCognate Group: G2699 (concision), G663 (severity), G3718 (rightly divide), G664 (sharply)\nVariants: ἀποφέρω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2986 יָבַל, H3947 לָקַח, H5375 נָשָׂא",
    668: "ἀποφεύγω (apopheúgō | ap-of-yoo'-go)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G5343\nStrong's: (figuratively) to escape\nKJV: —escape.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5343 \n\nCognate Group: G2699 (concision), G663 (severity), G3718 (rightly divide), G664 (sharply)\nVariants: ἀποφεύγω",
    669: "ἀποφθέγγομαι (apophthéngomai | ap-of-theng'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G5350\nStrong's: to enunciate plainly, i.e. declare\nKJV: —say, speak forth, utterance.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5350 \n\nCognate Group: G669 (say)\nVariants: ἀποφθέγγομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H3576 כָּזַב, H5012 נָבָא, H5042 נָבַע, H6049 עָנַן, H7080 קָסַם",
    670: "ἀποφορτίζομαι (apophortízomai | ap-of-or-tid'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and the middle voice of G5412\nStrong's: to unload\nKJV: —unlade.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5412 \n\nCognate Group: G669 (say)\nVariants: ἀποφορτίζομαι",
    671: "ἀπόχρησις (apóchrēsis | ap-okh'-ray-sis)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G575 and G5530\nStrong's: the act of using up, i.e. consumption\nKJV: —using.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5530 \n\nCognate Group: G669 (say)\nVariants: ἀπόχρησις",
    672: "ἀποχωρέω (apochōréō | ap-okh-o-reh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G5562\nStrong's: to go away\nKJV: —depart.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5562 \n\nCognate Group: G669 (say)\nVariants: ἀποχωρέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5472 סוּג",
    673: "ἀποχωρίζω (apochōrízō | ap-okh-o-rid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G5563\nStrong's: to rend apart; reflexively, to separate\nKJV: —depart (asunder).\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5563 \n\nCognate Group: G669 (say)\nVariants: ἀποχωρίζω, ἀποχωρίζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H4662 מִפְקָד",
    674: "ἀποψύχω (apopsýchō | ap-ops-oo'-kho)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G5594\nStrong's: to breathe out, i.e. faint\nKJV: —hearts failing.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5594 \n\nCognate Group: G669 (say)\nVariants: ἀποψύχω",
    675: "Ἄππιος (Áppios | ap'-pee-os)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: (in the genitive, i.e. possessive case) of Appius, the name of a Roman\nKJV: —Appii.\n\nCognate Group: G669 (say)\nVariants: Ἄππιος, Ἀππίου, Ἀππίου~Φόρον, Ἀππίου Φόρον",
    676: "ἀπρόσιτος (aprósitos | ap-ros'-ee-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of a comparative of G4314 and εἶμι (to go)\nStrong's: inaccessible\nKJV: —which no man can approach.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4314 \n\nCognate Group: G669 (say)\nVariants: ἀπρόσιτος",
    677: "ἀπρόσκοπος (apróskopos | ap-ros'-kop-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G4350\nStrong's: actively, inoffensive, i.e. not leading into sin; passively, faultless, i.e. not led into sin\nKJV: —none (void of, without) offence.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4350 \n\nCognate Group: G4350 (beat upon), G677 (none), G4348 (offence), G4349 (offence)\nVariants: ἀπρόσκοπος",
    678: "ἀπροσωπολήπτως (aprosōpolḗptōs | ap-ros-o-pol-ape'-tos)\n\nDerivation: adverb from a compound of G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of a presumed compound of G4383 and G2983 (compare G4381)\nStrong's: in a way not accepting the person, i.e. impartially\nKJV: —without respect of persons.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4383 \nSee: G2983 \nSee: G4381 \n\nCognate Group: G2146 (make a fair show), G4380 (have respect to persons), G4382 (respect of persons), G678 (without respect of persons), G4383 (appearance), G4381 (respecter of persons)\nVariants: ἀπροσωπολήπτως, ἀπροσωπολήμπτως",
    679: "ἄπταιστος (áptaistos | ap-tah'-ee-stos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G4417\nStrong's: not stumbling, i.e. (figuratively) without sin\nKJV: —from falling.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4417 \n\nCognate Group: G2146 (make a fair show), G4380 (have respect to persons), G4382 (respect of persons), G678 (without respect of persons), G4383 (appearance), G4381 (respecter of persons)\nVariants: ἄπταιστος",
    680: "ἅπτομαι (háptomai | hap'-tom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: reflexive of G681\nStrong's: properly, to attach oneself to, i.e. to touch (in many implied relations)\nKJV: —touch.\n\nSee: G681 \n\nCognate Group: G2146 (make a fair show), G4380 (have respect to persons), G4382 (respect of persons), G678 (without respect of persons), G4383 (appearance), G4381 (respecter of persons)\nVariants: ἅπτομαι, ἅπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H270 אָחַז, H1692 דָּבַק, H5060 נָגַע, H7126 קָרַב, H7971 שָׁלַח, H7981 שְׁלֵט",
    681: "ἅπτω (háptō | hap'-to)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: properly, to fasten to, i.e. (specially) to set on fire\nKJV: —kindle, light.\n\nCognate Group: G2146 (make a fair show), G4380 (have respect to persons), G4382 (respect of persons), G678 (without respect of persons), G4383 (appearance), G4381 (respecter of persons)\nVariants: ἅπτω, περιάπτω",
    682: "Ἀπφία (Apphía | ap-fee'-a)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: Apphia, a woman of Collosæ\nKJV: —Apphia.\n\nCognate Group: G2146 (make a fair show), G4380 (have respect to persons), G4382 (respect of persons), G678 (without respect of persons), G4383 (appearance), G4381 (respecter of persons)\nVariants: Ἀπφία",
    683: "ἀπωθέομαι (apōthéomai | ap-o-theh'-om-ahee) or ἀπώθομαι (apṓthomai | ap-o'-thom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and the middle voice of ὠθέω or ὤθω (to shove)\nStrong's: to push off, figuratively, to reject\nKJV: —cast away, put away (from), thrust away (from).\n\nSee: G575 \n\nCognate Group: G683 (cast away)\nVariants: ἀπωθέομαι, ἀπωθέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1272 בָּרַח, H1350 גָּאַל, H1504 גָּזַר, H1639 גָּרַע, H1644 גָּרַשׁ, H1760 דָּחָה, H1920 הָדַף, H1972 הָלָא, H2186 זָנַח, H3988 מָאַס, H5006 נָאַץ, H5080 נָדַח, H5428 נָתַשׁ, H5472 סוּג, H5647 עָבַד, H6544 פָּרַע, H7368 רָחַק, H7489 רָעַע, H7686 שָׁגָה",
    684: "ἀπώλεια (apṓleia | ap-o'-li-a)\n\nDerivation: from a presumed derivative of G622\nStrong's: ruin or loss (physical, spiritual or eternal)\nKJV: —damnable(-nation), destruction, die, perdition, X perish, pernicious ways, waste.\n\nSee: G622 \n\nCognate Group: G622 (destroy), G623 (Apollyon), G684 (damnable)\nVariants: ἀπώλεια \nHebrew Equivalents: H343 אֵיד, H657 אֶפֶס, H1091 בַּלָּהָה, H1478 גָּוַע, H1917 הַדָּם, H2555 חָמָס, H2764 חֵרֶם, H4001 מְבוּסָה, H4032 מָגֹור, H4046 מַגֵּפָה, H4103 מְהוּמָה, H4646 מַפָּח, H5647 עָבַד, H7200 רָאָה, H7588 שָׁאֹון, H7703 שָׁדַד, H7722 שֹׁוא, H7843 שָׁחַת, H7998 שָׁלָל, H8045 שָׁמַד, H8077 שְׁמָמָה",
    685: "ἀρά (ará | ar-ah')\n\nDerivation: probably from G142\nStrong's: properly, prayer (as lifted to Heaven), i.e. (by implication) imprecation\nKJV: —curse.\n\nSee: G142 \n\nCognate Group: G685 (curse), G2671 (cursed), G2672 (curse), G1944 (accursed), G686 (haply), G687 (therefore)\nVariants: ἀρά \nHebrew Equivalents: H200 אִוֶּלֶת, H5927 עָלָה, H7045 קְלָלָה",
    686: "ἄρα (ára | ar'-ah)\n\nDerivation: probably from G142 (through the idea of drawing a conclusion)\nStrong's: a particle denoting an inference more or less decisive (as follows)\nKJV: —haply, (what) manner (of man), no doubt, perhaps, so be, then, therefore, truly, wherefore. Often used in connection with other particles, especially G1065 or G3767 (after) or G1487 (before). Compare also G687 .\n\nSee: G142 \nSee: G1065 \nSee: G3767 \nSee: G1487 \nSee: G687 \n\nCognate Group: G685 (curse), G2671 (cursed), G2672 (curse), G1944 (accursed), G686 (haply), G687 (therefore)\nVariants: ἄρα",
    687: "ἆρα (âra | ar'-ah)\n\nDerivation: a form of G686, denoting an interrogation to which a negative answer is presumed\nKJV: —therefore.\n\nSee: G686 \n\nCognate Group: G685 (curse), G2671 (cursed), G2672 (curse), G1944 (accursed), G686 (haply), G687 (therefore)\nVariants: ἆρα, ὰρα",
    688: "Ἀραβία (Arabía | ar-ab-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H6152)\nStrong's: Arabia, a region of Asia\nKJV: —Arabia.\nSee: H6152\n\nCognate Group: G685 (curse), G2671 (cursed), G2672 (curse), G1944 (accursed), G686 (haply), G687 (therefore)\nVariants: Ἀραβία \nHebrew Equivalents: H6152 עֲרָב",
    689: "Ἀράμ (Arám | ar-am')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H7410)\nStrong's: Aram (i.e. Ram), an Israelite\nKJV: —Aram.\nSee: H7410\n\nCognate Group: G685 (curse), G2671 (cursed), G2672 (curse), G1944 (accursed), G686 (haply), G687 (therefore)\nVariants: Ἀράμ, Ἀδμίν, Ἀρμίν \nHebrew Equivalents: H7410 רָם",
    690: "Ἄραψ (Áraps | ar'-aps)\n\nDerivation: from G688\nStrong's: an Arab or native of Arabia\nKJV: —Arabian.\n\nSee: G688 \n\nCognate Group: G685 (curse), G2671 (cursed), G2672 (curse), G1944 (accursed), G686 (haply), G687 (therefore)\nVariants: Ἄραψ",
    691: "ἀργέω (argéō | arg-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G692\nStrong's: to be idle, i.e. (figuratively) to delay\nKJV: —linger.\n\nSee: G692 \n\nCognate Group: G692 (barren), G2673 (abolish), G691 (linger)\nVariants: ἀργέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H988 בָּטֵל, H989 בְּטֵל",
    692: "ἀργός (argós | ar-gos')\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G2041\nStrong's: inactive, i.e. unemployed; (by implication) lazy, useless\nKJV: —barren, idle, slow.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G2041 \n\nCognate Group: G692 (barren), G2673 (abolish), G691 (linger)\nVariants: ἀργός \nHebrew Equivalents: H4853 מַשָּׂא",
    693: "ἀργύρεος (argýreos | ar-goo'-reh-os)\n\nDerivation: from G696\nStrong's: made of silver\nKJV: —(of) silver.\n\nSee: G696 \n\nCognate Group: G692 (barren), G2673 (abolish), G691 (linger)\nVariants: ἀργύρεος, ἀργυροῦς \nHebrew Equivalents: H3701 כֶּסֶף",
    694: "ἀργύριον (argýrion | ar-goo'-ree-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a presumed derivative of G696\nStrong's: silvery, i.e. (by implication) cash; specially, a silverling (i.e. drachma or shekel)\nKJV: —money, (piece of) silver (piece).\n\nSee: G696 \n\nCognate Group: G692 (barren), G2673 (abolish), G691 (linger)\nVariants: ἀργύριον \nHebrew Equivalents: H3701 כֶּסֶף, H3800 כֶּתֶם",
    695: "ἀργυροκόπος (argyrokópos | ar-goo-rok-op'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G696 and G2875\nStrong's: a beater (i.e. worker) of silver\nKJV: —silversmith.\n\nSee: G696 \nSee: G2875 \n\nCognate Group: G692 (barren), G2673 (abolish), G691 (linger)\nVariants: ἀργυροκόπος \nHebrew Equivalents: H6884 צָרַף",
    696: "ἄργυρος (árgyros | ar'-goo-ros)\n\nDerivation: from ἀργός (shining)\nStrong's: silver (the metal, in the articles or coin)\nKJV: —silver.\n\nCognate Group: G692 (barren), G2673 (abolish), G691 (linger)\nVariants: ἄργυρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3701 כֶּסֶף",
    697: "Ἄρειος Πάγος (Áreios Págos | ar'-i-os pag'-os)\n\nDerivation: from Ἄρης (the name of the Greek deity of war) and a derivative of G4078\nStrong's: rock of Ares, a place in Athens\nKJV: —Areopagus, Mars' Hill.\n\nSee: G4078 \n\nCognate Group: G692 (barren), G2673 (abolish), G691 (linger)\nVariants: Ἄρειος Πάγος, Ἄρειος πάγος, πάγος",
    698: "Ἀρεοπαγίτης (Areopagítēs | ar-eh-op-ag-ee'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G697\nStrong's: an Areopagite or member of the court held on Mars' Hill\nKJV: —Areopagite.\n\nSee: G697 \n\nCognate Group: G692 (barren), G2673 (abolish), G691 (linger)\nVariants: Ἀρεοπαγίτης",
    699: "ἀρεσκεία (areskeía | ar-es'-ki-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G700\nStrong's: complaisance\nKJV: —pleasing.\n\nSee: G700 \n\nCognate Group: G2100 (please), G701 (please), G699 (pleasing), G700 (please), G2101 (acceptable), G441 (men-pleaser)\nVariants: ἀρεσκεία, ἀρέσκεια \nHebrew Equivalents: H2580 חֵן",
    700: "ἀρέσκω (aréskō | ar-es'-ko)\n\nDerivation: probably from G142 (through the idea of exciting emotion)\nStrong's: to be agreeable (or by implication, to seek to be so)\nKJV: —please.\n\nSee: G142 \n\nCognate Group: G2100 (please), G701 (please), G699 (pleasing), G700 (please), G2101 (acceptable), G441 (men-pleaser)\nVariants: ἀρέσκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2895 טֹוב, H3474 יָשַׁר, H4672 מָצָא, H6030 עָנָה, H6148 עָרַב, H7737 שָׁוָה, H8232 שְׁפַר",
    701: "ἀρεστός (arestós | ar-es-tos')\n\nDerivation: from G700\nStrong's: agreeable; by implication, fit\nKJV: —(things that) please(-ing), reason.\n\nSee: G700 \n\nCognate Group: G2100 (please), G701 (please), G699 (pleasing), G700 (please), G2101 (acceptable), G441 (men-pleaser)\nVariants: ἀρεστός \nHebrew Equivalents: H977 בָּחַר, H2896 טֹוב, H3477 יָשָׁר, H7468 רְעוּת, H7522 רָצֹון, H8307 שְׁרִירוּת, H8378 תַּאֲוָה",
    702: "Ἀρέτας (Arétas | ar-et'-as)\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Aretas, an Arabian\nKJV: —Aretas.\n\nCognate Group: G2100 (please), G701 (please), G699 (pleasing), G700 (please), G2101 (acceptable), G441 (men-pleaser)\nVariants: Ἀρέτας, Ἁρέτας",
    703: "ἀρέτη (arétē | ar-et'-ay)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G730\nStrong's: properly, manliness (valor), i.e. excellence (intrinsic or attributed)\nKJV: —praise, virtue.\n\nSee: G730 \n\nCognate Group: G703 (praise)\nVariants: ἀρέτη, ἀρετή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1935 הֹוד, H8416 תְּהִלָּה",
    704: "ἀρήν (arḗn | ar-ane')\n\nDerivation: perhaps the same as G730\nStrong's: a lamb (as a male)\nKJV: —lamb.\n\nSee: G730 \n\nCognate Group: G704 (lamb), G286 (lamb), G721 (lamb)\nVariants: ἀρήν \nHebrew Equivalents: H3532 כֶּבֶשׂ, H4806 מְרִיא",
    705: "ἀριθμέω (arithméō | ar-ith-meh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G706\nStrong's: to enumerate or count\nKJV: —number.\n\nSee: G706 \n\nCognate Group: G705 (number)\nVariants: ἀριθμέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H2706 חֹק, H4487 מָנָה, H5608 סָפַר, H6485 פָּקַד",
    706: "ἀριθμός (arithmós | ar-ith-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G142\nStrong's: a number (as reckoned up)\nKJV: —number.\n\nSee: G142 \n\nCognate Group: G705 (number)\nVariants: ἀριθμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H3187 יָחַשׂ, H4060 מִדָּה, H4193 מֹות, H4373 מִכְסָה, H4510 מִנְיָן, H4557 מִסְפָּר, H4562 מָסֹרֶת, H5610 סְפָר, H6485 פָּקַד, H6635 צָבָא, H7097 קָצֶה, H7218 רֹאשׁ",
    707: "Ἀριμαθαία (Arimathaía | ar-ee-math-ah'-ee-ah)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H7414)\nStrong's: Arimathæa (or Ramah), a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Arimathæa.\nSee: H7414\n\nCognate Group: G705 (number)\nVariants: Ἀριμαθαία, Ἁριμαθαία \nHebrew Equivalents: H7414 רָמָה",
    708: "Ἀρίσταρχος (Arístarchos | ar-is'-tar-khos)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G712 and G757\nStrong's: best ruling; Aristarchus, a Macedonian\nKJV: —Aristarchus.\n\nSee: G712 \nSee: G757 \n\nCognate Group: G705 (number)\nVariants: Ἀρίσταρχος",
    709: "ἀριστάω (aristáō | ar-is-tah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G712\nStrong's: to take the principle meal\nKJV: —dine.\n\nSee: G712 \n\nCognate Group: G705 (number)\nVariants: ἀριστάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H398 אָכַל, H5582 סָעַד",
    710: "ἀριστερός (aristerós | ar-is-ter-os')\n\nDerivation: apparently a comparative of the same as G712\nStrong's: the left hand (as second-best)\nKJV: —left (hand).\n\nSee: G712 \n\nCognate Group: G705 (number)\nVariants: ἀριστερός \nHebrew Equivalents: H8040 שְׂמֹאול",
    711: "Ἀριστόβουλος (Aristóboulos | ar-is-tob'-oo-los)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G712 and G1012\nStrong's: best counselling; Aristoboulus, a Christian\nKJV: —Aristobulus.\n\nSee: G712 \nSee: G1012 \n\nCognate Group: G705 (number)\nVariants: Ἀριστόβουλος",
    712: "ἄριστον (áriston | ar'-is-ton)\n\nDerivation: apparently neuter of a superlative from the same as G730\nStrong's: the best meal (or breakfast; perhaps from ἦρι (\"early\")), i.e. luncheon\nKJV: —dinner.\n\nSee: G730 \n\nCognate Group: G705 (number)\nVariants: ἄριστον \nHebrew Equivalents: H3899 לֶחֶם",
    713: "ἀρκετός (arketós | ar-ket-os')\n\nDerivation: from G714\nStrong's: satisfactory\nKJV: —enough, suffice (-ient).\n\nSee: G714 \n\nCognate Group: G841 (contentment), G713 (enough), G842 (content), G714 (be content)\nVariants: ἀρκετός",
    714: "ἀρκέω (arkéō | ar-keh'-o)\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary verb (but probably akin to G142 through the idea of raising a barrier)\nStrong's: properly, to ward off, i.e. (by implication) to avail (figuratively, be satisfactory)\nKJV: —be content, be enough, suffice, be sufficient.\n\nSee: G142 \n\nCognate Group: G841 (contentment), G713 (enough), G842 (content), G714 (be content)\nVariants: ἀρκέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1952 הֹון, H3557 כּוּל, H4672 מָצָא, H7451 רַע",
    715: "ἄρκτος (árktos | ark'-tos)\n\nDerivation: probably from G714\nStrong's: a bear (as obstructing by ferocity)\nKJV: —bear.\n\nSee: G714 \n\nCognate Group: G841 (contentment), G713 (enough), G842 (content), G714 (be content)\nVariants: ἄρκτος, ἄρκος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1677 דֹּב",
    716: "ἅρμα (hárma | har'-mah)\n\nDerivation: probably from G142 (perhaps with G1 (as a particle of union) prefixed)\nStrong's: a chariot (as raised or fitted together (compare G719))\nKJV: —chariot.\n\nSee: G142 \nSee: G1 \nSee: G719 \n\nCognate Group: G841 (contentment), G713 (enough), G842 (content), G714 (be content)\nVariants: ἅρμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H7392 רָכַב, H7409 רֶכֶשׁ",
    717: "Ἀρμαγεδδών (Armageddṓn | ar-mag-ed-dohn')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H2022 and H4023)\nStrong's: Armageddon (or Har-Meggiddon), a symbolic name\nKJV: —Armageddon.\nSee: H2022\nSee: H4023\n\nCognate Group: G717 (Armageddon)\nVariants: Ἀρμαγεδδών, Ἁρμαγεδών, Μαγεδών, Ἁρμαγεδ(δ)ών \nHebrew Equivalents: H2022 הַר, H4023 מְגִדֹּון",
    718: "ἁρμόζω (harmózō | har-mod'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G719\nStrong's: to joint, i.e. (figuratively) to woo (reflexively, to betroth)\nKJV: —espouse.\n\nSee: G719 \n\nCognate Group: G717 (Armageddon)\nVariants: ἁρμόζω, ἁρμόζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H527 אָמֹון, H655 אֹפֶן, H5116 נָוֶה, H5797 עֹז, H7919 שָׂכַל",
    719: "ἁρμός (harmós | har-mos')\n\nDerivation: from the same as G716\nStrong's: an articulation (of the body)\nKJV: —joint.\n\nSee: G716 \n\nCognate Group: G717 (Armageddon)\nVariants: ἁρμός",
    720: "ἀρνέομαι (arnéomai | ar-neh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: perhaps from G1 (as a negative particle) and the middle voice of G4483\nStrong's: to contradict, i.e. disavow, reject, abnegate\nKJV: —deny, refuse.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4483 \n\nCognate Group: G720 (deny)\nVariants: ἀρνέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H3584 כָּחַשׁ",
    721: "ἀρνίον (arníon | ar-nee'-on)\n\nDerivation: diminutive from G704\nStrong's: a lambkin\nKJV: —lamb.\n\nSee: G704 \n\nCognate Group: G704 (lamb), G286 (lamb), G721 (lamb)\nVariants: ἀρνίον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1121 בֵּן, H3532 כֶּבֶשׂ, H6810 צָעִיר",
    722: "ἀροτριόω (arotrióō | ar-ot-ree-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G723\nStrong's: to plow\nKJV: —plough.\n\nSee: G723 \n\nCognate Group: G704 (lamb), G286 (lamb), G721 (lamb)\nVariants: ἀροτριόω, ἀροτριάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2790 חָרַשׁ, H5737 עֲדַר",
    723: "ἄροτρον (árotron | ar'-ot-ron)\n\nDerivation: from ἀρόω (to till)\nStrong's: a plow\nKJV: —plough.\n\nCognate Group: G704 (lamb), G286 (lamb), G721 (lamb)\nVariants: ἄροτρον \nHebrew Equivalents: H4173 מֹורַג, H6256 עֵת",
    724: "ἁρπαγή (harpagḗ | har-pag-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G726\nStrong's: pillage (properly abstract)\nKJV: —extortion, ravening, spoiling.\n\nSee: G726 \n\nCognate Group: G704 (lamb), G286 (lamb), G721 (lamb)\nVariants: ἁρπαγή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1498 גָּזֵל, H2966 טְרֵפָה, H7998 שָׁלָל",
    725: "ἁρπαγμός (harpagmós | har-pag-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G726\nStrong's: plunder (properly concrete)\nKJV: —robbery.\n\nSee: G726 \n\nCognate Group: G726 (catch), G725 (robbery)\nVariants: ἁρπαγμός",
    726: "ἁρπάζω (harpázō | har-pad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G138\nStrong's: to seize (in various applications)\nKJV: —catch (away, up), pluck, pull, take (by force).\n\nSee: G138 \n\nCognate Group: G726 (catch), G725 (robbery)\nVariants: ἁρπάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1497 גָּזַל, H2862 חָתַף, H2963 טָרַף, H3920 לָכַד",
    727: "ἅρπαξ (hárpax | har'-pax)\n\nDerivation: from G726\nStrong's: rapacious\nKJV: —extortion, ravening.\n\nSee: G726 \n\nCognate Group: G726 (catch), G725 (robbery)\nVariants: ἅρπαξ \nHebrew Equivalents: H2963 טָרַף",
    728: "ἀῤῥαβών (arrhabṓn | ar-hrab-ohn')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H6162)\nStrong's: a pledge, i.e. part of the purchase-money or property given in advance as security for the rest\nKJV: —earnest.\nSee: H6162\n\nCognate Group: G728 (earnest)\nVariants: ἀῤῥαβών, ἀρραβών \nHebrew Equivalents: H6162 עֲרָבֹון",
    729: "ἄῤῥαφος (árrhaphos | ar'-hhraf-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of the same as G4476\nStrong's: unsewed, i.e. of a single piece\nKJV: —without seam.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4476 \n\nCognate Group: G728 (earnest)\nVariants: ἄῤῥαφος, ἄραφος",
    730: "ἄῤῥην (árrhēn | ar'-hrane) or ἄρσην (ársēn | ar'-sane)\n\nDerivation: probably from G142\nStrong's: male (as stronger for lifting)\nKJV: —male, man.\n\nSee: G142 \n\nCognate Group: G728 (earnest)\nVariants: ἄῤῥην, ἄρρην, ἄρσην \nHebrew Equivalents: H376 אִישׁ, H1121 בֵּן, H1397 גֶּבֶר, H2145 זָכָר, H3206 יֶלֶד",
    731: "ἄῤῥητος (árrhētos | ar'-hray-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and the same as G4490\nStrong's: unsaid, i.e. (by implication) inexpressible\nKJV: —unspeakable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4490 \n\nCognate Group: G728 (earnest)\nVariants: ἄῤῥητος, ἄρρητος",
    732: "ἄῤῥωστος (árrhōstos | ar'-hroce-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G4517\nStrong's: infirm\nKJV: —sick (folk, -ly).\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4517 \n\nCognate Group: G728 (earnest)\nVariants: ἄῤῥωστος, ἀρρωστέω, ἄρρωστος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2470 חָלָה",
    733: "ἀρσενοκοίτης (arsenokoítēs | ar-sen-ok-oy'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G730 and G2845\nStrong's: a sodomite\nKJV: —abuser of (that defile) self with mankind.\n\nSee: G730 \nSee: G2845 \n\nCognate Group: G728 (earnest)\nVariants: ἀρσενοκοίτης",
    734: "Ἀρτεμάς (Artemás | ar-tem-as')\n\nDerivation: contracted from a compound of G735 and G1435\nStrong's: gift of Artemis; Artemas (or Artemidorus), a Christian\nKJV: —Artemas.\n\nSee: G735 \nSee: G1435 \n\nCognate Group: G728 (earnest)\nVariants: Ἀρτεμάς, Ἀρτεμᾶς",
    735: "Ἄρτεμις (Ártemis | ar'-tem-is)\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as G736\nStrong's: prompt; Artemis, the name of a Grecian goddess borrowed by the Asiatics for one of their deities\nKJV: —Diana.\n\nSee: G736 \n\nCognate Group: G728 (earnest)\nVariants: Ἄρτεμις",
    736: "ἀρτέμων (artémōn | ar-tem'-ohn)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G737\nStrong's: properly, something ready (or else more remotely from G142 (compare G740); something hung up), i.e. (specially) the topsail (rather foresail or jib) of a vessel\nKJV: —mainsail.\n\nSee: G737 \nSee: G142 \nSee: G740 \n\nCognate Group: G728 (earnest)\nVariants: ἀρτέμων",
    737: "ἄρτι (árti | ar'-tee)\n\nDerivation: adverb from a derivative of G142 (compare G740) through the idea of suspension\nStrong's: just now\nKJV: —this day (hour), hence(-forth), here(-after), hither(-to), (even) now, (this) present.\n\nSee: G142 \nSee: G740 \n\nCognate Group: G728 (earnest)\nVariants: ἄρτι \nHebrew Equivalents: H6258 עַתָּה",
    738: "ἀρτιγέννητος (artigénnētos | ar-teeg-en'-nay-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G737 and G1084\nStrong's: just born, i.e. (figuratively) a young convert\nKJV: —new born.\n\nSee: G737 \nSee: G1084 \n\nCognate Group: G1084 (they that are born), G1080 (bear), G313 (beget), G738 (new born), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: ἀρτιγέννητος",
    739: "ἄρτιος (ártios | ar'-tee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G737\nStrong's: fresh, i.e. (by implication) complete\nKJV: —perfect.\n\nSee: G737 \n\nCognate Group: G739 (perfect), G2676 (perfection), G2677 (perfecting), G1822 (accomplish), G2675 (fit)\nVariants: ἄρτιος",
    740: "ἄρτος (ártos | ar'-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G142\nStrong's: bread (as raised) or a loaf\nKJV: —(shew-)bread, loaf.\n\nSee: G142 \n\nCognate Group: G740 (bread)\nVariants: ἄρτος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1715 דָּגָן, H2471 חַלָּה, H3899 לֶחֶם, H4682 מַצָּה, H6595 פַּת",
    741: "ἀρτύω (artýō | ar-too'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a presumed derivative of G142\nStrong's: to prepare, i.e. spice (with stimulating condiments)\nKJV: —season.\n\nSee: G142 \n\nCognate Group: G740 (bread)\nVariants: ἀρτύω",
    742: "Ἀρφαξάδ (Arphaxád | ar-fax-ad')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H775)\nStrong's: Arphaxad, a post-diluvian patriarch\nKJV: —Arphaxad.\nSee: H775\n\nCognate Group: G740 (bread)\nVariants: Ἀρφαξάδ \nHebrew Equivalents: H775 אַרְפַּכְשַׁד",
    743: "ἀρχάγγελος (archángelos | ar-khang'-el-os)\n\nDerivation: from G757 and G32\nStrong's: a chief angel\nKJV: —archangel.\n\nSee: G757 \nSee: G32 \n\nCognate Group: G743 (archangel), G2465 (equal unto the angels), G32 (angel)\nVariants: ἀρχάγγελος",
    744: "ἀρχαῖος (archaîos | ar-khah'-yos)\n\nDerivation: from G746\nStrong's: original or primeval\nKJV: —(them of) old (time).\n\nSee: G746 \n\nCognate Group: G758 (chief), G747 (author), G744 (old), G757 (reign over), G536 (first-fruits), G746 (beginning)\nVariants: ἀρχαῖος \nHebrew Equivalents: H517 אֵם, H868 אֶתְנַן, H3462 יָשֵׁן, H6924 קֶדֶם, H7218 רֹאשׁ, H7223 רִאשֹׁון, H7350 רָחֹוק",
    745: "Ἀρχέλαος (Archélaos | ar-khel'-ah-os)\n\nDerivation: from G757 and G2994\nStrong's: people-ruling; Archelaus, a Jewish king\nKJV: —Archelaus.\n\nSee: G757 \nSee: G2994 \n\nCognate Group: G758 (chief), G747 (author), G744 (old), G757 (reign over), G536 (first-fruits), G746 (beginning)\nVariants: Ἀρχέλαος",
    746: "ἀρχή (archḗ | ar-khay')\n\nDerivation: from G756\nStrong's: (properly abstract) a commencement, or (concretely) chief (in various applications of order, time, place, or rank)\nKJV: —beginning, corner, (at the, the) first (estate), magistrate, power, principality, principle, rule.\n\nSee: G756 \n\nCognate Group: G758 (chief), G747 (author), G744 (old), G757 (reign over), G536 (first-fruits), G746 (beginning)\nVariants: ἀρχή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1061 בִּכּוּר, H2426 חֵיל, H3117 יֹום, H3423 יָרַשׁ, H3474 יָשַׁר, H3653 כֵּן, H3712 כִּפָּה, H3871 לוּחַ, H4467 מַמְלָכָה, H4475 מֶמְשָׁלָה, H4941 מִשְׁפָּט, H4945 מַשְׁקֶה, H4951 מִשְׂרָה, H5769 עֹולָם, H5794 עַז, H6440 פָּנִים, H6788 צַמֶּרֶת, H6924 קֶדֶם, H7093 קֵץ, H7218 רֹאשׁ, H7350 רָחֹוק, H7985 שׇׁלְטָן, H8462 תְּחִלָּה, H8641 תְּרוּמָה",
    747: "ἀρχηγός (archēgós | ar-khay-gos')\n\nDerivation: from G746 and G71\nStrong's: a chief leader\nKJV: —author, captain, prince.\n\nSee: G746 \nSee: G71 \n\nCognate Group: G758 (chief), G747 (author), G744 (old), G757 (reign over), G536 (first-fruits), G746 (beginning)\nVariants: ἀρχηγός \nHebrew Equivalents: H441 אַלּוּף, H2280 חָבַשׁ, H5387 נָשִׂיא, H6285 פֵּאָה, H6485 פָּקַד, H6545 פֶּרַע, H7101 קָצִין, H7218 רֹאשׁ, H8269 שַׂר",
    748: "ἀρχιερατικός (archieratikós | ar-khee-er-at-ee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G746 and a derivative of G2413\nStrong's: high-priestly\nKJV: —of the high-priest.\n\nSee: G746 \nSee: G2413 \n\nCognate Group: G758 (chief), G747 (author), G744 (old), G757 (reign over), G536 (first-fruits), G746 (beginning)\nVariants: ἀρχιερατικός",
    749: "ἀρχιερεύς (archiereús | ar-khee-er-yuce')\n\nDerivation: from G746 and G2409\nStrong's: the high-priest (literally, of the Jews, typically, Christ); by extension a chief priest\nKJV: —chief (high) priest, chief of the priests.\n\nSee: G746 \nSee: G2409 \n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: ἀρχιερεύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H3547 כָּהַן",
    750: "ἀρχιποίμην (archipoímēn | ar-khee-poy'-mane)\n\nDerivation: from G746 and G4166\nStrong's: a head shepherd\nKJV: —chief shepherd.\n\nSee: G746 \nSee: G4166 \n\nCognate Group: G4167 (flock), G4165 (feed), G750 (chief shepherd), G4168 (flock), G4166 (shepherd)\nVariants: ἀρχιποίμην",
    751: "Ἄρχιππος (Árchippos | ar'-khip-pos)\n\nDerivation: from G746 and G2462\nStrong's: horse-ruler; Archippus, a Christian\nKJV: —Archippus.\n\nSee: G746 \nSee: G2462 \n\nCognate Group: G4167 (flock), G4165 (feed), G750 (chief shepherd), G4168 (flock), G4166 (shepherd)\nVariants: Ἄρχιππος",
    752: "ἀρχισυνάγωγος (archisynágōgos | ar-khee-soon-ag'-o-gos)\n\nDerivation: from G746 and G4864\nStrong's: director of the synagogue services\nKJV: —(chief) ruler of the synagogue.\n\nSee: G746 \nSee: G4864 \n\nCognate Group: G4167 (flock), G4165 (feed), G750 (chief shepherd), G4168 (flock), G4166 (shepherd)\nVariants: ἀρχισυνάγωγος",
    753: "ἀρχιτέκτων (architéktōn | ar-khee-tek'-tone)\n\nDerivation: from G746 and G5045\nStrong's: a chief constructor, i.e. \"architect\"\nKJV: —masterbuilder.\n\nSee: G746 \nSee: G5045 \n\nCognate Group: G4167 (flock), G4165 (feed), G750 (chief shepherd), G4168 (flock), G4166 (shepherd)\nVariants: ἀρχιτέκτων \nHebrew Equivalents: H2796 חָרָשׁ",
    754: "ἀρχιτελώνης (architelṓnēs | ar-khee-tel-o'-nace)\n\nDerivation: from G746 and G5057\nStrong's: a principle tax-gatherer\nKJV: —chief among the publicans.\n\nSee: G746 \nSee: G5057 \n\nCognate Group: G4167 (flock), G4165 (feed), G750 (chief shepherd), G4168 (flock), G4166 (shepherd)\nVariants: ἀρχιτελώνης",
    755: "ἀρχιτρίκλινος (architríklinos | ar-khee-tree'-klee-nos)\n\nDerivation: from G746 and a compound of G5140 and G2827 (a dinner-bed, because composed of three couches)\nStrong's: director of the entertainment\nKJV: —governor (ruler) of the feast.\n\nSee: G746 \nSee: G5140 \nSee: G2827 \n\nCognate Group: G4167 (flock), G4165 (feed), G750 (chief shepherd), G4168 (flock), G4166 (shepherd)\nVariants: ἀρχιτρίκλινος",
    756: "ἄρχομαι (árchomai | ar'-khom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice of G757 (through the implication, of precedence)\nStrong's: to commence (in order of time)\nKJV: —(rehearse from the) begin(-ning).\n\nSee: G757 \n\nCognate Group: G4167 (flock), G4165 (feed), G750 (chief shepherd), G4168 (flock), G4166 (shepherd)\nVariants: ἄρχομαι, ἄρχω",
    757: "ἄρχω (árchō | ar'-kho)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to be first (in political rank or power)\nKJV: —reign (rule) over.\n\nCognate Group: G758 (chief), G747 (author), G744 (old), G757 (reign over), G536 (first-fruits), G746 (beginning)\nVariants: ἄρχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1254 בָּרָא, H1404 גְּבֶרֶת, H2490 חָלַל, H2974 יָאַל, H3245 יָסַד, H4911 מָשַׁל, H5081 נָדִיב, H5128 נוּעַ, H5251 נֵס, H5257 נְסִיךְ, H5493 סוּר, H6030 עָנָה, H6113 עָצָר, H6260 עַתּוּד, H6544 פָּרַע, H7218 רֹאשׁ, H7287 רָדָה, H7891 שִׁיר, H7981 שְׁלֵט, H8199 שָׁפַט, H8271 שְׁרֵא",
    758: "ἄρχων (árchōn | ar'-khone)\n\nDerivation: present participle of G757\nStrong's: a first (in rank or power)\nKJV: —chief (ruler), magistrate, prince, ruler.\n\nSee: G757 \n\nCognate Group: G758 (chief), G747 (author), G744 (old), G757 (reign over), G536 (first-fruits), G746 (beginning)\nVariants: ἄρχων \nHebrew Equivalents: H113 אָדֹון, H410 אֵל, H582 אֱנֹושׁ, H1167 בַּעַל, H2356 חֹור, H2710 חָקַק, H3256 יָסַר, H3489 יָתֵד, H3816 לְאֹם, H3887 לוּץ, H4428 מֶלֶךְ, H4911 מָשַׁל, H5057 נָגִיד, H5081 נָדִיב, H5257 נְסִיךְ, H5387 נָשִׂיא, H5461 סָגָן, H5633 סֶרֶן, H5650 עֶבֶד, H6260 עַתּוּד, H6346 פֶּחָה, H6486 פְּקֻדָּה, H6545 פֶּרַע, H6744 צְלַח, H6936 קׇדְקֹד, H7101 קָצִין, H7218 רֹאשׁ, H7227 רַב, H7287 רָדָה, H7336 רָזַן, H7626 שֵׁבֶט, H7891 שִׁיר, H7984 שִׁלְטֹון, H8269 שַׂר",
    759: "ἄρωμα (árōma | ar'-o-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G142 (in the sense of sending off scent)\nStrong's: an aromatic\nKJV: —(sweet) spice.\n\nSee: G142 \n\nCognate Group: G758 (chief), G747 (author), G744 (old), G757 (reign over), G536 (first-fruits), G746 (beginning)\nVariants: ἄρωμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1314 בֶּשֶׂם",
    760: "Ἀσά (Asá | as-ah')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H609)\nStrong's: Asa, an Israelite\nKJV: —Asa.\nSee: H609\n\nCognate Group: G758 (chief), G747 (author), G744 (old), G757 (reign over), G536 (first-fruits), G746 (beginning)\nVariants: Ἀσά, Ἀσάφ \nHebrew Equivalents: H609 אָסָא, H622 אָסַף",
    761: "ἀσάλευτος (asáleutos | as-al'-yoo-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G4531\nStrong's: unshaken, i.e. (by implication) immovable (figuratively)\nKJV: —which cannot be moved, unmovable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4531 \n\nCognate Group: G758 (chief), G747 (author), G744 (old), G757 (reign over), G536 (first-fruits), G746 (beginning)\nVariants: ἀσάλευτος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2903 טֹופָפָה",
    762: "ἄσβεστος (ásbestos | as'-bes-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G4570\nStrong's: not extinguished, i.e. (by implication) perpetual\nKJV: —not to be quenched, unquenchable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4570 \n\nCognate Group: G758 (chief), G747 (author), G744 (old), G757 (reign over), G536 (first-fruits), G746 (beginning)\nVariants: ἄσβεστος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3808 לֹא",
    763: "ἀσέβεια (asébeia | as-eb'-i-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G765\nStrong's: impiety, i.e. (by implication) wickedness\nKJV: —ungodly(-liness).\n\nSee: G765 \n\nCognate Group: G4573 (worship), G763 (ungodly), G2152 (devout), G4574 (devotion), G4576 (devout), G2150 (godliness), G764 (commit ungodly), G765 (ungodly), G2153 (godly), G4575 (Augustus), G2151 (show piety)\nVariants: ἀσέβεια \nHebrew Equivalents: H1942 הַוָּה, H2087 זָדֹון, H2154 זִמָּה, H2403 חַטָּאָה, H2555 חָמָס, H4156 מֹועֵצָה, H4820 מִרְמָה, H5627 סָרָה, H5771 עָוֺן, H5949 עֲלִילָה, H6588 פֶּשַׁע, H7200 רָאָה, H7562 רֶשַׁע, H8441 תֹּועֵבַה",
    764: "ἀσεβέω (asebéō | as-eb-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G765\nStrong's: to be (by implied act) impious or wicked\nKJV: —commit (live, that after should live) ungodly.\n\nSee: G765 \n\nCognate Group: G4573 (worship), G763 (ungodly), G2152 (devout), G4574 (devotion), G4576 (devout), G2150 (godliness), G764 (commit ungodly), G765 (ungodly), G2153 (godly), G4575 (Augustus), G2151 (show piety)\nVariants: ἀσεβέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2102 זוּד, H2154 זִמָּה, H2554 חָמַס, H4784 מָרָה, H5753 עָוָה, H6231 עָשַׁק, H6586 פָּשַׁע, H7561 רָשַׁע, H8398 תֵּבֵל",
    765: "ἀσεβής (asebḗs | as-eb-ace')\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G4576\nStrong's: irreverent, i.e. (by extension) impious or wicked\nKJV: — ungodly (man).\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4576 \n\nCognate Group: G4573 (worship), G763 (ungodly), G2152 (devout), G4574 (devotion), G4576 (devout), G2150 (godliness), G764 (commit ungodly), G765 (ungodly), G2153 (godly), G4575 (Augustus), G2151 (show piety)\nVariants: ἀσεβής \nHebrew Equivalents: H191 אֱוִיל, H205 אָוֶן, H1121 בֵּן, H1800 דַּל, H2114 זוּר, H2398 חָטָא, H2400 חַטָּא, H2555 חָמָס, H2611 חָנֵף, H3685 כְּסִיל, H4775 מָרַד, H5947 עַלִּיז, H6586 פָּשַׁע, H7489 רָעַע, H7561 רָשַׁע, H7843 שָׁחַת",
    766: "ἀσέλγεια (asélgeia | as-elg'-i-a)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed σελγής (of uncertain derivation, but apparently meaning continent)\nStrong's: licentiousness (sometimes including other vices)\nKJV: —filthy, lasciviousness, wantonness.\n\nSee: G1 \n\nCognate Group: G4573 (worship), G763 (ungodly), G2152 (devout), G4574 (devotion), G4576 (devout), G2150 (godliness), G764 (commit ungodly), G765 (ungodly), G2153 (godly), G4575 (Augustus), G2151 (show piety)\nVariants: ἀσέλγεια",
    767: "ἄσημος (ásēmos | as'-ay-mos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and the base of G4591\nStrong's: unmarked, i.e. (figuratively) ignoble\nKJV: —mean.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4591 \n\nCognate Group: G4593 (note), G4953 (token), G2154 (easy to be understood), G4591 (signify), G4592 (miracle), G1978 (notable), G767 (mean)\nVariants: ἄσημος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5848 עָטַף",
    768: "Ἀσήρ (Asḗr | as-ayr')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H836)\nStrong's: Aser (i.e. Asher), an Israelite tribe\nKJV: —Aser.\nSee: H836\n\nCognate Group: G4593 (note), G4953 (token), G2154 (easy to be understood), G4591 (signify), G4592 (miracle), G1978 (notable), G767 (mean)\nVariants: Ἀσήρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H836 אָשֵׁר",
    769: "ἀσθένεια (asthéneia | as-then'-i-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G772\nStrong's: feebleness (of mind or body); by implication, malady; morally, frailty\nKJV: —disease, infirmity, sickness, weakness.\n\nSee: G772 \n\nCognate Group: G772 (more feeble), G771 (infirmity), G770 (be diseased), G769 (disease)\nVariants: ἀσθένεια \nHebrew Equivalents: H3782 כָּשַׁל, H6094 עַצֶּבֶת, H8213 שָׁפֵל",
    770: "ἀσθενέω (asthenéō | as-then-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G772\nStrong's: to be feeble (in any sense)\nKJV: —be diseased, impotent folk (man), (be) sick, (be, be made) weak.\n\nSee: G772 \n\nCognate Group: G772 (more feeble), G771 (infirmity), G770 (be diseased), G769 (disease)\nVariants: ἀσθενέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1669 דָּאַב, H1809 דָּלַל, H2470 חָלָה, H2844 חַת, H3782 כָּשַׁל, H3811 לָאָה, H4116 מָהַר, H4135 מוּל, H4571 מָעַד, H5869 עַיִן, H5999 עָמָל, H6484 פָּצַר, H6850 צָפַף, H7401 רָכַךְ, H7503 רָפָה, H7921 שָׁכֹל",
    771: "ἀσθένημα (asthénēma | as-then'-ay-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G770\nStrong's: a scruple of conscience\nKJV: —infirmity.\n\nSee: G770 \n\nCognate Group: G772 (more feeble), G771 (infirmity), G770 (be diseased), G769 (disease)\nVariants: ἀσθένημα",
    772: "ἀσθενής (asthenḗs | as-then-ace')\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and the base of G4599\nStrong's: strengthless (in various applications, literal, figurative and moral)\nKJV: —more feeble, impotent, sick, without strength, weak(-er, -ness, thing).\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4599 \n\nCognate Group: G772 (more feeble), G771 (infirmity), G770 (be diseased), G769 (disease)\nVariants: ἀσθενής \nHebrew Equivalents: H34 אֶבְיֹון, H536 אֻמְלַל, H1800 דַּל, H2197 זַעַף, H2865 חָתַת, H4116 מָהַר, H6041 עָנִי, H7330 רָזֶה, H7390 רַךְ, H7504 רָפֶה, H8217 שָׁפָל",
    773: "Ἀσία (Asía | as-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Asia, i.e. Asia Minor, or (usually) only its western shore\nKJV: —Asia.\n\nCognate Group: G772 (more feeble), G771 (infirmity), G770 (be diseased), G769 (disease)\nVariants: Ἀσία",
    774: "Ἀσιανός (Asianós | as-ee-an-os')\n\nDerivation: from G773\nStrong's: an Asian (i.e. Asiatic) or an inhabitant of Asia\nKJV: —of Asia.\n\nSee: G773 \n\nCognate Group: G772 (more feeble), G771 (infirmity), G770 (be diseased), G769 (disease)\nVariants: Ἀσιανός",
    775: "Ἀσιάρχης (Asiárchēs | as-ee-ar'-khace)\n\nDerivation: from G773 and G746\nStrong's: an Asiarch or president of the public festivities in a city of Asia Minor\nKJV: —chief of Asia.\n\nSee: G773 \nSee: G746 \n\nCognate Group: G772 (more feeble), G771 (infirmity), G770 (be diseased), G769 (disease)\nVariants: Ἀσιάρχης",
    776: "ἀσιτία (asitía | as-ee-tee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G777\nStrong's: fasting (the state)\nKJV: —abstinence.\n\nSee: G777 \n\nCognate Group: G772 (more feeble), G771 (infirmity), G770 (be diseased), G769 (disease)\nVariants: ἀσιτία",
    777: "ἄσιτος (ásitos | as'-ee-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G4621\nStrong's: without (taking) food\nKJV: —fasting.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4621 \n\nCognate Group: G772 (more feeble), G771 (infirmity), G770 (be diseased), G769 (disease)\nVariants: ἄσιτος",
    778: "ἀσκέω (askéō | as-keh'-o)\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as G4632\nStrong's: to elaborate, i.e. (figuratively) train (by implication, strive)\nKJV: —exercise.\n\nSee: G4632 \n\nCognate Group: G778 (exercise)\nVariants: ἀσκέω",
    779: "ἀσκός (askós | as-kos')\n\nDerivation: from the same as G778\nStrong's: a leathern (or skin) bag used as a bottle\nKJV: —bottle.\n\nSee: G778 \n\nCognate Group: G778 (exercise)\nVariants: ἀσκός \nHebrew Equivalents: H2573 חֵמֶת, H4997 נֹאד, H5035 נֶבֶל",
    780: "ἀσμένως (asménōs | as-men'-oce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from a derivative of the base of G2237\nStrong's: with pleasure\nKJV: —gladly.\n\nSee: G2237 \n\nCognate Group: G778 (exercise)\nVariants: ἀσμένως",
    781: "ἄσοφος (ásophos | as'-of-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G4680\nStrong's: unwise\nKJV: —fool.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4680 \n\nCognate Group: G778 (exercise)\nVariants: ἄσοφος",
    782: "ἀσπάζομαι (aspázomai | as-pad'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a particle of union) and a presumed form of G4685\nStrong's: to enfold in the arms, i.e. (by implication) to salute, (figuratively) to welcome\nKJV: —embrace, greet, salute, take leave.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4685 \n\nCognate Group: G782 (embrace), G783 (greeting)\nVariants: ἀσπάζομαι, ἀπασπάζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H7592 שָׁאַל",
    783: "ἀσπασμός (aspasmós | as-pas-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G782\nStrong's: a greeting (in person or by letter)\nKJV: —greeting, salutation.\n\nSee: G782 \n\nCognate Group: G782 (embrace), G783 (greeting)\nVariants: ἀσπασμός",
    784: "ἄσπιλος (áspilos | as'-pee-los)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G4695\nStrong's: unblemished (physically or morally)\nKJV: —without spot, unspotted.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4695 \n\nCognate Group: G784 (without spot)\nVariants: ἄσπιλος, ὑπερασπίζω",
    785: "ἀσπίς (aspís | as-pece')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a buckler (or round shield); used of a serpent (as coiling itself), probably the \"asp\"\nKJV: —asp.\n\nCognate Group: G784 (without spot)\nVariants: ἀσπίς \nHebrew Equivalents: H660 אֶפְעֶה, H6620 פֶּתֶן, H6848 צֶפַע, H8314 שָׂרָף",
    786: "ἄσπονδος (áspondos | as'-pon-dos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G4689\nStrong's: literally, without libation (which usually accompanied a treaty), i.e. (by implication) truceless\nKJV: —implacable, truce-breaker.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4689 \n\nCognate Group: G784 (without spot)\nVariants: ἄσπονδος",
    787: "ἀσσάριον (assárion | as-sar'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: an assarius or as, a Roman coin\nKJV: —farthing.\n\nCognate Group: G784 (without spot)\nVariants: ἀσσάριον",
    788: "ἆσσον (âsson | as'-son)\n\nDerivation: neuter comparative of the base of G1451\nStrong's: more nearly, i.e. very near\nKJV: —close.\n\nSee: G1451 \n\nCognate Group: G784 (without spot)\nVariants: ἆσσον, ὰσσον",
    789: "Ἄσσος (Ássos | as'-sos)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: Assus, a city of Asia MInor\nKJV: —Assos.\n\nCognate Group: G784 (without spot)\nVariants: Ἄσσος, Ἆσσος",
    790: "ἀστατέω (astatéō | as-tat-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G2476\nStrong's: to be non-stationary, i.e. (figuratively) homeless\nKJV: —have no certain dwelling-place.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G2476 \n\nCognate Group: G790 (have no certain dwelling-place)\nVariants: ἀστατέω",
    791: "ἀστεῖος (asteîos | as-ti'-os)\n\nDerivation: from ἄστυ (a city)\nStrong's: urbane, i.e. (by implication) handsome\nKJV: —fair.\n\nCognate Group: G790 (have no certain dwelling-place)\nVariants: ἀστεῖος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1277 בָּרִיא, H2896 טֹוב, H3399 יָרַט",
    792: "ἀστήρ (astḗr | as-tare')\n\nDerivation: probably from the base of G4766\nStrong's: a star (as strown over the sky), literally or figuratively\nKJV: —star.\n\nSee: G4766 \n\nCognate Group: G792 (star), G798 (star)\nVariants: ἀστήρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3556 כֹּוכָב, H6635 צָבָא",
    793: "ἀστήρικτος (astḗriktos | as-tay'-rik-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G4741\nStrong's: unfixed, i.e. (figuratively) vacillating\nKJV: —unstable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4741 \n\nCognate Group: G4740 (stedfastness), G4741 (fix), G793 (unstable), G1991 (confirm)\nVariants: ἀστήρικτος",
    794: "ἄστοργος (ástorgos | as'-tor-gos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of στέργω (to cherish affectionately)\nStrong's: hard-hearted towards kindred\nKJV: —without natural affection.\n\nSee: G1 \n\nCognate Group: G4740 (stedfastness), G4741 (fix), G793 (unstable), G1991 (confirm)\nVariants: ἄστοργος",
    795: "ἀστοχέω (astochéō | as-tokh-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1 (as a negative particle) and στοίχος (an aim)\nStrong's: to miss the mark, i.e. (figuratively) deviate from truth\nKJV: —err, swerve.\n\nSee: G1 \n\nCognate Group: G4740 (stedfastness), G4741 (fix), G793 (unstable), G1991 (confirm)\nVariants: ἀστοχέω",
    796: "ἀστραπή (astrapḗ | as-trap-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G797\nStrong's: lightning; by analogy, glare\nKJV: —lightning, bright shining.\n\nSee: G797 \n\nCognate Group: G796 (lightning)\nVariants: ἀστραπή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1300 בָּרָק",
    797: "ἀστράπτω (astráptō | as-trap'-to)\n\nDerivation: probably from G792\nStrong's: to flash as lightning\nKJV: —lighten, shine.\n\nSee: G792 \n\nCognate Group: G796 (lightning)\nVariants: ἀστράπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1300 בָּרָק",
    798: "ἄστρον (ástron | as'-tron)\n\nDerivation: neuter from G792\nStrong's: properly, a constellation; put for a single star (natural or artificial)\nKJV: —star.\n\nSee: G792 \n\nCognate Group: G792 (star), G798 (star)\nVariants: ἄστρον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1300 בָּרָק, H3556 כֹּוכָב, H6635 צָבָא, H7834 שַׁחַק, H8064 שָׁמַיִם",
    799: "Ἀσύγκριτος (Asýnkritos | as-oong'-kree-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G4793\nStrong's: incomparable; Asyncritus, a Christian\nKJV: —Asyncritos.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4793 \n\nCognate Group: G792 (star), G798 (star)\nVariants: Ἀσύγκριτος",
    800: "ἀσύμφωνος (asýmphōnos | as-oom'-fo-nos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G4859\nStrong's: inharmonious (figuratively)\nKJV: —agree not.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4859 \n\nCognate Group: G792 (star), G798 (star)\nVariants: ἀσύμφωνος",
    801: "ἀσύνετος (asýnetos | as-oon'-ay-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G4908\nStrong's: unintelligent; by implication, wicked\nKJV: —foolish, without understanding.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4908 \n\nCognate Group: G801 (foolish), G4907 (knowledge), G4920 (consider), G4908 (prudent)\nVariants: ἀσύνετος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3685 כְּסִיל, H5036 נָבָל, H5307 נָפַל",
    802: "ἀσύνθετος (asýnthetos | as-oon'-thet-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G4934\nStrong's: properly, not agreed, i.e. treacherous to compacts\nKJV: — covenant-breaker.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4934 \n\nCognate Group: G801 (foolish), G4907 (knowledge), G4920 (consider), G4908 (prudent)\nVariants: ἀσύνθετος \nHebrew Equivalents: H898 בָּגַד",
    803: "ἀσφάλεια (aspháleia | as-fal'-i-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G804\nStrong's: security (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —certainty, safety.\n\nSee: G804 \n\nCognate Group: G805 (make fast), G806 (assuredly), G804 (certain), G803 (certainty)\nVariants: ἀσφάλεια \nHebrew Equivalents: H982 בָּטַח, H983 בֶּטַח, H4349 מָכֹון, H6738 צֵל, H8252 שָׁקַט, H8454 תּוּשִׁיָּה, H8551 תָּמַךְ",
    804: "ἀσφαλής (asphalḗs | as-fal-ace')\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and sphallo (to \"fail\")\nStrong's: secure (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —certain(-ty), safe, sure.\n\nSee: G1 \n\nCognate Group: G805 (make fast), G806 (assuredly), G804 (certain), G803 (certainty)\nVariants: ἀσφαλής \nHebrew Equivalents: H833 אָשַׁר, H3653 כֵּן, H5810 עָזַז",
    805: "ἀσφαλίζω (asphalízō | as-fal-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G804\nStrong's: to render secure\nKJV: —make fast (sure).\n\nSee: G804 \n\nCognate Group: G805 (make fast), G806 (assuredly), G804 (certain), G803 (certainty)\nVariants: ἀσφαλίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2388 חָזַק, H8551 תָּמַךְ",
    806: "ἀσφαλῶς (asphalōs | as-fal-oce')\n\nDerivation: adverb from G804\nStrong's: securely (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —assuredly, safely.\n\nSee: G804 \n\nCognate Group: G805 (make fast), G806 (assuredly), G804 (certain), G803 (certainty)\nVariants: ἀσφαλῶς \nHebrew Equivalents: H983 בֶּטַח",
    807: "ἀσχημονέω (aschēmonéō | as-kay-mon-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G809\nStrong's: to be (i.e. act) unbecoming\nKJV: —behave self uncomely (unseemly).\n\nSee: G809 \n\nCognate Group: G805 (make fast), G806 (assuredly), G804 (certain), G803 (certainty)\nVariants: ἀσχημονέω, εὐσχημονέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6181 עֶרְיָה, H7034 קָלָה",
    808: "ἀσχημοσύνη (aschēmosýnē | as-kay-mos-oo'-nay)\n\nDerivation: from G809\nStrong's: an indecency; by implication, the pudenda\nKJV: —shame, that which is unseemly.\n\nSee: G809 \n\nCognate Group: G805 (make fast), G806 (assuredly), G804 (certain), G803 (certainty)\nVariants: ἀσχημοσύνη \nHebrew Equivalents: H216 אֹור, H6172 עֶרְוָה, H6627 צָאָה",
    809: "ἀσχήμων (aschḗmōn | as-kay'-mone)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G2192 (in the sense of its congener G4976)\nStrong's: properly, shapeless, i.e. (figuratively) inelegant\nKJV: —uncomely.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G2192 \nSee: G4976 \n\nCognate Group: G805 (make fast), G806 (assuredly), G804 (certain), G803 (certainty)\nVariants: ἀσχήμων \nHebrew Equivalents: H5039 נְבָלָה, H6172 עֶרְוָה",
    810: "ἀσωτία (asōtía | as-o-tee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G4982\nStrong's: properly, unsavedness, i.e. (by implication) profligacy\nKJV: —excess, riot.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G4982 \n\nCognate Group: G811 (riotous), G810 (excess)\nVariants: ἀσωτία \nHebrew Equivalents: H2151 זָלַל",
    811: "ἀσώτως (asṓtōs | as-o'-toce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from the same as G810\nStrong's: dissolutely\nKJV: —riotous.\n\nSee: G810 \n\nCognate Group: G811 (riotous), G810 (excess)\nVariants: ἀσώτως",
    812: "ἀτακτέω (ataktéō | at-ak-teh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G813\nStrong's: to be (i.e. act) irregular\nKJV: —behave self disorderly.\n\nSee: G813 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀτακτέω",
    813: "ἄτακτος (átaktos | at'-ak-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G5021\nStrong's: unarranged, i.e. (by implication) insubordinate (religiously)\nKJV: —unruly.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5021 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἄτακτος",
    814: "ἀτάκτως (atáktōs | at-ak'-toce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G813, irregularly (morally)\nKJV: —disorderly.\n\nSee: G813 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀτάκτως",
    815: "ἄτεκνος (áteknos | at'-ek-nos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5043\nStrong's: childless\nKJV: —childless, without children.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5043 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἄτεκνος \nHebrew Equivalents: H6185 עֲרִירִי, H7921 שָׁכֹל",
    816: "ἀτενίζω (atenízō | at-en-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1 (as a particle of union) and τείνω (to stretch)\nStrong's: to gaze intently\nKJV: —behold earnestly (stedfastly), fasten (eyes), look (earnestly, stedfastly, up stedfastly), set eyes.\n\nSee: G1 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀτενίζω",
    817: "ἄτερ (áter | at'-er)\n\nDerivation: a particle probably akin to G427\nStrong's: aloof, i.e. apart from (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —in the absence of, without.\n\nSee: G427 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἄτερ",
    818: "ἀτιμάζω (atimázō | at-im-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G820\nStrong's: to render infamous, i.e. (by implication) contemn or maltreat\nKJV: —despise, dishonour, suffer shame, entreat shamefully.\n\nSee: G820 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀτιμάζω, ἀτιμάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H936 בּוּז, H1792 דָּכָא, H3637 כָּלַם, H5034 נָבֵל, H5753 עָוָה, H7034 קָלָה, H7703 שָׁדַד, H7751 שׁוּט, H8074 שָׁמֵם, H8213 שָׁפֵל",
    819: "ἀτιμία (atimía | at-ee-mee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G820\nStrong's: infamy, i.e. (subjectively) comparative indignity, (objectively) disgrace\nKJV: —dishonour, reproach, shame, vile.\n\nSee: G820 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀτιμία \nHebrew Equivalents: H937 בּוּז, H954 בּוּשׁ, H3637 כָּלַם, H3639 כְּלִמָּה, H5771 עָוֺן, H7034 קָלָה, H7036 קָלֹון, H7333 רָזֹון",
    820: "ἄτιμος (átimos | at'-ee-mos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5092\nStrong's: (negatively) unhonoured or (positively) dishonoured\nKJV: —despised, without honour, less honourable (comparative degree).\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5092 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἄτιμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H959 בָּזָה, H1097 בְּלִי, H7034 קָלָה",
    821: "ἀτιμόω (atimóō | at-ee-mo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G820\nStrong's: used like G818, to maltreat\nKJV: —handle shamefully.\n\nSee: G820 \nSee: G818 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀτιμόω G873 \nHebrew Equivalents: H959 בָּזָה, H2151 זָלַל, H3637 כָּלַם, H7043 קָלַל, H7728 שֹׁובֵב",
    822: "ἀτμίς (atmís | at-mece')\n\nDerivation: from the same as G109\nStrong's: mist\nKJV: —vapour.\n\nSee: G109 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἀτμίς \nHebrew Equivalents: H6049 עָנַן, H6227 עָשָׁן, H7008 קִיטֹור, H8561 תִּמֹּר",
    823: "ἄτομος (átomos | at'-om-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and the base of G5114\nStrong's: uncut, i.e. (by implication) indivisible (an \"atom\" of time)\nKJV: — moment.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5114 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἄτομος",
    824: "ἄτοπος (átopos | at'-op-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5117\nStrong's: out of place, i.e. (figuratively) improper, injurious, wicked\nKJV: —amiss, harm, unreasonable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5117 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἄτοπος \nHebrew Equivalents: H205 אָוֶן, H2778 חָרַף, H7561 רָשַׁע, H7723 שָׁוְא",
    825: "Ἀττάλεια (Attáleia | at-tal'-i-ah)\n\nDerivation: from Ἄτταλος (a king of Pergamus)\nStrong's: Attaleia, a place in Pamphylia\nKJV: —Attalia.\n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: Ἀττάλεια",
    826: "αὐγάζω (augázō | ow-gad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G827\nStrong's: to beam forth (figuratively)\nKJV: —shine.\n\nSee: G827 \n\nCognate Group: G541 (brightness), G826 (shine)\nVariants: αὐγάζω, καταυγάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H934 בֹּהֶרֶת, H3544 כֵּהֶה",
    827: "αὐγή (augḗ | owg'-ay)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a ray of light, i.e. (by implication) radiance, dawn\nKJV: —break of day.\n\nCognate Group: G541 (brightness), G826 (shine)\nVariants: αὐγή \nHebrew Equivalents: H5054 נְגֹהָה",
    828: "Αὐγοῦστος (Augoûstos | ow'-goos-tos)\n\nDerivation: from Latin (\"august\")\nStrong's: Augustus, a title of the Roman emperor\nKJV: —Augustus.\n\nCognate Group: G541 (brightness), G826 (shine)\nVariants: Αὐγοῦστος, Αὔγουστος, Αὐγούστος",
    829: "αὐθάδης (authádēs | ow-thad'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G846 and the base of G2237\nStrong's: self-pleasing, i.e. arrogant\nKJV: —self-willed.\n\nSee: G846 \nSee: G2237 \n\nCognate Group: G829 (self-willed)\nVariants: αὐθάδης \nHebrew Equivalents: H3093 יָהִיר, H5794 עַז",
    830: "αὐθαίρετος (authaíretos | ow-thah'-ee-ret-os)\n\nDerivation: from G846 and the same as G140\nStrong's: self-chosen, i.e. (by implication) voluntary\nKJV: —of own accord, willing of self.\n\nSee: G846 \nSee: G140 \n\nCognate Group: G829 (self-willed)\nVariants: αὐθαίρετος",
    831: "αὐθεντέω (authentéō | ow-then-teh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G846 and an obsolete ἕντης (a worker)\nStrong's: to act of oneself, i.e. (figuratively) dominate\nKJV: —usurp authority over.\n\nSee: G846 \n\nCognate Group: G829 (self-willed)\nVariants: αὐθεντέω",
    832: "αὐλέω (auléō | ow-leh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G836\nStrong's: to play the flute\nKJV: —pipe.\n\nSee: G836 \n\nCognate Group: G829 (self-willed)\nVariants: αὐλέω",
    833: "αὐλή (aulḗ | ow-lay')\n\nDerivation: from the same as G109\nStrong's: a yard (as open to the wind); by implication, a mansion\nKJV: —court, (sheep-)fold, hall, palace.\n\nSee: G109 \n\nCognate Group: G829 (self-willed)\nVariants: αὐλή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1927 הֲדָרָה, H2682 חָצִיר, H2691 חָצֵר, H3957 לִשְׁכָּה, H5592 סַף, H5835 עֲזָרָה, H6607 פֶּתַח, H8179 שַׁעַר, H8651 תְּרַע",
    834: "αὐλητής (aulētḗs | ow-lay-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G832\nStrong's: a flute-player\nKJV: —minstrel, piper.\n\nSee: G832 \n\nCognate Group: G829 (self-willed)\nVariants: αὐλητής",
    835: "αὐλίζομαι (aulízomai | ow-lid'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G833\nStrong's: to pass the night (properly, in the open air)\nKJV: —abide, lodge.\n\nSee: G833 \n\nCognate Group: G829 (self-willed)\nVariants: αὐλίζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H956 בּוּת, H1980 הָלַךְ, H3885 לוּן, H6647 צְבַע, H7931 שָׁכַן",
    836: "αὐλός (aulós | ow-los')\n\nDerivation: from the same as G109\nStrong's: a flute (as blown)\nKJV: —pipe.\n\nSee: G109 \n\nCognate Group: G829 (self-willed)\nVariants: αὐλός \nHebrew Equivalents: H2485 חָלִיל, H6767 צְלָצַל, H8596 תֹּף",
    837: "αὐξάνω (auxánō | owx-an'-o)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of a primary verb\nStrong's: to grow (\"wax\"), i.e. enlarge (literal or figurative, active or passive)\nKJV: —grow (up), (give the) increase.\n\nCognate Group: G837 (grow), G5232 (grow exceedingly)\nVariants: αὐξάνω, αὔξω, ξαίνω, αὐξάνω/αὔξω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1431 גָּדַל, H3318 יָצָא, H5375 נָשָׂא, H6509 פָּרָה, H6555 פָּרַץ, H6743 צָלַח, H7235 רָבָה",
    838: "αὔξησις (aúxēsis | owx'-ay-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G837\nStrong's: growth\nKJV: —increase.\n\nSee: G837 \n\nCognate Group: G837 (grow), G5232 (grow exceedingly)\nVariants: αὔξησις",
    839: "αὔριον (aúrion | ow'-ree-on)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of the same as G109 (meaning a breeze, i.e. the morning air)\nStrong's: properly, fresh, i.e. (adverb with ellipsis of G2250) to-morrow\nKJV: —(to-)morrow, next day.\n\nSee: G109 \nSee: G2250 \n\nCognate Group: G837 (grow), G5232 (grow exceedingly)\nVariants: αὔριον \nHebrew Equivalents: H4279 מָחָר",
    840: "αὐστηρός (austērós | ow-stay-ros')\n\nDerivation: from a (presumed) derivative of the same as G109 (meaning blown)\nStrong's: rough (properly as a gale), i.e. (figuratively) severe\nKJV: —austere.\n\nSee: G109 \n\nCognate Group: G837 (grow), G5232 (grow exceedingly)\nVariants: αὐστηρός",
    841: "αὐτάρκεια (autárkeia | ow-tar'-ki-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G842\nStrong's: self-satisfaction, i.e. (abstractly) contentedness, or (concretely) a competence\nKJV: —contentment, sufficiency.\n\nSee: G842 \n\nCognate Group: G841 (contentment), G713 (enough), G842 (content), G714 (be content)\nVariants: αὐτάρκεια",
    842: "αὐτάρκης (autárkēs | ow-tar'-kace)\n\nDerivation: from G846 and G714\nStrong's: self-complacent, i.e. contented\nKJV: —content.\n\nSee: G846 \nSee: G714 \n\nCognate Group: G841 (contentment), G713 (enough), G842 (content), G714 (be content)\nVariants: αὐτάρκης \nHebrew Equivalents: H2706 חֹק",
    843: "αὐτοκατάκριτος (autokatákritos | ow-tok-at-ak'-ree-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G846 and a derivative or G2632\nStrong's: self-condemned\nKJV: —condemned of self.\n\nSee: G846 \nSee: G2632 \n\nCognate Group: G612 (answer), G2631 (condemnation), G470 (answer again), G351 (examination), G2923 (judge), G610 (sentence), G2924 (discerner), G1469 (make of the number), G350 (ask), G1253 (discern), G843 (condemned of self), G2632 (condemn), G2919 (avenge), G2917 (avenge), G1252 (contend), G87 (without partiality), G611 (answer), G178 (uncondemned), G2633 (condemn), G2920 (accusation), G2922 (to judge)\nVariants: αὐτοκατάκριτος",
    844: "αὐτόματος (autómatos | ow-tom'-at-os)\n\nDerivation: from G846 and the same as G3155\nStrong's: self-moved (\"automatic\"), i.e. spontaneous\nKJV: —of own accord, of self.\n\nSee: G846 \nSee: G3155 \n\nCognate Group: G612 (answer), G2631 (condemnation), G470 (answer again), G351 (examination), G2923 (judge), G610 (sentence), G2924 (discerner), G1469 (make of the number), G350 (ask), G1253 (discern), G843 (condemned of self), G2632 (condemn), G2919 (avenge), G2917 (avenge), G1252 (contend), G87 (without partiality), G611 (answer), G178 (uncondemned), G2633 (condemn), G2920 (accusation), G2922 (to judge)\nVariants: αὐτόματος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5599 סָפִיחַ",
    845: "αὐτόπτης (autóptēs | ow-top'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G846 and G3700\nStrong's: self-seeing, i.e. an eye-witness\nKJV: —eye-witness.\n\nSee: G846 \nSee: G3700 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: αὐτόπτης",
    846: "αὐτός (autós | ow-tos')\n\nDerivation: from the particle αὖ (perhaps akin to the base of G109 through the idea of a baffling wind) (backward)\nStrong's: the reflexive pronoun self, used (alone or in the comparative G1438) of the third person, and (with the proper personal pronoun) of the other persons\nKJV: —her, it(-self), one, the other, (mine) own, said, (self-), the) same, ((him-, my-, thy-)self, (your-)selves, she, that, their(-s), them(-selves), there(-at, - by, -in, -into, -of, -on, -with), they, (these) things, this (man), those, together, very, which. Compare G848 .\n\nSee: G109 \nSee: G1438 \nSee: G848 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: αὐτός",
    847: "αὐτοῦ (autoû | ow-too')\n\nDerivation: genitive (i.e. possessive) of G846, used as an adverb of location\nStrong's: properly, belonging to the same spot, i.e. in this (or that) place\nKJV: —(t-)here.\n\nSee: G846 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: αὐτοῦ, αὐτόπτης \nHebrew Equivalents: H6311 פֹּה",
    848: "αὑτοῦ (hautoû | how-too')\n\nDerivation: contracted for G1438\nStrong's: self (in some oblique case or reflexively, relation)\nKJV: —her (own), (of) him(-self), his (own), of it, thee, their (own), them(-selves), they.\n\nSee: G1438 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: αὑτοῦ, αὐτόπτης G899, G900",
    849: "αὐτόχειρ (autócheir | ow-tokh'-ire)\n\nDerivation: from G846 and G5495\nStrong's: self-handed, i.e. doing personally\nKJV: —with … own hands.\n\nSee: G846 \nSee: G5495 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: αὐτόχειρ",
    850: "αὐχμηρός (auchmērós | owkh-may-ros')\n\nDerivation: from αὐχμός (probably from a base akin to that of G109) (dust, as dried by wind)\nStrong's: properly, dirty, i.e. (by implication) obscure\nKJV: —dark.\n\nSee: G109 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: αὐχμηρός",
    851: "ἀφαιρέω (aphairéō | af-ahee-reh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G138\nStrong's: to remove (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —cut (smite) off, take away.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G138 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: ἀφαιρέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H369 אַיִן, H519 אָמָה, H622 אָסַף, H680 אָצַל, H1219 בָּצַר, H1438 גָּדַע, H1497 גָּזַל, H1556 גָּלַל, H1639 גָּרַע, H1819 דָּמָה, H1920 הָדַף, H2498 חָלַף, H3381 יָרַד, H3722 כָּפַר, H3772 כָּרַת, H3947 לָקַח, H3988 מָאַס, H4229 מָחָה, H4513 מָנַע, H5130 נוּף, H5186 נָטָה, H5337 נָצַל, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5493 סוּר, H5545 סָלַח, H5595 סָפָה, H5674 עָבַר, H5710 עָדָה, H6544 פָּרַע, H6584 פָּשַׁט, H6605 פָּתַח, H7311 רוּם, H7368 רָחַק, H7673 שָׁבַת, H7971 שָׁלַח",
    852: "ἀφανής (aphanḗs | af-an-ace')\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5316\nStrong's: non-apparent\nKJV: —that is not manifest.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5316 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: ἀφανής",
    853: "ἀφανίζω (aphanízō | af-an-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G852\nStrong's: to render unapparent, i.e. (actively) consume (becloud), or (passively) disappear (be destroyed)\nKJV: — corrupt, disfigure, perish, vanish away.\n\nSee: G852 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: ἀφανίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H369 אַיִן, H816 אָשַׁם, H1197 בָּעַר, H1572 גָּמָא, H1644 גָּרַשׁ, H2000 הָמַם, H2026 הָרַג, H2254 חָבַל, H2763 חָרַם, H3456 יָשַׁם, H3582 כָּחַד, H3615 כָּלָה, H3772 כָּרַת, H5422 נָתַץ, H5487 סוּף, H5595 סָפָה, H5647 עָבַד, H5791 עָוַת, H6789 צָמַת, H7673 שָׁבַת, H7843 שָׁחַת, H8045 שָׁמַד, H8074 שָׁמֵם",
    854: "ἀφανισμός (aphanismós | af-an-is-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G853\nStrong's: disappearance, i.e. (figuratively) abrogation\nKJV: —vanish away.\n\nSee: G853 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: ἀφανισμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H1530 גַּל, H2254 חָבַל, H2763 חָרַם, H4875 מְשֹׁואָה, H7843 שָׁחַת, H8045 שָׁמַד, H8047 שַׁמָּה, H8077 שְׁמָמָה",
    855: "ἄφαντος (áphantos | af'-an-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G5316\nStrong's: non-manifested, i.e. invisible\nKJV: —vanished out of sight.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5316 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: ἄφαντος",
    856: "ἀφεδρών (aphedrṓn | af-ed-rone')\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G575 and the base of G1476\nStrong's: a place of sitting apart, i.e. a privy\nKJV: —draught.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G1476 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: ἀφεδρών, ὀχετός",
    857: "ἀφειδία (apheidía | af-i-dee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1 (as a negative particle) and G5339\nStrong's: unsparingness, i.e. austerity (asceticism)\nKJV: —neglecting.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5339 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: ἀφειδία",
    858: "ἀφελότης (aphelótēs | af-el-ot'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1 (as a negative particle) and φέλλος (in the sense of a stone as stubbing the foot)\nStrong's: smoothness, i.e. (figuratively) simplicity\nKJV: —singleness.\n\nSee: G1 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: ἀφελότης",
    859: "ἄφεσις (áphesis | af'-es-is)\n\nDerivation: from G863\nStrong's: freedom; (figuratively) pardon\nKJV: —deliverance, forgiveness, liberty, remission.\n\nSee: G863 \n\nCognate Group: G3935 (hang down), G3929 (remission), G859 (deliverance), G863 (cry)\nVariants: ἄφεσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H657 אֶפֶס, H663 אֲפֵק, H1865 דְּרֹור, H2010 הֲנָחָה, H2670 חׇפְשִׁי, H3104 יֹובֵל, H5310 נָפַץ, H5799 עֲזָאזֵל, H6388 פֶּלֶג, H8029 שִׁלֵּשׁ, H8058 שָׁמַט",
    860: "ἁφή (haphḗ | haf-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G680\nStrong's: probably a ligament (as fastening)\nKJV: —joint.\n\nSee: G680 \n\nCognate Group: G3935 (hang down), G3929 (remission), G859 (deliverance), G863 (cry)\nVariants: ἁφή \nHebrew Equivalents: H5061 נֶגַע",
    861: "ἀφθαρσία (aphtharsía | af-thar-see'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G862\nStrong's: incorruptibility; genitive, unending existence; (figuratively) genuineness\nKJV: —immortality, incorruption, sincerity.\n\nSee: G862 \n\nCognate Group: G5351 (corrupt), G1311 (corrupt), G862 (not corruptible), G5256 (minister), G5349 (corruptible), G90 (uncorruptness), G1312 (corruption), G861 (immortality), G2704 (corrupt)\nVariants: ἀφθαρσία",
    862: "ἄφθαρτος (áphthartos | af'-thar-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G5351\nStrong's: undecaying (in essence or continuance)\nKJV: —not (in-, un-)corruptible, immortal.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5351 \n\nCognate Group: G5351 (corrupt), G1311 (corrupt), G862 (not corruptible), G5256 (minister), G5349 (corruptible), G90 (uncorruptness), G1312 (corruption), G861 (immortality), G2704 (corrupt)\nVariants: ἄφθαρτος",
    863: "ἀφίημι (aphíēmi | af-ee'-ay-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and ἵημι (to send\nStrong's: an intensive form of εἶμι, to go); to send forth, in various applications (as follow)\nKJV: —cry, forgive, forsake, lay aside, leave, let (alone, be, go, have), omit, put (send) away, remit, suffer, yield up.\n\nSee: G575 \n\nCognate Group: G3935 (hang down), G3929 (remission), G859 (deliverance), G863 (cry)\nVariants: ἀφίημι, ἐναφίημι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2308 חָדַל, H3318 יָצָא, H3722 כָּפַר, H5117 נוּחַ, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5414 נָתַן, H5428 נָתַשׁ, H5545 סָלַח, H5800 עָזַב, H6605 פָּתַח, H7043 קָלַל, H7503 רָפָה, H7662 שְׁבַק, H7971 שָׁלַח, H8058 שָׁמַט, H8159 שָׁעָה",
    864: "ἀφικνέομαι (aphiknéomai | af-ik-neh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and the base of G2425\nStrong's: to go (i.e. spread) forth (by rumor)\nKJV: —come abroad.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G2425 \n\nCognate Group: G3935 (hang down), G3929 (remission), G859 (deliverance), G863 (cry)\nVariants: ἀφικνέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1639 גָּרַע, H2707 חָקָה, H4672 מָצָא, H5060 נָגַע, H5186 נָטָה, H5381 נָשַׂג",
    865: "ἀφιλάγαθος (aphilágathos | af-il-ag'-ath-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5358\nStrong's: hostile to virtue\nKJV: —despiser of those that are good.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5358 \n\nCognate Group: G19 (goodness), G865 (despiser of those that are good), G17 (them that do well), G5358 (love of good men)\nVariants: ἀφιλάγαθος",
    866: "ἀφιλάργυρος (aphilárgyros | af-il-ar'-goo-ros)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5366\nStrong's: unavaricious\nKJV: —without covetousness, not greedy of filthy lucre.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5366 \n\nCognate Group: G19 (goodness), G865 (despiser of those that are good), G17 (them that do well), G5358 (love of good men)\nVariants: ἀφιλάργυρος",
    867: "ἄφιξις (áphixis | af'-ix-is)\n\nDerivation: from G864\nStrong's: properly, arrival, i.e. (by implication) departure\nKJV: —departing.\n\nSee: G864 \n\nCognate Group: G19 (goodness), G865 (despiser of those that are good), G17 (them that do well), G5358 (love of good men)\nVariants: ἄφιξις",
    868: "ἀφίστημι (aphístēmi | af-is'-tay-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G2476\nStrong's: to remove, i.e. (actively) instigate to revolt; usually (reflexively) to desist, desert, etc.\nKJV: —depart, draw (fall) away, refrain, withdraw self.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G2476 \n\nCognate Group: G646 (falling away), G1370 (division), G868 (depart)\nVariants: ἀφίστημι, ἀφίσταμαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H230 אֲזָד, H622 אָסַף, H1350 גָּאַל, H1540 גָּלָה, H1826 דָּמַם, H2095 זְהַר, H2308 חָדַל, H3363 יָקַע, H3582 כָּחַד, H3772 כָּרַת, H3988 מָאַס, H4185 מוּשׁ, H4513 מָנַע, H4549 מָסַס, H4560 מָסַר, H4603 מָעַל, H4775 מָרַד, H4784 מָרָה, H5034 נָבֵל, H5066 נָגַשׁ, H5074 נָדַד, H5080 נָדַח, H5106 נוּא, H5307 נָפַל, H5423 נָתַק, H5472 סוּג, H5493 סוּר, H5641 סָתַר, H5674 עָבַר, H5710 עָדָה, H5927 עָלָה, H5975 עָמַד, H6275 עָתַק, H6342 פָּחַד, H6586 פָּשַׁע, H6622 פָּתַר, H7368 רָחַק, H7368 רָחַק, H7725 שׁוּב, H7760 שׂוּם, H8159 שָׁעָה",
    869: "ἄφνω (áphnō | af'-no)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G852 (contraction)\nStrong's: unawares, i.e. unexpectedly\nKJV: —suddenly.\n\nSee: G852 \n\nCognate Group: G646 (falling away), G1370 (division), G868 (depart)\nVariants: ἄφνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6597 פִּתְאֹום",
    870: "ἀφόβως (aphóbōs | af-ob'-oce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from a compound of G1 (as a negative particle) and G5401\nStrong's: fearlessly\nKJV: —without fear.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5401 \n\nCognate Group: G3875 (advocate), G3870 (beseech), G3874 (comfort), G870 (without fear)\nVariants: ἀφόβως \nHebrew Equivalents: H6343 פַּחַד",
    871: "ἀφομοιόω (aphomoióō | af-om-oy-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G3666\nStrong's: to assimilate closely\nKJV: —make like.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G3666 \n\nCognate Group: G3664 (like), G3946 (like), G3666 (be like), G3668 (likewise), G3667 (made like to), G871 (make like), G3669 (similitude), G3665 (like as), G3670 (con- fess), G3945 (be like unto)\nVariants: ἀφομοιόω",
    872: "ἀφοράω (aphoráō | af-or-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G3708\nStrong's: to consider attentively\nKJV: —look.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G3708 \n\nCognate Group: G3664 (like), G3946 (like), G3666 (be like), G3668 (likewise), G3667 (made like to), G871 (make like), G3669 (similitude), G3665 (like as), G3670 (con- fess), G3945 (be like unto)\nVariants: ἀφοράω",
    873: "ἀφορίζω (aphorízō | af-or-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G575 and G3724\nStrong's: to set off by boundary, i.e. (figuratively) limit, exclude, appoint, etc.\nKJV: —divide, separate, sever.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G3724 \n\nCognate Group: G3724 (declare), G4309 (determine before), G592 (separate), G873 (divide)\nVariants: ἀφορίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H914 בָּדַל, H1305 בָּרַר, H1362 גָּבָהּ, H1605 גָּעַר, H2710 חָקַק, H2764 חֵרֶם, H4054 מִגְרָשׁ, H4720 מִקְדָּשׁ, H4733 מִקְלָט, H5130 נוּף, H5462 סָגַר, H5674 עָבַר, H6299 פָּדָה, H6504 פָּרַד, H7311 רוּם",
    874: "ἀφορμή (aphormḗ | af-or-may')\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G575 and G3729\nStrong's: a starting-point, i.e. (figuratively) an opportunity\nKJV: —occasion.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G3729 \n\nCognate Group: G3729 (run), G874 (occasion), G3730 (assault), G3731 (violence)\nVariants: ἀφορμή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1995 הָמֹון",
    875: "ἀφρίζω (aphrízō | af-rid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G876\nStrong's: to froth at the mouth (in epilepsy)\nKJV: —foam.\n\nSee: G876 \n\nCognate Group: G3729 (run), G874 (occasion), G3730 (assault), G3731 (violence)\nVariants: ἀφρίζω",
    876: "ἀφρός (aphrós | af-ros')\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary word\nStrong's: froth, i.e. slaver\nKJV: —foaming.\n\nCognate Group: G3729 (run), G874 (occasion), G3730 (assault), G3731 (violence)\nVariants: ἀφρός",
    877: "ἀφροσύνη (aphrosýnē | af-ros-oo'-nay)\n\nDerivation: from G878\nStrong's: senselessness, i.e. (euphemistically) egotism; (morally) recklessness\nKJV: —folly, foolishly(-ness).\n\nSee: G878 \n\nCognate Group: G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)\nVariants: ἀφροσύνη \nHebrew Equivalents: H200 אִוֶּלֶת, H2154 זִמָּה, H3685 כְּסִיל, H5039 נְבָלָה, H6612 פְּתִי, H7919 שָׂכַל, H8602 תָּפֵל",
    878: "ἄφρων (áphrōn | af'-rone)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5424\nStrong's: properly, mindless, i.e. stupid, (by implication) ignorant, (specially) egotistic, (practically) rash, or (morally) unbelieving\nKJV: —fool(-ish), unwise.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5424 \n\nCognate Group: G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)\nVariants: ἄφρων \nHebrew Equivalents: H191 אֱוִיל, H205 אָוֶן, H954 בּוּשׁ, H1100 בְּלִיַּעַל, H1198 בַּעַר, H3685 כְּסִיל, H3808 לֹא, H3887 לוּץ, H5036 נָבָל, H6102 עָצֵל, H6612 פְּתִי, H7919 שָׂכַל",
    879: "ἀφυπνόω (aphypnóō | af-oop-no'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G575 and G5258\nStrong's: properly, to become awake, i.e. (by implication) to drop (off) in slumber\nKJV: —fall asleep.\n\nSee: G575 \nSee: G5258 \n\nCognate Group: G879 (fall asleep), G1798 (dream), G1853 (X out of sleep), G5258 (sleep), G1797 (dream), G1852 (awake out of sleep)\nVariants: ἀφυπνόω",
    880: "ἄφωνος (áphōnos | af'-o-nos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5456\nStrong's: voiceless, i.e. mute (by nature or choice); figuratively, unmeaning\nKJV: —dumb, without signification.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5456 \n\nCognate Group: G879 (fall asleep), G1798 (dream), G1853 (X out of sleep), G5258 (sleep), G1797 (dream), G1852 (awake out of sleep)\nVariants: ἄφωνος, ἄμορφος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5956 עָלַם",
    881: "Ἀχάζ (Acház | akh-adz')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H271)\nStrong's: Achaz, an Israelite\nKJV: —Achaz.\nSee: H271\n\nCognate Group: G879 (fall asleep), G1798 (dream), G1853 (X out of sleep), G5258 (sleep), G1797 (dream), G1852 (awake out of sleep)\nVariants: Ἀχάζ, Ἀχάς, Ἄχαζ \nHebrew Equivalents: H270 אָחַז, H271 אָחָז",
    882: "Ἀχαΐα (Achaḯa | ach-ah-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Achaia (i.e. Greece), a country of Europe\nKJV: —Achaia.\n\nCognate Group: G879 (fall asleep), G1798 (dream), G1853 (X out of sleep), G5258 (sleep), G1797 (dream), G1852 (awake out of sleep)\nVariants: Ἀχαΐα, Ἀχαί̈α, Ἀχαΐα, Ἀχαϊα",
    883: "Ἀχαϊκός (Achaïkós | ach-ah-ee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G882\nStrong's: an Achaian; Achaicus, a Christian\nKJV: —Achaicus.\n\nSee: G882 \n\nCognate Group: G879 (fall asleep), G1798 (dream), G1853 (X out of sleep), G5258 (sleep), G1797 (dream), G1852 (awake out of sleep)\nVariants: Ἀχαϊκός",
    884: "ἀχάριστος (acháristos | ach-ar'-is-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of G5483\nStrong's: thankless, i.e. ungrateful\nKJV: —unthankful.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5483 \n\nCognate Group: G5479 (gladness), G4796 (rejoice in), G2168 (thank), G2169 (thankfulness), G5485 (acceptable), G5486 (gift), G5463 (farewell), G5484 (be- cause of), G2170 (thankful), G5487 (make accepted), G884 (unthankful), G5483 (deliver)\nVariants: ἀχάριστος",
    885: "Ἀχείμ (Acheím | akh-ime')\n\nDerivation: probably of Hebrew origin (compare H3137)\nStrong's: Achim, an Israelite\nKJV: —Achim.\nSee: H3137\n\nCognate Group: G5479 (gladness), G4796 (rejoice in), G2168 (thank), G2169 (thankfulness), G5485 (acceptable), G5486 (gift), G5463 (farewell), G5484 (be- cause of), G2170 (thankful), G5487 (make accepted), G884 (unthankful), G5483 (deliver)\nVariants: Ἀχείμ, Ἀχίμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3137 יֹוקִים",
    886: "ἀχειροποίητος (acheiropoíētos | akh-i-rop-oy'-ay-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5499\nStrong's: unmanufactured, i.e. inartificial\nKJV: —made without (not made with) hands.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5499 \n\nCognate Group: G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)\nVariants: ἀχειροποίητος",
    887: "ἀχλύς (achlýs | akh-looce')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: dimness of sight, i.e. (probably) a cataract\nKJV: —mist.\n\nCognate Group: G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)\nVariants: ἀχλύς",
    888: "ἀχρεῖος (achreîos | akh-ri'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of G5534 (compare G5532)\nStrong's: useless, i.e. (euphemistically) unmeritorious\nKJV: —unprofitable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5534 \nSee: G5532 \n\nCognate Group: G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)\nVariants: ἀχρεῖος \nHebrew Equivalents: H8217 שָׁפָל",
    889: "ἀχρειόω (achreióō | akh-ri-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G888\nStrong's: to render useless, i.e. spoil\nKJV: —become unprofitable.\n\nSee: G888 \n\nCognate Group: G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)\nVariants: ἀχρειόω, ἀχρειόομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H444 אָלַח, H3510 כָּאַב, H7489 רָעַע",
    890: "ἄχρηστος (áchrēstos | akh'-race-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5543\nStrong's: inefficient, i.e. (by implication) detrimental\nKJV: —unprofitable.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5543 \n\nCognate Group: G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)\nVariants: ἄχρηστος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5869 עַיִן",
    891: "ἄχρι (áchri | akh'-ree) or ἄχρις (áchris | akh'-rece)\n\nDerivation: akin to G206 (through the idea of a terminus)\nStrong's: (of time) until or (of place) up to\nKJV: —as far as, for, in(-to), till, (even, un-)to, until, while. Compare G3360 .\n\nSee: G206 \nSee: G3360 \n\nCognate Group: G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)\nVariants: ἄχρι",
    892: "ἄχυρον (áchyron | akh'-oo-ron)\n\nDerivation: perhaps remotely from χέω (to shed forth)\nStrong's: chaff (as diffusive)\nKJV: —chaff.\n\nCognate Group: G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)\nVariants: ἄχυρον \nHebrew Equivalents: H217 אוּר, H1098 בְּלִיל, H2563 חֹמֶר, H4671 מֹץ, H8401 תֶּבֶן",
    893: "ἀψευδής (apseudḗs | aps-yoo-dace')\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5579\nStrong's: veracious\nKJV: —that cannot lie.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5579 \n\nCognate Group: G5572 (false teacher), G5580 (false Christ), G5578 (false prophet), G5576 (be a false witness), G5575 (false witness), G5583 (liar), G5577 (false witness), G893 (that cannot lie), G5581 (falsely so called), G5574 (falsely), G5582 (lie), G5579 (lie), G5571 (false), G5573 (speaking lies)\nVariants: ἀψευδής",
    894: "ἄψινθος (ápsinthos | ap'-sin-thos)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: wormwood (as a type of bitterness, i.e. (figuratively) calamity)\nKJV: —wormwood.\n\nCognate Group: G5572 (false teacher), G5580 (false Christ), G5578 (false prophet), G5576 (be a false witness), G5575 (false witness), G5583 (liar), G5577 (false witness), G893 (that cannot lie), G5581 (falsely so called), G5574 (falsely), G5582 (lie), G5579 (lie), G5571 (false), G5573 (speaking lies)\nVariants: ἄψινθος, ἀψίνθιον",
    895: "ἄψυχος (ápsychos | ap'-soo-khos)\n\nDerivation: from G1 (as a negative particle) and G5590\nStrong's: lifeless, i.e. inanimate (mechanical)\nKJV: —without life.\n\nSee: G1 \nSee: G5590 \n\nCognate Group: G5572 (false teacher), G5580 (false Christ), G5578 (false prophet), G5576 (be a false witness), G5575 (false witness), G5583 (liar), G5577 (false witness), G893 (that cannot lie), G5581 (falsely so called), G5574 (falsely), G5582 (lie), G5579 (lie), G5571 (false), G5573 (speaking lies)\nVariants: ἄψυχος",
    896: "Βάαλ (Báal | bah'-al)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1168)\nStrong's: Baal, a Phœnician deity (used as a symbol of idolatry)\nKJV: —Baal.\nSee: H1168\n\nCognate Group: G5572 (false teacher), G5580 (false Christ), G5578 (false prophet), G5576 (be a false witness), G5575 (false witness), G5583 (liar), G5577 (false witness), G893 (that cannot lie), G5581 (falsely so called), G5574 (falsely), G5582 (lie), G5579 (lie), G5571 (false), G5573 (speaking lies)\nVariants: Βάαλ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1167 בַּעַל, H1168 בַּעַל",
    897: "Βαβυλών (Babylṓn | bab-oo-lone')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H894)\nStrong's: Babylon, the capitol of Chaldæa (literally or figuratively (as a type of tyranny))\nKJV: — Babylon.\nSee: H894\n\nCognate Group: G897 (Babylon)\nVariants: Βαβυλών \nHebrew Equivalents: H894 בָּבֶל",
    898: "βαθμός (bathmós | bath-mos')\n\nDerivation: from the same as G899\nStrong's: a step, i.e. (figuratively) grade (of dignity)\nKJV: —degree.\n\nSee: G899 \n\nCognate Group: G897 (Babylon)\nVariants: βαθμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H4609 מַעֲלָה, H4670 מִפְתָּן",
    899: "βάθος (báthos | bath'-os)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G901\nStrong's: profundity, i.e. (by implication) extent; (figuratively) mystery\nKJV: —deep(-ness, things), depth.\n\nSee: G901 \n\nCognate Group: G899 (deep)\nVariants: βάθος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2436 חֵיק, H3411 יְרֵכָה, H4615 מַעֲמָק, H4688 מְצֹולָה, H6009 עָמַק, H6013 עָמֹק, H7172 קַרְקַע, H8482 תַּחְתִּי",
    900: "βαθύνω (bathýnō | bath-oo'-no)\n\nDerivation: from G901\nStrong's: to deepen\nKJV: —deep.\n\nSee: G901 \n\nCognate Group: G899 (deep)\nVariants: βαθύνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6009 עָמַק",
    901: "βαθύς (bathýs | bath-oos')\n\nDerivation: from the base of G939\nStrong's: profound (as going down), literally or figuratively\nKJV: —deep, very early.\n\nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G899 (deep)\nVariants: βαθύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H5994 עֲמִיק, H6009 עָמַק, H6121 עָקֹב",
    902: "βαΐον (baḯon | bah-ee'-on)\n\nDerivation: a diminutive of a derivative probably of the base of G939\nStrong's: a palm twig (as going out far)\nKJV: —branch.\n\nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G899 (deep)\nVariants: βαΐον, βάϊον, βαΐον, βαΐον/βάϊον",
    903: "Βαλαάμ (Balaám | bal-ah-am')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1109)\nStrong's: Balaam, a Mesopotamian (symbolic of a false teacher)\nKJV: —Balaam.\nSee: H1109\n\nCognate Group: G903 (Balaam)\nVariants: Βαλαάμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1109 בִּלְעָם",
    904: "Βαλάκ (Balák | bal-ak')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1111)\nStrong's: Balak, a Moabite\nKJV: —Balac.\nSee: H1111\n\nCognate Group: G903 (Balaam)\nVariants: Βαλάκ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1111 בָּלָק",
    905: "βαλάντιον (balántion | bal-an'-tee-on)\n\nDerivation: probably remotely from G906 (as a depository)\nStrong's: a pouch (for money)\nKJV: —bag, purse.\n\nSee: G906 \n\nCognate Group: G905 (bag)\nVariants: βαλάντιον, βαλλάντιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H3599 כִּיס, H6872 צְרֹור",
    906: "βάλλω (bállō | bal'-lo)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to throw (in various applications, more or less violent or intense)\nKJV: —arise, cast (out), X dung, lay, lie, pour, put (up), send, strike, throw (down), thrust. Compare G4496 .\n\nSee: G4496 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: βάλλω, ἀμφιβάλλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2904 טוּל, H3032 יָדַד, H3384 יָרָה, H4272 מָחַץ, H5186 נָטָה, H5221 נָכָה, H5307 נָפַל, H5375 נָשָׂא, H6566 פָּרַשׂ, H6651 צָבַר, H6696 צוּר, H6923 קָדַם, H7049 קָלַע, H7411 רָמָה, H7760 שׂוּם, H7971 שָׁלַח, H7993 שָׁלַךְ, H8210 שָׁפַךְ, H8327 שָׁרַשׁ, H8628 תָּקַע",
    907: "βαπτίζω (baptízō | bap-tid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G911\nStrong's: to immerse, submerge; to make whelmed (i.e. fully wet); used only (in the New Testament) of ceremonial ablution, especially (technically) of the ordinance of Christian baptism\nKJV: —Baptist, baptize, wash.\n\nSee: G911 \n\nCognate Group: G909 (baptism), G911 (dip), G910 (Baptist), G908 (baptism), G907 (Baptist)\nVariants: βαπτίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2881 טָבַל",
    908: "βάπτισμα (báptisma | bap'-tis-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G907\nStrong's: baptism (technically or figuratively)\nKJV: —baptism.\n\nSee: G907 \n\nCognate Group: G909 (baptism), G911 (dip), G910 (Baptist), G908 (baptism), G907 (Baptist)\nVariants: βάπτισμα",
    909: "βαπτισμός (baptismós | bap-tis-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G907\nStrong's: ablution (ceremonial or Christian)\nKJV: —baptism, washing.\n\nSee: G907 \n\nCognate Group: G909 (baptism), G911 (dip), G910 (Baptist), G908 (baptism), G907 (Baptist)\nVariants: βαπτισμός",
    910: "Βαπτιστής (Baptistḗs | bap-tis-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G907\nStrong's: a baptizer, as an epithet of Christ's forerunner\nKJV: —Baptist.\n\nSee: G907 \n\nCognate Group: G909 (baptism), G911 (dip), G910 (Baptist), G908 (baptism), G907 (Baptist)\nVariants: Βαπτιστής, βαπτιστής",
    911: "βάπτω (báptō | bap'-to)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to whelm, i.e. cover wholly with a fluid; in the New Testament only in a qualified or special sense, i.e. (literally) to moisten (a part of one's person), or (by implication) to stain (as with dye)\nKJV: —dip.\n\nCognate Group: G909 (baptism), G911 (dip), G910 (Baptist), G908 (baptism), G907 (Baptist)\nVariants: βάπτω, ῥαίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H2881 טָבַל, H4272 מָחַץ, H6647 צְבַע",
    912: "Βαραββᾶς (Barabbâs | bar-ab-bas')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (H1347 and H5)\nStrong's: son of Abba; Bar-abbas, an Israelite\nKJV: —Barabbas.\nSee: H1347\nSee: H5\n\nCognate Group: G909 (baptism), G911 (dip), G910 (Baptist), G908 (baptism), G907 (Baptist)\nVariants: Βαραββᾶς \nHebrew Equivalents: H2 אַב",
    913: "Βαράκ (Barák | bar-ak')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1301)\nStrong's: Barak, an Israelite\nKJV: —Barak.\nSee: H1301\n\nCognate Group: G909 (baptism), G911 (dip), G910 (Baptist), G908 (baptism), G907 (Baptist)\nVariants: Βαράκ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1300 בָּרָק, H1301 בָּרָק",
    914: "Βαραχίας (Barachías | bar-akh-ee'-as)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1296)\nStrong's: Barachias (i.e. Berechijah), an Israelite\nKJV: —Barachias.\nSee: H1296\n\nCognate Group: G909 (baptism), G911 (dip), G910 (Baptist), G908 (baptism), G907 (Baptist)\nVariants: Βαραχίας \nHebrew Equivalents: H1296 בֶּרֶכְיָה",
    915: "βάρβαρος (bárbaros | bar'-bar-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a foreigner (i.e. non-Greek)\nKJV: —barbarian(-rous).\n\nCognate Group: G915 (barbarian)\nVariants: βάρβαρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1198 בַּעַר, H3937 לָעַז",
    916: "βαρέω (baréō | bar-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G926\nStrong's: to weigh down (figuratively)\nKJV: —burden, charge, heavy, press.\n\nSee: G926 \n\nCognate Group: G926 (grievous), G922 (burden), G916 (burden)\nVariants: βαρέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3513 כָּבַד, H3513 כָּבַד",
    917: "βαρέως (baréōs | bar-eh'-oce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G926\nStrong's: heavily (figuratively)\nKJV: —dull.\n\nSee: G926 \n\nCognate Group: G926 (grievous), G922 (burden), G916 (burden)\nVariants: βαρέως \nHebrew Equivalents: H2734 חָרָה, H3513 כָּבַד",
    918: "Βαρθολομαῖος (Bartholomaîos | bar-thol-om-ah'-yos)\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (H1247 and H8526)\nStrong's: son of Tolmai; Bar-tholomæus, a Christian apostle\nKJV: —Bartholomeus.\nSee: H1247\nSee: H8526\n\nCognate Group: G926 (grievous), G922 (burden), G916 (burden)\nVariants: Βαρθολομαῖος \nHebrew Equivalents: H8526 תַּלְמַי",
    919: "Βαριησοῦς (Bariēsoûs | bar-ee-ay-sooce')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (H1247 and H3091)\nStrong's: son of Jesus (or Joshua); Bar-jesus, an Israelite\nKJV: —Barjesus.\nSee: H1247\nSee: H3091\n\nCognate Group: G926 (grievous), G922 (burden), G916 (burden)\nVariants: Βαριησοῦς, Βαρϊησοῦς \nHebrew Equivalents: H3091 יְהֹושׁוּעַ",
    920: "Βαριωνᾶς (Bariōnâs | bar-ee-oo-nas')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (H1247 and H3124)\nStrong's: son of Jonas (or Jonah); Bar-jonas, an Israelite\nKJV: —Bar-jona.\nSee: H1247\nSee: H3124\n\nCognate Group: G926 (grievous), G922 (burden), G916 (burden)\nVariants: Βαριωνᾶς, Βαριωνᾶ, βαρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3124 יֹונָה",
    921: "Βαρνάβας (Barnábas | bar-nab'-as)\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (H1247 and H5029)\nStrong's: son of Nabas (i.e. prophecy); Barnabas, an Israelite\nKJV: —Barnabas.\nSee: H1247\nSee: H5029\n\nCognate Group: G926 (grievous), G922 (burden), G916 (burden)\nVariants: Βαρνάβας, Βαρναβᾶς \nHebrew Equivalents: H5029 נְבִיא",
    922: "βάρος (báros | bar'-os)\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as G939 (through the notion of going down\nStrong's: compare G899); weight; in the New Testament only, figuratively, a load, abundance, authority\nKJV: —burden(-some), weight.\n\nSee: G939 \nSee: G899 \n\nCognate Group: G926 (grievous), G922 (burden), G916 (burden)\nVariants: βάρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3519 כָּבֹוד",
    923: "Βαρσαβᾶς (Barsabâs | bar-sab-as')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (H1247 and probably H6634)\nStrong's: son of Sabas (or Tsaba); Bar-sabas, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: —Barsabas.\nSee: H1247\nSee: H6634\n\nCognate Group: G926 (grievous), G922 (burden), G916 (burden)\nVariants: Βαρσαβᾶς, Βαρσαββᾶς \nHebrew Equivalents: H6634 צְבָא",
    924: "Βαρτιμαῖος (Bartimaîos | bar-tim-ah'-yos)\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (H1247 and H2931)\nStrong's: son of Timæus (or the unclean); Bar-timæus, an Israelite\nKJV: —Bartimæus.\nSee: H1247\nSee: H2931\n\nCognate Group: G926 (grievous), G922 (burden), G916 (burden)\nVariants: Βαρτιμαῖος, Βαρτίμαιος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2931 טָמֵא",
    925: "βαρύνω (barýnō | bar-oo'-no)\n\nDerivation: from G926\nStrong's: to burden (figuratively)\nKJV: —overcharge.\n\nSee: G926 \n\nCognate Group: G926 (grievous), G922 (burden), G916 (burden)\nVariants: βαρύνω, καταβαρύνω G986",
    926: "βαρύς (barýs | bar-ooce')\n\nDerivation: from the same as G922\nStrong's: weighty, i.e. (fig) burdensome, grave\nKJV: —grievous, heavy, weightier.\n\nSee: G922 \n\nCognate Group: G926 (grievous), G922 (burden), G916 (burden)\nVariants: βαρύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H3358 יַקִּיר, H3513 כָּבַד, H3515 כָּבֵד, H3524 כַּבִּיר, H6099 עָצוּם, H7489 רָעַע",
    927: "βαρύτιμος (barýtimos | bar-oo'-tim-os)\n\nDerivation: from G926 and G5092\nStrong's: highly valuable\nKJV: —very precious.\n\nSee: G926 \nSee: G5092 \n\nCognate Group: G926 (grievous), G922 (burden), G916 (burden)\nVariants: βαρύτιμος",
    928: "βασανίζω (basanízō | bas-an-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G931\nStrong's: to torture\nKJV: —pain, toil, torment, toss, vex.\n\nSee: G931 \n\nCognate Group: G929 (torment), G928 (pain), G930 (tormentor), G931 (torment)\nVariants: βασανίζω",
    929: "βασανισμός (basanismós | bas-an-is-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G928\nStrong's: torture\nKJV: —torment.\n\nSee: G928 \n\nCognate Group: G929 (torment), G928 (pain), G930 (tormentor), G931 (torment)\nVariants: βασανισμός",
    930: "βασανιστής (basanistḗs | bas-an-is-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G928\nStrong's: a torturer\nKJV: —tormentor.\n\nSee: G928 \n\nCognate Group: G929 (torment), G928 (pain), G930 (tormentor), G931 (torment)\nVariants: βασανιστής",
    931: "βάσανος (básanos | bas'-an-os)\n\nDerivation: perhaps remotely from the same as G939 (through the notion of going to the bottom)\nStrong's: a touch-stone, i.e. (by analogy) torture\nKJV: —torment.\n\nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G929 (torment), G928 (pain), G930 (tormentor), G931 (torment)\nVariants: βάσανος \nHebrew Equivalents: H817 אָשָׁם, H3639 כְּלִמָּה, H4383 מִכְשֹׁול, H7269 רׇגְזָה",
    932: "βασιλεία (basileía | bas-il-i'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G935\nStrong's: properly, royalty, i.e. (abstractly) rule, or (concretely) a realm (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —kingdom, + reign.\n\nSee: G935 \n\nCognate Group: G934 (royal), G936 (king), G4821 (reign with), G937 (king's), G932 (kingdom), G935 (king), G938 (queen)\nVariants: βασιλεία \nHebrew Equivalents: H1004 בַּיִת, H4082 מְדִינָה, H4082 מְדִינָה, H4082 מְדִינָה, H4410 מְלוּכָה, H4438 מַלְכוּת, H4467 מַמְלָכָה, H4475 מֶמְשָׁלָה, H7985 שׇׁלְטָן",
    933: "βασίλειον (basíleion | bas-il'-i-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of G934\nStrong's: a palace\nKJV: —king's court.\n\nSee: G934 \n\nCognate Group: G934 (royal), G936 (king), G4821 (reign with), G937 (king's), G932 (kingdom), G935 (king), G938 (queen)\nVariants: βασίλειον, βασίλειος G994 \nHebrew Equivalents: H4467 מַמְלָכָה",
    934: "βασίλειος (basíleios | bas-il'-i-os)\n\nDerivation: from G935\nStrong's: kingly (in nature)\nKJV: —royal.\n\nSee: G935 \n\nCognate Group: G934 (royal), G936 (king), G4821 (reign with), G937 (king's), G932 (kingdom), G935 (king), G938 (queen)\nVariants: βασίλειος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4467 מַמְלָכָה",
    935: "βασιλεύς (basileús | bas-il-yooce')\n\nDerivation: probably from G939 (through the notion of a foundation of power)\nStrong's: a sovereign (abstractly, relatively, or figuratively)\nKJV: —king.\n\nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G934 (royal), G936 (king), G4821 (reign with), G937 (king's), G932 (kingdom), G935 (king), G938 (queen)\nVariants: βασιλεύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H660 אֶפְעֶה, H2710 חָקַק, H4397 מֲלְאָךְ, H4410 מְלוּכָה, H4428 מֶלֶךְ, H4756 מָרֵא, H4911 מָשַׁל, H5057 נָגִיד, H5081 נָדִיב, H5387 נָשִׂיא, H5461 סָגָן, H6620 פֶּתֶן, H7101 קָצִין, H8269 שַׂר",
    936: "βασιλεύω (basileúō | bas-il-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G935\nStrong's: to rule (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —king, reign.\n\nSee: G935 \n\nCognate Group: G934 (royal), G936 (king), G4821 (reign with), G937 (king's), G932 (kingdom), G935 (king), G938 (queen)\nVariants: βασιλεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3427 יָשַׁב, H4427 מָלַךְ, H4428 מֶלֶךְ",
    937: "βασιλικός (basilikós | bas-il-ee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G935\nStrong's: regal (in relation), i.e. (literally) belonging to (or befitting) the sovereign (as land, dress, or a courtier), or (figuratively) preeminent\nKJV: —king's, nobleman, royal.\n\nSee: G935 \n\nCognate Group: G934 (royal), G936 (king), G4821 (reign with), G937 (king's), G932 (kingdom), G935 (king), G938 (queen)\nVariants: βασιλικός, βασιλίσκος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4428 מֶלֶךְ",
    938: "βασίλισσα (basílissa | bas-il'-is-sah)\n\nDerivation: feminine from G936\nStrong's: a queen\nKJV: —queen.\n\nSee: G936 \n\nCognate Group: G934 (royal), G936 (king), G4821 (reign with), G937 (king's), G932 (kingdom), G935 (king), G938 (queen)\nVariants: βασίλισσα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1377 גְּבִירָה, H4436 מַלְכָּה, H7694 שֵׁגָל",
    939: "βάσις (básis | bas'-ece)\n\nDerivation: from βαίνω (to walk)\nStrong's: a pace (\"base\"), i.e. (by implication) the foot\nKJV: —foot.\n\nCognate Group: G934 (royal), G936 (king), G4821 (reign with), G937 (king's), G932 (kingdom), G935 (king), G938 (queen)\nVariants: βάσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H134 אֶדֶן, H753 אֹרֶךְ, H1366 גְּבוּל, H3247 יְסֹוד, H3595 כִּיֹּור, H3653 כֵּן, H4837 מַרְצֶפֶת, H7023 קִיר, H7413 רָמָה",
    940: "βασκαίνω (baskaínō | bas-kah'-ee-no)\n\nDerivation: akin to G5335\nStrong's: to malign, i.e. (by extension) to fascinate (by false representations)\nKJV: —bewitch.\n\nSee: G5335 \n\nCognate Group: G940 (bewitch)\nVariants: βασκαίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7489 רָעַע",
    941: "βαστάζω (bastázō | bas-tad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: perhaps remotely derived from the base of G939 (through the idea of removal)\nStrong's: to lift, literally or figuratively (endure, declare, sustain, receive, etc.)\nKJV: —bear, carry, take up.\n\nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G941 (bear)\nVariants: βαστάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5186 נָטָה, H5375 נָשָׂא",
    942: "βάτος (bátos | bat'-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a brier shrub\nKJV: —bramble, bush.\n\nCognate Group: G941 (bear)\nVariants: βάτος, βάτοσ1 \nHebrew Equivalents: H890 בׇּאְשָׁה, H5572 סְנֶה",
    943: "βάτος (bátos | bat'-os)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1324)\nStrong's: a bath, or measure for liquids\nKJV: —measure.\nSee: H1324\n\nCognate Group: G941 (bear)\nVariants: βάτος, βάτοσ2, κάβος, κάδος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1323 בַּת, H1324 בַּת",
    944: "βάτραχος (bátrachos | bat'-rakh-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a frog\nKJV: —frog.\n\nCognate Group: G941 (bear)\nVariants: βάτραχος \nHebrew Equivalents: H6854 צְפַרְדֵּעַ",
    945: "βαττολογέω (battologéō | bat-tol-og-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from Βάττος (a proverbial stammerer) and G3056\nStrong's: to stutter, i.e. (by implication) to prate tediously\nKJV: —use vain repetitions.\n\nSee: G3056 \n\nCognate Group: G945 (use vain repetitions)\nVariants: βαττολογέω, βατταλογέω",
    946: "βδέλυγμα (bdélygma | bdel'-oog-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G948\nStrong's: a detestation, i.e. (specially) idolatry\nKJV: —abomination.\n\nSee: G948 \n\nCognate Group: G946 (abomination), G947 (abominable), G948 (abhor)\nVariants: βδέλυγμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H433 אֱלֹוהַּ, H457 אֱלִיל, H1544 גִּלּוּל, H2553 חַמָּן, H4209 מְזִמָּה, H8251 שִׁקּוּץ, H8263 שֶׁקֶץ, H8441 תֹּועֵבַה",
    947: "βδελυκτός (bdelyktós | bdel-ook-tos')\n\nDerivation: from G948\nStrong's: detestable, i.e. (specially) idolatrous\nKJV: —abominable.\n\nSee: G948 \n\nCognate Group: G946 (abomination), G947 (abominable), G948 (abhor)\nVariants: βδελυκτός \nHebrew Equivalents: H8441 תֹּועֵבַה",
    948: "βδελύσσω (bdelýssō | bdel-oos'-so)\n\nDerivation: from a (presumed) derivative of βδέω (to stink)\nStrong's: to be disgusted, i.e. (by implication) detest (especially of idolatry)\nKJV: —abhor, abominable.\n\nCognate Group: G946 (abomination), G947 (abominable), G948 (abhor)\nVariants: βδελύσσω, βδελύσσομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1350 גָּאַל, H5074 נָדַד, H6087 עָצַב, H6973 קוּץ, H8251 שִׁקּוּץ, H8262 שָׁקַץ, H8581 תַּעָב, H8581 תַּעָב",
    949: "βέβαιος (bébaios | beb'-ah-yos)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G939 (through the idea of basality)\nStrong's: stable (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —firm, of force, stedfast, sure.\n\nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G949 (firm), G951 (confirmation), G950 (confirm)\nVariants: βέβαιος",
    950: "βεβαιόω (bebaióō | beb-ah-yo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G949\nStrong's: to stabilitate (figuratively)\nKJV: —confirm, (e-)stablish.\n\nSee: G949 \n\nCognate Group: G949 (firm), G951 (confirmation), G950 (confirm)\nVariants: βεβαιόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5324 נָצַב, H6965 קוּם",
    951: "βεβαίωσις (bebaíōsis | beb-ah'-yo-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G950\nStrong's: stabiliment\nKJV: —confirmation.\n\nSee: G950 \n\nCognate Group: G949 (firm), G951 (confirmation), G950 (confirm)\nVariants: βεβαίωσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H6783 צְמִיתֻת",
    952: "βέβηλος (bébēlos | beb'-ay-los)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G939 and βηλός (a threshold)\nStrong's: accessible (as by crossing the door-way), i.e. (by implication, of Jewish notions) heathenish, wicked\nKJV: —profane (person).\n\nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G952 (profane), G953 (profane)\nVariants: βέβηλος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2344 חֹול, H6292 פִּגּוּל",
    953: "βεβηλόω (bebēlóō | beb-ay-lo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G952\nStrong's: to desecrate\nKJV: —profane.\n\nSee: G952 \n\nCognate Group: G952 (profane), G953 (profane)\nVariants: βεβηλόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2490 חָלַל",
    954: "Βεελζεβούλ (Beelzeboúl | beh-el-zeb-ool')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (by parody on H1176)\nStrong's: dung-god; Beelzebul, a name of Satan\nKJV: —Beelzebub.\nSee: H1176\n\nCognate Group: G954 (Beelzebub)\nVariants: Βεελζεβούλ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1167 בַּעַל, H1176 בַּעַל זְבוּב",
    955: "Βελίαλ (Belíal | bel-ee'-al)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1100)\nStrong's: worthlessness; Belial, as an epithet of Satan\nKJV: —Belial.\nSee: H1100\n\nCognate Group: G955 (Belial)\nVariants: Βελίαλ, Βελιάρ, Βελίαρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1100 בְּלִיַּעַל, H1100 בְּלִיַּעַל",
    956: "βέλος (bélos | bel'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G906\nStrong's: a missile, i.e. spear or arrow\nKJV: —dart.\n\nSee: G906 \n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: βέλος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2671 חֵץ, H5402 נֶשֶׁק, H7626 שֵׁבֶט, H7973 שֶׁלַח",
    957: "βελτίον (beltíon | bel-tee'-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a compound of a derivative of G906 (used for the comparative of G18)\nStrong's: better\nKJV: —very well.\n\nSee: G906 \nSee: G18 \n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: βελτίον, βελτίων \nHebrew Equivalents: H2896 טֹוב, H3303 יָפֶה, H3477 יָשָׁר, H5276 נָעֵם",
    958: "Βενιαμίν (Beniamín | ben-ee-am-een')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1144)\nStrong's: Benjamin, an Israelite\nKJV: —Benjamin.\nSee: H1144\n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: Βενιαμίν, Βενιαμείν, Βενιαμ(ε)ίν \nHebrew Equivalents: H1121 בֵּן, H1144 בִּנְיָמִין",
    959: "Βερνίκη (Berníkē | ber-nee'-kay)\n\nDerivation: from a provincial form of G5342 and G3529\nStrong's: victorious; Bernice, a member of the Herodian family\nKJV: —Bernice.\n\nSee: G5342 \nSee: G3529 \n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: Βερνίκη",
    960: "Βέροια (Béroia | ber'-oy-ah)\n\nDerivation: perhaps a provincial from a derivative of G4008 (Perœa, i.e. the region beyond the coast-line)\nStrong's: Berœa, a place in Macedonia\nKJV: —Berea.\n\nSee: G4008 \n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: Βέροια",
    961: "Βεροιαῖος (Beroiaîos | ber-oy-ah'-yos)\n\nDerivation: from G960\nStrong's: a Berœoean or native of Berœa\nKJV: —of Berea.\n\nSee: G960 \n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: Βεροιαῖος",
    962: "Βηθαβαρά (Bēthabará | bay-thab-ar-ah')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1004 and H5679)\nStrong's: ferry-house; Bethabara (i.e. Bethabarah), a place on the Jordan\nKJV: —Bethabara.\nSee: H1004\nSee: H5679\n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: Βηθαβαρά, Βηθαραβά G1028, G1030 \nHebrew Equivalents: H1004 בַּיִת, H5679 עֲבָרָה",
    963: "Βηθανία (Bēthanía | bay-than-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin\nStrong's: date-house; Beth-any, a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Bethany.\n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: Βηθανία \nHebrew Equivalents: H1004 בַּיִת",
    964: "Βηθεσδά (Bēthesdá | bay-thes-dah')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (compare H1004 and H2617)\nStrong's: house of kindness; Beth-esda, a pool in Jerusalem\nKJV: —Bethesda.\nSee: H1004\nSee: H2617\n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: Βηθεσδά, Βηθζαθά \nHebrew Equivalents: H1004 בַּיִת, H2617 חֵסֵד",
    965: "Βηθλεέμ (Bēthleém | bayth-leh-em')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1036)\nStrong's: Bethleem (i.e. Beth-lechem), a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Bethlehem.\nSee: H1036\n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: Βηθλεέμ, Βηθλέεμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1004 בַּיִת, H1035 בֵּית לֶחֶם",
    966: "Βηθσαϊδά (Bēthsaïdá | bayth-sahee-dah')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (compare H1004 and H6719)\nStrong's: fishing-house; Bethsaida, a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Bethsaida.\nSee: H1004\nSee: H6719\n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: Βηθσαϊδά, Βηθσαϊδάν, Βηθσαϊδά(ν) \nHebrew Equivalents: H6719 צַיָּד",
    967: "Βηθφαγή (Bēthphagḗ | bayth-fag-ay')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (compare H1004 and H6291)\nStrong's: fig-house; Beth-phage, a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Bethphage.\nSee: H1004\nSee: H6291\n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: Βηθφαγή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1004 בַּיִת, H6291 פַּג",
    968: "βῆμα (bēma | bay'-ma)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G939\nStrong's: a step, i.e. foot-breath; by implication, a rostrum, i.e. a tribunal\nKJV: —judgment-seat, set (foot) on, throne.\n\nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: βῆμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H4026 מִגְדָּל, H4096 מִדְרָךְ",
    969: "βήρυλλος (bḗryllos | bay'-rool-los)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a \"beryl\"\nKJV: —beryl.\n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: βήρυλλος",
    970: "βία (bía | bee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: probably akin to G979 (through the idea of vital activity)\nStrong's: force\nKJV: —violence.\n\nSee: G979 \n\nCognate Group: G956 (dart)\nVariants: βία \nHebrew Equivalents: H657 אֶפֶס, H3154 יֶזַע, H3517 כְּבֵדֻת, H6531 פֶּרֶךְ, H6986 קֶטֶב, H8633 תֹּקֶף",
    971: "βιάζω (biázō | bee-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G979\nStrong's: to force, i.e. (reflexively) to crowd oneself (into), or (passively) to be seized\nKJV: —press, suffer violence.\n\nSee: G979 \n\nCognate Group: G971 (press), G973 (violent)\nVariants: βιάζω, βίαζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2040 הָרַס, H2388 חָזַק, H3533 כָּבַשׁ, H6113 עָצָר, H6484 פָּצַר, H6555 פָּרַץ, H8610 תָּפַשׂ",
    972: "βίαιος (bíaios | bee'-ah-yos)\n\nDerivation: from G970\nStrong's: violent\nKJV: —mighty.\n\nSee: G970 \n\nCognate Group: G971 (press), G973 (violent)\nVariants: βίαιος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5794 עַז, H5868 עֲיָם, H6064 עָנַשׁ, H6862 צַר, H6921 קָדִים",
    973: "βιαστής (biastḗs | bee-as-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G971\nStrong's: a forcer, i.e. (figuratively) energetic\nKJV: —violent.\n\nSee: G971 \n\nCognate Group: G971 (press), G973 (violent)\nVariants: βιαστής",
    974: "βιβλιαρίδιον (bibliarídion | bib-lee-ar-id'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: a diminutive of G975\nStrong's: a booklet\nKJV: —little book.\n\nSee: G975 \n\nCognate Group: G971 (press), G973 (violent)\nVariants: βιβλιαρίδιον, βιβλαρίδιον, βιβλιδάριον",
    975: "βιβλίον (biblíon | bib-lee'-on)\n\nDerivation: a diminutive of G976\nStrong's: a roll\nKJV: —bill, book, scroll, writing.\n\nSee: G976 \n\nCognate Group: G975 (bill), G976 (book)\nVariants: βιβλίον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1697 דָּבָר, H4039 מְגִלָּה, H4097 מִדְרָשׁ, H4557 מִסְפָּר, H5612 סֵפֶר, H8452 תֹּורָה",
    976: "βίβλος (bíblos | bib'-los)\n\nDerivation: properly, the inner bark of the papyrus plant, i.e. (by implication) a sheet or scroll of writing\nKJV: —book.\n\nCognate Group: G975 (bill), G976 (book)\nVariants: βίβλος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5612 סֵפֶר",
    977: "βιβρώσκω (bibrṓskō | bib-ro'-sko)\n\nDerivation: a reduplicated and prolonged form of an obsolete primary verb (perhaps causative of G1006)\nStrong's: to eat\nKJV: —eat.\n\nSee: G1006 \n\nCognate Group: G975 (bill), G976 (book)\nVariants: βιβρώσκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H398 אָכַל, H5350 נִקֻּד",
    978: "Βιθυνία (Bithynía | bee-thoo-nee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Bithynia, a region of Asia\nKJV: —Bithynia.\n\nCognate Group: G975 (bill), G976 (book)\nVariants: Βιθυνία, βιθυνία",
    979: "βίος (bíos | bee'-os)\n\nDerivation: a primary word\nStrong's: life, i.e. (literally) the present state of existence; by implication, the means of livelihood\nKJV: —good, life, living.\n\nCognate Group: G975 (bill), G976 (book)\nVariants: βίος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1952 הֹון, H2416 חַי, H3117 יֹום, H3899 לֶחֶם, H5232 נְכַס, H6635 צָבָא, H8141 שָׁנֶה",
    980: "βιόω (bióō | bee-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G979\nStrong's: to spend existence\nKJV: —live.\n\nSee: G979 \n\nCognate Group: G975 (bill), G976 (book)\nVariants: βιόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2421 חָיָה",
    981: "βίωσις (bíōsis | bee'-o-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G980\nStrong's: living (properly, the act, by implication, the mode)\nKJV: —manner of life.\n\nSee: G980 \n\nCognate Group: G975 (bill), G976 (book)\nVariants: βίωσις",
    982: "βιωτικός (biōtikós | bee-o-tee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G980\nStrong's: relating to the present existence\nKJV: —of (pertaining to, things that pertain to) this life.\n\nSee: G980 \n\nCognate Group: G975 (bill), G976 (book)\nVariants: βιωτικός",
    983: "βλαβερός (blaberós | blab-er-os')\n\nDerivation: from G984\nStrong's: injurious\nKJV: —hurtful.\n\nSee: G984 \n\nCognate Group: G975 (bill), G976 (book)\nVariants: βλαβερός",
    984: "βλάπτω (bláptō | blap'-to)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: properly, to hinder, i.e. (by implication) to injure\nKJV: —hurt.\n\nCognate Group: G975 (bill), G976 (book)\nVariants: βλάπτω",
    985: "βλαστάνω (blastánō | blas-tan'-o)\n\nDerivation: from βλαστός (a sprout)\nStrong's: to germinate; by implication, to yield fruit\nKJV: —bring forth, bud, spring (up).\n\nCognate Group: G975 (bill), G976 (book)\nVariants: βλαστάνω, βλαστάω, βλαστάνω/βλαστάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1580 גָּמַל, H1876 דָּשָׁא, H6509 פָּרָה, H6524 פָּרַח, H6692 צוּץ, H6779 צָמַח",
    986: "Βλάστος (Blástos | blas'-tos)\n\nDerivation: perhaps the same as the base of G985\nStrong's: Blastus, an officer of Herod Agrippa\nKJV: —Blastus.\n\nSee: G985 \n\nCognate Group: G975 (bill), G976 (book)\nVariants: Βλάστος",
    987: "βλασφημέω (blasphēméō | blas-fay-meh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G989\nStrong's: to vilify; specially, to speak impiously\nKJV: —(speak) blaspheme(-er, -mously, -my), defame, rail on, revile, speak evil.\n\nSee: G989 \n\nCognate Group: G989 (blasphemer), G988 (blasphemy), G987 (blaspheme)\nVariants: βλασφημέω, δυσφημέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H1442 גָּדַף, H3198 יָכַח, H5006 נָאַץ",
    988: "βλασφημία (blasphēmía | blas-fay-me'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G989\nStrong's: vilification (especially against God)\nKJV: —blasphemy, evil speaking, railing.\n\nSee: G989 \n\nCognate Group: G989 (blasphemer), G988 (blasphemy), G987 (blaspheme)\nVariants: βλασφημία \nHebrew Equivalents: H5007 נְאָצָה, H7955 שָׁלָה",
    989: "βλάσφημος (blásphēmos | blas'-fay-mos)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G984 and G5345\nStrong's: scurrilious, i.e. calumnious (against men), or (specially) impious (against God)\nKJV: —blasphemer(-mous), railing.\n\nSee: G984 \nSee: G5345 \n\nCognate Group: G989 (blasphemer), G988 (blasphemy), G987 (blaspheme)\nVariants: βλάσφημος",
    990: "βλέμμα (blémma | blem'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G991\nStrong's: vision (properly concrete; by implication, abstract)\nKJV: —seeing.\n\nSee: G991 \n\nCognate Group: G989 (blasphemer), G988 (blasphemy), G987 (blaspheme)\nVariants: βλέμμα",
    991: "βλέπω (blépō | blep'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to look at (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —behold, beware, lie, look (on, to), perceive, regard, see, sight, take heed. Compare G3700 .\n\nSee: G3700 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: βλέπω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H2372 חָזָה, H5027 נָבַט, H5048 נֶגֶד, H5870 עַיִן, H6049 עָנַן, H6437 פָּנָה, H6440 פָּנִים, H6493 פִּקֵּחַ, H7200 רָאָה, H8259 שָׁקַף",
    992: "βλητέος (blētéos | blay-teh'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G906\nStrong's: fit to be cast (i.e. applied)\nKJV: —must be put.\n\nSee: G906 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: βλητέος",
    993: "Βοανεργές (Boanergés | bo-an-erg-es')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (H1123 and H7266)\nStrong's: sons of commotion; Boanerges, an epithet of two of the apostles\nKJV: —Boanerges.\nSee: H1123\nSee: H7266\n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: Βοανεργές, Βοανηργές \nHebrew Equivalents: H1123 בֵּן, H7266 רְגַז",
    994: "βοάω (boáō | bo-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: apparently a prolonged form of a primary verb\nStrong's: to halloo, i.e. shout (for help or in a tumultuous way)\nKJV: —cry.\n\nCognate Group: G994 (cry)\nVariants: βοάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H1898 הָגָה, H1993 הָמָה, H2199 זָעַק, H2201 זַעַק, H3655 כָּנָה, H5098 נָהַם, H5101 נָהַק, H5375 נָשָׂא, H6476 פָּצַח, H6670 צָהַל, H6681 צָוַח, H6817 צָעַק, H6873 צָרַח, H7121 קָרָא, H7321 רוּעַ, H7481 רָעַם, H7580 שָׁאַג, H7650 שָׁבַע, H8159 שָׁעָה",
    995: "βοή (boḗ | bo-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G994\nStrong's: a halloo, i.e. call (for aid, etc.)\nKJV: —cry.\n\nSee: G994 \n\nCognate Group: G994 (cry)\nVariants: βοή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1995 הָמֹון, H2201 זַעַק, H6618 פְּתַלְתֹּל, H6963 קֹול, H7524 רֶצַח, H7775 שַׁוְעָה, H8467 תְּחִנָּה",
    996: "βοήθεια (boḗtheia | bo-ay'-thi-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G998\nStrong's: aid; specially, a rope or chain for frapping a vessel\nKJV: —help.\n\nSee: G998 \n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βοήθεια \nHebrew Equivalents: H247 אָזַר, H360 אֱיָלוּת, H4043 מָגֵן, H4679 מְצַד, H5337 נָצַל, H5797 עֹז, H5828 עֵזֶר, H7305 רֶוַח, H7775 שַׁוְעָה, H8454 תּוּשִׁיָּה, H8668 תְּשׁוּעָה",
    997: "βοηθέω (boēthéō | bo-ay-theh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G998\nStrong's: to aid or relieve\nKJV: —help, succor.\n\nSee: G998 \n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βοηθέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2363 חוּשׁ, H2388 חָזַק, H3467 יָשַׁע, H5583 סְעַד, H5756 עוּז, H5826 עָזַר, H5828 עֵזֶר, H5975 עָמַד, H6186 עָרַךְ, H6213 עָשָׂה, H7682 שָׂגַב, H7760 שׂוּם",
    998: "βοηθός (boēthós | bo-ay-thos')\n\nDerivation: from G995 and theo (to run)\nStrong's: a succorer\nKJV: —helper.\n\nSee: G995 \n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βοηθός \nHebrew Equivalents: H247 אָזַר, H3467 יָשַׁע, H4268 מַחֲסֶה, H4869 מִשְׂגָּב, H5643 סֵתֶר, H5797 עֹז, H6697 צוּר",
    999: "βόθυνος (bóthynos | both'-oo-nos)\n\nDerivation: akin to G900\nStrong's: a hole (in the ground); specially, a cistern\nKJV: —ditch, pit.\n\nSee: G900 \n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βόθυνος, βόθρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1460 גֵּו, H4718 מַקֶּבֶת, H6354 פַּחַת, H7845 שַׁחַת",
    1000: "βολή (bolḗ | bol-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G906\nStrong's: a throw (as a measure of distance)\nKJV: —cast.\n\nSee: G906 \n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βολή \nHebrew Equivalents: H2909 טָחָה",
    1001: "βολίζω (bolízō | bol-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1002\nStrong's: to heave the lead\nKJV: —sound.\n\nSee: G1002 \n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βολίζω",
    1002: "βολίς (bolís | bol-ece')\n\nDerivation: from G906\nStrong's: a missile, i.e. javelin\nKJV: —dart.\n\nSee: G906 \n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βολίς G1076 \nHebrew Equivalents: H2671 חֵץ, H3384 יָרָה, H6609 פְּתִחָה, H6791 צֵן, H7973 שֶׁלַח, H7982 שֶׁלֶט",
    1003: "Βοόζ (Boóz | bo-oz')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1162)\nStrong's: Booz, (i.e. Boaz), an Israelite\nKJV: —Booz.\nSee: H1162\n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: Βοόζ, Βόες, Βόος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1162 בֹּעַז",
    1004: "βόρβορος (bórboros | bor'-bor-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: mud\nKJV: —mire.\n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βόρβορος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2916 טִיט",
    1005: "βοῤῥᾶς (borrhâs | bor-hras')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: the north (properly, wind)\nKJV: —north.\n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βοῤῥᾶς, βορρᾶς \nHebrew Equivalents: H6828 צָפֹון",
    1006: "βόσκω (bóskō | bos'-ko)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of a primary verb (compare G977, G1016)\nStrong's: to pasture; by extension to, fodder; reflexively, to graze\nKJV: —feed, keep.\n\nSee: G977 \nSee: G1016 \n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βόσκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7200 רָאָה, H7257 רָבַץ",
    1007: "Βοσόρ (Bosór | bos-or')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1160)\nStrong's: Bosor (i.e. Beor), a Moabite\nKJV: —Bosor.\nSee: H1160\n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: Βοσόρ, Βεώρ, Βεωορσόρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1160 בְּעֹור",
    1008: "βοτάνη (botánē | bot-an'-ay)\n\nDerivation: from G1006\nStrong's: herbage (as if for grazing)\nKJV: —herb.\n\nSee: G1006 \n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βοτάνη \nHebrew Equivalents: H1877 דֶּשֶׁא, H2682 חָצִיר, H6212 עֶשֶׂב",
    1009: "βότρυς (bótrys | bot'-rooce)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a bunch (of grapes)\nKJV: —(vine) cluster (of the vine).\n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βότρυς \nHebrew Equivalents: H811 אֶשְׁכֹּול",
    1010: "βουλευτής (bouleutḗs | bool-yoo-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G1011\nStrong's: an adviser, i.e. (specially) a councillor or member of the Jewish Sanhedrin\nKJV: —counsellor.\n\nSee: G1011 \n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βουλευτής \nHebrew Equivalents: H3289 יָעַץ",
    1011: "βουλεύω (bouleúō | bool-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1012\nStrong's: to advise, i.e. (reflexively) deliberate, or (by implication) resolve\nKJV: —consult, take counsel, determine, be minded, purpose.\n\nSee: G1012 \n\nCognate Group: G998 (helper), G997 (help), G996 (help)\nVariants: βουλεύω, βουλεύομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H213 אוּץ, H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H1580 גָּמַל, H2161 זָמַם, H2656 חֵפֶץ, H2803 חָשַׁב, H3289 יָעַץ, H3559 כּוּן, H4427 מָלַךְ, H5066 נָגַשׁ, H6246 עֲשִׁת",
    1012: "βουλή (boulḗ | boo-lay')\n\nDerivation: from G1014\nStrong's: volition, i.e. (objectively) advice, or (by implication) purpose\nKJV: —+ advise, counsel, will.\n\nSee: G1014 \n\nCognate Group: G1013 (purpose), G1014 (be disposed), G1012 (+ advise)\nVariants: βουλή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1847 דַּעַת, H3289 יָעַץ, H3627 כְּלִי, H4150 מֹועֵד, H4209 מְזִמָּה, H4284 מַחֲשָׁבָה, H4428 מֶלֶךְ, H5475 סֹוד, H6098 עֵצָה, H6110 עַצֻּמָה, H6195 עׇרְמָה, H8454 תּוּשִׁיָּה",
    1013: "βούλημα (boúlēma | boo'-lay-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G1014\nStrong's: a resolve\nKJV: —purpose, will.\n\nSee: G1014 \n\nCognate Group: G1013 (purpose), G1014 (be disposed), G1012 (+ advise)\nVariants: βούλημα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1847 דַּעַת, H1934 הָוָא, H2308 חָדַל, H2530 חָמַד, H2654 חָפֵץ, H2895 טֹוב, H3289 יָעַץ, H3985 מָאֵן, H3988 מָאַס, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5753 עָוָה, H6098 עֵצָה, H6634 צְבָא, H7522 רָצֹון, H7760 שׂוּם, H8458 תַּחְבֻּלָה",
    1014: "βούλομαι (boúlomai | boo'-lom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice of a primary verb\nStrong's: to \"will,\" i.e. (reflexively) be willing\nKJV: —be disposed, minded, intend, list, (be, of own) will (-ing). Compare G2309 .\n\nSee: G2309 \n\nCognate Group: G1013 (purpose), G1014 (be disposed), G1012 (+ advise)\nVariants: βούλομαι",
    1015: "βουνός (bounós | boo-nos')\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: a hillock\nKJV: —hill.\n\nCognate Group: G1013 (purpose), G1014 (be disposed), G1012 (+ advise)\nVariants: βουνός \nHebrew Equivalents: H1116 בָּמָה, H1389 גִּבְעָה, H1530 גַּל, H2022 הַר, H3026 יְגַר שַׂהֲדוּתָא, H6652 צִבֻּר",
    1016: "βοῦς (boûs | booce)\n\nDerivation: probably from the base of G1006\nStrong's: an ox (as grazing), i.e. an animal of that species (\"beef\")\nKJV: —ox.\n\nSee: G1006 \n\nCognate Group: G1013 (purpose), G1014 (be disposed), G1012 (+ advise)\nVariants: βοῦς \nHebrew Equivalents: H441 אַלּוּף, H1241 בָּקָר, H6499 פַּר, H6776 צֶמֶד, H7794 שֹׁור",
    1017: "βραβεῖον (brabeîon | brab-i'-on)\n\nDerivation: from βραβεύς (an umpire of uncertain derivation)\nStrong's: an award (of arbitration), i.e. (specially) a prize in the public games\nKJV: —prize.\n\nCognate Group: G1013 (purpose), G1014 (be disposed), G1012 (+ advise)\nVariants: βραβεῖον",
    1018: "βραβεύω (brabeúō | brab-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G1017\nStrong's: to arbitrate, i.e. (genitive case) to govern (figuratively, prevail)\nKJV: —rule.\n\nSee: G1017 \n\nCognate Group: G1018 (rule), G1817 (raise up)\nVariants: βραβεύω",
    1019: "βραδύνω (bradýnō | brad-oo'-no)\n\nDerivation: from G1021\nStrong's: to delay\nKJV: —be slack, tarry.\n\nSee: G1021 \n\nCognate Group: G1018 (rule), G1817 (raise up)\nVariants: βραδύνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H309 אָחַר, H4102 מָהַהּ",
    1020: "βραδυπλοέω (bradyploéō | brad-oo-plo-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1021 and a prolonged form of G4126\nStrong's: to sail slowly\nKJV: —sail slowly.\n\nSee: G1021 \nSee: G4126 \n\nCognate Group: G1018 (rule), G1817 (raise up)\nVariants: βραδυπλοέω",
    1021: "βραδύς (bradýs | brad-ooce')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: slow; figuratively, dull\nKJV: —slow.\n\nCognate Group: G1018 (rule), G1817 (raise up)\nVariants: βραδύς",
    1022: "βραδύτης (bradýtēs | brad-oo'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G1021\nStrong's: tardiness\nKJV: —slackness.\n\nSee: G1021 \n\nCognate Group: G1018 (rule), G1817 (raise up)\nVariants: βραδύτης, βραδυτής",
    1023: "βραχίων (brachíōn | brakh-ee'-own)\n\nDerivation: properly, comparative of G1024, but apparently in the sense of βράσσω (to wield)\nStrong's: the arm, i.e. (figuratively) strength\nKJV: —arm.\n\nSee: G1024 \n\nCognate Group: G1023 (arm)\nVariants: βραχίων \nHebrew Equivalents: H248 אֶזְרֹועַ, H2220 זְרֹועַ, H3027 יָד, H7785 שֹׁוק",
    1024: "βραχύς (brachýs | brakh-ooce')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: short (of time, place, quantity, or number)\nKJV: —few words, little (space, while).\n\nCognate Group: G1023 (arm)\nVariants: βραχύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H4193 מֹות, H4592 מְעַט, H6996 קָטָן",
    1025: "βρέφος (bréphos | bref'-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: an infant (properly, unborn) literally or figuratively\nKJV: —babe, (young) child, infant.\n\nCognate Group: G1025 (babe), G3516 (babe), G3515 (be a child)\nVariants: βρέφος",
    1026: "βρέχω (bréchō | brekh'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to moisten (especially by a shower)\nKJV: —(send) rain, wash.\n\nCognate Group: G1025 (babe), G3516 (babe), G3515 (be a child)\nVariants: βρέχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2891 טָהֵר, H3381 יָרַד, H4306 מָטַר, H4529 מָסָה, H4549 מָסַס",
    1027: "βροντή (brontḗ | bron-tay')\n\nDerivation: akin to βρέμω (to roar)\nStrong's: thunder\nKJV: —thunder(-ing).\n\nCognate Group: G1027 (thunder)\nVariants: βροντή \nHebrew Equivalents: H7482 רַעַם",
    1028: "βροχή (brochḗ | brokh-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G1026\nStrong's: rain\nKJV: —rain.\n\nSee: G1026 \n\nCognate Group: G1027 (thunder)\nVariants: βροχή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1653 גֶּשֶׁם",
    1029: "βρόχος (bróchos | brokh'-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a noose\nKJV: —snare.\n\nCognate Group: G1027 (thunder)\nVariants: βρόχος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2465 חֶלֶד, H3027 יָד, H4170 מֹוקֵשׁ",
    1030: "βρυγμός (brygmós | broog-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G1031\nStrong's: a grating (of the teeth)\nKJV: —gnashing.\n\nSee: G1031 \n\nCognate Group: G1031 (gnash), G1030 (gnashing)\nVariants: βρυγμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H5098 נָהַם",
    1031: "βρύχω (brýchō | broo'-kho)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to grate the teeth (in pain or rage)\nKJV: —gnash.\n\nCognate Group: G1031 (gnash), G1030 (gnashing)\nVariants: βρύχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2786 חָרַק",
    1032: "βρύω (brýō | broo'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to swell out, i.e. (by implication) to gush\nKJV: —send forth.\n\nCognate Group: G1031 (gnash), G1030 (gnashing)\nVariants: βρύω",
    1033: "βρῶμα (brōma | bro'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G977\nStrong's: food (literally or figuratively), especially (ceremonially) articles allowed or forbidden by the Jewish law\nKJV: —meat, victuals.\n\nSee: G977 \n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: βρῶμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H400 אֹכֶל, H1098 בְּלִיל, H1267 בָּרוּת, H2964 טֶרֶף, H4303 מַטְעַם",
    1034: "βρώσιμος (brṓsimos | bro'-sim-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1035\nStrong's: eatable\nKJV: —meat.\n\nSee: G1035 \n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: βρώσιμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3978 מַאֲכָל",
    1035: "βρῶσις (brōsis | bro'-sis)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G977\nStrong's: (abstractly) eating (literally or figuratively); by extension (concretely) food (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —eating, food, meat.\n\nSee: G977 \n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: βρῶσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H396 אֲכִילָה, H398 אָכַל, H1262 בָּרָה, H3898 לָחַם, H4356 מִכְלָאָה, H6310 פֶּה",
    1036: "βυθίζω (bythízō | boo-thid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1037\nStrong's: to sink; by implication, to drown\nKJV: —begin to sink, drown.\n\nSee: G1037 \n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: βυθίζω",
    1037: "βυθός (bythós | boo-thos')\n\nDerivation: a variation of G899\nStrong's: depth, i.e. (by implication) the sea\nKJV: —deep.\n\nSee: G899 \n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: βυθός \nHebrew Equivalents: H4688 מְצֹולָה, H4688 מְצֹולָה",
    1038: "βυρσεύς (byrseús | boorce-yooce')\n\nDerivation: from βύρσα (a hide)\nStrong's: a tanner\nKJV: —tanner.\n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: βυρσεύς",
    1039: "βύσσινος (býssinos | boos'-see-nos)\n\nDerivation: from G1040\nStrong's: made of linen (neuter a linen cloth)\nKJV: —fine linen.\n\nSee: G1040 \n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: βύσσινος, λευκοβύσσινος \nHebrew Equivalents: H906 בַּד, H948 בּוּץ, H3768 כַּרְפַּס, H8336 שֵׁשׁ",
    1040: "βύσσος (býssos | boos'-sos)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H948)\nStrong's: white linen\nKJV: —fine linen.\nSee: H948\n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: βύσσος \nHebrew Equivalents: H948 בּוּץ, H2353 חוּר, H5466 סָדִין, H8336 שֵׁשׁ",
    1041: "βωμός (bōmós | bo'-mos)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G939\nStrong's: properly, a stand, i.e. (specially) an altar\nKJV: —altar.\n\nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: βωμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H1116 בָּמָה, H4196 מִזְבֵּחַ",
    1042: "γαββαθά (gabbathá | gab-bath-ah')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (compare H1355)\nStrong's: the knoll; gabbatha, a vernacular term for the Roman tribunal in Jerusalem\nKJV: — Gabbatha.\nSee: H1355\n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: γαββαθά, Γαββαθᾶ, Γαββαθα, Γαββαθά \nHebrew Equivalents: H1355 גַּב",
    1043: "Γαβριήλ (Gabriḗl | gab-ree-ale')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1403)\nStrong's: Gabriel, an archangel\nKJV: —Gabriel.\nSee: H1403\n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: Γαβριήλ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1403 גַּבְרִיאֵל",
    1044: "γάγγραινα (gángraina | gang'-grahee-nah)\n\nDerivation: from γραίνω (to gnaw)\nStrong's: an ulcer (\"gangrene\")\nKJV: —canker.\n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: γάγγραινα",
    1045: "Γάδ (Gád | gad)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1410)\nStrong's: Gad, a tribe of Israelites\nKJV: —Gad.\nSee: H1410\n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: Γάδ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1410 גָּד",
    1046: "Γαδαρηνός (Gadarēnós | gad-ar-ay-nos')\n\nDerivation: from Γαδαρά (a town east of the Jordan)\nStrong's: a Gadarene or inhabitant of Gadara\nKJV: —Gadarene.\n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: Γαδαρηνός",
    1047: "γάζα (gáza | gad'-zah)\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: a treasure\nKJV: —treasure.\n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: γάζα, γάζα2",
    1048: "Γάζα (Gáza | gad'-zah)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H5804)\nStrong's: Gazah (i.e. Azzah), a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Gaza.\nSee: H5804\n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: Γάζα, Γάζα1 \nHebrew Equivalents: H1489 גִּזְבָּר, H1596 גְּנַז, H5804 עַזָּה",
    1049: "γαζοφυλάκιον (gazophylákion | gad-zof-oo-lak'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: from G1047 and G5438\nStrong's: a treasure-house, i.e. a court in the temple for the collection-boxes\nKJV: —treasury.\n\nSee: G1047 \nSee: G5438 \n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: γαζοφυλάκιον, γαζοφυλακεῖον/γαζαφυλάκιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1595 גֶּנֶז, H3957 לִשְׁכָּה, H7665 שָׁבַר",
    1050: "Γάϊος (Gáïos | gah'-ee-os)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: Gaius (i.e. Caius), a Christian\nKJV: —Gaius.\n\nCognate Group: G1035 (eating), G1033 (meat)\nVariants: Γάϊος, Γάϊος/Γαῖος",
    1051: "γάλα (gála | gal'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: milk (figuratively)\nKJV: —milk.\n\nCognate Group: G1051 (milk)\nVariants: γάλα \nHebrew Equivalents: H2461 חָלָב",
    1052: "Γαλάτης (Galátēs | gal-at'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G1053\nStrong's: a Galatian or inhabitant of Galatia\nKJV: —Galatian.\n\nSee: G1053 \n\nCognate Group: G1051 (milk)\nVariants: Γαλάτης",
    1053: "Γαλατία (Galatía | gal-at-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Galatia, a region of Asia\nKJV: —Galatia.\n\nCognate Group: G1051 (milk)\nVariants: Γαλατία, Γαλλία",
    1054: "Γαλατικός (Galatikós | gal-at-ee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G1053\nStrong's: Galatic or relating to Galatia\nKJV: —of Galatia.\n\nSee: G1053 \n\nCognate Group: G1051 (milk)\nVariants: Γαλατικός",
    1055: "γαλήνη (galḗnē | gal-ay'-nay)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: tranquillity\nKJV: —calm.\n\nCognate Group: G1051 (milk)\nVariants: γαλήνη",
    1056: "Γαλιλαία (Galilaía | gal-il-ah'-yah)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1551)\nStrong's: Galilæa (i.e. the heathen circle), a region of Palestine\nKJV: —Galilee.\nSee: H1551\n\nCognate Group: G1051 (milk)\nVariants: Γαλιλαία \nHebrew Equivalents: H1551 גָּלִיל",
    1057: "Γαλιλαῖος (Galilaîos | gal-ee-lah'-yos)\n\nDerivation: from G1056\nStrong's: Galilean or belonging to Galilea\nKJV: —Galilean, of Galilee.\n\nSee: G1056 \n\nCognate Group: G1051 (milk)\nVariants: Γαλιλαῖος",
    1058: "Γαλλίων (Gallíōn | gal-lee'-own)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: Gallion (i.e. Gallio), a Roman officer\nKJV: —Gallio.\n\nCognate Group: G1051 (milk)\nVariants: Γαλλίων",
    1059: "Γαμαλιήλ (Gamaliḗl | gam-al-ee-ale')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1583)\nStrong's: Gamaliel (i.e. Gamliel), an Israelite\nKJV: —Gamaliel.\nSee: H1583\n\nCognate Group: G1051 (milk)\nVariants: Γαμαλιήλ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1583 גַּמְלִיאֵל",
    1060: "γαμέω (gaméō | gam-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1062\nStrong's: to wed (of either sex)\nKJV: —marry (a wife).\n\nSee: G1062 \n\nCognate Group: G1060 (marry), G1062 (marriage)\nVariants: γαμέω",
    1061: "γαμίσκω (gamískō | gam-is'-ko)\n\nDerivation: from G1062\nStrong's: to espouse (a daughter to a husband)\nKJV: —give in marriage.\n\nSee: G1062 \n\nCognate Group: G1060 (marry), G1062 (marriage)\nVariants: γαμίσκω, γαμίζω",
    1062: "γάμος (gámos | gam'-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: nuptials\nKJV: —marriage, wedding.\n\nCognate Group: G1060 (marry), G1062 (marriage)\nVariants: γάμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4960 מִשְׁתֶּה",
    1063: "γάρ (gár | gar)\n\nDerivation: a primary particle\nStrong's: properly, assigning a reason (used in argument, explanation or intensification; often with other particles)\nKJV: —and, as, because (that), but, even, for, indeed, no doubt, seeing, then, therefore, verily, what, why, yet.\n\nCognate Group: G1060 (marry), G1062 (marriage)\nVariants: γάρ",
    1064: "γαστήρ (gastḗr | gas-tare')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: the stomach; by analogy, the matrix; figuratively, a gourmand\nKJV: —belly, + with child, womb.\n\nCognate Group: G1060 (marry), G1062 (marriage)\nVariants: γαστήρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H990 בֶּטֶן, H2029 הָרָה, H3179 יָחַם, H5764 עוּל, H7130 קֶרֶב, H7358 רֶחֶם",
    1065: "γέ (gé | gheh)\n\nDerivation: a primary particle of emphasis or qualification (often used with other particles prefixed)\nKJV: —and besides, doubtless, at least, yet.\n\nCognate Group: G1060 (marry), G1062 (marriage)\nVariants: γέ, γε",
    1066: "Γεδεών (Gedeṓn | ghed-eh-own')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1439)\nStrong's: Gedeon (i.e. Gid(e)on), an Israelite\nKJV: —Gedeon (in the King James Version).\nSee: H1439\n\nCognate Group: G1060 (marry), G1062 (marriage)\nVariants: Γεδεών \nHebrew Equivalents: H1439 גִּדְעֹון",
    1067: "γέεννα (géenna | gheh'-en-nah)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1516 and H2011)\nStrong's: valley of (the son of) Hinnom; ge-henna (or Ge-Hinnom), a valley of Jerusalem, used (figuratively) as a name for the place (or state) of everlasting punishment\nKJV: —hell.\nSee: H1516\nSee: H2011\n\nCognate Group: G1067 (hell)\nVariants: γέεννα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1341 גֵּא, H1341 גֵּא, H1341 גֵּא, H1516 גַּיְא, H2011 הִנֹּם",
    1068: "Γεθσημανῆ (Gethsēmanē | gheth-say-man-ay')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (compare H1660 and H8081)\nStrong's: oil-press; Gethsemane, a garden near Jerusalem\nKJV: —Gethsemane.\nSee: H1660\nSee: H8081\n\nCognate Group: G1067 (hell)\nVariants: Γεθσημανῆ, Γεθσημανί \nHebrew Equivalents: H1660 גַּת, H8081 שֶׁמֶן",
    1069: "γείτων (geítōn | ghi'-tone)\n\nDerivation: from G1093\nStrong's: a neighbour (as adjoining one's ground); by implication, a friend\nKJV: —neighbour.\n\nSee: G1093 \n\nCognate Group: G1067 (hell)\nVariants: γείτων \nHebrew Equivalents: H1481 גּוּר, H7934 שָׁכֵן, H7934 שָׁכֵן",
    1070: "γελάω (geláō | ghel-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: to laugh (as a sign of joy or satisfaction)\nKJV: —laugh.\n\nCognate Group: G2606 (laugh to scorn), G1071 (laughter), G1070 (laugh)\nVariants: γελάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6711 צָחַק, H7832 שָׂחַק, H8055 שָׂמַח",
    1071: "γέλως (gélōs | ghel'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1070\nStrong's: laughter (as a mark of gratification)\nKJV: —laughter.\n\nSee: G1070 \n\nCognate Group: G2606 (laugh to scorn), G1071 (laughter), G1070 (laugh)\nVariants: γέλως \nHebrew Equivalents: H6712 צְחֹק, H7814 שְׂחֹוק",
    1072: "γεμίζω (gemízō | ghem-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: transitive from G1073\nStrong's: to fill entirely\nKJV: —fill (be) full.\n\nSee: G1073 \n\nCognate Group: G2606 (laugh to scorn), G1071 (laughter), G1070 (laugh)\nVariants: γεμίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2943 טָעַן",
    1073: "γέμω (gémō | ghem'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to swell out, i.e. be full\nKJV: —be full.\n\nCognate Group: G2606 (laugh to scorn), G1071 (laughter), G1070 (laugh)\nVariants: γέμω \nHebrew Equivalents: H4390 מָלֵא, H5375 נָשָׂא",
    1074: "γενεά (geneá | ghen-eh-ah')\n\nDerivation: from (a presumed derivative of) G1085\nStrong's: a generation; by implication, an age (the period or the persons)\nKJV: —age, generation, nation, time.\n\nSee: G1085 \n\nCognate Group: G1074 (age), G35 (without descent), G1075 (count by descent), G1076 (genealogy)\nVariants: γενεά \nHebrew Equivalents: H410 אֵל, H1755 דֹּור, H2233 זֶרַע, H2567 חָמַשׁ, H3117 יֹום, H3211 יָלִיד, H4940 מִשְׁפָּחָה, H5971 עַם, H7256 רִבֵּעַ, H8029 שִׁלֵּשׁ",
    1075: "γενεαλογέω (genealogéō | ghen-eh-al-og-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1074 and G3056\nStrong's: to reckon by generations, i.e. trace in genealogy\nKJV: —count by descent.\n\nSee: G1074 \nSee: G3056 \n\nCognate Group: G1074 (age), G35 (without descent), G1075 (count by descent), G1076 (genealogy)\nVariants: γενεαλογέω, γενεαλογέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H3187 יָחַשׂ",
    1076: "γενεαλογία (genealogía | ghen-eh-al-og-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G1075\nStrong's: tracing by generations, i.e. \"genealogy\"\nKJV: —genealogy.\n\nSee: G1075 \n\nCognate Group: G1074 (age), G35 (without descent), G1075 (count by descent), G1076 (genealogy)\nVariants: γενεαλογία",
    1077: "γενέσια (genésia | ghen-es'-ee-ah)\n\nDerivation: neuter plural of a derivative of G1078\nStrong's: birthday ceremonies\nKJV: —birthday.\n\nSee: G1078 \n\nCognate Group: G1074 (age), G35 (without descent), G1075 (count by descent), G1076 (genealogy)\nVariants: γενέσια, γενέθλια, γενέθλιος",
    1078: "γένεσις (génesis | ghen'-es-is)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G1074\nStrong's: nativity; figuratively, nature\nKJV: —generation, nature(-ral).\n\nSee: G1074 \n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: γένεσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H1755 דֹּור, H2233 זֶרַע, H3205 יָלַד, H4940 מִשְׁפָּחָה, H5271 נָעוּר, H8435 תֹּולְדָה",
    1079: "γενετή (genetḗ | ghen-et-ay)\n\nDerivation: feminine of a presumed derivative of the base of G1074\nStrong's: birth\nKJV: —birth.\n\nSee: G1074 \n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: γενετή \nHebrew Equivalents: H6133 עֵקֶר",
    1080: "γεννάω (gennáō | ghen-nah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a variation of G1085\nStrong's: to procreate (properly, of the father, but by extension of the mother); figuratively, to regenerate\nKJV: —bear, beget, be born, bring forth, conceive, be delivered of, gender, make, spring.\n\nSee: G1085 \n\nCognate Group: G1084 (they that are born), G1080 (bear), G313 (beget), G738 (new born), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: γεννάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3 אֵב, H1249 בַּר, H1416 גְּדוּד, H2981 יְבוּל, H3318 יָצָא, H3384 יָרָה, H4395 מְלֵאָה, H6510 פָּרָה, H8393 תְּבוּאָה, H8570 תְּנוּבָה",
    1081: "γέννημα (génnēma | ghen'-nay-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G1080\nStrong's: offspring; by analogy, produce (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —fruit, generation.\n\nSee: G1080 \n\nCognate Group: G1084 (they that are born), G1080 (bear), G313 (beget), G738 (new born), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: γέννημα, γένημα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1254 בָּרָא, H1431 גָּדַל, H1961 הָיָה, H2029 הָרָה, H2342 חוּל, H3205 יָלַד, H7069 קָנָה, H7760 שׂוּם",
    1082: "Γεννησαρέτ (Gennēsarét | ghen-nay-sar-et')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (compare H3672)\nStrong's: Gennesaret (i.e. Kinnereth), a lake and plain in Palestine\nKJV: —Gennesaret.\nSee: H3672\n\nCognate Group: G1084 (they that are born), G1080 (bear), G313 (beget), G738 (new born), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: Γεννησαρέτ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3672 כִּנְּרֹות",
    1083: "γέννησις (génnēsis | ghen'-nay-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G1080\nStrong's: nativity\nKJV: —birth.\n\nSee: G1080 \n\nCognate Group: G1084 (they that are born), G1080 (bear), G313 (beget), G738 (new born), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: γέννησις G1167 \nHebrew Equivalents: H3205 יָלַד, H4940 מִשְׁפָּחָה",
    1084: "γεννητός (gennētós | ghen-nay-tos')\n\nDerivation: from G1080\nStrong's: born\nKJV: —they that are born.\n\nSee: G1080 \n\nCognate Group: G1084 (they that are born), G1080 (bear), G313 (beget), G738 (new born), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: γεννητός \nHebrew Equivalents: H3205 יָלַד",
    1085: "γένος (génos | ghen'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1096\nStrong's: \"kin\" (abstract or concrete, literal or figurative, individual or collective)\nKJV: —born, country(-man), diversity, generation, kind(-red), nation, offspring, stock.\n\nSee: G1096 \n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: γένος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2177 זַן, H2233 זֶרַע, H2905 טוּר, H4327 מִין, H4940 מִשְׁפָּחָה, H5971 עַם",
    1086: "Γεργεσηνός (Gergesēnós | gher-ghes-ay-nos')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1622)\nStrong's: a Gergesene (i.e. Girgashite) or one of the aborigines of Palestine\nKJV: —Gergesene.\nSee: H1622\n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: Γεργεσηνός, Γερασηνός G1170, G1171 \nHebrew Equivalents: H1622 גִּרְגָּשִׁי",
    1087: "γερουσία (gerousía | gher-oo-see'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1088\nStrong's: the eldership, i.e. (collectively) the Jewish Sanhedrin\nKJV: —senate.\n\nSee: G1088 \n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: γερουσία \nHebrew Equivalents: H2205 זָקֵן",
    1088: "γέρων (gérōn | gher'-own)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity (compare G1094)\nStrong's: aged\nKJV: —old.\n\nSee: G1094 \n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: γέρων \nHebrew Equivalents: H2205 זָקֵן",
    1089: "γεύομαι (geúomai | ghyoo'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to taste; by implication, to eat; figuratively, to experience (good or ill)\nKJV: —eat, taste.\n\nCognate Group: G1089 (eat)\nVariants: γεύομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1104 בָּלַע, H2938 טָעַם, H3938 לָעַט",
    1090: "γεωργέω (geōrgéō | gheh-or-gheh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1092\nStrong's: to till (the soil)\nKJV: —dress.\n\nSee: G1092 \n\nCognate Group: G1089 (eat)\nVariants: γεωργέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6213 עָשָׂה",
    1091: "γεώργιον (geṓrgion | gheh-ore'-ghee-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a (presumed) derivative of G1092\nStrong's: cultivable, i.e. a farm\nKJV: —husbandry.\n\nSee: G1092 \n\nCognate Group: G1089 (eat)\nVariants: γεώργιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H5657 עֲבֻדָּה, H6776 צֶמֶד, H7704 שָׂדֶה",
    1092: "γεωργός (geōrgós | gheh-ore-gos')\n\nDerivation: from G1093 and the base of G2041\nStrong's: a land-worker, i.e. farmer\nKJV: —husbandman.\n\nSee: G1093 \nSee: G2041 \n\nCognate Group: G1089 (eat)\nVariants: γεωργός \nHebrew Equivalents: H157 אָהַב, H376 אִישׁ, H406 אִכָּר, H3009 יָגַב, H5647 עָבַד",
    1093: "γῆ (gē | ghay)\n\nDerivation: contracted from a primary word\nStrong's: soil; by extension a region, or the solid part or the whole of the terrene globe (including the occupants in each application)\nKJV: —country, earth(-ly), ground, land, world.\n\nCognate Group: G1093 (country), G1919 (earthly)\nVariants: γῆ \nHebrew Equivalents: H127 אֲדָמָה, H178 אֹוב, H376 אִישׁ, H776 אֶרֶץ, H841 אֲשַׂרְאֵלָה, H953 בֹּור, H1250 בָּר, H1366 גְּבוּל, H1471 גֹּוי, H1516 גַּיְא, H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H2022 הַר, H2465 חֶלֶד, H2724 חָרָבָה, H3004 יַבָּשָׁה, H4725 מָקֹום, H5892 עִיר, H5971 עַם, H6010 עֵמֶק, H6083 עָפָר, H6160 עֲרָבָה, H6850 צָפַף, H7704 שָׂדֶה, H8397 תֶּבֶל",
    1094: "γῆρας (gēras | ghay'-ras)\n\nDerivation: akin to G1088\nStrong's: senility\nKJV: —old age.\n\nSee: G1088 \n\nCognate Group: G1093 (country), G1919 (earthly)\nVariants: γῆρας \nHebrew Equivalents: H2207 זֹקֶן, H7869 שֵׂיב, H7872 שֵׂיבָה",
    1095: "γηράσκω (gēráskō | ghay-ras'-ko)\n\nDerivation: from G1094\nStrong's: to be senescent\nKJV: —be (wax) old.\n\nSee: G1094 \n\nCognate Group: G1093 (country), G1919 (earthly)\nVariants: γηράσκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1478 גָּוַע, H2204 זָקֵן",
    1096: "γίνομαι (gínomai | ghin'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: a prolongation and middle voice form of a primary verb\nStrong's: to cause to be (\"gen\"-erate), i.e. (reflexively) to become (come into being), used with great latitude (literal, figurative, intensive, etc.)\nKJV: —arise, be assembled, be(-come, -fall, -have self), be brought (to pass), (be) come (to pass), continue, be divided, draw, be ended, fall, be finished, follow, be found, be fulfilled, + God forbid, grow, happen, have, be kept, be made, be married, be ordained to be, partake, pass, be performed, be published, require, seem, be showed, X soon as it was, sound, be taken, be turned, use, wax, will, would, be wrought.\n\nCognate Group: G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)\nVariants: γίνομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H383 אִיתַי, H543 אָמֵן, H935 בֹּוא, H1069 בָּכַר, H1254 בָּרָא, H1934 הָוָא, H1961 הָיָה, H2009 הִנֵּה, H2372 חָזָה, H2421 חָיָה, H2485 חָלִיל, H2734 חָרָה, H3201 יָכֹל, H3205 יָלַד, H3212 יָלַךְ, H3254 יָסַף, H3318 יָצָא, H3335 יָצַר, H3559 כּוּן, H3947 לָקַח, H4058 מָדַד, H4672 מָצָא, H5060 נָגַע, H5075 נְדַד, H5307 נָפַל, H5414 נָתַן, H5647 עָבַד, H5674 עָבַר, H5927 עָלָה, H5953 עָלַל, H5975 עָמַד, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6923 קָדַם, H6965 קוּם, H7136 קָרָה, H7200 רָאָה, H7257 רָבַץ, H7760 שׂוּם, H8085 שָׁמַע",
    1097: "γινώσκω (ginṓskō | ghin-oce'-ko)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of a primary verb\nStrong's: to \"know\" (absolutely) in a great variety of applications and with many implications (as follow, with others not thus clearly expressed)\nKJV: —allow, be aware (of), feel, (have) know(-ledge), perceived, be resolved, can speak, be sure, understand.\n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: γινώσκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H995 בִּין, H2372 חָזָה, H3045 יָדַע, H3259 יָעַד, H3289 יָעַץ, H3615 כָּלָה, H3947 לָקַח, H4672 מָצָא, H5046 נָגַד, H5234 נָכַר, H7200 רָאָה, H8085 שָׁמַע, H8505 תָּכַן",
    1098: "γλεῦκος (gleûkos | glyoo'-kos)\n\nDerivation: akin to G1099\nStrong's: sweet wine, i.e. (properly) must (fresh juice), but used of the more saccharine (and therefore highly inebriating) fermented wine\nKJV: —new wine.\n\nSee: G1099 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: γλεῦκος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3196 יַיִן",
    1099: "γλυκύς (glykýs | gloo-koos')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: sweet (i.e. not bitter nor salt)\nKJV: —sweet, fresh.\n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: γλυκύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H4452 מָלַץ, H4966 מָתֹוק",
    1100: "γλῶσσα (glōssa | gloce-sah')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: the tongue; by implication, a language (specially, one naturally unacquired)\nKJV: —tongue.\n\nCognate Group: G1100 (tongue), G2084 (man of other tongue)\nVariants: γλῶσσα \nHebrew Equivalents: H3519 כָּבֹוד, H3956 לָשֹׁון, H6310 פֶּה, H8193 שָׂפָה",
    1101: "γλωσσόκομον (glōssókomon | gloce-sok'-om-on)\n\nDerivation: from G1100 and the base of G2889\nStrong's: properly, a case (to keep mouthpieces of wind-instruments in) i.e. (by extension) a casket or (specially) purse\nKJV: —bag.\n\nSee: G1100 \nSee: G2889 \n\nCognate Group: G1100 (tongue), G2084 (man of other tongue)\nVariants: γλωσσόκομον \nHebrew Equivalents: H727 אָרֹון",
    1102: "γναφεύς (gnapheús | gnaf-yuce')\n\nDerivation: by variation for a derivative from κνάπτω (to tease cloth)\nStrong's: a cloth-dresser\nKJV: —fuller.\n\nCognate Group: G1100 (tongue), G2084 (man of other tongue)\nVariants: γναφεύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H3526 כָּבַס",
    1103: "γνήσιος (gnḗsios | gnay'-see-os)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G1077\nStrong's: legitimate (of birth), i.e. genuine\nKJV: —own, sincerity, true.\n\nSee: G1077 \n\nCognate Group: G1103 (own)\nVariants: γνήσιος",
    1104: "γνησίως (gnēsíōs | gnay-see'-ose)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G1103\nStrong's: genuinely, i.e. really\nKJV: —naturally.\n\nSee: G1103 \n\nCognate Group: G1103 (own)\nVariants: γνησίως",
    1105: "γνόφος (gnóphos | gnof'-os)\n\nDerivation: akin to G3509\nStrong's: gloom (as of a storm)\nKJV: —blackness.\n\nSee: G3509 \n\nCognate Group: G1103 (own)\nVariants: γνόφος \nHebrew Equivalents: H651 אָפֵל, H2822 חֹשֶׁךְ, H5492 סוּפָה, H5591 סַעַר, H6049 עָנַן, H6205 עֲרָפֶל",
    1106: "γνώμη (gnṓmē | gno'-may)\n\nDerivation: from G1097\nStrong's: cognition, i.e. (subjectively) opinion, or (objectively) resolve (counsel, consent, etc.)\nKJV: —advice, + agree, judgment, mind, purpose, will.\n\nSee: G1097 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: γνώμη \nHebrew Equivalents: H1881 דָּת, H2940 טַעַם, H2942 טְעֵם, H5475 סֹוד",
    1107: "γνωρίζω (gnōrízō | gno-rid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G1097\nStrong's: to make known; subjectively, to know\nKJV: —certify, declare, make known, give to understand, do to wit, wot.\n\nSee: G1097 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: γνωρίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2324 חֲוָא, H3045 יָדַע, H3259 יָעַד, H5234 נָכַר, H5375 נָשָׂא",
    1108: "γνῶσις (gnōsis | gno'-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G1097\nStrong's: knowing (the act), i.e. (by implication) knowledge\nKJV: —knowledge, science.\n\nSee: G1097 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: γνῶσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H1844 דֵּעָה, H1847 דַּעַת, H3708 כַּעַס",
    1109: "γνώστης (gnṓstēs | gnoce'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G1097\nStrong's: a knower\nKJV: —expert.\n\nSee: G1097 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: γνώστης \nHebrew Equivalents: H3045 יָדַע, H3049 יִדְּעֹנִי",
    1110: "γνωστός (gnōstós | gnoce-tos')\n\nDerivation: from G1097\nStrong's: well-known\nKJV: —acquaintance, (which may be) known, notable.\n\nSee: G1097 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: γνωστός, γνώριμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3045 יָדַע",
    1111: "γογγύζω (gongýzō | gong-good'-zo)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: to grumble\nKJV: —murmur.\n\nCognate Group: G1111 (murmur), G1112 (grudging), G1113 (murmurer), G1234 (murmur)\nVariants: γογγύζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H596 אָנַן, H3869 לוּז, H3885 לוּן, H7279 רָגַן",
    1112: "γογγυσμός (gongysmós | gong-goos-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G1111\nStrong's: a grumbling\nKJV: —grudging, murmuring.\n\nSee: G1111 \n\nCognate Group: G1111 (murmur), G1112 (grudging), G1113 (murmurer), G1234 (murmur)\nVariants: γογγυσμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H205 אָוֶן, H8519 תְּלוּנָה",
    1113: "γογγυστής (gongystḗs | gong-goos-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G1111\nStrong's: a grumbler\nKJV: —murmurer.\n\nSee: G1111 \n\nCognate Group: G1111 (murmur), G1112 (grudging), G1113 (murmurer), G1234 (murmur)\nVariants: γογγυστής",
    1114: "γόης (góēs | go'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from γοάω (to wail)\nStrong's: properly, a wizard (as muttering spells), i.e. (by implication) an imposter\nKJV: —seducer.\n\nCognate Group: G1114 (seducer)\nVariants: γόης",
    1115: "Γολγοθᾶ (Golgothâ | gol-goth-ah')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (compare H1538)\nStrong's: the skull; Golgotha, a knoll near Jerusalem\nKJV: —Golgotha.\nSee: H1538\n\nCognate Group: G1114 (seducer)\nVariants: Γολγοθᾶ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1538 גֻּלְגֹּלֶת",
    1116: "Γόμοῤῥα (Gómorrha | gom'-or-hrhah)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H6017)\nStrong's: Gomorrha (i.e. Amorah), a place near the Dead Sea\nKJV: —Gomorrha.\nSee: H6017\n\nCognate Group: G1114 (seducer)\nVariants: Γόμοῤῥα, Γόμορρα \nHebrew Equivalents: H6017 עֲמֹרָה",
    1117: "γόμος (gómos | gom'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1073\nStrong's: a load (as filling), i.e. (specially) a cargo, or (by extension) wares\nKJV: —burden, merchandise.\n\nSee: G1073 \n\nCognate Group: G1114 (seducer)\nVariants: γόμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4853 מַשָּׂא",
    1118: "γονεύς (goneús | gon-yooce')\n\nDerivation: from the base of G1096\nStrong's: a parent\nKJV: —parent.\n\nSee: G1096 \n\nCognate Group: G1114 (seducer)\nVariants: γονεύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H1 אָב, H517 אֵם",
    1119: "γόνυ (góny | gon-oo')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: the \"knee\"\nKJV: —knee(X -l).\n\nCognate Group: G1119 (knee), G1120 (bow the knee)\nVariants: γόνυ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1290 בֶּרֶךְ, H1290 בֶּרֶךְ, H6915 קָדַד",
    1120: "γονυπετέω (gonypetéō | gon-oo-pet-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1119 and the alternate of G4098\nStrong's: to fall on the knee\nKJV: —bow the knee, kneel down.\n\nSee: G1119 \nSee: G4098 \n\nCognate Group: G1119 (knee), G1120 (bow the knee)\nVariants: γονυπετέω",
    1121: "γράμμα (grámma | gram'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G1125\nStrong's: a writing, i.e. a letter, note, epistle, book, etc.; plural learning\nKJV: —bill, learning, letter, scripture, writing, written.\n\nSee: G1125 \n\nCognate Group: G4270 (before ordain), G1121 (bill), G1124 (scripture), G1123 (written), G5261 (example), G1125 (describe)\nVariants: γράμμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1697 דָּבָר, H3789 כָּתַב, H5612 סֵפֶר",
    1122: "γραμματεύς (grammateús | gram-mat-yooce')\n\nDerivation: from G1121 . a writer, i.e. (professionally) scribe or secretary\nKJV: —scribe, town-clerk.\n\nSee: G1121 \n\nCognate Group: G1122 (scribe)\nVariants: γραμματεύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H1697 דָּבָר, H5608 סָפַר, H5921 עַל, H6213 עָשָׂה, H7860 שֹׁטֵר, H8200 שְׁפַט",
    1123: "γραπτός (graptós | grap-tos')\n\nDerivation: from G1125\nStrong's: inscribed (figuratively)\nKJV: —written.\n\nSee: G1125 \n\nCognate Group: G4270 (before ordain), G1121 (bill), G1124 (scripture), G1123 (written), G5261 (example), G1125 (describe)\nVariants: γραπτός \nHebrew Equivalents: H4385 מִכְתָּב",
    1124: "γραφή (graphḗ | graf-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G1125\nStrong's: a document, i.e. holy Writ (or its contents or a statement in it)\nKJV: —scripture.\n\nSee: G1125 \n\nCognate Group: G4270 (before ordain), G1121 (bill), G1124 (scripture), G1123 (written), G5261 (example), G1125 (describe)\nVariants: γραφή \nHebrew Equivalents: H3789 כָּתַב, H3791 כָּתָב, H4097 מִדְרָשׁ",
    1125: "γράφω (gráphō | graf'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to \"grave\", especially to write; figuratively, to describe\nKJV: —describe, write(-ing, -ten).\n\nCognate Group: G4270 (before ordain), G1121 (bill), G1124 (scripture), G1123 (written), G5261 (example), G1125 (describe)\nVariants: γράφω, καταγράφω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1881 דָּת, H2710 חָקַק, H3789 כָּתַב, H3789 כָּתַב, H5927 עָלָה, H7049 קָלַע, H7760 שׂוּם",
    1126: "γραώδης (graṓdēs | grah-o'-dace)\n\nDerivation: from γραύς (an old woman) and G1491\nStrong's: crone-like, i.e. silly\nKJV: —old wives'.\n\nSee: G1491 \n\nCognate Group: G4270 (before ordain), G1121 (bill), G1124 (scripture), G1123 (written), G5261 (example), G1125 (describe)\nVariants: γραώδης",
    1127: "γρηγορεύω (grēgoreúō | gray-gor-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1453\nStrong's: to keep awake, i.e. watch (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —be vigilant, wake, (be) watch(-ful).\n\nSee: G1453 \n\nCognate Group: G1454 (resurrection), G1453 (awake), G1127 (be vigilant), G1825 (raise up)\nVariants: γρηγορεύω, γρηγορέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5975 עָמַד, H8245 שָׁקַד",
    1128: "γυμνάζω (gymnázō | goom-nad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1131\nStrong's: to practise naked (in the games), i.e. train (figuratively)\nKJV: —exercise.\n\nSee: G1131 \n\nCognate Group: G1131 (naked), G1128 (exercise), G1129 (exercise), G1132 (nakedness)\nVariants: γυμνάζω",
    1129: "γυμνασία (gymnasía | goom-nas-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1128\nStrong's: training, i.e. (figuratively) asceticism\nKJV: —exercise.\n\nSee: G1128 \n\nCognate Group: G1131 (naked), G1128 (exercise), G1129 (exercise), G1132 (nakedness)\nVariants: γυμνασία",
    1130: "γυμνητεύω (gymnēteúō | goom-nayt-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G1131\nStrong's: to strip, i.e. (reflexively) go poorly clad\nKJV: —be naked.\n\nSee: G1131 \n\nCognate Group: G1131 (naked), G1128 (exercise), G1129 (exercise), G1132 (nakedness)\nVariants: γυμνητεύω, γυμνιτεύω",
    1131: "γυμνός (gymnós | goom-nos')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: nude (absolute or relative, literal or figurative)\nKJV: —naked.\n\nCognate Group: G1131 (naked), G1128 (exercise), G1129 (exercise), G1132 (nakedness)\nVariants: γυμνός \nHebrew Equivalents: H779 אָרַר, H1097 בְּלִי, H2513 חֶלְקָה, H4636 מַעֲרֹם, H6174 עָרֹום",
    1132: "γυμνότης (gymnótēs | goom-not'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G1131\nStrong's: nudity (absolute or comparative)\nKJV: —nakedness.\n\nSee: G1131 \n\nCognate Group: G1131 (naked), G1128 (exercise), G1129 (exercise), G1132 (nakedness)\nVariants: γυμνότης \nHebrew Equivalents: H5903 עֵירֹם",
    1133: "γυναικάριον (gynaikárion | goo-nahee-kar'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: a diminutive from G1135\nStrong's: a little (i.e. foolish) woman\nKJV: —silly woman.\n\nSee: G1135 \n\nCognate Group: G1133 (silly woman), G1135 (wife), G1134 (wife)\nVariants: γυναικάριον",
    1134: "γυναικεῖος (gynaikeîos | goo-nahee-ki'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1135\nStrong's: feminine\nKJV: —wife.\n\nSee: G1135 \n\nCognate Group: G1133 (silly woman), G1135 (wife), G1134 (wife)\nVariants: γυναικεῖος \nHebrew Equivalents: H734 אֹרַח, H802 אִשָּׁה",
    1135: "γυνή (gynḗ | goo-nay')\n\nDerivation: probably from the base of G1096\nStrong's: a woman; specially, a wife\nKJV: —wife, woman.\n\nSee: G1096 \n\nCognate Group: G1133 (silly woman), G1135 (wife), G1134 (wife)\nVariants: γυνή \nHebrew Equivalents: H802 אִשָּׁה, H954 בּוּשׁ, H1323 בַּת, H2114 זוּר, H2860 חָתָן, H2994 יְבֵמֶת, H2994 יְבֵמֶת, H3205 יָלַד, H4436 מַלְכָּה, H5039 נְבָלָה, H5291 נַעֲרָה, H5375 נָשָׂא, H6370 פִּילֶגֶשׁ, H7468 רְעוּת, H8198 שִׁפְחָה",
    1136: "Γώγ (Gṓg | gogue)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1463)\nStrong's: Gog, a symbolic name for some future Antichrist\nKJV: —Gog.\nSee: H1463\n\nCognate Group: G1136 (Gog)\nVariants: Γώγ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1463 גֹּוג, H4031 מָגֹוג",
    1137: "γωνία (gōnía | go-nee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: probably akin to G1119\nStrong's: an angle\nKJV: —corner, quarter.\n\nSee: G1119 \n\nCognate Group: G204 (chief corner), G1137 (corner)\nVariants: γωνία \nHebrew Equivalents: H3802 כָּתֵף, H4740 מַקְצֹועַ, H6438 פִּנָּה",
    1138: "Δαβίδ (Dabíd | dab-eed')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1732)\nStrong's: Dabid (i.e. David), the Israelite king\nKJV: —David.\nSee: H1732\n\nCognate Group: G204 (chief corner), G1137 (corner)\nVariants: Δαβίδ, Δαυίδ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1732 דָּוִד",
    1139: "δαιμονίζομαι (daimonízomai | dahee-mon-id'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1142\nStrong's: to be exercised by a dæmon\nKJV: —have a (be vexed with, be possessed with) devil(-s).\n\nSee: G1142 \n\nCognate Group: G1141 (devilish), G1140 (devil), G1139 (have a devil), G1142 (devil)\nVariants: δαιμονίζομαι",
    1140: "δαιμόνιον (daimónion | dahee-mon'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a derivative of G1142\nStrong's: a dæmonic being; by extension a deity\nKJV: —devil, god.\n\nSee: G1142 \n\nCognate Group: G1141 (devilish), G1140 (devil), G1139 (have a devil), G1142 (devil)\nVariants: δαιμόνιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H457 אֱלִיל, H1408 גַּד, H6728 צִיִּי, H7700 שֵׁד, H8163 שָׂעִיר",
    1141: "δαιμονιώδης (daimoniṓdēs | dahee-mon-ee-o'-dace)\n\nDerivation: from G1140 and G1142\nStrong's: dæmon-like\nKJV: —devilish.\n\nSee: G1140 \nSee: G1142 \n\nCognate Group: G1141 (devilish), G1140 (devil), G1139 (have a devil), G1142 (devil)\nVariants: δαιμονιώδης",
    1142: "δαίμων (daímōn | dah'-ee-mown)\n\nDerivation: from δαίω (to distribute fortunes)\nStrong's: a dæmon or supernatural spirit (of a bad nature)\nKJV: —devil.\n\nCognate Group: G1141 (devilish), G1140 (devil), G1139 (have a devil), G1142 (devil)\nVariants: δαίμων \nHebrew Equivalents: H1408 גַּד",
    1143: "δάκνω (dáknō | dak'-no)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of a primary root\nStrong's: to bite, i.e. (figuratively) thwart\nKJV: —bite.\n\nCognate Group: G1141 (devilish), G1140 (devil), G1139 (have a devil), G1142 (devil)\nVariants: δάκνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5391 נָשַׁךְ, H8313 שָׂרַף",
    1144: "δάκρυ (dákry | dak'-roo) or δάκρυον (dákryon | dak'-roo-on)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a tear\nKJV: —tear.\n\nCognate Group: G1141 (devilish), G1140 (devil), G1139 (have a devil), G1142 (devil)\nVariants: δάκρυ, δάκρυον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1832 דִּמְעָה, H5198 נָטָף",
    1145: "δακρύω (dakrýō | dak-roo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1144\nStrong's: to shed tears\nKJV: —weep. Compare G2799 .\n\nSee: G1144 \nSee: G2799 \n\nCognate Group: G1141 (devilish), G1140 (devil), G1139 (have a devil), G1142 (devil)\nVariants: δακρύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1058 בָּכָה, H5198 נָטָף, H5413 נָתַךְ, H7481 רָעַם",
    1146: "δακτύλιος (daktýlios | dak-too'-lee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1147\nStrong's: a finger-ring\nKJV: —ring.\n\nSee: G1147 \n\nCognate Group: G1141 (devilish), G1140 (devil), G1139 (have a devil), G1142 (devil)\nVariants: δακτύλιος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2885 טַבַּעַת, H5824 עִזְקָא",
    1147: "δάκτυλος (dáktylos | dak'-too-los)\n\nDerivation: probably from G1176\nStrong's: a finger\nKJV: —finger.\n\nSee: G1176 \n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: δάκτυλος \nHebrew Equivalents: H676 אֶצְבַּע, H3027 יָד, H3709 כַּף, H6995 קֹטֶן",
    1148: "Δαλμανουθά (Dalmanouthá | dal-man-oo-thah')\n\nDerivation: probably of Chaldee origin\nStrong's: Dalmanutha, a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Dalmanutha.\n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: Δαλμανουθά",
    1149: "Δαλματία (Dalmatía | dal-mat-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign derivation\nStrong's: Dalmatia, a region of Europe\nKJV: —Dalmatia.\n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: Δαλματία",
    1150: "δαμάζω (damázō | dam-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: a variation of an obsolete primary of the same meaning\nStrong's: to tame\nKJV: —tame.\n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: δαμάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2827 חֲשַׁל, H7453 רֵעַ",
    1151: "δάμαλις (dámalis | dam'-al-is)\n\nDerivation: probably from the base of G1150\nStrong's: a heifer (as tame)\nKJV: —heifer.\n\nSee: G1150 \n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: δάμαλις \nHebrew Equivalents: H1241 בָּקָר, H5695 עֵגֶל, H5697 עֶגְלָה, H6499 פַּר, H6510 פָּרָה",
    1152: "Δάμαρις (Dámaris | dam'-ar-is)\n\nDerivation: probably from the base of G1150\nStrong's: perhaps gentle; Damaris, an Athenian woman\nKJV: —Damaris.\n\nSee: G1150 \n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: Δάμαρις",
    1153: "Δαμασκηνός (Damaskēnós | dam-as-kay-nos')\n\nDerivation: from G1154\nStrong's: a Damascene or inhabitant of Damascus\nKJV: —Damascene.\n\nSee: G1154 \n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: Δαμασκηνός",
    1154: "Δαμασκός (Damaskós | dam-as-kos')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1834)\nStrong's: Damascus, a city of Syria\nKJV: —Damascus.\nSee: H1834\n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: Δαμασκός \nHebrew Equivalents: H1834 דַּמֶּשֶׂק",
    1155: "δανείζω (daneízō | dan-ide'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1156\nStrong's: to loan on interest; reflexively, to borrow\nKJV: —borrow, lend.\n\nSee: G1156 \n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: δανείζω, δανίζω, δαν(ε)ίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3867 לָוָה, H5791 עָוַת, H7592 שָׁאַל",
    1156: "δάνειον (dáneion | dan'-i-on)\n\nDerivation: from δάνος (a gift)\nStrong's: probably akin to the base of G1325 ; a loan\nKJV: —debt.\n\nSee: G1325 \n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: δάνειον, δάνιον, δάν(ε)ιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H5382 נָשָׁה, H5791 עָוַת",
    1157: "δανειστής (daneistḗs | dan-ice-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G1155\nStrong's: a lender\nKJV: —creditor.\n\nSee: G1155 \n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: δανειστής, δανιστής, δαν(ε)ιστής \nHebrew Equivalents: H5382 נָשָׁה, H7218 רֹאשׁ",
    1158: "Δανιήλ (Daniḗl | dan-ee-ale')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1840)\nStrong's: Daniel, an Israelite\nKJV: —Daniel.\nSee: H1840\n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: Δανιήλ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1840 דָנִיֵּאל",
    1159: "δαπανάω (dapanáō | dap-an-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1160\nStrong's: to expend, i.e. (in a good sense) to incur cost, or (in a bad one) to waste\nKJV: —be at charges, consume, spend.\n\nSee: G1160 \n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: δαπανάω",
    1160: "δαπάνη (dapánē | dap-an'-ay)\n\nDerivation: from δάπτω (to devour)\nStrong's: expense (as consuming)\nKJV: —cost.\n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: δαπάνη \nHebrew Equivalents: H5313 נִפְקָא",
    1161: "δέ (dé | deh)\n\nDerivation: a primary particle (adversative or continuative)\nStrong's: but, and, etc.\nKJV: —also, and, but, moreover, now (often unexpressed in English).\n\nCognate Group: G1147 (finger)\nVariants: δέ",
    1162: "δέησις (déēsis | deh'-ay-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G1189\nStrong's: a petition\nKJV: —prayer, request, supplication.\n\nSee: G1189 \n\nCognate Group: G1189 (beseech), G1162 (prayer), G4326 (need)\nVariants: δέησις \nHebrew Equivalents: H782 אֲרֶשֶׁת, H6039 עֱנוּת, H6618 פְּתַלְתֹּל, H7309 רְוָחָה, H7440 רִנָּה, H7769 שׁוּעַ, H7879 שִׂיחַ, H8467 תְּחִנָּה, H8605 תְּפִלָּה",
    1163: "δεῖ (deî | die)\n\nDerivation: 3rd person singular active present of G1210\nStrong's: also deon deh-on'; neuter active participle of the same; both used impersonally; it is (was, etc.) necessary (as binding)\nKJV: —behoved, be meet, must (needs), (be) need(-ful), ought, should.\n\nSee: G1210 \n\nCognate Group: G1163 (behoved)\nVariants: δεῖ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3899 לֶחֶם, H6595 פַּת, H7607 שְׁאֵר",
    1164: "δεῖγμα (deîgma | digh'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G1166\nStrong's: a specimen (as shown)\nKJV: —example.\n\nSee: G1166 \n\nCognate Group: G1163 (behoved)\nVariants: δεῖγμα",
    1165: "δειγματίζω (deigmatízō | digh-mat-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1164\nStrong's: to exhibit\nKJV: —make a shew.\n\nSee: G1164 \n\nCognate Group: G5262 (en-ample), G323 (shewing), G1166 (shew), G3856 (make a public example), G322 (appoint), G1165 (make a shew)\nVariants: δειγματίζω",
    1166: "δεικνύω (deiknýō | dike-noo'-o)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of an obsolete primary of the same meaning\nStrong's: to show (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —shew.\n\nCognate Group: G5262 (en-ample), G323 (shewing), G1166 (shew), G3856 (make a public example), G322 (appoint), G1165 (make a shew)\nVariants: δεικνύω, δείκνυμι, δείκνυμι/δεικνύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1254 בָּרָא, H1540 גָּלָה, H3045 יָדַע, H3318 יָצָא, H3384 יָרָה, H3920 לָכַד, H3925 לָמַד, H5046 נָגַד, H5148 נָחָה, H5414 נָתַן, H6186 עָרַךְ, H7200 רָאָה",
    1167: "δειλία (deilía | di-lee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1169\nStrong's: timidity\nKJV: —fear.\n\nSee: G1169 \n\nCognate Group: G5262 (en-ample), G323 (shewing), G1166 (shew), G3856 (make a public example), G322 (appoint), G1165 (make a shew)\nVariants: δειλία \nHebrew Equivalents: H367 אֵימָה, H4288 מְחִתָּה, H4816 מֹרֶךְ, H6103 עַצְלָה",
    1168: "δειλιάω (deiliáō | di-lee-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1167\nStrong's: to be timid\nKJV: —be afraid.\n\nSee: G1167 \n\nCognate Group: G5262 (en-ample), G323 (shewing), G1166 (shew), G3856 (make a public example), G322 (appoint), G1165 (make a shew)\nVariants: δειλιάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2648 חָפַז, H2865 חָתַת, H4549 מָסַס, H5110 נוּד, H6206 עָרַץ, H6342 פָּחַד",
    1169: "δειλός (deilós | di-los')\n\nDerivation: from δεός (dread)\nStrong's: timid, i.e. (by implication) faithless\nKJV: —fearful.\n\nCognate Group: G5262 (en-ample), G323 (shewing), G1166 (shew), G3856 (make a public example), G322 (appoint), G1165 (make a shew)\nVariants: δειλός \nHebrew Equivalents: H2730 חָרֵד, H3372 יָרֵא, H7390 רַךְ",
    1170: "δεῖνα (deîna | di'-nah)\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as G1171 (through the idea of forgetting the name as fearful, i.e. strange)\nStrong's: so and so (when the person is not specified)\nKJV: —such a man.\n\nSee: G1171 \n\nCognate Group: G5262 (en-ample), G323 (shewing), G1166 (shew), G3856 (make a public example), G322 (appoint), G1165 (make a shew)\nVariants: δεῖνα",
    1171: "δεινῶς (deinōs | di-noce')\n\nDerivation: adverb from a derivative of the same as G1169\nStrong's: terribly, i.e. excessively\nKJV: —grievously, vehemently.\n\nSee: G1169 \n\nCognate Group: G5262 (en-ample), G323 (shewing), G1166 (shew), G3856 (make a public example), G322 (appoint), G1165 (make a shew)\nVariants: δεινῶς",
    1172: "δειπνέω (deipnéō | dipe-neh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1173\nStrong's: to dine, i.e. take the principle (or evening) meal\nKJV: —sup (X -er).\n\nSee: G1173 \n\nCognate Group: G1173 (feast), G1172 (sup)\nVariants: δειπνέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3898 לָחַם",
    1173: "δεῖπνον (deîpnon | dipe'-non)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G1160\nStrong's: dinner, i.e. the chief meal (usually in the evening)\nKJV: —feast, supper.\n\nSee: G1160 \n\nCognate Group: G1173 (feast), G1172 (sup)\nVariants: δεῖπνον, δεῖπνος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3899 לֶחֶם, H6595 פַּת",
    1174: "δεισιδαιμονέστερος (deisidaimonésteros | dice-ee-dahee-mon-es'-ter-os)\n\nDerivation: the compound of a derivative of the base of G1169 and G1142\nStrong's: more religious than others\nKJV: —too superstitious.\n\nSee: G1169 \nSee: G1142 \n\nCognate Group: G1173 (feast), G1172 (sup)\nVariants: δεισιδαιμονέστερος, δεισιδαίμων",
    1175: "δεισιδαιμονία (deisidaimonía | dice-ee-dahee-mon-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G1174\nStrong's: religion\nKJV: —superstition.\n\nSee: G1174 \n\nCognate Group: G1175 (superstition)\nVariants: δεισιδαιμονία",
    1176: "δέκα (déka | dek'-ah)\n\nDerivation: a primary number\nStrong's: ten\nKJV: —(eight-)een, ten.\n\nCognate Group: G1176 (een)\nVariants: δέκα, δεκαέξ, δεκαοκτώ",
    1177: "δεκαδύο (dekadýo | dek-ad-oo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1176 and G1417\nStrong's: two and ten, i.e. twelve\nKJV: —twelve.\n\nSee: G1176 \nSee: G1417 \n\nCognate Group: G1176 (een)\nVariants: δεκαδύο G1275, G1277",
    1178: "δεκαπέντε (dekapénte | dek-ap-en'-teh)\n\nDerivation: from G1176 and G4002\nStrong's: ten and five, i.e. fifteen\nKJV: —fifteen.\n\nSee: G1176 \nSee: G4002 \n\nCognate Group: G1176 (een)\nVariants: δεκαπέντε",
    1179: "Δεκάπολις (Dekápolis | dek-ap'-ol-is)\n\nDerivation: from G1176 and G4172\nStrong's: the ten-city region; the Decapolis, a district in Syria\nKJV: —Decapolis.\n\nSee: G1176 \nSee: G4172 \n\nCognate Group: G1176 (een)\nVariants: Δεκάπολις",
    1180: "δεκατέσσαρες (dekatéssares | dek-at-es'-sar-es)\n\nDerivation: from G1176 and G5064\nStrong's: ten and four, i.e. fourteen\nKJV: —fourteen.\n\nSee: G1176 \nSee: G5064 \n\nCognate Group: G1176 (een)\nVariants: δεκατέσσαρες",
    1181: "δεκάτη (dekátē | dek-at'-ay)\n\nDerivation: feminine of G1182\nStrong's: a tenth, i.e. as a percentage or (technically) tithe\nKJV: —tenth (part), tithe.\n\nSee: G1182 \n\nCognate Group: G1176 (een)\nVariants: δεκάτη, δέκατος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4643 מַעֲשֵׂר, H6218 עָשֹׂור",
    1182: "δέκατος (dékatos | dek'-at-os)\n\nDerivation: ordinal from G1176\nStrong's: tenth\nKJV: —tenth.\n\nSee: G1176 \n\nCognate Group: G1176 (een)\nVariants: δέκατος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4643 מַעֲשֵׂר, H6218 עָשֹׂור",
    1183: "δεκατόω (dekatóō | dek-at-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1181\nStrong's: to tithe, i.e. to give or take a tenth\nKJV: —pay (receive) tithes.\n\nSee: G1181 \n\nCognate Group: G1176 (een)\nVariants: δεκατόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6237 עָשַׂר",
    1184: "δεκτός (dektós | dek-tos')\n\nDerivation: from G1209\nStrong's: approved; (figuratively) propitious\nKJV: — accepted(-table).\n\nSee: G1209 \n\nCognate Group: G1403 (feast), G1209 (accept), G1184 (accepted), G553 (look for), G1523 (receive), G587 (acceptable), G588 (accept), G2144 (acceptable), G4327 (accept), G594 (acceptation), G1561 (looking for)\nVariants: δεκτός \nHebrew Equivalents: H5414 נָתַן, H7521 רָצָה, H7522 רָצֹון",
    1185: "δελεάζω (deleázō | del-eh-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G1388\nStrong's: to entrap, i.e. (figuratively) delude\nKJV: —allure, beguile, entice.\n\nSee: G1388 \n\nCognate Group: G1403 (feast), G1209 (accept), G1184 (accepted), G553 (look for), G1523 (receive), G587 (acceptable), G588 (accept), G2144 (acceptable), G4327 (accept), G594 (acceptation), G1561 (looking for)\nVariants: δελεάζω",
    1186: "δένδρον (déndron | den'-dron)\n\nDerivation: probably from δρύς (an oak)\nStrong's: a tree\nKJV: —tree.\n\nCognate Group: G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)\nVariants: δένδρον \nHebrew Equivalents: H363 אִילָן, H424 אֵלָה, H437 אַלֹּון, H842 אֲשֵׁרָה, H6086 עֵץ, H6628 צֶאֶל",
    1187: "δεξιολάβος (dexiolábos | dex-ee-ol-ab'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1188 and G2983\nStrong's: a guardsman (as if taking the right) or light-armed soldier\nKJV: —spearman.\n\nSee: G1188 \nSee: G2983 \n\nCognate Group: G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)\nVariants: δεξιολάβος, δεξιοβόλος, δεξιόλαβος",
    1188: "δεξιός (dexiós | dex-ee-os')\n\nDerivation: from G1209\nStrong's: the right side or (feminine) hand (as that which usually takes)\nKJV: —right (hand, side).\n\nSee: G1209 \n\nCognate Group: G1188 (right)\nVariants: δεξιός \nHebrew Equivalents: H575 אָן, H3225 יָמִין",
    1189: "δέομαι (déomai | deh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice of G1210\nStrong's: to beg (as binding oneself), i.e. petition\nKJV: —beseech, pray (to), make request. Compare G4441 .\n\nSee: G1210 \nSee: G4441 \n\nCognate Group: G1189 (beseech), G1162 (prayer), G4326 (need)\nVariants: δέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2603 חָנַן",
    1190: "Δερβαῖος (Derbaîos | der-bah'-ee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1191\nStrong's: a Derbæan or inhabitant of Derbe\nKJV: —of Derbe.\n\nSee: G1191 \n\nCognate Group: G1189 (beseech), G1162 (prayer), G4326 (need)\nVariants: Δερβαῖος, Δουβέριος",
    1191: "Δέρβη (Dérbē | der-bay')\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Derbe, a place in Asia Minor\nKJV: —Derbe.\n\nCognate Group: G1189 (beseech), G1162 (prayer), G4326 (need)\nVariants: Δέρβη",
    1192: "δέρμα (dérma | der'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G1194\nStrong's: a hide\nKJV: —skin.\n\nSee: G1194 \n\nCognate Group: G1189 (beseech), G1162 (prayer), G4326 (need)\nVariants: δέρμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H216 אֹור",
    1193: "δερμάτινος (dermátinos | der-mat'-ee-nos)\n\nDerivation: from G1192\nStrong's: made of hide\nKJV: —leathern, of a skin.\n\nSee: G1192 \n\nCognate Group: G1189 (beseech), G1162 (prayer), G4326 (need)\nVariants: δερμάτινος \nHebrew Equivalents: H216 אֹור",
    1194: "δέρω (dérō | der'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: properly, to flay, i.e. (by implication) to scourge, or (by analogy) to thrash\nKJV: —beat, smite.\n\nCognate Group: G1189 (beseech), G1162 (prayer), G4326 (need)\nVariants: δέρω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6584 פָּשַׁט",
    1195: "δεσμεύω (desmeúō | des-myoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a (presumed) derivative of G1196\nStrong's: to be a binder (captor), i.e. to enchain (a prisoner), to tie on (a load)\nKJV: — bind.\n\nSee: G1196 \n\nCognate Group: G1189 (beseech), G1162 (prayer), G4326 (need)\nVariants: δεσμεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H481 אָלַם, H631 אָסַר, H2254 חָבַל, H2280 חָבַשׁ, H6658 צָדָה, H6887 צָרַר",
    1196: "δεσμέω (desméō | des-meh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1199\nStrong's: to tie, i.e. shackle\nKJV: —bind.\n\nSee: G1199 \n\nCognate Group: G1189 (beseech), G1162 (prayer), G4326 (need)\nVariants: δεσμέω G1298",
    1197: "δέσμη (désmē | des-may')\n\nDerivation: from G1196\nStrong's: a bundle\nKJV: —bundle.\n\nSee: G1196 \n\nCognate Group: G1189 (beseech), G1162 (prayer), G4326 (need)\nVariants: δέσμη \nHebrew Equivalents: H92 אֲגֻדָּה",
    1198: "δέσμιος (désmios | des'-mee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1199\nStrong's: a captive (as bound)\nKJV: —in bonds, prisoner.\n\nSee: G1199 \n\nCognate Group: G1199 (band), G1198 (in bonds)\nVariants: δέσμιος \nHebrew Equivalents: H631 אָסַר",
    1199: "δεσμόν (desmón | des-mon') or δεσμός (desmós | des-mos')\n\nDerivation: neuter and masculine respectively from G1210\nStrong's: a band, i.e. ligament (of the body) or shackle (of a prisoner); figuratively, an impediment or disability\nKJV: —band, bond, chain, string.\n\nSee: G1210 \n\nCognate Group: G1199 (band), G1198 (in bonds)\nVariants: δεσμόν, δεσμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H631 אָסַר, H2336 חֹוחַ, H4133 מֹוטָה, H4525 מַסְגֵּר, H4770 מַרְבֵּק, H5688 עֲבֹת, H5730 עֵדֶן, H6781 צָמִיד, H6872 צְרֹור, H7195 קֶשֶׁר",
    1200: "δεσμοφύλαξ (desmophýlax | des-mof-oo'-lax)\n\nDerivation: from G1199 and G5441\nStrong's: a jailer (as guarding the prisoners)\nKJV: —jailor, keeper of the prison.\n\nSee: G1199 \nSee: G5441 \n\nCognate Group: G1199 (band), G1198 (in bonds)\nVariants: δεσμοφύλαξ",
    1201: "δεσμωτήριον (desmōtḗrion | des-mo-tay'-ree-on)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G1199 (equivalent to G1196)\nStrong's: a place of bondage, i.e. a dungeon\nKJV: —prison.\n\nSee: G1199 \nSee: G1196 \n\nCognate Group: G1199 (band), G1198 (in bonds)\nVariants: δεσμωτήριον \nHebrew Equivalents: H615 אָסִיר, H1004 בַּיִת",
    1202: "δεσμώτης (desmṓtēs | des-mo'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G1201\nStrong's: (passively) a captive\nKJV: —prisoner.\n\nSee: G1201 \n\nCognate Group: G1199 (band), G1198 (in bonds)\nVariants: δεσμώτης \nHebrew Equivalents: H631 אָסַר, H4525 מַסְגֵּר",
    1203: "δεσπότης (despótēs | des-pot'-ace)\n\nDerivation: perhaps from G1210 and πόσις (a husband)\nStrong's: an absolute ruler (\"despot\")\nKJV: —Lord, master.\n\nSee: G1210 \n\nCognate Group: G1203 (Lord), G3617 (goodman), G3616 (guide the house)\nVariants: δεσπότης \nHebrew Equivalents: H113 אָדֹון, H136 אֲדֹנָי, H433 אֱלֹוהַּ, H3068 יְהֹוָה, H4911 מָשַׁל",
    1204: "δεῦρο (deûro | dyoo'-ro)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: here; used also imperative hither!; and of time, hitherto\nKJV: —come (hither), hither(-to).\n\nCognate Group: G1203 (Lord), G3617 (goodman), G3616 (guide the house)\nVariants: δεῦρο \nHebrew Equivalents: H3212 יָלַךְ, H3212 יָלַךְ",
    1205: "δεῦτε (deûte | dyoo'-teh)\n\nDerivation: from G1204 and an imperative form of εἶμι (to go)\nStrong's: come hither!\nKJV: —come, X follow.\n\nSee: G1204 \n\nCognate Group: G1203 (Lord), G3617 (goodman), G3616 (guide the house)\nVariants: δεῦτε \nHebrew Equivalents: H3212 יָלַךְ",
    1206: "δευτεραῖος (deuteraîos | dyoo-ter-ah'-yos)\n\nDerivation: from G1208\nStrong's: secondary, i.e. (specially) on the second day\nKJV: —next day.\n\nSee: G1208 \n\nCognate Group: G1203 (Lord), G3617 (goodman), G3616 (guide the house)\nVariants: δευτεραῖος",
    1207: "δευτερόπρωτος (deuteróprōtos | dyoo-ter-op'-ro-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1208 and G4413\nStrong's: second-first, i.e. (specially) a designation of the Sabbath immediately after the Paschal week (being the second after Passover day, and the first of the seven Sabbaths intervening before Pentecost)\nKJV: —second … after the first.\n\nSee: G1208 \nSee: G4413 \n\nCognate Group: G1203 (Lord), G3617 (goodman), G3616 (guide the house)\nVariants: δευτερόπρωτος G1310",
    1208: "δεύτερος (deúteros | dyoo'-ter-os)\n\nDerivation: as the comparative of G1417\nStrong's: (ordinal) second (in time, place, or rank; also adverb)\nKJV: —afterward, again, second(-arily, time).\n\nSee: G1417 \n\nCognate Group: G1203 (Lord), G3617 (goodman), G3616 (guide the house)\nVariants: δεύτερος, δεύτερον",
    1209: "δέχομαι (déchomai | dekh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice of a primary verb\nStrong's: to receive (in various applications, literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —accept, receive, take. Compare G2983 .\n\nSee: G2983 \n\nCognate Group: G1403 (feast), G1209 (accept), G1184 (accepted), G553 (look for), G1523 (receive), G587 (acceptable), G588 (accept), G2144 (acceptable), G4327 (accept), G594 (acceptation), G1561 (looking for)\nVariants: δέχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2236 זָרַק, H2388 חָזַק, H3557 כּוּל, H3947 לָקַח, H5375 נָשָׂא, H6901 קָבַל, H7521 רָצָה, H7725 שׁוּב",
    1210: "δέω (déō | deh'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to bind (in various applications, literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —bind, be in bonds, knit, tie, wind. See also G1163, G1189 .\n\nSee: G1163 \nSee: G1189 \n\nCognate Group: G1210 (bind)\nVariants: δέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H631 אָסַר, H2280 חָבַשׁ, H3808 לֹא, H6113 עָצָר, H6696 צוּר, H7194 קָשַׁר, H7576 רָתַק, H7760 שׂוּם",
    1211: "δή (dḗ | day)\n\nDerivation: probably akin to G1161\nStrong's: a particle of emphasis or explicitness; now, then, etc.\nKJV: —also, and, doubtless, now, therefore.\n\nSee: G1161 \n\nCognate Group: G1210 (bind)\nVariants: δή",
    1212: "δῆλος (dēlos | day'-los)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: clear\nKJV: —+ bewray, certain, evident, manifest.\n\nCognate Group: G1210 (bind)\nVariants: δῆλος \nHebrew Equivalents: H217 אוּר, H8537 תֹּם, H8655 תְּרָפִים",
    1213: "δηλόω (dēlóō | day-lo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1212\nStrong's: to make plain (by words)\nKJV: —declare, shew, signify.\n\nSee: G1212 \n\nCognate Group: G1213 (declare)\nVariants: δηλόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1541 גְּלָה, H2324 חֲוָא, H3045 יָדַע, H3384 יָרָה, H7200 רָאָה, H8085 שָׁמַע",
    1214: "Δημᾶς (Dēmâs | day-mas')\n\nDerivation: probably for G1216\nStrong's: Demas, a Christian\nKJV: —Demas.\n\nSee: G1216 \n\nCognate Group: G1213 (declare)\nVariants: Δημᾶς",
    1215: "δημηγορέω (dēmēgoréō | day-may-gor-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1218 and G58\nStrong's: to be a people-gatherer, i.e. to address a public assembly\nKJV: —make an oration.\n\nSee: G1218 \nSee: G58 \n\nCognate Group: G1213 (declare)\nVariants: δημηγορέω",
    1216: "Δημήτριος (Dēmḗtrios | day-may'-tree-os)\n\nDerivation: from Δημήτηρ (Ceres)\nStrong's: Demetrius, the name of an Ephesian and of a Christian\nKJV: —Demetrius.\n\nCognate Group: G1213 (declare)\nVariants: Δημήτριος",
    1217: "δημιουργός (dēmiourgós | day-me-oor-gos')\n\nDerivation: from G1218 and G2041\nStrong's: a worker for the people, i.e. mechanic (spoken of the Creator)\nKJV: —maker.\n\nSee: G1218 \nSee: G2041 \n\nCognate Group: G1217 (maker)\nVariants: δημιουργός",
    1218: "δῆμος (dēmos | day'-mos)\n\nDerivation: from G1210\nStrong's: the public (as bound together socially)\nKJV: —people.\n\nSee: G1210 \n\nCognate Group: G3927 (pilgrim), G1218 (people), G1553 (be absent), G1736 (be at home)\nVariants: δῆμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4940 מִשְׁפָּחָה, H5971 עַם, H7255 רֹבַע, H7626 שֵׁבֶט",
    1219: "δημόσιος (dēmósios | day-mos'ee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1218\nStrong's: public; (feminine singular dative case as adverb) in public\nKJV: —common, openly, publickly.\n\nSee: G1218 \n\nCognate Group: G3927 (pilgrim), G1218 (people), G1553 (be absent), G1736 (be at home)\nVariants: δημόσιος",
    1220: "δηνάριον (dēnárion | day-nar'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: a denarius (or ten asses)\nKJV: —pence, penny(-worth).\n\nCognate Group: G3927 (pilgrim), G1218 (people), G1553 (be absent), G1736 (be at home)\nVariants: δηνάριον",
    1221: "δήποτε (dḗpote | day'-pot-eh)\n\nDerivation: from G1211 and G4218\nStrong's: a particle of generalization; indeed, at any time\nKJV: —(what-)soever.\n\nSee: G1211 \nSee: G4218 \n\nCognate Group: G3927 (pilgrim), G1218 (people), G1553 (be absent), G1736 (be at home)\nVariants: δήποτε G1325",
    1222: "δήπου (dḗpou | day'-poo)\n\nDerivation: from G1211 and G4225\nStrong's: a particle of asseveration; indeed doubtless\nKJV: —verily.\n\nSee: G1211 \nSee: G4225 \n\nCognate Group: G3927 (pilgrim), G1218 (people), G1553 (be absent), G1736 (be at home)\nVariants: δήπου",
    1223: "διά (diá | dee-ah')\n\nDerivation: a primary preposition denoting the channel of an act\nStrong's: through (in very wide applications, local, causal, or occasional)\nKJV: —after, always, among, at, to avoid, because of (that), briefly, by, for (cause) … fore, from, in, by occasion of, of, by reason of, for sake, that, thereby, therefore, X though, through(-out), to, wherefore, with (-in). In composition it retains the same general importance.\n\nCognate Group: G1223 (after)\nVariants: διά",
    1224: "διαβαίνω (diabaínō | dee-ab-ah'-ee-no)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and the base of G939\nStrong's: to cross\nKJV: —come over, pass (through).\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G1223 (after)\nVariants: διαβαίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1980 הָלַךְ, H3381 יָרַד, H4422 מָלַט, H5674 עָבַר, H5927 עָלָה, H5975 עָמַד, H6805 צָעַד",
    1225: "διαβάλλω (diabállō | dee-ab-al'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G906\nStrong's: (figuratively) to traduce\nKJV: —accuse.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G906 \n\nCognate Group: G1228 (false accuser), G1225 (accuse)\nVariants: διαβάλλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H398 אָכַל, H7853 שָׂטַן",
    1226: "διαβεβαιόομαι (diabebaióomai | dee-ab-eb-ahee-o'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice of a compound of G1223 and G950\nStrong's: to confirm thoroughly (by words), i.e. asseverate\nKJV: —affirm constantly.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G950 \n\nCognate Group: G1228 (false accuser), G1225 (accuse)\nVariants: διαβεβαιόομαι",
    1227: "διαβλέπω (diablépō | dee-ab-lep'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G991\nStrong's: to look through, i.e. recover full vision\nKJV: —see clearly.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G991 \n\nCognate Group: G1228 (false accuser), G1225 (accuse)\nVariants: διαβλέπω",
    1228: "διάβολος (diábolos | dee-ab'-ol-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1225\nStrong's: a traducer; specially, Satan (compare H7854)\nKJV: —false accuser, devil, slanderer.\n\nSee: G1225 \nSee: H7854\n\nCognate Group: G1228 (false accuser), G1225 (accuse)\nVariants: διάβολος, Διάβολος \nHebrew Equivalents: H6862 צַר, H6887 צָרַר, H7854 שָׂטָן",
    1229: "διαγγέλλω (diangéllō | de-ang-gel'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and the base of G32\nStrong's: to herald thoroughly\nKJV: —declare, preach, signify.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G32 \n\nCognate Group: G1229 (declare), G31 (message), G1804 (shew forth), G518 (bring word), G2604 (setter forth), G4293 (foretell), G312 (declare), G2605 (declare)\nVariants: διαγγέλλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H5608 סָפַר, H5674 עָבַר",
    1230: "διαγίνομαι (diagínomai | dee-ag-in'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G1096\nStrong's: to elapse meanwhile\nKJV: —X after, be past, be spent.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G1096 \n\nCognate Group: G1229 (declare), G31 (message), G1804 (shew forth), G518 (bring word), G2604 (setter forth), G4293 (foretell), G312 (declare), G2605 (declare)\nVariants: διαγίνομαι",
    1231: "διαγινώσκω (diaginṓskō | dee-ag-in-o'-sko)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G1097\nStrong's: to know thoroughly, i.e. ascertain exactly\nKJV: —(would) enquire, know the uttermost.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G1097 \n\nCognate Group: G1229 (declare), G31 (message), G1804 (shew forth), G518 (bring word), G2604 (setter forth), G4293 (foretell), G312 (declare), G2605 (declare)\nVariants: διαγινώσκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1819 דָּמָה, H3045 יָדַע",
    1232: "διαγνωρίζω (diagnōrízō | dee-ag-no-rid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1123 and G1107\nStrong's: to tell abroad\nKJV: —make known.\n\nSee: G1123 \nSee: G1107 \n\nCognate Group: G1229 (declare), G31 (message), G1804 (shew forth), G518 (bring word), G2604 (setter forth), G4293 (foretell), G312 (declare), G2605 (declare)\nVariants: διαγνωρίζω G1337",
    1233: "διάγνωσις (diágnōsis | dee-ag'-no-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G1231\nStrong's: (magisterial) examination (\"diagnosis\")\nKJV: —hearing.\n\nSee: G1231 \n\nCognate Group: G1229 (declare), G31 (message), G1804 (shew forth), G518 (bring word), G2604 (setter forth), G4293 (foretell), G312 (declare), G2605 (declare)\nVariants: διάγνωσις",
    1234: "διαγογγύζω (diagongýzō | dee-ag-ong-good'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G1111\nStrong's: to complain throughout a crowd\nKJV: —murmur.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G1111 \n\nCognate Group: G1111 (murmur), G1112 (grudging), G1113 (murmurer), G1234 (murmur)\nVariants: διαγογγύζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3885 לוּן, H7279 רָגַן",
    1235: "διαγρηγορέω (diagrēgoréō | dee-ag-ray-gor-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G1127\nStrong's: to waken thoroughly\nKJV: —be awake.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G1127 \n\nCognate Group: G1111 (murmur), G1112 (grudging), G1113 (murmurer), G1234 (murmur)\nVariants: διαγρηγορέω",
    1236: "διάγω (diágō | dee-ag'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G71\nStrong's: to pass time or life\nKJV: —lead life, living.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G71 \n\nCognate Group: G1111 (murmur), G1112 (grudging), G1113 (murmurer), G1234 (murmur)\nVariants: διάγω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1980 הָלַךְ, H5674 עָבַר, H6589 פָּשַׂק",
    1237: "διαδέχομαι (diadéchomai | dee-ad-ekh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G1209\nStrong's: to receive in turn, i.e. (figuratively) succeed to\nKJV: —come after.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G1209 \n\nCognate Group: G1111 (murmur), G1112 (grudging), G1113 (murmurer), G1234 (murmur)\nVariants: διαδέχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H4932 מִשְׁנֶה, H6503 פַּרְבָּר",
    1238: "διάδημα (diádēma | dee-ad'-ay-mah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1223 and G1210\nStrong's: a \"diadem\" (as bound about the head)\nKJV: —crown. Compare G4735 .\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G1210 \nSee: G4735 \n\nCognate Group: G1111 (murmur), G1112 (grudging), G1113 (murmurer), G1234 (murmur)\nVariants: διάδημα \nHebrew Equivalents: H3804 כֶּתֶר, H6797 צָנִיף, H8509 תַּכְרִיךְ",
    1239: "διαδίδωμι (diadídōmi | dee-ad-id'-o-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G1325\nStrong's: to give throughout a crowd, i.e. deal out; also to deliver over (as to a successor)\nKJV: —(make) distribute(-ion), divide, give.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G1325 \n\nCognate Group: G1111 (murmur), G1112 (grudging), G1113 (murmurer), G1234 (murmur)\nVariants: διαδίδωμι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2505 חָלַק, H5307 נָפַל, H5414 נָתַן",
    1240: "διάδοχος (diádochos | dee-ad'-okh-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1237\nStrong's: a successor in office\nKJV: —room.\n\nSee: G1237 \n\nCognate Group: G1111 (murmur), G1112 (grudging), G1113 (murmurer), G1234 (murmur)\nVariants: διάδοχος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3027 יָד, H4932 מִשְׁנֶה, H8269 שַׂר",
    1241: "διαζώννυμι (diazṓnnymi | dee-az-own'-noo-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G2224\nStrong's: to gird tightly\nKJV: —gird.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G2224 \n\nCognate Group: G2224 (gird), G2223 (girdle), G1241 (gird), G4024 (gird)\nVariants: διαζώννυμι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2290 חֲגֹור",
    1242: "διαθήκη (diathḗkē | dee-ath-ay'-kay)\n\nDerivation: from G1303\nStrong's: properly, a disposition, i.e. (specially) a contract (especially a devisory will)\nKJV: —covenant, testament.\n\nSee: G1303 \n\nCognate Group: G1303 (appoint), G1242 (covenant)\nVariants: διαθήκη \nHebrew Equivalents: H264 אַחֲוָה, H1285 בְּרִית, H1697 דָּבָר, H3789 כָּתַב, H5715 עֵדוּת, H8003 שָׁלֵם, H8452 תֹּורָה",
    1243: "διαίρεσις (diaíresis | dee-ah'-ee-res-is)\n\nDerivation: from G1244\nStrong's: a distinction or (concretely) variety\nKJV: —difference, diversity.\n\nSee: G1244 \n\nCognate Group: G139 (heresy), G1243 (difference), G1244 (divide), G141 (heretic), G140 (choose), G138 (choose)\nVariants: διαίρεσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H1506 גֶּזֶר, H4256 מַחֲלֹקֶת, H5159 נַחֲלָה, H6390 פְּלַגָּה",
    1244: "διαιρέω (diairéō | dee-ahee-reh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G138\nStrong's: to separate, i.e. distribute\nKJV: —divide.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G138 \n\nCognate Group: G139 (heresy), G1243 (difference), G1244 (divide), G141 (heretic), G140 (choose), G138 (choose)\nVariants: διαιρέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H914 בָּדַל, H1334 בָּתַר, H1504 גָּזַר, H2505 חָלַק, H2673 חָצָה, H2686 חָצַץ, H5157 נָחַל, H5408 נָתַח, H6386 פְּלַג, H6537 פְּרַס",
    1245: "διακαθαρίζω (diakatharízō | dee-ak-ath-ar-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G2511\nStrong's: to cleanse perfectly, i.e. (specially) winnow\nKJV: —thoroughly purge.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G2511 \n\nCognate Group: G139 (heresy), G1243 (difference), G1244 (divide), G141 (heretic), G140 (choose), G138 (choose)\nVariants: διακαθαρίζω, διακαθαίρω",
    1246: "διακατελέγχομαι (diakatelénchomai | dee-ak-at-el-eng'-khom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1223 and a compound of G2596 and G1651\nStrong's: to prove downright, i.e. confute\nKJV: —convince.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G2596 \nSee: G1651 \n\nCognate Group: G139 (heresy), G1243 (difference), G1244 (divide), G141 (heretic), G140 (choose), G138 (choose)\nVariants: διακατελέγχομαι",
    1247: "διακονέω (diakonéō | dee-ak-on-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1249\nStrong's: to be an attendant, i.e. wait upon (menially or as a host, friend, or (figuratively) teacher); technically, to act as a Christian deacon\nKJV: —(ad-)minister (unto), serve, use the office of a deacon.\n\nSee: G1249 \n\nCognate Group: G1249 (deacon), G1247 (minister), G1248 (minister)\nVariants: διακονέω",
    1248: "διακονία (diakonía | dee-ak-on-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1249\nStrong's: attendance (as a servant, etc.); figuratively (eleemosynary) aid, (official) service (especially of the Christian teacher, or technically of the diaconate)\nKJV: —(ad-)minister(-ing, -tration, -try), office, relief, service(-ing).\n\nSee: G1249 \n\nCognate Group: G1249 (deacon), G1247 (minister), G1248 (minister)\nVariants: διακονία, δωροφορία \nHebrew Equivalents: H5288 נַעַר, H8334 שָׁרַת",
    1249: "διάκονος (diákonos | dee-ak'-on-os)\n\nDerivation: probably from an obsolete διάκω (to run on errands; compare G1377)\nStrong's: an attendant, i.e. (genitive case) a waiter (at table or in other menial duties); specially, a Christian teacher and pastor (technically, a deacon or deaconess)\nKJV: —deacon, minister, servant.\n\nSee: G1377 \n\nCognate Group: G1249 (deacon), G1247 (minister), G1248 (minister)\nVariants: διάκονος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5288 נַעַר, H8334 שָׁרַת",
    1250: "διακόσιοι (diakósioi | dee-ak-os'-ee-oy)\n\nDerivation: from G1364 and G1540\nStrong's: two hundred\nKJV: —two hundred.\n\nSee: G1364 \nSee: G1540 \n\nCognate Group: G1249 (deacon), G1247 (minister), G1248 (minister)\nVariants: διακόσιοι",
    1251: "διακούομαι (diakoúomai | dee-ak-oo'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1223 and G191\nStrong's: to hear throughout, i.e. patiently listen (to a prisoner's plea)\nKJV: —hear.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G191 \n\nCognate Group: G1249 (deacon), G1247 (minister), G1248 (minister)\nVariants: διακούομαι, διακούω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7896 שִׁית, H8085 שָׁמַע",
    1252: "διακρίνω (diakrínō | dee-ak-ree'-no)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G2919\nStrong's: to separate thoroughly, i.e. (literally and reflexively) to withdraw from, or (by implication) oppose; figuratively, to discriminate (by implication, decide), or (reflexively) hesitate\nKJV: —contend, make (to) differ(-ence), discern, doubt, judge, be partial, stagger, waver.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G2919 \n\nCognate Group: G612 (answer), G2631 (condemnation), G470 (answer again), G351 (examination), G2923 (judge), G610 (sentence), G2924 (discerner), G1469 (make of the number), G350 (ask), G1253 (discern), G843 (condemned of self), G2632 (condemn), G2919 (avenge), G2917 (avenge), G1252 (contend), G87 (without partiality), G611 (answer), G178 (uncondemned), G2633 (condemn), G2920 (accusation), G2922 (to judge)\nVariants: διακρίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H777 אַרְצָא, H974 בָּחַן, H977 בָּחַר, H1305 בָּרַר, H6567 פָּרָשׁ, H7378 רִיב, H7896 שִׁית, H8199 שָׁפַט",
    1253: "διάκρισις (diákrisis | dee-ak'-ree-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G1252\nStrong's: judicial estimation\nKJV: —discern(-ing), disputation.\n\nSee: G1252 \n\nCognate Group: G612 (answer), G2631 (condemnation), G470 (answer again), G351 (examination), G2923 (judge), G610 (sentence), G2924 (discerner), G1469 (make of the number), G350 (ask), G1253 (discern), G843 (condemned of self), G2632 (condemn), G2919 (avenge), G2917 (avenge), G1252 (contend), G87 (without partiality), G611 (answer), G178 (uncondemned), G2633 (condemn), G2920 (accusation), G2922 (to judge)\nVariants: διάκρισις \nHebrew Equivalents: H4657 מִפְלָשׂ",
    1254: "διακωλύω (diakōlýō | dee-ak-o-loo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G2967\nStrong's: to hinder altogether, i.e. utterly prohibit\nKJV: —forbid.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G2967 \n\nCognate Group: G612 (answer), G2631 (condemnation), G470 (answer again), G351 (examination), G2923 (judge), G610 (sentence), G2924 (discerner), G1469 (make of the number), G350 (ask), G1253 (discern), G843 (condemned of self), G2632 (condemn), G2919 (avenge), G2917 (avenge), G1252 (contend), G87 (without partiality), G611 (answer), G178 (uncondemned), G2633 (condemn), G2920 (accusation), G2922 (to judge)\nVariants: διακωλύω",
    1255: "διαλαλέω (dialaléō | dee-al-al-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G2980\nStrong's: to talk throughout a company, i.e. converse or (genitive case) publish\nKJV: —commune, noise abroad.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G2980 \n\nCognate Group: G612 (answer), G2631 (condemnation), G470 (answer again), G351 (examination), G2923 (judge), G610 (sentence), G2924 (discerner), G1469 (make of the number), G350 (ask), G1253 (discern), G843 (condemned of self), G2632 (condemn), G2919 (avenge), G2917 (avenge), G1252 (contend), G87 (without partiality), G611 (answer), G178 (uncondemned), G2633 (condemn), G2920 (accusation), G2922 (to judge)\nVariants: διαλαλέω",
    1256: "διαλέγομαι (dialégomai | dee-al-eg'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1223 and G3004\nStrong's: to say thoroughly, i.e. discuss (in argument or exhortation)\nKJV: —dispute, preach (unto), reason (with), speak.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G3004 \n\nCognate Group: G1260 (cast in mind), G1256 (dispute), G1261 (dispute)\nVariants: διαλέγομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1696 דָבַר, H7378 רִיב",
    1257: "διαλείπω (dialeípō | dee-al-i'-po)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G3007\nStrong's: to leave off in the middle, i.e. intermit\nKJV: —cease.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G3007 \n\nCognate Group: G4035 (remain), G2640 (remnant), G2641 (forsake), G3005 (remnant), G1257 (cease)\nVariants: διαλείπω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1819 דָּמָה, H2308 חָדַל, H3176 יָחַל, H3426 יֵשׁ, H4513 מָנַע, H7725 שׁוּב, H7953 שָׁלָה",
    1258: "διάλεκτος (diálektos | dee-al'-ek-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1256\nStrong's: a (mode of) discourse, i.e. \"dialect\"\nKJV: —language, tongue.\n\nSee: G1256 \n\nCognate Group: G4035 (remain), G2640 (remnant), G2641 (forsake), G3005 (remnant), G1257 (cease)\nVariants: διάλεκτος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3956 לָשֹׁון",
    1259: "διαλλάσσω (diallássō | dee-al-las'-so)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G236\nStrong's: to change thoroughly, i.e. (mentally) to conciliate\nKJV: —reconcile.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G236 \n\nCognate Group: G604 (reconcile), G1259 (reconcile), G2644 (reconcile), G3337 (change), G2643 (atonement), G525 (deliver), G465 (in exchange), G236 (change)\nVariants: διαλλάσσω, διαλλάσσομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H5493 סוּר, H6565 פָּרַר, H7521 רָצָה, H7725 שׁוּב",
    1260: "διαλογίζομαι (dialogízomai | dee-al-og-id'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G3049\nStrong's: to reckon thoroughly, i.e. (genitive case) to deliberate (by reflection or discussion)\nKJV: —cast in mind, consider, dispute, muse, reason, think.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G3049 \n\nCognate Group: G1260 (cast in mind), G1256 (dispute), G1261 (dispute)\nVariants: διαλογίζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2161 זָמַם, H2803 חָשַׁב",
    1261: "διαλογισμός (dialogismós | dee-al-og-is-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G1260\nStrong's: discussion, i.e. (internal) consideration (by implication, purpose), or (external) debate\nKJV: —dispute, doubtful(-ing), imagination, reasoning, thought.\n\nSee: G1260 \n\nCognate Group: G1260 (cast in mind), G1256 (dispute), G1261 (dispute)\nVariants: διαλογισμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H4284 מַחֲשָׁבָה, H6250 עֶשְׁתֹּנָה, H7453 רֵעַ",
    1262: "διαλύω (dialýō | dee-al-oo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G3089\nStrong's: to dissolve utterly\nKJV: —scatter.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G3089 \n\nCognate Group: G1260 (cast in mind), G1256 (dispute), G1261 (dispute)\nVariants: διαλύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2254 חָבַל, H3808 לֹא, H4549 מָסַס, H5425 נָתַר, H5753 עָוָה, H6561 פָּרַק, H7665 שָׁבַר, H8271 שְׁרֵא",
    1263: "διαμαρτύρομαι (diamartýromai | dee-am-ar-too'-rom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G3140\nStrong's: to attest or protest earnestly, or (by implication) hortatively\nKJV: —charge, testify (unto), witness.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G3140 \n\nCognate Group: G3143 (take to record), G3142 (to be testified), G3144 (martyr), G1957 (testify), G4303 (testify beforehand), G5576 (be a false witness), G5575 (false witness), G3141 (record), G5577 (false witness), G4828 (testify unto), G3140 (charge), G1263 (charge), G2649 (witness against), G4901 (also bear witness)\nVariants: διαμαρτύρομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2095 זְהַר, H3045 יָדַע, H5749 עוּד",
    1264: "διαμάχομαι (diamáchomai | dee-am-akh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G3164\nStrong's: to fight fiercely (in altercation)\nKJV: —strive.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G3164 \n\nCognate Group: G3143 (take to record), G3142 (to be testified), G3144 (martyr), G1957 (testify), G4303 (testify beforehand), G5576 (be a false witness), G5575 (false witness), G3141 (record), G5577 (false witness), G4828 (testify unto), G3140 (charge), G1263 (charge), G2649 (witness against), G4901 (also bear witness)\nVariants: διαμάχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H3898 לָחַם",
