    1323: "δίδραχμον (dídrachmon | did'-rakh-mon)\n\nDerivation: from G1364 and G1406\nStrong's: a double drachma (didrachm)\nKJV: —tribute.\n\nSee: G1364 \nSee: G1406 \n\nCognate Group: G5572 (false teacher), G2085 (teach other doctrine), G1322 (doctrine), G3547 (doctor of the law), G1317 (apt to teach), G1320 (doctor), G2567 (teacher of good things), G1321 (teach), G1319 (doctrine), G1318 (taught)\nVariants: δίδραχμον \nHebrew Equivalents: H3701 כֶּסֶף, H8255 שֶׁקֶל",
