    1325: "δίδωμι (dídōmi | did'-o-mee)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of a primary verb (which is used as an alternative in most of the tenses)\nStrong's: to give (used in a very wide application, properly, or by implication, literally or figuratively; greatly modified by the connection)\nKJV: —adventure, bestow, bring forth, commit, deliver (up), give, grant, hinder, make, minister, number, offer, have power, put, receive, set, shew, smite (+ with the hand), strike (+ with the palm of the hand), suffer, take, utter, yield.\n\nCognate Group: G1432 (without a cause), G3860 (betray), G467 (recompense), G3862 (ordinance), G1325 (adventure), G468 (recompense), G1431 (gift), G591 (deliver), G1434 (gift), G469 (reward), G1433 (give), G1435 (gift)\nVariants: δίδωμι, διδῶ \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H967 בָּזַר, H1129 בָּנָה, H1961 הָיָה, H1980 הָלַךְ, H1984 הָלַל, H2388 חָזַק, H2505 חָלַק, H3051 יָהַב, H3254 יָסַף, H3332 יָצַק, H3341 יָצַת, H3381 יָרַד, H3423 יָרַשׁ, H3559 כּוּן, H3615 כָּלָה, H4376 מָכַר, H4427 מָלַךְ, H4487 מָנָה, H5050 נָגַהּ, H5065 נָגַשׂ, H5117 נוּחַ, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5411 נָתִין, H5414 נָתַן, H5782 עוּר, H5844 עָטָה, H5975 עָמַד, H6148 עָרַב, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6329 פּוּק, H6680 צָוָה, H6845 צָפַן, H6966 קוּם, H7181 קָשַׁב, H7311 רוּם, H7725 שׁוּב, H7760 שׂוּם, H7896 שִׁית, H7999 שָׁלַם, H8199 שָׁפַט, H8567 תָּנָה",
    1326: "διεγείρω (diegeírō | dee-eg-i'-ro)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G1453\nStrong's: to wake fully; i.e. arouse (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —arise, awake, raise, stir up.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G1453 \n\nCognate Group: G1432 (without a cause), G3860 (betray), G467 (recompense), G3862 (ordinance), G1325 (adventure), G468 (recompense), G1431 (gift), G591 (deliver), G1434 (gift), G469 (reward), G1433 (give), G1435 (gift)\nVariants: διεγείρω",
    1327: "διέξοδος (diéxodos | dee-ex'-od-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G1841\nStrong's: an outlet through, i.e. probably an open square (from which roads diverge)\nKJV: —highway.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G1841 \n\nCognate Group: G3595 (guide), G3594 (guide), G3598 (journey), G1327 (highway), G1841 (decease), G1529 (coming), G3180 (wile)\nVariants: διέξοδος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3318 יָצָא, H4664 מִפְרָץ, H6388 פֶּלֶג, H8444 תֹּוצָאָה",
    1328: "διερμηνευτής (diermēneutḗs | dee-er-main-yoo-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G1329\nStrong's: an explainer\nKJV: —interpreter.\n\nSee: G1329 \n\nCognate Group: G1329 (expound), G2059 (interpret), G2058 (interpretation), G1328 (interpreter)\nVariants: διερμηνευτής, ἑρμηνευτής",
