    1349: "δίκη (díkē | dee'-kay)\n\nDerivation: probably from G1166\nStrong's: right (as self-evident), i.e. justice (the principle, a decision, or its execution)\nKJV: —judgment, punish, vengeance.\n\nSee: G1166 \n\nCognate Group: G1346 (justly), G1343 (righteousness), G1349 (judgment), G1347 (justification), G1344 (free), G1342 (just), G1345 (judgment), G1341 (righteous judgment)\nVariants: δίκη, καταδίκη \nHebrew Equivalents: H1697 דָּבָר, H1779 דִּין, H2742 חֲרוּץ, H4941 מִשְׁפָּט, H5359 נָקָם, H7378 רִיב",
    1350: "δίκτυον (díktyon | dik'-too-on)\n\nDerivation: probably from a primary verb δίκω (to cast)\nStrong's: a seine (for fishing)\nKJV: —net.\n\nCognate Group: G1346 (justly), G1343 (righteousness), G1349 (judgment), G1347 (justification), G1344 (free), G1342 (just), G1345 (judgment), G1341 (righteous judgment)\nVariants: δίκτυον \nHebrew Equivalents: H2762 חֶרֶךְ, H5442 סְבָךְ, H7568 רֶשֶׁת, H7639 שְׂבָכָה",
    1351: "δίλογος (dílogos | dil'-og-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1364 and G3056\nStrong's: equivocal, i.e. telling a different story\nKJV: —double-tongued.\n\nSee: G1364 \nSee: G3056 \n\nCognate Group: G1346 (justly), G1343 (righteousness), G1349 (judgment), G1347 (justification), G1344 (free), G1342 (just), G1345 (judgment), G1341 (righteous judgment)\nVariants: δίλογος",
