    1357: "διόρθωσις (diórthōsis | dee-or'-tho-sis)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1223 and a derivative of G3717, meaning to straighten thoroughly\nStrong's: rectification, i.e. (specially) the Messianic restauration\nKJV: —reformation.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G3717 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: διόρθωσις",
    1358: "διορύσσω (diorýssō | dee-or-oos'-so)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G3736\nStrong's: to penetrate burglariously\nKJV: —break through (up).\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G3736 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: διορύσσω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2864 חָתַר",
    1359: "Διόσκουροι (Dióskouroi | dee-os'-koo-roy)\n\nDerivation: from the alternate of G2203 and a form of the base of G2877\nStrong's: sons of Jupiter, i.e. the twins Dioscuri\nKJV: —Castor and Pollux.\n\nSee: G2203 \nSee: G2877 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: Διόσκουροι",
    1360: "διότι (dióti | dee-ot'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from G1223 and G3754\nStrong's: on the very account that, or inasmuch as\nKJV: —because (that), for, therefore.\n\nSee: G1223 \nSee: G3754 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: διότι",
    1361: "Διοτρεφής (Diotrephḗs | dee-ot-ref-ace')\n\nDerivation: from the alternate of G2203 and G5142\nStrong's: Jove-nourished; Diotrephes, an opponent of Christianity\nKJV: —Diotrephes.\n\nSee: G2203 \nSee: G5142 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: Διοτρεφής, Διοτρέφης",
    1362: "διπλοῦς (diploûs | dip-looce')\n\nDerivation: from G1364 and (probably) the base of G4119\nStrong's: two-fold\nKJV: —double, two-fold more.\n\nSee: G1364 \nSee: G4119 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: διπλοῦς, διπλόος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3717 כָּפַל, H4932 מִשְׁנֶה",
    1363: "διπλόω (diplóō | dip-lo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1362\nStrong's: to render two-fold\nKJV: —double.\n\nSee: G1362 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: διπλόω",
    1364: "δίς (dís | dece)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G1417\nStrong's: twice\nKJV: —again, twice.\n\nSee: G1417 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: δίς",
    1365: "διστάζω (distázō | dis-tad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1364\nStrong's: properly, to duplicate, i.e. (mentally) to waver (in opinion)\nKJV: —doubt.\n\nSee: G1364 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: διστάζω",
    1366: "δίστομος (dístomos | dis'-tom-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1364 and G4750\nStrong's: double-edged\nKJV: —with two edges, two-edged.\n\nSee: G1364 \nSee: G4750 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: δίστομος \nHebrew Equivalents: H6366 פֵּיָה, H8147 שְׁנַיִם",
    1367: "δισχίλιοι (dischílioi | dis-khil'-ee-oy)\n\nDerivation: from G1364 and G5507\nStrong's: two thousand\nKJV: —two thousand.\n\nSee: G1364 \nSee: G5507 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: δισχίλιοι",
    1368: "διϋλίζω (diÿlízō | dee-oo-lid'-zo)\n\n\nDerivation: from G1223 \n (to filter)\nStrong's: to strain out\nKJV: —strain at (probably by misprint).\n\nSee: G1223 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)",
    1369: "διχάζω (dicházō | dee-khad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G1364\nStrong's: to make apart, i.e. sunder (figuratively, alienate)\nKJV: —set at variance.\n\nSee: G1364 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: διχάζω",
    1370: "διχοστασία (dichostasía | dee-khos-tas-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G1364 and G4714\nStrong's: disunion, i.e. (figuratively) dissension\nKJV: —division, sedition.\n\nSee: G1364 \nSee: G4714 \n\nCognate Group: G646 (falling away), G1370 (division), G868 (depart)\nVariants: διχοστασία",
    1371: "διχοτομέω (dichotoméō | dee-khot-om-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of a derivative of G1364 and a derivative of τέμνω (to cut)\nStrong's: to bisect, i.e. (by extension) to flog severely\nKJV: —cut asunder (in sunder).\n\nSee: G1364 \n\nCognate Group: G1371 (cut asunder)\nVariants: διχοτομέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5408 נָתַח",
    1372: "διψάω (dipsáō | dip-sah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a variation of G1373\nStrong's: to thirst for (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —(be, be a-)thirst(-y).\n\nSee: G1373 \n\nCognate Group: G1372 (thirst), G1373 (thirst)\nVariants: διψάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2721 חֹרֶב, H3452 יְשִׁימֹון, H5888 עָיֵף, H6160 עֲרָבָה, H6723 צִיָּה, H6770 צָמֵא, H8264 שָׁקַק",
    1373: "δίψος (dípsos | dip'-sos)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: thirst\nKJV: —thirst.\n\nCognate Group: G1372 (thirst), G1373 (thirst)\nVariants: δίψος \nHebrew Equivalents: H6771 צָמֵא, H6772 צָמָא, H8414 תֹּהוּ",
    1374: "δίψυχος (dípsychos | dip'-soo-khos)\n\nDerivation: from G1364 and G5590\nStrong's: two-spirited, i.e. vacillating (in opinion or purpose)\nKJV: —double minded.\n\nSee: G1364 \nSee: G5590 \n\nCognate Group: G1374 (double minded), G5591 (natural), G5590 (heart), G3642 (feebleminded), G404 (refresh), G403 (revival)\nVariants: δίψυχος",
    1375: "διωγμός (diōgmós | dee-ogue-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G1377\nStrong's: persecution\nKJV: —persecution.\n\nSee: G1377 \n\nCognate Group: G1374 (double minded), G5591 (natural), G5590 (heart), G3642 (feebleminded), G404 (refresh), G403 (revival)\nVariants: διωγμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H4788 מָרוּד, H7291 רָדַף",
    1376: "διώκτης (diṓktēs | dee-oke'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G1377\nStrong's: a persecutor\nKJV: —persecutor.\n\nSee: G1377 \n\nCognate Group: G1374 (double minded), G5591 (natural), G5590 (heart), G3642 (feebleminded), G404 (refresh), G403 (revival)\nVariants: διώκτης",
    1377: "διώκω (diṓkō | dee-o'-ko)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged (and causative) form of a primary verb δίω (to flee\nStrong's: compare the base of G1169 and G1249); to pursue (literally or figuratively); by implication, to persecute\nKJV: —ensue, follow (after), given to, (suffer) persecute(-ion), press forward.\n\nSee: G1169 \nSee: G1249 \n\nCognate Group: G1377 (ensue)\nVariants: διώκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H340 אָיַב, H1272 בָּרַח, H1725 דָּהַר, H1765 דָּחַף, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2729 חָרַד, H5086 נָדַף, H5127 נוּס, H7287 רָדָה, H7291 רָדַף, H7323 רוּץ, H7703 שָׁדַד, H8199 שָׁפַט",
    1378: "δόγμα (dógma | dog'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G1380\nStrong's: a law (civil, ceremonial or ecclesiastical)\nKJV: —decree, ordinance.\n\nSee: G1380 \n\nCognate Group: G1379 (be subject to ordinances), G1378 (decree)\nVariants: δόγμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H633 אֱסָר, H1881 דָּת, H2942 טְעֵם, H3791 כָּתָב",
    1379: "δογματίζω (dogmatízō | dog-mat-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1378\nStrong's: to prescribe by statute, i.e. (reflexively) to submit to, ceremonially rule\nKJV: —be subject to ordinances.\n\nSee: G1378 \n\nCognate Group: G1379 (be subject to ordinances), G1378 (decree)\nVariants: δογματίζω, δογματίζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1881 דָּת, H3789 כָּתַב",
    1380: "δοκέω (dokéō | dok-eh'-o)\n\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of a primary verb, δόκω (dókō | dok'-o)\n (used only in an alternate in certain tenses\nStrong's: compare the base of G1166) of the same meaning; to think; by implication, to seem (truthfully or uncertainly)\nKJV: —be accounted, (of own) please(-ure), be of reputation, seem (good), suppose, think, trow.\n\nSee: G1166 \n\nCognate Group: G1391 (dignity), G3861 (strange), G1741 (glorious), G1740 (glorify), G4888 (glorify together), G1392 (glorify), G1380 (be accounted)\nVariants: δοκέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H1961 הָיָה, H2803 חָשַׁב, H2895 טֹוב, H3474 יָשַׁר, H5068 נָדַב, H5375 נָשָׂא, H6634 צְבָא",
    1381: "δοκιμάζω (dokimázō | dok-im-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1384\nStrong's: to test (literally or figuratively); by implication, to approve\nKJV: —allow, discern, examine, X like, (ap-)prove, try.\n\nSee: G1384 \n\nCognate Group: G1381 (allow), G1383 (trial), G1382 (experience), G1384 (approved), G96 (castaway)\nVariants: δοκιμάζω, δοκιμασία \nHebrew Equivalents: H974 בָּחַן, H977 בָּחַר, H2713 חָקַר, H3365 יָקַר, H6884 צָרַף",
    1382: "δοκιμή (dokimḗ | dok-ee-may')\n\nDerivation: from the same as G1384\nStrong's: test (abstractly or concretely); by implication, trustiness\nKJV: —experience(-riment), proof, trial.\n\nSee: G1384 \n\nCognate Group: G1381 (allow), G1383 (trial), G1382 (experience), G1384 (approved), G96 (castaway)\nVariants: δοκιμή",
    1383: "δοκίμιον (dokímion | dok-im'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a presumed derivative of G1382\nStrong's: a testing; by implication, trustworthiness\nKJV: —trial, trying.\n\nSee: G1382 \n\nCognate Group: G1381 (allow), G1383 (trial), G1382 (experience), G1384 (approved), G96 (castaway)\nVariants: δοκίμιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H2212 זָקַק, H3366 יְקָר, H4715 מִצְרֵף, H5948 עֲלִיל",
    1384: "δόκιμος (dókimos | dok'-ee-mos)\n\nDerivation: from G1380\nStrong's: properly, acceptable (current after assayal), i.e. approved\nKJV: —approved, tried.\n\nSee: G1380 \n\nCognate Group: G1381 (allow), G1383 (trial), G1382 (experience), G1384 (approved), G96 (castaway)\nVariants: δόκιμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2212 זָקַק, H2889 טָהֹור, H3366 יְקָר, H5674 עָבַר, H6338 פָּזַז",
