    1388: "δόλος (dólos | dol'-os)\n\nDerivation: from an obsolete primary verb, δέλλω (probably meaning to decoy\nStrong's: compare G1185); a trick (bait), i.e. (figuratively) wile\nKJV: —craft, deceit, guile, subtilty.\n\nSee: G1185 \n\nCognate Group: G1381 (allow), G1383 (trial), G1382 (experience), G1384 (approved), G96 (castaway)\nVariants: δόλος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1697 דָּבָר, H2611 חָנֵף, H4405 מִלָּה, H4820 מִרְמָה, H4860 מַשָּׁאֹון, H5643 סֵתֶר, H6195 עׇרְמָה, H7400 רָכִיל, H7423 רְמִיָּה, H7494 רַעַשׁ, H8432 תָּוֶךְ",
    1389: "δολόω (dolóō | dol-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1388\nStrong's: to ensnare, i.e. (figuratively) adulterate\nKJV: —handle deceitfully.\n\nSee: G1388 \n\nCognate Group: G1381 (allow), G1383 (trial), G1382 (experience), G1384 (approved), G96 (castaway)\nVariants: δολόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2505 חָלַק, H7270 רָגַל",
