    1391: "δόξα (dóxa | dox'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G1380\nStrong's: glory (as very apparent), in a wide application (literal or figurative, objective or subjective)\nKJV: —dignity, glory(-ious), honour, praise, worship.\n\nSee: G1380 \n\nCognate Group: G1391 (dignity), G3861 (strange), G1741 (glorious), G1740 (glorify), G4888 (glorify together), G1392 (glorify), G1380 (be accounted)\nVariants: δόξα \nHebrew Equivalents: H202 אֹון, H1320 בָּשָׂר, H1347 גָּאֹון, H1926 הָדָר, H1935 הֹוד, H1952 הֹון, H2073 זְבוּל, H2617 חֵסֵד, H2898 טוּב, H3027 יָד, H3308 יֳפִי, H3366 יְקָר, H3513 כָּבַד, H3519 כָּבֹוד, H4758 מַרְאֶה, H4853 מַשָּׂא, H5251 נֵס, H5797 עֹז, H6286 פָּאַר, H6643 צְבִי, H6944 קֹדֶשׁ, H7757 שׁוּל, H8389 תֹּאַר, H8416 תְּהִלָּה, H8443 תֹּועָפָה, H8544 תְּמוּנָה, H8597 תִּפְאָרָה",
    1392: "δοξάζω (doxázō | dox-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1391\nStrong's: to render (or esteem) glorious (in a wide application)\nKJV: —(make) glorify(-ious), full of (have) glory, honour, magnify.\n\nSee: G1391 \n\nCognate Group: G1391 (dignity), G3861 (strange), G1741 (glorious), G1740 (glorify), G4888 (glorify together), G1392 (glorify), G1380 (be accounted)\nVariants: δοξάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1342 גָּאָה, H1361 גָּבַהּ, H1431 גָּדַל, H1921 הָדַר, H3366 יְקָר, H3513 כָּבַד, H5115 נָוָה, H5139 נָזִיר, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5737 עֲדַר, H6286 פָּאַר, H6942 קָדַשׁ, H7160 קָרַן, H7311 רוּם",
    1393: "Δορκάς (Dorkás | dor-kas')\n\n\nStrong's: gazelle; Dorcas, a Christian woman\nKJV: —Dorcas.\n\nCognate Group: G1391 (dignity), G3861 (strange), G1741 (glorious), G1740 (glorify), G4888 (glorify together), G1392 (glorify), G1380 (be accounted)\nVariants: Δορκάς",
    1394: "δόσις (dósis | dos'-is)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G1325\nStrong's: a giving; by implication, (concretely) a gift\nKJV: —gift, giving.\n\nSee: G1325 \n\nCognate Group: G1391 (dignity), G3861 (strange), G1741 (glorious), G1740 (glorify), G4888 (glorify together), G1392 (glorify), G1380 (be accounted)\nVariants: δόσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H2706 חֹק, H4976 מַתָּן, H4991 מַתָּת",
    1395: "δότης (dótēs | dot'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G1325\nStrong's: a giver\nKJV: —giver.\n\nSee: G1325 \n\nCognate Group: G1391 (dignity), G3861 (strange), G1741 (glorious), G1740 (glorify), G4888 (glorify together), G1392 (glorify), G1380 (be accounted)\nVariants: δότης",
    1396: "δουλαγωγέω (doulagōgéō | doo-lag-ogue-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a presumed compound of G1401 and G71\nStrong's: to be a slave-driver, i.e. to enslave (figuratively, subdue)\nKJV: —bring into subjection.\n\nSee: G1401 \nSee: G71 \n\nCognate Group: G1399 (handmaid), G4889 (fellowservant), G1402 (bring into bondage), G1397 (bondage), G1396 (bring into subjection), G1401 (bond), G2615 (bring into bondage), G3787 (eye-service), G1398 (be in bondage)\nVariants: δουλαγωγέω",
    1397: "δουλεία (douleía | doo-li'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1398\nStrong's: slavery (ceremonially or figuratively)\nKJV: —bondage.\n\nSee: G1398 \n\nCognate Group: G1399 (handmaid), G4889 (fellowservant), G1402 (bring into bondage), G1397 (bondage), G1396 (bring into subjection), G1401 (bond), G2615 (bring into bondage), G3787 (eye-service), G1398 (be in bondage)\nVariants: δουλεία \nHebrew Equivalents: H5650 עֶבֶד, H6468 פְּעֻלָּה",
    1398: "δουλεύω (douleúō | dool-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1401\nStrong's: to be a slave to (literal or figurative, involuntary or voluntary)\nKJV: —be in bondage, (do) serve(-ice).\n\nSee: G1401 \n\nCognate Group: G1399 (handmaid), G4889 (fellowservant), G1402 (bring into bondage), G1397 (bondage), G1396 (bring into subjection), G1401 (bond), G2615 (bring into bondage), G3787 (eye-service), G1398 (be in bondage)\nVariants: δουλεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5647 עָבַד, H6399 פְּלַח, H8334 שָׁרַת",
    1399: "δούλη (doúlē | doo'-lay)\n\nDerivation: feminine of G1401\nStrong's: a female slave (involuntarily or voluntarily)\nKJV: —handmaid(-en).\n\nSee: G1401 \n\nCognate Group: G1399 (handmaid), G4889 (fellowservant), G1402 (bring into bondage), G1397 (bondage), G1396 (bring into subjection), G1401 (bond), G2615 (bring into bondage), G3787 (eye-service), G1398 (be in bondage)\nVariants: δούλη \nHebrew Equivalents: H5291 נַעֲרָה, H5647 עָבַד, H5650 עֶבֶד, H5971 עַם",
    1400: "δοῦλον (doûlon | doo'-lon)\n\nDerivation: neuter of G1401\nStrong's: subservient\nKJV: —servant.\n\nSee: G1401 \n\nCognate Group: G1399 (handmaid), G4889 (fellowservant), G1402 (bring into bondage), G1397 (bondage), G1396 (bring into subjection), G1401 (bond), G2615 (bring into bondage), G3787 (eye-service), G1398 (be in bondage)\nVariants: δοῦλον, δοῦλοσ1 G1529 \nHebrew Equivalents: H5291 נַעֲרָה, H5647 עָבַד, H5650 עֶבֶד, H5971 עַם",
    1401: "δοῦλος (doûlos | doo'-los)\n\nDerivation: from G1210\nStrong's: a slave (literal or figurative, involuntary or voluntary; frequently, therefore in a qualified sense of subjection or subserviency)\nKJV: —bond(-man), servant.\n\nSee: G1210 \n\nCognate Group: G1399 (handmaid), G4889 (fellowservant), G1402 (bring into bondage), G1397 (bondage), G1396 (bring into subjection), G1401 (bond), G2615 (bring into bondage), G3787 (eye-service), G1398 (be in bondage)\nVariants: δοῦλος, δοῦλοσ1, δοῦλοσ2 \nHebrew Equivalents: H5291 נַעֲרָה, H5647 עָבַד, H5650 עֶבֶד, H5971 עַם",
    1402: "δουλόω (doulóō | doo-lo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1401\nStrong's: to enslave (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —bring into (be under) bondage, X given, become (make) servant.\n\nSee: G1401 \n\nCognate Group: G1399 (handmaid), G4889 (fellowservant), G1402 (bring into bondage), G1397 (bondage), G1396 (bring into subjection), G1401 (bond), G2615 (bring into bondage), G3787 (eye-service), G1398 (be in bondage)\nVariants: δουλόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5647 עָבַד",
    1403: "δοχή (dochḗ | dokh-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G1209\nStrong's: a reception, i.e. convivial entertainment\nKJV: —feast.\n\nSee: G1209 \n\nCognate Group: G1403 (feast), G1209 (accept), G1184 (accepted), G553 (look for), G1523 (receive), G587 (acceptable), G588 (accept), G2144 (acceptable), G4327 (accept), G594 (acceptation), G1561 (looking for)\nVariants: δοχή \nHebrew Equivalents: H3899 לֶחֶם, H4960 מִשְׁתֶּה",
    1404: "δράκων (drákōn | drak'-own)\n\nDerivation: probably from an alternate form of δέρκομαι (to look)\nStrong's: a fabulous kind of serpent (perhaps as supposed to fascinate)\nKJV: —dragon.\n\nCognate Group: G1404 (dragon)\nVariants: δράκων \nHebrew Equivalents: H3715 כְּפִיר, H3882 לִוְיָתָן, H5175 נָחָשׁ, H6260 עַתּוּד, H6620 פֶּתֶן, H8577 תַּנִּין, H8577 תַּנִּין",
    1405: "δράσσομαι (drássomai | dras'-som-ahee)\n\nDerivation: perhaps akin to the base of G1404 (through the idea of capturing)\nStrong's: to grasp, i.e. (figuratively) entrap\nKJV: —take.\n\nSee: G1404 \n\nCognate Group: G1404 (dragon)\nVariants: δράσσομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H5401 נָשַׁק, H7061 קָמַץ",
    1406: "δραχμή (drachmḗ | drakh-may')\n\nDerivation: from G1405\nStrong's: a drachma or (silver) coin (as handled)\nKJV: —piece (of silver).\n\nSee: G1405 \n\nCognate Group: G1404 (dragon)\nVariants: δραχμή \nHebrew Equivalents: H150 אֲדַרְכֹּן, H1235 בֶּקַע, H1871 דַּרְכְּמֹון, H8255 שֶׁקֶל",
    1407: "δρέπανον (drépanon | drep'-an-on)\n\nDerivation: from δρέπω (to pluck)\nStrong's: a gathering hook (especially for harvesting)\nKJV: —sickle.\n\nCognate Group: G1404 (dragon)\nVariants: δρέπανον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1861 דׇּרְבֹון, H2770 חֶרְמֵשׁ, H4038 מַגָּל, H4211 מַזְמֵרָה, H4281 מַחֲרֵשָׁה",
    1408: "δρόμος (drómos | drom'-os)\n\nDerivation: from the alternate of G5143\nStrong's: a race, i.e. (figuratively) career\nKJV: —course.\n\nSee: G5143 \n\nCognate Group: G4274 (forerunner), G5143 (have course), G1408 (course)\nVariants: δρόμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4793 מֵרֹוץ, H4794 מְרוּצָה, H8229 שִׁפְעָה",
    1409: "Δρούσιλλα (Droúsilla | droo'-sil-lah)\n\nDerivation: a feminine diminutive of Drusus (a Roman name)\nStrong's: Drusilla, a member of the Herodian family\nKJV: —Drusilla.\n\nCognate Group: G4274 (forerunner), G5143 (have course), G1408 (course)\nVariants: Δρούσιλλα",
    1410: "δύναμαι (dýnamai | doo'-nam-ahee)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: to be able or possible\nKJV: —be able, can (do, + -not), could, may, might, be possible, be of power.\n\nCognate Group: G1411 (ability), G1743 (enable), G1414 (be mighty), G1410 (be able), G1412 (strengthen), G1413 (of great authority), G101 (be impossible), G1415 (able), G102 (could not do)\nVariants: δύναμαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1368 גִּבֹּור, H2308 חָדַל, H2428 חַיִל, H2973 יָאַל, H3254 יָסַף, H3546 כְּהַל, H3557 כּוּל, H3615 כָּלָה, H3811 לָאָה, H3985 מָאֵן, H4672 מָצָא, H6113 עָצָר",
    1411: "δύναμις (dýnamis | doo'-nam-is)\n\nDerivation: from G1410\nStrong's: force (literally or figuratively); specially, miraculous power (usually by implication, a miracle itself)\nKJV: —ability, abundance, meaning, might(-ily, -y, -y deed), (worker of) miracle(-s), power, strength, violence, mighty (wonderful) work.\n\nSee: G1410 \n\nCognate Group: G1411 (ability), G1743 (enable), G1414 (be mighty), G1410 (be able), G1412 (strengthen), G1413 (of great authority), G101 (be impossible), G1415 (able), G102 (could not do)\nVariants: δύναμις \nHebrew Equivalents: H202 אֹון, H410 אֵל, H582 אֱנֹושׁ, H1004 בַּיִת, H1363 גֹּבַהּ, H1368 גִּבֹּור, H1369 גְּבוּרָה, H1952 הֹון, H1995 הָמֹון, H2392 חֹזֶק, H2428 חַיִל, H2428 חַיִל, H2502 חָלַץ, H3027 יָד, H3519 כָּבֹוד, H3581 כֹּחַ, H3966 מְאֹד, H4264 מַחֲנֶה, H4421 מִלְחָמָה, H4979 מַתָּנָה, H5650 עֶבֶד, H5797 עֹז, H5971 עַם, H6310 פֶּה, H6381 פָּלָא, H6635 צָבָא",
    1412: "δυναμόω (dynamóō | doo-nam-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1411\nStrong's: to enable\nKJV: —strengthen.\n\nSee: G1411 \n\nCognate Group: G1411 (ability), G1743 (enable), G1414 (be mighty), G1410 (be able), G1412 (strengthen), G1413 (of great authority), G101 (be impossible), G1415 (able), G102 (could not do)\nVariants: δυναμόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1396 גָּבַר, H5810 עָזַז",
    1413: "δυνάστης (dynástēs | doo-nas'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G1410\nStrong's: a ruler or officer\nKJV: —of great authority, mighty, potentate.\n\nSee: G1410 \n\nCognate Group: G1411 (ability), G1743 (enable), G1414 (be mighty), G1410 (be able), G1412 (strengthen), G1413 (of great authority), G101 (be impossible), G1415 (able), G102 (could not do)\nVariants: δυνάστης \nHebrew Equivalents: H47 אַבִּיר, H117 אַדִּיר, H386 אֵיתָן, H582 אֱנֹושׁ, H1004 בַּיִת, H1368 גִּבֹּור, H1419 גָּדֹול, H1907 הַדָּבָר, H2388 חָזַק, H3384 יָרָה, H4005 מִבְחָר, H4911 מָשַׁל, H5068 נָדַב, H5631 סָרִיס, H6099 עָצוּם, H6184 עָרִיץ, H7227 רַב, H7336 רָזַן, H7563 רָשָׁע, H7989 שַׁלִּיט, H8269 שַׂר",
