    1416: "δύνω (dýnō | doo'-no) or δῦμι (dŷmi | doo'-mee)\n\n\nDerivation: prolonged forms of an obsolete primary δύο (dýo | doo'-o)\n (to sink)\nStrong's: to go \"down\"\nKJV: —set.\n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: δύνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H622 אָסַף, H935 בֹּוא, H2280 חָבַשׁ, H2502 חָלַץ, H6750 צָלַל, H7817 שָׁחַח",
    1417: "δύο (dýo | doo'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary numeral\nStrong's: \"two\"\nKJV: —both, twain, two.\n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: δύο, δισμυριάς",
    1418: "δυσ- (dys- | doos)\n\nDerivation: a primary inseparable particle of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: used only in composition as a prefix; hard, i.e. with difficulty\nKJV: —+ hard, + grievous, etc.\n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: δυσ-, δυσ",
