    1420: "δυσεντερία (dysentería | doos-en-ter-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1418 and a comparative of G1787 (meaning a bowel)\nStrong's: a \"dysentery\"\nKJV: —bloody flux.\n\nSee: G1418 \nSee: G1787 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: δυσεντερία, δυσεντέριον",
    1421: "δυσερμήνευτος (dysermḗneutos | doos-er-mane'-yoo-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1418 and a presumed derivative of G2059\nStrong's: difficult of explanation\nKJV: —hard to be uttered.\n\nSee: G1418 \nSee: G2059 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: δυσερμήνευτος",
    1422: "δύσκολος (dýskolos | doo'-kol-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1418 and κόλον (food)\nStrong's: properly, fastidious about eating (peevish), i.e. (genitive case) impracticable\nKJV: —hard.\n\nSee: G1418 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: δύσκολος \nHebrew Equivalents: H343 אֵיד",
    1423: "δυσκόλως (dyskólōs | doos-kol'-oce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G1422\nStrong's: impracticably\nKJV: —hardly.\n\nSee: G1422 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: δυσκόλως",
    1424: "δυσμή (dysmḗ | doos-may')\n\nDerivation: from G1416\nStrong's: the sun-set, i.e. (by implication) the western region\nKJV: —west.\n\nSee: G1416 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: δυσμή \nHebrew Equivalents: H268 אָחֹור, H314 אַחֲרֹון, H935 בֹּוא, H3220 יָם, H4606 מֵעָל, H4627 מַעֲרָב, H6160 עֲרָבָה",
    1425: "δυσνόητος (dysnóētos | doos-no'-ay-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1418 and a derivative of G3539\nStrong's: difficult of perception\nKJV: —hard to be understood.\n\nSee: G1418 \nSee: G3539 \n\nCognate Group: G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)\nVariants: δυσνόητος",
    1426: "δυσφημία (dysphēmía | doos-fay-mee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1418 and G5345\nStrong's: defamation\nKJV: —evil report.\n\nSee: G1418 \nSee: G5345 \n\nCognate Group: G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)\nVariants: δυσφημία",
    1427: "δώδεκα (dṓdeka | do'-dek-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1417 and G1176\nStrong's: two and ten, i.e. a dozen\nKJV: —twelve.\n\nSee: G1417 \nSee: G1176 \n\nCognate Group: G1427 (twelve), G1429 (twelve tribes), G1428 (twelfth)\nVariants: δώδεκα",
