    1429: "δωδεκάφυλον (dōdekáphylon | do-dek-af'-oo-lon)\n\nDerivation: from G1427 and G5443\nStrong's: the commonwealth of Israel\nKJV: —twelve tribes.\n\nSee: G1427 \nSee: G5443 \n\nCognate Group: G1427 (twelve), G1429 (twelve tribes), G1428 (twelfth)\nVariants: δωδεκάφυλον",
    1430: "δῶμα (dōma | do'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from δέμω (to build)\nStrong's: properly, an edifice, i.e. (specially) a roof\nKJV: —housetop.\n\nCognate Group: G1427 (twelve), G1429 (twelve tribes), G1428 (twelfth)\nVariants: δῶμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1406 גָּג",
