    1434: "δώρημα (dṓrēma | do'-ray-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G1433\nStrong's: a bestowment\nKJV: —gift.\n\nSee: G1433 \n\nCognate Group: G1432 (without a cause), G3860 (betray), G467 (recompense), G3862 (ordinance), G1325 (adventure), G468 (recompense), G1431 (gift), G591 (deliver), G1434 (gift), G469 (reward), G1433 (give), G1435 (gift)\nVariants: δώρημα",
    1435: "δῶρον (dōron | do'-ron)\n\n\nStrong's: a present; specially, a sacrifice\nKJV: —gift, offering.\n\nCognate Group: G1432 (without a cause), G3860 (betray), G467 (recompense), G3862 (ordinance), G1325 (adventure), G468 (recompense), G1431 (gift), G591 (deliver), G1434 (gift), G469 (reward), G1433 (give), G1435 (gift)\nVariants: δῶρον \nHebrew Equivalents: H814 אֶשְׁכָּר, H1215 בֶּצַע, H2065 זֶבֶד, H3899 לֶחֶם, H3948 לֶקַח, H3971 מאוּם, H4030 מִגְדָּנָה, H4242 מְחִיר, H4503 מִנְחָה, H4864 מַשְׂאֵת, H4979 מַתָּנָה, H5088 נֶדֶר, H7133 קׇרְבָּן, H7810 שַׁחַד, H7862 שַׁי, H8426 תֹּודָה",
    1436: "ἔα (éa | eh'-ah)\n\nDerivation: apparent imperative of G1439\nStrong's: properly, let it be, i.e. (as interjection) aha!\nKJV: —let alone.\n\nSee: G1439 \n\nCognate Group: G1432 (without a cause), G3860 (betray), G467 (recompense), G3862 (ordinance), G1325 (adventure), G468 (recompense), G1431 (gift), G591 (deliver), G1434 (gift), G469 (reward), G1433 (give), G1435 (gift)\nVariants: ἔα",
    1437: "ἐάν (eán | eh-an')\n\nDerivation: from G1487 and G302\nStrong's: a conditional particle; in case that, provided, etc.; often used in connection with other particles to denote indefiniteness or uncertainty\nKJV: —before, but, except, (and) if, (if) so, (what-, whither-)soever, though, when (-soever), whether (or), to whom, (who-)so(-ever). See G3361 .\n\nSee: G1487 \nSee: G302 \nSee: G3361 \n\nCognate Group: G1432 (without a cause), G3860 (betray), G467 (recompense), G3862 (ordinance), G1325 (adventure), G468 (recompense), G1431 (gift), G591 (deliver), G1434 (gift), G469 (reward), G1433 (give), G1435 (gift)\nVariants: ἐάν, ἐάνπερ",
    1438: "ἑαυτοῦ (heautoû | heh-ow-too')\n\nDerivation: from a reflexive pronoun otherwise obsolete and the genitive case (dative case or accusative case) of G846\nStrong's: him- (her-, it-, them-, also (in conjunction with the personal pronoun of the other persons) my-, thy-, our-, your-) self (selves), etc.\nKJV: —alone, her (own, -self), (he) himself, his (own), itself, one (to) another, our (thine) own(-selves), + that she had, their (own, own selves), (of) them(-selves), they, thyself, you, your (own, own conceits, own selves, -selves).\n\nSee: G846 \n\nCognate Group: G1432 (without a cause), G3860 (betray), G467 (recompense), G3862 (ordinance), G1325 (adventure), G468 (recompense), G1431 (gift), G591 (deliver), G1434 (gift), G469 (reward), G1433 (give), G1435 (gift)\nVariants: ἑαυτοῦ",
    1439: "ἐάω (eáō | eh-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: to let be, i.e. permit or leave alone\nKJV: —commit, leave, let (alone), suffer. See also G1436 .\n\nSee: G1436 \n\nCognate Group: G1432 (without a cause), G3860 (betray), G467 (recompense), G3862 (ordinance), G1325 (adventure), G468 (recompense), G1431 (gift), G591 (deliver), G1434 (gift), G469 (reward), G1433 (give), G1435 (gift)\nVariants: ἐάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1826 דָּמַם, H2308 חָדַל, H3051 יָהַב, H5117 נוּחַ, H5352 נָקָה, H5414 נָתַן, H7503 רָפָה, H7662 שְׁבַק",
    1440: "ἑβδομήκοντα (hebdomḗkonta | heb-dom-ay'-kon-tah)\n\nDerivation: from G1442 and a modified form of G1176\nStrong's: seventy\nKJV: —seventy, three score and ten.\n\nSee: G1442 \nSee: G1176 \n\nCognate Group: G1442 (seventh), G1440 (seventy), G1441 (seventy times)\nVariants: ἑβδομήκοντα",
    1441: "ἑβδομηκοντάκις (hebdomēkontákis | heb-dom-ay-kon-tak-is)\n\nDerivation: multiple adverb from G1440\nStrong's: seventy times\nKJV: —seventy times.\n\nSee: G1440 \n\nCognate Group: G1442 (seventh), G1440 (seventy), G1441 (seventy times)\nVariants: ἑβδομηκοντάκις \nHebrew Equivalents: H7657 שִׁבְעִים",
    1442: "ἕβδομος (hébdomos | heb'-dom-os)\n\nDerivation: ordinal from G2033\nStrong's: seventh\nKJV: —seventh.\n\nSee: G2033 \n\nCognate Group: G1442 (seventh), G1440 (seventy), G1441 (seventy times)\nVariants: ἕβδομος \nHebrew Equivalents: H7637 שְׁבִיעִי, H7676 שַׁבָּת",
    1443: "Ἐβέρ (Ebér | eb-er')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H5677)\nStrong's: Eber, a patriarch\nKJV: —Eber.\nSee: H5677\n\nCognate Group: G1442 (seventh), G1440 (seventy), G1441 (seventy times)\nVariants: Ἐβέρ, Ἔβερ, Ἕβερ \nHebrew Equivalents: H5677 עֵבֵר",
    1444: "Ἑβραϊκός (Hebraïkós | heb-rah-ee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G1443\nStrong's: Hebraic or the Jewish language\nKJV: —Hebrew.\n\nSee: G1443 \n\nCognate Group: G1444 (Hebrew), G1446 (Hebrew), G1447 (in Hebrew), G1445 (Hebrew)\nVariants: Ἑβραϊκός",
    1445: "Ἑβραῖος (Hebraîos | heb-rah'-yos)\n\nDerivation: from G1443\nStrong's: a Hebræan (i.e. Hebrew) or Jew\nKJV: —Hebrew.\n\nSee: G1443 \n\nCognate Group: G1444 (Hebrew), G1446 (Hebrew), G1447 (in Hebrew), G1445 (Hebrew)\nVariants: Ἑβραῖος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5676 עֵבֶר",
    1446: "Ἑβραΐς (Hebraḯs | heb-rah-is')\n\nDerivation: from G1443\nStrong's: the Hebraistic (Hebrew) or Jewish (Chaldee) language\nKJV: —Hebrew.\n\nSee: G1443 \n\nCognate Group: G1444 (Hebrew), G1446 (Hebrew), G1447 (in Hebrew), G1445 (Hebrew)\nVariants: Ἑβραΐς, Ἑβραί̈ς, Ἑβραΐς",
    1447: "Ἑβραϊστί (Hebraïstí | heb-rah-is-tee')\n\nDerivation: adverb from G1446\nStrong's: Hebraistically or in the Jewish (Chaldee) language\nKJV: —in (the) Hebrew (tongue).\n\nSee: G1446 \n\nCognate Group: G1444 (Hebrew), G1446 (Hebrew), G1447 (in Hebrew), G1445 (Hebrew)\nVariants: Ἑβραϊστί",
    1448: "ἐγγίζω (engízō | eng-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1451\nStrong's: to make near, i.e. (reflexively) approach\nKJV: —approach, be at hand, come (draw) near, be (come, draw) nigh.\n\nSee: G1451 \n\nCognate Group: G1448 (approach), G4331 (come nigh), G1451 (from)\nVariants: ἐγγίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2040 הָרַס, H2114 זוּר, H2363 חוּשׁ, H3176 יָחַל, H3369 יָקֹשׁ, H3671 כָּנָף, H4291 מְטָא, H5060 נָגַע, H5066 נָגַשׁ, H6960 קָוָה, H7126 קָרַב",
    1449: "ἐγγράφω (engráphō | eng-graf'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G1125\nStrong's: to \"engrave\", i.e. inscribe\nKJV: —write (in).\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G1125 \n\nCognate Group: G1448 (approach), G4331 (come nigh), G1451 (from)\nVariants: ἐγγράφω",
    1450: "ἔγγυος (éngyos | eng'-goo-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and γυῖον (a limb)\nStrong's: pledged (as if articulated by a member), i.e. a bondsman\nKJV: —surety.\n\nSee: G1722 \n\nCognate Group: G1450 (surety)\nVariants: ἔγγυος",
    1451: "ἐγγύς (engýs | eng-goos')\n\nDerivation: from a primary verb ἄγχω (to squeeze or throttle\nStrong's: akin to the base of G43); near (literally or figuratively, of place or time)\nKJV: —from, at hand, near, nigh (at hand, unto), ready.\n\nSee: G43 \n\nCognate Group: G1448 (approach), G4331 (come nigh), G1451 (from)\nVariants: ἐγγύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H251 אָח, H4136 מוּל, H6102 עָצֵל, H7126 קָרַב, H7138 קָרֹוב, H7200 רָאָה",
    1452: "ἐγγύτερον (engýteron | eng-goo'-ter-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of the comparative of G1451\nStrong's: nearer\nKJV: —nearer.\n\nSee: G1451 \n\nCognate Group: G1448 (approach), G4331 (come nigh), G1451 (from)\nVariants: ἐγγύτερον, ἐγγύς",
    1453: "ἐγείρω (egeírō | eg-i'-ro)\n\nDerivation: probably akin to the base of G58 (through the idea of collecting one's faculties)\nStrong's: to waken (transitively or intransitively), i.e. rouse (literally, from sleep, from sitting or lying, from disease, from death; or figuratively, from obscurity, inactivity, ruins, nonexistence)\nKJV: —awake, lift (up), raise (again, up), rear up, (a-)rise (again, up), stand, take up.\n\nSee: G58 \n\nCognate Group: G1454 (resurrection), G1453 (awake), G1127 (be vigilant), G1825 (raise up)\nVariants: ἐγείρω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6965 קוּם",
    1454: "ἔγερσις (égersis | eg'-er-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G1453\nStrong's: a resurgence (from death)\nKJV: —resurrection.\n\nSee: G1453 \n\nCognate Group: G1454 (resurrection), G1453 (awake), G1127 (be vigilant), G1825 (raise up)\nVariants: ἔγερσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H6965 קוּם",
    1455: "ἐγκάθετος (enkáthetos | eng-kath'-et-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and a derivative of G2524\nStrong's: subinduced, i.e. surreptitiously suborned as a lier-in-wait\nKJV: —spy.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G2524 \n\nCognate Group: G1454 (resurrection), G1453 (awake), G1127 (be vigilant), G1825 (raise up)\nVariants: ἐγκάθετος",
    1456: "ἐγκαίνια (enkaínia | eng-kah'-ee-nee-ah)\n\nDerivation: neuter plural of a presumed compound from G1722 and G2537\nStrong's: innovatives, i.e. (specially) renewal (of religious services after the Antiochian interruption)\nKJV: —dedication.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G2537 \n\nCognate Group: G1454 (resurrection), G1453 (awake), G1127 (be vigilant), G1825 (raise up)\nVariants: ἐγκαίνια",
    1457: "ἐγκαινίζω (enkainízō | eng-kahee-nid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1456\nStrong's: to renew, i.e. inaugurate\nKJV: —consecrate, dedicate.\n\nSee: G1456 \n\nCognate Group: G365 (renew), G341 (renew), G340 (renew), G1457 (consecrate), G342 (renewing), G2538 (newness), G2537 (new)\nVariants: ἐγκαινίζω",
    1458: "ἐγκαλέω (enkaléō | eng-kal-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G2564\nStrong's: to call in (as a debt or demand), i.e. bring to account (charge, criminate, etc.)\nKJV: —accuse, call in question, implead, lay to the charge.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G2564 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: ἐγκαλέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H6315 פּוּחַ, H7121 קָרָא",
    1459: "ἐγκαταλείπω (enkataleípō | eng-kat-al-i'-po)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G2641\nStrong's: to leave behind in some place, i.e. (in a good sense) let remain over, or (in a bad sense) to desert\nKJV: —forsake, leave.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G2641 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: ἐγκαταλείπω \nHebrew Equivalents: H898 בָּגַד, H3427 יָשַׁב, H3498 יָתַר, H3772 כָּרַת, H3988 מָאַס, H5428 נָתַשׁ, H5800 עָזַב, H6328 פּוּק, H7503 רָפָה, H7591 שְׁאִיָּה, H7604 שָׁאַר, H7725 שׁוּב, H7876 שָׁיָה, H7911 שָׁכַח",
    1460: "ἐγκατοικέω (enkatoikéō | eng-kat-oy-keh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G2730\nStrong's: to settle down in a place, i.e. reside\nKJV: —dwell among.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G2730 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: ἐγκατοικέω",
    1461: "ἐγκεντρίζω (enkentrízō | eng-ken-trid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and a derivative of G2759\nStrong's: to prick in, i.e. ingraft\nKJV: —graff in(-to).\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G2759 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: ἐγκεντρίζω",
    1462: "ἔγκλημα (énklēma | eng'-klay-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G1458\nStrong's: an accusation, i.e. offence alleged\nKJV: —crime laid against, laid to charge.\n\nSee: G1458 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: ἔγκλημα",
    1463: "ἐγκομβόομαι (enkombóomai | eng-kom-bo'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1722 and κομβόω (to gird)\nStrong's: to engirdle oneself (for labor), i.e. figuratively (the apron as being a badge of servitude) to wear (in token of mutual deference)\nKJV: —be clothed with.\n\nSee: G1722 \n\nCognate Group: G1463 (be clothed with)\nVariants: ἐγκομβόομαι",
    1464: "ἐγκοπή (enkopḗ | eng-kop-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G1465\nStrong's: a hindrance\nKJV: —X hinder.\n\nSee: G1465 \n\nCognate Group: G1464 (X hinder), G609 (cut off), G2870 (lamentation), G1581 (cut down), G2875 (cut down), G1465 (hinder)\nVariants: ἐγκοπή, ἐκκοπή",
    1465: "ἐγκόπτω (enkóptō | eng-kop'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G2875\nStrong's: to cut into, i.e. (figuratively) impede, detain\nKJV: —hinder, be tedious unto.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G2875 \n\nCognate Group: G1464 (X hinder), G609 (cut off), G2870 (lamentation), G1581 (cut down), G2875 (cut down), G1465 (hinder)\nVariants: ἐγκόπτω",
    1466: "ἐγκράτεια (enkráteia | eng-krat'-i-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1468\nStrong's: self-control (especially continence)\nKJV: —temperance.\n\nSee: G1468 \n\nCognate Group: G1467 (can contain), G192 (excess), G1466 (temperance), G193 (incontinent), G1468 (temperate)\nVariants: ἐγκράτεια",
    1467: "ἐγκρατεύομαι (enkrateúomai | eng-krat-yoo'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1468\nStrong's: to exercise self-restraint (in diet and chastity)\nKJV: —can(-not) contain, be temperate.\n\nSee: G1468 \n\nCognate Group: G1467 (can contain), G192 (excess), G1466 (temperance), G193 (incontinent), G1468 (temperate)\nVariants: ἐγκρατεύομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H662 אָפַק",
    1468: "ἐγκρατής (enkratḗs | eng-krat-ace')\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G2904\nStrong's: strong in a thing (masterful), i.e. (figuratively and reflexively) self-controlled (in appetite, etc.)\nKJV: —temperate.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G2904 \n\nCognate Group: G1467 (can contain), G192 (excess), G1466 (temperance), G193 (incontinent), G1468 (temperate)\nVariants: ἐγκρατής",
    1469: "ἐγκρίνω (enkrínō | eng-kree'-no)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G2919\nStrong's: to judge in, i.e. count among\nKJV: —make of the number.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G2919 \n\nCognate Group: G612 (answer), G2631 (condemnation), G470 (answer again), G351 (examination), G2923 (judge), G610 (sentence), G2924 (discerner), G1469 (make of the number), G350 (ask), G1253 (discern), G843 (condemned of self), G2632 (condemn), G2919 (avenge), G2917 (avenge), G1252 (contend), G87 (without partiality), G611 (answer), G178 (uncondemned), G2633 (condemn), G2920 (accusation), G2922 (to judge)\nVariants: ἐγκρίνω",
    1470: "ἐγκρύπτω (enkrýptō | eng-kroop'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G2928\nStrong's: to conceal in, i.e. incorporate with\nKJV: —hid in.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G2928 \n\nCognate Group: G612 (answer), G2631 (condemnation), G470 (answer again), G351 (examination), G2923 (judge), G610 (sentence), G2924 (discerner), G1469 (make of the number), G350 (ask), G1253 (discern), G843 (condemned of self), G2632 (condemn), G2919 (avenge), G2917 (avenge), G1252 (contend), G87 (without partiality), G611 (answer), G178 (uncondemned), G2633 (condemn), G2920 (accusation), G2922 (to judge)\nVariants: ἐγκρύπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2244 חָבָא, H2934 טָמַן, H5746 עוּג, H6845 צָפַן",
    1471: "ἔγκυος (énkyos | eng'-koo-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and the base of G2949\nStrong's: swelling inside, i.e. pregnant\nKJV: —great with child.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G2949 \n\nCognate Group: G612 (answer), G2631 (condemnation), G470 (answer again), G351 (examination), G2923 (judge), G610 (sentence), G2924 (discerner), G1469 (make of the number), G350 (ask), G1253 (discern), G843 (condemned of self), G2632 (condemn), G2919 (avenge), G2917 (avenge), G1252 (contend), G87 (without partiality), G611 (answer), G178 (uncondemned), G2633 (condemn), G2920 (accusation), G2922 (to judge)\nVariants: ἔγκυος",
    1472: "ἐγχρίω (enchríō | eng-khree'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G5548\nStrong's: to rub in (oil), i.e. besmear\nKJV: —anoint.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G5548 \n\nCognate Group: G612 (answer), G2631 (condemnation), G470 (answer again), G351 (examination), G2923 (judge), G610 (sentence), G2924 (discerner), G1469 (make of the number), G350 (ask), G1253 (discern), G843 (condemned of self), G2632 (condemn), G2919 (avenge), G2917 (avenge), G1252 (contend), G87 (without partiality), G611 (answer), G178 (uncondemned), G2633 (condemn), G2920 (accusation), G2922 (to judge)\nVariants: ἐγχρίω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7167 קָרַע",
    1473: "ἐγώ (egṓ | eg-o')\n\nDerivation: a primary pronoun of the first person I (only expressed when emphatic)\nKJV: —I, me. For the other cases and the plural see G1691, G1698, G1700, G2248, G2249, G2254, G2257, etc.\n\nSee: G1691 \nSee: G1698 \nSee: G1700 \nSee: G2248 \nSee: G2249 \nSee: G2254 \nSee: G2257 \n\nCognate Group: G1473 (I)\nVariants: ἐγώ",
    1474: "ἐδαφίζω (edaphízō | ed-af-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1475\nStrong's: to raze\nKJV: —lay even with the ground.\n\nSee: G1475 \n\nCognate Group: G1473 (I)\nVariants: ἐδαφίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3427 יָשַׁב, H5310 נָפַץ, H5428 נָתַשׁ, H7376 רָטָשׁ",
    1475: "ἔδαφος (édaphos | ed'-af-os)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G1476\nStrong's: a basis (bottom), i.e. the soil\nKJV: —ground.\n\nSee: G1476 \n\nCognate Group: G1473 (I)\nVariants: ἔδαφος \nHebrew Equivalents: H738 אֲרִי, H776 אֶרֶץ, H4144 מֹוסָד, H6083 עָפָר, H7172 קַרְקַע",
    1476: "ἑδραῖος (hedraîos | hed-rah'-yos)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of ἕζομαι (to sit)\nStrong's: sedentary, i.e. (by implication) immovable\nKJV: —settled, stedfast.\n\nCognate Group: G1477 (ground), G1476 (settled)\nVariants: ἑδραῖος",
    1477: "ἑδραίωμα (hedraíōma | hed-rah'-yo-mah)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G1476\nStrong's: a support, i.e. (figuratively) basis\nKJV: —ground.\n\nSee: G1476 \n\nCognate Group: G1477 (ground), G1476 (settled)\nVariants: ἑδραίωμα",
    1478: "Ἐζεκίας (Ezekías | ed-zek-ee'-as)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H2396)\nStrong's: Ezekias (i.e. Hezekeiah), an Israelite\nKJV: —Ezekias.\nSee: H2396\n\nCognate Group: G1477 (ground), G1476 (settled)\nVariants: Ἐζεκίας, Ἑζεκίας \nHebrew Equivalents: H2396 חִזְקִיָּה",
    1479: "ἐθελοθρησκεία (ethelothrēskeía | eth-el-oth-race-ki'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2309 and G2356\nStrong's: voluntary (arbitrary and unwarranted) piety, i.e. sanctimony\nKJV: —will worship.\n\nSee: G2309 \nSee: G2356 \n\nCognate Group: G1479 (will worship), G2357 (religious), G2356 (religion)\nVariants: ἐθελοθρησκεία, ἐθελοθρησκία",
    1480: "ἐθίζω (ethízō | eth-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1485\nStrong's: to accustom, i.e. (neuter passive participle) customary\nKJV: —custom.\n\nSee: G1485 \n\nCognate Group: G1479 (will worship), G2357 (religious), G2356 (religion)\nVariants: ἐθίζω",
    1481: "ἐθνάρχης (ethnárchēs | eth-nar'-khace)\n\nDerivation: from G1484 and G746\nStrong's: the governor (not king) of a district\nKJV: —ethnarch.\n\nSee: G1484 \nSee: G746 \n\nCognate Group: G1479 (will worship), G2357 (religious), G2356 (religion)\nVariants: ἐθνάρχης",
    1482: "ἐθνικός (ethnikós | eth-nee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G1484\nStrong's: national (\"ethnic\"), i.e. (specially) a Gentile\nKJV: —heathen (man).\n\nSee: G1484 \n\nCognate Group: G1484 (Gentile), G1482 (heathen), G1483 (after the manner of Gentiles)\nVariants: ἐθνικός",
    1483: "ἐθνικῶς (ethnikōs | eth-nee-koce')\n\nDerivation: adverb from G1482\nStrong's: as a Gentile\nKJV: —after the manner of Gentiles.\n\nSee: G1482 \n\nCognate Group: G1484 (Gentile), G1482 (heathen), G1483 (after the manner of Gentiles)\nVariants: ἐθνικῶς",
    1484: "ἔθνος (éthnos | eth'-nos)\n\nDerivation: probably from G1486\nStrong's: a race (as of the same habit), i.e. a tribe; specially, a foreign (non-Jewish) one (usually, by implication, pagan)\nKJV: —Gentile, heathen, nation, people.\n\nSee: G1486 \n\nCognate Group: G1484 (Gentile), G1482 (heathen), G1483 (after the manner of Gentiles)\nVariants: ἔθνος \nHebrew Equivalents: H339 אִי, H524 אֻמָּה, H776 אֶרֶץ, H1121 בֵּן, H1471 גֹּוי, H1995 הָמֹון, H2104 זוּזִים, H2233 זֶרַע, H2269 חֲבַר, H2428 חַיִל, H4325 מַיִם, H5387 נָשִׂיא, H5650 עֶבֶד, H5971 עַם, H6635 צָבָא",
    1485: "ἔθος (éthos | eth'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1486\nStrong's: a usage (prescribed by habit or law)\nKJV: —custom, manner, be wont.\n\nSee: G1486 \n\nCognate Group: G1485 (custom)\nVariants: ἔθος",
    1486: "ἔθω (éthō | eth'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to be used (by habit or conventionality); neuter perfect participle usage\nKJV: —be custom (manner, wont).\n\nCognate Group: G1485 (custom)\nVariants: ἔθω, εἴωθα",
    1487: "εἰ (ei | i)\n\nDerivation: a primary particle of conditionality\nStrong's: if, whether, that, etc.\nKJV: —forasmuch as, if, that, (al-)though, whether. Often used in connection or composition with other particles, especially as in G1489, G1490, G1499, G1508, G1509, G1512, G1513, G1536, G1537 . See also G1437 .\n\nSee: G1489 \nSee: G1490 \nSee: G1499 \nSee: G1508 \nSee: G1509 \nSee: G1512 \nSee: G1513 \nSee: G1536 \nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1437 \n\nCognate Group: G1485 (custom)\nVariants: εἰ",
    1488: "εἶ (eî | i)\n\nDerivation: second person singular present of G1510\nStrong's: thou art\nKJV: —art, be.\n\nSee: G1510 \n\nCognate Group: G1485 (custom)\nVariants: εἶ, εἰμί",
    1489: "εἴγε (eíge | i'-gheh)\n\nDerivation: from G1487 and G1065\nStrong's: if indeed, seeing that, unless, (with negative) otherwise\nKJV: —if (so be that, yet).\n\nSee: G1487 \nSee: G1065 \n\nCognate Group: G1485 (custom)\nVariants: εἴγε, εἰ, γέ G1624",
    1490: "εἰ δὲ μή(γε) (ei dè mḗ(ge) | i deh may'-(gheh))\n\nDerivation: from G1487, G1161, and G3361 (sometimes with G1065 added)\nStrong's: but if not\nKJV: —(or) else, if (not, otherwise), otherwise.\n\nSee: G1487 \nSee: G1161 \nSee: G3361 \nSee: G1065 \n\nCognate Group: G1485 (custom)\nVariants: εἰ δὲ μή(γε), εἰ, δέ, μή, γέ",
    1491: "εἶδος (eîdos | i'-dos)\n\nDerivation: from G1492\nStrong's: a view, i.e. form (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —appearance, fashion, shape, sight.\n\nSee: G1492 \n\nCognate Group: G2397 (countenance), G1491 (appearance)\nVariants: εἶδος, εὶδος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3303 יָפֶה, H4758 מַרְאֶה, H4940 מִשְׁפָּחָה, H4941 מִשְׁפָּט, H5869 עַיִן, H6079 עַפְעַף, H6106 עֶצֶם, H7897 שִׁית, H8389 תֹּאַר, H8389 תֹּאַר",
    1492: "εἴδω (eídō | i'-do)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: used only in certain past tenses, the others being borrowed from the equivalent G3700 and G3708 ; properly, to see (literally or figuratively); by implication, (in the perfect tense only) to know\nKJV: —be aware, behold, X can (+ not tell), consider, (have) know(-ledge), look (on), perceive, see, be sure, tell, understand, wish, wot. Compare G3700 .\n\nSee: G3700 \nSee: G3708 \nSee: G3700 \n\nCognate Group: G1492 (be aware)\nVariants: εἴδω, οἶδα",
    1493: "εἰδωλεῖον (eidōleîon | i-do-li'-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a presumed derivative of G1497\nStrong's: an image-fane\nKJV: —idol's temple.\n\nSee: G1497 \n\nCognate Group: G1493 (idol's temple), G1495 (idolatry), G1496 (idolater), G2712 (wholly given to idolatry), G1494 (offered to idols), G1497 (idol)\nVariants: εἰδωλεῖον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1004 בַּיִת",
    1494: "εἰδωλόθυτον (eidōlóthyton | i-do-loth'-oo-ton)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a compound of G1497 and a presumed derivative of G2380\nStrong's: an image-sacrifice, i.e. part of an idolatrous offering\nKJV: —(meat, thing that is) offered (in sacrifice, sacrificed) to (unto) idols.\n\nSee: G1497 \nSee: G2380 \n\nCognate Group: G1493 (idol's temple), G1495 (idolatry), G1496 (idolater), G2712 (wholly given to idolatry), G1494 (offered to idols), G1497 (idol)\nVariants: εἰδωλόθυτον, εἰδωλόθυτος, ἱερόθυτος",
    1495: "εἰδωλολατρεία (eidōlolatreía | i-do-lol-at-ri'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1497 and G2999\nStrong's: image-worship (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —idolatry.\n\nSee: G1497 \nSee: G2999 \n\nCognate Group: G1493 (idol's temple), G1495 (idolatry), G1496 (idolater), G2712 (wholly given to idolatry), G1494 (offered to idols), G1497 (idol)\nVariants: εἰδωλολατρεία, εἰδωλολατρία",
    1496: "εἰδωλολάτρης (eidōlolátrēs | i-do-lol-at'-race)\n\nDerivation: from G1497 and the base of G3000\nStrong's: an image- (servant or) worshipper (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —idolater.\n\nSee: G1497 \nSee: G3000 \n\nCognate Group: G1493 (idol's temple), G1495 (idolatry), G1496 (idolater), G2712 (wholly given to idolatry), G1494 (offered to idols), G1497 (idol)\nVariants: εἰδωλολάτρης",
    1497: "εἴδωλον (eídōlon | i'-do-lon)\n\nDerivation: from G1491\nStrong's: an image (i.e. for worship); by implication, a heathen god, or (plural) the worship of such\nKJV: —idol.\n\nSee: G1491 \n\nCognate Group: G1493 (idol's temple), G1495 (idolatry), G1496 (idolater), G2712 (wholly given to idolatry), G1494 (offered to idols), G1497 (idol)\nVariants: εἴδωλον \nHebrew Equivalents: H410 אֵל, H433 אֱלֹוהַּ, H457 אֱלִיל, H1116 בָּמָה, H1167 בַּעַל, H1544 גִּלּוּל, H1892 הֶבֶל, H2553 חַמָּן, H4656 מִפְלֶצֶת, H6090 עֹצֶב, H6459 פֶּסֶל, H6754 צֶלֶם, H8163 שָׂעִיר, H8251 שִׁקּוּץ, H8655 תְּרָפִים",
    1498: "εἴην (eíēn | i'-ane)\n\nDerivation: optative (i.e. English subjunctive) present of G1510 (including the other person)\nStrong's: might (could, would, or should) be\nKJV: —mean, + perish, should be, was, were.\n\nSee: G1510 \n\nCognate Group: G1493 (idol's temple), G1495 (idolatry), G1496 (idolater), G2712 (wholly given to idolatry), G1494 (offered to idols), G1497 (idol)\nVariants: εἴην, εἰμί",
    1499: "εἰ καί (ei kaí | i kahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1487 and G2532\nStrong's: if also (or even)\nKJV: —if (that), though.\n\nSee: G1487 \nSee: G2532 \n\nCognate Group: G1493 (idol's temple), G1495 (idolatry), G1496 (idolater), G2712 (wholly given to idolatry), G1494 (offered to idols), G1497 (idol)\nVariants: εἰ καί, εἰ, καί",
    1500: "εἰκῆ (eikē | i-kay')\n\nDerivation: probably from G1502 (through the idea of failure)\nStrong's: idly, i.e. without reason (or effect)\nKJV: —without a cause, (in) vain(-ly).\n\nSee: G1502 \n\nCognate Group: G1500 (without a cause)\nVariants: εἰκῆ, εἰκῇ",
    1501: "εἴκοσι (eíkosi | i'-kos-ee)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a score\nKJV: —twenty.\n\nCognate Group: G1500 (without a cause)\nVariants: εἴκοσι, εἴκοσι(ν) \nHebrew Equivalents: H6030 עָנָה",
    1502: "εἴκω (eíkō | i'-ko)\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary verb\nStrong's: properly, to be weak, i.e. yield\nKJV: —give place.\n\nCognate Group: G1500 (without a cause)\nVariants: εἴκω",
    1503: "εἴκω (eíkō | i'-ko)\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary verb (perhaps akin to G1502 through the idea of faintness as a copy)\nStrong's: to resemble\nKJV: —be like.\n\nSee: G1502 \n\nCognate Group: G1500 (without a cause)\nVariants: εἴκω, ἔοικα",
    1504: "εἰκών (eikṓn | i-kone')\n\nDerivation: from G1503\nStrong's: a likeness, i.e. (literally) statue, profile, or (figuratively) representation, resemblance\nKJV: —image.\n\nSee: G1503 \n\nCognate Group: G1504 (image)\nVariants: εἰκών \nHebrew Equivalents: H6754 צֶלֶם",
    1505: "εἰλικρίνεια (eilikríneia | i-lik-ree'-ni-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1506\nStrong's: clearness, i.e. (by implication) purity (figuratively)\nKJV: —sincerity.\n\nSee: G1506 \n\nCognate Group: G1506 (pure), G1505 (sincerity)\nVariants: εἰλικρίνεια",
    1506: "εἰλικρινής (eilikrinḗs | i-lik-ree-nace')\n\nDerivation: from εἵλη (the sun's ray) and G2919\nStrong's: judged by sunlight, i.e. tested as genuine (figuratively)\nKJV: —pure, sincere.\n\nSee: G2919 \n\nCognate Group: G1506 (pure), G1505 (sincerity)\nVariants: εἰλικρινής",
    1507: "εἱλίσσω (heilíssō | hi-lis'-so)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of a primary but defective verb εἵλω (of the same meaning)\nStrong's: to coil or wrap\nKJV: —roll together. See also G1667 .\n\nSee: G1667 \n\nCognate Group: G1506 (pure), G1505 (sincerity)\nVariants: εἱλίσσω, ἑλίσσω G1813",
    1508: "εἰ μή (ei mḗ | i may)\n\nDerivation: from G1487 and G3361\nStrong's: if not\nKJV: —but, except (that), if not, more than, save (only) that, saving, till.\n\nSee: G1487 \nSee: G3361 \n\nCognate Group: G1506 (pure), G1505 (sincerity)\nVariants: εἰ μή, εἰ, μή",
    1509: "εἰ μή τι (ei mḗ ti | i may tee)\n\nDerivation: from G1508 and the neuter of G5100\nStrong's: if not somewhat\nKJV: —except.\n\nSee: G1508 \nSee: G5100 \n\nCognate Group: G1506 (pure), G1505 (sincerity)\nVariants: εἰ μή τι, εἰ, μή, τὶς",
    1510: "εἰμί (eimí | i-mee')\n\nDerivation: the first person singular present indicative; a prolonged form of a primary and defective verb\nStrong's: I exist (used only when emphatic)\nKJV: —am, have been, X it is I, was. See also G1488, G1498, G1511, G1527, G2258, G2071, G2070, G2075, G2076, G2771, G2468, G5600 .\n\nSee: G1488 \nSee: G1498 \nSee: G1511 \nSee: G1527 \nSee: G2258 \nSee: G2071 \nSee: G2070 \nSee: G2075 \nSee: G2076 \nSee: G2771 \nSee: G2468 \nSee: G5600 \n\nCognate Group: G5607 (be), G1510 (am)\nVariants: εἰμί",
    1511: "εἶναι (eînai | i'-nahee)\n\nDerivation: present infinitive from G1510\nStrong's: to exist\nKJV: —am, was. come, is, X lust after, X please well, there is, to be, was.\n\nSee: G1510 \n\nCognate Group: G5607 (be), G1510 (am)\nVariants: εἶναι, εἰμί",
    1512: "εἴ περ (eí per | i per)\n\nDerivation: from G1487 and G4007\nStrong's: if perhaps\nKJV: —if so be (that), seeing, though.\n\nSee: G1487 \nSee: G4007 \n\nCognate Group: G5607 (be), G1510 (am)\nVariants: εἴ περ, εἴπερ, εἰ w. περ",
    1513: "εἴ πως (eí pōs | i poce)\n\nDerivation: from G1487 and G4458\nStrong's: if somehow\nKJV: —if by any means.\n\nSee: G1487 \nSee: G4458 \n\nCognate Group: G5607 (be), G1510 (am)\nVariants: εἴ πως, εἴπως",
    1514: "εἰρηνεύω (eirēneúō | i-rane-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1515\nStrong's: to be (act) peaceful\nKJV: —be at (have, live in) peace, live peaceably.\n\nSee: G1515 \n\nCognate Group: G1516 (peaceable), G1518 (peacemaker), G1517 (make peace), G1515 (one), G1514 (be at peace)\nVariants: εἰρηνεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7954 שְׁלָה, H7961 שָׁלֵו, H7999 שָׁלַם, H8252 שָׁקַט",
    1515: "εἰρήνη (eirḗnē | i-ray'-nay)\n\nDerivation: probably from a primary verb εἴρω (to join)\nStrong's: peace (literally or figuratively); by implication, prosperity\nKJV: —one, peace, quietness, rest, + set at one again.\n\nCognate Group: G1516 (peaceable), G1518 (peacemaker), G1517 (make peace), G1515 (one), G1514 (be at peace)\nVariants: εἰρήνη \nHebrew Equivalents: H983 בֶּטַח, H1980 הָלַךְ, H3948 לֶקַח, H6703 צַח, H7962 שַׁלְוָה, H7965 שָׁלֹום, H8252 שָׁקַט",
    1516: "εἰρηνικός (eirēnikós | i-ray-nee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G1515\nStrong's: pacific; by implication, salutary\nKJV: —peaceable.\n\nSee: G1515 \n\nCognate Group: G1516 (peaceable), G1518 (peacemaker), G1517 (make peace), G1515 (one), G1514 (be at peace)\nVariants: εἰρηνικός \nHebrew Equivalents: H3653 כֵּן, H7965 שָׁלֹום, H8003 שָׁלֵם",
    1517: "εἰρηνοποιέω (eirēnopoiéō | i-ray-nop-oy-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1518\nStrong's: to be a peace-maker, i.e. (figuratively) to harmonize\nKJV: —make peace.\n\nSee: G1518 \n\nCognate Group: G1516 (peaceable), G1518 (peacemaker), G1517 (make peace), G1515 (one), G1514 (be at peace)\nVariants: εἰρηνοποιέω",
    1518: "εἰρηνοποιός (eirēnopoiós | i-ray-nop-oy-os')\n\nDerivation: from G1515 and G4160\nStrong's: pacificatory, i.e. (subjectively) peaceable\nKJV: —peacemaker.\n\nSee: G1515 \nSee: G4160 \n\nCognate Group: G1516 (peaceable), G1518 (peacemaker), G1517 (make peace), G1515 (one), G1514 (be at peace)\nVariants: εἰρηνοποιός",
    1519: "εἰς (eis | ice)\n\nDerivation: a primary preposition\nStrong's: to or into (indicating the point reached or entered), of place, time, or (figuratively) purpose (result, etc.); also in adverbial phrases\nKJV: —(abundant-)ly, against, among, as, at, (back-)ward, before, by, concerning, + continual, + far more exceeding, for (intent, purpose), fore, + forth, in (among, at, unto, -so much that, -to), to the intent that, + of one mind, + never, of, (up-)on, + perish, + set at one again, (so) that, therefore(-unto), throughout, til, to (be, the end, -ward), (here-)until(-to), …ward, (where-)fore, with. Often used in composition with the same general import, but only with verbs (etc.) expressing motion (literally or figuratively).\n\nCognate Group: G1519 (ly)\nVariants: εἰς",
    1520: "εἷς (heîs | hice)\n\n (including the neuter (etc.) hen)\n\nDerivation: a primary numeral\nStrong's: one\nKJV: —a(-n, -ny, certain), + abundantly, man, one (another), only, other, some. See also G1527, G3367, G3391, G3762 .\n\nSee: G1527 \nSee: G3367 \nSee: G3391 \nSee: G3762 \n\nCognate Group: G1520 (one)\nVariants: εἷς",
    1521: "εἰσάγω (eiságō | ice-ag'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1519 and G71\nStrong's: to introduce (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —bring in(-to), (+ was to) lead into.\n\nSee: G1519 \nSee: G71 \n\nCognate Group: G1520 (one)\nVariants: εἰσάγω \nHebrew Equivalents: H622 אָסַף, H935 בֹּוא, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2388 חָזַק, H3051 יָהַב, H3318 יָצָא, H3365 יָקַר, H3947 לָקַח, H5090 נָהַג, H5954 עֲלַל, H6942 קָדַשׁ, H7121 קָרָא, H7725 שׁוּב",
    1522: "εἰσακούω (eisakoúō | ice-ak-oo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1519 and G191\nStrong's: to listen to\nKJV: —hear.\n\nSee: G1519 \nSee: G191 \n\nCognate Group: G5218 (obedience), G1522 (hear), G1873 (hear), G191 (give audience), G3878 (neglect to hear), G5219 (hearken), G5255 (obedient), G3876 (disobedience), G189 (audience)\nVariants: εἰσακούω \nHebrew Equivalents: H238 אָזַן, H2363 חוּשׁ, H3467 יָשַׁע, H3985 מָאֵן, H4784 מָרָה, H6030 עָנָה, H6279 עָתַר, H7181 קָשַׁב, H7521 רָצָה, H8085 שָׁמַע, H8104 שָׁמַר",
    1523: "εἰσδέχομαι (eisdéchomai | ice-dekh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1519 and G1209\nStrong's: to take into one's favor\nKJV: —receive.\n\nSee: G1519 \nSee: G1209 \n\nCognate Group: G1403 (feast), G1209 (accept), G1184 (accepted), G553 (look for), G1523 (receive), G587 (acceptable), G588 (accept), G2144 (acceptable), G4327 (accept), G594 (acceptation), G1561 (looking for)\nVariants: εἰσδέχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H6908 קָבַץ",
    1524: "εἴσειμι (eíseimi | ice'-i-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G1519 and εἶμι (to go)\nStrong's: to enter\nKJV: —enter (go) into.\n\nSee: G1519 \n\nCognate Group: G1403 (feast), G1209 (accept), G1184 (accepted), G553 (look for), G1523 (receive), G587 (acceptable), G588 (accept), G2144 (acceptable), G4327 (accept), G594 (acceptation), G1561 (looking for)\nVariants: εἴσειμι \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא",
