    1534: "εἶτα (eîta | i'-tah)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a particle of succession (in time or logical enumeration), then, moreover\nKJV: —after that(-ward), furthermore, then. See also G1899 .\n\nSee: G1899 \n\nCognate Group: G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)\nVariants: εἶτα, εὶτα",
    1535: "εἴτε (eíte | i'-teh)\n\nDerivation: from G1487 and G5037\nStrong's: if too\nKJV: —if, or, whether.\n\nSee: G1487 \nSee: G5037 \n\nCognate Group: G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)\nVariants: εἴτε",
    1536: "εἴ τις (eí tis | i tis)\n\nDerivation: from G1487 and G5100\nStrong's: if any\nKJV: —he that, if a(-ny) man('s thing, from any, ought), whether any, whosoever.\n\nSee: G1487 \nSee: G5100 \n\nCognate Group: G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)\nVariants: εἴ τις, εἰ, τὶς",
    1537: "ἐκ (ek | ek) or ἐξ (ex | ex)\n\nDerivation: a primary preposition denoting origin (the point whence action or motion proceeds), from, out (of place, time, or cause\nStrong's: literal or figurative; direct or remote)\nKJV: —after, among, X are, at, betwixt(-yond), by (the means of), exceedingly, (+ abundantly above), for(- th), from (among, forth, up), + grudgingly, + heartily, X heavenly, X hereby, + very highly, in, …ly, (because, by reason) of, off (from), on, out among (from, of), over, since, X thenceforth, through, X unto, X vehemently, with(-out). Often used in composition, with the same general import; often of completion.\n\nCognate Group: G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)\nVariants: ἐκ, ἐκπερισσῶς, ἐκφωνέω",
    1538: "ἕκαστος (hékastos | hek'-as-tos)\n\nDerivation: as if a superlative of ἕκας (afar)\nStrong's: each or every\nKJV: —any, both, each (one), every (man, one, woman), particularly.\n\nCognate Group: G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)\nVariants: ἕκαστος \nHebrew Equivalents: H120 אָדָם, H259 אֶחָד, H376 אִישׁ, H3117 יֹום, H3605 כֹּל, H3808 לֹא, H6591 פְּשַׁר, H8543 תְּמֹול",
    1539: "ἑκάστοτε (hekástote | hek-as'-tot-eh)\n\nDerivation: as if from G1538 and G5119\nStrong's: at every time\nKJV: —always.\n\nSee: G1538 \nSee: G5119 \n\nCognate Group: G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)\nVariants: ἑκάστοτε",
    1540: "ἑκατόν (hekatón | hek-at-on')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a hundred\nKJV: —hundred.\n\nCognate Group: G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)\nVariants: ἑκατόν",
    1541: "ἑκατονταέτης (hekatontaétēs | hek-at-on-tah-et'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G1540 and G2094\nStrong's: centenarian\nKJV: —hundred years old.\n\nSee: G1540 \nSee: G2094 \n\nCognate Group: G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)\nVariants: ἑκατονταέτης, ἑκατονταετής \nHebrew Equivalents: H1121 בֵּן",
    1542: "ἑκατονταπλασίων (hekatontaplasíōn | hek-at-on-ta-plah-sec'-own)\n\nDerivation: from G1540 and a presumed derivative of G4111\nStrong's: a hundred times\nKJV: —hundredfold.\n\nSee: G1540 \nSee: G4111 \n\nCognate Group: G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)\nVariants: ἑκατονταπλασίων \nHebrew Equivalents: H4967 מְתוּשָׁאֵל",
    1543: "ἑκατοντάρχης (hekatontárchēs | hek-at-on-tar'-khace) or ἑκατόνταρχος (hekatóntarchos | hek-at-on'-tar-khos)\n\nDerivation: from G1540 and G757\nStrong's: the captain of one hundred men\nKJV: —centurion.\n\nSee: G1540 \nSee: G757 \n\nCognate Group: G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)\nVariants: ἑκατοντάρχης, ἑκατόνταρχος \nHebrew Equivalents: H8269 שַׂר, H8269 שַׂר",
    1544: "ἐκβάλλω (ekbállō | ek-bal'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G906\nStrong's: to eject (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —bring forth, cast (forth, out), drive (out), expel, leave, pluck (pull, take, thrust) out, put forth (out), send away (forth, out).\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G906 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐκβάλλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1638 גָּרַס, H1640 גָּרַף, H1644 גָּרַשׁ, H1875 דָּרַשׁ, H2186 זָנַח, H2904 טוּל, H2956 טָרַד, H3318 יָצָא, H3423 יָרַשׁ, H3947 לָקַח, H5080 נָדַח, H5394 נָשַׁל, H5414 נָתַן, H5428 נָתַשׁ, H5590 סָעַר, H5674 עָבַר, H5927 עָלָה, H6403 פָּלַט, H6958 קֹוא, H7971 שָׁלַח, H7993 שָׁלַךְ",
    1545: "ἔκβασις (ékbasis | ek'-bas-is)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1537 and the base of G939 (meaning to go out)\nStrong's: an exit (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —end, way to escape.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἔκβασις",
    1546: "ἐκβολή (ekbolḗ | ek-bol-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G1544\nStrong's: ejection, i.e. (specially) a throwing overboard of the cargo\nKJV: —+ lighten the ship.\n\nSee: G1544 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐκβολή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1644 גָּרַשׁ, H2904 טוּל, H3318 יָצָא",
    1547: "ἐκγαμίζω (ekgamízō | ek-gam-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and a form of G1061 (compare G1548)\nStrong's: to marry off a daughter\nKJV: —give in marriage.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1061 \nSee: G1548 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐκγαμίζω G1679",
