    1550: "ἐκδαπανάω (ekdapanáō | ek-dap-an-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G1159\nStrong's: to expend (wholly), i.e. (figuratively) exhaust\nKJV: —spend.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1159 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐκδαπανάω, ἐκδαπανάομαι",
    1551: "ἐκδέχομαι (ekdéchomai | ek-dekh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G1209\nStrong's: to accept from some source, i.e. (by implication) to await\nKJV: —expect, look (tarry) for, wait (for).\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1209 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐκδέχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H977 בָּחַר, H995 בִּין, H6148 עָרַב, H6908 קָבַץ, H7114 קָצַר, H7760 שׂוּם",
