    1554: "ἐκδίδωμι (ekdídōmi | ek-did-o'-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G1325\nStrong's: to give forth, i.e. (specially) to lease\nKJV: —let forth (out).\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1325 \n\nCognate Group: G3927 (pilgrim), G1218 (people), G1553 (be absent), G1736 (be at home)\nVariants: ἐκδίδωμι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1961 הָיָה, H3318 יָצָא, H5414 נָתַן, H5647 עָבַד",
    1555: "ἐκδιηγέομαι (ekdiēgéomai | ek-dee-ayg-eh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and a compound of G1223 and G2233\nStrong's: to narrate through wholly\nKJV: —declare.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1223 \nSee: G2233 \n\nCognate Group: G3927 (pilgrim), G1218 (people), G1553 (be absent), G1736 (be at home)\nVariants: ἐκδιηγέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H5608 סָפַר, H7878 שִׂיחַ",
    1556: "ἐκδικέω (ekdikéō | ek-dik-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1558\nStrong's: to vindicate, retaliate, punish\nKJV: —a (re-)venge.\n\nSee: G1558 \n\nCognate Group: G1556 (a venge), G1558 (a venger), G1557 (avenge)\nVariants: ἐκδικέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5358 נָקַם, H6485 פָּקַד, H8199 שָׁפַט",
    1557: "ἐκδίκησις (ekdíkēsis | ek-dik'-ay-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G1556\nStrong's: vindication, retribution\nKJV: —(a-, re-)venge(-ance), punishment.\n\nSee: G1556 \n\nCognate Group: G1556 (a venge), G1558 (a venger), G1557 (avenge)\nVariants: ἐκδίκησις \nHebrew Equivalents: H639 אַף, H5359 נָקָם, H6485 פָּקַד, H8199 שָׁפַט, H8385 תַּאֲנָה, H8433 תֹּוכֵחָה",
    1558: "ἔκδικος (ékdikos | ek'-dik-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G1349\nStrong's: carrying justice out, i.e. a punisher\nKJV: —a (re-)venger.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1349 \n\nCognate Group: G1556 (a venge), G1558 (a venger), G1557 (avenge)\nVariants: ἔκδικος",
    1559: "ἐκδιώκω (ekdiṓkō | ek-dee-o'-ko)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G1377\nStrong's: to pursue out, i.e. expel or persecute implacably\nKJV: —persecute.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1377 \n\nCognate Group: G1556 (a venge), G1558 (a venger), G1557 (avenge)\nVariants: ἐκδιώκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1272 בָּרַח, H1920 הָדַף, H2957 טְרַד, H5358 נָקַם, H6789 צָמַת, H7291 רָדַף, H7323 רוּץ, H7368 רָחַק",
    1560: "ἔκδοτος (ékdotos | ek'-dot-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and a derivative of G1325\nStrong's: given out or over, i.e. surrendered\nKJV: —delivered.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1325 \n\nCognate Group: G1556 (a venge), G1558 (a venger), G1557 (avenge)\nVariants: ἔκδοτος",
    1561: "ἐκδοχή (ekdochḗ | ek-dokh-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G1551\nStrong's: expectation\nKJV: —looking for.\n\nSee: G1551 \n\nCognate Group: G1403 (feast), G1209 (accept), G1184 (accepted), G553 (look for), G1523 (receive), G587 (acceptable), G588 (accept), G2144 (acceptable), G4327 (accept), G594 (acceptation), G1561 (looking for)\nVariants: ἐκδοχή",
    1562: "ἐκδύω (ekdýō | ek-doo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and the base of G1416\nStrong's: to cause to sink out of, i.e. (specially as of clothing) to divest\nKJV: —strip, take off from, unclothe.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1416 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: ἐκδύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2502 חָלַץ, H6584 פָּשַׁט, H6605 פָּתַח",
    1563: "ἐκεῖ (ekeî | ek-i')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: there; by extension, thither\nKJV: —there, thither(-ward), (to) yonder (place).\n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: ἐκεῖ \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1973 הָלְאָה, H1988 הֲלֹם, H1992 הֵם, H4264 מַחֲנֶה, H5935 עַלְוָן, H8033 שָׁם",
    1564: "ἐκεῖθεν (ekeîthen | ek-i'-then)\n\nDerivation: from G1563\nStrong's: thence\nKJV: —from that place, (from) thence, there.\n\nSee: G1563 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: ἐκεῖθεν \nHebrew Equivalents: H8033 שָׁם",
    1565: "ἐκεῖνος (ekeînos | ek-i'-nos)\n\nDerivation: from G1563\nStrong's: that one (or (neuter) thing); often intensified by the article prefixed\nKJV: —he, it, the other (same), selfsame, that (same, very), X their, X them, they, this, those. See also G3778 .\n\nSee: G1563 \nSee: G3778 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: ἐκεῖνος \nHebrew Equivalents: H479 אִלֵּךְ, H581 אִנּוּן, H1791 דֵּךְ, H1931 הוּא, H1931 הוּא, H1975 הַלָּז, H1992 הֵם, H1992 הֵם, H2009 הִנֵּה, H2088 זֶה, H3653 כֵּן, H6256 עֵת",
    1566: "ἐκεῖσε (ekeîse | ek-i'-seh)\n\nDerivation: from G1563\nStrong's: thither\nKJV: —there.\n\nSee: G1563 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: ἐκεῖσε \nHebrew Equivalents: H8033 שָׁם",
    1567: "ἐκζητέω (ekzētéō | ek-zay-teh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G2212\nStrong's: to search out, i.e. (figuratively)investigate, crave, demand, (by Hebraism) worship\nKJV: —en- (re-)quire, seek after (carefully, diligently).\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G2212 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: ἐκζητέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1239 בָּקַר, H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H1875 דָּרַשׁ, H2076 זָבַח, H2470 חָלָה, H2713 חָקַר, H3423 יָרַשׁ, H5027 נָבַט, H5341 נָצַר, H5352 נָקָה, H5367 נָקַשׁ, H6485 פָּקַד",
