    1643: "ἐλαύνω (elaúnō | el-ow'-no)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of a primary verb (obsolete except in certain tenses as an alternative of this) of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: to push (as wind, oars or dæmonical power)\nKJV: —carry, drive, row.\n\nCognate Group: G1637 (oil)\nVariants: ἐλαύνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1986 הָלַם, H3332 יָצַק, H5065 נָגַשׂ, H7898 שַׁיִת",
    1644: "ἐλαφρία (elaphría | el-af-ree'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1645\nStrong's: levity (figuratively), i.e. fickleness\nKJV: —lightness.\n\nSee: G1645 \n\nCognate Group: G1637 (oil)\nVariants: ἐλαφρία",
    1645: "ἐλαφρός (elaphrós | el-af-ros')\n\nDerivation: probably akin to G1643 and the base of G1640\nStrong's: light, i.e. easy\nKJV: —light.\n\nSee: G1643 \nSee: G1640 \n\nCognate Group: G1637 (oil)\nVariants: ἐλαφρός \nHebrew Equivalents: H6996 קָטָן, H7031 קַל, H7044 קָלָל",
    1646: "ἐλάχιστος (eláchistos | el-akh'-is-tos)\n\nDerivation: superlative of ἔλαχυς (short)\nStrong's: used as equivalent to G3398 ; least (in size, amount, dignity, etc.)\nKJV: —least, very little (small), smallest.\n\nSee: G3398 \n\nCognate Group: G1637 (oil)\nVariants: ἐλάχιστος",
    1647: "ἐλαχιστότερος (elachistóteros | el-akh-is-tot'-er-os)\n\nDerivation: comparative of G1646\nStrong's: far less\nKJV: —less than the least.\n\nSee: G1646 \n\nCognate Group: G1637 (oil)\nVariants: ἐλαχιστότερος, ἐλάχιστος",
    1648: "Ἐλεάζαρ (Eleázar | el-eh-ad'-zar)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H499)\nStrong's: Eleazar, an Israelite\nKJV: —Eleazar.\nSee: H499\n\nCognate Group: G1637 (oil)\nVariants: Ἐλεάζαρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H499 אֶלְעָזָר",
    1649: "ἔλεγξις (élenxis | el'-eng-xis)\n\nDerivation: from G1651\nStrong's: refutation, i.e. reproof\nKJV: —rebuke.\n\nSee: G1651 \n\nCognate Group: G1650 (evidence), G1649 (rebuke), G1651 (convict)\nVariants: ἔλεγξις \nHebrew Equivalents: H7879 שִׂיחַ",
    1650: "ἔλεγχος (élenchos | el'-eng-khos)\n\nDerivation: from G1651\nStrong's: proof, conviction\nKJV: —evidence, reproof.\n\nSee: G1651 \n\nCognate Group: G1650 (evidence), G1649 (rebuke), G1651 (convict)\nVariants: ἔλεγχος, ἐλεγμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H1606 גְּעָרָה, H3198 יָכַח, H3198 יָכַח, H4751 מַר, H5007 נְאָצָה, H8433 תֹּוכֵחָה, H8433 תֹּוכֵחָה",
    1651: "ἐλέγχω (elénchō | el-eng'-kho)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: to confute, admonish\nKJV: —convict, convince, tell a fault, rebuke, reprove.\n\nCognate Group: G1650 (evidence), G1649 (rebuke), G1651 (convict)\nVariants: ἐλέγχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H819 אַשְׁמָה, H2713 חָקַר, H3198 יָכַח, H5060 נָגַע, H7561 רָשַׁע",
    1652: "ἐλεεινός (eleeinós | el-eh-i-nos')\n\nDerivation: from G1656\nStrong's: pitiable\nKJV: —miserable.\n\nSee: G1656 \n\nCognate Group: G1650 (evidence), G1649 (rebuke), G1651 (convict)\nVariants: ἐλεεινός",
    1653: "ἐλεέω (eleéō | el-eh-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1656\nStrong's: to compassionate (by word or deed, specially, by divine grace)\nKJV: —have compassion (pity on), have (obtain, receive, shew) mercy (on).\n\nSee: G1656 \n\nCognate Group: G448 (without mercy), G1656 (mercy), G415 (unmerciful), G1655 (merciful), G1653 (have compassion), G1654 (alms)\nVariants: ἐλεέω, ἐλεάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1058 בָּכָה, H1350 גָּאַל, H1926 הָדָר, H2433 חִין, H2550 חָמַל, H2603 חָנַן, H2623 חָסִיד, H2895 טֹוב, H3190 יָטַב, H5162 נָחַם, H5414 נָתַן, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6908 קָבַץ, H7355 רָחַם, H7725 שׁוּב, H8085 שָׁמַע",
    1654: "ἐλεημοσύνη (eleēmosýnē | el-eh-ay-mos-oo'-nay)\n\nDerivation: from G1656\nStrong's: compassionateness, i.e. (as exercised towards the poor) beneficence, or (concretely) a benefaction\nKJV: —alms(-deeds).\n\nSee: G1656 \n\nCognate Group: G448 (without mercy), G1656 (mercy), G415 (unmerciful), G1655 (merciful), G1653 (have compassion), G1654 (alms)\nVariants: ἐλεημοσύνη \nHebrew Equivalents: H571 אֶמֶת, H2617 חֵסֵד, H6666 צְדָקָה",
    1655: "ἐλεήμων (eleḗmōn | el-eh-ay'-mone)\n\nDerivation: from G1653\nStrong's: compassionate (actively)\nKJV: —merciful.\n\nSee: G1653 \n\nCognate Group: G448 (without mercy), G1656 (mercy), G415 (unmerciful), G1655 (merciful), G1653 (have compassion), G1654 (alms)\nVariants: ἐλεήμων \nHebrew Equivalents: H2587 חַנּוּן, H2617 חֵסֵד, H7349 רַחוּם, H7922 שֶׂכֶל",
    1656: "ἔλεος (éleos | el'-eh-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: compassion (human or divine, especially active)\nKJV: —(+ tender) mercy.\n\nCognate Group: G448 (without mercy), G1656 (mercy), G415 (unmerciful), G1655 (merciful), G1653 (have compassion), G1654 (alms)\nVariants: ἔλεος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2580 חֵן, H2617 חֵסֵד, H3468 יֶשַׁע, H4596 מְעִי, H7356 רַחַם, H7522 רָצֹון",
    1657: "ἐλευθερία (eleuthería | el-yoo-ther-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1658\nStrong's: freedom (legitimate or licentious, chiefly moral or ceremonial)\nKJV: —liberty.\n\nSee: G1658 \n\nCognate Group: G1659 (deliver), G558 (freeman), G1657 (liberty), G1658 (free)\nVariants: ἐλευθερία \nHebrew Equivalents: H2668 חֻפְשָׁה",
    1658: "ἐλεύθερος (eleútheros | el-yoo'-ther-os)\n\nDerivation: probably from the alternate of G2064\nStrong's: unrestrained (to go at pleasure), i.e. (as a citizen) not a slave (whether freeborn or manumitted), or (genitive case) exempt (from obligation or liability)\nKJV: —free (man, woman), at liberty.\n\nSee: G2064 \n\nCognate Group: G1659 (deliver), G558 (freeman), G1657 (liberty), G1658 (free)\nVariants: ἐλεύθερος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2356 חֹור, H2670 חׇפְשִׁי, H5315 נֶפֶשׁ, H8269 שַׂר",
    1659: "ἐλευθερόω (eleutheróō | el-yoo-ther-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1658\nStrong's: to liberate, i.e. (figuratively) to exempt (from moral, ceremonial or mortal liability)\nKJV: —deliver, make free.\n\nSee: G1658 \n\nCognate Group: G1659 (deliver), G558 (freeman), G1657 (liberty), G1658 (free)\nVariants: ἐλευθερόω",
    1660: "ἔλευσις (éleusis | el'-yoo-sis)\n\nDerivation: from the alternate of G2064\nStrong's: an advent\nKJV: —coming.\n\nSee: G2064 \n\nCognate Group: G1660 (coming)\nVariants: ἔλευσις",
    1661: "ἐλεφάντινος (elephántinos | el-ef-an'-tee-nos)\n\nDerivation: from ἔλεφας (an \"elephant\")\nStrong's: elephantine, i.e. (by implication) composed of ivory\nKJV: —of ivory.\n\nCognate Group: G1660 (coming)\nVariants: ἐλεφάντινος \nHebrew Equivalents: H8127 שֵׁן, H8143 שֶׁנְהַבִּים",
    1662: "Ἐλιακείμ (Eliakeím | el-ee-ak-ime')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H471)\nStrong's: Eliakim, an Israelite\nKJV: —Eliakim.\nSee: H471\n\nCognate Group: G1660 (coming)\nVariants: Ἐλιακείμ, Ἐλιακίμ, Ἐλιακίμ/Ἐλιακείμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H471 אֶלְיָקִים",
    1663: "Ἐλιέζερ (Eliézer | el-ee-ed'-zer)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H461)\nStrong's: Eliezer, an Israelite\nKJV: —Eliezer.\nSee: H461\n\nCognate Group: G1660 (coming)\nVariants: Ἐλιέζερ \nHebrew Equivalents: H461 אֱלִיעֶזֶר",
    1664: "Ἐλιούδ (Elioúd | el-ee-ood')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H410 and H1935)\nStrong's: God of majesty; Eliud, an Israelite\nKJV: —Eliud.\nSee: H410\nSee: H1935\n\nCognate Group: G1660 (coming)\nVariants: Ἐλιούδ \nHebrew Equivalents: H410 אֵל, H1935 הֹוד",
    1665: "Ἐλισάβετ (Elisábet | el-ee-sab'-et)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H472)\nStrong's: Elisabet, an Israelitess\nKJV: —Elisabeth.\nSee: H472\n\nCognate Group: G1660 (coming)\nVariants: Ἐλισάβετ \nHebrew Equivalents: H472 אֱלִישֶׁבַע",
    1666: "Ἐλισσαῖος (Elissaîos | el-is-sah'-yos)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H477)\nStrong's: Elissæus, an Israelite\nKJV: —Elissæus.\nSee: H477\n\nCognate Group: G1660 (coming)\nVariants: Ἐλισσαῖος, Ἐλισαῖος \nHebrew Equivalents: H477 אֱלִישָׁע",
    1667: "ἑλίσσω (helíssō | hel-is'-so)\n\nDerivation: a form of G1507\nStrong's: to coil or wrap\nKJV: —fold up.\n\nSee: G1507 \n\nCognate Group: G1660 (coming)\nVariants: ἑλίσσω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1556 גָּלַל, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2498 חָלַף",
    1668: "ἕλκος (hélkos | hel'-kos)\n\nDerivation: probably from G1670\nStrong's: an ulcer (as if drawn together)\nKJV: —sore.\n\nSee: G1670 \n\nCognate Group: G1660 (coming)\nVariants: ἕλκος \nHebrew Equivalents: H7822 שְׁחִין",
    1669: "ἑλκόω (helkóō | hel-ko'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1668\nStrong's: to cause to ulcerate, i.e. (passively) be ulcerous\nKJV: —full of sores.\n\nSee: G1668 \n\nCognate Group: G1660 (coming)\nVariants: ἑλκόω, ἑλκόομαι",
