    1671: "Ἑλλάς (Hellás | hel-las')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: Hellas (or Greece), a country of Europe\nKJV: —Greece.\n\nCognate Group: G1675 (Grecian), G1674 (Greek), G1672 (Gentile), G1671 (Greece), G1676 (Greek)\nVariants: Ἑλλάς",
    1672: "Ἕλλην (Héllēn | hel'-lane)\n\nDerivation: from G1671\nStrong's: a Hellen (Grecian) or inhabitant of Hellas; by extension a Greek-speaking person, especially a non-Jew\nKJV: — Gentile, Greek.\n\nSee: G1671 \n\nCognate Group: G1675 (Grecian), G1674 (Greek), G1672 (Gentile), G1671 (Greece), G1676 (Greek)\nVariants: Ἕλλην",
    1673: "Ἑλληνικός (Hellēnikós | hel-lay-nee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G1672\nStrong's: Hellenic, i.e. Grecian (in language)\nKJV: —Greek.\n\nSee: G1672 \n\nCognate Group: G1675 (Grecian), G1674 (Greek), G1672 (Gentile), G1671 (Greece), G1676 (Greek)\nVariants: Ἑλληνικός",
    1674: "Ἑλληνίς (Hellēnís | hel-lay-nis')\n\nDerivation: feminine of G1672\nStrong's: a Grecian (i.e. non-Jewish) woman\nKJV: —Greek.\n\nSee: G1672 \n\nCognate Group: G1675 (Grecian), G1674 (Greek), G1672 (Gentile), G1671 (Greece), G1676 (Greek)\nVariants: Ἑλληνίς",
    1675: "Ἑλληνιστής (Hellēnistḗs | hel-lay-nis-tace')\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G1672\nStrong's: a Hellenist or Greek-speaking Jew\nKJV: —Grecian.\n\nSee: G1672 \n\nCognate Group: G1675 (Grecian), G1674 (Greek), G1672 (Gentile), G1671 (Greece), G1676 (Greek)\nVariants: Ἑλληνιστής",
    1676: "Ἑλληνιστί (Hellēnistí | hel-lay-nis-tee')\n\nDerivation: adverb from the same as G1675\nStrong's: Hellenistically, i.e. in the Grecian language\nKJV: —Greek.\n\nSee: G1675 \n\nCognate Group: G1675 (Grecian), G1674 (Greek), G1672 (Gentile), G1671 (Greece), G1676 (Greek)\nVariants: Ἑλληνιστί",
    1677: "ἐλλογέω (ellogéō | el-log-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G3056 (in the sense of account)\nStrong's: to reckon in, i.e. attribute\nKJV: —impute, put on account.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G3056 \n\nCognate Group: G1677 (impute)\nVariants: ἐλλογέω, ἐλλογάω, ἐλλογέω/ἐλλογάω",
    1678: "Ἐλμωδάμ (Elmōdám | el-mo-dam')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (perhaps for H486)\nStrong's: Elmodam, an Israelite\nKJV: —Elmodam.\nSee: H486\n\nCognate Group: G1677 (impute)\nVariants: Ἐλμωδάμ, Ἐλμαδάμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H486 אַלְמֹודָד",
    1679: "ἐλπίζω (elpízō | el-pid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1680\nStrong's: to expect or confide\nKJV: —(have, thing) hope(-d) (for), trust.\n\nSee: G1680 \n\nCognate Group: G1680 (faith), G1679 (hope), G4276 (first trust), G560 (hope for again)\nVariants: ἐλπίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H982 בָּטַח, H1556 גָּלַל, H1875 דָּרַשׁ, H2490 חָלַל, H2620 חָסָה, H2836 חָשַׁק, H3176 יָחַל, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5445 סָבַל, H6960 קָוָה, H7126 קָרַב, H7365 רְחַץ, H8172 שָׁעַן, H8199 שָׁפַט, H8264 שָׁקַק",
    1680: "ἐλπίς (elpís | el-pece')\n\nDerivation: from a primary ἔλπω (to anticipate, usually with pleasure)\nStrong's: expectation (abstractly or concretely) or confidence\nKJV: —faith, hope.\n\nCognate Group: G1680 (faith), G1679 (hope), G4276 (first trust), G560 (hope for again)\nVariants: ἐλπίς \nHebrew Equivalents: H932 בֹּהַן, H982 בָּטַח, H2113 זְוָעָה, H2380 חָזוּת, H2617 חֵסֵד, H3689 כֶּסֶל, H4007 מַבָּט, H4268 מַחֲסֶה, H5082 נְדִיבָה, H5315 נֶפֶשׁ, H5833 עֶזְרָה, H6643 צְבִי, H6957 קַו, H7364 רָחַץ, H7664 שֵׂבֶר, H8431 תֹּוחֶלֶת, H8615 תִּקְוָה",
    1681: "Ἐλύμας (Elýmas | el-oo'-mas)\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Elymas, a wizard\nKJV: —Elymas.\n\nCognate Group: G1680 (faith), G1679 (hope), G4276 (first trust), G560 (hope for again)\nVariants: Ἐλύμας, Ἕτοιμας",
    1682: "ἐλοΐ (eloḯ | el-o-ee')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldean origin (H426 with pronominal suffix) my God\nKJV: —Eloi.\nSee: H426\n\nCognate Group: G1680 (faith), G1679 (hope), G4276 (first trust), G560 (hope for again)\nVariants: ἐλοΐ, ἐλωί̈, ἐλωΐ, ελωι \nHebrew Equivalents: H426 אֱלָהּ",
    1683: "ἐμαυτοῦ (emautoû | em-ow-too')\n\n\nDerivation: genitive case compound of G1700 KJV: —me, mine own (self), myself.\n\nSee: G1700 \nSee: G846 \n\nCognate Group: G1680 (faith), G1679 (hope), G4276 (first trust), G560 (hope for again)",
    1684: "ἐμβαίνω (embaínō | em-ba'-hee-no)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and the base of G939\nStrong's: to walk on, i.e. embark (aboard a vessel), reach (a pool)\nKJV: —come (get) into, enter (into), go (up) into, step in, take ship.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G1680 (faith), G1679 (hope), G4276 (first trust), G560 (hope for again)\nVariants: ἐμβαίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H3381 יָרַד, H5927 עָלָה",
    1685: "ἐμβάλλω (embállō | em-bal'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G906\nStrong's: to throw on, i.e. (figuratively) subject to (eternal punishment)\nKJV: —cast into.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G906 \n\nCognate Group: G1680 (faith), G1679 (hope), G4276 (first trust), G560 (hope for again)\nVariants: ἐμβάλλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H622 אָסַף, H935 בֹּוא, H2904 טוּל, H3245 יָסַד, H5307 נָפַל, H5414 נָתַן, H6398 פָּלַח, H6485 פָּקַד, H7412 רְמָה, H7760 שׂוּם, H7843 שָׁחַת, H7971 שָׁלַח, H7993 שָׁלַךְ, H8104 שָׁמַר, H8628 תָּקַע",
    1686: "ἐμβάπτω (embáptō | em-bap'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G911\nStrong's: to whelm on, i.e. wet (a part of the person, etc.) by contact with a fluid\nKJV: —dip.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G911 \n\nCognate Group: G1680 (faith), G1679 (hope), G4276 (first trust), G560 (hope for again)\nVariants: ἐμβάπτω, ἐμβαπτίζω",
    1687: "ἐμβατεύω (embateúō | em-bat-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and a presumed derivative of the base of G939\nStrong's: equivalent to G1684 ; to intrude on (figuratively)\nKJV: —intrude into.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G939 \nSee: G1684 \n\nCognate Group: G1687 (intrude into)\nVariants: ἐμβατεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2505 חָלַק, H5157 נָחַל",
    1688: "ἐμβιβάζω (embibázō | em-bib-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and βιβάζω (to mount\nStrong's: causative of G1684); to place on, i.e. transfer (aboard a vessel)\nKJV: —put in.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G1684 \n\nCognate Group: G1687 (intrude into)\nVariants: ἐμβιβάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1869 דָּרַךְ, H7392 רָכַב",
    1689: "ἐμβλέπω (emblépō | em-blep'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G991\nStrong's: to look on, i.e. (relatively) to observe fixedly, or (absolutely) to discern clearly\nKJV: —behold, gaze up, look upon, (could) see.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G991 \n\nCognate Group: G1687 (intrude into)\nVariants: ἐμβλέπω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5027 נָבַט, H6437 פָּנָה, H7200 רָאָה",
    1690: "ἐμβριμάομαι (embrimáomai | em-brim-ah'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and βριμάομαι (to snort with anger)\nStrong's: to have indignation on, i.e. (transitively) to blame, (intransitively) to sigh with chagrin, (specially) to sternly enjoin\nKJV: —straitly charge, groan, murmur against.\n\nSee: G1722 \n\nCognate Group: G1687 (intrude into)\nVariants: ἐμβριμάομαι, βριμάομαι",
    1691: "ἐμέ (emé | em-eh')\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of G3165\nStrong's: me\nKJV: —I, me, my(-self).\n\nSee: G3165 \n\nCognate Group: G1687 (intrude into)\nVariants: ἐμέ, ἐγώ",
    1692: "ἐμέω (eméō | em-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: to vomit\nKJV: —(will) spue.\n\nCognate Group: G1687 (intrude into)\nVariants: ἐμέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6892 קֵא",
    1693: "ἐμμαίνομαι (emmaínomai | em-mah'-ee-nom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G3105\nStrong's: to rave on, i.e. rage at\nKJV: —be mad against.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G3105 \n\nCognate Group: G1687 (intrude into)\nVariants: ἐμμαίνομαι",
