    1695: "Ἐμμαούς (Emmaoús | em-mah-ooce')\n\nDerivation: probably of Hebrew origin (compare H3222)\nStrong's: Emmaus, a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Emmaus.\nSee: H3222\n\nCognate Group: G1687 (intrude into)\nVariants: Ἐμμαούς, Ἐμμαοῦς, Οὐλαμμαούς \nHebrew Equivalents: H3222 יֵם",
    1696: "ἐμμένω (emménō | em-men'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G3306\nStrong's: to stay in the same place, i.e. (figuratively) persevere\nKJV: —continue.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G3306 \n\nCognate Group: G5278 (abide), G3887 (abide), G5281 (enduring), G1696 (continue), G4037 (wait for), G3306 (abide), G3438 (abode)\nVariants: ἐμμένω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2442 חָכָה, H6565 פָּרַר, H6965 קוּם",
    1697: "Ἐμμόρ (Emmór | em-mor')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H2544)\nStrong's: Emmor (i.e. Chamor), a Canaanite\nKJV: —Emmor.\nSee: H2544\n\nCognate Group: G5278 (abide), G3887 (abide), G5281 (enduring), G1696 (continue), G4037 (wait for), G3306 (abide), G3438 (abode)\nVariants: Ἐμμόρ, Ἑμμώρ, Ἐμμώρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H2543 חֲמֹור, H2544 חֲמֹור",
    1698: "ἐμοί (emoí | em-oy')\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of G3427\nStrong's: to me\nKJV: —I, me, mine, my.\n\nSee: G3427 \n\nCognate Group: G5278 (abide), G3887 (abide), G5281 (enduring), G1696 (continue), G4037 (wait for), G3306 (abide), G3438 (abode)\nVariants: ἐμοί, ἐγώ",
    1699: "ἐμός (emós | em-os')\n\nDerivation: from the oblique cases of G1473 (G1698, G1700, G1691)\nStrong's: my\nKJV: —of me, mine (own), my.\n\nSee: G1473 \nSee: G1698 \nSee: G1700 \nSee: G1691 \n\nCognate Group: G5278 (abide), G3887 (abide), G5281 (enduring), G1696 (continue), G4037 (wait for), G3306 (abide), G3438 (abode)\nVariants: ἐμός",
    1700: "ἐμοῦ (emoû | em-oo')\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of G3449\nStrong's: of me\nKJV: —me, mine, my.\n\nSee: G3449 \n\nCognate Group: G5278 (abide), G3887 (abide), G5281 (enduring), G1696 (continue), G4037 (wait for), G3306 (abide), G3438 (abode)\nVariants: ἐμοῦ, ἐγώ",
    1701: "ἐμπαιγμός (empaigmós | emp-aheeg-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G1702\nStrong's: derision\nKJV: —mocking.\n\nSee: G1702 \n\nCognate Group: G1703 (mocker), G1701 (mocking), G1702 (mock), G3816 (child)\nVariants: ἐμπαιγμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H7034 קָלָה, H7048 קַלָּסָה",
