    1704: "ἐμπεριπατέω (emperipatéō | em-per-ee-pat-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G4043\nStrong's: to perambulate on a place, i.e. (figuratively) to be occupied among persons\nKJV: —walk in.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G4043 \n\nCognate Group: G3961 (tread), G1704 (walk in), G2662 (trample), G4043 (go)\nVariants: ἐμπεριπατέω",
