    1706: "ἐμπίπτω (empíptō | em-pip'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G4098\nStrong's: to fall on, i.e. (literally) to be entrapped by, or (figuratively) be overwhelmed with\nKJV: —fall among (into).\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G4098 \n\nCognate Group: G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)\nVariants: ἐμπίπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1519 גִּיחַ, H2492 חָלַם, H3766 כָּרַע, H5307 נָפַל, H6293 פָּגַע, H6298 פָּגַשׁ",
    1707: "ἐμπλέκω (emplékō | em-plek'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G4120\nStrong's: to entwine, i.e. (figuratively) involve with\nKJV: —entangle (in, self with).\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G4120 \n\nCognate Group: G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)\nVariants: ἐμπλέκω, ἐμπλέκομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H5307 נָפַל",
    1708: "ἐμπλοκή (emplokḗ | em-plok-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G1707\nStrong's: elaborate braiding of the hair\nKJV: —plaiting.\n\nSee: G1707 \n\nCognate Group: G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)\nVariants: ἐμπλοκή, πλοκή",
    1709: "ἐμπνέω (empnéō | emp-neh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G4154\nStrong's: to inhale, i.e. (figuratively) to be animated by (bent upon)\nKJV: —breathe.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G4154 \n\nCognate Group: G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)\nVariants: ἐμπνέω",
    1710: "ἐμπορεύομαι (emporeúomai | em-por-yoo'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G4198\nStrong's: to travel in (a country as a pedlar), i.e. (by implication) to trade\nKJV: —buy and sell, make merchandise.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G4198 \n\nCognate Group: G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)\nVariants: ἐμπορεύομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2986 יָבַל, H3318 יָצָא, H5503 סָחַר, H7402 רָכַל, H7665 שָׁבַר",
    1711: "ἐμπορία (emporía | em-por-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: feminine from G1713\nStrong's: traffic\nKJV: —merchandise.\n\nSee: G1713 \n\nCognate Group: G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)\nVariants: ἐμπορία \nHebrew Equivalents: H4627 מַעֲרָב, H5503 סָחַר, H7402 רָכַל",
    1712: "ἐμπόριον (empórion | em-por'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter from G1713\nStrong's: a mart (\"emporium\")\nKJV: —merchandise.\n\nSee: G1713 \n\nCognate Group: G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)\nVariants: ἐμπόριον \nHebrew Equivalents: H2181 זָנָה, H5603 סָפַן, H7402 רָכַל",
    1713: "ἔμπορος (émporos | em'-por-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and the base of G4198\nStrong's: a (wholesale) tradesman\nKJV: —merchant.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G4198 \n\nCognate Group: G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)\nVariants: ἔμπορος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4627 מַעֲרָב, H5503 סָחַר, H7402 רָכַל",
    1714: "ἐμπρήθω (emprḗthō | em-pray'-tho)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and πρήθω (to blow a flame)\nStrong's: to enkindle, i.e. set on fire\nKJV: —burn up.\n\nSee: G1722 \n\nCognate Group: G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)\nVariants: ἐμπρήθω, ἐμπίμπρημι, ἐμπίπρημι",
    1715: "ἔμπροσθεν (émprosthen | em'-pros-then)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G4314\nStrong's: in front of (in place (literally or figuratively) or time)\nKJV: —against, at, before, (in presence, sight) of.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G4314 \n\nCognate Group: G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)\nVariants: ἔμπροσθεν \nHebrew Equivalents: H268 אָחֹור, H865 אֶתְמֹול, H6040 עֳנִי, H6440 פָּנִים, H6924 קֶדֶם, H7121 קָרָא, H7564 רִשְׁעָה",
    1716: "ἐμπτύω (emptýō | emp-too'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G4429\nStrong's: to spit at or on\nKJV: —spit (upon).\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G4429 \n\nCognate Group: G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)\nVariants: ἐμπτύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3417 יָרָק",
    1717: "ἐμφανής (emphanḗs | em-fan-ace')\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1722 and G5316\nStrong's: apparent in self\nKJV: —manifest, openly.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G5316 \n\nCognate Group: G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)\nVariants: ἐμφανής \nHebrew Equivalents: H1875 דָּרַשׁ, H3045 יָדַע, H3559 כּוּן",
    1718: "ἐμφανίζω (emphanízō | em-fan-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1717\nStrong's: to exhibit (in person) or disclose (by words)\nKJV: —appear, declare (plainly), inform, (will) manifest, shew, signify.\n\nSee: G1717 \n\nCognate Group: G5319 (appear), G5325 (pomp), G5320 (evidently), G5322 (lantern), G2015 (appearing), G5321 (manifestation), G5326 (spirit), G5316 (appear), G2014 (appear), G1718 (appear), G5324 (sight), G5318 (abroad), G2016 (notable)\nVariants: ἐμφανίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H3045 יָדַע, H3808 לֹא, H7200 רָאָה",
