    1720: "ἐμφυσάω (emphysáō | em-foo-sah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and φυσάω (to puff) (compare G5453)\nStrong's: to blow at or on\nKJV: —breathe on.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G5453 \n\nCognate Group: G1720 (breathe on)\nVariants: ἐμφυσάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H4058 מָדַד, H5301 נָפַח, H6315 פּוּחַ, H6327 פּוּץ",
    1721: "ἔμφυτος (émphytos | em'-foo-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and a derivative of G5453\nStrong's: implanted (figuratively)\nKJV: —engrafted.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G5453 \n\nCognate Group: G1720 (breathe on)\nVariants: ἔμφυτος",
    1722: "ἐν (en | en)\n\nDerivation: a primary preposition denoting (fixed) position (in place, time or state), and (by implication) instrumentality (medially or constructively), i.e. a relation of rest (intermediate between G1519 and G1537)\nStrong's: \"in,\" at, (up-)on, by, etc.\nKJV: —about, after, against, + almost, X altogether, among, X as, at, before, between, (here-)by (+ all means), for (… sake of), + give self wholly to, (here-)in(-to, -wardly), X mightily, (because) of, (up-)on, (open-)ly, X outwardly, one, X quickly, X shortly, (speedi-)ly, X that, X there(-in, -on), through(-out), (un-)to(-ward), under, when, where(-with), while, with(-in). Often used in compounds, with substantially the same import; rarely with verbs of motion, and then not to indicate direction, except (elliptically) by a separate (and different) preposition.\n\nSee: G1519 \nSee: G1537 \n\nCognate Group: G1722 (about)\nVariants: ἐν, ἐμμέσῳ, ἐννόμως \nHebrew Equivalents: H3789 כָּתַב",
    1723: "ἐναγκαλίζομαι (enankalízomai | en-ang-kal-id'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and a derivative of G43\nStrong's: to take in one's arms, i.e. embrace\nKJV: —take up in arms.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G43 \n\nCognate Group: G1722 (about)\nVariants: ἐναγκαλίζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2264 חִבֻּק",
    1724: "ἐνάλιος (enálios | en-al'-ee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G251\nStrong's: in the sea, i.e. marine\nKJV: —thing in the sea.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G251 \n\nCognate Group: G1722 (about)\nVariants: ἐνάλιος, ἐνάλιον",
    1725: "ἔναντι (énanti | en'-an-tee)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G473\nStrong's: in front (i.e. figuratively, presence) of\nKJV: —before.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G473 \n\nCognate Group: G1722 (about)\nVariants: ἔναντι",
    1726: "ἐναντίον (enantíon | en-an-tee'-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of G1727\nStrong's: (adverbially) in the presence (view) of\nKJV: —before, in the presence of.\n\nSee: G1727 \n\nCognate Group: G1722 (about)\nVariants: ἐναντίον \nHebrew Equivalents: H410 אֵל, H1100 בְּלִיַּעַל, H3808 לֹא, H5048 נֶגֶד, H5048 נֶגֶד, H5227 נֹכַח, H6040 עֳנִי, H6921 קָדִים, H7121 קָרָא",
    1727: "ἐναντίος (enantíos | en-an-tee'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1725\nStrong's: opposite; figuratively, antagonistic\nKJV: —(over) against, contrary.\n\nSee: G1725 \n\nCognate Group: G1722 (about)\nVariants: ἐναντίος \nHebrew Equivalents: H410 אֵל, H1100 בְּלִיַּעַל, H3808 לֹא, H5048 נֶגֶד, H5048 נֶגֶד, H5227 נֹכַח, H6040 עֳנִי, H6921 קָדִים, H7121 קָרָא",
    1728: "ἐνάρχομαι (enárchomai | en-ar'-khom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G756\nStrong's: to commence on\nKJV: —rule (by mistake for G757).\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G756 \nSee: G757 \n\nCognate Group: G2447 (poison), G1728 (rule)\nVariants: ἐνάρχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2490 חָלַל, H7101 קָצִין, H7223 רִאשֹׁון",
    1729: "ἐνδεής (endeḗs | en-deh-ace')\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1722 and G1210 (in the sense of lacking)\nStrong's: deficient in\nKJV: —lacking.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G1210 \n\nCognate Group: G2447 (poison), G1728 (rule)\nVariants: ἐνδεής \nHebrew Equivalents: H34 אֶבְיֹון, H1167 בַּעַל, H1249 בַּר, H2637 חָסֵר, H3685 כְּסִיל, H7457 רָעֵב",
    1730: "ἔνδειγμα (éndeigma | en'-dighe-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G1731\nStrong's: an indication (concretely)\nKJV: —manifest token.\n\nSee: G1731 \n\nCognate Group: G2447 (poison), G1728 (rule)\nVariants: ἔνδειγμα",
    1731: "ἐνδείκνυμι (endeíknymi | en-dike'-noo-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G1166\nStrong's: to indicate (by word or act)\nKJV: —do, show (forth).\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G1166 \n\nCognate Group: G2447 (poison), G1728 (rule)\nVariants: ἐνδείκνυμι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1580 גָּמַל, H3920 לָכַד, H7200 רָאָה",
    1732: "ἔνδειξις (éndeixis | en'-dike-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G1731\nStrong's: indication (abstractly)\nKJV: —declare, evident token, proof.\n\nSee: G1731 \n\nCognate Group: G2447 (poison), G1728 (rule)\nVariants: ἔνδειξις",
    1733: "ἕνδεκα (héndeka | hen'-dek-ah)\n\nDerivation: from (the neuter of) G1520 and G1176\nStrong's: one and ten, i.e. eleven\nKJV: —eleven.\n\nSee: G1520 \nSee: G1176 \n\nCognate Group: G2447 (poison), G1728 (rule)\nVariants: ἕνδεκα",
    1734: "ἑνδέκατος (hendékatos | hen-dek'-at-os)\n\nDerivation: ordinal from G1733\nStrong's: eleventh\nKJV: —eleventh.\n\nSee: G1733 \n\nCognate Group: G2447 (poison), G1728 (rule)\nVariants: ἑνδέκατος",
    1735: "ἐνδέχεται (endéchetai | en-dekh'-et-ahee)\n\nDerivation: third person singular present of a compound of G1722 and G1209\nStrong's: (impersonally) it is accepted in, i.e. admitted (possible)\nKJV: —can (+ not) be.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G1209 \n\nCognate Group: G2447 (poison), G1728 (rule)\nVariants: ἐνδέχεται, ἐνδέχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H6148 עָרַב",
    1736: "ἐνδημέω (endēméō | en-day-meh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1722 and G1218\nStrong's: to be in one's own country, i.e. home (figuratively)\nKJV: —be at home (present).\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G1218 \n\nCognate Group: G3927 (pilgrim), G1218 (people), G1553 (be absent), G1736 (be at home)\nVariants: ἐνδημέω",
    1737: "ἐνδιδύσκω (endidýskō | en-did-oos'-ko)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of G1746\nStrong's: to invest (with a garment)\nKJV: —clothe in, wear.\n\nSee: G1746 \n\nCognate Group: G3927 (pilgrim), G1218 (people), G1553 (be absent), G1736 (be at home)\nVariants: ἐνδιδύσκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3847 לָבַשׁ",
    1738: "ἔνδικος (éndikos | en'-dee-kos)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G1349\nStrong's: in the right, i.e. equitable\nKJV: —just.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G1349 \n\nCognate Group: G3927 (pilgrim), G1218 (people), G1553 (be absent), G1736 (be at home)\nVariants: ἔνδικος",
