    1782: "ἐντεῦθεν (enteûthen | ent-yoo'-then)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G1759\nStrong's: hence (literally or figuratively); (repeated) on both sides\nKJV: —(from) hence, on either side.\n\nSee: G1759 \n\nCognate Group: G1785 (commandment), G1781 (charge)\nVariants: ἐντεῦθεν, ἔνθεν \nHebrew Equivalents: H2008 הֵנָּה, H2008 הֵנָּה, H2088 זֶה, H2088 זֶה, H3541 כֹּה, H6311 פֹּה, H6311 פֹּה, H6311 פֹּה",
