    1793: "ἐντυγχάνω (entynchánō | en-toong-khan'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G5177\nStrong's: to chance upon, i.e. (by implication) confer with; by extension to entreat (in favor or against)\nKJV: —deal with, make intercession.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G5177 \n\nCognate Group: G1783 (intercession), G5177 (be), G5241 (make intercession for), G1793 (deal with)\nVariants: ἐντυγχάνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7130 קֶרֶב",
    1794: "ἐντυλίσσω (entylíssō | en-too-lis'-so)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and τυλίσσω (to twist\nStrong's: probably akin to G1507); to entwine, i.e. wind up in\nKJV: —wrap in (together).\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G1507 \n\nCognate Group: G1783 (intercession), G5177 (be), G5241 (make intercession for), G1793 (deal with)\nVariants: ἐντυλίσσω",
