    1796: "ἐνυβρίζω (enybrízō | en-oo-brid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1722 and G5195\nStrong's: to insult\nKJV: —do despite unto.\n\nSee: G1722 \nSee: G5195 \n\nCognate Group: G5195 (use despitefully), G1796 (do despite unto), G5196 (harm), G5197 (despiteful)\nVariants: ἐνυβρίζω",
