    1800: "Ἐνώς (Enṓs | en-oce')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H583)\nStrong's: Enos (i.e. Enosh), a patriarch\nKJV: —Enos.\nSee: H583\n\nCognate Group: G879 (fall asleep), G1798 (dream), G1853 (X out of sleep), G5258 (sleep), G1797 (dream), G1852 (awake out of sleep)\nVariants: Ἐνώς \nHebrew Equivalents: H582 אֱנֹושׁ, H583 אֱנֹושׁ",
