    1820: "ἐξαπορέομαι (exaporéomai | ex-ap-or-eh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1537 and G639\nStrong's: to be utterly at a loss, i.e. despond\nKJV: —(in) despair.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G639 \n\nCognate Group: G539 (deceit), G1818 (beguile), G538 (deceive)\nVariants: ἐξαπορέομαι, ἐξαπορέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6323 פּוּן",
    1821: "ἐξαποστέλλω (exapostéllō | ex-ap-os-tel'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G649\nStrong's: to send away forth, i.e. (on a mission) to despatch, or (peremptorily) to dismiss\nKJV: —send (away, forth, out).\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G649 \n\nCognate Group: G651 (apostleship), G649 (put in), G5570 (false teacher), G1821 (send), G652 (apostle), G3992 (send)\nVariants: ἐξαποστέλλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H8 אֹבֵד, H1644 גָּרַשׁ, H1980 הָלַךְ, H3318 יָצָא, H4284 מַחֲשָׁבָה, H5493 סוּר, H7725 שׁוּב, H7971 שָׁלַח",
    1822: "ἐξαρτίζω (exartízō | ex-ar-tid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and a derivative of G739\nStrong's: to finish out (time); figuratively, to equip fully (a teacher)\nKJV: —accomplish, thoroughly furnish.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G739 \n\nCognate Group: G739 (perfect), G2676 (perfection), G2677 (perfecting), G1822 (accomplish), G2675 (fit)\nVariants: ἐξαρτίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2266 חָבַר",
    1823: "ἐξαστράπτω (exastráptō | ex-as-trap'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G797\nStrong's: to lighten forth, i.e. (figuratively) to be radiant (of very white garments)\nKJV: —glistening.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G797 \n\nCognate Group: G739 (perfect), G2676 (perfection), G2677 (perfecting), G1822 (accomplish), G2675 (fit)\nVariants: ἐξαστράπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1300 בָּרָק, H3947 לָקַח, H7043 קָלַל",
    1824: "ἐξαυτῆς (exautēs | ex-ow'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and the genitive case singular feminine of G846 (G5610 being understood)\nStrong's: from that hour, i.e. instantly\nKJV: —by and by, immediately, presently, straightway.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G846 \nSee: G5610 \n\nCognate Group: G739 (perfect), G2676 (perfection), G2677 (perfecting), G1822 (accomplish), G2675 (fit)\nVariants: ἐξαυτῆς",
    1825: "ἐξεγείρω (exegeírō | ex-eg-i'-ro)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G1453\nStrong's: to rouse fully, i.e. (figuratively) to resuscitate (from death), release (from infliction)\nKJV: —raise up.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1453 \n\nCognate Group: G1454 (resurrection), G1453 (awake), G1127 (be vigilant), G1825 (raise up)\nVariants: ἐξεγείρω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1197 בָּעַר, H2342 חוּל, H2418 חֲיָא, H2904 טוּל, H3259 יָעַד, H3364 יָקַץ, H3364 יָקַץ, H5287 נָעַר, H5590 סָעַר, H5674 עָבַר, H5782 עוּר, H6965 קוּם, H7287 רָדָה, H7580 שָׁאַג, H7682 שָׂגַב, H8045 שָׁמַד",
    1826: "ἔξειμι (éxeimi | ex'-i-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and εἶμι (to go)\nStrong's: to issue, i.e. leave (a place), escape (to the shore)\nKJV: —depart, get (to land), go out.\n\nSee: G1537 \n\nCognate Group: G1454 (resurrection), G1453 (awake), G1127 (be vigilant), G1825 (raise up)\nVariants: ἔξειμι, ἔξειμι1",
    1827: "ἐξελέγχω (exelénchō | ex-el-eng'-kho)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G1651\nStrong's: to convict fully, i.e. (by implication) to punish\nKJV: —convince.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1651 \n\nCognate Group: G1454 (resurrection), G1453 (awake), G1127 (be vigilant), G1825 (raise up)\nVariants: ἐξελέγχω G1998 \nHebrew Equivalents: H3198 יָכַח",
    1828: "ἐξέλκω (exélkō | ex-el'-ko)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G1670\nStrong's: to drag forth, i.e. (figuratively) to entice (to sin)\nKJV: —draw away.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G1670 \n\nCognate Group: G1454 (resurrection), G1453 (awake), G1127 (be vigilant), G1825 (raise up)\nVariants: ἐξέλκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3423 יָרַשׁ, H4330 מִיץ, H4900 מָשַׁךְ, H5423 נָתַק, H7602 שָׁאַף",
