    1840: "ἐξισχύω (exischýō | ex-is-khoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G2480\nStrong's: to have full strength, i.e. be entirely competent\nKJV: —be able.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G2480 \n\nCognate Group: G1611 (+ be amazed), G1839 (amaze)\nVariants: ἐξισχύω",
    1841: "ἔξοδος (éxodos | ex'-od-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G3598\nStrong's: an exit, i.e. (figuratively) death\nKJV: —decease, departing.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G3598 \n\nCognate Group: G3595 (guide), G3594 (guide), G3598 (journey), G1327 (highway), G1841 (decease), G1529 (coming), G3180 (wile)\nVariants: ἔξοδος \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H2351 חוּץ, H3318 יָצָא, H4161 מֹוצָא, H4726 מָקֹור, H6675 צֹואָה, H6793 צִנָּה",
