    1843: "ἐξομολογέω (exomologéō | ex-om-ol-og-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G3670\nStrong's: to acknowledge or (by implication, of assent) agree fully\nKJV: —confess, profess, promise.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G3670 \n\nCognate Group: G437 (give thanks), G1843 (confess), G3672 (without controversy), G3671 (con- fession), G3670 (con- fess)\nVariants: ἐξομολογέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1927 הֲדָרָה, H1984 הָלַל, H3034 יָדָה, H3046 יְדַע, H7650 שָׁבַע",
    1844: "ἐξορκίζω (exorkízō | ex-or-kid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G3726\nStrong's: to exact an oath, i.e. conjure\nKJV: —adjure.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G3726 \n\nCognate Group: G1964 (forswear self), G1844 (adjure), G3728 (oath), G3726 (adjure), G1845 (exorcist), G1965 (perjured person), G3727 (oath)\nVariants: ἐξορκίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5927 עָלָה, H7650 שָׁבַע",
    1845: "ἐξορκιστής (exorkistḗs | ex-or-kis-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G1844\nStrong's: one that binds by an oath (or spell), i.e. (by implication) an \"exorcist\" (conjurer)\nKJV: —exorcist.\n\nSee: G1844 \n\nCognate Group: G1964 (forswear self), G1844 (adjure), G3728 (oath), G3726 (adjure), G1845 (exorcist), G1965 (perjured person), G3727 (oath)\nVariants: ἐξορκιστής",
