    1847: "ἐξουδενόω (exoudenóō | ex-oo-den-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and a derivative of the neuter of G3762\nStrong's: to make utterly nothing of, i.e. despise\nKJV: —set at nought. See also G1848 .\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G3762 \nSee: G1848 \n\nCognate Group: G1964 (forswear self), G1844 (adjure), G3728 (oath), G3726 (adjure), G1845 (exorcist), G1965 (perjured person), G3727 (oath)\nVariants: ἐξουδενόω, ἐξουδενέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H936 בּוּז, H947 בּוּס, H959 בָּזָה, H3782 כָּשַׁל, H3988 מָאַס, H5921 עַל, H7600 שַׁאֲנָן",
    1848: "ἐξουθενέω (exouthenéō | ex-oo-then-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: a variation of G1847 and meaning the same\nKJV: —contemptible, despise, least esteemed, set at nought.\n\nSee: G1847 \n\nCognate Group: G1964 (forswear self), G1844 (adjure), G3728 (oath), G3726 (adjure), G1845 (exorcist), G1965 (perjured person), G3727 (oath)\nVariants: ἐξουθενέω, ἐξουθενόω, ἐξουθενέω/ἐξουθενόω",
    1849: "ἐξουσία (exousía | ex-oo-see'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1832 (in the sense of ability)\nStrong's: privilege, i.e. (subjectively) force, capacity, competency, freedom, or (objectively) mastery (concretely, magistrate, superhuman, potentate, token of control), delegated influence\nKJV: —authority, jurisdiction, liberty, power, right, strength.\n\nSee: G1832 \n\nCognate Group: G1849 (authority), G1850 (exercise authority upon), G2715 (exercise authority), G1832 (be lawful)\nVariants: ἐξουσία \nHebrew Equivalents: H1884 דְּתָבָר, H4475 מֶמְשָׁלָה, H7982 שֶׁלֶט, H7985 שׇׁלְטָן, H7989 שַׁלִּיט, H8614 תִּפְתַּי",
    1850: "ἐξουσιάζω (exousiázō | ex-oo-see-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1849\nStrong's: to control\nKJV: —exercise authority upon, bring under the (have) power of.\n\nSee: G1849 \n\nCognate Group: G1849 (authority), G1850 (exercise authority upon), G2715 (exercise authority), G1832 (be lawful)\nVariants: ἐξουσιάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H4911 מָשַׁל, H7980 שָׁלַט",
    1851: "ἐξοχή (exochḗ | ex-okh-ay')\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1537 and G2192 (meaning to stand out)\nStrong's: prominence (figuratively)\nKJV: —principal.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G2192 \n\nCognate Group: G1849 (authority), G1850 (exercise authority upon), G2715 (exercise authority), G1832 (be lawful)\nVariants: ἐξοχή \nHebrew Equivalents: H8127 שֵׁן",
    1852: "ἐξυπνίζω (exypnízō | ex-oop-nid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1853\nStrong's: to waken\nKJV: —awake out of sleep.\n\nSee: G1853 \n\nCognate Group: G879 (fall asleep), G1798 (dream), G1853 (X out of sleep), G5258 (sleep), G1797 (dream), G1852 (awake out of sleep)\nVariants: ἐξυπνίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3364 יָקַץ, H5782 עוּר",
    1853: "ἔξυπνος (éxypnos | ex'-oop-nos)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and G5258\nStrong's: awake\nKJV: —X out of sleep.\n\nSee: G1537 \nSee: G5258 \n\nCognate Group: G879 (fall asleep), G1798 (dream), G1853 (X out of sleep), G5258 (sleep), G1797 (dream), G1852 (awake out of sleep)\nVariants: ἔξυπνος",
    1854: "ἔξω (éxō | ex'-o)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G1537\nStrong's: out(-side, of doors), literally or figuratively\nKJV: —away, forth, (with-)out (of, -ward), strange.\n\nSee: G1537 \n\nCognate Group: G1854 (away)\nVariants: ἔξω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1108 בַּלְעִי, H1249 בַּר, H2351 חוּץ, H6519 פְּרָזָה",
