    1856: "ἐξωθέω (exōthéō | ex-o-theh'-o) or ἐξώθω (exṓthō | ex-o'-tho)\n\nDerivation: from G1537 and ὠθέω (to push)\nStrong's: to expel; by implication, to propel\nKJV: —drive out, thrust in.\n\nSee: G1537 \n\nCognate Group: G1854 (away)\nVariants: ἐξωθέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1740 דּוּחַ, H1760 דָּחָה, H3512 כָּאָה, H3947 לָקַח, H5074 נָדַד, H5077 נָדָה, H5080 נָדַח, H5086 נָדַף, H5255 נָסַח, H7368 רָחַק, H8582 תָּעָה",
    1857: "ἐξώτερος (exṓteros | ex-o'-ter-os)\n\nDerivation: comparative of G1854\nStrong's: exterior\nKJV: —outer.\n\nSee: G1854 \n\nCognate Group: G1854 (away)\nVariants: ἐξώτερος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2435 חִיצֹון, H2691 חָצֵר, H7020 קִיצֹון",
    1858: "ἑορτάζω (heortázō | heh-or-tad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1859\nStrong's: to observe a festival\nKJV: —keep the feast.\n\nSee: G1859 \n\nCognate Group: G1858 (keep the feast), G1859 (feast)\nVariants: ἑορτάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2287 חָגַג",
    1859: "ἑορτή (heortḗ | heh-or-tay')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a festival\nKJV: —feast, holyday.\n\nCognate Group: G1858 (keep the feast), G1859 (feast)\nVariants: ἑορτή \nHebrew Equivalents: H2282 חַג, H2320 חֹדֶשׁ, H4150 מֹועֵד",
    1860: "ἐπαγγελία (epangelía | ep-ang-el-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1861\nStrong's: an announcement (for information, assent or pledge; especially a divine assurance of good)\nKJV: —message, promise.\n\nSee: G1861 \n\nCognate Group: G1861 (profess), G1860 (message), G4279 (promise before), G1862 (promise)\nVariants: ἐπαγγελία \nHebrew Equivalents: H92 אֲגֻדָּה, H5612 סֵפֶר, H6575 פָּרָשָׁה",
