    1864: "ἐπαγωνίζομαι (epagōnízomai | ep-ag-o-nid'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G75\nStrong's: to struggle for\nKJV: —earnestly contend for.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G75 \n\nCognate Group: G73 (conflict), G464 (strive against), G74 (agony), G1864 (earnestly contend for), G75 (fight), G2610 (subdue)\nVariants: ἐπαγωνίζομαι",
