    1870: "ἐπαισχύνομαι (epaischýnomai | ep-ahee-skhoo'-nom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G153\nStrong's: to feel shame for something\nKJV: —be ashamed.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G153 \n\nCognate Group: G2617 (confound), G151 (filthiness), G1870 (be ashamed), G150 (filthy), G152 (dishonesty), G153 (be ashamed)\nVariants: ἐπαισχύνομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H954 בּוּשׁ, H2659 חָפֵר, H5375 נָשָׂא",
    1871: "ἐπαιτέω (epaitéō | ep-ahee-teh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G154\nStrong's: to ask for\nKJV: —beg.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G154 \n\nCognate Group: G2617 (confound), G151 (filthiness), G1870 (be ashamed), G150 (filthy), G152 (dishonesty), G153 (be ashamed)\nVariants: ἐπαιτέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7592 שָׁאַל",
    1872: "ἐπακολουθέω (epakolouthéō | ep-ak-ol-oo-theh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G190\nStrong's: to accompany\nKJV: —follow (after).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G190 \n\nCognate Group: G1811 (follow), G3877 (attain), G1872 (follow), G4870 (follow), G190 (follow)\nVariants: ἐπακολουθέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H309 אָחַר, H1980 הָלַךְ, H6437 פָּנָה, H8454 תּוּשִׁיָּה",
