    1875: "ἐπάν (epán | ep-an')\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G302\nStrong's: a particle of indefinite contemporaneousness; whenever, as soon as\nKJV: —when.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G302 \n\nCognate Group: G5218 (obedience), G1522 (hear), G1873 (hear), G191 (give audience), G3878 (neglect to hear), G5219 (hearken), G5255 (obedient), G3876 (disobedience), G189 (audience)\nVariants: ἐπάν",
    1876: "ἐπάναγκες (epánankes | ep-an'-ang-kes)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a presumed compound of G1909 and G318\nStrong's: (adverbially) on necessity, i.e. necessarily\nKJV: —necessary.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G318 \n\nCognate Group: G5218 (obedience), G1522 (hear), G1873 (hear), G191 (give audience), G3878 (neglect to hear), G5219 (hearken), G5255 (obedient), G3876 (disobedience), G189 (audience)\nVariants: ἐπάναγκες",
    1877: "ἐπανάγω (epanágō | ep-an-ag'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G321\nStrong's: to lead up on, i.e. (technical) to put out (to sea); (intransitively) to return\nKJV: —launch (thrust) out, return.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G321 \n\nCognate Group: G5218 (obedience), G1522 (hear), G1873 (hear), G191 (give audience), G3878 (neglect to hear), G5219 (hearken), G5255 (obedient), G3876 (disobedience), G189 (audience)\nVariants: ἐπανάγω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7324 רוּק",
    1878: "ἐπαναμιμνήσκω (epanamimnḗskō | ep-an-ah-mim-nace'-ko)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G363\nStrong's: to remind of\nKJV: —put in mind.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G363 \n\nCognate Group: G5218 (obedience), G1522 (hear), G1873 (hear), G191 (give audience), G3878 (neglect to hear), G5219 (hearken), G5255 (obedient), G3876 (disobedience), G189 (audience)\nVariants: ἐπαναμιμνήσκω, ἐπαναμιμνῄσκω",
    1879: "ἐπαναπαύομαι (epanapaúomai | ep-an-ah-pow'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1909 and G373\nStrong's: to settle on; literally (remain) or figuratively (rely)\nKJV: —rest in (upon).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G373 \n\nCognate Group: G372 (rest), G1879 (rest in), G373 (take ease)\nVariants: ἐπαναπαύομαι, ἐπαναπαύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5117 נוּחַ, H8172 שָׁעַן",
    1880: "ἐπανέρχομαι (epanérchomai | ep-an-er'-khom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G424\nStrong's: to come up on, i.e. return\nKJV: —come again, return.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G424 \n\nCognate Group: G372 (rest), G1879 (rest in), G373 (take ease)\nVariants: ἐπανέρχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1980 הָלַךְ, H7725 שׁוּב",
    1881: "ἐπανίσταμαι (epanístamai | ep-an-is'-tam-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1909 and G450\nStrong's: to stand up on, i.e. (figuratively) to attack\nKJV: —rise up against.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G450 \n\nCognate Group: G372 (rest), G1879 (rest in), G373 (take ease)\nVariants: ἐπανίσταμαι, ἐπανίστημι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1869 דָּרַךְ, H2015 הָפַךְ, H5782 עוּר, H5782 עוּר, H5975 עָמַד, H6965 קוּם",
    1882: "ἐπανόρθωσις (epanórthōsis | ep-an-or'-tho-sis)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1909 and G461\nStrong's: a straightening up again, i.e. (figuratively) rectification (reformation)\nKJV: — correction.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G461 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἐπανόρθωσις",
