    1884: "ἐπαρκέω (eparkéō | ep-ar-keh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G714\nStrong's: to avail for, i.e. help\nKJV: —relieve.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G714 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἐπαρκέω",
    1885: "ἐπαρχία (eparchía | ep-ar-khee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1909 and G757 (meaning a governor of a district, \"eparch\")\nStrong's: a special region of government, i.e. a Roman præfecture\nKJV: —province.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G757 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἐπαρχία, ἐπαρχεία, ἐπάρχειος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4082 מְדִינָה",
    1886: "ἔπαυλις (épaulis | ep'-ow-lis)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and an equivalent of G833\nStrong's: a hut over the head, i.e. a dwelling\nKJV: —habitation.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G833 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἔπαυλις \nHebrew Equivalents: H1448 גְּדֵרָה, H2247 חָבָה, H2351 חוּץ, H2691 חָצֵר, H2918 טִירָה, H5116 נָוֶה, H7339 רְחֹב",
    1887: "ἐπαύριον (epaúrion | ep-ow'-ree-on)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G839\nStrong's: occurring on the succeeding day, i.e. (G2250 being implied) to-morrow\nKJV: —day following, morrow, next day (after).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G839 \nSee: G2250 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἐπαύριον \nHebrew Equivalents: H4279 מָחָר, H4283 מׇחֳרָת",
    1888: "ἐπαυτοφώρῳ (epautophṓrōi | ep-ow-tof-o'-ro)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G846 and (the dative case singular of) a derivative of φώρ (a thief)\nStrong's: in theft itself, i.e. (by analogy) in actual crime\nKJV: —in the very act.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G846 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἐπαυτοφώρῳ, αὐτόφωρος",
    1889: "Ἐπαφρᾶς (Epaphrâs | ep-af-ras')\n\nDerivation: contracted from G1891\nStrong's: Epaphras, a Christian\nKJV: —Epaphras.\n\nSee: G1891 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: Ἐπαφρᾶς",
    1890: "ἐπαφρίζω (epaphrízō | ep-af-rid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G875\nStrong's: to foam upon, i.e. (figuratively) to exhibit (a vile passion)\nKJV: —foam out.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G875 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἐπαφρίζω, ἀπαφρίζω",
    1891: "Ἐπαφρόδιτος (Epaphróditos | ep-af-rod'-ee-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 (in the sense of devoted to) and Ἀφροδίτη (Venus)\nStrong's: Epaphroditus, a Christian\nKJV: —Epaphroditus. Compare G1889 .\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1889 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: Ἐπαφρόδιτος",
    1892: "ἐπεγείρω (epegeírō | ep-eg-i'-ro)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G1453\nStrong's: to rouse upon, i.e. (figuratively) to excite against\nKJV: —raise, stir up.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1453 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἐπεγείρω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3381 יָרַד, H5526 סָכַךְ, H5782 עוּר, H6965 קוּם",
