    1896: "ἐπεῖδον (epeîdon | ep-i'-don)\n\nDerivation: and other moods and persons of the same tense; from G1909 and G1492\nStrong's: to regard (favorably or otherwise)\nKJV: —behold, look upon.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1492 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἐπεῖδον, ἐφοράω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7200 רָאָה",
    1897: "ἐπείπερ (epeíper | ep-i'-per)\n\nDerivation: from G1893 and G4007\nStrong's: since indeed (of cause)\nKJV: —seeing.\n\nSee: G1893 \nSee: G4007 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἐπείπερ G2080",
    1898: "ἐπεισαγωγή (epeisagōgḗ | ep-ice-ag-o-gay')\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1909 and G1521\nStrong's: a superintroduction\nKJV: —bringing in.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1521 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἐπεισαγωγή",
    1899: "ἔπειτα (épeita | ep'-i-tah)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G1534\nStrong's: thereafter\nKJV: —after that(-ward), then.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1534 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἔπειτα",
    1900: "ἐπέκεινα (epékeina | ep-ek'-i-nah)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and (the accusative case plural neuter of) G1565\nStrong's: upon those parts of, i.e. on the further side of\nKJV: —beyond.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1565 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἐπέκεινα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1973 הָלְאָה, H4605 מַעַל, H5704 עַד",
    1901: "ἐπεκτείνομαι (epekteínomai | ep-ek-ti'-nom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1909 and G1614\nStrong's: to stretch (oneself) forward upon\nKJV: —reach forth.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1614 \n\nCognate Group: G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)\nVariants: ἐπεκτείνομαι",
    1902: "ἐπενδύομαι (ependýomai | ep-en-doo'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1909 and G1746\nStrong's: to invest upon oneself\nKJV: —be clothed upon.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1746 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: ἐπενδύομαι",
    1903: "ἐπενδύτης (ependýtēs | ep-en-doo'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G1902\nStrong's: a wrapper, i.e. outer garment\nKJV: —fisher's coat.\n\nSee: G1902 \n\nCognate Group: G1416 (set), G554 (put off), G1902 (be clothed upon), G1744 (creep), G555 (putting off), G1562 (strip)\nVariants: ἐπενδύτης \nHebrew Equivalents: H4598 מְעִיל",
    1904: "ἐπέρχομαι (epérchomai | ep-er'-khom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2064\nStrong's: to supervene, i.e. arrive, occur, impend, attack, (figuratively) influence\nKJV: —come (in, upon).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2064 \n\nCognate Group: G1330 (come), G565 (come), G1525 (X arise), G4905 (accompany), G4281 (go before), G4022 (fetch a compass), G2064 (accompany), G1904 (come), G4334 (come), G1831 (come), G3928 (come), G3922 (come in privily)\nVariants: ἐπέρχομαι, ἐπεισέρχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H268 אָחֹור, H935 בֹּוא, H935 בֹּוא, H1468 גּוּז, H1518 גִּיחַ, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2498 חָלַף, H2904 טוּל, H3318 יָצָא, H5064 נָגַר, H5307 נָפַל, H5413 נָתַךְ, H5674 עָבַר, H5844 עָטָה, H5927 עָלָה, H6168 עָרָה, H6424 פָּלַס, H6597 פִּתְאֹום, H6965 קוּם, H7200 רָאָה, H7378 רִיב, H7725 שׁוּב, H7896 שִׁית, H7931 שָׁכַן",
    1905: "ἐπερωτάω (eperōtáō | ep-er-o-tah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2065\nStrong's: to ask for, i.e. inquire, seek\nKJV: —ask (after, questions), demand, desire, question.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2065 \n\nCognate Group: G1906 (answer), G1905 (ask), G2065 (ask)\nVariants: ἐπερωτάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H1875 דָּרַשׁ, H6030 עָנָה, H7136 קָרָה, H7592 שָׁאַל",
    1906: "ἐπερώτημα (eperṓtēma | ep-er-o'-tay-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G1905\nStrong's: an inquiry\nKJV: —answer.\n\nSee: G1905 \n\nCognate Group: G1906 (answer), G1905 (ask), G2065 (ask)\nVariants: ἐπερώτημα",
    1907: "ἐπέχω (epéchō | ep-ekh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2192\nStrong's: to hold upon, i.e. (by implication) to retain; (by extension) to detain; (with implication, of G3563) to pay attention to\nKJV: —give (take) heed unto, hold forth, mark, stay.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2192 \nSee: G3563 \n\nCognate Group: G1906 (answer), G1905 (ask), G2065 (ask)\nVariants: ἐπέχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H995 בִּין, H1214 בָּצַע, H2308 חָדַל, H2342 חוּל, H3176 יָחַל, H3811 לָאָה, H4513 מָנַע, H6113 עָצָר, H6960 קָוָה",
    1908: "ἐπηρεάζω (epēreázō | ep-ay-reh-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from a comparative of G1909 and (probably) ἀρειά (threats)\nStrong's: to insult, slander\nKJV: —use despitefully, falsely accuse.\n\nSee: G1909 \n\nCognate Group: G1906 (answer), G1905 (ask), G2065 (ask)\nVariants: ἐπηρεάζω",
    1909: "ἐπί (epí | ep-ee')\n\nDerivation: a primary preposition\nStrong's: properly, meaning superimposition (of time, place, order, etc.), as a relation of distribution (with the genitive case), i.e. over, upon, etc.; of rest (with the dative case) at, on, etc.; of direction (with the accusative case) towards, upon, etc.\nKJV: —about (the times), above, after, against, among, as long as (touching), at, beside, X have charge of, (be-, (where-))fore, in (a place, as much as, the time of, -to), (because) of, (up-)on (behalf of), over, (by, for) the space of, through(-out), (un-)to(-ward), with. In compounds it retains essentially the same import, at, upon, etc. (literally or figuratively).\n\nCognate Group: G1906 (answer), G1905 (ask), G2065 (ask)\nVariants: ἐπί",
    1910: "ἐπιβαίνω (epibaínō | ep-ee-bah'-ee-no)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and the base of G939\nStrong's: to walk upon, i.e. mount, ascend, embark, arrive\nKJV: —come (into), enter into, go abroad, sit upon, take ship.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G1906 (answer), G1905 (ask), G2065 (ask)\nVariants: ἐπιβαίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1869 דָּרַךְ, H1961 הָיָה, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2015 הָפַךְ, H2583 חָנָה, H3320 יָצַב, H5927 עָלָה, H5975 עָמַד, H6805 צָעַד, H7392 רָכַב",
    1911: "ἐπιβάλλω (epibállō | ep-ee-bal'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G906\nStrong's: to throw upon (literal or figurative, transitive or reflexive; usually with more or less force); specially (with G1438 implied) to reflect; impersonally, to belong to\nKJV: —beat into, cast (up-)on, fall, lay (on), put (unto), stretch forth, think on.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G906 \nSee: G1438 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐπιβάλλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H698 אׇרֳבָה, H935 בֹּוא, H1891 הָבַל, H1911 הָדָה, H5080 נָדַח, H5130 נוּף, H5186 נָטָה, H5307 נָפַל, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5414 נָתַן, H5428 נָתַשׁ, H5674 עָבַר, H5927 עָלָה, H6064 עָנַשׁ, H6566 פָּרַשׂ, H6923 קָדַם, H7725 שׁוּב, H7760 שׂוּם, H7896 שִׁית, H7971 שָׁלַח, H7993 שָׁלַךְ",
    1912: "ἐπιβαρέω (epibaréō | ep-ee-bar-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G916\nStrong's: to be heavy upon, i.e. (pecuniarily) to be expensive to; figuratively, to be severe towards\nKJV: —be chargeable to, overcharge.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G916 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐπιβαρέω",
    1913: "ἐπιβιβάζω (epibibázō | ep-ee-bee-bad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and a reduplicated derivative of the base of G939 (compare G307)\nStrong's: to cause to mount (an animal)\nKJV: —set on.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G939 \nSee: G307 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐπιβιβάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1869 דָּרַךְ, H3381 יָרַד, H7392 רָכַב",
    1914: "ἐπιβλέπω (epiblépō | ep-ee-blep'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G991\nStrong's: to gaze at (with favor, pity or partiality)\nKJV: —look upon, regard, have respect to.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G991 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐπιβλέπω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1204 בָּעַת, H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H5027 נָבַט, H5091 נָהָה, H5186 נָטָה, H5198 נָטָף, H5782 עוּר, H6437 פָּנָה, H6822 צָפָה, H6851 צַפְצָפָה, H7200 רָאָה, H7688 שָׁגַח, H7725 שׁוּב, H7751 שׁוּט, H8259 שָׁקַף",
    1915: "ἐπίβλημα (epíblēma | ep-ib'-lay-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G1911\nStrong's: a patch\nKJV: —piece.\n\nSee: G1911 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐπίβλημα",
    1916: "ἐπιβοάω (epiboáō | ep-ee-bo-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G994\nStrong's: to exclaim against\nKJV: —cry.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G994 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐπιβοάω G2100",
    1917: "ἐπιβουλή (epiboulḗ | ep-ee-boo-lay')\n\nDerivation: from a presumed compound of G1909 and G1014\nStrong's: a plan against someone, i.e. a plot\nKJV: —laying (lying) in wait.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1014 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐπιβουλή",
    1918: "ἐπιγαμβρεύω (epigambreúō | ep-ee-gam-bryoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and a derivative of G1062\nStrong's: to form affinity with, i.e. (specially) in a levirate way\nKJV: —marry.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1062 \n\nCognate Group: G1911 (beat into), G906 (arise), G1544 (bring forth)\nVariants: ἐπιγαμβρεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2859 חָתַן, H2992 יָבַם",
    1919: "ἐπίγειος (epígeios | ep-ig'-i-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G1093\nStrong's: worldly (physically or morally)\nKJV: —earthly, in earth, terrestrial.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1093 \n\nCognate Group: G1093 (country), G1919 (earthly)\nVariants: ἐπίγειος",
    1920: "ἐπιγίνομαι (epigínomai | ep-ig-in'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G1096\nStrong's: to arrive upon, i.e. spring up (as a wind)\nKJV: —blow.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1096 \n\nCognate Group: G1093 (country), G1919 (earthly)\nVariants: ἐπιγίνομαι",
    1921: "ἐπιγινώσκω (epiginṓskō | ep-ig-in-oce'-ko)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G1097\nStrong's: to know upon some mark, i.e. recognize; by implication, to become fully acquainted with, to acknowledge\nKJV: —(ac-, have, take)know(-ledge, well), perceive.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1097 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: ἐπιγινώσκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H995 בִּין, H1846 דָּעַךְ, H3045 יָדַע, H5234 נָכַר, H7200 רָאָה, H7919 שָׂכַל",
    1922: "ἐπίγνωσις (epígnōsis | ep-ig'-no-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G1921\nStrong's: recognition, i.e. (by implication) full discernment, acknowledgement\nKJV: —(ac-)knowledge(-ing, - ment).\n\nSee: G1921 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: ἐπίγνωσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H1847 דַּעַת",
    1923: "ἐπιγραφή (epigraphḗ | ep-ig-raf-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G1924\nStrong's: an inscription\nKJV: —superscription.\n\nSee: G1924 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: ἐπιγραφή",
    1924: "ἐπιγράφω (epigráphō | ep-ee-graf'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G1125\nStrong's: to inscribe (physically or mentally)\nKJV: —inscription, write in (over, thereon).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1125 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: ἐπιγράφω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3789 כָּתַב",
    1925: "ἐπιδείκνυμι (epideíknymi | ep-ee-dike'-noo-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G1166\nStrong's: to exhibit (physically or mentally)\nKJV: —shew.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1166 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: ἐπιδείκνυμι \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H6315 פּוּחַ",
    1926: "ἐπιδέχομαι (epidéchomai | ep-ee-dekh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G1209\nStrong's: to admit (as a guest or (figuratively) teacher)\nKJV: —receive.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1209 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: ἐπιδέχομαι",
    1927: "ἐπιδημέω (epidēméō | ep-ee-day-meh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1909 and G1218\nStrong's: to make oneself at home, i.e. (by extension) to reside (in a foreign country)\nKJV: —(be) dwelling (which were) there, stranger.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1218 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: ἐπιδημέω",
    1928: "ἐπιδιατάσσομαι (epidiatássomai | ep-ee-dee-ah-tas'-som-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1909 and G1299\nStrong's: to appoint besides, i.e. supplement (as a codicil)\nKJV: —add to.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1299 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: ἐπιδιατάσσομαι",
    1929: "ἐπιδίδωμι (epidídōmi | ep-ee-did'-o-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G1325\nStrong's: to give over (by hand or surrender)\nKJV: —deliver unto, give, let (+ (her drive)), offer.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1325 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: ἐπιδίδωμι, προσδίδωμι \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H4191 מוּת, H5414 נָתַן",
    1930: "ἐπιδιορθόω (epidiorthóō | ep-ee-dee-or-tho'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and a derivative of G3717\nStrong's: to straighten further, i.e. (figuratively) arrange additionally\nKJV: —set in order.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3717 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: ἐπιδιορθόω",
    1931: "ἐπιδύω (epidýō | ep-ee-doo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G1416\nStrong's: to set fully (as the sun)\nKJV: —go down.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1416 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: ἐπιδύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא",
    1932: "ἐπιείκεια (epieíkeia | ep-ee-i'-ki-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1933\nStrong's: suitableness, i.e. (by implication) equity, mildness\nKJV: —clemency, gentleness.\n\nSee: G1933 \n\nCognate Group: G1932 (clemency), G1933 (gentle)\nVariants: ἐπιείκεια",
    1933: "ἐπιεικής (epieikḗs | ep-ee-i-kace')\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G1503\nStrong's: appropriate, i.e. (by implication) mild\nKJV: —gentle, moderation, patient.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1503 \n\nCognate Group: G1932 (clemency), G1933 (gentle)\nVariants: ἐπιεικής \nHebrew Equivalents: H5546 סַלָּח",
    1934: "ἐπιζητέω (epizētéō | ep-eed-zay-teh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2212\nStrong's: to search (inquire) for; intensively, to demand, to crave\nKJV: —desire, enquire, seek (after, for).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2212 \n\nCognate Group: G1932 (clemency), G1933 (gentle)\nVariants: ἐπιζητέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H1875 דָּרַשׁ, H6485 פָּקַד",
    1935: "ἐπιθανάτιος (epithanátios | ep-ee-than-at'-ee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2288\nStrong's: doomed to death\nKJV: —appointed to death.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2288 \n\nCognate Group: G1932 (clemency), G1933 (gentle)\nVariants: ἐπιθανάτιος",
    1936: "ἐπίθεσις (epíthesis | ep-ith'-es-is)\n\nDerivation: from G2007\nStrong's: an imposition (of hands officially)\nKJV: —laying (putting) on.\n\nSee: G2007 \n\nCognate Group: G3866 (committed unto), G3908 (allege), G3331 (change), G4286 (purpose), G114 (cast off), G5087 (+ advise), G2007 (add unto), G4388 (purpose), G115 (disannulling), G4369 (add), G3346 (carry over), G1936 (laying on)\nVariants: ἐπίθεσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H5691 עֲגָבָה, H7195 קֶשֶׁר",
    1937: "ἐπιθυμέω (epithyméō | ep-ee-thoo-meh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2372\nStrong's: to set the heart upon, i.e. long for (rightfully or otherwise)\nKJV: —covet, desire, would fain, lust (after).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2372 \n\nCognate Group: G1939 (concupiscence), G1937 (covet), G2372 (fierceness), G1938 (+ lust after), G1761 (device), G1760 (think)\nVariants: ἐπιθυμέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H183 אָוָה, H559 אָמַר, H977 בָּחַר, H2530 חָמַד, H2654 חָפֵץ, H2836 חָשַׁק, H3700 כָּסַף, H7235 רָבָה, H7592 שָׁאַל, H8581 תַּעָב",
    1938: "ἐπιθυμητής (epithymētḗs | ep-ee-thoo-may-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G1937\nStrong's: a craver\nKJV: —+ lust after.\n\nSee: G1937 \n\nCognate Group: G1939 (concupiscence), G1937 (covet), G2372 (fierceness), G1938 (+ lust after), G1761 (device), G1760 (think)\nVariants: ἐπιθυμητής \nHebrew Equivalents: H183 אָוָה, H2530 חָמַד",
    1939: "ἐπιθυμία (epithymía | ep-ee-thoo-mee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1937\nStrong's: a longing (especially for what is forbidden)\nKJV: —concupiscence, desire, lust (after).\n\nSee: G1937 \n\nCognate Group: G1939 (concupiscence), G1937 (covet), G2372 (fierceness), G1938 (+ lust after), G1761 (device), G1760 (think)\nVariants: ἐπιθυμία \nHebrew Equivalents: H183 אָוָה, H185 אַוָּה, H827 אַשְׁפָּה, H2530 חָמַד, H2531 חֶמֶד, H2837 חֵשֶׁק, H3700 כָּסַף, H3824 לֵבָב, H5716 עֲדִי, H7522 רָצֹון, H8378 תַּאֲוָה",
    1940: "ἐπικαθίζω (epikathízō | ep-ee-kath-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2523\nStrong's: to seat upon\nKJV: —set on.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2523 \n\nCognate Group: G1939 (concupiscence), G1937 (covet), G2372 (fierceness), G1938 (+ lust after), G1761 (device), G1760 (think)\nVariants: ἐπικαθίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3427 יָשַׁב, H7392 רָכַב, H7931 שָׁכַן",
