    1942: "ἐπικάλυμα (epikályma | ep-ee-kal'-oo-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G1943\nStrong's: a covering, i.e. (figuratively) pretext\nKJV: —cloke.\n\nSee: G1943 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: ἐπικάλυμα, ἐπικάλυμμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H4374 מְכַסֶּה, H4539 מָסָךְ",
    1943: "ἐπικαλύπτω (epikalýptō | ep-ee-kal-oop'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2572\nStrong's: to conceal, i.e. (figuratively) forgive\nKJV: —cover.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2572 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: ἐπικαλύπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2645 חָפָה, H3680 כָּסָה, H3874 לוּט, H5628 סָרַח, H6566 פָּרַשׂ, H7939 שָׂכָר",
    1944: "ἐπικατάρατος (epikatáratos | ep-ee-kat-ar'-at-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and a derivative of G2672\nStrong's: imprecated, i.e. execrable\nKJV: —accursed.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2672 \n\nCognate Group: G685 (curse), G2671 (cursed), G2672 (curse), G1944 (accursed), G686 (haply), G687 (therefore)\nVariants: ἐπικατάρατος, ἐπάρατος",
    1945: "ἐπίκειμαι (epíkeimai | ep-ik'-i-mahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2749\nStrong's: to rest upon (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —impose, be instant, (be) laid (there-, up-)on, (when) lay (on), lie (on), press upon.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2749 \n\nCognate Group: G4029 (be bound with), G4295 (be first), G1945 (impose), G606 (be appointed), G4873 (sit with), G345 (guest), G480 (adversary), G3873 (be present), G2749 (be appointed), G2621 (keep)\nVariants: ἐπίκειμαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1970 הָכַר, H2554 חָמַס, H5414 נָתַן",
    1946: "Ἐπικούρειος (Epikoúreios | ep-ee-koo'-ri-os)\n\nDerivation: from Ἐπίκουρος (compare G1947) (a noted philosopher)\nStrong's: an Epicurean or follower of Epicurus\nKJV: —Epicurean.\n\nSee: G1947 \n\nCognate Group: G4029 (be bound with), G4295 (be first), G1945 (impose), G606 (be appointed), G4873 (sit with), G345 (guest), G480 (adversary), G3873 (be present), G2749 (be appointed), G2621 (keep)\nVariants: Ἐπικούρειος",
    1947: "ἐπικουρία (epikouría | ep-ee-koo-ree'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1909 and a (prolonged) form of the base of G2877 (in the sense of servant)\nStrong's: assistance\nKJV: —help.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2877 \n\nCognate Group: G4029 (be bound with), G4295 (be first), G1945 (impose), G606 (be appointed), G4873 (sit with), G345 (guest), G480 (adversary), G3873 (be present), G2749 (be appointed), G2621 (keep)\nVariants: ἐπικουρία",
    1948: "ἐπικρίνω (epikrínō | ep-ee-kree'-no)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2919\nStrong's: to adjudge\nKJV: —give sentence.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2919 \n\nCognate Group: G4029 (be bound with), G4295 (be first), G1945 (impose), G606 (be appointed), G4873 (sit with), G345 (guest), G480 (adversary), G3873 (be present), G2749 (be appointed), G2621 (keep)\nVariants: ἐπικρίνω",
    1949: "ἐπιλαμβάνομαι (epilambánomai | ep-ee-lam-ban'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1909 and G2983\nStrong's: to seize (for help, injury, attainment, or any other purpose; literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —catch, lay hold (up-)on, take (by, hold of, on).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2983 \n\nCognate Group: G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)\nVariants: ἐπιλαμβάνομαι, ἐπιλαμβάνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H270 אָחַז, H2388 חָזַק, H5710 עָדָה, H7059 קָמַט, H7121 קָרָא, H8264 שָׁקַק, H8610 תָּפַשׂ",
    1950: "ἐπιλανθάνομαι (epilanthánomai | ep-ee-lan-than'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1909 and G2990\nStrong's: to lose out of mind; by implication, to neglect\nKJV: —(be) forget(-ful of).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2990 \n\nCognate Group: G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)\nVariants: ἐπιλανθάνομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H5117 נוּחַ, H5382 נָשָׁה, H7623 שָׁבַח, H7911 שָׁכַח",
    1951: "ἐπιλέγομαι (epilégomai | ep-ee-leg'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1909 and G3004\nStrong's: to surname, select\nKJV: —call, choose.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3004 \n\nCognate Group: G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)\nVariants: ἐπιλέγομαι, ἐπιλέγω \nHebrew Equivalents: H977 בָּחַר, H1197 בָּעַר, H6908 קָבַץ",
    1952: "ἐπιλείπω (epileípō | ep-ee-li'-po)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G3007\nStrong's: to leave upon, i.e. (figuratively) to be insufficient for\nKJV: —fail.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3007 \n\nCognate Group: G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)\nVariants: ἐπιλείπω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7604 שָׁאַר",
    1953: "ἐπιλησμονή (epilēsmonḗ | ep-ee-lace-mon-ay')\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G1950\nStrong's: negligence\nKJV: —X forgetful.\n\nSee: G1950 \n\nCognate Group: G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)\nVariants: ἐπιλησμονή",
    1954: "ἐπίλοιπος (epíloipos | ep-il'-oy-pos)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G3062\nStrong's: left over, i.e. remaining\nKJV: —rest.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3062 \n\nCognate Group: G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)\nVariants: ἐπίλοιπος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3498 יָתַר, H7604 שָׁאַר",
