    1956: "ἐπιλύω (epilýō | ep-ee-loo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G3089\nStrong's: to solve further, i.e. (figuratively) to explain, decide\nKJV: —determine, expound.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3089 \n\nCognate Group: G2647 (destroy), G3089 (break), G3083 (ransom), G179 (endless), G630 (depart), G1956 (determine), G360 (depart), G3085 (+ redeemed), G2646 (guestchamber), G359 (departure), G3086 (deliverer), G1955 (interpretation), G3084 (redeem), G629 (deliverance), G487 (ransom)\nVariants: ἐπιλύω",
