    1958: "ἐπιμέλεια (epiméleia | ep-ee-mel'-i-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1959\nStrong's: carefulness, i.e. kind attention (hospitality)\nKJV: —+ refresh self.\n\nSee: G1959 \n\nCognate Group: G3143 (take to record), G3142 (to be testified), G3144 (martyr), G1957 (testify), G4303 (testify beforehand), G5576 (be a false witness), G5575 (false witness), G3141 (record), G5577 (false witness), G4828 (testify unto), G3140 (charge), G1263 (charge), G2649 (witness against), G4901 (also bear witness)\nVariants: ἐπιμέλεια \nHebrew Equivalents: H8250 שִׁקּוּי",
    1959: "ἐπιμελέομαι (epimeléomai | ep-ee-mel-eh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1909 and the same as G3199\nStrong's: to care for (physically or otherwise)\nKJV: —take care of.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3199 \n\nCognate Group: G3143 (take to record), G3142 (to be testified), G3144 (martyr), G1957 (testify), G4303 (testify beforehand), G5576 (be a false witness), G5575 (false witness), G3141 (record), G5577 (false witness), G4828 (testify unto), G3140 (charge), G1263 (charge), G2649 (witness against), G4901 (also bear witness)\nVariants: ἐπιμελέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H7760 שׂוּם",
    1960: "ἐπιμελῶς (epimelōs | ep-ee-mel-oce')\n\nDerivation: adverb from a derivative of G1959\nStrong's: carefully\nKJV: —diligently.\n\nSee: G1959 \n\nCognate Group: G3143 (take to record), G3142 (to be testified), G3144 (martyr), G1957 (testify), G4303 (testify beforehand), G5576 (be a false witness), G5575 (false witness), G3141 (record), G5577 (false witness), G4828 (testify unto), G3140 (charge), G1263 (charge), G2649 (witness against), G4901 (also bear witness)\nVariants: ἐπιμελῶς \nHebrew Equivalents: H629 אׇסְפַּרְנָא, H7535 רַק, H7836 שָׁחַר",
    1961: "ἐπιμένω (epiménō | ep-ee-men'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G3306\nStrong's: to stay over, i.e. remain (figuratively, persevere)\nKJV: —abide (in), continue (in), tarry.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3306 \n\nCognate Group: G3143 (take to record), G3142 (to be testified), G3144 (martyr), G1957 (testify), G4303 (testify beforehand), G5576 (be a false witness), G5575 (false witness), G3141 (record), G5577 (false witness), G4828 (testify unto), G3140 (charge), G1263 (charge), G2649 (witness against), G4901 (also bear witness)\nVariants: ἐπιμένω \nHebrew Equivalents: H4102 מָהַהּ",
    1962: "ἐπινεύω (epineúō | ep-een-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G3506\nStrong's: to nod at, i.e. (by implication) to assent\nKJV: —consent.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3506 \n\nCognate Group: G3143 (take to record), G3142 (to be testified), G3144 (martyr), G1957 (testify), G4303 (testify beforehand), G5576 (be a false witness), G5575 (false witness), G3141 (record), G5577 (false witness), G4828 (testify unto), G3140 (charge), G1263 (charge), G2649 (witness against), G4901 (also bear witness)\nVariants: ἐπινεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5234 נָכַר",
    1963: "ἐπίνοια (epínoia | ep-in'-oy-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G3563\nStrong's: attention of the mind, i.e. (by implication) purpose\nKJV: —thought.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3563 \n\nCognate Group: G3143 (take to record), G3142 (to be testified), G3144 (martyr), G1957 (testify), G4303 (testify beforehand), G5576 (be a false witness), G5575 (false witness), G3141 (record), G5577 (false witness), G4828 (testify unto), G3140 (charge), G1263 (charge), G2649 (witness against), G4901 (also bear witness)\nVariants: ἐπίνοια",
    1964: "ἐπιορκέω (epiorkéō | ep-ee-or-keh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1965\nStrong's: to commit perjury\nKJV: —forswear self.\n\nSee: G1965 \n\nCognate Group: G1964 (forswear self), G1844 (adjure), G3728 (oath), G3726 (adjure), G1845 (exorcist), G1965 (perjured person), G3727 (oath)\nVariants: ἐπιορκέω",
    1965: "ἐπίορκος (epíorkos | ep-ee'-or-kos)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G3727\nStrong's: on oath, i.e. (falsely) a forswearer\nKJV: —perjured person.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3727 \n\nCognate Group: G1964 (forswear self), G1844 (adjure), G3728 (oath), G3726 (adjure), G1845 (exorcist), G1965 (perjured person), G3727 (oath)\nVariants: ἐπίορκος \nHebrew Equivalents: H7650 שָׁבַע",
    1966: "ἐπιοῦσα (epioûsa | ep-ee-oo'-sah)\n\nDerivation: feminine singular participle of a comparative of G1909 and εἶμι (to go)\nStrong's: supervening, i.e. (G2250 or G3571 being expressed or implied) the ensuing day or night\nKJV: —following, next.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2250 \nSee: G3571 \n\nCognate Group: G1964 (forswear self), G1844 (adjure), G3728 (oath), G3726 (adjure), G1845 (exorcist), G1965 (perjured person), G3727 (oath)\nVariants: ἐπιοῦσα, ἔπειμι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1961 הָיָה",
    1967: "ἐπιούσιος (epioúsios | ep-ee-oo'-see-os)\n\nDerivation: perhaps from the same as G1966\nStrong's: tomorrow's; but more probably from G1909 and a derivative of the present participle feminine of G1510 ; for subsistence, i.e. needful\nKJV: —daily.\n\nSee: G1966 \nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1510 \n\nCognate Group: G1967 (daily)\nVariants: ἐπιούσιος",
    1968: "ἐπιπίπτω (epipíptō | ep-ee-pip'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4098\nStrong's: to embrace (with affection) or seize (with more or less violence; literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —fall into (on, upon) lie on, press upon.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4098 \n\nCognate Group: G1967 (daily)\nVariants: ἐπιπίπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1058 בָּכָה, H2505 חָלַק, H4448 מָלַל, H5307 נָפַל, H5956 עָלַם",
    1969: "ἐπιπλήσσω (epiplḗssō | ep-ee-place'-so)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4141\nStrong's: to chastise, i.e. (with words) to upbraid\nKJV: —rebuke.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4141 \n\nCognate Group: G1967 (daily)\nVariants: ἐπιπλήσσω",
    1970: "ἐπιπνίγω (epipnígō | ep-ee-pnee'-go)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4155\nStrong's: to throttle upon, i.e. (figuratively) overgrow\nKJV: —choke.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4155 \n\nCognate Group: G1967 (daily)\nVariants: ἐπιπνίγω",
    1971: "ἐπιποθέω (epipothéō | ep-ee-poth-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and potheo (to yearn)\nStrong's: to dote upon, i.e. intensely crave possession (lawfully or wrongfully)\nKJV: —(earnestly) desire (greatly), (greatly) long (after), lust.\n\nSee: G1909 \n\nCognate Group: G1967 (daily)\nVariants: ἐπιποθέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H707 אָרַג, H1638 גָּרַס, H1891 הָבַל, H2550 חָמַל, H2968 יָאַב, H3700 כָּסַף, H7369 רָחֵק, H8581 תַּעָב",
    1972: "ἐπιπόθησις (epipóthēsis | ep-ee-poth'-ay-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G1971\nStrong's: a longing for\nKJV: —earnest (vehement) desire.\n\nSee: G1971 \n\nCognate Group: G1967 (daily)\nVariants: ἐπιπόθησις",
    1973: "ἐπιπόθητος (epipóthētos | ep-ee-poth'-ay-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and a derivative of the latter part of G1971\nStrong's: yearned upon, i.e. greatly loved\nKJV: —longed for.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G1971 \n\nCognate Group: G1967 (daily)\nVariants: ἐπιπόθητος",
    1974: "ἐπιποθία (epipothía | ep-ee-poth-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1971\nStrong's: intense longing\nKJV: —great desire.\n\nSee: G1971 \n\nCognate Group: G1967 (daily)\nVariants: ἐπιποθία",
    1975: "ἐπιπορεύομαι (epiporeúomai | ep-ee-por-yoo'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4198\nStrong's: to journey further, i.e. travel on (reach)\nKJV: —come.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4198 \n\nCognate Group: G1967 (daily)\nVariants: ἐπιπορεύομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H309 אָחַר, H5674 עָבַר",
    1976: "ἐπιῤῥάπτω (epirrháptō | ep-ir-hrap'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and the base of G4476\nStrong's: to stitch upon, i.e. fasten with the needle\nKJV: —sew on.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4476 \n\nCognate Group: G1967 (daily)\nVariants: ἐπιῤῥάπτω, ἐπιράπτω, ἐπισυρράπτω, ἐπι(ρ)ράπτω, ἐπιρράπτω",
    1977: "ἐπιῤῥίπτω (epirrhíptō | ep-ir-hrip'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4496\nStrong's: to throw upon (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —cast upon.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4496 \n\nCognate Group: G4495 (cast off), G641 (cast), G1977 (cast upon), G4496 (cast)\nVariants: ἐπιῤῥίπτω, ἐπιρίπτω, ἐπι(ρ)ρίπτω, ἐπιρρίπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5307 נָפַל, H7993 שָׁלַךְ",
    1978: "ἐπίσημος (epísēmos | ep-is'-ay-mos)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and some form of the base of G4591\nStrong's: remarkable, i.e. (figuratively) eminent\nKJV: —notable, of note.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4591 \n\nCognate Group: G4593 (note), G4953 (token), G2154 (easy to be understood), G4591 (signify), G4592 (miracle), G1978 (notable), G767 (mean)\nVariants: ἐπίσημος \nHebrew Equivalents: H7194 קָשַׁר",
    1979: "ἐπισιτισμός (episitismós | ep-ee-sit-is-mos')\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1909 and a derivative of G4621\nStrong's: a provisioning, i.e. (concretely) food\nKJV: —victuals.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4621 \n\nCognate Group: G4593 (note), G4953 (token), G2154 (easy to be understood), G4591 (signify), G4592 (miracle), G1978 (notable), G767 (mean)\nVariants: ἐπισιτισμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H6720 צֵידָה",
    1980: "ἐπισκέπτομαι (episképtomai | ep-ee-skep'-tom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G1909 and the base of G4649\nStrong's: to inspect, i.e. (by implication) to select; by extension, to go to see, relieve\nKJV: —look out, visit.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4649 \n\nCognate Group: G1983 (look diligently), G244 (busybody in other men's matters), G1984 (the office of a), G1980 (look out)\nVariants: ἐπισκέπτομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H974 בָּחַן, H1239 בָּקַר, H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H1875 דָּרַשׁ, H3205 יָלַד, H5098 נָהַם, H5483 סוּס, H6485 פָּקַד, H8446 תּוּר",
    1981: "ἐπισκηνόω (episkēnóō | ep-ee-skay-no'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4637\nStrong's: to tent upon, i.e. (figuratively) abide with \nKJV: —rest upon.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4637 \n\nCognate Group: G2681 (lodge), G4638 (tabernacle), G4635 (tent-maker), G4637 (dwell), G4636 (tabernacle), G4633 (habitation), G1981 (rest upon), G4634 (tabernacles)\nVariants: ἐπισκηνόω",
    1982: "ἐπισκιάζω (episkiázō | ep-ee-skee-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and a derivative of G4639\nStrong's: to cast a shade upon, i.e. (by analogy) to envelop in a haze of brilliancy; figuratively, to invest with preternatural influence\nKJV: —overshadow.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4639 \n\nCognate Group: G644 (shadow), G4639 (shadow), G1982 (overshadow)\nVariants: ἐπισκιάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5526 סָכַךְ, H7931 שָׁכַן",
    1983: "ἐπισκοπέω (episkopéō | ep-ee-skop-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4648\nStrong's: to oversee; by implication, to beware\nKJV: —look diligently, take the oversight.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4648 \n\nCognate Group: G1983 (look diligently), G244 (busybody in other men's matters), G1984 (the office of a), G1980 (look out)\nVariants: ἐπισκοπέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1875 דָּרַשׁ, H3045 יָדַע, H5329 נָצַח, H6485 פָּקַד",
    1984: "ἐπισκοπή (episkopḗ | ep-is-kop-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G1980\nStrong's: inspection (for relief); by implication, superintendence; specially, the Christian \"episcopate\"\nKJV: —the office of a \"bishop\", bishoprick, visitation.\n\nSee: G1980 \n\nCognate Group: G1983 (look diligently), G244 (busybody in other men's matters), G1984 (the office of a), G1980 (look out)\nVariants: ἐπισκοπή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1244 בִּקֹּרֶת, H3374 יִרְאָה, H5475 סֹוד, H5532 סָכַן, H6485 פָּקַד, H6485 פָּקַד, H6486 פְּקֻדָּה, H6845 צָפַן, H7521 רָצָה",
    1985: "ἐπίσκοπος (epískopos | ep-is'-kop-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4649 (in the sense of G1983)\nStrong's: a superintendent, i.e. Christian officer in genitive case charge of a (or the) church (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —bishop, overseer.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4649 \nSee: G1983 \n\nCognate Group: G1983 (look diligently), G244 (busybody in other men's matters), G1984 (the office of a), G1980 (look out)\nVariants: ἐπίσκοπος \nHebrew Equivalents: H410 אֵל, H5065 נָגַשׂ, H6485 פָּקַד",
    1986: "ἐπισπάομαι (epispáomai | ep-ee-spah'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4685\nStrong's: to draw over, i.e. (with G203 implied) efface the mark of circumcision (by recovering with the foreskin)\nKJV: —become uncircumcised.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4685 \nSee: G203 \n\nCognate Group: G1983 (look diligently), G244 (busybody in other men's matters), G1984 (the office of a), G1980 (look out)\nVariants: ἐπισπάομαι, ἐπισπάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H4900 מָשַׁךְ, H7579 שָׁאַב, H8610 תָּפַשׂ",
    1987: "ἐπίσταμαι (epístamai | ep-is'-tam-ahee)\n\nDerivation: apparently a middle voice of G2186 (with G3563 implied)\nStrong's: to put the mind upon, i.e. comprehend, or be acquainted with\nKJV: —know, understand.\n\nSee: G2186 \nSee: G3563 \n\nCognate Group: G1983 (look diligently), G244 (busybody in other men's matters), G1984 (the office of a), G1980 (look out)\nVariants: ἐπίσταμαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H995 בִּין, H3045 יָדַע, H5341 נָצַר, H7919 שָׂכַל",
    1988: "ἐπιστάτης (epistátēs | ep-is-tat'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and a presumed derivative of G2476\nStrong's: an appointee over, i.e. commander (teacher)\nKJV: —master.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2476 \n\nCognate Group: G1988 (master)\nVariants: ἐπιστάτης \nHebrew Equivalents: H5057 נָגִיד, H5065 נָגַשׂ, H5329 נָצַח, H6496 פָּקִיד, H7287 רָדָה, H8269 שַׂר",
    1989: "ἐπιστέλλω (epistéllō | ep-ee-stel'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4724\nStrong's: to enjoin (by writing), i.e. (genitive case) to communicate by letter (for any purpose)\nKJV: —write (a letter, unto).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4724 \n\nCognate Group: G5288 (draw back), G1291 (charge), G4958 (short), G2689 (apparel), G2687 (appease), G1992 (\"epistle), G1989 (write), G5289 (draw back), G1293 (difference), G4724 (avoid)\nVariants: ἐπιστέλλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7971 שָׁלַח",
    1990: "ἐπιστήμων (epistḗmōn | ep-ee-stay'-mone)\n\nDerivation: from G1987\nStrong's: intelligent\nKJV: —endued with knowledge.\n\nSee: G1987 \n\nCognate Group: G5288 (draw back), G1291 (charge), G4958 (short), G2689 (apparel), G2687 (appease), G1992 (\"epistle), G1989 (write), G5289 (draw back), G1293 (difference), G4724 (avoid)\nVariants: ἐπιστήμων \nHebrew Equivalents: H995 בִּין, H3045 יָדַע, H7919 שָׂכַל",
    1991: "ἐπιστηρίζω (epistērízō | ep-ee-stay-rid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4741\nStrong's: to support further, i.e. reestablish\nKJV: —confirm, strengthen.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4741 \n\nCognate Group: G4740 (stedfastness), G4741 (fix), G793 (unstable), G1991 (confirm)\nVariants: ἐπιστηρίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3289 יָעַץ, H3559 כּוּן, H5181 נָחַת, H5324 נָצַב, H5564 סָמַךְ, H7514 רָפַק, H8172 שָׁעַן",
    1992: "ἐπιστολή (epistolḗ | ep-is-tol-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G1989\nStrong's: a written message\nKJV: —\"epistle,\" letter.\n\nSee: G1989 \n\nCognate Group: G5288 (draw back), G1291 (charge), G4958 (short), G2689 (apparel), G2687 (appease), G1992 (\"epistle), G1989 (write), G5289 (draw back), G1293 (difference), G4724 (avoid)\nVariants: ἐπιστολή \nHebrew Equivalents: H104 אִגְּרָא, H107 אִגֶּרֶת, H3627 כְּלִי, H3791 כָּתָב, H5612 סֵפֶר, H7855 שִׂטְנָה",
    1993: "ἐπιστομίζω (epistomízō | ep-ee-stom-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4750\nStrong's: to put something over the mouth, i.e. (figuratively) to silence\nKJV: —stop mouths.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4750 \n\nCognate Group: G5288 (draw back), G1291 (charge), G4958 (short), G2689 (apparel), G2687 (appease), G1992 (\"epistle), G1989 (write), G5289 (draw back), G1293 (difference), G4724 (avoid)\nVariants: ἐπιστομίζω",
    1994: "ἐπιστρέφω (epistréphō | ep-ee-stref'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4762\nStrong's: to revert (literally, figuratively or morally)\nKJV: —come (go) again, convert, (re-)turn (about, again).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4762 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἐπιστρέφω \nHebrew Equivalents: H622 אָסַף, H935 בֹּוא, H974 בָּחַן, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2015 הָפַךְ, H2803 חָשַׁב, H3665 כָּנַע, H5027 נָבַט, H5066 נָגַשׁ, H5307 נָפַל, H5381 נָשַׂג, H5437 סָבַב, H5472 סוּג, H5493 סוּר, H5800 עָזַב, H6437 פָּנָה, H7725 שׁוּב, H7760 שׂוּם, H7971 שָׁלַח, H8085 שָׁמַע, H8210 שָׁפַךְ",
    1995: "ἐπιστροφή (epistrophḗ | ep-is-trof-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G1994\nStrong's: reversion, i.e. morally, revolution\nKJV: —conversion.\n\nSee: G1994 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἐπιστροφή \nHebrew Equivalents: H4941 מִשְׁפָּט, H7725 שׁוּב, H8669 תְּשׁוּקָה",
    1996: "ἐπισυνάγω (episynágō | ep-ee-soon-ag'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4863\nStrong's: to collect upon the same place\nKJV: —gather (together).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4863 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἐπισυνάγω",
    1997: "ἐπισυναγωγή (episynagōgḗ | ep-ee-soon-ag-o-gay')\n\nDerivation: from G1996\nStrong's: a complete collection; especially a Christian meeting (for worship)\nKJV: —assembling (gathering) together.\n\nSee: G1996 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἐπισυναγωγή",
    1998: "ἐπισυντρέχω (episyntréchō | ep-ee-soon-trekh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4936\nStrong's: to hasten together upon one place (or a particular occasion)\nKJV: —come running together.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4936 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἐπισυντρέχω",
    1999: "ἐπισύστασις (episýstasis | ep-ee-soo'-stas-is)\n\nDerivation: from the middle voice of a compound of G1909 and G4921\nStrong's: a conspiracy, i.e. concourse (riotous or friendly)\nKJV: —that which cometh upon, + raising up.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4921 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἐπισύστασις, ἐπίστασις \nHebrew Equivalents: H5327 נָצָה, H5712 עֵדָה",
    2000: "ἐπισφαλής (episphalḗs | ep-ee-sfal-ace')\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1909 and σφάλλω (to trip)\nStrong's: figuratively, insecure\nKJV: —dangerous.\n\nSee: G1909 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἐπισφαλής",
    2001: "ἐπισχύω (epischýō | ep-is-khoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2480\nStrong's: to avail further, i.e. (figuratively) insist stoutly\nKJV: —be the more fierce.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2480 \n\nCognate Group: G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)\nVariants: ἐπισχύω",
    2002: "ἐπισωρεύω (episōreúō | ep-ee-so-ryoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G4987\nStrong's: to accumulate further, i.e. (figuratively) seek additionally\nKJV: —heap.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G4987 \n\nCognate Group: G2002 (heap), G4987 (heap)\nVariants: ἐπισωρεύω",
    2003: "ἐπιταγή (epitagḗ | ep-ee-tag-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G2004\nStrong's: an injunction or decree; by implication, authoritativeness\nKJV: —authority, commandment.\n\nSee: G2004 \n\nCognate Group: G2002 (heap), G4987 (heap)\nVariants: ἐπιταγή \nHebrew Equivalents: H6600 פִּתְגָּם",
    2004: "ἐπιτάσσω (epitássō | ep-ee-tas'-so)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G5021\nStrong's: to arrange upon, i.e. order\nKJV: —charge, command, injoin.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5021 \n\nCognate Group: G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)\nVariants: ἐπιτάσσω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H1314 בֶּשֶׂם, H3245 יָסַד, H5414 נָתַן, H6680 צָוָה, H6965 קוּם, H7560 רְשַׁם",
    2005: "ἐπιτελέω (epiteléō | ep-ee-tel-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G5055\nStrong's: to fulfill further (or completely), i.e. execute; by implication, to terminate, undergo\nKJV: —accomplish, do, finish, (make) (perfect), perform(X -ance).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5055 \n\nCognate Group: G5047 (perfection), G5046 (of full age), G5056 (+ continual), G5051 (finisher), G2005 (accomplish), G5052 (bring fruit to perfection), G4930 (end), G3838 (+ in wise), G4931 (end), G5050 (perfection), G5048 (consecrate), G5055 (accomplish), G5049 (to the end)\nVariants: ἐπιτελέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1214 בָּצַע, H1765 דָּחַף, H2164 זְמַן, H3615 כָּלָה, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6466 פָּעַל, H6999 קָטַר",
    2006: "ἐπιτήδειος (epitḗdeios | ep-ee-tay'-di-os)\n\nDerivation: from ἐπιτηδές (enough)\nStrong's: serviceable, i.e. (by implication) requisite\nKJV: —things which are needful.\n\nCognate Group: G5047 (perfection), G5046 (of full age), G5056 (+ continual), G5051 (finisher), G2005 (accomplish), G5052 (bring fruit to perfection), G4930 (end), G3838 (+ in wise), G4931 (end), G5050 (perfection), G5048 (consecrate), G5055 (accomplish), G5049 (to the end)\nVariants: ἐπιτήδειος",
    2007: "ἐπιτίθημι (epitíthēmi | ep-ee-tith'-ay-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G5087\nStrong's: to impose (in a friendly or hostile sense)\nKJV: —add unto, lade, lay upon, put (up) on, set on (up), + surname, X wound.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5087 \n\nCognate Group: G3866 (committed unto), G3908 (allege), G3331 (change), G4286 (purpose), G114 (cast off), G5087 (+ advise), G2007 (add unto), G4388 (purpose), G115 (disannulling), G4369 (add), G3346 (carry over), G1936 (laying on)\nVariants: ἐπιτίθημι \nHebrew Equivalents: H247 אָזַר, H935 בֹּוא, H1481 גּוּר, H2102 זוּד, H2161 זָמַם, H3034 יָדָה, H3332 יָצַק, H3369 יָקֹשׁ, H3947 לָקַח, H5108 נֹוב, H5117 נוּחַ, H5130 נוּף, H5234 נָכַר, H5307 נָפַל, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5414 נָתַן, H5437 סָבַב, H5564 סָמַךְ, H5689 עֲגַב, H5927 עָלָה, H6006 עָמַס, H6186 עָרַךְ, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6485 פָּקַד, H6584 פָּשַׁט, H6999 קָטַר, H7194 קָשַׁר, H7311 רוּם, H7392 רָכַב, H7401 רָכַךְ, H7737 שָׁוָה, H7751 שׁוּט, H7760 שׂוּם, H7760 שׂוּם, H7843 שָׁחַת, H7896 שִׁית, H7971 שָׁלַח",
    2008: "ἐπιτιμάω (epitimáō | ep-ee-tee-mah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G5091\nStrong's: to tax upon, i.e. censure or admonish; by implication, forbid\nKJV: —(straitly) charge, rebuke.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5091 \n\nCognate Group: G2009 (punishment), G2008 (charge)\nVariants: ἐπιτιμάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1605 גָּעַר",
    2009: "ἐπιτιμία (epitimía | ep-ee-tee-mee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1909 and G5092\nStrong's: properly, esteem, i.e. citizenship; used (in the sense of G2008) of a penalty\nKJV: —punishment.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5092 \nSee: G2008 \n\nCognate Group: G2009 (punishment), G2008 (charge)\nVariants: ἐπιτιμία",
    2010: "ἐπιτρέπω (epitrépō | ep-ee-trep'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and the base of G5157\nStrong's: to turn over (transfer), i.e. allow\nKJV: —give leave (liberty, license), let, permit, suffer.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5157 \n\nCognate Group: G2009 (punishment), G2008 (charge)\nVariants: ἐπιτρέπω, συγχωρέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H5800 עָזַב, H6186 עָרַךְ",
    2011: "ἐπιτροπή (epitropḗ | ep-ee-trop-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G2010\nStrong's: permission, i.e. (by implication) full power\nKJV: —commission.\n\nSee: G2010 \n\nCognate Group: G2009 (punishment), G2008 (charge)\nVariants: ἐπιτροπή",
    2012: "ἐπίτροπος (epítropos | ep-it'-rop-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G5158 (in the sense of G2011)\nStrong's: a commissioner, i.e. domestic manager, guardian\nKJV: —steward, tutor.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5158 \nSee: G2011 \n\nCognate Group: G2009 (punishment), G2008 (charge)\nVariants: ἐπίτροπος",
    2013: "ἐπιτυγχάνω (epitynchánō | ep-ee-toong-khan'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G5177\nStrong's: to chance upon, i.e. (by implication) to attain\nKJV: —obtain.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5177 \n\nCognate Group: G2009 (punishment), G2008 (charge)\nVariants: ἐπιτυγχάνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2760 חָרַךְ, H6743 צָלַח",
    2014: "ἐπιφαίνω (epiphaínō | ep-ee-fah'-ee-no)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G5316\nStrong's: to shine upon, i.e. become (literally) visible or (figuratively) known\nKJV: —appear, give light.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5316 \n\nCognate Group: G5319 (appear), G5325 (pomp), G5320 (evidently), G5322 (lantern), G2015 (appearing), G5321 (manifestation), G5326 (spirit), G5316 (appear), G2014 (appear), G1718 (appear), G5324 (sight), G5318 (abroad), G2016 (notable)\nVariants: ἐπιφαίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1540 גָּלָה, H2224 זָרַח, H3372 יָרֵא, H4672 מָצָא, H5782 עוּר, H6437 פָּנָה",
    2015: "ἐπιφάνεια (epipháneia | ep-if-an'-i-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2016\nStrong's: a manifestation, i.e. (specially) the advent of Christ (past or future)\nKJV: —appearing, brightness.\n\nSee: G2016 \n\nCognate Group: G5319 (appear), G5325 (pomp), G5320 (evidently), G5322 (lantern), G2015 (appearing), G5321 (manifestation), G5326 (spirit), G5316 (appear), G2014 (appear), G1718 (appear), G5324 (sight), G5318 (abroad), G2016 (notable)\nVariants: ἐπιφάνεια \nHebrew Equivalents: H3372 יָרֵא",
    2016: "ἐπιφανής (epiphanḗs | ep-if-an-ace')\n\nDerivation: from G2014\nStrong's: conspicuous, i.e. (figuratively) memorable\nKJV: —notable.\n\nSee: G2014 \n\nCognate Group: G5319 (appear), G5325 (pomp), G5320 (evidently), G5322 (lantern), G2015 (appearing), G5321 (manifestation), G5326 (spirit), G5316 (appear), G2014 (appear), G1718 (appear), G5324 (sight), G5318 (abroad), G2016 (notable)\nVariants: ἐπιφανής \nHebrew Equivalents: H3372 יָרֵא, H7200 רָאָה",
    2017: "ἐπιφαύω (epiphaúō | ep-ee-fow'-o)\n\nDerivation: a form of G2014\nStrong's: to illuminate (figuratively)\nKJV: —give light.\n\nSee: G2014 \n\nCognate Group: G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)\nVariants: ἐπιφαύω, ἐπιφαύσκω, ἐπιψαύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H167 אָהַל, H1984 הָלַל",
    2018: "ἐπιφέρω (epiphérō | ep-ee-fer'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G5342\nStrong's: to bear upon (or further), i.e. adduce (personally or judicially (accuse, inflict)), superinduce\nKJV: —add, bring (against), take.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5342 \n\nCognate Group: G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)\nVariants: ἐπιφέρω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1980 הָלַךְ, H5130 נוּף, H7335 רָזַם, H7369 רָחֵק, H7725 שׁוּב, H7971 שָׁלַח",
    2019: "ἐπιφωνέω (epiphōnéō | ep-ee-fo-neh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G5455\nStrong's: to call at something, i.e. exclaim\nKJV: —cry (against), give a shout.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5455 \n\nCognate Group: G4859 (consent), G2019 (cry), G4857 (concord), G4858 (music), G4856 (agree together), G5455 (call), G5456 (noise)\nVariants: ἐπιφωνέω, καταφωνέω",
    2020: "ἐπιφώσκω (epiphṓskō | ep-ee-foce'-ko)\n\nDerivation: a form of G2017\nStrong's: to begin to grow light\nKJV: —begin to dawn, X draw on.\n\nSee: G2017 \n\nCognate Group: G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)\nVariants: ἐπιφώσκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1984 הָלַל",
    2021: "ἐπιχειρέω (epicheiréō | ep-ee-khi-reh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G5495\nStrong's: to put the hand upon, i.e. undertake\nKJV: —go about, take in hand (upon).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5495 \n\nCognate Group: G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)\nVariants: ἐπιχειρέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1580 גָּמַל, H2803 חָשַׁב",
    2022: "ἐπιχέω (epichéō | ep-ee-kheh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and χέω (to pour)\nStrong's: \nKJV: —to pour upon:—pour in.\n\nSee: G1909 \n\nCognate Group: G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)\nVariants: ἐπιχέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2212 זָקַק, H3332 יָצַק, H5414 נָתַן, H7324 רוּק, H7760 שׂוּם",
    2023: "ἐπιχορηγέω (epichorēgéō | ep-ee-khor-ayg-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G5524\nStrong's: to furnish besides, i.e. fully supply, (figuratively) aid or contribute\nKJV: —add, minister (nourishment, unto).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5524 \n\nCognate Group: G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)\nVariants: ἐπιχορηγέω",
    2024: "ἐπιχορηγία (epichorēgía | ep-ee-khor-ayg-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2023\nStrong's: contribution\nKJV: —supply.\n\nSee: G2023 \n\nCognate Group: G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)\nVariants: ἐπιχορηγία",
    2025: "ἐπιχρίω (epichríō | ep-ee-khree'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G5548\nStrong's: to smear over\nKJV: —anoint.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G5548 \n\nCognate Group: G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)\nVariants: ἐπιχρίω",
    2026: "ἐποικοδομέω (epoikodoméō | ep-oy-kod-om-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G3618\nStrong's: to build upon, i.e. (figuratively) to rear up\nKJV: —build thereon (thereupon, on, upon).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3618 \n\nCognate Group: G3618 (build), G2733 (habitation), G3614 (home), G3617 (goodman), G3619 (building), G3616 (guide the house), G2731 (dwelling), G3622 (dispensation), G3615 (they of household), G3613 (habitation), G4925 (build together), G2732 (habitation), G3624 (home), G3611 (dwell), G3620 (edifying), G3621 (be steward), G2026 (build thereon), G3609 (of the house), G3623 (chamberlain)\nVariants: ἐποικοδομέω",
    2027: "ἐποκέλλω (epokéllō | ep-ok-el'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and ὀκέλλω (to urge)\nStrong's: to drive upon the shore, i.e. to beach a vessel\nKJV: —run aground.\n\nSee: G1909 \n\nCognate Group: G3618 (build), G2733 (habitation), G3614 (home), G3617 (goodman), G3619 (building), G3616 (guide the house), G2731 (dwelling), G3622 (dispensation), G3615 (they of household), G3613 (habitation), G4925 (build together), G2732 (habitation), G3624 (home), G3611 (dwell), G3620 (edifying), G3621 (be steward), G2026 (build thereon), G3609 (of the house), G3623 (chamberlain)\nVariants: ἐποκέλλω, ἐπικέλλω",
    2028: "ἐπονομάζω (eponomázō | ep-on-om-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G3687\nStrong's: to name further, i.e. denominate\nKJV: —call.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3687 \n\nCognate Group: G5581 (falsely so called), G3686 (called), G3687 (call), G2028 (call)\nVariants: ἐπονομάζω, ἐπονομάζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2142 זָכַר, H5344 נָקַב, H7121 קָרָא, H7121 קָרָא, H7760 שׂוּם",
    2029: "ἐποπτεύω (epopteúō | ep-opt-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and a derivative of G3700\nStrong's: to inspect, i.e. watch\nKJV: —behold.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3700 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: ἐποπτεύω",
    2030: "ἐπόπτης (epóptēs | ep-op'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and a presumed derivative of G3700\nStrong's: a looker-on\nKJV: —eye-witness.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3700 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: ἐπόπτης",
    2031: "ἔπος (épos | ep'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2036\nStrong's: a word\nKJV: —X say.\n\nSee: G2036 \n\nCognate Group: G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)\nVariants: ἔπος",
    2032: "ἐπουράνιος (epouránios | ep-oo-ran'-ee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G3772\nStrong's: above the sky\nKJV: —celestial, (in) heaven(-ly), high.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G3772 \n\nCognate Group: G2032 (celestial), G3771 (from heaven), G3772 (air), G3770 (heavenly)\nVariants: ἐπουράνιος \nHebrew Equivalents: H7706 שַׁדַּי, H8064 שָׁמַיִם",
    2033: "ἑπτά (heptá | hep-tah')\n\nDerivation: a primary number\nStrong's: seven\nKJV: —seven.\n\nCognate Group: G2035 (seven thousand), G2033 (seven), G2034 (seven times)\nVariants: ἑπτά",
    2034: "ἑπτάκις (heptákis | hep-tak-is')\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2033\nStrong's: seven times\nKJV: —seven times.\n\nSee: G2033 \n\nCognate Group: G2035 (seven thousand), G2033 (seven), G2034 (seven times)\nVariants: ἑπτάκις",
    2035: "ἑπτακισχίλιοι (heptakischílioi | hep-tak-is-khil'-ee-oy)\n\nDerivation: from G2034 and G5507\nStrong's: seven times a thousand\nKJV: —seven thousand.\n\nSee: G2034 \nSee: G5507 \n\nCognate Group: G2035 (seven thousand), G2033 (seven), G2034 (seven times)\nVariants: ἑπτακισχίλιοι",
    2036: "ἔπω (épō | ep'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb (used only in the definite past tense, the others being borrowed from G2046, G4483, and G5346)\nStrong's: to speak or say (by word or writing)\nKJV: —answer, bid, bring word, call, command, grant, say (on), speak, tell. Compare G3004 .\n\nSee: G2046 \nSee: G4483 \nSee: G5346 \nSee: G3004 \n\nCognate Group: G2035 (seven thousand), G2033 (seven), G2034 (seven times)\nVariants: ἔπω, λέγω",
    2037: "Ἔραστος (Érastos | er'-as-tos)\n\nDerivation: from ἐράω (to love)\nStrong's: beloved; Erastus, a Christian\nKJV: —Erastus.\n\nCognate Group: G2035 (seven thousand), G2033 (seven), G2034 (seven times)\nVariants: Ἔραστος",
    2038: "ἐργάζομαι (ergázomai | er-gad'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G2041\nStrong's: to toil (as a task, occupation, etc.), (by implication) effect, be engaged in or with, etc.\nKJV: —commit, do, labor for, minister about, trade (by), work.\n\nSee: G2041 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: ἐργάζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H707 אָרַג, H898 בָּגַד, H1580 גָּמַל, H2404 חָטַב, H3953 לָקַשׁ, H4399 מְלָאכָה, H5503 סָחַר, H5647 עָבַד, H5647 עָבַד, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6219 עָשֹׁות, H6466 פָּעַל, H7702 שָׂדַד, H8356 שָׁתָה",
    2039: "ἐργασία (ergasía | er-gas-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2040\nStrong's: occupation; by implication, profit, pains\nKJV: —craft, diligence, gain, work.\n\nSee: G2040 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: ἐργασία \nHebrew Equivalents: H4399 מְלָאכָה, H4639 מַעֲשֶׂה, H5650 עֶבֶד, H5656 עֲבֹדָה, H6100 עֶצְיֹון גֶּבֶר, H6467 פֹּעַל",
    2040: "ἐργάτης (ergátēs | er-gat'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G2041\nStrong's: a toiler; figuratively, a teacher\nKJV: —labourer, worker(-men).\n\nSee: G2041 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: ἐργάτης",
    2041: "ἔργον (érgon | er'-gon)\n\nDerivation: from a primary (but obsolete) ἔργω (to work)\nStrong's: toil (as an effort or occupation); by implication, an act\nKJV: —deed, doing, labour, work.\n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: ἔργον \nHebrew Equivalents: H734 אֹרַח, H1576 גְּמוּל, H1697 דָּבָר, H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H2706 חֹק, H3018 יְגִיעַ, H3627 כְּלִי, H3948 לֶקַח, H4193 מֹות, H4390 מָלֵא, H4399 מְלָאכָה, H4522 מַס, H4853 מַשָּׂא, H4916 מִשְׁלֹוחַ, H5450 סְבָלָה, H5647 עָבַד, H5647 עָבַד, H5656 עֲבֹדָה, H5656 עֲבֹדָה, H5949 עֲלִילָה, H6098 עֵצָה, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6466 פָּעַל, H6467 פֹּעַל, H6486 פְּקֻדָּה, H7200 רָאָה, H8441 תֹּועֵבַה, H8457 תַּזְנוּת",
    2042: "ἐρεθίζω (erethízō | er-eth-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from a presumed prolonged form of G2054\nStrong's: to stimulate (especially to anger)\nKJV: —provoke.\n\nSee: G2054 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: ἐρεθίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1624 גָּרָה, H4784 מָרָה, H5643 סֵתֶר, H7291 רָדַף",
    2043: "ἐρείδω (ereídō | er-i'-do)\n\nDerivation: of obscure affinity\nStrong's: to prop, i.e. (reflexively) get fast\nKJV: —stick fast.\n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: ἐρείδω \nHebrew Equivalents: H553 אָמַץ, H7725 שׁוּב, H8104 שָׁמַר, H8551 תָּמַךְ, H8610 תָּפַשׂ",
    2044: "ἐρεύγομαι (ereúgomai | er-yoog'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: to belch, i.e. (figuratively) to speak out\nKJV: —utter.\n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: ἐρεύγομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H5042 נָבַע, H7580 שָׁאַג, H8318 שֶׁרֶץ",
    2045: "ἐρευνάω (ereunáō | er-yoo-nah'-o)\n\nDerivation: apparently from G2046 (through the idea of inquiry)\nStrong's: to seek, i.e. (figuratively) to investigate\nKJV: —search.\n\nSee: G2046 \n\nCognate Group: G1830 (search diligently), G2045 (search)\nVariants: ἐρευνάω, ἐραυνάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H2664 חָפַשׂ, H2664 חָפַשׂ, H2710 חָקַק, H2713 חָקַר, H2713 חָקַר, H2834 חָשַׂף, H2834 חָשַׂף, H4959 מָשַׁשׁ, H5341 נָצַר, H5367 נָקַשׁ, H5549 סָלַל, H7592 שָׁאַל, H7592 שָׁאַל",
    2046: "ἐρέω (eréō | er-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: probably a fuller form of G4483\nStrong's: an alternate for G2036 in certain tenses; to utter, i.e. speak or say\nKJV: —call, say, speak (of), tell.\n\nSee: G4483 \nSee: G2036 \n\nCognate Group: G1830 (search diligently), G2045 (search)\nVariants: ἐρέω, λέγω",
    2047: "ἐρημία (erēmía | er-ay-mee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2048\nStrong's: solitude (concretely)\nKJV: —desert, wilderness.\n\nSee: G2048 \n\nCognate Group: G2049 (desolate), G2050 (desolation), G2047 (desert), G2048 (desert)\nVariants: ἐρημία \nHebrew Equivalents: H2717 חָרַב, H2723 חׇרְבָּה, H8077 שְׁמָמָה",
    2048: "ἔρημος (érēmos | er'-ay-mos)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity; lonesome, i.e. (by implication) waste (usually as a noun, G5561 being implied)\nKJV: —desert, desolate, solitary, wilderness.\n\nSee: G5561 \n\nCognate Group: G2049 (desolate), G2050 (desolation), G2047 (desert), G2048 (desert)\nVariants: ἔρημος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1116 בָּמָה, H2717 חָרַב, H3452 יְשִׁימֹון, H3582 כָּחַד, H4057 מִדְבָּר, H4057 מִדְבָּר, H4180 מֹורָשׁ, H4923 מְשַׁמָּה, H5045 נֶגֶב, H6160 עֲרָבָה, H6723 צִיָּה, H8074 שָׁמֵם, H8414 תֹּהוּ",
    2049: "ἐρημόω (erēmóō | er-ay-mo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2048\nStrong's: to lay waste (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —(bring to, make) desolate(-ion), come to nought.\n\nSee: G2048 \n\nCognate Group: G2049 (desolate), G2050 (desolation), G2047 (desert), G2048 (desert)\nVariants: ἐρημόω, ἐρημόομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1110 בָּלַק, H2717 חָרַב, H2763 חָרַם, H3456 יָשַׁם, H4057 מִדְבָּר, H7665 שָׁבַר, H7993 שָׁלַךְ, H8045 שָׁמַד, H8074 שָׁמֵם, H8159 שָׁעָה",
    2050: "ἐρήμωσις (erḗmōsis | er-ay'-mo-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G2049\nStrong's: despoliation\nKJV: —desolation.\n\nSee: G2049 \n\nCognate Group: G2049 (desolate), G2050 (desolation), G2047 (desert), G2048 (desert)\nVariants: ἐρήμωσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H2723 חׇרְבָּה, H8074 שָׁמֵם",
    2051: "ἐρίζω (erízō | er-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2054\nStrong's: to wrangle\nKJV: —strive.\n\nSee: G2054 \n\nCognate Group: G2049 (desolate), G2050 (desolation), G2047 (desert), G2048 (desert)\nVariants: ἐρίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1624 גָּרָה, H4784 מָרָה",
    2052: "ἐριθεία (eritheía | er-ith-i'-ah)\n\nDerivation: perhaps as the same as G2042\nStrong's: properly, intrigue, i.e. (by implication) faction\nKJV: —contention(-ious), strife.\n\nSee: G2042 \n\nCognate Group: G2052 (contention)\nVariants: ἐριθεία",
    2053: "ἔριον (érion | er'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: of obscure affinity\nStrong's: wool\nKJV: —wool.\n\nCognate Group: G2052 (contention)\nVariants: ἔριον \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H6785 צֶמֶר",
    2054: "ἔρις (éris | er'-is)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a quarrel, i.e. (by implication) wrangling\nKJV: —contention, debate, strife, variance.\n\nCognate Group: G2052 (contention)\nVariants: ἔρις",
    2055: "ἐρίφιον (eríphion | er-if'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: from G2056\nStrong's: a kidling, i.e. (genitive case) goat (symbolically, wicked person)\nKJV: —goat.\n\nSee: G2056 \n\nCognate Group: G2052 (contention)\nVariants: ἐρίφιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1423 גְּדִי, H3733 כַּר, H5795 עֵז, H6260 עַתּוּד, H8163 שָׂעִיר",
    2056: "ἔριφος (ériphos | er'-if-os)\n\nDerivation: perhaps from the same as G2053 (through the idea of hairiness)\nStrong's: a kid or (genitive case) goat\nKJV: —goat, kid.\n\nSee: G2053 \n\nCognate Group: G2052 (contention)\nVariants: ἔριφος, αἴξ \nHebrew Equivalents: H1423 גְּדִי, H3733 כַּר, H5795 עֵז, H6260 עַתּוּד, H8163 שָׂעִיר",
    2057: "Ἑρμᾶς (Hermâs | her-mas')\n\nDerivation: probably from G2060\nStrong's: Hermas, a Christian\nKJV: —Hermas.\n\nSee: G2060 \n\nCognate Group: G2052 (contention)\nVariants: Ἑρμᾶς",
    2058: "ἑρμηνεία (hermēneía | her-may-ni'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2059\nStrong's: translation\nKJV: —interpretation.\n\nSee: G2059 \n\nCognate Group: G1329 (expound), G2059 (interpret), G2058 (interpretation), G1328 (interpreter)\nVariants: ἑρμηνεία, διερμηνεία",
    2059: "ἑρμηνεύω (hermēneúō | her-mayn-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a presumed derivative of G2060 (as the god of language)\nStrong's: to translate\nKJV: —interpret.\n\nSee: G2060 \n\nCognate Group: G1329 (expound), G2059 (interpret), G2058 (interpretation), G1328 (interpreter)\nVariants: ἑρμηνεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3887 לוּץ, H8638 תִּרְגַּם",
    2060: "Ἑρμῆς (Hermēs | her-mace')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from G2046\nStrong's: Hermes, the name of the messenger of the Greek deities; also of a Christian\nKJV: —Hermes, Mercury.\n\nSee: G2046 \n\nCognate Group: G1329 (expound), G2059 (interpret), G2058 (interpretation), G1328 (interpreter)\nVariants: Ἑρμῆς",
    2061: "Ἑρμογένης (Hermogénēs | her-mog-en'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G2060 and G1096\nStrong's: born of Hermes; Hermogenes, an apostate Christian\nKJV: —Hermogenes.\n\nSee: G2060 \nSee: G1096 \n\nCognate Group: G1329 (expound), G2059 (interpret), G2058 (interpretation), G1328 (interpreter)\nVariants: Ἑρμογένης",
    2062: "ἑρπετόν (herpetón | her-pet-on')\n\nDerivation: neuter of a derivative of ἕρπω (to creep)\nStrong's: a reptile, i.e. (by Hebraism (compare H7431)) a small animal\nKJV: —creeping thing, serpent.\nSee: H7431\n\nCognate Group: G1329 (expound), G2059 (interpret), G2058 (interpretation), G1328 (interpreter)\nVariants: ἑρπετόν \nHebrew Equivalents: H2416 חַי, H3733 כַּר, H7429 רָמַס, H8318 שֶׁרֶץ",
    2063: "ἐρυθρός (erythrós | er-oo-thros')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity; red, i.e. (with G2281) the Red Sea\nKJV: —red.\n\nSee: G2281 \n\nCognate Group: G1329 (expound), G2059 (interpret), G2058 (interpretation), G1328 (interpreter)\nVariants: ἐρυθρός, Ἐρυθρός \nHebrew Equivalents: H123 אֱדֹם, H5486 סוּף",
    2064: "ἔρχομαι (érchomai | er'-khom-ahee)\n\n\nDerivation: middle voice of a primary verb (used only in the present and imperfect tenses, the others being supplied by a kindred (middle voice) ἐλεύθομαι (eleúthomai | el-yoo'-thom-ahee), or (active) ἔλθω (élthō | el'-tho)\n, which do not otherwise occur)\nStrong's: to come or go (in a great variety of applications, literally and figuratively)\nKJV: —accompany, appear, bring, come, enter, fall out, go, grow, X light, X next, pass, resort, be set.\n\nCognate Group: G1330 (come), G565 (come), G1525 (X arise), G4905 (accompany), G4281 (go before), G4022 (fetch a compass), G2064 (accompany), G1904 (come), G4334 (come), G1831 (come), G3928 (come), G3922 (come in privily)\nVariants: ἔρχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H235 אָזַל, H270 אָחַז, H734 אֹרַח, H935 בֹּוא, H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H1961 הָיָה, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2009 הִנֵּה, H2270 חָבֵר, H2490 חָלַל, H2976 יָאַשׁ, H3254 יָסַף, H3313 יָפַע, H3318 יָצָא, H3381 יָרַד, H3427 יָשַׁב, H3947 לָקַח, H4135 מוּל, H4853 מַשָּׂא, H5048 נֶגֶד, H5074 נָדַד, H5307 נָפַל, H5324 נָצַב, H5377 נָשָׁא, H5674 עָבַר, H5710 עָדָה, H5753 עָוָה, H5844 עָטָה, H5927 עָלָה, H5953 עָלַל, H6168 עָרָה, H6293 פָּגַע, H6908 קָבַץ, H7126 קָרַב, H7725 שׁוּב",
    2065: "ἐρωτάω (erōtáō | er-o-tah'-o)\n\nDerivation: apparently from G2046 (compare G2045)\nStrong's: to interrogate; by implication, to request\nKJV: —ask, beseech, desire, intreat, pray. Compare G4441 .\n\nSee: G2046 \nSee: G2045 \nSee: G4441 \n\nCognate Group: G1906 (answer), G1905 (ask), G2065 (ask)\nVariants: ἐρωτάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H2713 חָקַר, H7592 שָׁאַל",
    2066: "ἐσθής (esthḗs | es-thace')\n\nDerivation: from ἕννυμι (to clothe)\nStrong's: dress\nKJV: —apparel, clothing, raiment, robe.\n\nCognate Group: G2066 (apparel)\nVariants: ἐσθής",
    2067: "ἔσθησις (ésthēsis | es'-thay-sis)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2066\nStrong's: clothing (concretely)\nKJV: —government.\n\nSee: G2066 \n\nCognate Group: G2066 (apparel)\nVariants: ἔσθησις",
    2068: "ἐσθίω (esthíō | es-thee'-o)\n\nDerivation: strengthened for a primary ἔδω (to eat)\nStrong's: used only in certain tenses, the rest being supplied by G5315 ; to eat (usually literal)\nKJV: —devour, eat, live.\n\nSee: G5315 \n\nCognate Group: G2068 (devour)\nVariants: ἐσθίω, ἔσθω, ἐσθίω/ἔσθω \nHebrew Equivalents: H398 אָכַל, H1262 בָּרָה, H3243 יָנַק, H5307 נָפַל, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5582 סָעַד, H8082 שָׁמֵן",
    2069: "Ἐσλί (Eslí | es-lee')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (probably for H454)\nStrong's: Esli, an Israelite\nKJV: —Esli.\nSee: H454\n\nCognate Group: G2068 (devour)\nVariants: Ἐσλί, Ἑσλί \nHebrew Equivalents: H454 אֶלְיְהֹועֵינַי",
    2070: "ἐσμέν (esmén | es-men')\n\nDerivation: first person plural indicative of G1510\nStrong's: we are\nKJV: —are, be, have our being, X have hope, + (the gospel) was (preached unto) us.\n\nSee: G1510 \n\nCognate Group: G2068 (devour)\nVariants: ἐσμέν, εἰμί",
    2071: "ἔσομαι (ésomai | es'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: future of G1510\nStrong's: will be\nKJV: —shall (should) be (have), (shall) come (to pass), X may have, X fall, what would follow, X live long, X sojourn.\n\nSee: G1510 \n\nCognate Group: G2068 (devour)\nVariants: ἔσομαι, εἰμί",
    2072: "ἔσοπτρον (ésoptron | es'-op-tron)\n\nDerivation: from G1519 and a presumed derivative of G3700\nStrong's: a mirror (for looking into)\nKJV: —glass. Compare G2734 .\n\nSee: G1519 \nSee: G3700 \nSee: G2734 \n\nCognate Group: G2734 (behold as in a glass), G2072 (glass)\nVariants: ἔσοπτρον",
    2073: "ἑσπέρα (hespéra | hes-per'-ah)\n\nDerivation: feminine of an adjective hesperos (evening); the eve (G5610 being implied)\nKJV: —evening(-tide).\n\nSee: G5610 \n\nCognate Group: G2734 (behold as in a glass), G2072 (glass)\nVariants: ἑσπέρα \nHebrew Equivalents: H4606 מֵעָל, H5844 עָטָה, H6148 עָרַב, H6153 עֶרֶב, H6153 עֶרֶב",
    2074: "Ἐσρώμ (Esrṓm | es-rome)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H2696)\nStrong's: Esrom (i.e. Chetsron), an Israelite\nKJV: —Esrom.\nSee: H2696\n\nCognate Group: G2734 (behold as in a glass), G2072 (glass)\nVariants: Ἐσρώμ, Ἑσρώμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H2696 חֶצְרֹון",
    2075: "ἐστέ (esté | es-teh')\n\nSee: G1510 \n\nCognate Group: G2734 (behold as in a glass), G2072 (glass)\nVariants: ἐστέ, εἰμί Strong's: ye are\nKJV: —be, have been, belong.",
    2076: "ἐστί (estí | es-tee')\n\nSee: G1510 \n\nCognate Group: G2734 (behold as in a glass), G2072 (glass)\nVariants: ἐστί, εἰμί Strong's: he (she or it) is; also (with neuter plural) they are\nKJV: —are, be(-long), call, X can(-not), come, consisteth, X dure for a while, + follow, X have, (that) is (to say), make, meaneth, X must needs, + profit, + remaineth, + wrestle.",
    2077: "ἔστω (éstō | es'-to)\n\n\nDerivation: second person singular present imperative of G1510\nStrong's: be thou; also ἔστωσαν (éstōsan | es'-to-san)\nCognate Group: G2734 (behold as in a glass), G2072 (glass)\nVariants: ἔστω, εἰμί",
    2078: "ἔσχατος (éschatos | es'-khat-os)\n\nDerivation: a superlative probably from G2192 (in the sense of contiguity)\nStrong's: farthest, final (of place or time)\nKJV: —ends of, last, latter end, lowest, uttermost.\n\nSee: G2192 \n\nCognate Group: G2078 (ends of)\nVariants: ἔσχατος \nHebrew Equivalents: H309 אָחַר, H314 אַחֲרֹון, H319 אַחֲרִית, H622 אָסַף, H657 אֶפֶס, H732 אָרַח, H1419 גָּדֹול, H3411 יְרֵכָה, H4801 מֶרְחָק, H5486 סוּף, H7093 קֵץ, H7637 שְׁבִיעִי, H8503 תַּכְלִית",
    2079: "ἐσχάτως (eschátōs | es-khat'-oce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2078\nStrong's: finally, i.e. (with G2192) at the extremity of life\nKJV: —point of death.\n\nSee: G2078 \nSee: G2192 \n\nCognate Group: G2078 (ends of)\nVariants: ἐσχάτως",
    2080: "ἔσω (ésō | es'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G1519\nStrong's: inside (as preposition or adjective)\nKJV: — (with-)in(-ner, -to, -ward).\n\nSee: G1519 \n\nCognate Group: G2080 (within)\nVariants: ἔσω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6040 עֳנִי, H6441 פְּנִימָה, H7172 קַרְקַע",
    2081: "ἔσωθεν (ésōthen | es'-o-then)\n\nDerivation: from G2080\nStrong's: from inside; also used as equivalent to G2080 (inside)\nKJV: —inward(-ly), (from) within, without.\n\nSee: G2080 \nSee: G2080 \n\nCognate Group: G2080 (within)\nVariants: ἔσωθεν \nHebrew Equivalents: H6040 עֳנִי",
    2082: "ἐσώτερος (esṓteros | es-o'-ter-os)\n\nDerivation: comparative of G2080\nStrong's: interior\nKJV: —inner, within.\n\nSee: G2080 \n\nCognate Group: G2080 (within)\nVariants: ἐσώτερος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2435 חִיצֹון, H5945 עֶלְיֹון, H6440 פָּנִים, H6442 פְּנִימִי",
    2083: "ἑταῖρος (hetaîros | het-ah'-ee-ros)\n\nDerivation: from ἔτης (a clansman)\nStrong's: a comrade\nKJV: —fellow, friend.\n\nCognate Group: G2083 (fellow)\nVariants: ἑταῖρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2270 חָבֵר, H7200 רָאָה, H7453 רֵעַ",
    2084: "ἑτερόγλωσσος (heteróglōssos | het-er-og'-loce-sos)\n\nDerivation: from G2087 and G1100\nStrong's: other- tongued, i.e. a foreigner\nKJV: —man of other tongue.\n\nSee: G2087 \nSee: G1100 \n\nCognate Group: G1100 (tongue), G2084 (man of other tongue)\nVariants: ἑτερόγλωσσος",
    2085: "ἑτεροδιδασκαλέω (heterodidaskaléō | het-er-od-id-as-kal-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2087 and G1320\nStrong's: to instruct differently\nKJV: —teach other doctrine(-wise).\n\nSee: G2087 \nSee: G1320 \n\nCognate Group: G5572 (false teacher), G2085 (teach other doctrine), G1322 (doctrine), G3547 (doctor of the law), G1317 (apt to teach), G1320 (doctor), G2567 (teacher of good things), G1321 (teach), G1319 (doctrine), G1318 (taught)\nVariants: ἑτεροδιδασκαλέω",
    2086: "ἑτεροζυγέω (heterozygéō | het-er-od-zoog-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2087 and G2218\nStrong's: to yoke up differently, i.e. (figuratively) to associate discordantly\nKJV: —unequally yoke together with.\n\nSee: G2087 \nSee: G2218 \n\nCognate Group: G2218 (pair of balances), G2086 (unequally yoke together with)\nVariants: ἑτεροζυγέω",
    2087: "ἕτερος (héteros | het'-er-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: (an-, the) other or different\nKJV: —altered, else, next (day), one, (an-)other, some, strange.\n\nCognate Group: G2087 (altered)\nVariants: ἕτερος, ἀλλοιόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H251 אָח, H259 אֶחָד, H268 אָחֹור, H269 אָחֹות, H312 אַחֵר, H376 אִישׁ, H2088 זֶה, H2213 זֵר, H2319 חָדָשׁ, H3605 כֹּל, H5236 נֵכָר, H5750 עֹוד, H7453 רֵעַ, H8145 שֵׁנִי",
    2088: "ἑτέρως (hetérōs | het-er'-oce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2087\nStrong's: differently\nKJV: —otherwise.\n\nSee: G2087 \n\nCognate Group: G2087 (altered)\nVariants: ἑτέρως",
    2089: "ἔτι (éti | et'-ee)\n\nDerivation: perhaps akin to G2094\nStrong's: \"yet,\" still (of time or degree)\nKJV: —after that, also, ever, (any) further, (t-)henceforth (more), hereafter, (any) longer, (any) more(-one), now, still, yet.\n\nSee: G2094 \n\nCognate Group: G2087 (altered)\nVariants: ἔτι",
    2090: "ἑτοιμάζω (hetoimázō | het-oy-mad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2092\nStrong's: to prepare\nKJV: —prepare, provide, make ready. Compare G2680 .\n\nSee: G2092 \nSee: G2680 \n\nCognate Group: G2092 (prepared), G2091 (preparation), G2090 (prepare), G4282 (ordain before)\nVariants: ἑτοιμάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1254 בָּרָא, H2363 חוּשׁ, H3190 יָטַב, H3198 יָכַח, H3559 כּוּן, H4886 מָשַׁח, H5493 סוּר, H5782 עוּר, H6186 עָרַךְ, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6257 עָתַד, H6305 פְּדָיָה, H6329 פּוּק, H6437 פָּנָה, H6485 פָּקַד, H7257 רָבַץ, H8446 תּוּר, H8505 תָּכַן",
    2091: "ἑτοιμασία (hetoimasía | het-oy-mas-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2090\nStrong's: preparation\nKJV: —preparation.\n\nSee: G2090 \n\nCognate Group: G2092 (prepared), G2091 (preparation), G2090 (prepare), G4282 (ordain before)\nVariants: ἑτοιμασία \nHebrew Equivalents: H3559 כּוּן, H3653 כֵּן, H4349 מָכֹון",
    2092: "ἕτοιμος (hétoimos | het-oy'-mos)\n\nDerivation: from an old noun ἐτεός (fitness)\nStrong's: adjusted, i.e. ready\nKJV: —prepared, (made) ready(-iness, to our hand).\n\nCognate Group: G2092 (prepared), G2091 (preparation), G2090 (prepare), G4282 (ordain before)\nVariants: ἕτοιμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H328 אַט, H3559 כּוּן, H3700 כָּסַף, H4349 מָכֹון, H4803 מָרַט, H6186 עָרַךְ, H6260 עַתּוּד, H6800 צָנַע",
    2093: "ἑτοίμως (hetoímōs | het'-oy-moce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2092\nStrong's: in readiness\nKJV: —ready.\n\nSee: G2092 \n\nCognate Group: G2092 (prepared), G2091 (preparation), G2090 (prepare), G4282 (ordain before)\nVariants: ἑτοίμως",
    2094: "ἔτος (étos | et'-os)\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary word\nStrong's: a year\nKJV: —year.\n\nCognate Group: G2092 (prepared), G2091 (preparation), G2090 (prepare), G4282 (ordain before)\nVariants: ἔτος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3117 יֹום, H5704 עַד, H8141 שָׁנֶה, H8141 שָׁנֶה",
    2095: "εὖ (eû | yoo)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a primary εὖς (good)\nStrong's: (adverbially) well\nKJV: —good, well (done).\n\nCognate Group: G2092 (prepared), G2091 (preparation), G2090 (prepare), G4282 (ordain before)\nVariants: εὖ, εὖγε, εὺ \nHebrew Equivalents: H995 בִּין, H3190 יָטַב, H3190 יָטַב",
    2096: "Εὖα (Eûa | yoo'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H2332)\nStrong's: Eua (or Eva, i.e. Chavvah), the first woman\nKJV: —Eve.\nSee: H2332\n\nCognate Group: G2092 (prepared), G2091 (preparation), G2090 (prepare), G4282 (ordain before)\nVariants: Εὖα, Εὕα \nHebrew Equivalents: H2247 חָבָה, H2332 חַוָּה",
    2097: "εὐαγγελίζω (euangelízō | yoo-ang-ghel-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G32\nStrong's: to announce good news (\"evangelize\") especially the gospel\nKJV: —declare, bring (declare, show) glad (good) tidings, preach (the gospel).\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G32 \n\nCognate Group: G2099 (evangelist), G2097 (declare), G4283 (preach before the gospel), G2098 (gospel)\nVariants: εὐαγγελίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1319 בָּשַׂר",
    2098: "εὐαγγέλιον (euangélion | yoo-ang-ghel'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2097\nStrong's: a good message, i.e. the gospel\nKJV: —gospel.\n\nSee: G2097 \n\nCognate Group: G2099 (evangelist), G2097 (declare), G4283 (preach before the gospel), G2098 (gospel)\nVariants: εὐαγγέλιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1309 בְּשֹׂורָה",
    2099: "εὐαγγελιστής (euangelistḗs | yoo-ang-ghel-is-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G2097\nStrong's: a preacher of the gospel\nKJV: —evangelist.\n\nSee: G2097 \n\nCognate Group: G2099 (evangelist), G2097 (declare), G4283 (preach before the gospel), G2098 (gospel)\nVariants: εὐαγγελιστής",
    2100: "εὐαρεστέω (euarestéō | yoo-ar-es-teh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2101\nStrong's: to gratify entirely\nKJV: —please (well).\n\nSee: G2101 \n\nCognate Group: G2100 (please), G701 (please), G699 (pleasing), G700 (please), G2101 (acceptable), G441 (men-pleaser)\nVariants: εὐαρεστέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1980 הָלַךְ, H7451 רַע, H8334 שָׁרַת",
    2101: "εὐάρεστος (euárestos | yoo-ar'-es-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G701\nStrong's: fully agreeable\nKJV: —acceptable(-ted), wellpleasing.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G701 \n\nCognate Group: G2100 (please), G701 (please), G699 (pleasing), G700 (please), G2101 (acceptable), G441 (men-pleaser)\nVariants: εὐάρεστος",
    2102: "εὐαρέστως (euaréstōs | yoo-ar-es'-toce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2101\nStrong's: quite agreeably\nKJV: —acceptably, + please well.\n\nSee: G2101 \n\nCognate Group: G2100 (please), G701 (please), G699 (pleasing), G700 (please), G2101 (acceptable), G441 (men-pleaser)\nVariants: εὐαρέστως",
    2103: "Εὔβουλος (Eúboulos | yoo'-boo-los)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G1014\nStrong's: good-willer; Eubulus, a Christian\nKJV: —Eubulus.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G1014 \n\nCognate Group: G2100 (please), G701 (please), G699 (pleasing), G700 (please), G2101 (acceptable), G441 (men-pleaser)\nVariants: Εὔβουλος",
    2104: "εὐγενής (eugenḗs | yoog-en'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G1096\nStrong's: well born, i.e. (literally) high in rank, or (figuratively) generous\nKJV: —more noble, nobleman.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G1096 \n\nCognate Group: G2100 (please), G701 (please), G699 (pleasing), G700 (please), G2101 (acceptable), G441 (men-pleaser)\nVariants: εὐγενής \nHebrew Equivalents: H1419 גָּדֹול",
    2105: "εὐδία (eudía | yoo-dee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: feminine from G2095 and the alternate of G2203 (as the god of the weather)\nStrong's: a clear sky, i.e. fine weather\nKJV: —fair weather.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G2203 \n\nCognate Group: G2100 (please), G701 (please), G699 (pleasing), G700 (please), G2101 (acceptable), G441 (men-pleaser)\nVariants: εὐδία",
    2106: "εὐδοκέω (eudokéō | yoo-dok-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G1380\nStrong's: to think well of, i.e. approve (an act); specially, to approbate (a person or thing)\nKJV: —think good, (be well) please(-d), be the good (have, take) pleasure, be willing.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G1380 \n\nCognate Group: G2106 (think good), G2107 (desire)\nVariants: εὐδοκέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2530 חָמַד, H2654 חָפֵץ, H3474 יָשַׁר, H5414 נָתַן, H5753 עָוָה, H6345 פַּחְדָּה, H6743 צָלַח, H6915 קָדַד, H7521 רָצָה",
    2107: "εὐδοκία (eudokía | yoo-dok-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a presumed compound of G2095 and the base of G1380\nStrong's: satisfaction, i.e. (subjectively) delight, or (objectively) kindness, wish, purpose\nKJV: —desire, good pleasure (will), X seem good.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G1380 \n\nCognate Group: G2106 (think good), G2107 (desire)\nVariants: εὐδοκία \nHebrew Equivalents: H7522 רָצֹון",
    2108: "εὐεργεσία (euergesía | yoo-erg-es-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2110\nStrong's: beneficence (genitive case or specially)\nKJV: —benefit, good deed done.\n\nSee: G2110 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: εὐεργεσία \nHebrew Equivalents: H5949 עֲלִילָה",
    2109: "εὐεργετέω (euergetéō | yoo-erg-et-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2110\nStrong's: to be philanthropic\nKJV: —do good.\n\nSee: G2110 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: εὐεργετέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1580 גָּמַל, H1584 גָּמַר",
    2110: "εὐεργέτης (euergétēs | yoo-erg-et'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and the base of G2041\nStrong's: a worker of good, i.e. (specially) a philanthropist\nKJV: —benefactor.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G2041 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: εὐεργέτης",
    2111: "εὔθετος (eúthetos | yoo'-thet-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and a derivative of G5087\nStrong's: well placed, i.e. (figuratively) appropriate\nKJV: —fit, meet.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G5087 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: εὔθετος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4672 מָצָא",
    2112: "εὐθέως (euthéōs | yoo-theh'-oce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2117\nStrong's: directly, i.e. at once or soon\nKJV: —anon, as soon as, forthwith, immediately, shortly, straightway.\n\nSee: G2117 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: εὐθέως \nHebrew Equivalents: H1249 בַּר, H3474 יָשַׁר, H3474 יָשַׁר, H3559 כּוּן, H4339 מֵישָׁר, H5048 נֶגֶד, H5228 נָכֹחַ, H6597 פִּתְאֹום, H8205 שְׁפִי, H8505 תָּכַן",
    2113: "εὐθυδρομέω (euthydroméō | yoo-thoo-drom-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2117 and G1408\nStrong's: to lay a straight course, i.e. sail direct\nKJV: —(come) with a straight course.\n\nSee: G2117 \nSee: G1408 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: εὐθυδρομέω",
    2114: "εὐθυμέω (euthyméō | yoo-thoo-meh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2115\nStrong's: to cheer up, i.e. (intransitively) be cheerful; neuter comparative (adverbially) more cheerfully\nKJV: —be of good cheer (merry).\n\nSee: G2115 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: εὐθυμέω",
    2115: "εὔθυμος (eúthymos | yoo'-thoo-mos)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G2372\nStrong's: in fine spirits, i.e. cheerful\nKJV: —of good cheer, the more cheerfully.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G2372 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: εὔθυμος, εὐθύμως",
    2116: "εὐθύνω (euthýnō | yoo-thoo'-no)\n\nDerivation: from G2117\nStrong's: to straighten (level); technically, to steer\nKJV: —governor, make straight.\n\nSee: G2117 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: εὐθύνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3474 יָשַׁר, H5186 נָטָה",
    2117: "εὐθύς (euthýs | yoo-thoos')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from G2095 and G5087\nStrong's: straight, i.e. (literally) level, or (figuratively) true; adverbially (of time) at once\nKJV: —anon, by and by, forthwith, immediately, straightway.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G5087 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: εὐθύς, εὐθύσ1, εὐθύσ2 \nHebrew Equivalents: H1249 בַּר, H3474 יָשַׁר, H3474 יָשַׁר, H3559 כּוּן, H4339 מֵישָׁר, H5048 נֶגֶד, H5228 נָכֹחַ, H8205 שְׁפִי, H8505 תָּכַן",
    2118: "εὐθύτης (euthýtēs | yoo-thoo'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G2117\nStrong's: rectitude\nKJV: —righteousness.\n\nSee: G2117 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: εὐθύτης \nHebrew Equivalents: H2136 זָכוּ, H3476 יֹשֶׁר, H3477 יָשָׁר, H4334 מִישֹׁור, H8549 תָּמִים",
    2119: "εὐκαιρέω (eukairéō | yoo-kahee-reh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2121\nStrong's: to have good time, i.e. opportunity or leisure\nKJV: —have leisure (convenient time), spend time.\n\nSee: G2121 \n\nCognate Group: G2040 (labourer), G2039 (craft), G2108 (benefit), G2038 (commit), G1753 (operation), G1755 (operation), G1756 (effectual), G2109 (do good), G2110 (benefactor), G1754 (do), G2041 (deed)\nVariants: εὐκαιρέω",
    2120: "εὐκαιρία (eukairía | yoo-kahee-ree'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2121\nStrong's: a favorable occasion\nKJV: —opportunity.\n\nSee: G2121 \n\nCognate Group: G2120 (opportunity), G2121 (convenient), G170 (lack opportunity), G4340 (dur- for awhile), G171 (out of season), G2540 (X always), G2122 (conveniently)\nVariants: εὐκαιρία \nHebrew Equivalents: H6256 עֵת",
    2121: "εὔκαιρος (eúkairos | yoo'-kahee-ros)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G2540\nStrong's: well-timed, i.e. opportune\nKJV: —convenient, in time of need.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G2540 \n\nCognate Group: G2120 (opportunity), G2121 (convenient), G170 (lack opportunity), G4340 (dur- for awhile), G171 (out of season), G2540 (X always), G2122 (conveniently)\nVariants: εὔκαιρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H6256 עֵת",
    2122: "εὐκαίρως (eukaírōs | yoo-kah'-ee-roce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2121\nStrong's: opportunely\nKJV: —conveniently, in season.\n\nSee: G2121 \n\nCognate Group: G2120 (opportunity), G2121 (convenient), G170 (lack opportunity), G4340 (dur- for awhile), G171 (out of season), G2540 (X always), G2122 (conveniently)\nVariants: εὐκαίρως",
    2123: "εὐκοπώτερος (eukopṓteros | yoo-kop-o'-ter-os)\n\nDerivation: comparative of a compound of G2095 and G2873\nStrong's: better for toil, i.e. more facile\nKJV: —easier.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G2873 \n\nCognate Group: G2120 (opportunity), G2121 (convenient), G170 (lack opportunity), G4340 (dur- for awhile), G171 (out of season), G2540 (X always), G2122 (conveniently)\nVariants: εὐκοπώτερος, εὔκοπος, εὐκοπώτερον",
    2124: "εὐλάβεια (eulábeia | yoo-lab'-i-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2126\nStrong's: properly, caution, i.e. (religiously) reverence (piety); by implication, dread (concretely)\nKJV: —fear(-ed).\n\nSee: G2126 \n\nCognate Group: G2120 (opportunity), G2121 (convenient), G170 (lack opportunity), G4340 (dur- for awhile), G171 (out of season), G2540 (X always), G2122 (conveniently)\nVariants: εὐλάβεια \nHebrew Equivalents: H1674 דְּאָגָה",
    2125: "εὐλαβέομαι (eulabéomai | yoo-lab-eh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G2126\nStrong's: to be circumspect, i.e. (by implication) to be apprehensive; religiously, to reverence\nKJV: —(moved with) fear.\n\nSee: G2126 \n\nCognate Group: G2125 (fear), G2126 (devout)\nVariants: εὐλαβέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1481 גּוּר, H1672 דָּאַג, H1763 דְּחַל, H2013 הָסָה, H2342 חוּל, H2620 חָסָה, H2623 חָסִיד, H2803 חָשַׁב, H3025 יָגֹר, H3372 יָרֵא, H3808 לֹא, H5937 עָלַז, H6206 עָרַץ, H6342 פָּחַד, H8104 שָׁמַר",
    2126: "εὐλαβής (eulabḗs | yoo-lab-ace')\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G2983\nStrong's: taking well (carefully), i.e. circumspect (religiously, pious)\nKJV: —devout.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G2983 \n\nCognate Group: G2125 (fear), G2126 (devout)\nVariants: εὐλαβής \nHebrew Equivalents: H2623 חָסִיד, H5144 נָזַר",
    2127: "εὐλογέω (eulogéō | yoo-log-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2095 and G3056\nStrong's: to speak well of, i.e. (religiously) to bless (thank or invoke a benediction upon, prosper)\nKJV: —bless, praise.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G3056 \n\nCognate Group: G2129 (blessing bounty), G2128 (blessed), G2127 (bless), G1757 (bless)\nVariants: εὐλογέω, κατευλογέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1288 בָרַךְ, H1921 הָדַר, H1984 הָלַל, H3034 יָדָה, H3372 יָרֵא, H3498 יָתַר, H3513 כָּבַד, H5059 נָגַן, H7442 רָנַן, H7521 רָצָה, H7624 שְׁבַח",
    2128: "εὐλογητός (eulogētós | yoo-log-ay-tos')\n\nDerivation: from G2127\nStrong's: adorable\nKJV: —blessed.\n\nSee: G2127 \n\nCognate Group: G2129 (blessing bounty), G2128 (blessed), G2127 (bless), G1757 (bless)\nVariants: εὐλογητός \nHebrew Equivalents: H1288 בָרַךְ",
    2129: "εὐλογία (eulogía | yoo-log-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2127\nStrong's: fine speaking, i.e. elegance of language; commendation (\"eulogy\"), i.e. (reverentially) adoration; religiously, benediction; by implication, consecration; by extension, benefit or largess\nKJV: —blessing (a matter of) bounty (X -tifully), fair speech.\n\nSee: G2127 \n\nCognate Group: G2129 (blessing bounty), G2128 (blessed), G2127 (bless), G1757 (bless)\nVariants: εὐλογία, εὐγλωττία \nHebrew Equivalents: H1062 בְּכֹורָה, H1288 בָרַךְ, H1293 בְּרָכָה, H6529 פְּרִי, H8378 תַּאֲוָה",
    2130: "εὐμετάδοτος (eumetádotos | yoo-met-ad'-ot-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and a presumed derivative of G3330\nStrong's: good at imparting, i.e. liberal\nKJV: —ready to distribute.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G3330 \n\nCognate Group: G2129 (blessing bounty), G2128 (blessed), G2127 (bless), G1757 (bless)\nVariants: εὐμετάδοτος",
    2131: "Εὐνίκη (Euníkē | yoo-nee'-kay)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G3529\nStrong's: victorious; Eunice, a Jewess\nKJV: —Eunice.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G3529 \n\nCognate Group: G2129 (blessing bounty), G2128 (blessed), G2127 (bless), G1757 (bless)\nVariants: Εὐνίκη",
    2132: "εὐνοέω (eunoéō | yoo-no-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2095 and G3563\nStrong's: to be well- minded, i.e. reconcile\nKJV: —agree.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G3563 \n\nCognate Group: G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)\nVariants: εὐνοέω",
    2133: "εὔνοια (eúnoia | yoo'-noy-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2132\nStrong's: kindness; euphemistically, conjugal duty\nKJV: —benevolence, good will.\n\nSee: G2132 \n\nCognate Group: G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)\nVariants: εὔνοια",
    2134: "εὐνουχίζω (eunouchízō | yoo-noo-khid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2135\nStrong's: to castrate (figuratively, live unmarried)\nKJV: —make…eunuch.\n\nSee: G2135 \n\nCognate Group: G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)\nVariants: εὐνουχίζω",
    2135: "εὐνοῦχος (eunoûchos | yoo-noo'-khos)\n\nDerivation: from εὐνή (a bed) and G2192\nStrong's: a castrated person (such being employed in Oriental bed-chambers); by extension an impotent or unmarried man; by implication, a chamberlain (state-officer)\nKJV: —eunuch.\n\nSee: G2192 \n\nCognate Group: G2135 (eunuch)\nVariants: εὐνοῦχος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5631 סָרִיס",
    2136: "Εὐοδία (Euodía | yoo-od-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2137\nStrong's: fine travelling; Euodia, a Christian woman\nKJV: —Euodias.\n\nSee: G2137 \n\nCognate Group: G2135 (eunuch)\nVariants: Εὐοδία",
    2137: "εὐοδόω (euodóō | yoo-od-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2095 and G3598\nStrong's: to help on the road, i.e. (passively) succeed in reaching; figuratively, to succeed in business affairs\nKJV: —(have a) prosper(-ous journey).\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G3598 \n\nCognate Group: G2135 (eunuch)\nVariants: εὐοδόω, εὐοδόομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H5148 נָחָה, H6555 פָּרַץ, H6743 צָלַח, H7136 קָרָה, H7521 רָצָה, H7919 שָׂכַל",
    2138: "εὐπειθής (eupeithḗs | yoo-pi-thace')\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G3982\nStrong's: good for persuasion, i.e. (intransitively) complaint\nKJV: —easy to be intreated.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G3982 \n\nCognate Group: G2135 (eunuch)\nVariants: εὐπειθής",
    2139: "εὐπερίστατος (euperístatos | yoo-per-is'-tat-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and a derivative of a presumed compound of G4012 and G2476\nStrong's: well standing around, i.e. (a competitor) thwarting (a racer) in every direction (figuratively, of sin in genitive case)\nKJV: —which doth so easily beset.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G4012 \nSee: G2476 \n\nCognate Group: G2135 (eunuch)\nVariants: εὐπερίστατος, εὐπερίσπαστος",
    2140: "εὐποιΐα (eupoiḯa | yoo-poy-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2095 and G4160\nStrong's: well-doing, i.e. beneficence\nKJV: —to do good.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G4160 \n\nCognate Group: G2135 (eunuch)\nVariants: εὐποιΐα, εὐποιί̈α, εὐποιΐα",
    2141: "εὐπορέω (euporéō | yoo-por-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2090 and the base of G4197\nStrong's: (intransitively) to be good for passing through, i.e. (figuratively) have pecuniary means\nKJV: —ability.\n\nSee: G2090 \nSee: G4197 \n\nCognate Group: G2135 (eunuch)\nVariants: εὐπορέω, εὐπορέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H4672 מָצָא, H5381 נָשַׂג",
    2142: "εὐπορία (euporía | yoo-por-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2141\nStrong's: pecuniary resources\nKJV: —wealth.\n\nSee: G2141 \n\nCognate Group: G2135 (eunuch)\nVariants: εὐπορία \nHebrew Equivalents: H2428 חַיִל",
    2143: "εὐπρέπεια (euprépeia | yoo-prep'-i-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2095 and G4241\nStrong's: good suitableness, i.e. gracefulness\nKJV: —grace.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G4241 \n\nCognate Group: G2135 (eunuch)\nVariants: εὐπρέπεια \nHebrew Equivalents: H1348 גֵּאוּת, H1926 הָדָר, H4359 מִכְלָל, H4583 מָעֹון, H5116 נָוֶה, H5273 נָעִים",
    2144: "εὐπρόσδεκτος (euprósdektos | yoo-pros'-dek-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and a derivative of G4327\nStrong's: well-received, i.e. approved, favorable\nKJV: —acceptable(-ted).\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G4327 \n\nCognate Group: G1403 (feast), G1209 (accept), G1184 (accepted), G553 (look for), G1523 (receive), G587 (acceptable), G588 (accept), G2144 (acceptable), G4327 (accept), G594 (acceptation), G1561 (looking for)\nVariants: εὐπρόσδεκτος",
    2145: "εὐπρόσεδρος (euprósedros | yoo-pros'-ed-ros)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and the same as G4332\nStrong's: sitting well towards, i.e. (figuratively) assiduous (neuter, diligent service)\nKJV: —X attend upon.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G4332 \n\nCognate Group: G1403 (feast), G1209 (accept), G1184 (accepted), G553 (look for), G1523 (receive), G587 (acceptable), G588 (accept), G2144 (acceptable), G4327 (accept), G594 (acceptation), G1561 (looking for)\nVariants: εὐπρόσεδρος, εὐπάρεδρος",
    2146: "εὐπροσωπέω (euprosōpéō | yoo-pros-o-peh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2095 and G4383\nStrong's: to be of good countenance, i.e. (figuratively) to make a display\nKJV: —make a fair show.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G4383 \n\nCognate Group: G2146 (make a fair show), G4380 (have respect to persons), G4382 (respect of persons), G678 (without respect of persons), G4383 (appearance), G4381 (respecter of persons)\nVariants: εὐπροσωπέω",
    2147: "εὑρίσκω (heurískō | hyoo-ris'-ko),\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of a primary εὕρω (heúrō | hyoo'-ro), which (together with another cognate form) εὑρέω (heuréō | hyoo-reh'-o)\n\n is used for it in all the tenses except the present and imperfect\nStrong's: to find (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —find, get, obtain, perceive, see.\n\nCognate Group: G2147 (find)\nVariants: εὑρίσκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H8 אֹבֵד, H559 אָמַר, H935 בֹּוא, H1234 בָּקַע, H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H1869 דָּרַךְ, H3498 יָתַר, H4422 מָלַט, H4672 מָצָא, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5381 נָשַׂג, H6329 פּוּק, H7200 רָאָה, H7912 שְׁכַח, H8104 שָׁמַר",
    2148: "Εὐροκλύδων (Euroklýdōn | yoo-rok-loo'-dohn)\n\nDerivation: from Εὖρος (the east wind) and G2830\nStrong's: a storm from the East (or southeast), i.e. (in modern phrase) a Levanter\nKJV: —Euroklydon.\n\nSee: G2830 \n\nCognate Group: G2147 (find)\nVariants: Εὐροκλύδων, εὐρακύλων, εὐροκλύδων",
    2149: "εὐρύχωρος (eurýchōros | yoo-roo'-kho-ros)\n\nDerivation: from εὐρύς (wide) and G5561\nStrong's: spacious\nKJV: —broad.\n\nSee: G5561 \n\nCognate Group: G2147 (find)\nVariants: εὐρύχωρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1637 גֹּרֶן, H7337 רָחַב",
    2150: "εὐσέβεια (eusébeia | yoo-seb'-i-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2152\nStrong's: piety; specially, the gospel scheme\nKJV: —godliness, holiness.\n\nSee: G2152 \n\nCognate Group: G4573 (worship), G763 (ungodly), G2152 (devout), G4574 (devotion), G4576 (devout), G2150 (godliness), G764 (commit ungodly), G765 (ungodly), G2153 (godly), G4575 (Augustus), G2151 (show piety)\nVariants: εὐσέβεια \nHebrew Equivalents: H3374 יִרְאָה",
    2151: "εὐσεβέω (eusebéō | yoo-seb-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2152\nStrong's: to be pious, i.e. (towards God) to worship, or (towards parents) to respect (support)\nKJV: —show piety, worship.\n\nSee: G2152 \n\nCognate Group: G4573 (worship), G763 (ungodly), G2152 (devout), G4574 (devotion), G4576 (devout), G2150 (godliness), G764 (commit ungodly), G765 (ungodly), G2153 (godly), G4575 (Augustus), G2151 (show piety)\nVariants: εὐσεβέω",
    2152: "εὐσεβής (eusebḗs | yoo-seb-ace')\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G4576\nStrong's: well-reverent, i.e. pious\nKJV: —devout, godly.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G4576 \n\nCognate Group: G4573 (worship), G763 (ungodly), G2152 (devout), G4574 (devotion), G4576 (devout), G2150 (godliness), G764 (commit ungodly), G765 (ungodly), G2153 (godly), G4575 (Augustus), G2151 (show piety)\nVariants: εὐσεβής \nHebrew Equivalents: H2623 חָסִיד, H5081 נָדִיב, H6662 צַדִּיק",
    2153: "εὐσεβῶς (eusebōs | yoo-seb-oce')\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2152\nStrong's: piously\nKJV: —godly.\n\nSee: G2152 \n\nCognate Group: G4573 (worship), G763 (ungodly), G2152 (devout), G4574 (devotion), G4576 (devout), G2150 (godliness), G764 (commit ungodly), G765 (ungodly), G2153 (godly), G4575 (Augustus), G2151 (show piety)\nVariants: εὐσεβῶς",
    2154: "εὔσημος (eúsēmos | yoo'-say-mos)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and the base of G4591\nStrong's: well indicated, i.e. (figuratively) significant\nKJV: —easy to be understood.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G4591 \n\nCognate Group: G2154 (easy to be understood)\nVariants: εὔσημος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3677 כֶּסֶא",
    2155: "εὔσπλαγχνος (eúsplanchnos | yoo'-splangkh-nos)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G4698\nStrong's: well compassioned, i.e. sympathetic\nKJV: —pitiful, tender-hearted.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G4698 \n\nCognate Group: G2155 (pitiful), G4697 (have compassion), G4698 (bowels), G4184 (very pitiful)\nVariants: εὔσπλαγχνος",
    2156: "εὐσχημόνως (euschēmónōs | yoo-skhay-mon'-ose)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2158\nStrong's: decorously\nKJV: —decently, honestly.\n\nSee: G2158 \n\nCognate Group: G2155 (pitiful), G4697 (have compassion), G4698 (bowels), G4184 (very pitiful)\nVariants: εὐσχημόνως",
    2157: "εὐσχημοσύνη (euschēmosýnē | yoo-skhay-mos-oo'-nay)\n\nDerivation: from G2158\nStrong's: decorousness\nKJV: —comeliness.\n\nSee: G2158 \n\nCognate Group: G2155 (pitiful), G4697 (have compassion), G4698 (bowels), G4184 (very pitiful)\nVariants: εὐσχημοσύνη",
    2158: "εὐσχήμων (euschḗmōn | yoo-skhay'-mone)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G4976\nStrong's: well-formed, i.e. (figuratively) decorous, noble (in rank)\nKJV: —comely, honourable.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G4976 \n\nCognate Group: G2158 (comely)\nVariants: εὐσχήμων",
    2159: "εὐτόνως (eutónōs | yoo-ton'-oce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from a compound of G2095 and a derivative of τείνω (to stretch)\nStrong's: in a well-strung manner, i.e. (figuratively) intensely (in a good sense, cogently; in a bad one, fiercely)\nKJV: —mightily, vehemently.\n\nSee: G2095 \n\nCognate Group: G2158 (comely)\nVariants: εὐτόνως \nHebrew Equivalents: H7782 שֹׁופָר",
    2160: "εὐτραπελία (eutrapelía | yoo-trap-el-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2095 and a derivative of the base of G5157 (meaning well-turned, i.e. ready at repartee, jocose)\nStrong's: witticism, i.e. (in a vulgar sense) ribaldry\nKJV: —jesting.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G5157 \n\nCognate Group: G2158 (comely)\nVariants: εὐτραπελία",
    2161: "Εὔτυχος (Eútychos | yoo'-too-khos)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and a derivative of G5177\nStrong's: well- fated, i.e. fortunate; Eutychus, a young man\nKJV: —Eutychus.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G5177 \n\nCognate Group: G2158 (comely)\nVariants: Εὔτυχος",
    2162: "εὐφημία (euphēmía | yoo-fay-mee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2163\nStrong's: good language (\"euphemy\"), i.e. praise (repute)\nKJV: —good report.\n\nSee: G2163 \n\nCognate Group: G2158 (comely)\nVariants: εὐφημία, ἐυφημία",
    2163: "εὔφημος (eúphēmos | yoo'-fay-mos)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G5345\nStrong's: well spoken of, i.e. reputable\nKJV: —of good report.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G5345 \n\nCognate Group: G2158 (comely)\nVariants: εὔφημος",
    2164: "εὐφορέω (euphoréō | yoo-for-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G5409\nStrong's: to bear well, i.e. be fertile\nKJV: —bring forth abundantly.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G5409 \n\nCognate Group: G2158 (comely)\nVariants: εὐφορέω",
    2165: "εὐφραίνω (euphraínō | yoo-frah'-ee-no)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G5424\nStrong's: to put (middle voice or passively, be) in a good frame of mind, i.e. rejoice\nKJV: —fare, make glad, be (make) merry, rejoice.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G5424 \n\nCognate Group: G2165 (fare), G2167 (gladness)\nVariants: εὐφραίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H8055 שָׂמַח",
    2166: "Εὐφράτης (Euphrátēs | yoo-frat'-ace)\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin (compare H6578)\nStrong's: Euphrates, a river of Asia\nKJV: —Euphrates.\nSee: H6578\n\nCognate Group: G2165 (fare), G2167 (gladness)\nVariants: Εὐφράτης \nHebrew Equivalents: H6578 פְּרָת",
    2167: "εὐφροσύνη (euphrosýnē | yoo-fros-oo'-nay)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2165\nStrong's: joyfulness\nKJV: —gladness, joy.\n\nSee: G2165 \n\nCognate Group: G2165 (fare), G2167 (gladness)\nVariants: εὐφροσύνη \nHebrew Equivalents: H160 אַהֲבָה, H1420 גְּדוּלָה, H1524 גִּיל, H2305 חֶדְוָה, H3117 יֹום, H4960 מִשְׁתֶּה, H5035 נֶבֶל, H5116 נָוֶה, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5483 סוּס, H5531 סִכְלוּת, H6666 צְדָקָה, H7442 רָנַן, H7814 שְׂחֹוק, H8055 שָׂמַח, H8055 שָׂמַח, H8057 שִׂמְחָה, H8081 שֶׁמֶן, H8342 שָׂשֹׂון",
    2168: "εὐχαριστέω (eucharistéō | yoo-khar-is-teh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2170\nStrong's: to be grateful, i.e. (actively) to express gratitude (towards); specially, to say grace at a meal\nKJV: —(give) thank(-ful, -s).\n\nSee: G2170 \n\nCognate Group: G5479 (gladness), G4796 (rejoice in), G2168 (thank), G2169 (thankfulness), G5485 (acceptable), G5486 (gift), G5463 (farewell), G5484 (be- cause of), G2170 (thankful), G5487 (make accepted), G884 (unthankful), G5483 (deliver)\nVariants: εὐχαριστέω, ἐυχαριστέω",
    2169: "εὐχαριστία (eucharistía | yoo-khar-is-tee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2170\nStrong's: gratitude; actively, grateful language (to God, as an act of worship)\nKJV: —thankfulness, (giving of) thanks(-giving).\n\nSee: G2170 \n\nCognate Group: G5479 (gladness), G4796 (rejoice in), G2168 (thank), G2169 (thankfulness), G5485 (acceptable), G5486 (gift), G5463 (farewell), G5484 (be- cause of), G2170 (thankful), G5487 (make accepted), G884 (unthankful), G5483 (deliver)\nVariants: εὐχαριστία",
    2170: "εὐχάριστος (eucháristos | yoo-khar'-is-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and a derivative of G5483\nStrong's: well favored, i.e. (by implication) grateful\nKJV: —thankful.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G5483 \n\nCognate Group: G5479 (gladness), G4796 (rejoice in), G2168 (thank), G2169 (thankfulness), G5485 (acceptable), G5486 (gift), G5463 (farewell), G5484 (be- cause of), G2170 (thankful), G5487 (make accepted), G884 (unthankful), G5483 (deliver)\nVariants: εὐχάριστος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2580 חֵן",
    2171: "εὐχή (euchḗ | yoo-khay')\n\nDerivation: from G2172\nStrong's: properly, a wish, expressed as a petition to God, or in votive obligation\nKJV: —prayer, vow.\n\nSee: G2172 \n\nCognate Group: G2172 (pray), G4335 (X pray earnestly), G4336 (pray), G2171 (prayer)\nVariants: εὐχή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1259 בָּרָד, H5087 נָדַר, H5088 נֶדֶר, H5144 נָזַר, H8605 תְּפִלָּה",
    2172: "εὔχομαι (eúchomai | yoo'-khom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice of a primary verb\nStrong's: to wish; by implication, to pray to God\nKJV: —pray, will, wish.\n\nCognate Group: G2172 (pray), G4335 (X pray earnestly), G4336 (pray), G2171 (prayer)\nVariants: εὔχομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H631 אָסַר, H1156 בְּעָא, H2603 חָנַן, H5074 נָדַד, H5087 נָדַר, H5144 נָזַר, H5375 נָשָׂא, H6279 עָתַר, H6381 פָּלָא, H6419 פָּלַל, H8605 תְּפִלָּה",
    2173: "εὔχρηστος (eúchrēstos | yoo'-khrays-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G5543\nStrong's: easily used, i.e. useful\nKJV: —profitable, meet for use.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G5543 \n\nCognate Group: G2172 (pray), G4335 (X pray earnestly), G4336 (pray), G2171 (prayer)\nVariants: εὔχρηστος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2656 חֵפֶץ",
    2174: "εὐψυχέω (eupsychéō | yoo-psoo-kheh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2095 and G5590\nStrong's: to be in good spirits, i.e. feel encouraged\nKJV: —be of good comfort.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G5590 \n\nCognate Group: G2172 (pray), G4335 (X pray earnestly), G4336 (pray), G2171 (prayer)\nVariants: εὐψυχέω",
    2175: "εὐωδία (euōdía | yoo-o-dee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2095 and a derivative of G3605\nStrong's: good-scentedness, i.e. fragrance\nKJV: —sweet savour (smell, -smelling).\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G3605 \n\nCognate Group: G2175 (sweet savour)\nVariants: εὐωδία \nHebrew Equivalents: H5207 נִיחֹוחַ",
    2176: "εὐώνυμος (euṓnymos | yoo-o'-noo-mos)\n\nDerivation: from G2095 and G3686\nStrong's: properly, well-named (good-omened), i.e. the left (which was the lucky side among the pagan Greeks); neuter as adverbial, at the left hand\nKJV: —(on the) left.\n\nSee: G2095 \nSee: G3686 \n\nCognate Group: G2175 (sweet savour)\nVariants: εὐώνυμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H6828 צָפֹון",
    2177: "ἐφάλλομαι (ephállomai | ef-al'-lom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G242\nStrong's: to spring upon\nKJV: —leap on.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G242 \n\nCognate Group: G2175 (sweet savour)\nVariants: ἐφάλλομαι, ἐνάλλομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H6743 צָלַח",
    2178: "ἐφάπαξ (ephápax | ef-ap'-ax)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G530\nStrong's: upon one occasion (only)\nKJV: —(at) once (for all).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G530 \n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: ἐφάπαξ",
    2179: "Ἐφεσῖνος (Ephesînos | ef-es-ee'-nos)\n\nDerivation: from G2181\nStrong's: Ephesine, or situated at Ephesus\nKJV: —of Ephesus.\n\nSee: G2181 \n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: Ἐφεσῖνος G2385",
    2180: "Ἐφέσιος (Ephésios | ef-es'-ee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2181\nStrong's: an Ephesian or inhabitant of Ephesus\nKJV: —Ephesian, of Ephesus.\n\nSee: G2181 \n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: Ἐφέσιος",
    2181: "Ἔφεσος (Éphesos | ef'-es-os)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: Ephesus, a city of Asia Minor\nKJV: —Ephesus.\n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: Ἔφεσος",
    2182: "ἐφευρετής (epheuretḗs | ef-yoo-ret'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G1909 and G2147\nStrong's: a discoverer, i.e. contriver\nKJV: —inventor.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2147 \n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: ἐφευρετής",
    2183: "ἐφημερία (ephēmería | ef-ay-mer-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2184\nStrong's: diurnality, i.e. (specially) the quotidian rotation or class of the Jewish priests' service at the Temple, as distributed by families\nKJV: —course.\n\nSee: G2184 \n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: ἐφημερία \nHebrew Equivalents: H4256 מַחֲלֹקֶת, H4929 מִשְׁמָר, H4931 מִשְׁמֶרֶת",
    2184: "ἐφήμερος (ephḗmeros | ef-ay'-mer-os)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2250\nStrong's: for a day (\"ephemeral\"), i.e. diurnal\nKJV: —daily.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2250 \n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: ἐφήμερος",
    2185: "ἐφικνέομαι (ephiknéomai | ef-ik-neh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and a cognate of G2240\nStrong's: to arrive upon, i.e. extend to\nKJV: —reach.\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2240 \n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: ἐφικνέομαι",
    2186: "ἐφίστημι (ephístēmi | ef-is'-tay-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G1909 and G2476\nStrong's: to stand upon, i.e. be present (in various applications, friendly or otherwise, usually literal); \nKJV: —assault, come (in, to, unto, upon), be at hand (instant), present, stand (before, by, over).\n\nSee: G1909 \nSee: G2476 \n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: ἐφίστημι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2388 חָזַק, H3320 יָצַב, H3680 כָּסָה, H3898 לָחַם, H4513 מָנַע, H5324 נָצַב, H5327 נָצָה, H5414 נָתַן, H5564 סָמַךְ, H5774 עוּף, H5975 עָמַד, H6485 פָּקַד, H6965 קוּם, H7322 רוּף, H7725 שׁוּב, H7760 שׂוּם, H7896 שִׁית, H7919 שָׂכַל, H8138 שָׁנָה, H8199 שָׁפַט",
    2187: "Ἐφραίμ (Ephraím | ef-rah-im')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H669 or better H6085)\nStrong's: Ephraim, a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Ephraim.\nSee: H669\nSee: H6085\n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: Ἐφραίμ, Ἐφραΐμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H669 אֶפְרַיִם, H6085 עֶפְרֹון",
    2188: "ἐφφαθά (ephphathá | ef-fath-ah')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (H6606)\nStrong's: be opened!\nKJV: —Ephphatha.\nSee: H6606\n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: ἐφφαθά, εφφαθα \nHebrew Equivalents: H6606 פְּתַח",
    2189: "ἔχθρα (échthra | ekh'-thrah)\n\nDerivation: feminine of G2190\nStrong's: hostility; by implication, a reason for opposition\nKJV: —enmity, hatred.\n\nSee: G2190 \n\nCognate Group: G2178 (once), G530 (once)\nVariants: ἔχθρα \nHebrew Equivalents: H340 אָיַב, H342 אֵיבָה, H639 אַף, H6158 עֹרֵב, H7879 שִׂיחַ, H8135 שִׂנְאָה",
    2190: "ἐχθρός (echthrós | ech-thros')\n\nDerivation: from a primary ἔχθω (to hate)\nStrong's: hateful (passively, odious, or actively, hostile); usually as a noun, an adversary (especially Satan)\nKJV: —enemy, foe.\n\nCognate Group: G2190 (enemy), G2198 (life)\nVariants: ἐχθρός \nHebrew Equivalents: H340 אָיַב, H342 אֵיבָה, H398 אָכַל, H1471 גֹּוי, H2213 זֵר, H4193 מֹות, H6146 עָר, H6148 עָרַב, H6789 צָמַת, H6862 צַר, H6887 צָרַר, H6965 קוּם, H7451 רַע, H7789 שׁוּר, H8130 שָׂנֵא",
    2191: "ἔχιδνα (échidna | ekh'-id-nah)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain origin\nStrong's: an adder or other poisonous snake (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —viper.\n\nCognate Group: G2191 (viper)\nVariants: ἔχιδνα",
    2192: "ἔχω (échō | ekh'-o), including an alternate form σχέω (schéō | skheh'-o)\n\n; (used in certain tenses only)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to hold (used in very various applications, literally or figuratively, direct or remote; such as possession; ability, contiuity, relation, or condition)\nKJV: —be (able, X hold, possessed with), accompany, + begin to amend, can(+ -not), X conceive, count, diseased, do + eat, + enjoy, + fear, following, have, hold, keep, + lack, + go to law, lie, + must needs, + of necessity, + need, next, + recover, + reign, + rest, + return, X sick, take for, + tremble, + uncircumcised, use.\n\nCognate Group: G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)\nVariants: ἔχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H157 אָהַב, H270 אָחַז, H309 אָחַר, H383 אִיתַי, H410 אֵל, H1167 בַּעַל, H1692 דָּבַק, H1961 הָיָה, H1961 הָיָה, H2009 הִנֵּה, H2266 חָבַר, H2388 חָזַק, H2505 חָלַק, H2974 יָאַל, H3426 יֵשׁ, H3559 כּוּן, H3789 כָּתַב, H3830 לְבוּשׁ, H3947 לָקַח, H4135 מוּל, H4422 מָלַט, H4626 מַעַר, H4672 מָצָא, H4962 מַת, H5048 נֶגֶד, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5414 נָתַן, H5921 עַל, H5973 עִם, H5975 עָמַד, H6102 עָצֵל, H6113 עָצָר, H6256 עֵת, H6845 צָפַן, H7227 רַב, H7257 רָבַץ, H7693 שָׁגַל, H7760 שׂוּם, H7965 שָׁלֹום",
    2193: "ἕως (héōs | heh'-oce)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a conjunction, preposition and adverb of continuance, until (of time and place)\nKJV: —even (until, unto), (as) far (as), how long, (un-)til(-l), (hither-, un-, up) to, while(-s).\n\nCognate Group: G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)\nVariants: ἕως",
    2194: "Ζαβουλών (Zaboulṓn | dzab-oo-lone')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H2074)\nStrong's: Zabulon (i.e. Zebulon), a region of Palestine\nKJV: —Zabulon.\nSee: H2074\n\nCognate Group: G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)\nVariants: Ζαβουλών \nHebrew Equivalents: H2074 זְבוּלוּן",
    2195: "Ζακχαῖος (Zakchaîos | dzak-chah'-ee-yos)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (compare H2140)\nStrong's: Zacchæus, an Israelite\nKJV: —Zacchæus.\nSee: H2140\n\nCognate Group: G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)\nVariants: Ζακχαῖος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2140 זַכַּי",
    2196: "Ζαρά (Zará | dzar-ah')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H2226)\nStrong's: Zara, (i.e. Zerach), an Israelite\nKJV: —Zara.\nSee: H2226\n\nCognate Group: G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)\nVariants: Ζαρά, Ζάρα \nHebrew Equivalents: H2226 זֶרַח",
    2197: "Ζαχαρίας (Zacharías | dzakh-ar-ee'-as)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H2148)\nStrong's: Zacharias (i.e. Zechariah), the name of two Israelites\nKJV: —Zacharias.\nSee: H2148\n\nCognate Group: G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)\nVariants: Ζαχαρίας \nHebrew Equivalents: H2148 זְכַרְיָה",
    2198: "ζάω (záō | dzah'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to live (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —life(-time), (a-)live(-ly), quick.\n\nCognate Group: G2190 (enemy), G2198 (life)\nVariants: ζάω, ζῶ \nHebrew Equivalents: H2421 חָיָה",
    2199: "Ζεβεδαῖος (Zebedaîos | dzeb-ed-ah'-yos)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (compare H2067)\nStrong's: Zebedæus, an Israelite\nKJV: —Zebedee.\nSee: H2067\n\nCognate Group: G2190 (enemy), G2198 (life)\nVariants: Ζεβεδαῖος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2067 זַבְדִּי",
    2200: "ζεστός (zestós | dzes-tos')\n\nDerivation: from G2204\nStrong's: boiled, i.e. (by implication) calid (figuratively, fervent)\nKJV: —hot.\n\nSee: G2204 \n\nCognate Group: G2200 (hot), G2204 (be fervent)\nVariants: ζεστός",
    2201: "ζεῦγος (zeûgos | dzyoo'-gos)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2218\nStrong's: a couple, i.e. a team (of oxen yoked together) or brace (of birds tied together)\nKJV: —yoke, pair.\n\nSee: G2218 \n\nCognate Group: G2200 (hot), G2204 (be fervent)\nVariants: ζεῦγος \nHebrew Equivalents: H6187 עֵרֶךְ, H6776 צֶמֶד, H8147 שְׁנַיִם",
    2202: "ζευκτηρία (zeuktēría | dzook-tay-ree'-ah)\n\nDerivation: feminine of a derivative (at the second stage) from the same as G2218\nStrong's: a fastening (tiller-rope)\nKJV: —band.\n\nSee: G2218 \n\nCognate Group: G2200 (hot), G2204 (be fervent)\nVariants: ζευκτηρία",
    2203: "Ζεύς (Zeús | dzyooce)\n\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: in the oblique cases there is used instead of it a (probably cognate) name Δίς (Dís | deece)\n, which is otherwise obsolete; Zeus or Dis (among the Latins, Jupiter or Jove), the supreme deity of the Greeks\nKJV: —Jupiter.\n\nCognate Group: G2200 (hot), G2204 (be fervent)\nVariants: Ζεύς",
    2204: "ζέω (zéō | dzeh'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to be hot (boil, of liquids; or glow, of solids), i.e. (figuratively) be fervid (earnest)\nKJV: —be fervent.\n\nCognate Group: G2200 (hot), G2204 (be fervent)\nVariants: ζέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7311 רוּם, H7570 רָתַח",
    2205: "ζῆλος (zēlos | dzay'-los)\n\nDerivation: from G2204\nStrong's: properly, heat, i.e. (figuratively) \"zeal\" (in a favorable sense, ardor; in an unfavorable one, jealousy, as of a husband (figuratively, of God), or an enemy, malice)\nKJV: —emulation, envy(-ing), fervent mind, indignation, jealousy, zeal.\n\nSee: G2204 \n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: ζῆλος \nHebrew Equivalents: H7068 קִנְאָה",
    2206: "ζηλόω (zēlóō | dzay-lo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2205\nStrong's: to have warmth of feeling for or against\nKJV: —affect, covet (earnestly), (have) desire, (move with) envy, be jealous over, (be) zealous(-ly affect).\n\nSee: G2205 \n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: ζηλόω, ζηλεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H833 אָשַׁר, H977 בָּחַר, H5006 נָאַץ, H7065 קָנָא",
    2207: "ζηλωτής (zēlōtḗs | dzay-lo-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G2206\nStrong's: a \"zealot\"\nKJV: —zealous.\n\nSee: G2206 \n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: ζηλωτής \nHebrew Equivalents: H7067 קַנָּא, H7072 קַנֹּוא",
    2208: "Ζηλωτής (Zēlōtḗs | dzay-lo-tace')\n\nDerivation: the same as G2207\nStrong's: a Zealot, i.e. (specially) partisan for Jewish political independence\nKJV: —Zelotes.\n\nSee: G2207 \n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: Ζηλωτής, ζηλωτής G2421 \nHebrew Equivalents: H7067 קַנָּא, H7072 קַנֹּוא",
    2209: "ζημία (zēmía | dzay-mee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: probably akin to the base of G1150 (through the idea of violence)\nStrong's: detriment\nKJV: —damage, loss.\n\nSee: G1150 \n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: ζημία \nHebrew Equivalents: H6064 עָנַשׁ, H6066 עֹנֶשׁ",
    2210: "ζημιόω (zēmióō | dzay-mee-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2209\nStrong's: to injure, i.e. (reflexively or passively) to experience detriment\nKJV: —be cast away, receive damage, lose, suffer loss.\n\nSee: G2209 \n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: ζημιόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5375 נָשָׂא, H6064 עָנַשׁ",
    2211: "Ζηνᾶς (Zēnâs | dzay-nas')\n\nDerivation: probably contracted from a poetic form of G2203 and G1435\nStrong's: Jove-given; Zenas, a Christian\nKJV: —Zenas.\n\nSee: G2203 \nSee: G1435 \n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: Ζηνᾶς",
    2212: "ζητέω (zētéō | dzay-teh'-o)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: to seek (literally or figuratively); specially, (by Hebraism) to worship (God), or (in a bad sense) to plot (against life)\nKJV: —be (go) about, desire, endeavour, enquire (for), require, (X will) seek (after, for, means). Compare G4441 .\n\nSee: G4441 \n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: ζητέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H157 אָהַב, H995 בִּין, H1097 בְּלִי, H1156 בְּעָא, H1158 בָּעָה, H1243 בַּקָּרָה, H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H1246 בַּקָּשָׁה, H1875 דָּרַשׁ, H2470 חָלָה, H2658 חָפַר, H4672 מָצָא, H5341 נָצַר, H5921 עַל, H6485 פָּקַד, H6634 צְבָא, H7592 שָׁאַל, H7836 שָׁחַר",
    2213: "ζήτημα (zḗtēma | dzay'-tay-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2212\nStrong's: a search (properly concretely), i.e. (in words) a debate\nKJV: —question.\n\nSee: G2212 \n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: ζήτημα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1875 דָּרַשׁ",
    2214: "ζήτησις (zḗtēsis | dzay'-tay-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G2212\nStrong's: a searching (properly, the act), i.e. a dispute or its theme\nKJV: —question.\n\nSee: G2212 \n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: ζήτησις, ἐκζήτησις",
    2215: "ζιζάνιον (zizánion | dziz-an'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain origin\nStrong's: darnel or false grain\nKJV: —tares.\n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: ζιζάνιον",
    2216: "Ζοροβάβελ (Zorobábel | dzor-ob-ab'-el)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H2216)\nStrong's: Zorobabel (i.e. Zerubbabel), an Israelite\nKJV: —Zorobabel.\nSee: H2216\n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: Ζοροβάβελ, Ζοροβαβέλ \nHebrew Equivalents: H2216 זְרֻבָּבֶל",
    2217: "ζόφος (zóphos | dzof'-os)\n\nDerivation: akin to the base of G3509\nStrong's: gloom (as shrouding like a cloud)\nKJV: —blackness, darkness, mist.\n\nSee: G3509 \n\nCognate Group: G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)\nVariants: ζόφος",
    2218: "ζυγός (zygós | dzoo-gos')\n\nDerivation: from the root of ζεύγνυμι (to join, especially by a \"yoke\")\nStrong's: a coupling, i.e. (figuratively) servitude (a law or obligation); also (literally) the beam of the balance (as connecting the scales)\nKJV: —pair of balances, yoke.\n\nCognate Group: G2218 (pair of balances), G2086 (unequally yoke together with)\nVariants: ζυγός \nHebrew Equivalents: H2908 טְוָת, H3976 מֹאזֵן, H4294 מַטֶּה, H4884 מְשׂוּרָה, H5448 סֹבֶל, H5688 עֲבֹת, H5923 עֹל, H7070 קָנֶה, H7626 שֵׁבֶט, H7926 שְׁכֶם",
    2219: "ζύμη (zýmē | dzoo'-may)\n\nDerivation: probably from G2204\nStrong's: ferment (as if boiling up)\nKJV: —leaven.\n\nSee: G2204 \n\nCognate Group: G2220 (leaven), G2219 (leaven), G106 (unleavened)\nVariants: ζύμη \nHebrew Equivalents: H2557 חָמֵץ, H7603 שְׂאֹר",
    2220: "ζυμόω (zymóō | dzoo-mo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2219\nStrong's: to cause to ferment\nKJV: —leaven.\n\nSee: G2219 \n\nCognate Group: G2220 (leaven), G2219 (leaven), G106 (unleavened)\nVariants: ζυμόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2556 חָמֵץ",
    2221: "ζωγρέω (zōgréō | dzogue-reh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2226 and G64\nStrong's: to take alive (make a prisoner of war), i.e. (figuratively) to capture or ensnare\nKJV: —take captive, catch.\n\nSee: G2226 \nSee: G64 \n\nCognate Group: G2220 (leaven), G2219 (leaven), G106 (unleavened)\nVariants: ζωγρέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2421 חָיָה",
    2222: "ζωή (zōḗ | dzo-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G2198\nStrong's: life (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —life(-time). Compare G5590 .\n\nSee: G2198 \nSee: G5590 \n\nCognate Group: G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)\nVariants: ζωή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H1935 הֹוד, H2247 חָבָה, H2416 חַי, H2421 חָיָה, H2451 חׇכְמָה, H2617 חֵסֵד, H3117 יֹום, H3899 לֶחֶם, H4997 נֹאד",
    2223: "ζώνη (zṓnē | dzo'-nay)\n\nDerivation: probably akin to the base of G2218\nStrong's: a belt; by implication, a pocket\nKJV: —girdle, purse.\n\nSee: G2218 \n\nCognate Group: G2224 (gird), G2223 (girdle), G1241 (gird), G4024 (gird)\nVariants: ζώνη \nHebrew Equivalents: H73 אַבְנֵט, H232 אֵזֹור, H240 אָזֵן, H2290 חֲגֹור, H2290 חֲגֹור, H4206 מָזִיחַ, H7083 קֶסֶת",
    2224: "ζώννυμι (zṓnnymi | dzone'-noo-mi)\n\nDerivation: from G2223\nStrong's: to bind about (especially with a belt)\nKJV: —gird.\n\nSee: G2223 \n\nCognate Group: G2224 (gird), G2223 (girdle), G1241 (gird), G4024 (gird)\nVariants: ζώννυμι, ζωννύω, ζώννυμι/ζωννύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H247 אָזַר, H631 אָסַר, H2280 חָבַשׁ, H2296 חָגַר, H7760 שׂוּם",
    2225: "ζωογονέω (zōogonéō | dzo-og-on-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2226 and a derivative of G1096\nStrong's: to engender alive, i.e. (by analogy) to rescue (passively, be saved) from death\nKJV: —live, preserve.\n\nSee: G2226 \nSee: G1096 \n\nCognate Group: G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)\nVariants: ζωογονέω, ζῳογονέω, ζώογονέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2416 חַי, H2421 חָיָה",
    2226: "ζῶον (zōon | dzo'-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a derivative of G2198\nStrong's: a live thing, i.e. an animal\nKJV: —beast.\n\nSee: G2198 \n\nCognate Group: G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)\nVariants: ζῶον, ζῷον \nHebrew Equivalents: H2416 חַי",
    2227: "ζωοποιέω (zōopoiéō | dzo-op-oy-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2226 and G4160\nStrong's: to (re-)vitalize (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —make alive, give life, quicken.\n\nSee: G2226 \nSee: G4160 \n\nCognate Group: G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)\nVariants: ζωοποιέω, ζῳοποιέω, ζώοποιέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2421 חָיָה",
    2228: "ἤ (ḗ | ay)\n\nDerivation: a primary particle of distinction between two connected terms\nStrong's: disjunctive, or; comparative, than\nKJV: —and, but (either), (n-)either, except it be, (n-)or (else), rather, save, than, that, what, yea. Often used in connection with other particles. Compare especially G2235, G2260, G2273 .\n\nSee: G2235 \nSee: G2260 \nSee: G2273 \n\nCognate Group: G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)\nVariants: ἤ",
    2229: "ἦ (ē | ay)\n\nDerivation: an adverb of confirmation; perhaps intensive of G2228 ; used only (in the New Testament) before G3303\nStrong's: assuredly\nKJV: —surely.\n\nSee: G2228 \nSee: G3303 \n\nCognate Group: G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)\nVariants: ἦ, εἰ μήν, ἦ μήν G1623, G1638, G2446, G2447",
    2230: "ἡγεμονεύω (hēgemoneúō | hayg-em-on-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2232\nStrong's: to act as ruler\nKJV: —be governor.\n\nSee: G2232 \n\nCognate Group: G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)\nVariants: ἡγεμονεύω",
    2231: "ἡγεμονία (hēgemonía | hayg-em-on-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2232\nStrong's: government, i.e. (in time) official term\nKJV: —reign.\n\nSee: G2232 \n\nCognate Group: G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)\nVariants: ἡγεμονία \nHebrew Equivalents: H441 אַלּוּף, H1714 דֶּגֶל",
    2232: "ἡγεμών (hēgemṓn | hayg-em-ohn')\n\nDerivation: from G2233\nStrong's: a leader, i.e. chief person (or figuratively, place) of a province\nKJV: —governor, prince, ruler.\n\nSee: G2233 \n\nCognate Group: G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)\nVariants: ἡγεμών \nHebrew Equivalents: H410 אֵל, H441 אַלּוּף, H6346 פֶּחָה, H7277 רִגְמָה, H8269 שַׂר",
    2233: "ἡγέομαι (hēgéomai | hayg-eh'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice of a (presumed) strengthened form of G71\nStrong's: to lead, i.e. command (with official authority); figuratively, to deem, i.e. consider\nKJV: —account, (be) chief, count, esteem, governor, judge, have the rule over, suppose, think.\n\nSee: G71 \n\nCognate Group: G4285 (prefer), G2233 (account), G1834 (declare), G1335 (declaration)\nVariants: ἡγέομαι, ἐπιτροπεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H136 אֲדֹנָי, H148 אֲדַרְגָּזֵר, H191 אֱוִיל, H376 אִישׁ, H410 אֵל, H441 אַלּוּף, H802 אִשָּׁה, H1167 בַּעַל, H1172 בַּעֲלָה, H1377 גְּבִירָה, H1696 דָבַר, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2015 הָפַךְ, H2710 חָקַק, H2803 חָשַׁב, H3384 יָרָה, H3988 מָאַס, H4428 מֶלֶךְ, H4606 מֵעָל, H4911 מָשַׁל, H5057 נָגִיד, H5139 נָזִיר, H5162 נָחַם, H5333 נְצִיב, H5387 נָשִׂיא, H5461 סָגָן, H5971 עַם, H6040 עֳנִי, H6346 פֶּחָה, H7101 קָצִין, H7218 רֹאשׁ, H7704 שָׂדֶה, H7760 שׂוּם, H8269 שַׂר, H8308 שָׂרַךְ",
    2234: "ἡδέως (hēdéōs | hay-deh'-oce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from a derivative of the base of G2237\nStrong's: sweetly, i.e. (figuratively) with pleasure\nKJV: —gladly.\n\nSee: G2237 \n\nCognate Group: G4285 (prefer), G2233 (account), G1834 (declare), G1335 (declaration)\nVariants: ἡδέως \nHebrew Equivalents: H2896 טֹוב, H5276 נָעֵם, H6148 עָרַב",
    2235: "ἤδη (ḗdē | ay'-day)\n\nDerivation: apparently from G2228 (or possibly G2229) and G1211\nStrong's: even now\nKJV: —already, (even) now (already), by this time.\n\nSee: G2228 \nSee: G2229 \nSee: G1211 \n\nCognate Group: G4285 (prefer), G2233 (account), G1834 (declare), G1335 (declaration)\nVariants: ἤδη",
    2236: "ἥδιστα (hḗdista | hay'-dis-tah)\n\nDerivation: neuter plural of the superlative of the same as G2234\nStrong's: with great pleasure\nKJV: —most (very) gladly.\n\nSee: G2234 \n\nCognate Group: G4285 (prefer), G2233 (account), G1834 (declare), G1335 (declaration)\nVariants: ἥδιστα, ἡδέως",
    2237: "ἡδονή (hēdonḗ | hay-don-ay')\n\nDerivation: from ἁνδάνω (to please)\nStrong's: sensual delight; by implication, desire\nKJV: —lust, pleasure.\n\nCognate Group: G5369 (lover of pleasure), G2237 (lust)\nVariants: ἡδονή \nHebrew Equivalents: H2940 טַעַם, H7879 שִׂיחַ",
    2238: "ἡδύοσμον (hēdýosmon | hay-doo'-os-mon)\n\nDerivation: neuter of the compound of the same as G2234 and G3744\nStrong's: a sweet-scented plant, i.e. mint\nKJV: —mint.\n\nSee: G2234 \nSee: G3744 \n\nCognate Group: G5369 (lover of pleasure), G2237 (lust)\nVariants: ἡδύοσμον",
    2239: "ἦθος (ēthos | ay'-thos)\n\nDerivation: a strengthened form of G1485\nStrong's: usage, i.e. (plural) moral habits\nKJV: —manners.\n\nSee: G1485 \n\nCognate Group: G5369 (lover of pleasure), G2237 (lust)\nVariants: ἦθος, ὴθος",
    2240: "ἥκω (hḗkō | hay'-ko)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to arrive, i.e. be present (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —come.\n\nCognate Group: G2240 (come)\nVariants: ἥκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2342 חוּל, H2778 חָרַף, H3318 יָצָא, H5102 נָהַר, H5674 עָבַר, H5844 עָטָה, H5927 עָלָה, H5975 עָמַד, H6965 קוּם, H7725 שׁוּב, H7931 שָׁכַן, H8334 שָׁרַת",
    2241: "ἠλί (ēlí | ay-lee')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H410 with pronominal suffix)\nStrong's: my God\nKJV: — Eli.\nSee: H410\n\nCognate Group: G2240 (come)\nVariants: ἠλί, ἠλί1, ηλι, Ἠλί \nHebrew Equivalents: H410 אֵל, H5940 עֱלִי",
    2242: "Ἡλί (Hēlí | hay-lee')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H5941)\nStrong's: Heli (i.e. Eli), an Israelite\nKJV: —Heli.\nSee: H5941\n\nCognate Group: G2240 (come)\nVariants: Ἡλί, Ἠλί2 \nHebrew Equivalents: H5941 עֵלִי",
    2243: "Ἡλίας (Hēlías | hay-lee'-as)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H452)\nStrong's: Helias (i.e. Elijah), an Israelite\nKJV: —Elias.\nSee: H452\n\nCognate Group: G2243 (Elias)\nVariants: Ἡλίας, Ἠλίας \nHebrew Equivalents: H452 אֵלִיָּה",
    2244: "ἡλικία (hēlikía | hay-lik-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2245\nStrong's: maturity (in years or size)\nKJV: —age, stature.\n\nSee: G2245 \n\nCognate Group: G2244 (age)\nVariants: ἡλικία \nHebrew Equivalents: H1524 גִּיל, H6967 קֹומָה",
    2245: "ἡλίκος (hēlíkos | hay-lee'-kos)\n\nDerivation: from ἧλιξ (a comrade, i.e. one of the same age)\nStrong's: as big as, i.e. (interjectively) how much\nKJV: —how (what) great.\n\nCognate Group: G2244 (age)\nVariants: ἡλίκος",
    2246: "ἥλιος (hḗlios | hay'-lee-os)\n\nDerivation: from ἕλη (a ray\nStrong's: perhaps akin to the alternate of G138); the sun; by implication, light\nKJV: —+ east, sun.\n\nSee: G138 \n\nCognate Group: G2244 (age)\nVariants: ἥλιος \nHebrew Equivalents: H202 אֹון, H216 אֹור, H268 אָחֹור, H2535 חַמָּה, H2789 חֶרֶשׂ, H4217 מִזְרָח, H6924 קֶדֶם, H8064 שָׁמַיִם, H8121 שֶׁמֶשׁ, H8122 שֶׁמֶשׁ",
    2247: "ἧλος (hēlos | hay'-los)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a stud, i.e. spike\nKJV: —nail.\n\nCognate Group: G2244 (age)\nVariants: ἧλος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4212 מְזַמְּרָה, H4548 מַסְמֵר, H4548 מַסְמֵר, H7850 שֹׁטֵט",
    2248: "ἡμᾶς (hēmâs | hay-mas')\n\nDerivation: accusative case plural of G1473\nStrong's: us\nKJV: —our, us, we.\n\nSee: G1473 \n\nCognate Group: G2244 (age)\nVariants: ἡμᾶς, ἐγώ",
    2249: "ἡμεῖς (hēmeîs | hay-mice')\n\nDerivation: nominative plural of G1473\nStrong's: we (only used when emphatic)\nKJV: —us, we (ourselves).\n\nSee: G1473 \n\nCognate Group: G2244 (age)\nVariants: ἡμεῖς, ἐγώ",
    2250: "ἡμέρα (hēméra | hay-mer'-ah)\n\nDerivation: feminine (with G5610 implied) of a derivative of ἧμαι (to sit; akin to the base of G1476) meaning tame, i.e. gentle\nStrong's: day, i.e. (literally) the time space between dawn and dark, or the whole 24 hours (but several days were usually reckoned by the Jews as inclusive of the parts of both extremes); figuratively, a period (always defined more or less clearly by the context)\nKJV: —age, + alway, (mid-)day (by day, (-ly)), + for ever, judgment, (day) time, while, years.\n\nSee: G5610 \nSee: G1476 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἡμέρα \nHebrew Equivalents: H216 אֹור, H343 אֵיד, H819 אַשְׁמָה, H865 אֶתְמֹול, H1242 בֹּקֶר, H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H2320 חֹדֶשׁ, H2527 חֹם, H3117 יֹום, H3117 יֹום, H3117 יֹום, H3117 יֹום, H3119 יֹומָם, H3224 יְמִימָה, H3409 יָרֵךְ, H4325 מַיִם, H5794 עַז, H5844 עָטָה, H6153 עֶרֶב, H6256 עֵת, H6965 קוּם, H7307 רוּחַ, H7657 שִׁבְעִים, H8032 שִׁלְשֹׁום, H8543 תְּמֹול",
    2251: "ἡμέτερος (hēméteros | hay-met'-er-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2349\nStrong's: our\nKJV: —our, your (by a different reading).\n\nSee: G2349 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἡμέτερος",
    2252: "ἤμην (ḗmēn | ay'-mane)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of G2258\nStrong's: I was\nKJV: —be, was. (Sometimes unexpressed).\n\nSee: G2258 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἤμην, εἰμί",
    2253: "ἡμιθανής (hēmithanḗs | hay-mee-than-ace')\n\nDerivation: from a presumed compound of the base of G2255 and G2348\nStrong's: half dead, i.e. entirely exhausted\nKJV: —half dead.\n\nSee: G2255 \nSee: G2348 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἡμιθανής",
    2254: "ἡμῖν (hēmîn | hay-meen')\n\nDerivation: dative case plural of G1473\nStrong's: to (or for, with, by) us\nKJV: —our, (for) us, we.\n\nSee: G1473 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἡμῖν, ἐγώ",
    2255: "ἥμισυ (hḗmisy | hay'-mee-soo)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a derivative from an inseparable prefix akin to G260 (through the idea of partition involved in connection) and meaning semi-\nStrong's: (as noun) half\nKJV: —half.\n\nSee: G260 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἥμισυ, ἥμισυς \nHebrew Equivalents: H2677 חֵצִי, H4276 מַחֲצִית, H6386 פְּלַג",
    2256: "ἡμιώριον (hēmiṓrion | hay-mee-o'-ree-on)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G2255 and G5610\nStrong's: a half-hour\nKJV: —half an hour.\n\nSee: G2255 \nSee: G5610 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἡμιώριον, ἡμίωρος",
    2257: "ἡμῶν (hēmōn | hay-mone')\n\nDerivation: genitive case plural of G1473\nStrong's: of (or from) us\nKJV: —our (company), us, we.\n\nSee: G1473 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἡμῶν, ἐγώ",
    2258: "ἦν (ēn | ane)\n\nDerivation: imperfect of G1510\nStrong's: I (thou, etc.) was (wast or were)\nKJV: —+ agree, be, X have (+ charge of), hold, use, was(-t), were.\n\nSee: G1510 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἦν, εἰμί",
    2259: "ἡνίκα (hēníka | hay-nee'-kah)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: at which time\nKJV: —when.\n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἡνίκα",
    2260: "ἤπερ (ḗper | ay'-per)\n\nDerivation: from G2228 and G4007\nStrong's: than at all (or than perhaps, than indeed)\nKJV: —than.\n\nSee: G2228 \nSee: G4007 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἤπερ",
    2261: "ἤπιος (ḗpios | ay'-pee-os)\n\nDerivation: probably from G2031\nStrong's: properly, affable, i.e. mild or kind\nKJV: —gentle.\n\nSee: G2031 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἤπιος",
    2262: "Ἤρ (Ḗr | ayr)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H6147)\nStrong's: Er, an Israelite\nKJV: —Er.\nSee: H6147\n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: Ἤρ, ̓́Ηρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H6147 עֵר",
    2263: "ἤρεμος (ḗremos | ay'-rem-os)\n\nDerivation: perhaps by transposition from G2048 (through the idea of stillness)\nStrong's: tranquil\nKJV: —quiet.\n\nSee: G2048 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: ἤρεμος",
    2264: "Ἡρώδης (Hērṓdēs | hay-ro'-dace)\n\nDerivation: compound of ἥρως (a \"hero\") and G1491\nStrong's: heroic; Herod, the name of four Jewish kings\nKJV: —Herod.\n\nSee: G1491 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: Ἡρώδης, Ἡρῴδης",
    2265: "Ἡρωδιανοί (Hērōdianoí | hay-ro-dee-an-oy')\n\nDerivation: plural of a derivative of G2264\nStrong's: Herodians, i.e. partisans of Herod\nKJV: —Herodians.\n\nSee: G2264 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: Ἡρωδιανοί, Ἡρῳδιανοί, Ἡρώδιανοί",
    2266: "Ἡρωδιάς (Hērōdiás | hay-ro-dee-as')\n\nDerivation: from G2264\nStrong's: Herodias, a woman of the Heodian family\nKJV: —Herodias.\n\nSee: G2264 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: Ἡρωδιάς, Ἡρῳδιάς, Ἡρώδιάς",
    2267: "Ἡρωδίων (Hērōdíōn | hay-ro-dee'-ohn)\n\nDerivation: from G2264\nStrong's: Herodion, a Christian\nKJV: —Herodion.\n\nSee: G2264 \n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: Ἡρωδίων, Ἡρῳδίων, Ἡρώδίων",
    2268: "Ἡσαΐας (Hēsaḯas | hay-sah-ee'-as)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3470)\nStrong's: Hesaias (i.e. Jeshajah), an Israelite\nKJV: —Esaias.\nSee: H3470\n\nCognate Group: G2250 (age)\nVariants: Ἡσαΐας, Ἠσαί̈ας, Ἠσαΐας \nHebrew Equivalents: H3470 יְשַׁעְיָה",
    2269: "Ἠσαῦ (Ēsaû | ay-sow')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H6215)\nStrong's: Esau, an Edomite\nKJV: —Esau.\nSee: H6215\n\nCognate Group: G2269 (Esau)\nVariants: Ἠσαῦ \nHebrew Equivalents: H6215 עֵשָׂו",
    2270: "ἡσυχάζω (hēsycházō | hay-soo-khad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2272\nStrong's: to keep still (intransitively), i.e. refrain from labor, meddlesomeness or speech\nKJV: —cease, hold peace, be quiet, rest.\n\nSee: G2272 \n\nCognate Group: G2269 (Esau)\nVariants: ἡσυχάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1748 דּוּמָם, H2119 זָחַל, H2308 חָדַל, H2790 חָרַשׁ, H2814 חָשָׁה, H3427 יָשַׁב, H7257 רָבַץ, H7600 שַׁאֲנָן, H7673 שָׁבַת, H7931 שָׁכַן, H8252 שָׁקַט, H8257 שָׁקַע, H8268 שֹׁקֶת, H8367 שָׁתַק",
    2271: "ἡσυχία (hēsychía | hay-soo-khee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: feminine of G2272\nStrong's: (as noun) stillness, i.e. desistance from bustle or language\nKJV: —quietness, silence.\n\nSee: G2272 \n\nCognate Group: G2269 (Esau)\nVariants: ἡσυχία \nHebrew Equivalents: H308 אֲחַסְבַּי, H983 בֶּטַח, H2790 חָרַשׁ, H7961 שָׁלֵו, H8252 שָׁקַט, H8552 תָּמַם",
    2272: "ἡσύχιος (hēsýchios | hay-soo'-khee-os)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of a compound probably of a derivative of the base of G1476 and perhaps G2192\nStrong's: properly, keeping one's seat (sedentary), i.e. (by implication) still (undisturbed, undisturbing)\nKJV: —peaceable, quiet.\n\nSee: G1476 \nSee: G2192 \n\nCognate Group: G2269 (Esau)\nVariants: ἡσύχιος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5222 נֵכֶה",
    2273: "ἤτοι (ḗtoi | ay'-toy)\n\nDerivation: from G2228 and G5104\nStrong's: either indeed\nKJV: —whether.\n\nSee: G2228 \nSee: G5104 \n\nCognate Group: G2269 (Esau)\nVariants: ἤτοι",
    2274: "ἡττάω (hēttáō | hayt-tah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2276\nStrong's: to make worse, i.e. vanquish (literally or figuratively); by implication, to rate lower\nKJV: —be inferior, overcome.\n\nSee: G2276 \n\nCognate Group: G2269 (Esau)\nVariants: ἡττάω, ἑσσόομαι, ἡττάομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H898 בָּגַד, H1856 דָּקַר, H2865 חָתַת, H4549 מָסַס, H7561 רָשַׁע",
    2275: "ἥττημα (hḗttēma | hayt'-tay-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2274\nStrong's: a deterioration, i.e. (objectively) failure or (subjectively) loss\nKJV: —diminishing, fault.\n\nSee: G2274 \n\nCognate Group: G2269 (Esau)\nVariants: ἥττημα \nHebrew Equivalents: H4522 מַס",
    2276: "ἥττον (hḗtton | hate'-ton)\n\nDerivation: neuter of comparative of ἧκα (slightly) used for that of G2556\nStrong's: worse (as noun); by implication, less (as adverb)\nKJV: —less, worse.\n\nSee: G2556 \n\nCognate Group: G2269 (Esau)\nVariants: ἥττον, ἥσσων, ἥττων, ἥσσων/ἥττων, ἧττων",
    2277: "ἤτω (ḗtō | ay'-to)\n\nDerivation: third person singular imperative of G1510\nStrong's: let him (or it) be\nKJV: —let … be.\n\nSee: G1510 \n\nCognate Group: G2269 (Esau)\nVariants: ἤτω, εἰμί",
    2278: "ἠχέω (ēchéō | ay-kheh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2279\nStrong's: to make a loud noise, i.e. reverberate\nKJV: —roar, sound.\n\nSee: G2279 \n\nCognate Group: G2278 (roar)\nVariants: ἠχέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1949 הוּם, H1993 הָמָה, H2388 חָזַק, H2689 חֲצֹצְרָה, H6750 צָלַל, H7582 שָׁאָה",
    2279: "ἦχος (ēchos | ay'-khos)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a loud or confused noise (\"echo\"), i.e. roar; figuratively, a rumor\nKJV: —fame, sound.\n\nCognate Group: G2278 (roar)\nVariants: ἦχος, ἦχοσ1, ἦχοσ2, ἠχώ, ὴχος \nHebrew Equivalents: H255 אֹחַ, H1995 הָמֹון, H7588 שָׁאֹון, H8628 תָּקַע",
    2280: "Θαδδαῖος (Thaddaîos | thad-dah'-yos)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain origin\nStrong's: Thaddæus, one of the Apostles\nKJV: —Thaddæus.\n\nCognate Group: G2278 (roar)\nVariants: Θαδδαῖος",
    2281: "θάλασσα (thálassa | thal'-as-sah)\n\nDerivation: probably prolonged from G251\nStrong's: the sea (genitive case or specially)\nKJV: —sea.\n\nSee: G251 \n\nCognate Group: G2278 (roar)\nVariants: θάλασσα, Θάλασσα \nHebrew Equivalents: H339 אִי, H3220 יָם, H3225 יָמִין, H4310 מִי, H8486 תֵּימָן, H8585 תְּעָלָה, H8658 תַּרְשִׁישׁ",
    2282: "θάλπω (thálpō | thal'-po)\n\nDerivation: probably akin to θάλλω (to warm)\nStrong's: to brood, i.e. (figuratively) to foster\nKJV: —cherish.\n\nCognate Group: G2278 (roar)\nVariants: θάλπω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2552 חָמַם, H5532 סָכַן, H7257 רָבַץ",
    2283: "Θάμαρ (Thámar | tham'-ar)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H8559)\nStrong's: Thamar (i.e. Tamar), an Israelitess\nKJV: —Thamar.\nSee: H8559\n\nCognate Group: G2283 (Thamar)\nVariants: Θάμαρ, Θαμάρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H8559 תָּמָר",
    2284: "θαμβέω (thambéō | tham-beh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2285\nStrong's: to stupefy (with surprise), i.e. astound\nKJV: —amaze, astonish.\n\nSee: G2285 \n\nCognate Group: G1568 (affright), G1569 (greatly wondering), G2284 (amaze), G2285 (X amazed)\nVariants: θαμβέω, θαμβέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1204 בָּעַת, H2648 חָפַז, H6348 פָּחַז, H7264 רָגַז, H7290 רָדַם",
    2285: "θάμβος (thámbos | tham'-bos)\n\nDerivation: akin to an obsolete τάφω (to dumbfound)\nStrong's: stupefaction (by surprise), i.e. astonishment\nKJV: —X amazed, + astonished, wonder.\n\nCognate Group: G1568 (affright), G1569 (greatly wondering), G2284 (amaze), G2285 (X amazed)\nVariants: θάμβος \nHebrew Equivalents: H366 אָיֹם, H2849 חַתְחַת, H6343 פַּחַד, H6427 פַּלָּצוּת, H8639 תַּרְדֵּמָה",
    2286: "θανάσιμος (thanásimos | than-as'-ee-mos)\n\nDerivation: from G2288\nStrong's: fatal, i.e. poisonous\nKJV: —deadly.\n\nSee: G2288 \n\nCognate Group: G1568 (affright), G1569 (greatly wondering), G2284 (amaze), G2285 (X amazed)\nVariants: θανάσιμος, θανάσιμον",
    2287: "θανατήφορος (thanatḗphoros | than-at-ay'-for-os)\n\nDerivation: from (the feminine form of) G2288 and G5342\nStrong's: death-bearing, i.e. fatal\nKJV: —deadly.\n\nSee: G2288 \nSee: G5342 \n\nCognate Group: G1568 (affright), G1569 (greatly wondering), G2284 (amaze), G2285 (X amazed)\nVariants: θανατήφορος, θανατηφόρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4191 מוּת",
    2288: "θάνατος (thánatos | than'-at-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2348\nStrong's: (properly, an adjective used as a noun) death (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —X deadly, (be…) death.\n\nSee: G2348 \n\nCognate Group: G4880 (be dead with), G2289 (become dead), G2348 (be dead), G2288 (X deadly), G599 (be dead), G2349 (mortal), G110 (immortality)\nVariants: θάνατος, ἀθάνατος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1565 גַּלְמוּד, H1698 דֶּבֶר, H4112 מַהֲלֻמָּה, H4191 מוּת, H4191 מוּת, H4273 מַחַץ, H4688 מְצֹולָה, H6757 צַלְמָוֶת, H6913 קֶבֶר, H7585 שְׁאֹול, H7845 שַׁחַת",
    2289: "θανατόω (thanatóō | than-at-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2288 to kill (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —become dead, (cause to be) put to death, kill, mortify.\n\nSee: G2288 \n\nCognate Group: G4880 (be dead with), G2289 (become dead), G2348 (be dead), G2288 (X deadly), G599 (be dead), G2349 (mortal), G110 (immortality)\nVariants: θανατόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1698 דֶּבֶר, H2026 הָרַג, H2490 חָלַל, H4191 מוּת, H4191 מוּת, H5221 נָכָה, H6293 פָּגַע, H6789 צָמַת, H6848 צֶפַע, H8313 שָׂרַף",
    2290: "θάπτω (tháptō | thap'-to)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to celebrate funeral rites, i.e. inter\nKJV: —bury.\n\nCognate Group: G4880 (be dead with), G2289 (become dead), G2348 (be dead), G2288 (X deadly), G599 (be dead), G2349 (mortal), G110 (immortality)\nVariants: θάπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2590 חָנַט, H6912 קָבַר",
    2291: "Θάρα (Thára | thar'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H8646)\nStrong's: Thara (i.e. Terach), the father of Abraham\nKJV: —Thara.\nSee: H8646\n\nCognate Group: G4880 (be dead with), G2289 (become dead), G2348 (be dead), G2288 (X deadly), G599 (be dead), G2349 (mortal), G110 (immortality)\nVariants: Θάρα \nHebrew Equivalents: H8646 תֶּרַח",
    2292: "θαῤῥέω (tharrhéō | thar-hreh'-o)\n\nDerivation: another form for G2293\nStrong's: to exercise courage\nKJV: —be bold, X boldly, have confidence, be confident. Compare G5111 .\n\nSee: G2293 \nSee: G5111 \n\nCognate Group: G2293 (be of good cheer), G2292 (be bold)\nVariants: θαῤῥέω, θαρρέω",
    2293: "θαρσέω (tharséō | thar-seh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2294\nStrong's: to have courage\nKJV: —be of good cheer (comfort). Compare G2292 .\n\nSee: G2294 \nSee: G2292 \n\nCognate Group: G2293 (be of good cheer), G2292 (be bold)\nVariants: θαρσέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H561 אֵמֶר, H982 בָּטַח, H3372 יָרֵא",
    2294: "θάρσος (thársos | thar'-sos)\n\nDerivation: akin (by transposition) to θράσος (daring)\nStrong's: boldness (subjectively)\nKJV: —courage.\n\nCognate Group: G2293 (be of good cheer), G2292 (be bold)\nVariants: θάρσος",
    2295: "θαῦμα (thaûma | thos'-mah)\n\nDerivation: apparently from a form of G2300\nStrong's: wonder (properly concrete; but by implication, abstract)\nKJV: —admiration.\n\nSee: G2300 \n\nCognate Group: G2297 (wonderful thing), G2296 (admire), G2295 (admiration), G2298 (marvel)\nVariants: θαῦμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H2384 חִזָּיֹון, H8074 שָׁמֵם, H8178 שַׂעַר",
    2296: "θαυμάζω (thaumázō | thou-mad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2295\nStrong's: to wonder; by implication, to admire\nKJV: —admire, have in admiration, marvel, wonder.\n\nSee: G2295 \n\nCognate Group: G2297 (wonderful thing), G2296 (admire), G2295 (admiration), G2298 (marvel)\nVariants: θαυμάζω, ἐκθαυμάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1921 הָדַר, H2904 טוּל, H3235 יָמַר, H3655 כָּנָה, H4911 מָשַׁל, H5137 נָזָה, H5162 נָחַם, H5375 נָשָׂא, H7688 שָׁגַח, H8074 שָׁמֵם, H8159 שָׁעָה, H8392 תֵּבָה, H8539 תָּמַהּ",
    2297: "θαυμάσιος (thaumásios | thow-mas'-ee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2295\nStrong's: wondrous, i.e. (neuter as noun) a miracle\nKJV: —wonderful thing.\n\nSee: G2295 \n\nCognate Group: G2297 (wonderful thing), G2296 (admire), G2295 (admiration), G2298 (marvel)\nVariants: θαυμάσιος \nHebrew Equivalents: H226 אֹות, H4172 מֹורָא, H6381 פָּלָא, H8539 תָּמַהּ",
    2298: "θαυμαστός (thaumastós | thow-mas-tos')\n\nDerivation: from G2296\nStrong's: wondered at, i.e. (by implication) wonderful\nKJV: —marvel(-lous).\n\nSee: G2296 \n\nCognate Group: G2297 (wonderful thing), G2296 (admire), G2295 (admiration), G2298 (marvel)\nVariants: θαυμαστός \nHebrew Equivalents: H117 אַדִּיר, H3372 יָרֵא, H4103 מְהוּמָה, H6004 עָמַם, H6381 פָּלָא, H6382 פֶּלֶא",
    2299: "θεά (theá | theh-ah')\n\nDerivation: feminine of G2316\nStrong's: a female deity\nKJV: —goddess.\n\nSee: G2316 \n\nCognate Group: G2297 (wonderful thing), G2296 (admire), G2295 (admiration), G2298 (marvel)\nVariants: θεά",
    2300: "θεάομαι (theáomai | theh-ah'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of a primary verb\nStrong's: to look closely at, i.e. (by implication) perceive (literally or figuratively); by extension to visit\nKJV: —behold, look (upon), see. Compare G3700 .\n\nSee: G3700 \n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: θεάομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H7200 רָאָה",
    2301: "θεατρίζω (theatrízō | theh-at-rid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2302\nStrong's: to expose as a spectacle\nKJV: —make a gazing stock.\n\nSee: G2302 \n\nCognate Group: G2302 (spectacle), G2301 (make a gazing stock)\nVariants: θεατρίζω",
    2302: "θέατρον (théatron | theh'-at-ron)\n\nDerivation: from G2300\nStrong's: a place for public show (\"theatre\"), i.e. general audience-room; by implication, a show itself (figuratively)\nKJV: —spectacle, theatre.\n\nSee: G2300 \n\nCognate Group: G2302 (spectacle), G2301 (make a gazing stock)\nVariants: θέατρον",
    2303: "θεῖον (theîon | thi'-on)\n\nDerivation: probably neuter of G2304 (in its original sense of flashing)\nStrong's: sulphur\nKJV: —brimstone.\n\nSee: G2304 \n\nCognate Group: G2302 (spectacle), G2301 (make a gazing stock)\nVariants: θεῖον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1614 גׇּפְרִית",
    2304: "θεῖος (theîos | thi'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2316\nStrong's: godlike (neuter as noun, divinity)\nKJV: — divine, godhead.\n\nSee: G2316 \n\nCognate Group: G2312 (taught of God), G2320 (godhead), G2304 (divine), G2316 (X exceeding), G2305 (godhead), G112 (without God)\nVariants: θεῖος \nHebrew Equivalents: H410 אֵל, H430 אֱלֹהִים, H433 אֱלֹוהַּ",
    2305: "θειότης (theiótēs | thi-ot'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G2304\nStrong's: divinity (abstractly)\nKJV: —godhead.\n\nSee: G2304 \n\nCognate Group: G2312 (taught of God), G2320 (godhead), G2304 (divine), G2316 (X exceeding), G2305 (godhead), G112 (without God)\nVariants: θειότης",
    2306: "θειώδης (theiṓdēs | thi-o'-dace)\n\nDerivation: from G2303 and 1491\nStrong's: sulphur-like, i.e. sulphurous\nKJV: —brimstone.\n\nSee: G2303 \n\nCognate Group: G2312 (taught of God), G2320 (godhead), G2304 (divine), G2316 (X exceeding), G2305 (godhead), G112 (without God)\nVariants: θειώδης",
    2307: "θέλημα (thélēma | thel'-ay-mah)\n\nDerivation: from the prolonged form of G2309\nStrong's: a determination (properly, the thing), i.e. (actively) choice (specially, purpose, decree; abstractly, volition) or (passively) inclination\nKJV: — desire, pleasure, will.\n\nSee: G2309 \n\nCognate Group: G2307 (desire), G2308 (will), G2309 (desire)\nVariants: θέλημα \nHebrew Equivalents: H2655 חָפֵץ, H5949 עֲלִילָה, H6634 צְבָא, H7522 רָצֹון, H7891 שִׁיר, H8307 שְׁרִירוּת, H8649 תׇּרְמָה",
    2308: "θέλησις (thélēsis | thel'-ay-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G2309\nStrong's: determination (properly, the act), i.e. option\nKJV: —will.\n\nSee: G2309 \n\nCognate Group: G2307 (desire), G2308 (will), G2309 (desire)\nVariants: θέλησις \nHebrew Equivalents: H782 אֲרֶשֶׁת, H2656 חֵפֶץ, H6643 צְבִי, H7522 רָצֹון",
    2309: "θέλω (thélō | thel'-o) or ἐθέλω (ethélō | eth-el'-o), in certain tenses θελέω (theléō | thel-eh'-o), and ἐθελέω (etheléō | eth-el-eh'-o)\n\n, which are otherwise obsolete\n\nDerivation: apparently strengthened from the alternate form of G138\nStrong's: to determine (as an active option from subjective impulse; whereas G1014 properly denotes rather a passive acquiescence in objective considerations), i.e. choose or prefer (literally or figuratively); by implication, to wish, i.e. be inclined to (sometimes adverbially, gladly); impersonally for the future tense, to be about to; by Hebraism, to delight in\nKJV: —desire, be disposed (forward), intend, list, love, mean, please, have rather, (be) will (have, -ling, - ling(-ly)).\n\nSee: G138 \nSee: G1014 \n\nCognate Group: G2307 (desire), G2308 (will), G2309 (desire)\nVariants: θέλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H935 בֹּוא, H1819 דָּמָה, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2308 חָדַל, H2654 חָפֵץ, H3245 יָסַד, H3985 מָאֵן, H5753 עָוָה, H5753 עָוָה, H6004 עָמַם, H6634 צְבָא, H7200 רָאָה, H7521 רָצָה",
    2310: "θεμέλιος (themélios | them-el'-ee-os)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G5087\nStrong's: something put down, i.e. a substruction (of a building, etc.), (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —foundation.\n\nSee: G5087 \n\nCognate Group: G2310 (foundation), G2311 (found)\nVariants: θεμέλιος, θεμέλιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H759 אַרְמֹון, H787 אֹשׁ, H3245 יָסַד, H3245 יָסַד, H3411 יְרֵכָה, H4144 מֹוסָד, H4725 מָקֹום, H6194 עָרֵם, H8482 תַּחְתִּי",
    2311: "θεμελιόω (themelióō | them-el-ee-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2310\nStrong's: to lay a basis for, i.e. (literally) erect, or (figuratively) consolidate\nKJV: —(lay the) found(- ation), ground, settle.\n\nSee: G2310 \n\nCognate Group: G2310 (foundation), G2311 (found)\nVariants: θεμελιόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1129 בָּנָה, H1280 בְּרִיחַ, H3245 יָסַד, H3559 כּוּן, H5258 נָסַךְ",
    2312: "θεοδίδακτος (theodídaktos | theh-od-id'-ak-tos)\n\nDerivation: from G2316 and G1321\nStrong's: divinely instructed\nKJV: —taught of God.\n\nSee: G2316 \nSee: G1321 \n\nCognate Group: G2312 (taught of God), G2320 (godhead), G2304 (divine), G2316 (X exceeding), G2305 (godhead), G112 (without God)\nVariants: θεοδίδακτος, θεολόγος",
    2313: "θεομαχέω (theomachéō | theh-o-makh-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2314\nStrong's: to resist deity\nKJV: —fight against God.\n\nSee: G2314 \n\nCognate Group: G2314 (to fight against God), G3163 (fighting), G2313 (fight against God), G269 (not a brawler), G3164 (fight)\nVariants: θεομαχέω G2533",
    2314: "θεομάχος (theomáchos | theh-om'-akh-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2316 and G3164\nStrong's: an opponent of deity\nKJV: —to fight against God.\n\nSee: G2316 \nSee: G3164 \n\nCognate Group: G2314 (to fight against God), G3163 (fighting), G2313 (fight against God), G269 (not a brawler), G3164 (fight)\nVariants: θεομάχος",
    2315: "θεόπνευστος (theópneustos | theh-op'-nyoo-stos)\n\nDerivation: from G2316 and a presumed derivative of G4154\nStrong's: divinely breathed in\nKJV: —given by inspiration of God.\n\nSee: G2316 \nSee: G4154 \n\nCognate Group: G4151 (ghost), G2315 (given by inspiration of God), G4154 (blow), G4153 (spiritually), G1606 (give up the ghost), G4152 (spiritual)\nVariants: θεόπνευστος",
    2316: "θεός (theós | theh'-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity; a deity, especially (with G3588) the supreme Divinity\nStrong's: figuratively, a magistrate; by Hebraism, very\nKJV: —X exceeding, God, god(-ly, -ward).\n\nSee: G3588 \n\nCognate Group: G2312 (taught of God), G2320 (godhead), G2304 (divine), G2316 (X exceeding), G2305 (godhead), G112 (without God)\nVariants: θεός \nHebrew Equivalents: H47 אַבִּיר, H136 אֲדֹנָי, H136 אֲדֹנָי, H410 אֵל, H430 אֱלֹהִים, H430 אֱלֹהִים, H433 אֱלֹוהַּ, H457 אֱלִיל, H3068 יְהֹוָה, H5943 עִלַּי, H6091 עָצָב, H6697 צוּר, H6944 קֹדֶשׁ, H7706 שַׁדַּי",
    2317: "θεοσέβεια (theosébeia | theh-os-eb'-i-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2318\nStrong's: devoutness, i.e. piety\nKJV: —godliness.\n\nSee: G2318 \n\nCognate Group: G2317 (godliness), G2318 (worshipper of God)\nVariants: θεοσέβεια",
    2318: "θεοσεβής (theosebḗs | theh-os-eb-ace')\n\nDerivation: from G2316 and G4576\nStrong's: reverent of God, i.e. pious\nKJV: —worshipper of God.\n\nSee: G2316 \nSee: G4576 \n\nCognate Group: G2317 (godliness), G2318 (worshipper of God)\nVariants: θεοσεβής",
    2319: "θεοστυγής (theostygḗs | theh-os-too-gace')\n\nDerivation: from G2316 and the base of G4767\nStrong's: hateful to God, i.e. impious\nKJV: —hater of God.\n\nSee: G2316 \nSee: G4767 \n\nCognate Group: G2317 (godliness), G2318 (worshipper of God)\nVariants: θεοστυγής",
    2320: "θεότης (theótēs | theh-ot'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G2316\nStrong's: divinity (abstractly)\nKJV: —godhead.\n\nSee: G2316 \n\nCognate Group: G2312 (taught of God), G2320 (godhead), G2304 (divine), G2316 (X exceeding), G2305 (godhead), G112 (without God)\nVariants: θεότης",
    2321: "Θεόφιλος (Theóphilos | theh-of'-il-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2316 and G5384\nStrong's: friend of God; Theophilus, a Christian\nKJV: —Theophilus.\n\nSee: G2316 \nSee: G5384 \n\nCognate Group: G2312 (taught of God), G2320 (godhead), G2304 (divine), G2316 (X exceeding), G2305 (godhead), G112 (without God)\nVariants: Θεόφιλος",
    2322: "θεραπεία (therapeía | ther-ap-i'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2323\nStrong's: attendance (specially, medical, i.e. cure); figuratively and collectively, domestics\nKJV: —healing, household.\n\nSee: G2323 \n\nCognate Group: G2322 (healing), G2323 (cure)\nVariants: θεραπεία, οἰκετεία \nHebrew Equivalents: H4795 מָרוּק, H5650 עֶבֶד, H6116 עֲצָרָה, H8655 תְּרָפִים",
    2323: "θεραπεύω (therapeúō | ther-ap-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2324\nStrong's: to wait upon menially, i.e. (figuratively) to adore (God), or (specially) to relieve (of disease)\nKJV: —cure, heal, worship.\n\nSee: G2324 \n\nCognate Group: G2322 (healing), G2323 (cure)\nVariants: θεραπεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H2470 חָלָה, H3427 יָשַׁב, H5650 עֶבֶד, H6213 עָשָׂה, H8120 שְׁמַשׁ",
    2324: "θεράπων (therápōn | ther-ap'-ohn)\n\nDerivation: apparently a participle from an otherwise obsolete derivative of the base of G2330\nStrong's: a menial attendant (as if cherishing)\nKJV: —servant.\n\nSee: G2330 \n\nCognate Group: G2322 (healing), G2323 (cure)\nVariants: θεράπων \nHebrew Equivalents: H1121 בֵּן, H5291 נַעֲרָה, H5650 עֶבֶד, H8334 שָׁרַת",
    2325: "θερίζω (therízō | ther-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2330 (in the sense of the crop)\nStrong's: to harvest\nKJV: —reap.\n\nSee: G2330 \n\nCognate Group: G2325 (reap), G2326 (harvest)\nVariants: θερίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2790 חָרַשׁ, H5927 עָלָה, H6998 קָטַף, H7114 קָצַר",
    2326: "θερισμός (therismós | ther-is-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G2325\nStrong's: reaping, i.e. the crop\nKJV: —harvest.\n\nSee: G2325 \n\nCognate Group: G2325 (reap), G2326 (harvest)\nVariants: θερισμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H2758 חָרִישׁ, H6285 פֵּאָה, H7019 קַיִץ, H7105 קָצִיר",
    2327: "θεριστής (theristḗs | ther-is-tace')\n\nDerivation: from G2325\nStrong's: a harvester\nKJV: —reaper.\n\nSee: G2325 \n\nCognate Group: G2325 (reap), G2326 (harvest)\nVariants: θεριστής",
    2328: "θερμαίνω (thermaínō | ther-mah'-ee-no)\n\nDerivation: from G2329\nStrong's: to heat (oneself)\nKJV: —(be) warm(-ed, self).\n\nSee: G2329 \n\nCognate Group: G2325 (reap), G2326 (harvest)\nVariants: θερμαίνω, θερμαίνομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2552 חָמַם, H2787 חָרַר",
    2329: "θέρμη (thérmē | ther'-may)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G2330\nStrong's: warmth\nKJV: —heat.\n\nSee: G2330 \n\nCognate Group: G2325 (reap), G2326 (harvest)\nVariants: θέρμη, θέρμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H2552 חָמַם",
    2330: "θέρος (théros | ther'-os)\n\nDerivation: from a primary θέρω (to heat)\nStrong's: properly, heat, i.e. summer\nKJV: —summer.\n\nCognate Group: G2325 (reap), G2326 (harvest)\nVariants: θέρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H7019 קַיִץ, H7105 קָצִיר",
    2331: "Θεσσαλονικεύς (Thessalonikeús | thes-sal-on-ik-yoos')\n\nDerivation: from G2332\nStrong's: a Thessalonican, i.e. inhabitant of Thessalonice\nKJV: —Thessalonian.\n\nSee: G2332 \n\nCognate Group: G2325 (reap), G2326 (harvest)\nVariants: Θεσσαλονικεύς",
    2332: "Θεσσαλονίκη (Thessaloníkē | thes-sal-on-ee'-kay)\n\nDerivation: from Θεσσαλός (a Thessalian) and G3529\nStrong's: Thessalonice, a place in Asia Minor\nKJV: —Thessalonica.\n\nSee: G3529 \n\nCognate Group: G2325 (reap), G2326 (harvest)\nVariants: Θεσσαλονίκη",
    2333: "Θευδᾶς (Theudâs | thyoo-das')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain origin\nStrong's: Theudas, an Israelite\nKJV: —Theudas.\n\nCognate Group: G2325 (reap), G2326 (harvest)\nVariants: Θευδᾶς",
    2334: "θεωρέω (theōréō | theh-o-reh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2300 (perhaps by addition of G3708)\nStrong's: to be a spectator of, i.e. discern, (literally, figuratively (experience) or intensively (acknowledge))\nKJV: —behold, consider, look on, perceive, see. Compare G3700 .\n\nSee: G2300 \nSee: G3708 \nSee: G3700 \n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: θεωρέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2161 זָמַם, H2372 חָזָה, H2372 חָזָה, H3974 מָאֹור, H7200 רָאָה",
    2335: "θεωρία (theōría | theh-o-ree'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2334\nStrong's: spectatorship, i.e. (concretely) a spectacle\nKJV: —sight.\n\nSee: G2334 \n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: θεωρία",
    2336: "θήκη (thḗkē | thay'-kay)\n\nDerivation: from G5087\nStrong's: a receptacle, i.e. scabbard\nKJV: —sheath.\n\nSee: G5087 \n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: θήκη \nHebrew Equivalents: H1004 בַּיִת, H4678 מַצֶּבֶת",
    2337: "θηλάζω (thēlázō | thay-lad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from θηλή (the nipple)\nStrong's: to suckle, (by implication) to suck\nKJV: —(give) suck(-ling).\n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: θηλάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2949 טִפֻּח, H3243 יָנַק",
    2338: "θῆλυς (thēlys | thay'-loos)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2337\nStrong's: female\nKJV: —female, woman.\n\nSee: G2337 \n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: θῆλυς \nHebrew Equivalents: H745 אַרְיֵה, H802 אִשָּׁה, H860 אָתֹון, H1323 בַּת, H5347 נְקֵבָה",
    2339: "θήρα (thḗra | thay'-rah)\n\nDerivation: from θήρ (a wild animal, as game)\nStrong's: hunting, i.e. (figuratively) destruction\nKJV: —trap.\n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: θήρα \nHebrew Equivalents: H2963 טָרַף, H2964 טֶרֶף, H6718 צַיִד, H7568 רֶשֶׁת",
    2340: "θηρεύω (thēreúō | thay-ryoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2339\nStrong's: to hunt (an animal), i.e. (figuratively) to carp at\nKJV: —catch.\n\nSee: G2339 \n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: θηρεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H270 אָחַז, H1413 גָּדַד, H2963 טָרַף, H3369 יָקֹשׁ, H6148 עָרַב, H6679 צוּד, H8610 תָּפַשׂ",
    2341: "θηριομαχέω (thēriomachéō | thay-ree-om-akh-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2342 and G3164\nStrong's: to be a beast-fighter (in the gladiatorial show), i.e. (figuratively) to encounter (furious men)\nKJV: —fight with wild beasts.\n\nSee: G2342 \nSee: G3164 \n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: θηριομαχέω",
    2342: "θηρίον (thēríon | thay-ree'-on)\n\nDerivation: diminutive from the same as G2339\nStrong's: a dangerous animal\nKJV: —(venomous, wild) beast.\n\nSee: G2339 \n\nCognate Group: G2342 (beast)\nVariants: θηρίον \nHebrew Equivalents: H929 בְּהֵמָה, H2416 חַי, H2416 חַי, H6728 צִיִּי",
    2343: "θησαυρίζω (thēsaurízō | thay-sow-rid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2344\nStrong's: to amass or reserve (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —lay up (treasure), (keep) in store, (heap) treasure (together, up).\n\nSee: G2344 \n\nCognate Group: G2343 (lay up), G2344 (treasure)\nVariants: θησαυρίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6113 עָצָר, H6651 צָבַר, H6845 צָפַן",
    2344: "θησαυρός (thēsaurós | thay-sow-ros')\n\nDerivation: from G5087\nStrong's: a deposit, i.e. wealth (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —treasure.\n\nSee: G5087 \n\nCognate Group: G2343 (lay up), G2344 (treasure)\nVariants: θησαυρός \nHebrew Equivalents: H214 אֹוצָר, H1249 בַּר, H1595 גֶּנֶז, H1964 הֵיכָל, H2633 חֹסֶן, H3957 לִשְׁכָּה, H4301 מַטְמֹון, H8393 תְּבוּאָה",
    2345: "θιγγάνω (thingánō | thing-gan'-o)\n\nDerivation: a prolonged form of an obsolete primary θίγω (to finger)\nStrong's: to manipulate, i.e. have to do with; by implication, to injure\nKJV: —handle, touch.\n\nCognate Group: G2343 (lay up), G2344 (treasure)\nVariants: θιγγάνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5060 נָגַע",
    2346: "θλίβω (thlíbō | thlee'-bo)\n\nDerivation: akin to the base of G5147\nStrong's: to crowd (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —afflict, narrow, throng, suffer tribulation, trouble.\n\nSee: G5147 \n\nCognate Group: G2346 (afflict), G2347 (afflicted)\nVariants: θλίβω \nHebrew Equivalents: H340 אָיַב, H2502 חָלַץ, H3228 יְמִינִי, H3805 כֹתֶרֶת, H3944 לָצֹון, H4900 מָשַׁךְ, H6231 עָשַׁק, H6687 צוּף, H6862 צַר, H6887 צָרַר, H7492 רָעַץ, H7665 שָׁבַר",
    2347: "θλῖψις (thlîpsis | thlip'-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G2346\nStrong's: pressure (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —afflicted(-tion), anguish, burdened, persecution, tribulation, trouble.\n\nSee: G2346 \n\nCognate Group: G2346 (afflict), G2347 (afflicted)\nVariants: θλῖψις \nHebrew Equivalents: H343 אֵיד, H1674 דְּאָגָה, H3906 לַחַץ, H4035 מְגוּרָה, H4157 מוּעָקָה, H4689 מָצֹוק, H6040 עֳנִי, H6115 עֹצֶר, H6125 עָקָה, H6233 עֹשֶׁק, H6862 צַר, H6869 צָרָה, H7200 רָאָה, H7722 שֹׁוא",
    2348: "θνήσκω (thnḗskō | thnay'-sko)\n\n\nDerivation: a strengthened form of a simpler primary θάνω (thánō | than'-o)\n (which is used for it only in certain tenses)\nStrong's: to die (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —be dead, die.\n\nCognate Group: G4880 (be dead with), G2289 (become dead), G2348 (be dead), G2288 (X deadly), G599 (be dead), G2349 (mortal), G110 (immortality)\nVariants: θνήσκω, θνῄσκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2026 הָרַג, H2490 חָלַל, H4191 מוּת",
    2349: "θνητός (thnētós | thnay-tos')\n\nDerivation: from G2348\nStrong's: liable to die\nKJV: —mortal(-ity).\n\nSee: G2348 \n\nCognate Group: G4880 (be dead with), G2289 (become dead), G2348 (be dead), G2288 (X deadly), G599 (be dead), G2349 (mortal), G110 (immortality)\nVariants: θνητός \nHebrew Equivalents: H120 אָדָם, H2416 חַי, H4191 מוּת",
    2350: "θορυβέω (thorybéō | thor-oo-beh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2351\nStrong's: to be in tumult, i.e. disturb, clamor\nKJV: —make ado (a noise), trouble self, set on an uproar.\n\nSee: G2351 \n\nCognate Group: G5182 (trouble), G2350 (make ado), G2351 (tumult)\nVariants: θορυβέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1204 בָּעַת, H4102 מָהַהּ, H7477 רָעַל",
    2351: "θόρυβος (thórybos | thor'-oo-bos)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G2360\nStrong's: a disturbance\nKJV: —tumult, uproar.\n\nSee: G2360 \n\nCognate Group: G5182 (trouble), G2350 (make ado), G2351 (tumult)\nVariants: θόρυβος \nHebrew Equivalents: H17 אֲבֹוי, H1995 הָמֹון, H4103 מְהוּמָה, H6343 פַּחַד, H7460 רָעַד, H8643 תְּרוּעָה",
    2352: "θραύω (thraúō | throw'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to crush\nKJV: —bruise. Compare G4486 .\n\nSee: G4486 \n\nCognate Group: G5182 (trouble), G2350 (make ado), G2351 (tumult)\nVariants: θραύω, θραυματίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2648 חָפַז, H4127 מוּג, H4272 מָחַץ, H4549 מָסַס, H5062 נָגַף, H5405 נָשַׁת, H6087 עָצַב, H6206 עָרַץ, H6555 פָּרַץ, H7492 רָעַץ, H7533 רָצַץ",
    2353: "θρέμμα (thrémma | threm'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G5142\nStrong's: stock (as raised on a farm)\nKJV: —cattle.\n\nSee: G5142 \n\nCognate Group: G5182 (trouble), G2350 (make ado), G2351 (tumult)\nVariants: θρέμμα",
    2354: "θρηνέω (thrēnéō | thray-neh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2355\nStrong's: to bewail\nKJV: —lament, mourn.\n\nSee: G2355 \n\nCognate Group: G2355 (lamentation), G2354 (lament)\nVariants: θρηνέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H56 אָבַל, H1058 בָּכָה, H3213 יָלַל, H5091 נָהָה, H5110 נוּד, H5927 עָלָה, H7015 קִינָה, H8567 תָּנָה",
    2355: "θρῆνος (thrēnos | thray'-nos)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G2360\nStrong's: wailing\nKJV: —lamentation.\n\nSee: G2360 \n\nCognate Group: G2355 (lamentation), G2354 (lament)\nVariants: θρῆνος G2578 \nHebrew Equivalents: H4911 מָשַׁל, H5092 נְהִי, H6616 פָּתִיל, H7068 קִנְאָה, H8181 שֵׂעָר",
    2356: "θρησκεία (thrēskeía | thrace-ki'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2357\nStrong's: ceremonial observance\nKJV: —religion, worshipping.\n\nSee: G2357 \n\nCognate Group: G1479 (will worship), G2357 (religious), G2356 (religion)\nVariants: θρησκεία",
    2357: "θρησκός (thrēskós | thrace'-kos)\n\nDerivation: probably from the base of G2360\nStrong's: ceremonious in worship (as demonstrative), i.e. pious\nKJV: —religious.\n\nSee: G2360 \n\nCognate Group: G1479 (will worship), G2357 (religious), G2356 (religion)\nVariants: θρησκός, θρῆσκος",
    2358: "θριαμβεύω (thriambeúō | three-am-byoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a prolonged compound of the base of G2360\nStrong's: and a derivative of G680 (meaning a noisy iambus, sung in honor of Bacchus); to make an acclamatory procession, i.e. (figuratively) to conquer or (by Hebraism) to give victory\nKJV: —(cause) to triumph (over).\n\nSee: G2360 \nSee: G680 \n\nCognate Group: G2358 (to triumph)\nVariants: θριαμβεύω",
    2359: "θρίξ (thríx | threeks)\n\nDerivation: genitive case τριχός, etc.\nStrong's: of uncertain derivation; hair\nKJV: —hair. Compare G2864 .\n\nSee: G2864 \n\nCognate Group: G2358 (to triumph)\nVariants: θρίξ, δέρρις",
    2360: "θροέω (throéō | thro-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from θρέομαι to wail\nStrong's: to clamor, i.e. (by implication) to frighten\nKJV: —trouble.\n\nCognate Group: G2358 (to triumph)\nVariants: θροέω, θροέομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1993 הָמָה",
    2361: "θρόμβος (thrómbos | throm'-bos)\n\nDerivation: perhaps from G5142 (in the sense of thickening)\nStrong's: a clot\nKJV: —great drop.\n\nSee: G5142 \n\nCognate Group: G2358 (to triumph)\nVariants: θρόμβος",
    2362: "θρόνος (thrónos | thron'-os)\n\nDerivation: from θράω (to sit)\nStrong's: a stately seat (\"throne\"); by implication, power or (concretely) a potentate\nKJV: —seat, throne.\n\nCognate Group: G2362 (seat)\nVariants: θρόνος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1964 הֵיכָל, H2329 חוּג, H3678 כִּסֵּא, H3764 כׇּרְסֵא, H4437 מַלְכוּ, H4725 מָקֹום, H8034 שֵׁם",
    2363: "Θυάτειρα (Thyáteira | thoo-at'-i-rah)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Thyatira, a place in Asia Minor\nKJV: —Thyatira.\n\nCognate Group: G2362 (seat)\nVariants: Θυάτειρα",
    2364: "θυγάτηρ (thygátēr | thoo-gat'-air)\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary word (compare \"daughter\")\nStrong's: a female child, or (by Hebraism) descendant (or inhabitant)\nKJV: —daughter.\n\nCognate Group: G2362 (seat)\nVariants: θυγάτηρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H802 אִשָּׁה, H1323 בַּת, H1733 דֹּודָה",
    2365: "θυγάτριον (thygátrion | thoo-gat'-ree-on)\n\nDerivation: from G2364\nStrong's: a daughterling\nKJV: —little (young) daughter.\n\nSee: G2364 \n\nCognate Group: G2362 (seat)\nVariants: θυγάτριον",
    2366: "θύελλα (thýella | thoo'-el-lah)\n\nDerivation: from G2380 (in the sense of blowing) a storm\nKJV: —tempest.\n\nSee: G2380 \n\nCognate Group: G2362 (seat)\nVariants: θύελλα \nHebrew Equivalents: H6205 עֲרָפֶל",
    2367: "θύϊνος (thýïnos | thoo'-ee-nos)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2380 \nStrong's: (in the sense of blowing, denoting a certain fragrant tree); made of citron-wood\nKJV: —thyine.\n\nSee: G2380 \n\nCognate Group: G2362 (seat)\nVariants: θύϊνος",
    2368: "θυμίαμα (thymíama | thoo-mee'-am-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2370\nStrong's: an aroma, i.e. fragrant powder burnt in religious service; by implication, the burning itself\nKJV: —incense, odour.\n\nSee: G2370 \n\nCognate Group: G2362 (seat)\nVariants: θυμίαμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H801 אִשָּׁה, H1314 בֶּשֶׂם, H2113 זְוָעָה, H4729 מִקְטָר, H5238 נְכֹת, H5561 סַם, H6999 קָטַר, H7004 קְטֹרֶת, H7070 קָנֶה",
    2369: "θυμιαστήριον (thymiastḗrion | thoo-mee-as-tay'-ree-on)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2370\nStrong's: a place of fumigation, i.e. the alter of incense (in the Temple)\nKJV: —censer.\n\nSee: G2370 \n\nCognate Group: G2362 (seat)\nVariants: θυμιαστήριον, θυμιατήριον",
    2370: "θυμιάω (thymiáō | thoo-mee-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2380 (in the sense of smoking)\nStrong's: to fumigate, i.e. offer aromatic fumes\nKJV: —burn incense.\n\nSee: G2380 \n\nCognate Group: G2362 (seat)\nVariants: θυμιάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2076 זָבַח, H6999 קָטַר",
    2371: "θυμομαχέω (thymomachéō | thoo-mom-akh-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a presumed compound of G2372 and G3164\nStrong's: to be in a furious fight, i.e. (figuratively) to be exasperated\nKJV: —be highly displeased.\n\nSee: G2372 \nSee: G3164 \n\nCognate Group: G2362 (seat)\nVariants: θυμομαχέω",
    2372: "θυμός (thymós | thoo-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G2380\nStrong's: passion (as if breathing hard)\nKJV: —fierceness, indignation, wrath. Compare G5590 .\n\nSee: G2380 \nSee: G5590 \n\nCognate Group: G1939 (concupiscence), G1937 (covet), G2372 (fierceness), G1938 (+ lust after), G1761 (device), G1760 (think)\nVariants: θυμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H639 אַף, H1149 בְּנַס, H2195 זַעַם, H2197 זַעַף, H2528 חֱמָא, H2534 חֵמָה, H2740 חָרֹון, H2740 חָרֹון, H2750 חֳרִי, H2750 חֳרִי, H3581 כֹּחַ, H3708 כַּעַס, H4294 מַטֶּה, H4421 מִלְחָמָה, H5098 נָהַם, H5183 נַחַת, H5397 נְשָׁמָה, H5678 עֶבְרָה, H6310 פֶּה, H6963 קֹול, H7068 קִנְאָה, H7107 קָצַף, H7110 קֶצֶף, H7147 קְרִי, H7218 רֹאשׁ, H7264 רָגַז, H7307 רוּחַ, H8569 תְּנוּאָה, H8653 תַּרְעֵלָה",
    2373: "θυμόω (thymóō | tho-mo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2372\nStrong's: to put in a passion, i.e. enrage\nKJV: —be wroth.\n\nSee: G2372 \n\nCognate Group: G1939 (concupiscence), G1937 (covet), G2372 (fierceness), G1938 (+ lust after), G1761 (device), G1760 (think)\nVariants: θυμόω, θυμόομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1674 דְּאָגָה, H2194 זָעַם, H2196 זָעַף, H2534 חֵמָה, H2734 חָרָה, H2734 חָרָה, H3707 כַּעַס, H3988 מָאַס, H4843 מָרַר, H5162 נָחַם, H6058 עָנֵף, H7107 קָצַף, H7116 קָצֵר, H7264 רָגַז",
    2374: "θύρα (thýra | thoo'-rah)\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary word (compare \"door\")\nStrong's: a portal or entrance (the opening or the closure, literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —door, gate.\n\nCognate Group: G2377 (that kept the door), G2376 (window), G2374 (door)\nVariants: θύρα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1800 דַּל, H1817 דֶּלֶת, H4237 מֶחֱזָה, H5592 סַף, H6607 פֶּתַח, H8179 שַׁעַר, H8651 תְּרַע",
    2375: "θυρεός (thyreós | thoo-reh-os')\n\nDerivation: from G2374\nStrong's: a large shield (as door-shaped)\nKJV: —shield.\n\nSee: G2374 \n\nCognate Group: G2375 (shield)\nVariants: θυρεός \nHebrew Equivalents: H4043 מָגֵן, H5699 עֲגָלָה, H6793 צִנָּה",
    2376: "θυρίς (thyrís | thoo-rece')\n\nDerivation: from G2374\nStrong's: an aperture, i.e. window\nKJV: —window.\n\nSee: G2374 \n\nCognate Group: G2377 (that kept the door), G2376 (window), G2374 (door)\nVariants: θυρίς \nHebrew Equivalents: H699 אֲרֻבָּה, H2474 חַלֹּון, H3551 כַּו, H6607 פֶּתַח",
    2377: "θυρωρός (thyrōrós | thoo-ro-ros')\n\nDerivation: from G2374 and οὖρος (a watcher)\nStrong's: a gate- warden\nKJV: —that kept the door, porter.\n\nSee: G2374 \n\nCognate Group: G2377 (that kept the door), G2376 (window), G2374 (door)\nVariants: θυρωρός \nHebrew Equivalents: H6486 פְּקֻדָּה, H7778 שֹׁועֵר",
    2378: "θυσία (thysía | thoo-see'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2380\nStrong's: sacrifice (the act or the victim, literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —sacrifice.\n\nSee: G2380 \n\nCognate Group: G2379 (altar), G2380 (kill), G2378 (sacrifice)\nVariants: θυσία \nHebrew Equivalents: H801 אִשָּׁה, H2076 זָבַח, H2113 זְוָעָה, H2459 חֶלֶב, H4503 מִנְחָה, H5207 נִיחֹוחַ, H5930 עֹלָה, H8002 שֶׁלֶם, H8548 תָּמִיד",
    2379: "θυσιαστήριον (thysiastḗrion | thoo-see-as-tay'-ree-on)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2378\nStrong's: a place of sacrifice, i.e. an altar (special or genitive case, literal or figurative)\nKJV: —altar.\n\nSee: G2378 \n\nCognate Group: G2379 (altar), G2380 (kill), G2378 (sacrifice)\nVariants: θυσιαστήριον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1116 בָּמָה, H4056 מַדְבַּח, H4196 מִזְבֵּחַ, H4676 מַצֵּבָה, H4998 נָאָה",
    2380: "θύω (thýō | thoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: properly, to rush (breathe hard, blow, smoke), i.e. (by implication) to sacrifice (properly, by fire, but genitive case); by extension to immolate (slaughter for any purpose)\nKJV: —kill, (do) sacrifice, slay.\n\nCognate Group: G2379 (altar), G2380 (kill), G2378 (sacrifice)\nVariants: θύω, ἐπιθύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2076 זָבַח, H2873 טָבַח, H6999 קָטַר, H7843 שָׁחַת",
    2381: "Θωμᾶς (Thōmâs | tho-mas')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (compare H8380)\nStrong's: the twin; Thomas, a Christian\nKJV: —Thomas.\nSee: H8380\n\nCognate Group: G2379 (altar), G2380 (kill), G2378 (sacrifice)\nVariants: Θωμᾶς \nHebrew Equivalents: H8380 תָּאֹום",
    2382: "θώραξ (thṓrax | tho'-rax)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: the chest (\"thorax\"), i.e. (by implication) a corslet\nKJV: —breast-plate.\n\nCognate Group: G2382 (breast-plate)\nVariants: θώραξ \nHebrew Equivalents: H4358 מִכְלֹול, H5630 סִרְיֹן, H7448 רֶסֶן, H8302 שִׁרְיֹון, H8302 שִׁרְיֹון",
    2383: "Ἰάειρος (Iáeiros | ee-ah'-i-ros)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H2971)\nStrong's: Jairus (i.e. Jair), an Israelite\nKJV: —Jairus.\nSee: H2971\n\nCognate Group: G2382 (breast-plate)\nVariants: Ἰάειρος, Ἰάϊρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2971 יָאִיר",
    2384: "Ἰακώβ (Iakṓb | ee-ak-obe')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3290)\nStrong's: Jacob (i.e. Ja`akob), the progenitor of the Israelites\nKJV: —also an Israelite:—Jacob.\nSee: H3290\n\nCognate Group: G2385 (James), G2384 (also an Israelite:—Jacob)\nVariants: Ἰακώβ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3290 יַעֲקֹב",
    2385: "Ἰάκωβος (Iákōbos | ee-ak'-o-bos)\n\nDerivation: the same as G2384 Græcized\nStrong's: Jacobus, the name of three Israelites\nKJV: —James.\n\nSee: G2384 \n\nCognate Group: G2385 (James), G2384 (also an Israelite:—Jacob)\nVariants: Ἰάκωβος",
    2386: "ἴαμα (íama | ee'-am-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2390\nStrong's: a cure (the effect)\nKJV: —healing.\n\nSee: G2390 \n\nCognate Group: G2390 (heal), G2395 (physician), G2392 (cure), G2386 (healing)\nVariants: ἴαμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H724 אֲרוּכָה, H2920 טַל, H4832 מַרְפֵּא",
    2387: "Ἰαμβρῆς (Iambrēs | ee-am-brace')\n\nDerivation: of Egyptian origin\nStrong's: Jambres, an Egyptian\nKJV: —Jambres.\n\nCognate Group: G2387 (Jambres), G2389 (Jannes)\nVariants: Ἰαμβρῆς",
    2388: "Ἰαννά (Ianná | ee-an-nah')\n\nDerivation: probably of Hebrew origin (compare H3238)\nStrong's: Janna, an Israelite\nKJV: —Janna.\nSee: H3238\n\nCognate Group: G2387 (Jambres), G2389 (Jannes)\nVariants: Ἰαννά, Ἰανναί \nHebrew Equivalents: H3238 יָנָה",
    2389: "Ἰαννῆς (Iannēs | ee-an-nace')\n\nDerivation: of Egyptian origin\nStrong's: Jannes, an Egyptian\nKJV: —Jannes.\n\nCognate Group: G2387 (Jambres), G2389 (Jannes)\nVariants: Ἰαννῆς, Ἰάννης",
    2390: "ἰάομαι (iáomai | ee-ah'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice of apparently a primary verb\nStrong's: to cure (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —heal, make whole.\n\nCognate Group: G2390 (heal), G2395 (physician), G2392 (cure), G2386 (healing)\nVariants: ἰάομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2280 חָבַשׁ, H2421 חָיָה, H7495 רָפָא",
    2391: "Ἰάρεδ (Iáred | ee-ar'-ed)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3382)\nStrong's: Jared (i.e. Jered), an antediluvian\nKJV: —Jared.\nSee: H3382\n\nCognate Group: G2390 (heal), G2395 (physician), G2392 (cure), G2386 (healing)\nVariants: Ἰάρεδ, Ἰάρετ, Ἰαρέδ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3382 יֶרֶד",
    2392: "ἴασις (íasis | ee'-as-is)\n\nDerivation: from G2390\nStrong's: curing (the act)\nKJV: —cure, heal(-ing).\n\nSee: G2390 \n\nCognate Group: G2390 (heal), G2395 (physician), G2392 (cure), G2386 (healing)\nVariants: ἴασις \nHebrew Equivalents: H724 אֲרוּכָה, H3545 כֵּהָה, H4832 מַרְפֵּא, H4974 מְתֹם",
    2393: "ἴασπις (íaspis | ee'-as-pis)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin (see H3471)\nStrong's: \"jasper\", a gem\nKJV: —jasper.\nSee: H3471\n\nCognate Group: G2390 (heal), G2395 (physician), G2392 (cure), G2386 (healing)\nVariants: ἴασπις \nHebrew Equivalents: H3095 יַהֲלֹם, H3471 יָשְׁפֵה, H3539 כַּדְכֹּד",
    2394: "Ἰάσων (Iásōn | ee-as'-oan)\n\nDerivation: future active participle masculine of G2390\nStrong's: about to cure; Jason, a Christian\nKJV: —Jason.\n\nSee: G2390 \n\nCognate Group: G2390 (heal), G2395 (physician), G2392 (cure), G2386 (healing)\nVariants: Ἰάσων",
    2395: "ἰατρός (iatrós | ee-at-ros')\n\nDerivation: from G2390\nStrong's: a physician\nKJV: —physician.\n\nSee: G2390 \n\nCognate Group: G2390 (heal), G2395 (physician), G2392 (cure), G2386 (healing)\nVariants: ἰατρός \nHebrew Equivalents: H4832 מַרְפֵּא, H7497 רָפָא",
    2396: "ἴδε (íde | id'-eh)\n\nDerivation: second person singular imperative active of G1492\nStrong's: used as an interjection to denote surprise; lo!\nKJV: —behold, lo, see.\n\nSee: G1492 \n\nCognate Group: G2390 (heal), G2395 (physician), G2392 (cure), G2386 (healing)\nVariants: ἴδε G2623",
    2397: "ἰδέα (idéa | id-eh'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G1492\nStrong's: a sight (comparative figuratively \"idea\"), i.e. aspect\nKJV: —countenance.\n\nSee: G1492 \n\nCognate Group: G2397 (countenance), G1491 (appearance)\nVariants: ἰδέα, εἰδέα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1823 דְּמוּת, H4758 מַרְאֶה",
    2398: "ἴδιος (ídios | id'-ee-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: pertaining to self, i.e. one's own; by implication, private or separate\nKJV: —X his acquaintance, when they were alone, apart, aside, due, his (own, proper, several), home, (her, our, thine, your) own (business), private(-ly), proper, severally, their (own).\n\nCognate Group: G2397 (countenance), G1491 (appearance)\nVariants: ἴδιος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1992 הֵם, H2593 חָנִיךְ, H4351 מְכוּרָה, H5237 נׇכְרִי, H8377 תְּאֹו",
    2399: "ἰδιώτης (idiṓtēs | id-ee-o'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G2398\nStrong's: a private person, i.e. (by implication) an ignoramus (compare \"idiot\")\nKJV: —ignorant, rude, unlearned.\n\nSee: G2398 \n\nCognate Group: G2399 (ignorant)\nVariants: ἰδιώτης",
    2400: "ἰδού (idoú | id-oo')\n\nDerivation: second person singular imperative middle voice of G1492\nStrong's: used as imperative lo!; \nKJV: —behold, lo, see.\n\nSee: G1492 \n\nCognate Group: G2399 (ignorant)\nVariants: ἰδού \nHebrew Equivalents: H56 אָבַל, H431 אֲלוּ, H576 אֲנָא, H718 אֲרוּ, H1887 הֵא, H1972 הָלָא, H2005 הֵן, H2009 הִנֵּה, H2088 זֶה, H2372 חָזָה, H3541 כֹּה, H5844 עָטָה, H7200 רָאָה, H7535 רַק",
    2401: "Ἰδουμαία (Idoumaía | id-oo-mah'-yah)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H123)\nStrong's: Idumæa (i.e. Edom), a region East (and South) of Palestine\nKJV: —Idumæa.\nSee: H123\n\nCognate Group: G2399 (ignorant)\nVariants: Ἰδουμαία \nHebrew Equivalents: H123 אֱדֹם, H5715 עֵדוּת",
    2402: "ἱδρώς (hidrṓs | hid-roce')\n\nDerivation: a strengthened form of a primary idos (sweat)\nStrong's: perspiration\nKJV: —sweat.\n\nCognate Group: G2399 (ignorant)\nVariants: ἱδρώς \nHebrew Equivalents: H2188 זֵעָה",
    2403: "Ἰεζαβήλ (Iezabḗl | ee-ed-zab-ale')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H348)\nStrong's: Jezabel (i.e. Jezebel), a Tyrian woman (used as a synonym of a termagant or false teacher)\nKJV: —Jezabel.\nSee: H348\n\nCognate Group: G2403 (Jezabel)\nVariants: Ἰεζαβήλ, Ἰεζάβελ \nHebrew Equivalents: H348 אִיזֶבֶל",
    2404: "Ἱεράπολις (Hierápolis | hee-er-ap'-ol-is)\n\nDerivation: from G2413 and G4172\nStrong's: holy city; Hierapolis, a place in Asia Minor\nKJV: —Hierapolis.\n\nSee: G2413 \nSee: G4172 \n\nCognate Group: G2403 (Jezabel)\nVariants: Ἱεράπολις",
    2405: "ἱερατεία (hierateía | hee-er-at-i'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2407\nStrong's: priestliness, i.e. the sacerdotal function\nKJV: —office of the priesthood, priest's office.\n\nSee: G2407 \n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: ἱερατεία \nHebrew Equivalents: H646 אֵפֹוד, H3547 כָּהַן, H3550 כְּהֻנָּה",
    2406: "ἱεράτευμα (hieráteuma | hee-er-at'-yoo-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2407\nStrong's: the priestly fraternity, i.e. sacerdotal order (figuratively)\nKJV: —priesthood.\n\nSee: G2407 \n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: ἱεράτευμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H3547 כָּהַן",
    2407: "ἱερατεύω (hierateúō | hee-er-at-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: prolongation from G2409\nStrong's: to be a priest, i.e. perform his functions\nKJV: —execute the priest's office.\n\nSee: G2409 \n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: ἱερατεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3547 כָּהַן",
    2408: "Ἱερεμίας (Hieremías | hee-er-em-ee'-as)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3414)\nStrong's: Hieremias (i.e. Jermijah), an Israelite\nKJV: —Jeremiah.\nSee: H3414\n\nCognate Group: G2408 (Jeremiah)\nVariants: Ἱερεμίας, Ἰερεμίας \nHebrew Equivalents: H3414 יִרְמְיָה",
    2409: "ἱερεύς (hiereús | hee-er-yooce')\n\nDerivation: from G2413\nStrong's: a priest (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —(high) priest.\n\nSee: G2413 \n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: ἱερεύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H3547 כָּהַן, H3549 כָּהֵן",
    2410: "Ἱεριχώ (Hierichṓ | hee-er-ee-kho')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3405)\nStrong's: Jericho, a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Jericho.\nSee: H3405\n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: Ἱεριχώ, Ἰεριχώ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3405 יְרִיחֹו",
    2411: "ἱερόν (hierón | hee-er-on')\n\nDerivation: neuter of G2413\nStrong's: a sacred place, i.e. the entire precincts (whereas G3485 denotes the central sanctuary itself) of the Temple (at Jerusalem or elsewhere)\nKJV: —temple.\n\nSee: G2413 \nSee: G3485 \n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: ἱερόν",
    2412: "ἱεροπρεπής (hieroprepḗs | hee-er-op-rep-ace')\n\nDerivation: from G2413 and the same as G4241\nStrong's: reverent\nKJV: —as becometh holiness.\n\nSee: G2413 \nSee: G4241 \n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: ἱεροπρεπής",
    2413: "ἱερός (hierós | hee-er-os')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: sacred\nKJV: —holy.\n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: ἱερός \nHebrew Equivalents: H1004 בַּיִת, H3104 יֹובֵל, H3671 כָּנָף, H4720 מִקְדָּשׁ, H5835 עֲזָרָה",
    2414: "Ἱεροσόλυμα (Hierosólyma | hee-er-os-ol'-oo-mah)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3389)\nStrong's: Hierosolyma (i.e. Jerushalaim), the capitol of Palestine\nKJV: —Jerusalem. Compare G2419 .\n\nSee: G2419 \nSee: H3389\n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: Ἱεροσόλυμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H3389 יְרוּשָׁלַ͏ִם, H3390 יְרוּשָׁלֵם",
    2415: "Ἱεροσολυμίτης (Hierosolymítēs | hee-er-os-ol-oo-mee'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G2414\nStrong's: a Hierosolymite, i.e. inhabitant of Hierosolyma\nKJV: —of Jerusalem.\n\nSee: G2414 \n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: Ἱεροσολυμίτης",
    2416: "ἱεροσυλέω (hierosyléō | hee-er-os-ool-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2417\nStrong's: to be a temple-robber (figuratively)\nKJV: —commit sacrilege.\n\nSee: G2417 \n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: ἱεροσυλέω",
    2417: "ἱερόσυλος (hierósylos | hee-er-os'-oo-los)\n\nDerivation: from G2411 and G4813\nStrong's: a temple-despoiler\nKJV: —robber of churches.\n\nSee: G2411 \nSee: G4813 \n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: ἱερόσυλος",
    2418: "ἱερουργέω (hierourgéō | hee-er-oorg-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2411 and the base of G2041\nStrong's: to be a temple-worker, i.e. officiate as a priest (figuratively)\nKJV: —minister.\n\nSee: G2411 \nSee: G2041 \n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: ἱερουργέω",
    2419: "Ἱερουσαλήμ (Hierousalḗm | hee-er-oo-sal-ame')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3389)\nStrong's: Hierusalem (i.e. Jerushalem), the capitol of Palestine\nKJV: —Jerusalem. Compare G2414 .\n\nSee: G2414 \nSee: H3389\n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: Ἱερουσαλήμ, Ἰερουσαλήμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3389 יְרוּשָׁלַ͏ִם",
    2420: "ἱερωσύνη (hierōsýnē | hee-er-o-soo'-nay)\n\nDerivation: from G2413\nStrong's: sacredness, i.e. (by implication) the priestly office\nKJV: —priesthood.\n\nSee: G2413 \n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: ἱερωσύνη \nHebrew Equivalents: H3547 כָּהַן",
    2421: "Ἰεσσαί (Iessaí | es-es-sah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3448)\nStrong's: Jessæ (i.e. Jishai), an Israelite\nKJV: —Jesse.\nSee: H3448\n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: Ἰεσσαί \nHebrew Equivalents: H3448 יִשַׁי",
    2422: "Ἰεφθάε (Iephtháe | ee-ef-thah'-eh)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3316)\nStrong's: Jephthaë (i.e. Jiphtach), an Israelite\nKJV: —Jephthah.\nSee: H3316\n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: Ἰεφθάε \nHebrew Equivalents: H3316 יִפְתָּח",
    2423: "Ἰεχονίας (Iechonías | ee-ekh-on-ee'-as)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3204)\nStrong's: Jechonias (i.e. Jekonjah), an Israelite\nKJV: —Jechonias.\nSee: H3204\n\nCognate Group: G2407 (execute the priest's office), G2416 (commit sacrilege), G2413 (holy), G2411 (temple), G2412 (as becometh holiness), G2420 (priesthood), G749 (chief priest), G2417 (robber of churches), G1494 (offered to idols), G2409 (priest), G2418 (minister), G2406 (priesthood), G2405 (office of the priesthood)\nVariants: Ἰεχονίας \nHebrew Equivalents: H3204 יְכׇנְיָה",
    2424: "Ἰησοῦς (Iēsoûs | ee-ay-sooce')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3091)\nStrong's: Jesus (i.e. Jehoshua), the name of our Lord and two (three) other Israelites\nKJV: —Jesus.\nSee: H3091\n\nCognate Group: G2424 (Jesus)\nVariants: Ἰησοῦς \nHebrew Equivalents: H3091 יְהֹושׁוּעַ",
    2425: "ἱκανός (hikanós | hik-an-os')\n\nDerivation: from ἵκω ( ἱκάνω or ἱκνέομαι, akin to G2240) (to arrive)\nStrong's: competent (as if coming in season), i.e. ample (in amount) or fit (in character)\nKJV: —able, + content, enough, good, great, large, long (while), many, meet, much, security, sore, sufficient, worthy.\n\nSee: G2240 \n\nCognate Group: G2427 (make able), G2425 (able), G2426 (sufficiency)\nVariants: ἱκανός \nHebrew Equivalents: H376 אִישׁ, H1767 דַּי, H1952 הֹון, H3557 כּוּל, H4100 מָה, H4100 מָה, H4592 מְעַט, H7043 קָלַל, H7706 שַׁדַּי",
    2426: "ἱκανότης (hikanótēs | hik-an-ot'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G2425\nStrong's: ability\nKJV: —sufficiency.\n\nSee: G2425 \n\nCognate Group: G2427 (make able), G2425 (able), G2426 (sufficiency)\nVariants: ἱκανότης",
    2427: "ἱκανόω (hikanóō | hik-an-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2425\nStrong's: to enable, i.e. qualify\nKJV: —make able (meet).\n\nSee: G2425 \n\nCognate Group: G2427 (make able), G2425 (able), G2426 (sufficiency)\nVariants: ἱκανόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1767 דַּי, H6994 קָטֹן, H7227 רַב",
    2428: "ἱκετηρία (hiketēría | hik-et-ay-ree'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of the base of G2425 (through the idea of approaching for a favor)\nStrong's: intreaty\nKJV: —supplication.\n\nSee: G2425 \n\nCognate Group: G2428 (supplication)\nVariants: ἱκετηρία",
    2429: "ἱκμάς (hikmás | hik-mas')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: dampness\nKJV: —moisture.\n\nCognate Group: G2428 (supplication)\nVariants: ἱκμάς, ἰκμάς \nHebrew Equivalents: H3105 יוּבַל, H8102 שֶׁמֶץ",
    2430: "Ἰκόνιον (Ikónion | ee-kon'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: perhaps from G1504\nStrong's: image-like; Iconium, a place in Asia Minor\nKJV: —Iconium.\n\nSee: G1504 \n\nCognate Group: G2428 (supplication)\nVariants: Ἰκόνιον",
    2431: "ἱλαρός (hilarós | hil-ar-os')\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2436\nStrong's: propitious or merry (\"hilarious\"), i.e. prompt or willing\nKJV: —cheerful.\n\nSee: G2436 \n\nCognate Group: G2431 (cheerful), G2432 (cheerfulness)\nVariants: ἱλαρός \nHebrew Equivalents: H7522 רָצֹון",
    2432: "ἱλαρότης (hilarótēs | hil-ar-ot'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G2431\nStrong's: alacrity\nKJV: —cheerfulness.\n\nSee: G2431 \n\nCognate Group: G2431 (cheerful), G2432 (cheerfulness)\nVariants: ἱλαρότης \nHebrew Equivalents: H7522 רָצֹון",
    2433: "ἱλάσκομαι (hiláskomai | hil-as'-kom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from the same as G2436\nStrong's: to conciliate, i.e. (transitively) to atone for (sin), or (intransitively) be propitious\nKJV: —be merciful, make reconciliation for.\n\nSee: G2436 \n\nCognate Group: G2434 (propitiation), G2435 (mercyseat), G2436 (be it far), G2433 (be merciful)\nVariants: ἱλάσκομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H3722 כָּפַר, H5162 נָחַם, H5545 סָלַח",
    2434: "ἱλασμός (hilasmós | hil-as-mos')\n\n\nStrong's: atonement, i.e. (concretely) an expiator\nKJV: —propitiation.\n\nCognate Group: G2434 (propitiation), G2435 (mercyseat), G2436 (be it far), G2433 (be merciful)\nVariants: ἱλασμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H819 אַשְׁמָה, H2403 חַטָּאָה, H3725 כִּפֻּר, H5547 סְלִיחָה",
    2435: "ἱλαστήριον (hilastḗrion | hil-as-tay'-ree-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a derivative of G2433\nStrong's: an expiatory (place or thing), i.e. (concretely) an atoning victim, or (specially) the lid of the Ark (in the Temple)\nKJV: —mercyseat, propitiation.\n\nSee: G2433 \n\nCognate Group: G2434 (propitiation), G2435 (mercyseat), G2436 (be it far), G2433 (be merciful)\nVariants: ἱλαστήριον \nHebrew Equivalents: H3727 כַּפֹּרֶת, H5835 עֲזָרָה",
    2436: "ἵλεως (híleōs | hil'-eh-oce)\n\nDerivation: perhaps from the alternate form of G138\nStrong's: cheerful (as attractive), i.e. propitious; adverbially (by Hebraism) God be gracious!, i.e. (in averting some calamity) far be it\nKJV: —be it far, merciful.\n\nSee: G138 \n\nCognate Group: G2434 (propitiation), G2435 (mercyseat), G2436 (be it far), G2433 (be merciful)\nVariants: ἵλεως \nHebrew Equivalents: H2485 חָלִיל, H3723 כָּפָר, H5162 נָחַם, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5545 סָלַח, H7356 רַחַם, H7965 שָׁלֹום",
    2437: "Ἰλλυρικόν (Illyrikón | il-loo-ree-kon')\n\nDerivation: neuter of an adjective from a name of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: (the) Illyrican (shore), i.e. (as a name itself) Illyricum, a region of Europe\nKJV: —Illyricum.\n\nCognate Group: G2434 (propitiation), G2435 (mercyseat), G2436 (be it far), G2433 (be merciful)\nVariants: Ἰλλυρικόν",
    2438: "ἱμάς (himás | hee-mas')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from the same as G260\nStrong's: a strap, i.e. (specially) the tie (of a sandal) or the lash (of a scourge)\nKJV: —latchet, thong.\n\nSee: G260 \n\nCognate Group: G2434 (propitiation), G2435 (mercyseat), G2436 (be it far), G2433 (be merciful)\nVariants: ἱμάς \nHebrew Equivalents: H5688 עֲבֹת, H8288 שְׂרֹוךְ",
    2439: "ἱματίζω (himatízō | him-at-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2440\nStrong's: to dress\nKJV: —clothe.\n\nSee: G2440 \n\nCognate Group: G2441 (apparel), G2439 (clothe), G2440 (apparel)\nVariants: ἱματίζω",
    2440: "ἱμάτιον (himátion | him-at'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a presumed derivative of ennumi (to put on)\nStrong's: a dress (inner or outer)\nKJV: —apparel, cloke, clothes, garment, raiment, robe, vesture.\n\nCognate Group: G2441 (apparel), G2439 (clothe), G2440 (apparel)\nVariants: ἱμάτιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H899 בֶּגֶד, H2488 חֲלִיצָה, H3407 יְרִיעָה, H3801 כְּתֹנֶת, H3830 לְבוּשׁ, H4055 מַד, H4598 מְעִיל, H5688 עֲבֹת, H6785 צֶמֶר, H8008 שַׂלְמָה, H8071 שִׂמְלָה",
    2441: "ἱματισμός (himatismós | him-at-is-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G2439\nStrong's: clothing\nKJV: —apparel (X -led), array, raiment, vesture.\n\nSee: G2439 \n\nCognate Group: G2441 (apparel), G2439 (clothe), G2440 (apparel)\nVariants: ἱματισμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H899 בֶּגֶד, H3682 כְּסוּת, H3800 כֶּתֶם, H3830 לְבוּשׁ, H5914 עֶכֶס, H8008 שַׂלְמָה, H8071 שִׂמְלָה",
    2442: "ἱμείρομαι (himeíromai | him-i'-rom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from ἵμερος \nStrong's: (a yearning; of uncertain affinity); to long for\nKJV: —be affectionately desirous.\n\nCognate Group: G2442 (be affectionately desirous)\nVariants: ἱμείρομαι, ὁμείρομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2442 חָכָה",
    2443: "ἵνα (hína | hin'-ah)\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as the former part of G1438 (through the demonstrative idea\nStrong's: compare G3588); in order that (denoting the purpose or the result)\nKJV: —albeit, because, to the intent (that), lest, so as, (so) that, (for) to. Compare G3363 .\n\nSee: G1438 \nSee: G3588 \nSee: G3363 \n\nCognate Group: G2443 (albeit)\nVariants: ἵνα",
    2444: "ἱνατί (hinatí | hin-at-ee')\n\nDerivation: from G2443 and G5101\nStrong's: for what reason ?, i.e. why?\nKJV: —wherefore, why.\n\nSee: G2443 \nSee: G5101 \n\nCognate Group: G2443 (albeit)\nVariants: ἱνατί",
    2445: "Ἰόππη (Ióppē | ee-op'-pay)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3305)\nStrong's: Joppe (i.e. Japho), a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Joppa.\nSee: H3305\n\nCognate Group: G2443 (albeit)\nVariants: Ἰόππη \nHebrew Equivalents: H3305 יָפֹו",
    2446: "Ἰορδάνης (Iordánēs | ee-or-dan'-ace)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3383)\nStrong's: the Jordanes (i.e. Jarden), a river of Palestine\nKJV: —Jordan.\nSee: H3383\n\nCognate Group: G2443 (albeit)\nVariants: Ἰορδάνης \nHebrew Equivalents: H3383 יַרְדֵּן",
    2447: "ἰός (iós | ee-os')\n\nDerivation: perhaps from εἶμι (to go) or ἵημι (to send)\nStrong's: rust (as if emitted by metals); also venom (as emitted by serpents)\nKJV: —poison, rust.\n\nCognate Group: G2447 (poison), G1728 (rule)\nVariants: ἰός \nHebrew Equivalents: H1121 בֵּן, H2430 חֵילָה, H2534 חֵמָה, H6567 פָּרָשׁ",
    2448: "Ἰουδά (Ioudá | ee-oo-dah')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3063 or perhaps H3194)\nStrong's: Judah (i.e. Jehudah or Juttah), a part of (or place in) Palestine\nKJV: —Judah.\nSee: H3063\nSee: H3194\n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: Ἰουδά",
    2449: "Ἰουδαία (Ioudaía | ee-oo-dah'-yah)\n\nDerivation: feminine of G2453 (with G1093 implied)\nStrong's: the Judæan land (i.e. Judæa), a region of Palestine\nKJV: —Judæa.\n\nSee: G2453 \nSee: G1093 \n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: Ἰουδαία",
    2450: "Ἰουδαΐζω (Ioudaḯzō | ee-oo-dah-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2453\nStrong's: to become a Judæan, i.e. \"Judaize\"\nKJV: —live as the Jews.\n\nSee: G2453 \n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: Ἰουδαΐζω, ἰουδαί̈ζω, ἰουδαΐζω, Ἰουδαΐζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3054 יָהַד",
    2451: "Ἰουδαϊκός (Ioudaïkós | ee-oo-dah-ee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G2453\nStrong's: Judaïc, i.e. resembling a Judæan\nKJV: —Jewish.\n\nSee: G2453 \n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: Ἰουδαϊκός",
    2452: "Ἰουδαϊκῶς (Ioudaïkōs | ee-oo-dah-ee-koce')\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2451\nStrong's: Judaïcally or in a manner resembling a Judæan\nKJV: —as do the Jews.\n\nSee: G2451 \n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: Ἰουδαϊκῶς",
    2453: "Ἰουδαῖος (Ioudaîos | ee-oo-dah'-yos)\n\nDerivation: from G2448 (in the sense of G2455 as a country)\nStrong's: Judæan, i.e. belonging to Jehudah\nKJV: —Jew(-ess), of Judæa.\n\nSee: G2448 \nSee: G2455 \n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: Ἰουδαῖος",
    2454: "Ἰουδαϊσμός (Ioudaïsmós | ee-oo-dah-is-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G2450\nStrong's: \"Judaism\", i.e. the Jewish faith and usages\nKJV: —Jews' religion.\n\nSee: G2450 \n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: Ἰουδαϊσμός",
    2455: "Ἰούδας (Ioúdas | ee-oo-das')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3063)\nStrong's: Judas (i.e. Jehudah), the name of ten Israelites; also of the posterity of one of them and its region\nKJV: —Juda(-h, -s); Jude.\nSee: H3063\n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: Ἰούδας, Ἰωδά \nHebrew Equivalents: H3063 יְהוּדָה",
    2456: "Ἰουλία (Ioulía | ee-oo-lee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: feminine of the same as G2457\nStrong's: Julia, a Christian woman\nKJV: —Julia.\n\nSee: G2457 \n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: Ἰουλία, Ἀουλία, Ἰουνία",
    2457: "Ἰούλιος (Ioúlios | ee-oo'-lee-os)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: Julius, a centurion\nKJV: —Julius.\n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: Ἰούλιος",
    2458: "Ἰουνιᾶς (Iouniâs | ee-oo-nee'-as)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: Junias, a Christian\nKJV: —Junias.\n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: Ἰουνιᾶς",
    2459: "Ἰοῦστος (Ioûstos | ee-ooce'-tos)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin (\"just\")\nStrong's: Justus, the name of three Christian\nKJV: —Justus.\n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: Ἰοῦστος, Τίτιος",
    2460: "ἱππεύς (hippeús | hip-yooce')\n\nDerivation: from G2462\nStrong's: an equestrian, i.e. member of a cavalry corps\nKJV: —horseman.\n\nSee: G2462 \n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: ἱππεύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H5483 סוּס, H6571 פָּרָשׁ, H7323 רוּץ, H7392 רָכַב",
    2461: "ἱππικόν (hippikón | hip-pee-kon')\n\nDerivation: neuter of a derivative of G2462\nStrong's: the cavalry force\nKJV: —horse(-men).\n\nSee: G2462 \n\nCognate Group: G2452 (as do the Jews), G2451 (Jewish), G2450 (live as the Jews), G2453 (Jew), G2454 (Jews' religion), G2448 (Judah), G2449 (Judæa)\nVariants: ἱππικόν, ἱππικός",
    2462: "ἵππος (híppos | hip'-pos)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a horse\nKJV: —horse.\n\nCognate Group: G2462 (horse)\nVariants: ἵππος \nHebrew Equivalents: H5483 סוּס, H6571 פָּרָשׁ, H7393 רֶכֶב",
    2463: "ἶρις (îris | ee'-ris)\n\nDerivation: perhaps from G2046 (as a symbol of the female messenger of the pagan deities)\nStrong's: a rainbow (\"iris\")\nKJV: —rainbow.\n\nSee: G2046 \n\nCognate Group: G2463 (rainbow)\nVariants: ἶρις, ὶρις \nHebrew Equivalents: H6916 קִדָּה",
    2464: "Ἰσαάκ (Isaák | ee-sah-ak')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3327)\nStrong's: Isaac (i.e. Jitschak), the son of Abraham\nKJV: —Isaac.\nSee: H3327\n\nCognate Group: G2464 (Isaac)\nVariants: Ἰσαάκ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3327 יִצְחָק",
    2465: "ἰσάγγελος (isángelos | ee-sang'-el-los)\n\nDerivation: from G2470 and G32\nStrong's: like an angel, i.e. angelic\nKJV: —equal unto the angels.\n\nSee: G2470 \nSee: G32 \n\nCognate Group: G743 (archangel), G2465 (equal unto the angels), G32 (angel)\nVariants: ἰσάγγελος",
    2466: "Ἰσαχάρ (Isachár | ee-sakh-ar')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3485)\nStrong's: Isachar (i.e. Jissaskar), a son of Jacob (figuratively, his descendant)\nKJV: —Issachar.\nSee: H3485\n\nCognate Group: G743 (archangel), G2465 (equal unto the angels), G32 (angel)\nVariants: Ἰσαχάρ, Ἰσσαχάρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3485 יִשָּׂשכָר",
    2467: "ἴσημι (ísēmi | is'-ay-mee)\n\nSee: G1492 \n\nCognate Group: G743 (archangel), G2465 (equal unto the angels), G32 (angel)\nVariants: ἴσημι Strong's: to know\nKJV: —know.",
    2468: "ἴσθι (ísthi | is'-thee)\n\nDerivation: second person imperative present of G1510\nStrong's: be thou\nKJV: —+ agree, be, X give thyself wholly to.\n\nSee: G1510 \n\nCognate Group: G743 (archangel), G2465 (equal unto the angels), G32 (angel)\nVariants: ἴσθι, εἰμί",
    2469: "Ἰσκαριώτης (Iskariṓtēs | is-kar-ee-o'-tace)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (probably H377 and H7149)\nStrong's: inhabitant of Kerioth; Iscariotes (i.e. Keriothite), an epithet of Judas the traitor\nKJV: —Iscariot.\nSee: H377\nSee: H7149\n\nCognate Group: G743 (archangel), G2465 (equal unto the angels), G32 (angel)\nVariants: Ἰσκαριώτης, Ἰσκαριώθ, Σκαριώθ, Σκαριώτης \nHebrew Equivalents: H376 אִישׁ, H377 אִישׁ, H7152 קְרִיֹּות",
    2470: "ἴσος (ísos | ee'-sos)\n\nDerivation: probably from G1492 (through the idea of seeming)\nStrong's: similar (in amount and kind)\nKJV: —+ agree, as much, equal, like.\n\nSee: G1492 \n\nCognate Group: G2470 (+ agree), G2471 (equal), G2472 (like precious)\nVariants: ἴσος \nHebrew Equivalents: H259 אֶחָד, H283 אַחְיֹו, H906 בַּד, H4393 מְלֹא, H4911 מָשַׁל, H4971 מַתְכֹנֶת, H8382 תָּאַם",
    2471: "ἰσότης (isótēs | ee-sot'-ace)\n\n\nStrong's: likeness (in condition or proportion); by implication, equity\nKJV: —equal(-ity).\n\nCognate Group: G2470 (+ agree), G2471 (equal), G2472 (like precious)\nVariants: ἰσότης",
    2472: "ἰσότιμος (isótimos | ee-sot'-ee-mos)\n\nDerivation: from G2470 and G5092\nStrong's: of equal value or honor\nKJV: —like precious.\n\nSee: G2470 \nSee: G5092 \n\nCognate Group: G2470 (+ agree), G2471 (equal), G2472 (like precious)\nVariants: ἰσότιμος",
    2473: "ἰσόψυχος (isópsychos | ee-sop'-soo-khos)\n\nDerivation: from G2470 and G5590\nStrong's: of similar spirit\nKJV: —likeminded.\n\nSee: G2470 \nSee: G5590 \n\nCognate Group: G2470 (+ agree), G2471 (equal), G2472 (like precious)\nVariants: ἰσόψυχος \nHebrew Equivalents: H6187 עֵרֶךְ",
    2474: "Ἰσραήλ (Israḗl | is-rah-ale')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3478)\nStrong's: Israel (i.e. Jisrael), the adopted name of Jacob, including his descendants (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —Israel.\nSee: H3478\n\nCognate Group: G2475 (Israelite), G2474 (Israel)\nVariants: Ἰσραήλ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3478 יִשְׂרָאֵל",
    2475: "Ἰσραηλίτης (Israēlítēs | is-rah-ale-ee'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G2474\nStrong's: an \"Israelite\", i.e. descendant of Israel (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —Israelite.\n\nSee: G2474 \n\nCognate Group: G2475 (Israelite), G2474 (Israel)\nVariants: Ἰσραηλίτης",
    2476: "ἵστημι (hístēmi | his'-tay-mee)\n\n Derivation: a prolonged form of a primary στάω (stáō | stah'-o) (of the same meaning, and used for it in certain tenses)\nStrong's: to stand (transitively or intransitively), used in various applications (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —abide, appoint, bring, continue, covenant, establish, hold up, lay, present, set (up), stanch, stand (by, forth, still, up). Compare G5087 .\n\nSee: G5087 \n\nCognate Group: G2475 (Israelite), G2474 (Israel)\nVariants: ἵστημι, ἵστημι/ἱστάνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H914 בָּדַל, H1129 בָּנָה, H1362 גָּבָהּ, H1826 דָּמַם, H1916 הֲדֹם, H1961 הָיָה, H2654 חָפֵץ, H3245 יָסַד, H3318 יָצָא, H3320 יָצַב, H3322 יָצַג, H3332 יָצַק, H3335 יָצַר, H3427 יָשַׁב, H3559 כּוּן, H3772 כָּרַת, H4060 מִדָּה, H5186 נָטָה, H5193 נָטַע, H5324 נָצַב, H5414 נָתַן, H5564 סָמַךְ, H5650 עֶבֶד, H5674 עָבַר, H5674 עָבַר, H5927 עָלָה, H5975 עָמַד, H6524 פָּרַח, H6965 קוּם, H7126 קָרַב, H7311 רוּם, H7760 שׂוּם, H7931 שָׁכַן, H8254 שָׁקַל, H8511 תָּלָא, H8625 תְּקַל, H8628 תָּקַע",
    2477: "ἱστορέω (historéō | his-tor-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G1492\nStrong's: to be knowing (learned), i.e. (by implication) to visit for information (interview)\nKJV: —see.\n\nSee: G1492 \n\nCognate Group: G2477 (see)\nVariants: ἱστορέω",
    2478: "ἰσχυρός (ischyrós | is-khoo-ros')\n\nDerivation: from G2479\nStrong's: forcible (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —boisterous, mighty(-ier), powerful, strong(-er, man), valiant.\n\nSee: G2479 \n\nCognate Group: G2479 (ability), G2729 (prevail), G2478 (boisterous), G2480 (be able)\nVariants: ἰσχυρός \nHebrew Equivalents: H46 אָבִיר, H117 אַדִּיר, H386 אֵיתָן, H410 אֵל, H533 אַמִּיץ, H553 אָמַץ, H1219 בָּצַר, H1274 בְּרִי, H1277 בָּרִיא, H1368 גִּבֹּור, H1416 גְּדוּד, H1419 גָּדֹול, H2388 חָזַק, H2634 חָסֹן, H2710 חָקַק, H3515 כָּבֵד, H4013 מִבְצָר, H4581 מָעֹוז, H4869 מִשְׂגָּב, H5764 עוּל, H5794 עַז, H6091 עָצָב, H6099 עָצוּם, H6184 עָרִיץ, H7312 רוּם, H8623 תַּקִּיף",
    2479: "ἰσχύς (ischýs | is-khoos')\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of ἰς (force\nStrong's: compare ἔσχον, a form of G2192); forcefulness (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —ability, might(-ily), power, strength.\n\nSee: G2192 \n\nCognate Group: G2479 (ability), G2729 (prevail), G2478 (boisterous), G2480 (be able)\nVariants: ἰσχύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H47 אַבִּיר, H117 אַדִּיר, H553 אָמַץ, H1116 בָּמָה, H1347 גָּאֹון, H1369 גְּבוּרָה, H1396 גָּבַר, H1396 גָּבַר, H1433 גֹּדֶל, H1627 גָּרֹון, H1679 דֹּבֶא, H1935 הֹוד, H1952 הֹון, H1975 הַלָּז, H1995 הָמֹון, H2388 חָזַק, H2388 חָזַק, H2428 חַיִל, H2634 חָסֹן, H2981 יְבוּל, H3581 כֹּחַ, H3966 מְאֹד, H4637 מַעֲרָצָה, H4937 מִשְׁעֵן, H5794 עַז, H5797 עֹז, H6109 עׇצְמָה, H6260 עַתּוּד, H6780 צֶמַח, H8409 תִּגְרָה, H8454 תּוּשִׁיָּה, H8633 תֹּקֶף",
    2480: "ἰσχύω (ischýō | is-khoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2479\nStrong's: to have (or exercise) force (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —be able, avail, can do(-not), could, be good, might, prevail, be of strength, be whole, + much work.\n\nSee: G2479 \n\nCognate Group: G2479 (ability), G2729 (prevail), G2478 (boisterous), G2480 (be able)\nVariants: ἰσχύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H47 אַבִּיר, H247 אָזַר, H410 אֵל, H553 אָמַץ, H1368 גִּבֹּור, H1396 גָּבַר, H2388 חָזַק, H2428 חַיִל, H3201 יָכֹל, H3527 כָּבַר, H3581 כֹּחַ, H3766 כָּרַע, H4937 מִשְׁעֵן, H5060 נָגַע, H5329 נָצַח, H5381 נָשַׂג, H5810 עָזַז, H6105 עָצַם, H6113 עָצָר, H6184 עָרִיץ, H6555 פָּרַץ, H7116 קָצֵר, H7116 קָצֵר, H7311 רוּם, H8631 תְּקֵף",
    2481: "ἴσως (ísōs | ee'-soce)\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2470\nStrong's: likely, i.e. perhaps\nKJV: —it may be.\n\nSee: G2470 \n\nCognate Group: G2479 (ability), G2729 (prevail), G2478 (boisterous), G2480 (be able)\nVariants: ἴσως \nHebrew Equivalents: H194 אוּלַי, H389 אַךְ, H2005 הֵן",
    2482: "Ἰταλία (Italía | ee-tal-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: Italia, a region of Europe\nKJV: —Italy.\n\nCognate Group: G2479 (ability), G2729 (prevail), G2478 (boisterous), G2480 (be able)\nVariants: Ἰταλία",
    2483: "Ἰταλικός (Italikós | ee-tal-ee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G2482\nStrong's: Italic, i.e. belonging to Italia\nKJV: —Italian.\n\nSee: G2482 \n\nCognate Group: G2479 (ability), G2729 (prevail), G2478 (boisterous), G2480 (be able)\nVariants: Ἰταλικός",
    2484: "Ἰτουραΐα (Itouraḯa | ee-too-rah'-yah)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3195)\nStrong's: Ituræa (i.e. Jetur), a region of Palestine\nKJV: —Ituræa.\nSee: H3195\n\nCognate Group: G2479 (ability), G2729 (prevail), G2478 (boisterous), G2480 (be able)\nVariants: Ἰτουραΐα, Ἰτουραῖος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3195 יְטוּר, H3491 יָתוּר",
    2485: "ἰχθύδιον (ichthýdion | ikh-thoo'-dee-on)\n\nDerivation: diminutive from G2486\nStrong's: a petty fish\nKJV: —little (small) fish.\n\nSee: G2486 \n\nCognate Group: G2479 (ability), G2729 (prevail), G2478 (boisterous), G2480 (be able)\nVariants: ἰχθύδιον",
    2486: "ἰχθύς (ichthýs | ikh-thoos')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a fish\nKJV: —fish.\n\nCognate Group: G2486 (fish)\nVariants: ἰχθύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H1709 דָּג, H1710 דָּגָה",
    2487: "ἴχνος (íchnos | ikh'-nos)\n\nDerivation: from ἰκνέομαι (to arrive\nStrong's: compare G2240); a track (figuratively)\nKJV: —step.\n\nSee: G2240 \n\nCognate Group: G2487 (step)\nVariants: ἴχνος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H2714 חֵקֶר, H3709 כַּף, H6119 עָקֵב, H6172 עֶרְוָה, H6471 פַּעַם, H6541 פַּרְסָה, H6806 צַעַד, H7176 קֶרֶת",
    2488: "Ἰωάθαμ (Iōátham | ee-o-ath'-am)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3147)\nStrong's: Joatham (i.e. Jotham), an Israelite\nKJV: —Joatham.\nSee: H3147\n\nCognate Group: G2487 (step)\nVariants: Ἰωάθαμ, Ἰωαθάμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3147 יֹותָם",
    2489: "Ἰωάννα (Iōánna | ee-o-an'-nah)\n\nDerivation: feminine of the same as G2491\nStrong's: Joanna, a Christian\nKJV: —Joanna.\n\nSee: G2491 \n\nCognate Group: G2487 (step)\nVariants: Ἰωάννα, Ἰωανάν, Ἰωάν(ν)α",
    2490: "Ἰωαννᾶς (Iōannâs | ee-o-an-nas')\n\nDerivation: a form of G2491\nStrong's: Joannas, an Israelite\nKJV: —Joannas.\n\nSee: G2491 \n\nCognate Group: G2487 (step)\nVariants: Ἰωαννᾶς, Ἰωάννης, Ἰωανάν",
    2491: "Ἰωάννης (Iōánnēs | ee-o-an'-nace)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3110)\nStrong's: Joannes (i.e. Jochanan), the name of four Israelites\nKJV: —John.\nSee: H3110\n\nCognate Group: G2487 (step)\nVariants: Ἰωάννης, Ἰωνάθας, Ἰωάν(ν)ης \nHebrew Equivalents: H3110 יֹוחָנָן",
    2492: "Ἰώβ (Iṓb | ee-obe')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H347)\nStrong's: Job (i.e. Ijob), a patriarch\nKJV: —Job.\nSee: H347\n\nCognate Group: G2487 (step)\nVariants: Ἰώβ \nHebrew Equivalents: H347 אִיֹּוב",
    2493: "Ἰωήλ (Iōḗl | ee-o-ale')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3100)\nStrong's: Joel, an Israelite\nKJV: —Joel.\nSee: H3100\n\nCognate Group: G2487 (step)\nVariants: Ἰωήλ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3100 יֹואֵל",
    2494: "Ἰωνάν (Iōnán | ee-o-nan')\n\nDerivation: probably for G2491 or G2495\nStrong's: Jonan, an Israelite\nKJV: —Jonan.\n\nSee: G2491 \nSee: G2495 \n\nCognate Group: G2487 (step)\nVariants: Ἰωνάν, Ἰωνάμ",
    2495: "Ἰωνᾶς (Iōnâs | ee-o-nas')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3124)\nStrong's: Jonas (i.e. Jonah), the name of two Israelites\nKJV: —Jonas.\nSee: H3124\n\nCognate Group: G2495 (Jonas)\nVariants: Ἰωνᾶς \nHebrew Equivalents: H3124 יֹונָה",
    2496: "Ἰωράμ (Iōrám | ee-o-ram')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3141)\nStrong's: Joram, an Israelite\nKJV: —Joram.\nSee: H3141\n\nCognate Group: G2495 (Jonas)\nVariants: Ἰωράμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3141 יֹורָם",
    2497: "Ἰωρείμ (Iōreím | ee-o-rime')\n\nDerivation: perhaps for G2496\nStrong's: Jorim, an Israelite\nKJV: —Jorim.\n\nSee: G2496 \n\nCognate Group: G2495 (Jonas)\nVariants: Ἰωρείμ, Ἰωρίμ",
    2498: "Ἰωσαφάτ (Iōsaphát | ee-o-saf-at')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3092)\nStrong's: Josaphat (i.e. Jehoshaphat), an Israelite\nKJV: —Josaphat.\nSee: H3092\n\nCognate Group: G2495 (Jonas)\nVariants: Ἰωσαφάτ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3092 יְהֹושָׁפָט",
    2499: "Ἰωσή (Iōsḗ | ee-o-say')\n\nDerivation: genitive case of G2500\nStrong's: Jose, an Israelite\nKJV: —Jose.\n\nSee: G2500 \n\nCognate Group: G2495 (Jonas)\nVariants: Ἰωσή G2735",
    2500: "Ἰωσῆς (Iōsēs | ee-o-sace')\n\nDerivation: perhaps for G2501\nStrong's: Joses, the name of two Israelites\nKJV: —Joses. Compare G2499 .\n\nSee: G2501 \nSee: G2499 \n\nCognate Group: G2495 (Jonas)\nVariants: Ἰωσῆς",
    2501: "Ἰωσήφ (Iōsḗph | ee-o-safe')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3130)\nStrong's: Joseph, the name of seven Israelites\nKJV: —Joseph.\nSee: H3130\n\nCognate Group: G2501 (Joseph)\nVariants: Ἰωσήφ, Ἰωσήχ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3130 יֹוסֵף",
    2502: "Ἰωσίας (Iōsías | ee-o-see'-as)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H2977)\nStrong's: Josias (i.e. Joshiah), an Israelite\nKJV: —Josias.\nSee: H2977\n\nCognate Group: G2501 (Joseph)\nVariants: Ἰωσίας \nHebrew Equivalents: H2977 יֹאשִׁיָּה",
    2503: "ἰῶτα (iōta | ee-o'-tah)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (the tenth letter of the Hebrew alphabet)\nStrong's: \"iota\", the name of the eighth letter of the Greek alphabet, put (figuratively) for a very small part of anything\nKJV: —jot.\n\nCognate Group: G2501 (Joseph)\nVariants: ἰῶτα",
    2504: "κἀγώ (kagṓ | kag-o')\n\n\nDerivation: from G2532 \n and (or also, even, etc.) I, (to) me\nKJV: —(and, even, even so, so) I (also, in like wise), both me, me also.\n\nSee: G2532 \nSee: G1473 \n\nCognate Group: G2501 (Joseph)",
    2505: "καθά (kathá | kath-ah')\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and the neuter plural of G3739\nStrong's: according to which things, i.e. just as\nKJV: —as.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G3739 \n\nCognate Group: G2505 (as)\nVariants: καθά",
    2506: "καθαίρεσις (kathaíresis | kath-ah'-ee-res-is)\n\nDerivation: from G2507\nStrong's: demolition; figuratively, extinction\nKJV: —destruction, pulling down.\n\nSee: G2507 \n\nCognate Group: G2506 (destruction), G2507 (cast down)\nVariants: καθαίρεσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H2040 הָרַס",
    2507: "καθαιρέω (kathairéō | kath-ahee-reh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G138 (including its alternate)\nStrong's: to lower (or with violence) demolish (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —cast (pull, put, take) down, destroy.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G138 \n\nCognate Group: G2506 (destruction), G2507 (cast down)\nVariants: καθαιρέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1792 דָּכָא, H2040 הָרַס, H3381 יָרַד, H3772 כָּרַת, H5256 נְסַח, H5327 נָצָה, H5422 נָתַץ, H5428 נָתַשׁ, H5493 סוּר, H6555 פָּרַץ, H7300 רוּד",
    2508: "καθαίρω (kathaírō | kath-ah'-ee-ro)\n\nDerivation: from G2513\nStrong's: to cleanse, i.e. (specially) to prune; figuratively, to expiate\nKJV: —purge.\n\nSee: G2513 \n\nCognate Group: G2514 (purification), G169 (foul), G167 (uncleanness), G4027 (filth), G2508 (purge), G1571 (purge), G2512 (cleansing), G2511 (clean), G168 (filthiness), G2513 (clean)\nVariants: καθαίρω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1758 דּוּשׁ",
    2509: "καθάπερ (katháper | kath-ap'-er)\n\nDerivation: from G2505 and G4007\nStrong's: exactly as\nKJV: —(even, as well) as.\n\nSee: G2505 \nSee: G4007 \n\nCognate Group: G2514 (purification), G169 (foul), G167 (uncleanness), G4027 (filth), G2508 (purge), G1571 (purge), G2512 (cleansing), G2511 (clean), G168 (filthiness), G2513 (clean)\nVariants: καθάπερ, καθώσπερ \nHebrew Equivalents: H834 אֲשֶׁר",
    2510: "καθάπτω (katháptō | kath-ap'-to)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G680\nStrong's: to seize upon\nKJV: —fasten on.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G680 \n\nCognate Group: G2514 (purification), G169 (foul), G167 (uncleanness), G4027 (filth), G2508 (purge), G1571 (purge), G2512 (cleansing), G2511 (clean), G168 (filthiness), G2513 (clean)\nVariants: καθάπτω",
    2511: "καθαρίζω (katharízō | kath-ar-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2513\nStrong's: to cleanse (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —(make) clean(-se), purge, purify.\n\nSee: G2513 \n\nCognate Group: G2514 (purification), G169 (foul), G167 (uncleanness), G4027 (filth), G2508 (purge), G1571 (purge), G2512 (cleansing), G2511 (clean), G168 (filthiness), G2513 (clean)\nVariants: καθαρίζω, καθερίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H622 אָסַף, H1197 בָּעַר, H2212 זָקַק, H2398 חָטָא, H2891 טָהֵר, H3722 כָּפַר, H3836 לָבָן, H5337 נָצַל, H5352 נָקָה, H5545 סָלַח, H6663 צָדַק, H6884 צָרַף, H6942 קָדַשׁ",
    2512: "καθαρισμός (katharismós | kath-ar-is-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G2511\nStrong's: a washing off, i.e. (ceremonially) ablution, (morally) expiation\nKJV: —cleansing, + purge, purification(-fying).\n\nSee: G2511 \n\nCognate Group: G2514 (purification), G169 (foul), G167 (uncleanness), G4027 (filth), G2508 (purge), G1571 (purge), G2512 (cleansing), G2511 (clean), G168 (filthiness), G2513 (clean)\nVariants: καθαρισμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H817 אָשָׁם, H2891 טָהֵר, H2893 טׇהֳרָה, H3725 כִּפֻּר, H5352 נָקָה, H5674 עָבַר",
    2513: "καθαρός (katharós | kath-ar-os')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: clean (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —clean, clear, pure.\n\nCognate Group: G2514 (purification), G169 (foul), G167 (uncleanness), G4027 (filth), G2508 (purge), G1571 (purge), G2512 (cleansing), G2511 (clean), G168 (filthiness), G2513 (clean)\nVariants: καθαρός \nHebrew Equivalents: H1249 בַּר, H2134 זַךְ, H2135 זָכָה, H2219 זָרָה, H2889 טָהֹור, H2891 טָהֵר, H3476 יֹשֶׁר, H3559 כּוּן, H4356 מִכְלָאָה, H4839 מָרָק, H5343 נְקֵא, H5352 נָקָה, H5355 נָקִי, H5462 סָגַר, H6918 קָדֹושׁ, H7845 שַׁחַת, H8420 תָּו, H8537 תֹּם",
    2514: "καθαρότης (katharótēs | kath-ar-ot'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G2513\nStrong's: cleanness (ceremonially)\nKJV: —purification.\n\nSee: G2513 \n\nCognate Group: G2514 (purification), G169 (foul), G167 (uncleanness), G4027 (filth), G2508 (purge), G1571 (purge), G2512 (cleansing), G2511 (clean), G168 (filthiness), G2513 (clean)\nVariants: καθαρότης \nHebrew Equivalents: H2892 טֹהַר",
    2515: "καθέδρα (kathédra | kath-ed'-rah)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and the same as G1476\nStrong's: a bench (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —seat.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G1476 \n\nCognate Group: G2515 (seat)\nVariants: καθέδρα \nHebrew Equivalents: H4186 מֹושָׁב",
    2516: "καθέζομαι (kathézomai | kath-ed'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and the base of G1476\nStrong's: to sit down\nKJV: —sit.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G1476 \n\nCognate Group: G2516 (sit), G2523 (continue), G2521 (dwell)\nVariants: καθέζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H3427 יָשַׁב, H7931 שָׁכַן",
    2517: "καθεξῆς (kathexēs | kath-ex-ace')\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G1836\nStrong's: thereafter, i.e. consecutively; as a noun (by ellipsis of noun) a subsequent person or time\nKJV: —after(-ward), by (in) order.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G1836 \n\nCognate Group: G2516 (sit), G2523 (continue), G2521 (dwell)\nVariants: καθεξῆς",
    2518: "καθεύδω (katheúdō | kath-yoo'-do)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and εὕδω (to sleep)\nStrong's: to lie down to rest, i.e. (by implication) to fall asleep (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —(be a-)sleep.\n\nSee: G2596 \n\nCognate Group: G2518 (sleep)\nVariants: καθεύδω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3427 יָשַׁב, H3462 יָשֵׁן, H7901 שָׁכַב",
    2519: "καθηγητής (kathēgētḗs | kath-ayg-ay-tace')\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2596 and G2233\nStrong's: a guide, i.e. (figuratively) a teacher\nKJV: —master.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2233 \n\nCognate Group: G2518 (sleep)\nVariants: καθηγητής",
    2520: "καθήκω (kathḗkō | kath-ay'-ko)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G2240\nStrong's: to reach to, i.e. (neuter of present active participle, figuratively as adjective) becoming\nKJV: — convenient, fit.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2240 \n\nCognate Group: G2520 (convenient)\nVariants: καθήκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1696 דָבַר, H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H3117 יֹום, H4941 מִשְׁפָּט, H5656 עֲבֹדָה",
    2521: "κάθημαι (káthēmai | kath'-ay-mahee)\n\nDerivation: from G2596\nStrong's: and ἧμαι (to sit; akin to the base of G1476); to sit down; figuratively, to remain, reside\nKJV: —dwell, sit (by, down).\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G1476 \n\nCognate Group: G2516 (sit), G2523 (continue), G2521 (dwell)\nVariants: κάθημαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1961 הָיָה, H1980 הָלַךְ, H3427 יָשַׁב, H5526 סָכַךְ, H7392 רָכַב, H7901 שָׁכַב",
    2522: "καθημερινός (kathēmerinós | kath-ay-mer-ee-nos')\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G2250\nStrong's: quotidian\nKJV: —daily.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2250 \n\nCognate Group: G2516 (sit), G2523 (continue), G2521 (dwell)\nVariants: καθημερινός",
    2523: "καθίζω (kathízō | kath-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: another (active) form for G2516\nStrong's: to seat down, i.e. set (figuratively, appoint); intransitively, to sit (down); figuratively, to settle (hover, dwell)\nKJV: —continue, set, sit (down), tarry.\n\nSee: G2516 \n\nCognate Group: G2516 (sit), G2523 (continue), G2521 (dwell)\nVariants: καθίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1481 גּוּר, H1961 הָיָה, H3427 יָשַׁב, H5117 נוּחַ, H5307 נָפַל, H6296 פָּגַר, H6696 צוּר, H7392 רָכַב",
    2524: "καθίημι (kathíēmi | kath-ee'-ay-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G2596\nStrong's: and ἵημι (to send); to lower\nKJV: —let down.\n\nSee: G2596 \n\nCognate Group: G2516 (sit), G2523 (continue), G2521 (dwell)\nVariants: καθίημι \nHebrew Equivalents: H5117 נוּחַ, H5414 נָתַן, H7725 שׁוּב, H7993 שָׁלַךְ",
    2525: "καθίστημι (kathístēmi | kath-is'-tay-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G2476\nStrong's: to place down (permanently), i.e. (figuratively) to designate, constitute, convoy\nKJV: —appoint, be, conduct, make, ordain, set.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2476 \n\nCognate Group: G182 (unstable), G181 (commotion), G2525 (appoint)\nVariants: καθίστημι, καθιστάνω, καθίστημι/καθιστάνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H622 אָסַף, H935 בֹּוא, H2388 חָזַק, H3320 יָצַב, H3559 כּוּן, H4427 מָלַךְ, H4487 מָנָה, H4886 מָשַׁח, H4911 מָשַׁל, H4950 מִשְׁקָע, H5117 נוּחַ, H5258 נָסַךְ, H5324 נָצַב, H5414 נָתַן, H5975 עָמַד, H6485 פָּקַד, H6680 צָוָה, H6750 צָלַל, H6965 קוּם, H7725 שׁוּב, H7760 שׂוּם, H7896 שִׁית, H7981 שְׁלֵט",
    2526: "καθό (kathó | kath-o')\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G3739\nStrong's: according to which thing, i.e. precisely as, in proportion as\nKJV: —according to that, (inasmuch) as.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G3739 \n\nCognate Group: G182 (unstable), G181 (commotion), G2525 (appoint)\nVariants: καθό, καθολικός \nHebrew Equivalents: H834 אֲשֶׁר",
    2527: "καθόλου (kathólou | kath-ol'-oo)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G3650\nStrong's: on the whole, i.e. entirely\nKJV: —at all.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G3650 \n\nCognate Group: G182 (unstable), G181 (commotion), G2525 (appoint)\nVariants: καθόλου \nHebrew Equivalents: H1115 בִּלְתִּי",
    2528: "καθοπλίζω (kathoplízō | kath-op-lid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2596\nStrong's: and G3695 ; to equip fully with armor\nKJV: —arm.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G3695 \n\nCognate Group: G3695 (arm self), G3696 (armour), G2528 (arm), G3833 (all armour)\nVariants: καθοπλίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H8610 תָּפַשׂ",
    2529: "καθοράω (kathoráō | kath-or-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G3708\nStrong's: to behold fully, i.e. (figuratively) distinctly apprehend\nKJV: —clearly see.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G3708 \n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: καθοράω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7200 רָאָה",
    2530: "καθότι (kathóti | kath-ot'-ee)\n\nDerivation: from G2596\nStrong's: and G3739 and G5100 ; according to which certain thing, i.e. as far (or inasmuch) as\nKJV: —(according, forasmuch) as, because (that).\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G3739 \nSee: G5100 \n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: καθότι \nHebrew Equivalents: H834 אֲשֶׁר",
    2531: "καθώς (kathṓs | kath-oce')\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G5613\nStrong's: just (or inasmuch) as, that\nKJV: —according to, (according, even) as, how, when.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G5613 \n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: καθώς",
    2532: "καί (kaí | kahee)\n\nDerivation: apparently, a primary particle, having a copulative and sometimes also a cumulative force\nStrong's: and, also, even, so then, too, etc.; often used in connection (or composition) with other particles or small words\nKJV: —and, also, both, but, even, for, if, or, so, that, then, therefore, when, yet.\n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: καί",
    2533: "Καϊάφας (Kaïáphas | kah-ee-af'-as)\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin\nStrong's: the dell; Caiaphas (i.e. Cajepha), an Israelite\nKJV: —Caiaphas.\n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: Καϊάφας",
    2534: "καίγε (kaíge | kah'-ee-gheh)\n\nDerivation: from G2532 and G1065\nStrong's: and at least (or even, indeed)\nKJV: —and, at least.\n\nSee: G2532 \nSee: G1065 \n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: καίγε G2781",
    2535: "Κάϊν (Káïn | kah'-in)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H7014)\nStrong's: Cain, (i.e. Cajin), the son of Adam\nKJV: —Cain.\nSee: H7014\n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: Κάϊν \nHebrew Equivalents: H7013 קַיִן, H7014 קַיִן",
    2536: "Καϊνάν (Kaïnán | kah-ee-nan')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H7018)\nStrong's: Cainan (i.e. Kenan), the name of two patriarchs\nKJV: —Cainan.\nSee: H7018\n\nCognate Group: G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)\nVariants: Καϊνάν, Καϊνάμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H7018 קֵינָן",
    2537: "καινός (kainós | kahee-nos')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity; new (especially in freshness; while G3501 is properly so with respect to age\nKJV: —new.\n\nSee: G3501 \n\nCognate Group: G365 (renew), G341 (renew), G340 (renew), G1457 (consecrate), G342 (renewing), G2538 (newness), G2537 (new)\nVariants: καινός \nHebrew Equivalents: H312 אַחֵר, H2319 חָדָשׁ",
    2538: "καινότης (kainótēs | kahee-not'-ace)\n\nDerivation: from G2537\nStrong's: renewal (figuratively)\nKJV: —newness.\n\nSee: G2537 \n\nCognate Group: G365 (renew), G341 (renew), G340 (renew), G1457 (consecrate), G342 (renewing), G2538 (newness), G2537 (new)\nVariants: καινότης",
    2539: "καίπερ (kaíper | kah'-ee-per)\n\nDerivation: from G2532 and G4007\nStrong's: and indeed, i.e. nevertheless or notwithstanding\nKJV: —and yet, although.\n\nSee: G2532 \nSee: G4007 \n\nCognate Group: G365 (renew), G341 (renew), G340 (renew), G1457 (consecrate), G342 (renewing), G2538 (newness), G2537 (new)\nVariants: καίπερ",
    2540: "καιρός (kairós | kahee-ros')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: an occasion, i.e. set or proper time\nKJV: —X always, opportunity, (convenient, due) season, (due, short, while) time, a while. Compare G5550 .\n\nSee: G5550 \n\nCognate Group: G2120 (opportunity), G2121 (convenient), G170 (lack opportunity), G4340 (dur- for awhile), G171 (out of season), G2540 (X always), G2122 (conveniently)\nVariants: καιρός \nHebrew Equivalents: H314 אַחֲרֹון, H2165 זְמָן, H3117 יֹום, H4150 מֹועֵד, H5704 עַד, H5732 עִדָּן, H5844 עָטָה, H6106 עֶצֶם, H6256 עֵת, H6471 פַּעַם, H6738 צֵל, H7093 קֵץ, H7272 רֶגֶל, H8141 שָׁנֶה, H8447 תֹּור, H8454 תּוּשִׁיָּה, H8622 תְּקוּפָה",
    2541: "Καῖσαρ (Kaîsar | kah'-ee-sar)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: Cæsar, a title of the Roman emperor\nKJV: —Cæsar.\n\nCognate Group: G2120 (opportunity), G2121 (convenient), G170 (lack opportunity), G4340 (dur- for awhile), G171 (out of season), G2540 (X always), G2122 (conveniently)\nVariants: Καῖσαρ",
    2542: "Καισάρεια (Kaisáreia | kahee-sar'-i-a)\n\nDerivation: from G2541\nStrong's: Cæsaria, the name of two places in Palestine\nKJV: —Cæsarea.\n\nSee: G2541 \n\nCognate Group: G2120 (opportunity), G2121 (convenient), G170 (lack opportunity), G4340 (dur- for awhile), G171 (out of season), G2540 (X always), G2122 (conveniently)\nVariants: Καισάρεια",
    2543: "καίτοι (kaítoi | kah'-ee-toy)\n\nDerivation: from G2532 and G5104\nStrong's: and yet, i.e. nevertheless\nKJV: —although.\n\nSee: G2532 \nSee: G5104 \n\nCognate Group: G2120 (opportunity), G2121 (convenient), G170 (lack opportunity), G4340 (dur- for awhile), G171 (out of season), G2540 (X always), G2122 (conveniently)\nVariants: καίτοι",
    2544: "καίτοιγε (kaítoige | kah'-ee-toyg-eh)\n\nDerivation: from G2543 and G1065\nStrong's: and yet indeed, i.e. although really\nKJV: —nevertheless, though.\n\nSee: G2543 \nSee: G1065 \n\nCognate Group: G2120 (opportunity), G2121 (convenient), G170 (lack opportunity), G4340 (dur- for awhile), G171 (out of season), G2540 (X always), G2122 (conveniently)\nVariants: καίτοιγε",
    2545: "καίω (kaíō | kah'-yo)\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary verb\nStrong's: to set on fire, i.e. kindle or (by implication) consume\nKJV: —burn, light.\n\nCognate Group: G2545 (burn)\nVariants: καίω \nHebrew Equivalents: H228 אֲזָא, H398 אָכַל, H1197 בָּעַר, H1814 דָּלַק, H3341 יָצַת, H3344 יָקַד, H3852 לֶהָבָה, H5301 נָפַח, H5400 נָשַׂק, H5927 עָלָה, H6186 עָרַךְ, H6919 קָדַח, H8313 שָׂרַף",
    2546: "κἀκεῖ (kakeî | kak-i')\n\nDerivation: from G2532 and G1563\nStrong's: likewise in that place\nKJV: —and there, there (thither) also.\n\nSee: G2532 \nSee: G1563 \n\nCognate Group: G2545 (burn)\nVariants: κἀκεῖ",
