    2548: "κἀκεῖνος (kakeînos | kak-i'-nos)\n\nDerivation: from G2532 and G1565\nStrong's: likewise that (or those)\nKJV: —and him (other, them), even he, him also, them (also), (and) they.\n\nSee: G2532 \nSee: G1565 \n\nCognate Group: G2545 (burn)\nVariants: κἀκεῖνος",
    2549: "κακία (kakía | kak-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2556\nStrong's: badness, i.e. (subjectively) depravity, or (actively) malignity, or (passively) trouble\nKJV: —evil, malice(-iousness), naughtiness, wickedness.\n\nSee: G2556 \n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: κακία \nHebrew Equivalents: H7200 רָאָה",
    2550: "κακοήθεια (kakoḗtheia | kak-o-ay'-thi-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2556 and G2239\nStrong's: bad character, i.e. (specially) mischievousness\nKJV: —malignity.\n\nSee: G2556 \nSee: G2239 \n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: κακοήθεια",
    2551: "κακολογέω (kakologéō | kak-ol-og-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2556 and G3056\nStrong's: to revile\nKJV: —curse, speak evil of.\n\nSee: G2556 \nSee: G3056 \n\nCognate Group: G2551 (curse)\nVariants: κακολογέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7043 קָלַל",
    2552: "κακοπάθεια (kakopátheia | kak-op-ath'-i-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2256 and G3806\nStrong's: hardship\nKJV: —suffering affliction.\n\nSee: G2256 \nSee: G3806 \n\nCognate Group: G3663 (of like passions), G4834 (have compassion), G2552 (suffering affliction), G4236 (meekness), G3804 (affection), G3958 (feel), G3356 (have compassion), G4777 (be partaker of afflictions), G2553 (be afflicted), G4310 (suffer before), G4835 (having compassion one of another), G4841 (suffer with), G3805 (suffer), G3806 (affection)\nVariants: κακοπάθεια, καλοκαγαθία, κακοπαθία, κακοπάθεια/κακοπαθία \nHebrew Equivalents: H8513 תְּלָאָה",
    2553: "κακοπαθέω (kakopathéō | kak-op-ath-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2552\nStrong's: to undergo hardship\nKJV: —be afflicted, endure afflictions (hardness), suffer trouble.\n\nSee: G2552 \n\nCognate Group: G3663 (of like passions), G4834 (have compassion), G2552 (suffering affliction), G4236 (meekness), G3804 (affection), G3958 (feel), G3356 (have compassion), G4777 (be partaker of afflictions), G2553 (be afflicted), G4310 (suffer before), G4835 (having compassion one of another), G4841 (suffer with), G3805 (suffer), G3806 (affection)\nVariants: κακοπαθέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5999 עָמָל",
    2554: "κακοποιέω (kakopoiéō | kak-op-oy-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2555\nStrong's: to be a bad-doer, i.e. (objectively) to injure, or (genitive) to sin\nKJV: —do(ing) evil.\n\nSee: G2555 \n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: κακοποιέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5142 נְזַק, H5753 עָוָה, H7489 רָעַע",
    2555: "κακοποιός (kakopoiós | kak-op-oy-os')\n\nDerivation: from G2556 and G4160\nStrong's: a bad-doer; (specially), a criminal\nKJV: —evil-doer, malefactor.\n\nSee: G2556 \nSee: G4160 \n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: κακοποιός \nHebrew Equivalents: H954 בּוּשׁ, H7489 רָעַע",
    2556: "κακός (kakós | kak-os')\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary word\nStrong's: worthless (intrinsically, such; whereas G4190 properly refers to effects), i.e. (subjectively) depraved, or (objectively) injurious\nKJV: —bad, evil, harm, ill, noisome, wicked.\n\nSee: G4190 \n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: κακός \nHebrew Equivalents: H200 אִוֶּלֶת, H205 אָוֶן, H457 אֱלִיל, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2154 זִמָּה, H3887 לוּץ, H4066 מָדֹון, H4639 מַעֲשֶׂה, H4682 מַצָּה, H4846 מְרֹרָה, H5766 עֶוֶל, H5999 עָמָל, H6862 צַר, H7379 רִיב, H7451 רַע, H7489 רָעַע, H7562 רֶשַׁע, H7701 שֹׁד",
    2557: "κακοῦργος (kakoûrgos | kak-oor'-gos)\n\nDerivation: from G2556 and the base of G2041\nStrong's: a wrong-doer, i.e. criminal\nKJV: —evil-doer, malefactor.\n\nSee: G2556 \nSee: G2041 \n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: κακοῦργος",
    2558: "κακουχέω (kakouchéō | kak-oo-kheh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a presumed compound of G2556 and G2192\nStrong's: to maltreat\nKJV: —which suffer adversity, torment.\n\nSee: G2556 \nSee: G2192 \n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: κακουχέω, κακουχέομαι",
    2559: "κακόω (kakóō | kak-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2556\nStrong's: to injure; figuratively, to exasperate\nKJV: —make evil affected, entreat evil, harm, hurt, vex.\n\nSee: G2556 \n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: κακόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1792 דָּכָא, H3228 יְמִינִי, H3286 יָעַף, H3782 כָּשַׁל, H3905 לָחַץ, H6030 עָנָה, H6030 עָנָה, H6313 פּוּג, H7489 רָעַע, H7561 רָשַׁע, H7817 שָׁחַח",
    2560: "κακῶς (kakōs | kak-oce')\n\nDerivation: from G2556\nStrong's: badly (physically or morally)\nKJV: —amiss, diseased, evil, grievously, miserably, sick, sore.\n\nSee: G2556 \n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: κακῶς \nHebrew Equivalents: H779 אָרַר, H2470 חָלָה, H7043 קָלַל",
    2561: "κάκωσις (kákōsis | kak'-o-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G2559\nStrong's: maltreatment\nKJV: —affliction.\n\nSee: G2559 \n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: κάκωσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H343 אֵיד, H6030 עָנָה, H6041 עָנִי, H7200 רָאָה, H8577 תַּנִּין",
    2562: "καλάμη (kalámē | kal-am'-ay)\n\nDerivation: feminine of G2563\nStrong's: a stalk of grain, i.e. (collectively) stubble\nKJV: —stubble.\n\nSee: G2563 \n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: καλάμη \nHebrew Equivalents: H5296 נְעֹרֶת, H5955 עֹלֵלָה, H5995 עָמִיר, H7179 קַשׁ, H7641 שִׁבֹּל, H7898 שַׁיִת",
    2563: "κάλαμος (kálamos | kal'-am-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a reed (the plant or its stem, or that of a similar plant); by implication, a pen\nKJV: —pen, reed.\n\nCognate Group: G172 (harmless), G420 (patient), G2549 (evil), G2554 (do evil), G2555 (evil-doer), G2556 (bad), G1573 (faint), G2557 (evil-doer), G2550 (malignity)\nVariants: κάλαμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1903 הָגִין, H6256 עֵת, H7070 קָנֶה",
    2564: "καλέω (kaléō | kal-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: akin to the base of G2753\nStrong's: to \"call\" (properly, aloud, but used in a variety of applications, directly or otherwise)\nKJV: —bid, call (forth), (whose, whose sur-)name (was (called)).\n\nSee: G2753 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: καλέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H935 בֹּוא, H1696 דָבַר, H1961 הָיָה, H2142 זָכַר, H2199 זָעַק, H3947 לָקַח, H5954 עֲלַל, H7121 קָרָא, H7311 רוּם, H8034 שֵׁם",
    2565: "καλλιέλαιος (kalliélaios | kal-le-el'-ah-yos)\n\nDerivation: from the base of G2566 and G1636\nStrong's: a cultivated olive tree, i.e. a domesticated or improved one\nKJV: —good olive tree.\n\nSee: G2566 \nSee: G1636 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: καλλιέλαιος",
    2566: "καλλίον (kallíon | kal-lee'-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of the (irregular) comparative of G2570\nStrong's: (adverbially) better than many\nKJV: —very well.\n\nSee: G2570 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: καλλίον, καλός",
    2567: "καλοδιδάσκαλος (kalodidáskalos | kal-od-id-as'-kal-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2570 and G1320\nStrong's: a teacher of the right\nKJV: —teacher of good things.\n\nSee: G2570 \nSee: G1320 \n\nCognate Group: G5572 (false teacher), G2085 (teach other doctrine), G1322 (doctrine), G3547 (doctor of the law), G1317 (apt to teach), G1320 (doctor), G2567 (teacher of good things), G1321 (teach), G1319 (doctrine), G1318 (taught)\nVariants: καλοδιδάσκαλος",
    2568: "Καλοὶ Λιμένες (Kaloì Liménes | kal-oy' lee-men'-es)\n\nDerivation: plural of G2570 and G3040\nStrong's: Good Harbors, i.e. Fairhaven, a bay of Crete\nKJV: —fair havens.\n\nSee: G2570 \nSee: G3040 \n\nCognate Group: G5572 (false teacher), G2085 (teach other doctrine), G1322 (doctrine), G3547 (doctor of the law), G1317 (apt to teach), G1320 (doctor), G2567 (teacher of good things), G1321 (teach), G1319 (doctrine), G1318 (taught)\nVariants: Καλοὶ Λιμένες, Καλοὶ λιμένες",
    2569: "καλοποιέω (kalopoiéō | kal-op-oy-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2570 and G4160\nStrong's: to do well, i.e. live virtuously\nKJV: —well doing.\n\nSee: G2570 \nSee: G4160 \n\nCognate Group: G5572 (false teacher), G2085 (teach other doctrine), G1322 (doctrine), G3547 (doctor of the law), G1317 (apt to teach), G1320 (doctor), G2567 (teacher of good things), G1321 (teach), G1319 (doctrine), G1318 (taught)\nVariants: καλοποιέω",
    2570: "καλός (kalós | kal-os')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity; properly, beautiful, but chiefly (figuratively) good (literally or morally), i.e. valuable or virtuous (for appearance or use, and thus distinguished from G18, which is properly intrinsic)\nKJV: —X better, fair, good(-ly), honest, meet, well, worthy.\n\nSee: G18 \n\nCognate Group: G2570 (X better)\nVariants: καλός, Καλός, Καλοὶ~λιμένες, Καλοὶ λιμένες \nHebrew Equivalents: H2531 חֶמֶד, H3190 יָטַב, H3302 יָפָה, H3303 יָפֶה, H3303 יָפֶה, H3477 יָשָׁר, H3519 כָּבֹוד, H4209 מְזִמָּה, H5116 נָוֶה, H5273 נָעִים, H5276 נָעֵם, H8034 שֵׁם",
    2571: "κάλυμα (kályma | kal'-oo-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2572\nStrong's: a cover, i.e. veil\nKJV: —vail.\n\nSee: G2572 \n\nCognate Group: G602 (appearing), G343 (open), G2571 (vail), G2572 (cover), G2619 (cover), G601 (reveal)\nVariants: κάλυμα, κάλυμμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H3681 כָּסוּי, H4374 מְכַסֶּה, H4533 מַסְוֶה, H4539 מָסָךְ, H4908 מִשְׁכָּן",
    2572: "καλύπτω (kalýptō | kal-oop'-to)\n\nDerivation: akin to G2813 and G2928\nStrong's: to cover up (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —cover, hide.\n\nSee: G2813 \nSee: G2928 \n\nCognate Group: G602 (appearing), G343 (open), G2571 (vail), G2572 (cover), G2619 (cover), G601 (reveal)\nVariants: καλύπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3680 כָּסָה, H5640 סָתַם, H6822 צָפָה",
    2573: "καλῶς (kalōs | kal-oce')\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2570\nStrong's: well (usually morally)\nKJV: —(in a) good (place), honestly, + recover, (full) well.\n\nSee: G2570 \n\nCognate Group: G602 (appearing), G343 (open), G2571 (vail), G2572 (cover), G2619 (cover), G601 (reveal)\nVariants: καλῶς \nHebrew Equivalents: H2895 טֹוב, H3190 יָטַב, H3190 יָטַב",
    2574: "κάμηλος (kámēlos | kam'-ay-los)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H1581)\nStrong's: a \"camel\"\nKJV: —camel.\nSee: H1581\n\nCognate Group: G2574 (camel)\nVariants: κάμηλος, κάμιλος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1070 בֶּכֶר, H1580 גָּמַל, H1581 גָּמָל",
    2575: "κάμινος (káminos | kam'-ee-nos)\n\nDerivation: probably from G2545\nStrong's: a furnace\nKJV: —furnace.\n\nSee: G2545 \n\nCognate Group: G2574 (camel)\nVariants: κάμινος \nHebrew Equivalents: H861 אַתּוּן, H1731 דּוּד, H3536 כִּבְשָׁן, H3564 כּוּר, H6898 קֻבָּה",
    2576: "καμμύω (kammýō | kam-moo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2596 and the base of G3466\nStrong's: to shut down, i.e. close the eyes\nKJV: —close.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G3466 \n\nCognate Group: G2574 (camel)\nVariants: καμμύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6105 עָצַם, H8173 שָׁעַע",
    2577: "κάμνω (kámnō | kam'-no)\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary verb\nStrong's: properly, to toil, i.e. (by implication) to tire (figuratively, faint, sicken)\nKJV: —faint, sick, be wearied.\n\nCognate Group: G2574 (camel)\nVariants: κάμνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6962 קוּט",
    2578: "κάμπτω (kámptō | kamp'-to)\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary verb\nStrong's: to bend\nKJV: —bow.\n\nCognate Group: G2578 (bow)\nVariants: κάμπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1289 בְּרַךְ, H3766 כָּרַע, H6915 קָדַד, H7817 שָׁחַח",
    2579: "κἄν (kán | kan)\n\nDerivation: from G2532 and G1437\nStrong's: and (or even) if\nKJV: —and (also) if (so much as), if but, at the least, though, yet.\n\nSee: G2532 \nSee: G1437 \n\nCognate Group: G2578 (bow)\nVariants: κἄν",
    2580: "Κανᾶ (Kanâ | kan-ah')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (compare H7071)\nStrong's: Cana, a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Cana.\nSee: H7071\n\nCognate Group: G2578 (bow)\nVariants: Κανᾶ, Κανά \nHebrew Equivalents: H7071 קָנָה",
    2581: "Κανανίτης (Kananítēs | kan-an-ee'-tace)\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (compare H7067)\nStrong's: zealous; Cananites, an epithet\nKJV: —Canaanite (by mistake for a derivative from G5477).\n\nSee: G5477 \nSee: H7067\n\nCognate Group: G2578 (bow)\nVariants: Κανανίτης, Καναναῖος \nHebrew Equivalents: H7067 קַנָּא",
    2582: "Κανδάκη (Kandákē | kan-dak'-ay)\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Candacè, an Egyptian queen\nKJV: —Candace.\n\nCognate Group: G2578 (bow)\nVariants: Κανδάκη",
    2583: "κανών (kanṓn | kan-ohn')\n\nDerivation: from κάνη (a straight reed, i.e. rod)\nStrong's: a rule (\"canon\"), i.e. (figuratively) a standard (of faith and practice); by implication, a boundary, i.e. (figuratively) a sphere (of activity)\nKJV: —line, rule.\n\nCognate Group: G2583 (line)\nVariants: κανών \nHebrew Equivalents: H7070 קָנֶה",
    2584: "Καπερναούμ (Kapernaoúm | cap-er-nah-oom')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (probably H3723 and H5151)\nStrong's: Capernaum (i.e. Caphanachum), a place in Palestine\nKJV: —Capernaum.\nSee: H3723\nSee: H5151\n\nCognate Group: G2583 (line)\nVariants: Καπερναούμ, Καφαρναούμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3723 כָּפָר, H5151 נַחוּם",
    2585: "καπηλεύω (kapēleúō | kap-ale-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from κάπηλος (a huckster)\nStrong's: to retail, i.e. (by implication) to adulterate (figuratively)\nKJV: —corrupt.\n\nCognate Group: G2585 (corrupt)\nVariants: καπηλεύω",
    2586: "καπνός (kapnós | kap-nos')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: smoke\nKJV: —smoke.\n\nCognate Group: G2585 (corrupt)\nVariants: καπνός \nHebrew Equivalents: H6227 עָשָׁן",
    2587: "Καππαδοκία (Kappadokía | kap-pad-ok-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin\nStrong's: Cappadocia, a region of Asia Minor\nKJV: —Cappadocia.\n\nCognate Group: G2585 (corrupt)\nVariants: Καππαδοκία",
    2588: "καρδία (kardía | kar-dee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: prolonged from a primary κάρ (Latin cor, \"heart\")\nStrong's: the heart, i.e. (figuratively) the thoughts or feelings (mind); also (by analogy) the middle\nKJV: —(+ broken-)heart(-ed).\n\nCognate Group: G4641 (hardness of heart), G2589 (which knowest the hearts), G2588 (heart)\nVariants: καρδία \nHebrew Equivalents: H990 בֶּטֶן, H995 בִּין, H2403 חַטָּאָה, H3820 לֵב, H3824 לֵבָב, H4596 מְעִי, H5315 נֶפֶשׁ, H6203 עֹרֶף, H7130 קֶרֶב",
    2589: "καρδιογνώστης (kardiognṓstēs | kar-dee-og-noce'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G2588 and G1097\nStrong's: a heart-knower\nKJV: —which knowest the hearts.\n\nSee: G2588 \nSee: G1097 \n\nCognate Group: G4641 (hardness of heart), G2589 (which knowest the hearts), G2588 (heart)\nVariants: καρδιογνώστης",
    2590: "καρπός (karpós | kar-pos')\n\nDerivation: probably from the base of G726\nStrong's: fruit (as plucked), literally or figuratively\nKJV: —fruit.\n\nSee: G726 \n\nCognate Group: G2591 (Carpus), G2590 (fruit), G2592 (be fruitful), G2593 (fruitful), G175 (without fruit)\nVariants: καρπός \nHebrew Equivalents: H3 אֵב, H1061 בִּכּוּר, H2172 זִמְרָה, H2981 יְבוּל, H3018 יְגִיעַ, H3323 יִצְהָר, H6529 פְּרִי, H8378 תַּאֲוָה, H8393 תְּבוּאָה, H8570 תְּנוּבָה",
    2591: "Κάρπος (Kárpos | kar'-pos)\n\nDerivation: perhaps for G2590\nStrong's: Carpus, probably a Christian\nKJV: —Carpus.\n\nSee: G2590 \n\nCognate Group: G2591 (Carpus), G2590 (fruit), G2592 (be fruitful), G2593 (fruitful), G175 (without fruit)\nVariants: Κάρπος",
    2592: "καρποφορέω (karpophoréō | kar-pof-or-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2593\nStrong's: to be fertile (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —be (bear, bring forth) fruit(-ful).\n\nSee: G2593 \n\nCognate Group: G2591 (Carpus), G2590 (fruit), G2592 (be fruitful), G2593 (fruitful), G175 (without fruit)\nVariants: καρποφορέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H6524 פָּרַח",
    2593: "καρποφόρος (karpophóros | kar-pof-or'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2590 and G5342\nStrong's: fruitbearing (figuratively)\nKJV: —fruitful.\n\nSee: G2590 \nSee: G5342 \n\nCognate Group: G2591 (Carpus), G2590 (fruit), G2592 (be fruitful), G2593 (fruitful), G175 (without fruit)\nVariants: καρποφόρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2233 זֶרַע, H6529 פְּרִי",
    2594: "καρτερέω (karteréō | kar-ter-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2904 (transposed)\nStrong's: to be strong, i.e. (figuratively) steadfast (patient)\nKJV: —endure.\n\nSee: G2904 \n\nCognate Group: G4343 (perseverance), G4342 (attend continually), G2594 (endure)\nVariants: καρτερέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2388 חָזַק, H6284 פָּאָה",
    2595: "κάρφος (kárphos | kar'-fos)\n\nDerivation: from κάρφω (to wither)\nStrong's: a dry twig or straw\nKJV: —mote.\n\nCognate Group: G4343 (perseverance), G4342 (attend continually), G2594 (endure)\nVariants: κάρφος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2963 טָרַף",
    2596: "κατά (katá | kat-ah')\n\nDerivation: a primary particle\nStrong's: (prepositionally) down (in place or time), in varied relations (according to the case (genitive, dative or accusative) with which it is joined)\nKJV: —about, according as (to), after, against, (when they were) X alone, among, and, X apart, (even, like) as (concerning, pertaining to touching), X aside, at, before, beyond, by, to the charge of, (charita-)bly, concerning, + covered, (dai-)ly, down, every, (+ far more) exceeding, X more excellent, for, from … to, godly, in(-asmuch, divers, every, -to, respect of), … by, after the manner of, + by any means, beyond (out of) measure, X mightily, more, X natural, of (up-)on (X part), out (of every), over against, (+ your) X own, + particularly, so, through(-oughout, -oughout every), thus, (un-)to(-gether, -ward), X uttermost, where(-by), with. In composition it retains many of these applications, and frequently denotes opposition, distribution, or intensity.\n\nCognate Group: G4343 (perseverance), G4342 (attend continually), G2594 (endure)\nVariants: κατά, καθεῖς, καθημέραν, κατακύπτω",
    2597: "καταβαίνω (katabaínō | kat-ab-ah'-ee-no)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and the base of G939\nStrong's: to descend (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —come (get, go, step) down, fall (down).\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G305 (arise), G3397 (a), G2597 (come down)\nVariants: καταβαίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H935 בֹּוא, H1652 גָּשַׁם, H1692 דָּבַק, H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2244 חָבָא, H2782 חָרַץ, H3318 יָצָא, H3381 יָרַד, H3426 יֵשׁ, H3886 לוּעַ, H5060 נָגַע, H5074 נָדַד, H5140 נָזַל, H5181 נָחַת, H6437 פָּנָה, H7200 רָאָה, H7291 רָדַף, H7725 שׁוּב, H7931 שָׁכַן, H8257 שָׁקַע",
    2598: "καταβάλλω (katabállō | kat-ab-al'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G906\nStrong's: to throw down\nKJV: —cast down, lay.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G906 \n\nCognate Group: G305 (arise), G3397 (a), G2597 (come down)\nVariants: καταβάλλω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2040 הָרַס, H3947 לָקַח, H5307 נָפַל, H5422 נָתַץ, H5428 נָתַשׁ, H5640 סָתַם, H6555 פָּרַץ, H7843 שָׁחַת, H8213 שָׁפֵל",
    2599: "καταβαρέω (katabaréō | kat-ab-ar-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G916\nStrong's: to impose upon\nKJV: —burden.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G916 \n\nCognate Group: G305 (arise), G3397 (a), G2597 (come down)\nVariants: καταβαρέω",
    2600: "κατάβασις (katábasis | kat-ab'-as-is)\n\nDerivation: from G2597\nStrong's: a declivity\nKJV: —descent.\n\nSee: G2597 \n\nCognate Group: G305 (arise), G3397 (a), G2597 (come down)\nVariants: κατάβασις",
    2601: "καταβιβάζω (katabibázō | kat-ab-ib-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and a derivative of the base of G939\nStrong's: to cause to go down, i.e. precipitate\nKJV: —bring (thrust) down.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G939 \n\nCognate Group: G305 (arise), G3397 (a), G2597 (come down)\nVariants: καταβιβάζω G2854 \nHebrew Equivalents: H3381 יָרַד",
    2602: "καταβολή (katabolḗ | kat-ab-ol-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G2598\nStrong's: a deposition, i.e. founding; figuratively, conception\nKJV: —conceive, foundation.\n\nSee: G2598 \n\nCognate Group: G2602 (conceive)\nVariants: καταβολή",
    2603: "καταβραβεύω (katabrabeúō | kat-ab-rab-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G1018 (in its original sense)\nStrong's: to award the price against, i.e. (figuratively) to defraud (of salvation)\nKJV: —beguile of reward.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G1018 \n\nCognate Group: G2602 (conceive)\nVariants: καταβραβεύω",
    2604: "καταγγελεύς (katangeleús | kat-ang-gel-yooce')\n\nDerivation: from G2605\nStrong's: a proclaimer\nKJV: —setter forth.\n\nSee: G2605 \n\nCognate Group: G1229 (declare), G31 (message), G1804 (shew forth), G518 (bring word), G2604 (setter forth), G4293 (foretell), G312 (declare), G2605 (declare)\nVariants: καταγγελεύς",
    2605: "καταγγέλλω (katangéllō | kat-ang-gel'-lo)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and the base of G32\nStrong's: to proclaim, promulgate\nKJV: —declare, preach, shew, speak of, teach.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G32 \n\nCognate Group: G1229 (declare), G31 (message), G1804 (shew forth), G518 (bring word), G2604 (setter forth), G4293 (foretell), G312 (declare), G2605 (declare)\nVariants: καταγγέλλω",
    2606: "καταγελάω (katageláō | kat-ag-el-ah'-o)\n\n\nStrong's: to laugh down, i.e. deride\nKJV: —laugh to scorn.\n\nCognate Group: G2606 (laugh to scorn), G1071 (laughter), G1070 (laugh)\nVariants: καταγελάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1961 הָיָה, H2659 חָפֵר, H3932 לָעַג, H5970 עָלַץ, H7832 שָׂחַק",
    2607: "καταγινώσκω (kataginṓskō | kat-ag-in-o'-sko)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G1097\nStrong's: to note against, i.e. find fault with\nKJV: —blame, condemn.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G1097 \n\nCognate Group: G1110 (acquaintance), G1097 (allow), G1106 (advice), G4268 (foreknowledge), G1922 (acknowledging), G4774 (permission), G4267 (foreknow), G1107 (certify), G1921 (acknowledge), G1108 (knowledge), G176 (that cannot be condemned), G2607 (blame)\nVariants: καταγινώσκω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2713 חָקַר, H7561 רָשַׁע",
