    2673: "καταργέω (katargéō | kat-arg-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G691\nStrong's: to be (render) entirely idle (useless), literally or figuratively\nKJV: —abolish, cease, cumber, deliver, destroy, do away, become (make) of no (none, without) effect, fail, loose, bring (come) to nought, put away (down), vanish away, make void.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G691 \n\nCognate Group: G692 (barren), G2673 (abolish), G691 (linger)\nVariants: καταργέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H989 בְּטֵל",
    2674: "καταριθμέω (katarithméō | kat-ar-ith-meh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G705\nStrong's: to reckon among\nKJV: —number with.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G705 \n\nCognate Group: G692 (barren), G2673 (abolish), G691 (linger)\nVariants: καταριθμέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3187 יָחַשׂ, H4390 מָלֵא, H4557 מִסְפָּר",
    2675: "καταρτίζω (katartízō | kat-ar-tid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and a derivative of G739\nStrong's: to complete thoroughly, i.e. repair (literally or figuratively) or adjust\nKJV: —fit, frame, mend, (make) perfect(-ly join together), prepare, restore.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G739 \n\nCognate Group: G739 (perfect), G2676 (perfection), G2677 (perfecting), G1822 (accomplish), G2675 (fit)\nVariants: καταρτίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2342 חוּל, H3245 יָסַד, H3559 כּוּן, H3635 כְּלַל, H3661 כָּנַן, H6466 פָּעַל, H7737 שָׁוָה, H8356 שָׁתָה, H8551 תָּמַךְ",
    2676: "κατάρτισις (katártisis | kat-ar'-tis-is)\n\nDerivation: from G2675\nStrong's: thorough equipment (subjectively)\nKJV: —perfection.\n\nSee: G2675 \n\nCognate Group: G739 (perfect), G2676 (perfection), G2677 (perfecting), G1822 (accomplish), G2675 (fit)\nVariants: κατάρτισις",
    2677: "καταρτισμός (katartismós | kat-ar-tis-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G2675\nStrong's: complete furnishing (objectively)\nKJV: —perfecting.\n\nSee: G2675 \n\nCognate Group: G739 (perfect), G2676 (perfection), G2677 (perfecting), G1822 (accomplish), G2675 (fit)\nVariants: καταρτισμός",
    2678: "κατασείω (kataseíō | kat-as-i'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G4579\nStrong's: to sway downward, i.e. make a signal\nKJV: —beckon.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G4579 \n\nCognate Group: G739 (perfect), G2676 (perfection), G2677 (perfecting), G1822 (accomplish), G2675 (fit)\nVariants: κατασείω",
