    2682: "κατασκήνωσις (kataskḗnōsis | kat-as-kay'-no-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G2681\nStrong's: an encamping, i.e. (figuratively) a perch\nKJV: —nest.\n\nSee: G2681 \n\nCognate Group: G2681 (lodge), G4638 (tabernacle), G4635 (tent-maker), G4637 (dwell), G4636 (tabernacle), G4633 (habitation), G1981 (rest upon), G4634 (tabernacles)\nVariants: κατασκήνωσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H1129 בָּנָה, H4908 מִשְׁכָּן",
    2683: "κατασκιάζω (kataskiázō | kat-as-kee-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and a derivative of G4639\nStrong's: to overshade, i.e. cover\nKJV: —shadow.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G4639 \n\nCognate Group: G2681 (lodge), G4638 (tabernacle), G4635 (tent-maker), G4637 (dwell), G4636 (tabernacle), G4633 (habitation), G1981 (rest upon), G4634 (tabernacles)\nVariants: κατασκιάζω",
