    2691: "καταστρηνιάω (katastrēniáō | kat-as-tray-nee-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G4763\nStrong's: to become voluptuous against\nKJV: —begin to wax wanton against.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G4763 \n\nCognate Group: G2691 (begin to wax wanton against)\nVariants: καταστρηνιάω",
