    2704: "καταφθείρω (kataphtheírō | kat-af-thi'-ro)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G5351\nStrong's: to spoil entirely, i.e. (literally) to destroy; or (figuratively) to deprave; \nKJV: —corrupt, utterly perish.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G5351 \n\nCognate Group: G5351 (corrupt), G1311 (corrupt), G862 (not corruptible), G5256 (minister), G5349 (corruptible), G90 (uncorruptness), G1312 (corruption), G861 (immortality), G2704 (corrupt)\nVariants: καταφθείρω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1238 בָּקַק, H2254 חָבַל, H4743 מָקַק, H5034 נָבֵל, H7843 שָׁחַת, H8074 שָׁמֵם",
