    2710: "καταχράομαι (katachráomai | kat-akh-rah'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G5530\nStrong's: to overuse, i.e. misuse\nKJV: —abuse.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G5530 \n\nCognate Group: G2709 (under the earth)\nVariants: καταχράομαι, παραχράομαι",
    2711: "καταψύχω (katapsýchō | kat-ap-soo'-kho)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G5594\nStrong's: to cool down (off), i.e. refresh\nKJV: —cool.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G5594 \n\nCognate Group: G2709 (under the earth)\nVariants: καταψύχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H8172 שָׁעַן",
