    2714: "κατενώπιον (katenṓpion | kat-en-o'-pee-on)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G1799\nStrong's: directly in front of\nKJV: —before (the presence of), in the sight of.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G1799 \n\nCognate Group: G1493 (idol's temple), G1495 (idolatry), G1496 (idolater), G2712 (wholly given to idolatry), G1494 (offered to idols), G1497 (idol)\nVariants: κατενώπιον",
    2715: "κατεξουσιάζω (katexousiázō | kat-ex-oo-see-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G1850\nStrong's: to have (wield) full privilege over\nKJV: —exercise authority.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G1850 \n\nCognate Group: G1849 (authority), G1850 (exercise authority upon), G2715 (exercise authority), G1832 (be lawful)\nVariants: κατεξουσιάζω",
    2716: "κατεργάζομαι (katergázomai | kat-er-gad'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G2038\nStrong's: to work fully, i.e. accomplish; by implication, to finish, fashion\nKJV: —cause, to (deed), perform, work (out).\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2038 \n\nCognate Group: G2716 (cause)\nVariants: κατεργάζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H2799 חֲרֹשֶׁת, H3773 כָּרֻתָה, H4952 מִשְׁרָה, H5647 עָבַד, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6466 פָּעַל, H6687 צוּף, H7287 רָדָה",
    2717: "(Not Used)\n\n\nCognate Group: G2716 (cause)",
    2718: "κατέρχομαι (katérchomai | kat-er'-khom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G2064 (including its alternate)\nStrong's: to come (or go) down (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —come (down), depart, descend, go down, land.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2064 \n\nCognate Group: G2716 (cause)\nVariants: κατέρχομαι",
    2719: "κατεσθίω (katesthíō | kat-es-thee'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G2068 (including its alternate)\nStrong's: to eat down, i.e. devour (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —devour.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2068 \n\nCognate Group: G2716 (cause)\nVariants: κατεσθίω, κατέσθω, κατεσθίω/κατέσθω \nHebrew Equivalents: H398 אָכַל, H1104 בָּלַע, H1197 בָּעַר, H2628 חָסַל, H3615 כָּלָה, H5375 נָשָׂא, H7921 שָׁכֹל",
    2720: "κατευθύνω (kateuthýnō | kat-yoo-thoo'-no)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G2116\nStrong's: to straighten fully, i.e. (figuratively) direct\nKJV: —guide, direct.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2116 \n\nCognate Group: G2716 (cause)\nVariants: κατευθύνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H833 אָשַׁר, H3474 יָשַׁר, H3557 כּוּל, H3559 כּוּן, H5337 נָצַל, H6555 פָּרַץ, H6743 צָלַח, H8505 תָּכַן",
    2721: "κατεφίστημι (katephístēmi | kat-ef-is'-tay-mee)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G2186\nStrong's: to stand over against, i.e. rush upon (assault)\nKJV: —make insurrection against.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2186 \n\nCognate Group: G2716 (cause)\nVariants: κατεφίστημι, κατεφίσταμαι",
    2722: "κατέχω (katéchō | kat-ekh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G2192\nStrong's: to hold down (fast), in various applications (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —have, hold (fast), keep (in memory), let, X make toward, possess, retain, seize on, stay, take, withhold.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2192 \n\nCognate Group: G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)\nVariants: κατέχω \nHebrew Equivalents: H270 אָחַז, H309 אָחַר, H622 אָסַף, H631 אָסַר, H2388 חָזַק, H2505 חָלַק, H2631 חֲסַן, H3423 יָרַשׁ, H3427 יָשַׁב, H3920 לָכַד, H5157 נָחַל, H5307 נָפַל, H5702 עָגַן, H6113 עָצָר, H7685 שָׂגָה, H8610 תָּפַשׂ, H8630 תָּקַף",
    2723: "κατηγορέω (katēgoréō | kat-ay-gor-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2725\nStrong's: to be a plaintiff, i.e. to charge with some offence\nKJV: —accuse, object.\n\nSee: G2725 \n\nCognate Group: G2723 (accuse), G2724 (accusation), G2725 (accuser)\nVariants: κατηγορέω",
    2724: "κατηγορία (katēgoría | kat-ay-gor-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2725\nStrong's: a complaint (\"category\"), i.e. criminal charge\nKJV: —accusation (X -ed).\n\nSee: G2725 \n\nCognate Group: G2723 (accuse), G2724 (accusation), G2725 (accuser)\nVariants: κατηγορία",
    2725: "κατήγορος (katḗgoros | kat-ay'-gor-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G58\nStrong's: against one in the assembly, i.e. a complainant at law; specially, Satan\nKJV: —accuser.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G58 \n\nCognate Group: G2723 (accuse), G2724 (accusation), G2725 (accuser)\nVariants: κατήγορος, κατήγωρ \nHebrew Equivalents: H7379 רִיב",
    2726: "κατήφεια (katḗpheia | kat-ay'-fi-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2596 and perhaps a derivative of the base of G5316 (meaning downcast in look)\nStrong's: demureness, i.e. (by implication) sadness\nKJV: —heaviness.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G5316 \n\nCognate Group: G2723 (accuse), G2724 (accusation), G2725 (accuser)\nVariants: κατήφεια",
    2727: "κατηχέω (katēchéō | kat-ay-kheh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G2279\nStrong's: to sound down into the ears, i.e. (by implication) to indoctrinate (\"catechize\") or (genitive case) to apprise of\nKJV: —inform, instruct, teach.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2279 \n\nCognate Group: G2727 (inform)\nVariants: κατηχέω",
    2728: "κατιόω (katióō | kat-ee-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and a derivative of G2447\nStrong's: to rust down, i.e. corrode\nKJV: —canker.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2447 \n\nCognate Group: G2727 (inform)\nVariants: κατιόω, κατιόομαι",
    2729: "κατισχύω (katischýō | kat-is-khoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G2480\nStrong's: to overpower\nKJV: —prevail (against).\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G2480 \n\nCognate Group: G2479 (ability), G2729 (prevail), G2478 (boisterous), G2480 (be able)\nVariants: κατισχύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H68 אֶבֶן, H213 אוּץ, H247 אָזַר, H247 אָזַר, H553 אָמַץ, H1396 גָּבַר, H1431 גָּדַל, H2388 חָזַק, H3318 יָצָא, H3513 כָּבַד, H5810 עָזַז, H6105 עָצַם, H6113 עָצָר, H6680 צָוָה, H7789 שׁוּר, H8581 תַּעָב",
    2730: "κατοικέω (katoikéō | kat-oy-keh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2596 and G3611\nStrong's: to house permanently, i.e. reside (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —dwell(-er), inhabitant(-ter).\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G3611 \n\nCognate Group: G2479 (ability), G2729 (prevail), G2478 (boisterous), G2480 (be able)\nVariants: κατοικέω, κατοικίζω",
    2731: "κατοίκησις (katoíkēsis | kat-oy'-kay-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G2730\nStrong's: residence (properly, the act; but by implication, concretely, the mansion)\nKJV: —dwelling.\n\nSee: G2730 \n\nCognate Group: G3618 (build), G2733 (habitation), G3614 (home), G3617 (goodman), G3619 (building), G3616 (guide the house), G2731 (dwelling), G3622 (dispensation), G3615 (they of household), G3613 (habitation), G4925 (build together), G2732 (habitation), G3624 (home), G3611 (dwell), G3620 (edifying), G3621 (be steward), G2026 (build thereon), G3609 (of the house), G3623 (chamberlain)\nVariants: κατοίκησις \nHebrew Equivalents: H3427 יָשַׁב, H4186 מֹושָׁב",
    2732: "κατοικητήριον (katoikētḗrion | kat-oy-kay-tay'-ree-on)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2730\nStrong's: a dwelling-place\nKJV: —habitation.\n\nSee: G2730 \n\nCognate Group: G3618 (build), G2733 (habitation), G3614 (home), G3617 (goodman), G3619 (building), G3616 (guide the house), G2731 (dwelling), G3622 (dispensation), G3615 (they of household), G3613 (habitation), G4925 (build together), G2732 (habitation), G3624 (home), G3611 (dwell), G3620 (edifying), G3621 (be steward), G2026 (build thereon), G3609 (of the house), G3623 (chamberlain)\nVariants: κατοικητήριον \nHebrew Equivalents: H2073 זְבוּל, H3427 יָשַׁב, H4070 מְדֹור, H4186 מֹושָׁב, H4583 מָעֹון",
    2733: "κατοικία (katoikía | kat-oy-kee'-ah)\n\n\nStrong's: residence (properly, the condition; but by implication, the abode itself)\nKJV: —habitation.\n\nCognate Group: G3618 (build), G2733 (habitation), G3614 (home), G3617 (goodman), G3619 (building), G3616 (guide the house), G2731 (dwelling), G3622 (dispensation), G3615 (they of household), G3613 (habitation), G4925 (build together), G2732 (habitation), G3624 (home), G3611 (dwell), G3620 (edifying), G3621 (be steward), G2026 (build thereon), G3609 (of the house), G3623 (chamberlain)\nVariants: κατοικία \nHebrew Equivalents: H3427 יָשַׁב, H4070 מְדֹור, H4186 מֹושָׁב",
    2734: "κατοπτρίζομαι (katoptrízomai | kat-op-trid'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from a compound of G2596 and a derivative of G3700 (compare G2072)\nStrong's: to mirror oneself, i.e. to see reflected (figuratively)\nKJV: —behold as in a glass.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G3700 \nSee: G2072 \n\nCognate Group: G2734 (behold as in a glass), G2072 (glass)\nVariants: κατοπτρίζομαι, κατοπτρίζω",
    2735: "κατόρθωμα (katórthōma | kat-or'-tho-mah)\n\nDerivation: from a compound of G2596 and a derivative of G3717 (compare G1357)\nStrong's: something made fully upright, i.e. (figuratively) rectification (specially, good public administration)\nKJV: —very worthy deed.\n\nSee: G2596 \nSee: G3717 \nSee: G1357 \n\nCognate Group: G2734 (behold as in a glass), G2072 (glass)\nVariants: κατόρθωμα, διόρθωμα",
    2736: "κάτω (kátō | kat'-o); also (compare) κατωτέρω (katōtérō | kat-o-ter'-o)\n\nDerivation: (compare G2737); adverb from G2596\nStrong's: downwards\nKJV: —beneath, bottom, down, under.\n\nSee: G2737 \nSee: G2596 \n\nCognate Group: G2736 (beneath), G2737 (lower)\nVariants: κάτω, κατωτέρω \nHebrew Equivalents: H4295 מַטָּה, H8478 תַּחַת",
    2737: "κατώτερος (katṓteros | kat-o'-ter-os)\n\nDerivation: comparative from G2736\nStrong's: inferior (locally, of Hades)\nKJV: —lower.\n\nSee: G2736 \n\nCognate Group: G2736 (beneath), G2737 (lower)\nVariants: κατώτερος \nHebrew Equivalents: H8481 תַּחְתֹּון, H8482 תַּחְתִּי",
    2738: "καῦμα (kaûma | kow'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2545\nStrong's: properly, a burn (concretely), but used (abstractly) of a glow\nKJV: —heat.\n\nSee: G2545 \n\nCognate Group: G2738 (heat), G2739 (scorch)\nVariants: καῦμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H2527 חֹם, H2721 חֹרֶב, H3214 יְלֵל, H7019 קַיִץ",
    2739: "καυματίζω (kaumatízō | kow-mat-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2738\nStrong's: to burn\nKJV: —scorch.\n\nSee: G2738 \n\nCognate Group: G2738 (heat), G2739 (scorch)\nVariants: καυματίζω, καυματόω",
    2740: "καῦσις (kaûsis | kow'-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G2545\nStrong's: burning (the act)\nKJV: —be burned.\n\nSee: G2545 \n\nCognate Group: G2742 (heat), G2741 (fervent heat), G2740 (be burned), G2743 (sear with a hot iron)\nVariants: καῦσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H1197 בָּעַר, H3346 יְקֵדָא, H4634 מַעֲרָכָה",
    2741: "καυσόω (kausóō | kow-so'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2740\nStrong's: to set on fire\nKJV: —fervent heat.\n\nSee: G2740 \n\nCognate Group: G2742 (heat), G2741 (fervent heat), G2740 (be burned), G2743 (sear with a hot iron)\nVariants: καυσόω, καυσόομαι",
    2742: "καύσων (kaúsōn | kow'-sone)\n\nDerivation: from G2741\nStrong's: a glare\nKJV: —(burning) heat.\n\nSee: G2741 \n\nCognate Group: G2742 (heat), G2741 (fervent heat), G2740 (be burned), G2743 (sear with a hot iron)\nVariants: καύσων \nHebrew Equivalents: H2721 חֹרֶב, H6921 קָדִים, H8273 שָׁרָב",
    2743: "καυτηριάζω (kautēriázō | kow-tay-ree-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2545\nStrong's: to brand (\"cauterize\"), i.e. (by implication) to render unsensitive (figuratively)\nKJV: —sear with a hot iron.\n\nSee: G2545 \n\nCognate Group: G2742 (heat), G2741 (fervent heat), G2740 (be burned), G2743 (sear with a hot iron)\nVariants: καυτηριάζω, καυστηριάζω",
    2744: "καυχάομαι (kaucháomai | kow-khah'-om-ahee)\n\nDerivation: from some (obsolete) base akin to that of αὐχέω (to boast) and G2172\nStrong's: to vaunt (in a good or a bad sense)\nKJV: —(make) boast, glory, joy, rejoice.\n\nSee: G2172 \n\nCognate Group: G2620 (boast), G2746 (boasting), G2745 (boasting), G2744 (boast)\nVariants: καυχάομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H559 אָמַר, H1984 הָלַל, H5937 עָלַז, H5970 עָלַץ, H6286 פָּאַר, H7235 רָבָה, H7442 רָנַן, H7623 שָׁבַח",
    2745: "καύχημα (kaúchēma | kow'-khay-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2744\nStrong's: a boast (properly, the object; by implication, the act) in a good or a bad sense\nKJV: —boasting, (whereof) to glory (of), glorying, rejoice(-ing).\n\nSee: G2744 \n\nCognate Group: G2620 (boast), G2746 (boasting), G2745 (boasting), G2744 (boast)\nVariants: καύχημα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1346 גַּאֲוָה, H2305 חֶדְוָה, H8034 שֵׁם, H8416 תְּהִלָּה, H8431 תֹּוחֶלֶת, H8597 תִּפְאָרָה",
    2746: "καύχησις (kaúchēsis | kow'-khay-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G2744\nStrong's: boasting (properly, the act; by implication, the object), in a good or a bad sense\nKJV: —boasting, whereof I may glory, glorying, rejoicing.\n\nSee: G2744 \n\nCognate Group: G2620 (boast), G2746 (boasting), G2745 (boasting), G2744 (boast)\nVariants: καύχησις \nHebrew Equivalents: H8597 תִּפְאָרָה",
    2747: "Κεγχρεαί (Kenchreaí | keng-khreh-a'-hee)\n\nDerivation: probably from kegchros (millet)\nStrong's: Cenchreæ, a port of Corinth\nKJV: —Cencrea.\n\nCognate Group: G2620 (boast), G2746 (boasting), G2745 (boasting), G2744 (boast)\nVariants: Κεγχρεαί",
    2748: "Κεδρών (Kedrṓn | ked-rone')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H6939)\nStrong's: Cedron (i.e. Kidron), a brook near Jerusalem\nKJV: —Cedron.\nSee: H6939\n\nCognate Group: G2620 (boast), G2746 (boasting), G2745 (boasting), G2744 (boast)\nVariants: Κεδρών, κέδρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H730 אֶרֶז, H1265 בְּרֹושׁ, H6086 עֵץ, H6939 קִדְרֹון, H8391 תְּאַשּׁוּר",
    2749: "κεῖμαι (keîmai | ki'-mahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice of a primary verb\nStrong's: to lie outstretched (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —be (appointed, laid up, made, set), lay, lie. Compare G5087 .\n\nSee: G5087 \n\nCognate Group: G4029 (be bound with), G4295 (be first), G1945 (impose), G606 (be appointed), G4873 (sit with), G345 (guest), G480 (adversary), G3873 (be present), G2749 (be appointed), G2621 (keep)\nVariants: κεῖμαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H376 אִישׁ, H3259 יָעַד, H4071 מְדוּרָה, H5182 נְחַת, H5448 סֹבֶל, H7126 קָרַב, H7760 שׂוּם",
    2750: "κειρία (keiría | ki-ree'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a swathe, i.e. winding-sheet\nKJV: —graveclothes.\n\nCognate Group: G4029 (be bound with), G4295 (be first), G1945 (impose), G606 (be appointed), G4873 (sit with), G345 (guest), G480 (adversary), G3873 (be present), G2749 (be appointed), G2621 (keep)\nVariants: κειρία \nHebrew Equivalents: H4765 מַרְבַד",
    2751: "κείρω (keírō | ki'-ro)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to shear\nKJV: —shear(-er).\n\nCognate Group: G4029 (be bound with), G4295 (be first), G1945 (impose), G606 (be appointed), G4873 (sit with), G345 (guest), G480 (adversary), G3873 (be present), G2749 (be appointed), G2621 (keep)\nVariants: κείρω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1494 גַּזָז, H1548 גָּלַח, H7094 קָצַב, H7112 קָצַץ, H7200 רָאָה, H7353 רָחֵל",
    2752: "κέλευμα (kéleuma | kel'-yoo-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2753\nStrong's: a cry of incitement\nKJV: —shout.\n\nSee: G2753 \n\nCognate Group: G2753 (bid), G2752 (shout)\nVariants: κέλευμα, κέλευσμα",
    2753: "κελεύω (keleúō | kel-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a primary κέλλω (to urge on)\nStrong's: \"hail\"; to incite by word, i.e. order\nKJV: —bid, (at, give) command(-ment).\n\nCognate Group: G2753 (bid), G2752 (shout)\nVariants: κελεύω",
    2754: "κενοδοξία (kenodoxía | ken-od-ox-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2755\nStrong's: empty glorying, i.e. self-conceit\nKJV: —vain-glory.\n\nSee: G2755 \n\nCognate Group: G2758 (make of none effect), G2757 (vain), G2754 (vain-glory), G2761 (in vain), G2755 (desirous of vain-glory), G2756 (empty)\nVariants: κενοδοξία",
    2755: "κενόδοξος (kenódoxos | ken-od'-ox-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2756 and G1391\nStrong's: vainly glorifying, i.e. self-conceited\nKJV: —desirous of vain-glory.\n\nSee: G2756 \nSee: G1391 \n\nCognate Group: G2758 (make of none effect), G2757 (vain), G2754 (vain-glory), G2761 (in vain), G2755 (desirous of vain-glory), G2756 (empty)\nVariants: κενόδοξος, κενόδοξας",
    2756: "κενός (kenós | ken-os')\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary word\nStrong's: empty (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —empty, (in) vain.\n\nCognate Group: G2758 (make of none effect), G2757 (vain), G2754 (vain-glory), G2761 (in vain), G2755 (desirous of vain-glory), G2756 (empty)\nVariants: κενός \nHebrew Equivalents: H205 אָוֶן, H268 אָחֹור, H391 אַכְזָב, H657 אֶפֶס, H1891 הָבַל, H1892 הֶבֶל, H2600 חִנָּם, H2637 חָסֵר, H3576 כָּזַב, H3808 לֹא, H3808 לֹא, H7385 רִיק, H7387 רֵיקָם, H7723 שָׁוְא, H8264 שָׁקַק, H8267 שֶׁקֶר, H8414 תֹּהוּ",
    2757: "κενοφωνία (kenophōnía | ken-of-o-nee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a presumed compound of G2756 and G5456\nStrong's: empty sounding, i.e. fruitless discussion\nKJV: —vain.\n\nSee: G2756 \nSee: G5456 \n\nCognate Group: G2758 (make of none effect), G2757 (vain), G2754 (vain-glory), G2761 (in vain), G2755 (desirous of vain-glory), G2756 (empty)\nVariants: κενοφωνία, καινοφωνία",
    2758: "κενόω (kenóō | ken-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2756\nStrong's: to make empty, i.e. (figuratively) to abase, neutralize, falsify\nKJV: —make (of none effect, of no reputation, void), be in vain.\n\nSee: G2756 \n\nCognate Group: G2758 (make of none effect), G2757 (vain), G2754 (vain-glory), G2761 (in vain), G2755 (desirous of vain-glory), G2756 (empty)\nVariants: κενόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5999 עָמָל",
    2759: "κέντρον (kéntron | ken'-tron)\n\nDerivation: from κεντέω (to prick)\nStrong's: a point (\"centre\"), i.e. a sting (figuratively, poison) or goad (figuratively, divine impulse)\nKJV: —prick, sting.\n\nCognate Group: G2759 (prick)\nVariants: κέντρον \nHebrew Equivalents: H4964 מֶתֶג, H6987 קֹטֶב",
    2760: "κεντυρίων (kentyríōn | ken-too-ree'-ohn)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: a centurion, i.e. captain of one hundred soldiers\nKJV: —centurion.\n\nCognate Group: G2759 (prick)\nVariants: κεντυρίων",
    2761: "κενῶς (kenōs | ken-oce')\n\nDerivation: adverb from G2756\nStrong's: vainly, i.e. to no purpose\nKJV: —in vain.\n\nSee: G2756 \n\nCognate Group: G2758 (make of none effect), G2757 (vain), G2754 (vain-glory), G2761 (in vain), G2755 (desirous of vain-glory), G2756 (empty)\nVariants: κενῶς \nHebrew Equivalents: H7385 רִיק",
    2762: "κεραία (keraía | ker-ah'-yah)\n\nDerivation: feminine of a presumed derivative of the base of G2768\nStrong's: something horn-like, i.e. (specially) the apex of a Hebrew letter (figuratively, the least particle)\nKJV: —tittle.\n\nSee: G2768 \n\nCognate Group: G2758 (make of none effect), G2757 (vain), G2754 (vain-glory), G2761 (in vain), G2755 (desirous of vain-glory), G2756 (empty)\nVariants: κεραία",
    2763: "κεραμεύς (kerameús | ker-am-yooce')\n\nDerivation: from G2766\nStrong's: a potter\nKJV: —potter.\n\nSee: G2766 \n\nCognate Group: G2766 (tiling), G2765 (pitcher), G2764 (of a potter), G2763 (potter)\nVariants: κεραμεύς \nHebrew Equivalents: H3335 יָצַר",
    2764: "κεραμικός (keramikós | ker-am-ik-os')\n\nDerivation: from G2766\nStrong's: made of clay, i.e. earthen\nKJV: —of a potter.\n\nSee: G2766 \n\nCognate Group: G2766 (tiling), G2765 (pitcher), G2764 (of a potter), G2763 (potter)\nVariants: κεραμικός \nHebrew Equivalents: H6353 פֶּחָר",
    2765: "κεράμιον (kerámion | ker-am'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a presumed derivative of G2766\nStrong's: an earthenware vessel, i.e. jar\nKJV: —pitcher.\n\nSee: G2766 \n\nCognate Group: G2766 (tiling), G2765 (pitcher), G2764 (of a potter), G2763 (potter)\nVariants: κεράμιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1323 בַּת, H1375 גְּבִיעַ",
    2766: "κέραμος (kéramos | ker'-am-os)\n\nDerivation: probably from the base of G2767 (through the idea of mixing clay and water)\nStrong's: earthenware, i.e. a tile (by analogy, a thin roof or awning)\nKJV: —tiling.\n\nSee: G2767 \n\nCognate Group: G2766 (tiling), G2765 (pitcher), G2764 (of a potter), G2763 (potter)\nVariants: κέραμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3335 יָצַר",
    2767: "κεράννυμι (keránnymi | ker-an'-noo-mee)\n\n\nDerivation: prolonged form of a more primary κεράω (keráō | ker-ah'-o)\n (which is used in certain tenses)\nStrong's: to mingle, i.e. (by implication) to pour out (for drinking)\nKJV: —fill, pour out. Compare G3396 .\n\nSee: G3396 \n\nCognate Group: G2766 (tiling), G2765 (pitcher), G2764 (of a potter), G2763 (potter)\nVariants: κεράννυμι \nHebrew Equivalents: H4537 מָסַךְ",
    2768: "κέρας (kéras | ker'-as)\n\nDerivation: from a primary κάρ (the hair of the head)\nStrong's: a horn (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —horn.\n\nCognate Group: G2768 (horn)\nVariants: κέρας \nHebrew Equivalents: H2380 חָזוּת, H4740 מַקְצֹועַ, H7160 קָרַן, H7161 קֶרֶן",
    2769: "κεράτιον (kerátion | ker-at'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a presumed derivative of G2768\nStrong's: something horned, i.e. (specially) the pod of the carob-tree\nKJV: —husk.\n\nSee: G2768 \n\nCognate Group: G2768 (horn)\nVariants: κεράτιον",
    2770: "κερδαίνω (kerdaínō | ker-dah'-ee-no)\n\nDerivation: from G2771\nStrong's: to gain (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —(get) gain, win.\n\nSee: G2771 \n\nCognate Group: G2770 (gain), G2771 (gain)\nVariants: κερδαίνω, ἐπικερδαίνω",
    2771: "κέρδος (kérdos | ker'-dos)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: gain (pecuniary or genitive case)\nKJV: —gain, lucre.\n\nCognate Group: G2770 (gain), G2771 (gain)\nVariants: κέρδος",
    2772: "κέρμα (kérma | ker'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2751\nStrong's: a clipping (bit), i.e. (specially) a coin\nKJV: —money.\n\nSee: G2751 \n\nCognate Group: G2773 (changer of money), G2772 (money)\nVariants: κέρμα",
    2773: "κερματιστής (kermatistḗs | ker-mat-is-tace')\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2772\nStrong's: a handler of coins, i.e. money-broker\nKJV: —changer of money.\n\nSee: G2772 \n\nCognate Group: G2773 (changer of money), G2772 (money)\nVariants: κερματιστής",
    2774: "κεφάλαιον (kephálaion | kef-al'-ah-yon)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a derivative of G2776\nStrong's: a principal thing, i.e. main point; specially, an amount (of money)\nKJV: —sum.\n\nSee: G2776 \n\nCognate Group: G346 (briefly comprehend), G2774 (sum), G2776 (head), G2775 (wound in the head)\nVariants: κεφάλαιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H7218 רֹאשׁ",
    2775: "κεφαλαιόω (kephalaióō | kef-al-ahee-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2774\nStrong's: (specially) to strike on the head\nKJV: —wound in the head.\n\nSee: G2774 \n\nCognate Group: G346 (briefly comprehend), G2774 (sum), G2776 (head), G2775 (wound in the head)\nVariants: κεφαλαιόω, κεφαλιόω",
    2776: "κεφαλή (kephalḗ | kef-al-ay')\n\nDerivation: from the primary κάπτω (in the sense of seizing)\nStrong's: the head (as the part most readily taken hold of), literally or figuratively\nKJV: —head.\n\nCognate Group: G346 (briefly comprehend), G2774 (sum), G2776 (head), G2775 (wound in the head)\nVariants: κεφαλή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1538 גֻּלְגֹּלֶת, H4763 מְרַאֲשָׁה, H5315 נֶפֶשׁ, H6936 קׇדְקֹד, H7161 קֶרֶן, H7218 רֹאשׁ",
    2777: "κεφαλίς (kephalís | kef-al-is')\n\nDerivation: from G2776\nStrong's: properly, a knob, i.e. (by implication) a roll (by extension from the end of a stick on which the manuscript was rolled)\nKJV: —volume.\n\nSee: G2776 \n\nCognate Group: G346 (briefly comprehend), G2774 (sum), G2776 (head), G2775 (wound in the head)\nVariants: κεφαλίς \nHebrew Equivalents: H134 אֶדֶן, H2053 וָו, H3805 כֹתֶרֶת, H4039 מְגִלָּה, H7175 קֶרֶשׁ, H7218 רֹאשׁ",
    2778: "κῆνσος (kēnsos | kane'-sos)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: properly, an enrollment (\"census\"), i.e. (by implication) a tax\nKJV: —tribute.\n\nCognate Group: G346 (briefly comprehend), G2774 (sum), G2776 (head), G2775 (wound in the head)\nVariants: κῆνσος, ἐπικεφάλαιον",
    2779: "κῆπος (kēpos | kay'-pos)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a garden\nKJV: —garden.\n\nCognate Group: G346 (briefly comprehend), G2774 (sum), G2776 (head), G2775 (wound in the head)\nVariants: κῆπος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1588 גַּן, H1593 גַּנָּה, H1594 גִּנָּה",
    2780: "κηπουρός (kēpourós | kay-poo-ros')\n\nDerivation: from G2779 and οὖρος (a warden)\nStrong's: a garden-keeper, i.e. gardener\nKJV: —gardener.\n\nSee: G2779 \n\nCognate Group: G346 (briefly comprehend), G2774 (sum), G2776 (head), G2775 (wound in the head)\nVariants: κηπουρός",
    2781: "κηρίον (kēríon | kay-ree'-on)\n\nDerivation: diminutive from κηός (wax)\nStrong's: a cell for honey, i.e. (collectively) the comb\nKJV: —(honey-)comb.\n\nCognate Group: G346 (briefly comprehend), G2774 (sum), G2776 (head), G2775 (wound in the head)\nVariants: κηρίον G3059 \nHebrew Equivalents: H3293 יַעַר, H5317 נֹפֶת, H6688 צוּף",
    2782: "κήρυγμα (kḗrygma | kay'-roog-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2784\nStrong's: a proclamation (especially of the gospel; by implication, the gospel itself)\nKJV: —preaching.\n\nSee: G2784 \n\nCognate Group: G2784 (preacher), G4296 (before preach), G2783 (preacher), G2782 (preaching)\nVariants: κήρυγμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H6963 קֹול, H7150 קְרִיאָה",
    2783: "κῆρυξ (kēryx | kay'-roox)\n\nDerivation: from G2784\nStrong's: a herald, i.e. of divine truth (especially of the gospel)\nKJV: —preacher.\n\nSee: G2784 \n\nCognate Group: G2784 (preacher), G4296 (before preach), G2783 (preacher), G2782 (preaching)\nVariants: κῆρυξ \nHebrew Equivalents: H3744 כָּרֹוז",
    2784: "κηρύσσω (kērýssō | kay-roos'-so)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: to herald (as a public crier), especially divine truth (the gospel)\nKJV: —preacher(-er), proclaim, publish.\n\nCognate Group: G2784 (preacher), G4296 (before preach), G2783 (preacher), G2782 (preaching)\nVariants: κηρύσσω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2199 זָעַק, H3745 כְּרַז, H5414 נָתַן, H7121 קָרָא, H7321 רוּעַ",
    2785: "κῆτος (kētos | kay'-tos)\n\nDerivation: probably from the base of G5490\nStrong's: a huge fish (as gaping for prey)\nKJV: —whale.\n\nSee: G5490 \n\nCognate Group: G2784 (preacher), G4296 (before preach), G2783 (preacher), G2782 (preaching)\nVariants: κῆτος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1709 דָּג, H3882 לִוְיָתָן, H7293 רַהַב, H8577 תַּנִּין",
    2786: "Κηφᾶς (Kēphâs | kay-fas')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (compare H3710)\nStrong's: the Rock; Cephas (i.e. Kepha), a surname of Peter\nKJV: —Cephas.\nSee: H3710\n\nCognate Group: G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)\nVariants: Κηφᾶς \nHebrew Equivalents: H3710 כֵּף",
    2787: "κιβωτός (kibōtós | kib-o-tos')\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a box, i.e. the sacred ark and that of Noah\nKJV: —ark.\n\nCognate Group: G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)\nVariants: κιβωτός \nHebrew Equivalents: H727 אָרֹון, H4908 מִשְׁכָּן, H8392 תֵּבָה",
    2788: "κιθάρα (kithára | kith-ar'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: a lyre\nKJV: —harp.\n\nCognate Group: G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)\nVariants: κιθάρα \nHebrew Equivalents: H3658 כִּנֹּור, H5035 נֶבֶל, H5058 נְגִינָה, H5748 עוּגָב, H7030 קִיתָרֹס",
    2789: "κιθαρίζω (kitharízō | kith-ar-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2788\nStrong's: to play on a lyre\nKJV: —harp.\n\nSee: G2788 \n\nCognate Group: G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)\nVariants: κιθαρίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H5059 נָגַן",
    2790: "κιθαρῳδός (kitharōidós | kith-ar-o'-dos)\n\nDerivation: from G2788 and a derivative of the same as G5603\nStrong's: a lyre-singer(-player), i.e. harpist\nKJV: —harper.\n\nSee: G2788 \nSee: G5603 \n\nCognate Group: G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)\nVariants: κιθαρῳδός, κιθαρώδός",
    2791: "Κιλικία (Kilikía | kil-ik-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: Cilicia, a region of Asia Minor\nKJV: —Cilicia.\n\nCognate Group: G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)\nVariants: Κιλικία, Κίλιξ",
    2792: "κινάμωμον (kinámōmon | kin-am'-o-mon)\n\nDerivation: of foreign origin (compare H7076)\nStrong's: cinnamon\nKJV: —cinnamon.\nSee: H7076\n\nCognate Group: G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)\nVariants: κινάμωμον, κιννάμωμον",
    2793: "κινδυνεύω (kindyneúō | kin-doon-yoo'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2794\nStrong's: to undergo peril\nKJV: —be in danger, be (stand) in jeopardy.\n\nSee: G2794 \n\nCognate Group: G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)\nVariants: κινδυνεύω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2325 חוּב, H2803 חָשַׁב, H3369 יָקֹשׁ, H5533 סָכַן",
    2794: "κίνδυνος (kíndynos | kin'-doo-nos)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: danger\nKJV: —peril.\n\nCognate Group: G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)\nVariants: κίνδυνος \nHebrew Equivalents: H4712 מֵצַר",
    2795: "κινέω (kinéō | kin-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from κίω (poetic for εἶμι, to go)\nStrong's: to stir (transitively), literally or figuratively\nKJV: —(re-)move(-r), way.\n\nCognate Group: G3334 (move away), G2796 (moving), G2795 (move)\nVariants: κινέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2363 חוּשׁ, H4185 מוּשׁ, H4191 מוּת, H5086 נָדַף, H5110 נוּד, H5127 נוּס, H5128 נוּעַ, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5493 סוּר, H6329 פּוּק, H6471 פַּעַם, H7430 רָמַשׂ, H8317 שָׁרַץ",
    2796: "κίνησις (kínēsis | kin'-ay-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G2795\nStrong's: a stirring\nKJV: —moving.\n\nSee: G2795 \n\nCognate Group: G3334 (move away), G2796 (moving), G2795 (move)\nVariants: κίνησις G3076 \nHebrew Equivalents: H5205 נִיד",
    2797: "Κίς (Kís | kis)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H7027)\nStrong's: Cis (i.e. Kish), an Israelite\nKJV: —Cis.\nSee: H7027\n\nCognate Group: G3334 (move away), G2796 (moving), G2795 (move)\nVariants: Κίς \nHebrew Equivalents: H7027 קִישׁ",
    2798: "κλάδος (kládos | klad'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2806\nStrong's: a twig or bough (as if broken off)\nKJV: —branch.\n\nSee: G2806 \n\nCognate Group: G2798 (branch)\nVariants: κλάδος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1808 דָּלִיָּה, H3127 יֹונֶקֶת, H3709 כַּף, H5520 סֹךְ, H5595 סָפָה, H5634 סַרְעַפָּה, H6057 עָנָף, H6288 פְּאֹרָה, H7641 שִׁבֹּל",
    2799: "κλαίω (klaíō | klah'-yo)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain affinity\nStrong's: to sob, i.e. wail aloud (whereas 1145 is rather to cry silently)\nKJV: —bewail, weep.\n\nCognate Group: G2805 (wailing), G2799 (bewail)\nVariants: κλαίω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1058 בָּכָה, H1288 בָרַךְ, H3766 כָּרַע, H5198 נָטָף, H5594 סָפַד, H7121 קָרָא",
    2800: "κλάσις (klásis | klas'-is)\n\nDerivation: from G2806\nStrong's: fracture (the act)\nKJV: —breaking.\n\nSee: G2806 \n\nCognate Group: G2806 (break), G2801 (broken), G2800 (breaking)\nVariants: κλάσις",
    2801: "κλάσμα (klásma | klas'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2806\nStrong's: a piece (bit)\nKJV: —broken, fragment.\n\nSee: G2806 \n\nCognate Group: G2806 (break), G2801 (broken), G2800 (breaking)\nVariants: κλάσμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H6400 פֶּלַח, H6595 פַּת",
    2802: "Κλαύδη (Klaúdē | klow'-day)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Claude, an island near Crete\nKJV: —Clauda.\n\nCognate Group: G2806 (break), G2801 (broken), G2800 (breaking)\nVariants: Κλαύδη, Γαύδη, Καῦδα, Κλαῦδα",
    2803: "Κλαυδία (Klaudía | klow-dee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: feminine of G2804\nStrong's: Claudia, a Christian woman\nKJV: —Claudia.\n\nSee: G2804 \n\nCognate Group: G2806 (break), G2801 (broken), G2800 (breaking)\nVariants: Κλαυδία",
    2804: "Κλαύδιος (Klaúdios | klow'-dee-os)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: Claudius, the name of two Romans\nKJV: —Claudius.\n\nCognate Group: G2806 (break), G2801 (broken), G2800 (breaking)\nVariants: Κλαύδιος",
    2805: "κλαυθμός (klauthmós | klowth-mos')\n\nDerivation: from G2799\nStrong's: lamentation\nKJV: —wailing, weeping, X wept.\n\nSee: G2799 \n\nCognate Group: G2805 (wailing), G2799 (bewail)\nVariants: κλαυθμός \nHebrew Equivalents: H60 אֵבֶל, H1058 בָּכָה, H1065 בְּכִי, H3998 מְבוּכָה, H6091 עָצָב",
    2806: "κλάω (kláō | klah'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to break (specially, of bread)\nKJV: —break.\n\nCognate Group: G2806 (break), G2801 (broken), G2800 (breaking)\nVariants: κλάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1438 גָּדַע, H6566 פָּרַשׂ, H7533 רָצַץ",
    2807: "κλείς (kleís | klice)\n\nDerivation: from G2808\nStrong's: a key (as shutting a lock), literally or figuratively\nKJV: —key.\n\nSee: G2808 \n\nCognate Group: G2807 (key), G2808 (shut)\nVariants: κλείς, κλεῖς \nHebrew Equivalents: H4668 מַפְתֵּחַ, H7929 שִׁכְמָה",
    2808: "κλείω (kleíō | kli'-o)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to close (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —shut (up).\n\nCognate Group: G2807 (key), G2808 (shut)\nVariants: κλείω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1479 גּוּף, H5274 נָעַל, H5462 סָגַר",
    2809: "κλέμμα (klémma | klem'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2813\nStrong's: stealing (properly, the thing stolen, but used of the act)\nKJV: —theft.\n\nSee: G2813 \n\nCognate Group: G2807 (key), G2808 (shut)\nVariants: κλέμμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1589 גָּנַב, H1591 גְּנֵבָה",
    2810: "Κλεόπας (Kleópas | kleh-op'-as)\n\nDerivation: probably contracted from Κλεόπατρος (compound of G2811 and G3962)\nStrong's: Cleopas, a Christian\nKJV: —Cleopas.\n\nSee: G2811 \nSee: G3962 \n\nCognate Group: G2807 (key), G2808 (shut)\nVariants: Κλεόπας, Κλεοπᾶς",
    2811: "κλέος (kléos | kleh'-os)\n\nDerivation: from a shorter form of G2564\nStrong's: renown (as if being called)\nKJV: —glory.\n\nSee: G2564 \n\nCognate Group: G2807 (key), G2808 (shut)\nVariants: κλέος \nHebrew Equivalents: H8088 שֵׁמַע",
    2812: "κλέπτης (kléptēs | klep'-tace)\n\nDerivation: from G2813\nStrong's: a stealer (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —thief. Compare G3027 .\n\nSee: G2813 \nSee: G3027 \n\nCognate Group: G2813 (steal), G2812 (thief)\nVariants: κλέπτης \nHebrew Equivalents: H1590 גַּנָּב, H1590 גַּנָּב",
    2813: "κλέπτω (kléptō | klep'-to)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to filch\nKJV: —steal.\n\nCognate Group: G2813 (steal), G2812 (thief)\nVariants: κλέπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H1589 גָּנַב",
    2814: "κλῆμα (klēma | kaly'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2806\nStrong's: a limb or shoot (as if broken off)\nKJV: —branch.\n\nSee: G2806 \n\nCognate Group: G2814 (branch)\nVariants: κλῆμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1808 דָּלִיָּה, H2156 זְמֹורָה, H5189 נְטִישָׁה, H6057 עָנָף, H7105 קָצִיר, H8299 שָׂרִיג",
    2815: "Κλήμης (Klḗmēs | klay'-mace)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: merciful; Clemes (i.e. Clemens), a Christian\nKJV: —Clement.\n\nCognate Group: G2814 (branch)\nVariants: Κλήμης",
    2816: "κληρονομέω (klēronoméō | klay-ron-om-eh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2818\nStrong's: to be an heir to (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —be heir, (obtain by) inherit(-ance).\n\nSee: G2818 \n\nCognate Group: G3647 (perfect soundness), G2819 (heritage), G2817 (inheritance), G4789 (fellow -heir), G2820 (obtain an inheritance), G3648 (entire), G2624 (divide by lot), G2816 (be heir), G4345 (consort with), G2818 (heir)\nVariants: κληρονομέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H270 אָחַז, H962 בָּזַז, H2505 חָלַק, H3045 יָדַע, H3423 יָרַשׁ, H3920 לָכַד, H5157 נָחַל",
    2817: "κληρονομία (klēronomía | klay-ron-om-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2818\nStrong's: heirship, i.e. (concretely) a patrimony or (genitive case) a possession\nKJV: —inheritance.\n\nSee: G2818 \n\nCognate Group: G3647 (perfect soundness), G2819 (heritage), G2817 (inheritance), G4789 (fellow -heir), G2820 (obtain an inheritance), G3648 (entire), G2624 (divide by lot), G2816 (be heir), G4345 (consort with), G2818 (heir)\nVariants: κληρονομία \nHebrew Equivalents: H272 אֲחֻזָּה, H1366 גְּבוּל, H1486 גֹּורָל, H2465 חֶלֶד, H3423 יָרַשׁ, H3425 יְרֻשָּׁה, H5159 נַחֲלָה",
    2818: "κληρονόμος (klēronómos | klay-ron-om'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2819 and the base of G3551 (in its original sense of partitioning, i.e. (reflexively) getting by apportionment)\nStrong's: a sharer by lot, i.e. inheritor (literally or figuratively); by implication, a possessor\nKJV: —heir.\n\nSee: G2819 \nSee: G3551 \n\nCognate Group: G3647 (perfect soundness), G2819 (heritage), G2817 (inheritance), G4789 (fellow -heir), G2820 (obtain an inheritance), G3648 (entire), G2624 (divide by lot), G2816 (be heir), G4345 (consort with), G2818 (heir)\nVariants: κληρονόμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3423 יָרַשׁ",
    2819: "κλῆρος (klēros | klay'-ros)\n\nDerivation: probably from G2806 (through the idea of using bits of wood, etc., for the purpose\nStrong's: a die (for drawing chances); by implication, a portion (as if so secured); by extension, an acquisition (especially a patrimony, figuratively)\nKJV: —heritage, inheritance, lot, part.\n\nSee: G2806 \n\nCognate Group: G3647 (perfect soundness), G2819 (heritage), G2817 (inheritance), G4789 (fellow -heir), G2820 (obtain an inheritance), G3648 (entire), G2624 (divide by lot), G2816 (be heir), G4345 (consort with), G2818 (heir)\nVariants: κλῆρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1486 גֹּורָל, H2256 חֶבֶל, H2465 חֶלֶד, H3423 יָרַשׁ, H4940 מִשְׁפָּחָה, H5159 נַחֲלָה, H6565 פָּרַר, H7133 קׇרְבָּן",
    2820: "κληρόω (klēróō | klay-ro'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2819\nStrong's: to allot, i.e. (figuratively) to assign (a privilege)\nKJV: —obtain an inheritance.\n\nSee: G2819 \n\nCognate Group: G3647 (perfect soundness), G2819 (heritage), G2817 (inheritance), G4789 (fellow -heir), G2820 (obtain an inheritance), G3648 (entire), G2624 (divide by lot), G2816 (be heir), G4345 (consort with), G2818 (heir)\nVariants: κληρόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H3920 לָכַד, H5159 נַחֲלָה, H7121 קָרָא",
    2821: "κλῆσις (klēsis | klay'-sis)\n\nDerivation: from a shorter form of G2564\nStrong's: an invitation (figuratively)\nKJV: —calling.\n\nSee: G2564 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κλῆσις \nHebrew Equivalents: H7121 קָרָא",
    2822: "κλητός (klētós | klay-tos')\n\nDerivation: from the same as G2821\nStrong's: invited, i.e. appointed, or (specially), a saint\nKJV: —called.\n\nSee: G2821 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κλητός \nHebrew Equivalents: H4744 מִקְרָא, H7121 קָרָא",
    2823: "κλίβανος (klíbanos | klib'-an-os)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: an earthen pot used for baking in\nKJV: —oven.\n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κλίβανος \nHebrew Equivalents: H8574 תַּנּוּר",
    2824: "κλίμα (klíma | klee'-mah)\n\nDerivation: from G2827\nStrong's: a slope, i.e. (specially) a \"clime\" or tract of country\nKJV: —part, region.\n\nSee: G2827 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κλίμα \nHebrew Equivalents: H6438 פִּנָּה",
    2825: "κλίνη (klínē | klee'-nay)\n\nDerivation: from G2827\nStrong's: a couch (for sleep, sickness, sitting or eating)\nKJV: —bed, table.\n\nSee: G2827 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κλίνη, κλινάριον \nHebrew Equivalents: H4296 מִטָּה, H4904 מִשְׁכָּב, H6210 עֶרֶשׂ",
    2826: "κλινίδιον (klinídion | klin-id'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a presumed derivative of G2825\nStrong's: a pallet or little couch\nKJV: —bed.\n\nSee: G2825 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κλινίδιον",
    2827: "κλίνω (klínō | klee'-no)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to slant or slope, i.e. incline or recline (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —bow (down), be far spent, lay, turn to flight, wear away.\n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κλίνω \nHebrew Equivalents: H328 אַט, H3381 יָרַד, H3766 כָּרַע, H4185 מוּשׁ, H4191 מוּת, H5128 נוּעַ, H5186 נָטָה, H5428 נָתַשׁ, H5860 עִיט, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6437 פָּנָה, H6808 צָעָה, H7503 רָפָה, H7901 שָׁכַב",
    2828: "κλισία (klisía | klee-see'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2827\nStrong's: properly, reclination, i.e. (concretely and specially), a party at a meal\nKJV: —company.\n\nSee: G2827 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κλισία",
    2829: "κλοπή (klopḗ | klop-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G2813\nStrong's: stealing\nKJV: —theft.\n\nSee: G2813 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κλοπή \nHebrew Equivalents: H1589 גָּנַב",
    2830: "κλύδων (klýdōn | kloo'-dohn)\n\nDerivation: from κλύζω (to billow or dash over)\nStrong's: a surge of the sea (literally or figuratively)\nKJV: —raging, wave.\n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κλύδων \nHebrew Equivalents: H5191 נְטַל",
    2831: "κλυδωνίζομαι (klydōnízomai | kloo-do-nid'-zom-ahee)\n\nDerivation: middle voice from G2830\nStrong's: to surge, i.e. (figuratively) to fluctuate\nKJV: —toss to and fro.\n\nSee: G2830 \n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κλυδωνίζομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1644 גָּרַשׁ",
    2832: "Κλωπᾶς (Klōpâs | klo-pas')\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (corresponding to H256)\nStrong's: Clopas, an Israelite\nKJV: —Cleophas.\nSee: H256\n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: Κλωπᾶς",
    2833: "κνήθω (knḗthō | knay'-tho)\n\nDerivation: from a primary κνάω (to scrape)\nStrong's: to scratch, i.e. (by implication) to tickle\nKJV: —X itching.\n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κνήθω, κνήθομαι",
    2834: "Κνίδος (Knídos | knee'-dos)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: Cnidus, a place in Asia Minor\nKJV: —Cnidus.\n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: Κνίδος",
    2835: "κοδράντης (kodrántēs | kod-ran'-tace)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: a quadrans, i.e. the fourth part of an as\nKJV: —farthing.\n\nCognate Group: G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)\nVariants: κοδράντης",
    2836: "κοιλία (koilía | koy-lee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from κοῖλος (\"hollow\")\nStrong's: a cavity, i.e. (especially) the abdomen; by implication, the matrix; figuratively, the heart\nKJV: —belly, womb.\n\nCognate Group: G2836 (belly)\nVariants: κοιλία \nHebrew Equivalents: H990 בֶּטֶן, H1121 בֵּן, H1406 גָּג, H1512 גָּחֹון, H3770 כְּרֵשׂ, H4578 מֵעֶה, H7130 קֶרֶב, H7358 רֶחֶם",
    2837: "κοιμάω (koimáō | koy-mah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2749\nStrong's: to put to sleep, i.e. (passively or reflexively) to slumber; figuratively, to decease\nKJV: —(be a-, fall a-, fall on) sleep, be dead.\n\nSee: G2749 \n\nCognate Group: G2838 (taking of rest), G2837 (sleep)\nVariants: κοιμάω, κοιμάομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H956 בּוּת, H1961 הָיָה, H1980 הָלַךְ, H3286 יָעַף, H3427 יָשַׁב, H3462 יָשֵׁן, H3885 לוּן, H5181 נָחַת, H5440 סָבַךְ, H7257 רָבַץ, H7290 רָדַם, H7901 שָׁכַב",
    2838: "κοίμησις (koímēsis | koy'-may-sis)\n\nDerivation: from G2837\nStrong's: sleeping, i.e. (by implication) repose\nKJV: —taking of rest.\n\nSee: G2837 \n\nCognate Group: G2838 (taking of rest), G2837 (sleep)\nVariants: κοίμησις",
    2839: "κοινός (koinós | koy-nos')\n\nDerivation: probably from G4862\nStrong's: common, i.e. (literally) shared by all or several, or (ceremonially) profane\nKJV: —common, defiled, unclean, unholy.\n\nSee: G4862 \n\nCognate Group: G2842 (communicate), G2844 (companion), G2840 (call common), G4790 (communicate with), G2841 (communicate), G4791 (companion), G2843 (willing to communicate), G2839 (common)\nVariants: κοινός \nHebrew Equivalents: H259 אֶחָד, H2267 חֶבֶר",
    2840: "κοινόω (koinóō | koy-no'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2839\nStrong's: to make (or consider) profane (ceremonially)\nKJV: —call common, defile, pollute, unclean.\n\nSee: G2839 \n\nCognate Group: G2842 (communicate), G2844 (companion), G2840 (call common), G4790 (communicate with), G2841 (communicate), G4791 (companion), G2843 (willing to communicate), G2839 (common)\nVariants: κοινόω",
    2841: "κοινωνέω (koinōnéō | koy-no-neh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2844\nStrong's: to share with others (objectively or subjectively)\nKJV: —communicate, distribute, be partaker.\n\nSee: G2844 \n\nCognate Group: G2842 (communicate), G2844 (companion), G2840 (call common), G4790 (communicate with), G2841 (communicate), G4791 (companion), G2843 (willing to communicate), G2839 (common)\nVariants: κοινωνέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H977 בָּחַר, H2266 חָבַר, H6148 עָרַב",
    2842: "κοινωνία (koinōnía | koy-nohn-ee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from G2844\nStrong's: partnership, i.e. (literally) participation, or (social) intercourse, or (pecuniary) benefaction\nKJV: —(to) communicate(-ation), communion, (contri-)distribution, fellowship.\n\nSee: G2844 \n\nCognate Group: G2842 (communicate), G2844 (companion), G2840 (call common), G4790 (communicate with), G2841 (communicate), G4791 (companion), G2843 (willing to communicate), G2839 (common)\nVariants: κοινωνία \nHebrew Equivalents: H8667 תְּשׂוּמֶת",
    2843: "κοινωνικός (koinōnikós | koy-no-nee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G2844\nStrong's: communicative, i.e. (pecuniarily) liberal\nKJV: —willing to communicate.\n\nSee: G2844 \n\nCognate Group: G2842 (communicate), G2844 (companion), G2840 (call common), G4790 (communicate with), G2841 (communicate), G4791 (companion), G2843 (willing to communicate), G2839 (common)\nVariants: κοινωνικός",
    2844: "κοινωνός (koinōnós | koy-no-nos')\n\nDerivation: from G2839\nStrong's: a sharer, i.e. associate\nKJV: —companion, X fellowship, partaker, partner.\n\nSee: G2839 \n\nCognate Group: G2842 (communicate), G2844 (companion), G2840 (call common), G4790 (communicate with), G2841 (communicate), G4791 (companion), G2843 (willing to communicate), G2839 (common)\nVariants: κοινωνός \nHebrew Equivalents: H2270 חָבֵר, H2278 חֲבֶרֶת",
    2845: "κοίτη (koítē | koy'-tay)\n\nDerivation: from G2749\nStrong's: a couch; by extension, cohabitation; by implication, the male sperm\nKJV: —bed, chambering, X conceive.\n\nSee: G2749 \n\nCognate Group: G2842 (communicate), G2844 (companion), G2840 (call common), G4790 (communicate with), G2841 (communicate), G4791 (companion), G2843 (willing to communicate), G2839 (common)\nVariants: κοίτη \nHebrew Equivalents: H4904 מִשְׁכָּב, H7901 שָׁכַב, H7902 שְׁכָבָה",
    2846: "κοιτών (koitṓn | koy-tone')\n\nDerivation: from G2845\nStrong's: a bedroom\nKJV: —+ chamberlain.\n\nSee: G2845 \n\nCognate Group: G2842 (communicate), G2844 (companion), G2840 (call common), G4790 (communicate with), G2841 (communicate), G4791 (companion), G2843 (willing to communicate), G2839 (common)\nVariants: κοιτών \nHebrew Equivalents: H2315 חֶדֶר, H4747 מְקֵרָה, H4904 מִשְׁכָּב",
    2847: "κόκκινος (kókkinos | kok'-kee-nos)\n\nDerivation: from G2848 (from the kernel-shape of the insect)\nStrong's: crimson-colored\nKJV: —scarlet (colour, coloured).\n\nSee: G2848 \n\nCognate Group: G2847 (scarlet), G2848 (corn)\nVariants: κόκκινος \nHebrew Equivalents: H3758 כַּרְמִיל, H8144 שָׁנִי, H8438 תֹּולָע, H8439 תֹּולָע",
    2848: "κόκκος (kókkos | kok'-kos)\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary word\nStrong's: a kernel of seed\nKJV: —corn, grain.\n\nCognate Group: G2847 (scarlet), G2848 (corn)\nVariants: κόκκος \nHebrew Equivalents: H8438 תֹּולָע",
    2849: "κολάζω (kolázō | kol-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from κόλος (dwarf)\nStrong's: properly, to curtail, i.e. (figuratively) to chastise (or reserve for infliction)\nKJV: —punish.\n\nCognate Group: G2851 (punishment), G2849 (punish)\nVariants: κολάζω",
    2850: "κολακεία (kolakeía | kol-ak-i'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of κόλαξ (a fawner)\nStrong's: flattery\nKJV: — X flattering.\n\nCognate Group: G2850 (X flattering)\nVariants: κολακεία",
    2851: "κόλασις (kólasis | kol'-as-is)\n\nDerivation: from G2849\nStrong's: penal infliction\nKJV: —punishment, torment.\n\nSee: G2849 \n\nCognate Group: G2851 (punishment), G2849 (punish)\nVariants: κόλασις \nHebrew Equivalents: H3637 כָּלַם, H4383 מִכְשֹׁול",
    2852: "κολαφίζω (kolaphízō | kol-af-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of the base of G2849\nStrong's: to rap with the fist\nKJV: —buffet.\n\nSee: G2849 \n\nCognate Group: G2852 (buffet)\nVariants: κολαφίζω",
    2853: "κολλάω (kolláō | kol-lah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from κόλλα (\"glue\")\nStrong's: to glue, i.e. (passively or reflexively) to stick (figuratively)\nKJV: —cleave, join (self), keep company.\n\nCognate Group: G4347 (cleave), G2853 (cleave)\nVariants: κολλάω, κολλάομαι \nHebrew Equivalents: H1692 דָּבַק, H5060 נָגַע, H5066 נָגַשׁ, H5341 נָצַר, H7257 רָבַץ",
    2854: "κολλούριον (kolloúrion | kol-loo'-ree-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a presumed derivative of κολλύρα (a cake\nStrong's: prob akin to the base of G2853); properly, a poultice (as made of or in the form of crackers), i.e. (by analogy) a plaster\nKJV: — eyesalve.\n\nSee: G2853 \n\nCognate Group: G4347 (cleave), G2853 (cleave)\nVariants: κολλούριον",
    2855: "κολλυβιστής (kollybistḗs | kol-loo-bis-tace')\n\nDerivation: from a presumed derivative of κόλλυβος (a small coin\nStrong's: probably akin to G2854); a coin-dealer\nKJV: —(money-)changer.\n\nSee: G2854 \n\nCognate Group: G4347 (cleave), G2853 (cleave)\nVariants: κολλυβιστής",
    2856: "κολοβόω (kolobóō | kol-ob-o'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of the base of G2849\nStrong's: to dock, i.e. (figuratively) abridge\nKJV: —shorten.\n\nSee: G2849 \n\nCognate Group: G2856 (shorten)\nVariants: κολοβόω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7112 קָצַץ",
    2857: "Κολοσσαί (Kolossaí | kol-os-sah'-ee)\n\nDerivation: apparently feminine plural of kolossos (\"colossal\")\nStrong's: Colossæ, a place in Asia Minor\nKJV: —Colosse.\n\nCognate Group: G2856 (shorten)\nVariants: Κολοσσαί, Κολασσαί",
    2858: "Κολοσσαεύς (Kolossaeús | kol-os-sayoos')\n\nDerivation: from G2857\nStrong's: a Colossæan, (i.e. inhabitant of Colossæ\nKJV: —Colossian.\n\nSee: G2857 \n\nCognate Group: G2856 (shorten)\nVariants: Κολοσσαεύς, Κολασσαεύς G3137, G3144",
    2859: "κόλπος (kólpos | kol'-pos)\n\nDerivation: apparently a primary word\nStrong's: the bosom; by analogy, a bay\nKJV: —bosom, creek.\n\nCognate Group: G2859 (bosom)\nVariants: κόλπος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2436 חֵיק, H2651 חֹפֶן, H2684 חֹצֶן, H6747 צַלַּחַת",
    2860: "κολυμβάω (kolymbáō | kol-oom-bah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from κόλυμβος (a diver)\nStrong's: to plunge into water\nKJV: —swim.\n\nCognate Group: G2861 (pool), G2860 (swim)\nVariants: κολυμβάω",
    2861: "κολυμβήθρα (kolymbḗthra | kol-oom-bay'-thrah)\n\nDerivation: from G2860\nStrong's: a diving-place, i.e. pond for bathing (or swimming)\nKJV: —pool.\n\nSee: G2860 \n\nCognate Group: G2861 (pool), G2860 (swim)\nVariants: κολυμβήθρα \nHebrew Equivalents: H1295 בְּרֵכָה",
    2862: "κολωνία (kolōnía | kol-o-nee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: a Roman \"colony\" for veterans\nKJV: —colony.\n\nCognate Group: G2861 (pool), G2860 (swim)\nVariants: κολωνία",
    2863: "κομάω (komáō | kom-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2864\nStrong's: to wear tresses of hair\nKJV: —have long hair.\n\nSee: G2864 \n\nCognate Group: G2864 (hair), G2863 (have long hair)\nVariants: κομάω",
    2864: "κόμη (kómē | kom'-ay)\n\nDerivation: apparently from the same as G2865\nStrong's: the hair of the head (locks, as ornamental, and thus differing from G2359 ; which properly denotes merely the scalp)\nKJV: —hair.\n\nSee: G2865 \nSee: G2359 \n\nCognate Group: G2864 (hair), G2863 (have long hair)\nVariants: κόμη \nHebrew Equivalents: H6203 עֹרֶף, H6285 פֵּאָה, H6287 פְּאֵר, H6545 פֶּרַע",
    2865: "κομίζω (komízō | kom-id'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from a primary κομέω (to tend, i.e. take care of)\nStrong's: properly, to provide for, i.e. (by implication) to carry off (as if from harm; genitive case obtain)\nKJV: —bring, receive.\n\nCognate Group: G2864 (hair), G2863 (have long hair)\nVariants: κομίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2987 יְבַל, H3947 לָקַח, H5375 נָשָׂא",
    2866: "κομψότερον (kompsóteron | komp-sot'-er-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter comparative of a derivative of the base of 2865 (meaning, properly, well dressed, i.e. nice)\nStrong's: figuratively, convalescent\nKJV: —+ began to amend.\n\nCognate Group: G2864 (hair), G2863 (have long hair)\nVariants: κομψότερον",
    2867: "κονιάω (koniáō | kon-ee-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from κονία (dust\nStrong's: by analogy, lime); to whitewash\nKJV: —whiten.\n\nCognate Group: G2867 (whiten)\nVariants: κονιάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7874 שִׂיד",
    2868: "κονιορτός (koniortós | kon-ee-or-tos')\n\nDerivation: from the base of G2867 and ornumi (to \"rouse\")\nStrong's: pulverulence (as blown about)\nKJV: —dust.\n\nSee: G2867 \n\nCognate Group: G2867 (whiten)\nVariants: κονιορτός \nHebrew Equivalents: H80 אָבָק, H217 אוּר, H2563 חֹמֶר, H4671 מֹץ, H4716 מַק, H6083 עָפָר, H8229 שִׁפְעָה",
    2869: "κοπάζω (kopázō | kop-ad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from G2873\nStrong's: to tire, i.e. (figuratively) to relax\nKJV: —cease.\n\nSee: G2873 \n\nCognate Group: G2867 (whiten)\nVariants: κοπάζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2308 חָדַל, H3615 כָּלָה, H3637 כָּלַם, H6113 עָצָר, H7043 קָלַל, H7918 שָׁכַךְ, H8252 שָׁקַט, H8257 שָׁקַע, H8367 שָׁתַק",
    2870: "κοπετός (kopetós | kop-et-os')\n\nDerivation: from G2875\nStrong's: mourning (properly, by beating the breast)\nKJV: —lamentation.\n\nSee: G2875 \n\nCognate Group: G1464 (X hinder), G609 (cut off), G2870 (lamentation), G1581 (cut down), G2875 (cut down), G1465 (hinder)\nVariants: κοπετός \nHebrew Equivalents: H1065 בְּכִי, H4553 מִסְפֵּד, H5092 נְהִי",
    2871: "κοπή (kopḗ | kop-ay')\n\nDerivation: from G2875\nStrong's: cutting, i.e. carnage\nKJV: —slaughter.\n\nSee: G2875 \n\nCognate Group: G1464 (X hinder), G609 (cut off), G2870 (lamentation), G1581 (cut down), G2875 (cut down), G1465 (hinder)\nVariants: κοπή \nHebrew Equivalents: H4347 מַכָּה, H5062 נָגַף, H5221 נָכָה",
    2872: "κοπιάω (kopiáō | kop-ee-ah'-o)\n\nDerivation: from a derivative of G2873\nStrong's: to feel fatigue; by implication, to work hard\nKJV: —(bestow) labour, toil, be wearied.\n\nSee: G2873 \n\nCognate Group: G2873 (labour), G2872 (labour)\nVariants: κοπιάω \nHebrew Equivalents: H213 אוּץ, H2308 חָדַל, H2342 חוּל, H2470 חָלָה, H2490 חָלַל, H2826 חָשַׁל, H2974 יָאַל, H3021 יָגַע, H3287 יָעֵף, H3782 כָּשַׁל, H3811 לָאָה, H5774 עוּף, H5888 עָיֵף, H5999 עָמָל",
    2873: "κόπος (kópos | kop'-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2875\nStrong's: a cut, i.e. (by analogy) toil (as reducing the strength), literally or figuratively; by implication, pains\nKJV: —labour, + trouble, weariness.\n\nSee: G2875 \n\nCognate Group: G2873 (labour), G2872 (labour)\nVariants: κόπος \nHebrew Equivalents: H202 אֹון, H205 אָוֶן, H1478 גָּוַע, H2960 טֹרַח, H3015 יָגֹון, H3018 יְגִיעַ, H5999 עָמָל, H8432 תָּוֶךְ",
    2874: "κοπρία (kopría | kop-ree'-ah)\n\nDerivation: from κόπρος (ordure\nStrong's: perhaps akin to G2875); manure\nKJV: —dung(-hill).\n\nSee: G2875 \n\nCognate Group: G2873 (labour), G2872 (labour)\nVariants: κοπρία, κόπριον, κόπρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H665 אֵפֶר, H830 אַשְׁפֹּת, H1828 דֹּמֶן, H1828 דֹּמֶן, H5478 סוּחָה",
    2875: "κόπτω (kóptō | kop'-to)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to \"chop\"; specially, to beat the breast in grief\nKJV: —cut down, lament, mourn, (be-)wail. Compare the base of G5114 .\n\nSee: G5114 \n\nCognate Group: G1464 (X hinder), G609 (cut off), G2870 (lamentation), G1581 (cut down), G2875 (cut down), G1465 (hinder)\nVariants: κόπτω \nHebrew Equivalents: H622 אָסַף, H1413 גָּדַד, H1438 גָּדַע, H2179 זָנַב, H2404 חָטַב, H2672 חָצַב, H3772 כָּרַת, H3807 כָּתַת, H5062 נָגַף, H5221 נָכָה, H5594 סָפַד, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6327 פּוּץ, H6428 פָּלַשׁ, H6912 קָבַר, H6962 קוּט",
    2876: "κόραξ (kórax | kor'-ax)\n\nDerivation: perhaps from G2880\nStrong's: a crow (from its voracity)\nKJV: —raven.\n\nSee: G2880 \n\nCognate Group: G1464 (X hinder), G609 (cut off), G2870 (lamentation), G1581 (cut down), G2875 (cut down), G1465 (hinder)\nVariants: κόραξ \nHebrew Equivalents: H6158 עֹרֵב",
    2877: "κοράσιον (korásion | kor-as'-ee-on)\n\nDerivation: neuter of a presumed derivative of κόρη (a maiden)\nStrong's: a (little) girl\nKJV: —damsel, maid.\n\nCognate Group: G1464 (X hinder), G609 (cut off), G2870 (lamentation), G1581 (cut down), G2875 (cut down), G1465 (hinder)\nVariants: κοράσιον \nHebrew Equivalents: H802 אִשָּׁה, H3207 יַלְדָּה, H5288 נַעַר, H5291 נַעֲרָה",
    2878: "κορβᾶν (korbân | kor-ban') and κορβανᾶς (korbanâs | kor-ban-as')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew and Chaldee origin respectively (H7133)\nStrong's: a votive offering and the offering; a consecrated present (to the Temple fund); by extension (the latter term) the Treasury itself, i.e. the room where the contribution boxes stood\nKJV: —Corban, treasury.\nSee: H7133\n\nCognate Group: G2878 (Corban)\nVariants: κορβᾶν, κορβανᾶς, Κορβᾶν \nHebrew Equivalents: H7133 קׇרְבָּן",
    2879: "Κορέ (Koré | kor-eh')\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H7141)\nStrong's: Core (i.e. Korach), an Israelite\nKJV: —Core.\nSee: H7141\n\nCognate Group: G2878 (Corban)\nVariants: Κορέ, Κόρε \nHebrew Equivalents: H7140 קֶרַח, H7141 קֹרַח",
    2880: "κορέννυμι (korénnymi | kor-en'-noo-mee)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: to cram, i.e. glut or sate\nKJV: —eat enough, full.\n\nCognate Group: G2878 (Corban)\nVariants: κορέννυμι",
    2881: "Κορίνθιος (Korínthios | kor-in'-thee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2882\nStrong's: a Corinthian, i.e. inhabitant of Corinth\nKJV: —Corinthian.\n\nSee: G2882 \n\nCognate Group: G2878 (Corban)\nVariants: Κορίνθιος",
    2882: "Κόρινθος (Kórinthos | kor'-in-thos)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: Corinthus, a city of Greece\nKJV: —Corinth.\n\nCognate Group: G2878 (Corban)\nVariants: Κόρινθος",
    2883: "Κορνήλιος (Kornḗlios | kor-nay'-lee-os)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: Cornelius, a Roman\nKJV: —Cornelius.\n\nCognate Group: G2878 (Corban)\nVariants: Κορνήλιος",
    2884: "κόρος (kóros | kor'-os)\n\nDerivation: of Hebrew origin (H3734)\nStrong's: a cor, i.e. a specific measure\nKJV: —measure.\nSee: H3734\n\nCognate Group: G2878 (Corban)\nVariants: κόρος \nHebrew Equivalents: H2563 חֹמֶר, H3734 כֹּר",
    2885: "κοσμέω (kosméō | kos-meh'-o)\n\nDerivation: from G2889\nStrong's: to put in proper order, i.e. decorate (literally or figuratively); specially, to snuff (a wick)\nKJV: —adorn, garnish, trim.\n\nSee: G2889 \n\nCognate Group: G2889 (adorning), G2887 (of good behaviour), G2885 (adorn), G2886 (worldly)\nVariants: κοσμέω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2353 חוּר, H3259 יָעַד, H5710 עָדָה, H6186 עָרַךְ, H6822 צָפָה, H8626 תָּקַן",
    2886: "κοσμικός (kosmikós | kos-mee-kos')\n\nDerivation: from G2889 (in its secondary sense)\nStrong's: terrene (\"cosmic\"), literally (mundane) or figuratively (corrupt)\nKJV: —worldly.\n\nSee: G2889 \n\nCognate Group: G2889 (adorning), G2887 (of good behaviour), G2885 (adorn), G2886 (worldly)\nVariants: κοσμικός",
    2887: "κόσμιος (kósmios | kos'-mee-os)\n\nDerivation: from G2889 (in its primary sense)\nStrong's: orderly, i.e. decorous\nKJV: —of good behaviour, modest.\n\nSee: G2889 \n\nCognate Group: G2889 (adorning), G2887 (of good behaviour), G2885 (adorn), G2886 (worldly)\nVariants: κόσμιος, κοσμίως \nHebrew Equivalents: H8626 תָּקַן",
    2888: "κοσμοκράτωρ (kosmokrátōr | kos-mok-fat'-ore)\n\nDerivation: from G2889 and G2902\nStrong's: a world-ruler, an epithet of Satan\nKJV: —ruler.\n\nSee: G2889 \nSee: G2902 \n\nCognate Group: G2888 (ruler), G2901 (be strengthened), G3841 (Almighty), G2900 (mighty), G2903 (most excellent), G2902 (hold), G2904 (dominion)\nVariants: κοσμοκράτωρ",
    2889: "κόσμος (kósmos | kos'-mos)\n\nDerivation: probably from the base of G2865\nStrong's: orderly arrangement, i.e. decoration; by implication, the world (in a wide or narrow sense, including its inhabitants, literally or figuratively (morally))\nKJV: —adorning, world.\n\nSee: G2865 \n\nCognate Group: G2889 (adorning), G2887 (of good behaviour), G2885 (adorn), G2886 (worldly)\nVariants: κόσμος \nHebrew Equivalents: H134 אֶדֶן, H3627 כְּלִי, H4639 מַעֲשֶׂה, H5716 עֲדִי, H5716 עֲדִי, H6635 צָבָא, H8499 תְּכוּנָה, H8597 תִּפְאָרָה",
    2890: "Κούαρτος (Koúartos | koo'-ar-tos)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin (fourth)\nStrong's: Quartus, a Christian\nKJV: —Quartus.\n\nCognate Group: G2889 (adorning), G2887 (of good behaviour), G2885 (adorn), G2886 (worldly)\nVariants: Κούαρτος",
    2891: "κοῦμι (koûmi | koo'-mee)\n\nDerivation: of Chaldee origin (H6966)\nStrong's: cumi (i.e. rise!)\nKJV: —cumi.\nSee: H6966\n\nCognate Group: G2889 (adorning), G2887 (of good behaviour), G2885 (adorn), G2886 (worldly)\nVariants: κοῦμι, κοῦμ, κουμ \nHebrew Equivalents: H6965 קוּם, H6966 קוּם",
    2892: "κουστωδία (koustōdía | koos-to-dee'-ah)\n\nDerivation: of Latin origin\nStrong's: \"custody\", i.e. a Roman sentry\nKJV: —watch.\n\nCognate Group: G2889 (adorning), G2887 (of good behaviour), G2885 (adorn), G2886 (worldly)\nVariants: κουστωδία",
    2893: "κουφίζω (kouphízō | koo-fid'-zo)\n\nDerivation: from κοῦφος (light in weight)\nStrong's: to unload\nKJV: —lighten.\n\nCognate Group: G2889 (adorning), G2887 (of good behaviour), G2885 (adorn), G2886 (worldly)\nVariants: κουφίζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H7043 קָלַל",
    2894: "κόφινος (kóphinos | kof'-ee-nos)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a (small) basket\nKJV: —basket.\n\nCognate Group: G2889 (adorning), G2887 (of good behaviour), G2885 (adorn), G2886 (worldly)\nVariants: κόφινος \nHebrew Equivalents: H1731 דּוּד, H5536 סַל",
    2895: "κράββατος (krábbatos | krab'-bat-os)\n\nDerivation: probably of foreign origin\nStrong's: a mattress\nKJV: —bed.\n\nCognate Group: G2889 (adorning), G2887 (of good behaviour), G2885 (adorn), G2886 (worldly)\nVariants: κράββατος, κράβαττος",
    2896: "κράζω (krázō | krad'-zo)\n\nDerivation: a primary verb\nStrong's: properly, to \"croak\" (as a raven) or scream, i.e. (genitive case) to call aloud (shriek, exclaim, intreat)\nKJV: —cry (out).\n\nCognate Group: G2896 (cry), G2905 (cry out), G2906 (clamour), G349 (cry out)\nVariants: κράζω \nHebrew Equivalents: H2199 זָעַק, H5101 נָהַק, H6817 צָעַק, H7121 קָרָא, H7321 רוּעַ, H7581 שְׁאָגָה, H7650 שָׁבַע",
    2897: "κραιπάλη (kraipálē | krahee-pal'-ay)\n\nDerivation: probably from the same as G726\nStrong's: properly, a headache (as a seizure of pain) from drunkenness, i.e. (by implication) a debauch (by analogy, a glut)\nKJV: —surfeiting.\n\nSee: G726 \n\nCognate Group: G2896 (cry), G2905 (cry out), G2906 (clamour), G349 (cry out)\nVariants: κραιπάλη",
    2898: "κρανίον (kraníon | kran-ee'-on)\n\nDerivation: diminutive of a derivative of the base of G2768\nStrong's: a skull (\"cranium\")\nKJV: —Calvary, skull.\n\nSee: G2768 \n\nCognate Group: G2896 (cry), G2905 (cry out), G2906 (clamour), G349 (cry out)\nVariants: κρανίον \nHebrew Equivalents: H1538 גֻּלְגֹּלֶת",
    2899: "κράσπεδον (kráspedon | kras'-ped-on)\n\nDerivation: of uncertain derivation\nStrong's: a margin, i.e. (specially), a fringe or tassel\nKJV: —border, hem.\n\nCognate Group: G2899 (border)\nVariants: κράσπεδον \nHebrew Equivalents: H3671 כָּנָף, H6734 צִיצִת",
    2900: "κραταιός (krataiós | krat-ah-yos')\n\nDerivation: from G2904\nStrong's: powerful\nKJV: —mighty.\n\nSee: G2904 \n\nCognate Group: G2888 (ruler), G2901 (be strengthened), G3841 (Almighty), G2900 (mighty), G2903 (most excellent), G2902 (hold), G2904 (dominion)\nVariants: κραταιός \nHebrew Equivalents: H117 אַדִּיר, H533 אַמִּיץ, H1368 גִּבֹּור, H2388 חָזַק, H3372 יָרֵא, H4043 מָגֵן, H5794 עַז, H6105 עָצַם, H6184 עָרִיץ, H8632 תְּקֹף",
